INSERT INTO `english_note_item` VALUES (1,1,1,'sentence','My friend is outside now','我的朋友现在在外面，他第一次来 我去接他一下\nMy friend is outside now. It’s his first time here, so I’m just going to pick him up','My friend is outside now. It’s his first time here, so I’m just going to pick him up','我的朋友现在在外面，他第一次来，我去接他一下。','用于解释你要暂时离开一下。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'pick him up,first time here',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(2,1,2,'phrase','So we\'ll see. We shall see.','So we\'ll see. We shall see.\n可以翻译成 我们到时候看吧，我们走着瞧','So we\'ll see. We shall see.','我们到时候看吧 / 我们走着瞧。','带一点保留判断的语气。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'we shall see,we\'ll see',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(3,1,3,'phrase','I’m just very focused on…','I’m just very focused on…\n= 我现在很专注于……','I’m just very focused on…','我现在很专注于……','后面可接工作、学习、任务等。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'focused on',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(4,1,4,'vocab','interchange','interchange意思是：\n当动词：交换；互换；交替使用\n当名词：交流；立交枢纽 / 交通转换站','interchange','交换；互换；交替使用；交流；立交枢纽 / 交通转换站','这个词既可以作动词，也可以作名词。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'interchange',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(5,1,5,'example','interchange as a verb','These two words are often interchanged. 这两个词经常被互换使用。\nYou can interchange the labels when new people arrive. 新的人来了以后，你可以把标签换一下。','These two words are often interchanged.\nYou can interchange the labels when new people arrive.','这两个词经常被互换使用。新的人来了以后，你可以把标签换一下。','interchange 作动词。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'interchange,verb',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(6,1,6,'chunk','swap them / switch them out','• swap them\n• switch them out','swap them\nswitch them out','把它们换掉','和 interchange 相关的自然替换表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'swap,switch out',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(7,1,7,'example','interchange as a noun','an interchange of ideas 思想交流\na motorway interchange 高速公路立交枢纽','an interchange of ideas\na motorway interchange','思想交流；高速公路立交枢纽','interchange 作名词时的例子。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'interchange,noun',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(8,1,8,'vocab','hawthorn','hawthorn\n山楂','hawthorn','山楂','食物词汇。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'hawthorn',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(9,1,9,'example','hawthorn is very sour','hawthorn is very sour 山楂非常酸','hawthorn is very sour','山楂非常酸。','描述味道。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'sour,hawthorn',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(10,1,10,'example','plums or prunes','This is kind of like eating plums or prunes.\n• plum = 李子\n• prune = 西梅 / 李子干（常指干的）','This is kind of like eating plums or prunes.\nplum\nprune','这有点像在吃李子或西梅。plum = 李子；prune = 西梅 / 李子干。','用来帮助理解 hawthorn 的味道和口感。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'plum,prune',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(11,1,11,'sentence','Last week, we had a lot of food programs...','Last week, we had a lot of food programs, so I was running around like a chicken with my head cut off trying to get everything organized. And tonight is gonna be exactly the same, because we are short-staffed and we have an event that has 115 people coming.','Last week, we had a lot of food programs, so I was running around like a chicken with my head cut off trying to get everything organized. And tonight is gonna be exactly the same, because we are short-staffed and we have an event that has 115 people coming.','上周我们有很多餐饮活动，所以我忙得团团转，想把一切都安排好。今晚估计也一样，因为我们人手不足，而且有一个会来 115 人的活动。','完整场景句。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'food programs,short-staffed,115 people',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(12,1,12,'correction','food programs','food programs\n更自然的说法\nwe had a lot of food events\nor\nwe had a lot of food-related activities','we had a lot of food events\nwe had a lot of food-related activities','更自然的说法：我们有很多餐饮活动 / 餐饮相关活动。','food programs 在这个语境下不如 food events / food-related activities 自然。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'food events,food-related activities',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(13,1,13,'chunk','run around','run around means:\n• 忙来忙去\n• 到处跑\n• 忙得团团转','run around','忙来忙去；到处跑；忙得团团转','非常常见的口语短语。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'run around',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(14,1,14,'idiom','like a chicken with my head cut off','I was running around like a chicken with my head cut off\nmeans:\n我忙得像无头苍蝇一样乱转。\n• 直译：像一只被砍了头的鸡\n• 意译：像无头苍蝇一样','I was running around like a chicken with my head cut off','我忙得像无头苍蝇一样乱转。','一个非常生动的习语，实际翻译时常意译成“无头苍蝇”。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'idiom,chicken with my head cut off',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(15,1,15,'grammar','trying to get everything organized','trying to get everything organized\n\nbe + doing + trying to + verb\n\n• 把一切安排好\n• 把所有事情整理妥当','trying to get everything organized','把一切安排好；把所有事情整理妥当','这里可以顺手记 be + doing + trying to + verb 的表达方式。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'get everything organized',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(16,1,16,'vocab','gonna','And tonight is gonna be exactly the same\ngonna = going to in speech','And tonight is gonna be exactly the same','今晚也会完全一样。','gonna = going to 的口语形式。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'gonna,going to',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(17,1,17,'vocab','short-staffed','short-staffed means:\n• 人手不足\n• 缺人','short-staffed','人手不足；缺人','工作场景高频表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'short-staffed',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(18,1,18,'correction','115 people coming','we have an event that has 115 people coming\nMore natural versions would be:\nwe have an event with 115 people coming\nwe have an event with 115 attendees\nwe have 115 people coming to an event tonight','we have an event with 115 people coming\nwe have an event with 115 attendees\nwe have 115 people coming to an event tonight','更自然的表达：我们有一个会来 115 人的活动。','更自然的改写。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'115 attendees',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(19,1,19,'chunk','Useful chunks to remember','These are the best chunks to learn from this sentence:\n• run around\n• like a chicken with my head cut off\n• get everything organized\n• be exactly the same\n• be short-staffed\n• have an event coming up\n• have 115 people coming','run around\nlike a chicken with my head cut off\nget everything organized\nbe exactly the same\nbe short-staffed\nhave an event coming up\nhave 115 people coming','值得记忆的表达块','适合背诵和复用。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'useful chunks',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(20,1,20,'sentence','So we have a guest speaker this evening...','So we have a guest speaker this evening. Jamil is his first name, and he\'s doing a presentation called What\'s the Economy About Anyway? Yeah, so it\'s a free event, you just have to book in, and it\'s from, I think, 6:30 till 8 o\'clock tonight, and they\'re going to be in the big room just across.','So we have a guest speaker this evening. Jamil is his first name, and he\'s doing a presentation called What\'s the Economy About Anyway? It\'s a free event, you just have to book in, and they\'re going to be in the big room just across.','今晚有一位嘉宾讲者，名字叫 Jamil。他会做一个题为“经济到底是怎么回事？”的演讲。这是个免费活动，你只需要预约登记，他们会在对面那间大房间。','活动介绍整句。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'guest speaker,book in,presentation',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(21,1,21,'vocab','guest speaker','guest speaker = 嘉宾讲者 / 特邀演讲者','guest speaker','嘉宾讲者；特邀演讲者','活动、课堂都很常用。','We have a guest speaker today.\nTonight’s guest speaker is from Wellington.',NULL,NULL,'guest speaker',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(22,1,22,'phrase','do a presentation','do a presentation = 做一个展示 / 做一个演讲 / 做一个报告','do a presentation','做一个展示；做一个演讲；做一个报告','presentation 场景高频搭配。','She’s doing a presentation on climate change.\nHe’s doing a presentation called “Introduction to GIS.”',NULL,NULL,'do a presentation',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(23,1,23,'phrase','called ...','called … = 叫做…… / 题为……','called ...','叫做……；题为……','介绍标题时常用。','He’s doing a presentation called “Introduction to GIS.”',NULL,NULL,'called,title',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(24,1,24,'phrase','What’s the Economy About Anyway?','What’s the Economy About Anyway?\n这里 anyway 不是“无论如何”，而是语气词，表示：\n• 到底\n• 说到底\n• 究竟是怎么回事','What’s the Economy About Anyway?','经济到底是怎么回事？','anyway 在这里是语气词，不是“无论如何”。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'anyway',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(25,1,25,'phrase','book in','book in 在这里就是：\n预约登记 / 预订一个位置\n更自然书面一点可以说：\n• You just need to book in.\n• You just have to register.','book in\nYou just need to book in.\nYou just have to register.','预约登记；预订一个位置','新西兰日常很实用。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'book in,register',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(26,1,26,'phrase','the big room just across','the big room just across = 就在对面那间大房间','the big room just across','就在对面那间大房间','很自然的场地位置表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'big room just across',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(27,1,27,'sentence','the maximum number of people we can have in that room','the maximum number of people we can have in that room\n那个房间最多能容纳的人数','the maximum number of people we can have in that room','那个房间最多能容纳的人数','描述场地容量。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'maximum number',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(28,1,28,'phrase','show up','So we’ll see if they all show up\nshow up = 到场；出现；来了','So we’ll see if they all show up\nshow up','我们到时候看看他们会不会都来；到场；出现；来了','show up 是高频口语短语。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'show up',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(29,1,29,'phrase','I reckon','I reckon means:\n• I think\n• I guess\n• In my opinion\n= 我觉得…… / 我估计……','I reckon','我觉得……；我估计……','在新西兰、澳大利亚和非正式英式口语里很常见。','I reckon they will all show up.',NULL,NULL,'I reckon',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(30,1,30,'phrase','with everything happening right now','with everything happening right now\nThis means:\n考虑到现在发生的这些事情\nor\n在目前这种情况下','with everything happening right now','考虑到现在发生的这些事情；在目前这种情况下','表达当前整体情境。','With everything going on right now, people are stressed.\nWith everything happening at work, I’m really busy.',NULL,NULL,'with everything happening right now',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(31,1,31,'chunk','Useful chunks to remember','These are the best pieces to copy:\n• the maximum number of people\n• we can have in that room\n• we’ve got 115\n• we’ll see if they all show up\n• I reckon…\n• with everything happening right now','the maximum number of people\nwe can have in that room\nwe’ve got 115\nwe’ll see if they all show up\nI reckon…\nwith everything happening right now','值得记忆的表达块','适合直接背诵复用。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'useful chunks',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(32,1,32,'phrase','a slightly polished version','A slightly polished version 的意思是：一个稍微更润色过的版本','a slightly polished version','一个稍微更润色过的版本','常用于说明“我把句子稍微改自然了一点”。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'polished version',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(33,1,33,'sentence','And that one\'s not fully booked yet...','And that one\'s not fully booked yet, which I\'m shocked. I thought that one would have just been, like, booked down like a week. That one\'s only half booked, so still like 70 people.','And that one\'s not fully booked yet, which I\'m shocked. I thought that one would have just been booked out. That one\'s only half booked, so still like 70 people.','那个活动还没完全订满，这让我很惊讶。我本来以为一周前就应该满了。现在只订了一半，大概 70 人。','活动报名场景句。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'fully booked,half booked',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(34,1,34,'vocab','fully booked','fully booked = 订满了 / 满员了','fully booked','订满了；满员了','酒店、课程、活动都常用。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'fully booked',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(35,1,35,'phrase','which I’m shocked by','which I’m shocked by = 这让我很惊讶','which I’m shocked by','这让我很惊讶','表达惊讶。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'shocked by',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(36,1,36,'phrase','I thought that one would’ve already been...','I thought that one would have just been…\n更自然说法通常是：\n• I thought that one would’ve already been…\n• I thought that one would’ve been…','I thought that one would’ve already been...\nI thought that one would’ve been...','我本来以为它早就已经……了','更自然的缩略表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'would’ve',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(37,1,37,'vocab','booked out','booked out = 订满 / 约满','booked out','订满；约满','和 fully booked 接近。','It was booked out weeks ago.\nThe event got booked out really quickly.',NULL,NULL,'booked out',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(38,1,38,'correction','I forget where he’s originally from','I forget what he’s originally\nThis part is not complete English. It was probably meant to be:\n• I forget where he’s originally from\n• I forget what his background is','I forget where he’s originally from.\nI forget what his background is.','我忘了他原本是哪里人；我忘了他的背景是什么','原句不完整，这里是更自然的修正。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'originally from,background',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(39,1,39,'phrase','about 10 years apart','about 10 years apart\nA very useful expression.\n• We’re two years apart.\n• They were born five years apart.\n• They went there about ten years apart.','We’re two years apart.\nThey were born five years apart.\nThey went there about ten years apart.','相差十年左右','表示年龄、经历、时间上的差距。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'years apart',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(40,1,40,'phrase','give someone a tour of...','give someone a tour of…\n= show someone around a place\n• I gave him a tour of the campus.\n• She’s showing them around town.','give someone a tour of...\nI gave him a tour of the campus.\nShe’s showing them around town.','带某人参观……','也可以说 show someone around。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'tour of,show around',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(41,1,41,'vocab','comic book','comic book = 漫画书','comic book','漫画书','最常见说法。','I bought a comic book yesterday.\nHe loves reading comic books.',NULL,NULL,'comic book',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(42,1,42,'vocab','graphic novel','graphic novel = 图像小说 / 漫画小说（更完整、更长）','graphic novel','图像小说 / 漫画小说（更完整、更长）','通常比 comic book 更长、更完整。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'graphic novel',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(43,1,43,'sentence','A lot of comic books are written in capital letters.','A lot of comic books are written in capital letters.','A lot of comic books are written in capital letters.','好多漫画书都是用大写字母写的。','例句。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'capital letters',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(44,1,44,'vocab','uppercase','uppercase = 大写字母的；也可以当名词，表示大写','uppercase','大写字母的；大写','typing / 排版 / 表格 / 密码要求里很常见。','Please write your name in uppercase.\nThis word is in uppercase.\nWrite in uppercase.\nWrite in capital letters.',NULL,NULL,'uppercase,capital letters',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(45,1,45,'sentence','We still have two more sessions.','We still have two more sessions.\nWe still have one more class.\nWe still have two more meetings.\nWe still have three more lessons.','We still have two more sessions.\nWe still have one more class.\nWe still have two more meetings.\nWe still have three more lessons.','我们还有两节课。我们还有一节课 / 两个会议 / 三节课。','two more 的高频句型。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'two more sessions',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(46,1,46,'phrase','the last day of school term','the last day of school term = 学期最后一天','the last day of school term','学期最后一天','school term = 学期。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'school term',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(47,1,47,'phrase','the very last week of April','the very last week of April = 四月的最后一个星期','the very last week of April','四月的最后一个星期','very 在这里起强调作用。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'the very last',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(48,1,48,'vocab','send-off','send-off = 送别 / 临别告别 / 临行前的 farewell','send-off','送别；临别告别；临行前的 farewell','分别场景常用。','They gave him a great send-off.\nThis is your send-off before the holidays.',NULL,NULL,'send-off',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(49,1,49,'vocab','strips','strips 常见意思是：长条；细条；纸条；布条','strips','长条；细条；纸条；布条','strip 的复数。','paper strips\nstrips of cloth\nstrips of bacon\na strip of paper',NULL,NULL,'strips,strip',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(50,1,50,'phrase','shopping strip','shopping strip = 一排商店 / 商业街一带','shopping strip','一排商店；商业街一带','澳新英语中也会见到。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'shopping strip',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(51,1,51,'sentence','they all have different prompts on them','they all have different prompts on them\ndifferent prompts = 不同的提示问题 / 不同的话题引导','they all have different prompts on them','它们上面都有不同的提示问题 / 话题引导','课堂活动说明。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'prompts',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(52,1,52,'sentence','We can kind of do it in two different ways.','We can kind of do it in two different ways.','We can kind of do it in two different ways.','我们大概可以用两种不同的方法来做。','用于说明活动方式。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'two different ways',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(53,1,53,'phrase','pair someone up','pair someone up = 把某人两两分组 / 配对','pair someone up','把某人两两分组；配对','课堂和活动场景高频表达。','I’ll pair you up.\nYou’ll be paired up with a partner.',NULL,NULL,'pair up',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(54,1,54,'phrase','grab a question strip at random','grab a question strip at random = 随机拿一张问题纸条','grab a question strip at random','随机拿一张问题纸条','at random = 随机地。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'at random',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(55,1,55,'vocab','basically','basically = 从基本上说 / 简单来说 / 说白了 / 其实就是','basically','从基本上说；简单来说；说白了；其实就是','非常高频的口语解释词。','Basically, we need to finish this part first.\nSo basically, this system stores trap and catch data.\nSo basically, the project needs to be simplified.\nHe’s basically the leader of the group.\nThat’s basically what I mean.',NULL,NULL,'basically',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(56,1,56,'phrase','a wee discussion','a wee discussion = 稍微讨论一下 / 小小讨论一下','a wee discussion','稍微讨论一下；小小讨论一下','wee 在 NZ / Scottish / some British English 里很常见。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'wee discussion',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(57,1,57,'phrase','see how you guys get on','see how you guys get on = 看看你们做得怎么样','see how you guys get on','看看你们做得怎么样','get on 在这里指 do / manage / progress。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'get on',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51',1,'2026-04-04 16:09:51'),(58,1,58,'sentence','It can help strengthen the muscles in your mouth...','It can help strengthen the muscles in your mouth, which can improve your pronunciation.\n能加强你的口腔肌肉, 这将非常有利于自己的发音','It can help strengthen the muscles in your mouth, which can improve your pronunciation.','能加强你的口腔肌肉，这将非常有利于自己的发音。','适合讲发音训练。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'strengthen the muscles,pronunciation',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(59,1,59,'vocab','pharmacy technician','pharmacy technician = 药房技术员 / 药剂技术员，主要是协助药剂师','pharmacy technician','药房技术员 / 药剂技术员','主要协助药剂师。','She works as a pharmacy technician.\nA pharmacy technician helped me at the counter.',NULL,NULL,'pharmacy technician',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(60,1,60,'vocab','pharmacist','pharmacist = 药剂师，更高级的','pharmacist','药剂师','比 pharmacy technician 更高级。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'pharmacist',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(61,1,61,'sentence','I started learning English when I was quite young...','I started learning English when I was quite young, about 10 years old. But back then, we mainly focused on reading, writing, and exams, so I didn’t get much chance to practise speaking. The last time I really studied English before recently was at university, when I studied it for about two years during my bachelor’s degree. After graduation, I had a long break and didn’t study English at all. Then, about four years ago, I started learning it again, but I mostly just memorised vocabulary and didn’t practise speaking very much.','I started learning English when I was quite young, about 10 years old. But back then, we mainly focused on reading, writing, and exams, so I didn’t get much chance to practise speaking. The last time I really studied English before recently was at university, when I studied it for about two years during my bachelor’s degree. After graduation, I had a long break and didn’t study English at all. Then, about four years ago, I started learning it again, but I mostly just memorised vocabulary and didn’t practise speaking very much.','我大概十岁时开始学英语。但那时候我们主要专注于阅读、写作和考试，所以我几乎没有机会练口语。最近之前，我上一次真正系统学英语是在大学本科期间，大概学了两年。毕业后我有很长一段时间完全没学。然后大概四年前，我又开始学了，但主要只是背单词，没有怎么练口语。','适合自我介绍、学习背景口语。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'started learning English,practise speaking',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(62,1,62,'sentence','Because AI technology has been advancing so quickly recently...','Because AI technology has been advancing so quickly recently, I think it’s bad news for software engineers. Even people without an AI background can now write code. I think this means the advantage software engineers used to have is smaller than before.','Because AI technology has been advancing so quickly recently, I think it’s bad news for software engineers. Even people without an AI background can now write code. I think this means the advantage software engineers used to have is smaller than before.','由于最近 AI 技术发展得很快，我觉得这对软件工程师来说是个坏消息。即使没有 AI 背景的人现在也能写代码。我觉得这意味着软件工程师过去拥有的优势比以前小了。','职业发展观点表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'AI technology,software engineers',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(63,1,63,'sentence','So the job market is quite tough.','So the job market is quite tough.','So the job market is quite tough.','所以就业市场挺艰难的。','简洁有力的总结句。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'job market',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(64,1,64,'sentence','I take the 820 bus to Lincoln University...','I take the 820 bus to Lincoln University. Actually, Rolleston isn’t very far away, but the bus doesn’t go directly there. It goes around the town, so it takes me about 40 minutes to get to school.','I take the 820 bus to Lincoln University. Actually, Rolleston isn’t very far away, but the bus doesn’t go directly there. It goes around the town, so it takes me about 40 minutes to get to school.','我坐 820 路公交去林肯大学。其实 Rolleston 不算远，但公交不是直达。它会绕镇子，所以我大概要花 40 分钟到学校。','通勤表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'820 bus,Lincoln University',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(65,1,65,'sentence','What we’re going to do now is this...','What we’re going to do now is this: I’m going to give each of you a question card. This will be a standing activity so that you can swap partners more easily. First, you’ll start with a different person from the one you were just with. After a few minutes, you’ll exchange your question cards with your partner, find a new partner, and continue the conversation using those questions.','What we’re going to do now is this: I’m going to give each of you a question card. This will be a standing activity so that you can swap partners more easily. First, you’ll start with a different person from the one you were just with. After a few minutes, you’ll exchange your question cards with your partner, find a new partner, and continue the conversation using those questions.','我们现在要做的是：我会给你们每人一张问题卡。这会是一个站着进行的活动，这样你们更容易交换搭档。首先，你们会和刚才不同的人开始。几分钟后，你们会和搭档交换问题卡，再找一个新搭档，继续用这些问题聊天。','课堂活动说明整句。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'question card,swap partners',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(66,1,66,'phrase','What we’re gonna do now is…','What we’re gonna do now is…\n现在我们要做的是……','What we’re gonna do now is…','现在我们要做的是……','口语版活动说明开头。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'gonna do now',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(67,1,67,'phrase','exchange the questions','exchange the questions\n交换问题卡','exchange the questions','交换问题卡','课堂活动表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'exchange the questions',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(68,1,68,'phrase','I really put you to work','I really put you to work 的意思是：\n我真是让你忙起来了。\n或者更自然一点：我真是让你干了不少活。','I really put you to work.','我真是让你忙起来了 / 我真让你干了不少活。','带一点抱歉和感谢的语气。','I really put you to work today.\nSorry, I really put you to work.',NULL,NULL,'put you to work',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(69,1,69,'sentence','I study English outside class every day...','I study English outside class every day because there are only a few months left before I graduate. I need to prepare for future job interviews. On the one hand, I need to expand my vocabulary, including both everyday English and professional vocabulary. On another hand, I also practise speaking and listening to improve my communication skills, because I know I’ll face challenges in job interviews. So I feel quite worried about my future.','I study English outside class every day because there are only a few months left before I graduate. I need to prepare for future job interviews. On the one hand, I need to expand my vocabulary, including both everyday English and professional vocabulary. On another hand, I also practise speaking and listening to improve my communication skills, because I know I’ll face challenges in job interviews. So I feel quite worried about my future.','我每天在课外学英语，因为离毕业只剩几个月了。我需要为未来的求职面试做准备。一方面，我需要扩大词汇量，包括日常英语和专业词汇。另一方面，我也练习口语和听力来提高沟通能力，因为我知道求职面试中会遇到挑战。所以我对未来挺担心的。','学习计划和求职准备表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'outside class,job interviews',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(70,1,70,'phrase','serve customers','serve customers = 服务顾客\nhelp customers = 帮助顾客','serve customers\nhelp customers','服务顾客；帮助顾客','服务场景基础表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'serve customers,help customers',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(71,1,71,'sentence','I have the opposite opinion to yours.','I have the opposite opinion to yours.\n我有和你相反的想法','I have the opposite opinion to yours.','我有和你相反的想法。','礼貌表达不同意见。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'opposite opinion',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(72,1,72,'sentence','My partner asked me which I think is more difficult...','My partner asked me which I think is more difficult: vocabulary or grammar. I said vocabulary is more difficult for me because it feels almost unlimited, whereas grammar is more like a set of rules. Once you learn and remember the rules, you can apply them in real-life conversations. But vocabulary is much wider, so for me, vocabulary is harder.','My partner asked me which I think is more difficult: vocabulary or grammar. I said vocabulary is more difficult for me because it feels almost unlimited, whereas grammar is more like a set of rules. Once you learn and remember the rules, you can apply them in real-life conversations. But vocabulary is much wider, so for me, vocabulary is harder.','我的搭档问我词汇和语法哪个更难。我说词汇对我来说更难，因为它感觉几乎是无限的，而语法更像一套规则。一旦你学会并记住这些规则，就可以把它们应用到真实对话中。但词汇范围更广，所以对我来说词汇更难。','学习讨论表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'vocabulary,grammar',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(73,1,73,'phrase','pop in','Do you want to pop here ?\n• go quickly\n• come quickly\n• drop by briefly\nCan you pop in for a minute? 你能过来一下吗？','Can you pop in for a minute?','你能过来一下吗？','pop in / pop over 这类表达在 NZ / UK 口语里很自然。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'pop in',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(74,1,74,'phrase','be mindful of that','be mindful of that\n= 注意这一点 / 对这一点很留意','be mindful of that','注意这一点；对这一点很留意','很适合表达自己在有意识调整某件事。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'mindful of that',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(75,1,75,'example','I try to be very mindful of that...','I try to be very mindful of that because I speak very fast.','I try to be very mindful of that because I speak very fast.','我会很注意这一点，因为我说得很快。','结合 mindful 的自然例句。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'mindful,speak very fast',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(76,1,76,'sentence','Sometimes I can understand what other people are saying...','Sometimes I can understand what other people are saying because of the situation or the context, but without those clues, it’s hard for me to understand what they mean.','Sometimes I can understand what other people are saying because of the situation or the context, but without those clues, it’s hard for me to understand what they mean.','有时候我能因为场景或上下文而听懂别人在说什么，但如果没有这些线索，我就很难理解他们的意思。','描述听力理解困难的自然表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'context,clues',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(77,1,77,'sentence','I think the best age for a child to learn another language...','I think the best age for a child to learn another language is around three or four years old, because they don’t feel much pressure when learning languages. They just imitate and copy what other people say. I think that’s a very natural process.','I think the best age for a child to learn another language is around three or four years old, because they don’t feel much pressure when learning languages. They just imitate and copy what other people say. I think that’s a very natural process.','我觉得孩子学另一门语言最好的年龄大概是三四岁，因为他们学语言时不会感觉太大压力。他们只是模仿和复制别人说的话。我觉得这是一个很自然的过程。','教育和语言学习话题表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'best age,learn another language',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(78,1,78,'phrase','It’s okay to learn whenever you want.','But I think it’s okay to learn whenever you want.\nBut I think it’s fine whenever you want to start.','But I think it’s okay to learn whenever you want.\nBut I think it’s fine whenever you want to start.','但我觉得你想什么时候学都可以。/ 你想什么时候开始都行。','鼓励性表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'whenever you want',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(79,1,79,'correction','I didn’t hear too much of our native language speaking through','I didn’t hear too much of our native language speaking through','I didn’t hear too much of our native language speaking through.','我没有听到太多我们母语的痕迹透出来。','原句略生硬，但大意是“没太听出母语口音/母语影响”。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'native language coming through',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(80,1,80,'phrase','good work on that','good work on that = 这点做得不错','good work on that','这点做得不错。','反馈表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'good work on that',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(81,1,81,'phrase','stick to English','sticking to English = 坚持说英语 / 一直用英语\nLet’s stick to English.\nI didn’t hear much of your native language coming through, so good job sticking to English.','Let’s stick to English.\nI didn’t hear much of your native language coming through, so good job sticking to English.','坚持说英语 / 一直用英语。','课堂语言练习场景非常实用。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'stick to English',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(82,1,82,'phrase','blow out the candle','blow out the candle = 吹灭蜡烛','blow out the candle','吹灭蜡烛','生日场景常见。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'blow out the candle',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(83,1,83,'phrase','remind someone to do something','Parents keep reminding their child to be polite.\nremind someone to do something = 提醒某人做某事','Parents keep reminding their child to be polite.\nremind someone to do something','提醒某人做某事','高频固定搭配。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'remind someone to do something',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(84,1,84,'vocab','goodie bag / goody bag','goodie bag / goody bag = 礼品袋；小礼包；伴手小袋','goodie bag / goody bag','礼品袋；小礼包；伴手小袋','两种拼写都常见。','The kids each got a goody bag at the party.\nWe prepared goody bags for the guests.',NULL,NULL,'goodie bag,goody bag',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(85,1,85,'phrase','falling out of fashion','falling out of fashion = 越来越不流行','falling out of fashion','越来越不流行','时尚和趋势类表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'fall out of fashion',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(86,1,86,'idiom','over the hill','I\'m already over the hill\n我都已经不年轻了。','I\'m already over the hill.','我都已经不年轻了。','通常带一点自嘲，不一定真的很老。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'over the hill',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(87,1,87,'phrase','trip around the sun','another trip around the sun = 又过了一年 / 又过了一个生日年','another trip around the sun','又过了一年 / 又过了一个生日年','生日表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'trip around the sun',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(88,1,88,'phrase','Congrats on another successful trip around the sun.','Congrats on another successful trip around the sun.','Congrats on another successful trip around the sun.','恭喜你又成功绕太阳转了一圈。','很适合生日祝福。','Congrats!\nCongratulations!',NULL,NULL,'congrats,trip around the sun',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(89,1,89,'phrase','got tied up with sb','got tied up with sb\n这个场景适合用于 work meetings clients tasks phone calls','got tied up with sb','被某事缠住 / 耽搁住','多用于工作、会议、客户、任务、电话。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'got tied up',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(90,1,90,'phrase','got held up talking to my friend','got held up talking to my friend\ngot caught up talking with my friend','got held up talking to my friend\ngot caught up talking with my friend','因为和朋友说话被耽搁了','比 got tied up with sb 更适合朋友聊天场景。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'got held up,got caught up',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(91,1,91,'vocab','bottom line','Bottom line 的意思是：\n最重要的一点；归根结底；最终结果 / 最后的结论；利润底线 / 净利润','bottom line','最重要的一点；归根结底；最终结论；净利润','一词多义，口语最常见前两种。','Bottom line, we need more time.\nThe bottom line is that the project failed because of poor planning.\nThe company’s bottom line improved this year.\nBottom line, I don’t trust him.\nThe bottom line is we have to make a decision today.',NULL,NULL,'bottom line',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(92,1,92,'sentence','I\'d like to have just a small get together at the house.','I\'d like to have just a small get together at the house.\nis it a surprise party','I\'d like to have just a small get together at the house.\nIs it a surprise party?','我想就在家里办一个小型聚会。是惊喜派对吗？','聚会场景表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'get together,surprise party',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(93,1,93,'phrase','holiday gathering','holiday gathering = 节日聚会','holiday gathering','节日聚会','比 party 更温和自然。','We’re having a holiday gathering this weekend.\nIt was a small holiday gathering with family and friends.',NULL,NULL,'holiday gathering',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(94,1,94,'phrase','Do you need me to bring anything?','Do you need me to bring anything?','Do you need me to bring anything?','需要我带什么东西来吗？','赴约和聚会前很实用。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'bring anything',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(95,1,95,'vocab','ease','ease 可以是：\n动词 = 缓解，减轻\n名词 = 轻松，舒适','ease','缓解；减轻；轻松；舒适','可以作动词，也可以作名词。','ease the pain\nease the burden\nease tension\nwith ease\nfeel at ease',NULL,NULL,'ease',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(96,1,96,'phrase','ease the burden','this can help to ease the burden','this can help to ease the burden','这可以帮助减轻负担。','高频搭配。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'ease the burden',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(97,1,97,'phrase','with ease','with ease = 轻松地，毫不费力地','with ease','轻松地；毫不费力地','名词用法。','She passed the exam with ease.',NULL,NULL,'with ease',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(98,1,98,'phrase','feel at ease','feel at ease = 感到放松自在','feel at ease','感到放松自在','常见固定搭配。','He made me feel at ease.',NULL,NULL,'feel at ease',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(99,1,99,'phrase','all the other details will be in the invitation','all the other details will be in the invitation','all the other details will be in the invitation','其他细节都会写在邀请函里。','发邀请时很实用。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'invitation,details',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(100,1,100,'phrase','in moderation','in moderation = 适量地 / 有节制地','in moderation','适量地；有节制地','饮食、喝酒、运动等场景高频。','Coffee is fine in moderation.\nEverything is okay in moderation.\nEat sweets in moderation.',NULL,NULL,'in moderation',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(101,1,101,'phrase','it works for so many things in life','it works for so many things in life','it works for so many things in life','它适用于生活中的很多事情。','适合总结一个原则适用面很广。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'works for so many things in life',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(102,1,102,'phrase','a game changer','a game changer','a game changer','一个能改变局面的东西 / 巨大的改变','常用于技术、工具、家庭、效率等场景。','Video calling has been a game changer for my family, especially when I lived abroad.',NULL,NULL,'game changer',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(103,1,103,'vocab','impact','impact\n常见搭配：\nhave an impact on\nmake an impact\na major impact\nthe impacts of …','impact\nhave an impact on\nmake an impact\na major impact\nthe impacts of …','影响','抽象地说影响时常用单数；强调多种具体影响时可用 impacts。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'impact,make an impact',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(104,1,104,'phrase','at my fingertips','at my fingertips = easily available or accessible','at my fingertips','触手可及；很容易获得；了如指掌','既可表示资源触手可及，也可表示对系统很熟悉。','I have all the information at my fingertips.\nWith the internet, knowledge is at our fingertips.\nShe has the whole system at her fingertips.',NULL,NULL,'at my fingertips',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(105,1,105,'vocab','tragic','tragic = 悲剧的','tragic','悲剧的','基础词汇。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'tragic',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(106,1,106,'phrase','there is plenty of food to go around','there is plenty of food to go around','There is plenty of food to go around.','有很多食物，够大家分。','to go around = 够分给大家 / 足够每个人都有。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'go around',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(107,1,107,'phrase','stay on top of things','to stay on top of things = 把事情都掌控住 / 把事情都安排好 / 跟上所有要处理的事','stay on top of things','把事情都掌控住；安排好；跟上所有要处理的事','工作和生活场景都很常用。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'stay on top of things',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(108,1,108,'sentence','A digital calendar really helps me stay organized...','A digital calendar really helps me stay organized, not be late for things, and know what’s going on.\nThe calendar helps me stay on top of things at work.','A digital calendar really helps me stay organized, not be late for things, and know what’s going on.\nThe calendar helps me stay on top of things at work.','数字日历真的能帮助我安排好事情、不迟到，也知道最近发生什么。它能帮助我把工作上的事情都掌控住。','整合后的自然表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'digital calendar,stay organized',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(109,1,109,'phrase','not be late','not be late\nhelp 后面通常接：\nhelp someone do something\nhelp someone be something','not be late','不迟到','顺便复习 help 的搭配。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'not be late',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(110,1,110,'phrase','open up','open up\nIt opened up a whole new world.\nVirtual learning opened up a whole new world for me.','open up\nIt opened up a whole new world.\nVirtual learning opened up a whole new world for me.','打开；开启；打开一个全新的世界','非常实用的抽象表达。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'open up,a whole new world',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(111,1,111,'phrase','back in the day','back in the day = 以前 / 当年 / 从前那时候','back in the day','以前；当年；从前那时候','用于谈过去。','Back in the day, we didn’t have smartphones.\nI used to play basketball a lot back in the day.',NULL,NULL,'back in the day',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29',1,'2026-04-04 16:11:29'),(112,2,1,'grammar','I want you to think back to when ...','I want you to think back to when ...','I want you to think back to when ...','我想让你回想一下……的时候。','固定句型是 want someone to do something。','I want you to think back to when you first started learning English.',NULL,NULL,'think back to,want someone to do something',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(113,2,2,'phrase','for context','for context','for context','补充一下背景；给你一点背景信息。','常用于口语和写作中补充背景。','For context, I have been in New Zealand for about a year.',NULL,NULL,'for context,background',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(114,2,3,'phrase','As far as freedom is concerned, ...','As far as freedom is concerned, ...','As far as freedom is concerned, ...','就自由而言，……','也可以说 As far as freedom goes 或 When it comes to freedom。','As far as freedom is concerned, New Zealand is a good place to live.',NULL,NULL,'as far as freedom is concerned,when it comes to',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(115,2,4,'phrase','around my neighborhood','around my neighborhood','around my neighborhood','在我家附近；在我住的社区周围。','很自然的地点表达。','There are a lot of parks around my neighborhood.',NULL,NULL,'around my neighborhood,neighborhood',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(116,2,5,'phrase','as long as','as long as','as long as','只要……','最常见意思是“只要……”。','As long as you keep practising, your English will improve.',NULL,NULL,'as long as,condition',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(117,2,6,'phrase','be cautious with / be cautious about','be cautious with / be cautious about','be cautious with / be cautious about','在……方面很谨慎；对……很谨慎。','cautious with + 名词；cautious about + doing / 某件事。','They were very cautious with money. / They were cautious about making a decision.',NULL,NULL,'cautious with,cautious about',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(118,2,7,'sentence','We had a couple of shady characters in our neighborhood.','We had a couple of shady characters in our neighborhood.','We had a couple of shady characters in our neighborhood.','我们社区里有几个可疑的人。','a couple of 是固定搭配；shady characters 指可疑的人。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'a couple of,shady characters',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(119,2,8,'vocab','sleepover','sleepover','sleepover','在别人家过夜的小聚会。','常见于孩子、青少年之间。','I went to a few sleepovers when I was a kid.',NULL,NULL,'sleepover,stay over',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(120,2,9,'sentence','Get off our property.','Get off our property.','Get off our property.','离开我们的地盘。','说私人地盘、私人区域时很常用。','Get off our property right now.',NULL,NULL,'get off our property,property',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(121,2,10,'phrase','at that point','at that point','at that point','在那个时候；到那个节点；在那个阶段。','比 at that time 更有“发展到某一步”的感觉。','At that point, I did not know what to do.',NULL,NULL,'at that point,stage',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(122,2,11,'phrase','keep them under control / keep things under control','keep them under control / keep things under control','keep them under control / keep things under control','把他们控制住 / 把局面控制住。','under control 是很常见的固定搭配。','We need to keep the situation under control.',NULL,NULL,'under control,keep things under control',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(123,2,12,'phrase','talk to someone on the phone','talk to someone on the phone','talk to someone on the phone','通过电话跟某人说话。','也可以说 be on the phone with someone。','I am just talking to her on the phone.',NULL,NULL,'on the phone,talk to someone on the phone',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(124,2,13,'phrase','boundaries around TV / rules around TV / limits on TV time','boundaries around TV / rules around TV / limits on TV time','boundaries around TV / rules around TV / limits on TV time','在看电视这件事上的界限、规定、限制。','讨论育儿或家庭规则时很常用。','We have some rules around TV. / We have limits on TV time.',NULL,NULL,'rules around TV,limits on TV time',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(125,2,14,'phrase','feel peer pressure','feel peer pressure','feel peer pressure','感受到同伴压力。','peer pressure = 同伴压力。','Teenagers often feel peer pressure.',NULL,NULL,'peer pressure,feel peer pressure',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(126,2,15,'phrase','in this way / by this standard / in a standard way','in this way / by this standard / in a standard way','in this way / by this standard / in a standard way','用这种方式；按这个标准来说；用一种标准的方式。','这三个表达都自然，但意思不同。','In this way, children can learn more naturally. / By this standard, the result is quite good.',NULL,NULL,'in this way,by this standard,in a standard way',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(127,2,16,'vocab','spank someone','spank someone','spank someone','打某人的屁股。','通常指惩罚孩子时打屁股。','Some people think you should never spank children.',NULL,NULL,'spank,discipline',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(128,2,17,'phrase','beat someone up','beat someone up','beat someone up','把某人打一顿。','和 spank 不同，beat someone up 指揍一顿。','He got beaten up at school.',NULL,NULL,'beat someone up',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(129,2,18,'vocab','circumstances','circumstances','circumstances','情况；条件；环境。','更常见的是复数形式 circumstances。','It depends on the circumstances. / Under normal circumstances, I would agree.',NULL,NULL,'circumstances,under the circumstances',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(130,2,19,'sentence','What on earth would compel you to do this?','What on earth would compel you to do this?','What on earth would compel you to do this?','到底是什么驱使你这么做？','on earth 加强语气；compel 比 make 更正式。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'compel,on earth',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(131,2,20,'sentence','I do remember distinctly one time my dad was going to spank me and he just started cracking up.','I do remember distinctly one time my dad was going to spank me and he just started cracking up.','I do remember distinctly one time my dad was going to spank me and he just started cracking up.','我确实很清楚地记得，有一次我爸本来要打我屁股，结果他自己突然笑场了。','do remember 是强调；cracking up = 突然大笑起来。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'do remember,distinctly,crack up',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(132,2,21,'sentence','What did you get grounded for as a child?','What did you get grounded for as a child?','What did you get grounded for as a child?','你小时候通常因为什么被罚禁足？','get grounded for something 是固定搭配。','I got grounded for lying.',NULL,NULL,'grounded,get grounded for',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(133,2,22,'phrase','a common discipline tactic','a common discipline tactic','a common discipline tactic','一种很常见的管教方法 / 管教手段。','适合谈论育儿、教育和家庭管教。','That was a common discipline tactic.',NULL,NULL,'discipline tactic,parenting tactic',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(134,2,23,'phrase','take certain things away','take certain things away','take certain things away','把某些东西拿走；收走某些东西作为惩罚。','常见于育儿、处罚、限制 privileges 的场景。','My parents used to take my phone away.',NULL,NULL,'take away,privileges',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(135,2,24,'sentence','I feel like I remember getting really defiant.','I feel like I remember getting really defiant.','I feel like I remember getting really defiant.','我感觉我记得自己当时变得特别叛逆 / 特别不服管。','defiant 带明显反抗、不服、对着干的感觉。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'defiant,rebellious,stubborn',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(136,2,25,'vocab','explicit','explicit','explicit','明确的；清楚表达出来的；直白的。','最常见意思是“明确的、明说的”。','He gave me explicit instructions. / You need to be more explicit.',NULL,NULL,'explicit,implicit',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(137,2,26,'sentence','I was so sad that I had hit her that I snuck out of my room and into her room, and we started playing with our Barbie dolls.','I was so sad that I had hit her that I snuck out of my room and into her room, and we started playing with our Barbie dolls.','I was so sad that I had hit her that I snuck out of my room and into her room, and we started playing with our Barbie dolls.','我因为打了她而特别难过，于是我偷偷从自己房间跑到她房间，然后我们一起玩芭比娃娃。','had hit 表示先发生；started playing 在这个故事语境里更自然。',NULL,NULL,NULL,'had hit her,Barbie dolls,snuck into her room',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04',1,'2026-04-05 06:41:04'),(221,2,27,'vocab','casual work','casual work','casual work','临时工作；零工；非固定兼职。','casual work 常见于新西兰和澳洲职场语境，通常指没有固定长期排班、按需要安排的工作。中文可以理解为临时工作、零工、非固定兼职。','casual work',NULL,NULL,'casual work,part-time work',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(222,2,28,'vocab','causal','causal','causal','因果的。','causal 是形容词，表示“因果的”。最常见搭配是 a causal relationship，表示因果关系。','a causal relationship = 因果关系',NULL,NULL,'causal,causal relationship',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(223,2,29,'sentence','I just wanted to ask for permission before opening it.','就是想在打开前得到您的允许','I just wanted to ask for permission before opening it.','就是想在打开前得到您的允许。','这是一个很礼貌的表达，适合在打开某个物品、文件、包裹、柜子等之前，先征求对方同意。ask for permission = 请求许可。','I just wanted to ask for permission before opening it.',NULL,NULL,'ask for permission,before opening it,permission',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(224,2,30,'sentence','Have you seen anything that\'s caught your eye?','Have you seen anything that’s caught your eye? Like anything in here, or might be over here somewhere.','Have you seen anything that\'s caught your eye? Like anything in here, or might be over here somewhere.','你有看到什么让你眼前一亮的东西吗？比如这边这里的，或者也可能是在那边某个地方的。','caught your eye 是很自然的口语表达，意思是“吸引你的注意”“让你眼前一亮”。很适合购物、逛店、看展品时使用。','Have you seen anything that\'s caught your eye? Like anything in here, or might be over here somewhere.',NULL,NULL,'caught your eye,shopping,notice',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(225,2,31,'sentence','Looks pretty good. You found some stuff out.','Thanks, Jesper. Looks pretty good. You found some stuff out.','Thanks, Jesper. Looks pretty good. You found some stuff out.','你还真发现了一些东西。','find something out = 发现；弄清楚。这里带有“你还真查出来一些内容”的感觉。Looks pretty good 也是很自然的评价。','Thanks, Jesper. Looks pretty good. You found some stuff out.',NULL,NULL,'find out,looks pretty good,stuff',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(226,2,32,'sentence','They\'re just transferring stuff from one place to another, so that\'s why it\'s allowed.','They’re just transferring stuff from one place to another, so that’s why it’s allowed','They\'re just transferring stuff from one place to another, so that\'s why it\'s allowed.','他们只是把东西从一个地方转移到另一个地方，所以这是被允许的。','transfer stuff from one place to another 是很自然的表达，意思是把东西从一个地方搬到另一个地方。that\'s why it\'s allowed = 所以这就是为什么它是被允许的。','They\'re just transferring stuff from one place to another, so that\'s why it\'s allowed.',NULL,NULL,'transfer,from one place to another,allowed',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(227,2,33,'sentence','Do you have any idea how much it would be? It doesn\'t have a price on the mattress.','Do you have any idea that it doesn\'t have a price on the metress, I was wondering how much it would be?','Do you have any idea how much it would be? It doesn\'t have a price on the mattress.','我想问一下，这个床垫上没有标价。你知不知道它多少钱？','原始意思是想礼貌询问价格。这里整理成更自然版本：Do you have any idea how much it would be? It doesn\'t have a price on the mattress. mattress 注意拼写。','Do you have any idea how much it would be? It doesn\'t have a price on the mattress.',NULL,NULL,'mattress,price,how much',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(228,2,34,'sentence','We have a lot of furniture here now, but we didn\'t last week.','这里有很多家具，但是上周不是','We have a lot of furniture here now, but we didn\'t last week.','这里现在有很多家具，但是上周不是。','这个句子适合对比现在和过去。we didn\'t last week 省略了 have a lot of furniture here，口语里很自然。','We have a lot of furniture here now, but we didn\'t last week.',NULL,NULL,'furniture,now,last week,compare',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(229,2,35,'phrase','just chilling','Just chilling','Just chilling.','就随便待着；放松一下；在休息。','非常常见的口语表达，表示没干什么特别的事，就是放松、发呆、待着。','Just chilling.',NULL,NULL,'just chilling,chill,relax',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(230,2,36,'vocab','show off','show off','show off','1. 炫耀，显摆。2. 展示。','show off 既可以表示“炫耀、显摆”，也可以表示“展示某物给别人看”。要根据语境判断是褒义还是贬义。','He likes to show off. / She wanted to show off her new dress.',NULL,NULL,'show off,boast,display',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(231,2,37,'sentence','How young do you think I am?','How young do you thiank I am ?','How young do you think I am?','你认为我有多年轻？','这是自然的口语问句。这里保留了原始问法，并把 thiank 修正为 think。','How young do you think I am?',NULL,NULL,'How young do you think I am',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(232,2,38,'sentence','I was studying for a bit.','我只学了一阵子','I was studying for a bit.','我只学了一阵子。','for a bit = 一小会儿；一阵子。口语里非常常见。','I was studying for a bit.',NULL,NULL,'for a bit,study',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(233,2,39,'sentence','Pretty lucky to be here.','能在这里已经挺幸运了','Pretty lucky to be here.','能在这里已经挺幸运了。','口语里很自然，省略了 I\'m，完整写法可以是 I\'m pretty lucky to be here.','Pretty lucky to be here.',NULL,NULL,'pretty lucky,to be here',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(234,2,40,'vocab','bench','bench','bench','1. 长凳。2. 工作台。3. 替补席。4. 法官席。','bench 是多义词。最常见是长凳。体育里可以指替补席，法律语境里 the bench 指法官席，工作或木工语境里可以指工作台。','a park bench = 公园长椅；a wooden bench = 木凳 / 长凳；workbench = 工作台；He started on the bench. = 他一开始在替补席上。',NULL,NULL,'bench,workbench,substitute bench',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(235,2,41,'sentence','Do you want to help Tomas at the till?','你想帮助Tomas 收银吗？','Do you want to help Tomas at the till?','你想帮助 Tomas 收银吗？','at the till / on the till / at the register 都能用于收银场景。with the checkout 也自然。','Do you want to help Tomas at the till? / Do you want to help Tomas with the checkout? / Do you want to help me and Tomas at the register?',NULL,NULL,'till,register,checkout',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(236,2,42,'phrase','get rid of it','get rid of it','get rid of it','把它弄掉；把它去掉；把它处理掉。','很常见的口语短语，意思可以根据语境变化：去除、扔掉、处理。','get rid of it',NULL,NULL,'get rid of it,remove,throw away',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(237,2,43,'phrase','out in the back of Oxford','out in the back of Oxford','out in the back of Oxford','就在 Oxford 后面那一片。','这里有一种“在更后面、更外面那片区域”的感觉。','out in the back of Oxford',NULL,NULL,'back of Oxford,out in the back',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(238,2,44,'phrase','good haircut place','good haircut place','good haircut place','很好的理发的地方。','口语里能懂。更自然也可说 a good place to get a haircut。','good haircut place',NULL,NULL,'haircut place,get a haircut',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(239,2,45,'sentence','There\'s lots of housing going on.','there’s lots of housing going on','There\'s lots of housing going on.','那边正在搞很多住宅建设；那边最近住房建设很多。','housing 在这里指住房建设、住宅开发。going on 表示“正在进行”。','There\'s lots of housing going on.',NULL,NULL,'housing,housing development,going on',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38',1,'2026-04-05 07:41:38'),(240,2,46,'vocab','house / ho