ning errands','running errands','running errands','跑腿办事；出门办一些杂事。','很常见的生活口语。','I\'m running errands this afternoon. / She spent the morning running errands.',NULL,NULL,'running errands,errands',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04',1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04'),(259,2,65,'phrase','beat the crowds','beat the crowds','beat the crowds','赶在人多之前去；避开人群高峰。','出行、购物、景点场景常见。','We left early to beat the crowds. / Let\'s go now and beat the crowds.',NULL,NULL,'beat the crowds,crowds',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04',1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04'),(260,2,66,'vocab','catch up with / catch up on','catch up with / catch up on','catch up with / catch up on','catch up with = 和某人叙旧、赶上某人、最终影响到某人；catch up on = 补上、补做、补看、补听、补学。','这两个短语都非常常用，但对象不同：with 后常接人；on 后常接事情。','I\'m catching up with a friend this weekend. / He walks fast, so it\'s hard to catch up with him. / Lack of sleep is catching up with me. / I need to catch up on my homework. / I spent the weekend catching up on sleep.',NULL,NULL,'catch up with,catch up on',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04',1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04'),(261,2,67,'sentence','I\'m catching a matinee movie on Saturday.','I\'m catching a matinee movie on Saturday','I\'m catching a matinee movie on Saturday.','我周六要去看一场日场电影。','matinee 指日场演出、午场电影、白天场次。','I\'m catching a matinee movie on Saturday.',NULL,NULL,'matinee,movie',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04',1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04'),(262,2,68,'vocab','binge / binge-watch','binge / binge-watch','binge / binge-watch','暴饮暴食；一口气看很多；放纵式地大量做某事。','这个词通常带一点“过量、一口气、有点失控”的感觉。binge-watch = 狂刷、连看很多集。','He went on a binge. / I binge-watched that series. / She binge-watched TV all weekend. / binge drinking / shopping binge',NULL,NULL,'binge,binge-watch',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04',1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04'),(263,2,69,'sentence','I\'m just seeing where the weekend takes me.','I\'m just seeing where the weekend takes me.','I\'m just seeing where the weekend takes me.','我周末就随缘安排；我先不定计划，看看周末怎么发展。','一种很自然、随性的表达。','I\'m just seeing where the weekend takes me.',NULL,NULL,'weekend,