shutter blade','shutter blade','shutter blade','快门叶片。','常见于相机、镜头内部快门、某些机械装置里的叶片式快门。','shutter = 快门；blade = 叶片',NULL,NULL,'shutter blade,shutter,camera',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04',1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04'),(298,2,104,'vocab','extreme','extreme','extreme','极端的；非常强烈的；极度的；极端情况。','extreme 可作形容词，也可作名词（常见复数 extremes）。常见搭配有 extreme weather, extreme pain, extreme views, go to extremes, a bit extreme。','extreme weather / extreme pain / extreme views / He goes to extremes when he diets. / That sounds a bit extreme.',NULL,NULL,'extreme,extremes,go to extremes',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04',1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04'),(299,2,105,'vocab','biography / autobiography / bibliography','biography / autobiography / bibliography','biography / autobiography / bibliography','biography = 传记；autobiography = 自传；bibliography = 参考文献。','这三个词很容易混淆。','biography / autobiography / bibliography',NULL,NULL,'biography,autobiography,bibliography',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04',1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04'),(300,2,106,'phrase','inspire me','inspire me','inspire me','激励我；启发我；给我灵感。','inspire 比单纯的 encourage 更强，常带“被打动、被鼓舞、被启发”的感觉。','You inspire me. / Your story inspires me. / This painting inspires me.',NULL,NULL,'inspire me,inspire',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04',1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04'),(301,2,107,'sentence','I enjoy films that make you think.','I enjoy films that make you think','I enjoy films that make you think.','我喜欢那种能让人思考的电影。','自然表达电影偏好。','I enjoy films that make you think.',NULL,NULL,'make you think,films',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04',1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04'),(302,2,108,'vocab','passionate','passionate','passionate','充满热情的；热爱的；有激情的。','比 like 强很多。常见搭配：be passionate about something。','I\'m passionate about teaching. / She\'s passionate about music.',NULL,NULL,'passionate,be passionate about',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04',1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04'),(303,2,109,'sentence','I believe in gentle parenting.','I believe in gentle parenting.','I believe in gentle parenting.','我认同温和育儿。','believe in 在这里有“认同、相信、支持”的感觉。','I believe in gentle parenting.',NULL,NULL,'gentle parenting,believe in',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04',1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04'),(304,2,110,'phrase','drop the ball on something','we drop the ball on this','drop the ball on something','把某件事搞砸；在某件事上失误；没把该做的事做好。','drop the ball 是很常见的口语习语。你原来的 we drop the ball on this 语法上不算错，但说已经发生的失误时，更常见是 We dropped the ball on this. 现在或将来提醒不要失误时可说 Let\'s not drop the ball on this.','We dropped the ball on this. / I really dropped the ball on that project. / They dropped the ball by not telling us earlier. / Let\'s not drop the ball on this.',NULL,NULL,'drop the ball,dropped the ball,idiom,project mistake',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04',1,'2026-04-05 07:44:04'),(305,2,111,'vocab','permissive','permissive','permissive','宽松的；放任的；管得不严的。','常见场景 1：育儿 / 管教。这是很常见的用法。\n\n- permissive parents\n  放得比较松的父母\n- a permissive parenting style\n  宽松型育儿方式\n\n例如：\n- Her parents were very permissive.\n  她父母管得很松。\n\n常见场景 2：规则 / 制度。表示规则比较宽、限制少。\n\n- a permissive environment\n  比较宽松的环境\n- permissive laws\n  比较宽松的法律\n\n例如：\n- The school used to be more permissive.\n  那所学校以前更宽松。\n\n语感：这个词通常不是单纯“友好”，而是有一点：\n- 允许很多\n- 限制不多\n- 不太严格\n\n有时根据语境，可能带一点“太放任了”的感觉。\n\n和 strict 对比：\n- strict = 严格的\n- permissive = 宽松的 / 放任的\n\n例如：\n- My parents were strict.\n- My parents were quite permissive.\n\n你可以这样记：\npermissive parenting = 宽松型育儿\npermissive parents = 管得比较松的父母','permissive parents\n放得比较松的父母\n\na permissive parenting style\n宽松型育儿方式\n\nHer parents were very permissive.\n她父母管得很松。\n\na permissive environment\n比较宽松的环境\n\npermissive laws\n比较宽松的法律\n\nThe school used to be more permissive.\n那所学校以前更宽松。\n\nMy parents were strict.\nMy parents were quite permissive.\n\npermissive parenting = 宽松型育儿\npermissive parents = 管得比较松的父母',NULL,NULL,'permissive,permissive parents,permissive parenting,strict,parenting style',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 07:54:14',1,'2026-04-05 07:54:14'),(306,2,112,'sentence','be resistant to discipline','We were very resistant to discipline because it felt like an infringement on our children’s freedom.','We were very resistant to discipline because it felt like an infringement on our children’s freedom.','我们很抗拒管教，因为那让人觉得像是在侵犯孩子的自由。','这句话的整体意思是：\n我们当时很抗拒管教，因为那让人觉得像是在侵犯我们孩子的自由。\n\n句子可以拆成两部分：\n\n1. We were very resistant to discipline\n= 我们很抗拒管教。\nbe resistant to ... 表示“抗拒……；对……有抵触”。\n\n2. because it felt like an infringement on our children\'s freedom\n= 因为那感觉像是在侵犯我们孩子的自由。\nit felt like ... 表示“这感觉像……”。\n\n这里的重点知识点：\n\n1. be resistant to\n= 抗拒；抵触\n\n2. discipline\n在这里不是单纯“纪律”，而是育儿语境里的“管教、约束、教育中的规范和纠正”。\n\n3. it felt like ...\n= 感觉像……\n\n4. an infringement on ...\n= 对……的侵犯；侵害\n\n常见搭配：\nan infringement on privacy\nan infringement on rights\nan infringement on freedom\n\n5. our children\'s freedom\n= 我们孩子的自由\n这是所有格结构。\n\n补充理解：\n这句话并不是说“管教真的侵犯了孩子自由”，\n而是在表达说话的人主观上觉得：\n管教这件事好像是在限制或侵犯孩子的自由。\n\n更口语一点的改写：\nWe were really uncomfortable with discipline because it felt like we were limiting our children\'s freedom.','We were very resistant to discipline because it felt like an infringement on our children’s freedom.\nHe is resistant to change.\nSome children are resistant to rules.\nIt felt like a mistake.\nIt felt like too much pressure.\nan infringement on privacy\nan infringement on human rights\nan infringement on freedom\nWe were really uncomfortable with discipline because it felt like we were limiting our children’s freedom.',NULL,NULL,'resistant to,discipline,infringement on,children freedom,parenting',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 08:23:37',1,'2026-04-05 08:28:08'),(307,2,113,'sentence','We have two lightning-round questions.','we how two lighting round questions','We have two lightning-round questions.','我们有两个快问快答问题。\n或者：我们接下来有两个快速问题。','这句话里最值得记忆的自然表达是：\n\nWe have two lightning-round questions.\n\nlightning round 的意思是：\n快问快答环节\n快速回答环节\n\n它常见于这些场景：\n- 面试\n- 节目\n- 游戏\n- 课堂提问\n- 破冰活动\n\n核心知识点：\n\n1. lightning\n= 闪电\n\n2. lightning round\n= 快问快答环节 / 快速回答环节\n\n3. lightning-round questions\n= 快问快答问题\n\n这里通常会加连字符写成 lightning-round，作为复合修饰语会更自然。\n\n整句：\nWe have two lightning-round questions.\n意思就是：\n我们有两个快问快答问题。','We have two lightning-round questions.\n\nLet’s do a lightning round.\n\nNow for the lightning round.\n\nWe have two lightning-round questions.\n= 我们有两个快问快答问题。\n\nLet’s do a lightning round.\n= 我们来做一个快问快答环节吧。\n\nNow for the lightning round.\n= 现在进入快问快答环节。',NULL,NULL,'lightning round,lightning-round questions,question,interview,classroom',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 08:33:28',1,'2026-04-05 08:33:28'),(308,2,114,'sentence','You\'re supposed to be in charge in this situation.','supposed to be in charge in this situation','You\'re supposed to be in charge in this situation.','这种情况下应该由你负责。\n或者：在这种情况下，你本来应该是做主的人。','这句话里最值得记忆的自然表达是：\n\nYou\'re supposed to be in charge in this situation.\n\n这句话可以拆成几个重点：\n\n1. be supposed to\n= 应该……\n= 按理说应该……\n\n2. be in charge\n= 负责\n= 掌管\n= 做主\n\n3. in this situation\n= 在这种情况下\n\n所以整句合起来就是：\n\nYou\'re supposed to be in charge in this situation.\n= 这种情况下应该由你负责。\n\n语感上，这句话常带一点：\n- 提醒\n- 责备\n- 强调责任\n\n比如当别人没有承担起责任时，就可以这样说。','You\'re supposed to be in charge in this situation.\n\nHe\'s supposed to be in charge here.\n\nI thought you were in charge.\n\nYou\'re supposed to be in charge in this situation.\n= 这种情况下应该由你负责。\n\nHe\'s supposed to be in charge here.\n= 这里本来应该是他负责。\n\nI thought you were in charge.\n= 我还以为是你负责呢。',NULL,NULL,'be supposed to,be in charge,in this situation,responsibility',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 08:36:29',1,'2026-04-05 08:36:29'),(309,2,115,'vocab','the pendulum','the pendulum','the pendulum','本意是：钟摆；摆锤。\n引申义里常表示：风向在摆动；事情从一个极端摆到另一个极端；观念或做法来回变化。','the pendulum 本来的字面意思是钟摆，也就是钟表里来回摆动的那个部分。\n\n英语里很常见的引申用法是：\nthe pendulum swings\n\n它常用来表示：\n- 风向在变\n- 观念在来回摆动\n- 事情从一个极端摆到另一个极端\n\n这个表达很常用于这些场景：\n- 教育\n- 育儿\n- 政治\n- 社会观念\n- 管理方式\n\n比如说：\n以前太严格，后来太宽松，现在又开始变严格。\n这种“从一个极端摆到另一个极端”的感觉，就很适合用 pendulum。\n\n你可以这样记几个高频块：\n\n1. the pendulum swings\n= 风向在变\n= 观念在摆动\n\n2. the pendulum swings back\n= 风向摆回来了\n= 又开始往回转了\n\n3. the pendulum has swung too far\n= 已经摆得太过头了\n= 已经走向另一个极端了','The pendulum swings from side to side.\n\nThe pendulum has swung too far.\n\nThe pendulum is swinging back.\n\nIn parenting, the pendulum often swings between being too strict and too permissive.\n\nThe pendulum swings from side to side.\n= 钟摆左右摆动。\n\nThe pendulum has swung too far.\n= 风向已经摆得太过头了。\n= 事情已经走向另一个极端了。\n\nThe pendulum is swinging back.\n= 风向又摆回来了。\n= 观念又开始往回转了。\n\nIn parenting, the pendulum often swings between being too strict and too permissive.\n= 在育儿上，风向常常在“太严格”和“太放任”之间摆动。',NULL,NULL,'pendulum,the pendulum swings,the pendulum swings back,has swung too far',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 08:39:46',1,'2026-04-05 08:39:46'),(310,2,116,'phrase','all of that','All of that','all of that','所有那些东西；那一切；所有那些事。','all of that 是很常见、很口语的表达，通常用来概括前面已经提到的一整串事情、内容或情况。\n\n它的核心感觉是：\n- 所有那些东西\n- 那一切\n- 所有那些事\n- 前面提到的整套内容\n\n这个表达常常用于：\n- 概括前文提到的很多事情\n- 表达情绪反应\n- 总结一连串经历、问题或压力\n\n根据语境，它可以翻成：\n- 所有那些东西\n- 那一切\n- 所有那些事\n- 这一整套\n\n你也可以顺便记这几个相近表达：\n\n1. all of that\n= 那一切\n= 所有那些东西\n\n2. all of this\n= 这一切\n\n3. all that\n= 那些；那一切\n\n它们意思很接近，但语气有一点区别：\n- all of that = 那一切，稍微更完整一点\n- all of this = 这一切，指离说话人更近的内容\n- all that = 更口语、更省略','I remember all of that.\n\nAll of that sounds stressful.\n\nI don\'t want all of that.\n\nI had to deal with school, work, and family stuff — all of that at once.\n\nAll of that made me really tired.\n\nI\'m not interested in all of that.\n\nI remember all of that.\n= 我记得那一切。\n\nAll of that sounds stressful.\n= 那些听起来都很有压力。\n\nAll of that made me really tired.\n= 那一切让我非常累。',NULL,NULL,'all of that,all of this,all that,summary phrase',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 08:45:03',1,'2026-04-05 08:45:03'),(311,2,117,'sentence','That would not have been me.','That would not have been me','That would not have been me.','那不会是我。\n那种事不是我会做的。\n那不可能是我干的。','That would not have been me 是一个很自然的表达，常用来表示：\n\n- 否认\n- 撇清\n- 强调“那不是我的风格”\n- 表示“我不会那样做”\n\n它不一定只是字面上的“不是我这个人”，常常还带有：\n那不像我会做出来的事。\n\n所以有时可以理解成：\n- That doesn’t sound like me.\n- That’s not something I would do.\n\n句子拆解：\n\n1. that\n= 那件事\n= 那种情况\n= 对方描述的行为\n\n2. would not have been\n这里带一种假设、回看、推断的感觉：\n- 不会是……\n- 按理说不可能是……\n\n3. me\n= 我\n\n常见使用场景：\n\n1. 否认某件事是自己做的\nNo, that would not have been me.\n= 不，那不会是我。\n\n2. 表示“那不像我”\nBeing that rude would not have been me.\n= 那样没礼貌不像是我会做的事。\n\n3. 回头看以前的自己\nA few years ago, that would not have been me.\n= 几年前，那不会是我会做的事。\n\n和其他说法的区别：\n\n1. That wasn’t me.\n更直接地说“不是我干的”。\n\n2. That would not have been me.\n更像是在说：\n- 按当时情况推断，不会是我\n- 那不像我会做的事\n- 语气更委婉一点，也稍微更书面一点\n\n可以顺便记这几个相近表达：\n- That would not have been me.\n- That’s not something I’d do.\n- That doesn’t sound like me.','No, that would not have been me.\n\nThat kind of reaction would not have been me back then.\n\nBeing that aggressive would not have been me.\n\nThat wasn’t me.\n\nThat wouldn’t be me.\n\nThat’s not something I’d do.\n\nThat doesn’t sound like me.\n\nNo, that would not have been me.\n= 不，那不会是我。\n\nThat kind of reaction would not have been me back then.\n= 那种反应在当时不是我会有的。\n\nBeing that aggressive would not have been me.\n= 那么有攻击性不像是我会做出来的。\n\nThat’s not something I’d do.\n= 那不是我会做的事。',NULL,NULL,'that would not have been me,that is not something I would do,that does not sound like me',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:18:04',1,'2026-04-05 09:18:04'),(312,3,1,'vocab','happy / glad / delighted / thrilled / elated / overjoyed / ecstatic','happy / glad / delighted/thrilled/elated/overjoyed/ecstatic','happy / glad / delighted / thrilled / elated / overjoyed / ecstatic','开心程度和使用场景的一组词。','这组词可以按语气强度和场景来理解：\n\n日常小开心 / 通用：\nhappy\nglad\n\n礼貌、正式、邮件：\ndelighted\n\n兴奋型开心（offer、机会、旅行）：\nthrilled\n\n更偏成就感、振奋：\nelated\n\n情感型强烈喜悦（家人、平安、重大喜讯）：\noverjoyed\n\n狂喜、顶级开心（重大成功）：\necstatic\n\n实用选择规则：\n\n最安全通用 → happy\n听到消息后高兴 / 庆幸 → glad\n写邮件礼貌一点 → delighted\n很兴奋（机会 / 旅行 / offer） → thrilled\n考试通过 / 成功后振奋 → elated\n家人平安 / 团聚 / 温暖大喜讯 → overjoyed\n特别夸张的开心 → ecstatic\n\n小提醒：\n不要用力过猛。\n比如“今天午饭很好吃”，用 happy / glad 就够了，用 ecstatic 会太夸张，除非在开玩笑。','I’m happy today.\nI’m glad to hear that.\nI’m delighted to meet you.\nI’m thrilled about the offer.\nI felt elated after passing the exam.\nWe were overjoyed to see them safe.\nShe was ecstatic when she got the result.',NULL,NULL,'happy,glad,delighted,thrilled,elated,overjoyed,ecstatic',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(313,3,2,'vocab','sweltering','sweltering','sweltering','热到让人难受的；闷热难耐的。','sweltering = extremely hot and uncomfortable。\n通常用来形容天气热得让人不舒服。','It’s absolutely sweltering today.\nThe room was sweltering.',NULL,NULL,'sweltering,hot,weather',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(314,3,3,'vocab','disperse','disperse','disperse','散开；驱散；分散；分布。','disperse 是动词。\n可以表示人群散开、烟雾散去、叶子被风吹散等。\n你这里还学到了它在文学表达中的情绪感，可以写出秋天、风、落叶、萧瑟感。','The autumn wind dispersed the fallen leaves across the ground, and with them, my warmth—leaving a quiet, hollow chill behind.\n\nThe wind dispersed the leaves at my feet, and the sudden emptiness in the air felt strangely lonely.\n\nAs the wind dispersed the dry leaves, a thin gloom settled in my chest—like the season was quietly saying goodbye.\n\nThe wind dispersed the leaves, and somehow it made everything feel colder and a bit sadder.',NULL,NULL,'disperse,fallen leaves,autumn',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(315,3,4,'sentence','You really are a literature PhD, just as I thought.','你果然是文学博士','You really are a literature PhD, just as I thought.','你果然是文学博士。','just as I thought = 果然和我想的一样。','You really are a literature PhD, just as I thought.',NULL,NULL,'literature PhD,just as I thought',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(316,3,5,'vocab','sack barrow','Sack Barrow','sack barrow','两轮的推货车。','英式英语里常见，指搬运货物的小推车。','Can you grab the sack barrow?',NULL,NULL,'sack barrow,trolley',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(317,3,6,'sentence','Is it wrong to do something else for a little?','Is it wrong to do something else for a little?','Is it wrong to do something else for a little?','我暂时去做点别的可以吗？','表示想短暂去做别的事，语气较委婉。','Is it wrong to do something else for a little?',NULL,NULL,'do something else,for a little',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(318,3,7,'sentence','Looks like you’ve got the hang of it pretty well already.','看起来你已经挺快上手了/已经掌握得很好了','Looks like you’ve got the hang of it pretty well already.','看起来你已经挺快上手了 / 已经掌握得很好了。','get the hang of = 掌握要领；上手；学会怎么做。\n常见形式：\nget the hang of it\nget the hang of doing something','Don’t worry—once you practise a bit, you’ll get the hang of it.\nI’m still getting the hang of this new system.',NULL,NULL,'get the hang of,already',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(319,3,8,'vocab','work out','work out','work out','弄明白；想出；解决；进展顺利；锻炼；计算出。','work out 很常用，主要看语境：\n\n1. 弄明白 / 想出 / 解决\n2. 进展顺利 / 有好结果\n3. 锻炼\n4. 计算出','I can’t work out what this means.\nWe’ll work out a solution.\nCan you work out which category it goes in?\nEverything worked out in the end.\nIt didn’t work out.\nI work out three times a week.\nWork out the total cost.',NULL,NULL,'work out,solution,exercise,total cost',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(320,3,9,'sentence','I’m gonna look around a little bit more.','我打算去再随便看看','I’m gonna look around a little bit more.','我打算再随便看看。','look around = 四处看看；逛一逛。\na little bit more = 再多一点。','I’m gonna look around a little bit more.',NULL,NULL,'look around,a little bit more',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(321,3,10,'sentence','Is there a way to pick it up from here?','Is there that way to pick it up or do we pick it up through the front door ?','Is there a way to pick it up from here?','有什么办法可以从这里取货吗？','自然说法是：\nIs there a way to pick it up from here?\n\nWhatever works best for you = 看你怎么方便都行。','Is there a way to pick it up from here?\nWhatever works best for you.',NULL,NULL,'pick it up,whatever works best for you',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(322,3,11,'sentence','We’re parked over there with the trailer.','We’re parked over there with the trailer','We’re parked over there with the trailer.','我们的车和拖车停在那边。','trailer = 拖车。','We’re parked over there with the trailer.',NULL,NULL,'trailer,parked over there',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(323,3,12,'phrase','It tends to be ...','It tends to be ...','It tends to be ...','往往会……；通常会……。','用来表达一种常见倾向，不是绝对，但经常如此。','It tends to be quiet in the afternoon.\nIt tends to be more expensive there.',NULL,NULL,'tends to be,tendency',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(324,3,13,'sentence','If you end up with the same number, you can either stick with that question or throw them again.','If you end up with the same number, you can either stick with that question or throw them again...','If you end up with the same number, you can either stick with that question or throw them again.','如果你最后得到相同的数字，你可以继续用那个问题，或者再掷一次。','end up with = 最后得到\nstick with = 继续用；坚持\nthrow the dice again = 再掷一次骰子','If you end up with the same number, you can either stick with that question or throw them again.',NULL,NULL,'end up with,stick with,throw again,dice',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(325,3,14,'phrase','Feel free to chip in.','Feel free to chip in.','Feel free to chip in.','你也可以随时补充 / 插句话。','chip in = 插话补充；出一份力；凑一点钱。\n这里是“补充发言”的意思。','Feel free to chip in.',NULL,NULL,'chip in,discussion',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(326,3,15,'sentence','As you guys mentioned, language is really important. I feel the same, because when there’s a language barrier, I can’t communicate properly with local people. That really frustrates me, so I always try to talk to local people and improve.','As you guys mentioned, language is really important...','As you guys mentioned, language is really important. I feel the same, because when there’s a language barrier, I can’t communicate properly with local people. That really frustrates me, so I always try to talk to local people and improve.','正如你们提到的，语言真的很重要。我也有同感，因为当存在语言障碍时，我没办法和当地人顺畅沟通。这真的让我很沮丧，所以我总是尽量和当地人说话并提升自己。','这是很自然的一段课堂表达，适合表达观点、回应别人、讲个人感受。','As you guys mentioned, language is really important. I feel the same...',NULL,NULL,'language barrier,communicate properly,frustrates me',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(327,3,16,'phrase','get by in this country','get by in this country','get by in this country','在这个国家生活下去；在这里勉强应付日常生活；在这里过得去。','get by 很常用，表示：\n设法应付\n勉强过活\n靠现有能力生活\n\n比 survive 更口语、更自然。','I’m still improving my English, but I can get by in this country.\nWithout good English, it can be hard to get by in this country.\nSo that’s how I get by in this country.',NULL,NULL,'get by,survive,live in this country',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(328,3,17,'phrase','language barrier','language barrier','language barrier','语言障碍。','非常常见的表达。','There’s a bit of a language barrier.\nWe had a language barrier, so it was hard to communicate.',NULL,NULL,'language barrier,communicate',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(329,3,18,'vocab','go back to','go back to','go back to','回到某个地方；回到某个话题；追溯到。','常见意思：\n\n1. 回到某地\n2. 回到某个话题 / 事情\n3. 追溯到某个时间','I’ll go back to the office.\nLet’s go back to the main point.\nCan we go back to that question?\nThis tradition goes back to the 1800s.\nOur friendship goes back to high school.',NULL,NULL,'go back to,main point,goes back to',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(330,3,19,'vocab','1800 / eighteen hundred','1800','1800 / eighteen hundred','1800 作为年份时常读作 eighteen hundred；作为数字时常读作 one thousand eight hundred；作为电话号码时常读作 one eight hundred。','年份：\neighteen hundred\nthe eighteen hundreds\n\n数字：\none thousand eight hundred\n\n热线号码：\none eight hundred','This building was built in eighteen hundred.\nIt dates back to the eighteen hundreds.\nIt cost one thousand eight hundred dollars.\nCall one eight hundred...',NULL,NULL,'1800,eighteen hundred,one thousand eight hundred',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(331,3,20,'vocab','clumpy','clumpy','clumpy','结块的；成团的；一坨一坨的；不均匀的。','可用于食物、粉末、化妆、头发等。','The flour is clumpy.\nThe sauce turned clumpy.\nThis yogurt is a bit clumpy.\nMy mascara looks clumpy.\nThe hair gel made my hair clumpy.',NULL,NULL,'clumpy,texture,mascara',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(332,3,21,'phrase','on a regular basis','regular basis','on a regular basis','定期地；经常地；按固定频率。','常见搭配：\non a regular basis\non a weekly basis\non a monthly basis\non a fortnightly basis','We meet on a regular basis.\nI exercise on a regular basis.\nReports are reviewed on a monthly basis.\nI pay my rent on a fortnightly basis.',NULL,NULL,'regular basis,fortnightly basis,monthly basis',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(333,3,22,'vocab','texture','texture','texture','质地；纹理；口感；贴图纹理。','常见于材料、食物、计算机图形。','The texture of this fabric is soft.\nThe soup has a smooth texture.\nApply a texture to the model.',NULL,NULL,'texture,smooth texture,fabric',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(334,3,23,'vocab','scraggly / scraggle / straggly','scraggle','scraggly / scraggle / straggly','scraggly = 乱糟糟的；参差不齐的。scraggle = 变得乱糟糟。straggly = 更常见的“稀疏杂乱”。','常用于头发、胡子、植物、灌木。','He has a scraggly beard.\nScraggly bushes grew along the fence.',NULL,NULL,'scraggly,scraggle,straggly',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(335,3,24,'phrase','leave it like this / leave it as it is','leave it like this','leave it like this / leave it as it is','就这样放着；就保持这样吧。','常见自然说法：\n\nLeave it like this.\nJust leave it as it is.\nLet’s leave it like this for now.\nLeave it the way it is.\nLeave it there for now.\nJust leave it like that.','Leave it like this.\nJust leave it as it is.\nLet’s leave it like this for now.',NULL,NULL,'leave it like this,leave it as it is',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(336,3,25,'vocab','move around','move around','move around','四处走动；挪动物品；经常搬家；被调来调去。','常见意思：\n\n1. 四处走动\n2. 换位置 / 搬来搬去\n3. 经常搬家 / 到处跑\n4. 在不同人或部门之间流转','Please don’t move around too much.\nI need to move around after sitting all day.\nCan you help me move the boxes around?\nWe moved the furniture around.\nWe moved around a lot when I was a kid.\nThe staff get moved around depending on the shift.',NULL,NULL,'move around,furniture,staff',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(337,3,26,'vocab','dangly','dangly','dangly','吊着的；垂着的；摇摇晃晃的。','常见搭配：\ndangly earrings\na dangly bit / piece\ndangly straps / strings','She’s wearing dangly earrings.\nThere are dangly bits hanging off the bag.',NULL,NULL,'dangly,earrings,straps',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(338,3,27,'vocab','rear-view mirror','rear-view mirror','rear-view mirror','车内后视镜。','rear-view = 向后看的；后方视野的。\n相关：\nrear door\nrear seat\nrear end\nrear-view camera\nrear-view visibility','rear-view mirror = 后视镜\nrear-view camera = 倒车影像',NULL,NULL,'rear-view mirror,rear-view camera',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(339,3,28,'vocab','integrate into / integrate with','integrate into','integrate into / integrate with','融入；并入；整合进…… / 与……集成、兼容。','integrate into 强调“进入并成为其中一部分”。\nintegrate with 强调“与……对接 / 联动 / 兼容”。','It took me a while to integrate into the team.\nNew students are helped to integrate into school life.\nWe integrated the payment module into the app.\nThis tool integrates into our workflow.\nThis tool integrates with our workflow.',NULL,NULL,'integrate into,integrate with,workflow',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(340,3,29,'sentence','You haven’t done it for a while.','You haven\'t done it for a while','You haven’t done it for a while.','你有一阵子没做这个了。','for a while = 有一阵子。','You haven’t done it for a while.',NULL,NULL,'for a while,have not done',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(341,3,30,'phrase','be meant to do something','be meant to do sth','be meant to do something','原本应该；计划要；被安排要做某事。','常用于表达“本来打算”或“原本安排”。','I was meant to fly to Cyprus last week for work.',NULL,NULL,'be meant to,planned to',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(342,3,31,'vocab','dislocated / dislocation','dislocated','dislocated / dislocation','脱臼的；错位的；脱离原本环境的。','最常见是医学上的“脱臼”。\n\n1. a dislocated shoulder\n2. a dislocated finger\n3. dislocation = 名词，脱臼\n\n也可引申为位置错位或社区流离失所。','a dislocated shoulder\nMy husband dislocated his shoulder—the bone sort of popped out.\nMy husband had a dislocated shoulder; the bone popped out of place.\ndislocated communities',NULL,NULL,'dislocated,dislocation,shoulder',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(343,3,32,'vocab','twist','twist','twist','扭；拧；转折；新变化。','常见意思：\n\n1. 动词：扭、拧、旋转\n2. 名词：扭动\n3. 名词：故事或事情的转折\n4. 名词：新花样、新变化','Twist the cap off.\nHe twisted his ankle.\nGive it a twist.\nThere’s a twist in the story.\nWhat a twist!\na plot twist\na twist of fate\na modern twist on a classic dish\nThat was a bit of a twist.\nThings took an unexpected turn.',NULL,NULL,'twist,plot twist,twisted his ankle',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(344,3,33,'sentence','I am on a grandparent visa.','I am on a grandparent visa.','I am on a grandparent visa.','我持祖父母签证。','on a visa = 持某种签证身份。','I am on a grandparent visa.',NULL,NULL,'grandparent visa,visa',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(345,3,34,'sentence','I want to become a registered nurse in New Zealand.','I want to become a registered nurse in New Zealand.','I want to become a registered nurse in New Zealand.','我想成为新西兰的注册护士。','registered nurse = 注册护士。','I want to become a registered nurse in New Zealand.',NULL,NULL,'registered nurse,New Zealand',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(346,3,35,'sentence','I have four children, four grandchildren, and two great-grandchildren.','I have four children, four grandchildren, and two great-grandchildren.','I have four children, four grandchildren, and two great-grandchildren.','我有四个孩子、四个孙辈（或外孙辈），还有两个曾孙辈（或曾外孙辈）。','great-grandchildren = 曾孙辈 / 曾外孙辈。','I have four children, four grandchildren, and two great-grandchildren.',NULL,NULL,'grandchildren,great-grandchildren',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(347,3,36,'phrase','the big stretch of mountains','the big stretch of mountains','the big stretch of mountains','大片延伸的山脉。','stretch 在这里有“一大片延伸区域”的感觉。','the big stretch of mountains',NULL,NULL,'stretch of mountains,mountains',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(348,3,37,'phrase','it fits with that','it fits with that','it fits with that','这样就说得通了。','表示“这和前面的内容是吻合的”。','It fits with that.',NULL,NULL,'fits with,make sense',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(349,3,38,'sentence','Can we just go back to the next one, and then come back to this one after?','Can we just go back to the next one ,and then come back to this one after ?','Can we just go back to the next one, and then come back to this one after?','我们先回到下一个，然后再回来处理这个可以吗？','课堂或讨论场景里很自然的转换表达。','Can we just go back to the next one, and then come back to this one after?',NULL,NULL,'go back to,come back to',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(350,3,39,'phrase','symbolic of Canterbury / symbolic','这个很具有坎特伯雷的特性 / symbolic','symbolic of Canterbury / symbolic','很能代表坎特伯雷；具有象征意义的。','be symbolic of ... = 象征 / 代表……\n\n也常见：\nsymbolic gesture\nsymbolic meaning','That’s very symbolic of Canterbury.\nIt’s really symbolic of Canterbury.\nThat’s quite symbolic of Canterbury.\nIt’s become symbolic of Canterbury.\nThe silver fern is symbolic of New Zealand.\nIt was a symbolic gesture.\nIt has strong symbolic meaning.',NULL,NULL,'symbolic,be symbolic of,Canterbury',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(351,3,40,'vocab','shortcut','shortcut','shortcut','近路；捷径；快捷方式；快捷键。','常见意思：\n\n1. 近路 / 捷径\n2. 电脑或手机里的快捷方式 / 快捷键\n也可引申为成功捷径。','Let’s take a shortcut through the park.\nWhat’s the shortcut for copy?\na shortcut to success',NULL,NULL,'shortcut,keyboard shortcut',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(352,3,41,'vocab','portfolio','portifolio','portfolio','作品集；投资组合；职责范围。','最常见意思：\n\n1. 作品集\n2. 投资组合\n3. 工作职责范围\n\n注意拼写是 portfolio。','a design portfolio\na developer portfolio\ninvestment portfolio\nportfolio of responsibilities\nThe minister holds the finance portfolio.',NULL,NULL,'portfolio,developer portfolio,investment portfolio',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(353,3,42,'sentence','Will the photos we took today replace the cover image for our COMP639 course on the Learn page?','今天拍照的照片会把我门learn page上639课程封面的照片换掉吗','Will the photos we took today replace the cover image for our COMP639 course on the Learn page?','今天拍的照片会替换掉 Learn 页面上我们 COMP639 课程的封面图吗？','replace the cover image = 替换封面图。','Will the photos we took today replace the cover image for our COMP639 course on the Learn page?',NULL,NULL,'replace the cover image,Learn page,COMP639',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(354,3,43,'vocab','mandatory vs compulsory','mandatory  vs  compulsory','mandatory vs compulsory','两者都表示“必须的；强制的”，很多场景下可以互换。','Main difference:\n\nmandatory\n- 更正式\n- 更偏规则、政策、法律、工作要求\n\ncompulsory\n- 也表示必须\n- 更常见于教育、课程、官方制度\n- 有时听起来更制度化一些\n\n实用快捷记忆：\nmandatory → 常用于 actions, policies, procedures\ncompulsory → 常用于 subjects, courses, education, official requirements\n\n在很多场景中它们可以相互替换。','Wearing a helmet is mandatory on this site.\nAttendance at the safety briefing is mandatory.\nIt is mandatory to carry ID.\n\nEnglish is a compulsory subject in many schools.\nMilitary service is compulsory in some countries.\nThis course includes one compulsory module.\n\nIn many cases, they are interchangeable.',NULL,NULL,'mandatory,compulsory,interchangeable',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(355,3,44,'sentence','I’ll pop these out on the racks first, then I’ll have space for the new stuff.','先把这些上架/挂出去，然后我们就可以继续下一步','I’ll pop these out on the racks first, then I’ll have space for the new stuff.','我先把这些挂到外面货架上，这样就有地方放新东西了。','pop 在新西兰 / 英式口语里很常见，表示迅速放、挂、塞、去一下。','I’ll pop these on the rack.\nI’ll pop out the back for a sec.\npop it in\npop it on\npop out\npop in',NULL,NULL,'pop,on the racks,new stuff',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(356,3,45,'sentence','It’s been very quiet.','It\'s quiet ... It\'s been very quiet.','It’s been very quiet.','一直都很冷清。','在商店场景里，quiet 常表示生意冷清、没什么顾客。\nexpense = 开销。','It’s quiet, because you don’t have fuel expenses, oil expenses.\nPeople are not buying.\nThey wanna save money.\nIt’s been very quiet.',NULL,NULL,'quiet,expense,shop',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(357,3,46,'vocab','glow','glow','glow','发出柔和的光；光亮；红润；喜悦的神情。','glow 可以作动词，也可以作名词。\n\n动词：\n发出柔和的光\n\n名词：\n光亮\n红润\n喜悦的神情','The glass glows under UV light.\nThe stars glowed faintly.\nI was picking up the glass, and I was wondering whether it glowed.\nthe glow of the candle\nShe had a healthy glow.',NULL,NULL,'glow,UV light,candle',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(358,3,47,'phrase','Is that okay?','Is that okay?','Is that okay?','可以吗？','非常高频、自然的确认表达。','Is that okay?',NULL,NULL,'is that okay,permission',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(359,3,48,'phrase','I’ve never come across ... / come across','I’ve never come across …','I’ve never come across ... / come across','到目前为止，我都还没有遇到过……；偶然发现；给人某种印象；被理解为。','come across 的核心感觉是：\n碰到\n传达出来\n被感觉到\n\n常见用法：\n\n1. 偶然发现 / 偶然遇到\n2. 给人某种印象\n3. 被理解为 / 被传达为','I came across an old photo yesterday.\nHe comes across as very confident.\nI hope I didn’t come across as too critical.\nHave you ever come across the uranium glass before?',NULL,NULL,'come across,uranium glass,impression',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(360,3,49,'sentence','It doesn’t seem to make any difference.','It doesn’t seem to make any difference','It doesn’t seem to make any difference.','这看起来没什么区别。\n这似乎没有产生任何影响。','很自然的判断表达。','It doesn’t seem to make any difference.',NULL,NULL,'make any difference',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(361,3,50,'phrase','over the years / ever / I wonder / shine the torch on it','I’ve been to a lot of bookshops over the years...','over the years / ever / I wonder / shine the torch on it','这些年来；加强语气的 ever；我想知道……；我用手电照它。','这组内容里的重点：\n\n1. over the years\n= 这些年来 / 这么多年下来\n\n2. ever 放句尾加强“从来没有”的语气\n\n3. I wonder ...\n= 我在想……\n= 我想知道……\n= 不知道……\n\n4. I’ll shine the torch on it.\n= 我用手电筒照它。','I’ve been to a lot of bookshops over the years, but I’ve never found it, ever.\nI wonder if it still works.\nI wonder whether it’s real.\nI’ll shine the torch on it.',NULL,NULL,'over the years,ever,I wonder,torch',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(362,3,51,'sentence','That’s what it looks like when it glows.','That’s what it looks like when it glows.','That’s what it looks like when it glows.','它发光的时候就是那个样子。','很自然的说明句。','That’s what it looks like when it glows.',NULL,NULL,'glows,looks like',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(363,3,52,'sentence','A lot of people have it all displayed in cabinets.','A lot of people have it all displayed in cabinets.','A lot of people have it all displayed in cabinets.','很多人把这些东西都陈列在展示柜里。','displayed in cabinets = 陈列在柜子里。','A lot of people have it all displayed in cabinets.',NULL,NULL,'displayed in cabinets,cabinets',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(364,3,53,'sentence','Instead of normal lights, they use UV lights. At night, they glow, so they look really nice.','Instead of normal lights, they use UV lights...','Instead of normal lights, they use UV lights. At night, they glow, so they look really nice.','他们不用普通灯，而是用紫外线灯。到了晚上，这些东西会发光，所以看起来很好看。','instead of = 代替；不用……而用……','Instead of normal lights, they use UV lights. At night, they glow, so they look really nice.',NULL,NULL,'instead of,UV lights,glow',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(365,3,54,'sentence','I think I really like this one. I’ll buy this one and I’ll take it home and I’ll shut myself in a dark room and see if it glows then because that’s where it will glow if it’s pitch black. But I’ll still have that one because that’s a nice dish.','I think I really like this one...','I think I really like this one. I’ll buy this one and I’ll take it home and I’ll shut myself in a dark room and see if it glows then because that’s where it will glow if it’s pitch black. But I’ll still have that one because that’s a nice dish.','我觉得我真的很喜欢这个。我会买这个，把它带回家，把自己关在一个黑暗的房间里看看它到时候会不会发光，因为如果是漆黑一片，它就会在那里发光。不过我还是会把那个也留着，因为那个盘子也很好看。','这段里值得记的点：\n\nshut myself in a dark room\n= 把自己关在一间黑暗的屋子里\n\npitch black\n= 漆黑一片\n比 pitch black dark 更自然。','I’ll shut myself in a dark room.\nIt will glow if it’s pitch black.',NULL,NULL,'pitch black,shut myself in a dark room,glow',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(366,3,55,'phrase','You have a good time.','You have a good time','You have a good time.','祝你度过一段愉快的时光。','很自然的祝福表达。','You have a good time.',NULL,NULL,'have a good time',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(367,3,56,'sentence','The customer needs to pay 24 dollars, but they gave me 30. There’s no 30-dollar option on the screen. What do I put in?','有一位顾客需要付款24块...','The customer needs to pay 24 dollars, but they gave me 30. There’s no 30-dollar option on the screen. What do I put in?','有一位顾客要付 24 块，但他给了我 30。屏幕上没有 30 元这个选项，我该输入什么？','很实用的收银场景表达。','The customer needs to pay 24 dollars, but they gave me 30. There’s no 30-dollar option on the screen. What do I put in?',NULL,NULL,'customer,pay,screen,what do I put in',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(368,3,57,'vocab','permeate through / permeate into','permeate  throught /into','permeate through / permeate into','弥漫；渗入；浸入；也可指思想渗透进……','可用于气味、液体、声音、思想、文化等。','The smell permeated through the room.\nThe idea permeated into everyday life.',NULL,NULL,'permeate,through,into',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(369,3,58,'vocab','be heading to / be headed to','be heading to ... / be headed to…','be heading to / be headed to','正朝……去；准备去…… / 目的地是……；要去……','be heading to 更像动作过程。\nbe headed to 更像状态感。','I’m heading to the office.\nWe’re headed to Christchurch.',NULL,NULL,'heading to,headed to',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(370,3,59,'phrase','family reunion / reunited with my family','I\'d like to go to family reunion ...','family reunion / reunited with my family','家庭团聚；和家人团聚。','自然表达包括：\n\nI want my family to be together.\nI want to be reunited with my family.\nI want a family reunion.','I’d like to go to a family reunion.\nI want my family to be together.\nI want to be reunited with my family.\nI want a family reunion.',NULL,NULL,'family reunion,reunited with my family',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(371,3,60,'phrase','I wish that I could ... but ...','I wish that I could ... but','I wish that I could ... but ...','我希望我可以……但是……','很实用的固定表达，用来表示愿望和现实之间的落差。','I wish that I could go on a cruise, but that’s not happening right now.',NULL,NULL,'I wish that I could,but',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(372,3,61,'phrase','I was going to ...','I was going to .....','I was going to ...','我原本打算……','表示过去本来打算做某事。','I was going to backpack across Italy.',NULL,NULL,'I was going to,backpack',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(373,3,62,'vocab','compromise / reach a compromise / make compromises','to make some kind of compromise / compromise','compromise / reach a compromise / make compromises','妥协；折中方案；危及；削弱。','compromise 既可表示妥协，也可表示危及。\n\n妥协相关：\nreach a compromise\nfind a compromise\nmake compromises\nbe willing to compromise\n\n危及相关：\ncompromise safety\ncompromise quality\ncompromise security\ncompromise standards','We had different opinions, so we reached a compromise.\nIn teamwork, sometimes you need to compromise.\nThis could compromise security.\nDon’t compromise quality.',NULL,NULL,'compromise,reach a compromise,security',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(374,3,63,'sentence','Let’s take a look at a sample conversation so that you can try to imitate it when it’s your turn.','Let’s take a look at a sample conversation ...','Let’s take a look at a sample conversation so that you can try to imitate it when it’s your turn.','我们来看一段示范对话，这样轮到你的时候，你也可以试着模仿。','sample conversation = 示例对话\nimitate = 模仿','Let’s take a look at a sample conversation so that you can try to imitate it when it’s your turn.',NULL,NULL,'sample conversation,imitate',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(375,3,64,'phrase','off the beaten path','My city is off the beaten path','off the beaten path','不走寻常路的；不热门的；不在常规旅游路线上的；比较冷门但有特色的。','常用来形容冷门但有特色的地方。','My city is off the beaten path.',NULL,NULL,'off the beaten path,travel',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(376,3,65,'vocab','tourist attraction / sights / tourist spot / place to visit / scenic spot','景点','tourist attraction / sights / tourist spot / place to visit / scenic spot','景点；名胜；值得去的地方；风景点。','常见区别：\n\nattraction 最常用最万能\nsights 更偏观光名胜\ntourist spot 更口语\nplace to visit 最自然最通用\nscenic spot 更偏风景点，口语里没那么常用','tourist attraction\nsights\ntourist spot\nplace to visit\nscenic spot',NULL,NULL,'tourist attraction,sights,tourist spot,place to visit',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(377,3,66,'vocab','pastry','pastry','pastry','酥皮点心；糕点；甜酥点心。','常用于烘焙和甜点场景。','pastry',NULL,NULL,'pastry,bakery',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(378,3,67,'vocab','alley','alley','alley','小巷；巷子；胡同般的小路。','通常指两栋建筑之间比较窄的路。','alley',NULL,NULL,'alley,lane',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(379,3,68,'phrase','a birthday bash / bash','a birthday bash / bash','a birthday bash / bash','生日派对；热闹的生日聚会；猛打；猛撞；狠批。','bash 可作名词也可作动词。\n\n名词：\na bash = 派对 / 聚会\n\n动词：\nbash something = 猛打 / 猛撞 / 猛批','We’re going to a birthday bash tonight.\nI bashed my knee on the table.\nThe film was bashed by critics.',NULL,NULL,'birthday bash,bash,party',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(380,3,69,'phrase','throw a party / host a party / have a bash','throw a party / host a party / have a bash','throw a party / host a party / have a bash','办派对；举办派对；办一个热闹聚会。','区别：\nthrow a party = 最常用、最自然\nhost a party = 更正式\nhave a bash = 更口语、更热闹','throw a party\nhost a party\nhave a bash',NULL,NULL,'throw a party,host a party,have a bash',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(381,3,70,'vocab','intimate','intimate','intimate','亲密的；私密温馨的；亲密关系的；对某事非常熟悉的。','常见意思：\n\n1. 关系亲密\n2. 私人的、温馨私密的场合\n3. 亲密关系中的\n4. 对某事深入了解的\n\n注意和 imitate 区分。','They are intimate friends.\nIt was a small and intimate gathering.\nThe restaurant has an intimate atmosphere.\nThey are in an intimate relationship.\nShe has an intimate knowledge of the subject.',NULL,NULL,'intimate,atmosphere,knowledge,imitate',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(382,3,71,'sentence','Unless you can’t get her to come.','unless you can\'t get her to come','Unless you can’t get her to come.','除非你没办法让她来。','常放在生日惊喜、保密、安排场景里。','It’s a surprise birthday party, don’t tell her, unless you can’t get her to come.',NULL,NULL,'unless,get her to come,surprise party',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53',1,'2026-04-05 09:55:53'),(383,4,1,'phrase','ahead of time','ahead of time','ahead of time','提早；提前；事先。','ahead of time 常表示比预期时间更早，或者提前做好准备。\n\n常见用法：\n1. 提前做某事\n2. 事先安排\n\n近义表达：\nin advance\nearly\nbeforehand','Please let me know ahead of time.\nWe finished the task ahead of time.\nBook the tickets ahead of time.\nYou should prepare ahead of time.',NULL,NULL,'ahead of time,in advance,beforehand',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:18:51',1,'2026-04-05 10:18:51'),(384,4,2,'phrase','from different angles','from different angles','from different angles','从不同角度；从多方面。','常用来表示从不同角度看问题、分析方案或讨论事情。\n\n更正式的同义表达：\nfrom different perspectives\nfrom various viewpoints\n\n更普通一点的说法：\nin different ways','We should look at this problem from different angles.\nLet\'s discuss the plan from different angles.',NULL,NULL,'from different angles,perspectives,viewpoints',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42'),(385,4,3,'sentence','And so we\'re good to go.','And so we\'re good to go','And so we\'re good to go.','所以我们可以开始了；一切就绪；没问题了。','good to go 是非常常见的口语表达，表示已经准备好了，可以开始、可以继续，或者状态没问题。','And so we\'re good to go.\nEverything\'s set up, so we\'re good to go.',NULL,NULL,'good to go,ready',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42'),(386,4,4,'phrase','so visually','So visually','So visually','所以从视觉上来说；从画面上看；从视觉角度看。','常见于讲解界面、设计、流程图、PPT、架构图时。\n\n自然替代表达：\nFrom a visual perspective\nVisually speaking\nIf you look at the screen\nOn the screen, you can see ...','So visually, it looks like this.\nSo visually, you can see three sections.\nSo visually, this diagram shows ...\nSo visually, the flow goes from left to right.',NULL,NULL,'visually,visual perspective,diagram',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42'),(387,4,5,'vocab','badge','badge','badge','徽章；标识牌；胸牌；勋章。','badge 常见于工作场所、活动、身份识别、制服和奖励场景。','employee badge\nname badge\npolice badge',NULL,NULL,'badge,name badge',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42'),(388,4,6,'phrase','leverage the CodeBuild agent','leverage the CodeBuild Agent','leverage the CodeBuild agent','利用 CodeBuild agent；善用 CodeBuild agent 的能力。','leverage 在技术和职场英语里常表示“利用、善用、发挥……的优势”，不是字面上的“杠杆”。','We can leverage the CodeBuild agent to run our tests automatically.',NULL,NULL,'leverage,CodeBuild agent,tests',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42'),(389,4,7,'vocab','speed up','Speed up','speed up','加快速度；提速；加快进度。','既可以用于物理速度，也可以用于流程、项目、节奏、进展。','The car is speeding up.\nWe need to speed up the process.\nCan you speed up a bit?',NULL,NULL,'speed up,process,progress',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42'),(390,4,8,'phrase','finishing touches','finishing touches','finishing touches','最后的润色；收尾工作；最后完善的细节。','常见搭配：\nput the finishing touches on ...\n表示在快完成时做最后的小调整，让结果更完整、更精致。','I\'m just putting the finishing touches on my report.\nThe team is adding the finishing touches to the project.\nShe added the finishing touches to her presentation.',NULL,NULL,'finishing touches,put the finishing touches on',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42'),(391,4,9,'sentence','And this is what the exam tests you on.','And this is what the exam tests you on','And this is what the exam tests you on.','这就是考试考你的内容；这就是考试会考的部分。','test someone on something = 考某人某个内容。','Focus on these points, because this is what the exam tests you on.\nThe exam tests you on grammar.\nThe exam tests you on vocabulary.',NULL,NULL,'test you on,exam',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42'),(392,4,10,'phrase','so far so good','So far so good','so far so good','到目前为止一切顺利；目前还不错。','非常常见的口语表达，用来表示目前为止没出什么问题。','How’s your new job? — So far, so good.\nAny problems with the project? — So far, so good.',NULL,NULL,'so far so good',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42'),(393,4,11,'vocab','methodology','methodology','methodology','方法论；系统方法；系统化的工作方法。','比单纯的 method 更抽象、更系统，常用于研究、项目、学术和工作流程。','research methodology\nproject methodology',NULL,NULL,'methodology,method',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42'),(394,4,12,'vocab','perform','perform','perform','执行；进行；表现；表演。','在技术和工作场景里，perform 常可表示执行某个操作或进行某项任务。','perform a task\nperform an action\nperform well',NULL,NULL,'perform,execute',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42'),(395,4,13,'vocab','simplify','simplify','simplify','简化；使更简单。','常用于流程、解释、系统、设计、语言表达。','We need to simplify the process.\nCan you simplify this explanation?',NULL,NULL,'simplify,process',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42'),(396,4,14,'vocab','prerequisite','prerequisite','prerequisite','先决条件；前提；必备条件。','指某件事发生之前必须满足的条件。','Knowledge of Java is a prerequisite for this course.',NULL,NULL,'prerequisite,requirement',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42'),(397,4,15,'phrase','ramp up to 100%','ramp up to 100%','ramp up to 100%','逐步增加到 100%；完全启动；全速运行。','ramp up = 逐步增加、逐渐提升。\n\n常见场景：\n1. 系统 / 服务\n2. 项目 / 生产\n3. 团队资源','The server capacity will ramp up to 100% over the next hour.\nTraffic ramps up to 100% during peak hours.\nProduction will ramp up to 100% next month.\nThe team will ramp up to full strength in two weeks.',NULL,NULL,'ramp up,100%,capacity',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:20:42'),(398,4,16,'phrase','all of a sudden','all of a sudden','all of a sudden','突然；忽然；突如其来。','常用于口语、叙述、故事场景，表示事情发生得很快、出乎意料。','All of a sudden, it started raining.\nI was walking home when all of a sudden I heard a loud noise.\nAll of a sudden, everyone cheered.',NULL,NULL,'all of a sudden,suddenly',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:21:12',1,'2026-04-05 10:21:12'),(399,4,17,'vocab','rip through','rip through','rip through','很快完成；迅速传播；横扫；穿透而过。','常见意思：\n1. 很快做完 / 处理完\n2. 横扫 / 迅速传播\n3. 强行穿过 / 撕裂而过\n4. 技术场景里高速处理大量内容','He ripped through the report in an hour.\nShe ripped through her homework.\nThe fire ripped through the building.\nThe virus ripped through the community.\nThe bullet ripped through the wall.\nWe ripped through the backlog.\nThe script ripped through thousands of records.',NULL,NULL,'rip through,backlog,script',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:21:12',1,'2026-04-05 10:21:12'),(400,4,18,'vocab','backlog','backlog','backlog','积压任务；待办事项；工作堆积。','常见于项目、开发、客服、流程管理。','backlog item\nWe’re dealing with a backlog after the holiday.',NULL,NULL,'backlog,backlog item',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:21:12',1,'2026-04-05 10:21:12'),(401,4,19,'vocab','thoughtful','thoughtful','thoughtful','体贴的；细心的；为别人着想的；深思的。','常见两层意思：\n1. 体贴、细心\n2. 深思、认真思考','She is very thoughtful.\nThat was a thoughtful gift.\nHe\'s always thoughtful about others.\nHe gave a thoughtful answer.\nShe looked thoughtful.\nThat’s really thoughtful of you.\nVery thoughtful, thanks.',NULL,NULL,'thoughtful,gift,answer',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:21:12',1,'2026-04-05 10:21:12'),(402,4,20,'phrase','wander into','wander into','wander into','随便走进；闲逛到……里面去。','带一种不急不忙、随意走进去的感觉。','I wandered into the park and sat by the lake.\nShe wandered into the bookstore and spent hours browsing.',NULL,NULL,'wander into,bookstore,park',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:21:12',1,'2026-04-05 10:21:12'),(403,4,21,'phrase','feel determined / feel determined to do something','feel determined','feel determined / feel determined to do something','感到很有决心；下定决心做某事。','determined 表示坚定、有决心。','I feel determined.\nI feel determined to finish this assessment on time.',NULL,NULL,'feel determined,determined to',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:21:12',1,'2026-04-05 10:21:12'),(404,4,22,'phrase','a fairly recent one / the more the merrier / New Year\'s resolution / goes with the word / does not really deliver what it promises / hack your brain','a fairly recent one / the more the merrier / New Year\'s resolution / goes with the word / does not really deliver what it promises / hack your brain','a fairly recent one / the more the merrier / New Year\'s resolution / goes with the word / does not really deliver what it promises / hack your brain','这一组是零散但很实用的表达。','a fairly recent one\n= 一个相当新的 / 比较新的\n\nthe more the merrier\n= 人越多越热闹\n\nNew Year\'s resolution\n= 新年计划 / 新年决心\n\ngoes with the word\n= 和这个词搭配 / 和这个词相配\n\ndoes not really deliver what it promises\n= 并没有真正做到它承诺的效果\n\nhack your brain\n= 改造你的大脑 / 用技巧影响你的思维方式','The more the merrier.\nThat is a fairly recent one.\nMy New Year\'s resolution is to exercise more.\nThat colour goes with the word.\nIt does not really deliver what it promises.\nHack your brain.',NULL,NULL,'the more the merrier,New Year\'s resolution,hack your brain',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:37:00',1,'2026-04-05 10:37:00'),(405,4,23,'vocab','demanding','demanding','demanding','要求高的；费力的；累人的；让人吃不消的。','常见场景：\n\n1. 工作或任务要求高\n2. 人要求很多\n3. 学习很吃力\n4. 身体或精神消耗大\n5. 生活节奏很累\n\npretty demanding 是很自然的口语说法，会稍微软化语气。','This job is pretty demanding, but the team is good.\nHe is a bit demanding, but he knows his stuff.\nUniversity is really demanding, you have got to keep on top of everything.\nThat hike was demanding and my legs were stuffed.\nLife has been pretty demanding lately with work and the kids.',NULL,NULL,'demanding,pretty demanding',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:37:35',1,'2026-04-05 10:37:35'),(406,4,24,'phrase','Is it good for you? / Is that good for you?','Is it good for you?','Is it good for you? / Is that good for you?','这样可以吗；你觉得合适吗；你能接受吗。','这里通常不是问“对你有好处吗”，而是在征求对方同意，意思接近：\n\n可以吗\n行不行\n你方便吗\n\n自然近义表达：\nIs that okay\nDoes that work for you\nAre you happy with that\nSound good\nAll good for you','We will start you on the easy tasks today. Is it good for you?\nWe can meet at 10 am. Is that good for you?\nI will train you on the till first. Is that good for you?\nYou will be working weekends at first. Is that good for you?',NULL,NULL,'is it good for you,is that okay,does that work for you',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:37:44',1,'2026-04-05 10:37:44'),(407,4,25,'vocab','demand','demand','demand','要求；需求；压力。','这里重点是名词用法，常表示外界对人、工作、生活提出的要求。','the demands of work\nthe demands of learning English\nmodern life makes heavy demands on people',NULL,NULL,'demand,demands of work',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:38:03',1,'2026-04-05 10:38:03'),(408,4,26,'sentence','I am stuck on my assessment.','I am stuck on my assessment.','I am stuck on my assessment.','我的作业卡住了；我不知道该怎么写了。','如果想表达困惑或有点扛不住，也可以说：\n\nI am struggling with my assessment.\nI am having trouble with my assessment.','I am stuck on my assessment.\nI am struggling with my assessment.\nI am having trouble with my assessment.',NULL,NULL,'stuck on my assessment,struggling with',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:38:10',1,'2026-04-05 10:38:10'),(409,4,27,'vocab','awkward','awkward','awkward','尴尬的；不自在的；笨拙的；难处理的。','常见用法：\n\n1. awkward situation / moment / silence\n2. awkward person / teenager\n3. awkward to do something\n4. awkward with ...\n\n和 embarrassed 的区别：\nawkward 更偏描述情况、动作、互动本身带来的别扭感。\nembarrassed 更强调人的主观感受。','It was an awkward situation when I met my ex at the party.\nHe is a bit awkward with his hands.\nThe box is awkward to carry because it is huge.\nThere was an awkward silence after the argument.\nShe was an awkward teenager, always shy.\nThis table is awkward to move.\nI find it awkward to ask for help.\nHe is awkward with strangers.\nI feel awkward about speaking in public.',NULL,NULL,'awkward,awkward silence,awkward situation',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:38:33',1,'2026-04-05 10:38:33'),(410,4,28,'vocab','passion / compassionate','passion / compassionate','passion / compassionate','passion = 激情；热情；强烈兴趣。compassionate = 富有同情心的；有怜悯心的。','这两个词拼写有点像，但意思不同：\n\npassion 是名词。\ncompassionate 是形容词。','passion\ncompassionate',NULL,NULL,'passion,compassionate',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:38:41',1,'2026-04-05 10:38:41'),(411,4,29,'sentence','A domain can span across multiple accounts.','A domain can span across multiple accounts','A domain can span across multiple accounts.','一个域可以横跨多个账户。','span across = 横跨；跨越。','A domain can span across multiple accounts.',NULL,NULL,'span across,multiple accounts,domain',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:38:46',1,'2026-04-05 10:38:46'),(412,4,30,'phrase','on top of it / on top of that','on the top of it','on top of it / on top of that','另外；而且更糟的是；除此之外。','比喻用法里表示“另外 / 更糟的是 / 还有这个问题”。\n\n也有字面意思表示“在……上面”。','We are behind schedule, and on top of it, the server crashed.\nShe is busy with work, and on top of it, she is studying for exams.\nThe cherry is on the top of the cake.',NULL,NULL,'on top of it,on top of that',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:38:51',1,'2026-04-05 10:38:51'),(413,4,31,'sentence','I sat in on a meeting with the department head.','I sat in on a meeting with the department head','I sat in on a meeting with the department head.','我旁听了一场和部门负责人开的会议。','sit in on = 旁听；列席。\n通常表示不主导，不一定发言很多。','I sat in on a meeting with the department head.',NULL,NULL,'sit in on,meeting,department head',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:39:32',1,'2026-04-05 10:39:32'),(414,4,32,'phrase','pick up the slack','pick up the slack','pick up the slack','补位；顶上；弥补不足；多干别人没做完的活。','字面感觉是：别人松掉的部分，你把它捡起来补上。\n\n常见场景：\n1. 同事请假或离职\n2. 团队有人没做完\n3. 表达愿意多承担责任','I had to pick up the slack while she was on leave.\nThe rest of the team picked up the slack.\nI am happy to pick up the slack if needed.',NULL,NULL,'pick up the slack,cover for others',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:39:37',1,'2026-04-05 10:39:37'),(415,4,33,'phrase','pull an extra shift / pull a shift','pull an extra shift','pull an extra shift / pull a shift','多上一个班；顶一个班；临时上班。','很口语，常见于零售、服务业、医院和值班场景。','He pulled an extra shift to help out.',NULL,NULL,'extra shift,pull a shift',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:39:41',1,'2026-04-05 10:39:41'),(416,4,34,'sentence','It was quite frustrating because I had back-to-back cancellations with clients, which completely threw off my schedule.','It was quite frustrating because I had back-to-back cancellations with clients, which completely threw off my schedule.','It was quite frustrating because I had back-to-back cancellations with clients, which completely threw off my schedule.','这很让人沮丧，因为我接连遇到客户取消预约，这把我的安排完全打乱了。','back-to-back = 连续发生的；一个接一个的。\nthrow off = 扰乱；打乱；干扰。','It was quite frustrating because I had back-to-back cancellations with clients, which completely threw off my schedule.',NULL,NULL,'back-to-back,threw off my schedule,cancellations',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:39:50',1,'2026-04-05 10:39:50'),(417,4,35,'sentence','I pulled the graveyard shift last night, so I am running on very little sleep today.','I pulled the graveyard shift last night, so I am running on very little sleep today.','I pulled the graveyard shift last night, so I am running on very little sleep today.','我昨晚值了夜班，所以今天几乎没睡多少。','graveyard shift = 夜班。\nrunning on = 靠……维持运转。','I pulled the graveyard shift last night, so I am running on very little sleep today.',NULL,NULL,'graveyard shift,running on very little sleep',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:39:55',1,'2026-04-05 10:39:55'),(418,4,36,'phrase','I feel drained.','I feel drained','I feel drained.','我觉得被掏空了；我累坏了。','drained = 精疲力尽的，既可指体力也可指情绪被耗光。','I feel drained.',NULL,NULL,'drained,tired',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:39:59',1,'2026-04-05 10:39:59'),(419,4,38,'phrase','break free from this cycle','break free from this cycle','break free from this cycle','打破这种循环；逃离这种恶性循环。','break free 比 break 更强，表示摆脱、挣脱。','I want to break free from this cycle of stress and exhaustion.\nBreaking free from this cycle requires discipline.',NULL,NULL,'break free from this cycle,stress and exhaustion',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:40:05',1,'2026-04-05 10:40:05'),(420,4,39,'sentence','Not really, that is not the case','Not really, that is not the case. I think everyone should know how to handle life. Just because I study economics, it does not mean I want to get rich. There are plenty of paths around here, and people say, like animals, we just hope to make something of ourselves.','Not really, that is not the case. I think everyone should know how to handle life. Just because I study economics, it does not mean I want to get rich. There are plenty of paths around here, and people say, like animals, we just hope to make something of ourselves.','并不完全是这样。我觉得每个人都应该知道怎么应对生活。只是因为我学经济学，并不意味着我想发财。这里有很多道路，人们说，就像动物一样，我们只是希望自己能有所成就。','这一段里有很多很地道的块：\n\n1. that is not the case\n= 情况并非如此\n\n2. handle life\n= 应对生活；掌控生活\n比 deal with life 更口语。\n\n3. Just because ..., it does not mean ...\n= 只是因为……并不意味着……\n\n4. get rich\n= 发财\n\n5. plenty of paths\n= 很多道路 / 很多选择 / 很多机会\n\n6. make something of ourselves\n= 有所成就；有出息；发挥潜力','Not really, that is not the case.\nI think everyone should know how to handle life.\nJust because I study economics, it does not mean I want to get rich.\nThere are plenty of paths around here.\nWe just hope to make something of ourselves.',NULL,NULL,'that is not the case,handle life,just because does not mean,make something of ourselves',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:40:33',1,'2026-04-05 10:40:33'),(421,4,40,'phrase','on the fly','on the fly','on the fly','临时地；即时地；当场地；不提前准备地。','常见场景：\n1. 临时修改 / 即时处理\n2. 技术里动态生成 / 实时计算\n3. 说话或决策不打草稿','We fixed the bug on the fly.\nGenerate the report on the fly.\nThe data is calculated on the fly.\nWe create pagination parameters on the fly.\nHe answered the question on the fly.\nI did not prepare and just spoke on the fly.',NULL,NULL,'on the fly,generate on the fly,pagination parameters',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:40:38',1,'2026-04-05 10:40:38'),(422,4,41,'phrase','pay as you go / learn as you go','pay as you go','pay as you go / learn as you go','随用随付；边做边学；边走边调整。','pay as you go = 用多少付多少。\nas you go 还可推广到 learn / improve / figure it out 等表达。','You pay as you go.\nLearn as you go.\nImprove as you go.\nFigure it out as you go.\nDo not worry, you will learn as you go.',NULL,NULL,'pay as you go,learn as you go,figure it out as you go',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:40:42',1,'2026-04-05 10:40:42'),(423,4,42,'phrase','reinvent the wheel','Reinvent the wheel','reinvent the wheel','重复造轮子；做没必要的重复劳动。','常见于技术、产品、项目讨论。','reinvent the wheel',NULL,NULL,'reinvent the wheel',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:40:45',1,'2026-04-05 10:40:45'),(424,4,43,'vocab','fatigue','fatigue','fatigue','疲劳；疲惫。','可用于日常口语、工作学习、健康医疗场景。\n\n常见搭配：\nmental fatigue\nphysical fatigue\nchronic fatigue\nfatigue sets in','I am feeling a lot of fatigue after working all night.\nMental fatigue can make it hard to focus.\nLong hours of coding caused severe fatigue.\nFatigue reduces productivity and increases the risk of mistakes.\nChronic fatigue is a common symptom of stress and sleep deprivation.\nThe patient complained of constant fatigue and low energy.',NULL,NULL,'fatigue,mental fatigue,chronic fatigue',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:40:50',1,'2026-04-05 10:40:50'),(425,4,44,'vocab','self-worth / self-esteem','self-worth / self-esteem','self-worth / self-esteem','self-worth = 自我价值感；自我认同感。self-esteem = 自尊心。','sense of self-worth = 自我价值感。','This job helped me rebuild my self-worth.',NULL,NULL,'self-worth,self-esteem',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:40:54',1,'2026-04-05 10:40:54'),(426,4,45,'vocab','instant gratification','instant gratification','instant gratification','即时满足；立刻得到满足感。','instant = 立刻的。\ngratification = 满足、快感。','Social media encourages instant gratification.\nHe struggles to delay gratification.',NULL,NULL,'instant gratification,delay gratification',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:40:57',1,'2026-04-05 10:40:57'),(427,4,46,'vocab','fluctuate','fluctuate','fluctuate','波动；上下起伏。','表示数据、价格、气温、表现等上上下下变化。','Prices fluctuate.\nTemperatures fluctuate.\nPerformance fluctuates.\nFluctuate within a range.',NULL,NULL,'fluctuate,prices fluctuate',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:41:00',1,'2026-04-05 10:41:00'),(428,4,47,'vocab','inherent','inherent','inherent','内在的；固有的；本身就存在的。','表示某种特性天生就属于某个事物，不是后天加上的。\n\n常见搭配：\ninherent risk\ninherent limitation\ninherent complexity\ninherent problem\ninherent flaw','There are inherent risks in distributed systems.\nThis approach has inherent limitations.\nLatency is an inherent issue in network communication.',NULL,NULL,'inherent,inherent risk,inherent limitation',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:41:05',1,'2026-04-05 10:41:05'),(429,4,48,'phrase','a set of shelves','a set of shelves','a set of shelves','一整套搁架；一套层架。','通常指多个层板组成的架子。','I bought a set of shelves for the living room.',NULL,NULL,'set of shelves,shelves',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:41:10',1,'2026-04-05 10:41:10'),(430,4,49,'phrase','do a quick vacuum','do a quick vacuum','do a quick vacuum','快速吸尘；快速用吸尘器清理地面。','vacuum 可作名词也可作动词。\n另外 vacuum 还有“真空”的意思。','Do a quick vacuum before the guests arrive.\nSpace is almost a perfect vacuum.\nVacuum-packed food.',NULL,NULL,'quick vacuum,vacuum,vacuum-packed',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:41:13',1,'2026-04-05 10:41:13'),(431,4,50,'phrase','drag on / dragged on','dragged on','drag on / dragged on','拖很久；没完没了地持续。','通常描述会议、讨论、讲座、谈判、课程等拖长时间。\ndrag on 带负面感。\ngo on 更中性。','The meeting dragged on for three hours.\nThe lecture dragged on, and I started to lose focus.\nThe negotiations dragged on, but finally they reached an agreement.',NULL,NULL,'drag on,dragged on,meeting',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:41:19',1,'2026-04-05 10:41:19'),(432,4,51,'vocab','bonus','bonus','bonus','奖金；额外好处；附加价值；意外收获。','常见意思：\n1. 奖金\n2. 附加好处\n3. 额外收获','The company gave me a year-end bonus.\nThe hotel included breakfast as a bonus.\nLearning Spanish is useful, and as a bonus, it helps with traveling in Europe.',NULL,NULL,'bonus,year-end bonus,as a bonus',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:42:27',1,'2026-04-05 10:42:27'),(433,4,52,'vocab','thrill','thrill','thrill','兴奋；激动；刺激；使……感到兴奋。','既可作名词，也可作动词。\n\n常见搭配：\na thrill ride\nthrill of victory\nthrill seeker','I felt a thrill when I rode the roller coaster.\nThe thrill of winning the game was unforgettable.\nThe news thrilled everyone in the office.\nIt thrilled me to see her succeed.',NULL,NULL,'thrill,thrilled,thrill seeker',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:42:32',1,'2026-04-05 10:42:32'),(434,4,53,'sentence','Have you always been this confident?','Have you always been this confident?','Have you always been this confident?','你一直都这么自信吗？','很自然的口语问句。','Have you always been this confident?',NULL,NULL,'confident',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:42:38',1,'2026-04-05 10:42:38'),(435,4,54,'vocab','misconception','misconception','misconception','误解；错误观念。','指对某事理解不正确，或者存在偏差看法。\n\n常见搭配：\ncommon misconception\na widespread misconception\ncorrect a misconception','She cleared up the misconception about the project’s deadline.',NULL,NULL,'misconception,common misconception',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:42:46',1,'2026-04-05 10:42:46'),(436,4,55,'vocab','extrovert / introvert','extrovert -> introvert','extrovert / introvert','extrovert = 外向的人 / 外向的。introvert = 内向的人 / 内向的。','extrovert 常见作名词，形容外向的人。也可作形容词但较少。','She is an extrovert who loves parties and meeting new people.\nHe has an extrovert personality.',NULL,NULL,'extrovert,introvert',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(437,4,56,'vocab','glow up','glow up','glow up','外表、气质或整体状态的明显提升；脱胎换骨。','既可以指外貌变化，也可以指内在和外在一起提升。\n\n可作：\n1. 动词短语\n2. 名词（非正式）','She really had a glow up over the summer.\nAfter starting her new job and working out regularly, she had a real glow up.\nShe is really glowing up.\nLook at his glow up.\nHe had a major glow up since high school.\nHer glow up journey inspires everyone around her.',NULL,NULL,'glow up,major glow up,glow up journey',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(438,4,57,'vocab','magnetic','magnetic','magnetic','磁性的；有吸引力的；迷人的。','常见意思：\n1. 物理学上的磁性\n2. 比喻性的吸引力','The magnet is magnetic.\nShe has a magnetic personality.\nHis speech was magnetic, attracting everyone’s attention.\nmagnetic field\nmagnetic force\nmagnetic resonance imaging',NULL,NULL,'magnetic,magnetic personality,magnetic field',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(439,4,58,'vocab','narrative','narrative','narrative','叙述；故事线；叙事逻辑；话语体系；个人经历表达。','常见场景：\n1. 书面或口头故事叙述\n2. 媒体 / 产品 / 商业里的说法框架\n3. 面试 / 简历里的个人经历表达','The novel has a strong narrative.\nWe need a clear narrative for the product launch.\nHe has a strong career narrative.',NULL,NULL,'narrative,career narrative,product launch',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(440,4,59,'sentence','How are you holding up?','How are you holding up?','How are you holding up?','你还撑得住吗？你最近还好吗？','常用于关心别人状态，尤其是在压力、疲惫、困难时期。','How are you holding up?',NULL,NULL,'holding up,check in',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(441,4,60,'vocab','miserable','miserable','miserable','痛苦的；难受的；糟糕的；很不开心的。','常见意思：\n1. 情绪上痛苦、沮丧\n2. 处境糟糕\n3. 生活状态很差\n\n常见搭配：\nfeel miserable\nmake someone miserable\na miserable experience','I felt miserable after the argument.\nThe weather was miserable all week.\nHe was miserable at his old job.',NULL,NULL,'miserable,feel miserable',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(442,4,61,'phrase','set a goal to master just one sentence','set a goal to master just one sentence','set a goal to master just one sentence','设定一个目标，只掌握一句话。','很适合英语学习、自我管理和微习惯场景。','Set a goal to master just one sentence.',NULL,NULL,'set a goal,master one sentence',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(443,4,62,'vocab','dopamine','dopamine','dopamine','多巴胺。','常见于心理、神经科学、习惯养成和社交媒体语境。','a tiny drop of dopamine',NULL,NULL,'dopamine',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(444,4,63,'sentence','I have been expecting the flywheel to spin at full speed the moment I touch it.','I have been expecting the flywheel to spin at full speed the moment I touch it','I have been expecting the flywheel to spin at full speed the moment I touch it.','我一直以为我一碰飞轮，它就会立刻全速转起来。','这里表达的是一种不现实的预期：一开始就想要立刻见效。','I have been expecting the flywheel to spin at full speed the moment I touch it.',NULL,NULL,'flywheel,full speed',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(445,4,64,'phrase','get it doing','get it doing','get it doing','让它开始运转；让它动起来；让它开始工作。','比较口语、上下文依赖的表达。','get it doing',NULL,NULL,'get it doing',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(446,4,65,'vocab','obligation','obligation','obligation','义务；责任；必须履行的事情。','常见于法律、工作、人情和道德责任语境。','obligation',NULL,NULL,'obligation,responsibility',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(447,4,66,'vocab','stake / at stake / have a stake in','stake','stake / at stake / have a stake in','利益；风险；股份；赌注；押上。at stake = 面临风险；利害攸关。','常见用法：\n\n1. 利益 / 风险 / 牵涉的东西\n2. 股份 / 股权\n3. 赌注\n4. 动词：押上、投入\n\n技术语境很常见：\nsystem stability is at stake\nhave a stake in maintaining reliability','Everyone has a stake in the project’s success.\nWhat is at stake here is our company’s reputation.\nShe owns a 20 percent stake in the company.\nThey played cards for high stakes.\nHe staked his reputation on the deal.\nSystem stability is at stake.\nWe have a strong stake in maintaining reliability.',NULL,NULL,'stake,at stake,have a stake in',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(448,4,67,'vocab','pivot','pivot','pivot','转变方向；战略调整；转折点。','pivot 最常见是动词，表示在原有基础上快速调整方向，而不是完全从零重来。\n\n常见场景：\n1. 商业 / 战略调整\n2. 项目方向变化\n3. 产品或架构调整\n4. 名词：转折点','The company pivoted to a subscription-based model.\nWe had to pivot due to market changes.\nThat decision became a pivot in his career.\nWe pivoted the architecture to improve scalability and reliability.\nThe team successfully pivoted in response to new requirements.\nThis project required a rapid pivot under tight deadlines.',NULL,NULL,'pivot,pivot strategy,architecture',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(449,4,68,'vocab','spike / buzz / resentful','spike / buzz / resentful','spike / buzz / resentful','spike = 激增；飙升；尖峰。buzz = 嗡嗡声；热议；兴奋感。resentful = 感到愤愤不平的；心怀不满的。','这是三个独立词：\n\nspike 常见于数据、流量、价格突然升高。\nbuzz 常见于声音、社交热度、兴奋感。\nresentful 表示因为不公平或委屈而不满。','traffic spike\nmedia buzz\nShe felt resentful after being ignored.',NULL,NULL,'spike,buzz,resentful',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(450,4,69,'vocab','throughput','throughput','throughput','吞吐量；单位时间内处理量；产出效率。','常见于系统、网络、机器、工厂和流程效率场景。\n\n常见搭配：\nhigh throughput\nlow throughput\nnetwork throughput\nsystem throughput\nincrease throughput','The server has a throughput of 1000 requests per second.\nThe factory’s throughput has increased by 20 percent this year.',NULL,NULL,'throughput,network throughput,system throughput',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(451,4,70,'phrase','hard to come by','hard to come by','hard to come by','难找到；难得；稀有。','常见两层意思：\n1. 很难找到\n2. 很稀有、难得','Good jobs are hard to come by these days.\nAffordable housing is hard to come by in this city.',NULL,NULL,'hard to come by,rare',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(452,4,71,'phrase','a labor of love','a labor of love','a labor of love','出于热爱而做的事情；因为真心喜欢而投入的项目。','适合项目介绍、个人 passion 表达，但在特别正式的商业语境里不要过度使用。','Building this app was truly a labor of love.\nThis project has been a labor of love for our team.\nThis project was really a labor of love for me.',NULL,NULL,'a labor of love,project,passion',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(453,4,72,'phrase','dread it / dread doing something','To dread it','dread it / dread doing something','害怕它；非常不想面对；一想到就难受。','dread 比 do not like 强很多，通常是对即将发生的事有强烈抗拒。','I dread Mondays.\nI am starting to dread going to work.\nI dread it every time I have to present.\nI am kind of dreading it.\nI really dread checking the results.',NULL,NULL,'dread,dreading it',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(454,4,73,'vocab','thrifty','Thrifty','thrifty','节俭的；会省钱的；精打细算的。','thrifty 是正面表达。\ncheap 常带贬义，表示小气。\nfrugal 更正式一些，也表示节俭。','She is very thrifty with her money.\nI try to be thrifty when shopping.\nHe grew up in a thrifty family.',NULL,NULL,'thrifty,frugal,cheap',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(455,4,74,'vocab','lumbar support','lumbar support','lumbar support','腰部支撑。','lumbar = 腰椎的 / 下背部的。\n常见于椅子、车座、办公、健康场景。','This chair has good lumbar support.\nProper lumbar support helps prevent back pain.',NULL,NULL,'lumbar support,back pain',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(456,4,75,'vocab','selling point','selling point','selling point','卖点。','表示产品、服务、项目的吸引人之处。','selling point',NULL,NULL,'selling point',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(457,4,76,'vocab','throw on','throw on','throw on','随便穿上；匆忙套上；快速加上；播放。','常见意思：\n1. 随便穿上衣服\n2. 随便加点东西\n3. 快速放个音乐或打开点什么','I just threw on a hoodie and left.\nLet me throw on a jacket.\nThrow on some cheese.\nThrow on some music.',NULL,NULL,'throw on,hoodie,jacket',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(458,4,77,'vocab','tuck it in / tuck in','tuck it in','tuck it in / tuck in','把……塞进去；把衣服扎进去；把被子掖好。','常见场景：\n1. 衣服扎进裤子里\n2. 床单塞好\n3. 给孩子盖好被子','I want to tuck in the sheets so that they do not come loose in the night.\nDo not forget to tuck your shirt in.\nHe tucked in his shirt before the meeting.\nShe tucked the kids in and kissed them goodnight.',NULL,NULL,'tuck in,sheets,shirt',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(459,4,78,'vocab','figure out','figure out','figure out','弄明白；找出办法；解决。','figure out 很口语，强调通过想、试、分析最后明白或找到方法。\n\n和其他词的区别：\nfigure out = 弄明白 / 找办法\nunderstand = 理解\nsolve = 解决，偏结果','I cannot figure out why my code is not working.\nShe finally figured out the solution.\nWe need to figure out a way to fix this bug.',NULL,NULL,'figure out,solution,bug',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(460,4,79,'vocab','stickler for','stickler for','stickler for','对某件事非常坚持、严格要求的人；特别注重规则或标准的人。','常见于工作、习惯、整洁、质量、准时等语境。\n\n结构：\na stickler for + 名词','I am not much of a stickler for many things.\nShe is a stickler for punctuality.\nHe is a stickler for quality.\nMy dad is a stickler for neatness.',NULL,NULL,'stickler for,punctuality,quality,neatness',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(461,4,80,'phrase','every now and then','every now and then','every now and then','不时；偶尔；有时候。','表示不会经常发生，但偶尔会发生。','I like to go hiking every now and then.\nHe checks his emails every now and then.\nEvery now and then, we go out for dinner.',NULL,NULL,'every now and then,occasionally',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(462,4,81,'phrase','every other week','every other week','every other week','每隔一周；隔周一次。','和 every two weeks 意思一样，但口语更常见。','every other week',NULL,NULL,'every other week,every two weeks',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(463,4,82,'vocab','alternative','alternative','alternative','替代方案；替代的；另一个选择的。','既可作名词，也可作形容词。\n\n名词：\nan alternative to something\na viable alternative\noffer / provide / consider an alternative\n\n形容词：\nalternative energy\nalternative medicine\nalternative solution / lifestyle / approach','We need an alternative to this plan.\nI am looking for an alternative to coffee.\nPublic transport is a viable alternative to driving.\nThe teacher offered an alternative assignment.\nWe are looking for alternative solutions.\nSolar power is an alternative energy source.\nShe prefers alternative medicine to conventional drugs.\nThis is an alternative approach to solving the problem.',NULL,NULL,'alternative,viable alternative,alternative solution',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(464,4,83,'phrase','put it off / put off doing something','put it off','put it off / put off doing something','推迟；延期；拖延某事。','常见意思：\n1. 推迟做某事\n2. 拖延做某事，略带负面\n\n近义表达：\ndelay\npostpone\nhold off on','I am going to put off my homework until tomorrow.\nWe had to put off the meeting because of the storm.\nDo not put off making an important decision.\nI keep putting off cleaning my room.\nLet us hold off on making a decision until we get more data.',NULL,NULL,'put off,delay,postpone,hold off on',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(465,4,84,'phrase','make sure that it is relatively even','Make sure that it is relatively even.','Make sure that it is relatively even.','确保它相对平整；确保它相对均匀。','even 常见意思：\n1. 平坦、光滑\n2. 均匀、相等\n3. 公平、对等\n4. 稳定、不变\n\n这个句子可用于土壤、表面、糖霜、工作量分配等。','Make sure that the soil is relatively even before planting.\nMake sure that the frosting is relatively even on the cake.\nMake sure that the workload is relatively even among team members.',NULL,NULL,'relatively even,make sure,workload',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(466,4,85,'vocab','solidify','solidify','solidify','凝固；变坚固；巩固；使稳定。','既可表示物理上的变硬、凝固，也可表示抽象意义上的巩固关系、计划、支持、信心等。\n\n常见搭配：\nsolidify a relationship\nsolidify plans\nsolidify support\nsolidify confidence','The lava solidified as it cooled.\nThe jelly will solidify in the fridge.\nTheir shared experience solidified their friendship.\nThe chief executive officer speech solidified the team confidence in the project.',NULL,NULL,'solidify,confidence,friendship',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(467,4,86,'sentence','It is really needed.','it is really needed.','It is really needed.','它真的很有必要；这真的很需要。','简洁但很常用的评价句。','It is really needed.',NULL,NULL,'needed',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(468,4,87,'phrase','hence creating ...','hence creating one','hence creating ...','因此造成……；从而产生……。','hence 偏书面，意思是：\n因此\n所以\n由此\n从而\n\n常见结构：\n..., hence creating + 结果','They did not communicate clearly, hence creating confusion.\nThe deadline was changed at the last minute, hence creating delays.\nThe system was updated without notice, hence creating problems for users.',NULL,NULL,'hence,hence creating',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34',1,'2026-04-05 10:43:34'),(469,5,1,'vocab','stimulus / stimuli','stimulus pl:stimuli','stimulus / stimuli','stimulus = 刺激因素；刺激物。stimuli = stimulus 的复数。','常见场景：\n\n1. 生理 / 心理刺激\n2. 经济 / 商业\n3. 学习 / 行为激励\n\n常见搭配：\neconomic stimulus\nexternal stimulus\nprovide a stimulus for','Light is a stimulus for plant growth.\nThe government introduced an economic stimulus.\nPraise can be a strong stimulus for learning.',NULL,NULL,'stimulus,stimuli,economic stimulus',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(470,5,2,'phrase','along with','along with','along with','连同；以及；外加。','along with 常用于补充附带信息，意思接近 together with 或 together plus。','Then the system sends me a notification that my request has been processed, along with the details of my leave data.',NULL,NULL,'along with,together with',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(471,5,3,'sentence','He should not have lost his temper.','他本不应该发脾气【已经发脾气了，虚拟语气】','He should not have lost his temper.','他本不应该发脾气。','should not have done 表示过去本不该做，但实际上已经做了。\n\nlose one\'s temper\n= 发脾气','He should not have lost his temper.',NULL,NULL,'should not have,lose his temper',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(472,5,4,'sentence','I got very emotional when we were talking about our problems.','我们讨论我们的问题时，我变得情绪化','I got very emotional when we were talking about our problems.','我们谈到我们的问题时，我变得很情绪化。','get emotional = 变得情绪化；情绪上来。','I got very emotional when we were talking about our problems.',NULL,NULL,'get emotional,problems',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(473,5,5,'phrase','I told you I am a catch.','我很抢手的','I told you I am a catch.','我早就跟你说过了，我可是个很抢手的人。','I told you = 我早就跟你说过了 / 我不是跟你说过吗。\n\na catch = 条件很好、很值得追求的人，常用于感情或约会语境。\n\n相关表达：\nHe is a real catch.\nShe is quite a catch.\nYou are such a catch.','I told you I am a catch.\nAdmit it, I am a catch.\nI guess I am not a bad catch.\nPeople say I am quite a catch.',NULL,NULL,'a catch,I told you',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(474,5,6,'sentence','I get the feeling he was lying.','我感觉他撒谎了','I get the feeling he was lying.','我感觉他在撒谎。','I get the feeling ... = 我有种感觉……；我觉得……','I get the feeling he was lying.',NULL,NULL,'get the feeling,lying',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(475,5,7,'phrase','Are you still into yoga these days?','Are you still into yoga these days?','Are you still into yoga these days?','你最近还喜欢瑜伽吗 / 还在坚持瑜伽吗？','still into = 还在喜欢 / 还在坚持。\nthese days = 最近；这段时间。\n\n更自然变体：\nAre you still doing yoga these days?\nYou still into yoga?\nHave you still been practicing yoga lately?\nAre you keeping up with yoga these days?\nAre you still into yoga at the moment?','Are you still into yoga these days?\nAre you still doing yoga these days?\nYou still into yoga?',NULL,NULL,'still into,these days,yoga',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(476,5,8,'phrase','stay out past midnight','在外面过夜','stay out past midnight','待在外面到午夜之后；在外面待很晚。','这个表达更偏“在外面待到很晚，过了午夜”，不一定等于真正过夜住宿。','stay out past midnight',NULL,NULL,'stay out past midnight',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(477,5,9,'vocab','cheat on','cheat on','cheat on','对……不忠；在……上作弊；欺骗；违背原则。','常见意思：\n\n1. cheat on someone\n= 出轨；对某人不忠\n\n2. cheat on an exam / assignment / test\n= 在考试或作业中作弊\n\n3. 广义的欺骗或违背原则','She found out that he had been cheating on her.\nHe cheated on the exam.\nStudents who cheat on assignments risk failing the course.\nDo not cheat on your taxes.',NULL,NULL,'cheat on,exam,assignment,relationship',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(478,5,10,'vocab','conquer','conquer','conquer','征服；占领；克服；战胜。','常见意思：\n\n1. 字面：征服；占领\n2. 比喻：克服；战胜恐惧、困难、弱点\n\n常见搭配：\nconquer a fear\nconquer anxiety\nconquer a challenge\nconquer a difficulty\nconquer a territory\nconquer a city\nconquer an enemy\nconquer the market\nconquer hearts\nconquer minds','The army conquered the city after a long siege.\nShe finally conquered her fear of public speaking.',NULL,NULL,'conquer,fear,city,market',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(479,5,11,'sentence','He turned the page dramatically.','他夸张地翻书','He turned the page dramatically.','他很夸张地翻了一页。','dramatically = 戏剧性地；夸张地。','He turned the page dramatically.',NULL,NULL,'dramatically,turn the page',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(480,5,12,'phrase','a pile of','a pile of','a pile of','一堆；大量的。','偏口语，可接可数或不可数名词。','I have a pile of books to read.\nThere is a pile of laundry on the bed.\nI have a pile of work to do.',NULL,NULL,'a pile of,books,laundry,work',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(481,5,13,'phrase','I have no clue.','我一点也不知道 / 我完全不清楚','I have no clue.','我一点也不知道；我完全不清楚。','很自然的口语表达。','I have no clue.',NULL,NULL,'no clue',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(482,5,14,'vocab','childish','childish','childish','孩子气的；幼稚的；像孩子一样的。','childish 常有负面语气，表示幼稚。\n但在少数语境里，也可中性表示“孩子般的热情”。','His reaction was so childish.\nDo not be childish.\nShe has a childish enthusiasm for drawing.',NULL,NULL,'childish,enthusiasm',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(483,5,15,'phrase','This toaster has sentimental value.','这个吐司机有情感价值','This toaster has sentimental value.','这个烤面包机有情感价值。','sentimental value = 情感价值。\nsentimental 还可以表示多愁善感的、情绪化的。','This toaster has sentimental value.\nsentimental music',NULL,NULL,'sentimental value,toaster,sentimental',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(484,5,16,'sentence','They hear a loud crack, and the old fence falls down between their yards.','they hear a loud crack,The old fence falls dowm between their yards','They hear a loud crack, and the old fence falls down between their yards.','他们听到一声巨响，接着那道旧篱笆倒在了他们两家的院子之间。','a loud crack = 一声很大的裂响 / 断裂声。','They hear a loud crack, and the old fence falls down between their yards.',NULL,NULL,'loud crack,fence,yards',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(485,5,17,'vocab','settle','settle','settle','解决；安定下来；定居；结清；沉淀；平息。','常见意思：\n\n1. settle a problem / dispute / conflict\n= 解决问题 / 争端 / 冲突\n\n2. settle into\n= 适应；安顿下来\n\n3. settle in\n= 定居\n\n4. settle an invoice / claim\n= 结清；处理赔偿\n\n5. dust settles\n= 尘埃落定；事情平息\n\n常见搭配：\nsettle differences\nsettle the issue\nsettle on a solution\nthe dust has settled','They finally settled the dispute.\nShe settled into her new job quickly.\nThey settled in New Zealand in 2015.\nPlease settle the invoice by Friday.\nThe company settled the claim out of court.\nDust settled on the table.\nNow that the dust has settled, we can evaluate the outcome.\nAfter months of debate, the dust finally settled.',NULL,NULL,'settle,dispute,invoice,dust has settled',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(486,5,18,'phrase','not nearly as much as','do something nearly as much as ...','not nearly as much as','远不如……那么多；远不如……那么频繁；程度差很多。','最常见的是 not nearly as much as。\n\n相关表达：\nnot nearly as many as\nnot nearly as expensive as\n\n对比：\nalmost as much as = 几乎一样多\nnowhere near as much as = 差得远','I do not exercise nearly as much as I used to.\nHe does not contribute nearly as much as his colleagues.\nAI does not cost nearly as much as hiring a full team of specialists.',NULL,NULL,'not nearly as much as,almost as much as,nowhere near as much as',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(487,5,19,'phrase','in comparison with / to','in comparison with/to','in comparison with / to','与……相比；相比之下。','结构：\nin comparison with + 名词 / 代词 / 从句\n\n口语里更常见：\ncompared with\ncompared to','In comparison with the previous version, this one is faster.\nCompared with last year, sales improved.',NULL,NULL,'in comparison with,compared with,compared to',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(488,5,20,'phrase','could well be','coule well be','could well be','很可能；相当有可能。','比 could be 更强一点，表示相当有可能。','It could well be a mistake.\nIf we rush it, the software could well fail.',NULL,NULL,'could well be',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(489,5,21,'sentence','I switch from Line 7 to Line 8.','我从7号线换乘到8号线','I switch from Line 7 to Line 8.','我从 7 号线换乘到 8 号线。','switch from A to B = 从 A 换到 B。','I switch from Line 7 to Line 8.',NULL,NULL,'switch from,to,Line 7,Line 8',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(490,5,22,'vocab','come off','come off','come off','脱落；掉下来；显得；给人某种印象。','常见意思：\n\n1. 东西脱落 / 掉下来\n2. come off as ...\n= 给人某种印象；显得……\n\n结构：\ncome off as + 形容词 / 名词','The sticker always seems to come off.\nThe button came off my shirt.\nIt always seems to come off as rude.',NULL,NULL,'come off,come off as',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(491,5,23,'phrase','bring it up','bring it up','bring it up','提起；提出（某个话题或问题）。','常见于聊天、会议、关系沟通场景。','I did not want to bring it up.\nShe brought it up during the meeting.\nI do not know how to bring it up with him.\nShould I bring it up now or later?',NULL,NULL,'bring it up,meeting,topic',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32',1,'2026-04-05 12:24:32'),(492,6,1,'phrase','These pants are broken / ripped / The zip is broken / There is a hole in these pants','These pants are broken...','These pants are broken / These pants are ripped / The zip on these pants is broken / There is a hole in these pants','这条裤子坏了；这条裤子破了；这条裤子的拉链坏了；这条裤子有个洞。','这一组是描述裤子损坏情况的自然表达。\n\nThese pants are broken\n= 这条裤子坏了\n\nThese pants are ripped\n= 这条裤子破了\n\nThe zip on these pants is broken\n= 这条裤子的拉链坏了\n\nThere is a hole in these pants\n= 这条裤子有个洞','These pants are broken.\nThese pants are ripped.\nThe zip on these pants is broken.\nThere is a hole in these pants.',NULL,NULL,'pants,broken,ripped,zip,hole',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(493,6,2,'sentence','Are these all being thrown away?','Are these all being thrown away?','Are these all being thrown away?','这些都是要扔掉的吗？','很自然的工作场景问句，适合确认一批东西是不是要被处理掉。','Are these all being thrown away?',NULL,NULL,'thrown away,workplace',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(494,6,3,'phrase','get rid of','get rid of','get rid of','处理掉；扔掉；去掉。','很常见的口语表达，表示把东西弄走、处理掉。\n\n常见于库存、旧物、不要的东西。','We are getting rid of some items because they are not selling.\nThese items are not selling, so we are getting rid of them.',NULL,NULL,'get rid of,items,selling',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(495,6,4,'sentence','Can I help out on the till as well?','Can I help out on the till as well?','Can I help out on the till as well?','我也可以一起帮忙收银吗？','on the till 是很自然的新西兰 / 英式零售表达，表示在收银台工作。','Can I help out on the till as well?\nIf it is busy, I can help out on the till as well.',NULL,NULL,'help out,on the till,till',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(496,6,5,'sentence','If I put it here, it happens every time.','If I put it here, it happens every time.','If I put it here, it happens every time.','如果我放在这里，每次都会这样。','适合描述某个问题反复发生。','If I put it here, it happens every time.',NULL,NULL,'every time,happens',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(497,6,6,'sentence','Maybe you can wrap that with some paper.','Maybe you can put some paper around that a bit','Maybe you can wrap that with some paper.','也许你可以用纸把它包起来。','wrap something with paper = 用纸把某物包起来。','Maybe you can wrap that with some paper.',NULL,NULL,'wrap,paper',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(498,6,7,'sentence','Are you a permanent employee?','Are you a permanent employee?','Are you a permanent employee?','你是正式员工吗？','permanent employee = 正式员工；长期员工。','Are you a permanent employee?',NULL,NULL,'permanent employee',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(499,6,8,'sentence','How long have you been working here?','你在这里工作多久了？','How long have you been working here?','你在这里工作多久了？','现在完成进行时，问某人持续工作的时间。','How long have you been working here?',NULL,NULL,'how long,working here',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(500,6,9,'sentence','Can I put those hats on the shelf?','Can I put those hats on the shelf?','Can I put those hats on the shelf?','我可以把这些帽子放到架子上吗？','自然的工作场景确认句。','Can I put those hats on the shelf?',NULL,NULL,'shelf,hats',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(501,6,10,'sentence','We will come back and pick it up.','We’ll come back and pick it up.','We will come back and pick it up.','我们会回来取它。','pick it up = 取走；拿走。','We will come back and pick it up.',NULL,NULL,'pick it up,come back',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(502,6,11,'sentence','So if you have a sec to sort it out, I will come back and pick it up.','So if you have a sec to sort it out, I’ll come back and pick it up.','So if you have a sec to sort it out, I will come back and pick it up.','所以如果你有空处理一下，我就回来取它。','have a sec = 有一会儿空；sort it out = 处理一下，解决一下。','So if you have a sec to sort it out, I will come back and pick it up.',NULL,NULL,'have a sec,sort it out,pick it up',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(503,6,12,'sentence','Do you have smaller change?','Do you have smaller change?','Do you have smaller change?','你有零钱吗？你有小面额的钱吗？','change 这里表示零钱。','Do you have smaller change?',NULL,NULL,'smaller change,change',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(504,6,13,'sentence','You can ask them to put it in the trolley for donations.','你可以告诉他们放在捐赠的购物车里','You can ask them to put it in the trolley for donations.','你可以告诉他们放在捐赠购物车里。','donation trolley = 放捐赠物的购物车。','You can ask them to put it in the trolley for donations.',NULL,NULL,'donation,trolley',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(505,6,14,'sentence','Where should I put these two donation bags?','Where should I put these two donation bags?','Where should I put these two donation bags?','我应该把这两个捐赠袋子放在哪？','自然的工作场景问句。','Where should I put these two donation bags?',NULL,NULL,'donation bags',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(506,6,15,'vocab','superior','superior','superior','优越的；更好的；高人一等的。','常见两层意思：\n\n1. 表示优越、高人一等\n2. 口语里偶尔夸某物很棒、很高级\n\n但日常口语里直接用 superior 夸东西，不如 great / excellent 常见。','He thinks he is so superior.\nThis wine is so superior.',NULL,NULL,'superior',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(507,6,16,'vocab','carry on','To carry on','carry on','继续做某事；继续前进；持续进行；胡闹；大惊小怪。','常见意思：\n\n1. carry on with + 名词 / 动名词\n= 继续进行某事\n\n2. carry on\n= 继续\n\n3. 英式口语\n= 胡闹；大惊小怪','She decided to carry on with her studies despite the difficulties.\nPlease carry on with your work.\nHe carried on with his speech after a short pause.\nWe will carry on with the meeting after lunch.\nDo not worry, carry on.\nLife carries on no matter what happens.\nStop carrying on!',NULL,NULL,'carry on,carry on with',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(508,6,17,'phrase','Have a good rest of the day.','Have a good rest of the day','Have a good rest of the day.','希望你接下来的一天过得愉快；余下的时间顺利。','常用在告别或聊天结束时。','Have a good rest of the day.',NULL,NULL,'rest of the day',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(509,6,18,'sentence','It is similar to the background.','It’s similar to the background.','It is similar to the background.','它和背景很相似。','similar to = 和……相似。','It is similar to the background.',NULL,NULL,'similar to,background',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(510,6,19,'vocab','lovely','Lovely','lovely','太好了；真不错；令人愉快的；可爱的；让人满意的。','常见用法：\n\n1. 表示赞同或高兴\n2. 表示事情愉快或满意\n3. 用在问候或礼貌回应中\n\n在很多口语场景里，lovely 更像 great / nice / perfect，不是真的在说“可爱”。','A: I finished the report. B: Lovely!\nA: Do you want a cup of tea? B: Lovely, thanks.\nThe weather is lovely today.\nWe had a lovely time at the beach.\nSee you later. Lovely, see you!\nCan you send me the file? Lovely, I will do it now.',NULL,NULL,'lovely,great,nice',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(511,6,20,'phrase','go by a date','We go by a date','go by a date','按日期安排；按某个日期来做。','表示按约定日期来安排或判断。','We go by a date.',NULL,NULL,'go by a date',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(512,6,21,'sentence','Sometimes I shorten what I say, and you might not catch it.','Sometimes I shorten things, and you might not get it.','Sometimes I shorten what I say, and you might not catch it.','有时候我会说得比较简短，你可能听不懂。','自然变体：\nSometimes I use short forms, and you might not get what I mean.','Sometimes I shorten what I say, and you might not catch it.\nSometimes I use short forms, and you might not get what I mean.',NULL,NULL,'shorten,catch it,short forms',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(513,6,22,'phrase','There is no hesitation / Do not hesitate to ask','There is no hesitation','There is no hesitation / Do not hesitate to ask','没有半点犹豫；别犹豫，尽管问。','There is no hesitation = 没有犹豫。\nDo not hesitate to ask = 别犹豫，尽管问。\nThere is no uncertainty = 没有不确定。','There is no hesitation.\nDo not hesitate to ask.\nThere is no uncertainty.',NULL,NULL,'hesitation,do not hesitate,uncertainty',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(514,6,23,'vocab','clean out','clean out','clean out','彻底打扫；清空；把里面的东西清光。','常见意思：\n\n1. 彻底打扫、清空某个地方\n2. 把里面的东西吃光 / 拿光','I need to clean out my room.\nWe are cleaning out the garage this weekend.\nThey cleaned out the fridge.\nThe kids cleaned out the snacks.',NULL,NULL,'clean out,garage,fridge',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(515,6,24,'sentence','I need something to pick me up in the morning.','I need something to pick me up in the morning','I need something to pick me up in the morning.','我早上需要点东西让我提神。','pick me up 在这里表示提神、让人振作。','I need something to pick me up in the morning.',NULL,NULL,'pick me up,morning',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(516,6,25,'phrase','hit the spot','to hit the spot','hit the spot','正合我意；刚刚好；非常满足。','常用来形容食物、饮料、休息、建议等刚好满足需要。','This cup of coffee really hits the spot.\nA cold beer after work really hits the spot.\nA nap in the afternoon really hits the spot.\nThat advice really hit the spot.',NULL,NULL,'hit the spot,coffee,beer,advice',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(517,6,26,'phrase','stuck in the Stone Age','Stuck in the stone age','stuck in the Stone Age','落后；老掉牙；停留在很旧的观念或方式里。','常带幽默或批评语气，表示某人或某事太落后。','Using a flip phone in 2026? You are stuck in the Stone Age.\nSome people still think women should not work. They are stuck in the Stone Age.\nOur office is still using fax machines — we are stuck in the Stone Age.',NULL,NULL,'Stone Age,stuck in the Stone Age',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(518,6,27,'vocab','curse','curse','curse','诅咒；咒骂；脏话；不幸。','可作名词或动词。\n\n1. 名词：诅咒、不幸\n2. 动词：咒骂、诅咒\n3. 非正式：curse words = 脏话','He put a curse on the house.\nBad luck seems to be a family curse.\nShe cursed him for being late.\nHe cursed under his breath when he dropped the phone.\ncurse words\nswear words',NULL,NULL,'curse,curse words,swear words',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(519,6,28,'phrase','be in the doghouse','My wife cursed me and I can\'t use electricity. I\'m stuck in the doghouse','be in the doghouse','惹伴侣或家人生气了；被冷落；被责怪。','doghouse 是很常见的幽默表达，表示你因为做错事而“被打入冷宫”。\n\n相关自然表达：\nMy wife cursed me\n= 我老婆生气骂我，带幽默夸张感\n\nI am not allowed to use electricity\n= 我被禁止用电，夸张表达我现在很惨\n\nI am stuck in the doghouse for real this time\n= 这次我是真的惹老婆生气了','I am stuck in the doghouse.\nI am stuck in the doghouse for real this time.\nI am not allowed to use electricity.',NULL,NULL,'doghouse,not allowed',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(520,6,29,'phrase','defeat the purpose','To defeat the purpose','defeat the purpose','违背初衷；适得其反；让努力白费。','很常用的表达，表示本来为了某个目的去做事，结果反而把那个目的破坏了。','If you bring your own snacks to the party, it defeats the purpose of ordering pizza.\nWorking overtime to finish the project defeats the purpose if the quality drops.\nBuying a small car to save money, but spending it all on petrol defeats the purpose.',NULL,NULL,'defeat the purpose',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(521,6,30,'phrase','get nothing from it','To get nothing from it','get nothing from it','从中什么也得不到；没有收获。','可以指没有回报、没有好处、没有结果。','I got nothing from it.',NULL,NULL,'get nothing from it',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(522,6,31,'vocab','qualifier','qualifier','qualifier','限定条件；补充说明；资格赛选手；修饰语。','常见意思：\n\n1. 限定 / 补充说明\n2. 资格赛 / 晋级者\n3. 语法里的修饰词\n\n自然表达：\nThis comes with a qualifier.\nThere is one condition.\nThere is one catch.','That is true, but there is a qualifier.\nSmall qualifier: I am not 100 percent sure.\nHe got in as a qualifier.\nThis comes with a qualifier.',NULL,NULL,'qualifier,condition,catch',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(523,6,32,'vocab','a bummer','A bummer','a bummer','真扫兴；真倒霉；太遗憾了；真糟糕。','很常见的口语表达，可单独感叹，也可放进句子里。','Ah, bummer.\nThat is a bummer.\nIt is a bummer that the shop is closed.\nMissing the bus is such a bummer.',NULL,NULL,'bummer',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(524,6,33,'vocab','hypothetical','Hypothetical','hypothetical','假设的；假想的；假定的。','常见搭配：\nhypothetical situation\npurely hypothetical\njust hypothetically','Let us talk about a hypothetical situation.\nThis is purely hypothetical.\nJust hypothetically, what would you do?',NULL,NULL,'hypothetical,purely hypothetical',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(525,6,34,'phrase','put a lot of money into','Put a lot of money into','put a lot of money into','在……上投入很多钱。','常见近义表达：\nspend a lot of money on\nsink a lot of money into\npour money into','I have put a lot of money into this project.\nThey put a lot of money into renovating the house.\nI have already put so much money into it, I cannot quit now.\nBusinesses put a lot of money into advertising.\nI put a lot of effort into making those lessons for you.',NULL,NULL,'put money into,spend money on,sink money into,pour money into',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(526,6,35,'vocab','breast milk / formula milk','breast milk / formula milk','breast milk / formula milk','breast milk = 母乳。formula milk = 配方奶。','formula milk 指婴儿配方奶、奶粉冲的奶。','breast milk\nformula milk',NULL,NULL,'breast milk,formula milk',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(527,6,36,'phrase','get weaned off / be weaned off / wean yourself off','To get weaned off','get weaned off / be weaned off / wean yourself off','逐渐戒掉；慢慢减少依赖；逐步停用。','这个表达的核心感觉是“慢慢断掉”，不是一下子停。\n\n更口语近义表达：\ncut down on\nease off\nquit gradually\n\n对比：\nquit = 一下子戒\nget weaned off = 慢慢戒','I am trying to get weaned off coffee.\nThe doctor is helping him get weaned off the medication.\nI need to get weaned off my phone at night.\nbe weaned off something\nwean yourself off something',NULL,NULL,'weaned off,cut down on,ease off',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(528,6,37,'phrase','very handy','very handy','very handy','非常方便；非常实用；很有用。','常见场景：\n\n1. 形容物品或工具\n2. 形容技巧或信息\n3. 形容人很能干','This app is very handy for learning English.\nA pocket knife is very handy when camping.\nThat tip you gave me is very handy.\nShe is very handy around the house.',NULL,NULL,'handy,useful,practical',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(529,6,38,'phrase','only a select few things','Only a select few things','only a select few things','少数几件特别挑选的东西；只有少数几件。','带一点“精挑细选”或“范围很小”的感觉。','Only a select few things qualify for this award.\nA select few things are allowed in this area.\nJust a select few things are missing.\nThere are a select few things I still need to do.',NULL,NULL,'select few,only a select few',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(530,6,39,'phrase','on occasion / special occasion / rise to the occasion / mark the occasion','on occasion / on occasions','on occasion / for a special occasion / rise to the occasion / mark the occasion','偶尔；为了特别场合；在关键时刻顶住；纪念这个时刻。','这一组都和 occasion 有关。\n\non occasion = 偶尔\nfor a special occasion = 为了特别场合\nrise to the occasion = 临场发挥；关键时刻顶住\nmark the occasion = 庆祝 / 纪念这个时刻','I eat fast food on occasion.\nI only wear this suit for special occasions.\nHe really rose to the occasion.\nWe had a small dinner to mark the occasion.',NULL,NULL,'on occasion,special occasion,rise to the occasion,mark the occasion',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(531,6,40,'phrase','bulk up / bulked up','bulked up','bulk up / bulked up','练壮；增肌；扩充规模；增加体量。','常见两类意思：\n\n1. 说人\n= 变壮了；练结实了\n\n2. 说团队 / 内容 / 规模\n= 扩充；增加体量','He has really bulked up since last year.\nI am trying to bulk up before summer.\nThe company has bulked up its team.\nThey bulked up the report with more data.',NULL,NULL,'bulk up,bulked up',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(532,6,41,'vocab','pay off','Pay off','pay off','付清；得到回报；成功；见效。','常见意思：\n\n1. 付清债务\n2. 努力有回报\n3. 计划或冒险最后成功','I finally paid off my loan.\nShe is working hard to pay off her credit card debt.\nAll the hard work paid off.\nStudying late every night finally paid off.\nThe plan paid off in the end.\nTaking that risk paid off.',NULL,NULL,'pay off,loan,hard work',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(533,6,42,'sentence','Aircraft is a general term. It refers to any machine that can fly.','Aircraft is a general term. It refers to any machine that can fly.','Aircraft is a general term. It refers to any machine that can fly.','Aircraft 是一个总称，指任何能够飞行的机器。','aircraft 是集合性很强的词，单复数形式一样。','Aircraft is a general term. It refers to any machine that can fly.',NULL,NULL,'aircraft',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(534,6,43,'vocab','retrieve','retrieve','retrieve','取回；找回；检索；提取。','比较正式，常见于书面语和技术语境，强调“从某处找回或检索出来”。','The database can retrieve records from last year.\nHe went to retrieve his luggage from the lost-and-found.',NULL,NULL,'retrieve,database,luggage',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(535,6,44,'vocab','comprise','comprise','comprise','由……组成；包含。','注意：comprise 后面通常不加 of。\n\n整体包含部分：\nThe whole comprises the parts.','The system comprises three modules.\nThe course comprises lectures and labs.',NULL,NULL,'comprise,modules,labs',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(536,6,45,'vocab','delegate','Delegate','delegate','委派；授权；代表；被委派的人。','既可作动词，也可作名词。\n\n动词：\ndelegate tasks to someone\ndelegate responsibility\ndelegate authority\n\n名词：\ndelegate = 代表\n\n技术语境常见：\npermission delegation\ntask delegation\nIAM roles delegate access\nservice accounts delegate permissions','The manager delegates tasks to her team.\nYou should delegate responsibilities instead of doing everything yourself.\nIAM roles delegate permissions to users or services.\nEach country sends a delegate to the conference.\nThe delegates discussed the project plan.',NULL,NULL,'delegate,delegation,authority',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(537,6,46,'vocab','shiny','siny adjective','shiny','有光泽的；发亮的。','常见搭配：\nshiny hair\nshiny shoes\nshiny surface\nshiny metal\nshiny eyes\n\n和 bright 的区别：\nshiny 更强调表面反光。\nbright 更强调自己发出强光。','shiny hair\nshiny shoes\nshiny surface\nshiny metal\nshiny eyes',NULL,NULL,'shiny,bright',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(538,6,47,'phrase','I am being sarcastic.','I’m being sarcastic','I am being sarcastic.','我在讽刺；我在说反话；我在挖苦，不是认真的。','sarcastic = 用反话表达真实意思。\n\n相关词：\nsarcasm = 讽刺\nsarcastically = 讽刺地','I am being sarcastic.\nI am just being sarcastic.',NULL,NULL,'sarcastic,sarcasm',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(539,6,48,'phrase','pet the cat','pet the cat','pet the cat','摸猫；抚摸猫。','pet 作动词时表示抚摸动物。\n\n常见表达：\npet the cat\npet the dog\nI am petting the cat.\nHe is petting his dog.','pet the cat\npet the dog\nI am petting the cat.\nHe is petting his dog.',NULL,NULL,'pet the cat,petting',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(540,6,49,'vocab','imperceptible','imperceptible','imperceptible','难以察觉的；几乎感觉不到的；极其细微的。','常见场景：\n1. 声音很小\n2. 变化很小\n3. 表情很轻微\n\n更简单替代表达：\nbarely noticeable\nhardly noticeable','The sound was almost imperceptible.\nThere was an imperceptible change in temperature.\nHe gave an imperceptible smile.',NULL,NULL,'imperceptible,barely noticeable,hardly noticeable',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(541,6,50,'vocab','wavy / telescope / binoculars / monocular','wavy / telescope / binoculars / monocular','wavy / telescope / binoculars / monocular','wavy = 波浪状的。telescope = 望远镜。binoculars = 双筒望远镜。monocular = 单筒望远镜。','wavy 常用于头发、线条、边缘。\n\ntelescope 常指天文望远镜或长筒望远镜。\nbinoculars 是双筒的。\nmonocular 是单筒的。','This will leave my hair wavy.',NULL,NULL,'wavy,telescope,binoculars,monocular',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(542,6,51,'vocab','toss','toss','toss','轻轻一扔；抛；甩；翻拌。','核心感觉是动作快速、随意，不一定很用力。\n\n常见意思：\n1. 扔 / 抛\n2. 翻动 / 拌\n3. 甩 / 摆动\n\n常见搭配：\ntoss a coin\ntoss a ball\ntoss something aside\ntoss a salad\ntoss the noodles\ntoss your hair','Toss it to me.\nHe tossed the ball.\ntoss a coin\ntoss a ball\ntoss something aside\ntoss a salad\ntoss the noodles\nShe tossed her head.\nI toss my hair upside down.',NULL,NULL,'toss,coin,ball,salad,hair',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(543,6,52,'sentence','I got this when I was a lot younger.','I got this when I was a lot younger.','I got this when I was a lot younger.','我很小的时候就有这个了。','a lot younger = 年轻很多；小很多。','I got this when I was a lot younger.',NULL,NULL,'a lot younger',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(544,6,53,'phrase','to some extent / extent','I’m ready to some extent / extent','to some extent / extent','在某种程度上；程度；范围；限度。','自然表达：\nI am ready to some extent.\nI am somewhat ready.\nI am kind of ready.\nI am partly prepared.\nI am not fully ready, but I am getting there.\n\nextent 常见用法：\nto some extent\nto a great extent\nto a limited extent\nthe extent of the damage\nthe extent of the problem\nthe extent to which ...','I agree to some extent.\nIt is true to some extent.\nIt helped to a great extent.\nOnly to a limited extent.\nthe extent of the damage\nthe extent to which people rely on phones',NULL,NULL,'extent,to some extent,to a great extent',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(545,6,54,'phrase','sneak peek / sneak / sneaky','Last week, I gave you a sneak peek','sneak peek / sneak / sneaky','抢先看；偷看；偷偷做某事；鬼鬼祟祟的。','a sneak peek = 提前看一眼；先睹为快。\n\nsneak 常见用法：\nsneak in\nsneak out\nsneak up on\nsneak a look\nsneak a peek\n\nsneaky = 鬼鬼祟祟的；狡猾的','Last week, I gave you a sneak peek.\nHe sneaked into the room.\nShe sneaked out after dinner.\nDo not sneak up on me.\nI sneaked a peek at the gift.\nThat was a sneaky move.\nHe is being sneaky.',NULL,NULL,'sneak peek,sneak,sneaky',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(546,6,55,'phrase','They irritate his eyes / irritate','They irritate his eyes','They irritate his eyes / irritate','它们刺激他的眼睛；让他的眼睛不舒服。irritate = 刺激；惹恼。','irritate 的核心感觉是：让身体不舒服，或者让情绪不爽。\n\n1. 身体刺激\n2. 情绪惹恼\n\n相关词：\nirritated\nirritating\nirritation\n\n更口语替代表达：\nbug\nannoy\nmake something itchy\nmake something sore\nmake something sting\nmake something water','They irritate his eyes.\nThis smoke irritates my throat.\nThe detergent irritated my skin.\nHis attitude irritates me.\nIt irritates him when people are late.\nIt bugs me.',NULL,NULL,'irritate,eyes,irritated,irritating',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(547,6,56,'vocab','sensation','sensation','sensation','感觉；感受；刺激感；轰动的人或事。','常见意思：\n\n1. 身体上的感觉\n2. 情绪或直觉上的感觉\n3. 媒体语境里的轰动','I have a strange sensation in my chest.\na burning sensation\na tingling sensation\na numb sensation\na sensation of relief\na sensation that something is wrong\nThe new movie is a sensation.',NULL,NULL,'sensation,burning sensation,tingling sensation',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(548,6,57,'phrase','drip down','drip down','drip down','滴下来；往下滴；缓慢往下流。','强调液体一点点往下走。\n\n和 run down 的区别：\ndrip down = 滴、慢慢流\nrun down = 更像成股流下来','Water dripped down the wall.\nSweat dripped down my face.\nRainwater dripped down from the roof.\nTears ran down her cheeks.',NULL,NULL,'drip down,run down,sweat,water',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(549,6,58,'vocab','sweat / sweaty / sweating buckets / breaking a sweat','Sweat','sweat / sweaty / sweating buckets / breaking a sweat','汗；出汗；满身汗；汗如雨下；开始出汗。','常见口语表达：\n\nI am sweating a lot.\nI am all sweaty.\nI am sweating buckets.\nI am breaking a sweat.','I am sweating a lot.\nI am all sweaty.\nI am sweating buckets.\nI am breaking a sweat.',NULL,NULL,'sweat,sweaty,sweating buckets,breaking a sweat',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(550,6,59,'sentence','Did this come from a donation too? / Was this one donated as well?','这个也是别人捐赠的吗？','Did this come from a donation too? / Was this one donated as well?','这个也是别人捐赠的吗？','两个都自然。\n\ncome from a donation 更偏来源。\nwas donated 更直接说这是捐赠来的。','Did this come from a donation too?\nWas this one donated as well?',NULL,NULL,'donation,donated',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09',1,'2026-04-05 12:41:09'),(551,7,1,'vocab','shield','shield','shield','盾牌；防护物；保护；保护；挡住；庇护。','shield 可作名词，也可作动词。\n\n1. 名词\n= 盾牌；防护物；保护\n\n2. 动词\n= 保护；挡住；庇护\n\n常见搭配：\nriot shield\nface shield\nshield someone from something\nshield someone against something','a riot shield\nface shield\nSunscreen acts as a shield against UV.\nHe tried to shield his eyes from the sun.\nParents want to shield their kids from harm.',NULL,NULL,'shield,riot shield,face shield',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(552,7,2,'phrase','immerse yourself in','immerse yourself in','immerse yourself in','沉浸在……之中。','表示把自己完全投入到某个环境、活动、语言或体验里。','Immerse yourself in English.\nImmerse yourself in the culture.',NULL,NULL,'immerse yourself in',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(553,7,3,'phrase','inside out / right side out','inside out','inside out / right side out','里外反了；翻回正面。','inside out = 里外反了。\nright side out = 翻回正面。','The shirt is inside out.\nI have to turn it the right side out.',NULL,NULL,'inside out,right side out',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(554,7,4,'vocab','comfy','comfortable -> comfy','comfy','舒服的；舒适的。','comfy 是 comfortable 的口语缩写，更日常、更轻松。','Clothes can be comfy.\nWhat a comfy house you have.',NULL,NULL,'comfy,comfortable',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(555,7,5,'phrase','clean up a mess / clean up your messes','clean up a mess / clean up your messes','clean up a mess / clean up your messes','收拾烂摊子；把自己弄乱的东西收拾干净。','既可以指字面上的收拾，也可以指处理自己造成的问题。','You always leave stuff everywhere. Clean up your messes.',NULL,NULL,'clean up a mess,clean up your messes',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(556,7,6,'vocab','father figure / role model','Father figure / Role model','father figure / role model','父亲般的人；父亲角色；榜样。','father figure 指在生活中起到像父亲一样引导、照顾、支持作用的人，不一定是亲生父亲。\n\n常见搭配：\na strong father figure\nlack a father figure\nserve as a father figure','He is a father figure to me.\nMy coach became a father figure for many of us.\nShe did not have a father figure growing up.',NULL,NULL,'father figure,role model',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(557,7,7,'phrase','in charge of','incharge of + 名词 / 动名词','in charge of','负责……；主管……。','结构：\nin charge of + 名词\nin charge of + 动名词','She is in charge of the project.\nHe is in charge of hiring new staff.',NULL,NULL,'in charge of',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(558,7,8,'phrase','get into the habit of doing something','get in / into the habit of doing something','get into the habit of doing something','养成做某事的习惯。','强调开始进入这个习惯，慢慢养成。','Try to get into the habit of speaking English every day.\nI have gotten into the habit of cleaning up my messes.',NULL,NULL,'get into the habit of',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(559,7,9,'vocab','nostalgia / nostalgic','Nostalgia','nostalgia / nostalgic','怀旧；怀念过去；怀旧的。','nostalgia 指对过去事物、时光或经历的怀念情绪。\nnostalgic 是形容词。','Listening to old songs fills me with nostalgia.\nHe felt a wave of nostalgia when he visited his childhood home.\nI feel nostalgic about my school days.\nnostalgic memories\na sense of nostalgia',NULL,NULL,'nostalgia,nostalgic',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(560,7,10,'phrase','look back fondly on / at','look back fondly on/at','look back fondly on / at','带着美好感情回忆；甜蜜地回想。','look back = 回头看 / 回忆。\nfondly = 充满喜爱、温情地。\n\n用 on：\n更强调时间、经历、阶段\n\n用 at：\n更强调具体对象、场景、照片等','I look back fondly on my childhood summers.\nShe looks back fondly on her years at university.\nWe can look back fondly at the memories we made together.\nHe looked back fondly at his first classroom.\nWe look back fondly at the photos from that trip.',NULL,NULL,'look back fondly on,look back fondly at',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(561,7,11,'vocab','ideally','ideally','ideally','理想情况下；最好是。','常见于建议、计划、指导。\n\n近义或替代表达：\nin an ideal world\npreferably\noptimally','Ideally, we should finish this project by Friday.\nIdeally, I would like to take a year off to travel.\nIdeally, you want to keep your password secure.\nIdeally, the meeting should start at 9 a.m.\nIn an ideal world, everyone would have access to education.\nPreferably, we should finish this task today.\nThe machine works optimally at 70 degrees Celsius.',NULL,NULL,'ideally,preferably,optimally',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(562,7,12,'phrase','do the dishes / set it to dry / wash something by hand','doing the dishes / set it to dry / wash something by hand','do the dishes / set it to dry / wash something by hand','洗碗；让它晾干；手洗某物。','都是很实用的家务表达。','I am doing the dishes.\nSet it to dry.\nWash something by hand.',NULL,NULL,'do the dishes,set it to dry,wash by hand',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(563,7,13,'phrase','let it slide','let it slide','let it slide','算了吧；不追究了；放一马；睁一只眼闭一只眼。','表示对小错误、小问题、小冒犯选择不计较。\n\n近义表达：\nlet it go\ngive someone a pass\nturn a blind eye to something','He was late again, but I decided to let it slide this time.\nShe forgot to reply, but I will let it slide.\nDo not worry about the typo. We can let it slide.',NULL,NULL,'let it slide,let it go,give someone a pass',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(564,7,14,'phrase','in a row','in a row','in a row','连续地；接连不断地；一连。','常见搭配：\nX times in a row\nX days in a row\nX weeks in a row\nwin / lose / fail / forget + in a row','I worked late three nights in a row.\nHe won the game five times in a row.\nI forgot my keys two days in a row.',NULL,NULL,'in a row',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(565,7,15,'phrase','let it soak','let it soak','let it soak','让它泡一会儿；让它浸着。','很常见的生活表达，尤其洗锅、洗衣、去污场景。','The pan is dirty — let it soak for 10 minutes.\nIf the stain is tough, let it soak overnight.',NULL,NULL,'let it soak,stain,pan',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(566,7,16,'sentence','Do you have anything out the back?','Do you have anything out the back?','Do you have anything out the back?','你们后面仓库还有货吗？后面还有存货吗？','out the back 是英式 / 新西兰很自然的说法，指后面、后仓、后面储藏区。','Do you have anything out the back?',NULL,NULL,'out the back',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(567,7,17,'vocab','cat scratching post','cat scrathing post','cat scratching post','猫抓板；猫抓柱。','给猫抓挠用的东西。','cat scratching post',NULL,NULL,'cat scratching post',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(568,7,18,'vocab','leftovers / residue','leftovers / Residue','leftovers / residue','leftovers = 剩菜；剩余的东西。residue = 残余；残留物；残渣。','leftovers 更常见于食物剩下的部分。\nresidue 更常见于物理、化学、残渣或抽象残留感。','We had pizza last night, and there are some leftovers in the fridge.\nI usually take leftovers for lunch at work.\nThe law was a leftover from the 19th century.\nAfter boiling, a residue forms at the bottom of the pan.\nThe chemical reaction leaves a toxic residue.\nThe movie left a residue of sadness in me.',NULL,NULL,'leftovers,residue',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(569,7,19,'phrase','throw it in','To throw it in','throw it in','把它扔进去；把它加进去。','具体意思要看语境，常见是“扔进去”或“顺手加进去”。','Throw it in.',NULL,NULL,'throw it in',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(570,7,20,'phrase','get + noun + adjective','Get the water hot','get + noun + adjective','让某物变成某种状态。','这是很实用的句型：\n\nget the water hot\nget the dinner ready\nget the kids dressed','Get the water hot.\nGet the dinner ready.\nGet the kids dressed.',NULL,NULL,'get noun adjective',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(571,7,21,'phrase','picky eater','No one in my house is a picky eater','picky eater','挑食的人。','相关自然表达：\nMy family is not picky about food.\nEveryone in my family eats whatever.\nThere is no picky eater in my household.','No one in my house is a picky eater.\nMy family is not picky about food.\nEveryone in my family eats whatever.\nThere is no picky eater in my household.',NULL,NULL,'picky eater',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(572,7,22,'vocab','commiserate','commiserate','commiserate','同情；表示怜悯；一起感叹不幸。','常见结构：\ncommiserate with someone\n表示和某人一起为糟糕的处境感到难过。','I commiserated with her after the bad news.',NULL,NULL,'commiserate',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(573,7,23,'sentence','The Chinese lunar calendar explanation','在教会为大家解释中国的阴历与春节','The Chinese lunar calendar is based on the moon going around the Earth, so a month is roughly one lunar cycle. Some months have 30 days, some have 29. If you just kept it like that every year, the dates would slowly move earlier and earlier. Because Chinese New Year is the first day of the first month in the lunar calendar, it would eventually come too early. So people came up with a rule: after a certain period of time, they add an extra month, a leap month. That way, Chinese New Year always stays around January or February.','中国阴历以月亮绕地球运行为基础，一个月大致就是一个朔望月。有的月份 30 天，有的 29 天。如果每年都完全照这样算，日期会慢慢越来越提前。因为农历新年是农历正月初一，它最终会来得太早。所以人们想出了一个规则：过一段时间就加一个额外的月份，也就是闰月。这样，春节就会一直保持在一月或二月附近。','这是一段很自然、适合解释中国农历与春节日期为什么浮动的英文说明。','The Chinese lunar calendar is based on the moon going around the Earth...',NULL,NULL,'lunar calendar,Chinese New Year,leap month',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(574,7,24,'sentence','There are lots of big open grassy areas in New Zealand, but it is hard to find places that big in China.','在新西兰有很多大片的草坪，但是在中国很难找到这么大一块的草坪','There are lots of big open grassy areas in New Zealand, but it is hard to find places that big in China.','新西兰有很多大片开阔的草地，但在中国很难找到这么大的地方。','big open grassy areas = 大片开阔的草地。','There are lots of big open grassy areas in New Zealand, but it is hard to find places that big in China.',NULL,NULL,'grassy areas,New Zealand,China',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(575,7,25,'phrase','You will be a pro in no time / in no time','You\'ll be pro in no time / in no time','You will be a pro in no time / in no time','你很快就会变成高手；很快；马上；用不了多久。','in no time = 很快；马上。\n\n相关自然表达：\nYou will get the hang of it in no time.\nYou will be sweet in no time.\nYou will pick it up in no time.','You will be a pro in no time.\nDinner will be ready in no time.\nI will be back in no time.\nYou will get used to it in no time.\nYou will get the hang of it in no time.\nYou will pick it up in no time.',NULL,NULL,'in no time,pro,get the hang of it',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(576,7,26,'phrase','go with your gut','Go with your gut','go with your gut','凭直觉行事；相信第一感觉；跟着感觉走。','gut 在这里不是肠子的字面意思，而是直觉、本能判断。\n\n近义表达：\ntrust your instincts\nfollow your intuition\nlisten to your gut','Go with your gut. You know what is right.\nI did not overthink it — I went with my gut.\nIf something feels off, go with your gut.',NULL,NULL,'go with your gut,instincts,intuition',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(577,7,27,'phrase','I am on a mission','I\'m on a mission','I am on a mission','我现在很有目标感；我正在下定决心做一件事。','带一点专注、干劲、势在必行的感觉。','I am on a mission to improve my English fluency.\nI am on a mission to get fit this year.\nI am on a mission to fix this bug before lunch.\nI am on a mission today — do not distract me.',NULL,NULL,'on a mission',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(578,7,28,'phrase','I am not using my smartphone for a month.','I\'m not using my smartphone for a month','I am not using my smartphone for a month.','我这个月打算不用手机；我正在执行一个一个月不用手机的计划。','这里用现在进行时，是因为它强调：\n\n1. 这是一个有开始点和结束点的临时决定\n2. 这是正在进行中的计划或挑战\n\n而 do not use 更像一般陈述，不强调这个阶段性的安排。','I am not using my smartphone for a month.',NULL,NULL,'not using,my smartphone,for a month',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08',1,'2026-04-05 12:54:08'),(579,8,1,'phrase','crisp air / The air is so crisp','The air is so crisp','crisp air / The air is so crisp','清新的空气；空气很清爽。','crisp air 是非常地道的搭配，尤其在新西兰口语里很常见，表示空气清冷、清爽、很舒服。','The air is so crisp.\nSuch a crisp day today.\nThe air is nice and crisp this morning.',NULL,NULL,'crisp air,crisp day',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(580,8,2,'vocab','fancy','live in a fancy apartment / fancy doing','fancy','想要；喜欢；有兴趣；花哨的；高档的；自以为了不起。','fancy 常见意思有几种。1. fancy = 想要 / 喜欢 / 有兴趣，常见结构：fancy + 名词，fancy + doing something。2. fancy = 觉得 / 认为，带一点主观猜测。3. fancy = 花哨的 / 高档的 / 精致的。4. fancy oneself = 自以为了不起。固定表达：Fancy that. Take a fancy to. Not my fancy.','Do you fancy a coffee?\nI fancy going for a walk.\nI do not really fancy it.\nI fancy he has already left.\na fancy restaurant\nThat is a fancy watch.\nHe fancies himself a genius.\nFancy that!',NULL,NULL,'fancy,fancy doing,fancy restaurant',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(581,8,3,'phrase','let someone down','I feel like I am letting that guy down','let someone down','让某人失望；辜负某人。','非常常用、很地道的表达。相关自然说法：I kinda feel like I am letting him down. I feel bad, like I am letting that guy down.','I feel like I am letting that guy down.\nI do not want to let you down.\nHe let his team down.',NULL,NULL,'let someone down',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(582,8,4,'phrase','be worthy of / deserve / good enough','I am not worthy of him','be worthy of / deserve / good enough','配得上；值得；足够好。','I am not worthy of him 语气比较重，偏书面或情绪很深。更日常自然的说法：I do not feel worthy of him. I do not think I deserve him. He deserves better than me. I feel like I am not good enough for him. Honestly, he deserves way better.','I do not feel worthy of him.\nI do not think I deserve him.\nHe deserves better than me.\nI feel like I am not good enough for him.',NULL,NULL,'worthy of,deserve,good enough',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(583,8,5,'vocab','impress / impressed / impressive','impress','impress / impressed / impressive','给人留下深刻印象；佩服；令人印象深刻的。','常见结构：impress someone；be impressed with；be impressed by。常见搭配：deeply impressed，first impression，try to impress。','He really impressed me.\nHis English impressed everyone.\nI am impressed with your progress.\nWe were impressed with the service.\nThat is impressive.\nNot bad, I am impressed.',NULL,NULL,'impress,impressed,impressive',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(584,8,6,'phrase','hold on to','I want us to hold on to today','hold on to','抓住；保留；珍惜。','在这个句子里表示珍惜今天、抓住此刻，不让这一刻溜走。','I want us to hold on to today.\nHold on to this feeling.\nHold on to the memories.',NULL,NULL,'hold on to,memories,feeling',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(585,8,7,'phrase','by making them tea / yell at them','by making them tea / yell at them','by making them tea / yell at them','通过给他们泡茶；朝他们大叫。','两个都很实用：by doing something = 通过做某事。yell at someone = 朝某人大叫。','You are making his life a little bit easier by making them tea.\nDo not yell at them.',NULL,NULL,'by making them tea,yell at them',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(586,8,8,'phrase','friend filter / dream self','that the friend filter / dream self','friend filter / dream self','朋友滤镜；理想中的自己。','friend filter 表示因为对方是朋友，所以看法会受到关系影响。dream self 表示理想中的自己、想成为的那个自己。','Maybe that is the friend filter.\nMy dream self is more confident.',NULL,NULL,'friend filter,dream self',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(587,8,9,'phrase','make someone\'s life easier / make someone\'s day easier / heaps','you are making his life a little bit easier','make someone\'s life easier / make someone\'s day easier / heaps','让某人的生活更轻松一点；让某人的一天更轻松；很多。','很自然的表达。新西兰口语里：That helps him heaps. heaps = 很多，非常。','You are making his life a little bit easier.\nYou are making his day easier.\nThat helps him heaps.',NULL,NULL,'make life easier,make day easier,heaps',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(588,8,10,'sentence','I want to be a confident public speaker, but right now I get nervous even ordering coffee in English.','I want to be a confident public speaker,but now I just get nervous just ordering coffee in English','I want to be a confident public speaker, but right now I get nervous even ordering coffee in English.','我想成为一个自信的公众演讲者，但现在就连用英语点咖啡我都会紧张。','这里用 even ordering coffee 更自然，表示“连这么小的事都会紧张”。','I want to be a confident public speaker, but right now I get nervous even ordering coffee in English.',NULL,NULL,'public speaker,nervous,ordering coffee',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(589,8,11,'vocab','fantasy / fantastical','fantasy','fantasy / fantastical','幻想；想象世界；不现实的愿望；幻想风格的。','fantasy 可指不现实的想法，也可指奇幻类型。fantastical 是形容词。','That plan sounds like a fantasy.\nI love fantasy movies.',NULL,NULL,'fantasy,fantastical',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(590,8,12,'vocab','movie montage','movie montage','movie montage','电影蒙太奇；快速剪辑片段。','把多个短镜头快速剪在一起，用来表现时间流逝、训练过程、成长、经历总结或营造节奏。','movie montage',NULL,NULL,'movie montage,montage',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(591,8,13,'phrase','too much to carry / too heavy to carry / too much to handle','it\'s too much to carry','too much to carry / too heavy to carry / too much to handle','拿不动；承受不了；负担太重。','既可以指物理上太重，也可以比喻心理负担太大。相关表达：It is too heavy to carry. It is too much for me. I cannot carry this on my own. That is too much to handle.','It is too much to carry.\nIt is too heavy to carry.\nIt is too much for me.\nI cannot carry this on my own.\nThat is too much to handle.',NULL,NULL,'too much to carry,too much to handle',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(592,8,14,'phrase','like a failure / ordinary moment / make the journey feel cozy / It feels like a shield / but that is the trap','like a failure / ordinary moment / make the journey feel cozy / It feels like a shield / but that\'s the trap','like a failure / ordinary moment / make the journey feel cozy / It feels like a shield / but that is the trap','像个失败者；普通时刻；让这段旅程感觉温暖舒服；感觉像一层保护；但那就是陷阱。','这一组是表达感受和抽象比喻的短语，适合写作和口语表达。','I feel like a failure.\nIt was just an ordinary moment.\nSmall rituals can make the journey feel cozy.\nIt feels like a shield.\nBut that is the trap.',NULL,NULL,'failure,ordinary moment,cozy,shield,trap',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(593,8,15,'vocab','act out / acting out','acting out/act out','act out / acting out','通过外显行为表达内心情绪；把戏演出来。','常见意思：1. 心理或行为学 = 用外显行为表达内心情绪。2. 戏剧或表演 = 把某一幕演出来。','The child is acting out because he feels neglected.\nShe is acting out her anger through reckless driving.\nThey are acting out a scene from the play.',NULL,NULL,'act out,acting out',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(594,8,16,'vocab','scenario / stick to / audition','scenario / I\'m sticking to the script of the old Daniel / audition','scenario / stick to / audition','情景；坚持；遵守；试镜；试演。','scenario = 情景，设想的情况。stick to = 坚持；遵守。audition 可作名词也可作动词。','That is a possible scenario.\nI am sticking to the script of the old Daniel.\nYou can audition for a new role whenever you want.',NULL,NULL,'scenario,stick to,audition',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(595,8,17,'phrase','doodling / start to fade','just spend five minutes doodling on a piece of paper / start to fade','doodling / start to fade','涂鸦；开始褪去；开始消失；逐渐减弱。','doodle = 随手乱画。start to fade 可用于颜色、记忆、声音、感情、光线等多种场景。','Just spend five minutes doodling on a piece of paper.\nThe colour started to fade.\nThe memory started to fade.',NULL,NULL,'doodle,doodling,start to fade',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(596,8,18,'vocab','clumsy / awkward / statue / sculpture / monument / idol','clumsy / awkward / statue sculpture monument idol','clumsy / awkward / statue / sculpture / monument / idol','clumsy = 笨拙的。awkward = 尴尬的、难处理的。statue = 立体人物雕像。sculpture = 雕塑。monument = 纪念碑。idol = 偶像、宗教雕像。','clumsy 可形容人动作笨拙、东西笨重不方便，也可指处理起来别扭。awkward 也可以形容难处理、棘手。statue 相关对比：statue = 立体人物 / 神像；sculpture = 更广泛，任何雕塑；monument = 纪念碑，通常更大；idol = 偶像 / 宗教雕像。常见搭配：bronze statue，marble statue，ancient statue，lifelike statue，Statue of Liberty。','I feel clumsy today.\nDo not be so clumsy.\nThat was a clumsy move.\nThis is an awkward situation.\nThe table is in an awkward position.\nbronze statue\nmarble statue\nancient statue\nlifelike statue\nStatue of Liberty',NULL,NULL,'clumsy,awkward,statue,sculpture,monument,idol',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(597,8,19,'vocab','stumble','stumble','stumble','绊倒；踉跄；说话结巴；表现失常；偶然发现。','常见意思：1. 绊倒 / 踉跄。2. 说话结巴 / 表现不好。3. stumble upon / across = 偶然发现。对比：stumble over = 被……绊到；说话卡壳。run into = 偶然遇见人。','I stumbled on the stairs.\nHe stumbled and almost fell.\nShe stumbled over her words.\nHe stumbled during his interview.\nI stumbled upon a great cafe.\nShe stumbled across an old photo.',NULL,NULL,'stumble,stumble upon,stumble across,stumble over',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(598,8,20,'phrase','there is nowhere left to go / ruined canvases / whisper / stage / comeback','if you are perfect there\'s nowhere left to go / thousand ruined canvases in the trash / whisper / stage / comeback','there is nowhere left to go / ruined canvases / whisper / stage / comeback','没有剩下的进步空间；被毁掉的画布；低声说；舞台、阶段；复出、反击。','这一组包含几个高频表达：there is nowhere left to go = 没有进步空间了。ruined canvases = 被毁掉的画布。whisper 可作名词或动词。stage 可作名词：舞台、阶段；可作动词：组织、上演、策划。comeback = 复出；东山再起；机智反驳。','If you are perfect, there is nowhere left to go.\na thousand ruined canvases in the trash\nShe whispered a secret in my ear.\nI heard a whisper behind the door.\nShe walked onto the stage to give her speech.\nWe are in the final stage of the project.\nThey staged a protest outside the government building.\nThe singer made a spectacular comeback after ten years.\nHe had a clever comeback to her joke.',NULL,NULL,'whisper,stage,comeback,canvas',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(599,8,21,'phrase','growth mindset vocabulary set','growth mindset / belief / brief / discomfort / push through / spark / admit / red X / shout at you / fit here / shift / principle / trial and error / messed up / lucky star / default thought / varsity / core insight / chipped away / get out of the way / inevitable result / resilient / bucket of talent / stay motivated / excuse to quit / defense mechanism / starting line / finish line / seek out the difficult stuff / weightlifter / quit because it feels like too much / in control of my own progress','growth mindset vocabulary set','成长型思维相关的一组表达。','这一组内容围绕成长型思维、试错、坚持、自我认知。重点表达包括：A growth mindset is simply the belief that your basic abilities can be developed through dedication and hard work. belief = 信念；看法。brief = 简短的；简报；简要说明。discomfort = 不适；不安。push through = 咬牙坚持；硬撑过去。That is exactly the spark of a growth mindset. I have to admit. To me, a mistake felt like a big red X on a test paper. shout at you. this word does not fit here. That is a big shift for me. mistakes have consequences. Even then, the principle stays the same. trial and error = 试错法。I messed up = 我搞砸了。I stuffed it up = 新西兰口语。they were just born under a lucky star. that is the default thought. varsity = 校队。the core insight is that ... one key insight. had to be chipped away. get out of the way. inevitable result. resilient = 有韧性的；不轻易被打倒的。I was born with a small bucket of talent. it is hard to stay motivated. it gives us an excuse to quit. defense mechanism. starting line / finish line. you seek out the difficult stuff. weightlifter. You want to quit because it feels like too much. in control of my own progress。关于 mistakes 那句，更准确的表达是：People with a growth mindset do not fear mistakes; they learn from them.','Learning to cook is a process of trial and error.\nWe finally solved the problem through trial and error.\nI really messed up my schedule.\nThat is the default thought.\nThe core insight is that consistent practice matters.\nThe old paint was chipped away with a scraper.\nThe car could not pass because the truck was not getting out of the way.\nHis failure was an inevitable result of his laziness.\nShe is really resilient.\nIt is hard to stay motivated.\nYou seek out the difficult stuff.\nI want to feel in control of my own progress.',NULL,NULL,'growth mindset,trial and error,messed up,resilient,core insight',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(600,8,22,'phrase','emotion and imagery set','after talking about all this / excited but quiet inside / long road ahead / sprinting past me / trailing behind / cold shiver / feeling in the chest','emotion and imagery set','表达情绪和画面感的一组短语。','这一组适合写作、口语反思、演讲感受表达。after talking about all this。I feel excited but also a little quiet inside。It is like I am looking at a long road ahead of me。sprinting past me。be the one trailing behind。cold shiver。feeling in the chest。','After talking about all this, I feel excited but also a little quiet inside.\nIt is like I am looking at a long road ahead of me.\nSome people are sprinting past me.\nI do not want to be the one trailing behind.\nI felt a cold shiver.\nThere was a heavy feeling in my chest.',NULL,NULL,'long road ahead,trailing behind,cold shiver,feeling in the chest',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(601,8,23,'vocab','patch of soil / urge / push through it / pointless / cast a vote for / hard on yourself / lay down tracks / grip / traction','patch of soil / urge / push through it / pointless / end up doing nothing / cast a vote for / don\'t be hard on yourself / wipe it away / tracks are laid down one metre at a time / make the result inevitable / big shift / grip on the road','patch of soil / urge / push through it / pointless / cast a vote for / hard on yourself / lay down tracks / grip / traction','一小块土；冲动；硬撑过去；没意义；为……投票；别对自己太苛刻；铺设轨道；抓地力。','这一组包括：patch of soil = 一小块土。urge 名词：强烈冲动；动词：催促；强烈建议。push through it = 咬牙坚持；硬撑过去。it feels pointless = 感觉没意义。constant motivation = 持续不断的动力。end up doing nothing = 最后什么都没做。casting a vote for the person you want to become = 你每次选择，都是在为你想成为的人投票。Do not be hard on yourself = 别对自己太苛刻。you can wipe it away with a single finger = 你可以用一根手指把它擦掉。tracks are laid down one metre at a time = 轨道是一米一米铺设的。lay down = 铺设；建立。make the result inevitable = 让结果成为必然。That is a big shift in how I see things = 这是我看待事情方式上的一个大转变。grip on the road = 轮胎对路面的抓地力。traction = 更专业的说法。','There is a patch of soil in the backyard.\nI planted some herbs in a small patch of soil.\nI had a strong urge to check my phone.\nHe felt the urge to speak up.\nI urge you to apply for this role.\nI was exhausted, but I pushed through it.\nIt feels pointless now, but it will not always feel this way.\nWe think small steps do not count.\nHe is a liar. Nothing he says counts.\nChoosing an apple over a cookie.\nDo not be hard on yourself.\nThe bike\'s tyres have great grip on the road.\nThis car has good traction.',NULL,NULL,'patch of soil,urge,push through it,pointless,grip,traction',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(602,8,24,'phrase','talk yourself out of / show up for / technique / psychologist / implementation intention','I need a way to stop me from talking me out of my goals every morning / show up for / technique / psychologist / implementation intention','talk yourself out of / show up for / technique / psychologist / implementation intention','自己把自己劝退；为……出现并负责；技巧；心理学家；实施意图。','talk oneself out of something = 自己把自己劝退；劝自己放弃。show up for something = 出现；坚持；对……负责。technique = 技巧。psychologist = 心理学家。implementation intention = 实施意图 / 执行意图。','I need a way to stop myself from talking myself out of my goals every morning.\nI need a way to show up for my goals every morning.',NULL,NULL,'talk yourself out of,show up for,implementation intention',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(603,8,25,'phrase','enough / sufficient / bypass / out of the equation / bring someone to / physical paralysis / rule out / the latter / the former','You have enough time to do your homework / bypass / fail at discipline / vague / out of the equation / pre-programming my brain / internal debate / bring us to / physical paralysis / rule out the latter','enough / sufficient / bypass / out of the equation / bring someone to / physical paralysis / rule out / the latter / the former','足够；充分；绕过；不再作为考虑因素；把某人带到；身体僵住；排除；后者；前者。','这一组的重点：You have enough time to do your homework = 很自然的说法。You have sufficient time to do your homework = 更正式。bypass = 绕过；规避。a simple way to bypass overthinking。He tried to bypass the rules. You can bypass the login screen by using this shortcut. fail at discipline = 在自律这件事上失败。we made our goals too vague = 我们把目标设得太模糊了。this leaves too much room for your brain to argue with you = 这给大脑留下太多跟你抬杠的空间。you take the decision-making out of the equation = 你把做决定这件事从考虑因素里拿掉了。I am essentially pre-programming my brain = 我本质上是在预先给大脑编程。exhausting internal debate = 让人精疲力尽的内心争论。bring us to = 把我们带到；引导我们到某个阶段、结果或话题。How do you break the physical paralysis = 你怎么打破身体僵住的状态。相关：mental paralysis，freeze response。He ruled out the latter = 他排除了后者。rule out = 排除。the latter = 后者。the former = 前者。','You have enough time to do your homework.\nYou have sufficient time to do your homework.\nThe new road bypasses the city centre.\nHe tried to bypass the rules.\nYou take the decision-making out of the equation.\nThis brings us to an important question.\nHe ruled out the latter.\nWhy did he rule it out?',NULL,NULL,'enough,sufficient,bypass,out of the equation,rule out,latter,former',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(604,8,26,'phrase','comb your hair / refer to / procrastinator identity','comb your hair / refer to / being a procrastinator','comb your hair / refer to / being a procrastinator','梳头；指的是；参考；转交；拖延者身份表达。','comb your hair 的自然说法：Go comb your hair. You should comb your hair. Comb your hair first. Your hair is messy. Comb it. refer to 常见意思：1. 指的是 / 提到。2. 查阅 / 参考。3. 转交给。关于 procrastinator 的自然表达：I am moving away from being a procrastinator. I am trying to stay away from procrastination. I am working on not being a procrastinator anymore. How do we make these changes stick for life = 我们怎样让这些改变持续一生。So it is not about what I do, it is about who I identify as = 重点不只是我做什么，而是我把自己认定成什么样的人。self-image = 自我形象。','Go comb your hair.\nYou should comb your hair.\nWhen I say teacher, I refer to Mr. Wang.\nPlease refer to the manual.\nThe doctor referred him to a specialist.\nI am moving away from being a procrastinator.\nI am trying to stay away from procrastination.\nI am working on not being a procrastinator anymore.',NULL,NULL,'comb your hair,refer to,procrastinator,self-image',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(605,8,27,'phrase','understatement / exaggeration / performative / get into the whole thing / miffed / all good / work phrases / overwhelm','understatement / exaggeration / performative / get into the whole thing / miffed / it\'s all good / for a while at work / kept the customer updated / motivates you / values teamwork / next few years / what steps / overwhelm','understatement / exaggeration / performative / get into the whole thing / miffed / all good / work phrases / overwhelm','轻描淡写；夸张；作秀；深入讲整个事情；有点不爽；没事；工作表达；压倒、使不知所措。','这一组包括很多高频表达：understatement = 说得太轻；轻描淡写。That is an understatement. That is a bit of an understatement. That is putting it mildly. exaggeration = 夸大其词。performative = 有点作秀；表面功夫。更口语：It feels like it is just for show. I do not want to get into the whole thing = 我不想把整件事都讲出来 / 讲复杂。miffed = 有点恼火；有点受伤。It is all good / No worries 有时只是表面礼貌，不一定真的完全没事。更明确表示真没关系可说：It is really okay. Totally fine. All good, seriously. Do not worry about it, I mean it. for a while at work = 在工作中待了一会儿 / 一段时间，具体看上下文。I kept the customer updated until they got their order = 我一直给客户更新进展，直到他们拿到订单。What motivates you to do your best at work? = 什么激励你在工作中做到最好。A company that values teamwork and gives people opportunities to grow = 一家重视团队合作并给人成长机会的公司。Where do you see yourself in the next few years? = 你对未来几年的职业规划是什么。What steps are you taking to reach that goal? = 为了实现目标，你正在采取哪些步骤。overwhelm = 压倒；使不知所措；淹没。be overwhelmed by / with something。overwhelm someone。overwhelming = 压倒性的；令人应接不暇的。','That is an understatement.\nThat is a bit of an understatement.\nThat is putting it mildly.\nIt is kind of performative.\nIt feels like it is just for show.\nI do not want to get into the whole thing.\nHe could actually be feeling miffed.\nIt is really okay.\nAll good, seriously.\nI kept the customer updated until they got their order.\nWhat motivates you to do your best at work?\nA company that values teamwork and gives people opportunities to grow.\nWhere do you see yourself in the next few years?\nWhat steps are you taking to reach that goal?\nI was overwhelmed by the amount of work.\nThe workload was overwhelming.\nThe army was overwhelmed by the enemy.\nThe village was overwhelmed by the flood.',NULL,NULL,'understatement,exaggeration,performative,miffed,overwhelm',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(606,8,28,'vocab','awkward meanings table','awkward 基本含义','awkward','尴尬的；不自在的；笨拙的；不灵活的；难处理的；棘手的；不方便的；不合适的。','根据你的整理，awkward 可以分成几类常见意思：1. 尴尬的 / 不自在的。2. 笨拙的 / 不灵活的。3. 难处理 / 棘手的。4. 不方便的 / 不合适的。','It was an awkward moment when nobody knew what to say.\nHe gave me an awkward hug.\nThis is an awkward situation.\nThe table is in an awkward position.',NULL,NULL,'awkward,moment,hug,situation,position',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(607,8,29,'vocab','statue / sculpture / monument / idol comparison','statue sculpture monument idol 对比','statue / sculpture / monument / idol','statue = 立体人物 / 神像。sculpture = 任何雕塑。monument = 纪念碑，通常更大。idol = 偶像 / 宗教雕像。','这是你整理的词义对比，适合做区分记忆。','statue = 立体人物 / 神像\nsculpture = 更广泛，任何雕塑\nmonument = 纪念碑，更宏大\nidol = 偶像 / 宗教雕像',NULL,NULL,'statue,sculpture,monument,idol',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(608,8,30,'phrase','a beautiful song / forget the hours / abilities can be developed','a beautiful song / but we forget the hundreds of hours they spent being bad at it / A growth mindset is simply the belief that your basic abilities can be developed','a beautiful song / we forget the hundreds of hours / abilities can be developed','一首美妙的歌；我们忘了他们经历过长时间的不擅长；能力是可以被培养出来的。','适合成长型思维和学习反思场景。','a beautiful song\nbut we forget the hundreds of hours they spent being bad at it\nA growth mindset is simply the belief that your basic abilities can be developed through dedication and hard work.',NULL,NULL,'beautiful song,growth mindset,abilities developed',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(609,8,31,'vocab','belief','belief','belief','信念；信仰；观点；看法。','常见结构：belief in + 名词，belief that + 句子，hold a belief，strong belief，firm belief。','I have a strong belief in fairness.\nIt is my belief that he is honest.\nbelief in yourself\nthe belief that hard work pays off\nhold the belief that ...\na strong belief',NULL,NULL,'belief,belief in,belief that',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(610,8,32,'vocab','brief / briefly / in brief / brief someone on','brief','brief / briefly / in brief / brief someone on','简短的；简报；任务说明；简要说明。','brief 可作形容词、名词、动词。形容词：简短的。名词：简报、任务说明。动词：向……作简要说明。相关：briefly，in brief，brief someone on something。','a brief meeting\nHe gave a brief answer.\nFollow the brief.\ndesign brief\nThe manager briefed the team.\nin brief\nbriefly\nbrief someone on something',NULL,NULL,'brief,design brief,brief someone on',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(611,8,33,'vocab','discomfort','discomfort','discomfort','不适；不舒服；不安。','通常作名词。动词形式较正式，表示使不舒服、使不安。','discomfort',NULL,NULL,'discomfort',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(612,8,34,'vocab','push through','push through','push through','坚持完成；硬撑过去；推动强行通过。','常见意思：1. 坚持完成 / 咬牙撑过去。2. 推动法案、计划等带有强行通过的意思。','I was exhausted, but I pushed through.\nYou just have to push through the pain.\nThe government pushed through the new law.',NULL,NULL,'push through',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(613,8,35,'sentence','That is exactly the spark of a growth mindset.','That is exactly the spark of a growth mindset','That is exactly the spark of a growth mindset.','这正是成长型思维的火花。','spark 在这里是比喻，表示开端、苗头、起点。','That is exactly the spark of a growth mindset.',NULL,NULL,'spark,growth mindset',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(614,8,36,'sentence','It is about honouring it as the only way forward.','It\'s about honoring it as the only way forward','It is about honouring it as the only way forward.','这就是尊重它，把它当作唯一前进的方式。','honour / honor 这里表示承认其价值并认真对待。','It is about honouring it as the only way forward.',NULL,NULL,'honouring,way forward',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(615,8,37,'phrase','I have to admit / big red X / shout at you / fit here','I have to admit / To me, a mistake felt like a big red X on a test paper / shout at you / this word doesn\'t fit here','I have to admit / big red X / shout at you / fit here','我不得不承认；大大的红叉；对你大吼；这个词不适合放这里。','几个高频表达：\nI have to admit = 我不得不承认\na big red X on a test paper = 试卷上的大红叉\nshout at you = 对你大吼\nthis word does not fit here = 这个词不适合放这里','I have to admit.\nTo me, a mistake felt like a big red X on a test paper.\nDo not shout at you.\nThis word does not fit here.',NULL,NULL,'I have to admit,red X,shout at,fit here',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(616,8,38,'phrase','big shift / consequences / principle stays the same','That\'s a big shift for me / mistake has consequences / Even then,the principle stays the same','big shift / consequences / the principle stays the same','很大的转变；会有后果；即便如此，原则还是一样。','很适合反思和总结场景。','That is a big shift for me.\nMistakes have consequences.\nEven then, the principle stays the same.',NULL,NULL,'big shift,consequences,principle',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(617,8,39,'phrase','trial and error / messed up / stuffed it up / lucky star','trial and error / I messed up / I stuffed it up / they were just born under a lucky star','trial and error / messed up / stuffed it up / born under a lucky star','不断试错；搞砸了；弄错了；命好；天生幸运。','trial and error = 通过不断尝试、犯错、修正来找到方法。I messed up = 我搞砸了。I stuffed it up = 新西兰口语，意思接近搞砸了。born under a lucky star = 天生幸运。','Learning to cook is a process of trial and error.\nWe finally solved the problem through trial and error.\nI messed up.\nI really messed up my schedule.\nI stuffed it up.\nThey were just born under a lucky star.',NULL,NULL,'trial and error,messed up,stuffed it up,lucky star',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(618,8,40,'phrase','default thought / willing to lose / can afford to lose','how much are we willing to lose / How much can we afford to lose / that\'s the default thought','default thought / willing to lose / can afford to lose','默认的思维方式；我们愿意失去多少；我们能承受失去多少。','that is the default thought = 这是默认的思维方式。How much are we willing to lose? = 我们愿意失去多少？How much can we afford to lose? = 我们能承受多少损失？','That is the default thought.\nHow much are we willing to lose?\nHow much can we afford to lose?',NULL,NULL,'default thought,willing to lose,afford to lose',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55',1,'2026-04-05 13:23:55'),(619,8,41,'vocab','varsity','varsity','varsity','校队；大学代表队。','常用于学校体育语境，表示代表学校参加比赛的队伍。','He made the varsity team in his first year.',NULL,NULL,'varsity,team',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(620,8,42,'sentence','He missed 9000 shots in his career.','he missed 9000 shots in his career','He missed 9000 shots in his career.','他职业生涯里投丢了 9000 次。','常用来说明成功背后有大量失败和尝试。','He missed 9000 shots in his career.',NULL,NULL,'missed shots,career',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(621,8,43,'phrase','core insight / key insight / the key to','core insight','core insight / key insight / the key to','核心观点；关键洞察；……的关键。','core insight 和 key insight 都表示重要理解。口语里 the key to ... 更自然。','The core insight is that consistency matters.\nOne key insight is that mistakes help you learn.\nThe core insight of learning English is consistent practice.\nThe key to learning English is practising consistently.',NULL,NULL,'core insight,key insight,the key to',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(622,8,44,'phrase','chip away / be chipped away','had to be chipped away','chip away / be chipped away','一点一点剥掉；慢慢削弱；逐步敲掉。','chip away 强调一点点地去除、削弱或推进。','The old paint was chipped away with a scraper.\nWe chipped away at the problem until it became manageable.',NULL,NULL,'chip away,chipped away',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(623,8,45,'phrase','get out of the way','get out of the way','get out of the way','让开；别挡路；退一步别妨碍。','既可表示物理上让路，也可比喻不要妨碍别人做事。','The car could not pass because the truck was not getting out of the way.\nSometimes you just need to get out of the way and let people do their job.',NULL,NULL,'get out of the way',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(624,8,46,'phrase','inevitable result','inevitable result','inevitable result','不可避免的结果。','inevitable = 不可避免的。常用来表示某事迟早会发生。','His failure was an inevitable result of his laziness.\nClimate change will lead to inevitable results if we do nothing.',NULL,NULL,'inevitable result,inevitable',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(625,8,47,'vocab','resilient','That you resiliently refused to let it stop you / resilient','resilient / resiliently','有韧性的；有抗压能力的；不轻易被打倒的。','resilient 常用于形容人在压力、挫折之后还能恢复和坚持。','She is really resilient.\nYou have to stay resilient.\nYou resiliently refused to let it stop you.',NULL,NULL,'resilient,resiliently',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(626,8,48,'sentence','I was born with a small bucket of talent.','I was born with a small bucket of talent','I was born with a small bucket of talent.','我天赋不多；我天生才华有限。','一种自嘲、谦虚的说法，意思接近 I was not born with much talent.','I was born with a small bucket of talent.',NULL,NULL,'bucket of talent,not much talent',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(627,8,49,'phrase','stay motivated / excuse to quit / defence mechanism','it\'s hard to stay motivated / it gives us an excuse to quit / defense mechanism','stay motivated / excuse to quit / defence mechanism','保持动力；放弃的借口；防御机制。','这些表达常用于心理、习惯、自我反思语境。','It is hard to stay motivated.\nIt gives us an excuse to quit.\nThat can become a defence mechanism.',NULL,NULL,'stay motivated,excuse to quit,defence mechanism',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(628,8,50,'phrase','starting line / finish line','starting line / finish line','starting line / finish line','起跑线；终点线。','既可以字面用于比赛，也可以比喻用于人生、项目、学习过程。','We are still at the starting line.\nKeep going until you reach the finish line.',NULL,NULL,'starting line,finish line',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(629,8,51,'phrase','this led me to a question','this led me to a question','this led me to a question','这让我想到一个问题。','很自然的过渡表达，适合演讲、写作、思考类内容。','This led me to a question.',NULL,NULL,'led me to a question',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(630,8,52,'phrase','seek out the difficult stuff','you seek out the difficult stuff','seek out the difficult stuff','主动去挑战困难的东西；刻意找难的事情做。','seek out = 主动去找、刻意寻找。','You seek out the difficult stuff.',NULL,NULL,'seek out,difficult stuff',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(631,8,53,'vocab','weightlifter','weightlifter','weightlifter','举重运动员。','常用于体育语境。','He trains like a weightlifter.',NULL,NULL,'weightlifter',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(632,8,54,'sentence','You want to quit because it feels like too much.','You want to quit because it feels like too much','You want to quit because it feels like too much.','你想放弃，因为你觉得压力太大了；一切超出了承受范围。','很适合表达心理负担过重、想退出的状态。','You want to quit because it feels like too much.',NULL,NULL,'quit,feels like too much',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(633,8,55,'phrase','in control of my own progress','in control of my own progress','in control of my own progress','掌控着自己的进度；对自己的进步有掌控感。','很适合学习、自律、成长型思维场景。','I want to feel in control of my own progress.',NULL,NULL,'in control of my own progress',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(634,8,56,'phrase','after talking about all this / excited but quiet inside / long road ahead','after talking about all this / I feel excited but also a little quiet inside / It\'s like I\'m looking at a long road ahead of me','after talking about all this / excited but quiet inside / long road ahead','说完这些之后；既兴奋又有点沉静；眼前是一条很长的路。','这组表达很有画面感，适合做感受总结和内心独白。','After talking about all this, I feel excited but also a little quiet inside.\nIt is like I am looking at a long road ahead of me.',NULL,NULL,'long road ahead,quiet inside',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(635,8,57,'phrase','sprinting past me / trailing behind / cold shiver / feeling in the chest','spriting past me / be the one trailing behind / cold shiver / feeling in the chest','sprinting past me / trailing behind / cold shiver / feeling in the chest','从我身边飞快跑过去；落在后面；一阵冷颤；胸口的感觉。','这一组适合描写焦虑、比较、压力和身体感受。','Some people are sprinting past me.\nI do not want to be the one trailing behind.\nI felt a cold shiver.\nThere was a strange feeling in my chest.',NULL,NULL,'sprinting past,trailing behind,cold shiver,chest',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(636,8,58,'vocab','patch / patch of soil','patch of soil','patch / patch of soil','一小块；一片；一小块土。','patch 可表示一小块区域。常见搭配：a small patch of soil，a bare patch of soil，a fertile patch of soil，a patch of dry soil。','There is a patch of soil in the backyard.\nI planted some herbs in a small patch of soil.\nWe collected samples from a patch of soil near the river.',NULL,NULL,'patch,patch of soil',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(637,8,59,'phrase','when you feel the urge to look at someone else\'s progress','when you feel that urge to look at someone else\'s progress','when you feel the urge to look at someone else\'s progress','当你有那种想去看别人进度的冲动时。','适合比较心态、成长思维、社交媒体反思场景。','When you feel the urge to look at someone else\'s progress, pause and refocus.',NULL,NULL,'urge,someone else\'s progress',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(638,8,60,'vocab','urge','urge','urge','强烈的冲动；催促；强烈建议。','urge 可作名词或动词。名词表示忍不住想做某事的冲动。动词表示强烈建议、催促。','I had a strong urge to check my phone.\nHe felt the urge to speak up.\nI urge you to apply for this role.\nThe teacher urged us to finish early.',NULL,NULL,'urge,strong urge,urge someone to do',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(639,8,61,'phrase','push through it','push through it','push through it','咬牙坚持；硬撑过去；扛过去。','和 push through 类似，但更强调把某个具体阶段硬撑过去。','I was exhausted, but I pushed through it.\nJust push through it — you are almost there.\nIt is tough now, but you have to push through it.',NULL,NULL,'push through it',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(640,8,62,'phrase','it feels pointless / constant motivation / staying with it gently / end up doing nothing','it feels pointless / constant motivation / And that choice staying with it gently,is often the moment discipline turns into real success / end up doing nothing','it feels pointless / constant motivation / staying with it gently / end up doing nothing','感觉没意义；持续动力；温和地坚持下去；最后什么都没做。','这一组适合表达长期坚持中的心理波动。staying with it gently 强调不是靠蛮力，而是温和持续地做下去。','It feels pointless now, but it will not always feel this way.\nConstant motivation is unrealistic.\nStaying with it gently is often the moment discipline turns into real success.\nSometimes we end up doing nothing.',NULL,NULL,'pointless,constant motivation,end up doing nothing',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(641,8,63,'phrase','small steps do not count / take forever to see results','We think small steps don\'t count / take forever to see the any results','small steps do not count / take forever to see results','我们觉得小步前进不算数；要很久才能看到结果。','常见于习惯养成和长期目标语境。','We think small steps do not count.\nIt can take forever to see any results.',NULL,NULL,'small steps,count,take forever,results',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(642,8,64,'phrase','cast a vote for the person you want to become','casting a vote for the person you want to become','cast a vote for the person you want to become','为你想成为的那个人投票。','很形象的比喻，表示你每一次选择和行动，都在塑造未来的自己。','Every small action is a vote for the person you want to become.',NULL,NULL,'cast a vote,person you want to become',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(643,8,65,'phrase','choose an apple over a cookie','choosing an apple over cookie','choose an apple over a cookie','选择苹果而不是饼干。','适合用来表达更健康、更有利长期目标的选择。','I chose an apple over a cookie.',NULL,NULL,'apple over a cookie',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(644,8,66,'phrase','Do not be hard on yourself','Don\'t be hard on yourself','Do not be hard on yourself','别对自己太苛刻。','很常见的安慰、鼓励表达。','Do not be hard on yourself.',NULL,NULL,'hard on yourself',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(645,8,67,'sentence','You can wipe it away with a single finger.','you can wipe it away with a single finger','You can wipe it away with a single finger.','你可以用一根手指把它擦掉。','wipe away = 擦掉；抹去。','You can wipe it away with a single finger.',NULL,NULL,'wipe it away',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(646,8,68,'phrase','tracks are laid down one metre at a time','tracks are laid down one metre at a time','tracks are laid down one metre at a time','轨道是一米一米铺设的。','lay down = 铺设；建立。one metre at a time 强调渐进，一点一点完成。','Tracks are laid down one metre at a time.',NULL,NULL,'lay down,one metre at a time,tracks',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(647,8,69,'phrase','make the result inevitable','make the result inevitable','make the result inevitable','让结果变成必然。','inevitable = 不可避免的；必然的。','The daily habits make the result inevitable.',NULL,NULL,'make the result inevitable,inevitable',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(648,8,70,'sentence','That is a big shift in how I see things.','That is a big shift in how I see things','That is a big shift in how I see things.','这是我看待事情方式上的一个大转变。','很适合表达认知转变、思维方式变化。','That is a big shift in how I see things.',NULL,NULL,'big shift,see things',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(649,8,71,'sentence','You all would already be there in spirit.','You all already be there in spirit','You all would already be there in spirit.','你们其实在精神上早就已经在那里了。','in spirit = 在精神上；心里已经参与其中。','You all would already be there in spirit.',NULL,NULL,'in spirit',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(650,8,72,'vocab','grip / traction','grip on the road / traction','grip / traction','抓地力；附着力。','grip on the road 常用于轮胎对路面的抓地力。traction 是更专业的说法。','The bike\'s tyres have great grip on the road.\nThis car has good traction.',NULL,NULL,'grip,traction,road',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(651,8,73,'sentence','I need a way to stop myself from talking myself out of my goals every morning.','I need a way to stop me from talking me out of my goals every morning','I need a way to stop myself from talking myself out of my goals every morning.','我需要一个办法，阻止自己每天早上把自己的目标劝没了。','talk oneself out of something = 自己把自己说服放弃某事。','I need a way to stop myself from talking myself out of my goals every morning.',NULL,NULL,'talk yourself out of,goals',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(652,8,74,'phrase','show up for my goals','I need a way to show up for my goals every morning','show up for my goals','为自己的目标出现；坚持对自己的目标负责。','show up for something 在这里不是单纯“出现”，而是按时站到目标这边，持续投入。','I need a way to show up for my goals every morning.',NULL,NULL,'show up for,goals',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(653,8,75,'vocab','technique / psychologist / implementation intention','technique / psychologist / implementation intention','technique / psychologist / implementation intention','技巧；心理学家；实施意图。','implementation intention 常用于心理学和习惯养成语境，表示“先设定如果……那么我就……”的执行计划。','This technique is simple but effective.\nA psychologist might call this an implementation intention.',NULL,NULL,'technique,psychologist,implementation intention',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(654,8,76,'phrase','You have enough time / sufficient time','你有足够的时间来做作业','You have enough time to do your homework / You have sufficient time to do your homework','你有足够的时间做作业。','enough 更自然、更口语。sufficient 更正式、更书面。','You have enough time to do your homework.\nYou have sufficient time to do your homework.',NULL,NULL,'enough time,sufficient time',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(655,8,77,'phrase','a simple way to bypass overthinking','a simply way to bypass overthinking','a simple way to bypass overthinking','一个绕过过度思考的简单办法。','bypass = 绕过；规避。overthinking = 想太多。','This is a simple way to bypass overthinking.',NULL,NULL,'bypass overthinking',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(656,8,78,'vocab','bypass','bypass','bypass','绕过；越过；规避；旁路。','可作名词，也可作动词。用途很广：交通、医学、电脑、比喻表达都能用。','The new road bypasses the city centre.\nHe tried to bypass the rules.\nYou can bypass the login screen by using this shortcut.',NULL,NULL,'bypass',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(657,8,79,'phrase','fail at discipline / goals too vague / room for your brain to argue','fail at discipline / we made our goals too vague / this leave too much room for your brain to argue with you / My brain is an expert at arguing','fail at discipline / goals too vague / room for your brain to argue','在自律上失败；目标太模糊；给大脑留下太多抬杠空间。','这组表达很适合习惯养成、自我管理、拖延分析场景。','I fail at discipline when my goals are too vague.\nWe made our goals too vague.\nThis leaves too much room for your brain to argue with you.\nMy brain is an expert at arguing.',NULL,NULL,'discipline,vague goals,argue with you',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(658,8,80,'phrase','take the decision-making out of the equation / pre-programming my brain / exhausting internal debate','you take the decision-making out of the equation / I am essentially pre-programming my brain / exhausting internal debate','take the decision-making out of the equation / pre-programming my brain / exhausting internal debate','把做决定这件事拿掉；预先给大脑编程；让人精疲力尽的内心争论。','适合解释为什么提前设定规则能减少拖延和纠结。','You take the decision-making out of the equation.\nI am essentially pre-programming my brain.\nThat creates an exhausting internal debate.',NULL,NULL,'out of the equation,pre-programming my brain,internal debate',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43',1,'2026-04-05 13:29:43'),(659,8,81,'phrase','bring us to','bring us to','bring us to','把我们带到；引导我们到。','既可以表示实际把人带到某个地方，也可以表示把话题、过程、思路引到某个阶段、结果或问题。','This brings us to the next question.\nThat brings us to an important point.',NULL,NULL,'bring us to,bring someone to',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(660,8,82,'phrase','physical paralysis / mental paralysis / freeze response','How do you break the physical paralysis','physical paralysis / mental paralysis / freeze response','身体僵住；心理瘫住；冻结反应。','physical paralysis 在这里更像“身体卡住、动不了”的感觉，不一定真的是医学上的瘫痪。mental paralysis 表示心理层面的卡住。freeze response 指人在压力、恐惧下的冻结反应。','How do you break the physical paralysis?\nSometimes anxiety creates a kind of mental paralysis.\nIt can feel like a freeze response.',NULL,NULL,'physical paralysis,mental paralysis,freeze response',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(661,8,83,'phrase','rule out / the latter / the former','He ruled out the latter. Why did he rule it out?','rule out / the latter / the former','排除；后者；前者。','rule out = 排除某种可能。the latter = 后者。the former = 前者。','He ruled out the latter.\nWhy did he rule it out?\nThe former sounds more natural than the latter.',NULL,NULL,'rule out,the latter,the former',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(662,8,84,'phrase','another way of saying','It another way of saying','another way of saying','另一种说法。','常用来解释同义表达或更自然的改写。更完整常见句型是 It is another way of saying ...','It is another way of saying the same thing.\nThat is just another way of saying you are tired.',NULL,NULL,'another way of saying',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(663,8,85,'phrase','comb your hair','comb your hair','comb your hair','梳头。','很常用的日常表达。自然说法有：Go comb your hair. You should comb your hair. Comb your hair first. Your hair is messy. Comb it.','Go comb your hair.\nYou should comb your hair.\nComb your hair first.\nYour hair is messy. Comb it.',NULL,NULL,'comb your hair',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(664,8,86,'vocab','refer to','refer to','refer to','指的是；提到；查阅；参考；转交给。','refer to 常见有三种意思。第一，指的是、提到。第二，查阅、参考。第三，把某人或某事转交给更合适的人处理。','When I say teacher, I refer to Mr. Wang.\nPlease refer to the manual.\nThe doctor referred him to a specialist.\nYour case will be referred to the manager.',NULL,NULL,'refer to,manual,specialist',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(665,8,87,'phrase','being a procrastinator / procrastination','being a procrastinator','being a procrastinator / procrastination','拖延者；拖延。','更自然的表达有：I am moving away from being a procrastinator. I am trying to stay away from procrastination. I am working on not being a procrastinator anymore.','I am moving away from being a procrastinator.\nI am trying to stay away from procrastination.\nI am working on not being a procrastinator anymore.',NULL,NULL,'procrastinator,procrastination',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(666,8,88,'sentence','How do we make these changes stick for life?','How do we make these changes stick for life.','How do we make these changes stick for life?','我们怎样才能让这些改变持续一生？','make changes stick = 让改变真正持续下去，不是短期坚持一下。','How do we make these changes stick for life?',NULL,NULL,'make changes stick,for life',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(667,8,89,'sentence','So it is not about what I do, it is about how I identify.','So it is not about what I do ,it\'s about how I identity','So it is not about what I do, it is about how I identify.','所以重点不在于我做什么，而在于我如何认同自己。','这是在讲身份认同和习惯改变。更自然也可以说 it is about who I believe I am.','So it is not about what I do, it is about how I identify.',NULL,NULL,'identity,identify',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(668,8,90,'vocab','self-image','self-image','self-image','自我形象；自我认知。','指一个人怎么看自己，和身份认同、信心、习惯都有关。','Changing your habits can change your self-image.',NULL,NULL,'self-image',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(669,8,91,'phrase','cast a vote for','cast a vote for ....','cast a vote for','为……投票。','既可字面用于投票，也可比喻每个选择都在支持某种未来身份。','Every good habit is a vote for the person you want to become.',NULL,NULL,'cast a vote for',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(670,8,92,'phrase','mess up once / lose the election / forgiving and realistic','mess up once / lost the election / much more forgiving and realistic','mess up once / lose the election / forgiving and realistic','犯错一次；输掉选举；更宽容也更现实。','这里是延续 vote 的比喻。意思是一次犯错不等于整场都输了。','If you mess up once, you have not lost the election.\nThat way of thinking is much more forgiving and realistic.',NULL,NULL,'mess up once,lose the election,forgiving,realistic',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(671,8,93,'sentence','Which of the six strategies do you think is your missing piece?','Which of the six stratagies do you think is your missing piece','Which of the six strategies do you think is your missing piece?','你觉得这六种策略里，哪一个是你缺失的那一块？','missing piece 是很自然的比喻，表示关键但还缺的一环。','Which of the six strategies do you think is your missing piece?',NULL,NULL,'missing piece,strategies',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(672,8,94,'phrase','exaggeration for emphasis / nightmare shortened to mare','exaggeration for emphasis / When they say mare,it obviously shortened from nightmare','exaggeration for emphasis / mare from nightmare','为了强调而夸张；mare 是 nightmare 的缩略说法。','exaggeration for emphasis 表示有意夸大一点，让表达更有力。mare 在口语里可以是 nightmare 的缩略形式，尤其在英式口语里能听到。','That was just exaggeration for emphasis.\nWhat a mare of a day.',NULL,NULL,'exaggeration for emphasis,mare,nightmare',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(673,8,95,'vocab','understatement','understatement','understatement','轻描淡写；说得太保守；故意说得不严重。','和 exaggeration 相反。经典搭配有 That is an understatement. That is a bit of an understatement. That is putting it mildly.','That is an understatement.\nThat is a bit of an understatement.\nThat is putting it mildly.',NULL,NULL,'understatement,putting it mildly',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(674,8,96,'sentence','What it basically means is they had a mild and potentially slightly humorous occurrence at work.','What is basically means is they had a mild and peotentially slightly humorous occurrence at work','What it basically means is they had a mild and potentially slightly humorous occurrence at work.','它基本上的意思是，他们在工作中经历了一件不算严重、甚至略带一点好笑的小事。','这是对 understatement 类表达的一种解释式表述。','What it basically means is they had a mild and potentially slightly humorous occurrence at work.',NULL,NULL,'basically means,humorous occurrence',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(675,8,97,'vocab','performative','It\'s kind of performative','performative','有点作秀的；表面功夫的；为了给别人看的。','表示一个举动更像是展示给别人看，而不是真诚地出于内心。更口语可以说 It feels like it is just for show.','It is kind of performative.\nIt is a bit performative.\nIt feels like it is just for show.\nThat gesture is kind of performative, not sincere.',NULL,NULL,'performative,just for show',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(676,8,98,'phrase','get into the whole thing','So I don’t want to get into the whole thing.','get into the whole thing','把整件事都讲开；深入细说整件事。','I do not want to get into the whole thing 表示我不想把事情说得太复杂，或不想深入展开讲。','I do not want to get into the whole thing.\nAh, I do not want to get into the whole thing.',NULL,NULL,'get into the whole thing',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(677,8,99,'vocab','miffed','miffed','miffed','有点恼火的；有点受伤的；有点不爽的。','程度通常不算特别重，比 angry 轻，常带一点委屈或不开心。','He sounded fine, but he might have been a bit miffed.',NULL,NULL,'miffed',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(678,8,100,'phrase','It is all good / No worries / It is really okay / Totally fine','It\'s all good / No worries','It is all good / No worries / It is really okay / Totally fine','没事；别担心；真的没关系。','It is all good 和 No worries 有时只是礼貌说法，不一定代表对方完全没情绪。更明确表达真的没关系，可以说 It is really okay. Totally fine. All good, seriously. Do not worry about it, I mean it.','It is all good.\nNo worries.\nIt is really okay.\nTotally fine.\nAll good, seriously.\nDo not worry about it, I mean it.',NULL,NULL,'all good,no worries,totally fine',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(679,8,101,'phrase','for a while at work','for a while at work','for a while at work','在工作上忙了一会儿；在岗位上待了一段时间。','具体意思要结合上下文。可以表示短时间，也可以表示相对较长的一段时间。','I have been here for a while at work.\nLet us take a break; we have been busy for a while at work.',NULL,NULL,'for a while at work',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(680,8,102,'sentence','I kept the customer updated until they got their order.','I kept the customer updated until they got their order.','I kept the customer updated until they got their order.','我一直给客户更新进展，直到他们拿到订单。','keep someone updated = 持续给某人更新进展。','I kept the customer updated until they got their order.',NULL,NULL,'kept updated,customer,order',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(681,8,103,'sentence','What motivates you to do your best at work?','What motivates you to do your best at work ?','What motivates you to do your best at work?','是什么激励你在工作中做到最好？','很常见的面试题表达。','What motivates you to do your best at work?',NULL,NULL,'motivates you,do your best at work',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(682,8,104,'sentence','A company that values teamwork and gives people opportunities to grow.','A company that values teamwork and gives people opportunities to grow.','A company that values teamwork and gives people opportunities to grow.','一家重视团队合作并给人成长机会的公司。','values 在这里是动词，意思是重视、看重。','A company that values teamwork and gives people opportunities to grow.',NULL,NULL,'values teamwork,opportunities to grow',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(683,8,105,'sentence','Where do you see yourself in the next few years?','Where do you see yourself in the next few years?','Where do you see yourself in the next few years?','你对自己未来几年的职业规划是什么？','经典面试问题。','Where do you see yourself in the next few years?',NULL,NULL,'next few years,see yourself',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(684,8,106,'sentence','What steps are you taking to reach that goal?','What steps are you taking to reach that goal ?','What steps are you taking to reach that goal?','为了实现那个目标，你正在采取哪些步骤？','也很常见于面试、辅导、职业规划对话。','What steps are you taking to reach that goal?',NULL,NULL,'steps,reach that goal',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(685,8,107,'vocab','overwhelm','overwhem','overwhelm','压倒；击败；使不知所措；淹没。','overwhelm 常见意思有：压倒、让人无法应付、被大量信息或情绪冲击，以及字面上的淹没。','The army was overwhelmed by the enemy.\nI was overwhelmed by the amount of work.\nThe village was overwhelmed by the flood.',NULL,NULL,'overwhelm,overwhelmed',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(686,8,108,'phrase','be overwhelmed by / with something','be overwhelmed by / with something','be overwhelmed by / with something','被……压得喘不过气；被……冲得不知所措。','很常用来描述工作量、情绪、回应、消息等太多、太强烈，导致人有点扛不住。','I was overwhelmed by the response.\nWe were overwhelmed with work.',NULL,NULL,'be overwhelmed by,be overwhelmed with',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(687,8,109,'phrase','overwhelm someone','overwhelm someone','overwhelm someone','让某人不知所措；让某人承受不住。','可以是好消息、工作、情绪、责任等压得人有点承受不了。','The good news overwhelmed him.\nToo much pressure can overwhelm people.',NULL,NULL,'overwhelm someone',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(688,8,110,'vocab','overwhelming','Overwhelming','overwhelming','压倒性的；令人应接不暇的；巨大的。','既可以表示优势、力量上的压倒性，也可以表示数量、工作量、情绪大到让人不知所措。','It was an overwhelming victory.\nThe workload was overwhelming.',NULL,NULL,'overwhelming,victory,workload',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(689,8,111,'phrase','all this growth mindset wording set','People with the growth mindset don\'t tolerate mistakes / That\'s a big shift for me / mistakes have consequences / Even then, the principle stays the same','growth mindset wording corrections','成长型思维相关表达修正。','People with a growth mindset do not tolerate mistakes 这句话容易误导。更准确地说，拥有成长型思维的人不会害怕错误，而是会从错误中学习。相关表达还包括：That is a big shift for me. Mistakes have consequences. Even then, the principle stays the same.','People with a growth mindset do not fear mistakes; they learn from them.\nThat is a big shift for me.\nMistakes have consequences.\nEven then, the principle stays the same.',NULL,NULL,'growth mindset,mistakes,principle',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(690,8,112,'phrase','a little spark of peace','a little spark of peach','a little spark of peace','一点点平静的火花；一丝安宁。','这里更自然应是 peace，不是 peach。表示一种很小但真实存在的平静感。','I felt a little spark of peace.',NULL,NULL,'spark of peace',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(691,8,113,'phrase','Nothing he says counts','He is a liar; what he said doesn\'t count.','Nothing he says counts.','他说的话都不算数。','很自然的口语表达，表示一个人不可信，所以他说的话没有分量。','He is a liar. Nothing he says counts.',NULL,NULL,'counts,liar',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(692,8,114,'phrase','one key insight','one key insight','one key insight','一个重要洞察。','比 core insight of ... 更适合日常表达和说明重点。','One key insight is that consistency matters.',NULL,NULL,'key insight',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(693,8,115,'phrase','the key to learning English is practising consistently','The key to learning English is practicing consistently.','the key to learning English is practising consistently','学英语的关键是持续练习。','比 The core insight of learning English ... 更自然。','The key to learning English is practising consistently.',NULL,NULL,'key to learning English,practising consistently',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(694,8,116,'phrase','on stage / onto the stage / backstage / stage a comeback','on vs onto / on stage / backstage / stage a comeback','on stage / onto the stage / backstage / stage a comeback','在舞台上；走上舞台；在后台；策划复出。','on 表示已经在某个位置上，onto 表示移动到那个位置。stage a comeback 表示策划一次复出。','She is on the stage.\nShe walked onto the stage.\nThe actors were waiting backstage.\nHe staged a comeback.',NULL,NULL,'on stage,onto the stage,backstage,stage a comeback',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(695,8,117,'phrase','He deserves way better / I am not good enough for him','Honestly, he deserves way better. / I feel like I\'m not good enough for him.','He deserves way better / I am not good enough for him','他值得更好的人；我觉得自己配不上他。','这是对 worthy / deserve 那组表达的更口语、更自然补充，适合日常感情语境。','Honestly, he deserves way better.\nI feel like I am not good enough for him.',NULL,NULL,'deserves better,not good enough',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51',1,'2026-04-05 13:35:51'),(696,9,1,'phrase','back then','back then','back then','在那个时候；当时。','常用来回忆过去某个时期。','Back then, things were different.',NULL,NULL,'back then',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(697,9,2,'phrase','look forward to','look forward to','look forward to','盼望；期待。','look forward to 后面通常接名词或动名词。','I really look forward to meeting you next week.',NULL,NULL,'look forward to,meeting',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(698,9,3,'phrase','go through a hard time','going through a hard time','go through a hard time','度过困难时期；经历艰难阶段。','很常见的表达，表示正在经历压力、痛苦或困难。','She is going through a hard time.',NULL,NULL,'hard time',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(699,9,4,'sentence','You are living for everyone else.','you are living for everyone else','You are living for everyone else.','你在为别人而活。','常用于情感、人生选择、自我认同语境。','You are living for everyone else.',NULL,NULL,'living for everyone else',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(700,9,5,'sentence','I am physically here.','I\'m physcially here','I am physically here.','我人就在这里。','强调身体上在场，但有时暗示精神上未必投入。','I am physically here, but my mind is somewhere else.',NULL,NULL,'physically here',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(701,9,6,'vocab','inward / inwardly','inward','inward / inwardly','向内的；朝内的；内心的；内在地。','inward 可表示方向朝内，也可比喻内心层面的感受。inwardly 常作副词。','The door opens inward.\nHe turned his feet inward.\nShe felt an inward sense of relief.\nHe smiled, but felt inwardly nervous.',NULL,NULL,'inward,inwardly',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(702,9,7,'vocab','soul','soul','soul','灵魂；精神；内心深处；情感本质。','既可以是宗教、哲学里的灵魂，也可以指人的内在感受和真我。','Many people believe the soul lives on after death.\nMusic speaks to the soul.\nShe poured her soul into her work.\nHe felt it in his soul that something was wrong.',NULL,NULL,'soul',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(703,9,8,'sentence','It is not an act of selfishness.','It isn’t an act of selfishness.','It is not an act of selfishness.','这不是自私的表现。','act of selfishness = 自私的行为 / 自私的表现。','It is not an act of selfishness.',NULL,NULL,'selfishness',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(704,9,9,'phrase','an act of survival / survive','是为了活下去 / 自保','It is an act of survival / It is about survival / It is what I need to survive / I did it to survive','这是为了活下去；这是自保；这是生存本能。','表达不是出于自私，而是出于生存需要。','It is an act of survival.\nIt is about survival.\nIt is what I need to survive.\nI did it to survive.',NULL,NULL,'survival,survive',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(705,9,10,'phrase','when you put it that way','when you put it that way','when you put it that way','你这么一说；这样一解释的话；从这个角度来看。','常表示被说服了、开始理解对方角度，或半开玩笑地承认某种说法。','When you put it that way, it makes sense.\nWhen you put it that way, I guess you are right.\nWhen you put it that way, I can see your point.\nWhen you put it that way, it hits differently.',NULL,NULL,'when you put it that way',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(706,9,11,'vocab','bulb / light bulb moment','bulb','bulb / light bulb moment','灯泡；球茎；突然开窍的时刻。','bulb 常见意思是灯泡，也可表示植物球茎。light bulb moment 表示灵光一现、突然想通。','The bulb is broken.\nI need to change the bulb.\nIt was a light bulb moment when I finally understood recursion.',NULL,NULL,'bulb,light bulb moment',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(707,9,12,'vocab','breath vs breathe','breath vs breathe','breath vs breathe','breath = 呼吸、气息。breathe = 呼吸。','breath 是名词，breathe 是动词。','Take a deep breath.\nHold your breath.\nI was out of breath after running.\nBreathe in.\nBreathe out.\nI could not breathe properly.\nTry to breathe slowly.',NULL,NULL,'breath,breathe',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(708,9,13,'phrase','the water stays brown and dirty / muddy / cloudy','the water stays brown and dirty','the water stays brown and dirty / muddy / cloudy','水还是棕色的而且很脏；水很混；水看起来很浑浊。','muddy 更强调泥水混杂；cloudy 更强调看起来浑浊、不清澈。','The water stays brown and dirty.\nThe water is muddy.\nThe water looks cloudy.',NULL,NULL,'muddy,cloudy,water',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(709,9,14,'vocab','precisely','percisely','precisely','准确地；精确地；恰恰；正是如此。','既可表示精确，也可表示强调确认。口语里 Precisely! 就是“没错，就是这样”。','The train arrived at 10:00 precisely.\nYou measured it precisely.\nThat is precisely what I meant.\nPrecisely!\nThe problem lies precisely in the lack of communication.',NULL,NULL,'precisely',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(710,9,15,'phrase','small windows of silence / pockets of silence / moments of silence','small windows of silense','small windows of silence / pockets of silence / moments of silence','小段安静时间；短暂的宁静时刻。','pockets of silence 和 brief moments of silence 都很自然。','I only get small pockets of silence during the day.\nThere are only brief moments of silence at home.',NULL,NULL,'silence,pockets of silence',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(711,9,16,'sentence','We are doing nothing and letting the mud settle.','We’re doing nothing and letting the mud settle.','We are doing nothing and letting the mud settle.','我们什么也不做，让浑水自己沉淀。','很适合作比喻，表示不急着干预，让事情自然平静下来。','We are doing nothing and letting the mud settle.',NULL,NULL,'let the mud settle',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(712,9,17,'phrase','watch people walking by','just watch people walking by','watch people walking by','看看人来人往；只是看着路过的人。','很有生活感的表达，常用于放空、休息、街景场景。','Sometimes I just sit there and watch people walking by.',NULL,NULL,'walking by,watch people',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(713,9,18,'phrase','That is a perfect way to put it / spot on','that\'s a perfect way to put it','That is a perfect way to put it / That is a great way to put it / You could not have said it better / That is spot on','这个说法太贴切了；你说得太好了；太到位了。','常用于赞同别人表达得很准确。spot on 在英式和新西兰口语里很常见。','That is a perfect way to put it.\nThat is a great way to put it.\nThat is exactly how I would put it.\nYou could not have said it better.\nThat sums it up perfectly.\nYeah, that is spot on.',NULL,NULL,'way to put it,spot on',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(714,9,19,'sentence','You will not even recognise the person you used to be.','you even won\'t recognize the person you used to be','You will not even recognise the person you used to be.','你甚至都认不出曾经的自己。','这里 even 放在 won\'t 后面更自然。recognise 是英式拼写，recognize 是美式拼写。','You will not even recognise the person you used to be.',NULL,NULL,'used to be,even',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(715,9,20,'phrase','副词位置速查表','英语副词位置速查表（Only / Just / Even / Still / Already）','adverb position quick guide','副词位置通常放在助动词或情态动词后面，实义动词前面。','核心规律：主语 + 情态动词或助动词 + 副词 + 实义动词 + 其他成分。像 even、just、still、already 都常按这个位置放。','You will not even notice.\nI did not even try.\nI still remember.\nShe is still waiting.\nI have already finished.\nHe has already left.\nWe are just waiting.',NULL,NULL,'adverb position,even,still,already,just,only',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(716,9,21,'sentence','An adventure belongs only to you.','an adventure belongs only to you','An adventure belongs only to you.','一场冒险只属于你一个人。','belongs only to you 强调“只属于你”，不属于别人。','An adventure belongs only to you.',NULL,NULL,'belongs only to you,adventure',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(717,9,22,'phrase','they seem so solid / solid friendship / solid argument','they seem so solid','they seem so solid / solid friendship / solid argument','它们看起来很稳固；关系很稳固；论点很有力。','solid 不只用于物理上的结实，也可用于关系、团队、性格、论点。','They seem so solid.\nHer argument seems solid.\nOur friendship is solid.',NULL,NULL,'solid,solid friendship,solid argument',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(718,9,23,'vocab','flaw','flaw','flaw','缺点；瑕疵；缺陷；弱点。','常见搭配：inherent flaws，design flaws，fatal flaw，character flaws，reveal flaws，expose flaws。','Every system has flaws.\nThat design has a fatal flaw.',NULL,NULL,'flaw,inherent flaw,design flaw,fatal flaw',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(719,9,24,'phrase','I am messy / I am a hot mess','I\'m messy','I am messy / I am a hot mess','我很乱；我一团糟；我状态乱但还有点搞笑或可爱。','messy 可指房间、生活、感情、习惯都很乱。hot mess 是更口语、更有戏剧感的说法。','I am messy.\nI am a hot mess.\nI am messy when it comes to relationships.',NULL,NULL,'messy,hot mess',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(720,9,25,'phrase','That just reminded me of an old story','that reminds me a old story','That just reminded me of an old story / That makes me think of an old story / That takes me back to an old story','这让我想起一个老故事。','remind someone of something = 让某人想起某事。takes me back 更有文艺感和回忆感。','That just reminded me of an old story.\nThat makes me think of an old story.\nThat takes me back to an old story.\nThis song reminds me of my childhood.',NULL,NULL,'remind me of,old story,takes me back',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(721,9,26,'sentence','I could not love you without you being exactly the way you are.','you being exactly the way you are','I could not love you without you being exactly the way you are.','如果你不是现在这样的你，我就不会爱你。','without + doing 是固定结构。这里强调“正因为你就是现在这样的你，我才爱你”。','I could not love you without you being exactly the way you are.',NULL,NULL,'exactly the way you are,without doing',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(722,9,27,'vocab','realization','realization','realization','认识；领悟；意识到；实现。','一类是心理和思想上的意识到、顿悟；另一类是更正式的“实现”。','I had a sudden realization.\nThe realization hit me hard.\nShe came to the realization that she was wrong.\nThe realization of the plan took months.\nRealization of dreams requires effort.',NULL,NULL,'realization,sudden realization,come to a realization',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(723,9,28,'sentence','Why not make that relationship the most beautiful one you have?','why not make that relationship the most beautiful one you have','Why not make that relationship the most beautiful one you have?','为什么不把那段关系变成你拥有过最美的一段呢？','很适合写作、演讲、情感表达。','Why not make that relationship the most beautiful one you have?',NULL,NULL,'most beautiful relationship',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(724,9,29,'sentence','I watched 21 minutes in one go.','I watched 21 minutes in one go.','I watched 21 minutes in one go.','我一口气看了 21 分钟。','in one go = 一次性；一口气。很口语化，聊天里很好用。','I watched 21 minutes in one go.',NULL,NULL,'in one go',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:42:21'),(725,10,1,'vocab','stir-fried / stir-fry','stir-fried','stir-fried / stir-fry','炒的；翻炒；快炒。','stir = 搅拌、翻动。fry = 煎、炸、炒。stir-fry = 用油在高温下快速翻炒食材，是很典型的中式快炒方式。','This is stir-fried beef.\nWe stir-fried the vegetables.',NULL,NULL,'stir-fried,stir-fry',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(726,10,2,'phrase','How do you cope with ... ?','How do you cope with … ?','How do you cope with ... ?','你是如何应对……的？你怎么处理……？','很常用、很自然的表达，通常用来问压力、困难、挑战或情绪问题。','How do you cope with stress?\nHow do you cope with pressure at work?',NULL,NULL,'cope with',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(727,10,3,'phrase','tear the place apart','tearing the place apart','tear the place apart','把一个地方翻得乱七八糟；大肆搜查；破坏性地找东西。','常用于找东西找得很疯狂，或者把房间翻乱的场景。','I tore the place apart looking for my keys.',NULL,NULL,'tear the place apart',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(728,10,4,'sentence','It was my daughter\'s masterpiece, made using an egg tray and watercolours.','这是我女儿的杰作，用一个鸡蛋托盘和水彩制作的','It was my daughter\'s masterpiece, made using an egg tray and watercolours.','这是我女儿的杰作，用一个鸡蛋托盘和水彩做的。','masterpiece = 杰作。made using ... = 用……制作的。','It was my daughter\'s masterpiece, made using an egg tray and watercolours.',NULL,NULL,'masterpiece,egg tray,watercolours',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(729,10,5,'phrase','put you through / put you through to','put you through','put you through / put you through to','让你承受；让你经历；帮你转接到。','最常见有两个意思。1. 让某人经历不好的或艰难的事。2. 电话里表示“帮你转接给某人”。','I\'m sorry to put you through this.\nShe\'s been put through a lot this year.\nI\'ll put you through to the manager.',NULL,NULL,'put you through,put you through to',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(730,10,6,'vocab','ripple','ripple','ripple','波纹；涟漪；起伏声；逐渐扩散的感觉；起波纹；扩散。','ripple 可作名词和动词。名词可表示沙浪、水波纹、掌声笑声的起伏、或情绪扩散。动词可表示起伏、荡漾、扩散。','There was hardly a ripple on the pond\'s surface.\nA ripple of applause spread through the room.\nA ripple of fear passed through him.\nThe sea rippled and sparkled.\nThe wind rippled the wheat in the fields.\nA gasp rippled through the crowd.',NULL,NULL,'ripple,applause,fear',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(731,10,7,'vocab','dissolve','dissolve','dissolve','溶解；消散；消失；解散。','常用于液体中的溶解，也可表示感情、雾气、组织等逐渐消失或解散。','Sugar dissolves in water.\nThe tension slowly dissolved.',NULL,NULL,'dissolve',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(732,10,8,'sentence','This way shows us a direct visual representation of sound.','这种方式为我们演绎出了声音的直接视觉展现','This way shows us a direct visual representation of sound.','这种方式向我们展示了声音的直接视觉呈现。','visual representation = 视觉呈现；可视化表现。','This way shows us a direct visual representation of sound.',NULL,NULL,'visual representation,sound',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(733,10,9,'vocab','particularly','particluarly','particularly','尤其；特别；非常。','particularly 可表示“尤其、特别”，也可表示程度上的“非常”。语气比 especially 稍正式一些。','I like fruit, particularly apples.\nThis restaurant is particularly good for vegetarians.\nThe movie was particularly interesting.\nShe was particularly happy about the news.\nThis book is particularly useful for beginners.',NULL,NULL,'particularly,especially',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(734,10,10,'phrase','blow off steam','blow off steam','blow off steam','发泄情绪；释放压力。','很常见的口语表达，表示把积累的压力、怒气或情绪释放出来。','I go for a run to blow off steam.',NULL,NULL,'blow off steam',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(735,10,11,'phrase','a rounded sense of / overall sense / solid understanding / clear idea','rounded sense of','a rounded sense of / overall sense / solid understanding / clear idea','全面的理解；整体感觉；扎实的理解；清楚的认识。','rounded sense / overall sense 偏正式，强调全面性。solid understanding / clear idea 更口语，强调清楚、牢固。','A rounded sense of what those words or phrases mean.\nA good overall sense of what those words or phrases mean.\nA solid understanding of what those words or phrases mean.\nA clear idea of what those words or phrases mean.',NULL,NULL,'rounded sense,solid understanding,clear idea',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(736,10,12,'vocab','rigid','rigid','rigid','僵硬的；死板的；严格刻板的。','可用于身体上的僵硬、规则制度上的严格死板、以及思维和性格上的僵化。','His body was rigid with fear.\nThey follow a rigid schedule.\nHe has a rigid mindset.',NULL,NULL,'rigid,schedule,mindset',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(737,10,13,'phrase','have something in check / keep something in check','have something in check','have something in check / keep something in check','把某事控制住；把某事管控得当。','核心意思是控制在可接受范围内，没有失控。','I have my stress in check.\nThe company has its costs in check.\nShe keeps her emotions in check.',NULL,NULL,'in check,keep in check',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(738,10,14,'phrase','be supposed to do','be supposed to do','be supposed to do','应该做；按规定要做；被期望做。','可表示规定、期待、计划中的事情。过去式 was supposed to do 常表示“本该做但没做”。','You are supposed to finish the report today.\nStudents are supposed to wear uniforms.\nThe train is supposed to arrive at 6.\nI was supposed to meet him, but I forgot.',NULL,NULL,'be supposed to',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(739,10,15,'vocab','fascinate / fascinated by','fascinate','fascinate / fascinated by','使着迷；强烈吸引；对……着迷。','fascinate 是动词。be fascinated by / with something 表示对某事物着迷。','She is fascinated by ancient history.\nHe is fascinated by space exploration.\nThe speaker fascinated the audience with her stories.',NULL,NULL,'fascinate,fascinated by',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(740,10,16,'vocab','tricky / difficult vs complicated','tricky / diffcult vs complicate','tricky / difficult vs complicated','tricky = 难办的、难应付的。difficult = 难。complicated = 结构复杂、部分很多的。','tricky 通常有点棘手、不好处理的感觉。difficult 强调难度。complicated 强调结构复杂、因素多。','That puzzle is pretty tricky.\nThis task is difficult.\nThe system is complicated.',NULL,NULL,'tricky,difficult,complicated',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(741,10,17,'phrase','brush up on / refresh your skills','brush up on + sth / refreshing your skills','brush up on / refresh your skills','复习；重新熟悉；提升技能。','brush up on something = 重新捡起来复习。refresh your skills = 重新熟悉已有技能，不是从零开始学。','I need to brush up on my English.\nI am refreshing my skills before the interview.',NULL,NULL,'brush up on,refresh your skills',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(742,10,18,'vocab','legacy','legacy','legacy','遗产；留下的影响；遗留系统；遗留代码；历史数据。','legacy 有两个非常常见的意思。1. 一个人、公司、系统留下的长期影响或成果。2. 技术语境里的历史遗留系统、代码、数据。','His work left a lasting legacy.\nWe are maintaining a legacy system written in Java.\nLegacy code can be hard to refactor.',NULL,NULL,'legacy,legacy system,legacy code,legacy data',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(743,10,19,'phrase','bound to be / hard to spot','bound to be / hard to spot','bound to be / hard to spot','非常可能；很难发现。','bound to be 表示很有可能会发生。hard to spot 表示很难被注意到、找到。','If you study really hard, you are bound to get a good grade.\nThe mistake was hard to spot.',NULL,NULL,'bound to be,hard to spot',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(744,10,20,'phrase','your cup of tea','cup of tea 感兴趣的东西','your cup of tea','你感兴趣的东西；你的菜。','常用于表达喜好。not my cup of tea = 不是我的菜。','Maybe it is not a problem now if that is your cup of tea.\nThat kind of music is not really my cup of tea.',NULL,NULL,'cup of tea,not my cup of tea',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(745,10,21,'vocab','genuinely','genuinely','genuinely','真诚地；发自内心地；确实；真的。','强调真实、真心、没有套路。常见搭配有 genuinely interested, genuinely curious, genuinely surprised, genuinely concerned。','I am genuinely happy for you.\nShe genuinely cares about her students.\nHe is genuinely talented.\nThis is a genuinely good idea.',NULL,NULL,'genuinely,genuinely interested,genuinely curious',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(746,10,22,'phrase','definitely vs definitively','Definitively vs Definitely','definitely vs definitively','definitely = 肯定地、毫无疑问地。definitively = 最终地、权威地下定论。','definitely 是你大多数日常场景真正想用的。definitively 更正式，常见于学术、法律、医学、官方结论。','I will definitely come.\nYou are definitely right.\nThat is definitely a good idea.\nThe issue has been definitively resolved.\nThe study definitively proves the theory.\nHe was definitively diagnosed with the disease.',NULL,NULL,'definitely,definitively',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(747,10,23,'vocab','matter-of-factly','matter-of-factly','matter-of-factly','实事求是地；客观地；不带情绪地。','表示说话方式冷静、客观、就事论事。','He matter-of-factly explained that the system failed because of a configuration error.',NULL,NULL,'matter-of-factly',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(748,10,24,'sentence','Predict what you think should go in there.','预测这个应该是什么 / predict what should you think should go in there','Predict what you think should go in there.','预测你觉得里面应该放什么。','比原句更自然。结构是 predict + what you think + should go in there。','Predict what you think should go in there.',NULL,NULL,'predict,go in there',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(749,10,25,'phrase','win / gain his trust','win/gain his trust','win his trust / gain his trust','赢得他的信任。','两个都自然。gain 稍正式一点。','You need time to win his trust.\nShe worked hard to gain his trust.',NULL,NULL,'win trust,gain trust',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(750,10,26,'phrase','get insight into / gain insight into','get insight into sth','get insight into / gain insight into','深入了解；获得洞察；看透。','get insight into 更常见口语。gain insight into 稍正式一点。','This report helps us get insight into customer behaviour.\nLiving abroad helped me gain insight into different cultures.',NULL,NULL,'insight into,get insight into,gain insight into',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(751,10,27,'phrase','contrary to popular belief / on the contrary / be contrary to','contrary to popular belief','contrary to popular belief / on the contrary / be contrary to','与普遍看法相反；恰恰相反；与……相反。','contrary to popular belief 很常见，表示和大众认知不一样。on the contrary 表示“恰恰相反”。be contrary to 表示与某事相反。','Contrary to popular belief, old things are not necessarily better made.\nI do not dislike it. On the contrary, I love it.\nThis result is contrary to our expectations.',NULL,NULL,'contrary to popular belief,on the contrary,contrary to',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(752,10,28,'vocab','misguide / mislead / misdirected / misinformed','Misguide / Mislead / Misdirected / Misinformed','misguide / mislead / misdirected / misinformed','misguide = 给错误指导。mislead = 误导、让人形成错误印象。misdirected = 被引向错误方向的。misinformed = 获得了错误信息的。','这一组都和“错误信息、错误引导”有关，但侧重点不同。','He was misguided by bad advice.\nThe advertisement misled consumers.\nThe investigation was misdirected.\nThey were misinformed about the deadline.',NULL,NULL,'misguide,mislead,misdirected,misinformed',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(753,10,29,'phrase','survivorship bias','幸存者偏差','survivorship bias','幸存者偏差。','指人们只看到留下来的成功案例，而忽略了大量已经消失、失败或没留下来的样本。','This is a classic example of survivorship bias: old things are not all high quality—only the high-quality ones have lasted until now.\nContrary to popular belief, old things are not necessarily well made; rather, only the well-made ones have survived until today.',NULL,NULL,'survivorship bias',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(754,10,30,'vocab','visceral','visceral','visceral','本能的；发自内心的；强烈的。','visceral 常用来修饰 reaction, feeling, response, impact，不太直接修饰 words。','She had a visceral reaction when she saw the accident.\nHis speech had a visceral impact on the audience.\nShe had a visceral reaction and could not control herself completely.',NULL,NULL,'visceral reaction,visceral impact',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(755,10,31,'phrase','way too','way too expensive','way too','太……了；远远超过可接受程度。','way too 是非常常见的口语表达，意思相当于 much too / far too，但更口语。正式写作里更适合用 far too 或 much too。','This bag is way too heavy.\nIt is way too expensive for me.\nYou are driving way too fast.\nThat exam was way too hard.',NULL,NULL,'way too,too expensive',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21',1,'2026-04-05 13:48:21'),(756,11,1,'phrase','under the impression that','under the impression(that …)','under the impression that','以为；误以为；原本认为。','这是一个非常常见、很地道的表达，常暗示这个想法可能不正确或不完全正确。','I was under the impression that the meeting was today.\nShe\'s under the impression that the job is part-time.',NULL,NULL,'under the impression',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(757,11,2,'phrase','stick with me','Stick with me','stick with me','跟着我；别走开；听我说下去；支持我。','常见意思有三类：1. 跟着我。2. 先耐心听我讲。3. 支持我、别放弃我。','Stick with me and you\'ll be fine.\nStick with me for a second.\nPlease stick with me.\nThanks for sticking with me.\nStick with me — I\'ll show you how it works.\nStick with me, mate.\nJust stick with me for now.',NULL,NULL,'stick with me',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(758,11,3,'sentence','My fingers rambled over the keyboard.','finger ramble / 我的手指在键盘上乱敲。','My fingers rambled over the keyboard.','我的手指在键盘上乱敲。','这是比较文学化的表达，形容手指在键盘上随意乱动、乱敲。','My fingers rambled over the keyboard.',NULL,NULL,'keyboard,fingers,rambled',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(759,11,4,'vocab','tackle','tackle','tackle','处理；应对；解决；扑倒；擒抱；铲球；擒抱。','工作场景里 tackle 最常表示“着手解决问题”。体育里常表示扑倒、擒抱。也可作名词表示一次擒抱或铲球。','We need to tackle this issue quickly.\nShe\'s good at tackling complex problems.\nHe tackled the player to stop the try.\nZari tackles Lily in a hug.\nIt was a great tackle.',NULL,NULL,'tackle,issue,try,tackle in rugby',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(760,11,5,'phrase','It takes time to heal','需要时间来愈合','It takes time to heal.','需要时间来愈合。','heal 不仅能用于身体恢复，也常用于情感、心理、关系等层面的修复。','It takes time to heal.',NULL,NULL,'heal,time',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(761,11,6,'phrase','run around','描述自己很忙 / running around','run around','忙来忙去；到处奔波；两头忙。','常带一种很忙、很累、四处赶场的感觉。','I\'ve been running around a lot today.\nSorry I\'m late — I was running around all morning.\nShe\'s running around a lot with work and family.\nI\'m tired from running around all day.',NULL,NULL,'run around,busy',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(762,11,7,'phrase','I doubt it','我怀疑它','I doubt it.','我怀疑；我不太信；我觉得不太可能。','很常见的口语表达，用来表示怀疑对方说法或某件事发生的可能性。','I doubt it.',NULL,NULL,'I doubt it',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(763,11,8,'vocab','massive','It\'s massive','massive','巨大的；规模很大的；影响很大的；太厉害了。','可用于体积、面积、数量、项目规模，口语里也可表示“非常厉害、震撼”。','The stadium is massive.\nThat house is massive.\nIt\'s a massive project.\nThey made a massive profit.\nThat concert was massive.',NULL,NULL,'massive,project,profit,concert',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(764,11,9,'vocab','grilled','grilled','grilled','烤的；炙烤的。','表示食物经过明火、烤架或高温表面加热而烤熟。','I had grilled chicken for dinner.',NULL,NULL,'grilled',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(765,11,10,'sentence','You can just pull up by the front door.','你可以把车开到前门','You can just pull up by the front door.','你可以直接把车开到前门。','pull up 表示把车开到某个地方停下。','You can just pull up by the front door.',NULL,NULL,'pull up,front door',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(766,11,11,'vocab','long-sleeved / short-sleeved','长袖 / 短袖','long-sleeved / short-sleeved','长袖的；短袖的。','注意作定语时通常加连字符。','I bought a long-sleeved shirt.\nHe usually wears a short-sleeved T-shirt in summer.',NULL,NULL,'long-sleeved,short-sleeved',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(767,11,12,'sentence','It is too sunny here.','这里太晒了','It is too sunny here.','这里太晒了。','很自然的日常表达。','It is too sunny here.',NULL,NULL,'too sunny',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(768,11,13,'sentence','Chuck this in the car and we are pretty much out of here.','把这个放到车里，我门差不多可以出发了','Chuck this in the car and we are pretty much out of here.','把这个扔进车里，我们差不多就可以走了。','chuck = 随手放、扔。pretty much = 差不多。out of here = 离开这里。','Chuck this in the car and we are pretty much out of here.',NULL,NULL,'chuck,pretty much,out of here',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(769,11,14,'phrase','We are good to go','我们准备好了 / 我们可以出发 / 我们可以开始了','We are good to go.','我们准备好了；我们可以出发了；我们可以开始了。','非常常见的口语表达。','We are good to go.',NULL,NULL,'good to go',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(770,11,15,'phrase','Haven\'t seen you in a while','好久不见了','Haven\'t seen you in a while!','好久不见了！','很自然的口语寒暄。','Haven\'t seen you in a while!',NULL,NULL,'in a while,haven\'t seen you',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(771,11,16,'phrase','I have to go','我得走了 / 我得走开了','I have to go.','我得走了；我得先离开了。','比 I got to go 更标准；口语里 I gotta go 也很常见。','Sorry, I have to go. My bus is coming.',NULL,NULL,'have to go',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(772,11,17,'sentence','We\'ll hit the road to Hamilton.','我们出发去Hamliton','We\'ll hit the road to Hamilton.','我们要出发去 Hamilton 了。','hit the road = 出发，上路。','We\'ll hit the road to Hamilton.',NULL,NULL,'hit the road,Hamilton',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(773,11,18,'phrase','get a bit sick of','对…有点烦 / 开始厌倦…','get a bit sick of','对……有点烦；开始厌倦……。','很常见口语表达，比 be tired of 更随意一些。','I\'m getting a bit sick of this weather.',NULL,NULL,'sick of',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(774,11,19,'sentence','Did you meet your wife yourself, or was it a family setup?','你自己认识的你的妻子的吗还是家里安排的？','Did you meet your wife yourself, or was it a family setup?','你是自己认识你妻子的，还是家里安排你们认识的？','family setup 在这里表示家人安排的认识或相亲。set someone up 也常表示给某人介绍对象。','Did you meet your wife yourself, or was it a family setup?',NULL,NULL,'family setup,set someone up',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(775,11,20,'sentence','I was set up on a blind date last weekend.','上周末我被安排去相亲。','I was set up on a blind date last weekend.','上周末我被安排去相亲了。','be set up on a blind date = 被安排去相亲。','I was set up on a blind date last weekend.',NULL,NULL,'set up,blind date',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(776,11,21,'sentence','My friend set me up with her cousin.','我的朋友把我介绍给她的表亲','My friend set me up with her cousin.','我的朋友把我介绍给了她的表亲。','set someone up with someone = 给某人介绍恋爱对象。','My friend set me up with her cousin.',NULL,NULL,'set up with',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(777,11,22,'phrase','as long as','As long as','as long as','只要；在……期间；只要一直。','既可以表示条件“只要”，也可以表示时间持续“只要一直……”。','You can use my phone as long as you are careful.\nStay here as long as you need.\nI\'ll wait as long as it takes.',NULL,NULL,'as long as',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(778,11,23,'sentence','What time is it there now?','你那里现在是什么时间','What time is it there now?','你那边现在几点了？','最自然、最口语的表达。','What time is it there now?',NULL,NULL,'what time is it there now',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(779,11,24,'sentence','There is a two-hour time difference with New Zealand.','和新西兰有两小时的时差','There is a two-hour time difference with New Zealand.','和新西兰有两个小时的时差。','很标准的表达。','There is a two-hour time difference with New Zealand.',NULL,NULL,'time difference,New Zealand',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(780,11,25,'sentence','I am doing a master\'s degree.','我正在上硕士','I am doing a master\'s degree.','我正在读硕士。','最自然、最常用的表达之一。','I am doing a master\'s degree.',NULL,NULL,'master\'s degree',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(781,11,26,'phrase','take it seriously / the thing is / perfect timing','Take it seriously / The thing is / Perfect timing','take it seriously / the thing is / perfect timing','认真对待它；问题是；时机刚刚好。','take it seriously = 认真对待。the thing is = 问题是、关键是。perfect timing = 时机刚刚好，非常常用。','You need to take it seriously.\nThe thing is, we do not have enough time.\nYou called me—perfect timing!\nLunch arrived right when I was starving. Perfect timing.\nThis meeting is perfect timing for the project.',NULL,NULL,'take it seriously,the thing is,perfect timing',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(782,11,27,'phrase','blurry photo','Blurry photo','blurry photo','模糊的照片。','blurry = 模糊不清的。','This is a blurry photo.',NULL,NULL,'blurry photo',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(783,11,28,'vocab','sabotage','Sabotage','sabotage','蓄意破坏；暗中阻挠；破坏行为。','可作动词和名词。强调故意让某事失败，常带隐蔽性或间接性。','Someone tried to sabotage the project.\nHe sabotaged his own chances by being late.\nThe system failure was caused by sabotage.\nIndustrial sabotage shut down the factory.',NULL,NULL,'sabotage',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(784,11,29,'phrase','under the hood','under the hood','under the hood','引擎盖下面；内部实现；背后的工作原理。','字面意思是汽车引擎盖下方。技术语境里很常表示“系统内部是怎么运作的”。','Let me show you what is happening under the hood.',NULL,NULL,'under the hood',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15',1,'2026-04-05 13:56:15'),(785,12,1,'sentence','I\'ve got two assignments because I\'m studying two papers.','因为在学习两个科目所以有两个作业','I\'ve got two assignments because I\'m studying two papers.','因为我在学两门课，所以有两个作业。','papers 在新西兰和澳大利亚英语里常用来表示大学科目。assignment = 作业。','I\'ve got two assignments because I\'m studying two papers.',NULL,NULL,'assignments,papers',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(786,12,2,'sentence','I started my EAP course in June this year.','我六月份参加了EAP课程','I started my EAP course in June this year.','我今年六月开始上 EAP 课程。','很自然的表达。start a course 比 join a course 更常见。','I started my EAP course in June this year.',NULL,NULL,'EAP course,June',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(787,12,3,'sentence','The other assignment isn\'t computer-related.','另一个作业不是计算机相关的','The other assignment isn\'t computer-related.','另一个作业不是计算机相关的。','computer-related 很自然，表示“和计算机有关的”。','The other assignment isn\'t computer-related.',NULL,NULL,'computer-related,assignment',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(788,12,4,'sentence','My other assignment has nothing to do with computers.','另一个作业不是计算机相关的','My other assignment has nothing to do with computers.','我的另一个作业和计算机完全没关系。','比 computer-related 更随意，更像日常口语。','My other assignment has nothing to do with computers.',NULL,NULL,'has nothing to do with,computers',0,0,1,'2