d after that we only have theoretical subjects.','this goes into five items ,and after we have only theoretical subject','This is divided into five items, and after that we only have theoretical subjects.','这部分被分成五项，然后之后我们就只有理论课程了。','divide into 比 goes into 更自然、更准确。','This is divided into five items, and after that we only have theoretical subjects.',NULL,NULL,'divided into,theoretical subjects',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(795,12,11,'sentence','This part is broken down into five items, and after that we move on to purely theoretical subjects.','this goes into five items ,and after we have only theoretical subject','This part is broken down into five items, and after that we move on to purely theoretical subjects.','这部分被拆分成五项，然后之后我们转到纯理论课程。','break down into 很自然，move on to 表示转入下一个阶段。','This part is broken down into five items, and after that we move on to purely theoretical subjects.',NULL,NULL,'broken down into,move on to,purely theoretical',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(796,12,12,'phrase','reach out to someone','联系某人','reach out to someone','联系某人。','很自然的表达，尤其常用于邮件、工作沟通、主动联系。','Feel free to reach out to me anytime.',NULL,NULL,'reach out to',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(797,12,13,'sentence','But Manchester feels really chill to me.','但是曼彻斯特让我感到很放松','But Manchester feels really chill to me.','但曼彻斯特给我的感觉真的很放松。','feel chill 很口语，表示氛围轻松、舒服、不紧绷。','But Manchester feels really chill to me.',NULL,NULL,'chill,Manchester',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(798,12,14,'sentence','Is it something you\'re getting some revenue off?','你能中获得收入吗？','Is it something you\'re getting some revenue off?','你能从这个里面获得一些收入吗？','get revenue off something 表示“从某事中获得收益”，但更自然也可以说 make money from it。','Is it something you\'re getting some revenue off?',NULL,NULL,'revenue,get revenue off',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(799,12,15,'phrase','I\'m not bothered / I don\'t mind / It\'s all good / No worries','我不介意 / 我不在乎 / 没关系','I\'m not bothered / I don\'t mind / It\'s all good / No worries','我无所谓；我都可以；没关系；别担心。','I\'m not bothered 在英式和新西兰英语里很自然，表示“我无所谓”。I don\'t mind 更通用。It\'s all good 和 No worries 常用来表示“没关系”。','I\'m not bothered, you choose.\nI\'m not bothered if we eat here or somewhere else.\nI don\'t mind.\nIt\'s all good.\nNo worries.',NULL,NULL,'not bothered,don\'t mind,it\'s all good,no worries',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(800,12,16,'phrase','What\'s a typical day like?','“你（或某人）典型的一天是怎样的？”','What\'s a typical day like?','你平时一天通常是怎么过的？','用来问某人日常安排、生活或工作流程。','What\'s a typical day like for you?',NULL,NULL,'typical day',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(801,12,17,'sentence','If there are fences that need to be repaired, I\'ll fix them up.','If there are fences that need to be repaired, I will fix them up.','If there are fences that need to be repaired, I\'ll fix them up.','如果有围栏需要修，我就会把它们修好。','fix up = 修理好、整理好。','If there are fences that need to be repaired, I\'ll fix them up.',NULL,NULL,'fix up,fences,repaired',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(802,12,18,'phrase','take on board / may be perceived as being','take on board / may be perceived as being','take on board / may be perceived as being','吸收；接受；可能被认为是。','take on board 常表示认真听取并吸收意见。may be perceived as being 表示“可能被看作、被理解成……”。','You need to take that feedback on board.\nThat may be perceived as being too direct.',NULL,NULL,'take on board,perceived as being',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(803,12,19,'sentence','But I was more drawn to finance and office systems.','我现在更倾向于金融和办公系统','But I was more drawn to finance and office systems.','但我当时更被金融和办公系统吸引。','be drawn to 表示“被……吸引，更倾向于……”。','But I was more drawn to finance and office systems.',NULL,NULL,'drawn to,finance,office systems',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(804,12,20,'sentence','I\'m probably a bit overqualified for my role.','我可能在我的岗位上有点资历过高','I\'m probably a bit overqualified for my role.','我可能对现在这个岗位来说有点资历过高了。','overqualified = 资历高于岗位要求。','I\'m probably a bit overqualified for my role.',NULL,NULL,'overqualified,role',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(805,12,21,'vocab','prospective vs perspective','prospective vs perspective','prospective vs perspective','prospective = 未来可能的、潜在的。perspective = 观点、看法、角度。','prospective 常用于 prospective student, buyer, employee。perspective 常用于 from my perspective, a different perspective。','We are meeting prospective clients tomorrow.\nFrom my perspective, this plan is not practical.',NULL,NULL,'prospective,perspective',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(806,12,22,'sentence','I live in the coldest part of China, so the temperature can drop to minus 30 degrees.','I live in the coldest part of China, so the temperature can drop to minus 30 degrees','I live in the coldest part of China, so the temperature can drop to minus 30 degrees.','我住在中国最冷的地区，所以气温会降到零下 30 度。','drop to minus 30 degrees = 降到零下 30 度。','I live in the coldest part of China, so the temperature can drop to minus 30 degrees.',NULL,NULL,'coldest,minus 30 degrees,temperature',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(807,12,23,'sentence','Isn\'t Mumbai in the tropics? How can it have below-zero temperatures?','孟买不是在热带地区吗？怎么会有零下的气温呢？','Isn\'t Mumbai in the tropics? How can it have below-zero temperatures?','孟买不是在热带地区吗？怎么会有零下气温呢？','below-zero temperatures = 零下气温。','Isn\'t Mumbai in the tropics? How can it have below-zero temperatures?',NULL,NULL,'Mumbai,tropics,below-zero temperatures',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30',1,'2026-04-05 14:01:30'),(808,13,1,'vocab','renown','renown','renown','名声；声望。','正式词，常作名词，表示很高的名望。','She gained renown for her research.',NULL,NULL,'renown',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(809,13,2,'vocab','renowned','renowned','renowned','著名的；有名望的。','形容词，表示“很有名”。','It is a renowned university.',NULL,NULL,'renowned',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(810,13,3,'vocab','nonetheless','nonetheless','nonetheless','尽管如此；然而。','正式一点的转折词，意思接近 nevertheless。','The task was difficult; nonetheless, we finished it.',NULL,NULL,'nonetheless',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(811,13,4,'vocab','pursuit','pursuit','pursuit','追求。','常用于梦想、目标、事业等抽象追求。','The pursuit of happiness matters to everyone.',NULL,NULL,'pursuit',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(812,13,5,'phrase','in pursuit of','in pursuit of','in pursuit of','为了追求……。','后面常接梦想、目标、成功等名词。','He left his job in pursuit of his dream.',NULL,NULL,'in pursuit of',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(813,13,6,'vocab','engage','engage','engage','吸引；使参与；雇佣；交战。','这是一个多义高频词，具体意思看搭配。','The teacher used games to engage the students in learning.',NULL,NULL,'engage',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(814,13,7,'phrase','engage someone\'s interest','engage someone\'s interest/attention','engage someone\'s interest / engage someone\'s attention','吸引某人的兴趣；吸引某人的注意力。','常用于教学、演讲、广告语境。','The story engaged the audience\'s attention.',NULL,NULL,'engage interest,engage attention',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(815,13,8,'phrase','engage someone as','engage someone as xxx','engage someone as','雇佣某人为……。','比较正式，常见于合同、新闻、商业英语。','They engaged her as a consultant.',NULL,NULL,'engage as',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(816,13,9,'phrase','a chain of','a chain of','a chain of','一连串；一系列。','后面常接 events, problems, reactions 等。','A chain of events led to the failure.',NULL,NULL,'a chain of',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(817,13,10,'vocab','prior','prior','prior','先前的；事先的；更重要的。','最常见搭配是 prior experience, prior notice, prior to。','No prior experience is required.',NULL,NULL,'prior',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(818,13,11,'phrase','prior to','prior to','prior to','在……之前。','比 before 更正式。','Please contact us prior to 