ow in','额外加送；顺带提到；随手加进去。','上下文不同，意思不同。','They\'ll throw in a free case.\nHe threw in a few jokes during the meeting.',NULL,NULL,'throw in',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(884,13,77,'phrase','what\'s the catch','what\'s the catch','what\'s the catch','有什么隐藏条件？','常用于怀疑某件事好得不像真的。','The offer sounds amazing — what\'s the catch?',NULL,NULL,'what\'s the catch',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(885,13,78,'phrase','be in luck','be in luck','be in luck','运气好；走运。','很口语。','You are in luck today.',NULL,NULL,'be in luck',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(886,13,79,'vocab','remain','remain','remain','保持；仍然是。','后面可接形容词、名词或状态。','The rules remain unchanged.\nHe remained calm.',NULL,NULL,'remain',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(887,13,80,'vocab','roll over','roll over','roll over','顺延；滚动转入；翻滚。','在金融、合同、假期、余额里很常见。','The balance will roll over to next month.',NULL,NULL,'roll over',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(888,13,81,'vocab','fee','fee','fee','费用；服务费。','如 service fee, annual fee, membership fee。','There is an annual fee.',NULL,NULL,'fee',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(889,13,82,'phrase','too good to be true','too good to be true','too good to be true','好得不像真的。','表示怀疑事情好得不现实。','That deal seems too good to be true.',NULL,NULL,'too good to be true',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(890,13,83,'phrase','in ages','in ages','in ages','很久。','常用于否定句。','I haven\'t seen him in ages.',NULL,NULL,'in ages',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(891,13,84,'phrase','I\'m doing great / well','I\'m doing great/well.','I\'m doing great / I\'m doing well','我过得很好。','都是自然表达。','I\'m doing great, thanks.',NULL,NULL,'doing great,doing well',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(892,13,85,'phrase','run into','meeting someone accidentally : run into','run into','偶遇。','很常见的口语短语。','I ran into an old friend yesterday.',NULL,NULL,'run into',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(893,13,86,'phrase','catch up on','learn about recent past events : catch up on','catch up on','补看；补做；补了解。','常接 news, sleep, work, emails。','I need to catch up on the news.',NULL,NULL,'catch up on',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(894,13,87,'phrase','freak out','freak out','freak out','慌了；崩了；激动得不行。','语义根据语境可偏负面惊慌，也可偏正面激动。','She totally freaked out when she saw the spider.',NULL,NULL,'freak out',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(895,13,88,'phrase','lose it','lose it','lose it','情绪失控；崩溃。','通常偏负面。','He lost it during the argument.',NULL,NULL,'lose it',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(896,13,89,'vocab','shriek','shriek','shriek','尖叫。','比 scream 更偏高而尖的声音。','She let out a shriek.',NULL,NULL,'shriek',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(897,13,90,'vocab','bizarre','bizarre','bizarre','离奇的；古怪的。','比 strange 更强。','It was a bizarre coincidence.',NULL,NULL,'bizarre',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(898,13,91,'vocab','coincidence / coincident','coincident / coincidence','coincidence / coincident','coincidence = 巧合。coincident = 同时发生的；巧合的。','日常更常用名词 coincidence。','That was an amazing coincidence.',NULL,NULL,'coincidence,coincident',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(899,13,92,'vocab','silly / ridiculous','silly / ridiculous','silly / ridiculous','silly = 傻的；幼稚的。ridiculous = 荒谬的；可笑的。','ridiculous 语气更强，常不用 very，更自然是 absolutely ridiculous。','That was a silly mistake.\nThe idea sounds ridiculous.',NULL,NULL,'silly,ridiculous',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(900,13,93,'phrase','commitments','I can’t join the meeting because I have some other commitments','commitments','安排；承诺；责任。','这里表示其他已经安排好的事。','I can’t join the meeting because I have some other commitments.',NULL,NULL,'commitments',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(901,13,94,'phrase','go into effect','goes into effect','go into effect','生效。','不是“受到影响”。','The new rule goes into effect next week.',NULL,NULL,'go into effect',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(902,13,95,'vocab','watch','watch','watch','监测；监视；观察。','名词时可表示“值班监视”或“观察期”。','The area is under watch.',NULL,NULL,'watch',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(903,13,96,'phrase','take shelter from','take shelter from the storm','take shelter from','躲避；避开。','常接 storm, rain, attack 等。','They took shelter from the storm.',NULL,NULL,'take shelter from',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(904,13,97,'vocab','fulfil','fulfill','fulfil','实现；履行；满足。','英式拼写 fulfil，美式是 fulfill。','She fulfilled her promise.',NULL,NULL,'fulfil',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(905,13,98,'vocab','ultimate','ultimate','ultimate','最终的；根本的；终极的。','常见于 ultimate goal, ultimate decision。','That was his ultimate goal.',NULL,NULL,'ultimate',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(906,13,99,'phrase','be someone\'s undoing','be somebody\'s undoing','be someone\'s undoing','导致某人失败；毁了某人。','比较书面，但很地道。','Greed was his undoing.',NULL,NULL,'undoing',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(907,13,100,'vocab','strive','strive','strive','努力争取；奋力做到。','strive for + 名词；strive to + 动词。','We strive for excellence.\nShe strives to improve.',NULL,NULL,'strive,strive for,strive to',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41',1,'2026-04-05 14:52:41'),(908,13,101,'vocab','pose','pose','pose','造成；引起；提出；摆姿势。','常见于 pose a risk, pose a problem, pose a question。也可表示摆姿势拍照。','The changes pose a risk to safety.\nThe reporter posed a question.\nHe posed for a photo.',NULL,NULL,'pose,pose a risk,pose a question',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(909,13,102,'vocab','spill','spill','spill','洒出；溢出；泄露。','既可指液体洒出来，也可比喻秘密“说漏嘴”。','I spilled the milk.\nHe spilled the secret by accident.',NULL,NULL,'spill',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(910,13,103,'vocab','spray','spray','spray','喷；喷雾；喷剂。','可作动词和名词。','Spray the cleaner on the surface.\nUse a spray to water the plants.',NULL,NULL,'spray',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(911,13,104,'phrase','bug spray','bug spray','bug spray','驱虫喷雾；杀虫喷雾。','夏天、露营、户外场景很常见。','Take some bug spray with you when you go camping.',NULL,NULL,'bug spray',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(912,13,105,'vocab','splash','splash','splash','泼溅；飞溅；泼洒声。','可作动词和名词。','Water splashed onto the floor.\nThe children were splashing in the pool.',NULL,NULL,'splash',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(913,13,106,'vocab','sprinkle','sprinkle','sprinkle','撒；洒；少量散布。','常用于撒盐、撒糖、洒水等。','Sprinkle some salt on top.\nLeaves were sprinkled across the lawn.',NULL,NULL,'sprinkle',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(914,13,107,'phrase','border on','border on sth','border on','接近于；近乎。','常接 absurdity, cruelty, ridiculousness 等。','His behaviour borders on ridiculous.',NULL,NULL,'border on',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(915,13,108,'vocab','splendid','splendid','splendid','极好的；非常精彩的。','偏书面或英式语感。','It was a splendid performance.',NULL,NULL,'splendid',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(916,13,109,'vocab','excellent','excellent','excellent','优秀的；极好的。','非常常用的夸奖词。','She did an excellent job.',NULL,NULL,'excellent',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(917,13,110,'vocab','brilliant','brilliant','brilliant','出色的；极聪明的；非常棒的。','英式英语里很常用来表示“太棒了”。','That\'s a brilliant idea.',NULL,NULL,'brilliant',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(918,13,111,'vocab','distinguished','distinguished','distinguished','杰出的；有声望的。','常用于人物、职业成就。','He is a distinguished professor.',NULL,NULL,'distinguished',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(919,13,112,'vocab','exceptional','exceptional','exceptional','非凡的；特别优秀的。','比 very good 更强。','She showed exceptional talent.',NULL,NULL,'exceptional',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(920,13,113,'vocab','exquisite','exquisite','exquisite','精致的；优美的。','常用于设计、食物、工艺品。','The design is exquisite.',NULL,NULL,'exquisite',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(921,13,114,'vocab','fantastic','fantastic','fantastic','极好的；太棒了。','口语里很常见。','The trip was fantastic.',NULL,NULL,'fantastic',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(922,13,115,'vocab','gorgeous','gorgeous','gorgeous','非常漂亮的；华丽的。','常形容人、风景、衣服、设计。','That dress is gorgeous.',NULL,NULL,'gorgeous',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(923,13,116,'vocab','impressive','impressive','impressive','令人印象深刻的。','很常用。','Her progress is impressive.',NULL,NULL,'impressive',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(924,13,117,'vocab','magnificent','magnificent','magnificent','宏伟的；壮丽的；极好的。','常用于建筑、景色、表演。','The view was magnificent.',NULL,NULL,'magnificent',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(925,13,118,'vocab','marvellous','marvelous','marvellous','极好的；令人惊叹的。','英式拼写 marvellous，美式是 marvelous。','We had a marvellous time.',NULL,NULL,'marvellous',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(926,13,119,'vocab','outstanding','outstanding','outstanding','杰出的；突出的。','也可表示“未解决的、未支付的”，但这里是“杰出”。','She delivered an outstanding performance.',NULL,NULL,'outstanding',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(927,13,120,'vocab','wonderful','wonderful','wonderful','极好的；令人愉快的。','语气温和但非常正面。','That\'s wonderful news.',NULL,NULL,'wonderful',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(928,13,121,'vocab','superb','superb','superb','极佳的；上乘的。','正式和口语都能用。','The food was superb.',NULL,NULL,'superb',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(929,13,122,'vocab','dramatic','dramatic','dramatic','戏剧性的；引人注目的。','可用于变化、转折、效果很大。','There was a dramatic change in the weather.',NULL,NULL,'dramatic',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(930,13,123,'vocab','drama','drama','drama','戏剧；戏剧性事件。','日常里也可表示“狗血、麻烦事”。','I do not want any drama today.',NULL,NULL,'drama',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(931,13,124,'vocab','dramatically','dramatically','dramatically','显著地；急剧地；戏剧性地。','常修饰变化、提升、下降、转折，不适合直接修饰 creative man。','Her performance improved dramatically.\nThe temperature dropped dramatically overnight.',NULL,NULL,'dramatically',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(932,13,125,'vocab','redundant','redundant','redundant','多余的；被裁员的。','be made redundant = 被裁员。','Seventy workers were made redundant.',NULL,NULL,'redundant,made redundant',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(933,13,126,'vocab','lay-off','lay-off','lay-off','裁员；解雇。','名词形式。','The company announced a lay-off.',NULL,NULL,'lay-off',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(934,13,127,'vocab','workstation','workstation','workstation','工位；工作站。','办公室和 IT 都常用。','Each employee has a workstation.',NULL,NULL,'workstation',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(935,13,128,'vocab','defective','defective','defective','有缺陷的；有瑕疵的。','常用于产品、设备、零件。','The product was defective.',NULL,NULL,'defective',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(936,13,129,'vocab','defect','defect','defect','缺陷；瑕疵；叛逃。','最常见是名词“缺陷”。','The machine has a serious defect.',NULL,NULL,'defect',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(937,13,130,'phrase','two-for-one special','two for one special','two-for-one special','买一送一优惠；两件只付一件价。','零售促销高频表达。','The shop is running a two-for-one special.',NULL,NULL,'two-for-one special',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(938,13,131,'vocab','dough','dough','dough','生面团。','做面包、披萨、饺子皮都能用。','Let the dough rise for an hour.',NULL,NULL,'dough',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(939,13,132,'phrase','in replacement of','in replacement of','in replacement of','作为……的替代。','更自然的常见说法也有 in place of。','This part was installed in replacement of the old one.',NULL,NULL,'in replacement of',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(940,13,133,'phrase','stick together','stick together','stick together','黏在一起；团结一致。','可字面，也可比喻团队团结。','We need to stick together.',NULL,NULL,'stick together',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(941,13,134,'phrase','hook up','hook up','hook up','连接；介绍；搭上线；暧昧；联机。','意思很多，必须看语境。技术里是连接，社交里是介绍资源，感情里是短暂暧昧或发生关系，游戏里是联机。','Can you hook up the TV to the Wi-Fi?\nShe hooked me up with a discount.\nThey hooked up at the party.\nLet\'s hook up online and play.',NULL,NULL,'hook up',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(942,13,135,'phrase','in critical condition','in critical condition','in critical condition','处于危险期；情况危急。','最常见于医疗，也可引申用于机械、经济、环境系统。','After the accident, he was in critical condition.\nThe engine is in critical condition.',NULL,NULL,'in critical condition',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00',1,'2026-04-05 15:01:00'),(943,14,1,'phrase','make ends meet','Make ends meet','make ends meet','维持生计；勉强支付基本生活开销。','表示收入刚刚够支付房租、食物、账单等基本费用，常带“手头紧”的意思。','With rising costs, it is harder for some families to make ends meet.\nShe works two jobs to make ends meet.',NULL,NULL,'make ends meet,money,bills,expenses',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(944,14,2,'phrase','yet as contrast','Yet as a conjunction','yet','然而；可是。','作连词时，表示转折，意思接近 but。','She was tired, yet she continued working.',NULL,NULL,'yet,contrast,conjunction',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(945,14,3,'phrase','yet in negative sentences and questions','Yet as an adverb','yet','还；尚未；到目前为止。','常用于否定句和疑问句，表示某事到现在还没发生，但未来可能会发生。','She has not arrived yet.\nHave you finished the report yet?',NULL,NULL,'yet,not yet,questions,negative sentences',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(946,14,4,'phrase','as yet and the best is yet to come','As yet / the best is yet to come','as yet / the best is yet to come','as yet = 到目前为止；the best is yet to come = 最好的还在后头。','as yet 偏正式；the best is yet to come 很常见，语气积极。','As yet, no decisions have been made.\nThe best is yet to come.',NULL,NULL,'as yet,the best is yet to come',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(947,14,5,'phrase','yet another','Yet another delay','yet another','竟然又一个；又来一个。','常带不耐烦、无奈或惊讶语气。','Yet another delay — this is getting ridiculous.',NULL,NULL,'yet another,emphasis',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(948,14,6,'vocab','centenarian','centenarian','centenarian','百岁老人。','指活到 100 岁或以上的人。','The town is home to several centenarians.',NULL,NULL,'centenarian',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(949,14,7,'sentence','Would somebody explain what\'s going on?','Would somebody explain what\'s going on ?','Would somebody explain what\'s going on?','谁能解释一下发生什么了吗？','自然且礼貌，适合在一头雾水时请求别人说明情况。','Would somebody explain what\'s going on?',NULL,NULL,'what\'s going on,explain',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(950,14,8,'phrase','long faces','I have never seen so many long faces','long faces','愁眉苦脸；一脸不高兴。','long face 常用来形容人看起来失望、沮丧或不开心。','I have never seen so many long faces.',NULL,NULL,'long faces',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(951,14,9,'phrase','be in the dark','I\'m in the dark here!','be in the dark','不知情；一头雾水。','表示对某件事完全不了解，不清楚情况。','At least explain what\'s going on — I\'m in the dark here!',NULL,NULL,'in the dark',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(952,14,10,'phrase','it\'s a long story','It\'s a long story.','It\'s a long story.','说来话长。','很常见的固定表达，用于不想马上展开解释时。','It\'s a long story. I\'ll tell you later.',NULL,NULL,'it\'s a long story',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(953,14,11,'phrase','I\'m all ears','Now, I\'m all ears. Go on. Do tell.','I\'m all ears','我洗耳恭听。','表示“我很想听，请继续说”。很口语，也很常见。','Now I\'m all ears. Go on.',NULL,NULL,'all ears',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(954,14,12,'phrase','bound to be','bound to be','bound to be','肯定会；很可能会。','表示某件事几乎一定会发生。','There is bound to be some confusion at first.',NULL,NULL,'bound to be',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(955,14,13,'phrase','in my opinion','I would say in my opinion','in my opinion','在我看来；依我看。','比 I would say in my opinion 更简洁自然。','In my opinion, the news is true.',NULL,NULL,'in my opinion',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(956,14,14,'phrase','bored vs boring','boring Is human feeling but bored is for describing some situation','bored vs boring','bored 用来形容人的感受；boring 用来形容事物或情况。','人会 feel bored，事情会 be boring。','I felt bored during the class.\nThe class was boring.',NULL,NULL,'bored,boring',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(957,14,15,'phrase','on public transportation','When people on public transportation. on transportation not in transportation','on public transportation','在公共交通上。','常说 on public transportation，不说 in transportation。','People on public transportation often look tired.',NULL,NULL,'on public transportation',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(958,14,16,'phrase','share with each other','share with each other','share with each other','彼此分享。','简单自然的表达。','We should share our ideas with each other.',NULL,NULL,'share with each other',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(959,14,17,'phrase','shared area and common area','a common area is equaly to a share area','shared area / common area','共享区域；公共区域。','shared area 和 common area 都可以，但 common area 更常见于楼房、办公场所等语境。','The kitchen is a common area.\nThis is a shared area for all staff.',NULL,NULL,'shared area,common area',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(960,14,18,'sentence','I work as a freelancer.','I work as a freelancer','I work as a freelancer.','我是自由职业者。','自然的职业介绍句子。','I work as a freelancer.',NULL,NULL,'freelancer',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(961,14,19,'sentence','I like teaching because it\'s meaningful for me to do for a living.','I like teaching because it\'s a meaningful thing for me to do for a living','I like teaching because it\'s meaningful for me to do for a living.','我喜欢教学，因为对我来说，把它作为职业很有意义。','for a living 表示“作为职业、为了谋生”。','I like teaching because it\'s meaningful for me to do for a living.',NULL,NULL,'for a living,meaningful,teaching',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(962,14,20,'sentence','Do you think childhood is boring or adulthood is boring?','Do you think childhood is boring or adulthood is boring ?','Do you think childhood is boring or adulthood is boring?','你觉得童年无聊，还是成年生活无聊？','很适合口语讨论题。','Do you think childhood is boring or adulthood is boring?',NULL,NULL,'childhood,adulthood,boring',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(963,14,21,'sentence','Let\'s talk about celebrities and people connected to politics.','Let\'s talk about celebrities. the poeple who are connected to the politics.','Let\'s talk about celebrities and people connected to politics.','我们来聊聊名人和与政治有关的人。','connected to politics 比 connected to the politics 更自然。','Let\'s talk about celebrities and people connected to politics.',NULL,NULL,'celebrities,politics',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(964,14,22,'sentence','I want to become well-known in my major.','I want to become well-known, especially in my major...','I want to become well-known, especially in my major, because I truly want to become an expert in it.','我想在自己的专业领域变得有名，因为我真心想成为这个领域的专家。','适合表达自己的职业目标和志向。','I want to become well-known, especially in my major, because I truly want to become an expert in it.',NULL,NULL,'well-known,major,expert',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(965,14,23,'phrase','IELTS speaking scoring terms','fluency and coherence / pronunciation / vocabulary or lexical resource / grammar / hesitation','fluency and coherence / pronunciation / lexical resource / grammar / hesitation','一组 IELTS 口语评分和反馈常见术语。','fluency and coherence = 流利度与连贯性；lexical resource = 词汇资源；hesitation = 停顿、犹豫。','The IELTS speaking test is scored on fluency and coherence, pronunciation, lexical resource, and grammar.\nToo much hesitation can affect your score.',NULL,NULL,'IELTS,fluency,coherence,pronunciation,lexical resource,grammar,hesitation',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(966,14,24,'phrase','bang into someone','bang into sb','bang into someone','不小心撞上某人。','和 bump into 相近，但 bang into 更强调撞击感。','I banged into someone at the station.',NULL,NULL,'bang into',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(967,14,25,'phrase','lemme gimme wanna gonna','lemme / gimme / wanna / gonna','lemme / gimme / wanna / gonna','非常口语化的连读形式。','lemme = let me；gimme = give me；wanna = want to；gonna = going to。适合理解听力，不适合正式写作。','Lemme check.\nGimme a minute.\nI wanna go home.\nI\'m gonna call him.',NULL,NULL,'lemme,gimme,wanna,gonna',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(968,14,26,'phrase','break free','break free','break free','挣脱；摆脱束缚。','可用于字面和比喻义。','She wants to break free from that routine.',NULL,NULL,'break free',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(969,14,27,'phrase','what the heck is going on','what the heck is going on','What the heck is going on?','到底在搞什么？','带一点情绪，但不算太粗鲁。','What the heck is going on here?',NULL,NULL,'what the heck',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(970,14,28,'phrase','cheat on someone','cheat on someone 对....不忠','cheat on someone','对某人不忠；出轨。','常用于感情关系。','He cheated on his girlfriend.',NULL,NULL,'cheat on',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(971,14,29,'phrase','that\'s not gonna cut it','I don\'t think that\'s gonna cut it well','that\'s not gonna cut it','那不够好；那不够用；那行不通。','非常自然的口语表达，表示“那样还不够”。','I do not think that\'s gonna cut it.',NULL,NULL,'not gonna cut it',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(972,14,30,'phrase','insinuate and accidentally insinuated','I accidentally insinuated.','insinuate / I accidentally insinuated','insinuate = 含沙射影、暗示；I accidentally insinuated = 我不小心暗示了某件事。','多指间接表达，不直接明说。','I accidentally insinuated that he was lying.',NULL,NULL,'insinuate',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(973,14,31,'phrase','distraction occasion chubby','distraction / occasion / chubby','distraction / occasion / chubby','distraction = 分心、干扰；occasion = 场合、时刻；chubby = 圆胖的。','都是日常很常见的词。','The noise was a distraction.\nIt was a special occasion.\nThe baby looked chubby and cute.',NULL,NULL,'distraction,occasion,chubby',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(974,14,32,'sentence','Get out of my store, you jerk.','get out of my store you jerk','Get out of my store, you jerk.','滚出我的店，你这个混蛋。','语气很冲，带明显攻击性。','Get out of my store, you jerk.',NULL,NULL,'jerk,get out',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(975,14,33,'phrase','polar ice caps','polar ice caps','polar ice caps','极地冰盖。','环境、气候话题高频表达。','The polar ice caps are melting.',NULL,NULL,'polar ice caps',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(976,14,34,'phrase','beg to differ','beg to differ','beg to differ','恕我不同意。','比较礼貌、正式的不同意表达。','I understand your point, but I beg to differ.',NULL,NULL,'beg to differ',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(977,14,35,'phrase','mislead put forth have a bad feeling about','mislead / put forth / have bad felling about sth','mislead / put forth / have a bad feeling about','mislead = 误导；put forth = 提出；have a bad feeling about = 对……有不祥预感。','put forth 常见于正式表达，如 put forth an idea 或 proposal。','The ad misled customers.\nShe put forth a new proposal.\nI have a bad feeling about this.',NULL,NULL,'mislead,put forth,bad feeling',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(978,14,36,'phrase','kick someone out and misbehavior','kick sb out / misbehavior','kick someone out / misbehavior','kick someone out = 把某人赶出去；misbehavior = 不当行为。','常见于学校、店里、工作场景。','If someone misbehaves, I will kick them out.',NULL,NULL,'kick out,misbehavior',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(979,14,37,'phrase','singular they with someone','someone ... them','someone ... them','someone 后面接 them，是现代英语常见的单数 they 用法。','当性别未知或不重要时，them 很自然。','If someone misbehaves, I will kick them out.\nSomeone forgot their bag.',NULL,NULL,'singular they,someone them',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(980,14,38,'phrase','creep me out','creepy me out','creep me out','让我毛骨悚然。','常用来形容让人不舒服、发毛的东西。','That movie really creeps me out.',NULL,NULL,'creep me out',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(981,14,39,'phrase','kind of','kind of','kind of','有点；某种；有些。','既可以表示程度不那么强，也可以缓和语气。','I\'m kind of tired today.\nIt\'s kind of strange, don\'t you think?',NULL,NULL,'kind of',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(982,14,40,'phrase','scare the heck out of me','scared the heck out of me','scare the heck out of me','吓死我了。','比 scare me 更强，但仍属于口语、非正式表达。','That noise scared the heck out of me.',NULL,NULL,'scare the heck out of',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(983,14,41,'phrase','fill me in and sure thing','fill me in / sure thing','fill me in / sure thing','fill me in = 告诉我详情；sure thing = 没问题，我来做。','都非常常见的口语表达。','Can you fill me in on what happened?\nSure thing, I\'ll do it.',NULL,NULL,'fill me in,sure thing',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(984,14,42,'phrase','that\'s personal','that\'s personal','That\'s personal.','这是私人问题。','礼貌地表示不想回答某个问题。','I\'d rather not answer that — that\'s personal.',NULL,NULL,'that\'s personal',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(985,14,43,'phrase','come in from China','come in from China : arrive','come in from China','从中国过来；从中国抵达。','可以指从中国来到另一个国家或地点。','She came in from China last week.',NULL,NULL,'come in from China',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(986,14,44,'phrase','in that case','because of that : in that case','in that case','如果是这样的话。','很自然的逻辑承接表达。','In that case, we should wait.',NULL,NULL,'in that case',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(987,14,45,'phrase','have you heard that','I don\'t know if you have heard that','I don\'t know if you\'ve heard that','我不知道你有没有听说过那件事。','常用于开始讲八卦、新闻或新信息。','I don\'t know if you\'ve heard that, but he\'s moving to Australia.',NULL,NULL,'have heard that',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(988,14,46,'phrase','excuse me if I\'m being a bit nosy','excuse me if I am being a bit nosy','Excuse me if I\'m being a bit nosy.','如果我有点多管闲事，请见谅。','非常自然的礼貌开场，用来缓和私人问题。','Excuse me if I\'m being a bit nosy, but are you married?',NULL,NULL,'nosy',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(989,14,47,'phrase','don\'t get me wrong','don\'t get me wrong','Don\'t get me wrong.','别误会我的意思。','用来缓和批评、不同意见或敏感表达。','Don\'t get me wrong — I\'m just trying to help.',NULL,NULL,'don\'t get me wrong',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(990,14,48,'phrase','get a good look','I couldn\'t really get a good look','get a good look','看清楚；看个仔细。','非常常见，表示因为角度、光线、距离等原因没看清。','I couldn\'t really get a good look at the sign.',NULL,NULL,'get a good look',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(991,14,49,'phrase','lay down','lay down','lay down','放下；制定；放弃；录制。','高频多义短语。可字面放下，也可比喻立规矩、牺牲、录音。','She laid down the book on the table.\nThe company laid down strict guidelines.\nThe band went to the studio to lay down new tracks.',NULL,NULL,'lay down',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(992,14,50,'phrase','lay down arms and lay down the law','lay down arms / lay down the law','lay down arms / lay down the law','lay down arms = 放下武器；lay down the law = 强硬立规矩。','都是固定搭配。','The rebels were forced to lay down their arms.\nHe laid down the law about keeping the office clean.',NULL,NULL,'lay down arms,lay down the law',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(993,14,51,'phrase','contagious and come down with a cold','contagious / come down with a cold','contagious / come down with a cold','contagious = 会传染的；come down with a cold = 感冒了。','contagious 也可引申为“有感染力的”，如 laughter is contagious。','The disease is contagious.\nI think I\'m coming down with a cold.',NULL,NULL,'contagious,come down with',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(994,14,52,'phrase','in the meantime and at the same time','in the meantime / at the same time / in the same time','in the meantime / at the same time / in the same time','in the meantime = 在这期间；at the same time = 同时；in the same time = 在同样时长里。','描述“同时发生”通常用 at the same time，不用 in the same time。','I\'ll finish this report. In the meantime, you can start the slides.\nThey started talking at the same time.\nHe completed the task in the same time it took me to finish lunch.',NULL,NULL,'in the meantime,at the same time,in the same time',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(995,14,53,'phrase','blow something out of proportion','blow something out of proportion','blow something out of proportion','小题大做；把事情夸大。','表示把小问题说得像大问题一样严重。','Don\'t blow this out of proportion.',NULL,NULL,'blow out of proportion',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(996,14,54,'phrase','cut that out','cut that out','Cut that out.','别这样了；停下来。','口语里很常见，用来制止某人的行为。','Cut that out — you\'re being annoying.',NULL,NULL,'cut that out',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(997,14,55,'phrase','shoot the breeze','shoot the breeze','shoot the breeze','闲聊；吹牛聊天。','表示轻松随意地聊天，没有特别目的。','We sat on the porch and shot the breeze all afternoon.',NULL,NULL,'shoot the breeze',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(998,14,56,'phrase','at odds with','At odds with sth','at odds with','与……不一致；与……有冲突。','可用于观点、行为、规则等不一致。','Her actions are at odds with her words.',NULL,NULL,'at odds with',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(999,14,57,'phrase','put your thinking cap on','put your thinking cap on','put your thinking cap on','开动脑筋。','带一点轻松、鼓励意味的表达。','Put your thinking cap on and figure out this math problem.',NULL,NULL,'thinking cap',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1000,14,58,'phrase','what have you been up to lately','what have you been up to lately','What have you been up to lately?','你最近在忙什么？','非常自然的寒暄问法。','Hey, what have you been up to lately?',NULL,NULL,'what have you been up to lately',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1001,14,59,'phrase','turn something over in your head','turn something in one\'s head','turn something over in your head','反复琢磨某事。','比 turn something in your head 更自然。','I kept turning it over in my head all night.',NULL,NULL,'turn over in your head',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1002,14,60,'phrase','be sick and tired of','I\'m sick and tired of sb','be sick and tired of','烦透了；受够了。','语气比 just tired of 更强。','I\'m sick and tired of his excuses.',NULL,NULL,'sick and tired of',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1003,14,61,'phrase','look forward to and now that I think of it','look forward to / now that I think of it','look forward to / now that I think of it','look forward to = 期待；now that I think of it = 现在想起来。','look forward to 后面接名词或动名词。','I\'m looking forward to seeing you.\nNow that I think of it, he did mention that.',NULL,NULL,'look forward to,now that I think of it',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1004,14,62,'phrase','Do you like the way this looks','do you like the way this looks','Do you like the way this looks?','你觉得这个看起来怎么样？','买衣服、看搭配时非常自然。','Do you like the way this looks on me?',NULL,NULL,'the way this looks',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1005,14,63,'phrase','be educated at pass on settle down','to be educated / pass on / to settle down','be educated at / pass on / settle down','be educated at = 毕业于、受教育于；pass on = 递给、传下去、传递；settle down = 定居、安静下来。','都是非常常见的固定表达。','I was educated at Harvard.\nPlease pass on your resume to me.\nThey want to settle down in New Zealand.',NULL,NULL,'educated at,pass on,settle down',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1006,14,64,'phrase','brief overview and feel free','brief overview / feel free','brief overview / feel free','brief overview = 简要概述；feel free = 尽管、随时、不必拘束。','feel free to... 是非常自然的礼貌表达。','Let me give you a brief overview of what we do here.\nPlease feel free to ask any questions.',NULL,NULL,'brief overview,feel free',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1007,14,65,'phrase','narrow your eyes and narrow the income gap','narrow your eyes / narrow down income gap','narrow your eyes / narrow the income gap','narrow your eyes = 眯起眼睛；narrow the income gap = 缩小收入差距。','收入差距通常说 income gap。','He narrowed his eyes at me.\nThe government wants to narrow the income gap.',NULL,NULL,'narrow your eyes,income gap',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1008,14,66,'phrase','make it up to someone and my treat','make it up to someone / my treats','make it up to someone / my treat','make it up to someone = 补偿某人；my treat = 我请客。','my treat 是非常常见的口语。','I\'ll make it up to her by buying flowers.\nLunch is my treat.',NULL,NULL,'make it up to,my treat',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1009,14,67,'phrase','a twist of fate','a twist of fate','a twist of fate','命运的转折。','常用于小说、故事或人生经历描述。','It was a twist of fate that changed his life completely.',NULL,NULL,'a twist of fate',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1010,14,68,'phrase','take offence and fabricate','take offence / fabricate','take offence / fabricate','take offence = 被冒犯到、生气；fabricate = 捏造、编造。','take offence at something 是常见搭配。','He took offence at her comment.\nHe fabricated the whole story.',NULL,NULL,'take offence,fabricate',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1011,14,69,'phrase','deter from and put someone off','deter sb from / put sb off','deter someone from / put someone off','deter someone from = 阻止某人做；put someone off = 让某人打退堂鼓、失去兴趣。','日常英语里 put someone off 更常见、更口语。','The warnings did not deter him from trying.\nDon\'t let a few problems put you off.',NULL,NULL,'deter from,put off',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1012,14,70,'phrase','postpone break up work out get through cohabit','postpone / break up / work out / get through / cohabit','postpone / break up / work out / get through / cohabit','postpone = 推迟；break up = 分手；work out = 解决；get through = 熬过；cohabit = 同居。','work out 偏解决问题，get through 偏撑过去。','We had to postpone the meeting.\nThey broke up last year.\nWe\'ll work it out.\nYou\'ll get through this.\nThey cohabit without being married.',NULL,NULL,'postpone,break up,work out,get through,cohabit',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1013,14,71,'phrase','go down in history and formal public language','go down in history / dignitary / swear an oath / swear in / deliver / temper / tantrum','go down in history / dignitary / swear an oath / swear in / deliver a statement / temper / throw a tantrum','一组新闻、正式场合和情绪表达。','go down in history = 名留青史；swear in = 宣誓就职；throw a tantrum = 大发脾气。','That speech will go down in history.\nSeveral dignitaries attended the ceremony.\nShe swore an oath of office.\nThe judge swore him in.\nHe delivered a formal statement.\nHe has a bad temper.\nThe child threw a tantrum.',NULL,NULL,'go down in history,dignitary,swear an oath,swear in,deliver,temper,tantrum',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1014,14,72,'phrase','call off and communication phrases','call off / make some time / remote in / deem / call out / jump in / butt in / butt out / cheer up / get across','call off / make some time / remote in / deem / call out / jump in / butt in / butt out / cheer up / get across','一组关于取消、沟通、打断、安慰和表达清楚的短语。','jump in 可以是积极加入，butt in 常带不礼貌打断的意思。get across 表示把话讲清楚。','They called off the event.\nCan you make some time this week?\nCan you remote in and fix it for me?\nThe court deemed it necessary.\nHe called out the mistake.\nShe jumped in with a helpful comment.\nDon\'t butt in.\nButt out — it\'s none of your business.\nCheer up.\nI need to get my point across.',NULL,NULL,'call off,make some time,remote in,deem,call out,jump in,butt in,butt out,cheer up,get across',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1015,14,73,'phrase','travel and airport set','to-go box / get the check / drop off the vehicle / agritourism / transit flight / connecting flight / direct flight / flight attendant / baggage claim','to-go box / get the check / drop off the vehicle / agritourism / transit flight / connecting flight / direct flight / flight attendant / baggage claim','一组旅行、餐厅和机场高频表达。','都是很实用的生活英语。','Can I get a to-go box, please?\nCan I get the check, please?\nWhere should I drop off the vehicle?\nAgritourism is getting popular.\nWe booked a direct flight.\nThe connecting flight was delayed.\nThe flight attendant was helpful.\nWe met at baggage claim.',NULL,NULL,'to-go box,get the check,drop off vehicle,agritourism,transit flight,connecting flight,direct flight,flight attendant,baggage claim',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1016,14,74,'phrase','relationship and idiom set','pour your heart into / get around to / make someone\'s day / let someone down / drift apart / have it out / make up / hit it off / put up with / break a leg / spill the beans / bite the bullet / hit the jackpot / catch someone\'s eye / same boat / hit the road / blow someone off','pour your heart into / get around to / make someone\'s day / let someone down / drift apart / have it out / make up / hit it off / put up with / break a leg / spill the beans / bite the bullet / hit the jackpot / catch someone\'s eye / be in the same boat / hit the road / blow someone off','一组高频关系短语和常用习语。','这组在日常聊天、电影、口语里都很常见。','She pours her heart into her work.\nI still haven\'t got around to replying.\nThat message made my day.\nI do not want to let you down.\nWe drifted apart.\nThey had it out and cleared the air.\nThey made up.\nWe hit it off straight away.\nI can\'t put up with that.\nBreak a leg.\nSpill the beans.\nJust bite the bullet.\nThey hit the jackpot.\nHer resume caught the CEO\'s eye.\nWe\'re in the same boat.\nLet\'s hit the road.\nHe blew me off.',NULL,NULL,'pour your heart into,get around to,make someone\'s day,let down,drift apart,have it out,make up,hit it off,put up with,break a leg,spill the beans,bite the bullet,hit the jackpot,catch someone\'s eye,same boat,hit the road,blow off',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1017,14,75,'phrase','headquarters flush down the toilet burst foreign to suspect shut off','headquarters / flush down the toilet / burst / foreign to somebody / suspect / shut off','headquarters / flush something down the toilet / burst / be foreign to somebody / suspect / shut off','headquarters = 总部；flush something down the toilet = 冲进马桶；burst = 突然爆裂；be foreign to somebody = 对某人来说很陌生；suspect = 嫌疑人，也可作“怀疑”；shut off = 自动关闭、停止运作。','这一组属于日常生活和新闻里都很常见的基础表达。','The company headquarters is in Wellington.\nDo not flush that down the toilet.\nThe balloon burst.\nThat idea is foreign to me.\nThe police questioned a suspect.\nThe iron shuts off automatically.',NULL,NULL,'headquarters,flush down the toilet,burst,foreign to,suspect,shut off',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1018,14,76,'phrase','finals tuition scheduled sign up for major in figure out gory details','finals / tuition / be scheduled for / be scheduled to / sign up for / major in / figure out / gory details','finals / tuition / be scheduled for / be scheduled to / sign up for / major in / figure out / gory details','finals = 期末考试；tuition = 学费；be scheduled for = 安排在……；be scheduled to = 预定要做；sign up for = 报名参加；major in = 主修；figure out = 弄明白；gory details = 血腥细节，也可比喻让人不想听的尴尬细节。','这组主要是校园和工作场景常用表达。','I\'m studying for finals.\nTuition is expensive.\nThe event is scheduled for June.\nShe is scheduled to speak tomorrow.\nI signed up for the course.\nI major in applied computing.\nI finally figured it out.\nDo not tell me all the gory details.',NULL,NULL,'finals,tuition,scheduled for,scheduled to,sign up for,major in,figure out,gory details',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1019,14,77,'phrase','mad mad skills mad props prop against tripping let\'s bounce was like get over it my bad','mad / mad skills / mad props / prop against / tripping / let\'s bounce / was like / get over it / my bad','mad / mad skills / mad props / prop something against / tripping / let\'s bounce / someone was like / get over it / my bad','mad = 很、超，也可表示生气；mad skills = 很强的本事；mad props = 大大的尊重；prop something against = 把某物靠在……上；tripping = 发火、闹情绪；let\'s bounce = 我们走吧；someone was like = 某人当时说；get over it = 别再想了；my bad = 我的错。','这一组偏口语和俚语，适合看美剧、短视频、日常聊天时理解。','You have mad skills.\nMad props to you.\nHe propped his bike against the tree.\nHe was tripping because I got dirt on his car.\nLet\'s bounce.\nShe was like, “No way.”\nGet over it.\nMy bad.',NULL,NULL,'mad,mad skills,mad props,prop against,tripping,let\'s bounce,was like,get over it,my bad',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1020,14,78,'phrase','I\'m expecting what\'s new with you pride and joy','I\'m expecting / What\'s new with you / pride and joy','I\'m expecting / What\'s new with you? / pride and joy','I\'m expecting = 我怀孕了；What\'s new with you? = 你最近怎么样；pride and joy = 某人的骄傲和宝贝。','这一组都是日常生活里很常见的自然表达。','She\'s expecting her first baby.\nWhat\'s new with you?\nThat old car is his pride and joy.',NULL,NULL,'I\'m expecting,what\'s new with you,pride and joy',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1021,14,79,'phrase','food words appetizer appetite runny overseasoned season with inedible portion rubbery make a big deal','appetizer / appetite / runny / overseasoned / season with / inedible / portion / rubbery / make a big deal','appetizer / appetite / runny / overseasoned / season with / inedible / portion / rubbery / make a big deal','appetizer = 开胃菜；appetite = 食欲；runny = 太稀的；overseasoned = 调味过重的；season with = 用……调味；inedible = 难以下咽的；portion = 一份；rubbery = 像橡胶一样难嚼；make a big deal = 小题大做。','这一组主要是食物口感和餐桌语境。','We ordered an appetizer.\nI do not have much appetite today.\nThe soup is too runny.\nThe dish is overseasoned.\nSeason the chicken with pepper.\nThe meat was inedible.\nDo you have a children\'s portion?\nThe squid was rubbery.\nDo not make a big deal out of it.',NULL,NULL,'appetizer,appetite,runny,overseasoned,season with,inedible,portion,rubbery,make a big deal',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1022,14,80,'phrase','steering wheel what are you up to electrical vs electronic','steering wheel / what are you up to / electrical vs electronic','steering wheel / What are you up to? / electrical vs electronic','steering wheel = 方向盘；What are you up to? = 你在干嘛；electrical = 与电力、电气系统相关；electronic = 与电子元件、信息处理相关。','electrical 更偏电本身和大功率系统，electronic 更偏设备、信号、控制和数字化。','He grabbed the steering wheel.\nWhat are you up to?\nElectrical appliances use power, while electronic devices process signals.',NULL,NULL,'steering wheel,what are you up to,electrical,electronic',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1023,14,81,'phrase','have a good day replies and sort of tired','have a good day replies / I\'m sort of tired','Thanks, you too. / You too. / Cheers, you too. / I\'m sort of tired.','have a good day 的常见回复有 Thanks, you too. / You too. / Cheers, you too.；I\'m sort of tired = 我有点累。','这些都很自然，尤其适合新西兰日常交流。','Have a good day. — Thanks, you too.\nI\'m sort of tired today.',NULL,NULL,'have a good day,you too,cheers,I\'m sort of tired',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1024,14,82,'phrase','multi-million-dollar mansion pantry gorgeous ridiculous dual vanity ceramic tile','multi-million-dollar mansion / pantry / gorgeous / ridiculous / dual vanity / ceramic tile','multi-million-dollar mansion / pantry / gorgeous / ridiculous / dual vanity / ceramic tile','multi-million-dollar mansion = 价值数百万的豪宅；pantry = 食品储藏间；gorgeous = 非常漂亮；ridiculous = 离谱、夸张；dual vanity = 双洗手台；ceramic tile = 陶瓷砖。','这一组常见于看房视频、生活方式内容和房屋介绍。','This is a multi-million-dollar mansion in New Zealand.\nJust put it in the pantry.\nWhat a gorgeous view.\nThe rent is ridiculous.\nThe bathroom has a dual vanity and ceramic tiles.',NULL,NULL,'multi-million-dollar mansion,pantry,gorgeous,ridiculous,dual vanity,ceramic tile',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1025,14,83,'phrase','get something sorted what are you on about keen rip someone off','get those computers sorted / what are you on about / keen to figure it out / rip someone off','get something sorted / What are you on about? / be keen to figure it out / rip someone off','get something sorted = 把某事处理好；What are you on about? = 你在说什么啊；be keen to figure it out = 很想弄明白；rip someone off = 宰某人、坑某人。','这一组很有英式 / 新西兰口语感。','Let\'s get those computers sorted.\nWhat are you on about?\nI\'m really keen to figure it out.\nThat shop ripped me off.',NULL,NULL,'get sorted,on about,keen,rip someone off',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1026,14,84,'phrase','get dressed exact same knocked out shopping again','put on your clothes vs get dressed / exact same / knocked out / shopping again','get dressed / the exact same / get knocked out / You\'ve been shopping again.','get dressed = 穿戴整齐；the exact same = 一模一样的；get knocked out = 被打晕；You\'ve been shopping again. = 你又买东西了。','put on your clothes 更偏动作本身，get dressed 更适合“穿好准备出门”的语境。','Go and get dressed.\nThe exact same candy is half the price at the supermarket.\nHe got knocked out.\nYou\'ve been shopping again.',NULL,NULL,'get dressed,exact same,knocked out,shopping again',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1027,14,85,'phrase','part-time job application and waiting','part-time job application conversation','part-time job application / wait and stay patient / hold on to applications / work through them','一组关于兼职申请、等待回复、招聘流程的实用表达。','适合超市、零售、仓储和服务业求职场景。','I filled in the form, but I didn\'t get any response.\nThis is definitely the right way to apply, right?\nCan I have a chance to interview with someone here?\nThe interview process happens when you get approved.\nShe\'s probably holding on to all the applications and working through them.\nWait and stay patient.',NULL,NULL,'part-time job,apply,response,interview,wait and stay patient,hold on to applications,work through them',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1028,14,86,'phrase','kill a glass of wine and stress patterns','she would kill a glass of wine and an afternoon off / word stress patterns','kill a glass of wine / two-syllable and three-syllable stress patterns','kill a glass of wine = 很快喝完一杯酒；以及双音节、三音节单词重音规律总结。','kill 在这里是夸张口语，表示“迅速喝完”。后面是发音规则：双音节名词和形容词常重读第一音节，双音节动词常重读第二音节；-ion, -ic, -ity 等后缀前通常重读前一音节。','She would kill a glass of wine and enjoy an afternoon off.\nTAble, HAppy, reLAX, aMONG, edUCAtion, geoGRAPHic, reSponSIBility.',NULL,NULL,'kill a glass of wine,stress patterns,two-syllable,three-syllable,education,geographic,responsibility',0,0,1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31',1,'2026-04-05 15:40:31'),(1031,2,119,'phrase','Negative impact of technology','Negative impact of technology','Negative impact of technology','科技带来的负面影响\r\n也可以理解成：\r\n	•	技术的不良影响\r\n	•	科技对人类 / 社会 / 生活的负面作用','1. negative\r\n意思是：\r\n	•	负面的 不好的  消极的\r\n常见搭配：\r\n	•	negative effect 负面影响\r\n	•	negative influence 不良影响\r\n	•	negative attitude 消极态度\r\n2. impact\r\n这里是名词，意思是：\r\n	•	影响  冲击\r\n所以：\r\n	•	have an impact on 对……产生影响\r\n	•	a positive impact 正面影响\r\n	•	a negative impact 负面影响','1. impact 的常见搭配\r\n	•	have an impact on sth\r\n	•	make an impact on sth\r\n	•	the impact of sth on sb/sth：\r\n\r\n	•	Technology has a huge impact on our daily lives.\r\n	•	Social media has a negative impact on teenagers.',NULL,NULL,'',0,0,1,'2026-04-06 16:14:51',1,'2026-04-06 16:14:51'),(1032,15,1,'phrase','piles of','piles of','piles of','基本意思\r\n1. 表示数量很多，和这些很像：\r\n	•	a lot of\r\n	•	lots of\r\n	•	plenty of\r\n所以：\r\n	•	piles of books = 一大堆书\r\n	•	piles of work = 一大堆工作\r\n	•	piles of money = 很多钱\r\n	•	I’ve got piles of homework to do.\r\n我有一大堆作业要做。\r\n	•	There were piles of clothes on the bed.\r\n床上有一大堆衣服。\r\n	•	She has piles of experience in customer service.\r\n她在客户服务方面有很多经验。','','',NULL,NULL,'',0,0,1,'2026-04-06 16:30:00',1,'2026-04-06 16:30:00'),(1033,15,2,'phrase','referred to','referred to','referred to','1. 被称为 / 被叫作\r\n	•	He is often referred to as a genius.\r\n他经常被称为天才。\r\n这里常见结构是：\r\n	•	refer to A as B\r\n把 A 称为 B\r\n2. 提到 / 说到\r\n	•	She referred to your idea in the meeting.\r\n她在会议中提到了你的想法。\r\n这里 refer to = mention\r\n3. 指的是\r\n	•	When I said “manager”, I was referring to Tom.\r\n我说“经理”的时候，指的是 Tom。\r\n4. 查阅 / 参考\r\n	•	Please refer to the manual for details.\r\n详情请参阅说明书。\r\n5. 转交 / 转诊 / 送交处理\r\n	•	The patient was referred to a specialist.\r\n这位病人被转诊给专科医生。\r\n	•	The case was referred to the manager.\r\n这件事被交给经理处理。','referred 是什么形式\r\n它是 refer 的过去式 / 过去分词：\r\n	•	refer\r\n	•	referred\r\n	•	referring\r\n注意拼写：\r\nrefer → referred → referring\r\n因为重读在后面，所以双写 r','常见搭配\r\n	•	refer to\r\n	•	refer to A as B\r\n	•	be referred to as\r\n	•	refer to the manual\r\n	•	be referred to a specialist',NULL,NULL,'',0,0,1,'2026-04-06 16:40:49',1,'2026-04-06 16:40:49'),(1034,15,3,'vocab','GPS','GPS','GPS =  Global Positioning System','Global Positioning System的缩写','','',NULL,NULL,'',0,0,1,'2026-04-06 16:43:45',1,'2026-04-06 16:43:45'),(1035,15,4,'vocab','shady','shady','shady','1. 阴凉的\r\n指有树荫、没有太阳直晒的地方。\r\n• Let’s sit in a shady spot.\r\n我们坐到阴凉的地方吧。\r\n2. 可疑的，不太正当的\r\n• He looks a bit shady. 他看起来有点可疑。\r\n• That deal sounds shady. 那笔交易听起来不太靠谱。\r\n3. 不太光明正大 / 有问题\r\n• Some shady business 一些见不得光的生意\r\n• shady people 可疑的人','shady 是形容词。\r\n常见搭配\r\n• a shady place 阴凉的地方\r\n• a shady guy 可疑的人\r\n• a shady deal 可疑的交易\r\n• shady business 不正当的生意\r\n近义感觉\r\n如果表示“可疑”：\r\n• suspicious 更正式，强调“让人怀疑”\r\n• shady 更口语，带“有点不正经、不干净”的感觉','',NULL,NULL,'',0,0,1,'2026-04-07 11:20:00',1,'2026-04-07 11:20:00'),(1036,15,5,'phrase','feel compelled to do sth','feel compelled to do sth','feel compelled to do sth','感到不得不做某事','compel 是一个正式一点的动词，意思是：\r\n1. 迫使，强迫\r\n让某人不得不做某事。\r\n•	Nothing could compel him to change his mind. 没有什么能迫使他改变主意。\r\n•	The law compels employers to provide a safe workplace. 法律要求雇主提供安全的工作环境。\r\ncompel someone to do something\r\n\r\n2. 使不得不，使必须\r\n\r\n不是“拿枪逼着”，也可以是因为情况、现实、压力而不得不。\r\n•	Financial problems compelled her to leave school. 经济问题迫使她辍学。\r\n3. 强烈吸引，令人折服\r\n\r\n这个意思较少见，但也常用在写作里，表示“有很强的说服力或吸引力”。\r\n•	She gave a compelling argument. 她提出了一个很有说服力的论点。\r\n注意这里常见的是形容词 compelling。','常见搭配\r\n	•	compel sb to do sth\r\n	•	feel compelled to do sth = 感到不得不做某事\r\n	•	a compelling reason 充分的理由\r\n	•	a compelling story/argument 很有吸引力或说服力的故事/论点\r\n和 force 的区别\r\n	•	force 更直接、更强硬，偏“强迫”\r\n	•	compel 更正式，既可以是真强迫，也可以是“形势所迫”\r\n一句总结\r\ncompel = force in a formal way / make someone feel they must do something',NULL,NULL,'',0,0,1,'2026-04-07 11:25:15',1,'2026-04-07 11:25:15'),(1037,15,6,'vocab','extraordinary','extraordinary','extraordinary','1. 非凡的，了不起的\r\n\r\n指比一般情况强很多、特别突出。\r\n	•	She has an extraordinary talent for music.\r\n她有非凡的音乐天赋。\r\n	•	He achieved extraordinary success at a young age.\r\n他年纪轻轻就取得了非凡的成功。\r\n2. 非常特别的，不寻常的\r\n\r\n指不普通、不同寻常。\r\n	•	It was an extraordinary experience.\r\n那是一次非常特别的经历。\r\n	•	Nothing extraordinary happened today.\r\n今天没发生什么特别的事。','构词\r\n	•	extra- = 超出\r\n	•	ordinary = 普通的\r\n\r\n所以字面上就是：超出普通的\r\n常见搭配\r\n	•	extraordinary talent 非凡的天赋\r\n	•	extraordinary ability 非凡的能力\r\n	•	extraordinary success 非凡的成功\r\n	•	extraordinary experience 非同寻常的经历\r\n	•	something extraordinary 不寻常的事','•	She showed extraordinary courage in a difficult situation.\r\n她在困难情况下表现出了非凡的勇气。\r\n	•	This is not an ordinary event. It’s something extraordinary.\r\n这不是一件普通的事，而是一件非同寻常的事。',NULL,NULL,'extraordinary = very unusual or much better than normal',0,0,1,'2026-04-07 18:24:12',1,'2026-04-07 18:24:12'),(1038,15,7,'vocab','wrestle','wrestle','wrestle','1. 摔跤，扭打\r\n指两个人抱在一起较劲、摔跤。\r\n	•	The two boys were wrestling on the floor.\r\n两个男孩在地上扭打。\r\n\r\n也可以指体育项目里的“摔跤”。\r\n	•	He used to wrestle in high school.\r\n他高中时练过摔跤。\r\n2. 努力对付，奋力解决\r\n\r\n这个意思也很常见，尤其在书面或正式表达里。\r\n	•	She is wrestling with a difficult decision.\r\n她正在努力应对一个艰难的决定。\r\n	•	The company is wrestling with rising costs.\r\n这家公司正努力应对不断上涨的成本。\r\n\r\n这里的感觉是：\r\n很费劲地处理一个问题','词性\r\n\r\nwrestle 可以作动词。\r\n\r\n常见搭配\r\n	•	wrestle with sb 和某人摔跤\r\n	•	wrestle with a problem 努力解决问题\r\n	•	wrestle with a decision 苦苦思考一个决定','一句总结\r\n\r\nwrestle\r\n	•	字面：摔跤，扭打\r\n	•	引申：努力应付，费力解决\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n	•	wrestle with someone 跟某人摔跤\r\n	•	wrestle with an issue 跟一个问题较劲 / 努力处理一个问题',NULL,NULL,'',0,0,1,'2026-04-07 18:47:50',1,'2026-04-07 18:47:50'),(1039,15,8,'vocab','evolve','evolve','evolve','1. 逐渐发展，演变\r\n\r\n这是最常见的意思。\r\n	•	Language evolves over time.\r\n语言会随着时间而演变。\r\n	•	The company has evolved into a global business.\r\n这家公司已经发展成一家全球化企业。\r\n\r\n这里强调的是：\r\n慢慢变化，逐步发展\r\n2. 进化\r\n\r\n在生物学里也常用。\r\n	•	Humans evolved over millions of years.\r\n人类经过数百万年进化而来。','词性\r\nevolve = 动词\r\n\r\n常见搭配\r\n	•	evolve over time 随着时间演变\r\n	•	evolve into 发展成 / 演变成\r\n	•	evolve from 从……演变而来','•	My thinking has evolved a lot in recent years.\r\n这些年我的想法变化了很多。\r\n	•	The simple idea evolved into a successful product.\r\n这个简单的想法逐渐发展成了一个成功的产品。\r\n	•	Technology continues to evolve.\r\n技术在不断发展。',NULL,NULL,'•	evolution 名词，进化；发展；演变 	•	evolutionary 形容词，进化的；演变的',0,0,1,'2026-04-07 18:54:41',1,'2026-04-07 18:54:41'),(1040,15,9,'vocab','bonus','bonus','bonus','1. 奖金（最常见）\r\n\r\n公司给员工的额外收入。\r\n•	We get a bonus at the end of the year. 我们年底会拿到奖金。\r\n•	He received a performance bonus. 他拿到了绩效奖金。\r\n\r\n2. 额外的好处 / 意外收获\r\n\r\n不一定是钱，也可以是“加分项”。\r\n•	Free food is a nice bonus. 免费食物是个不错的额外福利。\r\n•	Living close to work is a bonus. 住得离公司近是个加分项。','常见搭配\r\n	•	year-end bonus 年终奖\r\n	•	performance bonus 绩效奖金\r\n	•	cash bonus 现金奖励\r\n	•	a nice bonus 一个不错的额外好处\r\n	•	as a bonus 作为额外奖励','•	They offered me a bonus to join the company.  他们给我一笔奖金让我加入公司。\r\n•	The flexible working hours are an added bonus. 弹性工作时间是额外的福利。',NULL,NULL,'bonus = something extra, especially money or a benefit',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 06:51:22',1,'2026-04-08 06:51:22'),(1041,15,10,'phrase','fall in love at first sight','fall in love at first sight / love at first sight','fall in love at first sight / love at first sight','一见钟情','•	love at first sight = 名词短语，表示“一见钟情”这个概念\r\n•	fall in love at first sight = 动作表达，“一见钟情了”','常见用法\r\n•	It was love at first sight. 那是一见钟情。\r\n•	Do you believe in love at first sight?  你相信一见钟情吗？\r\n•	He fell in love with her at first sight.  他对她一见钟情。',NULL,NULL,'',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 07:07:05',1,'2026-04-08 07:07:05'),(1042,15,11,'phrase','sci-fi','sci-fi','sci-fi','👉 科幻（science fiction 的缩写）','1. 作名词\r\n\r\n表示“科幻类型”\r\n•	I love sci-fi. 我喜欢科幻。\r\n•	This book is sci-fi. 这本书是科幻的。\r\n\r\n2. 作形容词\r\n\r\n修饰电影、书等\r\n•	a sci-fi movie 科幻电影\r\n•	a sci-fi novel 科幻小说','常见搭配\r\n•	sci-fi movie / film 科幻电影\r\n•	sci-fi series 科幻剧\r\n•	sci-fi novel 科幻小说\r\n•	sci-fi world 科幻世界',NULL,NULL,'',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 07:36:21',1,'2026-04-08 07:36:21'),(1043,15,12,'phrase','filthy rich','filthy rich','filthy rich','filthy rich = extremely rich\r\n👉 特别有钱 / 巨有钱 / 富得流油\r\n这个词组有点夸张，也比较口语化。\r\n•	rich = 有钱\r\n•	filthy rich = 非常非常有钱\r\n\r\n这里 filthy 不是“脏”的本意，而是起强调作用。','语气特点\r\n\r\n这个表达：\r\n	•	很口语\r\n	•	有点夸张\r\n	•	有时带一点羡慕、调侃，甚至一点酸\r\n\r\n所以正式场合一般不用。\r\n如果你想说得更正式一点，可以用：\r\n•	very wealthy\r\n•	extremely rich\r\n•	financially successful\r\n•	well-off（这个比 filthy rich 弱很多）','•	He’s filthy rich. 他超级有钱。\r\n•	They got filthy rich from real estate. 他们靠房地产赚得盆满钵满。\r\n•	You don’t have to be filthy rich to enjoy life. 你不需要特别有钱也能享受生活。',NULL,NULL,'',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 08:11:20',1,'2026-04-08 08:11:20'),(1044,15,13,'phrase','expand my horizons','expand my horizons','expand my horizons','👉 开阔我的眼界 / 拓宽我的视野','• expand = 扩大，拓展\r\n• horizons = 眼界，视野（不是字面“地平线”）\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nexpand my horizons = 让我看到更多、了解更多、接触更广的世界','🗣 常见用法\r\n• Travel helps me expand my horizons. 旅行能开阔我的眼界。\r\n• Studying abroad really expanded my horizons. 出国留学真的开阔了我的眼界。\r\n• I want to expand my horizons by learning new skills. 我想通过学习新技能来拓宽自己的视野。\r\n\r\n面试场景\r\n• I enjoy meeting people from different backgrounds because it helps expand my horizons.\r\n• Working in a different industry would help me expand my horizons.',NULL,NULL,'expand my horizons = 开阔眼界 / 拓宽视野',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 08:37:18',1,'2026-04-08 08:37:18'),(1045,15,14,'vocab','binoculars','binoculars','binoculars','👉 双筒望远镜','这个词通常用 复数形式：\r\n• a pair of binoculars\r\n一副双筒望远镜','类似词\r\n这类词和 glasses / scissors 很像，常用复数：\r\n• glasses 眼镜\r\n• scissors 剪刀\r\n• binoculars 双筒望远镜',NULL,NULL,'',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 14:39:28',1,'2026-04-08 14:39:28'),(1046,15,15,'phrase','lost value','lost value','lost value','👉 贬值 / 价值下降','🧠 用法\r\n可以用于：\r\n•钱  / 房子 / 车 / 商品 / 股票 / 游戏皮肤 / 某个东西的市场价值\r\n常见搭配\r\n• lose a lot of value 大幅贬值\r\n• lose value over time 随着时间贬值\r\n• begin to lose value 开始贬值','🌟 例句\r\n•The car lost value quickly. 这辆车很快就贬值了。\r\n• These skins have lost a lot of value. 这些皮肤贬值了很多。\r\n• Houses in that area are losing value. 那个地区的房子在贬值。',NULL,NULL,'',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 14:48:32',1,'2026-04-08 14:48:32'),(1047,15,16,'phrase','It was a big market','It was a big market','It was a big market','那是一个很大的市场。','1. 字面意思：很大的市场 / 集市\r\n比如菜市场、夜市、商场那种场所。\r\n•It was a big market with lots of people and shops.\r\n那是一个很大的市场，里面有很多人和店铺。\r\n\r\n2. 引申意思：很大的市场需求 / 很大的行业规模\r\n\r\n在商业语境里更常见。\r\n• At that time, it was a big market for online games.  那时候，网络游戏是一个很大的市场。','如果你想说“市场规模很大”\r\n\r\n更自然的说法有：\r\n• It was a huge market.\r\n• It was a large market.\r\n• There was a big market for it.\r\n它当时很有市场。',NULL,NULL,'',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 14:54:52',1,'2026-04-08 14:54:52'),(1048,15,17,'phrase','two bucks less','two bucks less','two bucks less','👉 少两块钱 / 便宜两美元（或两纽币等口语里的“块”）','解释\r\n• bucks = 口语里的“块钱”\r\n• two less = 少两个','例子\r\n• This one is two bucks less. 这个便宜两块。\r\n• I paid two bucks less than he did.  我比他少花了两块。\r\n比 two less bucks 更自然的是：\r\n• two bucks less\r\n• two dollars less','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 17:53:40',1,'2026-04-08 17:53:40'),(1049,15,18,'phrase','ring (something) up','ring (something) up','ring (something) up','✅ 核心意思\r\n\r\nring (something) up = 把商品录入收银系统 / 扫码结账\r\n\r\n👉 也就是你在收银台做的动作','🧠 为什么用 ring？\r\n来自过去的老式收银机（cash register）👇\r\n以前按键时会发出 “叮 (ring)” 的声音，所以就有了：\r\n👉 ring up = 记账 / 结账','✅ 常见用法\r\n• I’ll ring this up for you. 我帮你结账。\r\n• She rang up the items quickly. 她很快把商品录入了系统。\r\n• I forgot to ring it up. 我忘记算进去了\r\n\r\n🇳🇿 小补充（新西兰）\r\n\r\n在新西兰/英国也常说：\r\n• scan（更直观）\r\n• put it through the till\r\n\r\n👉 例如：\r\n	•	I forgot to scan this.\r\n	•	I didn’t put this through the till.','/static/uploads/english_note_item/5305ea44bcc845f4832421f3e2a184d2.jpg','老式的收音机','',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 18:08:15',1,'2026-04-08 18:08:15'),(1050,15,19,'vocab','Virus & bacteria','Virus & bacteria','Virus & bacteria','virus 👉 病毒\r\n• infection 👉 感染\r\n• disease 👉 疾病\r\n• illness 👉 生病（更口语）\r\n• germ 👉 细菌/病菌（泛指）','• bacteria 👉 细菌\r\n• pathogen 👉 病原体（更专业）\r\n• antibody 👉 抗体\r\n• immune system 👉 免疫系统\r\n• mutation 👉 变异\r\n• variant 👉 变种（疫情中很常见）\r\n\r\n🤧 3️⃣ 症状（超级实用）\r\n• fever 👉 发烧\r\n• cough 👉 咳嗽\r\n• sore throat 👉 喉咙痛\r\n• runny nose 👉 流鼻涕\r\n• fatigue 👉 疲劳\r\n• headache 👉 头痛','🗣️ 6️⃣ 实用句子\r\n• I think I might have a viral infection. 我可能感染病毒了\r\n• There’s a virus going around. 最近有病毒在传播\r\n• He has a high fever and a cough. 他发高烧还咳嗽\r\n• Have you been vaccinated? 你打疫苗了吗？','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 08:10:18',1,'2026-04-10 08:10:18'),(1051,15,20,'phrase','literal VS literally','literal VS literally','literal VS literally','✅ 1️⃣ literal（形容词）\r\n👉 字面上的 / 按原意的（不是比喻）\r\n🔊 发音 /ˈlɪtərəl/\r\n👉 用来描述“是真的，不是夸张或比喻”\r\n\r\n✅ 2️⃣ literally（副词）\r\n👉 字面地 / 真正地 /（口语里）强调\r\n🔊 发音 /ˈlɪtərəli/','literal\r\n✅ 例子\r\n• This is the literal meaning of the word.  👉 这是这个词的字面意思\r\n• Don’t take it literally.（常见搭配）👉 不要按字面理解\r\n\r\nliterally\r\n🟢 用法1：真正的（严格意义）\r\n👉 表示 100%真实\r\n• I literally saw him fall. 👉 我真的亲眼看到他摔倒\r\n• He literally ran 10 kilometers. 👉 他真的跑了10公里\r\n\r\n🟡 用法2：口语强调（⚠️很常见）\r\n👉 其实是“夸张用法”\r\n•I was literally dying of laughter.  👉 我笑死了（不是真的死 😂）\r\n•It was literally freezing. 👉 冷死了','在新西兰/日常英语里：\r\n👉 literally = 很常当“强调词”\r\n相当于：\r\n• really\r\n• super\r\n• so\r\n⭐ 常见口语\r\n• I literally have no idea.\r\n• It literally took forever.','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 08:25:06',1,'2026-04-10 08:25:06'),(1052,15,21,'phrase','have your eye on 👀','have your eye on 👀','have your eye on 👀','看上了 / 对…很感兴趣 / 想要某个东西','🧠 核心用法\r\n👉 表示你已经注意到某样东西，并且有点想要它','✅ 例句（很实用）\r\n• I’ve had my eye on that TV for a while. 👉 我已经看上那台电视很久了\r\n• She has her eye on a new car. 👉 她看上了一辆新车\r\n• I’ve got my eye on those shoes. 👉 我看中了那双鞋\r\n• What is something expensive that you have your eye on? 你看上了一些贵的什么东西了吗？\r\n\r\n🇳🇿 Kiwi / 日常口语\r\n👉 很常用，特别是买东西时：\r\n• I’ve got my eye on that one.  👉 我看中那个了','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 08:46:17',1,'2026-04-10 08:46:17'),(1053,15,22,'phrase','Renovate','Renovate','Renovate   /ˈrenəveɪt/','翻新 / 装修（旧房子或空间）','• renovate a house  👉 翻新房子\r\n• renovate the kitchen 👉 装修厨房\r\n• renovate an old building 👉 翻新老建筑','🗣️ 例句\r\n• We’re renovating our house.  👉 我们正在装修房子\r\n• They renovated the apartment last year.  👉 他们去年翻新了那套公寓\r\n\r\n🇳🇿 Kiwi / 日常说法\r\n\r\n👉 很常听到：\r\n• We’re doing some renos.  👉 我们在搞点装修（超级口语🔥）','/static/uploads/english_note_item/84be5e81950b49e388c67c2d01d757c1.jpg','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 14:01:25',1,'2026-04-10 14:01:25'),(1054,15,23,'phrase','It\'s','It\'s','It\'s = it has / it is','it has 和 it is 都可以简写成 it\'s','','','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 14:10:01',1,'2026-04-10 14:10:01'),(1055,15,24,'vocab','neighborhood / neighbourhood','neighborhood / neighbourhood','neighborhood / neighbourhood','社区 / 街区 / 居住区域\r\n🇺🇸 vs 🇬🇧 / 🇳🇿 拼写\r\n• neighborhood（美式 🇺🇸）\r\n• neighbourhood（英式 🇬🇧 / 新西兰 🇳🇿 更常用⭐）','1️⃣ 居住区域\r\n\r\n👉 你家附近那一片地方\r\n• I live in a quiet neighbourhood. 👉 我住在一个安静的社区\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 附近一带（更广一点）\r\n• There are lots of cafes in the neighbourhood. 👉 这一带有很多咖啡店\r\n\r\n🗣️ 常见搭配（很实用）\r\n• friendly neighbourhood 👉 友好的社区\r\n• safe neighbourhood 👉 安全的社区\r\n• local neighbourhood 👉 本地社区\r\n• in the neighbourhood 👉 在附近','• Do you know this neighbourhood?  👉 你熟悉这一带吗？\r\n• It’s a nice neighbourhood to live in.  👉 这是个很适合居住的地方','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 14:17:03',1,'2026-04-10 14:17:03'),(1056,15,25,'vocab','neighbor / neighbour','neighbor / neighbour','neighbor / neighbour','邻居','🔁 常见搭配\r\n• next-door neighbour  👉 隔壁邻居\r\n• upstairs/downstairs neighbour  👉 楼上 / 楼下邻居\r\n• neighbourhood 👉 社区','🗣️ 例句\r\n• My neighbour is very friendly. 👉 我的邻居很友好\r\n• We just met our new neighbours. 👉 我们刚认识了新邻居\r\n• Our neighbours are a bit noisy. 😅 👉 我们邻居有点吵\r\n\r\n🇳🇿 常见口语\r\n• We’re pretty close with our neighbours. 👉 我们和邻居关系很好\r\n• Have you met the neighbours yet? 👉 你见过邻居了吗？','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 14:20:22',1,'2026-04-10 14:20:22'),(1057,15,26,'phrase','stick to','stick to','stick to','坚持 / 遵守 / 不改变\r\nstick to = 坚持 + 不改变','1️⃣ 坚持做某事（最重要⭐）\r\n\r\n👉 不放弃\r\n• I need to stick to my plan. 👉 我要坚持我的计划\r\n• Stick to your goals. 👉 坚持你的目标\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 遵守规则 / 限制\r\n\r\n👉 按规定来\r\n• Please stick to the rules. 👉 请遵守规则\r\n• Stick to the schedule. 👉 按时间表来\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 只做某件事（不偏离）\r\n\r\n👉 不跑题 / 不改变\r\n• Let’s stick to the topic. 👉 我们别跑题\r\n• I’ll stick to English. 👉 我就用英语\r\n\r\n🗣️ 常见搭配\r\n• stick to a plan\r\n• stick to a diet 🍎\r\n• stick to a budget 💰\r\n• stick to the point','It is so hard to stick to a workout routine.  👉坚持日常锻炼太难了','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 14:33:36',1,'2026-04-10 14:33:36'),(1058,15,27,'phrase','tricky thing','tricky thing','tricky thing','👉 意思：棘手的事情 / 有点难处理的问题 / 不太容易搞定的事','👉 不是特别难，但有点麻烦、容易出错、需要技巧','• That’s a tricky thing to deal with. 👉 这事挺难处理的\r\n• The tricky thing is finding the right balance. ⭐  👉 难点在于找到合适的平衡\r\n• It’s a tricky thing to explain. 👉 这个不太好解释','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 14:47:09',1,'2026-04-10 14:47:09'),(1059,15,28,'vocab','Passion','Passion','Passion','热情 / 激情 / 强烈的兴趣或爱','1️⃣ 对某事的热爱\r\n• I have a passion for music.  👉 我非常热爱音乐\r\n• She’s passionate about teaching. 👉 她对教学很有热情\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 强烈情感（更偏情绪）\r\n• He spoke with passion. 👉 他说话很有激情\r\n\r\n🗣️ 高频搭配（很重要⭐）\r\n• have a passion for… 👉 对……充满热情\r\n• be passionate about… 👉 热爱……\r\n• follow your passion 👉 追随热爱','🇳🇿 日常口语\r\n• I’m really passionate about fitness. 👉 我真的很热爱健身','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 14:50:40',1,'2026-04-10 14:50:40'),(1060,15,29,'phrase','burn out / burnout','burn out / burnout','burn out / burnout','👉 burn out（动词）：过度劳累导致精疲力尽\r\n👉 burnout（名词）：职业倦怠 / 身心耗尽的状态','1️⃣ 动词（最常用）\r\n• I’m starting to burn out. 👉 我开始有点撑不住了 / 精疲力尽了\r\n• He burned out after working long hours. 👉 他长时间工作后彻底累垮了\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 名词\r\n• I’m dealing with burnout. 👉 我在经历职业倦怠\r\n• Burnout is common in stressful jobs. 👉 高压工作很容易倦怠','•I think I’m getting burnt out at work.\r\n👉 我感觉工作快把我搞崩了\r\n\r\n🗣️ 类似表达\r\n• I’m exhausted. 👉 我累坏了\r\n• I’m drained. 👉 我被耗干了\r\n• I’m overwhelmed. 👉 我压力很大','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 15:47:34',1,'2026-04-10 15:47:34'),(1061,15,30,'vocab','defect / flaw / imperfection','defect / flaw / imperfection','defect / flaw / imperfection','瑕疵','🧠 不同场景对应不同词（很重要⭐）\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 产品 / 物品上的小问题\r\n👉 defect / flaw\r\n• There’s a small defect in the product. 👉 产品有一点瑕疵\r\n• It has a minor flaw. 👉 有个小瑕疵\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 外观上的小瑕疵（比如皮肤）\r\n👉 imperfection ⭐（更自然）\r\n• No one is perfect — we all have imperfections. 👉 每个人都有小瑕疵\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 性格 / 抽象问题\r\n👉 flaw\r\n• That’s his biggest flaw.  👉 那是他最大的缺点','🗣️ 口语推荐（你优先用这个）\r\n👉 imperfection（最温和、最自然）','/static/uploads/english_note_item/1c1ae951d76e406fa4477c76ec27e8a1.jpg','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 17:52:50',1,'2026-04-10 17:57:22'),(1062,15,31,'phrase','that would fit down there as well','that would fit down there as well','that would fit down there as well','那个放在那边也刚好合适','• that 👉 那个（某个物品）\r\n• would fit 👉 会刚好放得下 / 合适\r\n• down there 👉 那下面 / 那边（比较口语）','🗣️ 类似表达（英文）\r\n• It would fit there as well. 👉 放在那里也可以\r\n• That would fit perfectly down there.  👉 放在下面刚刚好\r\n• We could put that down there.  👉 我们可以把那个放下面','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 15:41:57',1,'2026-04-11 15:41:57'),(1063,15,32,'phrase','stop banging against/into each other','stop banging against/into each other','stop banging against/into each other','👉 防止它们互相碰撞\r\n👉 避免它们彼此撞来撞去','It would certainly be perfect for stopping them from banging against each other.  👉这肯定很适合防止它们互相碰撞\r\n\r\n最推荐：\r\n\r\n👉 It would be perfect for stopping them from banging into each other.\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n这很适合防止它们互相碰撞。','💬 例子：\r\n• This foam would be perfect for stopping the dishes from banging into each other.\r\n这个泡沫垫很适合防止这些盘子互相碰撞。\r\n• That should help stop the bottles from knocking against each other.\r\n那样应该能防止瓶子互相磕碰。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-12 13:32:52',1,'2026-04-12 13:32:52'),(1064,15,33,'phrase','We were right about that','We were right about that','We were right about that','🧠 We were right about that 的核心意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 我们刚才对这件事的判断是对的。\r\n👉 我们之前猜得没错。\r\n👉 果然和我们想的一样。','✅ 常见语境\r\n1. 猜测某件事，后来证实了\r\n• 这个东西坏了\r\n• 那个人今天不会来\r\n• 这个价格会更贵\r\n• 这家店快关门了\r\n\r\n后来发现真的是这样，就可以说：\r\n\r\n👉 We were right about that.\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• Looks like the clock really doesn’t work. We were right about that. 看来这个钟果然坏了，我们刚才猜对了。\r\n• He didn’t show up in the end. We were right about that.  他最后果然没来，我们猜对了。\r\n\r\n2. 提前判断一个商品有问题\r\n• There really is a crack on the back. We were right about that.  背后果然有一道裂缝，我们刚才看得没错。\r\n• It is missing a part. We were right about that. 它确实少了一个零件，我们刚才判断对了。\r\n\r\n3. 对价格、折扣、规则的猜测\r\n• It was actually on sale. We were right about that. 它果然在打折，我们猜对了。\r\n• They do close early on Sundays. We were right about that. 他们星期天果然早关门，我们猜对了。\r\n\r\n4. 对某人的想法或反应的判断\r\n• She was upset about it. We were right about that. 她确实为那件事不高兴，我们猜得没错。\r\n• He didn’t like the idea. We were right about that. 他果然不喜欢那个主意，我们判断对了。','📌 这个句子通常需要一个“前情”\r\n\r\n也就是说，不能凭空说。\r\n它一般要先有一个“之前我们这么想”，然后后来验证了。\r\n\r\n典型结构：\r\n1. 我们先猜 / 判断\r\n2. 后来事实出来了\r\n3. 然后说：We were right about that.','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-12 14:33:19',1,'2026-04-12 14:33:19'),(1065,15,34,'phrase','put it in place','put it in place','put it in place','🧠 put it in place 的意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 把它放到合适的位置\r\n👉 把它放好\r\n👉 把它安放到位','✅ 这个短语什么时候能用\r\n\r\n它通常表示：\r\n• 把某个东西放到应该放的位置\r\n• 把某个部件装到正确位置\r\n• 把东西摆正、归位\r\n\r\n几个 put 的常见短语，比如：\r\n👉 put it away\r\n👉 put it back\r\n👉 put it on\r\n👉 put it down','1. 放东西\r\n• Put it in place. 把它放好。\r\n2. 安装部件\r\n• Once you put it in place, tighten the screws.  你把它放到位之后，再拧紧螺丝。\r\n\r\n3. 摆回正确位置\r\n• Just put it back in place.  把它放回原位就行。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-13 06:26:26',1,'2026-04-13 06:26:26'),(1066,15,35,'phrase','as for','as for','as for','通常表示：\r\n\r\n👉 至于……\r\n比如：\r\n• As for the price, I’m not sure. 至于价格，我不确定。\r\n更像是“说到这个 / 至于这个”\r\n有一点转话题、补充说明的感觉','as for 有一种：\r\n\r\n👉 “顺便说到这个”\r\n👉 “换到这个话题来说”\r\n👉 “至于这个嘛……”','💬 常见例子\r\n\r\n1. 说到某个人\r\n👉 As for John, he’s not coming. 至于 John，他不来了。\r\n\r\n2. 说到某件事\r\n👉 As for the meeting, it’s been cancelled.  至于会议，它已经取消了。\r\n\r\n3. 说到价格\r\n👉 As for the price, I think it’s reasonable.  至于价格，我觉得还算合理。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-13 06:52:32',1,'2026-04-13 06:52:32'),(1067,15,36,'phrase','up here','up here','up here','🧠 up here 的基本意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 这里上面\r\n👉 这上边\r\n👉 在这上面这个位置','1. 位置在上面\r\n比如：• 上层架子 / 高一点的地方 / 墙上 /  柜子上面\r\n• Put it up here. 把它放在这上面。\r\n• The jackets up here are more expensive.  这上面的夹克更贵。\r\n\r\n2. 说话人所在的这个位置\r\n\r\n有时候不一定真的“高”，只是表示：👉 我这里 / 我这边\r\n\r\n比如老师站在前面、店员站在柜台后面，可能会说：\r\n• Come up here. 到我这边来。\r\n\r\n这里的 up 不一定真的是“向上”，而是“到我这里来”。','📌 在商店场景里常见含义\r\n\r\n如果你在店里说：\r\nHow many items are up here?  👉 这上面有多少件商品？\r\n\r\nDid you sell one of the expensive jackets up here?  👉 这上面是不是卖掉了一件贵夹克？\r\n\r\n💬 例子对比\r\n\r\nPut it here.  把它放这儿。\r\n➡️ 只是“这里”\r\n\r\nPut it up here.  把它放这上面。\r\n➡️ 有“更高一点”的感觉\r\n\r\nCome over here.  到这边来。\r\n➡️ 强调朝这个方向过来','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-13 07:15:26',1,'2026-04-13 07:15:26'),(1068,15,37,'vocab','showcase','showcase','showcase','🧠 showcase 常见有两种词性：\r\n\r\n👉 名词   展示柜 / 陈列柜 / 展示场合\r\n👉 动词   展示 / 展现 / 突出呈现','1. 作为名词\r\n\r\nshowcase = 展示柜 / 陈列柜 / 展示场合\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• The necklace is in the showcase. 那条项链在展示柜里。\r\n• The event was a showcase for local artists. 这个活动是本地艺术家的展示平台。\r\n\r\n2. 作为动词\r\n\r\nshowcase = 展示 / 展现 / 突出呈现\r\n\r\n这个很常见，尤其在：产品介绍  /  展会  / 简历 / 项目描述 / 商业英语\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• This page showcases our new products.  这个页面展示了我们的新产品。\r\n• The exhibition showcases modern art. 这个展览展示现代艺术。\r\n• The project showcases his technical skills. 这个项目展示了他的技术能力。','💬 对比\r\n• This page shows our products.  这个页面展示我们的产品。\r\n✅ 普通说法\r\n• This page showcases our products.  这个页面重点展示我们的产品。\r\n✅ 更正式、更有宣传感','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-13 07:27:58',1,'2026-04-13 07:27:58'),(1069,15,38,'phrase','scrumptious','scrumptious','scrumptious','这东西很好吃','scrumptious 是一个比较生动、带点夸张的词，意思是：\r\n👉 非常美味的\r\n👉 特别好吃的\r\n👉 让人很想吃的\r\n\r\n它比普通的：\r\n• good\r\n• tasty\r\n• delicious\r\n更有一种 夸赞、可爱、很有食欲 的感觉。\r\n👉 tasty < delicious < scrumptious','💬 例子\r\n• This cake is scrumptious.  这个蛋糕太好吃了。\r\n• The meal was absolutely scrumptious. 这顿饭真是美味极了。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-13 15:55:33',1,'2026-04-13 15:55:33'),(1070,15,39,'phrase','burn out','burn out','burn out','🧠 burn out 是一个很常见的短语，意思主要有两类：\r\n\r\n👉 累垮 / 精疲力尽 / 职业倦怠\r\n👉 烧坏 / 燃尽','1. 人的状态：累垮了、倦怠了\r\n这是现在最常见的意思。表示一个人因为长期压力、工作太多、太累，最后变得：精神耗尽 /  没动力  / 很疲惫 /  有职业倦怠感\r\n\r\n• I’m starting to burn out. 我开始有点撑不住了。\r\n• She burned out after working long hours for months. 她连续几个月长时间工作后彻底累垮了。\r\n• A lot of teachers burn out. 很多老师都会出现职业倦怠。\r\n\r\n2. 物体：烧坏、烧尽\r\n比如灯泡、马达、电器等。\r\n\r\n• The light bulb burned out. 灯泡烧坏了。\r\n• The motor burned out. 马达烧坏了\r\n\r\n3. 火焰 / 能量：燃尽、耗尽\r\n• The fire burned out during the night.  火在夜里熄灭了','💬 很常见的搭配\r\n• burn out from work 因工作而累垮\r\n• feel burned out 感到精疲力尽\r\n• completely burned out  完全累垮了','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-13 16:28:46',1,'2026-04-13 16:28:46'),(1071,15,40,'phrase','Lay off','Lay off','Lay off','1. 裁员 / 解雇（通常因为公司原因）\r\n2. 少做一点 / 停一下 / 别再……了\r\n3. 别烦某人 / 别找某人麻烦\r\n\r\n根据语境可以翻成： 裁员 /  少碰  / 别再…… /  别烦 /  别找麻烦\r\n\r\n🎯 最简单记忆\r\n\r\nlay off\r\n\r\n👉 对人：裁员\r\n👉 对习惯：少碰 / 别再……\r\n👉 对语气：别烦 / 别找麻烦','1. 裁员 / 解雇（通常因为公司原因）\r\n\r\n这是最常见的意思之一。\r\n\r\n👉 lay off someone = 因为公司经营、预算、业务减少而裁掉某人\r\n不一定是员工做错了事。\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• The company laid off 200 workers. 公司裁掉了 200 名员工。\r\n• He got laid off last month.  他上个月被裁员了。\r\n\r\n📌 这里和 fire 不一样：\r\n• fire = 因为个人表现不好被开除\r\n• lay off = 因为公司原因被裁员\r\n\r\n2. 少做一点 / 停一下 / 别再……了\r\n这是口语里很常见的意思。\r\n\r\n👉 lay off something = 少碰一点 / 暂停 / 别再做了\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• You should lay off junk food. 你应该少吃垃圾食品。\r\n• Lay off the sugar. 少吃点糖。\r\n• Maybe lay off the coffee for a while. 也许你该暂时少喝点咖啡。\r\n\r\n3. 别烦某人 / 别找某人麻烦\r\n\r\n👉 Lay off!\r\n= 别烦了！ / 别再逼了！ / 别找我麻烦！\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• Lay off, okay? 别烦了，行吗？\r\n• Why don’t you lay off him for a bit? 你为什么不暂时别再烦他了?','📌 最常见的两个你先记住：\r\n• get laid off = 被裁员\r\n• lay off the sugar / coffee / junk food = 少吃糖 / 少喝咖啡 / 少吃垃圾食品','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-13 16:36:38',1,'2026-04-13 16:36:38'),(1072,15,41,'phrase','side gig','side gig','side gig','🧠 side gig 是一个很常见的口语表达，意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 副业\r\n👉 兼职赚外快的工作\r\n👉 主业之外做的活','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\nside = 旁边的、额外的\r\ngig = 工作、活儿、差事（很口语）\r\n\r\n所以 side gig 就是：\r\n\r\n👉 正职之外额外做的工作\r\n📌 语气感觉\r\n\r\nside gig 比 part-time job 更口语，也更现代一点。\r\n\r\n它常常暗示：不是主业 / 	是额外挣钱的  /  可能比较灵活 / 有时候是自己接单\r\n\r\n✅ 和别的词区别\r\n\r\nside gig   👉 副业、外快 \r\n强调：主业之外\r\n\r\npart-time job   👉 兼职\r\n强调：工作时间少，不一定有主业\r\n\r\nside hustle.   👉 副业 / 搞副业赚钱\r\n比 side gig 更有一种“积极搞钱”的感觉\r\n \r\n\r\n💬 对比\r\n• I have a part-time job at a café.  我在咖啡店有一份兼职。\r\n• I do graphic design as a side gig. 我把平面设计当副业做。\r\n• She started a side hustle selling handmade candles.  她开始靠卖手工蜡烛搞副业。','💬 例子\r\n• I’m looking for a side gig.  我在找一份副业。\r\n• Teaching online is just my side gig.  线上教学只是我的副业。\r\n• He has a full-time job and a side gig on weekends.  他有一份全职工作，周末还做副业。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-13 16:42:40',1,'2026-04-13 16:42:40'),(1073,15,42,'phrase','behind the scenes','behind the scenes','behind the scenes','🧠 behind the scenes 是一个很常见的表达，意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 在幕后\r\n👉 在台前看不到的地方\r\n👉 暗中 / 背后进行','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\n它可以表示：\r\n• 某件事不是公开进行的\r\n• 有人在背后做很多工作\r\n• 观众/外人看不到的过程','1. 字面意思：幕后\r\n\r\n比如拍电影、做节目、演出时：\r\n\r\n👉 behind the scenes = 镜头后面 / 幕后\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• We got to see what happens behind the scenes.  我们看到了幕后发生的事情。\r\n• She works behind the scenes in television. 她在电视行业做幕后工作。\r\n\r\n2. 引申意思：背后、暗中\r\n\r\n表示某件事表面上看不到，但实际上有人在背后推动、安排。\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• A lot of work happens behind the scenes.  有很多工作是在幕后完成的。\r\n• They were working behind the scenes to solve the problem.  他们一直在背后努力解决这个问题。\r\n\r\n📌 常见搭配\r\n\r\nbehind-the-scenes 作为形容词时要加连字符\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n• behind-the-scenes work = 幕后工作\r\n• behind-the-scenes footage = 幕后花絮\r\n• behind-the-scenes support = 幕后支持\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• He provides behind-the-scenes support.  他提供幕后支持。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 07:57:58',1,'2026-04-14 07:57:58'),(1074,15,43,'phrase','pepper in','pepper in','pepper in','🧠 pepper in / pepper something in 是一个比较形象的表达。\r\n\r\n它的感觉像：\r\n\r\n👉 像撒胡椒粉一样，零零散散地加进去\r\n所以它的意思通常是：\r\n\r\n👉 点缀着加入\r\n👉 穿插加入\r\n👉 零星地夹杂进去\r\n\r\npepper A with B\r\n\r\n更常见的结构是这个：\r\n\r\n👉 pepper something with something\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n• 在整体里穿插很多小东西\r\n• 零散地点缀进去\r\n• 夹杂进去','如果说：\r\n\r\n👉 pepper in some jokes：穿插加一些笑话进去\r\n\r\n👉 pepper in some English phrases\r\n就是： 夹杂加入一些英语短语','💬 例子\r\n\r\n语言里穿插一些词\r\n• She peppered her speech with jokes.  她在讲话中穿插了很多笑话。\r\n\r\n文章里夹杂例子\r\n• The article is peppered with examples.  这篇文章里穿插了很多例子。\r\n\r\n英语学习场景\r\n• Try to pepper in some natural phrases. 试着穿插一些自然表达。\r\n\r\n1. 说话时加点幽默\r\n👉 You can pepper in a few jokes. 你可以穿插加几个笑话。\r\n\r\n2. 写作时加例子\r\n👉 Pepper in some examples to make it clearer. 穿插加一些例子，这样会更清楚。\r\n\r\n3. 学英语时加自然表达\r\n👉 Try to pepper in some everyday phrases.  试着穿插加入一些日常表达。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 08:06:34',1,'2026-04-14 08:06:34'),(1075,15,44,'phrase','stick with your client','stick with your client','stick with your client','✅ 这个短语在这种语境里的感觉\r\n\r\n这里的 stick with 不是“坚持”那个意思，\r\n而是：\r\n\r\n👉 一直待在某人身边\r\n👉 继续陪着某人\r\n👉 保持跟进','stick with your client\r\n= 别离开客户，继续陪着/跟着/跟进客户','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 工作 / 服务场景\r\n• Stick with your client until everything is sorted out. 一直跟着你的客户，直到事情都处理好。\r\n\r\n2. 培训 / 指导场景\r\n• Stick with your client and make sure they’re okay. 陪着你的客户，确认他们没问题。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 08:17:04',1,'2026-04-14 08:17:04'),(1076,15,45,'phrase','strike up a conversation','strike up a conversation','strike up a conversation','🧠 strike up a conversation 是一个很常见的表达，意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 主动开始一段对话\r\n👉 跟别人搭话\r\n👉 开启聊天\r\n\r\n✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\n这个短语强调：\r\n• 不是别人先说\r\n• 而是你主动去和别人聊起来\r\n• 通常是比较自然地开启聊天','strike up a conversation 有一种：\r\n\r\n👉 轻松自然地搭话\r\n👉 开始聊起来\r\n\r\n✅ 常见搭配\r\n\r\nstrike up a conversation with someone\r\n\r\n👉 和某人搭话 / 跟某人聊起来','💬 例子\r\n• He struck up a conversation with the cashier. 他主动和收银员聊了起来。\r\n• She struck up a conversation with the person next to her. 她主动和旁边那个人搭话了。\r\n• It’s easy to strike up a conversation in a small shop.  在小店里很容易跟别人聊起来','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 08:21:05',1,'2026-04-14 08:21:05'),(1077,15,46,'phrase','pick and choose','pick and choose','pick and choose','🧠 pick and choose 是一个常见短语，意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 挑挑拣拣\r\n👉 有选择地挑选\r\n👉 只选自己想要的\r\n✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\n这个短语表示：\r\n• 不是什么都接受\r\n• 而是从很多东西里挑自己喜欢的、合适的\r\n• 有时语气中性，有时带一点“太挑了”的感觉','🎯 最简单记忆\r\n\r\npick and choose\r\n= 挑着选 / 挑挑拣拣\r\n\r\n👉 You can’t just pick and choose.\r\n你不能只挑自己想要的。','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 中性：从一堆东西里挑\r\n• You can pick and choose what you like. 你可以挑你喜欢的。\r\n\r\n2. 带一点“挑剔”的感觉\r\n• You can’t just pick and choose the easy parts. 你不能只挑容易的部分。\r\n\r\n3. 购物场景\r\n• Feel free to pick and choose. 你可以随便挑。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 08:29:57',1,'2026-04-14 08:29:57'),(1078,15,47,'phrase','I get the gist of it','I get the gist of it','I get the gist of it','✅ What it means\r\n\r\n👉 我明白大意了。\r\n👉 我抓到重点了。\r\n👉 我大概懂是什么意思了。','📌 Key point\r\n\r\ngist = the main idea / the general meaning\r\n\r\nSo:\r\nI get the gist of it means:\r\n👉 I understand the main point, even if I don’t understand every detail.\r\n\r\n✅ Similar natural expressions\r\n👉 I get the general idea.\r\n我懂大概意思了。\r\n\r\n👉 I get the main point.\r\n我明白重点了。\r\n\r\n👉 I kind of get it.\r\n我有点懂了。','💬 Examples\r\n• I didn’t catch every word, but I got the gist of it.\r\n我不是每个词都听懂了，但我明白大意了。\r\n• It was complicated, but I think I got the gist of it.\r\n这个有点复杂，不过我觉得我抓到重点了。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 08:34:29',1,'2026-04-14 08:34:29'),(1079,15,48,'phrase','pull apart','pull apart','pull apart','👉 拉开  👉 拆开  👉 扯开  👉 把……分开  👉 把……拆解开来分析','1.  字面意思：拉开 / 扯开 / 分开 \r\n\r\n例子\r\n• The two dogs had to be pulled apart. 那两只狗必须被拉开。\r\n• She pulled the curtains apart. 她把窗帘拉开了。\r\n这里就是把本来靠在一起的东西分开。\r\n\r\n2. 拆开某个东西\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• He pulled the toy apart. 他把玩具拆开了。\r\n• The machine was pulled apart for repairs. 机器被拆开来维修。\r\n这里有“拆解”的意思。\r\n\r\n3. 把一件事拆开来分析\r\n\r\n这个也很常见，尤其是在讨论、写作、学习里。\r\n👉 pull something apart = 把某个观点/作品/问题拆开来仔细分析\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• Let’s pull this argument apart. 我们把这个论点拆开来分析一下。\r\n• The reviewer pulled the film apart. 评论者把这部电影批得体无完肤 / 拆开细细批评。\r\n这里有时候会带一点“挑毛病、批判分析”的感觉。','💬 例子对比\r\n\r\n物理动作\r\n• Pull the boxes apart. 把这些箱子分开。\r\n\r\n拆东西\r\n• He pulled the phone apart to see how it worked. 他把手机拆开，想看看它是怎么工作的。\r\n\r\n分析【有时候可以是稍微负面一点的意思】\r\n• She pulled my idea apart. 她把我的想法拆开来分析了。\r\n有时也可理解成：她把我的想法批得很厉害。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 09:04:21',1,'2026-04-14 09:04:21'),(1080,15,49,'phrase','with no hesitation','with no hesitation','with no hesitation','🧠 with no hesitation 的意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 毫不犹豫地\r\n👉 没有任何迟疑地\r\n\r\n✅ 更常见、更自然的近义表达\r\n👉 without hesitation\r\n这个比 with no hesitation 更常见一点。\r\n• She agreed without hesitation. 她毫不犹豫地同意了。','✅ 基本意思\r\n• hesitation = 犹豫、迟疑\r\n• with no hesitation = 没有犹豫地','💬 例子\r\n• She said yes with no hesitation. 她毫不犹豫地答应了。\r\n• He jumped in with no hesitation. 他毫不犹豫地跳了进去。\r\n• I would choose that one with no hesitation. 我会毫不犹豫地选那个。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 09:08:10',1,'2026-04-14 09:08:10'),(1081,15,50,'phrase','To be all over the place','To be all over the place','To be all over the place','🧠 to be all over the place 是一个很常见的口语表达，意思通常是：\r\n\r\n👉 乱七八糟的\r\n👉 东一块西一块，没有条理\r\n👉 到处都是 / 很分散\r\n👉 状态很乱','✅ 常见意思\r\n\r\n1. 思路、说话、内容很乱\r\n\r\n这是最常见的用法。\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• My thoughts are all over the place today.  我今天脑子很乱。\r\n• Her presentation was all over the place.\r\n她的展示讲得东一块西一块，没有条理。\r\n👉 这里就是： 没有组织好，很散，很乱。\r\n\r\n2. 东西到处都是\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• Your clothes are all over the place. 你的衣服到处都是。\r\n• There were papers all over the place. 到处都是纸。\r\n👉 这里就是字面意思： 到处都是，摆得很乱。\r\n\r\n3. 情绪或状态很不稳定\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• I’ve been all over the place lately. 我最近状态很乱。\r\n👉 可能表示：\r\n• 情绪不稳定 / 生活节奏乱 /  注意力不集中','📌 “to be” 的作用\r\n\r\nto be all over the place\r\n\r\n这其实是这个短语的原形结构，意思就是：\r\n\r\n👉 处于一种很乱、很分散的状态\r\n\r\n比如放进句子里：\r\n• I don’t want my essay to be all over the place. 我不想让我的文章写得乱七八糟。\r\n• The room seems to be all over the place. 这个房间看起来乱糟糟的。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 09:14:02',1,'2026-04-14 09:14:02'),(1082,16,1,'phrase','hectic','hectic','hectic','🧠 hectic 是一个形容词，意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 很忙乱的\r\n👉 节奏很快、让人手忙脚乱的\r\n👉 忙得有点乱、很赶的\r\n\r\n因为 hectic 是形容词，所以前面常接：\r\n things /	work / days /	weeks  /	life  / it','👉 a hectic day\r\n👉 a hectic schedule\r\n👉 things have been hectic\r\n👉 work has been hectic\r\n👉 it’s been hectic lately','✅ 最常见的搭配\r\n\r\n1. a hectic day\r\n\r\n👉 忙乱的一天\r\n• It’s been a hectic day. 今天真是忙乱的一天。\r\n\r\n2. a hectic week  \r\n\r\n👉 忙乱的一周\r\n• I’ve had a hectic week. 我过了忙乱的一周。\r\n\r\n3. a hectic schedule\r\n\r\n👉 很满很赶的行程 / 日程很满\r\n• She has a hectic schedule. 她的行程很满。\r\n\r\n4. a hectic lifestyle / life\r\n\r\n👉 忙碌又混乱的生活方式\r\n• He lives a hectic life. 他过着很忙乱的生活。\r\n\r\n5. things have been hectic\r\n\r\n👉 最近事情一直很忙乱\r\n• Things have been hectic lately. 最近事情一直很忙。\r\n\r\n6. work has been hectic\r\n\r\n👉 最近工作很忙\r\n• Work has been hectic recently. 最近工作一直很忙。 \r\n\r\n7. it’s been hectic\r\n\r\n👉 这段时间一直很忙乱\r\n• Sorry, it’s been hectic. 抱歉，这阵子一直很忙。\r\n\r\n8. get hectic\r\n\r\n👉 变得忙乱起来 / 变得很混乱\r\n• Things usually get hectic before Christmas. 圣诞节前事情通常会变得很忙乱。\r\n\r\n9. too hectic\r\n\r\n👉 太忙了 / 太乱了\r\n• It’s a bit too hectic for me. 这对我来说有点太忙乱了。\r\n\r\n10. pretty / really / extremely hectic\r\n\r\n👉 很忙乱\r\n• It was really hectic this morning. 今天早上特别忙。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 09:49:25',1,'2026-04-14 09:49:25'),(1083,16,2,'phrase','A can of worms','A can of worms','A can of worms','🧠 a can of worms 是一个很常见的英语习语。\r\n意思是：\r\n👉 一个会引出很多麻烦的问题\r\n👉 一打开就会变得很复杂的事情\r\n👉 麻烦的潘多拉盒子','✅ 核心感觉\r\n\r\n这个表达的画面感是：\r\n\r\n👉 你一打开这个罐子，里面全是虫子\r\n所以意思就是：\r\n\r\n某件事一旦开始处理，就会冒出一大堆问题。\r\n\r\n📌 常见搭配\r\n\r\nopen a can of worms\r\n\r\n👉 捅出一堆麻烦\r\n👉 引发一连串复杂问题\r\n例子\r\n• Don’t open that can of worms. 别去碰那个麻烦事。\r\n• That question opened a can of worms. 那个问题一下子引出了一堆麻烦。','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 工作里\r\n• If we change that rule now, it’ll open a whole can of worms. 如果我们现在改那条规则，就会惹出一大堆麻烦。\r\n\r\n2. 日常里\r\n• I didn’t want to ask about it because it might be a can of worms. 我不想问那件事，因为那可能会引出很多麻烦。\r\n\r\n3. 家庭/关系里\r\n• Talking about money can be a real can of worms.  谈钱往往会引发很多麻烦。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 09:53:02',1,'2026-04-14 09:53:02'),(1084,16,3,'phrase','blow my mind','blow my mind','blow my mind','🧠 blow my mind 是一个很常见的口语表达。\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 让我特别震惊\r\n👉 让我觉得太不可思议了\r\n👉 让我大开眼界\r\n👉 让我惊呆了\r\n\r\nmind-blowing  令人震撼的 / 让人大开眼界的','✅ 基本结构\r\n最常见是：\r\n\r\n👉 It blows my mind. = 这让我很震惊。\r\n\r\n或者：\r\n👉 That blew my mind. = 那件事让我震惊了。\r\n\r\n📌 语气感觉\r\n\r\n这个短语比普通的：surprise  /  shock  /  amaze  \r\n更口语、更强烈一点\r\n它通常带一种感觉：\r\n\r\n👉 “哇，这也太夸张了吧。”','💬 例子\r\n\r\n现在时\r\n• It blows my mind how smart he is.  他这么聪明，真让我觉得不可思议。\r\n\r\n过去时\r\n• That movie really blew my mind. 那部电影真把我震到了。\r\n\r\n名词短语\r\n• The idea just blew my mind. 这个想法让我震惊了。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 10:08:04',1,'2026-04-14 10:08:04'),(1085,16,4,'phrase','essence of','essence of','essence of','🧠 essence of 的意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 ……的本质\r\n👉 ……的精髓\r\n👉 ……最核心的部分\r\n\r\n📌 essence 本身是什么意思\r\n\r\nessence = 最重要、最核心、最能代表某事物的部分\r\n\r\n所以它常常翻成：本质 /  精髓 /  核心 / 真髓','✅ 基本结构\r\n\r\nthe essence of + 名词\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n• the essence of life 生命的本质\r\n• the essence of the problem 问题的本质\r\n• the essence of good writing 好写作的精髓\r\n\r\n✅ 常见搭配\r\n• the essence of the matter = 事情的本质\r\n• the essence of the problem = 问题的核心\r\n• capture the essence of = 抓住……的精髓\r\n• the very essence of = ……最根本的本质','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 说本质\r\n\r\n👉 That’s the essence of the issue.\r\n那就是这个问题的本质。\r\n\r\n2. 说精髓\r\n\r\n👉 Simplicity is the essence of good design.\r\n简洁是好设计的精髓。\r\n\r\n3. 说核心\r\n\r\n👉 He captured the essence of the story.\r\n他抓住了这个故事的核心。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 14:51:44',1,'2026-04-14 14:51:44'),(1086,16,5,'phrase','out of the goodness of my heart','out of the goodness of my heart','out of the goodness of my heart','意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 出于我的好心\r\n👉 我是好心才这么做的\r\n👉 我纯粹是出于善意','','💬 例子\r\n\r\n👉 I helped him out of the goodness of my heart. 我帮他是出于好心。\r\n\r\n👉 She did it out of the goodness of her heart. 她这么做是出于好意。\r\n\r\n👉 I’m only doing this out of the goodness of my heart. 我这么做纯粹是出于好心。\r\n\r\n👉 I did it out of the goodness of my heart. 我是出于好心才这么做的。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 14:59:06',1,'2026-04-14 14:59:06'),(1087,16,6,'phrase','take accountability for','take accountability for','take accountability for','🧠 take accountability for 是一个很常见的搭配，意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 对……负责\r\n👉 为……承担责任\r\n👉 对……负起责任','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\n这个短语强调的不是普通“有责任”，而是：\r\n\r\n👉 愿意承认这是自己的责任\r\n👉 愿意为结果负责\r\n👉 不甩锅\r\n\r\ntake accountability  👉 强调主动承担责任\r\n• She took accountability for the failure. 她为这次失败承担了责任。（承担后果）\r\n\r\nbe responsible for  👉 表示客观上负责某事\r\n• She is responsible for the project. 她负责这个项目。 （职责）','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 工作场景\r\n👉 He needs to take accountability for his mistakes.  他需要为自己的错误负责。\r\n\r\n2. 团队场景\r\n👉 We should all take accountability for the outcome. 我们都应该对结果负责。\r\n\r\n3. 个人成长\r\n👉 You need to take accountability for your actions. 你要对自己的行为负责。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 15:10:07',1,'2026-04-14 15:10:07'),(1088,16,7,'phrase','all of a sudden','all of a sudden','all of a sudden','🧠 all of a sudden 是一个很常见的口语表达，意思是：\r\n👉 突然\r\n👉 一下子\r\n👉 冷不丁地','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\n它用来表示：\r\n• 某件事发生得很突然\r\n• 没有预兆\r\n• 一下子就变了','💬 例子\r\n\r\n👉 All of a sudden, it started raining.  突然就下雨了。\r\n\r\n👉 He was fine, and then all of a sudden he got angry. 他本来好好的，然后突然就生气了。\r\n\r\n👉 All of a sudden, the lights went out. 突然灯灭了。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 15:13:39',1,'2026-04-14 15:13:39'),(1089,16,8,'phrase','Hit or miss','Hit or miss','Hit or miss','🧠 hit or miss 是一个很常见的口语表达，意思是：\r\n👉 时好时坏\r\n👉 不稳定\r\n👉 碰运气\r\n👉 有时候行，有时候不行','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\n它表示某件事：\r\n• 没有稳定质量\r\n• 结果不确定\r\n• 有时成功，有时失败\r\n• 靠运气成分比较大\r\n\r\n✅ 很自然的句型\r\n• It’s a bit hit or miss.\r\n• They’re pretty hit or miss.\r\n• The results are hit or miss.','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 说质量不稳定\r\n👉 The food there is a bit hit or miss. 那里的食物有点时好时坏。\r\n\r\n2. 说学习效果不稳定\r\n👉 My listening is still hit or miss. 我的听力还是不太稳定。\r\n\r\n3. 说运气成分大\r\n👉 Finding good stuff at op shops is hit or miss. 在二手店淘到好东西很看运气。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 15:16:34',1,'2026-04-14 15:16:34'),(1090,16,9,'phrase','There’s some variability','There’s some variability','There’s some variability','👉 存在一些变化\r\n👉 有一定波动\r\n👉 有些不稳定 / 有差异','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\nvariability = 变化性、波动性、差异性\r\n\r\n所以这句话表示：\r\n\r\n👉 某件事不是完全固定的\r\n👉 它会有变化\r\n👉 不同情况之间会有差异\r\n\r\n💬 对比一下\r\n\r\nThere’s some variability 👉 比较中性、客观、正式\r\n\r\nIt’s hit or miss 👉 更口语，更像“看运气”\r\n\r\nIt’s inconsistent  👉 更直接，说“不稳定”','💬 例子\r\n1. 说质量有差异\r\n👉 There’s some variability in the quality. 质量上有一些差异。\r\n\r\n2. 说结果会波动\r\n👉 There’s some variability in the results.  结果会有一些波动。\r\n\r\n3. 说表现不完全稳定\r\n👉 There’s some variability from day to day. 每天之间会有一些变化。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 15:27:57',1,'2026-04-14 15:27:57'),(1091,16,10,'phrase','Tone of voice','Tone of voice','Tone of voice','👉 说话的语气\r\n👉 声音里的态度\r\n👉 讲话时给人的感觉','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\n它不是说“内容”本身，\r\n而是说：\r\n\r\n👉 你是怎么说这句话的\r\n同一句话，因为 tone of voice 不同，意思和感觉也会不一样。\r\n\r\n👉 It’s not what you said — it’s your tone of voice. 不是你说了什么，而是你的语气有问题。','💬 例子\r\n👉 I didn’t like his tone of voice. 我不喜欢他说话的语气。\r\n\r\n👉 Her tone of voice sounded upset.  她的语气听起来有点不高兴。 \r\n\r\n👉 Use a friendly tone of voice. 用友好的语气说。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 15:33:05',1,'2026-04-14 15:33:05'),(1092,16,11,'phrase','put emphasis on','put emphasis on','put emphasis on','名词  ： 强调 /   重点  /  着重之处\r\n所以 \r\n🧠 put emphasis on 的意思是：\r\n👉 强调……\r\n👉 把重点放在……上\r\n👉 着重于……','✅ 基本结构\r\n\r\nput emphasis on + 名词 / 内容\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n• put emphasis on speaking\r\n• put emphasis on teamwork\r\n• put emphasis on quality\r\n\r\n✅ 常见变形\r\n\r\nput more emphasis on\r\n👉 更强调……\r\n• We need to put more emphasis on listening and speaking. 我们需要更重视听力和口语。\r\n\r\nput too much emphasis on\r\n👉 过于强调……\r\n• Don’t put too much emphasis on grammar alone. 不要过度只强调语法。','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 学习场景\r\n👉 We should put more emphasis on speaking practice. 我们应该更强调口语练习。\r\n\r\n2. 工作场景\r\n👉 The company puts a lot of emphasis on customer service. 这家公司非常重视客户服务。\r\n\r\n3. 写作/表达 \r\n👉 You need to put more emphasis on the main point. 你需要更强调重点。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 15:38:33',1,'2026-04-14 15:38:33'),(1093,16,12,'phrase','rejuvenate','rejuvenate','rejuvenate','1.rejuvenate\r\n👉 动词\r\n意思是：\r\n	•	使恢复活力\r\n	•	使焕然一新\r\n	•	使重新有精神\r\n\r\n2. rejuvenating\r\n👉 形容词\r\n意思是：让人恢复精力的 /  让人焕发活力的  /  很治愈、很充电的\r\n\r\n3. rejuvenation\r\n👉 名词\r\n意思是：恢复活力  /  焕发新生 / 复苏  / 	回春','• A short holiday can rejuvenate you.\r\n一个短假期可以让你恢复元气。\r\n\r\n• A walk by the sea is rejuvenating. 在海边散步很让人恢复元气。\r\n• It was a rejuvenating weekend. 那是一个很让人充电的周末。\r\n\r\n• The holiday brought a sense of rejuvenation. 这个假期带来了一种恢复元气的感觉。\r\n• The company is in need of rejuvenation. 这家公司需要重新焕发活力。','🎯 最简单记忆\r\n\r\nrejuvenate\r\n\r\n= 使恢复活力\r\n\r\nrejuvenating\r\n\r\n= 让人恢复活力的\r\n\r\nrejuvenation\r\n\r\n= 恢复活力 / 焕发新生','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 16:11:33',1,'2026-04-14 16:11:33'),(1094,16,13,'phrase','narrate your life','narrate your life','narrate your life','🧠 narrate 是一个动词，意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 讲述\r\n👉 叙述\r\n👉 作旁白说明\r\nnarrate your life 这个词的是出现在如何学习英语的情景下，表示你可以用英语说出你时时刻刻正在做的事来提升你英语的表达','💬  这个词的其他例子\r\n\r\n1. 讲故事\r\n\r\n👉 He narrated the story clearly.  他把这个故事讲得很清楚。\r\n\r\n2. 做旁白\r\n👉 The documentary is narrated by David Attenborough. 这部纪录片的旁白由 David Attenborough 配音。\r\n\r\n3. 叙述经历\r\n👉 She narrated what happened that day. 她讲述了那天发生的事。','📌 和 tell 的区别\r\n\r\ntell \r\n👉 最普通的“告诉 / 讲”\r\n• Tell me the story.\r\n\r\nnarrate\r\n👉 更像“有条理地叙述 / 旁白式讲述”\r\n	•	Narrate the story\r\n听起来更正式一点，也更像“完整讲出来”','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 16:47:14',1,'2026-04-14 16:47:14'),(1095,16,14,'phrase','embrace your mistakes','embrace your mistakes','embrace your mistakes','👉 接受你的错误\r\n👉 坦然面对自己的错误\r\n👉 不要害怕犯错，而是把错误当成成长的一部分','💬 例子\r\n• You need to embrace your mistakes if you want to improve.\r\n如果你想进步，就要接受自己的错误。\r\n• Don’t be afraid to make mistakes — embrace them.\r\n不要害怕犯错，要坦然面对。\r\n• In language learning, you have to embrace your mistakes.\r\n在语言学习中，你得接受自己会犯错这件事。','👉 If you want to grow, you need to embrace your mistakes.\r\n如果你想成长，就要坦然面对自己的错误。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 16:49:22',1,'2026-04-14 16:49:22'),(1096,16,15,'phrase','Propel you forward','Propel you forward','Propel you forward','👉 推动你向前\r\n👉 促使你前进\r\n👉 让你不断往前走 / 往前发展\r\n\r\n🧠 propel 是一个动词，意思是：👉 推动 👉 推进 👉 驱使……向前','💬 例子\r\n1. 学习成长\r\n👉 Your mistakes can propel you forward. 你的错误可以推动你进步。\r\n\r\n2. 动力和目标\r\n👉 A clear goal will propel you forward. 明确的目标会推动你前进。\r\n\r\n3. 困难反而成为动力\r\n👉 Challenges can propel you forward if you use them well. 如果你善加利用，挑战也能推动你前进。','📌 语气感觉\r\n\r\n这个短语比普通的：\r\n• help you\r\n• push you\r\n\r\n更有一种：👉 带动力量地往前推进 👉 促成长、促发展 的感觉\r\n\r\n👉 Failure can propel you forward if you learn from it.\r\n如果你能从失败中学习，失败也能推动你前进。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 16:53:35',1,'2026-04-14 16:53:35'),(1097,16,16,'phrase','every single time','every single time','every single time','👉 每一次\r\n👉 每一次都\r\n👉 每一回都无一例外','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\n它比单独的 every time 更强一点。\r\n\r\nevery time = 每次\r\n\r\nevery single time  = 每一次，强调“真的是每一次都这样”\r\n\r\n📌 语气感觉\r\n\r\nevery single time 有一种：\r\n\r\n👉 一次都不例外\r\n👉 真的是每次都这样','👉 Every single time I go there, it rains. 我每次去那里都下雨。 \r\n\r\n👉 He makes the same mistake every single time. 他每一次都会犯同样的错误。\r\n\r\n👉 She gets nervous every single time she speaks in public. 她每一次公开讲话都会紧张。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 16:56:14',1,'2026-04-14 16:56:14'),(1098,16,17,'phrase','Capable of','Capable of','Capable of','👉 有能力做……\r\n👉 能够……\r\n👉 有本事……','✅ 基本结构\r\n\r\nbe capable of + 名词 / doing something\r\n\r\n1. 有能力做某事\r\n\r\n👉 He is capable of doing the job. 他有能力做这份工作。\r\n\r\n👉 She’s capable of handling it on her own. 她有能力自己处理这件事。\r\n\r\n2. 某物能做到某事\r\n\r\n👉 This system is capable of processing large amounts of data. 这个系统能够处理大量数据。\r\n\r\n👉 The car is capable of reaching 200 km/h. 这辆车能开到每小时 200 公里。\r\n\r\n3. 某人有可能做出某种行为\r\n\r\n有时也表示：👉 某人做得出……\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n👉 He’s capable of lying to everyone.  他做得出对所有人撒谎这种事。\r\n这个语气有时会偏负面。','💬 例子\r\n• I know you’re capable of more than this. 我知道你不止能做到这些。\r\n• Are you capable of finishing it by Friday?  你有能力在周五前完成吗？\r\n• This phone is capable of running multiple apps at once. 这部手机能同时运行多个应用。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 17:08:59',1,'2026-04-14 17:08:59'),(1099,16,18,'vocab','mentality','mentality','mentality  /menˈtæləti/','🧠 mentality 的意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 心态  👉 思维方式  👉 思想状态  👉 某一类人的普遍观念\r\n👉 Your mentality matters a lot. 你的心态非常重要。','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\n这个词强调的是：\r\n• 一个人怎么看事情\r\n• 一群人通常怎么想\r\n• 面对事情时的心理模式和思维习惯\r\n\r\n📌 常见搭配\r\n\r\npositive mentality  👉 积极心态\r\n\r\ngrowth mentality / growth mindset 👉 成长型心态\r\n\r\nwinner’s mentality 👉 赢家心态\r\n\r\nsurvival mentality  👉 生存型心态\r\n\r\nfixed mentality  👉 固定型心态 不过更常见的是 fixed mindset','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 说个人心态\r\n\r\n👉 You need a positive mentality.\r\n你需要一种积极的心态。\r\n\r\n2. 说群体观念\r\n\r\n👉 That old-school mentality is still common.\r\n那种老一套的观念现在还很常见。\r\n\r\n3. 说做事方式\r\n\r\n👉 He has a winner’s mentality.\r\n他有一种赢家心态。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 17:12:46',1,'2026-04-14 17:12:46'),(1100,16,19,'vocab','procrastinate','procrastinate','procrastinate','🧠 procrastinate 是动词，意思是：\r\n👉 拖延\r\n👉 把该做的事往后拖\r\n👉 迟迟不去做\r\n\r\n• procrastinator = 拖延者 \r\n所以如果你说某人是 a procrastinator，意思就是：\r\n👉 这个人总是把事情往后拖\r\n👉 该做的时候不做','📌 常见搭配\r\n\r\nprocrastinate on something\r\n👉 在某事上拖延\r\n• I’m procrastinating on my assignment. 我在拖我的作业。\r\n\r\nprocrastinate until…\r\n👉 一直拖到……\r\n• Don’t procrastinate until the last minute. 不要拖到最后一刻。\r\n\r\n💬 例子\r\n• I’m such a procrastinator. 我真是个拖延症患者。\r\n• He’s a procrastinator when it comes to studying. 说到学习，他很爱拖延。\r\n• Don’t be a procrastinator. 别老拖延\r\n• I know I should start now, but I keep procrastinating. 我知道我现在就该开始，但我还是一直在拖','','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 17:18:00',1,'2026-04-14 17:18:00'),(1101,16,20,'phrase','pick an example','pick an example','pick an example','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\n这里的 pick = 选择、挑选\r\n所以：\r\npick an example\r\n就是：👉 从很多例子里面挑一个','📌 和 give an example 的区别\r\n\r\npick an example  👉 强调 选一个例子\r\ngive an example  👉 强调 举一个例子给别人听\r\n\r\n💬 对比\r\n\r\nPick an example from the list. \r\n从列表里选一个例子。\r\n✅ 重点是“选”\r\n\r\nGive me an example. \r\n给我举一个例子。\r\n✅ 重点是“说出来”','• Pick an example and explain it. 选一个例子并解释它。\r\n• Let’s pick an example from everyday life. 我们选一个日常生活中的例子吧。\r\n• Can you pick an example from your childhood? 你能举一个你童年里的例子吗？','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-14 17:23:06',1,'2026-04-14 17:23:06'),(1102,16,21,'phrase','12 pm vs 12 am','12 pm vs 12 am','12 pm vs 12 am','👉 12 am = 半夜 12 点\r\n👉 12 pm = 中午 12 点','','','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-15 08:26:02',1,'2026-04-15 08:26:02'),(1103,16,22,'phrase','Do they usually focus on practical technical questions, or do they tend to ask more theoretical ones?','Do they usually focus on practical technical questions, or do they tend to ask more theoretical ones?','Do they usually focus on practical technical questions, or do they tend to ask more theoretical ones?','他们一般会问一些非常实用的技术问题 还是问一些偏理论的一些问题？\r\n还可以说：Do they usually ask very practical technical questions, or are the questions more theoretical?','📌 两个表达的区别\r\n\r\nvery practical technical questions  👉 很实用、很贴近实际工作的技术问题\r\n\r\nmore theoretical   👉 更偏理论的','💬 你也可以这样问\r\n\r\n👉 Do they usually ask practical questions based on real work, or more theory-based questions?\r\n他们通常会问基于实际工作的题，还是更偏理论的题？\r\n\r\n👉 Are the technical questions usually practical, or more on the theoretical side?\r\n技术问题通常是偏实用，还是更偏理论？\r\n\r\n🎯 最推荐你记这句\r\n👉 Do they usually ask very practical technical questions, or are the questions more theoretical?','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-15 08:35:09',1,'2026-04-15 08:35:09'),(1104,16,23,'phrase','to meet these requirements','to meet these requirements','to meet these requirements','✅ 意思\r\n\r\n👉 为了满足这些要求\r\n👉 达到这些要求','meet requirements = 满足要求 \r\n所以： to meet these requirements = 为了满足这些要求 / 达到这些要求\r\n\r\n2. satisfy the requirements  👉 比 meet 稍微正式一点\r\n\r\n意思也是： 满足要求\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• This document does not satisfy the requirements. 这份文件不符合要求。\r\n• Applicants must satisfy all the requirements. 申请者必须满足所有要求。\r\n\r\n3. fulfil the requirements\r\n👉 也是正确的  👉 英式英语里更常见 👉 有点正式\r\n\r\n意思也是：达到要求 / 履行要求 / 满足条件\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• You must fulfil the entry requirements. 你必须满足入学要求。\r\n• He fulfilled all the requirements for the role. 他满足了这个职位的所有要求。\r\n📌 在新西兰、英国体系里，你会比较常看到 fulfil。','💬 例子\r\n• You need more experience to meet these requirements.  你需要更多经验才能满足这些要求。\r\n• I’m working hard to meet these requirements. 我在努力达到这些要求。\r\n• Do I have the skills to meet these requirements? 我具备满足这些要求的技能吗？','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-15 16:38:25',1,'2026-04-15 16:38:25'),(1105,16,24,'phrase','a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances','a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances','a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances','一大组一起管理、一起运行的机器/实例','fleet 本来常见意思是：船队 / 	车队  / 机队\r\n\r\n在云计算里，它被引申成 👉 一大组一起管理、一起运行的机器/实例','💬 例子\r\n• The Auto Scaling group launches a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances.\r\n这个 Auto Scaling 组会启动一组 Amazon EC2 实例。\r\n• We manage a large fleet of EC2 instances across multiple regions.\r\n我们管理着分布在多个区域的一大批 EC2 实例。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-15 16:54:34',1,'2026-04-15 16:54:34'),(1106,16,25,'phrase','fundamentally different concepts','fundamentally different concepts','fundamentally different concepts','👉 本质上不同的概念\r\n👉 根本不同的概念','✅ 语气感觉\r\n\r\n这里的 fundamentally 比普通的 different 更强。\r\n\r\n不是说：👉 只是有一点不同\r\n\r\n而是说：👉 从根本、本质上就不一样\r\n\r\n✅ 单独拆开\r\n• fundamentally = 从根本上 / 本质上\r\n• different = 不同的\r\n• concepts = 概念\r\n\r\n• fundamental = 形容词  基本的 / 根本的 / 基础的\r\n• fundamentally = 副词  从根本上 / 本质上','💬 例子\r\n• These are fundamentally different concepts.\r\n这些是本质上不同的概念。\r\n• == and equals() represent fundamentally different concepts in Java.\r\n在 Java 中，== 和 equals() 代表的是本质上不同的概念。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-16 09:07:42',1,'2026-04-16 09:07:42'),(1107,16,26,'phrase','is subject to','is subject to','is subject to','🧠 is subject to 是一个很常见的正式表达，意思要看语境，但核心通常是：\r\n👉 受……影响   👉 受制于……    👉 取决于……    👉 需遵守……  👉 可能遭受…','✅ 常见意思\r\n\r\n1. 受……约束 / 受……管辖\r\n• This offer is subject to approval. 这个报价需经批准。\r\n• The contract is subject to local law. 该合同受当地法律约束。\r\n这里的感觉是：\r\n👉 要看……，要受……限制\r\n\r\n2. 取决于……\r\n• The schedule is subject to change.  日程可能会变动 / 日程视情况而定。\r\n\r\n3. 受……影响 / 易遭受……\r\n• Prices are subject to market conditions. 价格受市场情况影响。\r\n• The area is subject to flooding. 这个地区容易发生洪水。','💬 Java / 技术语境里也很常见\r\n• The final result is subject to business rules. 最终结果取决于业务规则。\r\n• This behavior is subject to JVM implementation. 这种行为取决于 JVM 的实现。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-16 09:20:22',1,'2026-04-16 09:20:22'),(1108,16,27,'phrase','comply with','comply with','comply with','🧠 comply with 的意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 遵守\r\n👉 符合\r\n👉 依照……要求去做','✅ 基本结构\r\ncomply with + rule / law / policy / requirement / standard\r\n\r\ncomply with 比 follow 更正式。\r\n它常用于： 法律 / 公司政策 / 合规 / 安全标准 / 技术要求\r\n\r\n所以它有一种：👉 “不是随便照做，而是正式地满足要求”的感觉。','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 法律 / 规定\r\n\r\n👉 All companies must comply with the law.\r\n所有公司都必须遵守法律。\r\n\r\n2. 公司制度\r\n\r\n👉 Employees are required to comply with company policy.\r\n员工必须遵守公司政策。\r\n\r\n3. 技术 / 安全要求\r\n\r\n👉 The system must comply with security requirements.\r\n这个系统必须符合安全要求。\r\n\r\n4. 新规则\r\n\r\n👉 We need to comply with the new rule.\r\n我们需要遵守这条新规定。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-16 15:05:25',1,'2026-04-16 15:05:25'),(1109,16,28,'vocab','upon','upon','upon','🧠 upon 是一个正式一点的介词，常见意思有：\r\n\r\n👉 在……时\r\n👉 一……就……\r\n👉 在……之后立即\r\n👉 基于 / 根据','✅ 常见意思 1：在……时 / 一……就……\r\n这是最常见的用法之一。\r\n\r\n• upon arrival  到达时 / 一到达\r\n• upon request  应要求 / 在提出请求时\r\n• upon launch 在启动时 / 一启动就\r\n• upon completion 完成时 / 一完成就\r\n\r\n例句\r\n\r\n👉 The package will be installed upon launch.\r\n程序会在启动时安装。\r\n\r\n👉 Upon arrival, please check in at the front desk.\r\n到达后请在前台登记。\r\n\r\n✅ 常见意思 2：基于 / 根据\r\n\r\n例子\r\n\r\n👉 The decision was made upon careful consideration.\r\n这个决定是在认真考虑后作出的。\r\n\r\n👉 Payment will be issued upon approval.\r\n批准后会付款。\r\n\r\n这里的 upon 有点像：	based on  / after  / 	following\r\n\r\n✅ 常见固定搭配\r\n• upon arrival = 到达时\r\n• upon request = 应要求\r\n• upon completion = 完成时\r\n• upon approval = 经批准后\r\n• upon launch = 启动时\r\n• upon receipt = 收到后','','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-16 15:13:50',1,'2026-04-16 15:13:50'),(1110,16,29,'vocab','intentionally','intentionally','intentionally','🧠 intentionally 的意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 故意地\r\n👉 有意地\r\n👉 刻意地\r\n👉 不是无意地','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\nintentionally 用来强调：\r\n\r\n👉 某个动作是有意识做的\r\n👉 不是 accident（意外）\r\n👉 不是 by mistake（弄错了）','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 日常表达\r\n\r\n👉 I didn’t do it intentionally.\r\n我不是故意这么做的。\r\n\r\n2. 工作 / 技术场景\r\n\r\n👉 The value was intentionally left blank.\r\n这个值是故意留空的。\r\n\r\n3. 系统 / 操作\r\n\r\n👉 The file was intentionally deleted.\r\n这个文件是被故意删除的。\r\n\r\n4. 说明原因\r\n\r\n👉 This feature is intentionally disabled.\r\n这个功能是被有意禁用的。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-17 10:12:18',1,'2026-04-17 10:12:18'),(1111,16,30,'phrase','listening comprehension','listening comprehension','listening comprehension','👉 听力理解\r\n👉 听懂能力','📌 语气感觉\r\n\r\n这是一个很常见的英语学习表达，尤其常见于：\r\n	•	英语考试\r\n	•	语言学习\r\n	•	IELTS / TOEFL / EAP\r\n	•	教学材料\r\n\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n• improve listening comprehension\r\n提高听力理解\r\n• listening comprehension skills. 听力理解能力\r\n• practice listening comprehension 练习听力理解','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 学英语\r\n\r\n👉 I want to improve my listening comprehension.\r\n我想提高我的听力理解能力。\r\n\r\n2. 考试场景\r\n\r\n👉 Listening comprehension is an important part of the test.\r\n听力理解是考试里很重要的一部分。\r\n\r\n3. 学习能力\r\n\r\n👉 My listening comprehension is better than my speaking.\r\n我的听力理解比口语更好。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-17 10:20:27',1,'2026-04-17 10:20:27'),(1112,16,31,'vocab','elevate','elevate','elevate','👉 提升\r\n👉 提高\r\n👉 抬高\r\n👉 使更好 / 更高级','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\nelevate 是一个比较正式、比较有“升级感”的词。\r\n\r\n它可以表示：\r\n	•	把位置抬高\r\n	•	把水平提高\r\n	•	把地位提升\r\n	•	把质量改善\r\n\r\n📌 语气感觉\r\n\r\nelevate 比 improve 更正式一点，也更有一种：\r\n\r\n👉 往更高层次提升\r\n👉 升级、拔高\r\n\r\n的感觉。','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 提升水平\r\n\r\n👉 This course helped me elevate my English skills.\r\n这门课帮助我提升了英语能力。\r\n\r\n2. 提升质量\r\n\r\n👉 We want to elevate the customer experience.\r\n我们想提升客户体验。\r\n\r\n3. 提升地位\r\n\r\n👉 The promotion elevated her to a leadership role.\r\n这次晋升把她提升到了领导岗位。\r\n\r\n4. 物理上抬高\r\n\r\n👉 The platform is elevated above the ground.\r\n这个平台被抬高在地面之上。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-17 10:22:20',1,'2026-04-17 10:22:20'),(1113,16,32,'phrase','Proper sequence','Proper sequence','Proper sequence','👉 正确的顺序\r\n👉 恰当的先后次序\r\n👉 合适的流程顺序','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\nproper = 合适的 / 正确的 / 恰当的\r\n\r\nsequence = 顺序 / 次序 / 先后排列\r\n\r\n所以： proper sequence 就是 👉 正确的顺序\r\n\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n	•	in the proper sequence\r\n	•	follow the proper sequence\r\n	•	arrange something in the proper sequence','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 操作步骤\r\n\r\n👉 Please follow the proper sequence of steps.\r\n请按照正确的步骤顺序操作。\r\n\r\n2. 学习流程\r\n\r\n👉 The topics should be taught in the proper sequence.\r\n这些内容应该按照合适的顺序来讲。\r\n\r\n3. 技术 / 系统\r\n\r\n👉 The tasks must run in the proper sequence.\r\n这些任务必须按正确顺序运行。\r\n\r\n4. 面试 / 表达\r\n\r\n👉 Make sure your answer is in a proper sequence.\r\n确保你的回答有合适的顺序。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-17 10:25:35',1,'2026-04-17 10:25:35'),(1114,16,33,'phrase','Revolve around','Revolve around','Revolve around','👉 围绕……展开\r\n👉 以……为中心\r\n👉 围着……转','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\n这个短语本来有“围绕某物旋转”的字面意思(比如月球围绕地球转)，\r\n但更常见的是引申义：\r\n\r\n👉 某件事主要和某个中心有关\r\n👉 重点都集中在……上\r\n\r\n📌 语气感觉\r\n\r\nrevolve around 比普通的：\r\n	•	be about\r\n	•	focus on\r\n\r\n更有一种：\r\n\r\n👉 “以……为核心、围着它转” 的感觉。\r\n\r\n👉 Most of my work revolves around backend development.\r\n我的大部分工作都围绕后端开发展开。','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 话题 / 讨论\r\n\r\n👉 The discussion revolves around customer needs.\r\n这场讨论围绕客户需求展开。\r\n\r\n2. 生活 / 工作\r\n\r\n👉 Her work revolves around data analysis.\r\n她的工作主要围绕数据分析展开。\r\n\r\n3. 家庭 / 个人生活\r\n\r\n👉 His life revolves around his family.\r\n他的生活以家庭为中心。\r\n\r\n4. 学习 / 项目\r\n\r\n👉 The project revolves around improving system performance.\r\n这个项目围绕提升系统性能展开。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-17 10:30:20',1,'2026-04-17 10:30:20'),(1115,16,34,'vocab','reassure','reassure','reassure','👉 使……安心\r\n👉 打消……的担忧\r\n👉 安慰并让……放心','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\nreassure someone\r\n= 通过语言、行动或解释，让对方不再担心\r\n\r\n它常见于：安慰别人  解释情况   缓解焦虑  让人放心\r\n\r\n📌 语气感觉\r\n\r\nreassure 比单纯的 comfort 更偏： 👉 通过解释或确认，让人放心\r\n\r\n不只是情绪安慰，还常常带有：\r\n• 说明事实\r\n• 保证情况\r\n• 消除疑虑\r\n\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n	•	reassure someone\r\n	•	reassure customers\r\n	•	reassure the team\r\n	•	reassure someone that…','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 安慰别人\r\n\r\n👉 I tried to reassure her.\r\n我试着让她安心。\r\n\r\n2. 工作场景\r\n\r\n👉 The manager reassured the team that no one would lose their job.\r\n经理让团队放心，说不会有人失去工作。\r\n\r\n3. 客户沟通\r\n\r\n👉 We need to reassure customers that their data is secure.\r\n我们需要让客户放心，他们的数据是安全的。\r\n\r\n4. 日常表达\r\n\r\n👉 His words reassured me.\r\n他的话让我安心了。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-17 10:40:38',1,'2026-04-17 10:40:38'),(1116,16,35,'phrase','on a regular basis','on a regular basis','on a regular basis','👉 定期地\r\n👉 经常地\r\n👉 在固定/规律的基础上','📌 语气感觉\r\n\r\n这个短语比：\r\n	•	regularly\r\n	•	often\r\n\r\n更正式一点。\r\n\r\n常见于：工作邮件 	申请材料 	面试回答  正式写作\r\n\r\n👉 I communicate with my team on a regular basis.\r\n我会定期和我的团队沟通。','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 工作场景\r\n\r\n👉 We meet on a regular basis.\r\n我们会定期开会。\r\n\r\n2. 学习场景\r\n\r\n👉 You should practice English on a regular basis.\r\n你应该定期练习英语。\r\n\r\n3. 日常生活\r\n\r\n👉 She exercises on a regular basis.\r\n她经常锻炼。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-17 10:42:03',1,'2026-04-17 10:42:03'),(1117,16,36,'phrase','divide and conquer','divide and conquer','divide and conquer','👉 分而治之\r\n👉 分而攻之\r\n👉 把大问题拆成小问题分别解决','💬 常见搭配\r\n• a divide and conquer strategy\r\n• a divide and conquer approach\r\n• use divide and conquer\r\n• apply divide and conquer\r\n\r\n📌 语气感觉\r\n\r\n这个短语非常常见于： 算法 / 编程 /  系统设计 /  问题解决 /	工作方法\r\n\r\n它表达的是一种思路： 👉 不要一次硬扛整个大问题  👉 而是先拆分，再逐个解决','💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 算法 / 编程\r\n\r\n👉 Merge sort uses a divide and conquer strategy.\r\n归并排序使用分而治之的策略。\r\n\r\n2. 解决问题\r\n\r\n👉 When facing a complex problem, I usually use a divide and conquer approach.\r\n面对复杂问题时，我通常会采用分而治之的方法。\r\n\r\n3. 工作任务\r\n\r\n👉 We divided the project into smaller parts and used a divide and conquer method to finish it efficiently.\r\n我们把项目拆成更小的部分，用分而治之的方法高效完成了它。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-17 10:50:14',1,'2026-04-17 10:50:14'),(1118,16,37,'phrase','placeholder','placeholder','placeholder','👉 占位符\r\n👉 占位内容\r\n👉 临时替代物','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\nplaceholder 用来表示：\r\n\r\n👉 先放一个“临时的东西”在这里\r\n👉 以后再换成真正的内容\r\n\r\n它很常见于：\r\n	•	输入框\r\n	•	网页设计\r\n	•	文档模板\r\n	•	代码\r\n	•	UI 界面\r\n\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n	•	placeholder text\r\n	•	placeholder image\r\n	•	placeholder value\r\n	•	use a placeholder','1. 输入框\r\n\r\n👉 Enter your name in the placeholder field.\r\n在占位输入框中输入你的名字。\r\n\r\n更常见是：\r\n👉 The text in the box is just a placeholder.\r\n框里的文字只是占位提示。\r\n\r\n2. 网页 / 设计\r\n\r\n👉 This image is only a placeholder for now.\r\n这张图片现在只是一个占位图。\r\n\r\n3. 文档 / 模板\r\n\r\n👉 We used a placeholder until the final content was ready.\r\n在最终内容准备好之前，我们先用了一个占位内容。\r\n\r\n4. 编程\r\n\r\n👉 Use a placeholder value before the real data is loaded.\r\n在真实数据加载前，先使用一个占位值。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-17 10:51:02',1,'2026-04-17 10:51:02'),(1119,16,38,'phrase','objective reality','objective reality','objective reality','👉 客观现实\r\n👉 客观存在的事实','objective = 客观的 \r\nreality = 现实 / 事实 / 真实存在的情况\r\n\r\n所以：objective reality  = 客观现实\r\n\r\n常见感觉\r\n\r\n这个短语强调：\r\n	•	不以个人意志为转移\r\n	•	不是主观想象\r\n	•	不是个人感受\r\n	•	是真实存在的','1.Variability is an objective reality. 变化性是一种客观现实。\r\n\r\n2.We must face objective reality. 我们必须面对客观现实。\r\n\r\n3. This is not just a personal opinion, but an objective reality. 这不只是个人观点，而是一种客观现实。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-20 07:24:05',1,'2026-04-20 07:24:05'),(1120,16,39,'phrase','stress and pressure','stress and pressure','stress and pressure','区分stress和pressure的含义\r\nstress 是主观感受到的压力，pressure 是外部施加的压力。','stress\r\n更偏心理上的压力感、紧张感、精神负担。\r\n比如：too much work / personal problems / deadlines 都会让人 feel stressed。\r\n\r\nI’m under a lot of stress.  我压力很大。\r\n\r\nThis job can be stressful.  这份工作可能让人压力很大。\r\n\r\npressure\r\n\r\n更偏外部施加的压力、要求、逼迫感。\r\n\r\n通常来自：deadlines / expectations / competition / responsibility\r\n\r\nThere is a lot of pressure to finish this project on time. 按时完成这个项目的压力很大。\r\n\r\nHe works well under pressure. 他在压力下工作表现很好。\r\n\r\n最简单理解\r\n\r\nstress = 你内心感受到的压力\r\npressure = 外部给你的压力\r\n\r\n例子帮助你区分\r\n\r\nStress affects my sleep sometimes.\r\n压力有时会影响我的睡眠。\r\n→ 更偏心理感受\r\n\r\nThere is a lot of pressure from management.\r\n管理层那边给了很大压力。\r\n→ 更偏外部来源','为什么面试里常说：\r\n\r\nHow do you handle stress and pressure?\r\n\r\n因为它想一起问两件事：\r\n• 你内心紧张、焦虑时怎么处理\r\n• 外部任务重、deadline 紧时你怎么应对\r\n\r\n很自然的搭配\r\n• deal with stress 应对压力感\r\n• work under pressure 在压力下工作\r\n• cope with stress 缓解/应对压力\r\n• pressure from deadlines 截止日期带来的压力','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-20 18:03:53',1,'2026-04-20 18:03:53'),(1121,16,40,'phrase','trade-off','trade-off','trade-off','◇ 意思：权衡；取舍；折中','⚖️ 感觉：\r\n想得到一个好处，往往就要放弃另一个好处。\r\n\r\n常见搭配\r\n• a trade-off between A and B\r\n• make a trade-off','例句\r\nThere is always a trade-off between speed and quality.\r\n速度和质量之间总是存在权衡。\r\n\r\nWe had to make a trade-off between cost and performance.\r\n我们不得不在成本和性能之间做取舍。\r\n\r\n☘️ 好记法：\r\ntrade-off = 有得有失','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-22 05:54:42',1,'2026-04-22 05:54:42'),(1122,16,41,'vocab','correspond','correspond','correspond\r\n🔊 Pronunciation /ˌkɒrəˈspɒnd/\r\n读音：cor-re-SPOND\r\n重音在 SPOND','🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n1. 对应；相当于\r\n2. 符合；一致\r\n3. 通信；通信联系','1. A corresponds to B\r\n\r\nA 对应 B\r\nThis field corresponds to the user ID in the database.\r\n这个字段对应数据库里的用户 ID。\r\n\r\nEach role corresponds to different permissions.\r\n每个角色对应不同的权限。\r\n\r\n2. A corresponds with B\r\n\r\nA 和 B 相符 / 一致\r\n\r\nThe result corresponds with our expectations.\r\n结果和我们的预期一致。\r\n\r\nHis explanation doesn’t correspond with the facts.\r\n他的解释和事实不符。\r\n\r\n3. correspond with someone\r\n\r\n与某人通信 / 联系\r\n\r\nWe corresponded by email for several months.\r\n我们通过邮件联系了几个月。','🗣️ Useful Sentences 实用句\r\n\r\nPlease provide the corresponding Chinese version.\r\n请提供对应的中文版本。\r\n\r\nWe need to make corresponding changes to the design.\r\n我们需要对设计做相应修改。\r\n\r\nThe data in this report corresponds to the data in the system.\r\n这份报告里的数据和系统里的数据相对应。\r\n\r\ncorrespond = co + respond\r\n\r\n可以理解为：\r\n互相回应 → 相互对应 / 保持联系\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncorrespond to = 对应\r\ncorrespond with = 相符 / 通信\r\ncorresponding = 对应的 / 相应的','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-26 10:54:47',1,'2026-04-26 10:54:47'),(1124,16,43,'vocab','migration','migration','migration','🔊 Pronunciation\r\n\r\n/maɪˈɡreɪʃən/\r\n读音：my-GRAY-shən\r\n重音在 GRAY','🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n1. 迁移；转移\r\n常用于系统、数据、项目、平台迁移。\r\n\r\n2. 移民；迁徙\r\n常用于人或动物从一个地方移动到另一个地方。\r\n\r\n✅ Common Patterns 常用搭配\r\n\r\n1. data migration\r\n\r\n数据迁移\r\n\r\nWe need to prepare a data migration plan.\r\n我们需要准备一个数据迁移计划。\r\n\r\n\r\n2. system migration\r\n\r\n系统迁移\r\n\r\nThe system migration was completed without major issues.\r\n系统迁移顺利完成，没有出现重大问题。\r\n\r\n\r\n3. migration plan\r\n\r\n迁移计划\r\n\r\nA clear migration plan can reduce production risks.\r\n清晰的迁移计划可以降低生产风险。\r\n\r\n\r\n4. cloud migration\r\n\r\n云迁移 / 迁移到云端\r\n\r\nThe company is planning a cloud migration next year.\r\n公司计划明年进行云迁移。\r\n\r\n\r\n5. migration risk\r\n\r\n迁移风险\r\nWe used a grey release strategy to reduce migration risk.\r\n我们采用灰度发布策略来降低迁移风险。','🗣️ Useful Sentences 实用句\r\n\r\nWe used a dual-write strategy during the migration.\r\n在迁移过程中，我们采用了双写策略。\r\n\r\nThe migration had minimal impact on users.\r\n这次迁移对用户影响很小。\r\n\r\nWe compared data between the old and new systems before the full migration.\r\n在全面迁移之前，我们对比了新旧系统的数据。\r\n\r\nA rollback plan is important for system migration.\r\n回滚方案对系统迁移很重要。\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆法\r\n\r\nmigrate = move from one place/system to another\r\nmigration = the process of moving\r\n\r\n你可以这样记：\r\nmigration = moving process 迁移的过程\r\n\r\n在 IT 项目里，migration 经常表示：\r\n\r\nmoving data or services from an old system to a new system\r\n把数据或服务从旧系统迁移到新系统。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/4c2ada1ac3894880adf4c55606daf27b.jpg','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-26 11:04:20',1,'2026-04-26 11:04:20'),(1125,16,44,'vocab','perspective','perspective','perspective','🔊 Pronunciation\r\n/pəˈspek.tɪv/\r\n读音：per-SPEK-tiv\r\n重音在 SPEK\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n1. 角度；观点；看法\r\n= a way of thinking about something\r\n\r\n2. 视角；观察角度\r\n= the position from which you look at something','💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\nper + spect + ive\r\n\r\nspect = look / see\r\n所以 perspective 可以理解为：\r\nthe way you look at something  你看待某事的方式 / 角度\r\n\r\n比如：technical perspective 技术角度\r\n\r\nbusiness perspective 业务角度\r\n\r\ncustomer perspective 客户角度\r\n\r\n✅ Common Patterns 常用搭配\r\n\r\n1. from my perspective\r\n\r\n从我的角度来看\r\n\r\nFrom my perspective, the system should be easier to maintain.\r\n从我的角度来看，这个系统应该更容易维护。\r\n\r\n2. from a customer’s perspective\r\n\r\n从客户的角度来看\r\n\r\nFrom a customer’s perspective, clear error messages are very important.\r\n从客户的角度来看，清晰的错误信息非常重要。\r\n\r\n3. from a technical perspective\r\n\r\n从技术角度来看\r\n\r\nFrom a technical perspective, this solution reduces database pressure.\r\n从技术角度来看，这个方案降低了数据库压力。\r\n\r\n4. a broader perspective\r\n\r\n更广泛的角度 / 更全局的视角\r\n\r\nWe need to look at this problem from a broader perspective.\r\n我们需要从更广泛的角度看这个问题。\r\n\r\n5. put something into perspective\r\n\r\n正确看待某事 / 把某事放到整体背景中理解\r\n\r\nThis experience helped me put the problem into perspective.\r\n这次经历帮助我从整体上理解这个问题。','🗣️ Useful Interview Sentences 面试常用句\r\n\r\nI looked at the problem from both a technical and business perspective.\r\n我从技术和业务两个角度看待这个问题。\r\n\r\nFrom the user’s perspective, the feature was not easy enough to use.\r\n从用户角度来看，这个功能还不够容易使用。\r\n\r\nI tried to understand the issue from different perspectives before making a decision.\r\n在做决定之前，我尝试从不同角度理解这个问题。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/5cd47333e25144f781c6c8a4dfd6f674.jpg','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-26 11:26:09',1,'2026-04-26 11:26:09'),(1126,16,45,'phrase','outcome','outcome','outcome','🔊 Pronunciation\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n= the result of an action, process, or situation\r\n某个行动、过程或情况最后产生的结果\r\n\r\n结果；成果；结局\r\n/ˈaʊt.kʌm/\r\n\r\n读音：OUT-kum\r\n重音在 OUT','✅ Common Patterns 常用搭配\r\n\r\n1. the outcome was positive\r\n\r\n结果是积极的 / 结果很好\r\n\r\nThe outcome was positive.\r\n结果很好。\r\n\r\n2. a successful outcome\r\n\r\n成功的结果\r\n\r\nClear communication helped us achieve a successful outcome.\r\n清晰的沟通帮助我们取得了成功的结果。\r\n\r\n3. the final outcome\r\n\r\n最终结果\r\n\r\nThe final outcome was better than expected.\r\n最终结果比预期更好。\r\n\r\n4. business outcome\r\n\r\n业务成果\r\n\r\nThe technical solution improved the business outcome.\r\n这个技术方案改善了业务成果。\r\n\r\n5. desired outcome\r\n\r\n期望的结果\r\n\r\nWe discussed the desired outcome before starting the task.\r\n开始任务前，我们讨论了期望的结果。','🗣️ Interview Sentences 面试常用句\r\n\r\nThe outcome was that the system became more stable.\r\n结果是系统变得更加稳定。\r\n\r\nThe outcome was positive because we reduced risks and improved efficiency.\r\n结果是积极的，因为我们降低了风险并提高了效率。\r\n\r\nAs an outcome, the team delivered the project on time.\r\n结果是团队按时交付了项目。\r\n\r\nThe outcome was improved customer satisfaction.\r\n结果是客户满意度提升了。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-26 12:53:28',1,'2026-04-26 12:53:28'),(1127,16,46,'phrase','think laterally and broadly','think laterally and broadly','think laterally and broadly','🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n从不同角度、更加全面地思考问题。','🧩 Breakdown\r\n\r\nlaterally ↔️\r\n= in a different or creative way\r\n= 从不同方向、不同角度思考\r\n比如：不只是按原来的方法解决问题，而是尝试新的思路。\r\n\r\nbroadly 🌍\r\n= from a wider view\r\n= 从更大的范围、更全局的角度思考\r\n比如：不仅考虑代码能不能实现，还考虑业务目标、用户体验、成本和风险。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nthink laterally and broadly about something\r\n从多个角度、全面地思考某事\r\n\r\nWe need to think laterally and broadly about this problem.\r\n我们需要从多个角度全面思考这个问题。\r\n\r\nI tried to think laterally and broadly before choosing the final solution.\r\n在选择最终方案之前，我尝试从多个角度全面思考。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nI had to think laterally and broadly because the issue was not only technical. It also affected delivery speed, customer experience, cost, and long-term maintenance.\r\n我必须从多个角度全面思考，因为这个问题不只是技术问题。它还影响交付速度、客户体验、成本和长期维护。\r\n\r\n🧠 Similar Phrases\r\n\r\nthink outside the box\r\n跳出框架思考\r\n\r\nlook at the bigger picture\r\n看大局\r\n\r\nconsider different perspectives\r\n考虑不同角度\r\n\r\ntake a wider view\r\n从更广的角度看问题\r\n\r\n🎯 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nlaterally = from different sides\r\n从不同方向看\r\n\r\nbroadly = see the bigger picture\r\n看得更全面\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nthink laterally and broadly\r\n= think from different sides and see the bigger picture\r\n= 从不同方向看问题，并看到更大的全局。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-26 14:29:46',1,'2026-04-26 14:29:46'),(1128,16,47,'phrase','take all … into account','take all … into account','take all … into account','🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n把所有……都考虑进去\r\n也可以理解为：\r\n在做决定或判断前，综合考虑所有相关因素。','🧩 Breakdown\r\n\r\ntake … into account\r\n= consider something before making a decision\r\n= 在做决定前考虑某事\r\n\r\nall available information\r\n= 所有可用信息\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ntake all available information into account\r\n把所有可用信息都考虑进去\r\n\r\n✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\ntake something into account\r\n考虑某事\r\n\r\nWe need to take customer feedback into account.\r\n我们需要把客户反馈考虑进去。\r\n\r\ntake all factors into account\r\n考虑所有因素\r\n\r\nI took all factors into account before making the decision.\r\n在做决定前，我考虑了所有因素。\r\n\r\ntake all available information into account\r\n考虑所有可用信息\r\n\r\nI took all available information into account when assessing the risk.\r\n在评估风险时，我考虑了所有可用信息。','💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nI took all available information into account, including technical risks, business impact, customer feedback, and rollback options.\r\n我考虑了所有可用信息，包括技术风险、业务影响、客户反馈和回滚方案。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\naccount 在这里可以理解为：\r\n📋 a list of things to consider\r\n一份需要考虑的清单\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ntake … into account\r\n= put it on your decision list\r\n= 把它放进你的决策考虑范围里。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-26 14:31:41',1,'2026-04-26 14:31:41'),(1129,16,48,'vocab','threshold','threshold','threshold','🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n门槛；界限；阈值\r\n\r\n在技术场景里，threshold 很常见，通常表示：\r\n一个临界值，超过或低于这个值，就会触发某种动作或变化。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nthreshold 可以想成一条线：\r\n\r\n低于这条线：正常\r\n超过这条线：触发动作\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nthreshold = trigger line\r\n阈值 = 触发线','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nthreshold\r\n= a limit or level where something starts to happen\r\n= 某件事情开始发生的临界点\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\n* CPU 使用率超过 80% 就报警\r\n* 错误率超过 5% 就触发告警\r\n* 请求量超过某个值就开始限流\r\n\r\n这里的 80% / 5% / 某个请求量 就是 threshold。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nset a threshold\r\n设置阈值\r\n\r\nWe set a threshold for error rates.\r\n我们为错误率设置了一个阈值。\r\n\r\nexceed a threshold\r\n超过阈值\r\n\r\nThe CPU usage exceeded the threshold.\r\nCPU 使用率超过了阈值。\r\n\r\nbelow the threshold\r\n低于阈值\r\n\r\nThe traffic is still below the threshold.\r\n流量仍然低于阈值。\r\n\r\nalert threshold\r\n告警阈值\r\n\r\nWe adjusted the alert threshold to reduce false alarms.\r\n我们调整了告警阈值，以减少误报。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nWe set clear monitoring thresholds so that the team could identify risks early before they affected customers.\r\n我们设置了清晰的监控阈值，这样团队可以在问题影响客户之前提前发现风险。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-26 17:10:38',1,'2026-04-26 17:10:38'),(1130,16,49,'phrase','promoted … within the …','promoted … within the …','promoted … within the …','🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n在……内部推广 / 促进 / 提升……\r\n\r\n这里的 promote 不一定是“升职”。\r\n在工作场景里，它常常表示：\r\n\r\n推广某个想法、方法、标准或行为。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\npromote = push something forward\r\n推动某事向前发展\r\n\r\nwithin the team = inside the team\r\n在团队内部\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\npromote something within the team\r\n= push a good idea or practice inside the team\r\n= 在团队内部推动一个好的想法或做法。','🧩 Breakdown\r\n\r\npromote\r\n= encourage or support something\r\n促进；推广；推动\r\n\r\nwithin\r\n= inside a group, company, or organisation\r\n在……内部\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\npromoted knowledge sharing within the team\r\n在团队内部推动知识分享','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\npromote something within the team\r\n在团队内部推动某事\r\n\r\nI promoted code review standards within the team.\r\n我在团队内部推动代码评审标准。\r\n\r\npromote best practices within the department\r\n在部门内部推广最佳实践\r\n\r\nWe promoted best practices within the department.\r\n我们在部门内部推广最佳实践。\r\n\r\npromote collaboration within the organisation\r\n在组织内部促进协作\r\n\r\nThe manager promoted collaboration within the organisation.\r\n经理在组织内部促进协作。\r\n\r\n💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nI promoted knowledge sharing within the team by organising regular technical discussions.\r\n我通过组织定期技术讨论，在团队内部推动知识分享。\r\n\r\nI promoted better communication within the project team to reduce misunderstandings.\r\n我在项目团队内部推动更好的沟通，以减少误解。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-27 07:49:50',1,'2026-04-27 07:49:50'),(1131,16,50,'vocab','colleague','colleague','colleague','🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n同事；同僚\r\n\r\n通常指和你在同一个公司、团队或行业里工作的人。\r\n\r\n🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\ncolleague\r\n= a person you work with\r\n= 和你一起工作的人\r\n\r\n比 workmate / coworker 稍微正式一点，适合面试和职场表达。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\ncolleague = co + league\r\n\r\nco = together\r\nleague = group / team\r\n\r\n所以可以记成：\r\n\r\ncolleague = someone in the same work group\r\n同一个工作圈子里的人 = 同事。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nmy colleague\r\n我的同事\r\n\r\nMy colleague helped me review the code.\r\n我的同事帮我检查了代码。\r\n\r\nteam colleague\r\n团队同事\r\n\r\nI discussed the issue with my team colleagues.\r\n我和值得团队同事讨论了这个问题。\r\n\r\nformer colleague\r\n前同事\r\n\r\nA former colleague recommended this role to me.\r\n一位前同事向我推荐了这个职位。\r\n\r\ncolleagues from other teams\r\n其他团队的同事\r\n\r\nI worked with colleagues from other teams to solve the problem.\r\n我和其他团队的同事一起解决了这个问题。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nI encouraged my colleagues to raise risks early and support each other.\r\n我鼓励同事们尽早提出风险，并互相支持。\r\n\r\nI worked closely with colleagues from product, testing, and operations teams.\r\n我和产品、测试、运营团队的同事密切合作。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/aab2a8957b2e4fd88e2594ebd7d87431.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-27 08:17:32',1,'2026-04-27 08:17:32'),(1132,16,51,'vocab','incident','incident','incident','🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n事件；事故；突发问题\r\n\r\n在工作和技术场景里，incident 通常指：\r\n一个影响正常运行、服务质量或安全的异常事件。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nincident 可以记成：\r\n\r\nsomething that happens unexpectedly\r\n意外发生的事情\r\n\r\n在 IT 面试里，你可以记：\r\n\r\nincident = unexpected service problem\r\n突发的服务问题 / 线上事故','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nincident\r\n= something unexpected that happens\r\n= 意外发生的事情\r\n\r\n在 IT 里可以理解为：\r\n\r\na system problem that affects users or services\r\n影响用户或服务的系统问题\r\n\r\n✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nproduction incident\r\n生产事故 / 线上事故\r\n\r\nWe had a production incident last night.\r\n昨晚我们发生了一次线上事故。\r\n\r\nsecurity incident\r\n安全事件\r\n\r\nThe team investigated a security incident.\r\n团队调查了一起安全事件。\r\n\r\nmajor incident\r\n重大事故 / 重大事件\r\n\r\nIt was treated as a major incident.\r\n它被当作重大事件处理。\r\n\r\nincident report\r\n事故报告 / 事件报告\r\n\r\nWe wrote an incident report after the issue was resolved.\r\n问题解决后，我们写了一份事故报告。','💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nWe reviewed the incident carefully, identified the root cause, and improved our monitoring to prevent similar issues in the future.\r\n我们认真复盘了这次事故，找到了根本原因，并改进了监控，避免类似问题再次发生。\r\n\r\n🔍 incident vs accident\r\n\r\nincident\r\n= 一个事件，可以是小问题，也可以是严重问题\r\n常用于工作、IT、安全、服务场景\r\n\r\naccident\r\n= 意外事故，通常有伤害、损坏或更明显的意外性\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\nThe system outage was a serious incident.\r\n系统宕机是一次严重事件。\r\n\r\nHe had a car accident.\r\n他出了车祸。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/82fb5b9952e340ba9880c5bdc4a4e5d0.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-27 08:30:10',1,'2026-04-27 08:30:10'),(1133,16,52,'vocab','emphasis','emphasis','emphasis','🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n强调；重点；重视\r\n\r\n= special importance or attention given to something\r\n对某件事给予特别的重要性或关注\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nemphasis 可以理解成：\r\n🔦 spotlight 聚光灯\r\n\r\n你把聚光灯打在哪里，哪里就是重点。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nemphasis = special focus\r\n强调 / 重点关注','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nemphasis\r\n= the main thing you want people to notice\r\n= 你希望别人注意到的重点\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe emphasis is on customer experience.\r\n重点是客户体验。\r\n\r\n意思是：客户体验是最重要、最需要关注的部分。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nput emphasis on something\r\n强调某事；重视某事\r\n\r\nWe put more emphasis on system reliability.\r\n我们更加重视系统可靠性。\r\n\r\nplace emphasis on something\r\n强调某事；把重点放在某事上\r\n\r\nThe project placed emphasis on user experience.\r\n这个项目把重点放在用户体验上。\r\n\r\nwith an emphasis on something\r\n重点关注某事\r\n\r\nI worked on backend systems with an emphasis on performance and maintainability.\r\n我从事后端系统开发，重点关注性能和可维护性。\r\n\r\nmain emphasis\r\n主要重点\r\n\r\nThe main emphasis was reducing risk.\r\n主要重点是降低风险。\r\n\r\n💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nIn this project, I placed strong emphasis on reliability, clear communication, and reducing production risk.\r\n在这个项目中，我非常重视系统可靠性、清晰沟通和降低生产风险。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a1ba7ab1910a49e28a7993947313adf3.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-27 09:46:09',1,'2026-04-27 09:46:09'),(1134,16,53,'phrase','campaign','campaign','campaign','Noun / Verb\r\n名词 / 动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n活动；运动；宣传活动；营销活动\r\n也可以作动词，表示：发起活动；开展运动；竞选\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\ncampaign 可以理解成：\r\n\r\na planned action for a goal\r\n为了一个目标而计划的一系列行动\r\n\r\n记住这句话：\r\n\r\ncampaign = goal + plan + actions\r\n活动 = 目标 + 计划 + 行动','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\ncampaign\r\n= a planned set of activities to achieve a goal\r\n= 为了达到某个目标而组织的一系列活动\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\n* 营销活动：marketing campaign\r\n* 广告活动：advertising campaign\r\n* 促销活动：promotion campaign\r\n* 竞选活动：election campaign\r\n* 公益活动：public awareness campaign\r\n\r\n✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nmarketing campaign\r\n营销活动\r\n\r\nThe company launched a new marketing campaign.\r\n公司发起了一项新的营销活动。\r\n\r\nadvertising campaign\r\n广告宣传活动\r\n\r\nThe advertising campaign increased brand awareness.\r\n这次广告活动提升了品牌知名度。\r\n\r\nelection campaign\r\n竞选活动\r\n\r\nHe worked on an election campaign.\r\n他参与了一场竞选活动。\r\n\r\ncampaign for something\r\n为某事发起运动 / 争取某事\r\n\r\nThey campaigned for better public transport.\r\n他们为改善公共交通发起活动。','💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nIn an e-commerce project, the system needed to support marketing campaigns quickly and reliably.\r\n在一个电商项目中，系统需要快速并可靠地支持营销活动。\r\n\r\nWe improved the backend architecture so the business team could launch campaigns more efficiently.\r\n我们优化了后端架构，让业务团队可以更高效地上线营销活动。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2bd69ea9fba7491eb60432684f430dd0.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-27 09:52:31',1,'2026-04-27 09:52:31'),(1135,16,54,'grammar','statistics','statistics','statistics','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nNoun 名词\r\n通常用复数形式，但可以表示一个学科或一组数据。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n统计学；统计数据\r\n\r\n= numbers or information collected and analysed to understand a situation\r\n通过收集和分析数字/信息来理解某种情况。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nstatistics 可以想成：\r\n\r\n📊 numbers that tell a story\r\n会讲故事的数字\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nstatistics = data + analysis + meaning\r\n统计 = 数据 + 分析 + 含义','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nstatistics 可以有两个常见意思：\r\n\r\n1. 统计数据\r\n比如：用户数量、销售额、错误率、通过率。\r\n\r\nThe statistics show that user activity increased.\r\n统计数据显示用户活跃度提高了。\r\n\r\n2. 统计学\r\n研究如何收集、分析和解释数据的学科。\r\n\r\nStatistics is important for data analysis.\r\n统计学对数据分析很重要。\r\n\r\n✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nshow statistics\r\n显示统计数据\r\n\r\nThe dashboard shows daily sales statistics.\r\n仪表盘显示每日销售统计数据。\r\n\r\ncollect statistics\r\n收集统计数据\r\n\r\nWe collected statistics about system performance.\r\n我们收集了系统性能方面的统计数据。\r\n\r\nanalyse statistics\r\n分析统计数据\r\n\r\nWe analysed the statistics to identify user behaviour patterns.\r\n我们分析统计数据来识别用户行为模式。\r\n\r\nofficial statistics\r\n官方统计数据\r\n\r\nThe report is based on official statistics.\r\n这份报告基于官方统计数据。','💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nI used system statistics to identify performance bottlenecks and improve service reliability.\r\n我使用系统统计数据来识别性能瓶颈并提高服务可靠性。\r\n\r\nThe statistics helped the team make a data-driven decision.\r\n这些统计数据帮助团队做出数据驱动的决策。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/46a49f5469484b4ab601412640658bfc.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-27 10:02:24',1,'2026-04-27 10:02:24'),(1136,16,55,'phrase','click-through rate','click-through rate','click-through rate','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nNoun phrase 名词短语\r\n常缩写为：CTR\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n点击率\r\n\r\n= the percentage of people who click a link, ad, button, or message after seeing it\r\n看到链接、广告、按钮或消息后，实际点击的人所占的百分比。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nclick-through = click and go through\r\n点击并进入\r\n\r\nrate = percentage\r\n比例 / 百分比\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nclick-through rate = clicks after seeing ÷ total views\r\n点击率 = 看到后点击的人数 ÷ 总展示次数。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nclick-through rate\r\n= clicks ÷ impressions × 100%\r\n\r\n也就是：\r\n\r\n有多少人“看到了”以后真的点进去。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\n一个广告被展示了 1,000 次，有 50 次点击：\r\n\r\nCTR = 50 ÷ 1,000 × 100% = 5%\r\n\r\n点击率就是 5%。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nhigh click-through rate\r\n高点击率\r\n\r\nThis campaign has a high click-through rate.\r\n这个营销活动的点击率很高。\r\n\r\nlow click-through rate\r\n低点击率\r\n\r\nThe email had a low click-through rate.\r\n这封邮件的点击率很低。\r\n\r\nimprove the click-through rate\r\n提升点击率\r\n\r\nWe changed the title to improve the click-through rate.\r\n我们修改了标题来提升点击率。\r\n\r\ntrack the click-through rate\r\n追踪点击率\r\n\r\nWe tracked the click-through rate of each push notification.\r\n我们追踪了每条推送通知的点击率。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nI used click-through rate to evaluate whether users were interested in the campaign message and to improve future content.\r\n我使用点击率来评估用户是否对营销信息感兴趣，并改进后续内容。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8d080c5db0b940b58d7653be9e0fcd56.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-27 11:00:43',1,'2026-04-27 11:00:43'),(1137,16,56,'vocab','assumption','assumption','assumption','🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n假设；假定；默认看法\r\n\r\n= something you believe is true without having full proof\r\n在没有充分证据的情况下，你认为某事是真的。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nassumption 可以理解成：\r\n\r\na starting belief before proof\r\n在证据之前的初始判断\r\n\r\n记住：\r\n\r\nassumption = believe first, check later\r\n假设 = 先认为可能是这样，再去验证。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nassumption\r\n= a belief you start with before checking the facts\r\n= 在确认事实之前先做出的判断\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nI made an assumption that the API was stable.\r\n我假设这个 API 是稳定的。\r\n\r\n意思是：我还没有完全验证，但我先认为它是稳定的。\r\n\r\n✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nmake an assumption\r\n做出假设\r\n\r\nWe should not make assumptions without checking the data.\r\n我们不应该在没有检查数据的情况下做假设。\r\n\r\nbased on an assumption\r\n基于一个假设\r\n\r\nThe plan was based on the assumption that traffic would increase.\r\n这个计划是基于流量会增加的假设。\r\n\r\ntest an assumption\r\n验证假设\r\n\r\nWe tested our assumptions before changing the system design.\r\n在修改系统设计之前，我们验证了自己的假设。\r\n\r\nwrong assumption\r\n错误的假设\r\n\r\nA wrong assumption can lead to a poor decision.\r\n错误的假设可能导致糟糕的决策。','💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nBefore making a decision, I tested my assumptions by checking system logs, user feedback, and production data.\r\n在做决定之前，我通过检查系统日志、用户反馈和生产数据来验证我的假设。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/893d7c787e5e4940a56c704b002c7d73.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-27 11:44:33',1,'2026-04-27 11:44:33'),(1138,16,57,'phrase','probe information','probe information','probe information','🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n深入了解信息；进一步核实信息；追问信息细节\r\n\r\n= to ask more questions or investigate details to understand the truth\r\n通过进一步提问或调查细节，来了解真实情况。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nprobe 可以想成：\r\n🔍 use a magnifying glass\r\n用放大镜仔细看\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nprobe information\r\n= look deeper into the information\r\n= 深入查看信息，找到真正的问题。','🧩 Breakdown\r\n\r\nprobe 🔍\r\n= investigate deeply\r\n深入调查；追问；探查\r\n\r\ninformation\r\n= facts or details\r\n信息；事实；细节\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nprobe information\r\n= dig deeper into the information\r\n= 深入挖掘信息，不只看表面','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nprobe information carefully\r\n仔细核实信息\r\n\r\nI probed the information carefully before making a decision.\r\n我在做决定前仔细核实了信息。\r\n\r\nprobe information from different sources\r\n从不同来源深入了解信息\r\n\r\nWe probed information from system logs, customer feedback, and production data.\r\n我们从系统日志、客户反馈和生产数据中深入了解信息。\r\n\r\nprobe further information\r\n进一步追问信息\r\n\r\nI probed further information to understand the root cause.\r\n我进一步追问信息，以了解根本原因。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nI probed the information by checking logs, asking follow-up questions, and comparing the data from different sources.\r\n我通过检查日志、追问细节，并对比不同来源的数据来核实信息。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/4abb2ed0adf049cead74034f2e9102b6.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-27 11:54:22',1,'2026-04-27 11:54:22'),(1139,16,58,'vocab','dual','dual','dual','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nAdjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n双的；双重的；两部分的\r\n\r\n= having two parts, two uses, or two functions\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\ndual 和 double 都和 “two” 有关。\r\n\r\n你可以这样记：\r\n\r\ndual = two-part / two-function\r\n双的 / 双重功能的\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\ndual-write = write to two systems\r\n双写 = 同时写入两个系统。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\ndual\r\n= two things together\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\n* dual system = 双系统\r\n* dual role = 双重角色\r\n* dual purpose = 双重用途\r\n* dual-write strategy = 双写策略','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\ndual role\r\n双重角色\r\n\r\nHe has a dual role as both developer and team lead.\r\n他有双重角色，既是开发人员，也是团队负责人。\r\n\r\ndual purpose\r\n双重用途\r\n\r\nThis tool has a dual purpose: testing and monitoring.\r\n这个工具有双重用途：测试和监控。\r\n\r\ndual-write strategy\r\n双写策略\r\n\r\nWe used a dual-write strategy during the system migration.\r\n在系统迁移过程中，我们使用了双写策略。\r\n\r\ndual citizenship\r\n双重国籍\r\n\r\nShe has dual citizenship.\r\n她有双重国籍。\r\n\r\n💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nWe used a dual-write strategy so the old and new systems could run in parallel and reduce migration risk.\r\n我们使用双写策略，让新旧系统并行运行，从而降低迁移风险。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/193d4e66c7bc4402976962bf25f4f5e1.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-27 13:28:54',1,'2026-04-27 13:28:54'),(1140,16,59,'vocab','entitlemententitlement','entitlement','entitlement','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nNoun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n权利；资格；应得的权益\r\n\r\n= the right to have or receive something\r\n有权获得某种东西或服务的资格。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nentitlement 可以这样记：\r\n\r\nentitle = give someone the right to something\r\n赋予某人某种权利\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nentitlement = the right or benefit you are entitled to\r\nentitlement = 你有资格获得的权利或权益。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nentitlement\r\n= something you are allowed to get because of a rule, membership, contract, or policy\r\n= 因为规则、会员身份、合同或政策，你有资格获得的权益。\r\n\r\n比如在你的项目里：\r\n\r\nmembership entitlement\r\n会员权益\r\n\r\n意思是：会员可以享受的服务或权限，比如存储空间、折扣、功能权限等。\r\n\r\n🔍 entitlement vs permission\r\n\r\nentitlement\r\n= 你“有资格获得”的权益\r\n强调：会员、合同、套餐、政策赋予你的权利\r\n\r\npermission\r\n= 你“被允许做某事”的权限\r\n强调：系统允许你执行某个操作\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\nA premium user has an entitlement to 1TB cloud storage.\r\n高级会员有资格使用 1TB 云存储空间。\r\n\r\nAn admin user has permission to edit the configuration.\r\n管理员用户有权限修改配置。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nmembership entitlement\r\n会员权益\r\n\r\nThe system manages membership entitlements for different product packages.\r\n这个系统管理不同产品套餐的会员权益。\r\n\r\nuser entitlement\r\n用户权益 / 用户权限资格\r\n\r\nEach user entitlement is linked to a specific membership package.\r\n每个用户权益都和一个具体的会员套餐相关。\r\n\r\nentitlement rules\r\n权益规则\r\n\r\nWe redesigned the entitlement rules to support more flexible product configuration.\r\n我们重新设计了权益规则，以支持更灵活的产品配置。\r\n\r\nservice entitlement\r\n服务权益 / 服务资格\r\n\r\nThe customer’s service entitlement depends on their subscription level.\r\n客户的服务权益取决于他们的订阅等级。\r\n\r\n💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nThe new system needed to support membership packages and entitlement rules more flexibly.\r\n新系统需要更灵活地支持会员套餐和权益规则。\r\n\r\nWe checked which entitlement fields were critical before migrating the data.\r\n在迁移数据之前，我们检查了哪些权益字段是关键字段。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a9312b0c8bf84553ad047635661e402f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-27 16:03:53',1,'2026-04-27 16:03:53'),(1141,16,60,'vocab','premature','premature','premature','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nAdjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n过早的；提前发生的；未成熟的\r\n\r\n= happening too early, before the right or expected time\r\n在合适或预期的时间之前发生。\r\n\r\n🔍 premature vs early\r\n\r\nearly  = 早的，中性词，不一定不好\r\n\r\nI arrived early.  我到得早。\r\n\r\npremature  = 过早的，通常带有“不合适 / 不成熟 / 风险”的感觉\r\nThe decision was premature.  这个决定太早了，还不成熟。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\npremature = too early\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n* premature baby      早产儿\r\n* premature decision     过早的决定\r\n* premature conclusion     过早下结论\r\n* premature release     过早发布 / 提前发布\r\n\r\n✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\npremature decision  过早的决定\r\n\r\nIt would be premature to make a decision now.  现在做决定还为时过早。\r\n\r\npremature conclusion  过早的结论\r\n\r\nDon’t jump to a premature conclusion.  不要过早下结论。\r\n\r\npremature baby 早产儿\r\n\r\nThe baby was born premature.  这个婴儿是早产的。\r\n\r\npremature release 过早发布\r\n\r\nA premature release may cause production issues. 过早发布可能会导致生产问题。','💼 Interview / Work Sentence\r\n\r\nIt would be premature to choose a solution before we fully understand the requirements and risks.\r\n在我们充分理解需求和风险之前就选择方案还为时过早。\r\n\r\nI avoided making a premature decision by checking the data and discussing the risks with the team.\r\n我通过检查数据并和团队讨论风险，避免了过早做决定。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/19544eec8ef4436e8c664eda1b24e5da.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-27 18:10:47',1,'2026-04-27 18:10:47'),(1142,16,61,'vocab','distortion','distortion','distortion','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nNoun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n扭曲；变形；失真\r\n\r\n= a change that makes something look, sound, or seem different from the real or original version\r\n让某个东西看起来、听起来或理解起来和真实情况不一样。\r\n\r\n💼 Work / GIS Sentence\r\n\r\nWe need to choose a suitable map projection to reduce distortion in the study area.\r\n我们需要选择合适的地图投影，以减少研究区域内的变形。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\ndistortion\r\n= not the real shape / not the true version\r\n\r\n可以用于很多场景：\r\n\r\n* 地图面积变形\r\n* 声音失真\r\n* 图片变形\r\n* 信息被歪曲\r\n* 数据被误导性呈现','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nmap distortion\r\n地图变形 / 地图失真\r\n\r\nMercator projection causes area distortion near the poles.\r\n墨卡托投影会在靠近两极的地方造成面积变形。\r\n\r\nimage distortion\r\n图像变形\r\n\r\nThe photo has some distortion around the edges.\r\n这张照片边缘有一些变形。\r\n\r\nsound distortion\r\n声音失真\r\n\r\nThere was a lot of sound distortion during the call.\r\n通话中有很多声音失真。\r\n\r\ndata distortion\r\n数据失真 / 数据被误导性呈现\r\n\r\nPoor sampling can lead to data distortion.\r\n抽样不合理可能导致数据失真。\r\n\r\n💼 Work / GIS Sentence\r\n\r\nWe need to choose a suitable map projection to reduce distortion in the study area.\r\n我们需要选择合适的地图投影，以减少研究区域内的变形。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/fa10aff906984a6c84e871358752681d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-28 09:36:26',1,'2026-04-28 09:36:26'),(1143,16,62,'vocab','easting','easting','easting','Noun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n东距；东向坐标\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\neast = 东\r\n-ing = 可以理解成方向相关的坐标\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\neasting = east + coordinate\r\neasting = 向东的坐标 / 东距\r\n\r\n记住：\r\n\r\neasting goes left to right on a map\r\neasting 在地图上通常是从左到右增加。\r\n\r\n= the eastward distance or x-coordinate in a map grid system\r\n在地图网格系统中，表示向东的距离，通常相当于 x 坐标。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\neasting 可以理解为：\r\n\r\nhow far east a point is on a map\r\n一个点在地图上向东有多远\r\n\r\n在 GIS / 地图坐标里，常常和 northing 一起出现：\r\n\r\n* easting = 东向坐标 / x 坐标\r\n* northing = 北向坐标 / y 坐标','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\neasting 可以理解为：\r\n\r\nhow far east a point is on a map\r\n一个点在地图上向东有多远\r\n\r\n在 GIS / 地图坐标里，常常和 northing 一起出现：\r\n\r\n* easting = 东向坐标 / x 坐标\r\n* northing = 北向坐标 / y 坐标','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b0ad1c40a3694ce29fe9ebe5117ee025.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-28 09:43:49',1,'2026-04-28 09:43:49'),(1144,16,63,'vocab','epic','epic','epic','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nNoun / Adjective\r\n名词 / 形容词\r\n\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n1. Noun 名词\r\n\r\n史诗；宏大的故事\r\n\r\n= a long story about heroic actions or important events\r\n关于英雄行为或重大事件的长篇故事。\r\n\r\nThe film is an epic about war and friendship.\r\n这部电影是一部关于战争和友谊的史诗。\r\n\r\n2. Adjective 形容词\r\n\r\n宏大的；壮观的；了不起的\r\n\r\n= very big, impressive, or exciting\r\n非常宏大、令人印象深刻或令人兴奋的。\r\n\r\nIt was an epic journey.\r\n那是一段壮观的旅程。\r\n\r\n3. Agile / Jira 项目管理里的意思\r\n\r\n大型需求；史诗级任务；大功能模块\r\n\r\n在 Jira / Agile 里，epic 指一个比较大的功能或目标，通常需要拆成多个 user stories。\r\n\r\nWe created an epic for the user management feature.\r\n我们为用户管理功能创建了一个 epic。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象一个 epic 就像一部很长的英雄电影 🎬：\r\n它太大了，不能一次讲完，所以要拆成很多小章节。\r\n\r\nepic = big story / big task\r\nepic = 大故事 / 大任务。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nepic 可以理解成：\r\n\r\nsomething big and important\r\n很大、很重要的东西\r\n\r\n在项目里：\r\n\r\nepic = a large piece of work\r\nepic = 一个大的工作项 / 大功能模块','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nan epic story\r\n史诗故事\r\n\r\nThis is an epic story about courage.\r\n这是一个关于勇气的史诗故事。\r\n\r\nan epic journey\r\n壮观的旅程\r\n\r\nWe had an epic journey through the mountains.\r\n我们经历了一段穿越群山的壮观旅程。\r\n\r\ncreate an epic\r\n创建一个 epic / 创建大型需求\r\n\r\nThe product owner created an epic for the migration project.\r\n产品负责人为迁移项目创建了一个 epic。\r\n\r\nbreak an epic into user stories\r\n把 epic 拆分成用户故事\r\n\r\nWe broke the epic into smaller user stories.\r\n我们把这个大型需求拆成了更小的用户故事。\r\n\r\n💼 Interview / Work Sentence\r\n\r\nIn Jira, we broke the epic into smaller user stories so the team could estimate and deliver the work more effectively.\r\n在 Jira 中，我们把这个大型需求拆成更小的用户故事，这样团队可以更有效地估算和交付工作。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/45650a7dc3ed49e399e02000acc6f1eb.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-28 09:51:53',1,'2026-04-28 09:51:53'),(1145,16,64,'vocab','ellipsoid','ellipsoid','ellipsoid','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nNoun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n椭球体；椭圆体\r\n\r\n= a 3D shape like a slightly stretched or flattened sphere\r\n一个像球体但被拉长或压扁的三维形状。\r\n\r\n🔍 ellipsoid vs sphere\r\n\r\nsphere = perfect ball shape  完美球体\r\n\r\nellipsoid = slightly stretched or flattened ball shape  被轻微拉长或压扁的球体\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\nA basketball is close to a sphere.\r\n篮球接近球体。\r\n\r\nThe Earth is better represented by an ellipsoid.\r\n地球更适合用椭球体表示。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nellipse = 椭圆\r\n-oid = like / shaped like\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nellipsoid = ellipse-like 3D shape\r\nellipsoid = 像椭圆一样的三维形状\r\n\r\n记住一句：\r\n\r\nellipsoid = a slightly squashed sphere\r\n椭球体 = 被轻微压扁的球。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nellipsoid 可以理解成：\r\n\r\na sphere that is not perfectly round\r\n不是完全球形的球体\r\n\r\n在 GIS / 地理坐标里，ellipsoid 通常指用来近似表示地球形状的数学模型。\r\n\r\n地球并不是完美的球体，而是：\r\n\r\nslightly flattened at the poles and wider at the equator\r\n两极略扁，赤道略宽\r\n\r\n所以 GIS 中会用 ellipsoid 来描述地球的近似形状。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nreference ellipsoid\r\n参考椭球体\r\n\r\nWGS84 uses a reference ellipsoid to model the shape of the Earth.\r\nWGS84 使用参考椭球体来模拟地球的形状。\r\n\r\nEarth ellipsoid\r\n地球椭球体\r\n\r\nThe Earth ellipsoid is slightly flattened at the poles.\r\n地球椭球体在两极略微扁平。\r\n\r\nellipsoid model\r\n椭球体模型\r\n\r\nA coordinate system is often based on an ellipsoid model.\r\n坐标系统通常基于一个椭球体模型。\r\n\r\n🗺️ GIS Sentence\r\n\r\nIn GIS, an ellipsoid is a simplified mathematical model of the Earth’s shape, used for coordinate systems and map projections.\r\n在 GIS 中，椭球体是地球形状的简化数学模型，用于坐标系统和地图投影。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/6dcfe7b1f5a44cbaa854214ccdcdb3b2.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-28 10:00:10',1,'2026-04-28 10:00:10'),(1146,16,65,'phrase','assume','assume','assume','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nVerb 动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n假设；认为；默认以为\r\n\r\n= to believe something is true without having full proof\r\n在没有充分证据的情况下，认为某事是真的。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nassume 可以记成：\r\n\r\nassume = believe before checking\r\nassume = 检查前先认为是真的。\r\n\r\n所以在工作中要小心：\r\n\r\nDon’t assume. Verify.\r\n不要想当然，要验证。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nassume\r\n= believe first, but not fully checked yet\r\n= 先认为是这样，但还没有完全确认。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nI assumed the meeting was at 10 a.m.\r\n我以为会议是上午 10 点。\r\n\r\n意思是：我当时这样认为，但可能没有确认。\r\n\r\n🔍 assume vs presume\r\n\r\nassume\r\n= 普通的“假设 / 以为”，证据可能不多\r\n\r\nI assumed he was busy.\r\n我以为他很忙。\r\n\r\npresume\r\n= 也是假设，但通常听起来更正式，或者基于一定理由\r\n\r\nI presumed he had already received the email.\r\n我推测他已经收到邮件了。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nassume that…\r\n假设 / 认为……\r\n\r\nI assumed that the data was correct.\r\n我以为这些数据是正确的。\r\n\r\ndon’t assume\r\n不要想当然\r\n\r\nDon’t assume anything without checking the facts.\r\n不要在没核实事实前想当然。\r\n\r\nit is safe to assume that…\r\n可以合理认为……\r\n\r\nIt is safe to assume that users need more time.\r\n可以合理认为用户需要更多时间。\r\n\r\nwrongly assume\r\n错误地认为\r\n\r\nWe wrongly assumed the old API was still stable.\r\n我们错误地以为旧 API 仍然稳定。\r\n\r\n💼 Work / Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nI did not simply assume the solution was safe. I checked the data, discussed the risks with the team, and tested the assumption before making a decision.\r\n我没有简单地假设这个方案是安全的。我检查了数据，和团队讨论风险，并在做决定前验证了这个假设。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c196e10822a64e45b1b8a63a21bd54ea.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-28 16:35:12',1,'2026-04-28 16:35:12'),(1147,17,1,'vocab','terrain','terrain','terrain','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nNoun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n地形；地势；地貌\r\n\r\n= the physical shape and features of land\r\n指土地表面的形状和特征，比如山地、平原、坡地、河谷等。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n你可以把 terrain 想成：\r\n\r\nland surface shape\r\n土地表面的形状\r\n\r\n记住一句：\r\n\r\nterrain = what the land looks like physically\r\nterrain = 土地实际长什么样。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nterrain\r\n= the shape of the land. = 地面的形状\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\n* flat terrain    平坦地形\r\n* steep terrain     陡峭地形\r\n* mountainous terrain     山地地形\r\n* rough terrain      崎岖地形\r\n\r\n🔍 terrain vs topography\r\n\r\nterrain\r\n更偏向“实际地形本身”。\r\n\r\nThe terrain is steep.\r\n这个地形很陡。\r\n\r\ntopography\r\n更偏向“地形特征的描述或数据表达”，常用于地图、测量、GIS。\r\n\r\nThe topography of the area was analysed using a DEM.\r\n该区域的地形特征通过 DEM 进行了分析。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nflat terrain\r\n\r\n平坦地形\r\n\r\nThe site is located on flat terrain.\r\n该地点位于平坦地形上。\r\n\r\nsteep terrain\r\n\r\n陡峭地形\r\n\r\nSteep terrain may increase construction costs.\r\n陡峭地形可能会增加施工成本。\r\n\r\nrough terrain\r\n\r\n崎岖地形\r\n\r\nIt is difficult to build roads across rough terrain.\r\n在崎岖地形上修路比较困难。\r\n\r\nterrain analysis\r\n\r\n地形分析\r\n\r\nTerrain analysis was used to assess slope and elevation.\r\n使用地形分析来评估坡度和海拔。\r\n\r\n🗺️ GIS Sentence\r\n\r\nThe DEM was used for terrain analysis, including slope and aspect calculation.\r\nDEM 被用于地形分析，包括坡度和坡向计算。\r\n\r\nTerrain conditions can affect site suitability, construction cost, and accessibility.\r\n地形条件会影响选址适宜性、建设成本和可达性。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/bbedc59ea550430a880b6be36d148227.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-29 17:05:06',1,'2026-04-29 17:05:06'),(1148,17,2,'vocab','governance','governance','governance','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nNoun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n治理；管理；管控机制\r\n\r\n= the way an organisation, system, or project is controlled, managed, and guided\r\n指一个组织、系统或项目如何被管理、监督和决策。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\ngovernance\r\n= rules + roles + decision-making + control\r\n\r\n也就是：\r\n\r\n谁负责？\r\n按什么规则做？\r\n谁来审批？\r\n如何监督风险和质量？','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\ndata governance\r\n\r\n数据治理\r\n\r\nGood data governance helps ensure data quality and security.\r\n良好的数据治理有助于确保数据质量和安全。\r\n\r\nproject governance\r\n\r\n项目治理 / 项目管控\r\n\r\nProject governance defines how decisions are made and who is responsible.\r\n项目治理定义了如何做决策以及谁负责。\r\n\r\nIT governance\r\n\r\nIT 治理\r\n\r\nIT governance ensures that technology supports business goals.\r\nIT 治理确保技术支持业务目标。\r\n\r\ngovernance framework\r\n\r\n治理框架\r\n\r\nWe followed a governance framework to manage risks and approvals.\r\n我们遵循治理框架来管理风险和审批。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 Work / Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nWe improved project governance by defining clear roles, approval steps, and risk controls.\r\n我们通过明确角色、审批步骤和风险控制来改进项目治理。\r\n\r\nStrong data governance was important because the migration involved customer-related information.\r\n强数据治理很重要，因为这次迁移涉及客户相关信息。\r\n\r\n🔍 governance vs management\r\n\r\nmanagement\r\n= day-to-day work management\r\n偏日常管理，比如安排任务、跟进进度。\r\n\r\ngovernance\r\n= higher-level rules and control\r\n偏更高层的规则、责任、审批和监督机制。\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\nManagement focuses on getting the work done.\r\n管理关注把事情做完。\r\n\r\nGovernance focuses on making sure the work is done in the right way.\r\n治理关注确保事情以正确方式完成。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/096a2ab233324c5c9ac97625391a7079.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-29 17:14:42',1,'2026-04-29 17:14:42'),(1149,17,3,'phrase','take .... seriously','take .... seriously','take .... seriously','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nPhrase 短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n认真对待……；重视……\r\n\r\n= to think something is important and give it proper attention\r\n认为某件事很重要，并认真处理它。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\ntake something seriously  = not ignore it  = 不忽视，认真看待。\r\n\r\n比如： take safety seriously  重视安全\r\n\r\ntake feedback seriously  认真对待反馈\r\n\r\ntake the problem seriously  重视这个问题\r\n\r\n🔍 seriously 的位置\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\ntake + something + seriously\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\ntake the problem seriously\r\ntake the warning seriously\r\ntake the customer’s concern seriously\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ take seriously the problem\r\n\r\n口语和普通写作中更自然的是：\r\n\r\n✅ take the problem seriously','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\ntake it seriously\r\n\r\n认真对待这件事\r\n\r\nYou should take it seriously.\r\n你应该认真对待这件事。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\ntake feedback seriously\r\n\r\n认真对待反馈\r\n\r\nI always take customer feedback seriously.\r\n我一直认真对待客户反馈。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\ntake safety seriously\r\n\r\n重视安全\r\n\r\nOur team takes safety seriously.\r\n我们团队非常重视安全。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\ntake this issue seriously\r\n\r\n认真对待这个问题\r\n\r\nWe need to take this issue seriously.\r\n我们需要认真对待这个问题。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 Work / Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nI took the risk seriously and discussed it with the team before making a decision.\r\n我认真对待这个风险，并在做决定前和团队进行了讨论。\r\n\r\nI take customer feedback seriously because it helps us improve the product.\r\n我认真对待客户反馈，因为它能帮助我们改进产品。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c48421b0d26544d789682e9497d26337.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-29 17:36:44',1,'2026-04-29 17:36:44'),(1150,17,4,'phrase','rotate to','rotate to','rotate to','Verb phrase 动词短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n旋转到……；轮换到……；切换到……\r\n\r\n= to turn or move something until it faces or reaches a particular position\r\n把某物转到某个方向、位置或状态。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n你可以记：\r\n\r\nrotate = move around a centre point\r\nrotate = 围绕中心点转动\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nrotate to = 转到某个方向 / 位置 / 状态.\r\n\r\n🔍 rotate vs turn\r\n\r\nturn  更普通，日常口语常用。\r\n\r\nTurn left. 向左转。\r\n\r\nrotate\r\n更偏技术、图像、地图、物体绕轴旋转。\r\n\r\nRotate the image 90 degrees.\r\n将图片旋转 90 度。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nrotate = 旋转 / 轮换\r\nrotate to + position / direction / role = 转到某个位置、方向或角色','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nrotate to the left / right\r\n\r\n向左 / 向右旋转\r\n\r\nRotate the image to the left.\r\n把图片向左旋转。\r\n\r\nRotate the map to the right.\r\n把地图向右旋转。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nrotate to 90 degrees\r\n\r\n旋转到 90 度\r\n\r\nRotate the object to 90 degrees.\r\n把这个物体旋转到 90 度。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nrotate to landscape mode\r\n\r\n旋转到横屏模式\r\n\r\nRotate your phone to landscape mode.\r\n把手机旋转到横屏模式。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nrotate to another team / role\r\n\r\n轮换到另一个团队 / 岗位\r\n\r\nI rotated to another team for three months.\r\n我轮换到另一个团队工作了三个月。\r\n\r\n💻 IT / UI Sentence\r\n\r\nUsers can rotate the image to the correct direction before saving it.\r\n用户可以在保存前把图片旋转到正确方向。\r\n\r\nThe screen will rotate to landscape mode automatically.\r\n屏幕会自动旋转到横屏模式。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/77335e684827408b958b4bb69b897375.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-30 05:30:33',1,'2026-04-30 05:30:33'),(1151,17,5,'phrase','key lesson','key lesson','key lesson','Noun phrase 名词短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n关键经验；重要教训；最重要的收获\r\n\r\n= the most important thing you learned from an experience\r\n从一次经历中学到的最重要的东西。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nkey 像一把钥匙 🔑，能打开重点。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nkey lesson = the lesson that unlocks the main learning\r\nkey lesson = 打开核心收获的“关键经验”。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nkey = important / main\r\n重要的；主要的\r\n\r\nlesson = something you learn from experience\r\n从经历中学到的经验或教训\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nkey lesson = the most important thing learned\r\n关键经验 / 最重要的收获\r\n\r\n🔍 lesson vs key lesson\r\n\r\nlesson  = 经验；教训；课程\r\n\r\nI learned a lesson from this mistake.  我从这个错误中学到了一个教训。\r\n\r\nkey lesson = 最重要、最核心的经验/教训\r\n\r\nThe key lesson was to check the data before making a decision.\r\n最关键的经验是在做决定前检查数据。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\na key lesson\r\n\r\n一个关键经验\r\n\r\nA key lesson from this project was to communicate risks early.\r\n这个项目的一个关键经验是要尽早沟通风险。\r\n\r\nthe key lesson I learned\r\n\r\n我学到的关键经验\r\n\r\nThe key lesson I learned was not to make assumptions too early.\r\n我学到的关键经验是不要太早做假设。\r\n\r\nthe key lesson I emphasised\r\n\r\n我强调的关键经验\r\n\r\nThe key lesson I emphasised was to validate assumptions before making decisions.\r\n我强调的关键经验是在做决定前验证假设。\r\n\r\nkey lessons from the project\r\n\r\n项目中的关键经验\r\n\r\nWe discussed the key lessons from the migration project.\r\n我们讨论了迁移项目中的关键经验。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nThe key lesson I learned was that technical decisions should be based on verified information, not assumptions.\r\n我学到的关键经验是，技术决策应该基于经过验证的信息，而不是假设。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2f9a177386e64bef90bd83fcecf012ab.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-30 07:18:02',1,'2026-04-30 07:18:02'),(1152,17,6,'vocab','portrait / landscape','portrait   landscape','portrait  landscape','1. portrait\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n竖版；纵向；人像\r\n\r\n= taller than it is wide\r\n高度大于宽度的方向。\r\n\r\n2. landscape\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n横版；横向；风景\r\n\r\n= wider than it is tall\r\n宽度大于高度的方向。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nportrait 通常拍人像，人是站着的，所以是 竖的。\r\n\r\nlandscape 通常拍风景，风景很宽，所以是 横的。\r\n\r\nPortrait is tall. Landscape is wide.   Portrait 是竖的，Landscape 是横的。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nportrait 就是：\r\n\r\nvertical orientation\r\n竖向 / 竖版\r\n\r\n常见场景：\r\n\r\n* portrait mode 竖屏模式\r\n* portrait photo 人像照片\r\n* portrait layout 竖版布局\r\n\r\n🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nlandscape 就是：\r\n\r\nhorizontal orientation\r\n横向 / 横版\r\n\r\n常见场景：\r\n\r\n* landscape mode 横屏模式\r\n* landscape photo 风景照片\r\n* landscape layout 横版布局','✅ Portrait Examples\r\n\r\nPlease rotate the image to portrait mode.\r\n请把图片旋转到竖屏模式。\r\n\r\nThe poster should be in portrait layout.\r\n这个海报应该用竖版布局。\r\n\r\n✅ Landscape Examples\r\n\r\nPlease rotate your phone to landscape mode.\r\n请把手机旋转到横屏模式。\r\n\r\nThe vocabulary card should be in landscape layout.\r\n这张单词卡应该用横版布局。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/18e4cdd1711f4bf6995c00a803c8ef80.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-30 14:48:20',1,'2026-04-30 14:48:20'),(1153,17,7,'vocab','coast vs shore','coast vs shore','coast vs shore','1. coast\r\n\r\n🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nNoun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n海岸；沿海地区\r\n\r\n2. shore\r\n\r\n🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nNoun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n岸；岸边；水边\r\n\r\n= the land right next to the sea, lake, or river\r\n紧挨着海、湖或河的岸边。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\ncoast 想成地图上一整条海岸线：\r\n\r\ncoast = big sea-side area\r\ncoast = 大范围沿海地区\r\n\r\nshore 想成你脚踩着水边的沙子：\r\n\r\nshore = the edge of the water\r\nshore = 水边那条岸\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nThe coast is the region. The shore is the edge.\r\ncoast 是沿海区域，shore 是水边边缘。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\ncoast 更强调 沿海区域 / 海岸线附近的大范围地区。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\nthe east coast 东海岸\r\n\r\nthe coast of New Zealand  新西兰海岸 / 新西兰沿海地区\r\n\r\n🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nshore 更强调 水边那一条地方，可以是海边、湖边、河边。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\nlake shore  湖岸\r\n\r\nriver shore  河岸\r\n\r\non the shore  在岸边','✅ coast Examples\r\n\r\nWe drove along the coast.\r\n我们沿着海岸开车。\r\n\r\nChristchurch is near the east coast of the South Island.\r\n基督城靠近南岛东海岸。\r\n\r\n✅ shore Examples\r\n\r\nThe children played on the shore.\r\n孩子们在岸边玩。\r\n\r\nWe walked along the shore of the lake.\r\n我们沿着湖边散步。\r\n\r\n💼 GIS / Map Sentence\r\n\r\nThe site is located near the coast, but not directly on the shore.\r\n该地点靠近沿海地区，但不直接位于岸边。\r\n\r\nCoastal areas may include towns, roads, and land near the sea, while the shore refers to the narrow area where land meets water.\r\ncoastal areas 可以包括靠近海的城镇、道路和土地，而 shore 指陆地与水体接触的狭窄区域。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b6dd0e94e52646ff9661d428f5eca49e.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-04-30 16:48:31',1,'2026-04-30 16:48:31'),(1154,17,8,'phrase','come down the road','come down the road','come down the road','Phrase 短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n以后会出现；未来会发生；接下来会来\r\n\r\n= something will happen or appear in the future\r\n表示某件事情在将来会出现。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象你站在路边，看见远处有东西慢慢过来。\r\n\r\ncome down the road = something is coming later\r\n以后会有事情慢慢出现。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\ndown the road\r\n= later / in the future\r\n= 以后，将来\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncome down the road\r\n= come in the future\r\n= 以后会出现 / 将来会发生','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nopportunities coming down the road\r\n\r\n未来会出现的机会\r\n\r\nI can see some good opportunities coming down the road.\r\n我觉得以后会有一些不错的机会出现。\r\n\r\nchanges coming down the road\r\n\r\n未来会有变化\r\n\r\nThere are some big changes coming down the road.\r\n接下来会有一些大的变化。\r\n\r\nproblems coming down the road\r\n\r\n以后可能出现的问题\r\n\r\nWe need to prepare for the problems coming down the road.\r\n我们需要为以后可能出现的问题做准备。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/29163e36dfa94d8292d1f1d5110d1496.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 07:49:00',1,'2026-05-01 07:49:00'),(1155,17,9,'vocab','overly','overly','overly','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nAdverb 副词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n过于；过分地；太……\r\n\r\n= too much; more than is reasonable or necessary\r\n超过合理或必要的程度。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nover- = 超过\r\n-ly = 副词后缀\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\noverly = too much\r\noverly = 过头了 / 太过了。\r\n\r\n🔍 overly vs too\r\n\r\ntoo\r\n更口语，最常用。\r\n\r\nThis is too difficult.\r\n这太难了。\r\n\r\noverly\r\n更正式一点，常用于工作、学术、书面表达。\r\n\r\nThe process is overly complicated.\r\n这个流程过于复杂。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\noverly = too much\r\n\r\n它通常带一点负面意思，表示：太过了，不太合适。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\n* overly complicated.     过于复杂\r\n* overly confident.    过于自信\r\n* overly sensitive      过于敏感\r\n* overly strict      过于严格','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\noverly complicated\r\n\r\n过于复杂\r\n\r\nThe system design is overly complicated.  这个系统设计过于复杂。\r\n\r\noverly cautious  过于谨慎\r\n\r\nWe should manage risks, but we should not be overly cautious.   我们应该管理风险，但不应该过于谨慎。\r\n\r\noverly dependent on    过于依赖……\r\n\r\nThe old system was overly dependent on manual checks.   旧系统过于依赖人工检查。\r\n\r\noverly optimistic  过于乐观\r\n\r\nThe timeline was overly optimistic.  这个时间计划过于乐观。\r\n\r\n💼 Work / Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nI avoided making an overly complex solution and focused on a practical design that the team could maintain. \r\n我避免设计过于复杂的方案，而是专注于一个团队可以维护的实用设计。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d8373828e0294c95834016eedc1365ea.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 09:32:36',1,'2026-05-01 09:32:36'),(1156,17,10,'vocab','energetic','energetic','energetic','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nAdjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n精力充沛的；充满活力的\r\n\r\n= having a lot of energy and enthusiasm\r\n有很多精力和热情。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nenergy = 能量\r\nenergetic = full of energy\r\n\r\n记住一句：\r\n\r\nenergetic = full of energy\r\nenergetic = 充满能量的 / 很有活力的。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nenergetic = full of energy\r\n\r\n可以形容：\r\n\r\n* 人很有活力\r\n* 孩子精力旺盛\r\n* 活动很热闹\r\n* 工作状态很积极\r\n\r\n🔍 energetic vs active\r\n\r\nenergetic\r\n强调“有精力、有活力”。\r\n\r\nShe is energetic.\r\n她很有活力。\r\n\r\nactive\r\n强调“经常活动、积极参与”。\r\n\r\nShe is active in class.\r\n她在课堂上很积极。\r\n\r\n一个人可以：\r\n\r\nactive but not energetic\r\n经常参与，但看起来不一定精力旺盛。\r\n\r\n也可以：\r\n\r\nenergetic and active\r\n既有活力，又积极参与。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nan energetic person\r\n\r\n精力充沛的人\r\n\r\nHe is an energetic person.\r\n他是一个精力充沛的人。\r\n\r\nenergetic children\r\n\r\n精力旺盛的孩子们\r\n\r\nThe children are very energetic today.\r\n孩子们今天特别有活力。\r\n\r\nfeel energetic\r\n\r\n感觉精力充沛\r\n\r\nI feel energetic after a good sleep.\r\n睡了个好觉后，我感觉精力充沛。\r\n\r\nan energetic team\r\n\r\n充满活力的团队\r\n\r\nWe have an energetic and motivated team.\r\n我们有一个充满活力、积极主动的团队。\r\n\r\n💼 Work / Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nI try to stay energetic and positive at work, especially when the team is under pressure.\r\n我努力在工作中保持精力充沛和积极，尤其是在团队有压力的时候。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/cd862feba3be4cc385cc754d9afcc168.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 09:39:00',1,'2026-05-01 09:39:00'),(1157,17,11,'phrase','triage','triage','triage','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nNoun / Verb\r\n名词 / 动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n分诊；优先级分类；按紧急程度处理\r\n\r\n= to quickly assess problems, cases, or tasks and decide which ones need attention first\r\n快速判断问题、任务或情况的严重程度，然后决定先处理哪个。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象急诊室门口有很多病人，护士先判断：\r\n\r\nred = urgent\r\nyellow = wait\r\ngreen = less urgent\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ntriage = sort by urgency\r\ntriage = 按紧急程度分类处理。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\ntriage originally comes from medical emergency situations.\r\n\r\n在医院急诊里，医生会先判断：\r\n\r\n谁最严重？谁需要马上处理？谁可以稍等？\r\n\r\n在工作和 IT 里，triage 就是：\r\n\r\n快速筛选问题，判断优先级，然后安排处理顺序。\r\n\r\n🔍 triage vs prioritize\r\n\r\nprioritize\r\n= decide what is more important\r\n决定什么更重要，范围更广。\r\n\r\nWe need to prioritize these tasks.\r\n我们需要给这些任务排优先级。\r\n\r\ntriage\r\n= quickly assess and sort issues, often when there are many problems or limited time\r\n通常用于问题很多、时间有限时，快速判断严重程度并分流。\r\n\r\nWe need to triage these bugs before the release.\r\n发布前我们需要对这些 bug 做优先级分类。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nbug triage\r\n\r\nbug 优先级分类 / bug 分流\r\n\r\nWe had a bug triage meeting this morning.\r\n今天早上我们开了一个 bug 分流会议。\r\n\r\ntriage issues  筛选并判断问题优先级\r\n\r\nThe support team triaged the customer issues.\r\n支持团队对客户问题进行了优先级分类。\r\n\r\ntriage process. 问题分流流程 / 优先级判断流程\r\n\r\nWe improved the triage process to respond to urgent incidents faster.\r\n我们改进了分流流程，以便更快响应紧急事件。\r\n\r\nmedical triage  医疗分诊\r\n\r\nMedical triage helps doctors treat the most urgent patients first.\r\n医疗分诊帮助医生优先治疗最紧急的病人。\r\n\r\n💼 Work / Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nI helped triage production issues by assessing their impact, urgency, and affected users before assigning them to the right team.\r\n我会根据影响范围、紧急程度和受影响用户来协助判断生产问题的优先级，然后分配给合适的团队。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/4221db4eb30c4095afed7fc878a3f5b8.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 09:45:31',1,'2026-05-01 09:45:31'),(1158,17,12,'phrase','diagnose','diagnose','diagnose','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nVerb 动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n诊断；判断问题原因；查明问题\r\n\r\n= to identify what a problem or illness is by examining the signs or symptoms\r\n通过检查现象、症状或线索，找出问题是什么。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象医生拿着听诊器检查病人，或者工程师看日志查 bug。\r\n\r\ndiagnose = examine signs and find the cause\r\ndiagnose = 检查迹象，然后找出原因。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\ndiagnose = find out what the problem is\r\n\r\n可以用于两类场景：\r\n\r\n1. 医疗场景\r\n医生诊断疾病。\r\n\r\nThe doctor diagnosed the patient with flu.\r\n医生诊断这个病人得了流感。\r\n\r\n2. 技术 / 工作场景\r\n排查系统、网络、设备的问题。\r\n\r\nWe need to diagnose the network issue.\r\n我们需要诊断这个网络问题。\r\n\r\n🔍 diagnose vs identify\r\n\r\nidentify  = 找出 / 识别，范围更广。\r\n\r\nWe identified the problem.   我们识别出了问题。\r\n\r\ndiagnose  = 更强调通过分析现象、症状、日志、数据，判断原因。\r\n\r\nWe diagnosed the root cause.   我们诊断出了根本原因。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\ndiagnose a problem 诊断问题 / 查明问题原因\r\n\r\nWe need to diagnose the problem before fixing it.\r\n修复之前，我们需要先查明问题原因。\r\n\r\ndiagnose an issue. 诊断一个问题\r\n\r\nThe engineer diagnosed the issue quickly.  工程师很快找出了问题原因。\r\n\r\ndiagnose a disease   诊断疾病\r\n\r\nThe doctor diagnosed the disease early.  医生很早就诊断出了这种疾病。\r\n\r\ndiagnose with   被诊断为……\r\n\r\nShe was diagnosed with diabetes.   她被诊断出患有糖尿病。\r\n\r\n💻 IT / Work Sentence\r\n\r\nI checked the logs and metrics to diagnose the root cause of the production issue.\r\n我检查了日志和指标，以诊断生产问题的根本原因。\r\n\r\nWe used monitoring tools to diagnose the performance problem.\r\n我们使用监控工具来诊断性能问题。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/cacc690d15e642338e9eb21890b012d7.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 10:02:42',1,'2026-05-01 10:02:42'),(1159,17,13,'phrase','physician','physician','physician','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nNoun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n医生；内科医生\r\n\r\n= a medical doctor, especially one who diagnoses illness and treats patients without surgery\r\n医生，尤其指通过诊断和药物治疗病人的医生，通常不是外科医生。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n可以这样记：\r\n\r\nphysician = physical health doctor\r\nphysician = 负责身体健康的医生。\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nA physician diagnoses and treats illness, usually without surgery.\r\nphysician 是诊断和治疗疾病的医生，通常不做手术。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nphysician = doctor\r\n\r\n但它比 doctor 更正式一点。\r\n\r\n在很多语境里：\r\n\r\nphysician 更偏 内科医生 / 临床医生\r\nsurgeon 是 外科医生\r\n\r\n🔍 physician vs doctor\r\n\r\ndoctor\r\n更常用，日常口语里说“医生”。\r\n\r\nI need to see a doctor.\r\n我需要看医生。\r\n\r\nphysician\r\n更正式，常用于医疗、书面语、医院或保险文件中。\r\n\r\nPlease consult your physician before taking this medicine.\r\n服用这种药前请咨询医生。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔍 physician vs surgeon\r\n\r\nphysician\r\n通常通过检查、诊断、药物治疗病人。\r\n\r\nThe physician diagnosed the patient with flu.\r\n医生诊断病人得了流感。\r\n\r\nsurgeon\r\n做手术的医生。\r\n\r\nThe surgeon performed the operation.\r\n外科医生进行了手术。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\na family physician\r\n\r\n家庭医生\r\n\r\nYou should see your family physician first.\r\n你应该先去看你的家庭医生。\r\n\r\na general physician\r\n\r\n普通内科医生 / 全科医生\r\n\r\nA general physician can diagnose common illnesses.\r\n普通内科医生可以诊断常见疾病。\r\n\r\nconsult a physician\r\n\r\n咨询医生 / 看医生\r\n\r\nPlease consult a physician if the symptoms continue.\r\n如果症状持续，请咨询医生。\r\n\r\nphysician’s advice\r\n\r\n医生的建议\r\n\r\nFollow your physician’s advice carefully.\r\n认真遵循医生的建议。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/033727aa958448efa1451713feb5ff6f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 10:07:28',1,'2026-05-01 10:07:28'),(1160,17,14,'vocab','emergency vs emerge','emergency vs emerge','emergency vs emerge','1. emergency\r\n\r\n🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nNoun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n紧急情况；突发事件\r\n\r\n= a serious or dangerous situation that needs immediate action\r\n需要立刻处理的严重或危险情况。\r\n\r\n2. emerge\r\n\r\n🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nVerb 动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n出现；浮现；显现；冒出来\r\n\r\n= to appear or become known\r\n某物出现，或者某个事实逐渐被人知道。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nemerge = something comes out / appears  出现\r\n\r\nemergency = something suddenly emerges and needs urgent action. 突然出现、需要马上处理的情况\r\n\r\n一句话记：\r\n\r\nWhen a serious problem emerges, it can become an emergency.\r\n当一个严重问题出现时，它可能变成紧急情况。','✅ Emergency Common Usage\r\n\r\nan emergency   一个紧急情况\r\n\r\nThis is an emergency.   这是紧急情况。\r\n\r\nemergency room / ER   急诊室\r\n\r\nHe was taken to the emergency room.   他被送去了急诊室。\r\n\r\nemergency services  紧急服务，比如救护车、消防、警察\r\n\r\nCall emergency services immediately.   立即拨打紧急服务电话。\r\n\r\nin an emergency  在紧急情况下\r\n\r\nIn an emergency, call 111 in New Zealand.  在新西兰遇到紧急情况，拨打 111。\r\n\r\n✅ Emergy Common Usage\r\n\r\nemerge from somewhere  从某处出现\r\n\r\nThe sun emerged from behind the clouds.  太阳从云后露出来。\r\n\r\na problem emerges. 问题出现\r\n\r\nA new problem emerged during testing.  测试过程中出现了一个新问题。\r\n\r\ndetails emerge  细节浮现\r\n\r\nMore details emerged after the investigation.  调查后更多细节浮现出来。','💼 Work / IT Example\r\n\r\nDuring testing, a performance issue emerged, but it was not an emergency because it did not affect production users.\r\n测试过程中出现了一个性能问题，但它不是紧急情况，因为没有影响生产用户。\r\n\r\nA production outage is an emergency and needs immediate action.\r\n生产环境宕机是紧急情况，需要立即处理。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9352167b6a724086a5e4d3443ed11ad0.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 10:14:16',1,'2026-05-01 10:14:16'),(1161,17,15,'vocab','emerge / appear / present','emerge / appear / present','emerge / appear / present','1. emerge\r\n\r\n出现；浮现；显现出来\r\n\r\n重点是：\r\n原来不明显 / 不知道，现在慢慢出现或被发现。\r\n常用于：* 问题出现  * 事实浮现  * 细节显现  * 从某处出来\r\n\r\n2. appear\r\n\r\n出现；看起来；显得\r\n\r\n重点是：\r\n某物进入视野，或者某种情况看起来是这样。\r\n\r\n常用于：A. 真的出现  B. 看起来 / 似乎\r\n\r\n3. present\r\n\r\n这里要小心，present 作动词时一般不是普通的“出现”。\r\n\r\nA. present something   B. present a problem / challenge / risk  C. present itself','最推荐你记这三句\r\n\r\nA problem emerged during testing.\r\n测试过程中暴露出一个问题。\r\n\r\nAn error message appeared on the screen.\r\n屏幕上出现了一条错误信息。\r\n\r\nThis presents a risk to the project.\r\n这给项目带来了风险。\r\n\r\n一句话记忆\r\n\r\nappear = show up  普通出现。\r\n\r\nemerge = come out gradually / become known  逐渐浮现、被发现。\r\n\r\npresent = show something or cause something  展示某物，或者带来某种问题/风险。','2. appear\r\n\r\n出现；看起来；显得\r\n\r\n重点是：\r\n某物进入视野，或者某种情况看起来是这样。\r\n\r\n常用于：\r\n\r\nA. 真的出现\r\n\r\nA message appeared on the screen.\r\n屏幕上出现了一条消息。\r\n\r\nHe suddenly appeared at the door.\r\n他突然出现在门口。\r\n\r\nB. 看起来 / 似乎\r\n\r\nIt appears that the system is working now.\r\n看起来系统现在正常运行了。\r\n\r\nShe appears tired.\r\n她看起来很累。\r\n\r\n感觉： 最普通、最常用。\r\n\r\n3. present\r\n\r\n这里要小心，present 作动词时一般不是普通的“出现”。\r\n\r\nA. present something\r\n\r\n展示；呈现；提交；介绍\r\n\r\nI will present my project tomorrow.\r\n我明天要展示我的项目。\r\n\r\nThe chart presents rainfall patterns across Canterbury.\r\n这张图展示了坎特伯雷的降雨模式。\r\n\r\nB. present a problem / challenge / risk\r\n\r\n带来 / 造成 / 构成问题、挑战、风险\r\n\r\nThis presents a serious problem.\r\n这带来了一个严重问题。\r\n\r\nData inconsistency may present a risk during migration.\r\n数据不一致可能在迁移过程中带来风险。\r\n\r\nC. present itself\r\n\r\n机会 / 问题自己出现\r\n\r\n这个比较正式：\r\n\r\nA new opportunity presented itself.\r\n一个新机会出现了。\r\n\r\nA problem presented itself during testing.\r\n测试过程中出现了一个问题。\r\n\r\n但日常更常说：\r\n\r\nA new problem emerged during testing.','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2aae722dbfd946c198917598fa089323.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 10:23:29',1,'2026-05-01 10:23:29'),(1162,17,16,'phrase','come down to','come down to','come down to','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nPhrasal verb 短语动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n归结为；最终取决于；说到底是……\r\n\r\n= the most important factor or final reason is something\r\n表示最后真正重要的因素是什么。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象很多因素都在往下掉，最后只剩下最核心的一个因素。\r\n\r\ncome down to = finally be about\r\ncome down to = 最后归结为…… / 最终关键是……','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\ncome down to + noun / -ing\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n最后关键就是……\r\n归根到底取决于……\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nIt comes down to cost.  说到底就是成本问题。\r\n\r\nThe decision comes down to risk and customer impact.\r\n这个决定归根到底取决于风险和客户影响。\r\n\r\n🔍 come down to vs depend on\r\n\r\ndepend on\r\n= 取决于，比较普通。\r\n\r\nIt depends on the budget.\r\n这取决于预算。\r\n\r\ncome down to\r\n= 归根到底取决于，更强调“最后真正关键的是”。\r\n\r\nIt comes down to the budget.\r\n说到底还是预算问题。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\ncome down to cost\r\n\r\n归结为成本\r\n\r\nThe final decision came down to cost.\r\n最终决定取决于成本。\r\n\r\ncome down to timing\r\n\r\n归结为时间安排\r\n\r\nIt may come down to timing.\r\n这可能最终取决于时间安排。\r\n\r\ncome down to priorities\r\n\r\n归结为优先级\r\n\r\nIt comes down to priorities.\r\n说到底是优先级问题。\r\n\r\ncome down to whether…\r\n\r\n最终取决于是否……\r\n\r\nIt comes down to whether we can finish it before Friday.\r\n这最终取决于我们能不能在周五前完成。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 Work / Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nThe technical decision came down to balancing reliability, complexity, and maintenance cost.\r\n这个技术决策归根到底是要平衡可靠性、复杂度和维护成本。\r\n\r\nIn the end, it came down to whether the solution could support rollback safely.\r\n最后，关键在于这个方案是否能够安全支持回滚。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d01b7b2493464efbb17ebefeebf0ceea.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 10:57:08',1,'2026-05-01 10:57:08'),(1163,17,17,'vocab','practitioner','practitioner','practitioner','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nNoun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n从业者；执业人员；实践者\r\n\r\n= a person who works in a profession or regularly practises a skill\r\n从事某个专业工作，或经常实践某种技能的人。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\npractice = 实践 / 执业\r\npractitioner = 做这个实践的人\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nA practitioner is someone who practises a profession.\r\npractitioner 是从事某个专业实践的人。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\npractitioner 来自 practice。\r\n\r\n可以理解为：\r\n\r\nsomeone who practises a profession\r\n从事某个专业的人 / 实际做这个工作的人\r\n\r\n它比 worker 更正式，常用于专业领域。\r\n\r\n🔍 practitioner vs professional\r\n\r\npractitioner\r\n更强调“实际从事某项工作的人 / 实践者”。\r\n\r\nShe is a healthcare practitioner.\r\n她是一名医疗从业者。\r\n\r\nprofessional\r\n更强调“专业人士 / 职业化 / 有专业能力的人”。\r\n\r\nShe is a healthcare professional.\r\n她是一名医疗专业人士。\r\n\r\n很多时候两者可以接近，但：\r\n\r\npractitioner = person who practises the work\r\n实际执业/实践的人\r\n\r\nprofessional = qualified or skilled person\r\n有专业能力或资质的人','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nmedical practitioner\r\n\r\n医疗从业者 / 医生\r\n\r\nYou should consult a medical practitioner if the symptoms continue.\r\n如果症状持续，你应该咨询医疗从业者。\r\n\r\nlegal practitioner\r\n\r\n法律从业者\r\n\r\nA legal practitioner can give professional legal advice.\r\n法律从业者可以提供专业法律建议。\r\n\r\nIT practitioner\r\n\r\nIT 从业者\r\n\r\nAs an IT practitioner, I focus on system reliability and maintainability.\r\n作为 IT 从业者，我关注系统可靠性和可维护性。\r\n\r\nGIS practitioner\r\n\r\nGIS 从业者 / GIS 实践者\r\n\r\nGIS practitioners use spatial data to support planning and decision-making.\r\nGIS 从业者使用空间数据支持规划和决策。\r\n\r\n💼 Work / Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nAs a software engineering practitioner, I try to make technical decisions based on evidence, not assumptions.\r\n作为一名软件工程实践者，我尽量基于证据而不是假设来做技术决策。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/525687a716f340ecaae456b6f117325a.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 11:39:54',1,'2026-05-01 11:39:54'),(1164,17,18,'phrase','skewed','skewed','skewed','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nAdjective / past participle\r\n形容词 / 过去分词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n歪的；倾斜的；偏斜的；有偏差的\r\n\r\n= not straight, not balanced, or not fairly represented\r\n表示某物不正、不平衡，或者数据/观点有偏差。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象一个方框被拉歪了，或者一组数据向一边倒。\r\n\r\nskewed = not straight or not balanced\r\nskewed = 不直 / 不平衡 / 有偏差。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nskewed 有两个常见意思：\r\n\r\n1. 物体歪了 / 斜了\r\n\r\nThe picture is skewed.\r\n图片歪了。\r\n\r\nThe label is slightly skewed.\r\n标签有点歪。\r\n\r\n更口语可以说：\r\n\r\nIt’s a bit crooked.\r\n有点歪。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 数据 / 结果 / 观点有偏差\r\n\r\nThe data is skewed.\r\n数据有偏差 / 分布偏斜。\r\n\r\nThe result may be skewed by a small sample size.\r\n结果可能因为样本太小而有偏差。\r\n\r\nThe survey was skewed toward younger users.\r\n这个调查偏向年轻用户。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nslightly skewed\r\n\r\n有点歪 / 略微偏斜\r\n\r\nThe image is still slightly skewed.\r\n图片还是有点歪。\r\n\r\nskewed data\r\n\r\n偏斜数据 / 有偏数据\r\n\r\nSkewed data can affect the analysis result.\r\n有偏数据会影响分析结果。\r\n\r\nskewed results\r\n\r\n有偏差的结果\r\n\r\nThe results may be skewed because the sample size is too small.\r\n因为样本量太小，结果可能有偏差。\r\n\r\nskewed toward\r\n\r\n偏向于……\r\n\r\nThe dataset is skewed toward urban areas.\r\n这个数据集偏向城市区域。\r\n\r\n💼 Work / IT Sentence\r\n\r\nThe test results were skewed because most users came from the same region.\r\n测试结果有偏差，因为大多数用户来自同一个地区。\r\n\r\nThe chart looks slightly skewed, so we should adjust the layout.\r\n这个图表看起来有点歪，所以我们应该调整一下布局。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/de819912eaf14fa3a0f273e9f628a93d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 17:22:36',1,'2026-05-01 17:22:36'),(1165,17,19,'phrase','each and every','each and every','each and every','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nPhrase 短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n每一个；每一位；所有的每一个\r\n\r\n= every single one, with strong emphasis\r\n强调“一个都不漏”。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\neach = 每一个，强调个体\r\nevery = 每一个，强调整体\r\n\r\neach and every 放在一起，是加强语气：\r\n\r\neach and every = every single one\r\n每一个，全部，一个不落。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n你可以把 each and every 想成：\r\n\r\neach one + every one = no one is missed\r\n每一个 + 所有每一个 = 一个都不漏。\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nEach and every means every single one.\r\neach and every = 每一个都，一个不漏。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\neach and every one\r\n\r\n每一个人 / 每一个东西\r\n\r\nI want to thank each and every one of you.\r\n我想感谢你们每一位。\r\n\r\neach and every day\r\n\r\n每一天，天天\r\n\r\nShe works hard each and every day.\r\n她每天都努力工作。\r\n\r\neach and every customer\r\n\r\n每一位客户\r\n\r\nWe take each and every customer seriously.\r\n我们认真对待每一位客户。\r\n\r\neach and every detail\r\n\r\n每一个细节\r\n\r\nWe checked each and every detail before release.\r\n发布前我们检查了每一个细节。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 Work / Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nIn the migration project, we checked each and every critical data field to reduce the risk of data inconsistency.\r\n在迁移项目中，我们检查了每一个关键数据字段，以降低数据不一致的风险。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/17b413904179423e888d01251f7296c6.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 17:26:06',1,'2026-05-01 17:26:06'),(1166,17,20,'phrase','as an example','as an example','as an example','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nPhrase 短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n作为一个例子；举个例子\r\n\r\n= used to introduce one example of what you are talking about\r\n用来引出一个例子，说明前面的观点。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n可以这样记：\r\n\r\nas an example = use this to explain the idea\r\nas an example = 用这个例子来说明观点。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nas an example\r\n= for example / as one example\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n我拿这个作为例子来说。\r\n\r\n🔍 as an example vs for example\r\n\r\nfor example\r\n更常用，更自然，用来直接举例。\r\n\r\nFor example, we used Kafka to handle asynchronous processing.\r\n\r\nas an example\r\n强调“把某个东西作为例子”。\r\n\r\nAs an example, we can look at the migration project.','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\ntake … as an example\r\n\r\n以……为例\r\n\r\nTake Christchurch as an example.\r\n以基督城为例。\r\n\r\nTake the migration project as an example.\r\n以这个迁移项目为例。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nuse … as an example\r\n\r\n用……作为例子\r\n\r\nI used this project as an example in my interview answer.\r\n我在面试回答中用这个项目作为例子。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nas an example of…\r\n\r\n作为……的例子\r\n\r\nThis case can be used as an example of good teamwork.\r\n这个案例可以作为良好团队合作的例子。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 Work / Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nAs an example, in my previous company, I worked on a membership system migration project.\r\n举个例子，在我上一家公司，我参与过一个会员系统迁移项目。\r\n\r\n更自然也可以说：\r\n\r\nFor example, in my previous company, I worked on a membership system migration project.\r\n例如，在我上一家公司，我参与过一个会员系统迁移项目。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e8d916a5c3134a3287514c7dd0bcca93.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 17:36:01',1,'2026-05-01 17:36:01'),(1167,17,21,'vocab','gigantic','gigantic','gigantic','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nAdjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n巨大的；庞大的；非常大的\r\n\r\n= extremely large\r\n非常大，比 big 或 huge 语气更强。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\ngigantic 和 giant 很像。\r\n\r\n你可以这样记：\r\n\r\ngigantic = giant-sized\r\ngigantic = 像巨人一样大的。\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nGigantic means extremely large.\r\ngigantic = 巨大的 / 非常大的。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\ngigantic = very, very big\r\n\r\n可以形容：\r\n\r\n* gigantic building     巨大的建筑\r\n* gigantic problem     巨大的问题\r\n* gigantic animal      巨大的动物\r\n* gigantic amount of data    海量数据\r\n\r\n🔍 gigantic vs huge vs giant\r\n\r\nhuge\r\n最常用，意思是“很大”。\r\n\r\nThis is a huge house.\r\n这是一栋很大的房子。\r\n\r\ngigantic\r\n更夸张，强调“大得惊人”。\r\n\r\nThis is a gigantic house.\r\n这是一栋巨大的房子。\r\n\r\ngiant\r\n可以作形容词，也可以作名词，常表示“巨型的 / 巨人”。\r\n\r\na giant panda\r\n大熊猫\r\n\r\na giant tree\r\n一棵巨大的树','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\na gigantic building\r\n\r\n一座巨大的建筑\r\n\r\nThere is a gigantic building in the city centre.\r\n市中心有一座巨大的建筑。\r\n\r\na gigantic problem\r\n\r\n一个巨大的问题\r\n\r\nData inconsistency became a gigantic problem during the migration.\r\n数据不一致在迁移过程中变成了一个巨大问题。\r\n\r\na gigantic amount of data\r\n\r\n海量数据\r\n\r\nThe system needs to process a gigantic amount of data every day.\r\n这个系统每天需要处理海量数据。\r\n\r\ngigantic waves\r\n\r\n巨浪\r\n\r\nGigantic waves hit the shore during the storm.\r\n暴风雨期间，巨浪拍打着岸边。\r\n\r\n💼 Work / IT Sentence\r\n\r\nWe had to migrate a gigantic amount of historical data to the new system.\r\n我们必须把海量历史数据迁移到新系统中。\r\n\r\nA small design mistake can become a gigantic problem later.\r\n一个小的设计错误后面可能会变成一个巨大问题。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/91379da10e35409f82a79e3768a30a9e.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 17:44:08',1,'2026-05-01 17:44:08'),(1168,17,22,'sentence','be filled with','be filled with','be filled with','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nPhrase 短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n充满……；装满……；满是……\r\n\r\n= to contain a lot of something\r\n表示某个地方、容器、时间、生活、心情等“充满了某种东西”。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nbe filled with + noun\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n里面有很多……\r\n被……装满 / 充满\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe room is filled with people.\r\n房间里挤满了人。\r\n\r\nHer eyes were filled with tears.\r\n她眼里充满了泪水。\r\n\r\n🔍 be filled with vs be full of\r\n\r\nbe full of\r\n更口语，更常用。\r\n\r\nThe room is full of people.\r\n房间里满是人。\r\n\r\nbe filled with\r\n稍微正式一点，也更强调“被装满 / 充满”的状态。\r\n\r\nThe room is filled with people.\r\n房间里挤满了人。\r\n\r\n两个很多时候可以互换。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nbe filled with joy\r\n\r\n充满喜悦\r\n\r\nThe children were filled with joy.\r\n孩子们充满了喜悦。\r\n\r\nbe filled with people\r\n\r\n挤满了人\r\n\r\nThe hall was filled with people.\r\n大厅里挤满了人。\r\n\r\nbe filled with hope\r\n\r\n充满希望\r\n\r\nHis heart was filled with hope.\r\n他的心中充满希望。\r\n\r\nbe filled with data\r\n\r\n充满数据 / 装满数据\r\n\r\nThe database was filled with historical records.\r\n数据库里装满了历史记录。\r\n\r\n💼 Work / IT Sentence\r\n\r\nThe migration table was filled with historical product records, so we had to validate the data carefully.\r\n迁移表里有大量历史产品记录，所以我们必须仔细验证数据。\r\n\r\nThe dashboard is filled with useful metrics for monitoring system health.\r\n这个仪表盘充满了用于监控系统健康状态的有用指标。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/1415ffed054e4f3296012bc671c34950.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 19:03:05',1,'2026-05-01 19:03:05'),(1169,17,23,'vocab','accomplish','accomplish','accomplish','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nVerb 动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n完成；实现；达成\r\n\r\n= to successfully finish something or achieve a goal\r\n成功完成某件事，或实现某个目标。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n可以这样记：\r\n\r\naccomplish = complete + success\r\naccomplish = 成功地完成。\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nAccomplish means to successfully finish something important or difficult.\r\naccomplish = 成功完成重要或有难度的事情。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\naccomplish = successfully complete / achieve\r\n\r\n它通常强调：\r\n\r\n这件事不是随便做完，而是有目标、有难度，并且成功完成了。\r\n\r\n🔍 accomplish vs complete vs achieve\r\ncomplete ： 完成 ，强调把事情做完\r\nachieve ： 实现；取得 ，强调达到目标或成果\r\naccomplish ： 成功完成；达成  强调完成有意义或有难度的事情','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\naccomplish a goal\r\n\r\n实现目标\r\n\r\nWe worked together to accomplish our goal.\r\n我们一起努力实现了目标。\r\n\r\naccomplish a task\r\n\r\n完成任务\r\n\r\nI accomplished the task before the deadline.\r\n我在截止日期前完成了任务。\r\n\r\naccomplish a mission\r\n\r\n完成使命 / 任务\r\n\r\nThe team accomplished the mission successfully.\r\n团队成功完成了任务。\r\n\r\naccomplish something important\r\n\r\n完成重要的事情\r\n\r\nWe accomplished something important in this project.\r\n我们在这个项目中完成了一件重要的事。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 Work / Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nIn the migration project, we accomplished the goal of keeping the old and new systems in sync without interrupting the business.\r\n在迁移项目中，我们实现了让新旧系统保持同步且不中断业务的目标。\r\n\r\nI felt proud because we accomplished the project under tight time pressure.\r\n我感到自豪，因为我们在时间紧张的情况下完成了这个项目。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d0c00f098a384e5393daa347f27e49fe.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 19:15:36',1,'2026-05-01 19:15:36'),(1170,17,24,'phrase','from scratch','from scratch','from scratch','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nPhrase 短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n从零开始；从头做起；白手起家\r\n\r\n= starting from the very beginning, without using something already prepared\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象你做蛋糕，不用蛋糕粉，也不用半成品，而是从面粉、鸡蛋、糖开始。\r\n\r\nfrom scratch = from zero, using no ready-made base\r\nfrom scratch = 从零开始，不用现成基础。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nfrom scratch = from zero\r\n\r\n表示不是在已有基础上改，而是从最开始自己做。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI built this website from scratch.\r\n我从零开始做了这个网站。\r\n\r\nWe had to start from scratch.\r\n我们不得不从头开始。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nbuild something from scratch\r\n\r\n从零开始搭建某物\r\n\r\nI built the system from scratch.\r\n我从零开始搭建了这个系统。\r\n\r\nstart from scratch\r\n\r\n从头开始\r\n\r\nAfter the design changed, we had to start from scratch.\r\n设计变更后，我们不得不从头开始。\r\n\r\nmake something from scratch\r\n\r\n从头制作某物\r\n\r\nShe made the cake from scratch.\r\n她从零开始做了这个蛋糕。\r\n\r\nlearn something from scratch\r\n\r\n从零开始学某事\r\n\r\nI learned Python from scratch.\r\n我从零开始学 Python。\r\n\r\n💼 Work / IT Sentence\r\n\r\nI built the project framework from scratch, including the basic structure, coding standards, and Git workflow.\r\n我从零开始搭建了项目框架，包括基础结构、编码规范和 Git 工作流。\r\n\r\nWe did not reuse the old module. Instead, we redesigned the new system from scratch.\r\n我们没有复用旧模块，而是从零重新设计了新系统。\r\n\r\n🔍 from scratch vs from the beginning\r\n\r\nfrom the beginning\r\n= 从开始，可以只是时间顺序上的“从一开始”。\r\n\r\nI watched the movie from the beginning.\r\n我从头开始看了这部电影。\r\n\r\nfrom scratch\r\n= 从零开始，强调没有现成基础、自己重新做。\r\n\r\nI built the app from scratch.\r\n我从零开始做了这个应用。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3b5a5911d27e4b538ab5014b224fc786.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-01 19:35:48',1,'2026-05-01 19:35:48'),(1171,17,25,'phrase','get dressed','get dressed','get dressed','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nVerb phrase 动词短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n穿好衣服；把衣服穿上\r\n\r\n= to put on clothes\r\n表示从没穿好衣服的状态，变成穿好衣服的状态。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nget + adjective/past participle 常表示“变成某种状态”。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nget dressed = become dressed\r\nget dressed = 变成穿好衣服的状态。\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nGet dressed before you go out.\r\n出门前把衣服穿好。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nget dressed\r\n= put on your clothes\r\n\r\n通常用于早上起床、出门前、洗澡后：\r\n\r\nI need to get dressed.\r\n我需要穿衣服了。\r\n\r\nHurry up and get dressed.\r\n快点穿好衣服。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nget dressed\r\n\r\n穿好衣服\r\n\r\nI got dressed quickly this morning.\r\n我今天早上很快穿好了衣服。\r\n\r\nget dressed for school\r\n\r\n穿好衣服去上学\r\n\r\nThe children are getting dressed for school.\r\n孩子们正在穿衣服准备去上学。\r\n\r\nget dressed up\r\n\r\n打扮起来；穿得正式一点\r\n\r\nWe got dressed up for the party.\r\n我们为参加派对特意打扮了一下。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔍 get dressed vs dress\r\n\r\nget dressed\r\n强调动作：穿好衣服。\r\n\r\nI got dressed at 7 a.m.\r\n我早上 7 点穿好衣服。\r\n\r\ndress\r\n可以表示“给某人穿衣服”，也可以表示“穿着某种风格”。\r\n\r\nShe dressed the baby.\r\n她给宝宝穿衣服。\r\n\r\nHe dresses well.\r\n他穿得很好。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3a38da07876c4653be7579776fa3e592.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-02 13:57:03',1,'2026-05-02 13:57:03'),(1172,17,26,'phrase','pop out','pop out','pop out','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nPhrasal verb 短语动词\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n突然出来；冒出来；短暂出去一下\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\npop 有“啪一下、突然”的感觉。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\npop out = come out suddenly / go out briefly\r\npop out = 突然冒出来 / 短暂出去一下。','1. 突然出来 / 冒出来\r\n\r\npop out 可以表示某个东西突然出现、弹出来。\r\n\r\nThe message popped out on the screen.\r\n屏幕上突然弹出了一条消息。\r\n\r\nHis eyes almost popped out when he saw the price.\r\n他看到价格时，眼睛都快瞪出来了。\r\n\r\nA button popped out of my shirt.\r\n我衬衫上的一颗扣子突然掉出来了 / 弹出来了。\r\n\r\n\r\n2. 短暂出去一下\r\n\r\n在英式 / 新西兰口语里，pop out 很常用，意思是：\r\n\r\n出去一下，很快回来\r\n\r\nI’ll pop out for a coffee.\r\n我出去买杯咖啡，很快回来。\r\n\r\nShe popped out to the supermarket.\r\n她去超市一下。\r\n\r\nI need to pop out for a few minutes.\r\n我需要出去几分钟。\r\n\r\n\r\n3. 不能用于“衣服上架”\r\n\r\n你刚才那句：\r\n\r\n❌ Is there any clothes need to pop out?\r\n\r\n不自然，因为 clothes don’t pop out。\r\n如果你想说“衣服需要摆出去 / 上架”，用：\r\n\r\nDo any clothes need to go out?\r\n有没有衣服需要上架？\r\n\r\nDo we need to put any clothes out?\r\n我们需要把什么衣服摆出去吗？\r\n\r\nAre there any clothes that need to go out on the racks?\r\n有没有衣服需要挂到衣架上？','🔍 pop out vs put out\r\n\r\npop out\r\n= 自己突然出来 / 人出去一下\r\n\r\nI’ll pop out for lunch.\r\n我出去吃个午饭。\r\n\r\nput out\r\n= 把东西摆出去 / 放出来\r\n\r\nWe need to put these clothes out.\r\n我们需要把这些衣服摆出去。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/96ee8a1dc7c941778531d5e0c628ff1f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 06:41:20',1,'2026-05-03 06:41:20'),(1173,17,27,'phrase','short on','short on','short on','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nPhrase 短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n缺少……；……不够；手头……不足\r\n\r\n= not having enough of something\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象你的钱、时间、人手“短了一截”。\r\n\r\nshort on = not enough\r\nshort on = 不够 / 缺少。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nshort on + noun\r\n意思是： ……不够   缺少……\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI’m short on cash.  我现金不够。\r\n\r\nWe’re short on time.  我们时间不够。\r\n\r\n🔍 short on vs lack\r\n\r\nshort on\r\n更口语、自然。\r\n\r\nWe’re short on time.\r\n我们时间不够。\r\n\r\nlack\r\n更正式，常用于书面或正式表达。\r\n\r\nThe project lacks sufficient resources.\r\n这个项目缺少足够资源。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nshort on cash\r\n\r\n现金不够\r\n\r\nSorry, I’m a bit short on cash.\r\n不好意思，我现金有点不够。\r\n\r\nshort on change\r\n\r\n零钱不够\r\n\r\nI’m short on change at the moment.\r\n我现在零钱不太够。\r\n\r\nshort on time\r\n\r\n时间不够\r\n\r\nWe’re short on time, so let’s keep it brief.\r\n我们时间不够，所以简单说。\r\n\r\nshort on staff\r\n\r\n人手不够\r\n\r\nWe’re short on staff today.\r\n我们今天人手不够。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/4223baf366014dfea70f38659ec80fb8.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 07:10:24',1,'2026-05-03 07:10:24'),(1174,17,28,'phrase','bring it up','bring it up','bring it up','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nPhrasal verb 短语动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n拿上来；拿过来；提起某事；提出某个话题\r\n\r\n= to bring something to a place, or to mention a topic in conversation\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nup 有“拿到前面 / 提到讨论中”的感觉。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nbring it up = bring it to attention\r\nbring it up = 把它带到大家注意的地方。\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nBring it up can mean “mention it” or “bring it to a place.”\r\nbring it up 可以表示“提起这件事”，也可以表示“把它拿过来”。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nbring it up 有两个常见意思：\r\n\r\n1. 拿上来 / 拿过来\r\n\r\n在商店、收银台、楼上楼下场景里：\r\n\r\nbring it up\r\n把它拿上来 / 拿过来\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI brought it up to the counter.\r\n我把它拿到收银台了。\r\n\r\nThis happened when I brought it up.\r\n这是我把它拿过来的时候发生的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 提起某事 / 提出话题\r\n\r\n在聊天、会议、讨论中：\r\n\r\nbring it up\r\n提起这件事 / 提出这个话题\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nHe brought it up in the meeting.\r\n他在会议上提到了这件事。\r\n\r\nThanks for bringing it up.\r\n谢谢你提起这个。\r\n\r\n🔍 bring it up vs pick it up\r\n\r\nbring it up\r\n= 把它拿过来 / 提起这件事\r\n\r\nI brought it up to the counter.\r\n我把它拿到收银台。\r\n\r\npick it up\r\n= 把它拿起来\r\n\r\nI picked it up and the handle broke.\r\n我拿起来时把手坏了。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nbring it up to the counter\r\n\r\n把它拿到收银台\r\n\r\nI brought it up to the counter, but then I noticed it was damaged.\r\n我把它拿到收银台，但后来发现它坏了。\r\n\r\nbring it up in a meeting\r\n\r\n在会议中提起这件事\r\n\r\nI will bring it up in the next meeting.\r\n我会在下次会议中提这件事。\r\n\r\nbring up an issue\r\n\r\n提出一个问题\r\n\r\nShe brought up an important issue.\r\n她提出了一个重要问题。\r\n\r\nbring up a topic\r\n\r\n提出一个话题\r\n\r\nI didn’t want to bring up that topic.\r\n我不想提那个话题。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 Work / Interview Sentence\r\n\r\nDuring the discussion, I brought up the risk of data inconsistency and suggested using CDC to keep the systems in sync.\r\n在讨论中，我提出了数据不一致的风险，并建议使用 CDC 来保持系统同步。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/177f8a268f494ae78dc637cc0c493074.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 07:18:43',1,'2026-05-03 07:18:43'),(1175,17,29,'phrase','go ahead','go ahead','go ahead','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nPhrase / Phrasal verb 短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n请吧；可以；继续；开始做吧\r\n\r\n= used to give someone permission to do something, or tell them to continue\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象有人站在你前面，问：“我可以走了吗？”\r\n你说：\r\n\r\nGo ahead.\r\n往前走吧 / 可以做了。\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nGo ahead = you can do it / continue.\r\ngo ahead = 可以做 / 继续吧。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\ngo ahead 很常用，意思像中文里的：\r\n\r\n好的，你做吧。\r\n可以，继续吧。\r\n请说 / 请开始。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nGo ahead.\r\n\r\n可以 / 请吧 / 继续。\r\n\r\nCan I ask a question?\r\n我可以问个问题吗？\r\n\r\nSure, go ahead.\r\n当然，请问吧。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\ngo ahead with something\r\n\r\n继续做某事 / 推进某事\r\n\r\nWe decided to go ahead with the project.\r\n我们决定继续推进这个项目。\r\n\r\nThe team will go ahead with the new design.\r\n团队会继续采用新设计。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\ngo ahead and do something\r\n\r\n直接做某事 / 去做吧\r\n\r\nYou can go ahead and submit the form.\r\n你可以直接提交表格。\r\n\r\nGo ahead and take a seat.\r\n请坐吧。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🛒 Shop / Daily Sentence\r\n\r\nGo ahead. I’ll wait here.\r\n你先去吧，我在这儿等。\r\n\r\nYou can go ahead and pay at the counter.\r\n你可以直接去收银台付款。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔍 go ahead vs continue\r\n\r\ncontinue\r\n更正式，意思是“继续”。\r\n\r\nPlease continue.\r\n请继续。\r\n\r\ngo ahead\r\n更口语，常用来表示“可以，做吧”。\r\n\r\nGo ahead.\r\n可以，继续吧。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d04ae4f04dec491488e71371e6d1d53e.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 07:27:08',1,'2026-05-03 07:27:08'),(1176,17,30,'phrase','put one off / put someone off','put one off / put someone off','put one off / put someone off','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nPhrasal verb 短语动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n让某人反感；让某人失去兴趣；让某人不想做某事\r\n\r\n= to make someone dislike something or not want to do something\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象你本来想靠近一样东西，但它让你往后退了一步。\r\n\r\nput me off = push me away from liking it\r\nput me off = 把我从“喜欢/想做”那里推开。\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nPut someone off means to make someone lose interest.\r\nput someone off = 让某人失去兴趣 / 被劝退。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nput someone off\r\n= 让某人“不想要了 / 不感兴趣了 / 被劝退了”\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe smell put me off.\r\n这个味道让我不想要了。\r\n\r\nThe high price put me off.\r\n这个高价格让我打消了念头。\r\n\r\n🔍 put off vs put someone off\r\n\r\nput off\r\n= 推迟\r\n\r\nWe had to put off the meeting.\r\n我们不得不推迟会议。\r\n\r\nput someone off\r\n= 让某人反感 / 不想做\r\n\r\nThe price put me off.\r\n这个价格让我不想买了。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\nput me off\r\n\r\n让我反感 / 让我不想要\r\n\r\nThe rude service really put me off.\r\n糟糕的服务真的让我很反感。\r\n\r\nput someone off doing something\r\n\r\n让某人不想做某事\r\n\r\nThe bad weather put me off going out.\r\n糟糕的天气让我不想出门。\r\n\r\nput someone off something\r\n\r\n让某人对某事失去兴趣\r\n\r\nThe smell put me off the food.\r\n这个味道让我不想吃这个食物了。\r\n\r\nDon’t let it put you off\r\n\r\n别因此被劝退 / 别因此失去兴趣\r\n\r\nThe first lesson is hard, but don’t let it put you off.\r\n第一节课很难，但别因此被劝退。\r\n\r\n🛒 Shop / Daily Sentence\r\n\r\nThe stain on the shirt put me off.\r\n衣服上的污渍让我不想买了。\r\n\r\nThe damage put me off buying it.\r\n这个损坏让我不想买它了。\r\n\r\nI liked it at first, but the scratch put me off.\r\n我一开始挺喜欢的，但那个划痕让我不想买了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/bd8b491f6f51444c986b513dda5cf9a3.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 07:44:14',1,'2026-05-03 07:44:14'),(1177,17,31,'vocab','rough','rough','rough','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nAdjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 Meaning\r\n\r\n粗糙的；不平整的；艰难的；大概的\r\n\r\n= not smooth, not easy, or not exact\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象一块石头表面不平，摸起来刮手：\r\n\r\nrough = not smooth\r\nrough = 不光滑 / 不平顺。\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nRough can describe texture, time, estimate, or behaviour.\r\nrough 可以形容触感、经历、估算，也可以形容行为粗暴。','🧩 Simple Understanding\r\n\r\nrough 有几个常见意思：\r\n\r\n1. 粗糙的 / 不光滑的\r\n\r\nThe surface is rough.\r\n表面很粗糙。\r\n\r\nThis fabric feels a bit rough.\r\n这块布摸起来有点粗糙。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 艰难的 / 难熬的\r\n\r\nI had a rough day.\r\n我今天过得很不顺 / 很累。\r\n\r\nIt was a rough week.\r\n这一周挺难熬的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 大概的 / 粗略的\r\n\r\nCan you give me a rough estimate?\r\n你能给我一个大概估算吗？\r\n\r\nThis is just a rough idea.\r\n这只是一个粗略想法。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n4. 粗暴的 / 不温柔的\r\n\r\nDon’t be too rough with it.\r\n别太粗暴地弄它。\r\n\r\nThe kids were playing rough.\r\n孩子们玩得有点太猛了。','✅ Common Usage\r\n\r\na rough surface\r\n\r\n粗糙的表面\r\n\r\nThe wall has a rough surface.\r\n这面墙表面很粗糙。\r\n\r\na rough day\r\n\r\n难熬的一天\r\n\r\nI had a rough day at work.\r\n我今天上班很累 / 很不顺。\r\n\r\na rough estimate\r\n\r\n粗略估算\r\n\r\nThe repair will cost around $200, as a rough estimate.\r\n粗略估计，维修大概要 200 刀。\r\n\r\nrough edges\r\n\r\n粗糙边缘；还不完善的地方\r\n\r\nThe design still has some rough edges.\r\n这个设计还有一些不完善的地方。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🛒 Shop / Second-hand Store Sentence\r\n\r\nThat’s just a little bit of rough wear.\r\n那只是有一点点磨损。\r\n\r\nThe fabric feels a bit rough, but it’s still wearable.\r\n这料子摸起来有点粗糙，但还是能穿。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f0da5d2b7ada4bdfa40371ca04ed47b7.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 07:52:02',1,'2026-05-03 07:52:02'),(1178,17,32,'vocab','drumroll','drumroll','drumroll','🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n“来点鼓声！”\r\n“激动人心的时刻到了！”\r\n“马上要揭晓了！”\r\n\r\n🔍 拆词记忆\r\n\r\ndrum = 鼓\r\nroll = 连续滚动、连续发出声音\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ndrum + roll = drumroll\r\n鼓连续滚动般地响：咚咚咚咚咚……','💬 最常用表达\r\n\r\nDrumroll, please.\r\n来点鼓声！/ 要揭晓了！\r\n\r\n这个表达很常见，语气轻松、幽默。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🗣️ 场景例句\r\n\r\nDrumroll, please… the winner is Sarah!\r\n来点鼓声……获胜者是 Sarah！\r\n\r\nOkay, drumroll, please. Let’s see the final price.\r\n好，激动人心的时刻到了。我们来看看最终价格。\r\n\r\nAnd now, drumroll… I passed the exam!\r\n现在揭晓……我考试通过了！','✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nDrumroll is the exciting drum sound before big news is announced.\r\ndrumroll 就是宣布重要消息前制造气氛的鼓声。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/72bb2f7914354548b36bcc0e27e29770.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 08:21:15',1,'2026-05-03 08:21:15'),(1179,17,33,'vocab','specialize','specialize','specialize','🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以翻译成：\r\n\r\n专门从事/专攻/擅长某个领域/专门研究\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nspecialize = focus on one specific area\r\n专注在某一个特定领域，而不是做很多杂的东西。','💬 常见结构\r\n\r\nspecialize in + 名词 / 领域\r\n\r\nI specialize in backend development.\r\n我专攻后端开发。\r\n\r\nThis company specializes in skincare products.\r\n这家公司专门做护肤品。\r\n\r\nThe doctor specializes in children’s health.\r\n这位医生专门研究儿童健康 / 是儿科方面的专家。','🧑‍💻 结合你的背景\r\n\r\n你可以说：\r\n\r\nI’m a software engineer, and I specialize in backend systems and microservices.\r\n我是一名软件工程师，专攻后端系统和微服务。\r\n\r\n或者面试中说：\r\n\r\nI specialize in Java backend development, distributed systems, and system performance optimisation.\r\n我专攻 Java 后端开发、分布式系统和系统性能优化。\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nspecialize in something = 专门做某一类事情。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3515f5d6127a43a28c9da67e8b05885c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 16:15:28',1,'2026-05-03 16:15:28'),(1180,17,34,'vocab','hospital gown','hospital gown','hospital gown','n. 病号服；医院检查服','🔍 拆词记忆\r\n\r\nhospital = 医院\r\ngown = 长袍；罩袍；宽松的衣服\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nhospital gown = 医院里穿的宽松病号服\r\n\r\n💬 常见表达\r\n\r\nput on a hospital gown 穿上病号服\r\n\r\nchange into a hospital gown 换上病号服\r\n\r\ntake off the hospital gown 脱下病号服','🗣️ 场景例句\r\n\r\nThe nurse asked me to put on a hospital gown.\r\n护士让我穿上病号服。\r\n\r\nPlease change into this hospital gown before the examination.\r\n检查前请换上这件病号服。\r\n\r\nDo I need to wear a hospital gown for the scan?\r\n做扫描检查需要穿病号服吗？\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nA hospital gown is the loose clothing patients wear in hospital.\r\nhospital gown 就是病人在医院检查或治疗时穿的宽松病号服。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/be80abffbaf2493695eb8c222d0c8f49.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 16:21:32',1,'2026-05-03 16:21:32'),(1181,17,35,'vocab','sanitary','sanitary','sanitary','adj. 卫生的；清洁的；符合卫生标准的\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以翻译成：\r\n\r\n卫生的\r\n清洁的\r\n符合卫生标准的\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意\r\n\r\nsanitary 比 clean 更正式一点，通常强调“符合卫生要求、对健康安全”。\r\n\r\nclean = 干净\r\nsanitary = 卫生、符合健康标准\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nSanitary means clean and safe for people’s health.\r\nsanitary 就是干净卫生、对健康安全。','💬 常见用法\r\n\r\nsanitary conditions\r\n卫生条件\r\n\r\nsanitary facilities\r\n卫生设施，比如厕所、洗手设施\r\n\r\na sanitary environment\r\n卫生的环境\r\n\r\nsanitary products\r\n卫生用品，尤其常指女性经期用品','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nThe kitchen must be kept sanitary.\r\n厨房必须保持卫生。\r\n\r\nThe hospital has strict sanitary standards.\r\n医院有严格的卫生标准。\r\n\r\nAre the toilets sanitary?\r\n厕所卫生吗？\r\n\r\nSanitary products are available in the bathroom.\r\n卫生用品在洗手间里有。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2634d4779399496badd6ebbf5265b411.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 16:28:34',1,'2026-05-03 16:28:34'),(1182,17,36,'phrase','to recuperate','to recuperate','to recuperate','v. 恢复；康复；休养\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nrecuperate = to get better after illness, injury, or tiredness\r\n意思是：生病、受伤或太累之后慢慢恢复过来。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以翻译成：康复/恢复体力/休养恢复\r\n\r\nTo recuperate means to rest and get your strength back.\r\nrecuperate 就是通过休息慢慢恢复体力和健康。','💬 常见用法\r\n\r\nrecuperate from + illness/injury/surgery\r\n从疾病/受伤/手术中恢复\r\n\r\ntake time to recuperate\r\n花时间休养恢复\r\n\r\nrecuperate at home\r\n在家休养','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nShe is recuperating from surgery.\r\n她正在手术后康复。\r\n\r\nI need a few days to recuperate.\r\n我需要几天时间恢复一下。\r\n\r\nHe went home to recuperate after the illness.\r\n他病后回家休养。\r\n\r\n🔍 和 recover 的区别\r\n\r\nrecover 更常用，意思比较广：恢复、找回、康复。\r\nrecuperate 更强调：休养一段时间后慢慢恢复体力或健康。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI’m recovering from a cold.\r\n我感冒正在恢复。更日常。\r\n\r\nI’m recuperating at home after surgery.\r\n我手术后正在家休养。更正式、更强调休养。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/5c32c874dd06491b986d10b0a21a0629.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 18:03:23',1,'2026-05-03 18:03:23'),(1183,17,37,'phrase','jump the line','jump the line','jump the line','phrase. 插队；不按顺序排队\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\njump the line = go in front of others without waiting your turn\r\n意思是：不等自己的顺序，直接插到别人前面。\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nTo jump the line means to go ahead of others without waiting your turn.\r\njump the line 就是不等自己顺序，直接插队。','🌏 新西兰更常用说法\r\n\r\n在新西兰，更自然的是：\r\n\r\njump the queue\r\n插队\r\n\r\n在美国英语里常说：\r\n\r\ncut in line\r\n插队\r\n\r\n💬 常见表达\r\n\r\nDon’t jump the line.\r\n别插队。\r\n\r\nHe jumped the queue.\r\n他插队了。\r\n\r\nSomeone cut in line in front of me.\r\n有人插到我前面了。','🗣️ 实用场景句\r\n\r\nSorry, there’s a queue here.\r\n不好意思，这边在排队。\r\n\r\nSorry, I think the line starts back there.\r\n不好意思，队伍应该从那边开始。\r\n\r\nExcuse me, we’re waiting in line.\r\n不好意思，我们正在排队。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/fafe4b061c48472cbeb98ae725ff4a78.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 18:07:29',1,'2026-05-03 18:07:29'),(1184,17,38,'phrase','step up','step up','step up','phr. v. 加强；站出来承担；走上前；提升\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nstep up 的感觉是：\r\n向前一步，承担更多，或者把力度提高。\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nStep up means to move forward, take responsibility, or increase effort.\r\nstep up 就是“向前一步”：站出来承担，或者加大力度。','常见意思有：\r\n\r\n1. 站出来 / 主动承担\r\nHe stepped up when the team needed help.\r\n团队需要帮助时，他站了出来。\r\n\r\n2. 加强 / 加大力度\r\nWe need to step up our efforts.\r\n我们需要加大努力。\r\n\r\n3. 提高 / 升级\r\nThe company stepped up production.\r\n公司提高了产量。\r\n\r\n4. 走上前 / 上前一步\r\nPlease step up to the counter.\r\n请走到柜台前。\r\n\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\nstep up efforts\r\n加大努力\r\n\r\nstep up security\r\n加强安保\r\n\r\nstep up production\r\n提高产量\r\n\r\nstep up to help\r\n站出来帮忙\r\n\r\nstep up to the challenge\r\n迎接挑战；站出来应对挑战','🗣️ 口语例句\r\n\r\nSomeone needs to step up.\r\n得有人站出来。\r\n\r\nThanks for stepping up.\r\n谢谢你主动承担。\r\n\r\nWe should step up our practice.\r\n我们应该加强练习。\r\n\r\nCan you step up to the counter, please?\r\n麻烦你到柜台前来一下。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/78ccaf3bd6364a29a2e0f056d814d874.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 18:14:47',1,'2026-05-03 18:14:47'),(1185,17,39,'phrase','run into issues','run into issues','run into issues','遇到问题；碰到麻烦\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nrun into 本来有“撞上、偶然遇到”的意思。\r\n所以 run into issues 就是：做事情过程中突然碰到问题。','💬 常见用法\r\n\r\nrun into an issue with + something\r\n在某方面遇到一个问题\r\n\r\nrun into some issues during + something\r\n在某个过程中遇到一些问题\r\n\r\nrun into technical issues\r\n遇到技术问题\r\n\r\nrun into a problem\r\n遇到一个问题','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nI ran into an issue with the payment.\r\n我付款时遇到了一个问题。\r\n\r\nWe ran into some issues during testing.\r\n我们在测试过程中遇到了一些问题。\r\n\r\nThe team ran into technical issues yesterday.\r\n团队昨天遇到了一些技术问题。\r\n\r\nLet me know if you run into any issues.\r\n如果你遇到任何问题，告诉我。\r\n\r\n✅ 更自然表达\r\n\r\n在工作/项目里，你可以说：\r\n\r\nWe ran into a few issues, but we fixed them.\r\n我们遇到了一些问题，但已经修好了。\r\n\r\nI ran into an issue when setting up the environment.\r\n我配置环境时遇到了一个问题。\r\n\r\nIf you run into any issues, just let me know.\r\n如果你遇到任何问题，直接告诉我。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/dd7bb8ea551b456482da2321a52df5ac.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 18:27:58',1,'2026-05-03 18:27:58'),(1186,17,40,'phrase','pull someone into the conversation','pull someone into the conversation','pull someone into the conversation','把某人拉进谈话；让某人加入讨论\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\npull someone into the conversation = invite or involve someone in a conversation\r\n意思是：让某人参与到当前的谈话或讨论里。\r\n\r\n这里的 pull 不是“真的拉”，而是“带入、引入、让参与”。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n把某人拉进谈话\r\n让某人加入讨论\r\n把某人带入这个话题','💬 常见用法\r\n\r\npull someone into the conversation\r\n把某人拉进谈话\r\n\r\nbring someone into the conversation\r\n让某人加入谈话，更自然、更常用\r\n\r\ninclude someone in the conversation\r\n把某人包括进讨论里，更正式一点\r\n\r\nget someone involved\r\n让某人参与进来','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nLet’s pull Sarah into the conversation.\r\n我们把 Sarah 拉进来一起聊吧。\r\n\r\nI didn’t mean to pull you into this conversation.\r\n我不是故意把你卷进这个话题里的。\r\n\r\nHe tried to pull me into the conversation, but I didn’t know what to say.\r\n他想让我加入谈话，但我不知道该说什么。\r\n\r\nCan we bring Tom into the conversation? He knows more about this.\r\n我们能把 Tom 拉进来聊吗？他更了解这个。\r\n\r\n🌏 更自然表达\r\n\r\n日常口语中，bring someone into the conversation 比 pull someone into the conversation 更自然一些。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nLet’s bring her into the conversation.\r\n我们让她也参与进来吧。\r\n\r\nI’ll bring James into the conversation because he worked on this part.\r\n我会让 James 加入讨论，因为这一部分是他做的。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 小区别\r\n\r\npull someone into the conversation\r\n有时感觉这个人可能本来不想参与，有点“被拉进来”的感觉。\r\n\r\nbring someone into the conversation\r\n更中性、更自然，表示“让某人加入讨论”。\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nPull someone into the conversation means to involve someone in a discussion.\r\n就是：让某人参与到谈话或讨论里。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/bf033e94ad224657a889248e9c86c6fc.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 18:37:03',1,'2026-05-03 18:37:03'),(1187,17,41,'vocab','cognitive','cognitive','cognitive','adj. 认知的；和思考、理解、学习、记忆有关的\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\ncognitive = related to thinking and understanding\r\n意思是：和大脑的思考、理解、学习、记忆、判断有关。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以翻译成：\r\n\r\n认知的\r\n思维方面的\r\n和大脑理解能力有关的','💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\ncognitive ability\r\n认知能力\r\n\r\ncognitive skills\r\n认知技能，比如记忆、注意力、解决问题能力\r\n\r\ncognitive development\r\n认知发展，常用于儿童成长\r\n\r\ncognitive decline\r\n认知能力下降，常用于老年人或疾病场景\r\n\r\ncognitive load\r\n认知负荷，学习或工作时大脑承受的信息量','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nReading helps children develop cognitive skills.\r\n阅读有助于孩子发展认知能力。\r\n\r\nSleep affects our cognitive performance.\r\n睡眠会影响我们的认知表现。\r\n\r\nToo much information can increase cognitive load.\r\n太多信息会增加认知负荷。\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nCognitive means related to how the brain thinks, learns, remembers, and understands.\r\ncognitive 就是和大脑如何思考、学习、记忆和理解有关的。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/72d7c9964154427b834b85871994098b.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 19:15:38',1,'2026-05-03 19:15:38'),(1188,17,42,'vocab','simultaneous','simultaneous','simultaneous','adj. 同时发生的；同步的\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nsimultaneous = happening at the same time\r\n意思是：两个或多个事情在同一时间发生。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以翻译成：同时的/同时发生的/同步的\r\n\r\n🔄 词形变化\r\n\r\nsimultaneous = 形容词：同时的\r\nsimultaneously = 副词：同时地\r\nsimultaneity = 名词：同时性','💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\nsimultaneous translation / interpretation\r\n同声传译\r\n\r\nsimultaneous events\r\n同时发生的事件\r\n\r\nsimultaneous access\r\n同时访问\r\n\r\nsimultaneous requests\r\n并发请求 / 同时请求\r\n\r\nsimultaneous update\r\n同步更新 / 同时更新','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nThe two meetings were simultaneous.\r\n这两个会议是同时进行的。\r\n\r\nThe system can handle multiple simultaneous requests.\r\n这个系统可以处理多个并发请求。\r\n\r\nThere was simultaneous translation during the conference.\r\n会议期间有同声传译。\r\n\r\nThey made the announcement simultaneously.\r\n他们同时发布了公告。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b5e2c06b83ee429b8a3b1d99a68a0de8.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 19:20:23',1,'2026-05-03 19:20:23'),(1189,17,43,'vocab','conference','conference','conference','n. 会议；大会；研讨会\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nconference = a large formal meeting where people discuss a topic\r\n通常指很多人参加的正式会议、大会、学术会议或行业会议。\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nA conference is a large formal meeting about a specific topic.\r\nconference 就是围绕某个主题举行的正式大型会议。','🔍 和 meeting 的区别\r\n\r\nmeeting\r\n普通会议，可大可小，比如团队开会。\r\n\r\nconference\r\n更正式、更大型，通常有主题、演讲、嘉宾、议程。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe have a team meeting at 10.\r\n我们 10 点有团队会议。\r\n\r\nI’m going to a tech conference.\r\n我要去参加一个科技大会。\r\n\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\nattend a conference\r\n参加会议\r\n\r\nhold a conference\r\n举办会议\r\n\r\na business conference\r\n商务会议\r\n\r\nan academic conference\r\n学术会议\r\n\r\na press conference\r\n新闻发布会\r\n\r\na video conference\r\n视频会议','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nI’m attending a conference next week.\r\n我下周要参加一个会议。\r\n\r\nThe company held a conference in Auckland.\r\n公司在奥克兰举办了一场大会。\r\n\r\nThere was simultaneous translation during the conference.\r\n会议期间有同声传译。\r\n\r\nThey answered questions at the press conference.\r\n他们在新闻发布会上回答了问题。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/4deb4ed37eb5471aab6274c283a9a1ca.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 19:24:23',1,'2026-05-03 19:24:23'),(1190,17,44,'phrase','get something sorted','get something sorted','get something sorted','🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n搞定某事\r\n把某事处理好\r\n把某事安排妥当\r\n把问题解决掉\r\n \r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nget something sorted = deal with something and make it organised or fixed\r\n意思是：把一个问题、事情、安排处理好，让它不再乱或不再有问题。','💬 常见用法\r\n\r\nget it sorted  把它搞定\r\n\r\nget this sorted  把这个处理好\r\n\r\nget everything sorted  把所有事情都安排好\r\n\r\nget the problem sorted 把这个问题解决\r\n\r\nget my visa sorted  把我的签证弄好','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nI need to get my car sorted.\r\n我得把车的问题处理好。\r\n\r\nDon’t worry, we’ll get it sorted.\r\n别担心，我们会把它搞定的。\r\n\r\nI’m trying to get my documents sorted.\r\n我正在整理/处理我的文件。\r\n\r\nHave you got your accommodation sorted?\r\n你的住宿安排好了吗？\r\n\r\n🌏 新西兰口语感觉\r\n\r\n在新西兰，sorted 很常用，意思接近：\r\n\r\nall good / organised / fixed\r\n都好了 / 安排好了 / 修好了\r\n\r\n比如别人帮你解决问题后可以说：\r\n\r\nSweet, that’s sorted. Cheers.\r\n太好了，搞定了，谢谢。\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nGet something sorted means to fix it, organise it, or deal with it properly.\r\n就是：把某件事处理好、安排好、搞定。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c767518781674e8ba737db6a7f6dd534.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-04 08:48:09',1,'2026-05-04 08:48:09'),(1191,17,45,'vocab','mendacity','mendacity','mendacity','n. 撒谎；虚假；不诚实\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nmendacity = the habit or act of lying\r\n意思是：说谎、不诚实、虚假陈述。\r\n\r\n这个词比较正式，常见于书面语、新闻评论、政治评论、文学里。日常口语里一般不会常用。','💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\npolitical mendacity  政治谎言 / 政治上的不诚实\r\n\r\na culture of mendacity 充满谎言的文化\r\n\r\naccuse someone of mendacity  指责某人撒谎 / 不诚实\r\n\r\nthe mendacity of the claim. 这个说法的虚假性','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nHe was accused of mendacity.\r\n他被指责撒谎。\r\n\r\nThe report exposed the mendacity of the company’s claims.\r\n这份报告揭露了该公司说法的虚假性。\r\n\r\nPeople were tired of political mendacity.\r\n人们厌倦了政治谎言。\r\n\r\n🔍 更常用的口语表达\r\n\r\n日常更常说：\r\n\r\nlying = 撒谎\r\ndishonesty = 不诚实\r\nfalse claims = 虚假说法\r\ndeception = 欺骗\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nHe is lying.\r\n他在撒谎。\r\n\r\nThat’s dishonest.\r\n那样不诚实。\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nMendacity means lying or being dishonest.\r\nmendacity 就是“撒谎、不诚实”，但语气比较正式。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e10cb9b82d9a458a9da5aefdaa127fef.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-04 08:57:02',1,'2026-05-04 08:57:02'),(1192,17,46,'phrase','be keen to figure it out','be keen to figure it out','be keen to figure it out','很想把它弄明白 / 很想搞清楚 / 很愿意想办法解决\r\n拆开看\r\n\r\nbe keen to + do something\r\n很想做某事；很愿意做某事\r\n\r\nfigure it out\r\n弄明白；想清楚；解决出来\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nI’m keen to figure it out.\r\n我很想把它弄明白。\r\n我愿意想办法解决。','I’m keen to figure it out, but I need a bit more time.\r\n我挺想把它弄明白的，但我还需要一点时间。\r\n\r\nWe’re keen to figure out what went wrong.\r\n我们很想搞清楚哪里出了问题。\r\n\r\nShe’s keen to figure out how the system works.\r\n她很想弄明白这个系统是怎么运行的。\r\n\r\n更自然口语\r\n\r\nI’m keen to work it out. 我挺想把它解决掉。\r\n\r\nI’m keen to get it sorted. 我挺想把它搞定。\r\n\r\nI’m keen to understand what happened. 我挺想弄清楚发生了什么。\r\n\r\n注意：如果后面有具体内容，常说：\r\n\r\nfigure out + something\r\nfigure out the problem\r\n弄清楚这个问题\r\n\r\nfigure out what happened  弄清楚发生了什么\r\n\r\nfigure it out 里的 it 指前面已经提到的事情。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ccce1eceff9743b09d0beaf005689838.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-04 09:04:59',1,'2026-05-04 09:04:59'),(1193,17,47,'phrase','rip someone off','rip someone off','rip someone off','phrasal verb. 宰客；敲竹杠；骗某人的钱\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nrip someone off = to charge someone too much money or cheat them financially\r\n意思是：收别人过高的价格，或者用不公平的方式骗钱。','💬 常见用法\r\n\r\nrip someone off坑某人 / 宰某人\r\n\r\nget ripped off  被坑了 / 被宰了\r\n\r\na rip-off  坑人货 / 太贵不值 / 骗钱的东西','They ripped me off at that shop.\r\n那家店坑了我。\r\n\r\nI think we got ripped off.\r\n我觉得我们被宰了。\r\n\r\n$50 for this? That’s a rip-off!\r\n这个要 50 刀？太坑了吧！\r\n\r\nBe careful, some tourist shops might rip you off.\r\n小心点，有些游客商店可能会宰客。\r\n\r\n🌏 新西兰口语感觉\r\n\r\n在新西兰，rip-off 很常见，尤其买东西觉得太贵、不值时可以说：\r\n\r\nThat’s a bit of a rip-off.\r\n这有点坑人 / 有点太贵了。\r\n\r\n更委婉一点可以说：\r\n\r\nThat seems a bit pricey.\r\n这个感觉有点贵。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意\r\n\r\nrip someone off 语气比较直接，带有“对方不诚实/不公平”的感觉。\r\n如果只是觉得贵，不想太冲，可以用：\r\n\r\nIt’s a bit expensive.\r\n有点贵。\r\n\r\nThat seems overpriced.\r\n这个感觉价格虚高。\r\n\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nRip someone off means to cheat someone by making them pay too much.\r\nrip someone off 就是通过让别人付太多钱来坑他们。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/247ecb1a32bd4faf8a3049926475ff31.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-04 09:08:55',1,'2026-05-04 09:08:55'),(1194,17,48,'phrase','mansion','mansion','mansion','n. 豪宅；大宅；大房子\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nmansion = a very large and expensive house\r\n意思是：非常大、很贵、通常很豪华的房子。','💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\na luxury mansion\r\n豪华大宅\r\n\r\na huge mansion\r\n巨大的豪宅\r\n\r\na beachfront mansion\r\n海边豪宅\r\n\r\na historic mansion\r\n历史悠久的大宅\r\n\r\nlive in a mansion\r\n住在豪宅里','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nHe lives in a mansion by the sea.\r\n他住在海边的一栋豪宅里。\r\n\r\nThe mansion has ten bedrooms and a swimming pool.\r\n这栋豪宅有十间卧室和一个游泳池。\r\n\r\nThey bought a luxury mansion in Auckland.\r\n他们在奥克兰买了一栋豪宅。\r\n\r\n🔍 和 house 的区别\r\n\r\nhouse 普通的“房子”。\r\n\r\nmansion   很大、很贵、很豪华的房子。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThis is my house.  这是我的房子。\r\n\r\nThat’s a mansion!  那可是豪宅啊！','/static/uploads/english_note_item/0982f6202fc14d4cb10a4ed00efcb32c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-04 09:12:59',1,'2026-05-04 09:12:59'),(1195,17,49,'phrase','jargon','jargon','jargon','n. 行话；术语；专业黑话\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\njargon = special words used by a particular group or profession\r\n意思是：某个行业、专业或群体内部常用的特殊词汇。','💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\ntechnical jargon. 技术术语 / 技术黑话\r\n\r\nmedical jargon  医学术语\r\n\r\nlegal jargon  法律术语\r\n\r\nbusiness jargon  商务套话 / 商业术语\r\n\r\navoid jargon 避免使用专业黑话\r\n\r\ntoo much jargon  太多术语','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nThe document is full of technical jargon.\r\n这份文件充满了技术术语。\r\n\r\nPlease avoid jargon and explain it in simple language.\r\n请避免使用术语，用简单的话解释。\r\n\r\nDoctors sometimes use medical jargon that patients don’t understand.\r\n医生有时会用病人听不懂的医学术语。\r\n\r\nCan you explain that without jargon?\r\n你能不用专业术语解释一下吗？\r\n\r\n🔍 和 terminology 的区别\r\n\r\nterminology\r\n更中性，指某个领域的“术语体系”。\r\n\r\njargon\r\n有时带一点负面感觉，表示“别人听不懂的专业黑话”。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThis course introduces basic programming terminology.\r\n这门课介绍基础编程术语。\r\n\r\nThe explanation had too much jargon.\r\n这个解释用了太多听不懂的行话。\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nJargon means special words used in a field that ordinary people may not understand.\r\njargon 就是某个领域里普通人可能听不懂的专业行话。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/47c19b49ded741b7b411699ec06a91c0.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-04 09:32:20',1,'2026-05-04 09:32:20'),(1196,17,50,'phrase','ridiculous','ridiculous','ridiculous','adj. 荒谬的；可笑的；离谱的\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nridiculous = very silly, unreasonable, or hard to believe\r\n意思是：非常不合理、很傻、很离谱，让人觉得难以相信。','💬 常见用法\r\n\r\nThat’s ridiculous.  太离谱了。/ 太荒唐了。\r\n\r\na ridiculous price  离谱的价格\r\n\r\na ridiculous idea  荒唐的想法\r\n\r\nlook ridiculous  看起来很可笑 / 很滑稽\r\n\r\nsound ridiculous  听起来很荒唐\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意\r\n\r\nridiculous 语气比较强，直接说别人 You’re ridiculous 可能有点冒犯。\r\n如果只是表达“不太合理”，可以说：\r\n\r\nThat doesn’t really make sense.\r\n这不太说得通。\r\n\r\nThat seems unreasonable.\r\n这看起来不太合理。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nRidiculous means so silly or unreasonable that it is hard to believe.\r\nridiculous 就是“傻到/离谱到让人难以相信”。','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\n$200 for this small bag? That’s ridiculous!\r\n这个小包要 200 刀？太离谱了！\r\n\r\nThe rule sounds ridiculous to me.\r\n这个规定我听着很荒唐。\r\n\r\nDon’t be ridiculous.\r\n别傻了。/ 别开玩笑了。\r\n\r\nI looked ridiculous in that oversized hat.\r\n我戴那顶超大的帽子看起来很滑稽。\r\n\r\n🌏 新西兰口语感觉\r\n\r\n在新西兰日常口语里，ridiculous 可以用来吐槽价格、规定、情况：\r\n\r\nThat price is ridiculous.\r\n这个价格太离谱了。\r\n\r\n更温和一点可以说：\r\n\r\nThat seems a bit much.\r\n这个有点过了。\r\n\r\nThat’s a bit over the top.\r\n这有点太夸张了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/4a867b83c5d340f6b6c5d09379f830b4.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-04 14:56:43',1,'2026-05-04 14:56:43'),(1197,17,51,'phrase','electrical vs electronic','electrical vs electronic','electrical vs electronic','🧠 核心区别\r\n\r\nelectrical = related to electricity, power, wiring, or electrical systems\r\n和电、电力、电线、电路、供电系统有关。\r\n\r\nelectronic = related to devices or systems that use electronic components, chips, circuits, or digital technology\r\n和电子设备、芯片、电路板、数字技术有关。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\nelectrical\r\n电气的；电力的；用电的；和供电/布线有关的\r\n\r\nelectronic\r\n电子的；电子设备的；和芯片/电路板/数字系统有关的','🔌 electrical\r\n\r\n常见搭配\r\n\r\nelectrical wiring 电线布线\r\n\r\nelectrical equipment 电气设备\r\n\r\nelectrical fault 电气故障\r\n\r\nelectrical engineer 电气工程师\r\n\r\nelectrical appliance 电器 / 家用电器\r\n\r\nelectrical safety 用电安全\r\nThere is an electrical fault in the house.\r\n房子里有电气故障。\r\n\r\nYou should call an electrician to check the electrical wiring.\r\n你应该找电工检查电线布线。\r\n\r\n💻 electronic\r\n\r\n常见搭配\r\n\r\nelectronic device 电子设备\r\n\r\nelectronic components  电子元件\r\n\r\nelectronic circuit  电子电路\r\n\r\nelectronic payment  电子支付\r\n\r\nelectronic signature 电子签名\r\n\r\nelectronic music 电子音乐\r\n\r\n例句\r\n\r\nThis phone is an electronic device.\r\n这部手机是一种电子设备。\r\n\r\nThe company produces electronic components.\r\n这家公司生产电子元件。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9296be80c3324f838889176d8a8bdbef.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-06 18:36:38',1,'2026-05-06 18:36:38'),(1198,17,52,'vocab','appetizer','appetizer','appetizer','n. 开胃菜；餐前小吃\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nappetizer = a small dish served before the main meal\r\n主菜之前吃的小份食物，用来“打开胃口”。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n开胃菜/餐前小吃/前菜\r\n\r\n🔍 记忆技巧\r\n\r\nappetizer 来自 appetite 食欲。\r\n\r\n可以这样记：\r\n\r\nappetite = 食欲\r\nappetizer = 让你有食欲的东西','💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\norder an appetizer 点一份开胃菜\r\n\r\nshare some appetizers 一起分享几份前菜\r\n\r\nappetizer menu 前菜菜单\r\n\r\nstarter 开胃菜，英式/新西兰餐厅里也常用','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nWe ordered some appetizers before the main course.\r\n我们在主菜前点了一些开胃菜。\r\n\r\nThe garlic bread is a popular appetizer here.\r\n这里的蒜蓉面包是很受欢迎的前菜。\r\n\r\nWould you like any appetizers to start with?\r\n你们想先来点开胃菜吗？\r\n\r\n🌏 餐厅口语\r\n\r\n服务员可能会说：\r\n\r\nWould you like a starter?\r\n你想来个前菜吗？\r\n\r\nDo you want to share some appetizers?\r\n你们想一起分享几份前菜吗？\r\n\r\n🔗 对应/相关词汇\r\n\r\nstarter = 前菜，尤其英式英语常用\r\nmain course = 主菜\r\ndessert = 甜点\r\nside dish = 配菜\r\nsnack = 小吃 / 零食','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ce9db505b4714265a831a5cdaa6377a7.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-06 18:49:50',1,'2026-05-06 18:49:50'),(1199,17,53,'phrase','I’m not the one …','I’m not the one …','I’m not the one …','phrase. 我不是那个……的人；不是我负责；别找我\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nI’m not the one … = I am not the person who did something / should do something / is responsible for something\r\n意思是：我不是做这件事的人，也不是应该负责的人。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n不是我做的\r\n不该怪我\r\n我不是负责人\r\n我不是你该问的人','🔍 句型结构\r\n\r\nI’m not the one + who + 句子\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI’m not the one who broke it.\r\n不是我弄坏的。\r\n\r\nI’m not the one who made that decision.\r\n那个决定不是我做的。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 语气注意\r\n\r\nI’m not the one … 有时听起来有点防御，像是在说：\r\n\r\n“别怪我。”\r\n“这不是我的问题。”\r\n\r\n所以在工作或礼貌场合，可以用更柔和的版本：\r\n\r\nI’m not sure I’m the right person to help with this.\r\n我不确定我是不是最适合帮这个的人。','💬 常见表达\r\n\r\nI’m not the one to blame.\r\n不该怪我。\r\n\r\nI’m not the one in charge.\r\n我不是负责人。\r\n\r\nI’m not the one you should be asking.\r\n你不该问我 / 我不是合适的人。\r\n\r\nI’m not the one who said that.\r\n那话不是我说的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nI’m not the one who lost the keys.\r\n不是我把钥匙弄丢的。\r\n\r\nI’m not the one to blame here.\r\n这事不该怪我。\r\n\r\nI’m not the one in charge of the schedule.\r\n我不是负责排班的人。\r\n\r\nI’m not the one you should talk to about this.\r\n这事你不该找我谈。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/89448da7059d4d81849a2ae68045664d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-07 05:35:44',1,'2026-05-07 05:35:44'),(1200,17,54,'vocab','appetite','appetite','appetite','n. 食欲；胃口\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nappetite = the feeling of wanting to eat\r\n想吃东西的感觉，也就是“胃口”。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n食欲\r\n胃口\r\n想吃东西的感觉','🔍 记忆技巧\r\n\r\n可以把 appetite 和 appetizer 放一起记：\r\n\r\nappetite = 食欲\r\nappetizer = 开胃菜，让你更有食欲\r\n\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\nhave a good appetite  胃口很好\r\n\r\nlose your appetite  失去食欲 / 没胃口\r\n\r\nwork up an appetite  活动后变得有胃口\r\n\r\na healthy appetite 健康的食欲 / 胃口不错\r\n\r\nno appetite 没胃口\r\n\r\n🌏 日常口语\r\n\r\n你可以说：\r\n\r\nI’m not very hungry.\r\n我不是很饿。\r\n\r\nI’ve lost my appetite.\r\n我没胃口了。\r\n\r\nThat smell killed my appetite.\r\n那个味道让我一点胃口都没了。\r\n\r\n🔗 对应/相关词汇\r\n\r\nhungry = 饿的\r\nhunger = 饥饿\r\ncraving = 强烈想吃某物的欲望\r\nfull = 饱的\r\nappetizer = 开胃菜','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nI don’t have much appetite today.\r\n我今天没什么胃口。\r\n\r\nThe long walk helped me work up an appetite.\r\n走了很久以后，我胃口变好了。\r\n\r\nShe lost her appetite because she was feeling sick.\r\n她因为不舒服没胃口。\r\n\r\nMy daughter has a good appetite today.\r\n我女儿今天胃口不错。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/abb0fa20c388492c85681258b9821cec.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-07 05:39:33',1,'2026-05-07 05:39:33'),(1201,17,55,'vocab','runny','runny','runny','adj. 太稀的；水水的；流动性强的\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nrunny = too liquid or watery\r\n形容东西太稀，容易流动。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n太稀的 / 水水的 /流动性太强的','🔍 记忆技巧\r\n\r\nrun = 跑 / 流动\r\nrunny = 会“流来流去”的\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nrunny sauce = 太稀的酱\r\nrunny egg yolk = 流心蛋黄\r\nrunny nose = 流鼻涕\r\ntoo runny 太稀了\r\n\r\n🔗 对应/相关词汇\r\n\r\nwatery = 水水的，味道淡\r\nthin = 稀的，不浓稠\r\nthick = 浓稠的\r\ncreamy = 奶油般顺滑浓稠的\r\nliquid = 液体的','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nThe sauce is too runny. 这个酱太稀了。\r\n\r\nThe batter is a bit runny. Add more flour. 这个面糊有点稀，加点面粉。\r\n\r\nI like my eggs with a runny yolk. 我喜欢蛋黄是流心的鸡蛋。\r\n\r\nMy daughter has a runny nose. 我女儿流鼻涕。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/33fc5f8f5ff441ee8f0be58604fc4ce2.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-07 06:01:25',1,'2026-05-07 06:01:25'),(1202,17,56,'phrase','overseasoned','overseasoned','overseasoned','adj. 调味过重的；调料放太多的\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\noverseasoned = having too much seasoning\r\n食物里盐、香料、调味料放太多，味道太重。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n调味过重的\r\n调料放太多的\r\n太咸 / 太香料味 / 味道太重\r\n\r\n🔍 记忆技巧\r\n\r\n拆开看：\r\n\r\nover- = 过度\r\nseason = 调味\r\n-ed = 被……的\r\n\r\n所以：overseasoned = 被过度调味的\r\n类似词：\r\novercooked = 煮过头的\r\noverpriced = 价格过高的\r\noverloaded = 负荷过重的','💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\noverseasoned soup 调味过重的汤\r\n\r\noverseasoned meat 调味过重的肉\r\n\r\na bit overseasoned 有点调味过重\r\n\r\ntoo much seasoning 调料太多\r\n\r\ntoo salty 太咸\r\n\r\n🔗 对应/相关词汇\r\n\r\nseasoning = 调味料\r\nseason with = 用……调味\r\nsalty = 咸的\r\nspicy = 辣的 / 香料味重的\r\nbland = 味道淡的\r\nwell-seasoned = 调味刚好的','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nThe soup is a bit overseasoned.\r\n这个汤调味有点重。\r\n\r\nThe chicken was overseasoned and too salty.\r\n这个鸡肉调味太重，而且太咸。\r\n\r\nI think the dish is slightly overseasoned, but still edible.\r\n我觉得这道菜调味稍微重了一点，但还是能吃。\r\n\r\nBe careful not to overseason the sauce.\r\n小心不要把酱调味过重。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/fc98bbb3ecc149dab55183a76cf5f719.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-07 06:12:28',1,'2026-05-07 06:12:28'),(1203,17,57,'phrase','season with','season with','season with','phrase. 用……调味\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nseason with = to add seasoning to food\r\n给食物加入盐、胡椒、香草或香料来调味。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n用……调味\r\n加……调味\r\n用……给食物提味','🔍 记忆技巧\r\n\r\n这里的 season 不是“季节”，而是动词：\r\n\r\nto season food = 给食物调味\r\n\r\n结构是：\r\n\r\nseason + food + with + 调味料\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nseason chicken with salt and pepper 用盐和胡椒给鸡肉调味\r\n\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\nseason with salt and pepper 用盐和胡椒调味\r\n\r\nseason with herbs 用香草调味\r\n\r\nseason with garlic 用大蒜调味\r\n\r\nseason with soy sauce 用酱油调味\r\n\r\nseason lightly 轻轻调味 / 少放调料\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意\r\n\r\nseason with 后面接调味料：\r\n\r\nseason with salt 用盐调味\r\n\r\nseason the meat 给肉调味\r\n\r\n不要说：season by salt ❌\r\n\r\n🔗 对应/相关词汇\r\n\r\nseasoning = 调味料\r\nsalt = 盐\r\npepper = 胡椒\r\nherbs = 香草\r\nspices = 香料\r\nmarinate = 腌制\r\nflavour = 味道 / 给……调味','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nSeason the chicken with salt and pepper.\r\n用盐和胡椒给鸡肉调味。\r\n\r\nThe chef seasoned the soup with herbs.\r\n厨师用香草给汤调味。\r\n\r\nYou can season the beef with garlic and soy sauce.\r\n你可以用大蒜和酱油给牛肉调味。\r\n\r\nDon’t season it too heavily.\r\n不要调味太重。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8f28267e6b364e8296cde444a51035aa.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-07 06:17:27',1,'2026-05-07 06:17:27'),(1204,17,58,'phrase','make a big deal','make a big deal','make a big deal','phrase. 小题大做；把事情看得太严重\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nmake a big deal = to treat something as more important or serious than it really is\r\n意思是：把一件其实没那么严重的事情，看得太严重，反应太大。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n小题大做 / 大惊小怪 / 把小事当成大事 / 反应过度','🔍 记忆技巧\r\n\r\nbig deal = 大事\r\n\r\nmake a big deal\r\n= 把一件事情“做成大事”\r\n\r\n所以：make a big deal = 小题大做\r\n\r\n常见完整结构是：\r\nmake a big deal out of + something  因为某事小题大做\r\n\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\nmake a big deal out of it\r\n因为这件事小题大做\r\n\r\ndon’t make a big deal out of it 别小题大做\r\n\r\nmake a big deal about something  对某事大惊小怪\r\n\r\nIt’s not a big deal.  这没什么大不了的。\r\n\r\nNo big deal.  没事，小事一桩。\r\n\r\n🔗 相关词汇\r\n\r\nbig deal = 大事\r\nno big deal = 没什么大不了\r\noverreact = 反应过度\r\nmake a fuss = 大惊小怪\r\ndrama = 戏剧化反应 / 小题大做\r\nblow things out of proportion = 把事情夸大','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nDon’t make a big deal out of it. 别小题大做。\r\n\r\nHe made a big deal out of a small mistake. 他因为一个小错误小题大做。\r\n\r\nI don’t want to make a big deal, but the food was cold. 我不想小题大做，但这个食物是冷的。\r\n\r\nIt’s not a big deal. We can fix it. 这没什么大不了的，我们可以解决。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a9c62478c5cd4dfbadaff9360487e9b1.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-07 06:23:34',1,'2026-05-07 06:23:34'),(1205,17,59,'phrase','I’m expecting…','I’m expecting…','I’m expecting…','意思是：我在等…… / 我预计…… / 我期待……\r\n\r\n⚠️ 特别注意\r\n\r\nI’m expecting 也可以表示： 我怀孕了。','常见用法\r\n\r\n1. I’m expecting + 名词\r\n我在等某人/某物。\r\nI’m expecting a call from my teacher.  我在等老师的电话。\r\n\r\nI’m expecting visitors this afternoon.  我今天下午有客人要来。\r\n\r\n2. I’m expecting + to do something 我预计/打算会做某事\r\n\r\nI’m expecting to finish it by Friday. 我预计周五前完成它。\r\n\r\nI’m expecting to hear back soon. 我预计很快会收到回复。\r\n\r\n3. I’m expecting + that + 句子 我预计某事会发生。\r\nI’m expecting that it will take about two hours.  我预计这大概要花两个小时。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d8ff25f39cc640e5b03c582dc8d47f37.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-07 06:29:06',1,'2026-05-07 06:29:06'),(1206,17,60,'phrase','prop something against something','prop something against something','prop something against something','phrase. 把某物靠在……上；把某物支在……上\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nprop something against something = to support something by leaning it against another object\r\n\r\n意思是：把一个东西斜着靠在另一个东西上，让它不要倒。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n把……靠在……上\r\n把……支在……上\r\n让……斜靠着……','prop 本身有 支撑；撑住 的意思。\r\n\r\nagainst = 靠着；贴着；抵着\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nprop the ladder against the wall\r\n= 把梯子靠在墙上\r\n\r\n画面感就是：\r\n一个东西自己站不稳，需要靠着另一个东西支撑。\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\nprop a ladder against the wall\r\n把梯子靠在墙上\r\n\r\nprop the bike against the fence\r\n把自行车靠在篱笆上\r\n\r\nprop the sign against the door\r\n把牌子靠在门边\r\n\r\nprop the board against the wall\r\n把木板靠在墙上\r\n\r\nprop your phone against a book\r\n把手机靠在书上支起来\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意结构\r\n\r\n常用结构是：\r\n\r\nprop + something + against + something\r\n \r\nprop the ladder against the wall ✅  把梯子靠在墙上。\r\n不要说：\r\nprop against the ladder the wall ❌\r\n\r\nlean something against something\r\n把某物靠在某物上，更常见、更日常\r\n\r\nsupport\r\n支撑\r\n\r\nhold up\r\n撑住；举起\r\n\r\nrest something against something\r\n把某物倚靠在某物上\r\n\r\nstand something against something\r\n把某物立靠在某物上','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nHe propped the ladder against the wall.\r\n他把梯子靠在墙上。\r\n\r\nI propped my bike against the fence.\r\n我把自行车靠在篱笆上。\r\n\r\nShe propped the sign against the door.\r\n她把牌子靠在门边。\r\n\r\nYou can prop your phone against a cup while watching the video.\r\n你看视频的时候可以把手机靠在杯子上支起来。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/562c262906d94dc38c21b2385398607c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-07 06:37:18',1,'2026-05-07 06:37:18'),(1207,17,61,'vocab','nuance','nuance','nuance','n. 细微差别；微妙之处；细腻含义\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nnuance = a small but important difference in meaning, feeling, or expression\r\n意思是：在意思、情感、语气、表达方式中的细小但重要的差别。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n细微差别 / 微妙差异 / 微妙之处 /细腻含义','🔍 记忆技巧\r\n\r\n学英语时，很多词中文翻译看起来一样，但用法和语气不同，这就是 nuance。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\ncheap = 便宜，但有时带“质量差”的感觉\r\ninexpensive = 价格不贵，更中性、更礼貌\r\n这两个词的区别就是一个 nuance。\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\na subtle nuance 微妙的差别\r\n\r\nunderstand the nuance 理解细微差别\r\n\r\nmiss the nuance 没理解微妙之处\r\n\r\nthe nuance of a word 一个词的细微含义\r\n\r\ncultural nuance 文化上的细微差别\r\n\r\nlanguage nuance 语言上的细微差别','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nThere is a subtle nuance between these two words.\r\n这两个词之间有一个微妙的差别。\r\n\r\nIt’s hard to understand the nuances of a language.\r\n理解一门语言的细微差别很难。\r\n\r\nThe translation is correct, but it misses some nuances.\r\n这个翻译是对的，但丢失了一些细微含义。\r\n\r\nHe explained the cultural nuances very clearly.\r\n他把文化上的细微差别解释得很清楚。\r\n\r\n🌏 学英语时很常用\r\n\r\n你可以问我：\r\n\r\nWhat’s the nuance between these two words?\r\n这两个词的细微区别是什么？\r\n\r\nCan you explain the nuance?\r\n你能解释一下这里的细微差别吗？\r\n\r\nWhat’s the nuance of this phrase?\r\n这个短语的语气/细微含义是什么？\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nNuance means a small but important difference in meaning, tone, or feeling.\r\nnuance 就是意思、语气或感觉上的细微但重要的差别。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/fca117240081414b84d217b2bd319f19.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-08 07:43:09',1,'2026-05-08 07:43:09'),(1208,17,62,'vocab','imply','imply','imply','v. 暗示；意味着；间接表达\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nimply = to suggest something without saying it directly\r\n意思是：没有直接说出来，但话里有这个意思。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n暗示 / 含有……意思 / 意味着 /话里有话 \r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nImply means to suggest something indirectly.\r\nimply 就是“不直接说，但话里暗示了某个意思”。','🔍 imply vs mean\r\n\r\nmean\r\n可以是直接意思，也可以是“意思是”。\r\n\r\nimply\r\n更强调：没有直接说，但暗示出来了。\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nWhat do you mean?\r\n你是什么意思？\r\n\r\nWhat are you implying?\r\n你在暗示什么？\r\n\r\n第二句语气更强，可能有点不高兴。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 语气注意\r\n\r\nWhat are you implying?\r\n这句话有时听起来像在质问：\r\n\r\n你什么意思？你是不是在暗示我什么？\r\n\r\n更温和可以说：\r\n\r\nWhat do you mean by that?\r\n你这是什么意思？\r\n\r\n🔍 记忆技巧\r\n\r\n可以这样记：\r\n\r\nimply = in + message\r\n意思藏在话里面，不直接说出来。\r\n\r\n比如别人说：\r\n\r\nYou’re here early today. 你今天来得挺早啊。\r\n\r\n可能只是陈述，也可能 imply：\r\nYou’re usually late.你平时经常迟到。\r\n\r\n这就是“暗示”。\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\nimply that + sentence 暗示……\r\n\r\nseem to imply 似乎暗示\r\n\r\nWhat are you implying? 你在暗示什么？\r\n\r\nI didn’t mean to imply that… 我不是想暗示……','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nAre you implying that I’m lazy?\r\n你是在暗示我懒吗？\r\n\r\nHis silence implied agreement.\r\n他的沉默意味着同意。\r\n\r\nThe article implies that prices may rise soon.\r\n这篇文章暗示价格可能很快上涨。\r\n\r\nI didn’t mean to imply that you were wrong.\r\n我不是想暗示你错了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/5f4d3a2b71044188bf720776d836489c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-08 08:02:16',1,'2026-05-08 08:02:16'),(1209,17,63,'phrase','bond with','bond with','bond with','phrase. 和……建立感情；和……建立亲密关系\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nbond with someone = to build a close emotional connection with someone\r\n意思是：和某人慢慢建立一种亲近、信任、有感情的关系。\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n和……建立感情\r\n和……建立亲密关系\r\n和……拉近关系\r\n和……产生连接感','🔍 记忆技巧\r\n\r\nbond 本身有“连接、纽带”的意思。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nbond with someone. = 和某人形成情感上的纽带。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nparents bond with their baby 父母和宝宝建立亲密关系\r\n\r\nstudents bond with classmates 学生和同学拉近关系\r\n\r\n🔍 bond with vs connect with\r\n\r\nbond with\r\n更强调感情变亲近，关系更深。\r\n\r\nconnect with\r\n可以是精神上、兴趣上、沟通上的连接，范围更广。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI connected with him because we both like programming.\r\n我和他聊得来，因为我们都喜欢编程。\r\n\r\nI bonded with him after working together for months.\r\n一起工作几个月后，我和他建立了更深的关系。\r\n\r\n\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\nbond with your child. 和你的孩子建立感情\r\n\r\nbond with your baby 和宝宝建立亲密关系\r\n\r\nbond with your teammates 和队友建立关系\r\n\r\nbond with animals 和动物建立感情\r\n\r\na bonding experience 一次拉近关系的经历','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nIt takes time to bond with a new baby.\r\n和新生儿建立亲密关系需要时间。\r\n\r\nI bonded with my classmates during the group project.\r\n我在小组项目中和同学们熟悉起来、建立了关系。\r\n\r\nPlaying badminton helps me bond with my wife.\r\n打羽毛球帮助我和妻子增进感情。\r\n\r\nVolunteering is a good way to bond with local people.\r\n做志愿者是和当地人建立联系的好方式。\r\n\r\n🌏 日常口语表达\r\n\r\nWe really bonded on that trip.\r\n我们在那次旅行中真的拉近了关系。\r\n\r\nI’m trying to bond with my new team.\r\n我正在努力和新团队建立关系。\r\n\r\nFood is a great way to bond with people.\r\n食物是拉近人与人关系的好方式。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ee885b8826a647a9a00b650d8be5fbf4.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-08 08:15:53',1,'2026-05-08 08:15:53'),(1210,17,64,'phrase','to head…','to head…','to head…','phrase. 前往……；朝……去；去……\r\n \r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nhead to / head for / head back / head out = to go or move in a particular direction\r\n意思是：往某个地方去，或者朝某个方向走。\r\n\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n去…… / 前往…… / 朝……走 / 动身去……\r\n\r\n🔍 记忆技巧\r\n\r\nhead 作为名词是“头”。\r\n作为动词时，可以想象：\r\n\r\nyour head is pointing toward a place\r\n你的头朝着某个地方，所以你正在往那里去。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nI’m heading to the supermarket. = 我正要去超市。','💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\nhead to + place\r\n去某个地方\r\n\r\nhead for + place\r\n朝某地去，常带“目标方向”的感觉\r\n\r\nhead back 回去\r\n\r\nhead home  回家\r\n\r\nhead out  出门；离开\r\n\r\nhead over to + place/person  过去某个地方 / 去某人那边\r\n\r\n🔍 head to vs go to\r\n\r\ngo to\r\n普通表达：去某地。\r\n\r\nhead to\r\n更口语，强调“正在朝那里去 / 准备去”。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI’m going to the supermarket.\r\n我要去超市。\r\n\r\nI’m heading to the supermarket.\r\n我正准备去/正在去超市。更自然口语。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意\r\n\r\nhead to 后面通常接地方：\r\n\r\nhead to school 去学校\r\n\r\nhead to work 去上班\r\n\r\nhead to town  去市中心\r\n\r\nhead to bed  去睡觉\r\n\r\n但有些固定表达不加 to：\r\n\r\nhead home ✅  回家\r\n\r\nhead back ✅  回去\r\n\r\nhead out ✅。出门','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nI’m heading to the supermarket.\r\n我正要去超市。\r\n\r\nWe’re heading home now.\r\n我们现在要回家了。\r\n\r\nShe headed back to the office after lunch.\r\n午饭后她回办公室了。\r\n\r\nDo you want to head over to the café?\r\n你想过去咖啡馆那边吗？\r\n\r\nI’m just heading out.\r\n我正准备出门。\r\n\r\n🌏 新西兰日常口语\r\n\r\n在新西兰，head to / head over / head out 很常用，比单纯说 go to 更自然一点。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nI’m heading to Pak’nSave later.\r\n我一会儿要去 Pak’nSave。\r\n\r\nI might head over after class.\r\n我下课后可能过去一趟。\r\n\r\nWe should head off soon.\r\n我们应该快点出发了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9d158de27ba2428ea602b737e2b5e90c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-08 08:35:01',1,'2026-05-08 08:35:01'),(1211,17,65,'phrase','rock up','rock up','rock up','phrasal verb. 露面；出现；到达\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nrock up = to arrive somewhere, often casually or unexpectedly\r\n\r\n意思是：某人到了某个地方，语气比较口语、随意。\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n出现 / 到场 / 过来 / 突然来了 / 随便一来\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nRock up means to arrive somewhere casually.\r\nrock up 就是“随便过来、露面、到场”。','🌏 新西兰 / 澳洲口语很常见\r\n\r\n在新西兰和澳洲，rock up 很常用，比 arrive 更口语。\r\n\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\nrock up late 迟到了 / 很晚才到\r\n\r\nrock up to class 来上课\r\n\r\nrock up at someone’s house 突然到某人家\r\n\r\nrock up without booking 没预约就来了\r\n\r\nrock up anytime 随时过来','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nHe rocked up late again.\r\n他又迟到了。\r\n\r\nYou can just rock up around 6.\r\n你大概 6 点左右直接过来就行。\r\n\r\nShe rocked up to the meeting without any notes.\r\n她来开会时什么笔记都没带。\r\n\r\nDon’t just rock up without calling first.\r\n别不先打电话就直接过来。\r\n\r\n🔍 rock up vs show up\r\n\r\nshow up\r\n更通用，表示“出现、到场”。\r\n\r\nrock up\r\n更口语、更随意，有时带一点“突然出现 / 不太正式”的感觉。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nHe showed up at 8.\r\n他 8 点到了。\r\n\r\nHe rocked up at 8.\r\n他 8 点晃过来了 / 他 8 点来了。语气更随意。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8017b45d60474d5bb8ba3be6d7ba6fe8.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-09 13:57:18',1,'2026-05-09 13:57:18'),(1212,18,1,'phrase','I was meant to (be)','I was meant to (be)','I was meant to (be)','1. I was meant to + 动词\r\n\r\n意思是：我本来应该…… / 我原本打算……\r\n\r\n2. It was meant to be…\r\n\r\n意思是：这本来是要…… / 这是命中注定的','1. I was meant to + 动词\r\n\r\n意思是：我本来应该…… / 我原本打算……\r\n\r\nI was meant to call you yesterday.\r\n我昨天本来应该给你打电话的。\r\n\r\nI was meant to go to the meeting, but I was sick.\r\n我本来应该去开会，但我生病了。\r\n\r\nI was meant to finish it today.\r\n我本来应该今天完成它。\r\n\r\n这个意思和你之前学的很像：\r\n\r\nI was supposed to…\r\n我本来应该…… / 我原本计划……\r\n\r\n2. It was meant to be…\r\n\r\n意思是：这本来是要…… / 这是命中注定的\r\n\r\nIt was meant to be a joke.\r\n这本来是个玩笑。\r\n\r\nIt was meant to be easy, but it turned out to be difficult.\r\n它本来应该很简单，但结果很难。\r\n\r\nMaybe it was meant to be.\r\n也许这是命中注定的。','一句话记住\r\n\r\nI was meant to… = I was supposed to…\r\n意思是：我本来应该 / 原本计划要做某事。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/cd8381c5119b4854b1dd2d9c30d38936.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-09 14:50:28',1,'2026-05-09 14:50:28'),(1213,18,2,'phrase','I was supposed to…','I was supposed to…','I was supposed to…','我本来应该……；我原本计划……；按理说我要……','🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nI was supposed to + 动词原形\r\n表示：原计划要做某事，但可能没有做成。\r\n\r\n常见用法\r\n\r\nI was supposed to go to the supermarket, but I didn’t.\r\n我本来应该去超市，但我没去。\r\n\r\nI was supposed to call you yesterday.\r\n我昨天本来应该给你打电话的。\r\n\r\nI was supposed to finish this task today.\r\n我本来应该今天完成这个任务。\r\n\r\nI was supposed to meet my friend, but I had something else to do.\r\n我本来要见朋友，但我有别的事。','和 “I was meant to” 很像\r\n\r\nI was supposed to…\r\n更常用，表示“本来应该 / 原计划”。\r\n\r\nI was meant to…\r\n也可以表示“本来应该 / 原本打算”，但有时也带“注定”的意思。\r\n\r\n口语里很自然\r\n\r\n你之前那句可以说：\r\n\r\nI was supposed to go to the supermarket, but I didn’t make it.\r\n我本来要去超市，但最后没去成。\r\n\r\nI was supposed to go, but something came up.\r\n我本来要去的，但临时有事。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/efff767c05034fb0bf120a6521dd4d4b.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-09 15:02:23',1,'2026-05-09 15:02:23'),(1214,18,3,'phrase','There was this...','There was this...','There was this...','有这么一个…… / 当时有个……','🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nThere was this + 人/东西/情况…\r\n\r\n意思是你要开始讲一个具体的人或事情，中文很像：\r\n\r\n“当时有这么一个……”\r\n“有个……”\r\n“我跟你说，有一个……”','例句\r\n\r\nThere was this little boy who wanted to buy a small statue.\r\n当时有个小男孩想买一个小雕像。\r\n\r\nThere was this customer who kept asking about the price.\r\n当时有个顾客一直问价格。\r\n\r\nThere was this lady who came in just before closing.\r\n当时有个女士快关门前进来了。\r\n\r\nThere was this guy who rocked up without booking.\r\n当时有个男的没预约就直接来了。\r\n\r\n和 There was a… 的区别\r\n\r\nThere was a little boy…\r\n语气比较普通：有一个小男孩……\r\n\r\nThere was this little boy…\r\n更像讲故事：当时有这么一个小男孩……\r\n\r\n这个 this 不是“这个”的意思，而是让故事听起来更具体、更口语。\r\n\r\n一句话记住\r\n\r\nThere was this… = 当时有这么一个……\r\n很适合讲你在店里、学校、路上遇到的人或事。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e059fc00415b429b8662b8bf65390c62.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-09 15:16:24',1,'2026-05-09 15:16:24'),(1215,18,4,'phrase','about five or so','about five or so','about five or so','大概五岁左右 / 大约五个左右\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nabout + number + or so\r\n表示：大约……左右\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nabout five or so\r\n= around five\r\n= about five\r\n= roughly five\r\n\r\n如果说人：\r\n\r\nHe was about five or so.\r\n他大概五岁左右。','⚠️ 注意\r\n\r\nabout 和 or so 都有“大约”的意思，所以一起用时有点重复，但在口语里很自然。\r\n\r\n更简洁可以说：\r\n\r\nHe was about five.\r\n他大概五岁。\r\n\r\nHe was five or so.\r\n他五岁左右。\r\n\r\nHe was around five.\r\n他大概五岁。','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nThere was this little boy, about five or so.\r\n当时有个小男孩，大概五岁左右。\r\n\r\nIt took about ten minutes or so.\r\n大概花了十分钟左右。\r\n\r\nThere were about twenty people or so at the meeting.\r\n会议上大概有二十个人左右。\r\n\r\nI stayed there for about an hour or so.\r\n我在那里待了大概一个小时左右。\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nabout five or so = around five / roughly five\r\n意思是：大概五个左右 / 大概五岁左右。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-09 17:24:49',1,'2026-05-09 17:24:49'),(1216,18,5,'phrase','peeled off tags','peeled off tags','peeled off tags','🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\npeel off = 把贴在表面的东西慢慢撕下来、剥下来。\r\n所以：\r\n\r\npeeled off tags\r\n= peeled tags off\r\n= 把标签撕下来了\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nPeel off tags means to remove stickers or labels by pulling them away from the surface.\r\npeeled off tags 就是：把标签/贴纸从物品上撕下来。','🔍 结构拆解\r\n\r\npeel off + something\r\n撕下某物\r\n\r\npeel something off + something\r\n把某物从……上撕下来\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nHe peeled off the price tag.\r\n他把价格标签撕下来了。\r\n\r\nHe peeled the price tag off another item.\r\n他把价格标签从另一个商品上撕下来了。\r\n\r\n🛒 店里很常用的表达\r\n\r\nprice tag\r\n价格标签\r\n\r\nprice sticker\r\n价格贴纸\r\n\r\nlabel\r\n标签\r\n\r\nbarcode sticker\r\n条形码贴纸\r\n\r\n所以你可以说：\r\n\r\nI think he peeled off a price tag from another item.\r\n我觉得他从另一个商品上撕下了一个价格标签。\r\n\r\nSomeone has peeled the sticker off.\r\n有人把贴纸撕掉了。\r\n\r\nThe price tag has been peeled off.\r\n价格标签被撕掉了。','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nHe probably peeled off tags from other items.\r\n他可能从其他商品上撕下了标签。\r\n\r\nThe label was peeled off, so I couldn’t see the price.\r\n标签被撕掉了，所以我看不到价格。\r\n\r\nDon’t peel off the barcode sticker.\r\n不要把条形码贴纸撕掉。\r\n\r\nIt looks like someone peeled the original price tag off.\r\n看起来有人把原来的价格标签撕掉了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2f2288998ed740649bded48e5116cd54.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-09 17:32:03',1,'2026-05-09 17:32:03'),(1217,18,6,'phrase','tell straight away','tell straight away','tell straight away','马上看出来；立刻判断出来；一眼就知道\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\ntell 在这里不是“告诉”，而是：\r\n\r\n看得出来 / 判断得出\r\n\r\nstraight away = immediately\r\n马上；立刻\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nI could tell straight away.\r\n我马上就看出来了。','✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nI could tell straight away = I knew immediately from what I saw.\r\n意思是：我一眼就看出来了。','🗣️ 例句\r\n\r\nI could tell straight away that something wasn’t right.\r\n我一眼就看出来有点不对劲。\r\n\r\nI could tell straight away he was nervous.\r\n我马上看出来他很紧张。\r\n\r\nShe could tell straight away that the price tag had been changed.\r\n她一眼就看出来价格标签被换过了。\r\n\r\nYou can tell straight away when someone is lying.\r\n别人撒谎的时候，你马上就能看出来。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/70d98a1cd3f24ab185c27ec2963cbed7.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-09 17:36:10',1,'2026-05-09 17:36:10'),(1218,18,7,'phrase','lovely','lovely','lovely','它更像中文里的：\r\n\r\n好嘞，谢谢\r\n太好了\r\n好的，很好\r\n不错，麻烦了','场景 1：顾客表示感谢/满意\r\n\r\n你帮顾客装袋、确认价格、找东西，顾客说：\r\n\r\nLovely.\r\n意思可能是：\r\n好的，谢谢。 / 太好了，谢谢。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\n你说：That’ll be $5.\r\n顾客说：Lovely.\r\n意思是：好的。\r\n\r\n你说：I’ll just check that price for you.\r\n顾客说：Lovely, thanks.\r\n意思是：好的，谢谢。\r\n\r\n场景 2：表示“很好 / 不错”\r\n\r\nThat’s lovely.\r\n那很好 / 那很不错。\r\n\r\nLovely, thank you.\r\n很好，谢谢。\r\n\r\n你怎么回应？\r\n\r\n如果顾客说 Lovely，你可以自然回应：\r\n\r\nNo worries.\r\n没事 / 不客气。\r\n\r\nAll good.\r\n没问题。\r\n\r\nYou’re welcome.\r\n不客气。\r\n\r\nSweet as.\r\n好嘞 / 没问题。新西兰口语。\r\n\r\n一句话记住\r\n\r\nLovely 在服务场景里经常表示：\r\n“好的，很好，谢谢。”\r\n\r\n但如果你自己想明确表达谢谢，最好说：\r\n\r\nLovely, thank you.\r\n或者\r\nThanks, that’s lovely.','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d8022f7e71c34aa5b7ed77770b39e588.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-10 07:15:17',1,'2026-05-10 07:15:17'),(1219,18,8,'vocab','apparently','apparently','apparently','adv. 看起来；似乎；据说；听说\r\n🧠 核心含义\r\n\r\napparently 表示：\r\n你听到了一些信息，或者根据情况判断，好像是这样，但你不是 100% 确定。\r\n\r\n可以理解成中文里的：\r\n\r\n看起来……  似乎……   据说……  听说……\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nApparently means it seems true, or people say it is true, but I’m not completely sure.\r\n\r\napparently = 好像是真的 / 听说是这样，但我不是百分百确定。','1. 表示“听说 / 据说”\r\n\r\n当信息是别人告诉你的，不是你亲眼确认的。\r\n\r\nApparently, she’s recovering.\r\n听说她正在恢复。\r\n\r\nApparently, the shop closes early today.\r\n听说这家店今天会早点关门。\r\n\r\nApparently, he’s moving to Auckland.\r\n听说他要搬去奥克兰。\r\n\r\n2. 表示“看起来 / 似乎”\r\n\r\n当你根据看到的情况做判断。\r\n\r\nApparently, everything is fine now.\r\n看起来现在一切都好了。\r\n\r\nApparently, the prognosis looks good.\r\n看起来预后不错。\r\n\r\nHe was apparently upset.\r\n他看起来有点不高兴。\r\n\r\n🔍 apparently vs obviously\r\n\r\napparently\r\n= 看起来 / 据说，但我不一定完全确定。\r\n\r\nObviously\r\n= 很明显，基本确定。\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nApparently, she’s recovering.\r\n听说她正在恢复。\r\n你只是听说，不一定亲眼确认。\r\n\r\nObviously, she’s recovering.\r\n很明显她正在恢复。\r\n你很确定，证据很明显。','🗣️ 你刚才那个场景可以这样说\r\n\r\nI’m so sorry to hear that, but apparently she’s recovering, and the prognosis looks good.\r\n听到这个我很难过，不过听说她正在恢复，而且预后不错。\r\n\r\n如果是很温暖的回复，可以说：\r\n\r\nI’m really sorry to hear that. Apparently, she’s recovering, and the prognosis looks good, which is a relief.\r\n听到这个我真的很难过。听说她正在恢复，而且预后不错，这也算让人松了一口气。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ee5be7bbf73249c4ad0dfe32348b5ec3.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-10 07:33:24',1,'2026-05-10 07:33:24'),(1220,18,9,'vocab','prognosis','prognosis','prognosis','n. 预后；病情发展预测\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nprognosis 通常用于医学场景，表示医生对病人未来恢复情况的判断。\r\n\r\n中文可以理解成：\r\n\r\n预后 / 恢复前景 / 病情发展预测\r\n\r\n常见表达\r\n\r\nThe prognosis looks good. 预后看起来不错。/ 恢复前景不错。\r\n\r\nThe prognosis is poor. 预后不好。\r\n\r\na good prognosis 良好的预后\r\n\r\na poor prognosis 不好的预后\r\n\r\nlong-term prognosis 长期预后','例句\r\n\r\nApparently, she’s recovering, and the prognosis looks good.\r\n听说她正在恢复，而且预后看起来不错。\r\n\r\nThe doctor said the prognosis is good.\r\n医生说预后不错。\r\n\r\nIt’s still too early to know the long-term prognosis.\r\n现在判断长期预后还太早。\r\n\r\n一句话记住\r\n\r\nPrognosis means a doctor’s prediction about how an illness or injury will develop.\r\nprognosis 就是医生对病情未来发展的判断，也就是“预后”。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/5afe2a12d58f45efad0395be0744deea.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-10 07:40:39',1,'2026-05-10 07:40:39'),(1221,18,10,'phrase','drop it round / drop it around','drop it round / drop it around','drop it round / drop it around','phrasal verb phrase\r\n把它送过来 / 顺路送过去 / 拿过来\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\ndrop something round / around\r\n= take something to someone’s place, usually casually or briefly\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n把某个东西送到别人那里，通常是顺路、临时、不正式地送过去。\r\n\r\n在新西兰、澳洲、英国口语里很常见。\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文理解\r\n\r\ndrop it round 可以理解成：\r\n\r\n把它送过来\r\n把它送过去\r\n顺路拿过去\r\n顺便送一下\r\n\r\n具体是“过来”还是“过去”，要看说话人的位置。','🔍 结构拆解\r\n\r\ndrop\r\n这里不是“掉下来”，而是“顺便送 / 放下”。\r\n\r\nit\r\n指那个东西。\r\n\r\nround / around\r\n到某人那里 / 去某个地方。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ndrop it round\r\n= 把它送到你那儿 / 送过去','🗣️ 常见例句\r\n\r\nCan we drop it round later this morning?\r\n我们今天上午晚点把它送过去可以吗？\r\n\r\nI’ll drop it round after work.\r\n我下班后把它送过去。\r\n\r\nCould you drop it around tomorrow?\r\n你明天能把它送过来吗？\r\n\r\nShe dropped the keys round last night.\r\n她昨晚把钥匙送过来了。\r\n\r\nWe can drop it round to your place.\r\n我们可以把它送到你家去。\r\n\r\n\r\n🆚 drop it round vs drop it off\r\n\r\ndrop it round / drop it around\r\n更偏新西兰、英国、澳洲口语，语气更随意，常表示送到某人那里。\r\n\r\ndrop it off\r\n更通用，也很常见，强调“把东西送到某处并留下”。\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nI’ll drop it round later.\r\n我晚点把它送过去。语气比较口语、随意。\r\n\r\nI’ll drop it off later. 我晚点把它送过去/放下。更通用。\r\n \r\n\r\n🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\ndrop it round later\r\n晚点送过去\r\n\r\ndrop it round this morning\r\n今天上午送过去\r\n\r\ndrop it round to your place\r\n送到你家去\r\n\r\ndrop the keys round\r\n把钥匙送过去\r\n\r\ndrop the parcel around\r\n把包裹送过去\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nDrop it round means to bring or take something to someone’s place casually.\r\ndrop it round 就是：顺便把东西送到某人那里。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/145df6c156a141e4af8d3fd223f4c7d9.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-10 08:02:40',1,'2026-05-10 08:02:40'),(1222,18,11,'phrase','would that feel right ？','would that feel right ？','would that feel right ？','那样感觉合适吗？/ 你觉得那样对吗？\r\n\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nfeel right = 感觉合适、感觉对、感觉自然\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nWould that feel right?\r\n= 那样会不会感觉合适？\r\n= 你觉得那样可以吗？\r\n\r\n这句话更偏向问对方的感受和判断，不是单纯问“可不可以”。','','✅ 常见例句\r\n\r\nWould that feel right to you? 你觉得那样合适吗？\r\n\r\nIt doesn’t feel right. 感觉不太对。\r\n\r\nThat feels right to me. 我觉得那样挺合适。\r\n\r\nI’m not sure if that feels right.\r\n我不确定那样是否合适。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔍 和类似表达的区别\r\n\r\nWould that feel right?\r\n强调：感觉是否合适 / 是否自然。\r\n\r\nWould that be alright?\r\n强调：这样可以吗？更常用、更礼貌。\r\n\r\nWould that work for you?\r\n强调：这样对你方便吗？\r\n\r\nDoes that sound okay?\r\n强调：听起来可以吗？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🛒 店里/日常场景更推荐\r\n\r\n如果你想问顾客“这样可以吗”，更自然说：\r\n\r\nWould that be alright?\r\n这样可以吗？\r\n\r\nWould that work for you?\r\n这样对你方便吗？\r\n\r\nIs that okay?\r\n这样可以吗？\r\n \r\n✅ 一句话记住\r\n\r\nWould that feel right? = Would that seem okay or appropriate to you?\r\n意思是：你觉得那样合适吗 / 感觉对吗？','','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-10 08:20:12',1,'2026-05-10 08:20:12'),(1223,18,12,'phrase','What’s that on?','What’s that on?','What’s that on?','我拿了两个东西问了他，我说这两个商品没有价格，他后来的意思是这个商品是一个套装的一部分，但是说这句话之前他说了what\'s that on ? 这是什么意思\r\n\r\n通过上下问可以理解出：\r\n\r\n这个是从哪儿来的？/ 这个属于什么东西上的？/ 这个原本是放在哪个套装里的？','What’s that on? 可以理解为：\r\n\r\nWhat is that part of?  这个是哪一套/哪个东西的一部分？\r\n\r\n或者：\r\nWhat’s that from?  这个是从哪儿来的？\r\n\r\n这句话为什么这样用？\r\n\r\non 有时可以表示“附在……上 / 属于……上面 / 在某个东西的一部分”。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nWhat’s this lid on?  这个盖子是哪个东西上的？\r\n\r\nWhat’s this piece from?  这个零件是从哪个东西上来的？\r\n\r\nWhat set is this part of?  这个属于哪个套装？\r\n\r\n你的场景可以这样理解\r\n\r\n你拿了两个没有价格的东西问他：\r\n\r\nThese two don’t have prices on them. 这两个没有价格。\r\n\r\n他说：\r\n\r\nWhat’s that on?  这个是哪个东西上的？/ 这个属于哪一套？\r\n\r\n然后他发现：\r\n\r\nThat’s part of a set.  那个是套装的一部分。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/72736133b2484ca98f39b947a52fd341.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-10 08:30:00',1,'2026-05-10 08:30:00'),(1224,18,13,'phrase','make it up','make it up','make it up','编造；补偿；和好；凑够\r\n🧠 核心意思\r\n\r\nmake it up 有好几个意思，要看场景。\r\n最常见的是：\r\n\r\n1. 编造一个故事 / 借口\r\n2. 补偿某人\r\n3. 和好\r\n4. 凑够数量','1. 编造 / 瞎说\r\n\r\nmake something up\r\n= 编造某事\r\n\r\n注意：如果中间有 it，要放中间：\r\n\r\nmake it up ✅\r\nmake up it ❌\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nHe made it up. 他编的。\r\n\r\nMaybe someone made it up.  可能有人编出来的。\r\n\r\nDon’t make it up. 别瞎编。\r\n\r\nI think he made up that story.\r\n我觉得他编了那个故事。\r\n\r\n2. 补偿 / 弥补\r\n\r\nmake it up to someone\r\n= 补偿某人\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nI’m sorry. I’ll make it up to you. 对不起，我会补偿你的。\r\n\r\nShe missed the meeting, so she tried to make it up to the team.\r\n她错过了会议，所以她想补偿团队。\r\n \r\n\r\n3. 和好\r\n\r\nmake up with someone\r\n= 和某人和好\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nThey had an argument, but they made up later. 他们吵了一架，但后来和好了。\r\n\r\nDid you make up with your friend? 你和朋友和好了吗？\r\n \r\n\r\n4. 凑够 / 组成\r\n\r\nmake up 也可以表示“组成”。\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nWomen make up 60% of the class. 女性占这个班的 60%。\r\n\r\nWe need two more people to make up a team. 我们还需要两个人才能组成一个队。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/91b86e9d2951463a9e3746e75084c2bb.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-10 09:36:16',1,'2026-05-10 09:36:16'),(1225,18,14,'phrase','When I first looked at it, I thought, “There’s no way it could be that cheap“','When I first looked at it, I thought, “There’s no way it could be that cheap“','When I first looked at it, I thought, “There’s no way it could be that cheap“','我第一眼看到它的时候，我就想：“它不可能这么便宜。”','1. when I first looked at it\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n当我第一眼看到它的时候\r\n我刚看到它的时候\r\n\r\n这里的 first 表示“最开始 / 第一眼”。\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nWhen I first looked at it, I thought it was broken.\r\n我第一眼看到它时，以为它坏了。\r\n\r\nWhen I first saw the price, I thought it was wrong.\r\n我第一眼看到价格时，以为价格错了。','3. There’s no way…\r\n\r\n这是非常常用的口语表达。\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n不可能……  绝对不会……  哪有可能……\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nThere’s no way that’s real. 那不可能是真的。\r\n\r\nThere’s no way he’s only five. 他不可能才五岁。\r\n\r\nThere’s no way it costs only two dollars. 它不可能只卖两块钱。\r\n \r\n4. it could be that cheap\r\n\r\nthat cheap = 那么便宜 / 便宜到那个程度\r\n\r\n这里的 that 不是“那个”，而是加强程度，意思像：\r\n\r\nso cheap 这么便宜 / 那么便宜\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nI didn’t know it was that expensive. 我不知道它那么贵。\r\n\r\nI didn’t expect it to be that small. 我没想到它那么小。\r\n\r\nThere’s no way it could be that cheap. 它不可能那么便宜。\r\n\r\n更自然的店里场景版本\r\n\r\nWhen I first looked at it, I thought there was no way it could be only two dollars.\r\n我第一眼看到它时，就觉得它不可能只卖两块钱。\r\n\r\nI could tell straight away something wasn’t right. There’s no way that item would be that cheap.\r\n我一眼就看出来有点不对劲。那个东西不可能那么便宜。\r\n\r\n最值得背的是：\r\n\r\nThere’s no way it could be that cheap.\r\n它不可能这么便宜。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a30094c4df7e45e08450358f50c157a9.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-10 09:41:10',1,'2026-05-10 09:41:10'),(1226,18,15,'phrase','spiral','spiral','spiral','spiral  /ˈspaɪrəl/\r\nnoun / verb / adjective\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n螺旋；盘旋；螺旋式上升/下降；逐渐失控\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nspiral means something moves or develops round and round, often getting bigger, worse, or out of control.\r\n\r\n它的核心画面是：\r\n一圈一圈地转，或者情况一步步变严重。','🌀 1. Noun: 螺旋形\r\n\r\na spiral staircase\r\n螺旋楼梯\r\n\r\na spiral pattern\r\n螺旋图案\r\n\r\nThe shell has a beautiful spiral.\r\n这个贝壳有一个漂亮的螺旋形。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💨 2. Verb: 盘旋；螺旋式移动\r\n\r\nSmoke spiralled into the sky.\r\n烟雾盘旋着升上天空。\r\n\r\nThe leaves spiralled down from the tree.\r\n树叶打着旋落下来。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n📉 3. Verb: 变得越来越糟；失控\r\n\r\nThe situation started to spiral.\r\n情况开始失控。\r\n\r\nPrices are spiralling.\r\n价格在不断上涨。\r\n\r\nThings spiralled out of control.\r\n事情彻底失控了。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ It’s starting to spiral.\r\n事情开始有点失控了。\r\n\r\n✅ Things are spiralling out of control.\r\n事情越来越控制不住了。\r\n\r\n✅ My stress started to spiral.\r\n我的压力开始越来越大。\r\n\r\n🪜 spiral staircase  螺旋楼梯\r\n\r\n🐚 spiral shell  螺旋贝壳\r\n\r\n🌀 spiral pattern  螺旋图案\r\n\r\n📈 spiralling prices 不断上涨的价格\r\n\r\n📉 downward spiral  恶性循环；越来越糟\r\n\r\n🚨 spiral out of control  失控\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence 实用句\r\n\r\nOnce things start to spiral, it can be hard to stop them.\r\n一旦事情开始失控，就很难停下来。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象一个 蚊香 / 弹簧 / 贝壳 / 螺旋楼梯：\r\n它们都是一圈一圈绕出去的形状。\r\n\r\n所以 spiral 的感觉就是：\r\n\r\nround and round, getting bigger or worse\r\n一圈一圈，越来越大，或者越来越糟。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a60db44e6e6f49fc9fc54abb8e0aa1db.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-11 12:46:57',1,'2026-05-11 12:46:57'),(1227,18,16,'vocab','lattice','lattice','lattice  /ˈlætɪs/','🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n格子结构；格栅；网格；晶格\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nlattice means a structure made from strips, lines, or bars crossing over each other.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n交叉的条状物形成规则的格子结构\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence 实用句\r\n\r\nThe lattice design lets light through but still gives some privacy.\r\n这种格栅设计可以透光，但也能提供一些隐私。\r\n \r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象一个花园里的 木格架 🪴：\r\n一条一条木条交叉在一起，藤蔓从格子中间爬上去。\r\n\r\n这就是：\r\n\r\nlattice = crossed strips forming a pattern\r\n交叉条状物形成的格子结构。','🪴 1. Garden / Fence 花园或围栏\r\n\r\na lattice fence\r\n格栅围栏\r\n\r\na wooden lattice screen\r\n木制格栅屏风\r\n\r\nThe vines are growing up the lattice.\r\n藤蔓正沿着格架往上爬。\r\n\r\n📌 这种 lattice 常见于花园里，让植物爬的木架子。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🥧 2. Food 食物：格子派皮\r\n\r\na lattice pie crust\r\n格子派皮\r\n\r\nThe apple pie has a lattice top.\r\n这个苹果派上面是格子形的派皮。\r\n\r\n📌 就是派上面一条一条交叉编起来的面皮。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔬 3. Science 科学：晶格\r\n\r\ncrystal lattice\r\n晶格\r\n\r\nAtoms are arranged in a lattice.\r\n原子按晶格结构排列。\r\n\r\n📌 在物理、化学、材料科学里，lattice 表示规则排列的结构。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ It has a lattice pattern.\r\n它是格子图案。\r\n\r\n✅ The fence has a lattice design.\r\n这个围栏是格栅设计。\r\n\r\n✅ The pie has a lattice top.\r\n这个派上面是格子形的。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3f0d35a1a26b4a3eb071adb3941c40df.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-11 14:16:46',1,'2026-05-11 14:16:46'),(1228,18,17,'phrase','build up','build up','build up','phrasal verb / noun phrase\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n逐渐增加；积累；增强；建立；夸大宣传\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nbuild up means something increases or develops gradually over time.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n一点一点累积起来 / 慢慢变多变强\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence 实用句\r\n\r\nDon’t let small problems build up — deal with them early.\r\n不要让小问题越积越多，要早点处理。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象你一块一块地往上垒积木 🧱。\r\n每加一块，就高一点。\r\n\r\n这就是：\r\n\r\nbuild up = grow or increase little by little\r\n一点一点积累、增加、变强。','1️⃣ 积累；堆积\r\n\r\nDust can build up quickly.\r\n\r\n灰尘会很快积起来。\r\n\r\nStress can build up over time.\r\n\r\n压力会随着时间慢慢积累。\r\n\r\nTraffic started to build up after 5 pm.\r\n\r\n下午 5 点以后交通开始堵起来。\r\n\r\n📌 这里的 build up = 越来越多，慢慢堆起来。\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 增强；培养；建立\r\n\r\nI’m trying to build up my confidence.\r\n\r\n我正在努力建立自信。\r\n\r\nYou need to build up your strength.\r\n\r\n你需要慢慢增强体力。\r\n\r\nShe built up a successful business.\r\n\r\n她慢慢建立起了一家成功的公司。\r\n\r\n📌 这里强调：慢慢发展起来，不是一夜之间完成。\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 夸大；吹捧；制造期待\r\n\r\nThe movie was really built up, but it wasn’t that good.\r\n\r\n这部电影之前被吹得很厉害，但其实没那么好。\r\n\r\nThey built him up as the next big star.\r\n\r\n他们把他包装成下一个大明星。\r\n\r\n📌 这里的 build up = 让别人觉得很厉害，制造期待。\r\n\r\n4️⃣ 名词：a build-up\r\n\r\na build-up = 积累；逐渐增加；铺垫；准备阶段\r\n\r\nThere was a build-up of rubbish outside the house.\r\n\r\n房子外面堆了很多垃圾。\r\n\r\nThere was a lot of build-up before the final match.\r\n\r\n决赛前有很多铺垫和宣传。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ It’s been building up for a while.\r\n这事已经积累一段时间了。\r\n\r\n✅ I need to build up my confidence.\r\n我需要慢慢建立自信。\r\n\r\n✅ The traffic is building up.\r\n车流开始变多了 / 开始堵了。\r\n\r\n✅ Don’t let stress build up.\r\n别让压力一直积累。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/fe252e12f56d4c92a820e19f914a03a8.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-11 14:52:47',1,'2026-05-11 14:52:47'),(1229,18,18,'phrase','It’s not necessarily …','It’s not necessarily …','It’s not necessarily …','意思是：\r\n不一定…… / 未必…… / 并不一定……','✅ 常见句型\r\n\r\nIt’s not necessarily true.\r\n这不一定是真的。\r\n\r\nIt’s not necessarily a bad thing.\r\n这未必是坏事。\r\n\r\nIt’s not necessarily expensive.\r\n它不一定贵。\r\n\r\nIt’s not necessarily because of money.\r\n这不一定是因为钱。','🗣️ 更自然口语\r\n\r\nNot necessarily.\r\n不一定。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nA: Is it cheaper online?\r\n网上买更便宜吗？\r\n\r\nB: Not necessarily.\r\n不一定。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n你可以这样记\r\n\r\nnecessary = 必要的\r\nnecessarily = 必然地；一定地\r\nnot necessarily = 不一定；未必\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nIt’s not necessarily true.\r\n这不一定是真的。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/cdb9f930723f4c5da7389fb7547232c7.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-11 15:10:43',1,'2026-05-11 15:10:43'),(1230,18,19,'phrase','comprehension','comprehension','comprehension','noun\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n理解；理解力；阅读理解；听力理解\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ncomprehension means the ability to understand something clearly.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n真正理解内容，而不是只看到或听到。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence 实用句\r\n\r\nReading more English articles can help improve your comprehension.\r\n多读英文文章可以帮助提高你的理解能力。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 comprehension 想成：\r\n\r\ncomplete understanding\r\n完整理解\r\n\r\n不是只认识单词，而是能明白整句话、整段话真正想表达什么。','1️⃣ 理解；理解能力\r\n\r\nHer comprehension of English has improved a lot.\r\n她的英语理解能力提高了很多。\r\n\r\nThis article is beyond my comprehension.\r\n这篇文章我理解不了。\r\n\r\nThe idea was difficult to comprehension. ❌\r\n这句话不对。\r\n\r\n应该说：\r\n\r\n✅ The idea was difficult to understand.\r\n这个想法很难理解。\r\n\r\n📌 注意：\r\ncomprehension 是名词，不能直接当动词用。\r\n\r\n2️⃣ Reading comprehension 阅读理解\r\n\r\nreading comprehension\r\n阅读理解\r\n\r\nThis test includes reading comprehension questions.\r\n这个考试包括阅读理解题。\r\n\r\nI want to improve my reading comprehension.\r\n我想提高我的阅读理解能力。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ Listening comprehension 听力理解\r\n\r\nlistening comprehension\r\n听力理解\r\n\r\nListening comprehension is harder for me than reading.\r\n对我来说，听力理解比阅读更难。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I understand the words, but I don’t fully understand the meaning.\r\n我认识这些词，但不完全理解意思。\r\n\r\n✅ My reading comprehension is getting better.\r\n我的阅读理解在变好。\r\n\r\n✅ I need to work on my listening comprehension.\r\n我需要提升我的听力理解。\r\n\r\n✅ It’s hard to take everything in.\r\n一下子全理解有点难。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/fb76cb04f7fe47f88b3b25247cb9eb7d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-11 15:33:34',1,'2026-05-11 15:33:34'),(1231,18,20,'phrase','from now on','from now on','from now on','phrase\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n从现在开始；从今以后；以后\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nfrom now on means starting now and continuing into the future.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n从这一刻开始，以后都这样。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 表示新的决定\r\n\r\nFrom now on, I’ll study English every day.\r\n从现在开始，我每天都会学英语。\r\n\r\nFrom now on, I’ll be more careful.\r\n从今以后，我会更小心。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 表示新的规则\r\n\r\nFrom now on, please arrive on time.\r\n从现在开始，请准时到。\r\n\r\nFrom now on, we need to check the prices carefully.\r\n从现在开始，我们需要仔细检查价格。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 表示习惯改变\r\n\r\nFrom now on, I’ll try to speak more English.\r\n从现在开始，我会尽量多说英语。\r\n\r\nFrom now on, I won’t leave things until the last minute.\r\n从今以后，我不会拖到最后一刻才做。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c07a80a90990419ca8f829438e61c04f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-12 07:26:50',1,'2026-05-12 07:26:50'),(1232,18,21,'phrase','do someone good','do someone good','do someone good','🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n对某人有好处；让某人受益；让某人感觉好一些\r\n\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ndo someone good means something is helpful, healthy, or beneficial for someone.\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n这件事会让你更好，对你有益。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence 实用句\r\n\r\nYou’ve been indoors all day. Some fresh air will do you good.\r\n你一整天都待在屋里。出去呼吸点新鲜空气会对你有好处。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 对身体有好处\r\n\r\nA good sleep will do you good.\r\n好好睡一觉会对你有好处。\r\n\r\nSome fresh air will do you good.\r\n出去呼吸点新鲜空气对你有好处。\r\n\r\nA walk after dinner will do you good.\r\n饭后散步对你有好处。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 对心情有好处\r\n\r\nA break will do you good.\r\n休息一下会让你好一些。\r\n\r\nTalking to someone might do you good.\r\n和别人聊聊可能会让你好受点。\r\n\r\nA holiday would do you good.\r\n去度个假会对你有好处。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 给建议时很自然\r\n\r\nYou’ve been working too hard. A day off would do you good.\r\n你最近工作太累了。休息一天会对你有好处。\r\n\r\nYou should get outside. It’ll do you good.\r\n你应该出去走走，这对你有好处。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ It’ll do you good.\r\n这会对你有好处的。\r\n\r\n✅ A bit of rest will do you good.\r\n休息一下会对你有好处。\r\n\r\n✅ Some time away might do you good.\r\n离开一阵子可能会让你好一些。\r\n\r\n✅ It did me good.\r\n这对我挺有帮助 / 让我感觉好多了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3a0d26bc1eb54a13981951378ecccf85.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-12 07:30:23',1,'2026-05-12 07:30:23'),(1233,18,22,'vocab','starry','starry','starry','🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n布满星星的；星光灿烂的\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nstarry means full of stars.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n天空里有很多星星，亮亮的、很漂亮。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n🌌 1. starry sky\r\n\r\na starry sky\r\n星空 / 满天星星的天空\r\n\r\nWe walked under the starry sky.\r\n我们在星空下散步。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🌙 2. starry night\r\n\r\na starry night\r\n星光灿烂的夜晚\r\n\r\nIt was a beautiful starry night.\r\n那是一个美丽的星夜。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n👀 3. starry-eyed\r\n\r\nstarry-eyed\r\n天真乐观的；充满幻想的；眼里有星星一样的\r\n\r\nShe was starry-eyed about moving overseas.\r\n她对搬到海外生活充满了美好的幻想。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ It’s such a starry night.\r\n今晚星星好多啊。\r\n\r\n✅ The sky is really starry tonight.\r\n今晚的天空星光灿烂。\r\n\r\n✅ Look at the stars — it’s beautiful.\r\n看那些星星，太美了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d04fa42bef8a455d842c485f3aad8aa6.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-12 07:32:38',1,'2026-05-12 07:32:38'),(1234,18,23,'vocab','stray','stray','stray','verb / adjective / noun\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n迷路；走失；离群的；流浪的；偏离主题\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nstray means to move away from the right place, group, path, or topic.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：离开原来的地方 / 路线 / 群体，跑偏了。\r\n\r\nAdjective 形容词：走失的；流浪的\r\n\r\n Noun 名词：流浪动物','1️⃣ Adjective 形容词：走失的；流浪的\r\n\r\n🐕 a stray dog\r\n\r\n一只流浪狗\r\n\r\n🐈 a stray cat\r\n\r\n一只流浪猫\r\n\r\nThere are a few stray cats near my house.\r\n我家附近有几只流浪猫。\r\n\r\n📌 这里的 stray 很常见，表示动物没有主人，或者走失了。\r\n\r\n2️⃣ Verb 动词：偏离；走失；离开原路\r\n\r\n🚶 Don’t stray too far from the path.\r\n\r\n不要离路太远。\r\n\r\n🧒 The child strayed from the group.\r\n\r\n那个孩子离开了队伍。\r\n\r\n💬 We’re straying from the main topic.\r\n\r\n我们有点偏离主题了。\r\n\r\n📌 这里的 stray = move away from where you should be.\r\n\r\n3️⃣ Noun 名词：流浪动物\r\n\r\n🐾 The shelter takes care of strays.\r\n\r\n这个收容所照顾流浪动物。\r\n\r\n这里 strays 通常指 stray cats or dogs。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ Is that a stray cat?\r\n那是只流浪猫吗？\r\n\r\n✅ Don’t stray too far.\r\n别走太远。\r\n\r\n✅ I think we’re straying off topic.\r\n我觉得我们有点跑题了。\r\n\r\n✅ The dog looks like a stray.\r\n这只狗看起来像流浪狗。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/39e2bb75353f4750adef545e6444c4a9.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-12 07:45:41',1,'2026-05-12 07:45:41'),(1235,18,24,'vocab','genuinely','genuinely','genuinely','adverb\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n真诚地；真正地；由衷地；确实地\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ngenuinely means truly, sincerely, or honestly.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n不是装的，不是假客气，而是真心的、真实的。\r\n\r\n✅ genuinely\r\n\r\n它来自形容词：\r\n\r\ngenuine = 真诚的；真实的\r\ngenuinely = 真诚地；真正地','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 真诚地 / 由衷地\r\n\r\nI’m genuinely sorry.\r\n我真心抱歉。\r\n\r\nI genuinely appreciate your help.\r\n我真心感谢你的帮助。\r\n\r\nShe genuinely cares about her students.\r\n她是真心关心她的学生。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 真正地 / 确实地\r\n\r\nI was genuinely surprised.\r\n我真的很惊讶。\r\n\r\nThat was genuinely funny.\r\n那个真的很好笑。\r\n\r\nHe seems genuinely interested.\r\n他看起来是真的感兴趣。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 强调不是假的\r\n\r\nHe was genuinely happy for me.\r\n他是真心为我高兴。\r\n\r\nI genuinely didn’t know.\r\n我真的不知道。\r\n\r\nThey made a genuinely good product.\r\n他们做出了一个真正好的产品。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I’m genuinely happy for you.\r\n我真心为你高兴。\r\n\r\n✅ I genuinely thought it was cheaper.\r\n我真的以为它更便宜。\r\n\r\n✅ That’s genuinely impressive.\r\n那真的很厉害。\r\n\r\n✅ I genuinely don’t mind.\r\n我真的不介意。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/fd3b066ea9c740cbad3c407e7f8ddea1.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-12 08:58:06',1,'2026-05-12 08:58:06'),(1236,18,25,'phrase','cheer someone up','cheer someone up','cheer someone up','cheer someone up\r\n/tʃɪə ˈsʌmwʌn ʌp/\r\nphrasal verb\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n让某人开心起来；安慰某人；使某人振作起来\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ncheer someone up means to make someone feel happier or less sad.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n别人心情不好，你做点什么让他开心一点、振作一点。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 让别人开心起来\r\n\r\nI tried to cheer her up.\r\n我试着让她开心起来。\r\n\r\nThis little gift might cheer him up.\r\n这个小礼物可能会让他开心点。\r\n\r\nA funny movie always cheers me up.\r\n搞笑电影总能让我开心起来。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 安慰别人\r\n\r\nShe was upset, so I tried to cheer her up.\r\n她很难过，所以我试着安慰她。\r\n\r\nLet’s take him out for coffee to cheer him up.\r\n我们带他出去喝杯咖啡，让他开心点吧。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 命令句：开心点 / 振作点\r\n\r\nCheer up!\r\n开心点！/ 振作点！\r\n\r\n⚠️ 但是要注意：\r\n如果别人真的很难过，直接说 Cheer up! 有时候会显得有点随便。更温柔可以说：\r\n\r\nI hope you feel better soon.\r\n希望你快点好起来。\r\n\r\nI’m here if you want to talk.\r\n如果你想聊聊，我在。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I just wanted to cheer you up.\r\n我只是想让你开心一点。\r\n\r\n✅ Maybe some fresh air will cheer you up.\r\n出去呼吸点新鲜空气可能会让你心情好点。\r\n\r\n✅ That really cheered me up.\r\n那真的让我心情好多了。\r\n\r\n✅ You always know how to cheer me up.\r\n你总是知道怎么让我开心起来。\r\n\r\nExamples\r\n\r\nI cheered up after the walk.\r\n散步之后我心情好了起来。\r\n\r\nThe walk cheered me up.\r\n这次散步让我心情好了起来。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence 实用句\r\n\r\nI brought you some chocolate to cheer you up.\r\n我给你带了点巧克力，想让你开心一点。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象一个人很难过 😔，你讲了个笑话、送了杯咖啡、陪他聊了聊。\r\n他的心情慢慢往上走 ⬆️。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncheer someone up = lift someone’s mood\r\n让某人的心情变好。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2f3d496b211e4f878f970f3f4589dadc.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-12 13:43:55',1,'2026-05-12 13:43:55'),(1237,18,26,'phrase','lick one’s lips','lick one’s lips','lick one’s lips','phrase / idiom\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n舔嘴唇；垂涎欲滴；非常期待\r\n\r\n注意：通常说 lick one’s lips，要用复数 lips。\r\n不太说 lick one’s lip，除非真的只舔一边嘴唇。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nlick one’s lips means someone touches their lips with their tongue, often because they are hungry, excited, or looking forward to something.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n看到好吃的或想到好事，忍不住舔嘴唇，表示很想要 / 很期待。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence 实用句\r\n\r\nThe smell of fresh bread made everyone lick their lips.\r\n新鲜面包的香味让每个人都馋得舔嘴唇。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象你看到一块很好吃的蛋糕 🍰，还没吃就已经开始舔嘴唇了。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nlick one’s lips = be hungry or excited for something\r\n馋了 / 很期待某事。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 真的舔嘴唇\r\n\r\nHe licked his lips after eating the cake.\r\n他吃完蛋糕后舔了舔嘴唇。\r\n\r\nShe licked her lips because they were dry.\r\n她舔了舔嘴唇，因为嘴唇干。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 看到好吃的，馋了\r\n\r\nThe children were licking their lips at the sight of the chocolate cake.\r\n孩子们看到巧克力蛋糕，馋得直舔嘴唇。\r\n\r\nThe smell of the roast chicken made me lick my lips.\r\n烤鸡的味道让我馋得舔嘴唇。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 比喻：非常期待 / 垂涎某个机会\r\n\r\nInvestors are licking their lips at the new opportunity.\r\n投资者对这个新机会很感兴趣，跃跃欲试。\r\n\r\nThe team will be licking their lips at the chance to win.\r\n这个队会非常期待赢的机会。\r\n\r\n📌 这个用法有时带一点“很想得到、很期待占到好处”的感觉。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ That cake looks amazing. I’m licking my lips already.\r\n那个蛋糕看起来太棒了，我已经馋了。\r\n\r\n✅ The kids were licking their lips when they saw the ice cream.\r\n孩子们看到冰淇淋都馋了。\r\n\r\n✅ They’ll be licking their lips at that opportunity.\r\n他们肯定会对那个机会很感兴趣。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/35c95a2935c342be845f679d39fbecb3.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-12 13:55:17',1,'2026-05-12 13:55:17'),(1238,18,27,'vocab','latch','latch','latch','noun / verb\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n门闩；插销；锁扣；扣上；抓住；理解并接受\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nlatch means a small device that keeps a door, gate, box, or lid closed.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n把东西扣住、锁住、固定住。','1️⃣ Noun 名词：门闩；锁扣；插销\r\n\r\n🔒 a door latch\r\n\r\n门闩 / 门锁扣\r\n\r\n🚪 a gate latch\r\n\r\n门栅锁扣\r\n\r\n🧰 a suitcase latch\r\n\r\n行李箱扣\r\n\r\nThe latch on the gate is broken.\r\n门栅上的锁扣坏了。\r\n\r\nMake sure the latch is closed.\r\n确认锁扣扣好了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ Verb 动词：扣上；闩上\r\n\r\nPlease latch the gate behind you.\r\n请你进来/出去后把门栅扣上。\r\n\r\nThe door didn’t latch properly.\r\n门没有扣好。\r\n\r\nI heard the box latch shut.\r\n我听见盒子“咔哒”一声扣上了。\r\n\r\n📌 这里的 latch 很像：\r\nclick shut / fasten shut\r\n“咔哒一下扣住”。\r\n\r\n3️⃣ Phrasal Verb: latch onto\r\n\r\n✅ latch onto something\r\n\r\n意思是：抓住；紧紧跟着；理解并接受某个想法\r\n\r\nThe baby latched onto the bottle.\r\n宝宝含住了奶瓶。\r\n\r\nHe quickly latched onto the idea.\r\n他很快理解并接受了这个想法。\r\n\r\nThe dog latched onto my sleeve.\r\n那只狗咬住/抓住了我的袖子。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ The door won’t latch.\r\n这门扣不上。\r\n\r\n✅ Can you latch the gate, please?\r\n你能把门栅扣上吗？\r\n\r\n✅ It didn’t latch properly.\r\n它没扣好。\r\n\r\n✅ He latched onto the idea straight away.\r\n他马上就理解并接受了这个想法。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/cfd5d105ab9f4ddb80ef065935c6de01.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-12 14:12:23',1,'2026-05-12 14:12:23'),(1239,18,28,'phrase','draw back','draw back','draw back','🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n后退；退缩；缩回；拉开；撤回\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ndrew back means someone or something moved backwards, often because of fear, surprise, disgust, or hesitation.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n身体往后一缩 / 心里打退堂鼓 / 把东西往后拉。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 身体后退 / 往后缩\r\n\r\nShe drew back in fear.\r\n她害怕地往后退了一下。\r\n\r\nHe drew back when the dog barked.\r\n狗叫的时候，他往后缩了一下。\r\n\r\nI drew back from the edge of the cliff.\r\n我从悬崖边退了回来。\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 因害怕或犹豫而退缩\r\n\r\nHe drew back from the challenge.\r\n他在挑战面前退缩了。\r\n\r\nShe almost agreed, but then drew back.\r\n她差点同意了，但后来又退缩了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 拉开 / 拉回某物\r\n\r\nHe drew back the curtain.\r\n他拉开了窗帘。\r\n\r\nShe drew back her hand quickly.\r\n她迅速把手缩了回来。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ He drew back a little.\r\n他稍微往后退了一下。\r\n\r\n✅ She drew back in surprise.\r\n她惊讶地往后缩了一下。\r\n\r\n✅ I drew my hand back.\r\n我把手缩了回来。\r\n\r\n✅ He drew back from the idea.\r\n他对这个想法有点退缩了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/345ffaa7126a4088a1ed472cb867d086.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-12 14:55:32',1,'2026-05-12 14:55:32'),(1240,18,29,'phrase','fell dead on the spot','fell dead on the spot','fell dead on the spot','phrase\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n当场倒地死亡；当场毙命；当场死去\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nfell dead on the spot means someone died immediately at that place.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n事情发生后，人马上倒下并当场死亡。','✅ Example Sentences 例句\r\n\r\nHe was struck by lightning and fell dead on the spot.\r\n他被闪电击中，当场倒地身亡。\r\n\r\nThe soldier was shot and fell dead on the spot.\r\n那个士兵中枪后当场倒地死亡。\r\n\r\nThe old tree collapsed, and the bird fell dead on the spot.\r\n那棵老树倒下了，那只鸟当场死了。','🗣️ More Natural / Softer Expressions 更自然或委婉说法\r\n\r\n这个表达有点直接、戏剧化、书面或新闻感。日常口语里可以说：\r\n\r\n✅ He died instantly.\r\n\r\n他当场死亡 / 立刻死了。\r\n\r\n✅ He died on the spot.\r\n\r\n他当场死亡。\r\n\r\n✅ He passed away at the scene.\r\n\r\n他在现场去世了。\r\n更委婉、正式。\r\n\r\n✅ He was killed instantly.\r\n\r\n他当场遇难。\r\n常用于事故、袭击等。\r\n\r\nfell dead on the spot 通常用于比较严重、突然的死亡场景，比如：\r\n\r\n* accident 事故\r\n* attack 袭击\r\n* lightning strike 雷击\r\n* shooting 枪击\r\n* heart attack 心脏病突发','/static/uploads/english_note_item/722baf0878eb410bbe252c7bcbef9bc4.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-12 15:13:37',1,'2026-05-12 15:13:37'),(1241,18,30,'phrase','tempt','tempt','tempt','verb\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n诱惑；引诱；吸引；使想做某事\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ntempt means to make someone want to do or have something, especially something they probably should not do or do not need.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n让你心动，让你忍不住想要。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 食物诱惑\r\n\r\nThe smell of fresh bread tempted me.\r\n新鲜面包的香味诱惑了我。\r\n\r\nI was tempted to buy a cake.\r\n我忍不住想买块蛋糕。\r\n\r\nDon’t tempt me!\r\n别诱惑我！\r\n\r\n📌 这个在口语里很常见，比如别人说：“要不要来点巧克力？”你可以开玩笑说：\r\n\r\nDon’t tempt me!\r\n别诱惑我，我真的会想买/想吃！\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 让人想做某事\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\nbe tempted to do something\r\n忍不住想做某事 / 有点想做某事\r\n\r\nI’m tempted to try it.\r\n我有点想试试。\r\n\r\nI’m tempted to buy it, but it’s a bit expensive.\r\n我有点想买，但它有点贵。\r\n\r\nShe was tempted to quit her job.\r\n她有点想辞职。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 引诱某人做不该做的事\r\n\r\nThe offer tempted him to lie.\r\n这个提议诱使他说谎。\r\n\r\nDon’t be tempted to spend all your money.\r\n不要被诱惑把钱全花了。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I’m tempted.\r\n我有点心动了。\r\n\r\n✅ I’m really tempted to buy it.\r\n我真的有点想买。\r\n\r\n✅ Don’t tempt me.\r\n别诱惑我。\r\n\r\n✅ That cake looks tempting.\r\n那个蛋糕看起来很诱人。\r\n\r\n✅ I was tempted, but I didn’t buy it.\r\n我当时挺心动的，但没买。\r\n\r\nExamples\r\n\r\nThe discount tempted me to buy it.\r\n这个折扣让我忍不住想买。\r\n\r\nThe shop window attracted a lot of customers.\r\n这个橱窗吸引了很多顾客。\r\n\r\n📌 tempt 常带有一点“我知道可能不该，但我想要”的感觉。\r\n📌 attract 更中性，只是“吸引”。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/907a81b51a5d413ba4c6758435b75356.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-12 15:24:25',1,'2026-05-12 15:24:25'),(1242,18,31,'phrase','I take it','I take it','I take it','phrase\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n我理解是……；我猜……；我认为应该是……','🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nI take it means:\r\n\r\nI assume / I understand / I guess\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n根据现在的信息，我理解是这样，对吗？\r\n\r\n它通常带有一点 “我推测 / 我理解” 的感觉，不是非常确定。','✅ Common Pattern 常见句型\r\n\r\n1️⃣ I take it that + sentence\r\n\r\nI take it that you agree with this plan.\r\n我理解你同意这个计划。\r\n\r\nI take it that the meeting is still on.\r\n我理解会议还是照常进行。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ I take it + sentence\r\n\r\n口语里 that 可以省略。\r\n\r\nI take it you’ve already finished the report.\r\n我猜你已经完成报告了。\r\n\r\nI take it you’re not coming tomorrow.\r\n我猜你明天不来了。\r\n\r\n🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I take it you’re happy with this approach?\r\n我理解你对这个方法满意，对吗？\r\n\r\n✅ I take it we should continue with the current design?\r\n我理解我们应该继续用现在这个设计，对吗？\r\n\r\n✅ I take it this is the final version?\r\n我理解这是最终版本，对吗？\r\n\r\n✅ I take it you’ve already spoken to him?\r\n我猜你已经和他说过了？','/static/uploads/english_note_item/792fdf23ee024ecd915c4f08e42c27f6.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 08:32:19',1,'2026-05-13 08:32:19'),(1243,18,32,'vocab','be covered with piles of something','be covered with piles of something','be covered with piles of something','🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n被一堆堆……覆盖；到处堆满了……\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nbe covered with piles of sth means a surface or place has many things stacked or spread all over it.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n某个地方上面到处都是一堆一堆的东西。\r\n\r\n比如：桌子上、地板上、办公室里，到处堆着纸、书、衣服等。','✅ Sentence Pattern 句型\r\n\r\nplace / surface + be covered with piles of + noun\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe desk was covered with piles of papers.\r\n桌子上堆满了一堆堆文件。\r\n\r\n📌 Common Examples 常见例句\r\n\r\n📝 1. Papers 文件\r\n\r\nHis desk was covered with piles of papers.\r\n他的桌子上堆满了一堆堆文件。\r\n\r\nThe office was covered with piles of old documents.\r\n办公室里到处都是一堆堆旧文件。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n📚 2. Books 书\r\n\r\nThe table was covered with piles of books.\r\n桌子上堆满了一堆堆书。\r\n\r\nHer room was covered with piles of textbooks.\r\n她房间里到处都是一堆堆课本。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n👕 3. Clothes 衣服\r\n\r\nThe floor was covered with piles of clothes.\r\n地板上堆满了一堆堆衣服。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ His desk was covered with papers.\r\n他的桌子上全是文件。\r\n更简单、更口语。\r\n\r\n✅ There were piles of papers everywhere.\r\n到处都是一堆堆文件。\r\n非常自然。\r\n\r\n✅ The whole office was full of papers.\r\n整个办公室都是文件。\r\n更口语。\r\n\r\n✅ The desk was buried under piles of papers.\r\n桌子被一堆堆文件“埋”住了。\r\n更形象。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2456b21d36474f62825ef6e12baf5ed3.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 17:00:52',1,'2026-05-13 17:00:52'),(1244,18,33,'phrase','cross-stitch','cross-stitch','cross-stitch','🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n十字绣；做十字绣\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ncross-stitch is a type of embroidery where you make many small X-shaped stitches to create a picture or pattern.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n用很多小小的 X 形针脚 绣出图案。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence 实用句\r\n\r\nI started a cross-stitch project on Sunday, but it might take me ages to finish it.\r\n我周日开始做一个十字绣作品，但可能要花很久才能完成。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 名词：十字绣\r\n\r\nI started a cross-stitch on Sunday.\r\n我周日开始做一个十字绣。\r\n\r\nThis cross-stitch pattern is really detailed.\r\n这个十字绣图案非常精细。\r\n\r\nShe gave me a handmade cross-stitch.\r\n她送了我一个手工十字绣。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 动词：做十字绣\r\n\r\nI like to cross-stitch in the evenings.\r\n我喜欢晚上做十字绣。\r\n\r\nShe cross-stitched a picture of a cat.\r\n她绣了一幅猫的十字绣。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I’ve started doing cross-stitch.\r\n我开始做十字绣了。\r\n\r\n✅ I’m working on a cross-stitch project.\r\n我正在做一个十字绣作品。\r\n\r\n✅ It’s going to take me ages to finish it.\r\n我估计要花很久才能完成。\r\n\r\n✅ Cross-stitch is harder than it looks.\r\n十字绣比看起来难多了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/1dd36e2387324d6aa1be5397bf673f98.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 17:47:06',1,'2026-05-13 17:47:06'),(1245,18,34,'vocab','addict','addict','addict','/ˈædɪkt/\r\nnoun\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n上瘾的人；沉迷者\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nAn addict is a person who cannot stop doing or using something, even when it causes problems.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n控制不住地依赖某个东西或行为。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 对药物、酒精等上瘾的人\r\n\r\nHe is a drug addict.\r\n他是一个吸毒成瘾者。\r\n\r\nShe used to be an alcohol addict.\r\n她以前有酒精成瘾问题。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 这类表达比较敏感，日常说别人时要小心。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 对某种活动非常沉迷的人\r\n\r\n这个用法比较轻松、口语化。\r\n\r\nI’m a coffee addict.\r\n我是个咖啡迷 / 离不开咖啡。\r\n\r\nHe’s a video game addict.\r\n他沉迷电子游戏。\r\n\r\nShe’s a shopping addict.\r\n她特别爱购物 / 有点购物上瘾。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I’m addicted to coffee.\r\n我对咖啡上瘾了。\r\n\r\n✅ He’s addicted to his phone.\r\n他手机上瘾。\r\n\r\n✅ I’m a bit of a coffee addict.\r\n我有点离不开咖啡。\r\n\r\n✅ She’s a total book addict.\r\n她特别爱看书。\r\n\r\nExamples\r\n\r\nI’m a coffee addict.\r\n我是个咖啡迷。\r\n\r\nI’m addicted to coffee.\r\n我对咖啡上瘾。\r\n\r\nCoffee addiction can be hard to break.\r\n咖啡成瘾可能很难戒掉。\r\n\r\n❌ Common Mistake 常见错误\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ I addict coffee.\r\n❌ I am addict to coffee.\r\n\r\n应该说：\r\n\r\n✅ I’m addicted to coffee.\r\n我对咖啡上瘾。\r\n\r\n✅ I’m a coffee addict.\r\n我是个咖啡迷。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence 实用句\r\n\r\nI’m a bit of a phone addict, so I’m trying to use my phone less.\r\n我有点手机上瘾，所以我正在努力少用手机。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/75c806ffa37544bb8678a15ad9e9d1d0.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 18:43:20',1,'2026-05-13 18:43:20'),(1246,18,35,'phrase','reluctant','reluctant','reluctant','adjective\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n不情愿的；勉强的；犹豫不愿意的\r\n\r\n你写的是 relucant，正确拼写是：\r\nreluctant ✅\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nreluctant means you do not really want to do something, but you may still do it.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n心里不太愿意，但可能还是会做。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ be reluctant to do something\r\n\r\n不情愿做某事\r\n\r\nI was reluctant to ask for help.\r\n我不太愿意开口求助。\r\n\r\nShe was reluctant to speak in front of the class.\r\n她不太愿意在全班面前讲话。\r\n\r\nHe is reluctant to change his mind.\r\n他不太愿意改变主意。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ feel reluctant\r\n\r\n感到不情愿 / 有点犹豫\r\n\r\nI felt reluctant at first, but later I agreed.\r\n一开始我有点不情愿，但后来我同意了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ a reluctant decision / choice\r\n\r\n一个勉强做出的决定 / 选择\r\n\r\nIt was a reluctant decision.\r\n这是一个勉强做出的决定。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I’m a bit reluctant to do that.\r\n我有点不太想那么做。\r\n\r\n✅ I was reluctant at first.\r\n我一开始不太情愿。\r\n\r\n✅ She seemed reluctant to join us.\r\n她看起来不太愿意加入我们。\r\n\r\n✅ He was reluctant, but he said yes in the end.\r\n他不太情愿，但最后还是答应了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f447e38b05db464eb514d87dda5ddbde.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 18:53:11',1,'2026-05-13 18:53:11'),(1247,18,36,'phrase','I’m still experimenting','I’m still experimenting','I’m still experimenting','spoken phrase\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n我还在尝试；我还在摸索；我还在试不同的方法\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nI’m still experimenting means:\r\n\r\nI’m trying different things to see what works best.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n我还没确定哪种最好，所以我还在不断试。','✅ Common Pattern 常见句型\r\n\r\n1. I’m still experimenting with + noun\r\n\r\nI’m still experimenting with tea.\r\n我还在尝试不同的茶。\r\n\r\nI’m still experimenting with different ingredients.\r\n我还在尝试不同的配料。\r\n\r\nI’m still experimenting with my study routine.\r\n我还在摸索我的学习安排。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. I’m still experimenting with how to + verb\r\n\r\nI’m still experimenting with how to make it taste better.\r\n我还在尝试怎么让它味道更好。\r\n\r\nI’m still experimenting with how to explain this clearly.\r\n我还在摸索怎么把这个解释清楚。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I’m still experimenting.\r\n我还在摸索。\r\n\r\n✅ I’m still experimenting with different teas.\r\n我还在尝试不同的茶。\r\n\r\n✅ I’m still trying things out.\r\n我还在试试看。\r\n更口语、更轻松。\r\n\r\n✅ I’m still figuring out what I like.\r\n我还在摸索自己喜欢什么。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/4ab88180bfb14e829422c3bfe027e0b8.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 19:07:29',1,'2026-05-13 19:07:29'),(1248,18,37,'vocab','photography','photography','photography','/fəˈtɒɡrəfi/ UK/NZ\r\n/fəˈtɑːɡrəfi/ US\r\nnoun\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n摄影；摄影术；摄影艺术\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nphotography means the activity, skill, or art of taking photos.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n用相机或手机拍照片的技术和艺术。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 摄影这件事\r\n\r\nI’m interested in photography.\r\n我对摄影感兴趣。\r\n\r\nPhotography is one of my hobbies.\r\n摄影是我的爱好之一。\r\n\r\nHe studied photography at university.\r\n他在大学学过摄影。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 某种摄影类型\r\n\r\nlandscape photography\r\n风景摄影\r\n\r\nportrait photography\r\n人像摄影\r\n\r\nwildlife photography\r\n野生动物摄影\r\n\r\nwedding photography\r\n婚礼摄影\r\n\r\nstreet photography\r\n街头摄影\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 摄影技术 / 风格\r\n\r\nGood lighting is important in photography.\r\n好的光线在摄影中很重要。\r\n\r\nHer photography style is very natural.\r\n她的摄影风格很自然。\r\n\r\nDigital photography has changed a lot over the years.\r\n数码摄影这些年变化很大。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I’m into photography.\r\n我挺喜欢摄影的。\r\n\r\n✅ I enjoy taking photos.\r\n我喜欢拍照。\r\n\r\n✅ I’m learning photography at the moment.\r\n我最近在学摄影。\r\n\r\n✅ I’m not a professional. I just do photography as a hobby.\r\n我不是专业的，我只是把摄影当作爱好。\r\n\r\n❌ Common Mistake 常见错误\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ I like take photography.\r\n\r\n更自然：\r\n\r\n✅ I like photography.\r\n我喜欢摄影。\r\n\r\n✅ I like taking photos.\r\n我喜欢拍照。\r\n\r\n✅ I’m interested in photography.\r\n我对摄影感兴趣。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence 实用句\r\n\r\nI’m interested in photography, especially landscape photography.\r\n我对摄影感兴趣，尤其是风景摄影。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/fd616003a284400b9edf8ef13fa9fafc.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-14 06:47:54',1,'2026-05-14 06:47:54'),(1249,18,38,'phrase','adopt','adopt','adopt','🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n收养；采用；采纳；正式通过\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nadopt means to choose to take something as your own.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n把某人、某物、某种方法正式接受过来，变成自己的。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 收养孩子 / 动物\r\n\r\nThey adopted a child.\r\n他们收养了一个孩子。\r\n\r\nWe adopted a stray cat.\r\n我们收养了一只流浪猫。\r\n\r\nThe dog was adopted from a shelter.\r\n这只狗是从动物收容所领养的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 采用方法 / 系统 / 策略\r\n\r\nThe company adopted a new system.\r\n公司采用了一个新系统。\r\n\r\nWe decided to adopt this approach.\r\n我们决定采用这个方法。\r\n\r\nMany schools have adopted online learning tools.\r\n很多学校已经采用了线上学习工具。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 采纳观点 / 态度\r\n\r\nShe adopted a positive attitude.\r\n她采取了积极的态度。\r\n\r\nHe adopted a more careful approach.\r\n他采取了更谨慎的方法。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n4. 正式通过法律 / 政策\r\n\r\nThe policy was adopted last year.\r\n这项政策去年被正式通过。\r\n\r\nThe proposal was adopted by the committee.\r\n这个提案被委员会采纳了。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ We adopted a cat from the shelter.\r\n我们从收容所领养了一只猫。\r\n\r\n✅ I think we should adopt this approach.\r\n我觉得我们应该采用这个方法。\r\n\r\n✅ The team adopted a new workflow.\r\n团队采用了一个新的工作流程。\r\n\r\n✅ They’ve adopted a more flexible policy.\r\n他们采用了更灵活的政策。\r\n\r\nExamples\r\n\r\nWe adopted a new system.\r\n我们采用了一个新系统。\r\n\r\nWe adapted the system for our team.\r\n我们把这个系统改成适合我们团队使用。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n❌ Common Mistake 常见错误\r\n\r\n不要混淆：\r\n\r\n❌ We adapted a new policy.\r\n如果意思是“采用政策”，不自然。\r\n\r\n✅ We adopted a new policy.\r\n我们采用了一项新政策。\r\n\r\n如果是“修改政策让它适合某个情况”，可以说：\r\n\r\n✅ We adapted the policy to suit our needs.\r\n我们调整了这项政策，以适应我们的需要。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence 实用句\r\n\r\nI think we should adopt this approach because it is simpler and easier for users to understand.\r\n我认为我们应该采用这个方法，因为它更简单，也更容易让用户理解。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b2e93938a35846408bf07ec13ab30443.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-14 06:56:01',1,'2026-05-14 06:56:01'),(1250,18,39,'phrase','From time to time','From time to time','From time to time','adverbial phrase\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n偶尔；有时；时不时\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nfrom time to time means sometimes, but not very often.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n不是经常发生，但偶尔会发生。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 偶尔做某事\r\n\r\nI go for a walk from time to time.\r\n我偶尔会去散步。\r\n\r\nI still play badminton from time to time.\r\n我偶尔还会打羽毛球。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 偶尔有某种感觉\r\n\r\nEveryone feels lonely from time to time.\r\n每个人都会偶尔感到孤独。\r\n\r\nI feel stressed from time to time.\r\n我偶尔会感到压力大。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 偶尔发生某事\r\n\r\nProblems can happen from time to time.\r\n问题偶尔会发生。\r\n\r\nThe system may slow down from time to time.\r\n系统有时可能会变慢。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nIt’s normal to feel lonely from time to time.\r\n偶尔感到孤独是很正常的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把它想成：\r\n\r\nfrom one time to another time\r\n从一个时间点到另一个时间点之间，偶尔发生一次\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nfrom time to time = occasionally = 偶尔 / 时不时.','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I do that from time to time.\r\n我偶尔会那样做。\r\n\r\n✅ It happens from time to time.\r\n这种事偶尔会发生。\r\n\r\n✅ I still think about it from time to time.\r\n我偶尔还会想起这件事。\r\n\r\n✅ We all feel lonely from time to time.\r\n我们都会偶尔感到孤独。\r\n\r\n⚠️ from time to time vs sometimes\r\n\r\nsometimes 更普通，任何场景都可以用。\r\nfrom time to time 更强调“不频繁，只是偶尔”。\r\n\r\nExamples\r\n\r\nI sometimes drink tea.\r\n我有时候喝茶。\r\n\r\nI drink tea from time to time.\r\n我偶尔喝茶。\r\n\r\n第二句听起来更像：\r\n“不是每天喝，只是偶尔喝一下。”','/static/uploads/english_note_item/dc4516064bfc49be983b99f0d3603f36.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-14 07:33:22',1,'2026-05-14 07:33:22'),(1251,18,40,'phrase','keen','keen','keen','adjective\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n感兴趣的；热衷的；愿意的；敏锐的\r\n\r\n在新西兰和英国英语里，keen 非常常用，口语里很自然。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nkeen means you are interested, enthusiastic, or willing to do something.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n挺想做 / 挺感兴趣 / 很乐意\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nI’m keen to improve my spoken English, especially natural New Zealand expressions.\r\n我很想提高我的英语口语，尤其是自然的新西兰表达。\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n你可以把 keen 理解成：\r\n\r\ninterested and willing\r\n感兴趣，而且愿意做\r\n\r\n所以别人问：\r\n\r\nAre you keen?\r\n就是：\r\n\r\nDo you want to do it? / Are you interested?\r\n你想去吗？你有兴趣吗？','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. be keen on + noun / verb-ing\r\n\r\n表示：喜欢；对……感兴趣\r\n\r\nI’m keen on hiking.\r\n我挺喜欢徒步。\r\n\r\nShe’s keen on photography.\r\n她对摄影很感兴趣。\r\n\r\nI’m not really keen on spicy food.\r\n我不太喜欢辣的食物。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. be keen to do something\r\n\r\n表示：很想做某事 / 愿意做某事\r\n\r\nI’m keen to learn more about it.\r\n我很想多了解一下。\r\n\r\nHe’s keen to join the project.\r\n他很想加入这个项目。\r\n\r\nI’m keen to give it a go.\r\n我挺想试试看。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. keen = sharp / strong 敏锐的\r\n\r\n这个用法稍微正式一点。\r\n\r\nShe has a keen eye for detail.\r\n她对细节很敏锐。\r\n\r\nHe has a keen interest in technology.\r\n他对技术有浓厚兴趣。','🗣️ Natural NZ Spoken English 新西兰常用口语\r\n\r\n✅ I’m keen.\r\n我愿意 / 我挺想去。\r\n\r\n✅ Are you keen?\r\n你想去吗？/ 你有兴趣吗？\r\n\r\n✅ Yeah, keen as.\r\n当然，非常愿意。\r\n这是很 Kiwi 的说法。\r\n\r\n✅ I’m keen to give it a try.\r\n我挺想试试看。\r\n\r\n✅ I’m not too keen on that.\r\n我不太感兴趣 / 不太喜欢那个。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c9aecc190c5b46138ad02eed24c85d6f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-14 08:37:33',1,'2026-05-14 08:37:33'),(1252,18,41,'phrase','hold up well','hold up well','hold up well','phrasal verb phrase\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n保持得不错；经受得住；撑得住；耐用\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nhold up well means something or someone stays in good condition after time, pressure, use, or difficulty.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n经历时间、压力或使用之后，状态仍然不错。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nConsidering how old it is, it still holds up really well.\r\n考虑到它已经这么旧了，它仍然保持得非常不错。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象一双鞋 👟 穿了很久，经历雨天、走路、跑步，但还没坏。\r\n\r\n这就叫：\r\n\r\nhold up well = remain in good condition\r\n经受住使用或时间考验，状态仍然不错。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 物品：耐用，保持得不错\r\n\r\nThese shoes hold up well.\r\n这双鞋挺耐穿。\r\n\r\nThe jacket has held up well after two years.\r\n这件夹克穿了两年还保持得不错。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 人：身体或情绪撑得住\r\n\r\nShe’s holding up well after the operation.\r\n她手术后状态还不错。\r\n\r\nHow are you holding up?\r\n你还好吗？/ 你撑得住吗？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 系统 / 网站：稳定，经受住压力\r\n\r\nThe system held up well under heavy traffic.\r\n系统在高流量下表现稳定。\r\n\r\nThe website is holding up well so far.\r\n网站目前运行得还不错。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ It holds up well.\r\n它很耐用 / 保持得不错。\r\n\r\n✅ It’s holding up well.\r\n它目前状态还不错。\r\n\r\n✅ The car is holding up pretty well.\r\n这辆车状态还挺好。\r\n\r\n✅ The system held up well during the test.\r\n系统在测试期间表现稳定。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/fc91264cb05747bea3ac5571f90c6160.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-14 12:30:32',1,'2026-05-14 12:30:32'),(1253,18,42,'phrase','short-sightedness','short-sightedness','short-sightedness','noun\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n近视；目光短浅\r\n\r\nshort-sightedness ✅\r\n\r\n也可以写成：\r\n\r\nshortsightedness ✅\r\n美式更常见，不加连字符。\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nshort-sightedness 有两个主要意思：\r\n\r\n1. 医学上：近视\r\n2. 比喻：目光短浅','🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nshort-sightedness 有两个主要意思：\r\n\r\n1. 医学上：近视\r\n\r\n意思是看近处清楚，但看远处模糊。\r\n\r\nI have short-sightedness.  我有近视。\r\n\r\n更日常口语常说：\r\n\r\nI’m short-sighted.  我近视。\r\n\r\n在美式英语里常说：\r\n\r\nI’m nearsighted. 我近视。\r\n\r\n2. 比喻：目光短浅\r\n\r\n意思是只考虑眼前，不考虑长期影响。\r\n\r\nThe decision shows short-sightedness.\r\n这个决定显示出目光短浅。\r\n\r\nIt was short-sightedness to cut the training budget.\r\n削减培训预算是目光短浅的做法。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I’m short-sighted, so I need glasses.\r\n我近视，所以需要戴眼镜。\r\n\r\n✅ I can’t see things far away clearly.\r\n我看不清远处的东西。\r\n\r\n✅ That’s a bit short-sighted.\r\n那有点目光短浅。\r\n\r\n✅ It’s short-sighted to focus only on short-term profit.\r\n只关注短期利润是目光短浅的。\r\n\r\nshort-sightedness vs short-sighted\r\nshort-sightedness  noun 名词               近视；目光短浅\r\nshort-sighted         adjective 形容词     近视的；目光短浅的\r\n\r\nI have short-sightedness.   我有近视。\r\n\r\nI’m short-sighted. 我近视。\r\n\r\nThat was a short-sighted decision.\r\n那是一个目光短浅的决定。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3f1f0a94774b4f0e8b552b82d6af1713.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-14 14:50:39',1,'2026-05-14 14:50:39'),(1254,18,43,'phrase','at the expense of','at the expense of','at the expense of','phrase\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n以……为代价；牺牲……；损害……\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nat the expense of means one thing is gained or improved, but another thing is harmed, reduced, or sacrificed.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n为了得到 A，牺牲了 B。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 以健康为代价\r\n\r\nHe worked long hours at the expense of his health.\r\n他长时间工作，以健康为代价。\r\n\r\nShe focused on her career at the expense of her personal life.\r\n她专注事业，却牺牲了个人生活。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 以质量为代价\r\n\r\nThe company reduced costs at the expense of quality.\r\n公司降低了成本，但牺牲了质量。\r\n\r\nDon’t improve speed at the expense of accuracy.\r\n不要为了提高速度而牺牲准确性。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 以别人利益为代价\r\n\r\nSome people make profits at the expense of others.\r\n有些人以牺牲他人的利益来赚钱。\r\n\r\nThe policy benefits large companies at the expense of small businesses.\r\n这项政策让大公司受益，却损害了小企业。\r\n\r\nat the expense of health 以健康为代价\r\n\r\nat the expense of quality  以质量为代价\r\n\r\nat the expense of safety  以安全为代价\r\n\r\nat the expense of accuracy  以准确性为代价\r\n\r\nat the expense of others  以他人为代价\r\n\r\nat the expense of personal life  以个人生活为代价','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ Don’t do it at the expense of your health.\r\n不要以健康为代价去做这件事。\r\n\r\n✅ We shouldn’t save money at the expense of quality.\r\n我们不应该为了省钱而牺牲质量。\r\n\r\n✅ Speed should not come at the expense of safety.\r\n速度不应该以安全为代价。\r\n\r\n✅ He succeeded, but at the expense of his family life.\r\n他成功了，但牺牲了家庭生活。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a4bf2c19886f4d0591ee7e6bc32efa00.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-14 15:15:34',1,'2026-05-14 15:15:34'),(1255,18,44,'vocab','illustrate','illustrate','illustrate','verb\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n说明；阐明；举例说明；配插图\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nillustrate means to make something clearer or easier to understand, often by using examples, pictures, charts, or explanations.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n让别人更容易看懂 / 理解。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 用例子说明\r\n\r\nThis example illustrates the problem clearly.\r\n这个例子清楚地说明了这个问题。\r\n\r\nLet me illustrate my point with an example.\r\n让我用一个例子来说明我的观点。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 用图片 / 图表说明\r\n\r\nThe diagram illustrates how the system works.\r\n这个图说明了系统是如何工作的。\r\n\r\nThe chart illustrates the change in rainfall over time.\r\n这个图表展示了降雨量随时间的变化。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 给书配插图\r\n\r\nShe illustrates children’s books.\r\n她给儿童书画插图。\r\n\r\nThe book is beautifully illustrated.\r\n这本书插图很漂亮。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ This example illustrates what I mean.\r\n这个例子说明了我的意思。\r\n\r\n✅ The picture illustrates the process.\r\n这张图说明了这个过程。\r\n\r\n✅ Let me illustrate it with a simple example.\r\n我用一个简单例子来说明一下。\r\n\r\n✅ It’s easier to understand when it’s illustrated visually.\r\n用图展示出来会更容易理解。\r\n\r\n🧩 illustrate a point. 说明一个观点\r\n\r\n📊 illustrate a trend. 展示一个趋势\r\n\r\n📈 illustrate a change 展示变化\r\n\r\n🖼️ illustrate a process  说明一个过程\r\n\r\n📚 illustrated book  插图书\r\n\r\n🎨 beautifully illustrated  插图精美的','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d0df7520d515409694c08a21b124601c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-15 13:32:07',1,'2026-05-15 13:32:07'),(1256,18,45,'phrase','raise their young','raise their young','raise their young','verb phrase\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n抚养幼崽；养育后代；照顾小动物长大\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nraise their young means animals or people care for their babies until they grow up.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n父母照顾孩子 / 动物照顾幼崽，让它们长大。\r\n\r\n这里的 young 是名词，意思是：\r\n\r\n幼崽；幼小的后代','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 动物养育幼崽\r\n\r\nBirds build nests to raise their young.\r\n鸟筑巢来抚养幼鸟。\r\n\r\nPenguins work together to raise their young.\r\n企鹅一起抚养幼崽。\r\n\r\nMany animals protect their young from danger.\r\n许多动物保护自己的幼崽免受危险。\r\n \r\n2. 人类抚养孩子\r\n\r\n人类也可以说：\r\n\r\nThey raised their children in New Zealand.\r\n他们在新西兰抚养孩子。\r\n\r\n但是对人更常说：\r\n\r\nraise children  抚养孩子\r\n\r\n对动物更常说：\r\n\r\nraise their young  抚养幼崽','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ They stay there to raise their young.\r\n它们留在那里抚养幼崽。\r\n\r\n✅ The mother bird feeds her young.\r\n鸟妈妈喂养她的幼鸟。\r\n\r\n✅ Animals need a safe place to raise their young.\r\n动物需要一个安全的地方来抚养后代。\r\n\r\n✅ They protect their young.\r\n它们保护自己的幼崽。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9b457dfeb1214312930733c710147dbc.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-15 14:34:52',1,'2026-05-15 14:34:52'),(1257,18,46,'phrase','way before','way before','way before','informal phrase\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n早在……之前；比……早很多；远早于……\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nway before means much earlier than something.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n不是刚早一点，而是早很多。\r\n\r\n这里的 way 不是“道路”，而是口语里的加强语气，表示：\r\n\r\nmuch / far / a lot\r\n非常；远远；很多','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 早在某个时间之前\r\n\r\nI knew him way before he became famous.\r\n我早在他出名之前就认识他了。\r\n\r\nShe moved to New Zealand way before me.\r\n她比我早很多就搬到新西兰了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 远早于某件事发生\r\n\r\nThis problem started way before the update.\r\n这个问题早在更新之前就开始了。\r\n\r\nWe had planned this way before the meeting.\r\n我们早在会议之前就计划好了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 口语中强调“很早”\r\n\r\nI arrived way before everyone else.\r\n我比其他人早到了很多。\r\n\r\nThat happened way before I joined the company.\r\n那件事发生在我加入公司很久以前。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ That was way before my time.\r\n那是我来之前很久的事了。/ 那是我出生前很久的事了。\r\n\r\n✅ I got there way before 9.\r\n我 9 点之前很早就到了。\r\n\r\n✅ We met way before university.\r\n我们早在大学之前就认识了。\r\n\r\n✅ He knew about it way before I did.\r\n他比我早很多就知道这件事了。\r\n\r\nExamples\r\n\r\nI arrived way before the class started.\r\n我在上课前很早就到了。\r\n\r\nI arrived just before the class started.\r\n我刚好在上课前到。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nI started learning English way before I came to New Zealand, but I still need more speaking practice.\r\n我早在来新西兰之前就开始学英语了，但我仍然需要更多口语练习。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n把 way before 想成：\r\n\r\nfar before / much earlier\r\n远在……之前 / 早很多\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nway before the meeting\r\n= 会议之前很久。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ccfdab3a1b6745a9a4a9c06f99002392.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-15 14:39:15',1,'2026-05-15 14:39:15'),(1258,18,47,'vocab','catchy','catchy','catchy','adjective\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n朗朗上口的；容易记住的；吸引人的\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ncatchy means something is easy to remember and attractive, especially a song, phrase, slogan, title, or tune.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n一下子抓住你的注意力，而且很容易记住。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nWe need a catchy title that is easy for people to remember.\r\n我们需要一个吸引人而且容易让人记住的标题。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n把 catchy 想成：\r\n\r\ncatch your attention\r\n抓住你的注意力\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncatchy = easy to remember and attractive\r\n容易记住，又吸引人。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 歌曲 / 旋律朗朗上口\r\n\r\nThis song is really catchy.\r\n这首歌真的很洗脑 / 很朗朗上口。\r\n\r\nThe melody is catchy.\r\n这个旋律很容易记住。\r\n\r\nIt has a catchy tune.\r\n它有一个很抓耳的旋律。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 标语 / 标题吸引人\r\n\r\nThat’s a catchy slogan.\r\n那个标语很吸引人，也容易记住。\r\n\r\nWe need a catchy title for the presentation.\r\n我们需要一个吸引人的 presentation 标题。\r\n\r\nThe app needs a catchy name.\r\n这个 app 需要一个好记又吸引人的名字。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 广告 / 内容容易吸引注意\r\n\r\nThe advertisement has a catchy phrase.\r\n这个广告有一句很抓人的话。\r\n\r\nThe headline is short and catchy.\r\n这个标题简短又吸引人。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ That song is so catchy.\r\n那首歌太洗脑了。\r\n\r\n✅ It’s catchy, isn’t it?\r\n挺朗朗上口的，对吧？\r\n\r\n✅ We need something short and catchy.\r\n我们需要一个简短又好记的东西。\r\n\r\n✅ That’s a pretty catchy name.\r\n这个名字挺好记、挺吸引人的。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d4445a8e617c40e3a93b969280d80b1b.jpg','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-15 14:48:05',1,'2026-05-15 14:48:05'),(1259,18,48,'phrase','chop up','chop up','chop up','phrasal verb\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n切碎；剁碎；切成小块\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nchop up means to cut something into small pieces, usually with a knife.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n把一个完整的东西切成很多小块。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nCould you chop up the vegetables while I boil the noodles?\r\n我煮面的时候，你能把蔬菜切一下吗？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象你拿刀 chop, chop, chop 🔪，最后食物变成很多小块。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nchop up = cut into small pieces\r\n切碎 / 切成小块。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 切碎食物\r\n\r\nChop up the onions.\r\n把洋葱切碎。\r\n\r\nCan you chop up the carrots?\r\n你能把胡萝卜切成小块吗？\r\n\r\nI chopped up some chicken for the noodles.\r\n我切了一些鸡肉块来煮面。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 动物把食物弄碎\r\n\r\n你之前学 arachnids 时有这个意思：\r\n\r\nThey have mouthparts for grabbing prey and chopping up food.\r\n它们有用来抓住猎物和切碎食物的口器。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I’ll chop up the vegetables.\r\n我来切蔬菜。\r\n\r\n✅ Just chop it up into small pieces.\r\n把它切成小块就行。\r\n\r\n✅ Chop up the chicken before you cook it.\r\n做之前先把鸡肉切成块。\r\n\r\n✅ I need to chop up some ginger.\r\n我需要切点姜。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/de53e5e964e4498fb9c9adaa6e9d7303.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-15 17:53:21',1,'2026-05-15 17:53:21'),(1260,18,49,'phrase','gigantic','gigantic','gigantic','adjective\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n巨大的；庞大的；非常大的\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ngigantic means extremely large.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n比 big / large 更夸张，表示“大得惊人”。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 形容物体很大\r\n\r\nThat building is gigantic.\r\n那栋建筑非常巨大。\r\n\r\nThey saw a gigantic whale.\r\n他们看到了一头巨大的鲸鱼。\r\n\r\nThere was a gigantic tree in the forest.\r\n森林里有一棵巨大的树。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 形容数量 / 规模很大\r\n\r\nIt was a gigantic project.\r\n那是一个庞大的项目。\r\n\r\nThe company made a gigantic profit.\r\n公司获得了巨额利润。\r\n\r\nWe faced a gigantic challenge.\r\n我们面临一个巨大的挑战。\r\n\r\n⚠️ gigantic vs huge vs giant\r\n\r\nhuge  很大的  最常用，口语自然\r\n\r\ngigantic 巨大的  更夸张，更强调“大得惊人”\r\n\r\ngiant  巨大的 / 巨人  可作形容词，也可作名词','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ That’s gigantic!\r\n那也太大了！\r\n\r\n✅ The portion was gigantic.\r\n那份量超大。\r\n\r\n✅ It’s a gigantic problem.\r\n这是个巨大的问题。\r\n\r\n✅ They built a gigantic shopping mall.\r\n他们建了一个巨大的购物中心。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/19918d48d0a141adb7efb920a2df8748.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-15 18:20:46',1,'2026-05-15 18:20:46'),(1261,18,50,'phrase','Skeleton','Skeleton','skeleton\r\n/ˈskelɪtən/','noun\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n骨架；骷髅；框架；梗概\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nSkeleton means the structure of bones inside a body.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n支撑身体的骨头结构。\r\n\r\nIt can also mean the basic structure of something, like a plan, system, or document.\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象一副完整的骨头架子 🦴：\r\n\r\nbone = one piece\r\n一块骨头\r\n\r\nskeleton = the whole structure\r\n整个骨架。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 人或动物的骨架\r\n\r\nThe human skeleton has 206 bones.\r\n人体骨骼有 206 块骨头。\r\n\r\nThe museum has a dinosaur skeleton.\r\n博物馆里有一副恐龙骨架。\r\n\r\nThe skeleton supports the body.\r\n骨架支撑身体。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 骷髅\r\n\r\nThere was a skeleton in the old cave.\r\n旧洞穴里有一具骷髅。\r\n\r\nThe Halloween decoration had a plastic skeleton.\r\n万圣节装饰里有一个塑料骷髅。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 框架 / 基本结构\r\n\r\nThis is just the skeleton of the report.\r\n这只是报告的基本框架。\r\n\r\nWe created a skeleton version of the website first.\r\n我们先做了网站的基本框架版本。\r\n\r\nThe code provides the skeleton of the application.\r\n这段代码提供了应用程序的基本结构。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ It’s just a skeleton plan at the moment.\r\n目前这只是一个初步框架。\r\n\r\n✅ We need to build the skeleton of the project first.\r\n我们需要先搭建项目的基本框架。\r\n\r\n✅ That’s a dinosaur skeleton.\r\n那是一副恐龙骨架。\r\n\r\n✅ The skeleton gives the body its shape.\r\n骨架让身体有形状。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/342f59b38beb4cde9b00370103d7ac10.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-15 18:47:26',1,'2026-05-15 18:47:26'),(1262,18,51,'phrase','well adapted to','well adapted to','well adapted to','🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n很好地适应……；非常适合……环境；适应能力强\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nwell adapted to means something or someone has developed features or abilities that help them live, survive, or work well in a particular environment or situation.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n很适合某个环境 / 条件 / 情况。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nCrustaceans are well adapted to aquatic environments because they have hard outer shells and specialised body parts.\r\n甲壳类动物非常适应水生环境，因为它们有坚硬的外壳和特殊的身体结构。','✅ Common Pattern 常见句型\r\n\r\nbe well adapted to + noun\r\n\r\nCrustaceans are well adapted to life in water.\r\n甲壳类动物非常适应水中生活。\r\n\r\nCamels are well adapted to desert environments.\r\n骆驼非常适应沙漠环境。\r\n\r\nThis plant is well adapted to dry conditions.\r\n这种植物非常适应干燥环境。','🗣️ Natural Examples 自然例句\r\n\r\n✅ Penguins are well adapted to cold climates.\r\n企鹅非常适应寒冷气候。\r\n\r\n✅ These animals are well adapted to their environment.\r\n这些动物非常适应它们的环境。\r\n\r\n✅ The system is well adapted to high traffic.\r\n这个系统很适合高流量场景。\r\n\r\n✅ He is well adapted to working under pressure.\r\n他很适应在压力下工作。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d1b8dfad41cd4740b133ad6c30463f04.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-16 12:31:58',1,'2026-05-16 12:31:58'),(1263,18,52,'phrase','aquatic','aquatic','aquatic','adjective\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n水生的；水中的；与水有关的\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\naquatic means something lives in water, grows in water, or is related to water.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n和水有关，尤其是生活在水里的。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nCrustaceans are aquatic animals with hard outer shells.\r\n甲壳类动物是有坚硬外壳的水生动物。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 水生动物\r\n\r\nFish are aquatic animals.\r\n鱼是水生动物。\r\n\r\nCrustaceans are well adapted to aquatic environments.\r\n甲壳类动物非常适应水生环境。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 水生植物\r\n\r\nSome aquatic plants grow under the water.\r\n一些水生植物生长在水下。\r\n\r\nWater lilies are aquatic plants.\r\n睡莲是水生植物。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 水上运动 / 水中活动\r\n\r\nSwimming is an aquatic sport.\r\n游泳是一项水上运动。\r\n\r\nThe school has an aquatic centre.\r\n学校有一个水上运动中心 / 游泳馆。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ This animal is aquatic.\r\n这种动物是水生的。\r\n\r\n✅ It lives in an aquatic environment.\r\n它生活在水生环境中。\r\n\r\n✅ Aquatic animals need water to survive.\r\n水生动物需要水才能生存。\r\n\r\n✅ The centre offers aquatic activities for kids.\r\n这个中心提供儿童水上活动。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b4ee7c3fd9094eab932db75abdacd44b.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-16 12:39:23',1,'2026-05-16 12:39:23'),(1264,18,53,'phrase','split up into','split up into','split up into','phrasal verb phrase\r\n\r\n中文意思\r\n\r\n分成……；拆分成……；被分成……\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nCore Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nsplit up into means:\r\n\r\nto separate one thing into several smaller parts or groups\r\n\r\n中文核心感觉：\r\n\r\n把一个整体分成几个部分。\r\n\r\nUseful Sentence 实用句\r\n\r\nSegmented worms have bodies that are split up into many ring-like segments.\r\n环节动物的身体被分成许多环状小节。','Common Pattern 常见句型\r\n\r\n1. be split up into + plural noun\r\n\r\n表示：被分成……\r\n\r\nThe class was split up into three groups.\r\n这个班被分成了三个小组。\r\n\r\nThe project was split up into several tasks.\r\n这个项目被拆分成了几个任务。\r\n\r\nThe worm’s body is split up into many segments.\r\n这条虫的身体被分成很多节。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. split something up into + plural noun\r\n\r\n表示：把某物分成……\r\n\r\nWe split the work up into smaller tasks.\r\n我们把工作拆分成更小的任务。\r\n\r\nThe teacher split us up into pairs.\r\n老师把我们分成两人一组。\r\n\r\nThey split the data up into different categories.\r\n他们把数据分成不同类别。','Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\nLet’s split the work up into smaller parts.\r\n我们把工作拆成小部分吧。\r\n\r\nWe were split up into groups.\r\n我们被分成了几个小组。\r\n\r\nThe task is easier if we split it up into steps.\r\n如果我们把任务分成几个步骤，就会更容易。\r\n\r\nsplit up into vs divided into\r\n\r\nsplit up into  分成 / 拆成   更口语\r\n\r\ndivided into   被分成   更正式，适合学术/科学解释','/static/uploads/english_note_item/54ae2019a0fe40a58d10e4370a643b1f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-16 12:57:02',1,'2026-05-16 12:57:02'),(1265,18,54,'phrase','at the tip','at the tip','at the tip','phrase\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n在尖端；在顶端；在末端\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nat the tip means at the very end or pointed part of something.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n在某个东西最尖、最前、最末端的位置。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 身体部位的尖端\r\n\r\nThere is a small cut at the tip of my finger.\r\n我的手指尖有一个小伤口。\r\n\r\nThe bee has a sting at the tip of its body.\r\n蜜蜂身体末端有一根刺。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 物体的尖端\r\n\r\nThe needle is sharp at the tip.\r\n针尖很锋利。\r\n\r\nThere is ink at the tip of the pen.\r\n笔尖上有墨水。\r\n\r\nThe arrow has a metal point at the tip.\r\n箭头尖端有一个金属尖。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 地理位置的最端点\r\n\r\nThe lighthouse is at the tip of the island.\r\n灯塔在岛的最尖端。\r\n\r\nCape Reinga is at the northern tip of New Zealand.\r\n雷因加角位于新西兰的最北端。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ It’s right at the tip.\r\n它就在尖端那里。\r\n\r\n✅ The tip is very sharp.\r\n这个尖端很锋利。\r\n\r\n✅ There’s a small mark at the tip.\r\n尖端那里有一个小印记。\r\n\r\n✅ Hold it near the tip.\r\n靠近尖端拿着它。\r\n\r\n⚠️ Special Expression: on the tip of my tongue\r\n\r\n这个很常用，意思不是“真的在舌尖上”，而是：\r\n\r\n话到嘴边，但一时想不起来。\r\n\r\nHis name is on the tip of my tongue.\r\n他的名字就在嘴边，但我一时想不起来。\r\n\r\nat the tip vs on the tip\r\n\r\nat the tip of…       在……的尖端/末端                             at the tip of the island\r\non the tip of….     在……表面尖端；常用于固定表达.  on the tip of my tongue\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe poison is stored at the tip of the scorpion’s tail.\r\n毒液储存在蝎子尾巴的尖端。\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n把 tip 想成一个东西最尖的地方，比如：\r\n\r\n针尖 🪡\r\n笔尖 ✒️\r\n手指尖 ☝️\r\n岛的最北端 🏝️\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nat the tip = at the very end or pointed part  在最尖端 / 最末端。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/7aceb088dbfb43fa9f96fcaf336753fe.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-16 13:37:07',1,'2026-05-16 13:37:07'),(1266,18,55,'phrase','cling onto','cling onto','cling onto','cling onto\r\n/klɪŋ ˈɒntuː/ NZ/UK\r\n/klɪŋ ˈɑːntuː/ US\r\nphrasal verb\r\n中文意思\r\n\r\n紧紧抓住；依附于；不愿放弃\r\n\r\nCore Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ncling onto means to hold something very tightly, usually because you are afraid, nervous, or do not want to lose it.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：紧紧抓着，不想松手。\r\n\r\nMemory Tip\r\n\r\n想象一个人快要掉下去，双手死死抓住绳子。\r\n\r\n这就是：\r\n\r\ncling onto = hold very tightly and not let go\r\n紧紧抓住，不松手。','cling onto someone’s hand. 紧紧抓住某人的手\r\n\r\ncling onto a rope  紧紧抓住绳子\r\n\r\ncling onto a branch. 紧紧抓住树枝\r\n\r\ncling onto hope\r\n\r\n抱着希望\r\n\r\ncling onto the past. 放不下过去\r\n\r\ncling onto old ideas. 固守旧观念\r\n\r\nCommon Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 真的用手抓住\r\n\r\nThe child clung onto his mother’s hand.\r\n那个孩子紧紧抓住妈妈的手。\r\n\r\nShe clung onto the rope to avoid falling.\r\n她紧紧抓住绳子，以免掉下去。\r\n\r\nThe monkey clung onto the branch.\r\n猴子紧紧抓住树枝。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 情感上不愿放弃\r\n\r\nHe still clings onto the past.\r\n他仍然放不下过去。\r\n\r\nShe clung onto hope, even when things were difficult.\r\n即使情况很困难，她仍然抱有希望。\r\n\r\nSome people cling onto old ideas.\r\n有些人固守旧观念。','Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\nHold on tight!\r\n抓紧！\r\n\r\nHe was clinging onto the railing.\r\n他紧紧抓着栏杆。\r\n\r\nDon’t cling onto the past.\r\n不要一直放不下过去。\r\n\r\nShe’s still clinging onto hope.\r\n她仍然抱着希望。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a3af06908d274d7a9d29c5c620f1d043.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-16 13:47:03',1,'2026-05-16 13:47:03'),(1267,18,56,'phrase','suck up','suck up','suck up','phrasal verb\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n吸收；吸走；拍马屁 / 讨好\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meanings 核心意思\r\n\r\nsuck up 有两个常见意思：\r\n\r\n1. 吸收 / 吸走\r\n\r\n表示液体、灰尘、空气等被吸进去。\r\n\r\nThe sponge sucked up the water.\r\n海绵吸收了水。\r\n\r\nThe vacuum cleaner sucked up the dust.\r\n吸尘器把灰尘吸走了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 拍马屁 / 讨好\r\n\r\n表示为了得到好处而刻意讨好别人。这个用法比较口语，有点负面。\r\n\r\nHe’s always sucking up to the boss.\r\n他总是拍老板马屁。\r\n\r\nDon’t suck up to the teacher just to get a better grade.\r\n不要为了拿高分去讨好老师。\r\n\r\n注意这个意思通常用：\r\n\r\nsuck up to someone\r\n讨好某人 / 拍某人的马屁','✅ Common Patterns 常见句型\r\n\r\n1. suck up + something\r\n\r\nThis towel can suck up a lot of water.\r\n这条毛巾能吸很多水。\r\n\r\nThe machine sucked up all the dirt.\r\n机器把所有脏东西都吸走了。\r\n\r\n2. suck up to + someone\r\n\r\nHe’s sucking up to the manager.\r\n他在讨好经理。\r\n\r\nShe doesn’t like people who suck up to others.\r\n她不喜欢那些拍别人马屁的人。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ The carpet sucked up the spill.\r\n地毯把洒出来的液体吸进去了。\r\n\r\n✅ The vacuum sucked up everything.\r\n吸尘器把东西都吸走了。\r\n\r\n✅ He’s such a suck-up.\r\n他真是个马屁精。\r\n\r\n✅ Stop sucking up.\r\n别拍马屁了。','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe sponge sucked up all the water on the table.\r\n海绵把桌子上的水都吸干了。\r\n\r\nHe keeps sucking up to the boss, and it’s really annoying.\r\n他老是拍老板马屁，真的很烦。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象一个吸尘器把灰尘“吸进去”：\r\n\r\nsuck up = pull something in by suction\r\n吸进去 / 吸走\r\n\r\n但对人说：\r\n\r\nsuck up to someone = try too hard to please them\r\n过度讨好别人 / 拍马屁。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/475dcb11ae00461bb999886629aa5cd3.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-16 17:17:06',1,'2026-05-16 17:17:06'),(1268,18,57,'phrase','hollow','hollow','hollow','adjective / noun / verb\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n空心的；中空的；凹陷的；空洞的\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nhollow means something has empty space inside.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n外面看起来是完整的，但里面是空的。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 物体是空心的\r\n\r\nThe tree trunk is hollow.\r\n这棵树的树干是空心的。\r\n\r\nThis chocolate egg is hollow inside.\r\n这个巧克力蛋里面是空的。\r\n\r\nBamboo stems are often hollow.\r\n竹子的茎通常是中空的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 声音空洞 / 回响\r\n\r\nHis voice sounded hollow in the empty room.\r\n他的声音在空房间里听起来很空洞。\r\n\r\nThe box made a hollow sound when I tapped it.\r\n我敲这个盒子时，它发出了空空的声音。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 感情 / 承诺空洞的\r\n\r\nIt was a hollow apology.\r\n那是一个空洞的道歉。\r\n👉 意思是：听起来不真诚。\r\n\r\nHis words felt hollow.\r\n他的话听起来很空洞 / 不真诚。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n4. 脸颊 / 眼睛凹陷\r\n\r\nHe had hollow cheeks after being ill.\r\n他生病后脸颊凹陷。\r\n\r\nHer eyes looked hollow and tired.\r\n她的眼睛看起来凹陷又疲惫。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ It’s hollow inside.\r\n它里面是空的。\r\n\r\n✅ The tree is hollow.\r\n这棵树是空心的。\r\n\r\n✅ That sounds a bit hollow.\r\n那听起来有点空洞 / 不真诚。\r\n\r\n✅ The wall sounded hollow when I knocked on it.\r\n我敲墙的时候，墙听起来是空的。\r\n\r\nhollow tree   空心树\r\n\r\nhollow log  空心木头\r\n\r\nhollow tube  空心管\r\n\r\nhollow sound   空洞的声音\r\n\r\nhollow eyes   凹陷的眼睛\r\n\r\nhollow cheeks   凹陷的脸颊\r\n\r\nhollow promise   空洞的承诺\r\n\r\nhollow apology   空洞 / 不真诚的道歉','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d905214e66254925b1fb22624554ac57.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-16 17:26:21',1,'2026-05-16 17:26:21'),(1269,18,58,'vocab','chomp','chomp','chomp','🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n大口咬；用力咬；咀嚼\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nchomp means to bite or chew something loudly or with strong bites.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n用力地、大口地咬东西。\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象一只鳄鱼张大嘴： CHOMP!\r\n\r\n这个声音感就是： chomp = 大口咬 / 用力咬。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nThe dog chomped my slipper.\r\n狗狗咬坏了我的拖鞋。\r\n\r\nHe chomped into the apple.\r\n他大口咬了一口苹果。\r\n\r\nThe crocodile chomped down on its prey.\r\n鳄鱼狠狠咬住了猎物。\r\n\r\nShe was chomping on a burger.\r\n她正在大口吃汉堡。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ He chomped down on the carrot.\r\n他用力咬了一口胡萝卜。\r\n\r\n✅ Stop chomping so loudly!\r\n别嚼得那么大声！\r\n\r\n✅ The horse chomped the carrot right out of my hand.\r\n马直接从我手里一口咬走了胡萝卜。\r\n\r\n✅ My little brother keeps chomping on his toys.\r\n我弟弟一直咬他的玩具。','⚠️ chomp vs bite\r\n\r\nbite         咬        普通用词\r\n\r\nchomp   大口咬 / 用力咬            更有声音感、力量感、画面感\r\n\r\nHe bit the apple.   他咬了苹果。\r\n\r\nHe chomped into the apple.    他大口咬进苹果。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe crocodile opened its mouth and chomped down on the fish.\r\n鳄鱼张开嘴，狠狠咬住了鱼。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ee84855c3f1840e6b1df4d9c04839745.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-16 17:36:31',1,'2026-05-16 17:36:31'),(1270,18,59,'phrase','pierce through','pierce through','pierce through','phrasal verb\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n刺穿；穿透；突破；深深影响\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\npierce through means to go through something using a sharp point or strong force.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n尖锐的东西或强烈的力量，从一边穿到另一边。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 物理上刺穿 / 穿透\r\n\r\nThe needle pierced through the thick fabric.\r\n针穿透了厚厚的布料。\r\n\r\nThe arrow pierced through the target.\r\n箭穿透了靶子。\r\n\r\nThe thorn pierced through his skin.\r\n刺扎进并刺穿了他的皮肤。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 光 / 声音穿透\r\n\r\nThe sunlight pierced through the clouds.\r\n阳光穿透了云层。\r\n\r\nHer voice pierced through the noise.\r\n她的声音穿透了噪音。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 情感上深深触动\r\n\r\nHis words pierced through her heart.\r\n他的话深深刺痛 / 触动了她的心。\r\n\r\n这个用法比较文学化，有情绪冲击感。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ The cold wind pierced through my coat.\r\n寒风穿透了我的外套。\r\n\r\n✅ The sound pierced through the silence.\r\n那个声音打破 / 穿透了寂静。\r\n\r\n✅ The truth finally pierced through his denial.\r\n真相最终穿透了他的否认。\r\n\r\n🔗 Common Collocations 常见搭配\r\n\r\npierce through the skin.  刺穿皮肤\r\n\r\npierce through fabric.  穿透布料\r\n\r\npierce through the clouds.  穿透云层\r\n\r\npierce through the darkness.  穿透黑暗\r\n\r\npierce through the noise.   穿透噪音\r\n\r\npierce through someone’s heart.   深深刺痛某人的心\r\n\r\n⚠️ pierce through vs break through\r\n\r\npierce through.  刺穿；穿透.  像针、箭、光、声音穿过去\r\n\r\nbreak through 突破；冲破.   强调突破障碍、限制、困难\r\n\r\nThe arrow pierced through the apple.   箭穿透了苹果。\r\n\r\nHe finally broke through his limits.    他终于突破了自己的极限。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe sunlight pierced through the clouds after the storm.\r\n暴风雨后，阳光穿透了云层。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n想象一支箭从木板中间穿过去：\r\n\r\npierce through = go through with a sharp point or strong force\r\n用尖锐或强力的方式穿过去。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f1bf7969ade14d42a3d718d2465d0460.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-16 17:47:08',1,'2026-05-16 17:47:08'),(1271,18,60,'vocab','allergy','allergy','allergy','/ˈælədʒi/\r\nnoun\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n过敏；过敏反应\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nAllergy means your body reacts badly to something that is usually harmless, such as pollen, dust, food, or animal hair.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n身体对某种东西反应过度。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 对某物过敏\r\n\r\nI have an allergy to pollen.\r\n我对花粉过敏。\r\n\r\nShe has a peanut allergy.\r\n她对花生过敏。\r\n\r\nHe has an allergy to cats.\r\n他对猫过敏。\r\n\r\n2. 过敏症状\r\n\r\nMy allergy gets worse in spring.\r\n我的过敏在春天会加重。\r\n\r\nThis medicine helps with my allergy symptoms.\r\n这个药可以缓解我的过敏症状。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I’m allergic to pollen.\r\n我对花粉过敏。\r\n\r\n✅ I have a food allergy.\r\n我有食物过敏。\r\n\r\n✅ My allergies are acting up today.\r\n我今天过敏又犯了。\r\n\r\n✅ Do you have any allergies?\r\n你有什么过敏吗？','/static/uploads/english_note_item/16c11da53b8448a1842f23ac2434c681.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-16 18:03:55',1,'2026-05-16 18:03:55'),(1272,18,61,'phrase','not quite sure yet','not quite sure yet','not quite sure yet','phrase\r\n\r\n中文意思\r\n\r\n还不太确定；还没有完全确定\r\n\r\nCore Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nnot quite sure yet means you are still thinking about something and you do not have a clear answer now.\r\n\r\n中文感觉：\r\n\r\n现在还在考虑，还没有完全确定。','Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nI’m not quite sure yet.\r\n我还不太确定。\r\n\r\nI’m not quite sure yet what I want to do.\r\n我还不太确定我想做什么。\r\n\r\nWe’re not quite sure yet if we can make it.\r\n我们还不太确定能不能做到 / 能不能参加。\r\n\r\nLet me think about it. I’m not quite sure yet.\r\n让我想想，我还不太确定。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nNatural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\nI’m still not sure.\r\n我还是不确定。\r\n\r\nI’m not 100% sure yet.\r\n我还不是百分之百确定。\r\n\r\nI’m still thinking about it.\r\n我还在考虑。\r\n\r\nI haven’t decided yet.\r\n我还没决定。','Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nI’m not quite sure yet, but I’ll let you know once I’ve decided.\r\n我还不太确定，但我决定后会告诉你。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d2bfff34c59e47e4bc1537c3ba3ac13b.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-17 08:11:52',1,'2026-05-17 08:11:52'),(1273,18,62,'vocab','cupboard','cupboard','cupboard','noun\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n橱柜；柜子；壁橱\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ncupboard means a cabinet or small storage space with doors, usually used for keeping things.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n用来放东西的柜子。\r\n\r\n⚠️ Pronunciation Note 发音重点\r\n\r\ncupboard 的发音不是按拼写读：\r\n\r\n❌ /cup-board/\r\n✅ /ˈkʌbəd/\r\n\r\n听起来像：\r\n\r\nKUB-əd\r\n\r\n中间的 p 基本不发音。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 厨房橱柜\r\n\r\nThe cups are in the cupboard.\r\n杯子在橱柜里。\r\n\r\nCan you put these plates back in the cupboard?\r\n你能把这些盘子放回橱柜里吗？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 储物柜 / 壁橱\r\n\r\nThe cleaning products are in the cupboard.\r\n清洁用品在柜子里。\r\n\r\nThere’s a delivery list in the cupboard.\r\n送货清单在柜子里。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ It’s in the cupboard.\r\n它在柜子里。\r\n\r\n✅ Check the cupboard.\r\n检查一下柜子。\r\n\r\n✅ I put it in the kitchen cupboard.\r\n我把它放在厨房橱柜里了。\r\n\r\n✅ Can you grab it from the cupboard?\r\n你能从柜子里拿一下吗？\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nYou can check the delivery list in the cupboard.\r\n你可以在柜子里查看送货清单。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/00aec7868d8d4991afd524aa965036e7.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-17 10:30:30',1,'2026-05-17 10:30:30'),(1274,18,63,'vocab','symptom','symptom','symptom','noun\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n症状；病征\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nA symptom is a sign that shows you may have an illness or medical condition.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n身体出现的某种不舒服表现，可能说明你生病了。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nIf your symptoms get worse, you should see a doctor.\r\n如果你的症状加重，你应该去看医生。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nFever is a common symptom of the flu.\r\n发烧是流感的常见症状。\r\n\r\nCough and sore throat are common symptoms of a cold.\r\n咳嗽和喉咙痛是感冒的常见症状。\r\n\r\nHe went to the doctor because of his symptoms.\r\n他因为出现症状去看医生。\r\n\r\nNausea can be a symptom of food poisoning.\r\n恶心可能是食物中毒的症状。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ What symptoms do you have?\r\n你有什么症状？\r\n\r\n✅ I have flu-like symptoms.\r\n我有类似流感的症状。\r\n\r\n✅ My symptoms are getting worse.\r\n我的症状越来越严重。\r\n\r\n✅ The medicine helped reduce my symptoms.\r\n这个药帮助缓解了我的症状。\r\n\r\nsymptom. 症状   病人自己感觉到的，比如头痛、恶心\r\n\r\nsign.  体征.  医生或别人能观察到的，比如皮疹、体温高\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\nHeadache is a symptom.\r\n头痛是症状。\r\n\r\nA rash can be a sign of an allergy.\r\n皮疹可能是过敏的体征。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/516df80e1c0f425b807e5ef0a24aad7b.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-17 14:15:36',1,'2026-05-17 14:15:36'),(1275,18,64,'vocab','crocodile vs alligator','crocodile vs alligator','crocodile vs alligator','1. 中文意思\r\n\r\ncrocodile\r\n鳄鱼\r\n\r\nalligator\r\n短吻鳄\r\n\r\n日常中文里很多人都说“鳄鱼”，但英语里 crocodile 和 alligator 是不同种类。','2. 最简单区别：看嘴巴形状\r\n\r\ncrocodile\r\n\r\n嘴巴更长、更窄，像 V shape\r\n\r\nA crocodile has a long, narrow, V-shaped snout.\r\n鳄鱼的嘴又长又窄，呈 V 形。\r\n\r\nalligator\r\n\r\n嘴巴更短、更宽，像 U shape\r\n\r\nAn alligator has a short, wide, U-shaped snout.\r\n短吻鳄的嘴更短更宽，呈 U 形。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 牙齿区别\r\n\r\ncrocodile\r\n\r\n闭嘴时，下排牙齿通常还能看到。\r\n\r\nYou can often see a crocodile’s teeth even when its mouth is closed.\r\n\r\nalligator\r\n\r\n闭嘴时，牙齿通常不太明显。\r\n\r\nAn alligator’s teeth are usually hidden when its mouth is closed.\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n4. 生活环境\r\n\r\ncrocodile\r\n\r\n通常可以生活在 淡水和咸水 中。\r\n\r\nCrocodiles can live in both freshwater and saltwater.\r\n\r\nalligator\r\n\r\n通常主要生活在 淡水 中，比如河流、湖泊、沼泽。\r\n\r\nAlligators usually live in freshwater, such as rivers, lakes, and swamps.\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n5. 记忆方法\r\n\r\nCrocodile = V-shaped mouth\r\n鳄鱼嘴巴像 V\r\n\r\nAlligator = U-shaped mouth\r\n短吻鳄嘴巴像 U\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nCrocodiles have narrower V-shaped snouts, while alligators have wider U-shaped snouts.\r\n鳄鱼的嘴更窄像 V，短吻鳄的嘴更宽像 U。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/adea0c5af274443ab36918784c4c9773.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-17 15:09:08',1,'2026-05-17 15:09:08'),(1276,18,65,'vocab','fringe','fringe','fringe','中文意思\r\n\r\n流苏；刘海；边缘；边界；作为边缘\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nCore Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nfringe means something at the edge of something, or decorative threads hanging from the edge of cloth.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n在边边上的东西。\r\n\r\nfringe vs margin\r\n\r\nfringe    边缘；外围；刘海；流苏                  常指地理、社会、头发或布料边缘\r\n\r\nmargin        页边空白；边际                            常用于书页、纸张、利润、差距\r\n\r\non the fringe of the city\r\n在城市边缘\r\n\r\nwrite notes in the margin\r\n在页边空白处写笔记\r\n\r\nUseful Sentence\r\n\r\nShe cut her fringe shorter because it kept getting in her eyes.\r\n她把刘海剪短了，因为它总是挡眼睛。','Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 流苏；穗边\r\n\r\nThe scarf has a fringe on both ends.\r\n这条围巾两端有流苏。\r\n\r\n2. 刘海\r\n\r\n在新西兰 / 英国英语里，fringe 常表示 刘海。\r\n美式英语更常说 bangs。\r\n\r\nShe has a fringe that covers her forehead.\r\n她留着遮住额头的刘海。\r\n\r\n3. 边缘；外围\r\n\r\nThe town is on the fringe of the city.\r\n这个小镇位于城市边缘。\r\n\r\nThey live on the fringes of society.\r\n他们生活在社会边缘。\r\n\r\n4. 动词：作为边缘；围绕\r\n\r\nThe forest fringes the lake.\r\n森林环绕着湖边。','Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\nI’m thinking of getting a fringe.\r\n我在考虑剪个刘海。\r\n\r\nYour fringe looks nice.\r\n你的刘海很好看。\r\n\r\nThe house is on the fringe of town.\r\n这栋房子在小镇边缘。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c8b9bb3ed90e450e8c45a9f02f3e6133.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-17 18:12:27',1,'2026-05-17 18:12:27'),(1277,18,66,'vocab','propel','propel','propel','verb 动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n推动；推进；驱动；促使\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\npropel means to push or move something forward.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n给某个东西力量，让它向前移动。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe propeller propels the boat through the water.\r\n螺旋桨推动小船在水中前进。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\npropel 和 propeller 很像：\r\n\r\npropeller = 螺旋桨\r\npropel = 推动 / 推进\r\n\r\n想象螺旋桨快速转动，把船往前推：\r\n\r\npropel = push forward with power.','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 推动物体向前\r\n\r\nThe engine propels the boat through the water.\r\n发动机推动小船在水中前进。\r\n\r\nThe rocket was propelled into space.\r\n火箭被推进太空。\r\n\r\nThe wind propelled the sailing boat forward.\r\n风推动帆船向前。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 推动某人成功 / 发展\r\n\r\nHer hard work propelled her to success.\r\n她的努力推动她走向成功。\r\n\r\nThis project could propel the company forward.\r\n这个项目可能推动公司向前发展。\r\n\r\nThe new technology helped propel the industry.\r\n这项新技术推动了这个行业的发展。\r\n\r\n🔗 Common Collocations 常见搭配\r\n\r\n🚀 propel a rocket.   推进火箭\r\n\r\n🚤 propel a boat.   推动小船\r\n\r\n⚙️ propel a machine.   驱动机器\r\n\r\n🌬️ be propelled by wind.    被风推动\r\n\r\n📈 propel growth.    推动增长\r\n\r\n🧑‍💼 propel someone’s career.     推动某人的职业发展\r\n\r\n⚠️ propel vs push\r\n\r\npush                推                 普通用词，用手推也可以\r\n\r\npropel       推进；驱动        更正式，强调持续给动力向前','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ The motor propels the machine.\r\n马达驱动这台机器。\r\n\r\n✅ The boat is propelled by an engine.\r\n这艘船由发动机驱动。\r\n\r\n✅ His passion propelled him forward.\r\n他的热情推动他不断前进。\r\n\r\n✅ That experience propelled my career.\r\n那段经历推动了我的职业发展。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/19d503cada364d9aacd14f7a10d41fd9.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-17 18:27:05',1,'2026-05-17 18:27:05'),(1278,18,67,'vocab','grasshopper','grasshopper','grasshopper','noun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n蚂蚱；蝗虫；草蜢\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nA grasshopper is a small jumping insect with long back legs. It usually lives in grass, fields, or plants.\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n一种会跳的昆虫，后腿很长，常见于草地或田野。\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n把它拆开：\r\n\r\ngrass = 草\r\nhopper = 会跳的人 / 动物\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ngrasshopper = an insect that hops in the grass\r\n在草丛中跳来跳去的昆虫。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nGrasshoppers have long back legs for jumping.\r\n蚂蚱有长长的后腿，用来跳跃。\r\n\r\nBirds eat grasshoppers.\r\n鸟吃蚂蚱。\r\n\r\nThere are many grasshoppers in the field.\r\n田野里有很多蚂蚱。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ Look! There’s a grasshopper on the leaf.\r\n看！叶子上有一只蚂蚱。\r\n\r\n✅ When I was a kid, I used to catch grasshoppers.\r\n我小时候常常抓蚂蚱。\r\n\r\n✅ The grasshopper jumped away.\r\n那只蚂蚱跳走了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/1e1a0df86bf04ab3ba9bbe1ed546505d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-17 18:33:40',1,'2026-05-17 18:33:40'),(1279,18,68,'vocab','scale','scale','scale','noun / verb\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n规模；大小；范围；比例尺；刻度；鱼鳞；攀爬；按比例缩放\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nscale 的核心意思和 size / level / proportion 有关。\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n大小、程度、比例，或者一层一层的表面。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 规模；大小；范围\r\n\r\nThe project is carried out on a large scale.\r\n这个项目是大规模进行的。\r\n\r\nThe company has expanded on a global scale.\r\n这家公司已经在全球范围内扩大业务。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 比例尺；比例\r\n\r\nThis map is drawn to a small scale.\r\n这张地图是按小比例尺绘制的。\r\n\r\nWe need to understand the scale of the problem.\r\n我们需要了解这个问题的规模。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 刻度；刻度盘\r\n\r\nLook at the scale on the thermometer.\r\n看一下温度计上的刻度。\r\n\r\nThe scale shows the weight in kilograms.\r\n这个秤显示公斤数。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n4️⃣ 鱼鳞 / 爬行动物的鳞片\r\n\r\nFish have scales on their bodies.\r\n鱼的身体上有鳞片。\r\n\r\nThe snake’s scales were shiny.\r\n蛇的鳞片很亮。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n5️⃣ 动词：攀爬；爬上\r\n\r\nHe scaled the wall easily.\r\n他轻松地爬上了那堵墙。\r\n\r\nThey scaled the mountain together.\r\n他们一起爬上了那座山。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n6️⃣ 动词：按比例缩放 / 调整大小\r\n\r\nYou can scale the image to fit the screen.\r\n你可以调整图片大小以适应屏幕。\r\n\r\nThe system needs to scale as traffic grows.\r\n随着流量增长，系统需要扩展。\r\n\r\n🔗 Common Collocations 常见搭配\r\n\r\n⚖️ large scale.    大规模\r\n\r\n🌍 global scale.  全球范围\r\n\r\n🗺️ map scale.  地图比例尺\r\n\r\n📏 scale up.   扩大\r\n\r\n📉 scale down.   缩小\r\n\r\n🐟 fish scales.  鱼鳞\r\n\r\n🧗 scale a wall / mountain.   爬墙 / 爬山','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ That’s on a huge scale.\r\n那是很大规模的。\r\n\r\n✅ We need to scale it down.\r\n我们需要把它缩小。\r\n\r\n✅ Can you scale the image up a bit?\r\n你能把图片放大一点吗？\r\n\r\n✅ The business is scaling fast.\r\n这个业务扩展得很快。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/57418cf5008f4e6e866dbb07d42d63ce.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-17 18:46:31',1,'2026-05-17 18:46:31'),(1280,18,69,'vocab','halter','halter','halter','/ˈhɔːltə/ NZ/UK\r\n/ˈhɔːltər/ US\r\nnoun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n头络；缰绳；吊带；挂脖衣服\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nhalter usually means a strap or rope that goes around an animal’s head, especially a horse, so you can lead or tie it.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n套在头上或脖子上的带子。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 马等动物的头络 / 缰绳\r\n\r\nHe put a halter on the horse.\r\n他给马戴上了头络。\r\n\r\nThe horse was tied with a halter.\r\n那匹马用头络拴着。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 挂脖衣服 / 吊带款式\r\n\r\nShe wore a halter top in summer.\r\n她夏天穿了一件挂脖吊带上衣。\r\n\r\nA halter dress ties behind the neck.\r\n挂脖裙的带子系在脖子后面。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ Put the halter on the horse.\r\n给马戴上头络。\r\n\r\n✅ Hold the halter rope.\r\n抓住头络绳。\r\n\r\n✅ She’s wearing a black halter top.\r\n她穿着一件黑色挂脖上衣。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/423760ec5f8f491d92f265fde0bb81d5.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-17 19:07:14',1,'2026-05-17 19:07:14'),(1281,18,70,'phrase','long for','long for','long for','phrasal verb 短语动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n渴望；渴求；思念；盼望\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nlong for means to want something very much, especially something you have wanted for a long time or feel deeply about.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n内心深处强烈地想要、思念或期待某事。\r\n\r\n⚠️ long for vs want\r\n\r\nwant.    想要.     普通、日常\r\n\r\nlong for.  渴望；思念.      更强烈、更有情感、更文学一点\r\n\r\nI want a coffee.\r\n我想要一杯咖啡。\r\n\r\nI long for a peaceful life.\r\n我渴望平静的生活。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nMany people long for a place where they feel understood and accepted.\r\n很多人都渴望一个能被理解和接纳的地方。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 渴望某物 / 某种生活\r\n\r\nShe longs for success.\r\n她渴望成功。\r\n\r\nThey long for a better life.\r\n他们渴望更好的生活。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 渴望做某事 / 经历某事\r\n\r\nHe longed for a chance to travel.\r\n他渴望有机会去旅行。\r\n\r\nI’ve been longing for the weekend all week.\r\n我这一整周都在盼周末。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 思念某人 / 某地\r\n\r\nI long for my hometown.\r\n我思念我的家乡。\r\n\r\nShe longed for love and acceptance.\r\n她渴望爱与接纳。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I’m longing for a break.\r\n我特别想休息一下。\r\n\r\n✅ I long for the days when life was simpler.\r\n我怀念以前生活更简单的日子。\r\n\r\n✅ We all long for peace.\r\n我们都渴望和平。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/360b6be58129494d84f1f68580b4f817.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-18 07:47:33',1,'2026-05-18 07:47:33'),(1282,18,71,'vocab','ascending','ascending','ascending','adjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n上升的；上行的；升高的；升序的\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nascending means moving upward, going higher, or arranged from low to high.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n往上走 / 越来越高 / 从小到大排列。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 上升的；向上的\r\n\r\nThe plane flew in an ascending direction.\r\n飞机朝上升的方向飞去。\r\n\r\nThe path was steep and ascending.\r\n这条路很陡，而且一直向上。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 登上的；上行的\r\n\r\nThey took the ascending path to reach the top.\r\n他们走上升的路到达山顶。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 升序的\r\n\r\nPlease list the numbers in ascending order.\r\n请把数字按升序排列。\r\n\r\nThe data is sorted in ascending order.\r\n这些数据是按升序排序的。','🔗 Common Collocations 常见搭配\r\n\r\n📈 ascending order.     升序.   \r\n\r\n⛰️ ascending path.    上升的路径.    \r\n\r\n✈️ ascending direction.   上升方向\r\n\r\n📊 ascending trend.    上升趋势\r\n\r\n🔢 ascending scale.     递增尺度\r\n\r\n⚠️ ascending vs descending\r\n\r\nSort the numbers in ascending order: 1, 2, 3, 4.\r\n按升序排列数字：1、2、3、4。\r\n\r\nSort the numbers in descending order: 4, 3, 2, 1.\r\n按降序排列数字：4、3、2、1。\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\nascend = 上升 / 攀登\r\nascending = 正在上升的 / 向上的\r\n\r\n想象一个人沿着山坡往上爬：\r\n\r\nascending = going upward\r\n向上走 / 上升。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/4b216cccbbc34261b5e07c7c7a438b52.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-18 08:44:58',1,'2026-05-18 08:44:58'),(1283,18,72,'phrase','ascend vs descend','ascend vs descend','ascend vs descend','🔤 Words\r\n\r\nascend /əˈsend/ — verb 动词\r\ndescend /dɪˈsend/ — verb 动词\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nascend = go up\r\n\r\n上升；登上；向上移动\r\n\r\nThe hikers ascended the mountain.\r\n徒步者登上了那座山。\r\n\r\ndescend = go down\r\n\r\n下降；下去；向下移动\r\n\r\nThe hikers descended the mountain.\r\n徒步者下了那座山。\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\nascend 里面可以想成 up ↑\r\ndescend 里面可以想成 down ↓\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nAscend means go up; descend means go down.\r\nascend 是向上，descend 是向下。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n📈 ascend\r\n\r\nThe plane began to ascend after take-off.\r\n飞机起飞后开始上升。\r\n\r\nShe ascended the stairs slowly.\r\n她慢慢上楼。\r\n\r\nHe ascended to a higher position in the company.\r\n他在公司升到了更高的职位。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n📉 descend\r\n\r\nThe plane began to descend for landing.\r\n飞机开始下降准备降落。\r\n\r\nShe descended the stairs carefully.\r\n她小心地下楼。\r\n\r\nDarkness descended over the city.\r\n黑暗降临在这座城市上空。','🔗 Word Family 词形变化\r\nverb:ascend 上升       noun: ascent 上升；攀登    adjective: ascending 上升的；升序的\r\n\r\nverb: descend 下降    noun:  descent 下降；血统   adjective: descending 下降的；降序的','/static/uploads/english_note_item/1b12f6f236e447cc918767ec3d5db7d8.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-18 08:59:18',1,'2026-05-18 08:59:18'),(1284,18,73,'phrase','mutual','mutual','mutual','🔤 Word\r\n\r\nmutual\r\n/ˈmjuːtʃuəl/\r\nadjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n相互的；彼此的；共同的\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nmutual means something is shared by two or more people, or felt/done by both sides.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n你对我这样，我也对你这样；双方都有。','🔗 Common Collocations 常见搭配\r\n\r\n🤝 mutual respect    相互尊重\r\n\r\n🔐 mutual trust     相互信任\r\n\r\n🎯 mutual goal    共同目标\r\n\r\n👥 mutual friend    共同的朋友\r\n\r\n💰 mutual benefit   互惠互利\r\n\r\n🧩 mutual understanding   相互理解\r\n\r\n🤝 mutual agreement   共同协议\r\n\r\n✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 相互的；彼此的\r\n\r\nThey have mutual respect for each other.\r\n他们彼此尊重。\r\n\r\nA good relationship needs mutual trust.\r\n一段好的关系需要相互信任。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 共同的；共有的\r\n\r\nWe have a mutual friend.\r\n我们有一个共同的朋友。\r\n\r\nThey discovered a mutual interest in music.\r\n他们发现彼此都对音乐感兴趣。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 互惠的；互利的\r\n\r\nThis agreement will bring mutual benefits to both sides.\r\n这个协议会给双方带来互惠互利。\r\n\r\nThe two companies built a mutual partnership.\r\n这两家公司建立了互利的合作关系。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nA healthy friendship is built on mutual trust, respect, and understanding.\r\n健康的友谊建立在相互信任、尊重和理解之上。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n把 mutual 想成：\r\n\r\nme ↔ you\r\n我对你，你也对我\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nmutual = both sides share the same feeling or action\r\n双方都有同样的感受或行为。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ We have a mutual friend.\r\n我们有一个共同的朋友。\r\n\r\n✅ The feeling is mutual.\r\n我也有同样的感觉。/ 彼此彼此。\r\n\r\n✅ It’s based on mutual trust.\r\n这是建立在相互信任的基础上的。\r\n\r\n✅ We need mutual respect.\r\n我们需要彼此尊重。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/34fad000e45541bb8b74103fa4521141.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-18 09:50:02',1,'2026-05-18 09:50:02'),(1285,18,74,'vocab','withdrawal','withdrawal','withdrawal','noun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n取款；提取；撤回；退出；戒断反应\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nwithdrawal 来自动词 withdraw，核心意思是：\r\n\r\ntaking something out or pulling something back\r\n把某物取出来，或者撤回来。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nI’d like to make an early withdrawal from my term deposit and check how the interest will be calculated.\r\n我想提前支取我的定期存款，并确认利息会怎么计算。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n把 withdrawal 想成：\r\n\r\nwith + draw + al\r\n\r\n这里的 withdraw 有“往回拉 / 取回”的感觉。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nwithdrawal = taking money out or pulling something back\r\n取款 / 提取 / 撤回。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 银行取款 / 提取资金\r\n\r\nI’d like to make a withdrawal from my account.\r\n我想从账户里取一笔钱。\r\n\r\nI’m asking about an early withdrawal from my term deposit.\r\n我想咨询定期存款提前支取。\r\n\r\nIs there a fee for early withdrawal?\r\n提前支取有手续费吗？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 撤回 / 退出\r\n\r\nThe withdrawal of the application took two days.\r\n撤回申请花了两天。\r\n\r\nThe company announced its withdrawal from the project.\r\n公司宣布退出这个项目。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 戒断反应\r\n\r\n和药物、酒精、咖啡因有关：\r\n\r\nHe had caffeine withdrawal symptoms.\r\n他有咖啡因戒断症状。\r\n\r\nWithdrawal symptoms can include headaches and anxiety.\r\n戒断症状可能包括头痛和焦虑。','🗣️ 电话银行常用句\r\n\r\n✅ I’d like to ask about early withdrawal from my term deposit.\r\n我想咨询定期存款提前支取。\r\n\r\n✅ Could you explain the early withdrawal process?\r\n你能解释一下提前支取流程吗？\r\n\r\n✅ Will there be an early withdrawal penalty?\r\n提前支取会有罚金吗？\r\n\r\n✅ How will the interest be calculated if I make an early withdrawal?\r\n如果我提前支取，利息会怎么算？\r\n\r\n🔗 Common Collocations 常见搭配\r\n\r\n💰 cash withdrawal.   现金取款\r\n\r\n🏦 bank withdrawal.  银行取款\r\n\r\n⏰ early withdrawal.    提前支取\r\n\r\n📄 withdrawal request.  支取申请 / 撤回申请\r\n\r\n💳 ATM withdrawal.   ATM 取款\r\n\r\n⚠️ withdrawal penalty.     提前支取罚金\r\n\r\n🤕 withdrawal symptoms.   戒断症状','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ea8a3073e3b2473b9135d064b9df69f0.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-19 08:25:12',1,'2026-05-19 08:25:12'),(1286,18,75,'vocab','tournament','tournament','tournament','/ˈtʊənəmənt/ NZ/UK\r\n/ˈtɝːnəmənt/ US\r\nnoun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n锦标赛；比赛会；联赛；系列比赛\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nA tournament is a competition with many players or teams, usually with several rounds, until one winner is decided.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n很多人或队伍参加，一轮一轮比赛，最后决出冠军。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe team advanced to the final of the tournament after winning three matches.\r\n这支队伍赢了三场比赛后，晋级到了锦标赛决赛。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n想象一个比赛表格：\r\n\r\n第一轮 → 半决赛 → 决赛 → 冠军 🏆\r\n\r\n这就是：\r\n\r\ntournament = a series of competitions to find the winner\r\n一系列比赛，最后决出冠军。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nHe won the tennis tournament.\r\n他赢得了网球锦标赛。\r\n\r\nOur school is hosting a debate tournament next month.\r\n我们学校下个月要举办一场辩论比赛。\r\n\r\nThe team entered a new tournament this season.\r\n这支队伍本赛季参加了一项新的锦标赛。\r\n\r\nShe was knocked out of the tournament in the first round.\r\n她在第一轮就被淘汰出局了。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3c53f528eb5848049207e1f368b6ef43.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-19 08:34:17',1,'2026-05-19 08:34:17'),(1287,18,76,'phrase','rescue','rescue','rescue','noun / verb 名词 / 动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n营救；救援；抢救\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nrescue means to save someone or something from danger, pain, or a difficult situation.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n把人、动物或东西从危险、困难中救出来。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 动词：营救 / 救出\r\n\r\nThe firefighters rescued the old man from the burning house.\r\n消防员把那位老人从着火的房子里救了出来。\r\n\r\nThe dog was rescued just in time.\r\n那只狗被及时救了出来。\r\n\r\nThey rescued the child from the river.\r\n他们把那个孩子从河里救了出来。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 名词：救援 / 营救\r\n\r\nThey launched a rescue operation to find the missing hikers.\r\n他们展开了一次救援行动，寻找失踪的徒步者。\r\n\r\nIt was a dramatic rescue.\r\n那是一次惊险的救援。','🔗 Common Collocations 常见搭配\r\n\r\n🚒 rescue team.  救援队\r\n\r\n🚁 rescue operation. 救援行动\r\n\r\n🐶 animal rescue.  动物救援\r\n\r\n⛰️ mountain rescue.  山地救援\r\n\r\n🌊 rescue at sea.  海上救援\r\n\r\n👷 rescue workers.  救援人员\r\n\r\n❤️ rescue someone’s life.  救某人的命\r\n🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ They rescued him from the water.\r\n他们把他从水里救了出来。\r\n\r\n✅ The rescue team arrived quickly.\r\n救援队很快到了。\r\n\r\n✅ She came to my rescue.\r\n她来帮我解围 / 救了我。\r\n\r\n✅ This dog is a rescue.\r\n这只狗是被救助/领养来的狗。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c303aa0875414c5791c23c63e48abc1c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-19 08:42:37',1,'2026-05-19 08:42:37'),(1288,18,77,'phrase','relocate','relocate','relocate','🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n迁移；搬迁；重新安置\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nrelocate means to move someone or something to a new place.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n从一个地方搬到另一个地方，通常比较正式。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nI’m planning to relocate to another city for better job opportunities.\r\n我计划搬到另一个城市，寻找更好的工作机会。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\nre- = again / again in a new way\r\nlocate = place / location\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nrelocate = locate again in a new place\r\n重新安置到一个新地方。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 人搬家 / 搬到新地方\r\n\r\nWe are planning to relocate next month.\r\n我们计划下个月搬家 / 迁居。\r\n\r\nShe relocated to Auckland for work.\r\n她因为工作搬到了奥克兰。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 公司 / 办公室搬迁\r\n\r\nThe company decided to relocate its head office.\r\n公司决定搬迁总部。\r\n\r\nThe factory will relocate to another city.\r\n工厂将搬到另一个城市。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 被重新安置\r\n\r\nThe village was relocated because of the dam project.\r\n由于大坝项目，这个村庄被整体迁移了。\r\n\r\nSome families were relocated after the flood.\r\n洪水后，一些家庭被重新安置。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ I’m relocating for work.\r\n我要因为工作搬家。\r\n\r\n✅ They relocated to a bigger office.\r\n他们搬到了一个更大的办公室。\r\n\r\n✅ Do you need help relocating?\r\n你需要帮忙搬迁吗？\r\n\r\n✅ The business relocated to reduce costs.\r\n这家公司为了降低成本搬迁了。','🔗 Common Collocations 常见搭配\r\n\r\n🚚 relocate to a new city  搬到一个新城市\r\n\r\n🏢 relocate a business   搬迁公司 / 业务\r\n\r\n👨‍👩‍👧 relocate a family   重新安置一个家庭\r\n\r\n👥 relocate staff / employees    调动员工 / 安置员工\r\n\r\n⏳ temporarily relocate  暂时搬迁\r\n\r\n📍 permanently relocate   永久搬迁','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ddbef0aeffb84e1a89df9ff4fd1cc5b3.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-19 08:49:26',1,'2026-05-19 08:49:26'),(1289,18,78,'vocab','stellar','stellar','stellar','adjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n极好的；出色的；卓越的；星星的；恒星的\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\nstellar 来自拉丁语 stella = star 星星。\r\n\r\n所以可以这样记：\r\n\r\nstellar = star-like excellent\r\n像星星一样闪耀、出色。','🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nstellar 有两个常见意思：\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 极好的；非常出色的\r\n\r\n这是最常用的口语和写作用法。\r\n\r\nextremely good; excellent; outstanding\r\n非常好，远超平均水平。\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 星星的；恒星的\r\n\r\n这是天文学里的意思。\r\n\r\nrelated to stars\r\n和星星 / 恒星有关的。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nYou did a stellar job.\r\n你做得非常出色。\r\n\r\nShe gave a stellar performance.\r\n她的表现非常出色。\r\n\r\nThe restaurant has received stellar reviews.\r\n这家餐厅收到了极高的评价。\r\n\r\nThe movie has a stellar cast.\r\n这部电影有很强大的演员阵容。\r\n🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ That was stellar!\r\n太棒了！\r\n\r\n✅ You did a stellar job.\r\n你做得太出色了。\r\n\r\n✅ Her performance was absolutely stellar.\r\n她的表现真的非常出色。\r\n\r\n✅ The service was stellar.\r\n服务非常棒。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ef01aa37a14a4b93818b25bb98be9855.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-19 10:40:37',1,'2026-05-19 10:40:37'),(1290,18,79,'vocab','translucent','translucent','translucent','/trænzˈluːsənt/\r\nadjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n半透明的；透光的；朦胧的\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ntranslucent means something lets light pass through, but you cannot see clearly through it.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n光能透过去，但看不清楚里面或后面的东西。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nThe curtain is translucent.\r\n这个窗帘是半透明的。\r\n\r\nThe leaf looked translucent in the sunlight.\r\n这片叶子在阳光下看起来半透明。\r\n\r\nThe glass is translucent, not transparent.\r\n这块玻璃是半透明的，不是完全透明的。\r\n\r\nThe paper is too thick. It’s not translucent enough.\r\n这张纸太厚了，不够透光。','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe bathroom window is translucent, so light can come in but people cannot see clearly through it.\r\n浴室窗户是半透明的，所以光可以进来，但别人看不清里面。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\ntrans- = through 穿过\r\nlucent = light 光\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ntranslucent = light passes through, but not clearly\r\n光能穿过，但看不清楚。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-19 16:24:34',1,'2026-05-19 16:24:34'),(1291,18,80,'phrase','arrange around','arrange around','arrange around','phrasal verb 短语动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n围绕……安排；围绕……布置；根据……安排\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\narrange around means to put or plan things around something or someone.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n以某个东西 / 某个人 / 某个时间为中心来安排。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 围绕某物布置\r\n\r\nThe chairs were arranged around the table.\r\n椅子围着桌子摆放。\r\n\r\nThe furniture was arranged around the fireplace.\r\n家具围绕壁炉布置。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 根据时间 / 日程安排\r\n\r\nWe arranged the meeting around his schedule.\r\n我们根据他的日程安排了会议。\r\n\r\nI arranged my day around the appointment.\r\n我围绕这个预约安排了一天的事情。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 围绕某人的需求安排\r\n\r\nThe plan was arranged around the children’s needs.\r\n这个计划是围绕孩子们的需求安排的。\r\n\r\nThe event was arranged around the guests’ arrival time.\r\n活动是根据客人的到达时间安排的。','It has a lime green back with black spots arranged around yellow patches.\r\n它有青绿色的背部，黑色斑点围绕着黄色斑块分布。\r\n\r\n或者更自然一点：\r\n\r\nIt has a lime green back, with black spots arranged around yellow markings.\r\n它有青绿色的背部，黑色斑点围绕着黄色花纹分布。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f1a75ab7ff804021ac54ff0d7ff73316.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-19 16:44:40',1,'2026-05-19 16:44:40'),(1292,18,81,'vocab','dwelling','dwelling','dwelling','noun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n住宅；住所；居所\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ndwelling means a place where people live.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n人居住的地方。\r\n\r\n它比 house 更正式，常见于法律、房地产、政府文件、建筑或统计资料里。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nThey live in a small dwelling near the lake.\r\n他们住在湖边的一所小住宅里。\r\n\r\nThe old building was converted into several dwellings.\r\n那栋老建筑被改造成了几套住宅。\r\n\r\nThis area has many private dwellings.\r\n这个地区有很多私人住宅。\r\n\r\nThe dwelling was damaged in the storm.\r\n这所住宅在暴风雨中受损了。','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe report shows that most dwellings in this area are privately owned.\r\n报告显示，这个地区大多数住宅都是私人拥有的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\ndwell = 居住\r\ndwelling = 居住的地方\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ndwelling = a place where people dwell/live\r\n人们居住的地方。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/819a6028c49447ac8c2c1f96dcb06ace.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-19 16:57:47',1,'2026-05-19 16:57:47'),(1293,18,82,'phrase','dwell','dwell','dwell','verb 动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n主要有两个意思：\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 居住；栖身\r\n\r\n比较正式或文学化，不如 live 常用。\r\n\r\nPeople used to dwell in caves.\r\n人们过去住在洞穴里。\r\n\r\nThey dwell in a small village.\r\n他们居住在一个小村庄里。\r\n\r\n日常口语更常说：\r\n\r\nThey live in a small village.\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 老是想着；纠结；沉湎于\r\n\r\n常用搭配：\r\n\r\ndwell on something\r\n\r\n意思是：反复想某事，尤其是不开心的事。\r\n\r\nDon’t dwell on the past.\r\n不要老想着过去。\r\n\r\nShe kept dwelling on her mistake.\r\n她一直纠结自己的错误。','例句\r\n\r\nThey dwell in the countryside.\r\n他们住在乡下。\r\n\r\nTheir dwelling is near the river.\r\n他们的住所靠近河边。','💡 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\ndwell = live somewhere\r\ndwelling = a place where people live','/static/uploads/english_note_item/0ac9555687fb4f5ea8e3e63527c97dd8.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-19 17:09:19',1,'2026-05-19 17:09:19'),(1294,18,83,'vocab','alumni','alumni','alumni','noun 名词，复数\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n校友；毕业生们\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nalumni means people who studied at a particular school, college, or university, especially people who have graduated.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n从某个学校毕业或曾经在那里学习过的人。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nOur alumni network is growing fast.\r\n我们的校友网络发展很快。\r\n\r\nMany successful alumni returned to give a speech.\r\n许多成功的校友回来发表演讲。\r\n\r\nThe university has a strong alumni association.\r\n这所大学有一个很强大的校友会。\r\n\r\nThe school keeps in touch with its alumni.\r\n学校和校友保持联系。','Examples\r\n\r\nHe is an alumnus of Lincoln University.\r\n他是林肯大学的男校友。\r\n\r\nShe is an alumna of Lincoln University.\r\n她是林肯大学的女校友。\r\n\r\nThey are alumni of Lincoln University.\r\n他们是林肯大学的校友。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nI hope to stay connected with the university alumni network after graduation.\r\n我希望毕业后继续和大学校友网络保持联系。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n可以把 alumni 想成：\r\n\r\npeople from the same school after graduation\r\n毕业后来自同一所学校的人。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/681c113519b34d1da2463033d9eb87ef.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-19 17:21:14',1,'2026-05-19 17:21:14'),(1295,18,84,'vocab','disguise','disguise','disguise','/dɪsˈɡaɪz/\r\nverb / noun 动词 / 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n伪装；掩饰；假扮；伪装物\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ndisguise means to change appearance or hide the real identity, feeling, or truth.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n把真实身份、真实样子或真实情绪藏起来。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nShe disguised her sadness with a smile.\r\n她用微笑掩饰自己的悲伤。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n想象一个人戴上假胡子、墨镜和帽子：\r\n\r\ndisguise = change how you look so people don’t recognise you\r\n改变外表，让别人认不出你。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 动词：伪装；假扮\r\n\r\nHe disguised himself as a waiter.\r\n他把自己伪装成服务员。\r\n\r\nThe thief wore a mask to disguise his identity.\r\n小偷戴着面具来掩饰自己的身份。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 动词：掩饰情绪 / 事实\r\n\r\nShe tried to disguise her nervousness.\r\n她试图掩饰自己的紧张。\r\n\r\nIt’s hard to disguise the truth.\r\n真相很难掩饰。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 名词：伪装；伪装物\r\n\r\nThe costume was a perfect disguise.\r\n这套服装是完美的伪装。\r\n\r\nHe went to the party in disguise.\r\n他乔装打扮去参加聚会。','🗣️ Natural Spoken English 口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ He was in disguise.\r\n他乔装打扮了。\r\n\r\n✅ She tried to disguise her feelings.\r\n她试图掩饰自己的感受。\r\n\r\n✅ I could see through his disguise.\r\n我看穿了他的伪装。\r\n\r\n✅ He disguised himself as a police officer.\r\n他把自己伪装成警察。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-19 17:45:13',1,'2026-05-19 17:45:13'),(1296,18,85,'vocab','canyon','canyon','canyon','noun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n峡谷；深谷\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nA canyon is a deep valley with very steep sides, often with a river flowing through it.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n很深、两边很陡的山谷，通常有河流穿过。','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe sunlight lit up the canyon walls, making them look bright orange.\r\n阳光照亮了峡谷岩壁，让它们看起来呈明亮的橙色。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n想象一条河把岩石切开，形成一个又深又陡的裂谷：\r\n\r\ncanyon = a deep rocky valley\r\n又深又陡的岩石峡谷。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nThe river flows through the canyon.\r\n河流流经峡谷。\r\n\r\nWe stood on the edge of the canyon and looked down.\r\n我们站在峡谷边缘向下看。\r\n\r\nThe Grand Canyon is very famous.\r\n大峡谷非常有名。\r\n\r\nWe hiked through the canyon.\r\n我们徒步穿过了峡谷。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e7ddc205992447709cab83569c49aba9.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-20 14:30:56',1,'2026-05-20 14:30:56'),(1297,18,86,'phrase','prehistoric','prehistoric','prehistoric','adjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n史前的；有史前时代特征的；非常古老的\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nprehistoric means relating to the time before written history.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n在人类有文字记录之前的，很久很久以前的。','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe museum has many prehistoric fossils and tools from early human life.\r\n这个博物馆有很多史前化石和早期人类生活使用的工具。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\npre- = before\r\nhistoric = history\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nprehistoric = before recorded history\r\n有文字记录的历史之前。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nDinosaurs lived in prehistoric times.\r\n恐龙生活在史前时代。\r\n\r\nScientists found a prehistoric fossil.\r\n科学家发现了一块史前化石。\r\n\r\nThese paintings are prehistoric rock art.\r\n这些绘画是史前岩画。\r\n\r\nPeople used stone tools in prehistoric times.\r\n史前时代的人们使用石器。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/165a8cde3ce6435c9118408ed28b6715.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-20 14:36:25',1,'2026-05-20 14:36:25'),(1298,19,1,'vocab','fossil','fossil','fossil','noun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n化石\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nA fossil is the remains or trace of an ancient animal or plant, preserved in rock for a very long time.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n远古动物或植物留下来的遗骸、痕迹，经过很久变成石头一样保存下来。','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe fossil shows that this animal lived millions of years ago.\r\n这块化石说明这种动物生活在数百万年前。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n想象一只恐龙很久很久以前留下骨头，后来被石头包住：\r\n\r\nfossil = ancient life preserved in rock\r\n被岩石保存下来的远古生命痕迹。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nScientists found a fossil of an ancient fish.\r\n科学家发现了一条古代鱼类的化石。\r\n\r\nThis rock contains a plant fossil.\r\n这块岩石里有植物化石。\r\n\r\nThe museum has many dinosaur fossils.\r\n博物馆里有很多恐龙化石。\r\n\r\nFossils help us learn about prehistoric life.\r\n化石帮助我们了解史前生命。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/295d79bdf0e04519b26d7c6a14d556d5.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-20 14:46:18',1,'2026-05-20 14:46:18'),(1299,19,2,'vocab','suspend','suspend','suspend','verb 动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n暂停；中止；暂时停职 / 停学；悬挂\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nsuspend means to stop something temporarily or hang something from above.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n暂时停下来，或者把东西悬在空中。','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe meeting was suspended due to a technical issue.\r\n由于技术问题，会议被暂停了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n想象一个暂停按钮 ⏸️：\r\n\r\nsuspend = pause something for a while\r\n暂时停一下，以后可能继续。\r\n\r\n⚠️ suspend vs stop\r\nstop  停止  可以是暂时，也可以是永久\r\n\r\nsuspend   暂停；暂时中止   强调“暂时停下，以后可能恢复”\r\n\r\nThey stopped the project.\r\n他们停止了这个项目。可能不再继续。\r\n\r\nThey suspended the project.\r\n他们暂停了这个项目。以后可能恢复。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 暂停；中止\r\n\r\nThe company decided to suspend the project.\r\n公司决定暂停这个项目。\r\n\r\nThe train service was suspended because of bad weather.\r\n由于天气不好，火车服务暂停了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 停职；停学\r\n\r\nHe was suspended from school for three days.\r\n他被停学三天。\r\n\r\nThe employee was suspended while the investigation continued.\r\n调查期间，该员工被暂时停职。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 悬挂；吊起\r\n\r\nThe light was suspended from the ceiling.\r\n灯从天花板上悬挂下来。\r\n\r\nA bridge was suspended over the river.\r\n一座桥悬在河上。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/5ddd9ed9baa245d4886749319c238eed.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-20 15:51:58',1,'2026-05-20 15:51:58'),(1300,19,3,'vocab','vantage','vantage','vantage','noun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n有利位置；优势；有利条件\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nvantage means a position or situation that gives you a good view, better understanding, or an advantage.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n站在一个更有利的位置，看得更清楚，判断得更好。','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe lookout offers a perfect vantage point for viewing the mountains.\r\n这个观景台提供了一个欣赏群山的绝佳位置。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n可以把 vantage 和 advantage 放一起记：\r\n\r\nvantage = a position that gives you an advantage\r\n一个能给你优势的位置。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 有利的观察位置\r\n\r\nFrom this vantage point, we can see the whole valley.\r\n从这个有利位置，我们可以看到整个山谷。\r\n\r\nThe hill provides a good vantage point for watching the sunset.\r\n这座小山是看日落的好位置。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 优势；有利条件\r\n\r\nExperience gave him a strong vantage in the competition.\r\n经验让他在比赛中占有优势。\r\n\r\n更常见也可以说：\r\n\r\nExperience gave him an advantage in the competition.\r\n经验让他在比赛中有优势。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2309557d950f428a80c41244173ea9e4.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-20 16:11:47',1,'2026-05-20 16:11:47'),(1301,19,4,'phrase','sweeping view','sweeping view','sweeping view','noun phrase 名词短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n开阔的景色；壮阔的全景；一览无余的景观\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nA sweeping view means a very wide and impressive view where you can see a large area.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n视野非常开阔，可以看到很大一片景色。\r\n\r\n通常是从高处看到的，比如山顶、塔顶、阳台、观景台。','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe lookout offers a sweeping view of the coastline.\r\n这个观景台可以看到海岸线的壮阔全景。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\nsweeping 有“横扫、覆盖很大范围”的感觉。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nsweeping view = a view that spreads widely across a large area\r\n像视线横扫过去一样，看到很大一片景色。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nThe hotel has a sweeping view of the ocean.\r\n这家酒店可以俯瞰大海，视野非常开阔。\r\n\r\nFrom the hill, we had a sweeping view of the valley.\r\n从山上，我们看到了山谷的壮阔全景。\r\n\r\nThe balcony offers sweeping views of the city.\r\n这个阳台可以看到城市的开阔景色。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2b7eb7df6a444e17bc7a14f0c3a4f9bf.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-20 16:40:33',1,'2026-05-20 16:40:33'),(1302,19,5,'phrase','accessible by','accessible by','accessible by','phrase 短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n可通过……到达；可乘……抵达\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\naccessible by means a place can be reached using a particular transport method, road, path, or route.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n某个地方可以通过某种方式到达。','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe lookout is accessible by car, but the last section must be walked.\r\n这个观景台可以开车到达，但最后一段需要步行。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\naccessible = easy to reach / able to be reached\r\nby = using a method\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\naccessible by bus = can be reached by bus\r\n可以乘公交到达。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nThe city is accessible by train.\r\n这座城市可以乘火车到达。\r\n\r\nThe village is only accessible by car.\r\n这个村子只能开车到达。\r\n\r\nThe island is accessible by ferry.\r\n这个岛可以乘渡轮到达。\r\n\r\nThe viewpoint is accessible by a short walking track.\r\n这个观景点可以通过一小段步道到达。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/40463c9cfca94757a32ec16c5c752fa7.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-20 16:49:58',1,'2026-05-20 16:49:58'),(1303,19,6,'phrase','zip line','zip line','zip line','noun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n滑索；高空滑索\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nA zip line is a strong cable stretched between two points. A person wears a harness and slides along the cable.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n人系着安全带，沿着钢索从高处滑到另一边。','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe zip line was scary at first, but the sweeping view made it worth it.\r\n滑索一开始有点吓人，但开阔壮丽的景色让它很值得。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\nzip 有“快速移动”的感觉，line 是“线”。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nzip line = a line you zip along\r\n一条让你快速滑过去的线。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nWe went zip lining through the forest.\r\n我们在森林里玩了滑索。\r\n\r\nThe zip line offers an amazing view of the valley.\r\n这条滑索可以看到山谷的壮丽景色。\r\n\r\nShe was nervous at first, but she loved the zip line.\r\n她一开始有点紧张，但后来很喜欢滑索。\r\n\r\nThe adventure park has three zip lines.\r\n这个冒险公园有三条滑索。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/7f22bd55561a45dbb939084b5b7418c3.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-20 17:02:02',1,'2026-05-20 17:02:02'),(1304,19,7,'phrase','soar over the gorge','soar over the gorge','soar over the gorge','/sɔːr ˈəʊvə ðə ɡɔːdʒ/ NZ/UK\r\n/sɔːr ˈoʊvər ðə ɡɔːrdʒ/ US\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n在峡谷上空翱翔 / 飞越峡谷\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nsoar means to fly or move high in the air smoothly and impressively.\r\ngorge means a deep, narrow valley with steep sides.\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nsoar over the gorge = 在深峡谷上空高高飞过 / 滑翔而过','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe zip line lets visitors soar over the gorge and enjoy a breathtaking view below.\r\n这条滑索让游客飞越峡谷，并欣赏脚下令人惊叹的景色。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nWe soared over the gorge on the zip line.\r\n我们坐滑索飞越峡谷。\r\n\r\nThe eagle soared over the gorge.\r\n老鹰在峡谷上空翱翔。\r\n\r\nFrom the zip line, you can soar over the gorge and enjoy a sweeping view.\r\n从滑索上，你可以飞越峡谷，欣赏壮阔的全景。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/5df98de149e74473bb294d1dc94fc16f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-20 17:05:16',1,'2026-05-20 17:05:16'),(1305,19,8,'phrase','Extreme eatery','Extreme eatery','Extreme eatery','noun phrase 名词短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n极限餐厅；特色刺激餐厅；位于特殊地点的餐饮场所\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nextreme eatery usually means a restaurant or food place that offers a very unusual, exciting, or adventurous dining experience.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n不只是吃饭，而是在一个特别刺激、特别不寻常的地方吃饭。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\n* 悬崖边餐厅\r\n* 高空餐厅\r\n* 水下餐厅\r\n* 洞穴餐厅\r\n* 山顶餐厅\r\n* 滑索/冒险景区里的餐厅','⚠️ 注意\r\n\r\neatery 是比较口语化的词，意思是 restaurant / food place。\r\nextreme eatery 不是特别常见的固定搭配，但可以作为旅游、广告、视频标题里的创意表达。\r\n\r\n更自然一点可以说：\r\n\r\nan adventurous dining experience\r\n一次充满冒险感的用餐体验\r\n\r\na restaurant in an extreme location\r\n一家位于极限地点的餐厅\r\n\r\na cliffside restaurant with a sweeping view\r\n一家拥有壮阔景色的悬崖边餐厅','✅ Example Sentences 例句\r\n\r\nWe had lunch at an extreme eatery on the edge of a cliff.\r\n我们在一家悬崖边的极限餐厅吃了午饭。\r\n\r\nThis extreme eatery is famous for its sweeping view of the valley.\r\n这家极限餐厅以山谷的壮阔全景而闻名。\r\n\r\nThe food was good, but the location made the eatery unforgettable.\r\n食物不错，但真正让人难忘的是它的位置。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/aa864c0c7de64eba95d25a48cefef010.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-20 17:12:29',1,'2026-05-20 17:12:29'),(1306,19,9,'vocab','Georgia','Georgia','Georgia','乔治亚 / 格鲁吉亚\r\n这是一个国家，位于 欧洲和亚洲交界处，高加索地区。\r\n\r\n英文：\r\n\r\nGeorgia is a country between Europe and Asia.\r\n乔治亚是一个位于欧亚交界处的国家。\r\n\r\n中文里以前常说 格鲁吉亚，现在也常见 乔治亚。','','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/0767563362eb485789cf9fc503d62e70.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-20 17:21:48',1,'2026-05-20 17:21:48'),(1307,19,10,'vocab','blend','blend','blend','verb / noun 动词 / 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n混合；融合；协调；混合物\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nblend means to mix two or more things together smoothly, or to fit in well with other things.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n混在一起，而且融合得比较自然、协调。','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe design blends modern style with traditional elements.\r\n这个设计融合了现代风格和传统元素。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n想象把水果放进 blender 搅拌机：\r\n\r\nblend = mix smoothly\r\n混合得很顺滑、很自然。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 动词：混合；搅拌\r\n\r\nShe blended the fruit into a smoothie.\r\n她把水果搅拌成果昔。\r\n\r\nBlend the ingredients until smooth.\r\n把食材搅拌到顺滑。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 动词：融合；协调\r\n\r\nThe colours blend well together.\r\n这些颜色搭配得很协调。\r\n\r\nThe new building blends in with the old town.\r\n这座新建筑和老城区很协调地融为一体。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 动词：融入群体\r\n\r\nHe blended in quickly with his new classmates.\r\n他很快融入了新同学中。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n4️⃣ 名词：混合物；混合风格\r\n\r\nThis coffee is a special blend.\r\n这款咖啡是特别调配的混合咖啡。\r\n\r\nThe song is a blend of traditional and modern music.\r\n这首歌融合了传统音乐和现代音乐。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3f29e42da15544278a1a50007234530e.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-20 17:45:54',1,'2026-05-20 17:45:54'),(1308,19,11,'phrase','put on bandages','put on bandages','put on bandages','verb phrase 动词短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n包扎伤口；缠绷带；贴/包上绷带\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nput on bandages means to cover a wound or injured area with bandages.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n用绷带把受伤的地方包起来，保护伤口。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nShe put on bandages to protect the wound.\r\n她包上绷带来保护伤口。\r\n\r\nThe nurse put on bandages after cleaning the cut.\r\n护士清理伤口后给它包上了绷带。\r\n\r\nWe put on bandages to stop the bleeding.\r\n我们包扎伤口来止血。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🗣️ 更自然的说法\r\n\r\n如果是“给某人包扎伤口”，更自然可以说：\r\n\r\nput a bandage on someone’s wound\r\n给某人的伤口贴/包上绷带\r\n\r\nbandage the wound\r\n包扎伤口\r\n\r\ndress the wound\r\n处理/包扎伤口，更正式，医疗场景常用','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/80f1407ab0034d78befeca008621255f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-21 06:19:08',1,'2026-05-21 06:19:08'),(1309,19,12,'vocab','anti-','anti-','anti-','anti-\r\n/ˈænti/ 或 /ˈæntaɪ/\r\nprefix 前缀\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n反对；对抗；防止；抗……的；相反的\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nanti- 通常表示：\r\n\r\nagainst / opposite to / preventing something\r\n反对某事、对抗某物、防止某事发生。','✅ 常见含义\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 反对；反……\r\n\r\nanti-war = 反战的\r\nanti-smoking = 反吸烟的\r\nanti-discrimination = 反歧视的\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 抗……；对抗……\r\n\r\nantibiotic = 抗生素\r\nantiviral = 抗病毒的\r\nanti-inflammatory = 抗炎的\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 防止……\r\n\r\nantifreeze = 防冻液\r\nanti-theft = 防盗的\r\nanti-aging = 抗衰老的\r\n\r\n4️⃣ 相反方向\r\n\r\nanticlockwise = 逆时针的\r\n相当于 opposite to clockwise。','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThis cream has anti-aging ingredients.\r\n这款面霜含有抗衰老成分。\r\n\r\nThe school has an anti-bullying policy.\r\n学校有反霸凌政策。\r\n\r\nAntibiotics are used to fight bacterial infections.\r\n抗生素用于对抗细菌感染。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n把 anti- 想成：\r\n\r\n站在对面说 “No!”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nanti- = against / prevent / opposite\r\n反对、阻止、对抗、相反。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f540003efeb545edaf25d4458f9fa165.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-21 06:34:49',1,'2026-05-21 06:34:49'),(1310,19,13,'vocab','bio-  geo-  psych- hydro- thermo-','bio-  geo-  psych- hydro- thermo-','bio-  geo-  psych- hydro- thermo-','bio 生命，geo 地球，psych 心理，hydro 水；\r\nthermo 热，eco 生态，socio 社会，cardio 心；\r\ndent 牙齿，hem 血液，logy 就是“……学”。','','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b1c351e3669e4f44b0ef142273c093c4.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-21 07:07:21',1,'2026-05-21 07:07:21'),(1311,19,14,'vocab','metropolis','metropolis','metropolis','🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n大都市；主要城市；中心城市\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nmetropolis means a very large and important city, often the main city of a region or country.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n规模大、人口多、经济文化重要的大城市。\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n可以把 metropolis 想成：\r\n\r\nmetro + city\r\n\r\n像地铁、商业区、高楼、人流很多的城市中心。\r\n\r\nmetropolis = a big important city\r\n大而重要的城市。','✅ Examples 例句\r\n\r\nAuckland is New Zealand’s largest metropolis.\r\n奥克兰是新西兰最大的都市。\r\n\r\nShanghai is a modern metropolis.\r\n上海是一座现代化大都市。\r\n\r\nThe city grew from a small town into a major metropolis.\r\n这座城市从一个小镇发展成了一个重要的大都市。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/75ceedb653ba4115baf12f017179a205.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-21 07:17:10',1,'2026-05-21 07:17:10'),(1312,19,15,'vocab','verbal','verbal','verbal','adjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n口头的；言语的；用语言表达的\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nverbal means using words, especially spoken words.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n用语言表达的，通常指口头说出来的。','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nA verbal agreement is useful, but a written agreement is safer.\r\n口头协议有用，但书面协议更保险。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\nverb = 动词 / 说话相关\r\n-al = 形容词后缀\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nverbal = related to words or speaking\r\n和语言、说话有关的。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nShe gave a clear verbal explanation.\r\n她给出了清楚的口头解释。\r\n\r\nThey reached a verbal agreement.\r\n他们达成了口头协议。\r\n\r\nHe received a verbal warning from his boss.\r\n他收到了老板的口头警告。\r\n\r\nPlease confirm it in writing, not just verbally.\r\n请用书面形式确认，不要只是口头说。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c8314a97088f43fd9c246f8154f1ab61.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-21 07:43:39',1,'2026-05-21 07:43:39'),(1313,19,16,'sentence','some 800 miles away from Jakarta','some 800 miles away from Jakarta','some 800 miles away from Jakarta','这里的 some 不是“一些”的意思，而是表示：\r\n\r\n✅ 大约；约；差不多\r\n\r\nsome 800 miles away from Jakarta\r\n= about 800 miles away from Jakarta\r\n= approximately 800 miles away from Jakarta\r\n\r\n中文就是：\r\n\r\n距离雅加达大约 800 英里','🔍 这种 some 的用法\r\n\r\nsome + 数字 / 数量\r\n表示 around / about / approximately。\r\n\r\n例句\r\n\r\nThe village is some 50 kilometres from the city.\r\n这个村子距离城市大约 50 公里。\r\n\r\nThe island lies some 800 miles away from Jakarta.\r\n这个岛距离雅加达大约 800 英里。\r\n\r\nSome 2,000 people attended the event.\r\n大约 2000 人参加了这个活动。\r\n\r\nThe building is some 300 years old.\r\n这栋建筑大约有 300 年历史。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n📌 语气感觉\r\n\r\nsome + number 比 about 稍微更书面一点，常见于：\r\n\r\n* 书籍\r\n* 新闻\r\n* 纪录片\r\n* 地理介绍\r\n* 历史说明\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe temple was built some 1,000 years ago.\r\n这座寺庙建于大约 1000 年前。','📌 语气感觉\r\n\r\nsome + number 比 about 稍微更书面一点，常见于：\r\n\r\n* 书籍\r\n* 新闻\r\n* 纪录片\r\n* 地理介绍\r\n* 历史说明\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe temple was built some 1,000 years ago.\r\n这座寺庙建于大约 1000 年前。\r\n\r\n所以你看到：\r\n\r\nsome + 数字\r\n\r\n很多时候就可以直接理解为：\r\n\r\nabout / approximately = 大约','/static/uploads/english_note_item/eb9d70b2fefc4272b236be86335f3255.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-21 09:09:03',1,'2026-05-21 09:09:03'),(1314,19,17,'sentence','building a new city from scratch will only lead to more pollution','building a new city from scratch will only lead to more pollution','building a new city from scratch will only lead to more pollution','从头建一座新城市只会带来更多污染','句子拆解\r\n\r\nbuilding a new city. 建一座新城市\r\n\r\nfrom scratch.   从零开始；从头开始\r\n\r\nwill only lead to.   只会导致；最终只会造成\r\n\r\nmore pollution.  更多污染\r\n\r\n重点短语：from scratch\r\n\r\nfrom scratch = 从零开始，没有现成基础。\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nI learned English from scratch.\r\n我从零开始学英语。\r\n\r\nThey built the business from scratch.\r\n他们白手起家创办了这家公司。\r\n\r\nlead to\r\n\r\nlead to = 导致；造成\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nToo much traffic can lead to air pollution.\r\n太多交通会导致空气污染。\r\n\r\n更自然翻译\r\n这里的 only 有一种强调和负面判断：\r\n\r\n不是“可能会”，而是说话者认为：\r\n这样做不会解决问题，反而只会制造更多污染。','','','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-21 13:26:43',1,'2026-05-21 13:26:43'),(1315,19,18,'vocab','scratch','scratch','scratch','verb / noun 动词 / 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n刮；抓；挠；划伤；划痕；抓痕；草稿\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nscratch means to rub or cut a surface lightly with something sharp, such as fingernails or a tool.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n用指甲或尖的东西在表面抓、挠、划，留下痕迹或缓解痒。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nI’m learning JavaScript from scratch.\r\n我正在从零开始学习 JavaScript。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n想象猫用爪子抓沙发：\r\n\r\nscratch = use nails or something sharp to rub/cut a surface\r\n用指甲或尖锐物抓、挠、划表面。','','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nShe scratched her arm because it was itchy.\r\n她因为痒而挠了挠胳膊。\r\n\r\nBe careful not to scratch the table.\r\n小心不要划伤桌子。\r\n\r\nThere is a scratch on the car door.\r\n车门上有一道划痕。\r\n\r\nWe only had time to scratch a quick lunch.\r\n我们只能匆匆吃了点午饭。\r\n这里 scratch 有“勉强凑合 / 匆忙弄出”的感觉。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/56ff8189bf824ba1bb40eab21d4055e6.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-21 13:28:27',1,'2026-05-21 13:28:27'),(1316,19,19,'phrase','take some pressure off','take some pressure off','take some pressure off','verb phrase 动词短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n减轻一些压力；缓解负担；让某人轻松一点\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\ntake some pressure off means to reduce stress, responsibility, or difficulty for someone.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n把一部分压力拿走，让人没那么紧张或没那么累。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nFinishing this part early will take some pressure off us before the deadline.\r\n提前完成这部分会在截止日期前减轻我们一些压力。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💡 Memory Tip 记忆小贴士\r\n\r\n想象肩膀上背着一个很重的包，有人帮你拿走一部分：\r\n\r\ntake some pressure off = reduce the weight/stress\r\n把压力拿走一点，负担变轻。','⚠️ take pressure off vs put pressure on\r\n\r\ntake pressure off   减轻压力.      压力变小\r\n\r\nput pressure on.     给……施压.   压力变大\r\n\r\nThis helper will take some pressure off the manager.\r\n这个助手会减轻经理的一些压力。\r\n\r\nThe deadline puts pressure on the team.\r\n截止日期给团队带来了压力。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nThis will take some pressure off me.\r\n这样会帮我减轻一些压力。\r\n\r\nHaving another person on the team will take some pressure off us.\r\n团队里多一个人会让我们轻松一些。\r\n\r\nThe extra funding should take some pressure off the project.\r\n额外资金应该能缓解这个项目的压力。\r\n\r\nCan you help me with this task? It would take some pressure off.\r\n你能帮我处理这个任务吗？这样我会轻松一些。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/01306b31cdc046b99abc4e68db92527b.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-21 13:39:24',1,'2026-05-21 13:39:24'),(1317,19,20,'vocab','Relative','Relative','Relative','adjective / noun 形容词 / 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n相对的；比较的；亲戚；亲属\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nrelative 有两个常见意思：\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 形容词：相对的；比较而言的\r\n\r\nrelative means something is judged by comparing it with something else.\r\n\r\n不是绝对的，而是和别的东西比较出来的。\r\n\r\nThe cost is relatively low.\r\n费用相对较低。\r\n\r\nIt is a relatively small city.\r\n这是一个相对较小的城市。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 名词：亲戚；亲属\r\n\r\nrelative also means a person in your family.\r\n\r\nWe are visiting our relatives this weekend.\r\n这个周末我们要去看亲戚。\r\n\r\nShe has many relatives in Australia.\r\n她在澳大利亚有很多亲戚。','','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/29c18f2c7da142a59a7f4a1178071ac0.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-21 14:06:41',1,'2026-05-21 14:06:41'),(1318,19,21,'phrase','assert dominance','assert dominance','assert dominance','verb phrase 动词短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n显示支配地位；宣示权威；确立主导地位\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nassert dominance means to show clearly that you are stronger, more powerful, or in control.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n通过行为、姿态、语言等告诉别人：“我是更强的 / 我在掌控局面。”','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nThe lion roared to assert dominance over the other males.\r\n那只狮子咆哮着，向其他雄狮显示自己的统治地位。\r\n\r\nHe kept interrupting others to assert dominance in the meeting.\r\n他在会议中不断打断别人，以显示自己的主导地位。\r\n\r\nThe company made an aggressive move to assert dominance in the market.\r\n这家公司采取激进举措，以确立市场主导地位。','He spoke first to assert dominance.\r\n他先发言，以显示主导地位。\r\n\r\nShe is the dominant player on the team.\r\n她是队里最具主导地位的球员。\r\n⚠️ 使用注意\r\n\r\n这个短语有时带有 强势、压迫、控制欲 的感觉。\r\n描述动物、竞争、市场时很自然；描述人际关系时要小心，可能听起来比较负面。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nSome animals use body language to assert dominance over others.\r\n有些动物会用肢体语言向其他动物显示支配地位。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b267d1b4f4d6438ba2eef4d399239692.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-21 14:19:20',1,'2026-05-21 14:19:20'),(1319,19,22,'grammar','opponent','opponent','opponent','noun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n对手；竞争者；反对者；敌手\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nopponent means someone who competes against you or disagrees with you.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\n站在你对面，和你比赛、竞争、辩论或反对你的人。\r\n\r\n⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nA good opponent can push you to become better.\r\n一个好的对手能推动你变得更强。','⚠️ opponent vs competitor vs enemy\r\nopponent 对手；反对者  比赛、辩论、政治、观点上的对立方\r\n\r\ncompetitor. 竞争者. 商业、比赛中竞争的人或公司\r\n\r\nenemy.  敌人.  敌意更强，关系更恶劣\r\n\r\nWe respect our opponent.\r\n我们尊重我们的对手。\r\n\r\nThis company has many competitors.\r\n这家公司有很多竞争对手。\r\n\r\nThey became enemies after the war.\r\n战争后他们成了敌人。','✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nOur team will play against a strong opponent tomorrow.\r\n我们队明天将对阵一个强劲的对手。\r\n\r\nHe is a worthy opponent.\r\n他是一位值得尊敬的对手。\r\n\r\nShe was a strong opponent of the new policy.\r\n她是这项新政策的强烈反对者。\r\n\r\nThe champion faced many tough opponents.\r\n这位冠军遇到了很多强大的对手。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-21 14:24:28',1,'2026-05-21 14:24:28'),(1320,19,23,'phrase','beg the question','beg the question','beg the question','idiom 习语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n预设结论；把需要证明的观点当成前提；引出一个问题\r\n\r\n如果你想表达“这就引出了一个问题”，日常更推荐：\r\n\r\nThis raises the question: …\r\n这就引出了一个问题：……','🧠 Core Meaning 核心意思\r\n\r\nbeg the question 有两个常见用法：\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 逻辑学 / 批判性思维：预设结论\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n在论证中，把还没有证明的结论直接当成前提。\r\n\r\nassume the conclusion instead of proving it\r\n把结论当成前提，而不是去证明它。\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nThis product is the best because no other product is better.\r\n这个产品是最好的，因为没有其他产品比它好。\r\n这里其实没有真正证明，只是在绕圈。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 日常口语：引出一个问题\r\n\r\n现在很多人也用它表示：\r\n\r\nraise the question\r\n这就引出了一个问题。\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nThe project is delayed again, which begs the question: do we need a better plan?\r\n项目又延期了，这就引出了一个问题：我们是不是需要一个更好的计划？','⭐ Useful Sentence\r\n\r\nThe claim that the policy is good because it is beneficial begs the question.\r\n说“这项政策是好的，因为它有益”其实预设了结论。\r\n\r\n✅ Common Uses 常见用法\r\n\r\nHis argument begs the question.\r\n他的论证预设了结论。\r\n\r\nThat explanation begs the question of why it happened in the first place.\r\n这个解释引出了一个问题：它一开始为什么会发生？\r\n\r\nSaying “it is true because I believe it” begs the question.\r\n说“这是真的，因为我相信它是真的”就是预设结论。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2038f679bfb24c4d8ac05db9cbc7927f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-21 14:37:21',1,'2026-05-21 14:37:21'),(1321,19,24,'vocab','medieval','medieval','medieval','adjective\r\n中世纪的；中古时期的\r\n\r\n🧠 Meaning\r\n\r\nmedieval means related to the Middle Ages, roughly the period in European history between the 5th century and the 15th century.\r\n\r\n中文可以理解为：\r\n\r\n中世纪的 / 欧洲中古时期的','adjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n中世纪的；中古时期的\r\n\r\n🧠 核心理解\r\n\r\nmedieval = related to the Middle Ages\r\n和欧洲“中世纪”有关的。','✅ Common Phrases\r\n\r\n* medieval castle：中世纪城堡\r\n* medieval history：中世纪历史\r\n* medieval times：中世纪时期\r\n* medieval village：中世纪村庄\r\n\r\n📌 Example\r\n\r\nWe visited a medieval castle in Europe.\r\n我们参观了一座欧洲的中世纪城堡。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\nmedi- 像 middle，表示“中间”。\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nmedieval ≈ Middle Ages → 中世纪的','/static/uploads/english_note_item/57fc97eae7e3497e9df53f7570beb331.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-22 11:10:47',1,'2026-05-22 11:10:47'),(1322,19,25,'vocab','intact','intact','intact','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nadjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n完整无损的；未受损坏的；保持原样的\r\n\r\n🧠 核心理解\r\n\r\nintact means something is still complete and not broken, damaged, or changed.\r\n可以理解为：经历了一些事情之后，仍然完好，没有坏。','✅ Common Uses｜常见搭配\r\n\r\nremain intact：保持完整\r\nkeep something intact：保持某物完整\r\nsurvive intact：完整保存下来\r\nleave something intact：让某物保持原样\r\n\r\n📌 Example Sentences｜例句\r\n\r\nThe old building remained intact after the earthquake.\r\n地震之后，那座老建筑仍然完好无损。\r\n\r\nLuckily, the phone was still intact after it fell on the floor.\r\n幸运的是，手机掉到地上后仍然完好无损。','🔁 Comparison｜对比\r\n\r\nintact vs complete\r\n\r\nintact 强调：没有坏，保持原样。\r\ncomplete 强调：部分齐全，没有缺少。\r\n\r\nThe vase is intact.\r\n花瓶没坏，完好无损。\r\n\r\nThe report is complete.\r\n报告内容齐全，已经完成。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip｜记忆技巧\r\n\r\n记住这句话：\r\n\r\nintact = still in one piece\r\n意思是：仍然是一整块，没有坏。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/11b514d03d214f0a872cafcc5f6fbad8.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-22 11:24:46',1,'2026-05-22 11:24:46'),(1323,19,26,'vocab','authorities','authorities','authorities','🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n有关部门；当局；官方机构','🧠 核心理解\r\n\r\nauthorities 指有权力处理问题的官方人员或机构，比如：\r\n\r\n* police 警察\r\n* government departments 政府部门\r\n* immigration authorities 移民局/移民部门\r\n* health authorities 卫生部门\r\n* school authorities 学校管理部门\r\n* local authorities 地方政府/市政部门\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip｜记忆技巧\r\n\r\nauthority 里面有 author 的感觉。\r\n谁有权“写规则”？官方机构。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nauthorities = the people or departments with official power\r\n有正式权力处理事情的人或部门。\r\n\r\n记住一句：\r\n\r\nReport it to the authorities.\r\n把这件事报告给有关部门。','✅ 常见搭配 Common Collocations\r\n\r\nreport something to authorities\r\n向有关部门报告某事\r\n\r\nhand something over to authorities\r\n把某物交给当局\r\n\r\nprovide information to authorities\r\n向有关部门提供信息\r\n\r\nsubmit documents to authorities\r\n向官方机构提交文件\r\n\r\nappeal to authorities\r\n向当局申诉 / 求助\r\n\r\nknown to authorities\r\n被有关部门知道 / 已在警方或官方记录中\r\n\r\n📌 Example Sentences｜不同场景例句\r\n\r\n🚓 1. 警察 / 犯罪场景\r\n\r\nThe incident was reported to authorities immediately.\r\n这起事件被立即报告给了有关部门。\r\n\r\nWitnesses gave the video footage to authorities.\r\n目击者把视频资料交给了警方。\r\n\r\nThe suspect was already known to authorities.\r\n这名嫌疑人之前已经被警方注意到 / 在警方记录中。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🏫 2. 学校场景\r\n\r\nThe bullying case was reported to school authorities.\r\n这起霸凌事件被报告给了学校管理部门。\r\n\r\nParents complained to authorities about the unsafe playground.\r\n家长向有关部门投诉 playground 不安全。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🏥 3. 卫生 / 公共安全场景\r\n\r\nThe disease outbreak was reported to health authorities.\r\n疾病爆发被报告给了卫生部门。\r\n\r\nRestaurants must provide food safety records to authorities when requested.\r\n餐馆在被要求时必须向有关部门提供食品安全记录。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🛂 4. 移民 / 海关场景\r\n\r\nYou may need to show these documents to immigration authorities.\r\n你可能需要向移民部门出示这些文件。\r\n\r\nThe goods were declared to customs authorities.\r\n这些物品已经向海关申报。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🏢 5. 政府 / 市政场景\r\n\r\nThe company submitted the application to local authorities.\r\n公司向地方政府提交了申请。\r\n\r\nResidents raised their concerns to authorities after the flooding.\r\n洪水之后，居民向有关部门反映了他们的担忧。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d706ffeeb6404f5aa7836906e54056d1.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-22 11:43:00',1,'2026-05-22 11:43:00'),(1324,19,27,'phrase','specialize in','specialize in','specialize in','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nphrasal verb / verb phrase\r\n动词短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n专门从事；专攻；擅长于；以……为专业\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 核心理解\r\n\r\nspecialize in 的核心意思是：\r\n\r\nfocus on one particular area and become good at it\r\n专注在某一个领域，并且在这个领域很专业。\r\n\r\n它常用来描述：\r\n\r\n* 一个人的专业方向\r\n* 一家公司主要做什么\r\n* 一个医生/律师/工程师擅长什么\r\n* 一个课程或研究项目专注什么方向\r\n\r\nI specialize in this area.\r\n我专攻这个领域。','✅ Common Uses｜常见搭配\r\n\r\nspecialize in + field / subject\r\n专攻某个领域 / 学科\r\n\r\nspecialize in + service\r\n专门提供某种服务\r\n\r\nspecialize in + type of work\r\n专门做某类工作\r\n\r\nspecialize in + technology\r\n专注某种技术\r\n\r\nspecialize in treating + disease\r\n专门治疗某种疾病','📌 Example Sentences｜不同场景例句\r\n\r\n💼 1. 工作 / 职业场景\r\n\r\nOur company specializes in cloud-based software solutions.\r\n我们公司专门做基于云的软件解决方案。\r\n\r\nHe specializes in backend development and system architecture.\r\n他专注于后端开发和系统架构。\r\n\r\nThis team specializes in building high-throughput systems.\r\n这个团队专门构建高吞吐量系统。\r\n\r\nThe agency specializes in digital marketing for small businesses.\r\n这家公司专门为小企业做数字营销。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🎓 2. 学习 / 专业方向\r\n\r\nShe specializes in environmental science.\r\n她专攻环境科学。\r\n\r\nMy research project specializes in rainfall interpolation and image similarity analysis.\r\n我的研究项目专注于降雨插值和图像相似度分析。\r\n\r\nThe course specializes in practical data analysis skills.\r\n这门课程专注于实用的数据分析技能。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🏥 3. 医疗场景\r\n\r\nThis doctor specializes in children’s dental care.\r\n这位医生专门做儿童牙科护理。\r\n\r\nThe hospital specializes in heart disease treatment.\r\n这家医院专门治疗心脏病。\r\n\r\nShe specializes in treating skin problems.\r\n她专门治疗皮肤问题。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧑‍🍳 4. 餐厅 / 商店场景\r\n\r\nThis restaurant specializes in seafood.\r\n这家餐厅主打海鲜。\r\n\r\nThe bakery specializes in French pastries.\r\n这家面包店专门做法式点心。\r\n\r\nThat shop specializes in second-hand furniture.\r\n那家店专门卖二手家具。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧑‍💻 5. 技术 / IT 场景\r\n\r\nThe system specializes in processing large volumes of messages.\r\n这个系统专门处理大量消息。\r\n\r\nThis tool specializes in image processing.\r\n这个工具专门用于图像处理。\r\n\r\nThe model specializes in detecting patterns in data.\r\n这个模型专门识别数据中的模式。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2b2b09c114c5491f9a110b3354cf1506.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-22 11:52:39',1,'2026-05-22 11:52:39'),(1325,19,28,'phrase','antiquities','antiquities','antiquities','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nnoun plural 复数名词\r\n单数形式：antiquity /ænˈtɪkwəti/\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n古物；古董；文物；古代遗迹；古代艺术品\r\n\r\n🧠 核心理解\r\n\r\nantiquities 指的是来自很久以前的东西，通常有历史、文化或考古价值。\r\n\r\n可以理解为：\r\n\r\nancient objects from the past\r\n从古代留下来的、有历史价值的东西。\r\n\r\n它常见于这些场景：\r\n\r\n* 博物馆里的古代文物\r\n* 考古发现的物品\r\n* 古埃及、古希腊、古罗马文物\r\n* 被非法买卖或走私的古物\r\n* 历史遗迹和古代艺术品','✅ Common Collocations｜常见搭配\r\n\r\nancient antiquities\r\n古代文物\r\n\r\nvaluable antiquities\r\n珍贵古物\r\n\r\nstolen antiquities\r\n被盗文物\r\n\r\ntrade in antiquities\r\n古物交易 / 文物交易\r\n\r\nantiquities market\r\n古董 / 文物市场\r\n\r\nantiquities dealer\r\n古董商 / 文物商人\r\n\r\nmuseum of antiquities\r\n古物博物馆\r\n\r\ncollection of antiquities\r\n古物收藏\r\n\r\nreturn antiquities to their country of origin\r\n把文物归还原属国\r\n\r\nantiquities vs antiques\r\nantiquities  古物；文物        更古老，通常有考古、历史、文化价值\r\n\r\nantiques   古董     通常指老家具、老物件、收藏品，不一定是古代文物\r\n\r\nThe museum displays Roman antiquities.\r\n博物馆展示罗马文物。\r\n👉 很古老，有历史和考古价值。\r\n\r\nShe collects antique furniture.\r\n她收藏古董家具。\r\n👉 可能是一两百年前的家具，不一定是“古代文物”。\r\n\r\nantiquities vs artifacts\r\n\r\nantiquities   古物；文物     强调古代、历史价值\r\n\r\nartifacts   人工制品；器物      更广泛，任何人造物都可以是 artifact\r\n\r\nThe archaeologists found ancient artifacts.\r\n考古学家发现了古代器物。\r\n👉 强调“人造物”。\r\n\r\n⚠️ Grammar Note｜语法提醒\r\n\r\nantiquities 通常用复数，因为常指“一批古物 / 一类文物”。\r\n\r\n常见说法：\r\n\r\na collection of antiquities  一批古物收藏\r\n\r\nmany antiquities  许多文物\r\n\r\nstolen antiquities.   被盗文物\r\n\r\n单数 antiquity 也可以表示：\r\n\r\n1. 古代.   in antiquity = 在古代\r\n2. 古物，但不如复数常见\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\nThis tradition dates back to antiquity.\r\n这个传统可以追溯到古代。\r\n\r\nSome of these artifacts are important antiquities.\r\n其中一些器物是重要文物。\r\n👉 这些 artifact 具有古代文物价值。\r\n\r\n🗣️ Natural Speaking｜自然表达\r\n\r\n如果你在博物馆看到古物，可以说：\r\n\r\nThese antiquities are really impressive.\r\n这些古物真的很震撼。\r\n\r\n如果你想说“古代文物很有历史价值”：\r\n\r\nAntiquities help us understand ancient cultures.\r\n古物帮助我们了解古代文化。\r\n\r\n如果你看到新闻说文物被归还：\r\n\r\nThe stolen antiquities were returned to their country of origin.\r\n被盗文物被归还给了原属国。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip｜记忆技巧\r\n\r\nantiquities 可以和 ancient 一起记。\r\n\r\nantique = 古老的 / 古董的\r\nantiquities = 古代留下来的文物\r\n\r\n记住一句：\r\n\r\nAntiquities are ancient objects with historical value.\r\nantiquities 就是有历史价值的古代物品。','📌 Example Sentences｜不同场景例句\r\n\r\n🏛️ 1. 博物馆场景\r\n\r\nThe museum has a large collection of Greek and Roman antiquities.\r\n这家博物馆收藏了大量古希腊和古罗马文物。\r\n\r\nVisitors can see Egyptian antiquities, including statues and pottery.\r\n游客可以看到埃及古物，包括雕像和陶器。\r\n\r\nSome antiquities are displayed behind glass to protect them.\r\n一些文物被放在玻璃后面展示，以保护它们。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧱 2. 考古 / 历史场景\r\n\r\nArchaeologists discovered several antiquities near the old temple.\r\n考古学家在古庙附近发现了几件古物。\r\n\r\nThese antiquities tell us how people lived thousands of years ago.\r\n这些古物告诉我们几千年前人们是如何生活的。\r\n\r\nThe site contains many antiquities from the medieval period.\r\n这个遗址包含许多中世纪时期的文物。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🚔 3. 新闻 / 法律场景\r\n\r\nThe police seized a number of stolen antiquities.\r\n警方查获了一批被盗文物。\r\n\r\nThe country is trying to recover antiquities that were taken overseas.\r\n这个国家正试图追回被带到海外的文物。\r\n\r\nTrading in stolen antiquities is illegal.\r\n买卖被盗文物是违法的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💰 4. 古董市场 / 收藏场景\r\n\r\nHe works as an antiquities dealer.\r\n他是一名古物商人。\r\n\r\nThe antiquities market can be difficult to regulate.\r\n文物市场可能很难监管。\r\n\r\nCollectors paid a high price for the rare antiquities.\r\n收藏家为这些稀有古物支付了高价。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✍️ 5. 学术 / 写作场景\r\n\r\nThe study examines the cultural value of ancient antiquities.\r\n这项研究考察古代文物的文化价值。\r\n\r\nAntiquities are important evidence for understanding ancient civilisations.\r\n古物是理解古代文明的重要证据。\r\n\r\nThe preservation of antiquities is a major issue in cultural heritage management.\r\n文物保护是文化遗产管理中的一个重要问题。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d6e270a650274fa684e38d2af87380b1.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-22 12:19:08',1,'2026-05-22 12:19:08'),(1326,19,29,'phrase','come across','come across','come across','come across\r\n/kʌm əˈkrɒs/ 🇬🇧\r\n/kʌm əˈkrɑːs/ 🇺🇸\r\n\r\n🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nphrasal verb 动词短语\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n偶然遇到；偶然发现；给人……印象\r\n\r\n🧠 核心理解\r\n\r\ncome across 有两个常见意思：\r\n\r\n1. find or meet something/someone by chance\r\n    偶然发现 / 偶然遇到\r\n2. give a particular impression\r\n    给人某种印象 / 显得……\r\n\r\n✅ 用法 2：给人……印象 / 显得……\r\n\r\n📌 Structure\r\n\r\ncome across as + adjective / noun\r\n\r\n📌 Meaning\r\n\r\n别人听你说话、看你行为后，对你产生某种感觉。\r\n\r\n👤 人际交流场景\r\n\r\nHe comes across as friendly and confident.\r\n他给人的感觉友好又自信。\r\n\r\nShe came across as very professional in the interview.\r\n她在面试中给人感觉非常专业。\r\n\r\nI hope I didn’t come across as rude.\r\n我希望我没有显得很没礼貌。\r\n\r\n💼 面试 / 工作场景\r\n\r\nIn the presentation, he came across as well-prepared.\r\n在展示中，他给人的感觉是准备充分。\r\n\r\nThe manager comes across as strict but fair.\r\n这位经理给人的感觉是严格但公平。\r\n\r\nYour answer comes across as honest and natural.\r\n你的回答听起来诚实又自然。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip｜记忆技巧\r\n\r\nacross 有“横穿、经过”的感觉。\r\n你可以想象：\r\n\r\n你走路时，正好“穿过”某个地方，然后碰巧看到一个东西。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncome across = 走着走着碰上了 → 偶然遇到 / 偶然发现','✅ 用法 1：偶然发现 / 偶然遇到\r\n\r\n📌 Structure\r\n\r\ncome across + something / someone\r\n\r\n📌 Meaning\r\n\r\n不是特意找，是“碰巧看到、碰巧遇到”。\r\n\r\n🌳 日常生活场景\r\n\r\nI came across an old photo when I was cleaning my room.\r\n我打扫房间时偶然发现了一张旧照片。\r\n\r\nShe came across a small café while walking around the city.\r\n她在城市里闲逛时偶然发现了一家小咖啡馆。\r\n\r\nI came across this jacket in a second-hand shop.\r\n我在二手店里偶然看到了这件夹克。\r\n\r\n📚 学习 / 阅读场景\r\n\r\nI came across this word in a book.\r\n我在书里遇到了这个单词。\r\n\r\nWhile reading the article, I came across an interesting idea.\r\n读这篇文章时，我偶然看到一个有趣的观点。\r\n\r\nI came across a useful website for learning English.\r\n我偶然发现了一个学英语的有用网站。\r\n\r\n💻 工作 / 技术场景\r\n\r\nI came across a bug while testing the system.\r\n我测试系统时发现了一个 bug。\r\n\r\nI came across this error when I deployed the application.\r\n我部署应用程序时遇到了这个错误。\r\n\r\nOur team came across a performance issue during testing.\r\n我们团队在测试过程中发现了一个性能问题。\r\n\r\n✅ 用法 3：信息表达出来 / 被理解成\r\n\r\n有时候 come across 也可以表示“信息、想法被别人理解到”。\r\n\r\nHis message didn’t come across clearly.\r\n他的意思没有表达清楚。\r\n\r\nThe main idea comes across well in your report.\r\n你的报告很好地传达了主要观点。\r\n\r\nThe emotion comes across strongly in the story.\r\n这个故事里的情感表达得很强烈。','🗣️ Natural Speaking｜自然口语表达\r\n\r\nI came across this word today. What does it mean?\r\n我今天遇到这个单词，它是什么意思？\r\n\r\nI came across a good explanation online.\r\n我在网上偶然看到一个很好的解释。\r\n\r\nYou came across really well in the interview.\r\n你在面试中给人的感觉很好。\r\n\r\nSorry, I didn’t mean to come across as rude.\r\n不好意思，我不是想显得没礼貌。\r\n\r\n记住一句：\r\n\r\nI came across this word in a book.\r\n我在书里偶然遇到了这个单词。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-22 12:27:43',1,'2026-05-22 12:27:43'),(1327,19,30,'phrase','is set to be','is set to be','is set to be','/ɪz set tə bi/\r\n\r\n🏷️ Structure\r\n\r\nbe set to + verb\r\n这里的 set 不是“放置”，而是表示：\r\n\r\n已经安排好 / 预计会 / 很可能会\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n预计将会是；被安排成为；很可能成为\r\n\r\n🧠 核心理解\r\n\r\nis set to be 常用于新闻、报告、正式写作中，表示：\r\n\r\nsomething is expected or planned to become something\r\n\r\n可以理解为：\r\n\r\n根据目前情况看，它将会变成某种状态。','✅ 常见用法 1：预计将成为……\r\n\r\n📌 Pattern\r\n\r\nsomething is set to be + noun / adjective\r\n\r\n📌 Example Sentences\r\n\r\nThe project is set to be completed next month.\r\n这个项目预计下个月完成。\r\n\r\nThe new system is set to be faster and more reliable.\r\n新系统预计会更快、更可靠。\r\n\r\nThe event is set to be the largest conference of the year.\r\n这次活动预计将成为今年最大的会议。\r\n\r\nThis technology is set to be widely used in healthcare.\r\n这项技术预计将在医疗领域被广泛使用。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ 常见用法 2：被安排为 / 定为……\r\n\r\n有时候 is set to be 不只是“预计”，也可以表示“已经安排好了”。\r\n\r\nThe meeting is set to be held on Friday.\r\n会议定于周五举行。\r\n\r\nThe interview is set to be online.\r\n面试被安排为线上进行。\r\n\r\nThe launch is set to be at 9 a.m.\r\n发布会定在早上 9 点。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ 常见用法 3：新闻 / 报告中表示“即将……”\r\n\r\n新闻里很常见：\r\n\r\nThe company is set to be acquired by a larger firm.\r\n这家公司即将被一家更大的公司收购。\r\n\r\nThe city is set to be transformed by the new transport project.\r\n这座城市将因新的交通项目而发生改变。\r\n\r\nThe policy is set to be introduced later this year.\r\n这项政策预计将在今年晚些时候推出。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ 和你的项目/实习场景相关例句\r\n\r\nThe dashboard is set to be used for monitoring operational performance.\r\n这个看板预计将用于监控运营表现。\r\n\r\nThe prototype is set to be developed within one semester.\r\n这个原型预计将在一个学期内完成。\r\n\r\nThe workflow map is set to be one of the main project outputs.\r\n工作流图预计将成为该项目的主要成果之一。\r\n\r\nThe data pipeline is set to be tested using sample production documents.\r\n这个数据管道预计将使用样本文档进行测试。','is set to be vs is expected to be\r\n\r\nis expected to be  预计会是  强调预测\r\n\r\nis set to be  预计/安排将会是 有“计划已经定下来”的感觉\r\n\r\nThe event is expected to be successful.\r\n这次活动预计会成功。\r\n👉 更偏预测。\r\n\r\nThe event is set to be held in Auckland.\r\n这次活动定于在奥克兰举行。\r\n👉 更偏安排。\r\n\r\n1. 后面可以接形容词\r\n\r\nThe weather is set to be cold tomorrow.\r\n明天天气预计会很冷。\r\n\r\n2. 后面可以接名词\r\n\r\nHe is set to be the next manager.\r\n他很可能成为下一任经理。\r\n\r\n3. 后面可以接过去分词，表示被动\r\n\r\nThe report is set to be released next week.\r\n报告预计下周发布。\r\n\r\nThe building is set to be renovated.\r\n这栋楼预计将被翻新。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/aa35fe0390d94d86bff940137c8be106.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-22 16:29:12',1,'2026-05-22 16:29:12'),(1328,19,31,'vocab','peculiar','peculiar','peculiar','peculiar /pɪˈkjuːliə/ 🇬🇧\r\npeculiar /pɪˈkjuːljər/ 🇺🇸\r\n\r\n🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nadjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n奇怪的；不寻常的；特别的；特有的\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 核心理解\r\n\r\npeculiar means something is strange, unusual, or different from what you normally expect.\r\n\r\n可以理解为：\r\n\r\n有点奇怪，但不一定是坏事。\r\n\r\n它可以形容：\r\n\r\n人：行为奇怪\r\n东西：味道、声音、气味奇怪\r\n情况：事情不寻常\r\n特征：某地、某人、某物特有的特点\r\n\r\n⚠️ Grammar Note｜语法提醒\r\n\r\n1. peculiar to + place/person/thing\r\n\r\n表示“某地 / 某人 / 某物特有的”。\r\n\r\nThis tradition is peculiar to the village.\r\n这个传统是这个村子特有的。\r\n\r\n2. something peculiar about…\r\n\r\n表示“……有点奇怪”。\r\n\r\nThere is something peculiar about his answer.\r\n他的回答有点奇怪。\r\n\r\n3. 可以放在名词前面\r\n\r\na peculiar smell\r\n一种奇怪的味道\r\n\r\na peculiar situation\r\n一种不寻常的情况','✅ Common Uses｜常见搭配\r\n\r\na peculiar smell\r\n一种奇怪的味道\r\n\r\na peculiar sound\r\n一种奇怪的声音\r\n\r\na peculiar feeling\r\n一种奇怪的感觉\r\n\r\na peculiar habit\r\n一个奇怪的习惯\r\n\r\na peculiar expression\r\n奇怪的表情\r\n\r\nsomething peculiar about someone/something\r\n某人/某物有点奇怪\r\n\r\nbe peculiar to something/somewhere\r\n是某物/某地特有的','📌 Example Sentences｜不同场景例句\r\n\r\n🏠 1. 日常生活场景\r\n\r\nThere is a peculiar smell in the kitchen.\r\n厨房里有一股奇怪的味道。\r\n\r\nI heard a peculiar noise outside the window.\r\n我听到窗外有一种奇怪的声音。\r\n\r\nThis soup tastes a bit peculiar.\r\n这个汤尝起来有点怪。\r\n\r\nHe has a peculiar way of laughing.\r\n他笑的方式有点奇怪。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n👤 2. 描述人 / 行为\r\n\r\nShe gave me a peculiar look.\r\n她用一种奇怪的眼神看着我。\r\n\r\nHe is a little peculiar, but very kind.\r\n他有点奇怪，但人很好。\r\n\r\nHis behaviour seemed peculiar today.\r\n他今天的行为看起来有点反常。\r\n\r\nIt was peculiar that he left without saying goodbye.\r\n他没说再见就走了，这有点奇怪。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n📚 3. 学习 / 阅读场景\r\n\r\nI came across a peculiar word in the article.\r\n我在文章里遇到了一个奇怪的单词。\r\n\r\nThe story has a peculiar ending.\r\n这个故事有一个很奇特的结尾。\r\n\r\nThis sentence sounds peculiar to me.\r\n这个句子对我来说听起来有点怪。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 4. 工作 / 项目场景\r\n\r\nThere is something peculiar about this data.\r\n这组数据有点不对劲。\r\n\r\nThe system showed a peculiar error after the update.\r\n系统更新后出现了一个奇怪的错误。\r\n\r\nWe noticed a peculiar pattern in customer behaviour.\r\n我们注意到客户行为中有一种不寻常的模式。\r\n\r\nThe report revealed a peculiar difference between the two groups.\r\n报告显示这两个组之间有一个不寻常的差异。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🌍 5. “特有的”用法\r\n\r\nThis custom is peculiar to this region.\r\n这个习俗是这个地区特有的。\r\n\r\nSome animals have features peculiar to their environment.\r\n有些动物有适应其环境的独特特征。\r\n\r\nThis style of architecture is peculiar to medieval Europe.\r\n这种建筑风格是中世纪欧洲特有的。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9a57c205c106473cb081438e1c070f2a.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-22 16:56:53',1,'2026-05-22 16:56:53'),(1331,19,34,'vocab','wonder','wonder','wonder','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nverb / noun\r\n动词 / 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n想知道；感到好奇；惊叹；奇迹；奇观\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 核心理解\r\n\r\nwonder 的核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n你的脑子里出现一个问题，或者你看到某个东西后觉得很惊奇。\r\n\r\n所以它有两个主要方向：\r\n\r\n1. 想知道 / 好奇\r\n2. 惊叹 / 奇迹','✅ Meaning 1｜想知道；好奇\r\n\r\n📌 Common Pattern\r\n\r\nI wonder + question word / if / whether…\r\n\r\n🌱 日常场景\r\n\r\nI wonder where he went.\r\n我想知道他去哪儿了。\r\n\r\nI wonder if it will rain tomorrow.\r\n我不知道明天会不会下雨。\r\n\r\n🎓 学习场景\r\n\r\nI wonder what this word means.\r\n我想知道这个单词是什么意思。\r\n\r\nI wonder why this sentence uses the past tense.\r\n我想知道为什么这个句子用了过去式。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ Meaning 2｜礼貌地询问\r\n\r\nI wonder if… 可以让请求听起来更委婉。\r\n\r\n💬 口语场景\r\n\r\nI wonder if you could help me.\r\n不知道你能不能帮我一下。\r\n\r\nI was wondering if I could ask you a question.\r\n我想问你一个问题，不知道方不方便。\r\n\r\n👉 I was wondering if… 比 Can you…? 更委婉。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ Meaning 3｜惊叹；奇迹；奇观\r\n\r\n📌 As a noun\r\n\r\nwonder = 奇迹；令人惊叹的东西\r\n\r\nThe Great Wall is one of the wonders of the world.\r\n长城是世界奇观之一。\r\n\r\nIt’s a wonder that no one was hurt.\r\n没人受伤真是个奇迹。','✅ Common Collocations｜常见搭配\r\n\r\nwonder if / whether：想知道是否\r\nwonder why / what / where / how：想知道为什么 / 什么 / 哪里 / 如何\r\nno wonder：难怪\r\na sense of wonder：惊奇感\r\nnatural wonder：自然奇观\r\nwork wonders：产生奇效\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n📌 Useful Examples｜实用例句\r\n\r\n1. no wonder｜难怪\r\n\r\nNo wonder you’re tired — you worked all day.\r\n难怪你累了，你工作了一整天。\r\n\r\n2. work wonders｜效果很好\r\n\r\nA good sleep can work wonders.\r\n好好睡一觉会有奇效。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔁 Comparison｜对比\r\n\r\nwonder vs want to know\r\n\r\nwonder 更自然、更柔和，带有“好奇”的感觉。\r\nwant to know 更直接，语气可能更强。\r\n\r\nI wonder where she is.\r\n我想知道她在哪里。\r\n👉 自然、柔和。\r\n\r\nI want to know where she is.\r\n我想知道她在哪里。\r\n👉 更直接，有时像在追问。\r\n\r\nwonder vs wander\r\n\r\nwonder   /ˈwʌndə/    想知道；惊叹\r\n\r\nwander    /ˈwɒndə/ /ˈwɑːndər/     闲逛；漫步\r\n\r\nI wonder why he left.\r\n我想知道他为什么走了。\r\n\r\nWe wandered around the park.\r\n我们在公园里闲逛。\r\n\r\n⚠️ Grammar Note｜语法提醒\r\n\r\nwonder 后面经常接间接疑问句，语序不要倒装。\r\n\r\n✅ I wonder where he is.\r\n我想知道他在哪里。\r\n\r\n❌ I wonder where is he.\r\n\r\n✅ I wonder what this means.\r\n我想知道这是什么意思。\r\n\r\n❌ I wonder what does this mean.','/static/uploads/english_note_item/55faa271560b43419fb993c6406916b5.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-23 16:03:58',1,'2026-05-23 16:03:58'),(1332,19,35,'phrase','cell wall','cell wall','cell wall','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nnoun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n细胞壁\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 核心理解\r\n\r\ncell wall 是细胞外面的一层比较硬的结构，主要作用是：\r\n\r\n保护细胞，并帮助细胞保持形状。\r\n\r\n可以简单理解为：\r\n\r\ncell wall = the strong outer wall of some cells\r\n某些细胞外面的“硬墙”。','✅ Common Uses｜常见搭配\r\n\r\nplant cell wall\r\n植物细胞壁\r\n\r\nbacterial cell wall\r\n细菌细胞壁\r\n\r\ncell wall structure\r\n细胞壁结构\r\n\r\ncell wall function\r\n细胞壁功能\r\n\r\ncell wall provides support\r\n细胞壁提供支撑','📌 Example Sentences｜例句\r\n\r\n🌱 生物学习场景\r\n\r\nPlant cells have a cell wall.\r\n植物细胞有细胞壁。\r\n\r\nThe cell wall helps the plant cell keep its shape.\r\n细胞壁帮助植物细胞保持形状。\r\n\r\n🦠 细菌场景\r\n\r\nMany bacteria have a cell wall.\r\n许多细菌有细胞壁。\r\n\r\nSome antibiotics work by damaging the bacterial cell wall.\r\n一些抗生素通过破坏细菌细胞壁起作用。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b8291dd55cfc41bf8edb7dca73e72af4.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-23 16:22:09',1,'2026-05-23 16:22:09'),(1333,19,36,'vocab','texture','texture','texture','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nnoun 名词\r\n也可以作 verb：给……增加质感 / 纹理\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n质地；手感；口感；纹理；肌理\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 核心理解\r\n\r\ntexture 指一个东西摸起来、看起来，或者吃起来的“感觉”。\r\n\r\n可以理解为：\r\n\r\nsurface or feeling of something\r\n某物表面的感觉 / 质感。\r\n\r\n它可以用于：\r\n\r\n* 食物的口感\r\n* 衣服或材料的手感\r\n* 皮肤、头发的质地\r\n* 图片、墙面、艺术作品的纹理','✅ Common Uses｜常见搭配\r\n\r\nsmooth texture.   光滑的质地\r\n\r\nrough texture.    粗糙的质地\r\n\r\nsoft texture.    柔软的质地\r\n\r\ncreamy texture.    顺滑浓稠的口感\r\n\r\ncrispy texture.    酥脆的口感\r\n\r\nskin texture.   皮肤质地\r\n\r\nfabric texture.    布料质感\r\n\r\nvisual texture.     视觉纹理','📌 Example Sentences｜不同场景例句\r\n\r\n🍰 1. 食物口感\r\n\r\nThis cake has a soft and fluffy texture.\r\n这个蛋糕口感柔软蓬松。\r\n\r\nThe soup has a creamy texture.\r\n这个汤有一种顺滑浓稠的口感。\r\n\r\n👕 2. 衣服 / 材料手感\r\n\r\nI like the texture of this fabric.\r\n我喜欢这种布料的手感。\r\n\r\nThe wall has a rough texture.\r\n这面墙有粗糙的纹理。\r\n\r\n🎨 3. 图片 / 艺术 / 设计\r\n\r\nThe painting has a lot of texture.\r\n这幅画很有肌理感。\r\n\r\nThis image needs more texture to look realistic.\r\n这张图片需要更多纹理才显得真实。\r\n\r\n⚠️ Grammar Note｜语法提醒\r\n\r\ntexture 作名词时，可以说：\r\n\r\nthe texture of something\r\n某物的质感 / 纹理\r\n\r\nThis bread has a dry texture.\r\n这个面包口感有点干。\r\n\r\nI don’t like the texture of mushrooms.\r\n我不喜欢蘑菇的口感。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip｜记忆技巧\r\n\r\ntexture 可以联想到 textile（纺织品 / 布料）。\r\n\r\n布料最明显的特点就是：\r\n\r\n摸起来有不同的手感和纹理。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ntexture = 质感 / 纹理 / 口感\r\n\r\n记住一句：\r\n\r\nI like the texture of this fabric.\r\n我喜欢这个布料的手感。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e086cce793ca44de976a0c025002520f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-23 16:32:08',1,'2026-05-23 16:32:08'),(1334,19,37,'phrase','outstanding','outstanding','outstanding','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nadjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n1. 优秀的；杰出的\r\n2. 未解决的；未完成的；未支付的\r\n\r\n🧠 核心理解\r\n\r\noutstanding 有两个常见意思：\r\n\r\n1. very good / excellent\r\n非常优秀的，突出表现的。\r\n\r\n2. not yet finished, solved, or paid\r\n还没有完成、解决或支付的。\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip｜记忆技巧\r\n\r\noutstanding = stand out\r\n站出来、很突出。\r\n\r\n所以它可以表示：\r\n\r\n表现突出 → 杰出的\r\n问题还站在那里没解决 → 未解决的\r\n\r\n记住一句：\r\n\r\nOutstanding can mean excellent or unresolved.\r\noutstanding 可以表示“优秀的”，也可以表示“未解决的”。','✅ Meaning 1｜优秀的；杰出的\r\n\r\n📌 常见搭配\r\n\r\noutstanding performance：杰出的表现\r\noutstanding student：优秀学生\r\noutstanding achievement：杰出成就\r\noutstanding result：优秀结果\r\n\r\n📌 Examples\r\n\r\nShe gave an outstanding presentation.\r\n她做了一场非常出色的展示。\r\n\r\nHis performance was outstanding.\r\n他的表现很优秀。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ Meaning 2｜未解决的；未完成的；未支付的\r\n\r\n📌 常见搭配\r\n\r\noutstanding issue：遗留问题 / 未解决的问题\r\noutstanding task：未完成的任务\r\noutstanding payment：未付款项\r\noutstanding balance：未结清余额\r\n\r\n📌 Examples\r\n\r\nWe still have some outstanding issues from last meeting.\r\n我们上次会议还有一些未解决的问题。\r\n\r\nPlease pay the outstanding balance by Friday.\r\n请在周五前支付未结清余额。','⚠️ Grammar Note｜语法提醒\r\n\r\n如果你说“遗留问题”，最自然是：\r\n\r\noutstanding issues\r\n未解决的问题 / 遗留问题\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nLet’s discuss the outstanding issues first.\r\n我们先讨论一下遗留问题。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c88240697c8249bc967b03e587f4a557.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-26 14:53:40',1,'2026-05-26 14:53:40'),(1335,19,38,'phrase','mission','mission','mission','🏷️ Part of Speech\r\n\r\nnoun 名词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\n任务；使命；重要目标；行动任务\r\n\r\n🧠 核心理解\r\n\r\nmission 指一个人、团队或组织要完成的重要任务或目标。\r\n\r\n可以理解为：\r\n\r\nmission = an important task or purpose','✅ Common Uses｜常见搭配\r\n\r\ncomplete a mission   完成任务\r\n\r\na rescue missiom. 救援任务\r\n\r\na space mission. 太空任务\r\n\r\ncompany mission. 公司使命\r\n\r\nmission statement 使命宣言 / 宗旨说明\r\n\r\non a mission 带着明确目标去做某事','📌 Example Sentences｜例句\r\n\r\n🚀 任务 / 行动场景\r\n\r\nThe team completed the mission successfully.\r\n团队成功完成了任务。\r\n\r\nThe astronauts prepared for their space mission.\r\n宇航员为他们的太空任务做准备。\r\n\r\n🏢 公司 / 组织场景\r\n\r\nThe company’s mission is to make technology more accessible.\r\n这家公司的使命是让科技更容易被使用。\r\n\r\nOur mission is to improve customer service.\r\n我们的目标是改善客户服务。\r\n\r\n💬 口语表达\r\n\r\nHe is on a mission to improve his English.\r\n他下定决心要提高英语。\r\n\r\nShe is on a mission to find the best coffee in town.\r\n她一心想找到城里最好喝的咖啡。\r\n\r\n⚠️ Grammar Note｜语法提醒\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\nmission to do something\r\n做某事的使命 / 任务\r\n\r\non a mission to do something\r\n一心要做某事\r\n\r\nThe mission of the project is to compare interpolation methods.\r\n这个项目的任务是比较不同插值方法。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Memory Tip｜记忆技巧\r\n\r\nmission 可以记成：\r\n\r\nimportant job with a purpose\r\n带有明确目的的重要任务。\r\n\r\n记住一句：\r\n\r\nI’m on a mission.\r\n我有一个明确目标。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/7783ca02bde548709c52bda756e9a43e.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-26 15:21:12',1,'2026-05-26 15:21:12'),(1336,19,39,'vocab','swat','swat','swat','🔤 Word\r\n\r\nswat\r\n/ swɒt / NZ/UK\r\n/ swɑːt / US\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\nv. 拍打；猛拍\r\nn. 拍打的一下\r\n\r\n常见意思是：用手、报纸、苍蝇拍等快速打一下，通常是为了赶走或打死昆虫。\r\n\r\n🧩 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象一只蚊子在你耳边飞：\r\nswat! 一下拍过去。\r\n这个词的声音本身就像“啪”的一下。','✅ 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. swat a fly\r\n\r\n拍苍蝇\r\n\r\nExample:\r\nI tried to swat a fly, but it flew away.\r\n我想拍一只苍蝇，但它飞走了。\r\n\r\n2. swat at something\r\n\r\n朝某物拍打\r\n\r\nExample:\r\nShe swatted at the mosquito on her arm.\r\n她拍打胳膊上的蚊子。\r\n\r\n3. swat something away\r\n\r\n把某物拍开 / 挥开\r\n\r\nExample:\r\nHe swatted the bee away.\r\n他把蜜蜂挥开了。','🗣️ 口语小句\r\n\r\nI need to swat this mosquito.\r\n我得把这只蚊子拍掉。\r\n\r\nDon’t swat at the bee. Just move away slowly.\r\n别拍那只蜜蜂，慢慢走开就好。','','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-28 07:10:57',1,'2026-05-28 07:10:57'),(1337,19,40,'vocab','comprehensively','comprehensively','comprehensively','/ˌkɒm.prɪˈhen.sɪv.li/ NZ/UK\r\n/ˌkɑːm.prəˈhen.sɪv.li/ US\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思\r\n\r\nadv. 全面地；彻底地；综合地\r\n\r\n来自形容词：\r\n\r\ncomprehensive = 全面的；综合的\r\ncomprehensively = 以全面的方式\r\n\r\n🧩 记忆方法\r\n\r\ncomprehensive = complete + detailed\r\n全面的 + 详细的\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncomprehensively = in a complete and detailed way\r\n以完整、详细、全面的方式','✅ 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. consider something comprehensively\r\n\r\n全面地考虑某事\r\n\r\nDifferent perspectives can help us consider an issue more comprehensively.\r\n不同的观点可以帮助我们更全面地考虑一个问题。\r\n\r\n2. understand something comprehensively\r\n\r\n全面地理解某事\r\n\r\nWe need to understand the problem comprehensively before making a decision.\r\n在做决定之前，我们需要全面地理解这个问题。\r\n\r\n3. analyse something comprehensively\r\n\r\n全面地分析某事\r\n\r\nThe report analyses the data comprehensively.\r\n这份报告全面地分析了数据。','🔁 相近表达\r\n\r\ncomprehensively 比较正式，适合写作、报告、presentation。\r\n\r\n口语里也可以说：\r\n\r\nfully\r\n完全地 / 全面地\r\n\r\nfrom different angles\r\n从不同角度\r\n\r\nin a more complete way\r\n以更完整的方式\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nDifferent opinions help us look at the issue from different angles.\r\n不同意见帮助我们从不同角度看问题。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/032920d3604447269b0d347b84d608c3.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-05-28 07:54:13',1,'2026-05-28 07:54:13'),(1338,19,41,'vocab','compatibility','compatibility','compatibility','Pronunciation: /kəmˌpætəˈbɪləti/\r\nPart of speech: noun（名词）\r\n中文意思： 兼容性；相容性；匹配程度；合得来\r\n\r\n拆词记忆：\r\n\r\ncom-（一起）\r\n\r\n* pat（适合）\r\n* -ibility（能力）\r\n\r\n→ 一起适合的能力\r\n→ 兼容性、相容性\r\n\r\n记一句：\r\n\r\nIf two things can work together smoothly, they have compatibility.\r\n如果两样东西能顺利一起工作，它们就有兼容性。','🎯 Core Meaning\r\n\r\ncompatibility = the ability of two or more things to work well together or exist together successfully\r\n\r\n表示：\r\n\r\n① （设备/软件）兼容\r\n② （人与人）合得来、性格匹配\r\n③ （想法/制度）相容、一致\r\n\r\n👉 核心感觉：\r\n\r\n“能一起正常运作，不冲突”\r\n\r\n❤️ Scenario 2 — Relationships（人与人合得来）\r\n\r\n表示人与人的匹配程度。\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\n* They have excellent compatibility as a couple.\r\n    他们作为情侣很合拍。\r\n* Personality compatibility matters in a relationship.\r\n    性格契合在关系里很重要。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n📚 Scenario 3 — Ideas / Systems（制度、想法兼容）\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\n* We need to ensure compatibility between the old and new systems.\r\n    我们需要确保新旧系统兼容。\r\n* There is little compatibility between these policies.\r\n    这些政策之间相容性不高。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 Word Family\r\n\r\n* compatible (adj.) → 兼容的；合得来的\r\n* incompatibility (n.) → 不兼容\r\n* incompatible (adj.) → 不兼容的\r\n\r\n例：\r\n\r\n* This charger is compatible with your phone.\r\n    这个充电器适用于你的手机。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚖️ Compare\r\n\r\ncompatibility vs compatibility with\r\n\r\n* compatibility → 兼容性（概念）\r\n* compatibility with → 与……兼容\r\n\r\n例：\r\n\r\n✅ compatibility with macOS\r\n与 macOS 的兼容性\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🌱 Common Collocations\r\n\r\n* compatibility issue → 兼容问题\r\n* check compatibility → 检查兼容性\r\n* software compatibility → 软件兼容\r\n* backward compatibility → 向后兼容\r\n* relationship compatibility → 关系契合度\r\n* cross-platform compatibility → 跨平台兼容','💻 Scenario 1 — Technology（技术兼容）\r\n\r\n通常表示：\r\n\r\nsoftware / hardware compatibility\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\n* Please check the compatibility before installing the software.\r\n    安装软件前请检查兼容性。\r\n* This app has good compatibility with Mac computers.\r\n    这个应用和 Mac 电脑兼容性很好。\r\n* The game supports cross-platform compatibility.\r\n    这个游戏支持跨平台兼容。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3e83045b69d94d06931f053535769d99.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-02 09:33:36',1,'2026-06-02 09:33:36'),(1339,19,42,'phrase','Progress well','Progress well','Progress well','Phrase: progress well\r\nPronunciation: /prəˈɡres wel/\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 中文意思：\r\n进展顺利；发展得不错；推进良好\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🎯 Core Meaning\r\n\r\nprogress (v.) = 取得进展、向前推进\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nprogress well\r\n\r\n进展得好\r\n推进顺利\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意：\r\n\r\n这个表达通常直接把 progress 当动词用。\r\n\r\n📚 Grammar（常见结构）\r\n\r\n✅ Things + progress well\r\n\r\n* The project is progressing well.\r\n    项目正在顺利推进。\r\n* Our work progressed well.\r\n    我们的工作进展顺利。\r\n* Recovery has progressed well.\r\n    恢复情况很好。','💻 Scenario 1 — Project\r\n\r\n* The software upgrade progressed well.\r\n    软件升级进行顺利。\r\n* The migration project is progressing well.\r\n    迁移项目正在顺利推进。\r\n\r\n（这个和你之前做系统迁移场景特别像。）\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🎓 Scenario 2 — Learning\r\n\r\n* My English has progressed well recently.\r\n    我最近英语进步不错。\r\n* Her studies are progressing well.\r\n    她的学习进展顺利。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🏥 Scenario 3 — Health\r\n\r\n* The treatment progressed well.\r\n    治疗进展顺利。\r\n* His recovery is progressing well.\r\n    他的恢复情况不错。','🧠 Memory Tip\r\n\r\n🚶 progress = 往前走\r\n\r\nprogress well\r\n→ 走得很顺\r\n\r\n一句记住：\r\n\r\nEverything is progressing well.\r\n一切都进展顺利。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d9292a527e2d4690905764b782c4f731.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-02 09:41:37',1,'2026-06-02 09:41:37'),(1340,19,43,'phrase','be calling from','be calling from','be calling from','be calling from = “从……打电话来 / 我现在在……给你打电话”\r\n\r\n常用于电话里说明 你在哪里打电话，或者 代表哪个地方/公司打电话。\r\n\r\n2. 结构\r\n\r\nI’m calling from + 地点 / 公司 / 部门\r\n\r\n中文意思：\r\n\r\n我从……打电话来。','3. 常见场景\r\n\r\n📞 场景 1：说明自己所在地点\r\n\r\nI’m calling from New Zealand.\r\n我现在从新西兰打电话来。\r\n\r\nI’m calling from Christchurch.\r\n我从基督城打电话来。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🏢 场景 2：说明自己来自某个公司或机构\r\n\r\nI’m calling from Skinny.\r\n我是 Skinny 打来的。\r\n\r\nI’m calling from the bank.\r\n我是银行这边打来的。\r\n\r\nI’m calling from Student Job Search.\r\n我是 Student Job Search 打来的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧑‍💼 场景 3：客服 / 工作电话\r\n\r\nHi, I’m calling from customer service.\r\n你好，我是客服部打来的。\r\n\r\nI’m calling from the admissions office.\r\n我是招生办公室打来的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n4. 和 call from 的区别\r\n\r\ncall from 是普通动词短语：\r\n\r\nCan I call from your phone?\r\n我可以用你的电话打吗？\r\n\r\nbe calling from 更常用于电话正在进行中：\r\n\r\nI’m calling from Auckland.\r\n我现在从奥克兰打电话来。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n5. 电话里很实用的句子\r\n\r\nWhere are you calling from?\r\n你是从哪里打来的？\r\n\r\nAre you calling from New Zealand?\r\n你是从新西兰打来的吗？\r\n\r\nI’m calling from my mobile.\r\n我是用手机打的。\r\n\r\nI’m calling from overseas.\r\n我是从海外打来的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n6. Skinny 漫游场景可以这样说\r\n\r\nHi, I’m calling from overseas. I’d like to check my roaming charges.\r\n你好，我现在从海外打电话来。我想查一下我的漫游扣费。\r\n\r\nI’m calling from Japan, and I want to check why my credit was deducted.\r\n我现在从日本打电话来，我想查一下为什么我的余额被扣了。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/46dc4f2c2c8e4270b86df88986f71dc6.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-04 09:12:19',1,'2026-06-04 09:12:19'),(1341,19,44,'phrase','end up doing','end up doing','end up doing','end up doing something = 最后做了某事 / 结果做了某事\r\n它强调：\r\n一开始可能没有计划这样做，但最后结果变成这样。','3. 常见用法\r\n\r\n✅ 场景 1：最后做了某事\r\n\r\nI ended up staying at home.\r\n我最后还是待在家里了。\r\n\r\nWe ended up eating noodles for dinner.\r\n我们最后晚饭吃了面条。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ 场景 2：原本没计划，但结果发生了\r\n\r\nI planned to study, but I ended up watching TV.\r\n我本来打算学习，但结果看电视了。\r\n\r\nShe wanted to buy one thing, but she ended up spending $200.\r\n她本来只想买一样东西，结果花了 200 刀。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ 场景 3：工作 / 面试 / 兼职\r\n\r\nDid you end up working for them?\r\n你最后有没有给他们工作？\r\n\r\nNo, I didn’t end up working for them.\r\n没有，我最后没有给他们工作。\r\n\r\nYes, I ended up working there for two days.\r\n是的，我最后在那里干了两天。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n4. 和 finally 的区别\r\n\r\nfinally = 最后，强调时间顺序\r\nend up doing = 结果，强调事情的发展结果\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\nI finally found a job.\r\n我终于找到工作了。\r\n\r\nI ended up working in a supermarket.\r\n结果我在一家超市工作了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n5. 很自然的口语句子\r\n\r\nI ended up going home early.\r\n我最后提前回家了。\r\n\r\nWe ended up not going.\r\n我们最后没去。\r\n\r\nHe ended up paying for everyone.\r\n结果他给所有人买单了。\r\n\r\nI didn’t end up using it.\r\n我最后没用它。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3f94bc983a2a48919b6afbaf69d2d05f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-04 09:35:33',1,'2026-06-04 09:35:33'),(1342,19,45,'phrase','at all','at all','at all','1. 核心意思\r\n\r\nat all = 到底 / 究竟 / 任何一点 / 完全\r\n\r\n它的意思会根据句子类型变化：\r\n\r\n疑问句里：到底有没有 / 任何一点\r\n否定句里：完全不 / 一点也不\r\n条件句里：如果有任何……\r\n\r\n2. 疑问句里：到底有没有？\r\n\r\nat all 放在疑问句里，表示你想确认“有没有任何一点”。\r\n\r\nDid you work for them at all?\r\n你到底有没有给他们工作过？ / 有没有哪怕工作过一次？\r\n\r\nDid they contact you at all?\r\n他们有没有联系过你？哪怕一次？\r\n\r\nDid you use your phone at all while roaming?\r\n你漫游时有没有用过手机？哪怕一点点？\r\n\r\n📌 语气比普通问题更强调“我想确认有没有”。\r\n\r\n3. 否定句里：完全不 / 一点也不\r\n\r\nI didn’t work for them at all.\r\n我完全没有给他们工作过。\r\n\r\nI don’t understand it at all.\r\n我一点也不明白。\r\n\r\nThe roaming charge doesn’t make sense at all.\r\n这个漫游扣费完全说不通。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n4. 和普通句子的区别\r\n\r\nDid you work for them?\r\n你有没有给他们工作？\r\n\r\nDid you work for them at all?\r\n你到底有没有给他们工作过？哪怕一次？\r\n\r\nI didn’t use data.\r\n我没用流量。\r\n\r\nI didn’t use data at all.\r\n我完全没用流量。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n5. 常见口语句子\r\n\r\nNot at all.\r\n一点也不。/ 没关系。/ 不客气。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThank you so much.\r\n太谢谢你了。\r\n\r\nNot at all.\r\n不客气。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nNo problem at all.\r\n完全没问题。\r\n\r\nIt’s not expensive at all.\r\n它一点也不贵。\r\n\r\nI’m not sure at all.\r\n我完全不确定。','6. 记忆技巧 🧠\r\n\r\n把 at all 记成：\r\n\r\n任何一点点\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nDid you call them at all?\r\n你有没有打过电话给他们？哪怕一次？\r\n\r\nI didn’t call them at all.\r\n我完全没给他们打过电话。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2b83f4970e614a02851242fa943952e8.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-04 09:42:19',1,'2026-06-04 09:42:19'),(1343,19,46,'phrase','hear back','hear back','hear back','核心意思\r\n\r\nhear back = 收到回复 / 得到回音\r\n\r\n通常指你联系了别人、申请了工作、发了邮件之后，等待对方回复你。','基本结构\r\n\r\nhear back from + 人 / 公司 / 机构\r\n\r\n中文意思：\r\n\r\n收到……的回复\r\n\r\n✅ I heard back from them.\r\n我收到他们的回复了。\r\n\r\n✅ I haven’t heard back from Skinny yet.\r\n我还没收到 Skinny 的回复。\r\n\r\n✅ Have you heard back from the company?\r\n你收到那家公司的回复了吗？','常见场景\r\n\r\n📧 场景 1：等邮件 / 消息回复\r\n\r\nI emailed them yesterday, but I haven’t heard back yet.\r\n我昨天给他们发了邮件，但还没收到回复。\r\n\r\nLet me know when you hear back from them.\r\n你收到他们回复后告诉我。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 场景 2：工作申请 / 面试\r\n\r\nI applied for the job, but I haven’t heard back.\r\n我申请了那份工作，但还没收到回复。\r\n\r\nDid you hear back after the interview?\r\n你面试后收到回复了吗？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n☎️ 场景 3：客服 / 投诉 / 查询\r\n\r\nI contacted Skinny about my roaming charges, but I haven’t heard back yet.\r\n我联系了 Skinny 查询漫游扣费，但还没收到回复。\r\n\r\nI’m still waiting to hear back from customer service.\r\n我还在等客服回复。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n4. 和 reply 的区别\r\n\r\nreply = 回复这个动作\r\nhear back = 收到对方的回复，更强调“我这边等到了回音”\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\nThey replied to my email.\r\n他们回复了我的邮件。\r\n\r\nI heard back from them.\r\n我收到他们的回复了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n5. 很自然的口语句子\r\n\r\nI’ll wait to hear back from them.\r\n我会等他们回复。\r\n\r\nI still haven’t heard back.\r\n我还是没收到回复。\r\n\r\nHopefully, I’ll hear back soon.\r\n希望我很快能收到回复。\r\n\r\nHave you heard back from Student Job Search?\r\n你收到 Student Job Search 的回复了吗？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n6. 记忆技巧 🧠\r\n\r\nhear back 可以记成：\r\n\r\nhear = 听到\r\nback = 回来\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nhear back = 听到回来的消息 = 收到回复\r\n\r\n常用搭配：\r\n\r\nhear back from someone\r\n收到某人的回复。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8b25c28be2d24064938ddb157479a825.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-04 09:47:07',1,'2026-06-04 09:47:07'),(1344,19,47,'vocab','archive','archive','archive','1. 核心意思\r\n\r\narchive 可以作 名词，也可以作 动词。\r\n\r\narchive = 档案 / 归档 / 存档\r\n\r\n常见意思是：把旧的信息、邮件、文件保存起来，不删除，但从当前页面或收件箱里移走。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 词性和发音\r\n\r\narchive\r\n/ˈɑːr.kaɪv/\r\n\r\nnoun 名词：档案，档案库\r\nverb 动词：归档，存档','📧 场景 1：邮件里\r\n\r\nArchive this email.\r\n把这封邮件归档。\r\n\r\nI archived the message by mistake.\r\n我不小心把这条消息归档了。\r\n\r\nArchived emails are not deleted.\r\n归档的邮件没有被删除。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💻 场景 2：文件 / 数据\r\n\r\nWe need to archive old records.\r\n我们需要把旧记录存档。\r\n\r\nThe system archives inactive users automatically.\r\n系统会自动归档不活跃用户。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🏛️ 场景 3：档案库\r\n\r\nThe documents are stored in the archive.\r\n这些文件保存在档案库里。\r\n\r\nYou can search the archive for old reports.\r\n你可以在档案库里搜索旧报告。','4. 和 delete 的区别\r\n\r\narchive = 归档，不删除，还能找回来\r\ndelete = 删除，可能进垃圾箱或被永久删除\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\nI archived the email.\r\n我把邮件归档了。\r\n意思是：它不在 inbox 里了，但还在邮箱里。\r\n\r\nI deleted the email.\r\n我把邮件删除了。\r\n意思是：它被移到 trash 或删除了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n5. 很自然的口语句子\r\n\r\nWhere can I find archived emails?\r\n我在哪里能找到归档邮件？\r\n\r\nI think I archived it accidentally.\r\n我觉得我不小心把它归档了。\r\n\r\nDon’t delete it. Just archive it.\r\n别删它，归档就行。\r\n\r\nThis project has been archived.\r\n这个项目已经被归档了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n6. 记忆技巧 🧠\r\n\r\n把 archive 记成：\r\n\r\nold but useful information\r\n\r\n也就是：\r\n\r\n旧的，但以后可能还要用，所以保存起来。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\narchive = save it, hide it from the active list, but don’t delete it\r\n归档 = 保存起来，从当前列表隐藏，但不删除。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3ce7a8daf99244bc893caa7ffd1062b6.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-04 10:39:18',1,'2026-06-04 10:39:18'),(1345,19,48,'vocab','manufacture','manufacture','manufacture','verb 动词：制造，生产\r\nnoun 名词：制造，生产；制造业\r\n\r\n核心意思\r\n\r\nmanufacture = 制造 / 生产\r\n\r\n通常指在工厂里大规模生产产品，尤其是机器、电子设备、零件、药品、衣服等。','🏭 场景 1：工厂生产产品\r\n\r\nThe company manufactures wildlife tracking devices.\r\n这家公司制造野生动物追踪设备。\r\n\r\nThese sensors are manufactured in New Zealand.\r\n这些传感器是在新西兰制造的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 场景 2：制造业 / 生产流程\r\n\r\nThe project focuses on manufacturing operations.\r\n这个项目关注制造业运营流程。\r\n\r\nPaper-based documents are still common in manufacturing.\r\n纸质文件在制造业中仍然很常见。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n📊 场景 3：数据和流程改进\r\n\r\nThe system helps improve manufacturing efficiency.\r\n这个系统帮助提高制造效率。\r\n\r\nWe can use data to monitor the manufacturing process.\r\n我们可以用数据监控制造过程。','4. 常见搭配\r\n\r\nmanufacture products\r\n制造产品\r\n\r\nmanufacturing process\r\n制造流程\r\n\r\nmanufacturing operations\r\n制造运营\r\n\r\nmanufacturing company\r\n制造公司\r\n\r\nadvanced manufacturing\r\n先进制造\r\n\r\nmanufacturing data\r\n制造数据\r\n\r\nmanufacturing efficiency\r\n制造效率\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n5. 和 make / produce 的区别\r\n\r\nmake\r\n最普通，生活中做任何东西都可以用。\r\n\r\nI made dinner.\r\n我做了晚饭。\r\n\r\nproduce\r\n强调生产、产出，可以用于农产品、电影、报告、产品等。\r\n\r\nNew Zealand produces a lot of dairy products.\r\n新西兰生产很多乳制品。\r\n\r\nmanufacture\r\n更正式，通常指工厂或工业化制造。\r\n\r\nThe company manufactures electronic devices.\r\n这家公司制造电子设备。\r\n\r\nI understand that Lotek NZ is involved in advanced manufacturing and data-driven wildlife tracking technologies.\r\n我了解到 Lotek NZ 从事先进制造和数据驱动的野生动物追踪技术。\r\n\r\nThis project aims to improve visibility in manufacturing operations by converting paper-based documents into structured digital data.\r\n这个项目旨在通过把纸质文件转换成结构化数字数据，提升制造运营的可见性。\r\n\r\nMy software engineering background can help me understand data pipelines in a manufacturing environment.\r\n我的软件工程背景可以帮助我理解制造环境中的数据管道。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d65289080b3943ae881433cc3ed78f26.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-07 20:40:27',1,'2026-06-07 20:40:27'),(1346,19,49,'vocab','Feasible','Feasible','Feasible','核心意思\r\n\r\nfeasible = 可行的 / 做得到的 / 现实可行的\r\n\r\n通常用来表示一个计划、项目、方法在现实条件下可以完成。\r\n\r\n2. 发音 + 词性\r\n\r\nfeasible\r\n/ˈfiː.zə.bəl/\r\n\r\nadjective 形容词：可行的，行得通的','3. 常见用法\r\n\r\n✅ 场景 1：项目是否可行\r\n\r\nThis project is feasible within one semester.\r\n这个项目在一个学期内是可行的。\r\n\r\nWe need to keep the scope small to make it feasible.\r\n我们需要把范围控制小一点，让它变得可行。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ 场景 2：技术方案是否能实现\r\n\r\nOCR for handwritten documents may not always be feasible.\r\n对手写文件做 OCR 不一定总是可行。\r\n\r\nA simple dashboard is feasible for the proof of concept.\r\n做一个简单的数据看板作为概念验证是可行的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ 场景 3：面试 / 项目讨论\r\n\r\nI would focus on one workflow segment to ensure the project is feasible.\r\n我会专注于一个工作流程片段，以确保项目可行。\r\n\r\nFull ERP integration may not be feasible within the project timeframe.\r\n在项目时间范围内，完整的 ERP 集成可能不太可行。','4. 常见搭配\r\n\r\nfeasible solution\r\n可行的解决方案\r\n\r\nfeasible approach\r\n可行的方法\r\n\r\ntechnically feasible\r\n技术上可行\r\n\r\ncommercially feasible\r\n商业上可行\r\n\r\nfinancially feasible\r\n经济上可行\r\n\r\nwithin the timeframe\r\n在时间范围内可行\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n5. 和 possible 的区别\r\n\r\npossible = 可能的\r\n强调“有没有可能发生”。\r\n\r\nfeasible = 可行的\r\n强调“现实条件下能不能做成”。\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\nIt is possible to build a full system.\r\n做一个完整系统是有可能的。\r\n\r\nBut it may not be feasible within one semester.\r\n但在一个学期内可能不现实。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n6. 面试中可以用的句子\r\n\r\nTo make the project feasible, I would focus on one document workflow first.\r\n为了让项目可行，我会先专注于一个文件流程。\r\n\r\nA human-in-the-loop approach may be more feasible for handwritten fields.\r\n对于手写字段，人工参与审核的方法可能更可行。\r\n\r\nI think a proof-of-concept system is feasible if we keep the scope realistic.\r\n如果我们把范围控制得现实一些，我认为做一个概念验证系统是可行的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n7. 记忆技巧 🧠\r\n\r\nfeasible 可以记成：\r\n\r\ncan be done in the real world\r\n\r\n也就是：\r\n\r\n不是只停留在想法上，而是在现实条件下能做成。\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nFeasible means possible and practical.\r\nfeasible 的意思是：既可能，又实际可行。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/214acf8d36864ec7b24e7fd17cb440d9.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-07 21:02:26',1,'2026-06-07 21:02:26'),(1347,19,50,'vocab','analytics','analytics','analytics','核心意思\r\n\r\nanalytics = 数据分析 / 分析工具 / 分析结果\r\n\r\n它通常指用数据来发现规律、趋势、问题，并帮助做决定。\r\n\r\n在你的项目里：\r\n\r\nGroup Analytics\r\n= 小组数据分析页面\r\n\r\nSuper Admin Analytics\r\n= 超级管理员数据分析页面\r\n\r\nanalytics\r\n/ˌæn.əˈlɪt.ɪks/\r\n\r\nnoun 名词：数据分析，分析学，分析功能\r\n\r\n注意：\r\nanalytics 通常看起来像复数，但经常当作一个整体概念使用。','📊 场景 1：网站 / 系统里的数据分析\r\n\r\nThe analytics page shows catch trends and line performance.\r\n这个数据分析页面显示捕获趋势和路线表现。\r\n\r\nWe added analytics to help users understand their data.\r\n我们添加了数据分析功能，帮助用户理解数据。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 场景 2：商业 / 运营分析\r\n\r\nBusiness analytics helps companies make better decisions.\r\n商业数据分析帮助公司做出更好的决策。\r\n\r\nThe dashboard provides operational analytics.\r\n这个看板提供运营数据分析。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧑‍💻 场景 3：项目 / 面试\r\n\r\nThis project uses analytics to improve manufacturing visibility.\r\n这个项目使用数据分析来提高制造流程的可见性。\r\n\r\nAnalytics can turn raw data into useful insights.\r\n数据分析可以把原始数据变成有用的洞察。','4. 常见搭配\r\n\r\ndata analytics\r\n数据分析\r\n\r\nbusiness analytics\r\n商业分析\r\n\r\nweb analytics\r\n网站数据分析\r\n\r\ngroup analytics\r\n小组数据分析\r\n\r\nplatform analytics\r\n平台数据分析\r\n\r\nanalytics dashboard\r\n数据分析看板\r\n\r\nanalytics report\r\n数据分析报告\r\n\r\nadvanced analytics\r\n高级数据分析\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n5. 和 analysis 的区别\r\n\r\nanalysis = 分析这个动作或分析结果，范围很广。\r\nanalytics = 更偏“用数据和工具做系统化分析”。\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\nI did an analysis of the problem.\r\n我对这个问题做了分析。\r\n\r\nThe system provides analytics for managers.\r\n这个系统为管理者提供数据分析功能。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n6. 口语里适合吗？\r\n\r\nanalytics 适合工作、学习、项目和技术场景。\r\n日常聊天中不太常用。\r\n\r\n比如面试中很自然：\r\n\r\nI’m interested in data analytics and dashboard development.\r\n我对数据分析和看板开发感兴趣。\r\n\r\nThis feature provides useful analytics for decision-making.\r\n这个功能为决策提供有用的数据分析。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n7. 记忆技巧 🧠\r\n\r\nanalytics = data + insights\r\n\r\n也就是：\r\n\r\n把数据变成有用的信息和决策依据。\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nAnalytics helps people understand data and make better decisions.\r\n数据分析帮助人们理解数据并做出更好的决策。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/642796ab12ad4c0b93a90e5f59b3db81.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-07 21:16:06',1,'2026-06-07 21:16:06'),(1348,19,51,'phrase','on-premise / on-premises','on-premise / on-premises','on-premise / on-premises','premise 有两个常见意思：\r\n\r\nA. 前提 / 假设\r\n\r\n用于逻辑、讨论、 argument 里，表示一个观点建立在什么基础上。\r\n\r\npremise = a basic idea or assumption that an argument is based on\r\n前提；假设；基础观点\r\n\r\nB. premises 经营场所 / 房屋 / 场地\r\n\r\n通常用复数 premises，表示公司、商店、学校等所在的建筑或场地。\r\n\r\npremises = the land and buildings owned or used by a company or organisation\r\n场地；经营场所；公司/机构所在地\r\n\r\non-premise 中premise对应的含义是场所的意义。\r\n\r\non-premise / on-premises = 本地部署的 / 部署在公司内部服务器上的\r\n\r\n在 IT 里，它表示系统、软件、数据库或 ERP 不是放在云端，而是运行在公司自己的服务器、机房或内部网络里。\r\n\r\n更标准的写法是：\r\n\r\non-premises\r\n\r\n但口语和很多公司文档里也常写：\r\n\r\non-premise\r\n\r\nadjective 形容词：本地部署的，内部部署的\r\nadverb 副词：在本地，在公司内部','🖥️ 场景 1：公司内部系统\r\n\r\nThe ERP system is on-premises.\r\n这个 ERP 系统是本地部署的。\r\n\r\nDynamics NAV is hosted on-premises.\r\nDynamics NAV 部署在公司内部服务器上。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n☁️ 场景 2：和云服务对比\r\n\r\nThe company does not use a cloud-based ERP system. It uses an on-premises system.\r\n这家公司不用云端 ERP，而是使用本地部署系统。\r\n\r\nOn-premises systems may have stricter access controls.\r\n本地部署系统可能有更严格的访问控制。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔐 场景 3：安全和权限限制\r\n\r\nBecause the ERP is on-premises, direct integration may be limited.\r\n因为 ERP 是本地部署的，直接集成可能会受限制。\r\n\r\nWe may need to work with sample exports instead of direct database access.\r\n我们可能需要使用样本导出数据，而不是直接访问数据库。','4. 常见搭配\r\n\r\non-premises system\r\n本地部署系统\r\n\r\non-premises ERP\r\n本地部署的 ERP\r\n\r\non-premises database\r\n本地数据库\r\n\r\non-premises server\r\n本地服务器\r\n\r\non-premises deployment\r\n本地部署\r\n\r\ncloud-based system\r\n云端系统\r\n\r\nERP integration\r\nERP 集成\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n5. 和 cloud-based 的区别\r\n\r\non-premises = 系统在公司自己的服务器上\r\ncloud-based = 系统在云端，比如 Azure、AWS、Google Cloud\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\nThe ERP is on-premises.\r\nERP 是本地部署的。\r\n意思是：数据和系统主要在公司内部服务器或内部网络里。\r\n\r\nThe dashboard is cloud-based.\r\n这个看板是云端的。\r\n意思是：它运行在云服务上，可以通过互联网访问。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n6. 面试中可以用的句子\r\n\r\nSince the ERP system is on-premises, I would not assume direct access to the database.\r\n因为 ERP 系统是本地部署的，我不会默认可以直接访问数据库。\r\n\r\nA feasible approach would be to use sample exports, such as CSV files, for the proof of concept.\r\n一个可行的方法是使用样本导出数据，比如 CSV 文件，来做概念验证。\r\n\r\nFor security reasons, full integration with the on-premises ERP may be considered as a future step.\r\n出于安全原因，与本地部署 ERP 的完整集成可以作为未来步骤。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n7. 记忆技巧 🧠\r\n\r\npremises = 场地 / 公司所在地\r\non-premises = 在公司自己的场地里\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nOn-premises means the system runs on the company’s own servers, not in the cloud.\r\non-premises 的意思是系统运行在公司自己的服务器上，而不是云端。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d5644b81bf6948878a720a444dc502d4.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-07 21:33:16',1,'2026-06-07 21:33:16'),(1349,19,52,'phrase','on the spot','on the spot','on the spot','1. 核心意思\r\n\r\non the spot = 当场 / 现场 / 立即\r\n\r\n它常用来表示：事情就在那个地方、那个时刻发生，不是之后再处理。','✅ 场景 1：当场做某事\r\n\r\nThe manager made a decision on the spot.\r\n经理当场做了决定。\r\n\r\nThey offered me the job on the spot.\r\n他们当场给了我这份工作。\r\n\r\nI had to answer the question on the spot.\r\n我不得不当场回答这个问题。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ 场景 2：现场指导 / 现场帮助\r\n\r\nThe supervisor gave me some guidance on the spot.\r\n主管当场给了我一些指导。\r\n\r\nIf I make a mistake, they can correct me on the spot.\r\n如果我犯错了，他们可以现场纠正我。\r\n\r\nIt would be helpful to have some on-the-spot guidance.\r\n如果能有一些现场指导，会很有帮助。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ 场景 3：让某人有压力，被迫马上回答\r\n\r\nDon’t put me on the spot.\r\n别让我当场为难。/ 别突然让我回答。\r\n\r\nThe interviewer put me on the spot with a difficult question.\r\n面试官用一个难题让我当场有点尴尬。\r\n\r\n这个用法很常见：\r\nput someone on the spot = 让某人当场难堪 / 让某人被迫马上回答','4. 常见搭配\r\n\r\ndecide on the spot\r\n当场决定\r\n\r\nanswer on the spot\r\n当场回答\r\n\r\nhire someone on the spot\r\n当场雇用某人\r\n\r\ngive guidance on the spot\r\n现场给指导\r\n\r\ncorrect someone on the spot\r\n当场纠正某人\r\n\r\nput someone on the spot\r\n让某人当场为难\r\n\r\non-the-spot guidance\r\n现场指导\r\n\r\non-the-spot decision\r\n当场决定\r\n\r\n6. 和 immediately / at the scene 的区别\r\n\r\non the spot\r\n强调 当场、现场、马上处理。\r\n\r\nimmediately\r\n只强调 马上，不一定在现场。\r\n\r\nat the scene\r\n强调 在现场，常用于事故、新闻、警察场景。\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\nThey fixed the issue on the spot.\r\n他们当场把问题解决了。\r\n\r\nThey fixed the issue immediately.\r\n他们马上解决了问题。\r\n\r\nPolice arrived at the scene.\r\n警察到达现场。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n7. 记忆技巧 🧠\r\n\r\nspot = 一个具体地点 / 点\r\non the spot = 就在那个点上\r\n\r\n所以可以记成：\r\n\r\nright there, right away\r\n就在现场，马上处理。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e5a85869e335446bb5843abb59215b27.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-09 14:37:41',1,'2026-06-09 14:37:41'),(1350,19,53,'phrase','you know the drill','you know the drill','you know the drill','核心意思\r\n\r\nyou know the drill = 你知道流程 / 老规矩 / 你懂该怎么做\r\n\r\n它通常用于大家已经熟悉某个流程，不需要重新详细解释。\r\n发音 + 词性\r\n\r\nyou know the drill\r\n/juː nəʊ ðə drɪl/\r\n\r\nidiom 习语\r\n\r\n这里的 drill 不是“钻头”，而是：\r\n\r\n固定流程 / 训练步骤 / 常规操作','记忆技巧 🧠\r\n\r\ndrill 可以理解成“反复练习的流程”。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nyou know the drill\r\n= 你已经练过很多次了，流程你知道。\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nYou know the drill = 老规矩，你懂的。\r\n\r\n常见场景\r\n\r\n✅ 会议里\r\n\r\nLet’s start with introductions. You know the drill.\r\n我们先做自我介绍。老规矩，你们知道流程。\r\n\r\n✅ 工作中\r\n\r\nPlease update the report before Friday. You know the drill.\r\n请周五前更新报告。老规矩，你知道怎么做。\r\n\r\n✅ 老师对学生\r\n\r\nSubmit your assignment online. You know the drill.\r\n在线提交作业。流程你们都知道。\r\n\r\n✅ 日常生活\r\n\r\nShoes off at the door — you know the drill.\r\n进门脱鞋，老规矩。\r\n\r\n语气感觉\r\n\r\n这个表达比较 口语、轻松、自然。\r\n\r\n它通常表示：\r\n\r\nI don’t need to explain it again.\r\n我不用再解释一遍了。\r\n\r\n但不是很严厉，更多是熟人之间、团队之间的自然说法。','相关表达\r\n\r\nYou know what to do.\r\n你知道该怎么做。\r\n\r\nSame as usual.\r\n和往常一样。\r\n\r\nAs usual.\r\n照常。\r\n\r\nThe usual routine.\r\n常规流程。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d95ab2f666d1458791def53c1befc0e7.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-09 18:02:35',1,'2026-06-09 18:02:35'),(1351,19,54,'sentence','I will go with a quick round of introductions','I will go with a quick round of introductions','I will go with a quick round of introductions','核心意思\r\n\r\nI will go with a quick round of introductions.\r\n= 我会先安排大家快速做一轮自我介绍。\r\n\r\n更自然一点也可以说：\r\n\r\nLet’s start with a quick round of introductions.\r\n我们先快速做一轮自我介绍吧。','重点表达：a quick round of introductions\r\n\r\na round of introductions\r\n= 一轮自我介绍\r\n\r\nquick\r\n= 快速的 / 简短的\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\na quick round of introductions\r\n= 一轮简短的自我介绍\r\n\r\n会议里常用说法\r\n\r\nLet’s start with a quick round of introductions.\r\n我们先快速做一轮自我介绍。\r\n\r\nWe’ll begin with a quick round of introductions.\r\n我们先从一轮简短的自我介绍开始。\r\n\r\nBefore we get started, let’s do a quick round of introductions.\r\n在正式开始之前，我们先快速做一下自我介绍。\r\n\r\nI’ll ask everyone to briefly introduce themselves.\r\n我会请大家简单介绍一下自己。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n4. “I will go with” 的感觉\r\n\r\nI will go with… 在这里意思接近：\r\n\r\n我会选择 / 我打算采用……\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI’ll go with the first option.\r\n我选第一个选项。\r\n\r\nI’ll go with a short introduction first.\r\n我会先做一个简短介绍。\r\n\r\n不过在会议主持中，更自然的是：\r\n\r\n✅ Let’s start with…\r\n✅ We’ll begin with…','Let’s start with a quick round of introductions. Could everyone briefly share their name, role, and what they’ll be working on?\r\n\r\n中文：\r\n我们先快速做一轮自我介绍。大家可以简单说一下自己的名字、角色，以及接下来负责什么内容。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/45dccff845e0438c9962915d00e69998.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-09 18:17:18',1,'2026-06-09 18:17:18'),(1352,19,55,'vocab','anticipate','anticipate','anticipate','核心意思\r\n\r\nanticipate = 预料 / 预期 / 预计 / 提前想到\r\n\r\n它表示你在事情发生之前，已经想到它可能会发生，并做好准备。\r\n\r\nanticipate    /ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/\r\n\r\nverb 动词','常见用法\r\n\r\n✅ 预料某事会发生\r\n\r\nWe anticipate some delays.\r\n我们预计会有一些延误。\r\n\r\nThe company anticipates strong growth next year.\r\n公司预计明年会有强劲增长。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ 提前想到问题 / 风险\r\n\r\nWe need to anticipate potential problems.\r\n我们需要提前考虑可能出现的问题。\r\n\r\nA good project plan should anticipate risks.\r\n一个好的项目计划应该提前预判风险。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ 期待某事，有一点正式\r\n\r\nThe students are eagerly anticipating the start of the project.\r\n学生们正热切期待项目开始。\r\n\r\n这个意思接近 look forward to，但更正式。\r\n\r\n常见搭配\r\n\r\nanticipate problems\r\n预料问题\r\n\r\nanticipate risks\r\n预判风险\r\n\r\nanticipate delays\r\n预计延误\r\n\r\nanticipate demand\r\n预测需求\r\n\r\nanticipate changes\r\n预料变化\r\n\r\nanticipate someone’s needs\r\n提前想到某人的需求','和 expect / predict 的区别\r\n\r\nexpect\r\n= 期待 / 认为会发生，最常用。\r\n\r\nI expect the meeting will be online.\r\n我预计会议会在线上进行。\r\n\r\nanticipate\r\n= 更强调 提前想到并准备，更正式。\r\n\r\nWe anticipate some technical issues, so we prepared a backup plan.\r\n我们预料到可能会有技术问题，所以准备了备用方案。\r\n\r\npredict\r\n= 预测，通常基于数据、趋势或分析。\r\n\r\nThe model predicts rainfall patterns.\r\n这个模型预测降雨模式。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n6. 项目 / 面试中很好用的句子\r\n\r\nI will try to anticipate potential issues and prepare solutions in advance.\r\n我会尽量提前预判潜在问题，并提前准备解决方案。\r\n\r\nThis project requires us to anticipate data quality issues, especially with handwritten documents.\r\n这个项目需要我们提前考虑数据质量问题，尤其是手写文档方面。\r\n\r\nWe need to anticipate how the system might scale in the future.\r\n我们需要提前考虑这个系统未来如何扩展。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n7. 记忆技巧 🧠\r\n\r\nanti- 有“之前 / 预先”的感觉，\r\nanticipate 就是：\r\n\r\nthink before it happens\r\n事情发生前就先想到。\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nanticipate = 预料到，并提前准备。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d759a5e13aab4e73b8991c55b6fe517b.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-10 09:01:39',1,'2026-06-10 09:01:39'),(1353,19,56,'phrase','on behalf of','on behalf of','on behalf of','/ɒn bɪˈhɑːf əv/\r\n代表……；以……的名义；代替……\r\n\r\non behalf of = as a representative of\r\n表示你是代表某个人、团队、公司或组织说话、写信或做事。\r\n\r\n中文可以理解为：\r\n\r\n代表……\r\n以……的名义\r\n受……委托','🔹 Common Usage 常见用法\r\n\r\non behalf of + person / team / company / organisation\r\n\r\non behalf of my team\r\n代表我的团队\r\n\r\non behalf of the company\r\n代表公司\r\n\r\non behalf of the examiner\r\n代表考官 / 评审老师\r\n\r\non behalf of Lincoln University\r\n代表林肯大学','🔹 Useful Sentence Patterns 实用句型\r\n\r\n1. I am writing on behalf of …\r\n\r\nI am writing on behalf of my supervisor.\r\n我代表我的导师写这封邮件。\r\n\r\nI am writing on behalf of the company regarding the project schedule.\r\n我代表公司就项目时间安排写信。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. On behalf of …, I would like to …\r\n\r\nOn behalf of our team, I would like to thank you for your support.\r\n我谨代表我们团队感谢您的支持。\r\n\r\nOn behalf of Lincoln University, I would like to welcome you.\r\n我谨代表林肯大学欢迎您。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. share information on behalf of …\r\n\r\nI would like to share the following information on behalf of the examiner.\r\n我想代表评审老师分享以下信息。\r\n\r\nSamantha shared the schedule on behalf of the examiner.\r\nSamantha 代表评审老师分享了时间安排。\r\n\r\n🔹 Memory Tip 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 behalf 想成：\r\nbe + half → 我站在别人“这一边”帮他说话。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\non behalf of someone\r\n= 站在某人那一边，代表他说话或做事。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔹 Mini Practice 小练习\r\n\r\n你可以这样说：\r\n\r\nI am writing on behalf of myself and my project group.\r\n我代表我自己和我的项目小组写信。\r\n\r\nOn behalf of the students, I would like to ask a question.\r\n我代表学生们想问一个问题。\r\n\r\nI attended the meeting on behalf of my supervisor.\r\n我代表我的导师参加了会议。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a03eebeb62824865ba9e48391707210d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-16 14:38:57',1,'2026-06-16 14:38:57'),(1354,19,57,'vocab','regard','regard','regard','/ rɪˈɡɑːd /\r\nv. 认为；看作\r\nn. 关注；尊重；问候','1. regard as\r\n\r\n✅ 把……看作 / 认为……是\r\n\r\nregard + someone/something + as + noun/adjective\r\n\r\nI regard him as a good supervisor.\r\n我认为他是一位好导师。\r\n\r\nThis project is regarded as a valuable learning opportunity.\r\n这个项目被看作是一次很有价值的学习机会。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意：\r\n不能说：regard him to be…\r\n更自然说：regard him as…\r\n\r\n2. regarding\r\n\r\n✅ 关于…… / 就……而言\r\n\r\nregarding = about，但更正式，常用于邮件、通知、合同。\r\n\r\nI am writing regarding the Industry Project schedule.\r\n我写信是关于 Industry Project 的时间安排。\r\n\r\nPlease contact me regarding your internship placement.\r\n关于你的实习安排，请联系我。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. with regard to\r\n\r\n✅ 关于…… / 至于……\r\n\r\n比 regarding 更正式一点。\r\n\r\nWith regard to the contract, please sign it before Friday.\r\n关于合同，请在周五前签署。\r\n\r\nWith regard to the project timeline, we need to confirm the start date.\r\n关于项目时间线，我们需要确认开始日期。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n4. regards\r\n\r\n✅ 问候；邮件结尾\r\n\r\n邮件结尾常见：\r\n\r\nKind regards,\r\n亲切问候 / 此致\r\n\r\nBest regards,\r\n诚挚问候\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n问候','🔹 结合你的原句\r\n\r\nregarding the Industry Project schedule\r\n= about the Industry Project schedule\r\n= 关于 Industry Project 的时间安排\r\n\r\n完整句子：\r\n\r\nI would like to share the following details on behalf of the examiner regarding the Industry Project schedule.\r\n我想代表评审老师分享以下关于 Industry Project 时间安排的信息。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/53ba55672e954ff3ad52f775017bbdc2.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-16 14:44:50',1,'2026-06-16 14:44:50'),(1355,19,58,'vocab','setting','setting','setting','noun 名词\r\n\r\n① 环境 / 场合\r\n② 故事/电影的背景\r\n③ 设置，通常用复数 settings\r\n\r\nsetting = 环境；场合；背景；场景\r\n\r\n它强调：某件事发生的地方、情况或氛围。','① 环境 / 场合\r\n\r\nin a professional setting\r\n在职业场合中 / 在职场环境中\r\n\r\nin a school setting\r\n在学校环境中\r\n\r\nin a business setting\r\n在商务场合中\r\n\r\nin a medical setting\r\n在医疗场景中\r\n\r\n例句：\r\nThis phrase sounds more natural in a professional setting.\r\n这个表达在职场场合中听起来更自然。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n② 故事/电影的背景\r\n\r\nThe setting of the story is New Zealand.\r\n这个故事的背景是新西兰。\r\n\r\nThe movie has a beautiful countryside setting.\r\n这部电影有一个美丽的乡村背景。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n③ 设置，通常用复数 settings\r\n\r\nphone settings\r\n手机设置\r\n\r\nprivacy settings\r\n隐私设置\r\n\r\nlanguage settings\r\n语言设置\r\n\r\n例句：\r\nYou can change the language in the settings.\r\n你可以在设置里改语言。','4. 记忆方法\r\n\r\nsetting = scene + situation\r\n一个事情发生的场景 + 情境\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nprofessional setting\r\n= professional situation\r\n= professional environment\r\n= 职业场景 / 职场环境','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a0e13718fc674dce87a6b67131cebc34.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-17 09:19:20',1,'2026-06-17 09:19:20'),(1356,19,59,'phrase','controversial','controversial','controversial','adj. 形容词\r\n\r\n中文意思：有争议的；引起争论的','核心意思\r\n\r\nSomething controversial causes people to have strongly different opinions.\r\n\r\n也就是：一件事让很多人意见分歧，有人支持，有人反对。\r\n\r\n常见搭配\r\n\r\na controversial topic\r\n一个有争议的话题\r\n\r\na controversial issue\r\n一个有争议的问题\r\n\r\na controversial decision\r\n一个有争议的决定\r\n\r\na controversial figure\r\n一个有争议的人物\r\n\r\nhighly controversial\r\n非常有争议的','例句\r\n\r\nThis is a controversial topic.\r\n这是一个有争议的话题。\r\n\r\nThe government made a controversial decision.\r\n政府做出了一个有争议的决定。\r\n\r\nHe is a controversial figure in politics.\r\n他是政坛上一个有争议的人物。\r\n\r\nThe new policy is highly controversial.\r\n这项新政策非常有争议。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n口语里怎么用？\r\n\r\n可以直接说：\r\n\r\nThat’s a bit controversial.\r\n这个有点争议。\r\n\r\nIt’s a controversial issue.\r\n这是个有争议的问题。\r\n\r\nI don’t want to say anything too controversial.\r\n我不想说太有争议的话。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n记忆方法\r\n\r\ncontroversial = controversy + al\r\n\r\ncontroversy = 争议，争论\r\ncontroversial = 有争议的\r\n\r\n可以记成：\r\n\r\n很多人站在两边吵架 → 这件事就是 controversial\r\n有人支持，有人反对 → controversial\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n对比：controversial vs debatable\r\n\r\ncontroversial\r\n更强调“容易引起争论、情绪和分歧”。\r\n\r\ndebatable\r\n更强调“可以讨论、不一定确定”。\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nThis policy is controversial.\r\n这个政策很有争议。\r\n可能很多人强烈反对或支持。\r\n\r\nWhether it will work is debatable.\r\n它是否有效还可以讨论。\r\n重点是不确定、值得商榷。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/1d1cb0aa24a748029c30e3ccd95cd18b.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-18 09:09:52',1,'2026-06-18 09:09:52'),(1357,19,60,'phrase','chop','chop','chop','v. 动词\r\n砍；劈；切碎\r\n\r\nn. 名词\r\n一块排骨；砍的动作\r\n\r\n核心意思\r\n\r\nchop = 用刀、斧头等 快速用力地切 / 砍\r\n\r\n重点是动作比较“用力、快速、一下下地切”。','常见用法\r\n\r\nchop vegetables\r\n切菜 / 把蔬菜切碎\r\n\r\nchop onions\r\n切洋葱\r\n\r\nchop wood\r\n劈柴\r\n\r\nchop something into pieces\r\n把某物切成块\r\n\r\nchop down a tree\r\n砍倒一棵树\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n例句\r\n\r\nCan you chop the onions?\r\n你能把洋葱切一下吗？\r\n\r\nHe chopped the wood with an axe.\r\n他用斧头劈柴。\r\n\r\nChop the carrots into small pieces.\r\n把胡萝卜切成小块。\r\n\r\nThey chopped down the old tree.\r\n他们砍倒了那棵老树。','口语里常见吗？\r\n\r\n很常见，尤其在做饭时：\r\n\r\nchop it up\r\n把它切碎\r\n\r\nchop them into pieces\r\n把它们切成块\r\n\r\nfinely chopped\r\n切得很碎的\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nAdd some finely chopped garlic.\r\n加一些切碎的大蒜。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n对比：chop vs cut\r\n\r\ncut\r\n普通的“切”，范围很广。\r\n\r\nchop\r\n更强调“用力、快速地切成块”。\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nCut the paper.\r\n剪 / 切纸。\r\n这里不能用 chop。\r\n\r\nChop the onions.\r\n切洋葱。\r\n通常是切碎、切块。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象一个厨师拿着大菜刀：\r\n\r\nchop chop chop!\r\n咔咔咔地切菜。\r\n\r\n所以 chop 就是：\r\n用力切、剁、砍。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/da2157146ced4ac19c564d49b7a4b8f0.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-18 09:22:21',1,'2026-06-18 09:22:21'),(1358,19,61,'phrase','school function','school function','school function','n. 名词短语\r\n学校活动；学校举办的正式或半正式活动\r\n核心意思\r\n\r\nschool function = an event organised by a school\r\n学校组织的活动。\r\n\r\n这里的 function 不是“功能”，而是 活动 / 场合 / 聚会 的意思。','常见场景\r\n\r\na school function\r\n一次学校活动\r\n\r\nattend a school function\r\n参加学校活动\r\n\r\na school function for parents\r\n面向家长的学校活动\r\n\r\nschool functions and events\r\n学校活动和各类事件\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n例句\r\n\r\nI need to attend a school function tonight.\r\n我今晚要参加一个学校活动。\r\n\r\nParents are invited to the school function.\r\n家长被邀请参加学校活动。\r\n\r\nThe school function will start at 6 pm.\r\n学校活动晚上 6 点开始。\r\n\r\nShe helped organise the school function.\r\n她帮忙组织了这次学校活动。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n可能包括什么？\r\n\r\nschool function 可以指：\r\n\r\nschool concert\r\n学校音乐会\r\n\r\nsports day\r\n运动会\r\n\r\nparent evening\r\n家长会 / 家长活动\r\n\r\ngraduation ceremony\r\n毕业典礼\r\n\r\nfundraising event\r\n筹款活动\r\n\r\ncultural day\r\n文化日活动\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nfunction 的这个意思\r\n\r\nfunction 在正式一点的英语里，可以表示：\r\n\r\nan official or social event\r\n正式活动 / 社交活动\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\na business function\r\n商务活动\r\n\r\na family function\r\n家庭聚会 / 家庭活动\r\n\r\na school function\r\n学校活动\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n口语提醒\r\n\r\n在日常口语里，很多人也会直接说：\r\n\r\nschool event\r\n学校活动\r\n\r\n比 school function 更普通、更自然。\r\n\r\n所以你可以说：\r\n\r\nI’m going to a school event tonight.\r\n我今晚要去参加一个学校活动。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f406d9eb689b4303949a7b838b74e07d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-18 09:33:12',1,'2026-06-18 09:33:12'),(1359,19,62,'phrase','rhythm vs rhyme','rhythm vs rhyme','rhythm vs rhyme','1. rhythm\r\n\r\n/ˈrɪð.əm/\r\nn. 节奏；韵律\r\n\r\nMeaning:\r\nThe beat or pattern of sounds, music, speech, or movement.\r\n\r\n中文：\r\n声音、音乐、说话或动作中的 节奏感 / 节拍规律。\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\nThis song has a strong rhythm.\r\n这首歌节奏很强。\r\n\r\nTry to speak with a natural rhythm.\r\n试着用自然的节奏说话。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. rhyme\r\n\r\n/raɪm/\r\nn. 押韵；韵脚\r\nv. 押韵\r\n\r\nMeaning:\r\nWords rhyme when they have the same or similar ending sound.\r\n\r\n中文：\r\n两个词的 结尾发音相同或相似。\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\n“Cat” rhymes with “hat”.\r\ncat 和 hat 押韵。\r\n\r\nCan you find a word that rhymes with “time”?\r\n你能找到一个和 time 押韵的词吗？','🎵 Easy Memory\r\n\r\nrhythm = beat\r\n节奏：dum-da-dum-da\r\n\r\nrhyme = same ending sound\r\n押韵：time / rhyme / climb','✅ Compare in one sentence\r\n\r\nA poem can have rhythm and rhyme.\r\n一首诗可以有节奏，也可以有押韵。\r\n\r\nrhythm = how it flows\r\n它读起来的节奏感。\r\n\r\nrhyme = how words sound alike at the end\r\n词尾听起来相似。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/6b3e25ce969743eea07f4ab488f8ad08.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-18 10:16:17',1,'2026-06-18 10:16:17'),(1360,19,63,'phrase','cantaloupe','cantaloupe','cantaloupe','/ˈkæn.tə.luːp/ 美式常见\r\nn. 名词\r\n哈密瓜；甜瓜的一种\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n核心意思\r\n\r\ncantaloupe 是一种 melon，通常外皮有网纹，里面是橙色果肉。\r\n\r\n中文里常翻译成：\r\n\r\n哈密瓜 / 甜瓜 / 网纹瓜\r\n\r\n不过严格说，中文的“哈密瓜”和英文 cantaloupe 不一定完全是同一种品种，但日常交流中可以这样理解。','常见用法\r\n\r\na cantaloupe\r\n一个哈密瓜 / 甜瓜\r\n\r\ncantaloupe slices\r\n哈密瓜片\r\n\r\nfresh cantaloupe\r\n新鲜哈密瓜\r\n\r\ncantaloupe melon\r\n哈密瓜 / 甜瓜','例句\r\n\r\nI bought a cantaloupe at the supermarket.\r\n我在超市买了一个哈密瓜。\r\n\r\nWould you like some cantaloupe?\r\n你想吃点哈密瓜吗？\r\n\r\nCantaloupe is sweet and juicy.\r\n哈密瓜又甜又多汁。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n和 melon 的关系\r\n\r\nmelon\r\n瓜类的总称，比如西瓜、哈密瓜、甜瓜。\r\n\r\ncantaloupe\r\nmelon 的一种，通常指橙色果肉的甜瓜。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nWatermelon is a kind of melon.\r\n西瓜是一种瓜。\r\n\r\nCantaloupe is also a kind of melon.\r\n哈密瓜也是一种瓜。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n记忆方法\r\n\r\ncantaloupe 可以记成：\r\n\r\ncan + ta + loupe\r\n想象：你打开一个 can，里面装着一块橙色的哈密瓜。\r\n\r\n重点记：\r\ncantaloupe = orange-fleshed melon = 哈密瓜 / 甜瓜.','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9b92b598a107460f961a1639f8d2436e.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-18 10:24:24',1,'2026-06-18 10:24:24'),(1361,19,64,'vocab','skewer','skewer','skewer','n. 名词\r\n烤肉签；竹签；金属签\r\n\r\nv. 动词\r\n用签子串起来；刺穿\r\n\r\n核心意思\r\n\r\nskewer = a long thin stick used to hold pieces of food together, especially for grilling.\r\n\r\n也就是：\r\n用来把肉、蔬菜等串起来烤的 签子 / 串签。','常见用法\r\n\r\na wooden skewer\r\n一根竹签 / 木签\r\n\r\na metal skewer\r\n一根金属签\r\n\r\nchicken skewers\r\n鸡肉串\r\n\r\nlamb skewers\r\n羊肉串\r\n\r\nbeef skewers\r\n牛肉串\r\n\r\nskewer the meat\r\n把肉串起来\r\n\r\nput the meat on skewers\r\n把肉串到签子上','Put the chicken pieces on skewers.\r\n把鸡肉块串到签子上。\r\n\r\nWe grilled some lamb skewers.\r\n我们烤了一些羊肉串。\r\n\r\nSoak wooden skewers in water before grilling.\r\n烧烤前把竹签泡在水里。\r\n\r\nShe skewered the vegetables and grilled them.\r\n她把蔬菜串起来烤。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n和 kebab 的区别\r\n\r\nskewer\r\n重点是“签子”或“用签子串起来”。\r\n\r\nkebab\r\n重点是“烤肉串 / 串烧这种食物”。\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nUse a skewer to make kebabs.\r\n用签子做烤肉串。\r\n\r\nI ordered two chicken kebabs.\r\n我点了两串鸡肉串。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n口语中怎么说？\r\n\r\n在日常点餐时可以说：\r\n\r\nOne chicken skewer, please.\r\n请给我一串鸡肉串。\r\n\r\nTwo lamb skewers, please.\r\n请给我两串羊肉串。\r\n\r\n更口语也可以说：\r\n\r\nmeat on a stick\r\n串在棍子上的肉 / 肉串\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n记忆方法\r\n\r\nskewer 发音像 “sky-er”。\r\n想象一根长签子把肉串起来，举得很高，像指向天空。\r\n\r\nskewer = 串肉的签子 / 用签子串起来.','/static/uploads/english_note_item/7f92ef6d9aa84afb804598e62a2bbe98.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-18 10:29:38',1,'2026-06-18 10:29:38'),(1362,19,65,'phrase','executive function','executive function','executive function','/ɪɡˈzek.jə.tɪv ˈfʌŋk.ʃən/\r\n\r\nn. 名词短语\r\n执行功能；大脑的管理能力\r\n核心意思\r\n\r\nexecutive function 指大脑用来 计划、控制、管理自己行为和注意力 的能力。\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n大脑里的“项目经理”\r\n帮你安排任务、控制冲动、记住目标、按计划完成事情。','主要包括什么？\r\n\r\nplanning\r\n计划能力\r\n\r\nfocus / attention control\r\n专注力 / 注意力控制\r\n\r\nworking memory\r\n工作记忆，短时间记住并使用信息\r\n\r\nself-control\r\n自我控制\r\n\r\ntime management\r\n时间管理\r\n\r\nproblem-solving\r\n解决问题\r\n\r\ntask switching\r\n任务切换能力','Executive function helps children plan and complete tasks.\r\n执行功能帮助孩子计划并完成任务。\r\n\r\nPoor executive function can make it hard to stay organised.\r\n执行功能较弱会让人很难保持有条理。\r\n\r\nSleep, exercise, and routines can support executive function.\r\n睡眠、运动和规律作息可以帮助执行功能。\r\n\r\nChildren develop executive function gradually.\r\n孩子的执行功能是逐渐发展的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n常见场景\r\n\r\n这个词常出现在：\r\n\r\neducation\r\n教育\r\n\r\npsychology\r\n心理学\r\n\r\nchild development\r\n儿童发展\r\n\r\nADHD discussions\r\n关于 ADHD 的讨论\r\n\r\nlearning support\r\n学习支持\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n注意：不是“公司高管功能”\r\n\r\n这里的 executive 不是“高管本人”，而是像 manager / controller 一样的意思。\r\n\r\nexecutive function\r\n不是：行政功能 / 高管功能\r\n而是：大脑的管理和控制能力\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n记忆方法\r\n\r\nexecutive = 管理者\r\nfunction = 功能\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nexecutive function = brain manager function\r\n大脑管理者功能 → 执行功能。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9f08b28250bf44b096a0404211c32676.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-18 10:58:53',1,'2026-06-18 10:58:53'),(1363,19,66,'phrase','look this up','look this up','look this up','phrasal verb 短语动词\r\n\r\n中文意思\r\n\r\n查一下这个 / 查找这个信息\r\n\r\n通常指：\r\n在网上、词典、资料库、书里查找某个信息。','look + something + up\r\n查找某事 / 某个词 / 某个信息\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nCan you look this up?\r\n你能查一下这个吗？\r\n\r\nI’ll look it up online.\r\n我会上网查一下。\r\n\r\nLet me look up the meaning of this word.\r\n让我查一下这个单词的意思。\r\n\r\n你刚才说的句子\r\n\r\nlook this up\r\n= 查一下这个\r\n\r\n更自然完整地说：\r\n\r\nCan you look this up?\r\n你能查一下这个吗？\r\n\r\n或者更口语：\r\n\r\nCould you check this for me?\r\n你能帮我查一下吗？','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/29641cf5572b4ee798332f932dbdb896.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-18 15:20:06',1,'2026-06-18 15:20:06'),(1364,19,67,'vocab','somewhat','somewhat','somewhat','adv. 副词\r\n\r\n中文意思\r\n\r\n有点儿；稍微；在某种程度上\r\n\r\n比 a little 更正式一点，比 very 弱很多。','常见用法\r\n\r\nsomewhat + adjective / adverb\r\n稍微……；有点……\r\n\r\n例句\r\n\r\nI’m somewhat tired.\r\n我有点累。\r\n\r\nThe result was somewhat surprising.\r\n结果有点令人惊讶。\r\n\r\nThis explanation is somewhat confusing.\r\n这个解释有点让人困惑。\r\n\r\nHe looked somewhat nervous during the interview.\r\n他在面试中看起来有点紧张。','I’m a bit tired.\r\n我有点累。\r\n\r\n写作、报告、正式表达可以说：\r\n\r\nThe result is somewhat different.\r\n结果有些不同。\r\n\r\n记忆小技巧\r\n\r\nsome = 一些\r\nwhat = 什么 / 程度\r\n\r\nsomewhat 可以理解成：\r\n有那么一点程度 = 有点儿 / 稍微','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a37185a813b745bdbcd9606d427a7646.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-18 15:37:11',1,'2026-06-18 15:37:11'),(1365,19,68,'vocab','commodity','commodity','commodity','n. 名词\r\n\r\n中文意思\r\n\r\n商品；日用品；大宗商品\r\n\r\n它常指可以被买卖的基础商品，尤其是：\r\n\r\noil 石油\r\ngold 黄金\r\nwheat 小麦\r\ncoffee 咖啡豆\r\ncotton 棉花\r\n\r\n这些都可以叫 commodities。','a valuable commodity\r\n有价值的商品 / 宝贵资源\r\n\r\ncommodity prices\r\n大宗商品价格\r\n\r\nagricultural commodities\r\n农产品大宗商品\r\n\r\nbasic commodities\r\n基本生活商品','Oil is an important commodity.\r\n石油是一种重要的大宗商品。\r\n\r\nCommodity prices have increased recently.\r\n大宗商品价格最近上涨了。\r\n\r\nTime is a valuable commodity.\r\n时间是一种宝贵的资源。\r\n\r\n注意\r\n\r\ncommodity 不只是普通 “商品”。\r\n普通商店里的商品可以说：\r\n\r\nproduct = 产品\r\ngoods = 货物 / 商品\r\nitem = 一件商品\r\n\r\n而 commodity 更常用于经济、贸易、农业、能源等语境，表示“基础可交易商品”。\r\n\r\n记忆小技巧\r\n\r\ncommodity 可以理解成：\r\n\r\ncommon + goods\r\n很多人都需要、可以大量买卖的基础商品。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b013445c165f453b9d0ca443c512ffcf.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-18 16:34:45',1,'2026-06-18 16:34:45'),(1366,19,69,'phrase','as long as','as long as','as long as','conj. 连词 / phrase 短语\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n中文意思\r\n\r\n1. 只要……\r\n2. 和……一样长 / 长达……','1. 只要……\r\n\r\n表示条件，和 if 很像，但语气更强调“满足这个条件就可以”。\r\n\r\nYou can go out as long as you finish your homework.\r\n只要你完成作业，就可以出去。\r\n\r\nI’ll help you as long as I have time.\r\n只要我有时间，我就帮你。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 和……一样长 / 长达……\r\n\r\n表示时间或长度。\r\n\r\nThis bridge is as long as that one.\r\n这座桥和那座桥一样长。\r\n\r\nThe meeting lasted as long as three hours.\r\n会议长达三个小时。','as long as + sentence\r\n只要 + 一个完整句子\r\n\r\nAs long as you keep practising, your English will improve.\r\n只要你坚持练习，你的英语就会进步。\r\n\r\nAs long as the weather is good, we’ll go hiking.\r\n只要天气好，我们就去徒步。\r\n\r\nYou can borrow my car if you drive carefully.\r\n如果你小心开，可以借我的车。\r\n\r\nYou can borrow my car as long as you drive carefully.\r\n只要你小心开，就可以借我的车。\r\n语气更像：这个条件必须满足。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n口语常用句\r\n\r\nAs long as it works, I’m happy.\r\n只要它能用，我就满意。\r\n\r\nAs long as you’re okay, that’s all that matters.\r\n只要你没事，那才是最重要的。\r\n\r\nYou can do it your way, as long as the result is good.\r\n你可以按你的方式做，只要结果好就行。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n记忆小技巧\r\n\r\nas long as 可以想成：\r\n\r\n“这条条件线够长，就可以继续走。”\r\n\r\n所以意思就是：\r\n只要条件成立，就可以。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/53413023b4044c79aa690bedf1ef919d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-18 16:49:46',1,'2026-06-18 16:49:46'),(1367,19,70,'phrase','in turn','in turn','in turn','词性\r\n短语 / adverb phrase\r\n\r\n中文意思\r\n\r\n1. 依次，轮流\r\n2. 反过来，进而，又导致\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nturn 有“轮到”的意思。\r\n所以 in turn 可以理解为：\r\n\r\n轮到它了 → 依次 / 反过来产生影响','1️⃣ 依次 / 轮流\r\n\r\n= one by one\r\n\r\nEach student answered the question in turn.\r\n每个学生依次回答问题。\r\n\r\nThe team members spoke in turn during the meeting.\r\n团队成员在会议中轮流发言。\r\n\r\n📌 这个意思强调：一个接一个，按顺序来。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 反过来 / 进而\r\n\r\n= as a result / which then causes something\r\n\r\nClear requirements help developers understand the task, which in turn improves the final product.\r\n清晰的需求帮助开发人员理解任务，这反过来会提升最终产品质量。\r\n\r\nGood communication reduces mistakes, which in turn saves time.\r\n良好的沟通减少错误，进而节省时间。\r\n\r\n📌 这个意思强调：A 导致 B，B 又导致 C。','✅ 常用搭配\r\n\r\neach in turn\r\n每个依次\r\n\r\nwhich in turn…\r\n这反过来……\r\n\r\nin turn leads to…\r\n进而导致……\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔥 你项目里可以这样用\r\n\r\nA user requirements analyst collects user needs and turns them into user stories. These user stories, in turn, help developers build the right features.\r\n用户需求分析师收集用户需求，并把它们转化为用户故事。这些用户故事反过来帮助开发人员构建正确的功能。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/11f15ed2541943fa8c7d2599ff9e235b.jpg','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-22 09:31:47',1,'2026-06-22 09:31:47'),(1368,19,71,'vocab','dump','dump','dump','中文意思\r\n\r\n动词 v.\r\n\r\n1. 倾倒；倒掉；丢弃\r\n    把垃圾、废物、东西随便扔掉。\r\n2. 甩掉；抛弃某人\r\n    常用于感情关系里，比较口语。\r\n3. 把大量东西放下 / 扔下\r\n    比如把文件、数据、东西一股脑放到某处。\r\n4. 导出 / 转储数据\r\n    在 IT 里常见，表示把数据导出来保存。','1. 倒掉 / 扔掉\r\n\r\ndump rubbish / trash\r\n倒垃圾 / 扔垃圾\r\n\r\nDon’t dump rubbish here.\r\n不要在这里倒垃圾。\r\n\r\n2. 甩掉某人\r\n\r\ndump someone\r\n甩掉某人\r\n\r\nShe dumped her boyfriend.\r\n她甩了她男朋友。\r\n\r\n这个用法比较口语，语气有点直接。\r\n\r\n3. 大量放下 / 扔下\r\n\r\ndump something on the table\r\n把东西一股脑扔到桌上\r\n\r\nHe dumped his bag on the floor.\r\n他把包往地上一扔。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n4. IT 里的 dump\r\n\r\ndump data\r\n导出数据 / 转储数据\r\n\r\ndatabase dump\r\n数据库转储文件 / 数据库导出文件\r\n\r\nWe need to dump the database before deployment.\r\n部署前我们需要导出数据库。','名词用法\r\n\r\na dump\r\n\r\n1. 垃圾场\r\n    a rubbish dump / garbage dump\r\n    垃圾场\r\n2. 脏乱的地方\r\n    This room is a dump.\r\n    这个房间像垃圾堆一样。\r\n3. 数据转储文件\r\n    a memory dump\r\n    内存转储文件\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\ndump 的核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n把东西“哗啦一下倒出去 / 扔出去”\r\n\r\n所以它可以表示：\r\n\r\n倒垃圾 → dump trash\r\n甩人 → dump someone\r\n导出数据 → dump data\r\n脏乱地方 → a dump','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f5aa6e8c2a0d4bb5ad0ca1c3ecc68342.jpg','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-22 09:45:19',1,'2026-06-22 09:45:19'),(1369,19,72,'phrase','walk me through','walk me through','walk me through','phr. 短语\r\n\r\n核心意思\r\n\r\n一步一步给我讲清楚 / 带我过一遍流程\r\n\r\n不是“真的走路”，而是让别人按步骤解释一个过程。','常见中文意思\r\n1. 带我过一遍\r\n\r\nCan you walk me through the process?\r\n你能带我过一遍这个流程吗？\r\n\r\n2. 一步一步教我\r\n\r\nCould you walk me through how to use this system?\r\n你能一步一步教我怎么用这个系统吗？\r\n\r\n3. 详细解释给我听\r\n\r\nPlease walk me through your workflow.\r\n请详细给我讲一下你们的工作流程。','职场常用句\r\n问业务流程时很实用：\r\n\r\nCould you walk me through the full workflow?\r\n你能带我完整过一遍整个工作流程吗？\r\n\r\nCould you walk me through what happens after the user submits the data?\r\n用户提交数据之后，会发生什么？你能一步一步讲一下吗？\r\n\r\nCould you walk me through how the data moves into your ERP system?\r\n你能给我讲一下数据是怎么进入你们 ERP 系统的吗？\r\n\r\nCould you walk me through this screen?\r\n你能给我讲一下这个页面吗？\r\n\r\n语气感觉\r\n\r\nwalk me through 很自然、很礼貌、很适合职场。\r\n比 explain it to me 更像是在说：\r\n\r\n“请按步骤带我理解一下。”\r\n\r\n结构\r\n\r\nwalk + someone + through + something\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nwalk me through the process\r\n带我过一遍流程\r\n\r\nwalk us through the system\r\n带我们了解一下这个系统\r\n\r\nwalk the client through the proposal\r\n带客户过一遍方案\r\n\r\n对比\r\nexplain\r\n\r\n普通解释。\r\n\r\nCan you explain this?\r\n你能解释一下这个吗？\r\n\r\nwalk me through\r\n\r\n强调按步骤、按流程讲。\r\n\r\nCan you walk me through this?\r\n你能一步一步带我看一下这个吗？\r\n\r\n记忆小技巧\r\n\r\n想象你不熟悉一个系统，别人像导游一样带你一步一步走：\r\n\r\nwalk me through = 像带路一样，带我理解整个过程。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f2b48efb73d3426e880a92c46e193ad9.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-22 10:38:35',1,'2026-06-22 10:38:35'),(1370,19,73,'phrase','end-to-end','end-to-end','end-to-end','发音：/ˌend tuː ˈend/\r\n词性：adjective / adverb\r\n中文意思：端到端的；从头到尾的；全流程的\r\n\r\n核心理解\r\n\r\nend-to-end = 从开始到结束，覆盖整个流程。\r\n\r\n它常用于 IT、系统、业务流程、测试、服务交付 里。','常见用法\r\n\r\n1. end-to-end process\r\n端到端流程；完整业务流程\r\n\r\nWe need to understand the end-to-end process.\r\n我们需要了解完整的业务流程。\r\n\r\n2. end-to-end testing\r\n端到端测试\r\n\r\nThe team performed end-to-end testing before release.\r\n团队在发布前做了端到端测试。\r\n\r\n3. end-to-end solution\r\n完整解决方案\r\n\r\nThis platform provides an end-to-end solution for order management.\r\n这个平台为订单管理提供完整解决方案。\r\n\r\n4. end-to-end workflow\r\n完整工作流\r\n\r\nCould you walk me through the end-to-end workflow?\r\n你能带我了解一下完整工作流吗？\r\n\r\n你的会议里可以这样说\r\n\r\nI’d like to understand your end-to-end business workflow, from user input to ERP processing and final output.\r\n我想了解你们完整的业务流程，从用户输入数据，到 ERP 系统处理，再到最终输出结果。','易混对比\r\n\r\nend-to-end\r\n强调“全流程覆盖”\r\n\r\nend-to-end testing\r\n端到端测试\r\n\r\nstep by step\r\n强调“一步一步讲”\r\n\r\nCould you explain it step by step?\r\n你能一步一步解释吗？\r\n\r\noverall\r\n强调“整体上”\r\n\r\nI want to understand the overall process.\r\n我想了解整体流程。\r\n\r\n记忆法\r\n\r\n想象一条业务流水线：\r\nUser input → System processing → ERP → Report/output\r\n从第一个 end 到最后一个 end，就是 end-to-end。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8b0f7e9f10594d129849d237fe31fc44.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-22 10:49:17',1,'2026-06-22 10:49:17'),(1371,19,74,'phrase','What processing steps are involved?','What processing steps are involved?','What processing steps are involved?','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n涉及哪些处理步骤？\r\n也可以理解为：\r\n\r\n中间会经过哪些加工 / 审核 / 转换 / 系统处理？\r\n\r\n这句话非常适合问业务流程、系统流程、ERP、数据流。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆公式\r\n\r\nWhat + 名词 + are involved?\r\n\r\n= 涉及哪些……？\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nWhat teams are involved?\r\n涉及哪些团队？\r\n\r\nWhat systems are involved?\r\n涉及哪些系统？\r\n\r\nWhat documents are involved?\r\n涉及哪些文件？\r\n\r\nWhat risks are involved?\r\n涉及哪些风险？','🧱 词块拆解\r\n1. processing steps ⚙️\r\n\r\n意思是：处理步骤 / 加工步骤\r\n\r\n这里的 processing 来自 process，表示“处理、加工”。\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\ndata processing steps\r\n数据处理步骤\r\n\r\norder processing steps\r\n订单处理步骤\r\n\r\napproval processing steps\r\n审批处理步骤\r\n\r\n2. are involved 🔗\r\n\r\n意思是：被涉及 / 包含在其中\r\n\r\n这个表达很职场，比 What steps do you do? 更自然。\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\n❌ What steps do you do?\r\n不太自然。\r\n\r\n✅ What steps are involved?\r\n涉及哪些步骤？\r\n\r\n🏢 职场使用场景\r\n📊 问数据流程\r\n\r\nWhat processing steps are involved after the user submits the data?\r\n用户提交数据之后，会涉及哪些处理步骤？\r\n\r\n🧾 问订单流程\r\n\r\nWhat processing steps are involved before the order is approved?\r\n订单被批准之前，会经过哪些处理步骤？\r\n\r\n🏭 问 ERP 流程\r\n\r\nWhat processing steps are involved before the data flows into the ERP system?\r\n数据流入 ERP 系统之前，会经过哪些处理步骤？\r\n\r\n✅ 问审批流程\r\n\r\nWhat approval steps are involved?\r\n涉及哪些审批步骤？','👍 最实用会议问法\r\n\r\nCould you walk me through what processing steps are involved?\r\n你能带我了解一下中间涉及哪些处理步骤吗？\r\n\r\n更完整一点：\r\n\r\nAfter the user submits the data, what processing steps are involved before it goes into the ERP system?\r\n用户提交数据之后，在进入 ERP 系统之前，会涉及哪些处理步骤？\r\n\r\n🧠 小总结\r\n\r\nWhat processing steps are involved?\r\n不是在问“你做什么步骤”，而是在更专业地问：\r\n\r\n这个流程中间包含哪些处理环节？\r\n\r\n关键词记住：\r\n\r\n⚙️ processing steps = 处理步骤\r\n🔗 are involved = 被涉及 / 包含在内\r\n👍 What ... are involved? = 涉及哪些……？','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8ddf3ba11a7f48ea819f0199276d98db.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-22 10:57:46',1,'2026-06-22 10:57:46'),(1372,19,75,'phrase','How does it flow into your ERP system?','How does it flow into your ERP system?','How does it flow into your ERP system?','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n它是怎么流转到你们 ERP 系统里的？\r\n\r\n这里的 it 通常指：\r\n\r\n📊 data 数据\r\n🧾 order 订单\r\n📄 request 请求\r\n👤 user information 用户信息','🧠 记忆公式\r\n\r\nHow does + something + flow into + system?\r\n\r\n= 某个东西是怎么流转到某个系统里的？\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nHow does customer information flow into the CRM system?\r\n客户信息是如何流转到 CRM 系统里的？\r\n\r\nHow does payment data flow into the accounting system?\r\n支付数据是如何流转到会计系统里的？\r\n\r\nHow does inventory data flow into the ERP system?\r\n库存数据是如何流转到 ERP 系统里的？\r\n\r\nflow into 🔄\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n流入 / 流转到 / 进入\r\n\r\n在系统、数据、业务流程里非常常用。\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nThe data flows into the database.\r\n数据流入数据库。\r\n\r\nThe order flows into the ERP system.\r\n订单流转到 ERP 系统。\r\n\r\n🔍 flow into vs enter\r\nenter\r\n\r\n普通的“进入”。\r\n\r\nThe data enters the ERP system.\r\n数据进入 ERP 系统。\r\n\r\nflow into\r\n\r\n更强调流程感、系统之间的流转，更适合业务分析。\r\n\r\nThe data flows into the ERP system.\r\n数据流转到 ERP 系统中。\r\n\r\n👍 更自然的会议问法\r\n\r\nCould you explain how the data flows into your ERP system?\r\n你能解释一下数据是如何流转到你们 ERP 系统的吗？\r\n\r\nCould you walk me through how it flows into your ERP system?\r\n你能带我一步一步了解它是如何流转到你们 ERP 系统的吗？\r\n\r\nIs this process manual, automated, or integrated through an API?\r\n这个过程是手动的、自动的，还是通过 API 集成的？\r\n\r\n✅ 小总结\r\n\r\nHow does it flow into your ERP system?\r\n\r\n可以理解为：\r\n\r\n🔄 flow into = 流转到 / 进入\r\n🏢 ERP system = 企业资源计划系统\r\n📊 整句话 = 它是怎么进入你们 ERP 系统的？\r\n\r\n这句话很适合在需求分析、业务访谈、系统调研时使用。','🏢 职场使用场景\r\n📊 问数据流\r\n\r\nHow does the data flow into your ERP system?\r\n数据是如何流转到你们 ERP 系统的？\r\n\r\n🧾 问订单流\r\n\r\nHow does the order flow into your ERP system?\r\n订单是如何进入你们 ERP 系统的？\r\n\r\n🔗 问系统集成\r\n\r\nDoes it flow into your ERP system automatically or manually?\r\n它是自动流入 ERP 系统，还是手动录入的？\r\n\r\n⚙️ 问接口\r\n\r\nDoes it flow into your ERP system through an API?\r\n它是通过 API 进入你们 ERP 系统的吗？','/static/uploads/english_note_item/066cd871f29249b987277bbd21b651b6.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-22 11:11:16',1,'2026-06-22 11:11:16'),(1373,19,76,'phrase','What does the user receive from that system?','What does the user receive from that system?','What does the user receive from that system?','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n用户会从那个系统中收到什么？\r\n也可以理解为：\r\n\r\n系统最终会给用户什么结果 / 输出 / 反馈？\r\n\r\n这句话常用于问：\r\n\r\n📄 报告\r\n📧 邮件通知\r\n✅ 确认信息\r\n📊 数据结果\r\n🧾 发票 / 订单状态\r\n🔔 系统提醒','🏢 职场使用场景\r\n📊 问系统输出\r\n\r\nWhat does the user receive from that system?\r\n用户会从那个系统收到什么结果？\r\n\r\n📧 问通知\r\n\r\nDoes the user receive a confirmation email from the system?\r\n用户会收到系统发出的确认邮件吗？\r\n\r\n🧾 问订单结果\r\n\r\nWhat does the customer receive after the order is processed?\r\n订单处理完成后，客户会收到什么？\r\n\r\n📄 问报表\r\n\r\nDoes the system generate a report for the user?\r\n系统会为用户生成报告吗？\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆公式\r\n\r\nWhat does + person + receive + from + system?\r\n\r\n= 某人会从某个系统收到什么？\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nWhat does the customer receive from the booking system?\r\n客户会从预订系统收到什么？\r\n\r\nWhat does the manager receive from the reporting system?\r\n经理会从报表系统收到什么？\r\n\r\nWhat does the user receive after submitting the form?\r\n用户提交表单后会收到什么？','🔍 receive vs get\r\nget\r\n\r\n更口语，意思是“得到 / 收到”。\r\n\r\nWhat does the user get?\r\n用户会得到什么？\r\n\r\nreceive\r\n\r\n更正式，更适合职场和系统流程。\r\n\r\nWhat does the user receive from the system?\r\n用户会从系统收到什么？\r\n\r\n👍 更自然的会议问法\r\n\r\nWhat does the user receive at the end of the process?\r\n流程结束时，用户会收到什么？\r\n\r\nWhat output does the system provide to the user?\r\n系统会向用户提供什么输出？\r\n\r\nDoes the user receive a report, notification, or confirmation?\r\n用户会收到报告、通知还是确认信息？\r\n\r\nWhat is the final outcome for the user?\r\n对用户来说，最终结果是什么？\r\n\r\n✅ 小总结\r\n\r\nWhat does the user receive from that system?\r\n\r\n关键词记住：\r\n\r\n👤 the user = 用户\r\n📥 receive = 收到 / 获得\r\n🖥️ from that system = 从那个系统\r\n🎯 整句 = 系统最终给用户什么结果？\r\n\r\n这句话很适合在需求分析、业务访谈、ERP 流程调研中使用。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/934df220bc05434ab7e0ead8aca48d94.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-22 11:17:18',1,'2026-06-22 11:17:18'),(1374,19,77,'phrase','Would it be possible to...?','Would it be possible to...?','Would it be possible to...?','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n是否可以……？\r\n有没有可能……？\r\n\r\n这是一个非常礼貌、正式、职场常用的请求句型。\r\n\r\n比 Can I...? / Can you...? 更委婉。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆小技巧\r\n\r\n把它记成一个“礼貌请求开头”：\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to...?\r\n= 我想请求一件事，但我说得很礼貌。\r\n\r\n✅ 小总结\r\n\r\n👍 Would it be possible to...?\r\n= 是否可以……？\r\n\r\n📌 常用于：\r\n申请权限、约会议、请求资料、请求延期、提出建议。\r\n\r\n最适合职场的一句话：\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to + 动词原形...?','🧱 句型结构\r\n✅ 基本公式\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to + 动词原形...?\r\n\r\n= 是否可以做某事？\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to have a read-only account?\r\n是否可以给我一个只读账号？\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to schedule a meeting?\r\n是否可以安排一个会议？\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to extend the deadline?\r\n是否可以延长截止日期？\r\n\r\n🔍 对比：Can I...? vs Would it be possible to...?\r\nCan I...?\r\n\r\n比较直接、口语。\r\n\r\nCan I have a read-only account?\r\n我可以有一个只读账号吗？\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to...?\r\n\r\n更礼貌、更委婉、更适合职场。\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to have a read-only account?\r\n是否可以给我一个只读账号？\r\n\r\n👍 你的完整句子\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to have a read-only account so I can better familiarize myself with your business system?\r\n\r\n中文意思：\r\n\r\n是否可以给我一个只读账号，这样我可以更好地熟悉你们的业务系统？\r\n\r\n⭐ 更自然的职场版本\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to set up a read-only account for me, so I can better understand your business system and workflow?\r\n\r\n中文意思：\r\n\r\n是否可以给我开通一个只读账号，这样我可以更好地了解你们的业务系统和工作流程？','🏢 职场常用场景\r\n🔐 申请权限\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to have a read-only account?\r\n是否可以给我一个只读账号？\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to access the system in read-only mode?\r\n是否可以用只读模式访问这个系统？\r\n\r\n📅 安排会议\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to meet sometime this week?\r\n这周是否可以找个时间见面？\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to have a short meeting tomorrow?\r\n明天是否可以开一个简短会议？\r\n\r\n⏰ 请求延期\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to extend the deadline by one week?\r\n是否可以把截止日期延后一周？\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to submit it next Monday?\r\n是否可以下周一提交？\r\n\r\n📄 请求资料\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to share the document with me?\r\n是否可以把这个文件分享给我？\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to send me the latest version?\r\n是否可以发我最新版？','/static/uploads/english_note_item/59dff92a437f44bc8b6f274f6e7e5aac.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-22 11:32:33',1,'2026-06-22 11:32:33'),(1375,19,78,'phrase','familiarize myself with','familiarize myself with','familiarize myself with','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n让自己熟悉……\r\n使自己了解……\r\n\r\n它比 learn about 更正式，更适合职场、学习、系统调研。\r\n\r\n🧱 短语拆解\r\nfamiliarize 📚\r\n\r\n使熟悉；让……了解\r\n\r\nmyself 👤\r\n\r\n我自己\r\n\r\nwith 🔗\r\n\r\n和某个东西建立熟悉关系\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nfamiliarize myself with the system\r\n= 让自己熟悉这个系统\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆公式\r\n\r\nfamiliarize myself with + 名词\r\n\r\n= 让自己熟悉某事物\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nfamiliarize myself with the system\r\n熟悉系统\r\n\r\nfamiliarize myself with the workflow\r\n熟悉工作流程\r\n\r\nfamiliarize myself with the business rules\r\n熟悉业务规则\r\n\r\nfamiliarize myself with the user interface\r\n熟悉用户界面','🏢 职场常用句\r\n🔐 熟悉系统\r\n\r\nI want to familiarize myself with your business system.\r\n我想熟悉一下你们的业务系统。\r\n\r\n📊 熟悉流程\r\n\r\nI need some time to familiarize myself with the workflow.\r\n我需要一些时间熟悉这个工作流程。\r\n\r\n📄 熟悉文档\r\n\r\nI’ll familiarize myself with the project documents first.\r\n我会先熟悉一下项目文档。\r\n\r\n🧑‍💻 熟悉代码\r\n\r\nI’m trying to familiarize myself with the codebase.\r\n我正在熟悉这个代码库。\r\n\r\n✅ 你的句子里怎么用\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to have a read-only account so I can better familiarize myself with your business system?\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n是否可以给我一个只读账号，这样我可以更好地熟悉你们的业务系统？\r\n\r\n这里的 better familiarize myself with 很自然，表示：\r\n\r\n更好地了解 / 熟悉 / 掌握','🔍 对比：learn about vs familiarize myself with\r\nlearn about\r\n\r\n比较普通：了解一下。\r\n\r\nI want to learn about your system.\r\n我想了解你们的系统。\r\n\r\nfamiliarize myself with\r\n\r\n更正式：通过查看、使用、阅读，让自己熟悉起来。\r\n\r\nI want to familiarize myself with your system.\r\n我想熟悉一下你们的系统。\r\n\r\n👍 小总结\r\n\r\nfamiliarize myself with...\r\n= 让自己熟悉……\r\n\r\n很适合用于：\r\n\r\n🔹 新工作\r\n🔹 新系统\r\n🔹 新项目\r\n🔹 新流程\r\n🔹 新代码库\r\n\r\n最常用句：\r\n\r\nI’d like to familiarize myself with your system and workflow.\r\n我想熟悉一下你们的系统和工作流程。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c3122f143b8b43c6a8dfd816456a96ad.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-22 14:00:50',1,'2026-06-22 14:00:50'),(1376,19,79,'phrase','mentioned it briefly','mentioned it briefly','mentioned it briefly','🧩 1. 核心意思\r\n\r\nmentioned it briefly = 简单提到过 / 简短说了一下\r\n\r\n👉 不是详细解释，只是“顺便说了一句”。','🧠 3. 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象开会时：\r\n\r\n👨‍💼 老板说：\r\n“By the way, we also did usability testing.”\r\n顺便说一下，我们也做了可用性测试。\r\n\r\n然后马上换话题了。➡️\r\n\r\n这就叫：\r\n\r\nHe mentioned it briefly.\r\n他只是简单提了一下。','🧱 4. 常用句型\r\n\r\n✅ I think you mentioned it briefly.\r\n我记得你简单提到过这个。\r\n\r\n✅ You mentioned it briefly earlier.\r\n你刚才简单提到过。\r\n\r\n✅ I know you mentioned it briefly, but could you explain it in more detail?\r\n我知道你简单提到过，但你能详细解释一下吗？\r\n\r\n🏢 5. 职场高频用法\r\n\r\nI think you mentioned it briefly, but just to double-check, did you carry out any usability testing?\r\n\r\n📌 中文：\r\n我记得你简单提到过这个，但我想再确认一下，你们有没有做过可用性测试？\r\n\r\n这个句子很适合在：\r\n会议里、面试里、项目讨论里使用。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔁 6. 替代表达\r\n\r\n🌿 touched on it briefly\r\n= 简单谈到过\r\n\r\n例：\r\nYou touched on it briefly earlier.\r\n你刚才简单谈到过这个。\r\n\r\n📝 briefly talked about it\r\n= 简单讲了一下\r\n\r\n例：\r\nWe briefly talked about it yesterday.\r\n我们昨天简单聊过这个。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ 7. 注意区别\r\n\r\nmentioned it briefly\r\n✅ 提到过，但没详细讲\r\n中文：简单提了一下\r\n\r\nexplained it in detail\r\n✅ 详细解释了\r\n中文：详细说明了\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\nHe mentioned the problem briefly.\r\n他简单提了一下这个问题。\r\n\r\nHe explained the problem in detail.\r\n他详细解释了这个问题。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ 最好记的一句话\r\n\r\nYou mentioned it briefly, but I’d like to understand it in more detail.\r\n你简单提到过这个，但我想更详细地了解一下。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3c51a83a57f0428aaf80596503f224c4.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-23 09:45:23',1,'2026-06-23 09:45:23'),(1377,19,80,'phrase','formalize that process','formalize that process','formalize that process','🔹 中文意思\r\n\r\n把那个流程正式化 / 规范化 / 制度化\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n把原来比较随意的做法，变成有步骤、有记录、有标准的正式流程。\r\n\r\n🧩 拆开理解\r\n\r\nformalize\r\n= 使正式化；使规范化\r\n\r\nprocess\r\n= 流程；过程\r\n\r\nformalize that process\r\n= 把那个流程变成正式流程','🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n原来只是：\r\n\r\n朋友试用一下 → 口头反馈 → 随便改改\r\n\r\n正式化之后变成：\r\n\r\n📝 测试计划\r\n✅ 测试步骤\r\n📋 反馈表\r\n📊 结果记录\r\n🔁 改进流程\r\n\r\n这就叫：\r\n\r\nformalize that process\r\n\r\n🏢 常见使用场景\r\n\r\n1. 测试流程\r\nDid you formalize the testing process?\r\n你们有没有把测试流程正式化？\r\n\r\n2. 审批流程\r\nWe need to formalize the approval process.\r\n我们需要把审批流程规范化。\r\n\r\n3. 业务流程\r\nThe company wants to formalize its business processes.\r\n公司想把业务流程制度化。\r\n\r\n4. 反馈流程\r\nWe formalized the feedback process by using a survey form.\r\n我们通过问卷表把反馈流程正式化了。','🔹 原句理解\r\n\r\nDid you formalize that process at all?\r\n\r\n自然中文：\r\n你们有没有把那个流程正式化过？\r\n或者：\r\n你们有没有哪怕稍微规范化一下那个流程？\r\n\r\n这里 at all 有“到底有没有 / 任何程度上有没有”的感觉。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ 职场自然表达\r\n\r\nWe didn’t fully formalize the process, but we did collect feedback in a structured way.\r\n我们没有完全把流程正式化，但我们确实用比较有结构的方式收集了反馈。\r\n\r\nThe process was informal at first, but later we formalized it with clear steps and documentation.\r\n这个流程一开始比较随意，但后来我们通过明确步骤和文档把它正式化了。\r\n\r\n🔁 对比理解\r\n\r\ninformal process\r\n非正式流程\r\n例如：朋友试用、口头反馈、没有记录\r\n\r\nformalized process\r\n正式化流程\r\n例如：测试计划、反馈表、记录、标准步骤\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ 最好记的一句话\r\n\r\nFormalize that process = make the process official, structured, and documented.\r\n把流程变得正式、有结构、有文档记录。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d56e217180df432d87971b0127dc23ea.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-23 09:55:25',1,'2026-06-23 09:55:25'),(1378,19,81,'phrase','kind of','kind of','kind of','kind of\r\n\r\n/ˈkaɪnd əv/\r\n口语里常读成：kinda /ˈkaɪndə/','🔹 核心意思\r\n\r\nkind of 在口语里最常见有两个意思：\r\n\r\n1. 有点儿 / 稍微\r\n\r\n用来弱化语气，不说得太绝对。\r\n\r\nI’m kind of tired.\r\n我有点累。\r\n\r\nIt’s kind of difficult.\r\n这个有点难。\r\n\r\nI kind of like it.\r\n我有点喜欢它。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 某种类型的 / 一种\r\n\r\n这里是字面意思，表示“种类”。\r\n\r\nWhat kind of food do you like?\r\n你喜欢什么类型的食物？\r\n\r\nThis is a kind of software tool.\r\n这是一种软件工具。\r\n\r\n🧩 拆开理解\r\n\r\nkind = 种类 / 类型\r\nof = ……的\r\n\r\n所以字面上：\r\n\r\nkind of = 一种……\r\n\r\n但在口语中，经常变成：\r\n\r\nkind of = 有点儿 / 算是 / 不是特别确定地说','🗣️ 口语高频用法\r\n\r\n✅ kind of + adjective\r\n\r\n有点……\r\n\r\nIt’s kind of expensive.\r\n这个有点贵。\r\n\r\nThe process is kind of confusing.\r\n这个流程有点让人困惑。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ kind of + verb\r\n\r\n有点想 / 算是做了\r\n\r\nI kind of understand.\r\n我有点明白了。\r\n\r\nI kind of agree with you.\r\n我有点同意你。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ kind of + noun\r\n\r\n一种……\r\n\r\nIt’s a kind of user testing.\r\n这是一种用户测试。\r\n\r\nThis is a kind of informal feedback.\r\n这是一种非正式反馈。\r\n\r\n🏢 放在职场句子里\r\n\r\nWe kind of tested it with friends and family.\r\n我们算是用朋友和家人做了一些测试。\r\n语气：比较随意，不太正式。\r\n\r\n更专业可以说：\r\n\r\nWe tested it informally with friends and family.\r\n我们和朋友家人做了非正式测试。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意\r\n\r\nkind of 很口语，适合聊天、会议中自然表达。\r\n但在正式报告、正式邮件中，最好少用。\r\n\r\n正式替换：\r\n\r\nkind of difficult → somewhat difficult\r\n有些困难\r\n\r\nkind of useful → somewhat useful\r\n有一定帮助\r\n\r\nkind of tested it → tested it informally\r\n非正式测试过\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ 最好记的一句话\r\n\r\nkind of = 有点儿 / 算是 / 某种类型的\r\n\r\n例句：\r\nI kind of understand it now.\r\n我现在有点明白了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/06577d13d74b4146a67698fd05deca7a.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-23 10:04:33',1,'2026-06-23 10:04:33'),(1379,19,82,'vocab','Feel free to start now','Feel free to start now','Feel free to start now','🔹 中文意思\r\n\r\n你现在可以开始了 / 请随时开始 / 不用客气，现在开始吧\r\n\r\n语气比较礼貌、友好，不是命令。','🧩 拆开理解\r\n\r\nfeel free to + 动词原形\r\n= 请随意做…… / 你可以放心做……\r\n\r\nstart now\r\n= 现在开始\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nFeel free to start now\r\n= 你可以现在开始了\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🗣️ 使用场景\r\n\r\n1. 面试 / 会议\r\n\r\nFeel free to start now.\r\n你现在可以开始了。\r\n\r\n比如面试官对你说：\r\n“你可以开始你的 presentation 了。”\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 项目 / 任务\r\n\r\nFeel free to start now if you’re ready.\r\n如果你准备好了，现在就可以开始。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 课堂 / 活动\r\n\r\nFeel free to start now. You have 10 minutes.\r\n现在可以开始了，你们有 10 分钟时间。','✅ 更自然的表达\r\n\r\n直接礼貌版\r\n\r\nFeel free to start now.\r\n你现在可以开始了。\r\n\r\n更温和版\r\n\r\nFeel free to start whenever you’re ready.\r\n你准备好了就可以开始。\r\n\r\n更口语版\r\n\r\nYou can start now.\r\n你现在可以开始。\r\n\r\n更正式版\r\n\r\nYou may begin now.\r\n你现在可以开始。\r\n适合考试、正式场合。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意\r\n\r\nFeel free to… 不是“感觉自由”的意思。\r\n它真正的意思是：\r\n\r\nDon’t hesitate to…\r\n不用犹豫，可以做……\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nFeel free to ask questions.\r\n有问题随时问。\r\n\r\nFeel free to contact me.\r\n请随时联系我。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ 最好记的一句话\r\n\r\nFeel free to start now = You can start now, no need to wait.\r\n你现在可以开始了，不用等。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/600c1debd9a94249b9008232dfbe56af.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-23 10:51:00',1,'2026-06-23 10:51:00'),(1380,19,83,'phrase','visually appealing','visually appealing','visually appealing','🔹 词性\r\n\r\nadjective phrase\r\n形容词短语\r\n\r\n🔹 中文意思\r\n\r\n视觉上有吸引力的 / 美观的 / 看起来好看的\r\n\r\n它用来形容一个设计、图片、网页、海报、产品等看起来舒服、有美感、吸引人。','🧩 拆开理解\r\n\r\n👁️ visually\r\n\r\n= 从视觉上看 / 外观上\r\n\r\n例：\r\nThe page is visually clear.\r\n这个页面视觉上很清晰。\r\n\r\n✨ appealing\r\n\r\n= 有吸引力的 / 让人喜欢的\r\n\r\n例：\r\nThe design is appealing.\r\n这个设计很吸引人。\r\n\r\n👁️ + ✨ visually appealing\r\n\r\n= 看起来很美观、很吸引人','✅ 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. 描述设计\r\n\r\nThe design is visually appealing.\r\n这个设计看起来很美观。\r\n\r\n2. 描述网页\r\n\r\nThe website is clean and visually appealing.\r\n这个网站很干净，也很有视觉吸引力。\r\n\r\n3. 描述图片 / 海报\r\n\r\nThe poster should be visually appealing and easy to read.\r\n这个海报应该美观，而且容易阅读。\r\n\r\n4. 描述作品\r\n\r\nYour presentation looks more visually appealing now.\r\n你的演示文稿现在看起来更美观了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🏢 职场自然表达\r\n\r\nWe want the interface to be simple, clear, and visually appealing.\r\n我们希望这个界面简单、清晰，而且视觉上有吸引力。\r\n\r\nThe layout is functional, but it could be more visually appealing.\r\n这个布局功能上没问题，但可以更美观一些。\r\n\r\n🔁 近义表达\r\n\r\nattractive\r\n有吸引力的，好看的\r\n\r\nbeautiful-looking\r\n看起来漂亮的\r\n\r\nwell-designed\r\n设计得好的\r\n\r\npolished\r\n精致的、完成度高的\r\n\r\nprofessional-looking\r\n看起来专业的\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ 最好记的一句话\r\n\r\nvisually appealing = nice to look at\r\n看起来好看、有吸引力。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c0bab9fc37d04004a5c4bca50d800b33.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-23 11:08:10',1,'2026-06-23 11:08:10'),(1381,19,84,'vocab','appeal','appeal','appeal','🔹 词性\r\n\r\nverb / noun\r\n动词 / 名词\r\n\r\n1. 动词：appeal = 有吸引力 / 吸引\r\n\r\n中文意思\r\n\r\n吸引某人 / 对某人有吸引力\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\nappeal to + someone\r\n= 对某人有吸引力\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nThis design appeals to young users.\r\n这个设计对年轻用户有吸引力。\r\n\r\nThe idea doesn’t really appeal to me.\r\n这个想法对我没有太大吸引力。\r\n\r\nSimple and clean layouts appeal to many users.\r\n简单干净的布局吸引很多用户。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 名词：appeal = 吸引力\r\n\r\n中文意思\r\n\r\n吸引力 / 魅力\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nThe product has strong visual appeal.\r\n这个产品有很强的视觉吸引力。\r\n\r\nThe app’s appeal comes from its simple design.\r\n这个 app 的吸引力来自它简单的设计。\r\n\r\n3. 另一个意思：appeal = 呼吁 / 上诉\r\n\r\n这个意思也常见，但和 visually appealing 里的意思不一样。\r\n\r\nappeal for help\r\n\r\n呼吁帮助\r\n\r\nThey appealed for support.\r\n他们呼吁支持。\r\n\r\nappeal against a decision\r\n\r\n对决定提出上诉 / 申诉\r\n\r\nHe appealed against the decision.\r\n他对这个决定提出了上诉。','🧩 和 appealing 的关系\r\n\r\nappeal = 吸引\r\nappealing = 有吸引力的\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nThe design appeals to users.\r\n这个设计吸引用户。\r\n\r\nThe design is appealing.\r\n这个设计很有吸引力。\r\n\r\nThe design is visually appealing.\r\n这个设计在视觉上很有吸引力。','⚠️ 注意\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\nThe design is visually appeal. ❌\r\n\r\n要说：\r\n\r\nThe design is visually appealing. ✅\r\n这个设计视觉上很有吸引力。\r\n\r\n或者：\r\n\r\nThe design has visual appeal. ✅\r\n这个设计有视觉吸引力。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ 最好记的一句话\r\n\r\nappeal to someone = attract someone / make someone interested\r\n吸引某人，让某人感兴趣。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8a2db9124e684f119227fec8e437910e.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-23 11:21:01',1,'2026-06-23 11:21:01'),(1382,19,85,'phrase','raise a ticket','raise a ticket','raise a ticket','短语\r\n提交工单 / 创建问题单 / 发起支持请求\r\n\r\n常用于 IT、客服、系统维护、bug 反馈、内部支持流程。','3. 常见场景\r\n\r\nIT 问题\r\n\r\nI’ll raise a ticket with IT.\r\n我会向 IT 部门提交一个工单。\r\n\r\n系统 bug\r\n\r\nCan you raise a ticket for this bug?\r\n你能为这个 bug 提交一个工单吗？\r\n\r\n客服支持\r\n\r\nThe customer raised a ticket about the payment issue.\r\n客户针对付款问题提交了一个工单。\r\n\r\n项目管理\r\n\r\nLet’s raise a ticket so we can track this properly.\r\n我们提交一个工单吧，这样可以正式跟踪这个问题。','4. 职场更自然表达\r\n\r\n✅ raise a ticket\r\n提交一个工单，英式/新西兰职场常见\r\n\r\n✅ create a ticket\r\n创建一个工单，更通用\r\n\r\n✅ submit a support ticket\r\n提交支持请求，比较正式\r\n\r\n✅ log a ticket\r\n登记一个工单，也常见于 IT 支持\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n5. 不自然说法\r\n\r\n❌ raise ticket\r\n少了 a，不自然。\r\n\r\n✅ raise a ticket\r\n✅ raise the ticket\r\n✅ raise this as a ticket\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n6. 你可以这样说\r\n\r\nI’ll raise a ticket for this issue.\r\n我会为这个问题提交一个工单。\r\n\r\nCould you please raise a ticket for me?\r\n你能帮我提交一个工单吗？\r\n\r\nI raised a ticket yesterday, but I haven’t received any update yet.\r\n我昨天提交了一个工单，但还没有收到任何更新。\r\n\r\nThis should be raised as a ticket so the support team can investigate it.\r\n这个应该提交成工单，这样支持团队可以调查。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/5cccdf0e8e3e4c58a4992b81e108f1ff.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-24 08:30:46',1,'2026-06-24 08:30:46'),(1383,19,86,'vocab','streamline','streamline','streamline','verb 动词\r\n使……更高效；简化流程；优化\r\n\r\nnoun 名词\r\n流线型；流畅的形状\r\n但在职场里最常见的是动词。\r\n\r\nstreamline = make a process simpler, faster, and more efficient\r\n\r\n中文可以理解为：\r\n\r\n简化流程 / 优化流程 / 提高效率 / 精简步骤','近义表达\r\n\r\nsimplify\r\n简化，比较通用\r\n\r\nimprove efficiency\r\n提高效率\r\n\r\noptimize\r\n优化，偏技术/系统\r\n\r\nmake something more efficient\r\n让某事更高效，口语自然','常见搭配\r\n\r\nstreamline the process\r\n优化流程 / 简化流程\r\n\r\nstreamline the workflow\r\n优化工作流程\r\n\r\nstreamline operations\r\n优化运营\r\n\r\nstreamline communication\r\n简化沟通流程\r\n\r\nstreamline the system\r\n优化系统\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n6. 职场例句\r\n\r\nWe need to streamline the approval process.\r\n我们需要优化审批流程。\r\n\r\nThis tool helps streamline our daily workflow.\r\n这个工具可以帮助我们优化日常工作流程。\r\n\r\nThe new system streamlines data entry and reduces manual work.\r\n新系统简化了数据录入，并减少了人工操作。\r\n\r\nWe are trying to streamline communication between different teams.\r\n我们正在努力简化不同团队之间的沟通流程。\r\n\r\nWe want to streamline this workflow.\r\n我们想优化这个工作流程。\r\n\r\nThe goal is to streamline the process and reduce duplication.\r\n目标是简化流程并减少重复工作。\r\n\r\nCan we streamline this part of the system?\r\n我们能不能优化系统的这一部分？','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f527028e55d8432fb83ba2e8af594ed0.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-24 09:09:23',1,'2026-06-24 09:09:23'),(1384,19,87,'vocab','indicator','indicator','indicator','noun 名词\r\n\r\n中文意思：\r\n指标 / 指示器 / 信号 / 标志 / 显示某种情况的东西\r\n\r\nindicator = something that shows or suggests a situation\r\n\r\n也就是：\r\n\r\n👉 一个能“显示情况”的东西\r\n👉 一个帮助你判断状态的信号或数据\r\n\r\n拆开记忆\r\n\r\nindicate = 表明 / 指示\r\n-or = 做某事的人或东西\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nindicator\r\n= something that indicates something\r\n= 能表明某种情况的东西\r\n\r\n记忆画面：\r\n🚗 汽车仪表盘上的小灯亮了\r\n👉 它不是问题本身，但它提示你有问题\r\n这就是 indicator。','常见用法 Common Uses\r\n\r\n📈 数据 / 报告中：指标\r\n\r\nindicator = metric / measure\r\n\r\nSales volume is a key indicator of business growth.\r\n销售量是业务增长的一个关键指标。\r\n\r\nCustomer satisfaction is an important indicator of service quality.\r\n客户满意度是服务质量的重要指标。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🖥️ 系统 / 仪表盘中：指示器\r\n\r\nindicator = signal / status light\r\n\r\nA red indicator means there is an error.\r\n红色指示器表示有错误。\r\n\r\nThe dashboard shows several system health indicators.\r\n仪表盘显示了几个系统健康指标。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n👀 生活 / 现象中：迹象，信号\r\n\r\nindicator = sign\r\n\r\nLow attendance can be an indicator of low engagement.\r\n出勤率低可能是参与度低的一个信号。\r\n\r\nBody language is often an indicator of how someone feels.\r\n肢体语言通常能反映一个人的感受。\r\n\r\n常见搭配 Collocations\r\n\r\n✅ key indicator\r\n关键指标\r\n\r\n✅ performance indicator\r\n绩效指标\r\n\r\n✅ economic indicator\r\n经济指标\r\n\r\n✅ health indicator\r\n健康指标 / 系统健康指标\r\n\r\n✅ risk indicator\r\n风险指标\r\n\r\n✅ status indicator\r\n状态指示器\r\n\r\n✅ leading indicator\r\n先行指标，提前反映趋势\r\n\r\n✅ lagging indicator\r\n滞后指标，事情发生后才反映结果','职场例句\r\n\r\n📊 项目 / 数据\r\n\r\nWe use several indicators to measure project progress.\r\n我们使用几个指标来衡量项目进展。\r\n\r\n🖥️ 系统状态\r\n\r\nThis indicator helps us understand the system status.\r\n这个指标帮助我们了解系统状态。\r\n\r\n📈 业务分析\r\n\r\nThis number is not a perfect indicator, but it gives us a useful signal.\r\n这个数字不是完美的指标，但能给我们一个有用的信号。\r\n\r\n👥 用户参与度\r\n\r\nWhat indicators do you use to track user engagement?\r\n你们用哪些指标来跟踪用户参与度？','/static/uploads/english_note_item/036f5381d0c1449c9766ff5fc111d50c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-24 09:44:39',1,'2026-06-24 09:44:39'),(1385,19,88,'vocab','hand over','hand over','hand over','词性\r\n\r\nphrasal verb 短语动词\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 核心意思\r\n\r\nhand over = give something to someone else / transfer responsibility\r\n\r\n中文常见意思：\r\n\r\n交给 / 移交 / 交接 / 转交 / 把责任或控制权交给别人\r\n\r\nhand over\r\n= 用手把东西递过去\r\n后来引申为：\r\n👉 把任务、责任、权力、文件、系统等交给别人','hand over the project\r\n交接项目\r\n\r\n✅ hand over the work\r\n交接工作\r\n\r\n✅ hand over the documents\r\n转交文件\r\n\r\n✅ hand over responsibility\r\n移交责任\r\n\r\n✅ hand over control\r\n移交控制权\r\n\r\n✅ hand over to someone\r\n交给某人\r\n\r\n✅ handover document\r\n交接文档\r\n\r\n✅ handover meeting\r\n交接会议\r\n\r\nhand over vs hand in\r\n\r\n🤝 hand over\r\n\r\n强调：交给另一个人 / 移交责任或控制权\r\n\r\nI handed over the project to Sarah.\r\n我把项目交接给了 Sarah。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n📝 hand in\r\n\r\n强调：提交作业、表格、申请等\r\n\r\nI handed in my assignment yesterday.\r\n我昨天提交了作业。\r\n\r\nI’ll hand it over to you now.\r\n现在我把它交给你。\r\n\r\nLet me hand over to my colleague.\r\n我把接下来的部分交给我的同事。\r\n\r\nWe need to complete the handover by Friday.\r\n我们需要在周五前完成交接。\r\n\r\nCan you walk me through the handover process?\r\n你能带我了解一下交接流程吗？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 小贴士\r\n\r\n在会议里经常听到：\r\n\r\nI’ll hand over to Jack.\r\n意思是：\r\n我接下来把话交给 Jack。\r\n\r\n不是“把 Jack 交出去”，而是：\r\n👉 让 Jack 接着讲 / 接手下一部分。','📄 交文件 / 交东西\r\n\r\nPlease hand over the documents to the manager.\r\n请把文件交给经理。\r\n\r\nHe handed over the keys to the new tenant.\r\n他把钥匙交给了新租客。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 工作交接\r\n\r\nI’ll hand over the project to my colleague next week.\r\n我下周会把这个项目交接给我的同事。\r\n\r\nWe need to hand over the system before the deadline.\r\n我们需要在截止日期前移交这个系统。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧑‍💻 IT / 项目场景\r\n\r\nThe developer handed over the code to the support team.\r\n开发人员把代码交接给了支持团队。\r\n\r\nCan you prepare a handover document?\r\n你能准备一份交接文档吗？\r\n\r\n注意这里：\r\nhand over = 动词，交接\r\nhandover = 名词，交接 / 交接文档\r\n\r\n 职场例句\r\n\r\nI’ll hand over my tasks before I go on leave.\r\n我休假前会把任务交接好。\r\n\r\nCould you hand this over to the support team?\r\n你能把这个转交给支持团队吗？\r\n\r\nWe had a handover meeting this morning.\r\n我们今天早上开了一个交接会议。\r\n\r\nThe project has been handed over to the operations team.\r\n这个项目已经移交给运营团队了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/48d34db7cbfc435ea58c06999bfaed1a.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-24 09:57:53',1,'2026-06-24 09:57:53'),(1386,19,89,'sentence','Technology is not behaving this morning.','Technology is not behaving this morning.','Technology is not behaving this morning.','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nTechnology is not behaving this morning.\r\n= The computer, internet, software, or devices are not working properly this morning.\r\n\r\n中文意思：\r\n\r\n今天早上这些电子设备/系统不太听话。\r\n今天早上技术设备一直出问题。\r\n\r\n⚖️ behave vs work\r\n\r\nbehave\r\n\r\n更像拟人化表达，语气轻松自然。\r\n常用于设备、系统“不听话”。\r\n\r\nMy laptop is not behaving.\r\n我的电脑不太听话。\r\n\r\nwork\r\n\r\n更直接，表示“工作/运行”。\r\n\r\nMy laptop is not working.\r\n我的电脑不能用了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🗣️ 你可以这样说\r\n\r\nSorry, technology is not behaving today.\r\n不好意思，今天设备不太听话。\r\n\r\nMy internet is not behaving this morning.\r\n今天早上我的网络不太稳定。\r\n\r\nThe system is not behaving properly.\r\n系统不太正常。\r\n\r\nGive me a second — my screen sharing isn’t behaving.\r\n给我一下，我的屏幕共享不太正常。','🧠 拆开理解\r\n\r\ntechnology = 技术设备 / 系统 / 软件 / 网络\r\nbehave = 表现好 / 听话 / 正常运行\r\nnot behaving = 不听话 / 不正常工作\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nTechnology is not behaving this morning.\r\n= 今天早上电脑、网络或系统不太正常。\r\n\r\n🤖 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象你的电脑、打印机、网络都像小孩子一样：\r\n\r\n💻 电脑卡住\r\n🖨️ 打印机不工作\r\n📶 网络断断续续\r\n🎤 麦克风没声音\r\n\r\n你就可以说：\r\n\r\nTechnology is not behaving this morning.\r\n今天早上这些设备不听话。\r\n\r\n🔗 常见搭配\r\n\r\n✅ not behaving properly\r\n不太正常 / 没有正常工作\r\n\r\n✅ not behaving as expected\r\n没有按预期运行\r\n\r\n✅ the system is not behaving\r\n系统不正常\r\n\r\n✅ my laptop is not behaving\r\n我的电脑不太正常\r\n\r\n✅ the Wi-Fi is not behaving\r\nWi-Fi 不太稳定\r\n\r\n✅ the screen sharing is not behaving\r\n屏幕共享不正常\r\n\r\n⭐ 小贴士\r\n\r\n这句话很适合会议开场时用，语气比 “There is a technical problem” 更轻松、更自然。\r\n\r\n正式一点可以说：\r\n\r\nWe’re experiencing some technical issues this morning.\r\n我们今天早上遇到了一些技术问题。','🖥️ 电脑卡住\r\n\r\nMy laptop is not behaving today.\r\n我电脑今天不太正常。\r\n\r\n📶 网络不好\r\n\r\nThe Wi-Fi isn’t behaving this morning.\r\n今天早上 Wi-Fi 不太稳定。\r\n\r\n🎤 会议设备出问题\r\n\r\nSorry, my microphone is not behaving.\r\n不好意思，我的麦克风不太正常。\r\n\r\n🖨️ 打印机出问题\r\n\r\nThe printer is not behaving again.\r\n打印机又不听话了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 职场例句\r\n\r\nSorry, technology is not behaving this morning. Give me a second.\r\n不好意思，今天早上设备有点不听话。给我一点时间。\r\n\r\nThe screen sharing isn’t behaving properly. I’ll try again.\r\n屏幕共享不太正常，我再试一下。\r\n\r\nThe system isn’t behaving as expected.\r\n系统没有按预期运行。\r\n\r\nMy camera doesn’t seem to be behaving. Can you see me now?\r\n我的摄像头好像不太正常。你现在能看到我吗？','/static/uploads/english_note_item/823b2c1507ad4fcc9233e331a3bdb4af.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-24 10:55:11',1,'2026-06-24 10:55:11'),(1387,19,90,'sentence','Technology is not behaving this morning.','Technology is not behaving this morning.','Technology is not behaving this morning.','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nTechnology is not behaving this morning.\r\n= The computer, internet, software, or devices are not working properly this morning.\r\n\r\n中文意思：\r\n\r\n今天早上这些电子设备/系统不太听话。\r\n今天早上技术设备一直出问题。\r\n⚖️ behave vs work\r\n\r\nbehave\r\n\r\n更像拟人化表达，语气轻松自然。\r\n常用于设备、系统“不听话”。\r\n\r\nMy laptop is not behaving.\r\n我的电脑不太听话。\r\n\r\nwork\r\n\r\n更直接，表示“工作/运行”。\r\n\r\nMy laptop is not working.\r\n我的电脑不能用了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🗣️ 你可以这样说\r\n\r\nSorry, technology is not behaving today.\r\n不好意思，今天设备不太听话。\r\n\r\nMy internet is not behaving this morning.\r\n今天早上我的网络不太稳定。\r\n\r\nThe system is not behaving properly.\r\n系统不太正常。\r\n\r\nGive me a second — my screen sharing isn’t behaving.\r\n给我一下，我的屏幕共享不太正常。','🧠 拆开理解\r\n\r\ntechnology = 技术设备 / 系统 / 软件 / 网络\r\nbehave = 表现好 / 听话 / 正常运行\r\nnot behaving = 不听话 / 不正常工作\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nTechnology is not behaving this morning.\r\n= 今天早上电脑、网络或系统不太正常。\r\n\r\n🤖 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象你的电脑、打印机、网络都像小孩子一样：\r\n\r\n💻 电脑卡住\r\n🖨️ 打印机不工作\r\n📶 网络断断续续\r\n🎤 麦克风没声音\r\n\r\n你就可以说：\r\n\r\nTechnology is not behaving this morning.\r\n今天早上这些设备不听话。\r\n\r\n🔗 常见搭配\r\n\r\n✅ not behaving properly\r\n不太正常 / 没有正常工作\r\n\r\n✅ not behaving as expected\r\n没有按预期运行\r\n\r\n✅ the system is not behaving\r\n系统不正常\r\n\r\n✅ my laptop is not behaving\r\n我的电脑不太正常\r\n\r\n✅ the Wi-Fi is not behaving\r\nWi-Fi 不太稳定\r\n\r\n✅ the screen sharing is not behaving\r\n屏幕共享不正常\r\n\r\n⭐ 小贴士\r\n\r\n这句话很适合会议开场时用，语气比 “There is a technical problem” 更轻松、更自然。\r\n\r\n正式一点可以说：\r\n\r\nWe’re experiencing some technical issues this morning.\r\n我们今天早上遇到了一些技术问题。','🖥️ 电脑卡住\r\n\r\nMy laptop is not behaving today.\r\n我电脑今天不太正常。\r\n\r\n📶 网络不好\r\n\r\nThe Wi-Fi isn’t behaving this morning.\r\n今天早上 Wi-Fi 不太稳定。\r\n\r\n🎤 会议设备出问题\r\n\r\nSorry, my microphone is not behaving.\r\n不好意思，我的麦克风不太正常。\r\n\r\n🖨️ 打印机出问题\r\n\r\nThe printer is not behaving again.\r\n打印机又不听话了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 职场例句\r\n\r\nSorry, technology is not behaving this morning. Give me a second.\r\n不好意思，今天早上设备有点不听话。给我一点时间。\r\n\r\nThe screen sharing isn’t behaving properly. I’ll try again.\r\n屏幕共享不太正常，我再试一下。\r\n\r\nThe system isn’t behaving as expected.\r\n系统没有按预期运行。\r\n\r\nMy camera doesn’t seem to be behaving. Can you see me now?\r\n我的摄像头好像不太正常。你现在能看到我吗？','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3d60279412ff4963a27cd415b5b98ee1.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-24 10:58:12',1,'2026-06-24 10:58:12'),(1388,19,91,'vocab','comment on','comment on','comment on','词性\r\n\r\nphrasal verb / verb phrase 动词短语\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🎯 3. 核心意思\r\n\r\ncomment on = give an opinion or explanation about something\r\n\r\n中文意思：\r\n\r\n评论…… / 评价…… / 对……发表看法 / 解释说明一下……\r\n\r\n重点是：\r\n👉 针对某个话题、问题、数据、情况，说出你的看法或解释。\r\n\r\ncomment = 评论 / 发表意见\r\non = 关于 / 针对\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncomment on something\r\n= 针对某事发表看法\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nCan you comment on this issue?\r\n你能对这个问题发表一下看法吗？','🔗 6. 常见搭配\r\n\r\n✅ comment on the issue\r\n对这个问题发表看法\r\n\r\n✅ comment on the result\r\n评论 / 解释结果\r\n\r\n✅ comment on the progress\r\n评价进展\r\n\r\n✅ comment on the proposal\r\n评价提案\r\n\r\n✅ comment on the design\r\n评价设计\r\n\r\n✅ comment on the data\r\n解释 / 评论数据\r\n\r\n✅ comment on why/how…\r\n解释为什么 / 如何……\r\n\r\n⚖️ 8. comment on vs explain\r\n\r\n💬 comment on\r\n\r\n强调：发表看法 / 给出评价 / 简单说明\r\n语气比较开放，适合会议提问。\r\n\r\nCan you comment on the proposal?\r\n你能对这个提案谈谈看法吗？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧾 explain\r\n\r\n强调：解释清楚原因、过程或细节\r\n更直接要求对方讲明白。\r\n\r\nCan you explain the proposal?\r\n你能解释一下这个提案吗？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🗣️ 9. 你可以这样说\r\n\r\nCan you comment on that?\r\n你能对此说说看法吗？\r\n\r\nCould you comment on this part?\r\n你能对这一部分发表一下看法吗？\r\n\r\nWould you be able to comment on the workflow?\r\n你能对这个工作流程说说看法吗？\r\n\r\nCan you comment on how this data flows into the ERP system?\r\n你能说明一下这些数据是如何流入 ERP 系统的吗？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ 小贴士\r\n\r\n在职场会议里，comment on 比 explain 更委婉。\r\n\r\n比如你想问客户系统流程，不想显得太强硬，可以说：\r\n\r\nCould you comment on how the approval process works?\r\n您能简单说明一下审批流程是怎么运作的吗？','常见用法 Common Uses\r\n\r\n💼 会议 / 工作中\r\n\r\nCan you comment on the current progress?\r\n你能评论一下目前的进展吗？\r\n\r\nCould you comment on this proposal?\r\n你能对这个提案发表一下看法吗？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n📊 数据 / 报告中\r\n\r\nCan you comment on these numbers?\r\n你能解释一下这些数字吗？\r\n\r\nThe manager commented on the sales performance.\r\n经理对销售表现进行了评价。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧑‍💻 IT / 项目场景\r\n\r\nCan you comment on the system design?\r\n你能对这个系统设计说说看法吗？\r\n\r\nCould you comment on why this issue happened?\r\n你能解释一下为什么会出现这个问题吗？\r\n\r\n💼 7. 职场例句\r\n\r\nCould you comment on the current status of the project?\r\n你能说明一下项目目前的状态吗？\r\n\r\nCan you comment on the main risks here?\r\n你能谈一下这里的主要风险吗？\r\n\r\nWould you be able to comment on how the system handles user data?\r\n你能解释一下系统是如何处理用户数据的吗？\r\n\r\nI can’t really comment on that at the moment.\r\n我现在不太方便对此发表意见。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9b85f631bb5d4118b1188ef18f2194e0.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-24 11:08:23',1,'2026-06-24 11:08:23'),(1389,19,92,'sentence','So, as we said at the workshop, that’s not something that we encourage as good practice, but you seem to have made it work, so that’s good.','So, as we said at the workshop, that’s not something that we encourage as good practice, but you seem to have made it work, so that’s good.','So, as we said at the workshop, that’s not something that we encourage as good practice, but you seem to have made it work, so that’s good.','所以，正如我们在 workshop 里说过的那样，这种做法并不是我们鼓励的良好实践。不过你看起来已经把它做成功了，所以也挺好的。\r\n\r\n核心语气\r\n\r\n这句话的语气是：\r\n\r\n委婉提醒 + 轻微保留 + 认可结果\r\n\r\n不是强烈批评，而是说：\r\n\r\n“方法不太推荐，但你确实做出来了。”','4. 拆开理解\r\n\r\nas we said at the workshop\r\n\r\n正如我们在 workshop 里说过的\r\n\r\n这里的 as = 正如 / 像……一样\r\n\r\nAs we discussed earlier, …\r\n正如我们之前讨论过的……\r\n\r\nthat’s not something that we encourage\r\n\r\n这不是我们鼓励的事情\r\n\r\n更自然理解：\r\n\r\nWe don’t usually recommend doing it this way.\r\n我们通常不推荐这样做。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nas good practice\r\n\r\n作为良好实践 / 推荐做法\r\n\r\ngood practice = 好的做法，规范做法\r\n在技术、项目、学习中很常见。\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nUsing clear variable names is good practice.\r\n使用清晰的变量名是一种好习惯 / 好做法。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nyou seem to have made it work\r\n\r\n你看起来已经让它成功运行了\r\n\r\nmake something work = 让某事可行 / 让某物正常运行\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nI finally made the code work.\r\n我终于让代码跑起来了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nso that’s good\r\n\r\n所以这也不错\r\n\r\n这里是在认可结果：\r\n\r\n方法不一定标准，但结果是可以的。\r\n\r\n🧾 简单回应\r\n\r\nThanks, I understand. I’ll keep that in mind for next time.\r\n谢谢，我明白了。下次我会注意这一点。\r\n\r\n更职场一点\r\n\r\nThanks for the feedback. I understand it may not be the recommended approach, and I’ll try to follow the suggested practice next time.\r\n谢谢您的反馈。我明白这可能不是推荐做法，下次我会尽量按照建议的实践来做。\r\n\r\n如果你想解释一下\r\n\r\nThanks, I understand. I used this approach to make it work within the time available, but I’ll review the recommended practice and improve it next time.\r\n谢谢，我明白。我是为了在有限时间内让它先跑通才用了这个方法，但我会查看推荐做法，下次改进。','重点短语\r\n\r\n✅ as we said at the workshop\r\n正如我们在 workshop 里说过的\r\n\r\n✅ encourage as good practice\r\n鼓励作为良好实践\r\n\r\n✅ good practice\r\n好的做法 / 推荐做法 / 规范做法\r\n\r\n✅ make it work\r\n让它可行 / 让它正常运行\r\n\r\n✅ you seem to have…\r\n你看起来已经……','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f084885e7a884fcc93f4aa189bc08ea2.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-24 11:16:23',1,'2026-06-24 11:16:23'),(1390,19,93,'phrase','🔮 This is going to be…','🔮 This is going to be…','🔮 This is going to be…','1. 发音\r\n\r\nThis is going to be…\r\n/ðɪs ɪz ˈɡoʊɪŋ tə bi/\r\n口语中常读成：This is gonna be…\r\n/ðɪs ɪz ˈɡʌnə bi/\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 词性\r\n\r\nsentence pattern 句型表达\r\n\r\n中文意思：\r\n\r\n这将会是……\r\n接下来会是……\r\n这个会变成/会成为……\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. 核心意思\r\n\r\nThis is going to be…\r\n= I expect this will be…\r\n\r\n表示你对接下来事情的判断、预测或提前说明。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a simple question.\r\n这会是一个简单的问题。\r\n\r\nThis is going to be difficult.\r\n这会有点难。','4. 拆开理解\r\n\r\nThis\r\n\r\n这个 / 这件事 / 接下来我要说的事\r\n\r\nis going to be\r\n\r\n将会是 / 很可能会是\r\n\r\na really straightforward question\r\n\r\n一个非常简单直接的问题\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a really straightforward question.\r\n= 我接下来要问一个非常简单直接的问题。\r\n\r\n6. 常见搭配\r\n\r\n✅ This is going to be easy.\r\n这会很简单。\r\n\r\n✅ This is going to be difficult.\r\n这会很难。\r\n\r\n✅ This is going to be quick.\r\n这会很快。\r\n\r\n✅ This is going to be a short meeting.\r\n这会是一个简短会议。\r\n\r\n✅ This is going to be a simple process.\r\n这会是一个简单流程。\r\n\r\n✅ This is going to be a really straightforward question.\r\n这会是一个非常直接的问题。\r\n\r\n8. going to be vs will be\r\n\r\ngoing to be\r\n\r\n更口语，更像“我已经预感/判断接下来会这样”。\r\n\r\nThis is going to be useful.\r\n这个会很有用。\r\n\r\nwill be\r\n\r\n更直接、更正式一点。\r\n\r\nThis will be useful.\r\n这会有用。\r\n\r\n在日常会议里，This is going to be… 很自然。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n9. 你可以这样说\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a really straightforward question.\r\n我接下来问一个非常简单直接的问题。\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a quick one.\r\n这个问题很快。\r\n\r\nThis is going to be more of a general question.\r\n这个更像是一个泛泛的问题。\r\n\r\nThis is going to be about the approval process.\r\n这个问题会关于审批流程。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n10. 小贴士\r\n\r\n在会议中，This is going to be… 常用来“提前铺垫”，让对方知道你接下来要问的问题类型。\r\n\r\n比如你想显得礼貌自然，可以说：\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a really straightforward question: how does the approval process work?\r\n我接下来问一个很简单直接的问题：审批流程是怎么运作的？','5. 常见用法\r\n\r\n🗣️ 提问前铺垫\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a quick question.\r\n我接下来问一个很快的问题。\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a straightforward question.\r\n我接下来问一个简单直接的问题。\r\n\r\n💼 会议中说明接下来内容\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a short update.\r\n接下来会是一个简短更新。\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a high-level overview.\r\n接下来会是一个高层次概览。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 提前提醒\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a bit tricky.\r\n这个可能会有点棘手。\r\n\r\nThis is going to be more complicated than expected.\r\n这可能会比预期更复杂。\r\n\r\n7. 职场例句\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a quick question about the workflow.\r\n我接下来会问一个关于工作流程的简单问题。\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a high-level question, not a technical one.\r\n这会是一个高层次的问题，不是技术细节问题。\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a short update on our progress.\r\n接下来我会简短更新一下我们的进展。\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a bit of a challenge, but we can handle it.\r\n这可能会有点挑战，但我们能处理。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b5103233ae8c4decb524539fd0d986f9.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-24 11:23:39',1,'2026-06-24 11:23:39'),(1391,19,94,'vocab','straightforward','straightforward','straightforward','词性\r\n\r\nadjective 形容词\r\n\r\n中文意思：\r\n\r\n简单直接的 / 清楚明了的 / 不复杂的 / 坦率的\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🎯 3. 核心意思\r\n\r\nstraightforward = simple, clear, and easy to understand or do\r\n\r\n也就是：\r\n\r\n👉 事情很清楚，没有绕来绕去\r\n👉 步骤不复杂，容易理解或完成\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 4. 拆开记忆\r\n\r\nstraight = 直的\r\nforward = 向前\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nstraightforward\r\n= straight + forward\r\n= 一条路直直往前走，没有弯路\r\n\r\n记忆画面：\r\n\r\n🛣️ 一条笔直的路\r\n➡️ 直接通向目的地\r\n= straightforward','常见搭配 Collocations\r\n\r\n✅ a straightforward question\r\n一个简单直接的问题\r\n\r\n✅ a straightforward process\r\n一个清楚简单的流程\r\n\r\n✅ a straightforward task\r\n一个简单明确的任务\r\n\r\n✅ a straightforward answer\r\n一个直接明了的回答\r\n\r\n✅ a straightforward explanation\r\n一个清楚明了的解释\r\n\r\n✅ quite straightforward\r\n相当简单 / 很清楚\r\n\r\n✅ fairly straightforward\r\n比较简单\r\n\r\n✅ not straightforward\r\n不简单 / 不太直接 / 比较复杂\r\n\r\n⚖️ 8. straightforward vs simple\r\n\r\nstraightforward\r\n\r\n强调：清楚、直接、没有复杂步骤\r\n\r\nThe process is straightforward.\r\n这个流程清楚简单。\r\n\r\nsimple\r\n\r\n强调：简单、不难\r\n\r\nThe process is simple.\r\n这个流程很简单。\r\n\r\n区别感觉：\r\n\r\nstraightforward 更适合职场、流程、解释、问题。\r\nsimple 更通用，口语更基础。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🗣️ 9. 你可以这样说\r\n\r\nThis is going to be a really straightforward question.\r\n我接下来要问一个非常简单直接的问题。\r\n\r\nIt’s quite straightforward.\r\n这个挺简单明了的。\r\n\r\nThe workflow is pretty straightforward.\r\n这个工作流程挺清楚的。\r\n\r\nI just need a straightforward explanation.\r\n我只需要一个清楚直接的解释。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ 小贴士\r\n\r\nstraightforward 在职场里很常用，语气比 easy 更专业。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThis is an easy question.\r\n这个问题很简单。\r\n\r\nThis is a straightforward question.\r\n这是一个简单直接的问题。\r\n\r\n第二句听起来更自然、更职场。','常见用法 Common Uses\r\n\r\n🗣️ 问题简单直接\r\n\r\nThis is a straightforward question.\r\n这是一个简单直接的问题。\r\n\r\n💼 流程清楚\r\n\r\nThe process is straightforward.\r\n这个流程很清楚 / 不复杂。\r\n\r\n🧑‍💻 操作简单\r\n\r\nThe setup is quite straightforward.\r\n这个设置过程很简单。\r\n\r\n👤 人很坦率\r\n\r\nHe is very straightforward.\r\n他很坦率 / 说话很直接。\r\n\r\n职场例句\r\n\r\nThis should be a straightforward task.\r\n这应该是一个很简单明确的任务。\r\n\r\nThe approval process is fairly straightforward.\r\n审批流程还算清楚简单。\r\n\r\nCould you give me a straightforward answer?\r\n你能给我一个直接明了的回答吗？\r\n\r\nIt’s not as straightforward as it looks.\r\n它没有看起来那么简单。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ef963ddab7904d4c95b84a737ee60508.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-24 11:36:37',1,'2026-06-24 11:36:37');
INSERT INTO `english_note_item` VALUES (1392,19,95,'vocab','dummy','dummy','dummy','n. / adj. / v.\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n假的、模拟的、占位用的，不是真正工作的东西。','🧪 1. dummy data\r\n\r\n假数据 / 测试数据\r\n\r\nWe used dummy data for the demo.\r\n我们演示时用了假数据。\r\n\r\n记忆：\r\n🧪 实验室里用“假样本”测试，不是真实数据。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🪪 2. dummy account\r\n\r\n测试账号 / 假账号\r\n\r\nCan we create a dummy account for testing?\r\n我们可以创建一个测试账号来测试吗？\r\n\r\n记忆：\r\n🪪 一张临时测试身份卡，不是真实用户。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💳 3. dummy payment\r\n\r\n模拟支付 / 假支付\r\n\r\nThe payment wasn’t real; it was a dummy payment.\r\n这次支付不是真的，只是模拟支付。\r\n\r\n记忆：\r\n💳 刷了一下“假银行卡”，页面显示成功，但钱没有真的转走。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧱 4. dummy version\r\n\r\n占位版本 / 临时版本\r\n\r\nThis is just a dummy version of the feature.\r\n这只是这个功能的临时占位版本。\r\n\r\n记忆：\r\n🧱 先放一块“积木”占位置，以后再换成真正功能。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🎭 5. dummy it / dummy it up\r\n\r\n临时做个假的 / 模拟一下\r\n\r\nWe didn’t integrate Stripe; we just dummied it.\r\n我们没有接入 Stripe，只是做了个假的模拟版本。\r\n\r\n记忆：\r\n🎭 功能戴上“假面具”，看起来像真的，但其实只是演示。','🧠 你那句话\r\n\r\nYou know, just kind of dummied it.\r\n\r\n自然翻译：\r\n你懂的，就是大概做了个假的模拟版本。\r\n就是先临时凑了个占位功能，没有真正完整实现。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔍 dummy vs mock\r\n\r\ndummy 🧱\r\n强调：假的、占位的、测试用的东西。\r\n常见：dummy data / dummy account / dummy payment\r\n\r\nmock 🪞\r\n强调：模拟真实功能，常用于开发和测试。\r\n常见：mock API / mock service / mockup\r\n\r\n例句：\r\nWe used dummy data.\r\n我们用了假数据。\r\n\r\nWe mocked the payment API.\r\n我们模拟了支付接口。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e34a6dcbce6849cf8e9f4fffa430a83e.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-25 09:39:21',1,'2026-06-25 09:39:21'),(1393,19,96,'phrase','There is no point','There is no point','There is no point','phrase 短语\r\n\r\n✅ 中文意思\r\n\r\n没有意义；没必要；没有用\r\n\r\n它不是说“没有点”，而是说：\r\n做某件事没有价值 / 不值得做。','🔧 常见结构\r\n\r\n1. There is no point.\r\n\r\n没有意义。/ 没必要。\r\n\r\n例句：\r\nThere is no point.\r\n这没有意义。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. There is no point in + doing something\r\n\r\n做某事没有意义 / 没必要做某事\r\n\r\n例句：\r\nThere is no point in asking again.\r\n再问一遍没有意义。\r\n\r\nThere is no point in arguing.\r\n争论没有意义。\r\n\r\nThere is no point in building a full payment system for a demo.\r\n为了一个演示去做完整支付系统没有意义。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. There is no point + sentence\r\n\r\n也可以接一个完整想法，但更常见还是用 in doing。\r\n\r\n例句：\r\nThere is no point if nobody uses it.\r\n如果没人用，那就没有意义。','✅ There is no point.\r\n\r\n这没有意义。\r\n\r\n✅ That’s pointless.\r\n\r\n那没有意义。\r\n\r\n✅ There’s not much point.\r\n\r\n没太大意义。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象你做了一个按钮：\r\n\r\nDonate $10\r\n\r\n但是它没有连接支付系统，也不会真的扣款。\r\n别人问：为什么还要做完整支付集成？\r\n\r\n你可以说：\r\n\r\nThere is no point in integrating real payment services for a simple demo.\r\n只是简单演示的话，接入真实支付服务没有意义。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔍 对比学习\r\n\r\nThere is no point in doing something\r\n\r\n强调：做这件事没有意义\r\n\r\nThere is no point in waiting.\r\n等下去没有意义。\r\n\r\nIt doesn’t make sense to do something\r\n\r\n强调：这样做不合理 / 逻辑上说不通\r\n\r\nIt doesn’t make sense to wait here all day.\r\n在这里等一整天不合理。\r\n\r\nThat’s pointless\r\n\r\n更直接，语气稍强：那很没意义 / 很无用\r\n\r\nThat’s pointless.\r\n那没意义。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d4be2423c0fa49f9aeaa663edb24801a.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-25 09:51:39',1,'2026-06-25 09:51:39'),(1394,19,97,'phrase','take all the credit','take all the credit','take all the credit','phrase 短语\r\n\r\n✅ 中文意思\r\n\r\n把所有功劳都揽到自己身上；独占功劳\r\n\r\n这里的 credit = 功劳 / 认可 / 表扬\r\n不是“信用卡”的 credit。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n一个团队一起完成了项目。\r\n大家都加班、写代码、测试、修 bug。\r\n\r\n结果开会时，一个人站起来说：\r\n\r\n“I did everything.”\r\n“全是我做的。”\r\n\r\n这就是：\r\n\r\nHe took all the credit.\r\n他把所有功劳都揽到自己身上了。','🔧 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. take all the credit\r\n\r\n独占所有功劳\r\n\r\nHe took all the credit.\r\n他把所有功劳都揽到自己身上了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. take credit for something\r\n\r\n把某事的功劳归到自己身上\r\n\r\nHe took credit for my idea.\r\n他把我的想法说成是他的功劳。\r\n\r\nMy manager took credit for my work.\r\n我经理把我的工作成果说成是他的功劳。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n3. give someone credit\r\n\r\n承认某人的功劳；给某人应有的认可\r\n\r\nYou should give her credit.\r\n你应该承认她的功劳。\r\n\r\nGive credit where credit is due.\r\n该是谁的功劳，就承认是谁的功劳。','🔍 对比学习\r\n\r\ntake credit\r\n\r\n把功劳算到自己身上\r\n\r\nHe took credit for the design.\r\n他把设计的功劳揽到自己身上。\r\n\r\nget credit\r\n\r\n得到认可 / 得到功劳\r\n\r\nShe didn’t get enough credit for her work.\r\n她的工作没有得到足够认可。\r\n\r\ngive credit\r\n\r\n给予认可 / 承认功劳\r\n\r\nWe should give credit to the whole team.\r\n我们应该承认整个团队的功劳。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n❌ 常见错误\r\n\r\n❌ He took all credits.\r\n\r\n不自然。这里一般用不可数 credit。\r\n\r\n✅ He took all the credit.\r\n\r\n他把所有功劳都揽到自己身上了。\r\n\r\n❌ He got all the credit by himself.\r\n\r\n不太自然。\r\n\r\n✅ He took all the credit for himself.\r\n\r\n他把所有功劳都归到自己身上了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/4e01d037a089401aa1bf390c9e27c424.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-25 09:58:41',1,'2026-06-25 09:58:41'),(1395,19,98,'phrase','be up to','be up to','be up to','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n在忙；在做；最近在搞什么\r\n\r\n这个短语非常口语，经常用来问别人近况。','🧩 1. What have you been up to?\r\n\r\n✅ 意思\r\n\r\n你最近在忙什么？\r\n\r\n这是最常见、最自然的用法。\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nWhat have you been up to lately?\r\n你最近在忙什么？\r\n\r\nGood to hear what you’ve been up to.\r\n很高兴听到你最近在忙什么 / 了解你的近况。\r\n\r\n🌟 口语感觉\r\n\r\n比 What did you do recently? 更自然。\r\n更像朋友、同事之间聊天。\r\n\r\n🛠️ 2. I’ve been up to…\r\n\r\n✅ 意思\r\n\r\n我最近在忙……\r\n\r\n不过注意：\r\n英语里更常说 I’ve been working on…\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nI’ve been up to a lot recently.\r\n我最近忙了很多事。\r\n\r\nI’ve been working on my industry project.\r\n我最近在做我的行业项目。\r\n\r\nI’ve been preparing for my internship.\r\n我最近在准备实习。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🕵️ 3. be up to something\r\n\r\n✅ 意思\r\n\r\n在搞什么；在偷偷做什么\r\n\r\n这个有时候带一点怀疑语气。\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nWhat are you up to?\r\n你在干嘛呢？\r\n\r\nHe looks suspicious. He’s up to something.\r\n他看起来很可疑，好像在搞什么事。\r\n\r\n🔍 对比学习\r\n\r\n🕒 What are you doing?\r\n\r\n你现在在做什么？\r\n重点：现在。\r\n\r\n📆 What have you been up to?\r\n\r\n你最近在忙什么？\r\n重点：最近这段时间。\r\n\r\n🕵️ What are you up to?\r\n\r\n你在干嘛呢？/ 你是不是在搞什么？\r\n根据语气，可能很普通，也可能有点怀疑。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 常见错误\r\n\r\n❌ What did you up to?\r\n\r\n不对。\r\n\r\n✅ What have you been up to?\r\n\r\n你最近在忙什么？\r\n\r\n❌ I am up to my project.\r\n\r\n不自然。\r\n\r\n✅ I’ve been working on my project.\r\n\r\n我最近在做项目。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象朋友好久没见你，问你：\r\n\r\n“What have you been up to?”\r\n\r\n他不是问你“站到哪里去了”，而是在问：\r\n\r\n“你最近都忙啥呢？”\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🗣️ 你可以这样回答\r\n\r\nNot much, just studying.\r\n没什么，就是学习。\r\n\r\nI’ve been pretty busy with uni.\r\n我最近学校挺忙的。\r\n\r\nI’ve been working on my project.\r\n我最近在做项目。\r\n\r\nI’ve been trying to improve my spoken English.\r\n我最近在努力提高英语口语。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a533630a96e34aabb53cd9ef382aa51d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-25 10:52:06',1,'2026-06-25 10:52:06'),(1396,19,99,'phrase','be meant to','be meant to','be meant to','phrase 短语\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n本来应该；原本打算；被认为应该\r\n\r\n它来自 mean 的过去分词 meant。\r\n在口语里，meant to 很常见。','🧩 1. be meant to = 应该 / 本来应该\r\n\r\n✅ 意思\r\n\r\n某件事按规则、计划、设计来说应该这样。\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nAre these meant to be closed?\r\n这些是不是本来应该关闭？\r\n\r\nIs this page meant to be public?\r\n这个页面本来应该是公开的吗？\r\n\r\nThe button is meant to submit the form.\r\n这个按钮应该是用来提交表单的。\r\n\r\nThis feature is meant to help users donate more easily.\r\n这个功能是为了帮助用户更容易捐赠。\r\n\r\n🧩 1. be meant to = 应该 / 本来应该\r\n\r\n✅ 意思\r\n\r\n某件事按规则、计划、设计来说应该这样。\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nAre these meant to be closed?\r\n这些是不是本来应该关闭？\r\n\r\nIs this page meant to be public?\r\n这个页面本来应该是公开的吗？\r\n\r\nThe button is meant to submit the form.\r\n这个按钮应该是用来提交表单的。\r\n\r\nThis feature is meant to help users donate more easily.\r\n这个功能是为了帮助用户更容易捐赠。\r\n\r\n🛠️ 2. be meant to do something = 应该做某事 / 被设计来做某事\r\n\r\n✅ 意思\r\n\r\n强调：设计目的 / 预期用途\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nThis system is meant to reduce manual work.\r\n这个系统是为了减少人工操作。\r\n\r\nThe report is meant to show monthly sales data.\r\n这个报告是用来展示月度销售数据的。\r\n\r\nThe read-only account is meant to let us view the system safely.\r\n只读账号是为了让我们安全地查看系统。\r\n\r\n🧭 3. be meant to = 原本打算\r\n\r\n✅ 意思\r\n\r\n表示：本来计划要做，但可能没做成。\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nI was meant to call you yesterday, but I forgot.\r\n我昨天本来应该给你打电话，但我忘了。\r\n\r\nWe were meant to finish it last week.\r\n我们本来应该上周完成它。\r\n\r\nThe meeting was meant to start at 10.\r\n会议原本应该 10 点开始。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💞 4. be meant to be = 命中注定 / 注定如此\r\n\r\n✅ 意思\r\n\r\n这个用法比较情感化，常用于关系、人生安排。\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nMaybe it wasn’t meant to be.\r\n也许这件事本来就不该成。\r\n\r\nThey are meant to be together.\r\n他们是命中注定要在一起的。','🔍 对比学习\r\n\r\n🧱 meant to\r\n\r\n本来应该 / 设计目的 / 原本打算\r\n\r\nThis button is meant to save the file.\r\n这个按钮应该是用来保存文件的。\r\n\r\n📏 supposed to\r\n\r\n应该 / 按规定应该\r\n\r\nYou’re supposed to submit it by Friday.\r\n你应该周五前提交。\r\n\r\n🎯 intended to\r\n\r\n旨在 / 意图是\r\n\r\n更正式，常用于报告、文档、项目说明。\r\n\r\nThis feature is intended to improve usability.\r\n这个功能旨在提升可用性。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ 常见错误\r\n\r\n❌ This button meant to save the file.\r\n\r\n少了 is。\r\n\r\n✅ This button is meant to save the file.\r\n\r\n这个按钮是用来保存文件的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n❌ Are these mean to be closed?\r\n\r\n不对，应该用过去分词 meant。\r\n\r\n✅ Are these meant to be closed?\r\n\r\n这些是不是本来应该关闭？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象一个按钮写着 Submit，但点击后没有提交表单。\r\n你可以问开发者：\r\n\r\nIs this button meant to submit the form?\r\n这个按钮本来是用来提交表单的吗？\r\n\r\n也就是在问：\r\n\r\n它原本设计的目的是什么？','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8aa600c4a5eb42878395feb60c41a897.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-25 11:16:36',1,'2026-06-25 11:16:36'),(1397,19,100,'phrase','evolve into','evolve into','evolve into','逐渐发展成…… / 演变成……\r\n\r\n🔊 读音\r\nevolve into /ɪˈvɒlv ˈɪntuː/\r\n美式也常读：/ɪˈvɑːlv ˈɪntuː/\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思 Core Meaning\r\nto gradually develop or change into something else\r\n经过一段时间，慢慢发展成另一种形式、状态或结果。\r\n\r\n重点感觉：\r\n不是突然变成，而是 slowly change / gradually develop。','🧩 常见用法 Common Usage\r\n\r\n🌱 1. A evolve into B\r\nA 逐渐发展成 B\r\n\r\nA small idea evolved into a successful business.\r\n一个小想法逐渐发展成了一家成功的公司。\r\n\r\n🛠️ 2. a prototype / tool / system evolves into…\r\n原型、工具、系统逐渐升级成……\r\n\r\nThe simple prototype evolved into a complete platform.\r\n这个简单原型逐渐发展成了一个完整平台。\r\n\r\n🤝 3. friendship evolves into a relationship\r\n友谊逐渐发展成恋爱关系\r\n\r\nTheir friendship evolved into a romantic relationship.\r\n他们的友谊逐渐发展成了恋爱关系。\r\n\r\n🧬 4. species evolve into…\r\n物种进化成……\r\n\r\nSome animals evolved into different species over time.\r\n一些动物随着时间进化成了不同物种。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💬 例句 Examples\r\n\r\nIt started as a small project, but it evolved into a full business system.\r\n它一开始只是一个小项目，但后来逐渐发展成了一个完整的业务系统。\r\n\r\nOur initial idea evolved into a more practical solution after several discussions.\r\n经过几次讨论后，我们最初的想法逐渐发展成了一个更实用的解决方案。\r\n\r\nThe company evolved into a global brand.\r\n这家公司逐渐发展成了一个全球品牌。','⭐ 你的项目里可以这样说\r\n\r\nOur initial prototype evolved into a more complete platform with user management, reporting, and approval features.\r\n我们最初的原型逐渐发展成了一个更完整的平台，包含用户管理、报表和审批功能。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3ab5604123d74a7b8f1b57bba421d6ca.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-25 15:50:44',1,'2026-06-25 15:50:44'),(1398,19,101,'phrase','kick off','kick off','kick off','🎯 核心意思 Core Meaning\r\nto start something\r\n表示某件事情正式开始，常用于会议、项目、活动、比赛等。\r\n\r\n中文可以理解为：\r\n启动、开始、拉开序幕','🧩 常见用法 Common Usage\r\n\r\n🚀 1. kick off a meeting\r\n开始一个会议\r\n\r\nLet’s kick off the meeting.\r\n我们开始开会吧。\r\n\r\n📁 2. kick off a project\r\n启动一个项目\r\n\r\nWe will kick off the project next Monday.\r\n我们下周一启动这个项目。\r\n\r\n🎉 3. kick off an event\r\n拉开活动序幕\r\n\r\nThe festival kicked off with a music performance.\r\n这个节日以一场音乐表演拉开序幕。\r\n\r\n⚽ 4. kick off a game\r\n开球 / 比赛开始\r\n\r\nThe match kicks off at 7 p.m.\r\n比赛晚上 7 点开始。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💬 例句 Examples\r\n\r\nCan we kick off with a quick introduction?\r\n我们可以先从一个简短的自我介绍开始吗？\r\n\r\nThe workshop kicked off with a short presentation.\r\n这个 workshop 以一个简短的演示开始。\r\n\r\nBefore we kick off, does anyone have any questions?\r\n在我们开始之前，有人有问题吗？\r\n\r\n⚠️ 常见错误 Common Mistakes\r\n\r\n❌ Let’s kick off the work.\r\n✅ Let’s kick off the project.\r\n更自然。kick off 常接 project / meeting / event / session。\r\n\r\n❌ The meeting kicked off at 9 and finished at 10.\r\n✅ 可以，但更自然：The meeting started at 9 and finished at 10.\r\n如果只是普通描述时间，start 更常见；kick off 更有“正式启动”的感觉。\r\n\r\n❌ I kick off to learn English.\r\n✅ I started learning English.\r\n个人开始学习某事，一般不用 kick off。\r\n\r\nLet’s start the meeting.\r\n我们开始会议吧。\r\n➡️ 普通表达。\r\n\r\nLet’s kick off the meeting.\r\n我们正式开始会议吧。\r\n➡️ 更自然、更职场口语。\r\n\r\nWe launched a new product.\r\n我们发布了一个新产品。\r\n➡️ launch 更强调“推出”。','🧠 记忆画面 Memory Image\r\n\r\n想象足球比赛 ⚽\r\n裁判一吹哨，球员一脚把球踢出去。\r\n比赛正式开始。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nkick off = 像足球开球一样，正式开始一件事。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ 职场口语可以这样用\r\n\r\nShall we kick off with a quick overview of the project?\r\n我们先从项目概览开始，可以吗？\r\n\r\nI’ll kick off by walking you through the main workflow.\r\n我先带大家过一下主要流程。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/81c080d295b64e80991a1ea4e773a8aa.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-25 16:38:53',1,'2026-06-25 16:38:53'),(1399,19,102,'vocab','analytic','analytic','analytic','🏷️ 词性 Part of Speech\r\n\r\n1. adj. 形容词：分析的\r\n\r\n这是最常见用法。\r\n\r\nanalytic thinking\r\n分析性思维\r\n\r\nanalytic skills\r\n分析能力\r\n\r\nan analytic approach\r\n分析式方法\r\n\r\n🏷️ 词性 Part of Speech\r\n\r\n1. adj. 形容词：分析的\r\n\r\n这是最常见用法。\r\n\r\nanalytic thinking\r\n分析性思维\r\n\r\nanalytic skills\r\n分析能力\r\n\r\nan analytic approach\r\n分析式方法','🏷️ 1. analytic\r\n\r\nadj. 形容词：分析的 / 善于分析的\r\n也可作 noun 名词，但名词用法比较专业、少见。\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nShe has an analytic mind.\r\n她有很强的分析头脑。\r\n\r\nWe need an analytic approach to solve this problem.\r\n我们需要用分析式的方法来解决这个问题。\r\n\r\nThis role requires strong analytic thinking.\r\n这个岗位需要很强的分析性思维。\r\n\r\n🏷️ 2. analytical\r\n\r\nadj. 形容词：分析的 / 善于分析的\r\n比 analytic 更常用于职场表达，尤其是 analytical skills。\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nI have strong analytical skills.\r\n我有很强的分析能力。\r\n\r\nShe is very analytical when reviewing data.\r\n她在查看数据时很善于分析。\r\n\r\nThe company needs someone with an analytical mindset.\r\n公司需要一个有分析型思维的人。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🏷️ 3. analysis\r\n\r\nnoun 名词：分析\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nI did an analysis of the sales data.\r\n我对销售数据做了分析。\r\n\r\nThe report includes a detailed analysis of user behaviour.\r\n这份报告包含对用户行为的详细分析。\r\n\r\nBased on my analysis, the main issue is data quality.\r\n根据我的分析，主要问题是数据质量。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🏷️ 4. analyse / analyze\r\n\r\nverb 动词：分析\r\n🇬🇧 analyse = 英式拼写\r\n🇺🇸 analyze = 美式拼写\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nI need to analyse the data before making a decision.\r\n在做决定之前，我需要分析数据。\r\n\r\nWe analysed the system logs to find the root cause.\r\n我们分析了系统日志来找到根本原因。\r\n\r\nCan you analyze the customer feedback?\r\n你能分析一下客户反馈吗？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🏷️ 5. analytics\r\n\r\nnoun 名词：数据分析 / 分析学\r\n常用于技术、商业、报表、数据领域。\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nI’m interested in data analytics.\r\n我对数据分析感兴趣。\r\n\r\nThe platform provides real-time analytics.\r\n这个平台提供实时数据分析。\r\n\r\nBusiness analytics helps companies make better decisions.\r\n商业分析帮助公司做出更好的决策。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🏷️ 6. analyst\r\n\r\nnoun 名词：分析师\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nShe works as a business analyst.\r\n她是一名业务分析师。\r\n\r\nA data analyst needs strong SQL and communication skills.\r\n数据分析师需要很强的 SQL 和沟通能力。\r\n\r\nThe analyst prepared a report for the management team.\r\n这位分析师为管理团队准备了一份报告。\r\n\r\n\r\n✅ 所以你平时想表达“分析”这个名词，优先用：\r\n\r\nanalysis = 分析\r\nanalytics = 数据分析 / 分析学\r\nanalyst = 分析师','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/5947264b88c4466fa285f2eb8d66eea5.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-25 17:03:43',1,'2026-06-25 17:03:43'),(1400,19,103,'phrase','in the same email thread','in the same email thread','in the same email thread','🎯 核心意思 Core Meaning\r\n在同一个邮件对话里 / 在原来的邮件链里回复\r\n\r\n这里的 email thread 指的是一串相关邮件组成的“邮件对话链”。\r\n所以 in the same email thread 就是：\r\n不要重新开一封新邮件，而是在之前那封邮件下面点 Reply / Reply all 继续回复。','🧩 拆开理解\r\n\r\n📧 email = 邮件\r\n🧵 thread = 线、线索、连续的一串内容\r\n📨 email thread = 邮件链 / 邮件对话串\r\n🔁 same email thread = 同一个邮件链\r\n\r\n✅ 常见用法 Common Usage\r\n\r\n1. Please reply in the same email thread.\r\n    请在同一个邮件链里回复。\r\n2. I’ll send the update in the same email thread.\r\n    我会在同一个邮件链里发送更新。\r\n3. Could you keep everyone in the same email thread?\r\n    你能把大家都保留在同一个邮件链里吗？\r\n4. Don’t start a new email. Just reply in the same thread.\r\n    不要新建邮件，直接在原来的邮件链里回复。','⚠️ 容易犯错 Common Mistake\r\n\r\n❌ in the same email\r\n这个不够准确，听起来像“在同一封邮件里面”。\r\n\r\n✅ in the same email thread\r\n更准确，表示“同一个邮件对话链”。\r\n\r\n❌ on the same email thread\r\n有些人会说，但更自然、更常见的是：\r\n\r\n✅ in the same email thread\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面 Memory Image\r\n\r\n想象一串邮件像一根线 🧵：\r\n老师、你、Deborah、公司联系人都在这根线上。\r\n你如果 reply in the same email thread，就是继续把信息接在这根线上。\r\n如果你重新发新邮件，就像另开了一根线，别人可能看不到之前的上下文。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/599ac5898ce449739416f5ae2b247b62.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-26 08:02:29',1,'2026-06-26 08:02:29'),(1401,19,104,'phrase','lean over','lean over','lean over','/liːn ˈəʊvə/ 英式\r\n/liːn ˈoʊvər/ 美式\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思 Core Meaning\r\nlean over = 身体或物体向某个方向倾斜 / 探身过去 / 倾斜在……上方\r\n\r\n重点是：\r\n不是完全倒下，而是“斜着、偏向某处”。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面 Memory Image\r\n\r\n想象一棵树被风吹歪了，树冠已经伸到车库上方，但还没有完全倒下。\r\n这个状态就是：\r\n\r\nlean over = 斜着“探过去” / 倾斜在上方','🧩 常见用法 Common Usage\r\n\r\n🌳 1. 物体倾斜在某物上方\r\nA tree is leaning over my garage.\r\n一棵树正倾斜在我的车库上方。\r\n\r\n🧍 2. 人探身过去\r\nShe leaned over to pick up the phone.\r\n她俯身过去拿手机。\r\n\r\n🪟 3. 身体靠过去看/说话\r\nHe leaned over the table and whispered something.\r\n他探过桌子小声说了些什么。','💬 Example Sentences\r\n\r\n🌪️ After the storm, a tree was leaning over the garage.\r\n暴风雨后，一棵树倾斜在车库上方。\r\n\r\n👂 Could you lean over a bit? I can’t hear you clearly.\r\n你能稍微靠过来一点吗？我听不太清。\r\n\r\n📱 I leaned over to check the message on his phone.\r\n我探身过去看他手机上的消息。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ 常见错误 Common Mistakes\r\n\r\n❌ The tree is leaning on my garage.\r\n这句话更像是：树已经靠在车库上/压在车库上。\r\n\r\n✅ The tree is leaning over my garage.\r\n树是“倾斜在车库上方”，可能还没碰到车库。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8671c0d1a6114239af41c77605304987.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-06-29 09:20:11',1,'2026-06-29 09:20:11'),(1402,19,105,'vocab','novelty','novelty','novelty','1️⃣ 新奇的东西；新颖性 ⭐⭐⭐\r\nThe novelty of the new technology attracted many customers.\r\n这项新技术的新颖性吸引了很多客户。\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 新鲜感（短暂的兴趣） ⭐⭐⭐\r\nThe novelty soon wore off.\r\n新鲜感很快消失了。\r\n\r\n💡 wear off = 逐渐消失\r\n\r\n3️⃣ 小玩意；新奇商品 ⭐⭐\r\n\r\n通常指一些有趣但不一定实用的小物品。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n* funny toys\r\n* unusual gifts\r\n* creative gadgets\r\n\r\n例：\r\n\r\nThey sell novelty items at the gift shop.\r\n他们在礼品店卖一些新奇小商品。','🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n⭐ novelty item\r\n\r\n新奇商品 / 小玩意\r\n\r\nThis is just a novelty item, not a practical tool.\r\n这只是个新奇玩意，不是实用工具。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ novelty value\r\n\r\n新颖价值；新鲜感价值\r\n\r\nThe product has high novelty value but limited practical use.\r\n这个产品新颖性很高，但实际用途有限。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ the novelty of something\r\n\r\n某事物的新鲜感\r\n\r\nI enjoyed the novelty of working remotely.\r\n我很享受远程工作的新鲜感。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ wear off\r\n\r\n新鲜感消退\r\n\r\nAfter a few weeks, the novelty wore off.\r\n几周后，新鲜感消失了。','💬 工作/技术场景例句（适合你的软件背景）\r\n\r\nAI 项目：\r\n\r\nThe novelty of using AI in document processing attracted attention from customers.\r\n\r\nAI 用于文档处理的新颖性吸引了客户关注。\r\n\r\n软件设计：\r\n\r\nThe novelty of this approach is that it supports multiple OCR engines.\r\n\r\n这个方法的新颖之处在于它支持多个 OCR 引擎。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n一句话记忆：\r\n\r\nNovelty = something new, unusual, and interesting, especially because it is different from what people normally see.\r\n\r\n👉 novelty = 新奇感 / 新颖性 / 新奇物品','/static/uploads/english_note_item/111ad447f9be4e72b29e79fccdbf57b1.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-07-27 15:18:11',1,'2026-07-27 15:18:11'),(1403,19,106,'phrase','cruise through','cruise through','cruise through','🚢 核心意思\r\n\r\ncruise through = 轻松完成；顺利通过\r\n\r\nTo do something easily, without much difficulty.\r\n\r\n不费力地完成某事 / 轻松通过某个阶段','🧠 词源理解\r\n\r\n🚢 cruise = 平稳航行\r\n\r\n想象一艘邮轮：\r\n\r\n船不需要加速、不需要绕路，平稳地穿过海面。\r\n\r\n➡️ cruise through something\r\n= 像邮轮一样轻松穿过某件事情','① 📝 轻松通过考试、测试\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n* She cruised through the exam.\r\n\r\n她轻松通过了考试。\r\n\r\n意思：\r\n\r\nThe exam was very easy for her.\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n② 💻 轻松完成任务 / 工作\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n* The developer cruised through the coding task.\r\n\r\n这个开发人员轻松完成了编码任务。\r\n\r\n（软件工程中很常用）\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n③ 🏆 轻松赢得比赛\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n* The team cruised through the competition.\r\n\r\n这个队轻松赢得了比赛。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易混表达\r\n\r\n✅ cruise through\r\n\r\n强调：\r\n\r\n很容易，没有遇到困难\r\n\r\n* I cruised through the interview.\r\n    我很轻松地通过了面试。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ get through\r\n\r\n强调：\r\n\r\n完成、熬过（不一定容易）\r\n\r\n* I finally got through the interview.\r\n    我终于完成了面试。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n✅ breeze through\r\n\r\n和 cruise through 很接近：\r\n\r\n* She breezed through the exam.\r\n* She cruised through the exam.\r\n\r\n两个都表示：\r\n轻松通过\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🗣️ 口语例句\r\n\r\n* The first few weeks of the project were easy. We just cruised through them.\r\n    项目前几周很简单，我们顺利完成了。\r\n* I thought the interview would be difficult, but I cruised through it.\r\n    我原以为面试会很难，但结果轻松通过了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆口诀\r\n\r\n🚢 cruise = 船平稳前进\r\n➡️ cruise through = 像坐邮轮一样轻松穿过去\r\n\r\n困难像海面，自己像邮轮 → 平稳通过。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/6d62e6b10d714c16a5c997888790de2f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-04 18:21:05',1,'2026-08-04 18:21:05'),(1404,19,107,'phrase','hew to something','hew to something','hew to something','坚持；遵守；遵循','English:\r\nTo follow a rule, principle, belief, or standard closely.\r\n\r\n中文：\r\n严格遵守某种规则、原则、标准或信念。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n1️⃣ hew to + principle / rule / tradition\r\n\r\n遵守原则、规则、传统\r\n\r\n常见搭配：\r\n\r\n* hew to a principle\r\n    坚持原则\r\n* hew to tradition\r\n    遵循传统\r\n* hew to the rules\r\n    遵守规则','💬 例句\r\n\r\n🏢 工作场景\r\n\r\nThe company hews to strict quality standards.\r\n公司严格遵守质量标准。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚖️ 原则\r\n\r\nHe always hews to his principles.\r\n他始终坚持自己的原则。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🏛️ 传统\r\n\r\nThe village still hews to ancient traditions.\r\n这个村庄仍然遵循古老的传统。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ 常见错误\r\n\r\n❌ 不要理解成：\r\n\r\n“砍某个东西”\r\n\r\n因为 hew 单独表示：\r\n🪓 砍、劈、削\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThey hewed the wood.\r\n他们砍木头。\r\n\r\n但是：\r\n\r\nhew to something\r\n= 遵循、坚持\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象：\r\n\r\n🪓 古代工匠用斧头不断削刻木头，沿着一条线精准加工。\r\n\r\nhew = 砍削，沿着方向加工\r\n⬇️\r\nhew to = 沿着某个原则方向走\r\n\r\n➡️ 坚持某个标准，不偏离\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ 使用频率\r\n\r\n⭐⭐☆☆☆（较正式）\r\n\r\n常见于：\r\n\r\n* 新闻报道 📰\r\n* 商业文件 📄\r\n* 学术写作 🎓\r\n\r\n日常口语中通常用：\r\n✅ follow\r\n✅ stick to\r\n替代。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e37ebd79293b4b5bac8ec191f647c02e.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-04 18:23:55',1,'2026-08-04 18:23:55'),(1405,20,1,'vocab','omit','omit','omit','🔊 动词 (verb)\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思：省略；遗漏；删除；不包括\r\n指故意不写、不说、不做某件事，或者不小心漏掉某个内容。','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* omit something\r\n    省略 / 漏掉某事\r\n    Please omit this section.\r\n    请省略这一部分。\r\n* omit something from something\r\n    从……中删去 / 省略……\r\n    His name was omitted from the list.\r\n    他的名字被从名单中漏掉了。\r\n* omit to do something\r\n    忘记 / 未做某事（较正式）\r\n    He omitted to mention the problem.\r\n    他没有提到这个问题。','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* You can omit this field if it is not required.\r\n    如果这个字段不是必填项，可以省略。\r\n* Some important information was omitted from the report.\r\n    报告中遗漏了一些重要信息。\r\n* The system should not omit any required fields.\r\n    系统不应该遗漏任何必填字段。\r\n\r\n🔍 omit vs skip vs miss\r\n\r\n* omit = 从内容中省略、漏掉，较正式\r\n* skip = 主动跳过某一步/某项\r\n* miss = 没注意到、错过、漏掉\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe omitted the unnecessary fields from the output.\r\n我们从输出中删除了不必要的字段。\r\n\r\nWe skipped the validation step.\r\n我们跳过了验证步骤。\r\n\r\nThe OCR missed one handwritten number.\r\nOCR 漏识别了一个手写数字。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆：\r\nomit = leave out（不包括 / 省掉）\r\n\r\n👉 在技术文档里很常见：\r\nomit unnecessary fields = 省略不必要的字段\r\nomitted field = 被遗漏的字段\r\ninformation omitted = 信息被省略','/static/uploads/english_note_item/44732b572666412381810fd0f885af40.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-12 08:14:03',1,'2026-08-12 08:14:03'),(1406,20,2,'phrase','in the same boat','in the same boat','in the same boat','🎯 核心意思\r\n处境相同；面临同样的问题或困难','通常表示几个人或几件事处于类似的情况。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* We’re in the same boat.\r\n    我们处境一样。\r\n* They’re all in the same boat.\r\n    他们都面临同样的情况。\r\n* These fields are in the same boat.\r\n    这些字段都属于类似的情况。','💬 例句\r\n\r\nAll these fields are in the same boat, so they should follow the same review logic.\r\n这些字段都属于同一种情况，所以应该采用相同的 review 逻辑。\r\n\r\nDon’t worry, we’re all in the same boat.\r\n别担心，我们大家都面临同样的问题。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 常见错误\r\n\r\n❌ on the same boat\r\n✅ in the same boat\r\n\r\n固定搭配一定是 in the same boat。\r\n\r\n🔍 对比学习\r\n\r\n* in the same boat\r\n    强调“处境相同”，比较口语化\r\n* in the same situation\r\n    处于相同情况，更中性\r\n* fall into the same category\r\n    属于同一类别，更适合技术/工作语境\r\n* be handled in the same way\r\n    应以相同方式处理\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象几个人都坐在同一条船里。\r\n船遇到风浪时，所有人面对的是同一个问题。\r\n\r\n👉 same boat = same situation','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c423066ae71949098b8152deceb25d8f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-14 07:24:58',1,'2026-08-14 07:24:58'),(1407,20,3,'vocab','outlier','outlier','outlier','🎯 核心意思\r\n异常值；离群值；与其他情况明显不同的人或事物\r\n\r\n在数据、统计、业务规则中，outlier 常指明显偏离正常范围的值。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* an outlier\r\n    一个异常值\r\n* detect outliers\r\n    检测异常值\r\n* remove outliers\r\n    移除异常值\r\n* an outlier in the data\r\n    数据中的异常值','💬 例句\r\n\r\n4090 would be considered an outlier if the expected range is 3.9–4.1 V.\r\n如果正常范围是 3.9–4.1 V，那么 4090 就会被认为是异常值。\r\n\r\nThis value is an outlier and should be reviewed manually.\r\n这个值是异常值，应该进行人工审核。\r\n\r\nMost values are around 4.0, but this one is an outlier.\r\n大多数值都在 4.0 左右，但这个值明显异常。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 常见错误\r\n\r\noutlier ≠ error\r\n\r\n* outlier：异常、偏离正常范围，但不一定是错误\r\n* error：明确的错误\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n4090 mV 可能是合理值，只是如果系统按 V 来解释，它就会成为一个 outlier。\r\n\r\n🔍 对比学习\r\n\r\n* outlier = 离群值、异常值\r\n* exception = 例外情况\r\n* anomaly = 异常现象，偏技术用语\r\n* invalid value = 不符合规则的值\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象一排数字：\r\n\r\n3.9　4.0　4.1　4.0　👉 4090\r\n\r\n4090 明显“站在其他数据之外”。\r\n\r\n👉 out + lier → lying outside the group → 离群值','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f61977870d9443498f1d29e9f414ebde.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-14 08:49:29',1,'2026-08-14 08:49:29'),(1408,20,4,'vocab','reflection','reflection','reflection','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nreflection /rɪˈflekʃən/ n.\r\n\r\n1. 反思；思考；回顾 ⭐\r\n    指认真回顾一件事情，思考自己学到了什么、哪里做得好、哪里可以改进。\r\n2. 倒影；映像\r\n    指镜子、水面等反射出来的影像。\r\n3. 反映；体现\r\n    表示某件事是另一件事的体现或结果。','💬 例句\r\n\r\nI wrote a reflection on my OCR project.\r\n我写了一篇关于 OCR 项目的反思总结。\r\n\r\nThrough reflection, I identified several ways to improve OCR accuracy.\r\n通过反思，我发现了几种提高 OCR 准确率的方法。\r\n\r\nThis experience gave me an opportunity for reflection.\r\n这次经历给了我一个反思的机会。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* self-reflection → 自我反思\r\n* personal reflection → 个人反思\r\n* critical reflection → 批判性反思 / 深度反思\r\n* a reflection on sth → 对某事的反思\r\n* time for reflection → 用于思考的时间\r\n* upon reflection → 仔细想过之后\r\n\r\n💬 例如：\r\n\r\nUpon reflection, I realized that document layout had a significant impact on OCR accuracy.\r\n仔细思考后，我意识到文档布局对 OCR 准确率有很大影响。','🪞 第二个常见意思：倒影\r\n\r\nI saw my reflection in the mirror.\r\n我在镜子里看到了自己的倒影。\r\n\r\n🌊 记忆画面：\r\n你站在湖边，水面上出现你的 reflection（倒影）；看到自己的倒影后，你开始 reflection（反思）。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔍 Reflection vs Summary\r\n\r\nSummary = 总结“发生了什么”\r\nReflection = 思考“我从中学到了什么”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nSummary:\r\n\r\nI analyzed three types of documents.\r\n我分析了三种文档。\r\n\r\nReflection:\r\n\r\nBy analyzing three types of documents, I learned that document layout and handwriting quality can significantly affect OCR accuracy.\r\n通过分析三种文档，我认识到文档布局和手写质量会显著影响 OCR 准确率。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nreflect = 反射 / 思考\r\nreflect + -ion → reflection\r\n\r\n镜子会 reflect 光线 → 出现 reflection（倒影）\r\n人把经历“反射”回自己的脑子里重新思考 → reflection（反思）。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e5bab2c762994f70933b7570c2fa445f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-15 12:22:44',1,'2026-08-15 12:22:44'),(1409,20,5,'phrase','get + somebody + to + 动词原形','get + somebody + to + 动词原形','get + somebody + to + 动词原形','🔤 核心结构\r\n\r\nget + somebody + to + 动词原形\r\n\r\n👉 表示：让 / 请 / 说服某人去做某事\r\n\r\n这里的 get 不是“得到”，而是带有“促使某人做某事”的意思。\r\n\r\n🧩 句子结构\r\n\r\nI’ll get the technical team to check it.\r\n\r\n* I = 我\r\n* get = 让 / 请\r\n* the technical team = 技术团队\r\n* to check = 去检查\r\n* it = 它','💬 你的原句\r\n\r\nI will get the technical team here to provide me with what they should be.\r\n\r\n👉 我会让这边的技术团队告诉我，它们正确应该是什么。\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nget the technical team to provide…\r\n= 让技术团队提供……\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🟢 常见例句\r\n\r\nI’ll get John to help you.\r\n我会让 John 帮你。\r\n\r\nCan you get him to call me?\r\n你能让他给我打个电话吗？\r\n\r\nWe need to get the developer to fix this issue.\r\n我们需要让开发人员解决这个问题。\r\n\r\nI’ll get someone to look into it. ⭐\r\n我会找人调查一下这个问题。\r\n\r\n\r\n🆚 get sb to do vs make sb do\r\n\r\nget sb to do\r\n👉 让 / 请 / 想办法让某人做\r\n语气比较自然、柔和。\r\n\r\nmake sb do\r\n👉 强迫 / 迫使某人做\r\n语气更强。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI got him to check the file.\r\n= 我让他检查了文件。\r\n\r\nI made him check the file.\r\n= 我逼他检查了文件。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意结构区别：\r\n\r\nget sb to do ✅\r\nmake sb do ✅\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆口诀\r\n\r\n🟦 get 人 to do = 找人 / 让人去做\r\n\r\n职场中特别实用：\r\n\r\nI’ll get the team to check it.\r\nI’ll get someone to confirm it.\r\nI’ll get our engineer to look into it.','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3111243ad2cd4533b2bb85d2d2bbe27f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-16 07:11:50',1,'2026-08-16 07:11:50'),(1410,20,6,'phrase','get into sth','get into sth','get into sth','🧩 词性\r\n\r\nphrasal verb 短语动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 核心意思\r\n\r\n进入 / 开始涉及 / 深入某事\r\n\r\n具体意思要看后面的 sth 是什么。','① 💬 开始涉及某个话题、领域\r\n\r\n这是你刚才句子里的意思。\r\n\r\nget into + topic / detail / issue / negatives\r\n\r\n* We’re getting into more complicated cases.\r\n    我们开始涉及更复杂的情况了。\r\n* I don’t want to get into too much detail.\r\n    我不想深入太多细节。\r\n* It gets confusing when we get into negatives.\r\n    一涉及负数，就容易让人搞混。\r\n\r\n💡 这里可以理解成：\r\n\r\nget into = start dealing with / discussing\r\n= 开始处理 / 讨论 / 涉及\r\n\r\n② 🚪 进入某个地方\r\n\r\nget into + car / room / building\r\n\r\n* Get into the car.\r\n    上车。\r\n* How did he get into the building?\r\n    他是怎么进入这栋楼的？\r\n\r\n⚠️ 常见搭配：\r\n\r\nget into a car ✅\r\nget on a bus/train/plane ✅\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n③ 🎯 开始从事 / 对……产生兴趣\r\n\r\n* I’m getting into Python.\r\n    我开始对 Python 感兴趣 / 开始深入学 Python。\r\n* She got into running recently.\r\n    她最近开始喜欢上跑步了。\r\n\r\n🧠 有一种：\r\n“慢慢进入这个圈子/状态” 的感觉。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n④ 😬 陷入某种情况\r\n\r\n常见：\r\n\r\nget into trouble\r\n= 惹上麻烦 / 陷入麻烦\r\n\r\nget into debt\r\n= 陷入债务\r\n\r\nget into an argument\r\n= 和别人争吵起来\r\n\r\n例：\r\n\r\nHe got into trouble at work.\r\n他在工作中惹上了麻烦。','🆚 get into vs enter\r\n\r\nenter → 单纯“进入”，比较正式\r\n\r\nget into → 更口语，而且含义更丰富\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nHe entered the room.\r\n他进入房间。\r\n\r\nHe got into a discussion about OCR accuracy.\r\n他开始讨论 OCR 准确率的问题。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象你走进一个房间：\r\n\r\nget → 到达\r\ninto → 进入里面\r\n\r\n👉 从“进入一个房间”延伸成：\r\n\r\n进入一个话题 → 开始涉及\r\n进入一个领域 → 开始钻研\r\n进入麻烦 → 陷入麻烦\r\n\r\n⭐ 一句话记忆\r\n\r\nget into sth = 进入某事 → 开始涉及 / 深入 / 陷入某事','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b32e4f53c6454aa8ab06ecdf249f08f1.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-16 07:25:38',1,'2026-08-16 07:25:38'),(1411,20,7,'phrase','sensible','sensible','sensible','🧩 词性\r\n\r\nadjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 核心意思\r\n\r\n明智的；合理的；理智的；切合实际的\r\n\r\n强调一个人、决定、做法是 有判断力、现实、靠谱的。','💬 常见用法\r\n\r\n* a sensible decision\r\n    明智的决定\r\n* a sensible approach\r\n    合理的做法\r\n* a sensible suggestion\r\n    合理的建议\r\n* It makes sense to be sensible about it.\r\n    对这件事保持理智是合理的。','🧪 例句\r\n\r\nThat sounds like a sensible solution.\r\n听起来是个很合理的解决方案。\r\n\r\nIt would be sensible to test it first.\r\n先测试一下会比较明智。\r\n\r\nShe is very sensible with money.\r\n她花钱很理智。\r\n\r\n🆚 sensible vs sensitive\r\n\r\n这两个特别容易混：\r\n\r\nsensible = 明智的、理智的 ✅\r\nsensitive = 敏感的\r\n\r\n* a sensible person = 一个理智的人\r\n* a sensitive person = 一个敏感的人\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆\r\n\r\n把 sensible 想成：\r\n\r\n有 sense（判断力）的人 → sensible → 明智的、靠谱的\r\n\r\n⭐ 一句话记：\r\n\r\nsensible = practical + reasonable + wise\r\n= 实际、合理、明智','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9ee31e57a618498e87b457b6b93df1a3.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-16 07:34:12',1,'2026-08-16 07:34:12'),(1412,20,8,'phrase','probably isn’t gonna be','probably isn’t gonna be','probably isn’t gonna be','🇨🇳 核心意思\r\n\r\n大概不会是…… / 很可能不是……\r\n\r\n表示你根据现有情况做一个不完全确定的判断。','🧩 句型\r\n\r\nSomething + probably isn’t gonna be + 名词 / 形容词\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n* It probably isn’t gonna be too low.\r\n    它大概不会太低。\r\n* It probably isn’t gonna be a problem.\r\n    这大概不会是个问题。\r\n* The value probably isn’t gonna be negative.\r\n    这个值大概不会是负数。\r\n\r\n💬 你的原句\r\n\r\nIt probably isn’t gonna be something low.\r\n\r\n👉 它大概不会是一个很低的值。\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nsomething low\r\n= 某个较低的值 / 某个很低的数值\r\n\r\n在你们讨论数值范围时，可以理解成：\r\n\r\na low value\r\n= 一个较低的数值','🆚 probably vs maybe\r\n\r\nprobably = 很可能，大概率\r\n👉 把握更大\r\n\r\nmaybe = 也许，可能\r\n👉 不确定性更强\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nIt probably isn’t a problem.\r\n大概率不是问题。\r\n\r\nMaybe it isn’t a problem.\r\n也许不是问题。\r\n\r\n🗣️ gonna 是什么？\r\n\r\ngonna = going to\r\n\r\n只适合：\r\n✅ 口语\r\n✅ 非正式聊天\r\n\r\n正式邮件/报告建议写：\r\n\r\nIt probably isn’t going to be too low.\r\n\r\n而口语中：\r\n\r\nIt probably isn’t gonna be too low.\r\n\r\n非常自然。\r\n\r\n🧠 一句话记忆\r\n\r\nprobably isn’t gonna be = 大概率不会是……\r\n\r\n⭐ 工作会议里很好用：\r\n\r\nIt probably isn’t gonna be an issue.\r\n👉 这大概率不会是个问题。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/075cf5887049418daa0b656a25561042.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-16 07:50:47',1,'2026-08-16 07:50:47'),(1413,20,9,'phrase','just to get it','just to get it','just to get it','🔤 结构\r\n\r\njust + to + 动词原形\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\n* just = 只是 / 就是\r\n* to get it = 为了拿到它 / 得到它 / 搞定它 / 确认它\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 核心意思\r\n\r\n“只是为了先把它弄到 / 拿到 / 确认下来”\r\n\r\n具体怎么翻译，要看 it 指什么。','💬 你的句子\r\n\r\nJust to get it before you move off.\r\n\r\n👉 就是想在你离开/转去做别的事情之前，先把它拿到或确认下来。\r\n\r\n在工作会议里，get it 很可能不是字面“拿到”，而是：\r\n\r\n* get the information = 获取信息\r\n* get the value = 得到数值\r\n* get confirmation = 得到确认\r\n* get it sorted = 把它处理好','🧩 常见例句\r\n\r\nI just want to get it confirmed.\r\n我只是想先把它确认下来。\r\n\r\nJust to get it clear, what value should we use?\r\n就是想确认清楚，我们应该用哪个值？\r\n\r\nI need to get it before Friday.\r\n我需要在周五之前拿到它。\r\n\r\n⚠️ get it 还有一个很常见的意思\r\n\r\nget it = 明白了 / 理解了\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI get it now.\r\n我现在明白了。\r\n\r\nDo you get it?\r\n你明白了吗？\r\n\r\n但在你的这句话里，just to get it before you move off 更像是：\r\n\r\n👉 先把某个信息、答案或确认拿到手\r\n\r\n而不是“理解”。\r\n\r\n🧠 一句话记忆\r\n\r\njust to get it = 只是为了先把它拿到 / 搞定 / 确认下来','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8963d84a7bb44341b73507182cc6a323.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-16 08:01:56',1,'2026-08-16 08:01:56'),(1414,20,10,'phrase','move off','move off','move off','🧩 词性\r\n\r\nphrasal verb 短语动词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 核心意思\r\n\r\n离开；走开；转去做别的事情','① 🚶 离开某个地方\r\n\r\nThe bus moved off slowly.\r\n公交车慢慢开走了。\r\n\r\nHe moved off without saying goodbye.\r\n他没道别就离开了。\r\n\r\n这里更接近：\r\n\r\nmove off = leave / move away\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n② 💼 转去做下一件事\r\n\r\n在工作、会议、讨论里很常见。\r\n\r\nBefore you move off, can I confirm one thing?\r\n在你转去做下一件事之前，我能确认一件事吗？\r\n\r\nLet’s move off this topic and discuss the next issue.\r\n我们先结束这个话题，讨论下一个问题。\r\n\r\n你刚才那句：\r\n\r\nJust to get it before you move off.\r\n\r\n更自然理解成：\r\n\r\n“就是想在你转去做别的事情之前，先把这个确认下来。”','🆚 move off vs move on\r\n\r\nmove off\r\n👉 离开当前位置 / 从当前事情转开\r\n\r\nmove on\r\n👉 继续往下 / 进入下一阶段或下一个话题\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nBefore you move off, I need one more answer.\r\n你离开/转去做别的事情之前，我还需要一个答案。\r\n\r\nLet’s move on to the next question.\r\n我们继续看下一个问题。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆\r\n\r\noff = 离开\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nmove + off → 移动开 → 离开 / 转开\r\n\r\n⭐ 一句话记：\r\n\r\nmove off = 离开当前地方或当前事情，转去别处。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b4f4e8ad4a7941f187f335ddbc674d78.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-16 08:09:14',1,'2026-08-16 08:09:14'),(1415,20,11,'vocab','presumably','presumably','presumably','🔤 音标\r\n\r\n/prɪˈzjuːməbli/\r\n\r\n🧩 词性\r\n\r\nadverb 副词\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 核心意思\r\n\r\n大概；想必；据推测；很可能\r\n\r\n表示：根据已有信息进行合理推测，但并不是百分之百确定。','💬 常见用法\r\n\r\n* Presumably, he knows about it.\r\n    想必他知道这件事。\r\n* The value is presumably correct.\r\n    这个值大概是正确的。\r\n* Presumably, they’ll confirm it tomorrow.\r\n    他们大概明天会确认。','🆚 presumably vs probably\r\n\r\nprobably\r\n= 很可能，强调“概率高”\r\n\r\npresumably\r\n= 据推测 / 想必，强调“根据现有情况推断”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nHe’s probably at work.\r\n他很可能在上班。\r\n\r\nHe’s presumably at work because his car isn’t here.\r\n根据情况推测，他应该在上班，因为他的车不在这里。\r\n\r\n🧠 词根记忆\r\n\r\npresume = 推测；假定\r\npresumably = 据推测地 → 想必 / 大概\r\n\r\n⭐ 一句话记\r\n\r\npresumably = based on what we know, probably…\r\n👉 根据目前知道的情况推测，大概……','/static/uploads/english_note_item/af2be434bf00417ba503d0ce932d286a.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-16 08:14:50',1,'2026-08-16 08:14:50'),(1416,20,12,'phrase','fair enough','fair enough','fair enough','🧩 类型\r\n\r\n固定口语表达\r\n\r\n🇨🇳 核心意思\r\n\r\n根据语气不同，常见有：\r\n\r\n有道理 / 可以理解 / 行吧 / 好的，这我接受\r\n\r\n它不是字面上的“足够公平”。','💬 常见场景\r\n\r\nA: We need more time to test it.\r\n我们需要更多时间测试。\r\n\r\nB: Fair enough.\r\n👉 有道理 / 可以理解。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\nA: I don’t think this value should be included.\r\n我觉得这个值不应该包含进去。\r\n\r\nB: Fair enough. Let’s remove it.\r\n👉 行，有道理。那我们删掉它吧。\r\n\r\n🎯 语气特点\r\n\r\nFair enough. 通常表示：\r\n\r\n“我听懂你的理由了，而且我接受这个说法。”\r\n\r\n不一定表示你 100% 同意，但至少认为对方的理由是合理的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🆚 fair enough vs I agree\r\n\r\nI agree.\r\n= 我同意。\r\n👉 明确表示同意观点。\r\n\r\nFair enough.\r\n= 有道理 / 这个理由我接受。\r\n👉 更像是在认可对方的解释或立场。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nA: I can’t finish it today because I’m waiting for the technical team.\r\n今天我完成不了，因为我还在等技术团队。\r\n\r\nB: Fair enough.\r\n👉 可以理解。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🗣️ 很自然的搭配\r\n\r\nYeah, fair enough.\r\n嗯，有道理。\r\n\r\nOkay, fair enough.\r\n好的，可以理解。\r\n\r\nThat’s fair enough.\r\n这样也合理。\r\n\r\n🧠 一句话记\r\n\r\nfair enough = your reason sounds reasonable, so I accept it\r\n\r\n👉 “你的理由合理，我接受。”','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/34746b9585754153a877d76cdb3ac8e7.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-16 08:43:44',1,'2026-08-16 08:43:44'),(1417,20,13,'phrase','subsequently','subsequently','subsequently','🇨🇳 核心意思\r\n\r\n随后；后来；之后\r\n\r\n表示：某件事情发生之后，另一件事情接着发生。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆\r\n\r\nsubsequent = 随后的\r\nsubsequently = 随后地 / 后来\r\n\r\n可以直接记：\r\n\r\nA happened. Subsequently, B happened.\r\nA发生了，随后B发生了。','✏️ 例句\r\n\r\nHe joined the company in 2020 and subsequently became a manager.\r\n他2020年加入公司，后来成为了经理。\r\n\r\nThe problem was identified and subsequently fixed.\r\n问题被发现，随后被修复了。\r\n\r\nThe document was scanned and subsequently processed by the OCR system.\r\n文档被扫描，随后由 OCR 系统处理。','🔄 相近词\r\n\r\n* then → 然后，最口语\r\n* later → 后来\r\n* afterwards → 之后\r\n* subsequently → 随后，更正式，常用于报告、论文、工作表达\r\n\r\n💡 你的 OCR 项目汇报中很适合用：\r\n\r\nThe low-accuracy fields were identified and subsequently optimized.\r\n低准确率字段被识别出来，随后进行了优化。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b98f94043ca04d288d9240e8e0ccc5a6.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-17 06:20:08',1,'2026-08-17 06:20:08'),(1418,20,14,'phrase','mathematically','mathematically','mathematically','🇨🇳 核心意思\r\n\r\n从数学上来说；在数学上；用数学方法\r\n\r\n它来自：\r\n\r\nmathematical = 数学的\r\nmathematically = 在数学上 / 从数学角度看','🧠 记忆\r\n\r\nmathematically possible\r\n从数学上来说是可能的\r\n\r\nmathematically correct\r\n在数学上是正确的','✏️ 例句\r\n\r\nMathematically, the answer is correct.\r\n从数学上来说，这个答案是正确的。\r\n\r\nIt is mathematically impossible.\r\n从数学上来说，这是不可能的。\r\n\r\nThe two values are mathematically equivalent.\r\n这两个值在数学上是等价的。\r\n\r\nMathematically, -26 is greater than -29.\r\n从数学上来说，-26 大于 -29。\r\n\r\n🔗 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* mathematically correct → 数学上正确\r\n* mathematically possible → 数学上可行\r\n* mathematically impossible → 数学上不可能\r\n* mathematically equivalent → 数学上等价\r\n* mathematically speaking → 从数学角度来说\r\n\r\n💡 特别适合你前面说的负数问题：\r\n\r\nMathematically speaking, -26 is better than -29 if a higher value is preferred.\r\n从数学角度来说，如果数值越高越好，那么 -26 比 -29 更好。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/48c8a80e90a74c35a1df41a2d2ed9d97.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-17 06:26:32',1,'2026-08-17 06:26:32'),(1419,20,15,'phrase','necessarily','necessarily','necessarily','🎯 核心意思\r\nnecessarily = 必然地；一定地；必定地\r\n\r\n但在日常英语里，它最常见的用法其实是：\r\n\r\nnot necessarily = 不一定；未必','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. not necessarily + 动词 / 形容词\r\n表示“不一定……”\r\n\r\n* That’s not necessarily true.\r\n    那不一定是真的。\r\n* It’s not necessarily a problem.\r\n    这未必是个问题。\r\n\r\n2. don’t / doesn’t necessarily mean…\r\n非常常见：\r\n\r\nA doesn’t necessarily mean B.\r\n= A 不一定意味着 B\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n* A high confidence score doesn’t necessarily mean the OCR result is correct.\r\n    高置信度不一定意味着 OCR 结果就是正确的。\r\n* A lower value doesn’t necessarily mean a worse result.\r\n    更低的数值不一定意味着更差的结果。\r\n\r\n3. don’t necessarily need to…\r\n= 不一定需要……\r\n\r\n* We don’t necessarily need to extract this field.\r\n    我们不一定需要提取这个字段。','💬 例句\r\n\r\nIt’s recommended for testing, not necessarily for us to extract the value from the paper.\r\n这是针对测试的建议，不一定是让我们从纸质文件中提取这个值。\r\n\r\nMore expensive products are not necessarily better.\r\n更贵的产品不一定更好。\r\n\r\nYou don’t necessarily have to change the OCR model.\r\n你不一定非要更换 OCR 模型。\r\n\r\nFailure to recognize the field doesn’t necessarily mean the entire document should be rejected.\r\n字段识别失败不一定意味着整份文档都应该被丢弃。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ 常见错误\r\n\r\n❌ not necessary = 不一定\r\n\r\n这是错的。\r\n\r\n✅ not necessary\r\n= 没有必要\r\n\r\n✅ not necessarily\r\n= 不一定 / 未必\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\nIt is not necessary to review this field.\r\n没有必要审核这个字段。\r\n\r\nThis field is not necessarily wrong.\r\n这个字段不一定是错的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔍 对比学习\r\n\r\nnecessarily → 必然地 / 一定地\r\nnot necessarily → 不一定 / 未必\r\ndefinitely → 肯定地\r\nprobably → 很可能\r\npossibly → 有可能\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nIt is definitely wrong.\r\n它肯定是错的。\r\n\r\nIt is probably wrong.\r\n它很可能是错的。\r\n\r\nIt is not necessarily wrong.\r\n它不一定是错的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n看到：\r\n\r\nnot necessarily\r\n\r\n不要逐字翻译成“没有必要地”。\r\n\r\n直接把整个短语记成：\r\n\r\n👉 “不一定 / 未必”\r\n\r\n最推荐你记住这个万能句型：\r\n\r\nA doesn’t necessarily mean B.\r\n⭐ A 不一定意味着 B。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8e382ffa42be434482ef56444bf114ee.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-17 06:40:39',1,'2026-08-17 06:40:39'),(1420,20,16,'phrase','run short on time','run short on time','run short on time','🎯 核心意思\r\n时间快不够了 / 时间很紧 / 没剩多少时间了\r\n\r\n这里的 run short on… 表示：\r\n\r\n👉 某样东西逐渐变得不够用\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nWe’re running short on time.\r\n= 我们时间快不够了。\r\n= 我们时间有点紧了。','① be running short on + 名词\r\n强调“正在变得越来越不够”。\r\n\r\n* We’re running short on time.\r\n    我们时间快不够了。\r\n* We’re running short on money.\r\n    我们的钱快不够了。\r\n* We’re running short on supplies.\r\n    我们的物资快用完了。\r\n\r\n② run short of + 名词\r\n也很常见，意思基本一样。\r\n\r\n* We’re running short of time.\r\n    我们时间不多了。\r\n\r\n💬 工作场景例句\r\n\r\nWe’re running short on time, so let’s focus on the main issue.\r\n我们时间不多了，所以先关注主要问题。\r\n\r\nI’m running short on time, so I’ll keep this brief.\r\n我时间有点紧，所以我就长话短说。\r\n\r\nSince we’re running short on time, let’s move on to the next topic.\r\n因为时间快不够了，我们进入下一个话题吧。\r\n\r\n⭐ 非常实用的会议表达\r\n\r\nWe’re running a little short on time.\r\n我们的时间稍微有点紧。\r\n\r\n加上 a little 会更委婉，非常适合会议。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nWe’re running a little short on time, so maybe we can discuss this later.\r\n我们的时间有点紧，也许这个可以稍后再讨论。\r\n\r\n⚠️ run short on ≠ run out of\r\n\r\nrun short on time\r\n→ 时间快不够了，但还有一些\r\n\r\nrun out of time\r\n→ 时间已经用完 / 没时间了\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\nWe’re running short on time.\r\n我们时间不多了。⏳\r\n\r\nWe’ve run out of time.\r\n我们已经没时间了。⌛\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nshort = 短缺的、不足的\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nrun short on time\r\n≈ time is becoming short\r\n→ 剩余时间越来越少\r\n\r\n📌 你工作会议里最值得记的一句：\r\n\r\nWe’re running a little short on time, so let’s move on.\r\n我们的时间有点紧了，我们继续下一个吧。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/54cbd5be58d3424eb0e72e33638fe6ac.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 05:53:26',1,'2026-08-18 05:53:26'),(1421,20,17,'phrase','per','per','per','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nper 常见有两个意思：\r\n\r\n① 每…… / 每个……\r\n② 按照…… / 根据……','🧩 用法 1：每……\r\n\r\n结构：\r\n\r\n数量 + per + 单位\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n* $20 per hour\r\n    每小时 20 美元\r\n* 100 requests per second\r\n    每秒 100 个请求\r\n* three times per week\r\n    每周三次\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\nThe system can process 50 files per minute.\r\n这个系统每分钟可以处理 50 个文件。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧩 用法 2：按照…… / 根据……\r\n\r\n这种用法在工作邮件、商务沟通、正式表达中很常见。\r\n\r\nper + 名词\r\n\r\n≈ according to\r\n≈ as stated in\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nper your request\r\n按照你的要求\r\n\r\nper the document\r\n根据文档\r\n\r\nper the snippet\r\n根据这个截图/片段\r\n\r\nper our discussion\r\n按照我们之前讨论的内容','💬 例句：\r\n\r\nPer your request, I’ve updated the document.\r\n按照你的要求，我已经更新了文档。\r\n\r\nPer our discussion, I’ll change the validation logic.\r\n按照我们之前讨论的内容，我会修改验证逻辑。\r\n\r\nYour mapping per the snippet is correct.\r\n你根据这个截图所做的对应关系是正确的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ per vs according to\r\n\r\nper\r\n👉 更简洁、更商务、更正式\r\n\r\naccording to\r\n👉 更通用，日常和正式场景都可以\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nPer the document, this field is required.\r\n根据文档，这个字段是必填的。\r\n\r\nAccording to the document, this field is required.\r\n根据文档，这个字段是必填的。\r\n\r\n两句意思基本一样。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⭐ 工作中非常值得记的搭配\r\n\r\nper your request\r\n按照你的要求\r\n\r\nper our discussion\r\n按照我们的讨论\r\n\r\nper the specification\r\n根据规范\r\n\r\nper the document\r\n根据文档\r\n\r\nper the snippet\r\n根据截图/片段\r\n\r\n🧠 一句话记忆\r\n\r\nper = 每……；按照……\r\n\r\n看到：\r\n\r\n$50 per hour\r\n→ 每小时 50 美元\r\n\r\n看到：\r\n\r\nper your request\r\n→ 按照你的要求','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f914d5b72350435798ce67b06a7e220e.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 05:57:29',1,'2026-08-18 05:57:29'),(1422,20,18,'phrase','Carry out','Carry out','Carry out','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n执行；实施；开展；完成\r\n\r\n它通常表示：\r\n\r\n👉 按照计划、任务、命令、实验、调查等，把某件事情真正做出来。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧩 常见结构\r\n\r\ncarry out + 任务 / 计划 / 实验 / 调查 / 检查\r\n\r\n常见搭配：\r\n\r\n* carry out a task\r\n    执行任务\r\n* carry out a plan\r\n    实施计划\r\n* carry out an experiment\r\n    进行实验\r\n* carry out an investigation\r\n    开展调查\r\n* carry out a test\r\n    进行测试\r\n* carry out an inspection\r\n    进行检查\r\n* carry out maintenance\r\n    进行维护','💬 例句\r\n\r\nWe need to carry out more tests before release.\r\n我们需要在发布之前进行更多测试。\r\n\r\nThe team carried out an investigation into the issue.\r\n团队对这个问题进行了调查。\r\n\r\nI’ll carry out the changes we discussed.\r\n我会执行我们讨论过的修改。\r\n\r\nThe system automatically carries out the validation process.\r\n系统会自动执行验证流程。','💼 工作场景\r\n\r\n你做软件开发时非常实用：\r\n\r\nWe carried out several OCR tests on the new documents.\r\n我们对新文档进行了几次 OCR 测试。\r\n\r\nThe next step is to carry out performance testing.\r\n下一步是进行性能测试。\r\n\r\nI need to carry out some adjustments to improve the recognition rate.\r\n我需要进行一些调整来提高识别率。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ carry out vs do\r\n\r\ndo\r\n→ 很通用的“做”\r\n\r\ncarry out\r\n→ 更正式，强调执行一个明确的任务、计划或流程\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\ndo a test ✅\r\n进行测试\r\n\r\ncarry out a test ✅\r\n进行测试，更正式、更像工作/技术表达\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ carry out vs execute\r\n\r\ncarry out\r\n→ 日常工作和商务英语很常见，比较自然\r\n\r\nexecute\r\n→ 更正式、更技术化，也常用于代码、命令、计划\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\ncarry out a plan\r\n实施计划\r\n\r\nexecute a command\r\n执行命令\r\n\r\n在程序里一般说：\r\n\r\nexecute a query / command / script\r\n\r\n而不是：\r\n\r\ncarry out a query ❌\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\ncarry = 携带\r\nout = 出去\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n👉 把一个计划、任务“带出来并真正做完”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncarry out = 执行 / 实施\r\n\r\n⭐ 一句话记住\r\n\r\ncarry out a task\r\n= 执行一项任务','/static/uploads/english_note_item/97da36a6569b452aa042240167858b7d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 06:06:11',1,'2026-08-18 06:06:11'),(1423,20,19,'phrase','carry on vs carry out','carry on vs carry out','carry on vs carry out','🎯 核心区别\r\n\r\ncarry on = 继续做\r\n👉 强调：事情已经开始，现在继续\r\n\r\ncarry out = 执行 / 实施 / 开展\r\n👉 强调：把任务、计划、测试等真正做出来','🧩 carry on：继续\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\ncarry on + doing sth\r\n继续做某事\r\n\r\ncarry on with + 名词\r\n继续某件事\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\nPlease carry on working.\r\n请继续工作。\r\n\r\nLet’s carry on with the testing.\r\n我们继续测试吧。\r\n\r\nHe carried on talking.\r\n他继续说了下去。\r\n\r\n✅ carry on ≈ continue\r\n\r\n🧩 carry out：执行 / 实施\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\ncarry out + task / plan / test / investigation\r\n\r\n常见搭配：\r\n\r\n* carry out a task\r\n    执行任务\r\n* carry out a plan\r\n    实施计划\r\n* carry out a test\r\n    进行测试\r\n* carry out an investigation\r\n    开展调查\r\n* carry out maintenance\r\n    进行维护\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\nWe need to carry out more tests.\r\n我们需要进行更多测试。\r\n\r\nThe team carried out the plan successfully.\r\n团队成功实施了这个计划。\r\n\r\n✅ carry out ≈ perform / execute','⚠️ 最关键对比\r\n\r\nLet’s carry on with the test.\r\n我们继续这个测试。\r\n👉 测试已经开始了\r\n\r\nLet’s carry out a test.\r\n我们进行一次测试。\r\n👉 强调执行一次测试\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💼 工作场景对比\r\n\r\nWe’ll carry on with the OCR testing tomorrow.\r\n我们明天继续 OCR 测试。\r\n\r\nWe’ll carry out OCR testing tomorrow.\r\n我们明天会开展 OCR 测试。\r\n\r\n区别：\r\n\r\ncarry on with OCR testing\r\n→ 之前已经做过，现在继续\r\n\r\ncarry out OCR testing\r\n→ 明天安排执行这项测试\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ 结构也不一样\r\n\r\n✅ carry on doing something\r\n\r\nCarry on checking the files.\r\n继续检查文件。\r\n\r\n✅ carry on with something\r\n\r\nCarry on with the review.\r\n继续审核。\r\n\r\n✅ carry out something\r\n\r\nCarry out the review.\r\n执行这次审核。\r\n\r\n❌ carry out doing something\r\n通常不这样说。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\non = 往下继续\r\n👉 carry on = 继续\r\n\r\nout = 把事情做出来\r\n👉 carry out = 执行\r\n\r\n⭐ 一句话记住\r\n\r\ncarry on = keep doing it\r\n继续做\r\n\r\ncarry out = do/execute it\r\n把它执行出来','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2a48e1af25ff493fa27d13f2e68e477b.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 06:14:45',1,'2026-08-18 06:14:45'),(1424,20,20,'phrase','skew','skew','skew','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nskew 可以作 动词 / 名词 / 形容词。\r\n\r\n最常用的意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 使歪斜、使偏斜\r\n👉 使数据/结果产生偏差、失真','🧩 ① skew = 使……产生偏差\r\n\r\n在数据分析、OCR、统计、实验结果里非常常见。\r\n\r\nskew the results/data\r\n= 使结果 / 数据产生偏差\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\nA few outliers can skew the results.\r\n几个异常值可能会使结果产生偏差。\r\n\r\nIncorrect OCR results may skew the statistics.\r\n错误的 OCR 识别结果可能会使统计数据失真。\r\n\r\nThis could skew the accuracy rate.\r\n这可能会导致准确率出现偏差。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧩 ② skew = 歪斜 / 倾斜\r\n\r\n特别适合描述扫描文档、图片、文字。\r\n\r\nThe scanned page is slightly skewed.\r\n扫描的页面有一点歪斜。\r\n\r\nThe text is skewed to the left.\r\n文字向左倾斜了。\r\n\r\nWe need to correct the skew before OCR processing.\r\n在 OCR 处理之前，我们需要校正倾斜。\r\n\r\n📌 OCR 中经常看到：\r\n\r\nskew detection\r\n→ 倾斜检测\r\n\r\nskew correction\r\n→ 倾斜校正\r\n\r\ndeskew\r\n→ 把歪斜的图片/文档校正摆正\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧩 ③ skewed = 有偏差的 / 歪斜的\r\n\r\n这是工作中非常常见的形式。\r\n\r\nskewed data\r\n→ 有偏差的数据\r\n\r\nskewed results\r\n→ 有偏差的结果\r\n\r\na skewed image\r\n→ 歪斜的图片\r\n\r\n💬：\r\n\r\nThe recognition results may be skewed because of the poor scan quality.\r\n由于扫描质量较差，识别结果可能存在偏差。','⚖️ skew vs tilt\r\n\r\ntilt → 单纯表示物体倾斜\r\n\r\nThe camera is tilted.\r\n相机歪了。\r\n\r\nskew → 除了“歪斜”，还强调偏离正常状态 / 导致结果偏差\r\n\r\nThe page is skewed.\r\n页面歪斜了。\r\n\r\nThe outliers skewed the results.\r\n异常值使结果产生了偏差。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 skew 记成：\r\n\r\nskew = 歪了 → 偏了\r\n\r\n📄 页面“歪了” → skewed page\r\n📊 数据“偏了” → skewed data\r\n📈 结果“失真了” → skewed results\r\n\r\n⭐ 对你做 OCR 项目来说，最值得记住的是：\r\n\r\nThe page is slightly skewed, which may affect OCR accuracy.\r\n页面有轻微倾斜，这可能会影响 OCR 的识别准确率。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/02a38d6026574f2fb9f71e87607f76f7.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 07:28:04',1,'2026-08-18 07:28:04'),(1425,20,21,'phrase','commonwealth','commonwealth','commonwealth','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ncommonwealth 作名词，基本含义是：\r\n\r\n国家、政治共同体、联邦/共同体\r\n\r\n不过最常见的是大写的：\r\n\r\nthe Commonwealth\r\n👉 英联邦\r\n\r\n也就是由英国和许多曾经属于大英帝国的国家组成的国家组织。','💬 常见搭配：\r\n\r\nCommonwealth countries\r\n→ 英联邦国家\r\n\r\na member of the Commonwealth\r\n→ 英联邦成员国\r\n\r\nthe Commonwealth Games\r\n→ 英联邦运动会\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\nNew Zealand is a member of the Commonwealth.\r\n新西兰是英联邦成员国。\r\n\r\nMany Commonwealth countries use English as an official language.\r\n许多英联邦国家把英语作为官方语言之一。\r\n\r\n🧠 拆开记忆\r\n\r\ncommon = 共同的\r\nwealth = 财富 / 福祉\r\n\r\n所以它最初可以理解成：\r\n\r\ncommon + wealth → common good / common welfare\r\n👉 共同福祉 → 共同体\r\n\r\n⚠️ 这里不要简单把它理解成 “共同的财富”。在现代英语中，它主要是一个政治和国家组织相关的词。 \r\n\r\n⭐ 最值得记的一句：\r\n\r\nNew Zealand is part of the Commonwealth.\r\n新西兰是英联邦的一员。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/be4dba7ddd444ce49a4a4f3b34c050b5.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 08:42:44',1,'2026-08-18 08:42:44'),(1426,20,22,'phrase','organic','organic','organic','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\norganic adj.\r\n👉 有机的\r\n👉 有机种植的 / 不使用人工化肥、农药的\r\n👉 引申：自然形成的、自然发展的','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\norganic food\r\n→ 有机食品\r\n\r\norganic vegetables\r\n→ 有机蔬菜 🥬\r\n\r\norganic milk\r\n→ 有机牛奶 🥛\r\n\r\norganic farming\r\n→ 有机农业\r\n\r\norganic matter\r\n→ 有机物\r\n\r\norganic chemistry\r\n→ 有机化学 🧪\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nI usually buy organic vegetables.\r\n我通常买有机蔬菜。\r\n\r\nOrganic food is often more expensive.\r\n有机食品通常更贵。\r\n\r\nThe soil contains a lot of organic matter.\r\n这种土壤含有大量有机物。\r\n\r\n🌱 一个很常见的引申义\r\n\r\norganic growth\r\n👉 自然增长 / 内生增长\r\n\r\n这里的 organic 不再是“有机食品”的“有机”，而是强调自然产生，而不是人为强行推动。\r\n\r\nThe company achieved organic growth.\r\n公司实现了自然增长。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意：organic ≠ organization\r\n\r\n这两个词看起来有点像，但意思完全不同：\r\n\r\norganic → 有机的 🌱\r\norganization → 组织 🏢\r\norganize → 组织、安排\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆：\r\n\r\norganic → 🌱 自然生长 → 有机的 / 自然形成的\r\n\r\n⭐ 超市里看到：\r\n\r\n100% Organic\r\n通常就是：100% 有机（食品/产品）。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/df4b0722fa30414d8cd67de18ab514d5.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 08:49:52',1,'2026-08-18 08:49:52'),(1427,20,23,'phrase','spectacular','spectacular','spectacular','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nspectacular adj.\r\n👉 壮观的\r\n👉 精彩的\r\n👉 令人惊叹的\r\n\r\n通常形容视觉效果、景色、表演、成功等非常震撼。','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\nspectacular view\r\n→ 壮观的景色\r\n\r\nspectacular scenery\r\n→ 壮丽的风景\r\n\r\nspectacular performance\r\n→ 精彩的表演\r\n\r\nspectacular success\r\n→ 巨大的成功\r\n\r\nspectacular sunset\r\n→ 壮观的日落','💬 例句\r\n\r\nThe view from the top was spectacular.\r\n山顶的景色非常壮观。\r\n\r\nThey gave a spectacular performance.\r\n他们带来了一场精彩的表演。\r\n\r\nThe project was a spectacular success.\r\n这个项目取得了巨大的成功。\r\n\r\n⚖️ spectacular vs beautiful\r\n\r\nbeautiful\r\n→ 美丽的，范围很广\r\n\r\nspectacular\r\n→ 不只是美，而是震撼、壮观、让人眼前一亮\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe lake is beautiful.\r\n这个湖很美。\r\n\r\nThe mountain view is spectacular.\r\n这片山景壮观得令人惊叹。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n可以联想到：\r\n\r\nspectacle = 壮观场面 / 景象\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nspectacular\r\n= 像一场 spectacle 一样令人震撼\r\n\r\n⭐ 最值得记的一句：\r\n\r\nThe scenery was absolutely spectacular.\r\n这里的景色简直太壮观了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/95d640e18c314eafb6da1a3d1890582e.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 09:00:45',1,'2026-08-18 09:00:45'),(1428,20,24,'phrase','give rise to','give rise to','give rise to','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ngive rise to + 名词\r\n👉 导致；引起；产生；孕育；形成\r\n\r\n它的核心不是只表示“导致坏结果”，而是：\r\n\r\n使某件事产生、出现\r\n\r\n所以不同语境下可以灵活翻译成：\r\n\r\n导致 / 引起 / 产生 / 孕育 / 形成 / 发源出','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\ngive rise to problems\r\n→ 引发问题\r\n\r\ngive rise to concerns\r\n→ 引起担忧\r\n\r\ngive rise to confusion\r\n→ 引起混淆\r\n\r\ngive rise to errors\r\n→ 导致错误\r\n\r\ngive rise to rivers\r\n→ 孕育河流 / 使河流发源\r\n\r\nMajor mountain ranges include the Himalaya, the Andes and the Rocky Mountains, each of which gives rise to some of the world’s greatest rivers.\r\n\r\n👉 主要山脉包括喜马拉雅山脉、安第斯山脉和落基山脉，这些山脉都孕育了世界上一些最重要的大河。\r\n\r\n更自然地翻译：\r\n\r\n👉 世界上一些最重要的大河都发源于这些山脉。\r\n\r\n这里的：\r\n\r\ngive rise to rivers\r\n≈ give birth to rivers / form rivers\r\n\r\n更自然理解为：\r\n\r\n👉 孕育河流\r\n👉 成为河流的发源地','💬 更多例句\r\n\r\nPoor image quality can give rise to OCR errors.\r\n较差的图像质量可能会导致 OCR 错误。\r\n\r\nThis issue may give rise to confusion.\r\n这个问题可能会引起混淆。\r\n\r\nThese mountains give rise to several major rivers.\r\n这些山脉孕育了 / 发源出几条主要河流。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚖️ give rise to vs lead to\r\n\r\nlead to\r\n👉 更常见、更自然\r\n👉 口语和写作都常用\r\n\r\ngive rise to\r\n👉 更正式\r\n👉 更强调“某事使另一件事产生出来”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe error led to incorrect results.\r\n这个错误导致了错误结果。\r\n\r\nThe error gave rise to several unexpected problems.\r\n这个错误引发了几个意料之外的问题。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nto 在这里是介词，所以后面通常接：\r\n\r\n名词 / 名词短语\r\n\r\n✅ give rise to problems\r\n✅ give rise to confusion\r\n✅ give rise to several rivers\r\n\r\n不直接接动词原形：\r\n\r\n❌ give rise to make errors\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nrise = 出现、升起、产生\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ngive rise to something\r\n≈ 让某事物“产生出来”\r\n\r\n👉 导致 / 引起 / 产生 / 孕育\r\n\r\n⭐ 这个例句里最值得记：\r\n\r\nThese mountains give rise to several major rivers.\r\n👉 这些山脉孕育了几条主要河流。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9197755861844377a724d0af12ed9649.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 09:24:19',1,'2026-08-18 09:24:19'),(1429,20,25,'vocab','dimension','dimension','dimension','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ndimension n.\r\n👉 尺寸；大小；维度；方面\r\n\r\n这个词很常见，具体意思取决于语境。','🧩 ① dimension = 尺寸 / 大小\r\n\r\n常用于描述物体的长、宽、高。\r\n\r\nthe dimensions of the box\r\n→ 这个盒子的尺寸\r\n\r\n💬 What are the dimensions of this table?\r\n这张桌子的尺寸是多少？\r\n\r\n通常可能包括：\r\n\r\nlength = 长度\r\nwidth = 宽度\r\nheight = 高度\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ndimensions = 长 × 宽 × 高等尺寸信息\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧩 ② dimension = 维度\r\n\r\n在数学、数据、计算机里非常常见。\r\n\r\ntwo-dimensional / 2D\r\n→ 二维的\r\n\r\nthree-dimensional / 3D\r\n→ 三维的\r\n\r\nhigh-dimensional data\r\n→ 高维数据\r\n\r\n💬 This model works with high-dimensional data.\r\n这个模型可以处理高维数据。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧩 ③ dimension = 方面 / 层面\r\n\r\n这是一个很常见的引申义。\r\n\r\na social dimension\r\n→ 社会层面\r\n\r\nthe economic dimension of the problem\r\n→ 这个问题的经济层面\r\n\r\n💬 We need to consider the technical dimension of the project.\r\n我们需要考虑这个项目的技术层面。','🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\nphysical dimensions\r\n→ 物理尺寸\r\n\r\nscreen dimensions\r\n→ 屏幕尺寸\r\n\r\nimage dimensions\r\n→ 图片尺寸\r\n\r\nthree dimensions\r\n→ 三个维度\r\n\r\nanother dimension\r\n→ 另一个层面\r\n\r\nadd a new dimension to something\r\n→ 给某事增加一个新的层面\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nThe image dimensions are 1920 by 1080 pixels.\r\n这张图片的尺寸是 1920 × 1080 像素。\r\n\r\nThe problem has several different dimensions.\r\n这个问题有几个不同的层面。\r\n\r\nA cube has three dimensions.\r\n立方体有三个维度。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ dimension vs size\r\n\r\nsize\r\n👉 更日常、更笼统\r\n= 大小\r\n\r\ndimension\r\n👉 更具体、更技术化\r\n= 尺寸 / 维度\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWhat size is the box?\r\n这个盒子多大？\r\n\r\nWhat are the dimensions of the box?\r\n这个盒子的长宽高分别是多少？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n可以记成：\r\n\r\ndimension = 一个事物“有多大 / 有几个方向 / 有几个层面”\r\n\r\n所以它可以表示：\r\n\r\n尺寸 📏\r\n维度 📐\r\n层面 🧩\r\n\r\n⭐ 最值得记：\r\n\r\nWhat are the dimensions of this image?\r\n👉 这张图片的尺寸是多少？','/static/uploads/english_note_item/39943fbbe4d244469948eecac4d5146f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 09:32:21',1,'2026-08-18 09:32:21'),(1430,20,26,'sentence','The mean elevation of the Earth’s land surface is 840 metres.','The mean elevation of the Earth’s land surface is 840 metres.','The mean elevation of the Earth’s land surface is 840 metres.','地球陆地表面的平均海拔是 840 米。','The mean elevation\r\n→ 平均海拔 / 平均高程\r\n\r\n这里 mean = average（平均的）\r\n\r\nelevation = 海拔；高程\r\n\r\nof the Earth’s land surface\r\n→ 地球陆地表面的\r\n\r\n* Earth’s = 地球的\r\n* land = 陆地\r\n* surface = 表面\r\n* land surface = 陆地表面\r\n\r\nis 840 metres\r\n→ 是 840 米\r\n\r\n所以整个结构：\r\n\r\nThe mean elevation + of the Earth’s land surface + is 840 metres.\r\n\r\n= 地球陆地表面的平均海拔是840米。','📌 mean 在这里很重要\r\n\r\n你之前可能更熟悉：\r\n\r\nmean = 意思是 / 意味着\r\n\r\nWhat does this word mean?\r\n这个单词是什么意思？\r\n\r\n但在数学、统计、地理中：\r\n\r\nmean = 平均数 / 平均的\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nmean temperature → 平均温度\r\nmean annual rainfall → 年平均降雨量\r\nmean elevation → 平均海拔\r\narithmetic mean → 算术平均数\r\n\r\n⭐ 这句话最值得一起记的搭配就是：\r\n\r\nmean elevation = 平均海拔 / 平均高程','/static/uploads/english_note_item/1305b302f1d74c02a26773c2e0c8fc28.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 09:47:27',1,'2026-08-18 09:47:27'),(1431,20,27,'vocab','fascination','fascination','fascination','fascination /ˌfæs.ɪˈneɪ.ʃən/\r\n重音在 NAY：fas-ci-NA-tion\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nfascination n.\r\n👉 着迷；强烈的兴趣；吸引力；魅力\r\n\r\n它不是普通的 interest（兴趣），而是强调：\r\n\r\n某件东西非常吸引你，让你特别感兴趣，甚至着迷。','🧩 最常见结构：fascination with\r\n\r\na fascination with + 名词\r\n👉 对……的着迷 / 浓厚兴趣\r\n\r\nhave a fascination with…\r\n→ 对……非常着迷\r\n\r\n💬 He has always had a fascination with space.\r\n他一直对太空非常着迷。 🚀\r\n\r\n💬 She developed a fascination with ancient history.\r\n她开始对古代历史产生了浓厚兴趣。\r\n\r\n🧩 fascination = 吸引力 / 魅力\r\n\r\n也可以表示某个东西本身具有的魅力、吸引力。\r\n\r\nthe fascination of travel\r\n→ 旅行的魅力\r\n\r\nthe fascination of the natural world\r\n→ 大自然的魅力\r\n\r\n💬 I can understand the fascination of living in the mountains.\r\n我能理解住在山区的魅力。','🧩 词族一起记\r\n\r\nfascinate v.\r\n👉 使着迷；深深吸引\r\n\r\nThe natural world fascinates me.\r\n大自然让我着迷。\r\n\r\n⬇️\r\n\r\nfascinated adj.\r\n👉 感到着迷的（形容人的感受）\r\n\r\nI’m fascinated by astronomy.\r\n我对天文学非常着迷。\r\n\r\n⬇️\r\n\r\nfascinating adj.\r\n👉 迷人的；极有吸引力的（形容事物）\r\n\r\nIt’s a fascinating book.\r\n这是一本非常吸引人的书。\r\n\r\n⬇️\r\n\r\nfascination n.\r\n👉 着迷；浓厚兴趣；吸引力\r\n\r\nI have a fascination with astronomy.\r\n我对天文学有着浓厚的兴趣。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚖️ fascination vs interest\r\n\r\ninterest\r\n👉 兴趣\r\n程度比较普通：\r\n\r\nI have an interest in geography.\r\n我对地理感兴趣。\r\n\r\nfascination\r\n👉 浓厚兴趣 / 着迷 ❤️\r\n程度明显更强：\r\n\r\nI have a fascination with geography.\r\n我对地理非常着迷。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ 介词特别注意\r\n\r\n最常见：\r\n\r\nfascination with something ✅\r\n\r\nHe has a fascination with maps.\r\n他非常痴迷于地图。\r\n\r\n而 fascinated 通常搭配：\r\n\r\nbe fascinated by / with something\r\n\r\nI’m fascinated by maps.\r\n我对地图非常着迷。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把这一组一起记：\r\n\r\nfascinate → 使人着迷 ❤️\r\nfascinated → 人感到着迷 😍\r\nfascinating → 东西很迷人 ✨\r\nfascination → 着迷 / 强烈的兴趣 🧲\r\n\r\n⭐ 最值得记：\r\n\r\nhave a fascination with something\r\n👉 对某事物有浓厚的兴趣 / 对某事物着迷','/static/uploads/english_note_item/93abadfb8c6c49d5902507069c945c1f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 09:55:20',1,'2026-08-18 09:55:20'),(1432,20,28,'vocab','phenomena','phenomena','phenomena','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nphenomena n.\r\n👉 现象；事物；特殊事件\r\n\r\n它是 phenomenon 的复数形式。\r\n\r\nphenomenon = 一个现象\r\nphenomena = 多个现象','🧩 最常见用法\r\n\r\nnatural phenomena\r\n→ 自然现象\r\n\r\nweather phenomena\r\n→ 天气现象\r\n\r\nsocial phenomena\r\n→ 社会现象\r\n\r\nphysical phenomena\r\n→ 物理现象\r\n\r\ngeographical phenomena\r\n→ 地理现象','💬 例句\r\n\r\nEarthquakes and volcanic eruptions are natural phenomena.\r\n地震和火山喷发都是自然现象。\r\n\r\nScientists study various weather phenomena.\r\n科学家研究各种天气现象。\r\n\r\nThis is an interesting social phenomenon.\r\n这是一个有趣的社会现象。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点：phenomenon vs phenomena\r\n\r\n这是最重要的一点：\r\n\r\none phenomenon ✅\r\n一个现象\r\n\r\ntwo phenomena ✅\r\n两个现象\r\n\r\n❌ two phenomenons\r\n在正式英语里通常不用这个复数形式。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n可以这样记：\r\n\r\nphenomenon → 单数\r\nphenomena → 复数\r\n\r\n就像：\r\n\r\ncriterion → criteria\r\n标准 → 多个标准\r\n\r\ndatum → data\r\n数据点 → 数据\r\n\r\n⭐ 最值得记：\r\n\r\nnatural phenomena = 自然现象\r\nphenomenon = 单数\r\nphenomena = 复数','/static/uploads/english_note_item/53e3e09cc72d4bbd99c6149e49237591.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 10:39:14',1,'2026-08-18 10:39:14'),(1433,20,29,'phrase','introduce a problem','introduce a problem','introduce a problem','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nintroduce a problem\r\n👉 引入问题 / 带来问题 / 导致新的问题\r\n\r\n这里的 introduce 不是我们最熟悉的：\r\n\r\nintroduce myself → 自我介绍\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\nintroduce = bring something new into a situation\r\n把某个原本没有的东西带进来\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nintroduce a problem\r\n= 带来一个新的问题','🧩 技术工作中非常常见\r\n\r\n尤其在软件开发、系统设计、数据处理中：\r\n\r\nintroduce problems\r\n→ 引入问题\r\n\r\nintroduce errors\r\n→ 引入错误\r\n\r\nintroduce bugs\r\n→ 引入 bug\r\n\r\nintroduce complexity\r\n→ 增加 / 引入复杂性\r\n\r\nintroduce risk\r\n→ 引入风险\r\n\r\nintroduce bias\r\n→ 引入偏差\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nThis change may introduce new problems.\r\n这个改动可能会带来新的问题。\r\n\r\nPoor preprocessing can introduce errors into the OCR results.\r\n不恰当的预处理可能会给 OCR 结果引入错误。\r\n\r\nAdding more rules could introduce unnecessary complexity.\r\n增加更多规则可能会带来不必要的复杂性。\r\n\r\nThis approach solves one problem but introduces another.\r\n这种方法解决了一个问题，但又带来了另一个问题。\r\n\r\n⭐ 最后这一句在工作讨论中非常实用。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚖️ introduce problems vs cause problems\r\n\r\ncause problems\r\n👉 导致问题\r\n\r\n强调：A 导致了 B\r\n\r\nintroduce problems\r\n👉 引入 / 带来原本不存在的问题\r\n\r\n强调：做了某个改变、增加某个东西之后，新问题随之出现。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe update caused some problems.\r\n这次更新导致了一些问题。\r\n\r\nThe new logic introduced several problems.\r\n新的逻辑引入了几个原本没有的问题。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔗 和你刚学的 give rise to 对比\r\n\r\ngive rise to problems\r\n→ 引发问题，比较正式\r\n\r\ncause problems\r\n→ 导致问题，最普通\r\n\r\nintroduce problems\r\n→ 引入新问题，技术场景特别常见\r\n\r\n🧠 可以这样记：\r\n\r\nintroduce a person\r\n👤 把一个人带进来 → 介绍\r\n\r\nintroduce a new feature\r\n⚙️ 把一个新功能加进来 → 引入\r\n\r\nintroduce a problem\r\n⚠️ 把一个新问题带进来 → 引入问题\r\n\r\n⭐ This solution may introduce new problems.\r\n👉 这个解决方案可能会带来新的问题。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/539bdcb59def4d82b06c45601c4bd9ef.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 10:43:10',1,'2026-08-18 10:43:10'),(1434,20,30,'vocab','magnitude','magnitude','magnitude','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nmagnitude n.\r\n👉 大小；程度；量级；震级\r\n\r\n核心概念可以记成：\r\n\r\nhow large, strong, or important something is\r\n某事物到底有多大、多强或多严重','🧩 ① magnitude = 大小 / 程度\r\n\r\n常用于比较正式的表达。\r\n\r\nthe magnitude of the problem\r\n→ 问题的严重程度 / 规模\r\n\r\nthe magnitude of the change\r\n→ 变化的幅度\r\n\r\n💬 We didn’t realize the magnitude of the problem.\r\n我们之前没有意识到这个问题有多严重。\r\n\r\n🌍 ② magnitude = 震级\r\n\r\n地理中非常常见：\r\n\r\nearthquake magnitude\r\n→ 地震震级\r\n\r\na magnitude 7 earthquake\r\n→ 7级地震\r\n\r\n💬 The earthquake had a magnitude of 7.2.\r\n这次地震的震级为 7.2。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意：\r\n\r\nmagnitude = 地震本身释放能量的大小\r\nintensity = 某个地点感受到的震动强度 / 烈度\r\n所以二者不是完全一样的。\r\n\r\n📐 ③ magnitude = 数学中的“大小”\r\n\r\n在数学、物理中：\r\n\r\nmagnitude of a vector\r\n→ 向量的模 / 大小\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n\\vec v=(3,4)\r\n\r\n它的 magnitude：\r\n\r\n|\\vec v|=\\sqrt{3^2+4^2}=5\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nThe magnitude of the vector is 5.\r\n这个向量的模是 5。\r\n\r\n🧩 ④ order of magnitude = 数量级\r\n\r\n这是非常重要的固定搭配：\r\n\r\norder of magnitude\r\n👉 数量级\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n10 → 10² → 10³ → 10⁴\r\n\r\n每增加一个数量级，大约就是 ×10。\r\n\r\n💬 The new system is an order of magnitude faster.\r\n新系统的速度提高了大约一个数量级。','🔗 常见搭配\r\n\r\nthe magnitude of the problem → 问题的严重程度\r\nearthquake magnitude → 地震震级\r\nmagnitude 6.5 earthquake → 6.5级地震\r\nmagnitude of a vector → 向量的模\r\norder of magnitude → 数量级\r\ngreater magnitude → 更大的规模 / 程度\r\n\r\n⚖️ magnitude vs size\r\n\r\nsize\r\n👉 普通的“大小”，日常用词\r\n\r\nmagnitude\r\n👉 强调程度、规模、强度或数值上的大小，更正式、更技术化\r\n\r\nthe size of the box 📦\r\n→ 箱子的大小\r\n\r\nthe magnitude of the earthquake 🌍\r\n→ 地震的震级\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n看到 magnitude，不要只记“大小”，而是想：\r\n\r\nHow big / strong is it?\r\n\r\n🌍 地震有多强 → magnitude\r\n📐 向量有多大 → magnitude\r\n⚠️ 问题有多严重 → magnitude\r\n🔢 数值是什么量级 → order of magnitude\r\n\r\n⭐ The earthquake had a magnitude of 7.2.\r\n👉 这次地震的震级为 7.2。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9ba8a86cae3d464696233ad816e227c8.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-18 11:24:38',1,'2026-08-18 11:24:38'),(1435,20,31,'vocab','vital','vital','vital','🧩 词性\r\nadjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nvital = 至关重要的；必不可少的；维持生命所必需的\r\n\r\n它比 important 语气更强，表示“如果没有它，会造成严重影响”。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* be vital to sth = 对……至关重要\r\n* be vital for sth = 对……很重要 / 必不可少\r\n* play a vital role in… = 在……中发挥至关重要的作用\r\n* vital information = 关键信息\r\n* vital signs = 生命体征','💬 例句\r\n\r\nWater is vital to human life.\r\n水对人类生命至关重要。\r\n\r\nCommunication is vital for teamwork.\r\n沟通对团队合作非常重要。\r\n\r\nShe played a vital role in the project.\r\n她在这个项目中发挥了至关重要的作用。\r\n\r\nThe doctor checked his vital signs.\r\n医生检查了他的生命体征。\r\n\r\n⚠️ vital vs important\r\n\r\nimportant = 重要的\r\nvital = 极其重要的、不可缺少的\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nExercise is important for health.\r\n锻炼对健康很重要。\r\n\r\nOxygen is vital for life.\r\n氧气对生命是必不可少的。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆技巧\r\n\r\n可以把 vital 和 vital signs（生命体征） 联系起来：\r\n\r\nvital → life → 对生命重要 → 至关重要的','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/65b3c76fd21d435398870a16d6e0c36c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-19 09:12:30',1,'2026-08-19 09:12:30'),(1436,20,32,'vocab','variation','variation','variation','🧩 词性\r\nnoun 名词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nvariation = 变化；差异；变体；变动\r\n\r\n它通常表示：\r\n同一种东西在不同情况下出现了一些不同。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* variation in sth = ……方面的变化 / 差异\r\n* variation between A and B = A 和 B 之间的差异\r\n* a variation of/on sth = ……的变体 / 变化形式\r\n* seasonal variation = 季节性变化\r\n* temperature variation = 温度变化\r\n* slight variation = 轻微差异','💬 例句\r\n\r\nThere is a lot of variation in temperature during the day.\r\n一天之中的温度变化很大。\r\n\r\nWe found some variations between the two documents.\r\n我们发现这两份文档之间存在一些差异。\r\n\r\nThis design is a variation of the original version.\r\n这个设计是原版本的一个变体。\r\n\r\n💼 工作中很实用的表达\r\n\r\nThere may be some variation in the document layout.\r\n文档布局可能会有一些变化。\r\n\r\n这个句子很适合描述 OCR 项目里不同文件的版式差异。\r\n\r\n⚠️ variation vs change\r\n\r\n* change = 某个东西发生了改变\r\n* variation = 一组东西之间存在不同，或某个数值在一定范围内波动\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe document format has changed.\r\n文档格式变了。\r\n\r\nThere are variations in the document format.\r\n不同文档的格式存在差异。\r\n\r\n🧠 词根记忆\r\n\r\nvary = 变化、不同\r\n→ variation = 变化 / 差异\r\n→ various = 各种各样的\r\n→ variety = 多样性；种类','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/7e8eb339013c4af287a0bfd2692129d0.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-19 09:28:54',1,'2026-08-19 09:28:54'),(1437,20,33,'phrase','fade away','fade away','fade away','🧩 词性\r\nphrasal verb 短语动词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nfade away = 逐渐消失；慢慢减弱；渐渐淡去\r\n\r\n强调的是：不是突然消失，而是一点一点变弱、变淡，最后几乎没有了。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见场景\r\n\r\n* 声音逐渐消失\r\n* 记忆逐渐淡去\r\n* 光线逐渐变暗\r\n* 疼痛/感觉逐渐减弱\r\n* 希望、兴趣等慢慢消失','💬 例句\r\n\r\nThe sound slowly faded away.\r\n声音慢慢消失了。\r\n\r\nThe pain began to fade away.\r\n疼痛开始逐渐减轻。\r\n\r\nHer memories of that place faded away over time.\r\n她对那个地方的记忆随着时间逐渐淡去了。\r\n\r\nThe light faded away as the sun went down.\r\n随着太阳落山，光线渐渐暗了下来。\r\n\r\n⚠️ fade vs fade away\r\n\r\n* fade = 变淡、褪色、减弱\r\n* fade away = 逐渐消失到几乎没有\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe color faded.\r\n颜色褪了。\r\n\r\nThe sound faded away.\r\n声音渐渐消失了。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆技巧\r\n\r\nfade = 淡掉\r\naway = 离开\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nfade away = 一点一点淡掉，最后“离开”了\r\n\r\n很适合记成：\r\nslowly disappear = fade away','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/127b2b2a25284f64ba0e398ecee79e6d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-19 09:30:51',1,'2026-08-19 09:30:51'),(1438,20,34,'phrase','pick up','pick up','pick up','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\npick up 是非常常用的口语短语，意思很多，要看语境。\r\n\r\n最常见可以理解成：\r\n拿起 / 接人 / 学会 / 好转 / 增强 / 接收到','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* pick up something = 拿起某物\r\n* pick someone up = 开车去接某人\r\n* pick up a language/skill = 自然而然学会\r\n* business picks up = 生意好转\r\n* wind/rain picks up = 风雨增强\r\n* pick up a signal = 接收到信号','💬 例句\r\n\r\nCan you pick me up at the airport?\r\n你能去机场接我吗？\r\n\r\nI picked up some English from my coworkers.\r\n我从同事那里学会了一些英语表达。\r\n\r\nBusiness usually picks up in summer.\r\n生意通常在夏天会好起来。\r\n\r\nThe wind is picking up.\r\n风越来越大了。\r\n\r\n🌦️ 你刚才天气预报里的意思\r\n\r\nnorthwesterly winds picking up\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\npick up = become stronger = 增强\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nThe wind is picking up.\r\n= 风开始变大了 / 风力正在增强。\r\n\r\n⚠️ pick up vs increase\r\n\r\nincrease = 增加，比较正式、客观\r\npick up = 增强、好转，口语感更强\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWind speeds will increase.\r\n风速将增加。——比较正式\r\n\r\nThe wind will pick up.\r\n风会变大。——更自然、更口语\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆技巧\r\n\r\n可以把 pick up 想成：\r\n\r\n从低处“往上走” → 状态变强、变好、增加\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nwind picks up\r\n→ 风力往上走\r\n→ 风越来越大','/static/uploads/english_note_item/1ed8d76e6aaf41a09cd7226fe5e48b8d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-19 10:24:15',1,'2026-08-19 10:24:15'),(1439,20,35,'phrase','a hint of / hint of','a hint of / hint of','a hint of / hint of','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\na hint of = 一点点……；一丝……；轻微的……迹象\r\n\r\n强调数量或程度很少、很轻微。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* a hint of sadness = 一丝悲伤\r\n* a hint of doubt = 一丝怀疑\r\n* a hint of blue = 一点点蓝色\r\n* a hint of garlic = 一点蒜味\r\n* a hint of rain = 一点要下雨的迹象','💬 例句\r\n\r\nThere was a hint of sadness in her voice.\r\n她的声音里带着一丝悲伤。\r\n\r\nThe sauce has a hint of garlic.\r\n这个酱汁有一点蒜味。\r\n\r\nI can see a hint of blue in the sky.\r\n我能看到天空中有一点蓝色。\r\n\r\n🌦️ 天气预报里也很常见\r\n\r\na hint of rain\r\n= 有一点下雨的迹象\r\n\r\na hint of spring\r\n= 有一点春天的感觉 / 春意初现\r\n\r\n⚠️ hint of vs a little\r\n\r\na little = 一点，比较直接\r\na hint of = 一丝、隐约的一点，更自然、更细腻\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThere is a little red in the sky.\r\n天空有一点红色。\r\n\r\nThere is a hint of red in the sky.\r\n天空中隐约带着一丝红色。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆技巧\r\n\r\nhint 本身有“暗示、提示”的意思。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\na hint of something\r\n≈ 某种东西“露出了一点点迹象”\r\n→ 一丝…… / 一点点……','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/35a70b91e3174dd1a1bb593ea6930437.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-19 10:29:17',1,'2026-08-19 10:29:17'),(1440,20,36,'vocab','attainment','attainment','attainment','🧩 词性\r\nnoun 名词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nattainment = 达到；取得；成就；达到的水平\r\n\r\n它来自动词 attain：\r\n\r\nattain = 达到；获得\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nattainment = 达到某个目标或水平这件事','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* educational attainment = 受教育程度 / 教育成就\r\n* academic attainment = 学业水平 / 学业成绩\r\n* high attainment = 高水平成就\r\n* attainment of a goal = 达成目标\r\n* attainment of objectives = 实现目标','💬 例句\r\n\r\nEducational attainment is closely linked to employment opportunities.\r\n受教育程度与就业机会密切相关。\r\n\r\nThe attainment of this goal will require more time.\r\n实现这个目标需要更多时间。\r\n\r\nStudents showed high levels of academic attainment.\r\n学生表现出了较高的学业水平。\r\n\r\n⚠️ attainment vs achievement\r\n\r\nachievement = 成就，强调“做成了一件事情”\r\nattainment = 达到某个标准、目标或水平\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWinning the competition was a great achievement.\r\n赢得比赛是一项很大的成就。\r\n\r\nEducational attainment has improved.\r\n整体受教育程度提高了。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆技巧\r\n\r\nattain = reach 达到\r\n\r\n→ attainment = 达到某个水平 / 目标\r\n\r\n特别是看到：\r\n\r\neducational attainment\r\n\r\n直接记成：\r\n\r\n受教育程度\r\n这个搭配在统计、人口、教育类文章里非常常见。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/61924b4227184030aa42749012c29968.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-19 10:58:20',1,'2026-08-19 10:58:20'),(1441,20,37,'vocab','literacy','literacy','literacy','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nliteracy = 读写能力；识字能力\r\n\r\n最常见意思是：\r\nthe ability to read and write\r\n= 阅读和书写的能力','🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* literacy rate = 识字率\r\n* adult literacy = 成人识字能力\r\n* basic literacy skills = 基本读写能力\r\n* digital literacy = 数字素养 / 数字技术使用能力\r\n* financial literacy = 金融素养\r\n* health literacy = 健康素养','💬 例句\r\n\r\nThe country has a high literacy rate.\r\n这个国家的识字率很高。\r\n\r\nImproving literacy is important for education and employment.\r\n提高读写能力对教育和就业很重要。\r\n\r\nDigital literacy is becoming increasingly important.\r\n数字素养正变得越来越重要。\r\n\r\n⚠️ literacy vs literate\r\n\r\nliteracy = 名词，读写能力\r\nliterate = 形容词，有读写能力的；识字的\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nHe is literate.\r\n他识字。\r\n\r\nHis literacy skills are good.\r\n他的读写能力很好。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆技巧\r\n\r\nliteracy 可以和 literature 文学 联想：\r\n\r\n能读、能写\r\n→ literacy = 读写能力\r\n\r\n📊 如果你是在统计图表里看到：\r\n\r\nadult literacy rate\r\n通常就是：\r\n\r\n成人识字率','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d46e59437d6140aa96f487946e21fb40.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-19 11:37:55',1,'2026-08-19 11:37:55'),(1442,20,38,'vocab','Inequality','Inequality','Inequality','🧩 词性\r\nnoun 名词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ninequality = 不平等；不均等；差距\r\n\r\n通常指人在收入、机会、教育、健康、社会地位等方面存在不公平的差异。','🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* income inequality = 收入不平等\r\n* social inequality = 社会不平等\r\n* economic inequality = 经济不平等\r\n* gender inequality = 性别不平等\r\n* wealth inequality = 财富差距\r\n* reduce inequality = 减少不平等','💬 例句\r\n\r\nIncome inequality remains a major issue in many countries.\r\n收入不平等在很多国家仍然是一个重大问题。\r\n\r\nEducation can help reduce social inequality.\r\n教育可以帮助减少社会不平等。\r\n\r\nThere is a large inequality in access to healthcare.\r\n在获得医疗服务方面存在很大的不平等。\r\n\r\n⚠️ inequality vs difference\r\n\r\ndifference = 差异，中性，不一定不公平\r\ninequality = 不平等，通常带有“分配不均、不公平”的含义\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThere are differences in income.\r\n收入存在差异。\r\n\r\nThere is significant income inequality.\r\n收入分配存在明显不平等。\r\n\r\n🧠 词根记忆\r\n\r\nequal = 平等的\r\n→ equality = 平等\r\n→ inequality = 不平等\r\n\r\n前缀 in- = not\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ninequality = not equal = 不平等\r\n\r\n📊 在统计、社会学、经济学文章里非常常见。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a98b9c23b88d4eb1b69e156864d11d20.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-19 11:41:08',1,'2026-08-19 11:41:08'),(1443,20,39,'vocab','frost','frost','frost','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n1. 霜；白霜\r\n    指天气很冷时，地面、草、车窗等表面形成的一层薄冰晶。\r\n2. 结霜（动词）','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* There was frost on the grass this morning.\r\n    今天早上草地上有一层霜。\r\n* The car windows were covered with frost.\r\n    汽车窗户上结满了霜。\r\n* It frosted overnight.\r\n    夜里结霜了。','🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* heavy frost → 严重的霜 / 大霜\r\n* a light frost → 轻霜\r\n* ground frost → 地面霜冻\r\n* frosty night → 有霜的寒冷夜晚\r\n* frost damage → 霜冻造成的损害\r\n* frost warning → 霜冻警报\r\n\r\n🌡️ frost vs freeze\r\n\r\n* frost：强调表面出现的霜\r\n* freeze：强调温度低于冰点、东西冻结\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n* There was frost on the grass.\r\n    草上有霜。\r\n* The water froze overnight.\r\n    水一夜之间冻住了。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n想象新西兰冬天早晨，你出门看到 草地和汽车挡风玻璃上覆盖着一层白白的冰晶 —— 这就是 frost。\r\n\r\n你之前看到的 “on a frosty night” 里的 frosty 就是：\r\n👉 frosty = 有霜的；严寒的\r\n\r\nIt went out on a frosty night.\r\n它是在一个有霜的寒冷夜晚出去的。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e429a1e0b919430397bc0a7e1ecbcf8f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-20 08:21:01',1,'2026-08-20 08:21:01'),(1444,20,40,'vocab','East eastern easterly','East eastern easterly','East eastern easterly','📌 east / eastern / easterly\r\n\r\n这三个词都和“东”有关，但用法不同。\r\n\r\n🧭 east\r\n\r\n🔊 /iːst/\r\n🧩 noun / adjective / adverb\r\n🎯 东；东方；向东\r\n\r\n常见用法：\r\n\r\n* the east = 东方 / 东部\r\n* east coast = 东海岸\r\n* go east = 向东走\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\n* The sun rises in the east.\r\n    太阳从东方升起。\r\n* We drove east.\r\n    我们向东开。','🌏 eastern\r\n\r\n🔊 /ˈiːstən/\r\n🧩 adjective\r\n🎯 东部的；东方的\r\n\r\n它强调“位于东部”。\r\n\r\n常见用法：\r\n\r\n* eastern China = 中国东部\r\n* eastern side = 东侧\r\n* eastern region = 东部地区\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\n* Christchurch is on the eastern side of the South Island.\r\n    基督城位于南岛东部。','🌬️ easterly\r\n\r\n🔊 /ˈiːstəli/\r\n🧩 adjective / noun / adverb\r\n🎯 从东方吹来的；向东的\r\n\r\n这个词在天气预报里特别常见。\r\n\r\n最重要的：\r\n\r\n* an easterly wind = 东风\r\n* 意思是：风从东边吹过来\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\n* Easterly winds are expected tomorrow.\r\n    明天预计有东风。\r\n* A cool easterly is developing.\r\n    一股凉爽的东风正在形成。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 风向的命名是按“风从哪里来”：\r\n\r\n* easterly wind = 从东往西吹\r\n* westerly wind = 从西往东吹\r\n\r\n🔍 一眼对比\r\n\r\n* east = 东 / 向东\r\n* eastern = 东部的\r\n* easterly = 东风的 / 从东方来的\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆：\r\neast → 地点/方向\r\neastern → 区域位置\r\neasterly → 风向、气流方向\r\n\r\n比如天气预报里：\r\neasterly winds = 东风\r\n而不是“向东吹的风”。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c0dfa533745f4c4880de3f340055ab38.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-20 08:35:21',1,'2026-08-20 08:35:21'),(1445,20,41,'phrase','there we go','there we go','there we go','🎯 常见口语表达，意思会根据场景变化。\r\n\r\n最常见的是：好了 / 搞定了 / 这就对了 / 成了\r\n\r\n比如你终于把一个东西弄好：\r\n\r\n* There we go!\r\n    好了！搞定了！\r\n\r\n比如电脑终于连上：\r\n\r\n* There we go. It’s working now.\r\n    好了，现在能用了。\r\n\r\n比如你在帮别人调整东西，调到正确位置：\r\n\r\n* There we go.\r\n    对，就是这样。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 它和 here we go 不一样：\r\n\r\n* There we go → 事情终于好了、完成了\r\n* Here we go → 开始了 / 要来了','💬 对比：\r\n\r\n* There we go. I fixed it.\r\n    好了，我修好了。\r\n* Here we go! The game is starting.\r\n    开始了！比赛要开始了。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆：\r\nthere we go = 到那个“正确状态”了 → 搞定了','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d96f70b25bd4484184fa4fd5f2905417.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-20 08:40:33',1,'2026-08-20 08:40:33'),(1446,20,42,'phrase','get clipped by','get clipped by','get clipped by','🎯 核心意思\r\nget clipped by = 被……擦到 / 被……边缘影响到','getting clipped by those showers\r\n= 被那些阵雨擦到一点 / 受到那些阵雨边缘影响\r\n\r\n它通常不是说“正面遭遇大雨”，而是：\r\n👉 阵雨主体从旁边经过，某个地方只是被边缘扫到。\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\n* Christchurch may get clipped by those showers this afternoon.\r\n    今天下午基督城可能会被那些阵雨边缘影响到。\r\n* The eastern coast could get clipped by a few showers.\r\n    东海岸可能会被几阵雨稍微扫到。\r\n\r\n🧠 clip 在这里的感觉\r\n你可以想象一片降雨云从旁边经过：\r\n\r\n🌧️🌧️🌧️ →\r\n　　　🏠\r\n\r\n房子没有处在降雨最中心，只是雨区的边缘“擦过”它。\r\n\r\n⚠️ clip 平时还有“剪、夹”的意思，但在这里不是那个意思。\r\n\r\n🔍 对比\r\n\r\n* get hit by showers = 被阵雨直接袭击，影响更明显\r\n* get clipped by showers = 被阵雨边缘擦到，影响较轻\r\n* avoid the showers = 避开阵雨\r\n\r\n所以天气预报里听到 getting clipped by those showers，可以很自然地理解成：\r\n\r\n👉 “会被阵雨稍微扫到一点。”','🧩 1. 天气：被边缘影响到\r\n\r\n* We might get clipped by a few showers this afternoon.\r\n    我们今天下午可能会被几阵雨稍微扫到。\r\n\r\n这里强调：不是正面影响，只是边缘擦过。\r\n\r\n🧩 2. 交通 / 运动：被撞到、擦到\r\n\r\n* He got clipped by a car while crossing the road.\r\n    他过马路时被一辆车擦撞了一下。\r\n* The cyclist got clipped by another rider.\r\n    那个骑车的人被另一名骑手擦到了。\r\n\r\n这里的 clip 很像：\r\n👉 side-swipe / brush against\r\n不是一定严重撞击，更常见是“擦碰”。\r\n\r\n🧩 3. 体育：被对手碰到、击中\r\n\r\n* He got clipped by an elbow during the game.\r\n    他比赛时被一个肘击碰到了。\r\n* The boxer got clipped by a left hook.\r\n    那名拳击手被一个左勾拳击中了。\r\n\r\n这里可以理解成：\r\n👉 突然被击中一下\r\n\r\n🧩 4. 物体：被边缘碰到\r\n\r\n* I got clipped by the door as it swung open.\r\n    门突然打开时擦到我了。\r\n* She got clipped by a branch while running through the bush.\r\n    她跑过灌木丛时被树枝刮了一下。\r\n\r\n这里是：\r\n👉 被快速擦过 / 刮到\r\n\r\n🧩 5. 比喻：被小幅削减、影响\r\n这个用法相对少一点，但也能见到：\r\n\r\n* Our budget got clipped by 10 percent.\r\n    我们的预算被削减了 10%。\r\n* His hours got clipped by the company.\r\n    他的工时被公司削减了。\r\n\r\n这里的 clip ≈ cut / reduce。\r\n\r\n🧠 一眼记忆\r\n\r\nget clipped by = 被某个东西“擦、碰、削”到一点\r\n\r\n* showers → 被雨带边缘扫到\r\n* car → 被车擦撞\r\n* elbow/punch → 被击中\r\n* branch/door → 被刮到\r\n* budget/hours → 被削减\r\n\r\n⚠️ get clipped by a car 和 get hit by a car 不完全一样：\r\n\r\n* get clipped by a car → 更强调擦碰、侧面碰到\r\n* get hit by a car → 更直接地说“被车撞了”，程度可能更严重','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d7cdcfd292dd4e7fbdad3aac7d6947c9.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-20 09:00:37',1,'2026-08-20 09:00:37'),(1447,20,43,'vocab','widespread','widespread','widespread','🔊 /ˈwaɪdspred/\r\n🧩 adjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nwidespread = 广泛的；大范围的；普遍的\r\n\r\n它强调某件事覆盖的地区很大，或者很多人/很多地方都有。','🌧️ 天气预报里特别常见\r\n\r\n* widespread rain\r\n    大范围降雨\r\n* widespread showers\r\n    大范围阵雨\r\n* widespread frost\r\n    大范围霜冻\r\n* widespread cloud\r\n    大范围云层\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\n* Widespread rain is expected across the South Island.\r\n    南岛预计会出现大范围降雨。\r\n* There could be widespread frost tomorrow morning.\r\n    明天早晨可能会有大范围霜冻。\r\n\r\n🌍 日常用法\r\n\r\n* The problem is widespread.\r\n    这个问题非常普遍。\r\n* There is widespread support for the proposal.\r\n    这项提议获得了广泛支持。\r\n\r\n🧠 拆开记忆\r\n\r\nwide = 宽广的\r\nspread = 扩散、展开\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nwide + spread → widespread\r\n👉 扩散得很广 → 广泛的 / 大范围的\r\n\r\n🔍 widespread vs scattered\r\n\r\n* widespread showers = 很多地区都有阵雨，覆盖范围广\r\n* scattered showers = 零零散散的阵雨，只在部分地区出现\r\n\r\n天气预报里这两个词非常值得一起记。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/54e271fd9d94415ab4223364a7b870ff.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-20 09:22:32',1,'2026-08-20 09:22:32'),(1448,20,44,'phrase','roll in','roll in','roll in','🔊 /rəʊl ɪn/\r\n🧩 phrasal verb 短语动词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nroll in = 逐渐涌入；滚滚而来；慢慢进入并覆盖\r\n\r\n它的画面感很强：\r\n\r\nroll = 滚动\r\nin = 进入\r\n\r\n所以字面上就是：\r\n\r\n👉 “滚着进来”','在天气里常用来形容云、雾、雨、风暴等一大片慢慢移过来。\r\n\r\n🌦️ 天气预报常见用法\r\n\r\n* clouds roll in\r\n    云层逐渐涌来\r\n* fog rolls in\r\n    雾逐渐飘进来\r\n* showers roll in\r\n    阵雨逐渐移入\r\n* a storm rolls in\r\n    风暴逐渐逼近\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\n* Dark clouds are rolling in from the west.\r\n    乌云正从西边滚滚而来。\r\n* Some showers will roll in this afternoon.\r\n    今天下午会有一些阵雨逐渐移入。\r\n* Fog started rolling in from the coast.\r\n    雾开始从海岸一带逐渐涌进来。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n☁️☁️☁️ → → → 🏠\r\n\r\n不是突然出现，而是：\r\n\r\n远处出现 → 越来越近 → 慢慢覆盖过来\r\n\r\n这就是 roll in 的感觉。','🧩 日常口语中的其他用法\r\n\r\n1. 人大量到来\r\n\r\n* The guests started rolling in around 7 p.m.\r\n    客人晚上7点左右开始陆续到来。\r\n\r\n2. 钱大量进账\r\n\r\n* The money started rolling in.\r\n    钱开始源源不断地进来了。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 这里通常带有一种：\r\n\r\n👉 一批一批地来 / 接连不断地来\r\n\r\n🔍 roll in vs come in\r\n\r\n* come in = 进来，普通表达\r\n* roll in = 一大片 / 一批一批 / 很有画面感地涌进来\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nClouds are coming in.\r\n云正在过来。\r\n\r\nClouds are rolling in.\r\n云正一大片一大片地涌过来。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/7e623981c3ab4c8e9f98a23345a0cf08.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-20 09:40:14',1,'2026-08-20 09:40:14'),(1449,20,45,'phrase','break apart','break apart','break apart','🔊 /breɪk əˈpɑːt/\r\n🧩 phrasal verb 短语动词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nbreak apart = 分裂开；散开；瓦解；碎成几部分\r\n\r\n可以拆开理解：\r\n\r\n* break = 打破、断裂\r\n* apart = 分开地、彼此分离\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nbreak + apart → break apart\r\n👉 从一个整体，变成几个分开的部分','🌦️ 天气预报里常见\r\n\r\n天气里常用来形容：\r\n\r\n* cloud 云层\r\n* rain band 雨带\r\n* showers 阵雨\r\n* weather system 天气系统\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\n* The cloud will break apart later this afternoon.\r\n    下午晚些时候云层会逐渐散开。\r\n* The rain band is starting to break apart.\r\n    这条雨带正在开始瓦解。\r\n* The showers should break apart as they move north.\r\n    这些阵雨向北移动时应该会逐渐变得零散。\r\n\r\n🧠 天气里的画面\r\n\r\n原来：\r\n\r\n☁️☁️☁️☁️☁️\r\n\r\n后来：\r\n\r\n☁️　　☁️　　　☁️\r\n\r\n也就是：\r\n\r\ncontinuous → scattered\r\n连续成片 → 逐渐零散','🧩 其他常见语义\r\n\r\n1. 东西裂开 / 散架\r\n\r\n* The chair started to break apart.\r\n    椅子开始散架了。\r\n\r\n2. 组织、团体瓦解\r\n\r\n* The group began to break apart.\r\n    这个团体开始瓦解。\r\n\r\n3. 关系破裂\r\n\r\n* Their relationship started to break apart.\r\n    他们的关系开始破裂。\r\n\r\n🔍 break apart vs break up\r\n\r\n* break apart → 强调“一个整体裂成几部分”\r\n* break up → 也可表示分裂，但更常用于情侣分手、会议结束、团体解散\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n* The clouds broke apart.\r\n    云层散开了。\r\n* They broke up last year.\r\n    他们去年分手了。\r\n\r\n🧠 和 roll in 一起记\r\n\r\n* roll in = 涌进来、逐渐覆盖\r\n* break apart = 散开、逐渐瓦解\r\n\r\n天气里这两个非常适合成对记忆。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9852ec9a66cc448d9296d49648c04820.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-20 09:53:25',1,'2026-08-20 09:53:25'),(1450,20,46,'vocab','instability','instability','instability','🔊 /ˌɪnstəˈbɪləti/\r\n🧩 noun 名词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ninstability = 不稳定；不稳定状态\r\n\r\n它来自：\r\n\r\n* stable = 稳定的\r\n* unstable = 不稳定的\r\n* instability = 不稳定性 / 不稳定状态','🌦️ 天气预报里非常常见\r\n\r\n在气象里，instability 通常指：\r\n\r\n👉 大气不稳定\r\n\r\n也就是空气容易上升，容易形成：\r\n\r\n* ☁️ towering clouds 高耸云\r\n* 🌧️ showers 阵雨\r\n* ⛈️ thunderstorms 雷暴\r\n* 🌨️ hail 冰雹\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\n* There is some instability in the atmosphere this afternoon.\r\n    今天下午大气有一些不稳定。\r\n* The instability could trigger a few thunderstorms.\r\n    这种不稳定状态可能会引发几场雷暴。\r\n* We’ll see increasing instability during the day.\r\n    白天大气不稳定程度会逐渐增加。\r\n\r\n🧠 天气里的逻辑\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\nwarm air near the ground + colder air above\r\n地面附近较暖 + 高空较冷\r\n\r\n⬇️\r\n\r\n空气容易往上升\r\n\r\n⬇️\r\n\r\n☁️🌧️⛈️\r\n\r\n所以天气预报里听到：\r\n\r\natmospheric instability\r\n= 大气不稳定\r\n\r\n通常意味着天气更容易变得多变、对流活跃。\r\n\r\n🧩 日常其他用法\r\n\r\n* political instability\r\n    政治不稳定\r\n* economic instability\r\n    经济不稳定\r\n* financial instability\r\n    金融不稳定\r\n* emotional instability\r\n    情绪不稳定\r\n\r\n🔍 stable / unstable / instability\r\n\r\n* stable weather = 稳定的天气\r\n* unstable air = 不稳定空气\r\n* atmospheric instability = 大气不稳定性\r\n\r\n🧠 最简单记忆：\r\n\r\ninstability = things are not staying stable\r\n👉 某个系统维持不了稳定状态','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/1b83fbecf9f84b059c0f98c424dc0144.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-20 10:20:23',1,'2026-08-20 10:20:23'),(1451,20,47,'vocab','stretch','stretch','stretch','🔊 /stretʃ/\r\n🧩 verb / noun 动词 / 名词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nstretch = 拉伸；伸展；延伸；持续一段距离/时间','它的核心画面就是：\r\n\r\n👉 把某个东西“拉长、展开”\r\n\r\n🧍 1. 拉伸身体 / 伸展\r\n\r\n* stretch your arms\r\n    伸展手臂\r\n* I need to stretch my legs.\r\n    我得伸伸腿。\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\n* She stretched before running.\r\n    她跑步前做了拉伸。\r\n\r\n🗺️ 2. 延伸、绵延\r\n\r\n这个在天气和地理里很常见。\r\n\r\n* The rain band stretches across the South Island.\r\n    这条雨带横跨南岛。\r\n* The mountains stretch along the coast.\r\n    山脉沿着海岸绵延。\r\n\r\n👉 这里的 stretch = extend 延伸\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⏳ 3. 持续一段时间\r\n\r\n* The meeting stretched into the evening.\r\n    会议一直持续到了晚上。\r\n* The wet weather may stretch into Friday.\r\n    潮湿天气可能会持续到周五。\r\n\r\n这里有一种：\r\n👉 时间被“拉长”了\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n📏 4. noun：一段距离 / 一段时间\r\n\r\n* a long stretch of road\r\n    一长段公路\r\n* a stretch of coastline\r\n    一段海岸线\r\n* a dry stretch of weather\r\n    一段持续的干燥天气\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\n* This is a beautiful stretch of coast.\r\n    这是一段非常漂亮的海岸线。','🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* stretch across = 横跨\r\n* stretch from A to B = 从 A 延伸到 B\r\n* stretch along = 沿着……延伸\r\n* stretch into = 持续到……\r\n* stretch out = 伸展开 / 躺开\r\n\r\n🧠 一眼记忆\r\n\r\nstretch = 拉长\r\n\r\n所以可以引申成：\r\n\r\n* 身体拉长 → 伸展\r\n* 地图上的区域拉长 → 延伸、绵延\r\n* 时间拉长 → 持续\r\n* 一段被拉长的区域 → 一段距离\r\n\r\n🌦️ 如果你是在天气预报里看到：\r\n\r\na band of rain stretching across the country\r\n\r\n就是：\r\n\r\n👉 一条横跨全国延伸的雨带。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/15caebd879464c318082f848fe6bd8a0.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-20 10:30:37',1,'2026-08-20 10:30:37'),(1452,20,48,'phrase','correspond one-to-one with','correspond one-to-one with','correspond one-to-one with','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ncorrespond one-to-one with = 与……一一对应','强调：\r\n\r\nA 里的每一个项目，都能在 B 里找到唯一对应的一个项目。\r\n\r\n也就是：\r\n\r\nA1 ↔ B1\r\nA2 ↔ B2\r\nA3 ↔ B3\r\n\r\n🧩 常见结构\r\n\r\nA corresponds one-to-one with B\r\n\r\nA 与 B 一一对应。\r\n\r\n复数主语时：\r\n\r\nThese fields correspond one-to-one with the fields in the Test Sheet PDF.\r\n这些字段和 Test Sheet PDF 中的字段一一对应。\r\n\r\n也可以说：\r\n\r\nEach field corresponds to exactly one field in the PDF.\r\n每个字段都只对应 PDF 中的一个字段。','💬 例句\r\n\r\nThe database fields correspond one-to-one with the fields on the form.\r\n数据库字段和表单上的字段一一对应。\r\n\r\nEach extracted value corresponds one-to-one with a field in the source document.\r\n每个提取出来的值都与源文档中的一个字段一一对应。\r\n\r\nThese columns correspond one-to-one with the attributes in the data model.\r\n这些列与数据模型中的属性一一对应。\r\n\r\n📌 你的 OCR 项目里很适合的表达\r\n\r\nThese fields correspond one-to-one with the fields in the Test Sheet PDF.\r\n\r\n如果强调“数据库字段和 PDF 字段”：\r\n\r\nThe database fields correspond one-to-one with the fields in the Test Sheet PDF.\r\n\r\n或者更偏程序员表达：\r\n\r\nThere is a one-to-one mapping between these fields and the fields in the Test Sheet PDF.\r\n\r\n= 这些字段和 Test Sheet PDF 中的字段之间存在一一映射关系。\r\n\r\n⚠️ correspond to vs correspond one-to-one with\r\n\r\ncorrespond to\r\n= 对应于，但不一定严格一一对应\r\n\r\nThis value corresponds to the voltage field.\r\n这个值对应 voltage 字段。\r\n\r\ncorrespond one-to-one with\r\n= 明确强调一对一\r\n\r\nEach database field corresponds one-to-one with a PDF field.\r\n每个数据库字段都与一个 PDF 字段严格一一对应。\r\n\r\n💡 技术场景里还可以记一个非常常用的说法\r\n\r\none-to-one mapping\r\n\r\n= 一一映射\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThere is a one-to-one mapping between the PDF fields and the database fields.\r\n\r\n在软件开发、数据库、OCR 字段映射场景中，这个表达尤其常见。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9b5c989feaac4204b6b440ddf86bba55.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-20 17:49:20',1,'2026-08-20 17:49:20'),(1453,20,49,'vocab','prevail','prevail','prevail','🎯 词性\r\nverb 动词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n1. 盛行；普遍存在\r\n2. 占优势；获胜\r\n3. 成功说服某人（常见于 prevail on/upon someone to do something）\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* prevail in / among\r\n    在……中盛行\r\n* prevail over\r\n    战胜；压倒\r\n* prevail on/upon someone to do something\r\n    说服某人做某事','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* These customs still prevail in some rural areas.\r\n    这些习俗在一些农村地区仍然盛行。\r\n* Common sense eventually prevailed.\r\n    最终理性占了上风。\r\n* Our team prevailed over a strong opponent.\r\n    我们队战胜了一个强劲的对手。\r\n* She prevailed on him to stay for dinner.\r\n    她说服他留下来吃晚饭。','🌦️ 和 prevailing 的关系\r\n\r\nprevail = 动词\r\n→ 盛行、占优势\r\n\r\nprevailing = 形容词\r\n→ 盛行的、占主导的\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n* Westerly winds prevail in this region.\r\n    这个地区盛行西风。\r\n* The prevailing winds are westerly.\r\n    这里的盛行风是西风。\r\n\r\n⚠️ prevail vs win\r\n\r\n* win：更直接，赢比赛、奖项、竞争\r\n* prevail：更正式，强调“最终占上风”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n* They won the match.\r\n    他们赢了比赛。\r\n* Justice prevailed.\r\n    正义最终占了上风。\r\n\r\n💡 记忆\r\n\r\nprevail = become dominant / come out on top\r\n\r\n可以记成：\r\n\r\nprevail → 占上风 → 最终胜出','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8e2347361059402facedbe1e774d0353.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-21 09:48:46',1,'2026-08-21 09:48:46'),(1454,20,50,'vocab','obstacle','obstacle','obstacle','🎯 词性\r\nnoun 名词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n1. 障碍物\r\n2. 障碍；阻碍；困难\r\n它既可以指真实存在、挡住路的东西，也可以指抽象的困难。','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* an obstacle to sth\r\n    ……的障碍\r\n* an obstacle to doing sth\r\n    做某事的障碍\r\n* overcome an obstacle\r\n    克服障碍\r\n* face / encounter an obstacle\r\n    面临 / 遇到障碍\r\n* remove an obstacle\r\n    消除障碍','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* Lack of experience can be an obstacle to finding a good job.\r\n    缺乏经验可能是找到好工作的一个障碍。\r\n* We encountered several obstacles during the project.\r\n    我们在项目过程中遇到了几个障碍。\r\n* She managed to overcome every obstacle.\r\n    她成功克服了所有障碍。\r\n* The fallen tree was blocking the road and became a major obstacle.\r\n    倒下的树挡住了道路，成为一个很大的障碍物。\r\n\r\n⚠️ obstacle vs problem\r\n\r\nproblem\r\n→ 问题，需要解决\r\n\r\nobstacle\r\n→ 挡在你实现目标路上的东西\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n* We have a problem with the database.\r\n    数据库出了问题。\r\n* Limited time is a major obstacle to completing the project.\r\n    时间有限是完成项目的一大障碍。\r\n\r\n💡 记忆\r\n\r\n把它想成：\r\n\r\ngoal → obstacle → overcome → success\r\n\r\n目标 → 遇到障碍 → 克服 → 成功\r\n\r\n所以最值得记住的搭配是：\r\n\r\novercome an obstacle = 克服障碍','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a5cfb5ee45224c8c9edcf7959ddf660b.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-21 11:23:42',1,'2026-08-21 11:23:42'),(1455,20,51,'vocab','indicator','indicator','indicator','🎯 词性\r\nnoun 名词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n1. 指标；迹象；信号\r\n2. 指示器；显示装置\r\n3. 转向灯（英式英语里也可以这样说）\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* an indicator of sth\r\n    ……的指标 / 迹象\r\n* a key indicator\r\n    关键指标\r\n* economic indicator\r\n    经济指标\r\n* performance indicator\r\n    绩效指标\r\n* status indicator\r\n    状态指示器\r\n* warning indicator\r\n    警告指示器','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* High CPU usage can be an indicator of a performance problem.\r\n    CPU 使用率很高可能是性能问题的一个迹象。\r\n* Customer satisfaction is an important indicator of service quality.\r\n    客户满意度是衡量服务质量的重要指标。\r\n* The red light is a warning indicator.\r\n    红灯是一个警告指示灯。\r\n* This dashboard shows several key performance indicators.\r\n    这个仪表盘显示了几个关键绩效指标。','💻 在软件开发里非常常见\r\n\r\nindicator 经常表示某种“状态或情况的显示”。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n* loading indicator\r\n    加载指示器\r\n* progress indicator\r\n    进度指示器\r\n* status indicator\r\n    状态指示器\r\n* error indicator\r\n    错误提示标识\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe UI should display a loading indicator while the document is being processed.\r\n文档处理期间，界面应该显示一个加载指示器。\r\n\r\n⚠️ indicator vs indication\r\n\r\nindicator\r\n→ 一个具体的“指标 / 信号 / 东西”\r\n\r\nindication\r\n→ 某件事表现出来的“迹象”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nHigh error rates are an indicator of a system problem.\r\n高错误率是系统存在问题的一个指标。\r\n\r\nThere is no indication that the system has failed.\r\n没有迹象表明系统已经失败。\r\n\r\n💡 词汇家族\r\n\r\n* indicate v. 指示；表明\r\n* indicator n. 指标；指示器\r\n* indication n. 迹象；表明\r\n* indicative adj. 表明……的；指示性的\r\n\r\n💡 记忆\r\n\r\nindicate → 表明\r\nindicator → 用来表明某种状态的东西\r\n\r\n可以记成：\r\n\r\nindicator = 指标 / 指示器 / 信号','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f7a734276bce48e4a4664c62ed015d18.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-21 11:53:26',1,'2026-08-21 11:53:26'),(1456,20,52,'phrase','recur & recurrence','recur & recurrence','recur & recurrence','🔊 发音\r\n\r\n* recur /rɪˈkɜːr/ — verb 动词\r\n* recurrence /rɪˈkʌrəns/ — noun 名词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nrecur = 再次发生；反复出现；复发\r\n强调“某件事又发生了”。\r\n\r\nrecurrence = 再次发生；反复出现；复发\r\n是 recur 的名词形式，强调“再次发生这件事”。','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\nrecur\r\n\r\n* recur regularly → 定期反复发生\r\n* recur frequently → 频繁出现\r\n* the problem recurs → 问题再次出现\r\n\r\nrecurrence\r\n\r\n* prevent recurrence → 防止再次发生\r\n* risk of recurrence → 再次发生 / 复发的风险\r\n* recurrence of the issue → 问题再次出现\r\n* recurrence rate → 复发率 / 再发生率','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* The same problem keeps recurring.\r\n    同样的问题一直反复出现。\r\n* If the error recurs, check the log first.\r\n    如果错误再次出现，先检查日志。\r\n* We need to identify the root cause and prevent recurrence.\r\n    我们需要找出根本原因，并防止问题再次发生。\r\n* There has been no recurrence of the issue.\r\n    这个问题没有再次出现。\r\n\r\n🔄 词形关系\r\n\r\nrecur → recurrence → recurring\r\n\r\n* recur = 动词：再次发生\r\n    The issue may recur.\r\n* recurrence = 名词：再次发生\r\n    We want to prevent a recurrence.\r\n* recurring = 形容词：反复发生的\r\n    This is a recurring issue.\r\n\r\n⚠️ recur vs occur\r\n\r\noccur = 发生\r\n\r\nThe error occurred yesterday.\r\n错误昨天发生了。\r\n\r\nrecur = 再次发生\r\n\r\nThe error recurred today.\r\n错误今天又出现了。\r\n\r\n💡 记忆方法\r\n\r\nre- = again 再一次\r\n\r\nre + occur 的感觉 → recur = 又发生\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nrecur = 又发生\r\nrecurrence = “又发生”这件事\r\n\r\n📌 工作中很好用的一句：\r\n\r\nWe need to find the root cause to prevent recurrence.\r\n我们需要找到根本原因，防止问题再次发生。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/896ee6df3ee34c6a88044abfa35774a1.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-21 18:16:12',1,'2026-08-21 18:16:12'),(1457,20,53,'vocab','vaccine','vaccine','vaccine','📌 vaccine /ˈvæk.siːn/\r\n词性： noun 名词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nvaccine = 疫苗\r\n\r\n指用于帮助身体建立免疫力、预防某种疾病的制剂。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* get a vaccine → 接种疫苗\r\n* receive a vaccine → 接种疫苗\r\n* develop a vaccine → 研发疫苗\r\n* vaccine dose → 一剂疫苗\r\n* vaccine effectiveness → 疫苗有效性\r\n* flu vaccine → 流感疫苗\r\n* COVID-19 vaccine → 新冠疫苗','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* I got the flu vaccine last week.\r\n    我上周接种了流感疫苗。\r\n* Scientists are developing a new vaccine.\r\n    科学家正在研发一种新疫苗。\r\n* This vaccine requires two doses.\r\n    这种疫苗需要接种两剂。\r\n\r\n🔄 vaccine vs vaccination\r\n\r\nvaccine = 疫苗本身\r\n\r\nThe vaccine is available now.\r\n这种疫苗现在已经可以接种了。\r\n\r\nvaccination = 接种疫苗这一行为\r\n\r\nVaccination can help prevent disease.\r\n接种疫苗有助于预防疾病。\r\n\r\n💡 相关词\r\n\r\n* vaccinate /ˈvæk.sɪ.neɪt/ → 给……接种疫苗\r\n* vaccinated → 已接种疫苗的\r\n* vaccination → 疫苗接种\r\n\r\n📌 记忆：\r\n\r\nvaccine = 疫苗\r\nvaccinate = 打疫苗\r\nvaccination = 接种疫苗这件事','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/83ddbdf754d74f38b09fd987adb16cbe.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-21 18:24:29',1,'2026-08-21 18:24:29'),(1458,20,54,'vocab','can halve their electricity bills','can halve their electricity bills','can halve their electricity bills','🔊 halve /hɑːv/\r\nv. 减半；使减少一半\r\n\r\n🎯 整句话：\r\ncan halve their electricity bills\r\n= 可以把他们的电费减少一半 / 可以让电费减半','🧩 结构：\r\nhalve + something = 把某物减半\r\n\r\n* halve the cost = 把成本减半\r\n* halve the time = 把时间缩短一半\r\n* halve electricity bills = 让电费减半\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\nInstalling solar panels can halve your electricity bills.\r\n安装太阳能板可以让你的电费减少一半。\r\n\r\n⚠️ halve ≠ half\r\n\r\n* half → 通常是名词/形容词：一半的\r\n* halve → 动词：使减半\r\n\r\n例如：\r\nThe bill was cut in half. = 账单减少了一半。\r\nWe halved the bill. = 我们把账单减半了。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/32d1ff4e191e4e268869f99f75cc946c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 09:56:24',1,'2026-08-22 09:56:24'),(1459,20,55,'vocab','irrigation','irrigation','irrigation','🔊 /ˌɪrɪˈɡeɪʃən/\r\n词性：noun 名词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思：灌溉；灌溉系统\r\n\r\n指为了帮助农作物、草地等生长，人工给土地供水。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* irrigation system = 灌溉系统\r\n* irrigation water = 灌溉用水\r\n* irrigation canal = 灌溉渠\r\n* drip irrigation = 滴灌\r\n* irrigation equipment = 灌溉设备','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* Farmers rely on irrigation during dry periods.\r\n    干旱时期，农民依靠灌溉。\r\n* The farm uses a modern irrigation system.\r\n    这个农场使用现代化的灌溉系统。\r\n* Drip irrigation can reduce water waste.\r\n    滴灌可以减少水资源浪费。\r\n\r\n🧠 词形联系\r\n\r\n* irrigate /ˈɪrɪɡeɪt/ → v. 灌溉\r\n* irrigation → n. 灌溉\r\n\r\n👉 They irrigate the fields.\r\n他们给田地灌溉。\r\n\r\n👉 The fields need irrigation.\r\n这些田地需要灌溉。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 发音重点：\r\nir-ri-GA-tion\r\n重音在 GA：/ˌɪrɪˈɡeɪʃən/','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/1f1c6e9a89814915a056a87865886ef5.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 09:59:02',1,'2026-08-22 09:59:02'),(1460,20,56,'vocab','machinery','machinery','machinery','🔊 /məˈʃiːnəri/\r\n词性：noun 名词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思：机械；机器设备；机械装置的总称\r\n\r\nmachinery 通常不是指“一台机器”，而是指一整套、很多台机器或设备。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* heavy machinery = 重型机械\r\n* farm machinery = 农业机械\r\n* industrial machinery = 工业机械\r\n* machinery equipment = 机械设备\r\n* operate machinery = 操作机械\r\n* machinery maintenance = 机械维护','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* The factory uses modern machinery.\r\n    这家工厂使用现代化机械设备。\r\n* Farmers rely on heavy machinery during harvest season.\r\n    收获季节，农民依赖重型农业机械。\r\n* Only trained workers are allowed to operate this machinery.\r\n    只有受过培训的工人才可以操作这些机械设备。\r\n\r\n⚠️ machinery vs. machine\r\n\r\n* machine = 一台具体的机器，可数\r\n    a machine / two machines\r\n* machinery = 机械设备的总称，通常不可数\r\n    ✅ some machinery\r\n    ✅ a piece of machinery\r\n    ❌ a machinery\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nmachine → 一台机器\r\nmachinery → 一整套机器设备\r\n\r\n👉 The machine is broken.\r\n这台机器坏了。\r\n\r\n👉 The machinery is expensive.\r\n这套机械设备很贵。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/0b0203904a8e4c7099c4e69d39859d05.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 10:01:30',1,'2026-08-22 10:01:30'),(1461,20,57,'vocab','upfront','upfront','upfront','🔊 /ˌʌpˈfrʌnt/\r\n词性：adjective / adverb 形容词 / 副词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思 1：预先的；前期的；一开始就要支付的\r\n🎯 核心意思 2：坦率的；直截了当的','这是你刚才句子里的意思：\r\n\r\nupfront costs\r\n= 前期成本 / 初始费用\r\n\r\n🧩 常见搭配：\r\n\r\n* upfront cost = 前期成本\r\n* upfront payment = 预付款\r\n* upfront fee = 预先支付的费用\r\n* pay upfront = 预先付款\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思 1：预先的；前期的；一开始就要支付的\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\n* There is a high upfront cost.\r\n    前期成本很高。\r\n* You need to pay $500 upfront.\r\n    你需要先付 500 美元。','🎯 核心意思 2：坦率的；直截了当的\r\n\r\n这里通常形容一个人说话很直接。\r\n\r\n* be upfront about something\r\n    = 对某事坦诚说明\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\n* He was upfront about the risks.\r\n    他很坦率地说明了风险。\r\n* I want to be upfront with you.\r\n    我想跟你坦白说。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意两种意思不要混淆\r\n\r\nupfront cost\r\n→ 前期成本\r\n\r\nbe upfront with someone\r\n→ 对某人坦诚、直率\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆：\r\n\r\nup + front → “放到最前面”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\n* 钱放到最前面付 → 预先支付\r\n* 话放到前面直接说 → 坦率、直接','/static/uploads/english_note_item/1d3d3b37aa9d47ee9dd79386b0be7eba.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 10:06:53',1,'2026-08-22 10:06:53'),(1462,20,58,'vocab','hurdle','hurdle','hurdle','🔊 /ˈhɜːdəl/\r\n词性：noun / verb 名词 / 动词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思 1：障碍；难关\r\n🎯 核心意思 2：跨栏；跨越障碍','🎯 核心意思 1：障碍；难关\r\n\r\n原意是田径比赛里的“跨栏”，所以经常用来比喻需要克服的问题或障碍。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见搭配：\r\n\r\n* a major hurdle = 一个主要障碍\r\n* a big hurdle = 一个大难题\r\n* overcome a hurdle = 克服障碍\r\n* clear a hurdle = 跨过障碍 / 克服难关\r\n* remain a hurdle = 仍然是一个障碍\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\n* Cost remains a major hurdle.\r\n    成本仍然是一个主要障碍。\r\n* The upfront costs remain a hurdle for many homeowners.\r\n    对很多房主来说，前期成本仍然是一个障碍。\r\n* We still have a few hurdles to overcome.\r\n    我们还有几个难关需要克服。\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思 2：跨栏；跨越障碍\r\n\r\n作动词时：\r\n\r\nhurdle over something\r\n= 跳过 / 跨过某物\r\n\r\n💬 The athlete hurdled over the barrier.\r\n运动员跨过了障碍物。\r\n\r\n⚠️ hurdle vs. obstacle\r\n\r\n* hurdle → 强调“可以想办法跨过去的难关”，很常用于商业、项目、成本等语境\r\n* obstacle → 更泛指任何阻碍、障碍物\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe high upfront cost is a hurdle.\r\n高额前期成本是一个需要克服的难题。\r\n\r\nA fallen tree was an obstacle on the road.\r\n一棵倒下的树是路上的障碍物。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法：\r\n\r\n把 hurdle 想成运动员面前的“跨栏”。\r\n\r\n👉 You don’t stop at a hurdle — you get over it.\r\n遇到 hurdle，不是停下来，而是想办法跨过去。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ba10028a4832440da0520d51ffc9e200.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 10:12:19',1,'2026-08-22 10:12:19'),(1463,20,59,'vocab','surplus','surplus','surplus','🔊 /ˈsɜːpləs/\r\n词性：noun / adjective 名词 / 形容词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思：剩余；过剩；盈余\r\n\r\n表示超过实际需要的数量。','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* a surplus of something = 某物的过剩\r\n* budget surplus = 预算盈余\r\n* trade surplus = 贸易顺差\r\n* surplus energy = 多余的能源\r\n* surplus electricity = 多余的电力\r\n* surplus food = 过剩的食物\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\n* The solar panels produce surplus electricity during the day.\r\n    太阳能板白天会产生多余的电力。\r\n* The country recorded a trade surplus last year.\r\n    这个国家去年实现了贸易顺差。\r\n* Any surplus energy can be stored in a battery.\r\n    多余的能源可以储存在电池里。\r\n\r\n⚠️ surplus vs. excess\r\n\r\n* surplus → 超过需求后“剩下来的”，常见于经济、能源、库存\r\n* excess → 超过正常或合理范围，常带“过多”的感觉\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nsurplus electricity\r\n= 用不完剩下的电\r\n\r\nexcess electricity consumption\r\n= 过度的用电量\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nsurplus = more than needed\r\n\r\n👉 need 100 → have 130 → surplus = 30\r\n\r\n也就是：\r\n需要 100，但有 130，多出来的 30 就是 surplus。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3f0e2a71b3d640b0a807ba880cd1e603.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 10:16:04',1,'2026-08-22 10:16:04'),(1464,20,60,'vocab','subsidy','subsidy','subsidy','🔊 /ˈsʌbsədi/\r\n词性：noun 名词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思：补贴；津贴；政府补助\r\n\r\n通常指政府或机构提供的钱，目的是降低某种成本，或者鼓励某个行业、产品或行为。','🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* government subsidy = 政府补贴\r\n* energy subsidy = 能源补贴\r\n* housing subsidy = 住房补贴\r\n* agricultural subsidy = 农业补贴\r\n* receive a subsidy = 获得补贴\r\n* provide a subsidy = 提供补贴\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\n* The government offers a subsidy for solar panels.\r\n    政府为太阳能板提供补贴。\r\n* Farmers can apply for a government subsidy.\r\n    农民可以申请政府补贴。\r\n* The subsidy helps reduce the upfront cost.\r\n    这项补贴有助于降低前期成本。\r\n\r\n🔄 单复数\r\n\r\n* subsidy = 一项补贴\r\n* subsidies = 多项补贴\r\n\r\n⚠️ subsidy vs. rebate\r\n\r\n* subsidy → 政府或机构给予的补贴\r\n* rebate → 买完之后返还一部分钱\r\n\r\n🧠 发音重点\r\n\r\nSUB-si-dy\r\n/ˈsʌb.sə.di/\r\n\r\n重音在第一音节：SUB\r\n\r\n👉 subsidy → subsidies\r\n单数变复数时：-y → -ies','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/18b2afb8230d42edb961db31ce9e328a.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 10:19:16',1,'2026-08-22 10:19:16'),(1465,20,61,'vocab','stationary','stationary','stationary','🔊 /ˈsteɪʃənəri/\r\n词性：adjective 形容词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思：静止的；不动的；固定的\r\n\r\n表示某个物体没有移动。','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* remain stationary = 保持静止\r\n* a stationary vehicle = 静止的车辆\r\n* stationary bike = 健身单车 / 固定式自行车\r\n* stationary object = 静止物体','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* The car remained stationary at the traffic lights.\r\n    汽车停在红绿灯前没有移动。\r\n* The machine must be stationary before maintenance begins.\r\n    维修开始前，机器必须处于静止状态。\r\n* I use a stationary bike at the gym.\r\n    我在健身房用固定式健身单车。\r\n\r\n⚠️ stationary vs. stationery\r\n\r\n这两个词发音几乎一样，但意思完全不同：\r\n\r\n* stationary = 静止的，不动的\r\n* stationery = 文具\r\n\r\n💬 对比：\r\nThe car is stationary.\r\n车是静止的。\r\n\r\nI bought some stationery.\r\n我买了一些文具。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nstationary 里面有 station\r\n→ station = 站、车站\r\n→ 停在那里不动\r\n→ stationary = 静止的','/static/uploads/english_note_item/036040b49c334853be16d22a5ad7f8cd.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 10:33:26',1,'2026-08-22 10:33:26'),(1466,20,62,'vocab','inhabitant','inhabitant','inhabitant','🔊 /ɪnˈhæbɪtənt/\r\n词性：noun 名词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思：居民；居住者\r\n\r\n指住在某个地方的人或动物。','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* local inhabitants = 当地居民\r\n* the inhabitants of a city = 一个城市的居民\r\n* island inhabitants = 岛上的居民\r\n* native inhabitants = 本地居民 / 原住居民\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\n* The island has about 5,000 inhabitants.\r\n    这个岛大约有 5,000 名居民。\r\n* Most of the inhabitants live near the coast.\r\n    大多数居民住在沿海地区。\r\n* The forest is home to many animal inhabitants.\r\n    这片森林是许多动物的栖息地。\r\n\r\n⚠️ inhabitant vs. resident\r\n\r\n* inhabitant → 强调“居住在某个地方的人”，常见于地理、人口描述，稍正式\r\n* resident → 更常用于日常生活、行政、身份语境\r\n\r\n例如：\r\nThe city has one million inhabitants.\r\n这座城市有一百万居民。\r\n\r\nI’m a resident of Christchurch.\r\n我是基督城居民。\r\n\r\n🧠 词形联系\r\n\r\n* inhabit = 居住于\r\n* inhabitant = 居民\r\n* habitat = 栖息地\r\n\r\n👉 People inhabit the island.\r\n人们居住在这个岛上。\r\n\r\n👉 They are the island’s inhabitants.\r\n他们是这个岛上的居民。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f1c83d30011d43fe87dbf37e4eb71b9f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 10:56:02',1,'2026-08-22 10:56:02'),(1467,20,63,'vocab','megacity / megacities','megacity / megacities','megacity / megacities','🔊 megacity /ˈmeɡəsɪti/\r\n词性：noun 名词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思：特大城市；超大城市\r\n\r\n通常指人口超过 1,000 万 的城市。','🧩 单复数\r\n\r\n* megacity = 一个特大城市\r\n* megacities = 多个特大城市\r\n\r\n👉 复数变化：\r\ncity → cities\r\n所以：\r\nmegacity → megacities\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\n* Tokyo is one of the world’s largest megacities.\r\n    东京是世界上最大的特大城市之一。\r\n* Many megacities face problems such as traffic congestion and air pollution.\r\n    许多特大城市面临交通拥堵和空气污染等问题。\r\n* Rapid urbanization has led to the growth of megacities.\r\n    快速城市化推动了特大城市的发展。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* a rapidly growing megacity = 快速发展的特大城市\r\n* the world’s megacities = 世界上的特大城市\r\n* megacity population = 特大城市人口\r\n* megacity development = 特大城市发展\r\n\r\n⚠️ 拼写注意：\r\n\r\n❌ megcity\r\n✅ megacity\r\n\r\n🧠 拆词记忆\r\n\r\nmega- = 巨大的、超大的\r\ncity = 城市\r\n\r\n👉 mega + city = megacity\r\n= 超大城市','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/dc82f0e1c09e4904b5d5c0044b73fd7f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 11:02:46',1,'2026-08-22 11:02:46'),(1468,20,64,'vocab','aid','aid','aid','🔊 /eɪd/\r\n词性：noun / verb 名词 / 动词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思：帮助；援助；协助\r\n\r\n1️⃣ 作名词：帮助；援助\r\n\r\n2️⃣ 作动词：帮助；协助','1️⃣ 作名词：帮助；援助\r\n\r\n常用于比较正式的语境。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见搭配：\r\n\r\n* financial aid = 经济援助 / 助学金\r\n* government aid = 政府援助\r\n* humanitarian aid = 人道主义援助\r\n* foreign aid = 对外援助\r\n* first aid = 急救\r\n* come to someone’s aid = 前来帮助某人\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\n* The country received international aid after the earthquake.\r\n    地震后，这个国家得到了国际援助。\r\n* Many students apply for financial aid.\r\n    很多学生申请经济援助。','2️⃣ 作动词：帮助；协助\r\n\r\naid someone in doing something\r\n= 帮助某人做某事\r\n\r\naid in something\r\n= 有助于某事\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\n* This technology can aid in reducing energy costs.\r\n    这项技术有助于降低能源成本。\r\n* The new system aids workers in completing the task faster.\r\n    新系统帮助员工更快完成任务。\r\n\r\n⚠️ aid vs. help\r\n\r\n* help → 最常用，口语和书面语都很自然\r\n* aid → 更正式，常用于政府、医疗、灾害、经济等语境\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nCan you help me?\r\n你能帮我吗？✅ 日常最自然\r\n\r\nThe government provided financial aid.\r\n政府提供了经济援助。✅ 正式语境\r\n\r\n🧠 高频短语\r\n\r\nfirst aid = 急救\r\n\r\n这个非常常见，建议一起记。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9e529a325bf3496290aa27faf085e622.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 11:09:32',1,'2026-08-22 11:09:32'),(1469,20,65,'phrase','relatively recent','relatively recent','relatively recent','🔊 relatively /ˈrelətɪvli/\r\n🔊 recent /ˈriːsənt/\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思：相对较新的；相对较近发生的\r\n\r\n这里 relatively = 相对来说；比较而言，所以：\r\n\r\nrelatively recent\r\n= 相对较新的 / 比较近期的','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* This is a relatively recent development.\r\n    这是一个相对较新的发展。\r\n* Broadband is a relatively recent technology compared with the telephone.\r\n    与电话相比，宽带是一项相对较新的技术。\r\n* Urbanization in this region is relatively recent.\r\n    这个地区的城市化是相对较近才发生的。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见结构\r\n\r\n* relatively recent phenomenon = 相对较新的现象\r\n* relatively recent development = 相对较新的发展\r\n* relatively recent change = 相对近期的变化\r\n\r\n⚠️ recent vs. relatively recent\r\n\r\n* recent = 最近的\r\n* relatively recent = 相对而言算比较新的，不一定真的“非常最近”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe internet is relatively recent compared with printing.\r\n互联网和印刷术相比，是相对较新的事物。\r\n\r\n🧠 可以直接记成：\r\n\r\nrelatively = relatively speaking = 相对来说\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nrelatively recent = 相对来说比较新的','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/80a1504ae0a848ca8cb6a33b8af7c60c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 11:41:38',1,'2026-08-22 11:41:38'),(1470,20,66,'vocab','dominate','dominate','dominate','🔊 /ˈdɒməneɪt/\r\n词性：verb 动词\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思：支配；占主导地位；控制；在……中占优势\r\n\r\n强调某个人、事物或力量明显比其他的更强、更重要，或者占据主要位置。','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* dominate the market = 主导市场\r\n* dominate the industry = 主导行业\r\n* dominate the competition = 在竞争中占绝对优势\r\n* dominate the discussion = 主导讨论\r\n* be dominated by = 被……主导 /  dominated by','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* A few large companies dominate the market.\r\n    几家大型公司主导着这个市场。\r\n* Cars dominate transport in many cities.\r\n    在许多城市，汽车在交通方式中占主导地位。\r\n* The conversation was dominated by one topic.\r\n    整场谈话主要围绕一个话题展开。\r\n\r\n⚠️ dominate vs. control\r\n\r\n* dominate → 强调“占主导、比其他的更强”\r\n* control → 强调“直接控制、掌控”\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThis company dominates the market.\r\n这家公司占据市场主导地位。\r\n\r\nThis company controls the system.\r\n这家公司控制这个系统。\r\n\r\n🧠 词形联系\r\n\r\n* dominate = 主导；支配\r\n* dominant = 占主导地位的\r\n* dominance = 主导地位；优势\r\n\r\n👉 a dominant company = 一家占主导地位的公司\r\n👉 market dominance = 市场主导地位','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8e24d1438c174540862e581a68330d69.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 11:46:54',1,'2026-08-22 11:46:54'),(1471,20,67,'phrase','drift across','drift across','drift across','🎯 核心意思\r\n缓慢地飘过 / 漂过 / 移过\r\n\r\ndrift = 漂、飘、缓慢移动\r\nacross = 穿过、横过','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* clouds drift across the sky\r\n    云朵飘过天空\r\n* smoke drifts across the road\r\n    烟雾飘过道路\r\n* showers drift across the region\r\n    阵雨缓慢移过这个地区\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\nA few showers may drift across the coast this afternoon.\r\n今天下午可能有几阵雨缓慢移过沿海地区。\r\n\r\n⚠️ drift across vs move across\r\n\r\n* move across = 普通地移动经过\r\n* drift across = 慢慢地、自然地飘过去，通常没有很强的动力感\r\n\r\n🌦️ 天气预报里特别常见：\r\nCloud is drifting across the South Island.\r\n云层正在缓慢移过南岛。\r\n\r\n另外，drift across 是原形；drifting across 是现在分词形式。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a091ddb8c9d54aaabcd5c72ea967da4f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 20:06:48',1,'2026-08-22 20:06:48'),(1472,20,68,'phrase','question mark','question mark','question mark','🔊 读音：/ˈkwestʃən mɑːk/ 🇬🇧\r\n美式：/ˈkwestʃən mɑːrk/\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n1. 问号：?\r\n2. 疑问 / 不确定性\r\n3. 值得怀疑的地方','🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* add a question mark\r\n    加一个问号\r\n* put a question mark at the end\r\n    在结尾加问号\r\n* end with a question mark\r\n    以问号结尾\r\n* a question mark over something\r\n    某事存在疑问 / 不确定性\r\n* raise a question mark over something\r\n    使人对某事产生怀疑\r\n* leave a question mark\r\n    留下疑问','💬 例句\r\n\r\nDon’t forget to add a question mark at the end of the sentence.\r\n别忘了在句子结尾加问号。\r\n\r\nThis sentence should end with a question mark.\r\n这个句子应该以问号结尾。\r\n\r\nWhy is there a question mark here?\r\n为什么这里有一个问号？\r\n\r\nYou don’t need a question mark because this isn’t a question.\r\n你不需要加问号，因为这不是一个问句。\r\n\r\nThere is still a big question mark over the project.\r\n这个项目目前仍然存在很大的不确定性。\r\n\r\nHis ability to manage the team is still a question mark.\r\n他管理团队的能力仍然是个未知数。\r\n\r\nThe test results put a question mark over the reliability of the system.\r\n测试结果让人对这个系统的可靠性产生了怀疑。\r\n\r\nThe missing data leaves a question mark over the final result.\r\n缺失的数据让最终结果仍然存在疑问。\r\n\r\n💻 工作 / 程序员场景\r\n\r\nI put a question mark next to this field because I’m not sure about the value.\r\n我在这个字段旁边加了一个问号，因为我不确定这个值。\r\n\r\nThere is still a question mark over how this API handles invalid input.\r\n这个 API 如何处理无效输入目前还存在疑问。\r\n\r\nThe performance issue is still a question mark.\r\n这个性能问题目前还没有定论。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 常见区别\r\n\r\nquestion mark = 问号 / 疑问\r\nquestion = 问题\r\ndoubt = 怀疑\r\nuncertainty = 不确定性\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI have a question.\r\n我有一个问题。\r\n\r\nThere is a question mark over this result.\r\n这个结果存在疑问。\r\n\r\n📌 很实用的口语表达\r\n\r\nThat’s still a bit of a question mark.\r\n这个目前还有点不确定。\r\n\r\n这个表达在工作讨论里很好用。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ec910f800fdb460fbca7da8cfebb79ba.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 20:15:11',1,'2026-08-22 20:15:11'),(1473,20,69,'phrase','to put this in perspective','to put this in perspective','to put this in perspective','🎯 核心意思\r\n为了让这件事更容易理解 / 放到更大的背景下来看 / 做个对比你就明白了\r\n\r\n这个短语常用于：先给出一个数字、事实或情况，然后通过比较或补充背景，让听者真正理解它有多大、多严重、多特别。','🧩 拆开理解\r\n\r\n* put something in perspective\r\n    = 把某事放到合适的背景中看\r\n* to put this in perspective\r\n    = 为了让你更直观地理解这件事','💬 常见例句\r\n\r\nThe system processes 200 million messages a month. To put this in perspective, that’s more than 6 million messages a day.\r\n这个系统每个月处理 2 亿条消息。为了让你更直观地理解，相当于每天超过 600 万条。\r\n\r\nThe mountain is 3,000 metres high. To put that in perspective, it’s almost three times the height of Mount Cook’s lower surrounding peaks.\r\n这座山高 3000 米。做个对比你就更容易理解它有多高。\r\n\r\nThe file took five minutes to process. To put this in perspective, our target is only two and a half minutes.\r\n这个文件处理用了 5 分钟。作为对比，我们的目标只有 2 分半。\r\n\r\nThe error rate is only 1%. To put that in perspective, that still means 10,000 failed requests out of one million.\r\n错误率只有 1%。但换个角度看，一百万次请求里仍然有一万次失败。\r\n\r\n💻 工作里很好用\r\n\r\nTo put this in perspective, the new workflow cuts the processing time by almost half.\r\n为了更直观地说明，新流程几乎把处理时间缩短了一半。\r\n\r\nTo put this in perspective, most of the failed fields come from handwritten content.\r\n从整体背景来看，大多数识别失败的字段都来自手写内容。\r\n\r\n⚠️ this / that 都可以\r\n\r\n* To put this in perspective…\r\n    更贴近刚刚正在讲的内容\r\n* To put that in perspective…\r\n    更常见，回指前面刚说过的数字或事实\r\n\r\n📌 很自然的口语模板：\r\n\r\nTo put that in perspective, …\r\n= 做个对比你就明白了，……\r\n\r\n例如：\r\nTo put that in perspective, that’s twice as much as last year.\r\n做个对比你就明白了，这是去年的两倍。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/487f822e1449408da5ca0b175807eca8.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 20:42:33',1,'2026-08-22 20:42:33'),(1474,20,70,'phrase','a pinch of salt','a pinch of salt','a pinch of salt','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n字面意思：一小撮盐\r\n\r\n* a pinch = 用拇指和食指捏起的一小撮\r\n* salt = 盐','所以：\r\n\r\na pinch of salt\r\n= 一小撮盐\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nAdd a pinch of salt to the soup.\r\n往汤里加一小撮盐。\r\n\r\nYou only need a pinch of salt.\r\n你只需要一点点盐。\r\n\r\nMix in a pinch of salt and some pepper.\r\n加入一小撮盐和一些胡椒。\r\n\r\n🧩 非常重要的固定表达\r\n\r\ntake something with a pinch of salt 🇬🇧\r\n= 对某事半信半疑 / 不要完全当真\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI’d take what he says with a pinch of salt.\r\n他说的话我不会完全相信。\r\n\r\nYou should take online reviews with a pinch of salt.\r\n网上的评论不能完全当真。\r\n\r\n🇺🇸 美式英语更常说：\r\n\r\ntake something with a grain of salt\r\n\r\n意思完全一样。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 对比：\r\n\r\n* a pinch of salt → 一小撮盐\r\n* with a pinch of salt → 半信半疑地看待\r\n* a grain of salt → 一粒盐；也常用于美式固定表达\r\n\r\n📌 很实用的一句：\r\n\r\nTake that with a pinch of salt.\r\n这话听听就好，别全信。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/fa88781a1198495bbb96a468d8a24a08.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 21:06:51',1,'2026-08-22 21:06:51'),(1475,20,71,'vocab','pristine','pristine','pristine','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n1. 崭新的；保存完好的\r\n2. 纯净的；未受污染的\r\n3. 一尘不染的；非常整洁的','🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* pristine condition = 保存完好的状态\r\n* pristine environment = 原生态、未受污染的环境\r\n* pristine beach = 洁净原始的海滩\r\n* pristine water = 清澈纯净的水\r\n* pristine white shirt = 洁白如新的衬衫','💬 例句\r\n\r\nThe car is still in pristine condition.\r\n这辆车仍然保存得非常好，几乎像新的一样。\r\n\r\nThe island is famous for its pristine beaches.\r\n这个岛以洁净、原生态的海滩而闻名。\r\n\r\nWe need to protect this pristine environment.\r\n我们需要保护这片未受污染的自然环境。\r\n\r\nThe room was absolutely pristine.\r\n这个房间干净得一尘不染。\r\n\r\nThe document was kept in pristine condition.\r\n这份文件保存得完好无损。\r\n\r\n⚠️ pristine vs clean\r\n\r\n* clean = 干净的，普通表达\r\n* pristine = 极其干净、完好，几乎没有被破坏或使用过\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe beach is clean.\r\n海滩很干净。\r\n\r\nThe beach is pristine.\r\n海滩非常纯净、原生态，几乎没有受到人为破坏。\r\n\r\n📌 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 pristine 想成：\r\n\r\n“像刚出厂、刚形成、没人碰过一样完美。”\r\n\r\n很适合形容 nature / beach / condition / environment / water。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/0de52386e0104157a8cc3a45b121a7cc.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 21:09:21',1,'2026-08-22 21:09:21'),(1476,20,72,'phrase','be home to','be home to','be home to','be home to + 人 / 动物 / 事物\r\n= 是……的所在地 / 栖息地 / 家园 / 拥有……\r\n\r\n它不是简单的“家到……”，而是一个很常见的固定表达。','🧩 常见结构\r\n\r\nA is home to B\r\n= A 是 B 的所在地 / A 拥有 B\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nNew Zealand is home to many unique bird species.\r\n新西兰是许多独特鸟类的家园。\r\n\r\nThis region is home to several large technology companies.\r\n这个地区有好几家大型科技公司。\r\n\r\nThe forest is home to hundreds of animal species.\r\n这片森林是数百种动物的栖息地。\r\n\r\nChristchurch is home to many parks and gardens.\r\n基督城拥有很多公园和花园。\r\n\r\nThe database is home to millions of records.\r\n这个数据库里存有数百万条记录。\r\n\r\n⚠️ home to vs live in\r\n\r\n* A is home to B\r\n    强调 某地拥有 / 容纳 B\r\n* B lives in A\r\n    强调 B 住在 A\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nNew Zealand is home to kiwi birds.\r\n新西兰是几维鸟的家园。\r\n\r\nKiwi birds live in New Zealand.\r\n几维鸟生活在新西兰。\r\n\r\n📌 很实用的模板：\r\n\r\nThis area is home to…\r\n这个地区有……\r\n\r\nThe country is home to…\r\n这个国家拥有……\r\n\r\nThe lake is home to…\r\n这个湖是……的栖息地。','拥有 / 坐落着 / 是……所在地\r\n\r\n不过如果是在介绍景点，更自然的表达还有：\r\n\r\n* New Zealand is home to the famous Ninety Mile Beach.\r\n    新西兰有著名的九十英里海滩。\r\n* Ninety Mile Beach is located in New Zealand.\r\n    九十英里海滩位于新西兰。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f35aa2c110db48a1a55a00dd270c68ef.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-22 21:20:12',1,'2026-08-22 21:20:12'),(1477,20,73,'phrase','equivalent to','equivalent to','equivalent to','🎯 核心意思\r\nequivalent to = 相当于；等同于；与……具有同等价值/效果\r\n\r\n强调两样东西虽然形式可能不同，但在价值、效果、数量、意义或功能上相同或相近。','🧩 常见结构\r\n\r\nA is equivalent to B\r\n= A 相当于 B / A 等同于 B\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\n* One kilometre is equivalent to 1,000 metres.\r\n    1 公里等于 1000 米。\r\n* This qualification is equivalent to a university degree.\r\n    这个资格证书相当于大学学位。\r\n* Two hours of exercise is equivalent to about 10,000 steps.\r\n    两小时的运动量大约相当于一万步。\r\n* In programming, these two approaches are roughly equivalent to each other.\r\n    在编程中，这两种方法大致是等效的。','💻 工作场景\r\n\r\n* This value is equivalent to the value in the test sheet.\r\n    这个值等同于 test sheet 里的值。\r\n* 4090 mV is equivalent to 4.09 V.\r\n    4090 毫伏相当于 4.09 伏。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 容易混淆\r\n\r\nequal to → 更强调“数值完全相等”\r\nequivalent to → 更强调“意义、价值、效果、功能相当”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n1000 mV is equal to 1 V.\r\n1000 mV = 1 V。\r\n\r\nThis certificate is equivalent to a degree.\r\n这个证书相当于一个学位。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b8aed34ead8546429708e20c122ddc17.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-23 16:25:43',1,'2026-08-23 16:25:43'),(1478,20,74,'phrase','national grid','national grid','national grid','🎯 核心意思\r\nnational grid = 国家电网；全国电力输送网络\r\n\r\n这里的 grid 指的是把发电站、输电线路、变电站和用户连接起来的整个电力系统。','🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* the national grid 全国电网\r\n* connect to the national grid 接入国家电网\r\n* feed electricity into the national grid 向国家电网输送电力\r\n* supply power to the national grid 向电网供电\r\n* off-grid 离网的，不依赖国家电网','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* The solar panels can feed surplus electricity back into the national grid.\r\n    太阳能板可以把多余的电力输送回国家电网。\r\n* The house is connected to the national grid.\r\n    这栋房子接入了国家电网。\r\n* Some remote homes are not connected to the national grid.\r\n    一些偏远住宅没有接入国家电网。\r\n\r\n⚠️ grid 单独是什么意思？\r\n\r\ngrid 本身有“网格、网络系统”的意思。\r\n在电力语境中，通常就是：\r\n\r\npower grid / electricity grid = 电网\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nnational grid = 全国性的电网系统。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/cc25d3dd5af64721b60c3e1fd09c69a2.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-23 16:49:54',1,'2026-08-23 16:49:54'),(1479,20,75,'vocab','electrified','electrified','electrified','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nelectrified 不只有“电气化的”这一个意思，常见有下面几种。\r\n1. 电气化的\r\n2. 通电的 / 带电的\r\n3. 使某个地区接通电力\r\n4. 让人非常兴奋、激动\r\n5. 形容气氛非常热烈、紧张','1. 电气化的\r\n\r\n表示原本依赖汽油、柴油、蒸汽等，现在改成使用电力。\r\n\r\n* The farm is fully electrified.\r\n    这个农场已经全面电气化。\r\n* The company is moving toward an electrified vehicle fleet.\r\n    这家公司正在把车队逐步电动化。\r\n* The railway was electrified in the 1980s.\r\n    这条铁路在 20 世纪 80 年代完成了电气化。\r\n* The orchard uses electrified machinery instead of diesel-powered equipment.\r\n    这个果园使用电动机械，而不是柴油设备。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n2. 通电的 / 带电的\r\n\r\n强调某个物体本身有电，接触可能有危险。\r\n\r\n* Do not touch the electrified fence.\r\n    不要碰带电围栏。\r\n* The wires are still electrified.\r\n    这些电线仍然带电。\r\n* The security system includes an electrified fence.\r\n    这个安保系统包括一道通电围栏。\r\n\r\n这里很常见：\r\n\r\nelectrified fence = 电围栏 / 带电围栏\r\n\r\n3. 使某个地区接通电力\r\n\r\n常用于历史、基础设施语境。\r\n\r\n* The village was electrified in the 1950s.\r\n    这个村庄在 20 世纪 50 年代通了电。\r\n* Many rural areas were electrified during that period.\r\n    那个时期很多农村地区实现了通电。\r\n\r\n这里的 electrified 可以理解成：\r\n\r\nconnected to an electricity supply\r\n\r\n4. 让人非常兴奋、激动\r\n\r\n这是一个很容易忽略的引申义。\r\n\r\nelectrified = extremely excited / thrilled\r\n\r\n* The crowd was electrified by the performance.\r\n    这场表演让观众异常兴奋。\r\n* The news electrified the whole team.\r\n    这个消息让整个团队都振奋起来。\r\n* Her speech electrified the audience.\r\n    她的演讲让全场观众非常激动。\r\n\r\n🧠 可以理解成中文里的：\r\n\r\n“像过电一样，一下子被点燃了。”\r\n\r\n5. 形容气氛非常热烈、紧张\r\n\r\n也可以说某个地方或气氛被“点燃”。\r\n\r\n* The stadium was electrified after the winning goal.\r\n    制胜球之后，整个体育场的气氛都沸腾了。\r\n* The room became electrified when the results were announced.\r\n    结果公布时，整个房间的气氛一下子紧张而兴奋起来。','⚠️ 几个意思对比\r\n\r\nan electrified railway\r\n→ 电气化铁路\r\n\r\nan electrified fence\r\n→ 带电围栏\r\n\r\nan electrified village\r\n→ 已经通电的村庄\r\n\r\nan electrified crowd\r\n→ 情绪被点燃、异常兴奋的人群\r\n\r\n所以看到 electrified 时，要根据后面的名词判断：\r\n\r\n设备/铁路/农场 → 电气化\r\n电线/围栏 → 带电\r\n村庄/地区 → 通电\r\n人群/观众/气氛 → 非常兴奋、被点燃','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2bb39be5afe64294a1598624c86bda64.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-23 22:07:26',1,'2026-08-23 22:07:26'),(1480,20,76,'phrase','commercial','commercial','commercial','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n1. 商业的；用于赚钱的\r\n2. 商用的；专业经营的\r\n3. 广告\r\n4. 商业化的；迎合市场的','1. 商业的；用于赚钱的\r\n\r\n这是最常见的意思。\r\n\r\n* commercial activity\r\n    商业活动\r\n* commercial business\r\n    商业企业\r\n* commercial property\r\n    商业地产\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\n* The land is used for commercial purposes.\r\n    这块土地用于商业用途。\r\n* They developed the product for commercial use.\r\n    他们开发这个产品是为了商业使用。\r\n\r\n2. 商用的；专业经营的\r\n\r\n强调不是家庭自己用，而是用于正式经营。\r\n\r\n* commercial kitchen\r\n    商用厨房\r\n* commercial vehicle\r\n    商用车辆\r\n* commercial farm\r\n    商业农场\r\n* commercial orchard\r\n    商业果园\r\n\r\n你之前那句话：\r\n\r\nthe world’s first fully electrified commercial orchard\r\n\r\n= 世界上第一个全面电气化的商业果园\r\n\r\n这里 commercial orchard 指：\r\n\r\n以出售水果、盈利为目的经营的果园\r\n\r\n不是自家后院种几棵果树那种。\r\n\r\n3. 广告\r\n\r\ncommercial 还可以作名词：\r\n\r\na commercial = 商业广告，尤其是电视/广播广告\r\n\r\n* I saw the commercial on TV.\r\n    我在电视上看到了那个广告。\r\n* There are too many commercials during the show.\r\n    这个节目中间的广告太多了。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n4. 商业化的；迎合市场的\r\n\r\n有时候带一点“为了赚钱、迎合大众市场”的意味。\r\n\r\n* The film was a huge commercial success.\r\n    这部电影在商业上非常成功。\r\n* His music has become more commercial.\r\n    他的音乐变得更商业化、更迎合市场了。','🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* commercial use 商业用途\r\n* commercial purposes 商业目的\r\n* commercial property 商业地产\r\n* commercial vehicle 商用车辆\r\n* commercial success 商业成功\r\n* commercial orchard 商业果园\r\n* TV commercial 电视广告\r\n\r\n⚠️ commercial vs business\r\n\r\ncommercial 通常是形容词，强调“商业用途、盈利性质”。\r\n\r\n* commercial building\r\n    商业建筑\r\n\r\nbusiness 更强调“公司、业务、生意”。\r\n\r\n* run a business\r\n    经营一家公司\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆：\r\n\r\ncommerce = 商业、贸易\r\n→ commercial = 商业的\r\n\r\n所以看到 commercial + 名词，很多时候可以直接理解成：\r\n\r\n“商用的 / 用来经营赚钱的……”','/static/uploads/english_note_item/5bb2be159a3d4e0cb721108c22c3443b.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-23 22:21:58',1,'2026-08-23 22:21:58'),(1481,20,77,'vocab','orchard','orchard','orchard','🎯 核心意思\r\norchard = 果园\r\n\r\n通常指专门种植果树、坚果树的大片土地。','🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* apple orchard 苹果园\r\n* cherry orchard 樱桃园\r\n* commercial orchard 商业果园\r\n* fruit orchard 果园\r\n* orchard owner 果园主\r\n* orchard workers 果园工人\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\n* They own a large apple orchard.\r\n    他们拥有一个很大的苹果园。\r\n* The orchard produces thousands of boxes of fruit every year.\r\n    这个果园每年生产成千上万箱水果。\r\n* The workers are harvesting apples in the orchard.\r\n    工人们正在果园里采摘苹果。\r\n* The orchard uses electric machinery instead of diesel equipment.\r\n    这个果园使用电动机械，而不是柴油设备。','the world’s first fully electrified commercial orchard\r\n\r\n= 世界上第一个全面电气化的商业果园\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\ncommercial = 商业经营的\r\norchard = 果园\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncommercial orchard = 商业果园\r\n\r\n⚠️ orchard vs farm\r\n\r\norchard\r\n→ 专门种果树的地方\r\n\r\nfarm\r\n→ 更广，可以种庄稼、养动物、种水果等\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nan apple orchard\r\n苹果园\r\n\r\na dairy farm\r\n奶牛场\r\n\r\n🧠 发音重点\r\n\r\norchard 不要读成：\r\n\r\n❌ our chat\r\n\r\n更接近：\r\n\r\n✅ OR-chəd\r\n\r\n你可以先练：\r\n\r\nor — orchard — commercial orchard','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d807a317e45c4aab83bea6df5f3829bc.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-23 22:26:32',1,'2026-08-23 22:26:32'),(1482,20,78,'vocab','photovoltaic','photovoltaic','photovoltaic','可以拆开读：\r\nphoto + voltaic\r\n\r\n🎯 核心意思\r\nphotovoltaic = 光伏的；利用太阳光发电的\r\n\r\n它主要用在太阳能发电领域，表示：\r\n\r\n把太阳光直接转换成电能','🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* photovoltaic panel 光伏板\r\n* photovoltaic system 光伏系统\r\n* photovoltaic power generation 光伏发电\r\n* photovoltaic cells 光伏电池\r\n* solar photovoltaic system 太阳能光伏系统','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* The house uses photovoltaic panels to generate electricity.\r\n    这栋房子使用光伏板发电。\r\n* Photovoltaic systems can reduce electricity costs.\r\n    光伏系统可以降低电费。\r\n* The farm installed a large photovoltaic system.\r\n    这个农场安装了一套大型光伏系统。\r\n\r\n⚠️ photovoltaic vs solar\r\n\r\nsolar = 太阳能的，范围更广\r\n比如：\r\n\r\n* solar energy 太阳能\r\n* solar heating 太阳能供暖\r\n\r\nphotovoltaic = 专门指“把光转成电”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nsolar panel 日常最常说\r\nphotovoltaic panel 更技术、更正式\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆\r\n\r\nphoto = 光\r\nvoltaic = 电\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nphotovoltaic = 光 → 电\r\n\r\n也就是我们常说的：\r\n\r\n光伏发电','/static/uploads/english_note_item/12a3b13165974adf84d88e5121011ac5.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-23 22:32:47',1,'2026-08-23 22:32:47'),(1483,20,79,'vocab','consent','consent','consent','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nconsent = 同意；许可；准许\r\n比普通的 agree 更正式，常见于：\r\n法律、医疗、合同、隐私、权限 等场景。','1. 名词：同意；许可\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\n* give consent 给予同意\r\n* obtain consent 获得同意\r\n* with someone’s consent 经某人同意\r\n* without consent 未经同意\r\n* written consent 书面同意\r\n* parental consent 家长同意\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\n* You need the owner’s consent before making any changes.\r\n    做任何修改之前，你需要得到所有者的同意。\r\n* The hospital obtained her written consent.\r\n    医院取得了她的书面同意。\r\n* They used the data without my consent.\r\n    他们未经我的同意使用了这些数据。\r\n* Parental consent is required for children under 16.\r\n    16岁以下儿童需要家长同意。\r\n\r\n2. 动词：同意；准许\r\n\r\n结构：\r\n\r\nconsent to + 名词 / 动名词\r\n\r\n* He consented to the proposal.\r\n    他同意了这个提议。\r\n* She consented to sharing the information.\r\n    她同意共享这些信息。\r\n* The patient consented to the treatment.\r\n    患者同意接受治疗。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意：\r\n\r\n✅ consent to something\r\n❌ consent something\r\n\r\n3. consent vs agree\r\n\r\nagree\r\n更日常、更广泛，普通“同意”。\r\n\r\n* I agree with you.\r\n    我同意你的观点。\r\n\r\nconsent\r\n更正式，强调“给予许可”。\r\n\r\n* I consent to the use of my personal data.\r\n    我同意使用我的个人数据。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nagree = 我觉得可以 / 我赞同\r\nconsent = 我正式授权你这么做','🧩 很常见的实际表达\r\n\r\n* user consent 用户同意\r\n* informed consent 知情同意\r\n* explicit consent 明确同意\r\n* consent form 同意书\r\n* consent to data processing 同意数据处理\r\n* without prior consent 未经事先同意\r\n\r\n💻 软件/隐私场景\r\n\r\n* Users must give consent before their data is collected.\r\n    在收集用户数据之前，必须先获得用户同意。\r\n* The app asks for consent to access your location.\r\n    这个应用会请求你同意访问位置信息。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆：\r\n\r\n看到 consent，可以先想到：\r\n\r\nformal permission = 正式许可 / 正式同意','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2d3f03d7bc44414483e72e9d40f1d052.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-23 22:53:26',1,'2026-08-23 22:53:26'),(1484,20,80,'phrase','offshore','offshore','offshore','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\noffshore = 离岸的；近海的；海外的\r\n\r\n它来自：\r\n\r\n* off = 离开\r\n* shore = 海岸\r\n\r\n所以最直观的理解就是：离开海岸、在海上的。','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. offshore wind farm\r\n海上风电场\r\n\r\n* New Zealand has significant offshore wind potential.\r\n    新西兰有很大的海上风电潜力。\r\n\r\n2. offshore oil / offshore drilling\r\n海上石油 / 海上钻探\r\n\r\n* The company is involved in offshore oil drilling.\r\n    这家公司从事海上石油钻探。\r\n\r\n3. offshore platform\r\n海上钻井平台 / 海上作业平台\r\n\r\n* Workers stay on the offshore platform for several weeks.\r\n    工人会在海上平台上待几个星期。\r\n\r\n4. offshore company / offshore account\r\n离岸公司 / 离岸账户\r\n\r\n这里的 offshore 不是真的强调“在海上”，而是指设立在外国司法管辖区的。\r\n\r\n* The company holds money in an offshore account.\r\n    这家公司把资金放在离岸账户中。\r\n\r\n5. offshore development / offshore team 💻\r\n海外开发 / 海外团队\r\n\r\nIT 工作里也很常见：\r\n\r\n* We have an offshore development team in India.\r\n    我们在印度有一个海外开发团队。','offshore wind farm = 海上风电场\r\nonshore wind farm = 陆上风电场\r\n\r\n💡 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象你站在海岸 shore 上，一艘船逐渐驶 off 海岸：\r\n\r\noff + shore → offshore → 离岸的 / 海上的\r\n\r\n📌 特别常见搭配：\r\n\r\noffshore wind / offshore drilling / offshore platform / offshore company / offshore account / offshore team','/static/uploads/english_note_item/1488c4971b6b45ff865274ce56247e06.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-24 10:22:05',1,'2026-08-24 10:22:05'),(1485,20,81,'phrase','wipe away your tears','wipe away your tears','wipe away your tears','wipe away your tears = 擦去你的眼泪 / 把眼泪擦干\r\n\r\n这里的 wipe away 是一个常见短语：\r\n\r\nwipe away + 东西\r\n= 把……擦掉 / 擦去\r\n\r\n🧩 拆开理解\r\n\r\n* wipe = 擦\r\n* away = 掉、去除\r\n* tears = 眼泪','所以：\r\n\r\nwipe away your tears\r\n= 把你的眼泪擦掉\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\n* She wiped away her tears and smiled.\r\n    她擦去眼泪，笑了起来。\r\n* He gently wiped away her tears.\r\n    他轻轻地帮她擦去眼泪。\r\n* Wipe away your tears. Everything will be okay.\r\n    擦干眼泪吧，一切都会好起来的。\r\n\r\n🧩 wipe away 的其他用法\r\n\r\n* wipe away the dust\r\n    擦掉灰尘\r\n* wipe away the sweat\r\n    擦去汗水\r\n* wipe away the blood\r\n    擦掉血迹\r\n\r\n⚠️ wipe vs wipe away\r\n\r\nwipe 更强调“擦这个动作”：\r\n\r\n* Wipe the table.\r\n    擦一下桌子。\r\n\r\nwipe away 更强调“把某物擦掉、去除”：\r\n\r\n* Wipe away the dust.\r\n    把灰尘擦掉。\r\n\r\n💡 很自然的一句话：\r\n\r\nShe wiped away her tears with the back of her hand.\r\n她用手背擦去了眼泪。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/7c7b76bd12f24c64bb560499dc7a6823.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-24 11:18:10',1,'2026-08-24 11:18:10'),(1486,20,82,'phrase','take + something + in a certain way','take + something + in a certain way','take + something + in a certain way','🔊 核心理解\r\n这里的 take 不是“拿”，而是：\r\n\r\n看待 / 理解 / 对待某事\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\ntake + something + in a certain way\r\n= 以某种方式理解、看待或接受某事','🎯 常见结构\r\n\r\ntake + sth + seriously\r\n认真对待某事\r\n\r\n* You should take this problem seriously.\r\n    你应该认真对待这个问题。\r\n\r\ntake + sth + lightly\r\n不太当回事\r\n\r\n* Don’t take his warning lightly.\r\n    不要不把他的警告当回事。\r\n\r\ntake + sth + personally\r\n把某事当成针对自己\r\n\r\n* Don’t take it personally.\r\n    别往心里去。\r\n\r\ntake + sth + badly / well\r\n对某事反应不好 / 接受得很好\r\n\r\n* He took the criticism badly.\r\n    他很难接受这个批评。\r\n* She took the news well.\r\n    她很好地接受了这个消息。','🧩 with 结构\r\n\r\ntake + sth + with + 某种态度\r\n\r\n* take it with caution\r\n    谨慎看待\r\n* take it with a pinch of salt\r\n    对它持保留态度，不要全信\r\n* I’d take what he said with a pinch of salt.\r\n    我不会完全相信他说的话。\r\n\r\n💬 常用口语\r\n\r\n* How did you take what he said?\r\n    你是怎么理解他说的话的？\r\n* I took it as a joke.\r\n    我把它当成了玩笑。\r\n* Don’t take it the wrong way.\r\n    别误会我的意思。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 容易混淆\r\n\r\ntake sth in\r\n= 理解、吸收信息\r\n\r\n* There was too much information to take in.\r\n    信息太多，一下子消化不了。\r\n\r\n而：\r\n\r\ntake sth in a certain way\r\n= 以某种方式理解某事\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nI took his comment in the wrong way.\r\n我误解了他的评论。\r\n\r\n💡 一句话记忆\r\n\r\ntake 不一定是“拿”，还可以表示“你是怎么理解/接受这件事的”。\r\n\r\n最值得记的几个搭配：\r\n\r\ntake it seriously / take it personally / take it badly / take it well / take it with a pinch of salt / take it the wrong way','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b14e2b34aaf04d2fa5e96b4865020cdb.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-24 12:42:27',1,'2026-08-24 12:42:27'),(1487,20,83,'vocab','proportionate','proportionate','proportionate','proportionate','🎯 核心意思\r\nproportionate = 成比例的；相称的；与……相匹配的\r\n\r\n最常见结构：\r\n\r\nbe proportionate to + 名词\r\n= 与……成比例 / 与……相称\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\n* The punishment should be proportionate to the offence.\r\n    惩罚应该与违法行为的严重程度相称。\r\n* Your salary should be proportionate to your responsibilities.\r\n    你的工资应该与你承担的责任相匹配。\r\n* The response was not proportionate to the problem.\r\n    这种反应和问题本身的严重程度不相称。','🗣️ 适合口语吗？\r\n\r\n可以，但偏正式。在日常口语里，很多时候会用更简单的表达：\r\n\r\n* in proportion to\r\n* match\r\n* be appropriate for\r\n* be in line with\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe punishment should match the seriousness of the offence.\r\n比 be proportionate to 更口语一些。\r\n\r\n⚠️ proportionate vs proportional\r\n\r\n两者都可以表示“成比例的”，但：\r\n\r\n* proportionate：更常用于“合适、相称”\r\n* proportional：更常用于数学、数量关系\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe punishment was proportionate to the crime.\r\n惩罚与罪行相称。\r\n\r\nThe cost is proportional to the size.\r\n成本与尺寸成比例。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9c78c27ff0ce4120a2870dafdb03ed83.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-24 13:48:00',1,'2026-08-24 13:48:00'),(1488,20,84,'vocab','escalate','escalate','escalate','🎯 核心意思\r\nescalate = 升级；加剧；恶化；逐步扩大\r\n\r\n它本身有一种“情况变得更严重/更高一级”的感觉。','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. escalate into + 更严重的情况\r\n= 升级成……\r\n\r\n* The argument escalated into a fight.\r\n    争吵升级成了打架。\r\n\r\n2. escalate rapidly / quickly\r\n= 迅速升级、迅速恶化\r\n\r\n* The situation escalated quickly.\r\n    情况很快恶化了。\r\n\r\n3. escalate a problem / conflict\r\n= 使问题 / 冲突升级\r\n\r\n* His comments only escalated the conflict.\r\n    他的话只让冲突更加严重。\r\n\r\n4. escalate an issue 💼\r\n在工作场景里非常常见：\r\n\r\n= 把问题上报给更高级别的人处理\r\n\r\n* We need to escalate this issue to the manager.\r\n    我们需要把这个问题升级上报给经理。\r\n* If the problem continues, I’ll escalate it.\r\n    如果问题继续存在，我会把它升级处理。','🗣️ 适合口语吗？\r\n\r\n适合，而且工作口语中很常见，尤其是：\r\n\r\n* IT support\r\n* customer service\r\n* project management\r\n* incident handling\r\n\r\n比如程序员经常说：\r\n\r\nI’ve escalated the issue to the infrastructure team.\r\n我已经把这个问题升级给基础设施团队处理了。\r\n\r\n⚠️ escalate vs increase\r\n\r\nincrease = 单纯增加\r\n\r\nescalate = 不只是增加，通常带有“越来越严重 / 上升到更高等级”的感觉\r\n\r\n* The cost increased.\r\n    成本增加了。\r\n* The conflict escalated.\r\n    冲突升级了。\r\n\r\n💡 一句话记：\r\n\r\nescalate = go to a higher or more serious level\r\n= 上升到更高、更严重的级别。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/16de89b8352b42f1bdce83e06ae2e5f9.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-24 13:59:28',1,'2026-08-24 13:59:28'),(1489,20,85,'phrase','be calculated to do something','be calculated to do something','be calculated to do something','意在……；旨在……；经过设计会导致……','All criminal acts directed against a State and intended or calculated to create a state of terror…\r\n\r\n可以理解为：\r\n\r\n所有针对国家、意图制造恐怖状态，或其行为本身足以/旨在在人们心中造成恐怖状态的犯罪行为……\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\n* intended to create = 有意图去制造\r\n* calculated to create = 被设计成会制造 / 其效果就是会造成\r\n\r\n所以 intended or calculated to create 可以翻成：\r\n\r\n意图或旨在造成……\r\n\r\n或者更自然：\r\n\r\n意图造成，或者其行为本身足以造成……','⚠️ 这个 calculate 是比较老式、正式的用法，不是日常口语里的“计算”。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n* His remarks were calculated to provoke anger.\r\n    他那些话是故意为了激怒别人。\r\n* The campaign was calculated to influence public opinion.\r\n    这场宣传活动旨在影响公众舆论。\r\n\r\n📌 你可以直接记：\r\n\r\nbe calculated to do = be designed/intended to do\r\n= 旨在…… / 故意为了……','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f8349577beaa4c1a8c171df938416d33.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-24 14:09:39',1,'2026-08-24 14:09:39'),(1490,20,86,'vocab','fatal & fatality','fatal & fatality','fatal & fatality','🔊 发音\r\n\r\n* fatal /ˈfeɪ.təl/ — adjective 形容词\r\n* fatality /fəˈtæl.ə.ti/ — noun 名词\r\n🎯 核心区别\r\n\r\nfatal = 致命的；严重到无法继续的\r\nfatality = 死亡；死亡人数；死亡事故','🧩 1. fatal\r\n\r\n常见搭配：\r\n\r\n* fatal accident\r\n    致命事故\r\n* fatal injury\r\n    致命伤\r\n* fatal disease\r\n    致命疾病\r\n* fatal error 💻\r\n    致命错误\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\nThe application crashed because of a fatal error.\r\n应用程序因为一个致命错误崩溃了。\r\n\r\nHe suffered a fatal injury.\r\n他受了致命伤。','🧩 2. fatality\r\n\r\n常见搭配：\r\n\r\n* one fatality\r\n    一人死亡\r\n* several fatalities\r\n    数人死亡\r\n* no fatalities\r\n    无人员死亡\r\n* fatality rate\r\n    死亡率\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\nThe crash resulted in one fatality.\r\n这起车祸造成一人死亡。\r\n\r\nThere were no fatalities.\r\n没有人员死亡。\r\n\r\n💡 词形关系\r\n\r\nfatal → fatality\r\n\r\n可以理解为：\r\n\r\nfatal = 会导致死亡的\r\n↓\r\nfatality = 导致出来的结果：死亡\r\n\r\n📌 最值得记住：\r\n\r\nfatal error = 致命错误\r\nfatal accident = 致命事故\r\nfatality = 死亡 / 死亡人数\r\nfatality rate = 死亡率','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3f48d099d4f54ce29416d5f52891bdba.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-24 14:41:27',1,'2026-08-24 14:41:27'),(1491,20,87,'vocab','tow','tow','tow','🎯 核心意思\r\ntow = 拖；牵引；拖走\r\n\r\n通常指用车、船等把另一个东西拖着移动。','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n1. tow a car\r\n= 拖车\r\n\r\n* My car was towed away.\r\n    我的车被拖走了。\r\n\r\n2. tow a boat\r\n= 拖船 / 拖着一艘船\r\n\r\n* The boat was towed back to shore.\r\n    那艘船被拖回了岸边。\r\n\r\n3. tow truck\r\n= 拖车 / 道路救援车\r\n\r\n* We had to call a tow truck.\r\n    我们不得不叫一辆拖车。\r\n\r\n4. in tow\r\n= 被拖着；跟在后面\r\n\r\n* He arrived with three children in tow.\r\n    他来了，后面还跟着三个孩子。\r\n\r\n这个 in tow 很有意思，可以不是真的“被拖”，而是比喻“跟着”。\r\n\r\n⚠️ tow vs pull\r\n\r\npull = 拉，最普通\r\ntow = 用车辆、船只等“拖行”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n* Pull the door.\r\n    拉门。\r\n* Tow the broken car.\r\n    把坏掉的车拖走。\r\n\r\n💡 记忆：\r\n\r\ntow = 用车或船拖着走。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/88b37c765d34487f9b1f724679837207.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-24 14:44:52',1,'2026-08-24 14:44:52'),(1492,20,88,'phrase','pay for itself','pay for itself','pay for itself','🎯 核心意思\r\n回本；赚回成本；带来的收益足以抵消购买/投入成本。\r\n\r\n这里的 pay 不是“付款给自己”，而是表示：\r\n\r\nthe money it saves or earns covers its cost\r\n它节省或赚到的钱，最终抵消了它本身的成本。','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* It pays for itself.\r\n    它能自己回本。\r\n* It pays for itself quickly.\r\n    它很快就能回本。\r\n* It will pay for itself in three years.\r\n    它三年内就能回本。\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\n* The solar panels will pay for themselves in a few years.\r\n    这些太阳能板几年内就能回本。\r\n* This machine is expensive, but it pays for itself through lower operating costs.\r\n    这台机器虽然贵，但通过降低运营成本可以回本。\r\n* The upgrade paid for itself within a year.\r\n    这次升级一年内就收回了成本。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意单复数\r\n\r\n* It pays for itself.\r\n* They pay for themselves.','It’s resilience that pays for itself pretty quickly.\r\n\r\n这里 pays for itself pretty quickly 就是：\r\n👉 很快就能体现价值并收回相应投入。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/eafcf219e1484fbea5c8357bb26552be.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 11:17:42',1,'2026-08-25 11:17:42'),(1493,20,89,'phrase','get our skates on','get our skates on','get our skates on','🎯 核心意思\r\n赶紧行动起来；加快速度；别再拖了\r\n\r\n这是一个比较口语化的表达，尤其常见于英式英语。\r\n\r\n你之前那句：\r\n\r\nWe have a long way to go and we need to get our skates on.\r\n👉 我们还有很长的路要走，得赶紧行动起来了。','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* We need to get our skates on.\r\n    我们得加快速度了。\r\n* You’d better get your skates on.\r\n    你最好赶紧了。\r\n* If we want to finish today, we’ll have to get our skates on.\r\n    如果想今天完成，我们就得抓紧了。','💡 为什么是 skates？\r\n\r\n可以想象成：\r\n穿上溜冰鞋 → 速度立刻变快\r\n\r\n所以它引申成：\r\n\r\nget moving / hurry up / speed things up\r\n\r\n⚖️ 和 hurry up 的区别\r\n\r\n* hurry up → 最直接：快点\r\n* get your skates on → 更有画面感、更口语、更英式\r\n* get moving → 赶紧动起来\r\n\r\n⚠️ 常见结构：\r\nget + 人称代词 + skates on\r\n\r\n* get my skates on\r\n* get your skates on\r\n* get our skates on\r\n* get their skates on','/static/uploads/english_note_item/81cd4bd50301437499fd5c56e5d2181e.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 11:20:21',1,'2026-08-25 11:20:21'),(1494,20,90,'phrase','extend beyond','extend beyond','extend beyond','🎯 核心意思\r\n超出……；延伸到……之外；影响不只局限于……\r\n\r\n这里的 extend = 延伸、扩大\r\nbeyond = 超过、在……之外\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nextend beyond + 范围/对象\r\n= 超出某个范围，不仅仅影响这一部分\r\n\r\n💬 你之前那句：\r\n\r\nThe benefits of wider solar adoption extend beyond individual farms.\r\n👉 更广泛采用太阳能所带来的好处，并不只局限于单个农场。\r\n👉 它的好处还会影响到更广的社区、行业甚至整个国家。','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n* The benefits extend beyond cost savings.\r\n    好处不仅仅是省钱。\r\n* His influence extends beyond the company.\r\n    他的影响力超出了公司范围。\r\n* The problem extends beyond one department.\r\n    这个问题不只涉及一个部门。\r\n* The impact extends beyond the local community.\r\n    这种影响已经超出了当地社区。\r\n\r\n⚖️ extend beyond vs go beyond\r\n\r\n两者都可以表示“超出”。\r\n\r\n* extend beyond → 更偏“范围、影响、作用延伸到……之外”\r\n* go beyond → 更口语、更广泛，“超过、不止于”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe benefits extend beyond money.\r\n强调“好处的范围还延伸到别的方面”。\r\n\r\nThe benefits go beyond money.\r\n更口语：好处不只是钱。','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f7b4fd1e97f34d448fa5803b06f0f7d1.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 11:23:23',1,'2026-08-25 11:23:23'),(1495,20,91,'vocab','adoption','adoption','adoption','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n① 采用；采纳；普及\r\n\r\n来自 adopt = 采用、采纳\r\n\r\n\r\n② 收养\r\n\r\n这是 adoption 另一个很常见的意思。\r\n\r\n* child adoption\r\n    儿童收养\r\n* They are considering adoption.\r\n    他们正在考虑收养孩子。','① 采用；采纳；普及\r\n\r\n来自 adopt = 采用、采纳\r\n\r\n在科技、政策、能源、商业语境里非常常见。\r\n\r\nsolar adoption\r\n= 太阳能的采用 / 普及\r\n\r\ntechnology adoption\r\n= 技术采用 / 技术普及\r\n\r\nAI adoption\r\n= AI 的应用与普及\r\n\r\n💬 你之前那句：\r\n\r\nThe benefits of wider solar adoption extend beyond individual farms.\r\n\r\n👉 更广泛采用太阳能所带来的好处，并不只局限于单个农场。\r\n\r\n这里的 adoption 就是：\r\nthe use or acceptance of something new\r\n对某项新技术、方法或制度的采用。','② 收养\r\n\r\n这是 adoption 另一个很常见的意思。\r\n\r\n* child adoption\r\n    儿童收养\r\n* They are considering adoption.\r\n    他们正在考虑收养孩子。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* widespread adoption → 广泛采用 / 普及\r\n* rapid adoption → 快速普及\r\n* mass adoption → 大规模普及\r\n* adoption rate → 采用率 / 普及率\r\n* drive adoption → 推动采用\r\n* encourage adoption → 鼓励采用\r\n\r\n💬 例句：\r\n\r\nElectric vehicles are seeing rapid adoption.\r\n电动汽车正在快速普及。\r\n\r\nThe company wants to encourage the adoption of AI tools.\r\n这家公司希望推动 AI 工具的使用。\r\n\r\n⚖️ adopt vs adoption\r\n\r\n* adopt → 动词：采用 / 收养\r\n* adoption → 名词：采用 / 收养\r\n\r\nMany farms have adopted solar power.\r\n很多农场已经采用了太阳能。\r\n\r\nSolar adoption is increasing.\r\n太阳能的普及率正在上升。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e64e6f6b322148aa9f131f41b4dd5a35.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 11:29:02',1,'2026-08-25 11:29:02'),(1496,20,92,'phrase','massive difference','massive difference','massive difference','🎯 核心意思\r\n巨大的差别；非常大的影响；产生巨大作用\r\n\r\n这里的 massive 不一定是字面“体积巨大”，在口语里常表示：\r\n\r\nvery large / very significant\r\n👉 非常大的、非常显著的','🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* make a massive difference\r\n    产生巨大影响 / 起很大作用\r\n* a massive difference in cost\r\n    成本上的巨大差异\r\n* a massive difference to someone/something\r\n    对某人/某事产生巨大影响\r\n\r\n💬 你之前那句：\r\n\r\nSmall and mid-scale solar installations can make a massive difference for farmers, rural communities, and New Zealand as a whole.\r\n\r\n👉 中小型太阳能设施可以给农民、农村社区以及整个新西兰带来非常大的改变。\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nmake a massive difference\r\n≈ have a huge impact','💬 更多例句：\r\n\r\n* A small change can make a massive difference.\r\n    一个小小的改变也可能产生巨大影响。\r\n* Better insulation makes a massive difference to heating costs.\r\n    更好的保温措施会大幅降低取暖成本。\r\n* There’s a massive difference between the two systems.\r\n    这两个系统之间差别非常大。\r\n\r\n⚖️ massive difference vs big difference\r\n\r\n* big difference → 很大的差别，最常用\r\n* huge difference → 巨大差别，口语常见\r\n* massive difference → 强调程度非常大，语气更强\r\n\r\n✅ 很自然的口语表达：\r\n\r\nIt makes a massive difference.\r\n👉 这真的差别很大 / 这真的很有用。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/7518b5740def4e9fb40623e906b38885.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 11:31:30',1,'2026-08-25 11:31:30'),(1497,20,93,'phrase','as a whole','as a whole','as a whole','🎯 核心意思\r\n整体来看；作为一个整体；总的来说\r\n\r\n它强调：不要只看某一部分，而是看整个群体、系统、国家、公司等。','🧩 常见结构\r\n\r\n* the country as a whole\r\n    整个国家\r\n* society as a whole\r\n    整个社会\r\n* the company as a whole\r\n    整个公司\r\n* the system as a whole\r\n    整个系统\r\n\r\n💬 你之前那句：\r\n\r\nSmall and mid-scale solar installations can make a massive difference for farmers, rural communities, and New Zealand as a whole.\r\n\r\n👉 中小型太阳能设施可以给农民、农村社区，以及整个新西兰带来巨大影响。\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nNew Zealand as a whole\r\n= New Zealand considered as one complete country\r\n= 从整个新西兰的角度来看','💬 更多例句：\r\n\r\n* The economy as a whole is improving.\r\n    整体经济正在改善。\r\n* The team performed well as a whole.\r\n    整个团队总体表现不错。\r\n* The project benefits the community as a whole.\r\n    这个项目让整个社区受益。\r\n\r\n⚖️ as a whole vs overall\r\n\r\n* as a whole → 强调“把所有部分看成一个整体”\r\n* overall → 强调“总体来说”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe company as a whole is doing well.\r\n👉 整个公司都表现不错。\r\n\r\nOverall, the company is doing well.\r\n👉 总体来说，公司表现不错。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c2a6fa8414b846da86a45b158457c2c2.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 11:43:58',1,'2026-08-25 11:43:58'),(1498,20,94,'vocab','electrician','electrician','electrician','🎯 核心意思\r\n电工；电气技师\r\n\r\n指安装、维修、检查电线、电路、电气设备的人。','🧩 词形关系\r\n\r\n* electric → 电的\r\n* electrical → 电气的\r\n* electrician → 电工 / 电气技师\r\n\r\n💬 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* qualified electrician → 合格电工\r\n* licensed electrician → 持证电工\r\n* call an electrician → 叫电工来\r\n* hire an electrician → 雇一名电工\r\n* electrician jobs → 电工岗位','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* We need to call an electrician.\r\n    我们得叫个电工来。\r\n* The electrician fixed the wiring problem.\r\n    电工修好了线路问题。\r\n* Solar installations are increasing demand for electricians.\r\n    太阳能安装正在增加对电工的需求。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 容易混淆\r\n\r\n* electrician → 人，电工\r\n* electrical engineer → 电气工程师\r\n* technician → 技术员，范围更广\r\n\r\n✅ 口语里很常用：\r\n\r\nI’ll get an electrician to check it.\r\n👉 我会找个电工来检查一下。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8aef773395964621b7728e988ab077ba.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 11:55:49',1,'2026-08-25 11:55:49'),(1499,20,95,'vocab','reliance','reliance','reliance','🎯 核心意思\r\n依赖；依靠','它是 rely 的名词形式。\r\n\r\n* rely on → 依赖……\r\n* reliance on → 对……的依赖\r\n\r\n🧩 常见搭配\r\n\r\n* reliance on fossil fuels → 对化石燃料的依赖\r\n* reliance on imported energy → 对进口能源的依赖\r\n* reduce reliance on → 减少对……的依赖\r\n* heavy reliance on → 高度依赖\r\n* increasing reliance on → 越来越依赖','💬 例句\r\n\r\n* We need to reduce our reliance on fossil fuels.\r\n    我们需要减少对化石燃料的依赖。\r\n* The country has a heavy reliance on imported energy.\r\n    这个国家高度依赖进口能源。\r\n* Solar power can reduce reliance on the national grid.\r\n    太阳能可以减少对国家电网的依赖。\r\n\r\n⚖️ reliance vs dependence\r\n两者都可以表示“依赖”。\r\n\r\n* reliance → 更强调“依靠、倚重”\r\n* dependence → 更强调“依赖状态”，有时带“离不开”的感觉\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nreliance on technology\r\n对技术的依赖\r\n\r\ndependence on drugs\r\n对药物的依赖\r\n\r\n💡 一句话记住：\r\n\r\nrely on = 动词\r\nreliance on = 名词','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c0d1ade58d2b4386afec4d9f630e3e70.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 12:14:55',1,'2026-08-25 12:14:55'),(1500,20,96,'phrase','flick over','flick over','flick over','快速地翻过去、切换过去，或迅速转入另一种状态。\r\n\r\nflick 表示“轻快、迅速地拨一下”；over 表示“转到另一边”。','🧩 常见用法 ①：切换频道、页面或画面\r\n\r\n常用结构：flick over to + 频道／页面／节目\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法 ②：快速翻到某一页\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法 ③：系统迅速切换到另一种供电或运行模式\r\n\r\n常用结构：flick over to + 新模式','💬 Can you flick over to the news?\r\n\r\n你能切到新闻频道吗？\r\n\r\n💬 I flicked over to another channel during the adverts.\r\n\r\n广告期间，我切到了另一个频道。\r\n\r\n💬 Flick over to the next screen.\r\n\r\n切换到下一个画面。\r\n\r\n💬 She flicked over to the last page of the report.\r\n\r\n她快速翻到了报告的最后一页。\r\n\r\n💬 Flick over to page 20.\r\n\r\n快速翻到第20页。\r\n\r\n💬 When the power goes out, the system flicks over to battery power.\r\n\r\n停电时，系统会迅速切换到电池供电。\r\n\r\n💬 The generator automatically flicked over when the main power failed.\r\n\r\n主电源发生故障时，系统自动切换到了发电机供电。\r\n\r\n💬 The system flicked over to battery power.\r\n\r\n系统一下子切换到了电池供电。\r\n\r\n💬 The system switched over to battery power.\r\n\r\n系统切换到了电池供电。\r\n\r\n💬 The power failed, but the system immediately flicked over.\r\n\r\n主电源中断了，但系统立即切换到了备用供电。\r\n\r\n📌 近义表达：switch over to\r\n\r\n⚠️ 相关短语：\r\n\r\nflick through a book：快速翻阅一本书\r\n\r\nturn the page：翻页\r\n\r\nflip the page over：把这一页翻过去\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\nPeople with solar and batteries don’t even notice that the power’s gone out, because it flicks over and is charging back up during the day.\r\n\r\n装有太阳能和电池的人甚至不会注意到停电，因为系统会立即切换到电池供电，并在白天重新充电。\r\n\r\n这里的完整意思是：\r\n\r\nIt flicks over to battery power.\r\n\r\n它会立即切换到电池供电。\r\n\r\n由于切换到什么供电模式已经很清楚，所以 to battery power 被省略了。\r\n\r\n🆚 flick over / switch over / change over\r\n\r\n短语	意思	语感\r\nflick over	快速切换过去	口语、生动，强调速度快\r\nswitch over	切换到另一系统或模式	最通用、最自然\r\nchange over	从一套系统转换到另一套	强调转换过程\r\nflip over	翻面、翻页	强调把东西翻到另一面\r\n\r\n📌 switch over 更标准、常见；flick over 更生动，给人一种“啪一下就切过去了”的感觉。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n表示“切换到……”时，一般使用：\r\n\r\n✅ flick over to battery power\r\n❌ flick over battery power\r\n\r\n但如果上下文已经明确，可以省略后面的内容：\r\n\r\n🧠 形象记忆\r\n\r\n想象停电的一瞬间，电力开关“啪”地拨到电池一侧：\r\n\r\nflick＝迅速拨一下\r\nover＝转到另一边\r\n\r\n➡️ flick over＝快速翻过去／迅速切换过去','/static/uploads/english_note_item/6ba132de00e548d49f2706f1d9b4327b.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 13:46:20',1,'2026-08-25 13:46:20'),(1501,20,97,'vocab','optimistic','optimistic','optimistic','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n乐观的；对未来或某件事情抱有信心的。\r\n\r\n表示相信事情会顺利发展，或者最终会出现好的结果。','🧩 常见用法 ①：be optimistic about + 名词／动名词\r\n\r\n表示“对……感到乐观”。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法 ②：be optimistic that + 完整句子\r\n\r\n表示“乐观地认为……”。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法 ③：remain / feel / sound optimistic\r\n\r\n表示“保持乐观／感到乐观／听起来很乐观”。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法 ④：过于乐观的估计或计划\r\n\r\noptimistic 有时含有“估计得太乐观、不太现实”的意思。','💬 I’m optimistic about the future.\r\n\r\n我对未来持乐观态度。\r\n\r\n💬 Farmers are optimistic about adopting solar energy.\r\n\r\n农民对采用太阳能持乐观态度。\r\n\r\n💬 She’s optimistic about finding a new job.\r\n\r\n她对找到新工作很有信心。\r\n\r\n💬 We’re optimistic that the project will be completed on time.\r\n\r\n我们乐观地认为这个项目会按时完成。\r\n\r\n💬 The panel was optimistic that momentum was building.\r\n\r\n专家小组乐观地认为，发展势头正在增强。\r\n\r\n💬 Despite the difficulties, she remained optimistic.\r\n\r\n尽管面临困难，她仍然保持乐观。\r\n\r\n💬 I feel optimistic about our chances of success.\r\n\r\n我对我们成功的机会感到乐观。\r\n\r\n💬 You sound very optimistic.\r\n\r\n你听起来非常乐观。\r\n\r\n💬 Finishing the entire project in two days seems optimistic.\r\n\r\n两天内完成整个项目似乎过于乐观。\r\n\r\n💬 That delivery date is a little optimistic.\r\n\r\n那个交付日期定得有点过于乐观。\r\n\r\n💬 Your estimate may be overly optimistic.\r\n\r\n你的估计可能过于乐观了。\r\n\r\n💬 I’m optimistic about the project.\r\n\r\n我相信这个项目最终会取得好结果。\r\n\r\n💬 I’m positive about the project.\r\n\r\n我对这个项目持积极态度。\r\n\r\n💬 I’m confident that the project will succeed.\r\n\r\n我确信这个项目会成功。\r\n\r\n💬 She is optimistic about the future.\r\n\r\n她对未来很乐观。\r\n\r\n💬 He is pessimistic about the economy.\r\n\r\n他对经济前景很悲观。\r\n\r\n📌 that 后面接完整句子：\r\n\r\n✅ optimistic that the situation will improve\r\n❌ optimistic the situation\r\n\r\n📌 这里不一定是在表扬，而是在委婉地表示：\r\n\r\n这个计划可能不太现实。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\nWhile New Zealand may be trailing other countries in solar adoption, the panel was optimistic that momentum was building.\r\n\r\n虽然新西兰在太阳能应用方面可能落后于其他国家，但专家小组仍乐观地认为，发展势头正在增强。\r\n\r\n句子结构：\r\n\r\nbe trailing other countries：落后于其他国家\r\n\r\nbe optimistic that...：乐观地认为……\r\n\r\nmomentum is building：发展势头正在增强\r\n\r\n🆚 optimistic / positive / confident\r\n\r\n单词	核心意思	常见搭配\r\noptimistic	相信未来会有好结果	optimistic about / optimistic that\r\npositive	积极的；持正面态度的	positive attitude / stay positive\r\nconfident	对自己的能力或结果有信心	confident about / confident that\r\n\r\n📌 optimistic 更强调“对未来结果的乐观期待”；confident 表达的把握通常更强。\r\n\r\n🆚 optimistic / pessimistic\r\n\r\n单词	意思\r\noptimistic	乐观的\r\npessimistic	悲观的\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n表示“对某事乐观”，使用 about：\r\n\r\n✅ I’m optimistic about the result.\r\n❌ I’m optimistic for the result.\r\n\r\noptimistic 是形容词，optimist 是“乐观主义者”：\r\n\r\n✅ She is optimistic.\r\n\r\n✅ She is an optimist.\r\n❌ She is an optimistic.\r\n\r\n注意重音在 mis：\r\n\r\nop-ti-MIS-tic\r\n/ˌɒp.tɪˈmɪs.tɪk/\r\n\r\n🧠 词族记忆\r\n\r\noptimism /ˈɒptɪmɪzəm/：乐观；乐观主义\r\n\r\noptimist /ˈɒptɪmɪst/：乐观主义者\r\n\r\noptimistic /ˌɒptɪˈmɪstɪk/：乐观的\r\n\r\noptimistically /ˌɒptɪˈmɪstɪkli/：乐观地\r\n\r\npessimistic：悲观的\r\n\r\n🧠 形象记忆\r\n\r\n想象一个人看到乌云后面的阳光，相信天气很快就会转好：\r\n\r\noptimistic＝相信未来会出现好的结果。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ae9ec1f4260d465a8ee8cdc5f50f3f46.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 14:25:18',1,'2026-08-25 14:25:18'),(1502,20,98,'phrase','skepticism / skeptic / skeptical','skepticism / skeptic / skeptical','skepticism / skeptic / skeptical','🎯 核心感觉\r\n\r\n这组词表示：\r\n\r\n不轻易相信某个说法，需要看到证据之后才会相信。\r\n\r\n它不一定表示完全否定，而是：\r\n\r\n“I’m not convinced yet.”\r\n\r\n“我目前还没有被说服。”','🧩 skepticism：怀疑态度\r\n\r\nskepticism 是不可数名词，表示对某个说法、计划或观点的怀疑。\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\nskepticism about + 名词\r\n\r\nskepticism over + 名词\r\n\r\nexpress skepticism：表示怀疑\r\n\r\nwidespread skepticism：普遍的怀疑\r\n\r\ngrowing skepticism：越来越强的怀疑\r\n\r\n🧩 skeptic：持怀疑态度的人\r\n\r\nskeptic 是可数名词，指不轻易相信某件事的人。\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\na skeptic：一个持怀疑态度的人\r\n\r\nsolar skeptics：对太阳能持怀疑态度的人\r\n\r\nclimate skeptics：气候变化怀疑者\r\n\r\nconvince the skeptics：说服怀疑者\r\n\r\n🧩 skeptical：怀疑的；不确信的\r\n\r\nskeptical 是形容词，用来形容一个人的态度。\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\nbe skeptical about + 名词／动名词\r\n\r\nbe skeptical of + 人／事物／说法\r\n\r\nbe skeptical that + 完整句子\r\n\r\nremain skeptical：仍然持怀疑态度\r\n\r\n🧩 skeptical about / skeptical of\r\n\r\n搭配	常见使用场景	例子\r\nskeptical about	对某个话题、计划或可能性持怀疑态度	skeptical about the plan\r\nskeptical of	不相信某个人、说法、产品或证据	skeptical of his claims','💬 There is still considerable skepticism about the benefits of solar energy.\r\n\r\n人们对太阳能的益处仍然存在相当大的怀疑。\r\n\r\n💬 The proposal was met with skepticism.\r\n\r\n这个提议遭到了质疑。\r\n\r\n💬 Some farmers expressed skepticism about the upfront costs.\r\n\r\n一些农民对前期成本表示怀疑。\r\n\r\n💬 Even the skeptics were impressed by the results.\r\n\r\n就连那些持怀疑态度的人也对结果印象深刻。\r\n\r\n💬 The project still has many skeptics.\r\n\r\n仍有许多人对这个项目持怀疑态度。\r\n\r\n💬 The evidence may help convince the skeptics.\r\n\r\n这些证据可能有助于说服怀疑者。\r\n\r\n💬 I’m skeptical about the proposed solution.\r\n\r\n我对这个提议的解决方案持怀疑态度。\r\n\r\n💬 Many people are skeptical of these claims.\r\n\r\n许多人对这些说法持怀疑态度。\r\n\r\n💬 I’m skeptical that the project can be completed in two days.\r\n\r\n我不太相信这个项目能在两天内完成。\r\n\r\n💬 She remained skeptical despite the positive results.\r\n\r\n尽管结果不错，她仍然持怀疑态度。\r\n\r\n💬 I’m skeptical about the new policy.\r\n\r\n我对这项新政策持怀疑态度。\r\n\r\n💬 I’m skeptical of companies that promise instant results.\r\n\r\n我不太相信那些承诺立即见效的公司。\r\n\r\n💬 There is skepticism about the new technology.\r\n\r\n人们对这项新技术持怀疑态度。\r\n\r\n💬 I have some doubts about the plan.\r\n\r\n我对这个计划有些疑问。\r\n\r\n💬 The police treated his behaviour with suspicion.\r\n\r\n警方对他的行为产生了怀疑。\r\n\r\n💬 He looked at the figures skeptically.\r\n\r\n他怀疑地看着这些数字。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 你写的 skepticial 拼写不正确，正确形式是：\r\n\r\n✅ skeptical\r\n❌ skepticial\r\n\r\n🇬🇧 英式拼写：scepticism / sceptic / sceptical\r\n🇺🇸 美式拼写：skepticism / skeptic / skeptical\r\n\r\n两套拼写都正确，但不要混着写。新西兰通常采用英式拼写 scepticism / sceptical，不过美式拼写也很常见。\r\n\r\n🔊 读音与词性\r\n\r\n单词	读音	词性	中文意思\r\nskepticism	/ˈskeptɪsɪzəm/	名词	怀疑态度；怀疑主义\r\nskeptic	/ˈskeptɪk/	名词	持怀疑态度的人\r\nskeptical	/ˈskeptɪkəl/	形容词	怀疑的；不确信的\r\n\r\n📌 be met with skepticism\r\n\r\n表示一个观点、提议或声明“受到质疑”。\r\n\r\n⚠️ skeptic 指“人”，不能直接表示“怀疑态度”。\r\n\r\n✅ He is a skeptic.\r\n他是一个持怀疑态度的人。\r\n\r\n❌ He has a skeptic.\r\n\r\n✅ He has some skepticism.\r\n\r\n他对此有些怀疑。\r\n\r\n📌 两者经常可以互换，但 skeptical of 的“不信任”语气有时更强。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\nWhile New Zealand may be trailing other countries in solar adoption, the panel was optimistic that momentum was building, despite some skepticism.\r\n\r\n虽然新西兰在太阳能应用方面可能落后于其他国家，但尽管仍存在一些质疑，专家小组仍乐观地认为发展势头正在增强。\r\n\r\n这里的：\r\n\r\nsome skepticism：一些怀疑或质疑\r\n\r\noptimistic：乐观的\r\n\r\nmomentum was building：发展势头正在增强\r\n\r\noptimism 和 skepticism 在句中形成对比：\r\n\r\n一方面有人持怀疑态度，另一方面专家小组对未来仍然乐观。\r\n\r\n🆚 skepticism / doubt / suspicion\r\n\r\n单词	核心意思	语感\r\nskepticism	因证据不足而不轻易相信	理性、审慎的怀疑\r\ndoubt	不确定、不相信	最普通、最通用\r\nsuspicion	怀疑有人做了坏事或事情有问题	带有警觉和不信任\r\n\r\n🆚 skeptic / cynical person\r\n\r\n表达	含义\r\nskeptic	因证据不足而不轻易相信的人\r\ncynical person	认为别人通常自私、不真诚的人\r\n\r\n📌 skeptic 不一定消极，只是希望看到更多证据。\r\n\r\nA skeptic asks:\r\n\r\n“Where is the evidence?”\r\n\r\n怀疑者会问：“证据在哪里？”\r\n\r\nA cynical person thinks:\r\n\r\n“People only do this for themselves.”\r\n\r\n愤世嫉俗的人认为：“人们做这件事只是为了自己。”\r\n\r\n⚠️ 常见错误\r\n\r\n不要使用错误拼写 skepticial：\r\n\r\n❌ I’m skepticial about it.\r\n\r\n✅ I’m skeptical about it.\r\n\r\nskeptic 是人，skeptical 是人的态度：\r\n\r\n✅ He is a skeptic.\r\n他是一个怀疑者。\r\n\r\n✅ He is skeptical.\r\n他持怀疑态度。\r\n\r\n❌ He is skepticism.\r\n\r\nskepticism 是不可数名词，通常不加 a：\r\n\r\n❌ I have a skepticism about it.\r\n\r\n✅ I have some skepticism about it.\r\n\r\n✅ I’m skeptical about it.\r\n\r\n新西兰写作中更适合采用英式拼写：\r\n\r\nscepticism\r\n\r\nsceptic\r\n\r\nsceptical\r\n\r\n🧠 词汇家族\r\n\r\nskepticism / scepticism：怀疑态度\r\n\r\nskeptic / sceptic：怀疑者\r\n\r\nskeptical / sceptical：怀疑的\r\n\r\nskeptically / sceptically：怀疑地\r\n\r\n🧠 一句话记住\r\n\r\nskepticism＝怀疑态度\r\nskeptic＝持怀疑态度的人\r\nskeptical＝感到怀疑的\r\n\r\n💡 记忆场景：\r\n\r\n有人宣传一种新产品能“立刻解决所有问题”，你没有马上相信，而是问：\r\n\r\n“Do you have any evidence?”\r\n\r\n“你有证据吗？”\r\n\r\n这种态度就是 skepticism；你是一个 skeptic；你对此感到 skeptical。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8ef402ee764449b8bac6296758afe6e8.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 14:43:35',1,'2026-08-25 14:43:35'),(1503,20,99,'phrase','feed into','feed into','feed into','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nfeed into = 促成；影响；为……提供信息/数据；输入到……中\r\n\r\n它的核心画面是：\r\n\r\nA → 不断输入/流入 → B → 对 B 产生影响','🧩 常见用法 1：影响 / 促成某个结果\r\n\r\nfeed into + decision / problem / trend / result\r\n\r\n表示某件事成为另一个结果的影响因素。\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nCustomer feedback feeds into our product decisions.\r\n客户反馈会影响 / 用于形成我们的产品决策。\r\n\r\nRising costs are feeding into higher prices.\r\n成本上涨正在推动价格上涨。\r\n\r\nSeveral factors feed into this problem.\r\n有几个因素共同导致 / 促成了这个问题。\r\n\r\n💻 常见用法 2：把数据 / 信息输入到系统中\r\n\r\n在 IT、数据分析、工作场景里非常常见：\r\n\r\ndata / information → feed into → system / model / report\r\n\r\nThe OCR results feed into the review system.\r\nOCR 识别结果会输入到审核系统中。\r\n\r\nThis data feeds into our reporting dashboard.\r\n这些数据会进入我们的报表仪表盘。\r\n\r\nThe extracted values are fed into the database.\r\n提取出来的值会被输入到数据库中。','💬 很实用的工作表达\r\n\r\nThis information will feed into our final decision.\r\n这些信息将作为我们最终决策的依据。\r\n\r\nThe OCR results feed into the next stage of the workflow.\r\nOCR 结果会进入工作流的下一阶段。\r\n\r\nAll these factors feed into the final result.\r\n所有这些因素都会影响最终结果。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 注意被动形式：\r\n\r\nbe fed into = 被输入到……\r\n\r\n⚠️ feed into vs lead to\r\n\r\nfeed into\r\n👉 强调“作为其中一个因素，持续影响/贡献”\r\n\r\nlead to\r\n👉 强调“最终导致某个结果”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nSeveral issues fed into the delay.\r\n几个问题共同造成了这次延误。\r\n\r\nThe system failure led to a delay.\r\n系统故障导致了延误。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象很多条小管道：\r\n\r\ncustomer feedback ↘\r\nsales data → decision\r\nmarket trends ↗\r\n\r\n这些信息都像水一样 feed into 一个最终结果。\r\n\r\n👉 所以 feed into ≈ 流入 → 影响 / 贡献于 / 输入到。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/1546677c4ee14b4d986ca587eade850b.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 15:31:33',1,'2026-08-25 15:31:33'),(1504,20,100,'vocab','disruptive','disruptive','disruptive','🎯 词性\r\nadjective 形容词','🧩 常见用法 1：扰乱秩序的\r\n\r\n常用来形容人、行为、事件。\r\n\r\ndisruptive behaviour\r\n扰乱秩序的行为\r\n\r\na disruptive student\r\n一个扰乱课堂秩序的学生\r\n\r\nHis disruptive behaviour affected the whole class.\r\n他扰乱秩序的行为影响了整个班级。\r\n\r\nConstruction work can be very disruptive.\r\n建筑施工可能会严重影响正常生活。\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法 2：造成业务 / 系统中断的\r\n\r\n工作、IT 场景很常见。\r\n\r\nThe software update was highly disruptive to our daily operations.\r\n这次软件更新严重影响了我们的日常运营。\r\n\r\nWe want to deploy the change in a less disruptive way.\r\n我们希望以一种对现有系统影响更小的方式部署这个变更。\r\n\r\nThe migration should not be disruptive to users.\r\n这次迁移不应该影响用户的正常使用。\r\n\r\n🚀 常见用法 3：颠覆性的\r\n\r\n在商业、科技领域，disruptive 不一定是负面的。\r\n\r\ndisruptive technology\r\n颠覆性技术\r\n\r\ndisruptive innovation\r\n颠覆式创新\r\n\r\nAI is a potentially disruptive technology.\r\nAI 是一种具有潜在颠覆性的技术。\r\n\r\nThe company introduced a disruptive business model.\r\n这家公司推出了一种颠覆传统的商业模式。\r\n\r\n这里强调：\r\n\r\n改变原来的行业规则 / 商业模式','💬 很实用的工作表达\r\n\r\nThis change could be disruptive to the existing workflow.\r\n这个改动可能会干扰现有工作流程。\r\n\r\nWe need to minimise disruptive changes.\r\n我们需要尽量减少会影响现有系统的改动。\r\n\r\nThe deployment was less disruptive than expected.\r\n这次部署对正常业务的影响比预期小。\r\n\r\n⚠️ disruptive vs destructive\r\n\r\n这两个词很容易看混：\r\n\r\ndisruptive\r\n👉 扰乱、打断、颠覆\r\n不一定造成真正的破坏\r\n\r\ndestructive\r\n👉 破坏性的、毁灭性的\r\n强调造成实际损害\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe protest was disruptive.\r\n抗议活动扰乱了正常秩序。\r\n\r\nThe earthquake was destructive.\r\n地震造成了严重破坏。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\ndisruptive\r\n\r\n可以联想：\r\n\r\nnormal flow → 💥 disruption → flow 被打断\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ndisruptive ≈ 打乱正常流程的\r\n\r\n📌 一句话记：\r\n\r\nSomething disruptive interrupts or changes the normal way things work.\r\ndisruptive 的东西会打断或改变原本正常的运行方式。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/34e5176516794615acd13998e9207485.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 15:53:34',1,'2026-08-25 15:53:34'),(1505,20,101,'vocab','outnumber','outnumber','outnumber','🎯 词性\r\nverb 动词','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\nWomen outnumber men in this class.\r\n这个班里女生比男生多。\r\n\r\nThe enemy soldiers outnumbered us three to one.\r\n敌军人数是我们的三倍。\r\n\r\nIn some regions, sheep outnumber people.\r\n在一些地区，羊的数量比人还多。\r\n\r\nApplications outnumbered available positions.\r\n申请人数超过了可提供的职位数量。','💬 很实用的表达\r\n\r\nA outnumbers B by 2 to 1.\r\nA 的数量是 B 的两倍。\r\n\r\nWe were heavily outnumbered.\r\n我们在人数上处于明显劣势。\r\n\r\nThe requests far outnumber our current capacity.\r\n这些请求的数量远远超过我们目前的处理能力。\r\n\r\n⚠️ outnumber vs exceed\r\n\r\noutnumber\r\n👉 专门强调数量 / 人数更多\r\n\r\nFemale students outnumber male students.\r\n女生人数比男生多。\r\n\r\nexceed\r\n👉 更广泛，可以是数量、金额、速度、限制等“超过”\r\n\r\nThe cost exceeded $10,000.\r\n成本超过了 1 万美元。\r\n\r\n所以不能说：\r\n\r\n❌ The cost outnumbered $10,000.\r\n\r\n应该说：\r\n\r\n✅ The cost exceeded $10,000.\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nout + number\r\n\r\n可以直接理解成：\r\n\r\n在 number（数量）上 out（超过）别人\r\n\r\n👉 outnumber = 数量上超过\r\n\r\n📌 一句话记：\r\n\r\nIf A outnumbers B, there are more A’s than B’s.\r\n如果 A outnumbers B，就表示 A 的数量比 B 多。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d49f03dd8a7149eda6ca11db07c71a27.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 18:32:45',1,'2026-08-25 18:32:45'),(1506,20,102,'phrase','generational shift','generational shift','generational shift','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ngenerational shift = 代际转变；世代变化；不同一代人之间出现的观念、行为或偏好变化\r\n\r\n它通常不是指“某一个人的改变”，而是：\r\n\r\n👉 一代人和另一代人相比，整体想法或行为发生了明显变化','🧩 拆开理解\r\n\r\ngenerational\r\n= 一代人的；代际的\r\n\r\nshift\r\n= 转变；变化\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ngenerational shift\r\n= 一代人与下一代之间的整体变化\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\na generational shift in attitudes\r\n观念上的代际转变\r\n\r\na generational shift in the workplace\r\n职场中的代际变化\r\n\r\na major generational shift\r\n重大的代际转变\r\n\r\nreflect a generational shift\r\n反映出代际变化','💬 例句\r\n\r\nThere has been a generational shift in attitudes toward work-life balance.\r\n人们对工作与生活平衡的看法出现了明显的代际转变。\r\n\r\nThe rise of remote work reflects a broader generational shift in workplace expectations.\r\n远程办公的兴起反映了职场期待上更广泛的代际变化。\r\n\r\nYounger consumers are driving a generational shift toward sustainable products.\r\n年轻消费者正在推动向可持续产品转变的代际趋势。\r\n\r\nThis is not just a temporary trend; it may represent a generational shift.\r\n这不仅仅是一个暂时的趋势，它可能代表一种世代性的转变。\r\n\r\n🗣️ 口语里自然吗？\r\n\r\n✅ 很自然，尤其适合：\r\n\r\n新闻\r\n\r\n商业讨论\r\n\r\n社会趋势\r\n\r\n职场\r\n\r\n人口变化\r\n\r\n消费习惯\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nI think we\'re seeing a generational shift in how people think about careers.\r\n我觉得我们正在看到人们对职业看法上的一种代际转变。\r\n\r\n⚠️ generational shift vs generation gap\r\n\r\ngenerational shift\r\n👉 强调不同世代之间发生了整体变化\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThere has been a generational shift toward flexible working.\r\n\r\n人们正在发生代际性的转变，越来越倾向灵活办公。\r\n\r\ngeneration gap\r\n👉 强调两代人之间的差异或隔阂\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThere is a generation gap between parents and their children.\r\n\r\n父母和孩子之间存在代沟。\r\n\r\n📌 可以记成：\r\n\r\ngenerational shift = 变化\r\ngeneration gap = 差距 / 代沟\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象两代人：\r\n\r\n👴 Older generation\r\n“Work in the office 9–5.”\r\n\r\n⬇️ SHIFT\r\n\r\n👩‍💻 Younger generation\r\n“Flexible hours + remote work.”\r\n\r\n这就是一个：\r\n\r\n👉 generational shift\r\n\r\n📌 一句话记忆：\r\n\r\nA generational shift is a broad change in attitudes or behaviour from one generation to another.\r\ngenerational shift 就是一代人与下一代人之间出现的整体观念或行为变化。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/0d1ddf113f244086af87607c8afc2c6c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 20:40:28',1,'2026-08-25 20:40:28'),(1507,20,103,'phrase','have ... in place','have ... in place','have ... in place','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nhave ... in place = 已经准备好 / 已经建立好 / 已经落实好……\r\n\r\n这里的 in place 不是“在某个地方”，而是：\r\n\r\n👉 已经就位、已经安排妥当，可以开始发挥作用','🧩 常见结构\r\n\r\nhave + 名词 + in place\r\n\r\n常见搭配：\r\n\r\nhave a system in place\r\n已经建立好一套系统\r\n\r\nhave a process in place\r\n已经有一套流程\r\n\r\nhave measures in place\r\n已经采取了相关措施\r\n\r\nhave safeguards in place\r\n已经有保护机制\r\n\r\nhave a plan in place\r\n已经制定好计划\r\n\r\nhave monitoring in place\r\n已经建立了监控机制\r\n\r\n💻 工作 / IT 场景非常常用\r\n\r\nWe already have a monitoring system in place.\r\n我们已经建立了一套监控系统。\r\n\r\nWe need to have a proper error-handling process in place before launch.\r\n上线之前，我们需要把完善的错误处理流程建立起来。\r\n\r\nWe have several safeguards in place to prevent data loss.\r\n我们已经有多项保护措施来防止数据丢失。\r\n\r\nDo we have a rollback plan in place?\r\n我们已经准备好回滚方案了吗？\r\n\r\nOnce we have the API in place, we can start integrating the frontend.\r\n一旦 API 搭建完成，我们就可以开始集成前端。','💬 很自然的口语表达\r\n\r\nDo we have anything in place for this?\r\n这件事我们现在有没有什么现成的安排 / 机制？\r\n\r\nWe already have that in place.\r\n这个我们已经弄好了 / 已经有了。\r\n\r\n这句在会议里特别常见。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nA: Do we need additional monitoring?\r\nB: We already have that in place.\r\n\r\nA：我们需要增加监控吗？\r\nB：这个我们已经有了。\r\n\r\n⚠️ have ... in place vs put ... in place\r\n\r\n这两个很重要：\r\n\r\nhave ... in place\r\n👉 强调现在已经有了\r\n\r\nWe have a backup process in place.\r\n我们已经有备份流程了。\r\n\r\nput ... in place\r\n👉 强调把它建立起来 / 落实\r\n\r\nWe need to put a backup process in place.\r\n我们需要建立一套备份流程。\r\n\r\n📌 可以记成：\r\n\r\nput in place = 建起来\r\nhave in place = 已经建好了\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象上线之前：\r\n\r\n✅ API ready\r\n\r\n✅ Monitoring ready\r\n\r\n✅ Rollback plan ready\r\n\r\n✅ Error handling ready\r\n\r\n所有东西都已经就位：\r\n\r\n👉 Everything is in place.\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nhave something in place\r\n≈ 某个机制 / 流程 / 计划已经就位，可以用了\r\n\r\n📌 一句话记：\r\n\r\nWe have the necessary controls in place.\r\n我们已经落实好了必要的控制措施。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/591f4004920b4615a0fcd2223ee87ea2.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 20:43:42',1,'2026-08-25 20:43:42'),(1508,20,104,'phrase','a cascading range of things','a cascading range of things','a cascading range of things','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\na cascading range of things = 一连串接连发生、层层传导的事情 / 一系列连锁反应\r\n\r\n这里的重点是 cascading。\r\n\r\ncascade 本来是“瀑布、层层落下”，所以 cascading 带有这种画面：\r\n\r\nA 发生 → 引发 B → B 又引发 C → C 再影响 D\r\n\r\n也就是中文里常说的：\r\n\r\n👉 一连串的连锁反应\r\n👉 层层传导的一系列影响','🧩 拆开理解\r\n\r\ncascading\r\n= 逐级发生的；连锁的；层层传递的\r\n\r\nrange of things\r\n= 一系列事情 / 各种事情\r\n\r\n合起来：\r\n\r\na cascading range of things\r\n\r\n≈ 一系列彼此关联、一个接一个发生的事情','💬 例句\r\n\r\nOne small error can trigger a cascading range of problems.\r\n一个小错误可能引发一连串的问题。\r\n\r\nThe outage caused a cascading range of issues across several systems.\r\n这次宕机在多个系统中造成了一系列连锁问题。\r\n\r\nThat decision led to a cascading range of consequences.\r\n那个决定带来了一连串的后果。\r\n\r\n💻 IT 场景特别常见\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nDatabase failure\r\n↓\r\nAPI timeout\r\n↓\r\nrequest backlog\r\n↓\r\nCPU spike\r\n↓\r\nservice outage\r\n\r\n这就可以说：\r\n\r\nThe database failure caused a cascading series of failures.\r\n数据库故障引发了一连串的系统故障。\r\n\r\n或者：\r\n\r\nIt triggered a cascading range of issues across the platform.\r\n它在整个平台上引发了一系列连锁问题。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 更自然的搭配\r\n\r\n虽然 a cascading range of things 能理解，但英语里更常见的是：\r\n\r\na cascade of problems\r\n\r\na cascading series of events\r\n\r\na cascading series of failures\r\n\r\na chain reaction\r\n\r\na series of knock-on effects\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nIt caused a cascade of problems.\r\n它引发了一连串的问题。\r\n\r\n这通常比 a cascading range of things 更自然。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象多米诺骨牌：\r\n\r\n🁢 → 🁢 → 🁢 → 🁢 → 🁢\r\n\r\n第一个倒下以后，后面的一个接一个倒。\r\n\r\n这就是：\r\n\r\ncascading\r\n\r\n📌 一句话记：\r\n\r\ncascading = one thing causes another, which causes another.\r\n一个事情引发另一个事情，再继续向后传导。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/1d869f77153140a8b2ea4e54658c7905.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 21:19:14',1,'2026-08-25 21:19:14'),(1509,20,105,'phrase','in lockstep','in lockstep','in lockstep','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nin lockstep = 步调一致地；同步地；紧密一致地\r\n\r\n它可以表示两种感觉：\r\n\r\n一起同步变化\r\n\r\n严格保持一致、没有偏离','🧩 来源理解\r\n\r\nlockstep 原本指士兵：\r\n\r\n👥👥👥\r\n大家迈同样的步子、保持完全一致。\r\n\r\n所以后来引申成：\r\n\r\n👉 同步行动\r\n👉 同步变化\r\n👉 保持一致\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法 2：步调一致 / 紧密配合\r\n\r\nThe two teams worked in lockstep throughout the project.\r\n两个团队在整个项目过程中都紧密配合、步调一致。\r\n\r\nThe departments need to operate in lockstep.\r\n各部门需要协调一致地运作。\r\n\r\nDevelopment and testing should move in lockstep.\r\n开发和测试应该同步推进。\r\n\r\n这个在项目管理、软件开发里很好用。','💬 常见用法 1：同步变化\r\n\r\n这个用法在新闻、经济、数据分析里很常见。\r\n\r\nHouse prices and rents tend to move in lockstep.\r\n房价和租金往往会同步变化。\r\n\r\nDemand has risen in lockstep with population growth.\r\n需求随着人口增长而同步上升。\r\n\r\nCosts increased in lockstep with inflation.\r\n成本随着通胀同步上涨。\r\n\r\n📌 很常见的结构：\r\n\r\nmove / rise / fall / grow in lockstep with + 名词\r\n\r\n= 与……同步变化\r\n\r\n⚠️ 有时带一点负面意思\r\n\r\nin lockstep 有时也暗示：\r\n\r\n👉 大家机械地保持一致\r\n👉 缺乏独立思考\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe members voted in lockstep with the leadership.\r\n成员们完全按照领导层的立场一致投票。\r\n\r\n这里就有一点：\r\n\r\n“所有人都跟着走”\r\n\r\n的感觉。\r\n\r\n💻 IT / 工作场景\r\n\r\nThe frontend and backend need to evolve in lockstep.\r\n前端和后端需要同步演进。\r\n\r\nOur monitoring capabilities should grow in lockstep with system complexity.\r\n我们的监控能力应该随着系统复杂度的增加而同步提升。\r\n\r\nThe database schema and API changes must move in lockstep.\r\n数据库结构和 API 的修改必须同步进行。\r\n\r\n⚠️ in lockstep vs in sync\r\n\r\nin sync\r\n👉 更口语、更广泛\r\n= 同步、协调\r\n\r\nThe systems are in sync.\r\n这些系统是同步的。\r\n\r\nin lockstep\r\n👉 更强调严格一致、同步推进\r\n\r\nThe two systems evolved in lockstep.\r\n两个系统一直同步演进。\r\n\r\n📌 强度上可以理解为：\r\n\r\nin sync < in lockstep\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象一排士兵：\r\n\r\n🚶🚶🚶🚶\r\n\r\n左脚一起迈\r\n右脚一起迈\r\n速度完全一样\r\n\r\n这就是：\r\n\r\nin lockstep\r\n\r\n📌 一句话记：\r\n\r\nIf two things move in lockstep, they change or progress together at almost the same pace.\r\n如果两个东西 move in lockstep，就是它们几乎以相同的节奏同步变化或推进。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e8b76b62fd9a4a5f841cb5f0d2208e98.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-25 21:27:43',1,'2026-08-25 21:27:43'),(1510,20,106,'phrase','chop and change','chop and change','chop and change','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nchop and change = 反复改变；改来改去；一会儿这样一会儿那样\r\n\r\n通常带一点负面感觉：\r\n\r\n👉 没有稳定下来\r\n👉 总是在换主意 / 换方案 / 换做法','🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\nchop and change between A and B\r\n在 A 和 B 之间反复切换\r\n\r\nWe kept chopping and changing the design.\r\n我们一直在反复修改设计。\r\n\r\nYou can’t keep chopping and changing your mind.\r\n你不能总是改来改去、反复变卦。\r\n\r\nThe company has chopped and changed its strategy several times.\r\n这家公司已经多次反复调整战略。\r\n\r\n💻 工作 / IT 场景\r\n\r\nWe should avoid chopping and changing the API design once development has started.\r\n开发开始后，我们应该避免反复修改 API 设计。\r\n\r\nThe requirements keep chopping and changing.\r\n需求一直在变来变去。\r\n\r\nIf we chop and change too often, it will slow down development.\r\n如果我们改得太频繁，就会拖慢开发进度。\r\n\r\n🗣️ 口语里自然吗？','✅ 很自然，尤其是英式英语、澳新英语里比较常见。\r\n\r\n比如会议里可以说：\r\n\r\nWe’ve been chopping and changing too much.\r\n我们最近改来改去太频繁了。\r\n\r\nLet’s decide on one approach instead of chopping and changing.\r\n我们定一个方案吧，别再反复改了。\r\n\r\n⚠️ chop and change vs change\r\n\r\nchange\r\n👉 普通的“改变”\r\n\r\nWe changed the design.\r\n我们修改了设计。\r\n\r\nchop and change\r\n👉 反复改、不断换\r\n\r\nWe kept chopping and changing the design.\r\n我们一直反复修改设计。\r\n\r\n所以 chop and change 的重点不是“改了一次”，而是：\r\n\r\nchange → change again → change again\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆画面\r\n\r\n想象一个人：\r\n\r\n方案 A ✅\r\n↓\r\n“不行，换 B”\r\n↓\r\n“还是换回 A”\r\n↓\r\n“再试 C”\r\n\r\n这就是：\r\n\r\n👉 chop and change\r\n\r\n📌 一句话记：\r\n\r\nchop and change = keep changing your plans, decisions, or methods repeatedly.\r\n就是对计划、决定或做法反复改来改去。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/dcc42698c95845b58127bea574580bf6.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-26 13:14:40',1,'2026-08-26 13:14:40'),(1511,20,107,'phrase','a fair bit of','a fair bit of','a fair bit of','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\na fair bit of = 相当多的；不少的\r\n\r\n它比 a bit of 强很多。\r\n\r\na bit of = 一点\r\n\r\na fair bit of = 不少 / 相当多','🧩 常见结构\r\n\r\na fair bit of + 不可数名词\r\n\r\na fair bit of time\r\n不少时间\r\n\r\na fair bit of work\r\n相当多的工作\r\n\r\na fair bit of money\r\n不少钱\r\n\r\na fair bit of experience\r\n相当丰富的经验\r\n\r\na fair bit of effort\r\n不少努力','💬 常见例句\r\n\r\nThis project requires a fair bit of time.\r\n这个项目需要相当多的时间。\r\n\r\nWe still have a fair bit of work to do.\r\n我们还有不少工作要做。\r\n\r\nIt took a fair bit of effort to fix the issue.\r\n修复这个问题花了不少功夫。\r\n\r\nHe has a fair bit of experience in software development.\r\n他在软件开发方面有相当丰富的经验。\r\n\r\n🗣️ 口语里常见吗？\r\n\r\n✅ 很常见，而且很自然。\r\n\r\n尤其在 英式英语、澳大利亚英语、新西兰英语 里很常见。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThere’s still a fair bit to do.\r\n还有不少事情要做。\r\n\r\nIt costs a fair bit.\r\n这个挺贵的 / 要花不少钱。\r\n\r\n这里甚至可以省略后面的名词：\r\n\r\na fair bit = quite a lot\r\n\r\n⚠️ a bit of vs a fair bit of\r\n\r\na bit of work\r\n👉 一点工作\r\n\r\na fair bit of work\r\n👉 相当多的工作\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe have a bit of work left.\r\n我们还剩一点工作。\r\n\r\nWe have a fair bit of work left.\r\n我们还剩不少工作。\r\n\r\n意思差别很明显。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n不要把这里的 fair 理解成“公平的”。\r\n\r\n在这个表达里：\r\n\r\nfair ≈ considerable / quite a lot\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\na fair bit of\r\n≈ quite a lot of\r\n\r\n📌 一句话记：\r\n\r\nWe spent a fair bit of time on it.\r\n我们在这件事上花了相当多的时间。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ec3cd5c29e9d47e0b72c9c358022d189.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-26 17:28:20',1,'2026-08-26 17:28:20'),(1512,20,108,'phrase','circulate into','circulate into','circulate into','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ncirculate into = 流入；循环进入；传播进入\r\n\r\n但要注意：circulate into 不是特别固定、特别常见的短语搭配。\r\n实际使用时，要看你说的是 液体、空气、信息，还是人群。','🧩 1. 液体 / 空气“循环进入”\r\n\r\nWarm air circulates into the room.\r\n暖空气循环进入房间。\r\n\r\nBlood circulates into the surrounding tissues.\r\n血液流入并循环到周围组织。\r\n\r\n这里的感觉是：\r\n\r\ncirculate = 循环流动\r\ninto = 进入\r\n\r\n所以整体是：\r\n\r\n👉 循环着进入某个地方\r\n\r\n🧩 2. 信息 / 消息“传播进入”\r\n\r\n这种用法可以理解，但很多时候英语会用更自然的表达：\r\n\r\nThe information began to circulate within the company.\r\n这个消息开始在公司内部传播。\r\n\r\nRumours circulated through the community.\r\n谣言在社区中传播开来。\r\n\r\n比起：\r\n\r\ncirculate into the company\r\n\r\n更自然的是：\r\n\r\ncirculate within / through the company','⚠️ circulate into vs flow into\r\n\r\n如果强调“进入”：\r\n\r\nflow into 更自然。\r\n\r\nWater flows into the tank.\r\n水流入水箱。\r\n\r\n如果强调“循环”：\r\n\r\ncirculate through / around 更自然。\r\n\r\nWater circulates through the cooling system.\r\n水在冷却系统中循环。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncirculate into\r\n👉 强调“循环流动并进入”\r\n\r\n但很多具体场景下，母语者更常用：\r\n\r\nflow into / circulate through / circulate around\r\n\r\n💻 IT / 数据场景\r\n\r\n如果你想表达“数据进入系统”，一般不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ Data circulates into the system.\r\n\r\n更自然：\r\n\r\n✅ Data flows into the system.\r\n数据流入系统。\r\n\r\n✅ Data is fed into the system.\r\n数据被输入系统。\r\n\r\n✅ Information circulates through the network.\r\n信息在网络中传播 / 流转。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\ncirculate = 循环、流转、传播\r\ninto = 进入\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncirculate into\r\n≈ 循环着进入 / 流转进入\r\n\r\n但一句话记住：\r\n\r\n👉 强调“进入”用 flow into / feed into 更自然\r\n👉 强调“循环传播”用 circulate through / around / within 更自然','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f4f7ae79120d486f8cb177fe808f44b4.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-26 17:36:48',1,'2026-08-26 17:36:48'),(1513,20,109,'phrase','coupled with','coupled with','coupled with','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ncoupled with = 加上；再加上；与……结合在一起\r\n\r\n它通常表示：\r\n\r\n👉 A 和 B 两个因素结合起来，共同产生某个结果','🧩 常见结构\r\n\r\nA, coupled with B, + 结果\r\n\r\n= A 再加上 B，导致……\r\n\r\nHigh demand, coupled with limited supply, pushed prices up.\r\n高需求再加上供应有限，推高了价格。\r\n\r\nHis experience, coupled with strong technical skills, made him a good candidate.\r\n他的经验加上扎实的技术能力，使他成为很合适的候选人。\r\n\r\nHeavy rain, coupled with strong winds, caused widespread disruption.\r\n暴雨加上强风，造成了大范围影响。\r\n\r\n💻 工作 / IT 场景\r\n\r\nHigh traffic, coupled with inefficient queries, caused the database to slow down.\r\n高流量加上低效查询，导致数据库变慢。\r\n\r\nPoor error handling, coupled with limited monitoring, made the issue harder to diagnose.\r\n较差的错误处理机制再加上有限的监控，让问题更难排查。\r\n\r\nOCR accuracy, coupled with human review, can improve overall reliability.\r\nOCR 准确率结合人工审核，可以提高整体可靠性。\r\n\r\n🗣️ 口语里自然吗？','✅ 自然，但比 together with / combined with 稍正式一点。\r\n\r\n常见于：\r\n\r\n新闻\r\n\r\n工作汇报\r\n\r\n技术讨论\r\n\r\n学术写作\r\n\r\n口语中也可以说：\r\n\r\nThat, coupled with the delay, caused a lot of problems.\r\n那个问题再加上延误，造成了很多麻烦。\r\n\r\n⚠️ coupled with vs combined with\r\n\r\ncoupled with\r\n👉 强调两个因素“搭配在一起”，共同产生影响\r\n\r\ncombined with\r\n👉 更普通、更中性，表示“与……结合”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nHigh costs, coupled with low demand, hurt the business.\r\n高成本加低需求，对业务造成了影响。\r\n\r\nRed combined with blue makes purple.\r\n红色和蓝色混合会变成紫色。\r\n\r\n所以讲因素共同作用时，coupled with 很自然。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\ncouple 本来就有：\r\n\r\n一对、两个东西配在一起\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nA coupled with B\r\n\r\n就是：\r\n\r\nA + B → 一起作用\r\n\r\n📌 一句话记：\r\n\r\nPoor planning, coupled with weak communication, caused the delay.\r\n计划不周再加上沟通不足，导致了延误。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/63943525f36a4c2cb229063658b1d0c7.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-26 21:13:10',1,'2026-08-26 21:13:10'),(1514,21,1,'phrase','put aside','put aside','put aside','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nput aside = 把……放到一边；暂时不考虑；留出 / 存下','🧩 用法 1：把东西放到一边\r\n\r\nShe put the book aside and answered the phone.\r\n她把书放到一边，然后接电话。\r\n\r\nPlease put those documents aside for now.\r\n请先把那些文件放到一边。\r\n\r\n🧩 用法 2：暂时不考虑 / 撇开\r\n\r\n这个用法非常常见：\r\n\r\nput aside + differences / concerns / feelings / arguments\r\n\r\nWe need to put aside our differences and work together.\r\n我们需要暂时搁置分歧，一起合作。\r\n\r\nPutting aside the cost, this is a good solution.\r\n先不考虑成本的话，这是一个不错的方案。\r\n\r\nLet’s put that issue aside for the moment.\r\n我们暂时先搁置这个问题。\r\n\r\n👉 很像中文：\r\n\r\n“先把这个放一边不谈。”\r\n\r\n💰 用法 3：留出 / 存下一部分\r\n\r\nput aside money / time\r\n\r\nI try to put aside some money every month.\r\n我每个月都会尽量存一些钱。\r\n\r\nWe should put aside some time to review the design.\r\n我们应该留出一些时间来审核设计。\r\n\r\nShe has put aside enough money for the trip.\r\n她已经为这次旅行存够了钱。\r\n\r\n💻 工作 / IT 场景\r\n\r\nLet’s put aside the UI issue and focus on the API first.\r\n我们先把 UI 的问题放一放，优先处理 API。\r\n\r\nWe need to put aside some time for testing.\r\n我们需要留出一些时间做测试。\r\n\r\nPutting aside performance concerns, the current design is quite flexible.\r\n暂且不考虑性能问题，目前这个设计还是比较灵活的。','⚠️ put aside vs set aside\r\n\r\n两者非常接近。\r\n\r\nput aside\r\n👉 更口语，常表示“放一边 / 暂时不管”\r\n\r\nset aside\r\n👉 也可以表示“留出”，而且稍正式\r\n\r\nPut aside your phone and listen.\r\n把手机放一边，听我说。\r\n\r\nWe set aside two hours for testing.\r\n我们专门留了两个小时做测试。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nput = 放\r\naside = 到旁边\r\n\r\n所以最原始的画面就是：\r\n\r\n📄 → ➡️ → 📚\r\n\r\n把某样东西放到旁边\r\n\r\n然后引申成：\r\n\r\n问题放一边 → 暂时不考虑\r\n钱放一边 → 存起来\r\n时间放一边 → 预留出来\r\n\r\n📌 一句话记：\r\n\r\nLet’s put that aside for now.\r\n这件事我们现在先放一放。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/475e0b7c889d41738d674467a2a9fb94.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-26 21:47:04',1,'2026-08-26 21:47:04'),(1515,21,2,'phrase','engage with','engage with','engage with','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nengage with = 与……互动；参与；认真处理 / 接触 / 思考某事\r\n\r\n它不是只有一个固定中文意思，常见要看对象是什么。','🧩 用法 1：与人互动 / 沟通\r\n\r\nWe need to engage with customers more effectively.\r\n我们需要更有效地与客户互动 / 沟通。\r\n\r\nThe company is trying to engage with local communities.\r\n公司正在努力与当地社区建立互动。\r\n\r\n这里的 engage with someone\r\n≈ interact with / communicate with\r\n\r\n🧩 用法 2：参与某个话题 / 活动 / 过程\r\n\r\nStudents are encouraged to engage with the discussion.\r\n鼓励学生参与讨论。\r\n\r\nEmployees need to engage with the new process.\r\n员工需要积极参与并适应新的流程。\r\n\r\n🧩 用法 3：认真思考 / 处理某个问题\r\n\r\n这个用法在学术、工作场景里很常见。\r\n\r\nThe report does not fully engage with the problem.\r\n这份报告没有充分回应 / 深入处理这个问题。\r\n\r\nWe need to engage with these concerns rather than ignore them.\r\n我们需要认真处理这些担忧，而不是忽视它们。\r\n\r\n这里不是简单的“接触”，而是：\r\n\r\n👉 认真面对、分析、回应\r\n\r\n💻 工作 / IT 场景\r\n\r\nWe should engage with users early in the design process.\r\n我们应该在设计早期就与用户沟通互动。\r\n\r\nThe team needs to engage with the feedback from testers.\r\n团队需要认真处理测试人员的反馈。\r\n\r\nDevelopers should engage with security requirements from the beginning.\r\n开发人员应该从一开始就认真考虑并落实安全需求。\r\n\r\n🗣️ 口语里自然吗？','✅ 很自然，但比 talk to 更正式一些。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nI’ve been engaging with the client about this issue.\r\n我一直在和客户就这个问题进行沟通。\r\n\r\n不过日常口语里，如果只是“跟某人说话”，更常见：\r\n\r\ntalk to / speak with\r\n\r\n而 engage with 更强调：\r\n\r\n有互动、有参与、有实质性的交流\r\n\r\n⚠️ engage with vs deal with\r\n\r\nengage with\r\n👉 强调主动参与、认真回应、互动\r\n\r\ndeal with\r\n👉 强调处理、解决\r\n\r\nWe need to engage with customer feedback.\r\n我们需要认真听取并回应客户反馈。\r\n\r\nWe need to deal with this bug.\r\n我们需要处理这个 bug。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 engage 想成：\r\n\r\n“真正参与进去”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nengage with + 人\r\n= 与某人互动\r\n\r\nengage with + idea/problem/feedback\r\n= 认真面对、思考、回应\r\n\r\n📌 一句话记：\r\n\r\nengage with = actively interact with or seriously deal with something.\r\n就是主动参与、互动，或者认真处理某件事。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b45089e2235c41169e447675a54d1dd3.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-26 22:09:50',1,'2026-08-26 22:09:50'),(1516,21,3,'phrase','keep pace','keep pace','keep pace','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nkeep pace = 跟上步伐；保持同样速度；跟上发展\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\nkeep pace with + 人 / 事物\r\n\r\n= 跟上……的速度或发展','🧩 用法 1：跟上某人的速度\r\n\r\nI had to walk faster to keep pace with him.\r\n我得走快一点才能跟上他的步伐。\r\n\r\nShe struggled to keep pace with the other runners.\r\n她很难跟上其他跑者的速度。\r\n\r\n🧩 用法 2：跟上发展 / 变化\r\n\r\n这个用法在工作、科技、新闻里特别常见。\r\n\r\nCompanies need to keep pace with technological change.\r\n公司需要跟上技术变化的步伐。\r\n\r\nOur systems must keep pace with business growth.\r\n我们的系统必须跟上业务增长。\r\n\r\nSalaries have not kept pace with inflation.\r\n工资并没有跟上通货膨胀的速度。\r\n\r\n💻 工作 / IT 场景\r\n\r\nThe infrastructure needs to keep pace with increasing traffic.\r\n基础设施需要跟上不断增长的流量。\r\n\r\nMonitoring capabilities should keep pace with system complexity.\r\n监控能力应该跟上系统复杂度的提升。\r\n\r\nWe need to keep pace with changing requirements.\r\n我们需要跟上不断变化的需求。\r\n\r\n🗣️ 口语里自然吗？','✅ 很自然，也很常用。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nTechnology is changing so fast that it’s hard to keep pace.\r\n技术变化太快了，很难跟得上。\r\n\r\n这里后面甚至不需要 with：\r\n\r\nkeep pace = 保持跟得上\r\n\r\n⚠️ keep pace with vs keep up with\r\n\r\n两者非常接近。\r\n\r\nkeep up with\r\n👉 更口语、更日常\r\n\r\nI can’t keep up with all these changes.\r\n这些变化太多了，我都跟不上。\r\n\r\nkeep pace with\r\n👉 稍正式，强调“速度 / 发展节奏保持一致”\r\n\r\nInvestment must keep pace with demand.\r\n投资必须跟上需求增长。\r\n\r\n📌 可以简单记：\r\n\r\nkeep up with = 跟得上\r\nkeep pace with = 保持同样的发展速度\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\npace = 步伐 / 速度\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nkeep + pace\r\n= 保持这个步伐\r\n\r\n👉 keep pace with = 跟上……的步伐\r\n\r\n📌 一句话记：\r\n\r\nWe need to keep pace with change.\r\n我们需要跟上变化的步伐。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/3ed683880f0c432083b158f8d915180c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-26 22:20:40',1,'2026-08-26 22:20:40'),(1517,21,4,'phrase','capacity vs capability vs compatibility','capacity vs capability vs compatibility','capacity vs capability vs compatibility','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n这三个词最核心的区别可以记成：\r\n\r\ncapacity = 能处理多少\r\n→ How much can it handle?\r\n\r\ncapability = 能不能做 / 能做什么\r\n→ What can it do?\r\n\r\ncompatibility = 能不能和别的东西一起正常工作\r\n→ Can they work together?\r\n\r\n最简单地说：\r\n\r\ncapacity = 量\r\ncapability = 能力\r\ncompatibility = 兼容性','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\ncapacity = 容量 / 承载能力\r\n\r\n强调“数量、规模、负载上限”。\r\n\r\n常见搭配：\r\n\r\nstorage capacity\r\n存储容量\r\n\r\nserver capacity\r\n服务器承载能力\r\n\r\nprocessing capacity\r\n处理能力\r\n\r\nproduction capacity\r\n生产能力\r\n\r\nat full capacity\r\n满负荷运行\r\n\r\nincrease capacity\r\n提高容量 / 承载能力\r\n\r\ncapability = 能力 / 功能\r\n\r\n强调“有没有能力做某件事”。\r\n\r\n常见搭配：\r\n\r\ntechnical capability\r\n技术能力\r\n\r\nsystem capability\r\n系统能力 / 系统功能\r\n\r\nmonitoring capability\r\n监控能力\r\n\r\nOCR capability\r\nOCR 识别能力\r\n\r\ncapability to do something\r\n做某事的能力\r\n\r\ndevelop capabilities\r\n培养 / 建立能力\r\n\r\ncompatibility = 兼容性\r\n\r\n强调两个系统、设备、软件等能否一起正常运行。\r\n\r\n常见搭配：\r\n\r\nsoftware compatibility\r\n软件兼容性\r\n\r\nbrowser compatibility\r\n浏览器兼容性\r\n\r\nbackward compatibility\r\n向后兼容\r\n\r\ncompatibility issue\r\n兼容性问题\r\n\r\ncompatibility with something\r\n与某物的兼容性','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\ncapacity\r\n\r\nThe server is running at full capacity.\r\n服务器正在满负荷运行。\r\n\r\nWe need more capacity to handle the increased traffic.\r\n我们需要更大的处理能力来应对增长的流量。\r\n\r\nThe system does not have enough capacity to process all these requests.\r\n系统没有足够的处理容量来处理所有这些请求。\r\n\r\ncapability\r\n\r\nThe system has the capability to process handwritten text.\r\n这个系统具备处理手写文字的能力。\r\n\r\nWe need to improve our monitoring capabilities.\r\n我们需要提升监控能力。\r\n\r\nThe new version adds several new capabilities.\r\n新版本增加了几个新的功能。\r\n\r\ncompatibility\r\n\r\nWe need to check compatibility with older versions.\r\n我们需要检查与旧版本的兼容性。\r\n\r\nThe update caused some compatibility issues.\r\n这次更新造成了一些兼容性问题。\r\n\r\nThis library has good compatibility with the latest version of Python.\r\n这个库与最新版 Python 的兼容性很好。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n如果放在同一个 IT 系统里理解，会非常清楚。\r\n\r\n假设有一个 OCR 系统：\r\n\r\nCan it process 10,000 documents per day?\r\n\r\n这里问的是：\r\n\r\n“它一天能处理多少？”\r\n\r\n→ capacity\r\n\r\nThe system has enough capacity to process 10,000 documents per day.\r\n这个系统有足够的处理能力每天处理一万份文档。\r\n\r\nCan it recognise handwritten text?\r\n\r\n这里问的是：\r\n\r\n“它有没有识别手写文字这个功能？”\r\n\r\n→ capability\r\n\r\nThe system has handwriting recognition capability.\r\n这个系统具备手写识别能力。\r\n\r\nCan it work with SQL Server?\r\n\r\n这里问的是：\r\n\r\n“它能不能和 SQL Server 一起正常运行？”\r\n\r\n→ compatibility\r\n\r\nWe need to check its compatibility with SQL Server.\r\n我们需要检查它与 SQL Server 的兼容性。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\ncapacity vs capability\r\n\r\n这是最容易混的一组。\r\n\r\ncapacity\r\n强调“能做多少”。\r\n\r\n比如服务器本来就能处理请求，只是流量太大，扛不住：\r\n\r\nThe server doesn\'t have enough capacity to handle 100,000 requests per second.\r\n服务器没有足够的承载能力处理每秒十万个请求。\r\n\r\n这里不是说服务器“不会处理请求”，而是：\r\n\r\n会处理，但量太大。\r\n\r\ncapability\r\n强调“能不能做”。\r\n\r\nThe system doesn\'t have the capability to recognise handwriting.\r\n这个系统不具备识别手写文字的能力。\r\n\r\n这里意味着：\r\n\r\n它本身就没有这个功能。\r\n\r\n所以可以记成：\r\n\r\ncapacity = quantity / load\r\n数量、负载\r\n\r\ncapability = ability / function\r\n能力、功能\r\n\r\ncapability vs compatibility\r\n\r\ncapability\r\n= 自己有什么能力\r\n\r\ncompatibility\r\n= 和别人能不能配合\r\n\r\nThe software has powerful reporting capabilities.\r\n这个软件有强大的报表功能。\r\n\r\nWe found a compatibility issue between the software and the database.\r\n我们发现软件和数据库之间存在兼容性问题。\r\n\r\ncapacity vs ability\r\n\r\ncapacity 有时也可以表示人的“能力”，例如：\r\n\r\nHe has a great capacity for learning.\r\n他有很强的学习能力。\r\n\r\n但这里更偏：\r\n\r\n“潜力、吸收能力、承受能力”。\r\n\r\n而 ability 更直接表示：\r\n\r\n“会不会做某件事”。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n不要把 capacity 和 capability 都简单翻译成“能力”。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe server lacks capacity.\r\n\r\n通常不是：\r\n\r\n❌ 服务器没有能力。\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\n✅ 服务器容量 / 承载能力不够。\r\n\r\ncapability 常常用复数 capabilities 表示“功能”。\r\n\r\nThe system has several useful capabilities.\r\n这个系统具有几个实用功能。\r\n\r\n在软件行业里非常常见。\r\n\r\ncompatibility 后面常接 with。\r\n\r\ncompatibility with Windows\r\n与 Windows 的兼容性\r\n\r\ncompatibility with older versions\r\n与旧版本的兼容性\r\n\r\n如果重点是“处理更多流量”，通常用 capacity，不是 capability。\r\n\r\n✅ We need to increase server capacity.\r\n\r\n更自然。\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n❌ We need to increase server capability.\r\n\r\n除非你是想增加服务器“新的功能”。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\ncapacity\r\n\r\n想象一个水桶 🪣\r\n\r\n问题是：\r\n\r\nHow much can it hold?\r\n它能装多少？\r\n\r\n→ capacity = 容量 / 承载量\r\n\r\ncapability\r\n\r\n想象一个工具箱 🧰\r\n\r\n问题是：\r\n\r\nWhat can it do?\r\n它会做什么？\r\n\r\n→ capability = 能力 / 功能\r\n\r\ncompatibility\r\n\r\n想象两个拼图 🧩 + 🧩\r\n\r\n问题是：\r\n\r\nCan they fit together?\r\n它们能不能拼在一起？\r\n\r\n→ compatibility = 兼容性\r\n\r\n一句话记忆：\r\n\r\ncapacity = How much?\r\n能处理多少？\r\n\r\ncapability = Can it do it?\r\n它能不能做？\r\n\r\ncompatibility = Can they work together?\r\n它们能不能一起正常工作？\r\n\r\n来源','/static/uploads/english_note_item/5538529656664a3581a0d43a1e67f125.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-27 11:21:09',1,'2026-08-27 11:21:09'),(1518,21,5,'phrase','an avalanche of sth','an avalanche of sth','an avalanche of sth','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nan avalanche of sth\r\n= 大量突然涌来的……；铺天盖地的……；一大堆接踵而来的……\r\n\r\n它来自字面意思：\r\n\r\navalanche = 雪崩\r\n\r\n想象山上的雪突然全部冲下来：\r\n\r\n🏔️ → ❄️❄️❄️❄️❄️\r\n\r\n所以引申为：\r\n\r\n👉 某种东西数量非常大，而且突然大量出现。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nan avalanche of questions\r\n大量问题接连涌来\r\n\r\nan avalanche of emails\r\n大量邮件蜂拥而来\r\n\r\nan avalanche of complaints\r\n大量投诉涌来\r\n\r\nan avalanche of information\r\n海量信息一下子涌来\r\n\r\nan avalanche of criticism\r\n铺天盖地的批评\r\n\r\nan avalanche of applications\r\n大量申请蜂拥而至\r\n\r\nan avalanche of requests\r\n大量请求涌来\r\n\r\n这个表达尤其适合强调：\r\n\r\n“数量多 + 来得快 + 一下子压过来”。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nWe received an avalanche of emails after the announcement.\r\n公告发布后，我们收到了大量蜂拥而来的邮件。\r\n\r\nThe support team was hit by an avalanche of customer complaints.\r\n客服团队遭遇了大量客户投诉。\r\n\r\nAfter the system went live, we received an avalanche of requests.\r\n系统上线后，我们收到了大量请求。\r\n\r\nThe report triggered an avalanche of criticism.\r\n这份报告引发了铺天盖地的批评。\r\n\r\nThere was an avalanche of information to process.\r\n有海量信息需要处理。\r\n\r\nShe was faced with an avalanche of questions from reporters.\r\n她面对记者们接连不断的大量提问。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n如果你看到：\r\n\r\nan avalanche of complaints\r\n\r\n不要简单理解成：\r\n\r\n“很多投诉”。\r\n\r\n它比：\r\n\r\na lot of complaints\r\n\r\n更有画面感。\r\n\r\nan avalanche of complaints\r\n= 投诉像雪崩一样一下子大量涌来\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe company faced an avalanche of complaints after the outage.\r\n\r\n可以自然翻译成：\r\n\r\n系统宕机后，公司收到了铺天盖地的投诉。\r\n\r\n这里强调的是：\r\n\r\noutage\r\n↓\r\n大量投诉突然出现\r\n↓\r\n团队一下子被淹没\r\n\r\n所以 avalanche 带有一种：\r\n\r\n“数量非常大，来势很猛”\r\n\r\n的感觉。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nan avalanche of vs a lot of\r\n\r\na lot of\r\n= 很多\r\n最普通、中性\r\n\r\nWe received a lot of emails.\r\n我们收到了很多邮件。\r\n\r\nan avalanche of\r\n= 大量突然涌来，强调来势很猛\r\n\r\nWe received an avalanche of emails.\r\n我们一下子收到了海量邮件。\r\n\r\nan avalanche of vs a flood of\r\n\r\na flood of\r\n= 大量涌入\r\n\r\nan avalanche of\r\n= 更强调“突然、大量、压倒性”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\na flood of messages\r\n大量消息涌入\r\n\r\nan avalanche of messages\r\n大量消息像雪崩一样突然涌来\r\n\r\n两者都很自然，但 avalanche 的画面更强。\r\n\r\nan avalanche of vs a cascade of\r\n\r\nan avalanche of\r\n👉 强调“数量巨大、突然涌来”\r\n\r\na cascade of\r\n👉 强调“一个引发另一个，形成连锁反应”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nan avalanche of complaints\r\n大量投诉突然涌来\r\n\r\na cascade of failures\r\n一连串连锁故障\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\navalanche = 多\r\ncascade = 连锁\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\navalanche 后面通常用 of\r\n\r\n✅ an avalanche of emails\r\n\r\n✅ an avalanche of complaints\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ an avalanche emails\r\n\r\n它通常用于大量、可积累的东西\r\n\r\n特别常见：\r\n\r\nemails\r\nquestions\r\nrequests\r\ncomplaints\r\ncriticism\r\ninformation\r\napplications\r\n\r\n不是所有名词都自然。\r\n\r\n通常带一点“应接不暇”的感觉\r\n\r\nan avalanche of work\r\n可以理解，但比：\r\n\r\na huge amount of work\r\n\r\n更强调：\r\n\r\n工作突然大量压过来。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象一座雪山：\r\n\r\n🏔️\r\n\r\n刚开始只有一点雪。\r\n\r\n突然：\r\n\r\n❄️❄️❄️❄️❄️\r\n⬇️⬇️⬇️⬇️\r\n🌊 一下全部冲下来\r\n\r\n这就是：\r\n\r\navalanche = 雪崩\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nan avalanche of emails\r\n= 邮件像雪崩一样涌来\r\n\r\nan avalanche of complaints\r\n= 投诉像雪崩一样涌来\r\n\r\n一句话记忆：\r\n\r\nan avalanche of sth = a huge amount of something arriving suddenly.\r\n\r\n= 某种东西突然大量涌来。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b5b27eaaf869473f851e4664eaa957bd.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-27 11:24:37',1,'2026-08-27 11:24:37'),(1519,21,6,'vocab','obligation','obligation','obligation','🎯 核心意思\r\nobligation = 义务；责任；必须做的事情\r\n\r\n通常指因为法律、道德、工作、承诺或身份，而“应该做 / 必须做”的事情。\r\n\r\n最常见结构：\r\n\r\nhave an obligation to do sth\r\n= 有义务做某事\r\n\r\nan obligation on sb\r\n= 对某人施加的义务 / 某人承担的责任','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n法律或正式意义上的“义务”\r\n\r\nlegal obligation\r\n法律义务\r\n\r\nCompanies have an obligation to protect personal data.\r\n公司有义务保护个人数据。\r\n\r\n道德上的“责任”\r\n\r\nmoral obligation\r\n道德责任\r\n\r\nWe have a moral obligation to help people in need.\r\n我们在道德上有责任帮助有困难的人。\r\n\r\n工作、家庭等方面必须履行的责任\r\n\r\nfamily obligations\r\n家庭责任\r\n\r\nwork obligations\r\n工作上的责任\r\n\r\nI can\'t go out tonight because of family obligations.\r\n我今晚不能出去，因为有家庭方面的事情要处理。\r\n\r\nfeel under an obligation to do sth\r\n\r\n= 感到有责任 / 不得不做某事\r\n\r\nI felt under an obligation to help him.\r\n我觉得自己有责任帮助他。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nYou have an obligation to follow the law.\r\n你有义务遵守法律。\r\n\r\nEmployers have an obligation to provide a safe workplace.\r\n雇主有义务提供安全的工作环境。\r\n\r\nParents have certain obligations towards their children.\r\n父母对子女负有一定的责任。\r\n\r\nI don\'t want you to feel under any obligation to come.\r\n我不希望你觉得自己非来不可。\r\n\r\nThe company failed to meet its legal obligations.\r\n这家公司未能履行其法律义务。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n你之前的原句是：\r\n\r\nOpportunity supports stronger obligations on platforms to address harmful algorithms.\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nstronger obligations on platforms\r\n= 对平台施加更严格的义务 / 要求平台承担更多责任\r\n\r\n整句话可以理解为：\r\n\r\nOpportunity 支持要求平台承担更严格的责任，以应对有害算法。\r\n\r\n这里的结构非常值得记：\r\n\r\nobligations on + 人 / 机构\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe law places new obligations on employers.\r\n这项法律给雇主规定了新的义务。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nobligation vs responsibility\r\n\r\nobligation\r\n更强调“必须履行的义务”，常来自法律、规则、合同或道德要求。\r\n\r\nYou have a legal obligation to report it.\r\n你在法律上有义务报告这件事。\r\n\r\nresponsibility\r\n更强调“职责、责任”，范围更广，也可以只是你负责某件事。\r\n\r\nIt\'s my responsibility to manage the team.\r\n管理这个团队是我的职责。\r\n\r\nobligation vs duty\r\n\r\nduty\r\n也表示“职责、义务”，常用于职业、身份、道德职责。\r\n\r\nA police officer has a duty to protect the public.\r\n警察有保护公众的职责。\r\n\r\nobligation 往往更强调“受到约束，必须做”。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nobligation 后面常接 to do\r\n\r\n✅ an obligation to help\r\n有义务帮助\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ an obligation for help\r\n\r\n注意重音\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\nob-LI-ga-tion\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\nob-li-GA-tion\r\n\r\n/ˌɒb.lɪˈɡeɪ.ʃən/\r\n\r\nobligation 是可数名词\r\n\r\na legal obligation\r\n一项法律义务\r\n\r\nlegal obligations\r\n多项法律义务\r\n\r\n常见搭配要整体记\r\n\r\nmeet an obligation\r\n履行义务\r\n\r\nfulfil an obligation\r\n履行义务\r\n\r\nhave an obligation to do sth\r\n有义务做某事\r\n\r\nplace/impose an obligation on sb\r\n给某人施加义务\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n可以把 obligation 和 obligate 联系起来：\r\n\r\nobligate = 迫使；使负有义务\r\nobligation = 被要求必须做的事情 → 义务\r\n\r\n记一句最实用的：\r\n\r\nYou have an obligation to do it.\r\n你有义务做这件事。\r\n\r\n再把你的原句搭配一起记：\r\n\r\nstronger obligations on platforms\r\n= 对平台提出更严格的责任要求。\r\n\r\nSources','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2544e5f04373430a919015233a6a9134.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-27 21:59:35',1,'2026-08-27 21:59:35'),(1520,21,7,'phrase','behavioural profiling','behavioural profiling','behavioural profiling','🎯 核心意思\r\nbehavioural profiling = 行为画像 / 行为特征分析\r\n\r\n指通过收集和分析一个人的行为数据，来判断他的兴趣、习惯、偏好、消费倾向等。\r\n\r\n常见于：\r\n互联网平台\r\n广告推荐\r\n社交媒体\r\n数据隐私\r\n算法推荐','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n用户行为画像\r\n\r\nPlatforms use behavioural profiling to understand users\' interests.\r\n平台通过行为画像来了解用户的兴趣。\r\n\r\n广告定向\r\n\r\nBehavioural profiling can be used to target advertisements.\r\n行为画像可以用于精准投放广告。\r\n\r\n数据隐私与监管语境\r\n\r\nThe law places restrictions on behavioural profiling.\r\n法律对行为画像分析施加了限制。\r\n\r\n算法推荐\r\n\r\nBehavioural profiling may influence what content users see online.\r\n行为画像可能影响用户在网上看到的内容。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nSocial media companies use behavioural profiling to personalise content.\r\n社交媒体公司使用行为画像来个性化内容。\r\n\r\nBehavioural profiling raises concerns about privacy.\r\n行为画像引发了人们对隐私的担忧。\r\n\r\nThe platform collects user data for behavioural profiling.\r\n该平台收集用户数据用于行为画像分析。\r\n\r\nChildren may be particularly vulnerable to behavioural profiling.\r\n儿童可能特别容易受到行为画像分析的影响。\r\n\r\nThe government wants stronger protections against behavioural profiling.\r\n政府希望加强针对行为画像的保护措施。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n你之前的原句是：\r\n\r\nOpportunity supports stronger obligations on platforms to address harmful algorithms, addictive design, behavioural profiling, data leaks, and other systemic risks.\r\n\r\n这里的：\r\n\r\nbehavioural profiling\r\n= 行为画像 / 用户行为特征分析\r\n\r\n整段：\r\n\r\nharmful algorithms\r\n有害算法\r\n\r\naddictive design\r\n成瘾性设计\r\n\r\nbehavioural profiling\r\n行为画像\r\n\r\ndata leaks\r\n数据泄露\r\n\r\nother systemic risks\r\n其他系统性风险\r\n\r\n所以这部分可以理解为：\r\n\r\n要求平台应对有害算法、成瘾性设计、行为画像、数据泄露以及其他系统性风险。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nbehavioural profiling vs user profiling\r\n\r\nbehavioural profiling\r\n强调根据“行为”建立画像，例如：\r\n\r\n点击什么\r\n看什么视频\r\n停留多久\r\n购买什么\r\n\r\nuser profiling\r\n范围更广，除了行为，还可能包括：\r\n\r\n年龄\r\n职业\r\n位置\r\n兴趣\r\n设备信息\r\n\r\nbehavioural profiling vs behavioural tracking\r\n\r\nbehavioural tracking\r\n= 行为追踪\r\n\r\n重点是“记录用户做了什么”。\r\n\r\nbehavioural profiling\r\n= 行为画像\r\n\r\n重点是“根据这些行为推断这个人是什么类型的用户”。\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\ntracking → 收集行为\r\nprofiling → 分析行为并建立画像\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n英式英语写 behavioural\r\n\r\n✅ behavioural\r\n❌ behavioral\r\n\r\nbehavioral 是美式拼写。\r\n\r\n你学英音，所以建议记：\r\n\r\nbehaviour\r\nbehavioural\r\n\r\nprofiling 不只是“个人资料”\r\n\r\nprofile 作名词可以表示“简介、档案”，但：\r\n\r\nprofiling\r\n在这里不是“写个人简介”，而是：\r\n\r\n分析数据 → 建立用户画像\r\n\r\npronunciation 注意\r\n\r\nbehavioural：\r\n\r\nbih-HAY-vyuh-rəl\r\n\r\n重音在 HAY：\r\n\r\nbe-HAV-iour-al ❌\r\nbe-HAY-viour-al ✅\r\n\r\nprofiling：\r\n\r\nPRO-file-ing\r\n\r\n英音：\r\n\r\n/ˈprəʊ.faɪ.lɪŋ/\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n拆开记：\r\n\r\nbehaviour\r\n= 行为\r\n\r\nprofile\r\n= 画像 / 特征档案\r\n\r\nbehavioural profiling\r\n= 根据你的行为建立一个 profile\r\n\r\n想象一个社交媒体平台记录：\r\n\r\n你点了什么\r\n看了多久\r\n买了什么\r\n搜索了什么\r\n\r\n然后系统得出：\r\n\r\n“这个用户喜欢旅游、科技和汽车。”\r\n\r\n这整个过程就是：\r\n\r\nbehavioural profiling\r\n行为画像。\r\n\r\nSources','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9bbed6ffbf6d4bf4b7c5146756490484.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-27 22:05:22',1,'2026-08-27 22:05:22'),(1521,21,8,'vocab','alongside','alongside','alongside','🎯 核心意思\r\nalongside = 在……旁边；与……一起；与……同时\r\n\r\n它既可以表示真实空间上的“在旁边”，也常用于抽象语境，表示：\r\n\r\n与……并行\r\n和……一起\r\n在……同时进行','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n在……旁边\r\n\r\nThe car was parked alongside the road.\r\n汽车停在路边。\r\n\r\n与……一起；和……并肩\r\n\r\nShe worked alongside experienced engineers.\r\n她和有经验的工程师一起工作。\r\n\r\n与……同时发生 / 实施\r\n\r\nThe new policy will be introduced alongside other reforms.\r\n这项新政策将与其他改革措施同时推出。\r\n\r\nalongside each other\r\n\r\n= 并排地；彼此并肩\r\n\r\nThe two buildings stand alongside each other.\r\n两栋建筑并排而立。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nHe worked alongside me for three years.\r\n他和我一起工作了三年。\r\n\r\nThe new system will operate alongside the existing one.\r\n新系统将与现有系统并行运行。\r\n\r\nThese protections should be introduced alongside the legislation.\r\n这些保护措施应当与该立法同时推出。\r\n\r\nThe boat came alongside the pier.\r\n船靠到了码头旁边。\r\n\r\nNew technology should develop alongside stronger regulation.\r\n新技术的发展应该伴随着更严格的监管。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n你之前的原句是：\r\n\r\nStronger protections should commence alongside this legislation, not be deferred to a later phase.\r\n\r\n这里的：\r\n\r\nalongside this legislation\r\n= 与这项立法同时\r\n= 和这项立法一起实施\r\n\r\n所以整句意思是：\r\n\r\n更有力的保护措施应该与这项立法同步开始实施，而不是推迟到之后的阶段。\r\n\r\n这里 alongside 不是“在旁边”的物理位置，而是：\r\n\r\nat the same time as\r\n= 与……同时\r\n\r\n这个用法在政策、商业、技术语境里很常见。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nalongside vs beside\r\n\r\nbeside\r\n主要表示物理位置：\r\n\r\nShe sat beside me.\r\n她坐在我旁边。\r\n\r\nalongside\r\n既可以表示位置，也可以表示“与……一起工作 / 同时进行”。\r\n\r\nShe worked alongside me.\r\n她和我一起工作。\r\n\r\nalongside vs together with\r\n\r\ntogether with\r\n= 连同；和……一起\r\n\r\nThe report was released together with the new policy.\r\n报告与新政策一同发布。\r\n\r\nalongside\r\n更有一种“并行、同步”的感觉。\r\n\r\nThe system runs alongside the old system.\r\n新旧系统并行运行。\r\n\r\nalongside vs at the same time as\r\n\r\nat the same time as\r\n更直接表示“同时”。\r\n\r\nalongside\r\n更简洁、更正式，尤其常见于：\r\n\r\npolicy\r\ntechnology\r\nbusiness\r\nproject\r\nlegislation\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nalongside 后面直接接名词\r\n\r\n✅ alongside this legislation\r\n\r\n✅ alongside the existing system\r\n\r\n不需要加 with：\r\n\r\n❌ alongside with this legislation\r\n\r\nalongside 本身就有“和……一起”的意思\r\n\r\n所以不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ together alongside\r\n\r\n通常二选一即可。\r\n\r\n发音注意\r\n\r\nalongside：\r\n\r\n/əˌlɒŋˈsaɪd/\r\n\r\n重点在最后：\r\n\r\na-long-SIDE\r\n\r\n前面的 a 通常弱读成 /ə/。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n拆开记：\r\n\r\nalong = 沿着\r\nside = 旁边\r\n\r\nalong + side\r\n= 沿着一侧\r\n→ 在旁边\r\n→ 并肩\r\n→ 一起 / 同时进行\r\n\r\n你可以重点记两个最实用搭配：\r\n\r\nwork alongside sb\r\n= 和某人一起工作\r\n\r\noperate / commence alongside sth\r\n= 与某事同时运行 / 开始\r\n\r\n比如你原句：\r\n\r\ncommence alongside this legislation\r\n= 与这项立法同步开始。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/6ce82f56180d49c6892de0f26bfd58cf.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-27 22:14:52',1,'2026-08-27 22:14:52'),(1522,21,9,'phrase','defer to','defer to','defer to','🎯 核心意思\r\ndefer to = 听从；尊重并采纳……的意见；把决定权让给……\r\n\r\n这个短语通常表示：\r\n\r\n因为对方更有经验、更有权威、职位更高，\r\n所以你选择听从对方的判断。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n听从某人的意见\r\n\r\nI’ll defer to your judgment.\r\n我会听从你的判断。\r\n\r\n尊重专家 / 权威意见\r\n\r\nWe should defer to the experts on this issue.\r\n在这个问题上，我们应该听取专家的意见。\r\n\r\n把决定权交给别人\r\n\r\nI’ll defer to the manager on that decision.\r\n关于那个决定，我会交给经理来定。\r\n\r\n常见结构\r\n\r\ndefer to sb\r\n听从某人\r\n\r\ndefer to sb’s judgment\r\n听从某人的判断\r\n\r\ndefer to expert advice\r\n听从专家建议\r\n\r\ndefer to authority\r\n服从权威','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nI’ll defer to you on this matter.\r\n这件事我听你的。\r\n\r\nWe decided to defer to the doctor’s advice.\r\n我们决定听从医生的建议。\r\n\r\nOn technical issues, I usually defer to the engineers.\r\n在技术问题上，我通常听工程师的意见。\r\n\r\nThe committee deferred to the legal team’s judgment.\r\n委员会采纳了法律团队的判断。\r\n\r\nShe tends to defer to more experienced colleagues.\r\n她往往会听从更有经验的同事。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n你前面的句子里出现的是：\r\n\r\nnot be deferred to a later phase\r\n\r\n这里其实不是短语 defer to = 听从。\r\n\r\n这里的结构是：\r\n\r\ndefer sth to a later phase\r\n= 把某事推迟到后面的阶段\r\n\r\n也就是说：\r\n\r\ndefer to sb\r\n= 听从某人\r\n\r\ndefer sth to a later time / phase\r\n= 把某事推迟到以后\r\n\r\n原句：\r\n\r\nStronger protections should commence alongside this legislation, not be deferred to a later phase.\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n更有力的保护措施应该与这项立法同步开始实施，而不应该被推迟到后续阶段。\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nbe deferred to a later phase\r\n= 被推迟到后面的阶段\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\ndefer to vs listen to\r\n\r\nlisten to\r\n只是“听某人的话 / 听取意见”，比较口语。\r\n\r\nYou should listen to your doctor.\r\n你应该听医生的话。\r\n\r\ndefer to\r\n更正式，而且带有“尊重对方权威或专业判断”的感觉。\r\n\r\nI defer to your expertise.\r\n我尊重并听从你的专业判断。\r\n\r\ndefer to vs follow\r\n\r\nfollow someone’s advice\r\n= 按照某人的建议做\r\n\r\ndefer to someone\r\n= 把判断权更多地交给对方\r\n\r\ndefer vs delay / postpone\r\n\r\ndefer\r\n= 推迟，比较正式\r\n\r\nThe decision was deferred until next week.\r\n这个决定被推迟到下周。\r\n\r\ndelay\r\n= 延迟，范围最广\r\n\r\nThe flight was delayed.\r\n航班延误了。\r\n\r\npostpone\r\n= 延期，常用于会议、活动、计划\r\n\r\nThe meeting was postponed.\r\n会议被延期了。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\ndefer to sb 和 defer sth to... 不是一个意思\r\n\r\ndefer to the expert\r\n= 听从专家\r\n\r\ndefer the decision to next week\r\n= 把决定推迟到下周\r\n\r\ndefer to 后面常接人、权威、判断、意见\r\n\r\n✅ defer to the manager\r\n\r\n✅ defer to expert judgment\r\n\r\n不要把 defer to 直接理解成“推迟到”\r\n\r\n只有当结构是：\r\n\r\ndefer sth to a later time\r\n\r\n才表示“把某事推迟到……”\r\n\r\n发音\r\n\r\ndefer /dɪˈfɜː/\r\n\r\n前面弱读：\r\n\r\ndi-FER\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n可以记成两个完全不同的模式：\r\n\r\ndefer to + 人\r\n→ “让给他来判断”\r\n→ 听从、尊重\r\n\r\ndefer sth to + 时间\r\n→ “把事情往后放”\r\n→ 推迟\r\n\r\n最值得记的两个句子：\r\n\r\nI’ll defer to your judgment.\r\n我会听从你的判断。\r\n\r\nThe decision was deferred to a later date.\r\n这个决定被推迟到了之后的日期。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/454d2c96f8dd48a0b829372de0b0b673.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-27 22:19:41',1,'2026-08-27 22:19:41'),(1523,21,10,'vocab','substitute','substitute','substitute','🎯 核心意思\r\nsubstitute = 替代品；代替者；用……代替……\r\n\r\n核心感觉就是：\r\n\r\nA 不用了 → 换成 B','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n名词：替代品；代用品\r\n\r\nThere is no substitute for experience.\r\n经验是无可替代的。\r\n\r\nSugar substitutes are widely used.\r\n代糖被广泛使用。\r\n\r\n名词：替补人员\r\n\r\nThe coach brought on a substitute.\r\n教练换上了一名替补队员。\r\n\r\n动词：用某物代替另一物\r\n\r\nYou can substitute olive oil for butter.\r\n你可以用橄榄油代替黄油。\r\n\r\nsubstitute A for B\r\n\r\n= 用 A 代替 B\r\n\r\n这里一定要注意顺序：\r\n\r\nsubstitute A for B\r\n= 用 A 替换 B\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe substituted water for milk.\r\n我们用水代替了牛奶。\r\n\r\nbe a substitute for\r\n\r\n= 是……的替代品\r\n\r\nThis app is not a substitute for professional advice.\r\n这个应用不能替代专业建议。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nNothing can substitute for real experience.\r\n没有什么能替代真实经验。\r\n\r\nWe need to find a substitute for this material.\r\n我们需要为这种材料找一个替代品。\r\n\r\nYou can substitute honey for sugar.\r\n你可以用蜂蜜代替糖。\r\n\r\nThe injured player was replaced by a substitute.\r\n受伤的球员被替补队员换下了。\r\n\r\nTechnology can support teachers, but it cannot substitute for them completely.\r\n技术可以帮助教师，但不能完全取代教师。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n你之前那段原句里有：\r\n\r\nAn age restriction isn\'t a substitute for making the platforms themselves safer.\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\na substitute for\r\n= ……的替代品 / 能代替……\r\n\r\n整句意思：\r\n\r\n年龄限制不能代替让平台本身变得更安全这件事。\r\n\r\n也就是说：\r\n\r\n不能因为设置了年龄限制，就不去改善平台本身的安全性。\r\n\r\n这里非常值得记：\r\n\r\nbe a substitute for sth\r\n= 可以替代某事物\r\n\r\nnot be a substitute for sth\r\n= 不能代替某事物\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nsubstitute vs replace\r\n\r\nreplace\r\n更常用，强调“把原来的换掉”。\r\n\r\nWe replaced the old system with a new one.\r\n我们用新系统替换了旧系统。\r\n\r\nsubstitute\r\n更强调“找一个东西来代替另一个东西”。\r\n\r\nWe substituted a cheaper material for the original one.\r\n我们用更便宜的材料代替了原材料。\r\n\r\nsubstitute vs alternative\r\n\r\nsubstitute\r\n= 替代品，重点是“顶替原来的东西”\r\n\r\nalternative\r\n= 另一种选择，不一定完全替代原来的东西\r\n\r\nThis medicine has a cheaper substitute.\r\n这种药有更便宜的替代品。\r\n\r\nWe need an alternative approach.\r\n我们需要另一种方法。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nsubstitute A for B 的顺序很容易搞反\r\n\r\n✅ substitute A for B\r\n= 用 A 代替 B\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nsubstitute tea for coffee\r\n= 用茶代替咖啡\r\n\r\nreplace 的结构不一样\r\n\r\nsubstitute A for B\r\n\r\n但：\r\n\r\nreplace B with A\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe substituted tea for coffee.\r\n= We replaced coffee with tea.\r\n\r\n名词常用结构\r\n\r\na substitute for sth\r\n= ……的替代品\r\n\r\nThere is no substitute for practice.\r\n练习是无可替代的。\r\n\r\n英音发音注意\r\n\r\nsubstitute：\r\n\r\n/ˈsʌb.stɪ.tjuːt/\r\n\r\n前面重读：\r\n\r\nSUB-sti-tute\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 substitute 想成：\r\n\r\nsub = 在下面 / 代替位置\r\nstitute = 放置\r\n\r\n所以就是：\r\n\r\n把另一个东西“放到原来的位置上”\r\n\r\n→ 替代\r\n→ 替代品\r\n\r\n重点记两个结构：\r\n\r\nsubstitute A for B\r\n= 用 A 代替 B\r\n\r\na substitute for B\r\n= B 的替代品\r\n\r\n你原句里的：\r\n\r\nisn\'t a substitute for making the platforms safer\r\n= 不能替代让平台变得更安全这件事。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/7de781b1fecc47bba6cd06393629e1eb.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-27 22:26:54',1,'2026-08-27 22:26:54'),(1524,21,11,'phrase','full backing','full backing','full backing','🎯 核心意思\r\nfull backing = 全力支持；完全支持；充分支持\r\n\r\n这里的 backing = support，表示“支持、援助”。\r\n\r\n所以 full backing 可以理解为：\r\n\r\n100% support\r\n= 全力支持','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\ngive sb/sth your full backing\r\n= 全力支持某人 / 某事\r\n\r\nThe board gave the proposal its full backing.\r\n董事会全力支持这项提案。\r\n\r\nhave the full backing of sb\r\n= 得到某人的全力支持\r\n\r\nThe plan has the full backing of the government.\r\n这项计划得到了政府的全力支持。\r\n\r\nreceive full backing\r\n= 获得全面支持\r\n\r\nThe project received full backing from senior management.\r\n这个项目得到了高层管理人员的全力支持。\r\n\r\nwith the full backing of sb\r\n= 在某人的全力支持下\r\n\r\nShe made the decision with the full backing of her team.\r\n她在团队的全力支持下作出了这个决定。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nYou have my full backing.\r\n我全力支持你。\r\n\r\nThe proposal has the full backing of the board.\r\n这项提案得到了董事会的全力支持。\r\n\r\nThe new policy received full backing from the committee.\r\n这项新政策得到了委员会的全面支持。\r\n\r\nHe took the decision with the full backing of his colleagues.\r\n他在同事们的全力支持下作出了这个决定。\r\n\r\nThe project cannot succeed without strong financial backing.\r\n没有强有力的资金支持，这个项目无法成功。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n如果原文里出现：\r\n\r\nfull backing\r\n\r\n通常就是：\r\n\r\nfull support\r\n= 全力支持\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe proposal received the full backing of the government.\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n这项提案得到了政府的全力支持。\r\n\r\n这里 backing 不是“背景”或“后面”，而是：\r\n\r\nsupport from people, organisations, money, or authority\r\n来自个人、组织、资金或权力层面的支持\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nfull backing vs full support\r\n\r\nfull backing\r\n= 全力支持\r\n稍微更正式，常见于：\r\n\r\n政治\r\n商业\r\n组织决策\r\n新闻\r\n\r\nfull support\r\n= 全力支持\r\n更通用，口语里也更常见。\r\n\r\nYou have my full support.\r\n我完全支持你。\r\n\r\nYou have my full backing.\r\n我全力支持你。\r\n\r\n两句意思非常接近。\r\n\r\nfull backing vs financial backing\r\n\r\nfull backing\r\n= 全面支持，不一定只指钱\r\n\r\nfinancial backing\r\n= 资金支持\r\n\r\nThe company needs financial backing.\r\n这家公司需要资金支持。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nbacking 表示“支持”时通常是不可数名词\r\n\r\n✅ full backing\r\n\r\n✅ financial backing\r\n\r\n一般不说：\r\n\r\n❌ a full backing\r\n\r\n常见搭配要整体记\r\n\r\ngive full backing\r\n给予全力支持\r\n\r\nreceive full backing\r\n获得全力支持\r\n\r\nhave the full backing of sb\r\n得到某人的全力支持\r\n\r\nbacking 不等于 background\r\n\r\nbacking\r\n= 支持\r\n\r\nbackground\r\n= 背景\r\n\r\n这两个不要混。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 backing 想成：\r\n\r\nsomeone is standing at your back\r\n有人站在你背后支持你\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nbacking\r\n→ 背后支持\r\n→ 支持\r\n\r\nfull backing\r\n→ 所有人都站在你背后\r\n→ 全力支持\r\n\r\n最好记这一句：\r\n\r\nYou have my full backing.\r\n我全力支持你。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/5edddbef73234a9a820cac0946d54349.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-27 22:30:41',1,'2026-08-27 22:30:41'),(1525,21,12,'vocab','shrinkage','shrinkage','shrinkage','🎯 核心意思\r\nshrinkage = 收缩；缩小；减少；缩水\r\n\r\n它来自：\r\n\r\nshrink = 缩小；收缩；缩水\r\n\r\n所以 shrinkage 就是“发生缩小、减少的现象或程度”。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n衣物、材料的“缩水”\r\n\r\nFabric shrinkage can occur after washing.\r\n布料清洗后可能会缩水。\r\n\r\nThis material has very little shrinkage.\r\n这种材料几乎不缩水。\r\n\r\n尺寸、体积的“收缩”\r\n\r\nThe concrete showed some shrinkage as it dried.\r\n混凝土干燥时出现了一些收缩。\r\n\r\n数量、规模的“减少”\r\n\r\nThe industry has experienced significant shrinkage.\r\n这个行业经历了明显的萎缩。\r\n\r\n商业 / 零售中的“库存损耗”\r\n\r\n在零售行业，shrinkage 还有一个很常见的专业意思：\r\n\r\ninventory shrinkage\r\n= 库存损耗 / 账实不符导致的库存减少\r\n\r\n原因可能包括：\r\n\r\ntheft 盗窃\r\ndamage 损坏\r\nadministrative errors 管理错误\r\nfraud 欺诈\r\n\r\nThe store is trying to reduce inventory shrinkage.\r\n这家商店正在努力降低库存损耗。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThe shirt suffered some shrinkage after washing.\r\n这件衬衫洗过之后有些缩水。\r\n\r\nWe need to allow for shrinkage when cutting the fabric.\r\n裁剪布料时我们需要考虑缩水。\r\n\r\nThe company is facing a shrinkage in demand.\r\n这家公司正面临需求萎缩。\r\n\r\nThe economy experienced a period of shrinkage.\r\n经济经历了一段收缩期。\r\n\r\nRetailers lose millions every year because of inventory shrinkage.\r\n零售商每年都会因为库存损耗损失数百万。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n如果你是在商业或者经济文章里看到：\r\n\r\nshrinkage in demand\r\n\r\n意思通常是：\r\n\r\n需求减少\r\n需求萎缩\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThere has been a noticeable shrinkage in consumer demand.\r\n\r\n= 消费者需求出现了明显下降。\r\n\r\n如果是在衣服或材料语境里：\r\n\r\nshrinkage\r\n\r\n通常就是：\r\n\r\n缩水 / 收缩率\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThis fabric has a shrinkage rate of 3%.\r\n\r\n= 这种布料的缩水率是 3%。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nshrinkage vs decrease\r\n\r\ndecrease\r\n= 减少、下降\r\n最通用。\r\n\r\nThere was a decrease in sales.\r\n销售额下降了。\r\n\r\nshrinkage\r\n= 缩小、萎缩\r\n更强调“整体规模变小”。\r\n\r\nThere has been shrinkage in the market.\r\n市场规模出现了萎缩。\r\n\r\nshrinkage vs contraction\r\n\r\ncontraction\r\n= 收缩\r\n\r\n在经济、医学、肌肉等语境里很常见。\r\n\r\neconomic contraction\r\n= 经济收缩\r\n\r\nshrinkage\r\n更强调实际尺寸、规模或数量变小。\r\n\r\nshrinkage vs reduction\r\n\r\nreduction\r\n= 减少、削减\r\n\r\n通常强调“减少这个动作或结果”。\r\n\r\ncost reduction\r\n= 成本削减\r\n\r\nshrinkage\r\n往往强调自然发生的“缩小、萎缩”。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nshrinkage 是名词\r\n\r\nshrink\r\n= 动词\r\n\r\nThe shirt shrank.\r\n衬衫缩水了。\r\n\r\nshrinkage\r\n= 名词\r\n\r\nThere was some shrinkage.\r\n出现了一些缩水。\r\n\r\nshrink 的过去式是 shrank\r\n\r\n现在时：\r\n\r\nshrink\r\n\r\n过去式：\r\n\r\nshrank\r\n\r\n过去分词：\r\n\r\nshrunk\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nMy sweater has shrunk.\r\n我的毛衣缩水了。\r\n\r\n不要把 shrinkage 只理解成“衣服缩水”\r\n\r\n它还可以表示：\r\n\r\n市场萎缩\r\n人口减少\r\n体积收缩\r\n库存损耗\r\n\r\n发音注意\r\n\r\nshrinkage：\r\n\r\n/ˈʃrɪŋ.kɪdʒ/\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\nshrink-age /eɪdʒ/\r\n\r\n最后的 -age 在这里读：\r\n\r\n/ɪdʒ/\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n先记：\r\n\r\nshrink = 变小\r\n\r\n再加：\r\n\r\n-age = 名词后缀\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nshrink + age\r\n→ shrinkage\r\n→ 变小这件事\r\n→ 收缩 / 缩水 / 萎缩\r\n\r\n最实用的三个搭配可以一起记：\r\n\r\nfabric shrinkage\r\n= 布料缩水\r\n\r\nmarket shrinkage\r\n= 市场萎缩\r\n\r\ninventory shrinkage\r\n= 库存损耗','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8da0343b5b5d40f1b44eb1344544675d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-28 14:44:57',1,'2026-08-28 14:44:57'),(1526,21,13,'vocab','discrepancy','discrepancy','discrepancy','🎯 核心意思\r\ndiscrepancy = 差异；不一致；出入；不符\r\n\r\n它通常表示：\r\n\r\n两个本来应该一致的东西，实际上却对不上。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\n数据不一致\r\n金额对不上\r\n记录有出入\r\n报告和实际情况不符','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n数据 / 数字之间的差异\r\n\r\nThere is a discrepancy between the two figures.\r\n这两个数字之间存在差异。\r\n\r\n记录和实际情况不一致\r\n\r\nWe found a discrepancy in the records.\r\n我们发现记录中有一处不一致。\r\n\r\n金额、账目有出入\r\n\r\nThere was a discrepancy in the final amount.\r\n最终金额存在出入。\r\n\r\n两种说法不一致\r\n\r\nThere are discrepancies between the two reports.\r\n这两份报告之间存在不一致之处。\r\n\r\n常见结构\r\n\r\na discrepancy between A and B\r\n= A 和 B 之间的不一致\r\n\r\na discrepancy in sth\r\n= 某处存在出入\r\n\r\nidentify / find / detect a discrepancy\r\n= 发现不一致\r\n\r\nresolve a discrepancy\r\n= 解决不一致问题','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThere is a discrepancy between the database and the report.\r\n数据库和报表之间存在不一致。\r\n\r\nWe need to investigate this discrepancy.\r\n我们需要调查这个差异。\r\n\r\nThe system detected a discrepancy in the transaction amount.\r\n系统检测到交易金额存在不一致。\r\n\r\nThe auditor found several discrepancies in the financial records.\r\n审计人员在财务记录中发现了几处出入。\r\n\r\nPlease check whether there are any discrepancies between the two files.\r\n请检查这两个文件之间是否存在任何不一致。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n在软件、银行、数据处理系统里，discrepancy 非常常见。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe system should flag any discrepancy between the OCR result and the database record.\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n系统应该标记 OCR 识别结果与数据库记录之间的任何不一致。\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\ndiscrepancy between A and B\r\n= A 和 B 对不上\r\n\r\n非常适合描述：\r\n\r\nOCR 数据 vs 数据库数据\r\n报表 vs 原始数据\r\n订单金额 vs 实际付款金额\r\n库存记录 vs 实际库存\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\ndiscrepancy vs difference\r\n\r\ndifference\r\n= 差别、不同\r\n最普通、最宽泛。\r\n\r\nThere is a difference between the two systems.\r\n这两个系统存在差异。\r\n\r\ndiscrepancy\r\n= 本来应该一致，但实际上有出入\r\n\r\nThere is a discrepancy between the invoice and the payment record.\r\n发票和付款记录对不上。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ndifference = 只是不同\r\ndiscrepancy = 不该不同却不同了\r\n\r\ndiscrepancy vs inconsistency\r\n\r\ninconsistency\r\n= 不一致、不连贯\r\n\r\n更强调：\r\n\r\n前后逻辑不一致\r\n标准不一致\r\n行为不一致\r\n\r\ndiscrepancy\r\n更常用于：\r\n\r\n数字\r\n数据\r\n记录\r\n金额\r\n报表\r\n\r\ndiscrepancy vs mismatch\r\n\r\nmismatch\r\n= 不匹配\r\n\r\n更口语、技术感也比较强。\r\n\r\nThere is a mismatch between the expected value and the actual value.\r\n预期值和实际值不匹配。\r\n\r\ndiscrepancy\r\n更正式，尤其常见于：\r\n\r\nfinancial records\r\nreports\r\naudits\r\ndata validation\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n常见介词是 between\r\n\r\n✅ a discrepancy between A and B\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\na discrepancy between the report and the database\r\n\r\ndiscrepancy 通常表示“不应该存在的差异”\r\n\r\n所以它不等于普通的 difference。\r\n\r\n复数拼写注意\r\n\r\ndiscrepancy\r\n→ discrepancies\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n❌ discrepancys\r\n\r\n发音注意\r\n\r\n/dɪˈskrep.ən.si/\r\n\r\n重点在：\r\n\r\nCREP\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\nDIS-cre-pan-cy\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\ndis-CREP-an-cy\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n可以把 discrepancy 想成：\r\n\r\n两个数字放在一起核对：\r\n\r\nSystem: 100\r\nActual: 92\r\n\r\n中间差了 8。\r\n\r\n这个“对不上”的地方就是：\r\n\r\ndiscrepancy\r\n\r\n所以可以记：\r\n\r\ndiscrepancy = something doesn’t match\r\n= 有东西对不上\r\n\r\n最实用的一句：\r\n\r\nThere is a discrepancy between the two records.\r\n这两条记录之间存在不一致。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/bc8d42fb75664f7aa66092ae75cb6375.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-28 14:49:35',1,'2026-08-28 14:49:35'),(1527,21,14,'phrase','not a great deal of change','not a great deal of change','not a great deal of change','🎯 核心意思\r\nnot a great deal of change = 没有太大变化；变化不多\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\na great deal of = 大量的；很多的\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of change\r\n= not much change\r\n= 没有多少变化\r\n\r\n这个表达比 not much change 稍微更正式、更自然一些，尤其常见于采访、报告和口语说明。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n表示整体变化不大\r\n\r\nThere has not been a great deal of change.\r\n没有发生太大的变化。\r\n\r\n表示某段时间内变化有限\r\n\r\nThere hasn\'t been a great deal of change over the past year.\r\n过去一年没有太大变化。\r\n\r\n表示系统、政策、情况基本稳定\r\n\r\nWe haven\'t seen a great deal of change in the system.\r\n我们没有看到这个系统发生太大变化。\r\n\r\n常见结构\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of + 不可数名词\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of change\r\n变化不多\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of progress\r\n进展不大\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of difference\r\n差别不大\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of time\r\n时间不多','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThere hasn\'t been a great deal of change since last year.\r\n从去年以来没有太大变化。\r\n\r\nWe haven\'t seen a great deal of change in customer behaviour.\r\n我们没有看到客户行为发生太大变化。\r\n\r\nThere was not a great deal of difference between the two results.\r\n这两个结果之间没有太大差异。\r\n\r\nWe don\'t have a great deal of time left.\r\n我们剩下的时间不多了。\r\n\r\nThe new policy has not led to a great deal of change.\r\n这项新政策并没有带来太大的变化。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of change\r\n\r\n可以直接拆成：\r\n\r\nnot\r\n= 不\r\n\r\na great deal of\r\n= 大量的\r\n\r\nchange\r\n= 变化\r\n\r\n所以整句：\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of change\r\n= 没有大量变化\r\n= 没有太大变化\r\n\r\n实际口语里最自然的中文通常翻成：\r\n\r\n“变化不大。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of change vs not much change\r\n\r\nnot much change\r\n= 没有太大变化\r\n\r\n更简单、更口语。\r\n\r\nThere hasn\'t been much change.\r\n没什么变化。\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of change\r\n意思一样，但稍微更完整、更正式一点。\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of change vs little change\r\n\r\nlittle change\r\n= 几乎没什么变化\r\n\r\n语气往往比 not a great deal of change 更强一些。\r\n\r\nThere has been little change.\r\n几乎没有变化。\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of change\r\n= 有一些变化，但不多。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\na great deal of 后面通常接不可数名词\r\n\r\n✅ a great deal of change\r\n\r\n✅ a great deal of time\r\n\r\n✅ a great deal of work\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ a great deal of changes\r\n\r\n如果是可数名词复数，一般用：\r\n\r\na large number of changes\r\n很多变化\r\n\r\n这里的 deal 不是“交易”\r\n\r\na great deal of\r\n是固定表达：\r\n\r\n= a lot of\r\n= 很多\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of 不等于完全没有\r\n\r\n它只是表示：\r\n\r\n有一点，但不多。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n先记固定表达：\r\n\r\na great deal of = 很多\r\n\r\n然后前面加 not：\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of\r\n= 不很多\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of change\r\n= 变化不多\r\n\r\n最实用的一句：\r\n\r\nThere hasn\'t been a great deal of change.\r\n没有发生太大的变化。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/6d870e5748c140d094ec7ce7b9c2d926.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-28 15:49:18',1,'2026-08-28 15:49:18'),(1528,21,15,'vocab','smuggle','smuggle','smuggle','🎯 核心意思\r\nsmuggle = 走私；偷运；偷偷带入 / 带出\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\nsecretly move something or someone\r\n= 偷偷地把某物或某人运过去\r\n\r\n通常带有：\r\n\r\n违法\r\n躲避检查\r\n偷偷进行\r\n\r\n这些含义。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n走私货物\r\n\r\nsmuggle goods\r\n= 走私货物\r\n\r\nThey were caught smuggling cigarettes across the border.\r\n他们因跨境走私香烟被抓。\r\n\r\n偷运违禁品\r\n\r\nsmuggle drugs / weapons\r\n= 走私毒品 / 武器\r\n\r\nThe police discovered a plan to smuggle drugs into the country.\r\n警方发现了一个向该国走私毒品的计划。\r\n\r\n偷偷把人带入 / 带出某地\r\n\r\nsmuggle sb into / out of somewhere\r\n= 偷偷把某人带入 / 带出某地\r\n\r\nThey tried to smuggle people across the border.\r\n他们试图偷偷把人带过边境。\r\n\r\n日常语境：偷偷带东西进去\r\n\r\n这个用法不一定特别严重，也可以带一点幽默感：\r\n\r\nShe smuggled some snacks into the cinema.\r\n她偷偷把一些零食带进了电影院。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nHe was arrested for trying to smuggle drugs into the country.\r\n他因试图向该国走私毒品而被捕。\r\n\r\nThey smuggled the goods across the border at night.\r\n他们在夜间偷偷把货物运过了边境。\r\n\r\nSomeone tried to smuggle a phone into the prison.\r\n有人试图偷偷把手机带进监狱。\r\n\r\nShe smuggled a bottle of water into the concert.\r\n她偷偷把一瓶水带进了演唱会。\r\n\r\nThe documents were smuggled out of the country.\r\n这些文件被秘密带出了这个国家。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\nsmuggle sth into + 地方\r\n= 偷偷把某物带进……\r\n\r\nsmuggle sth out of + 地方\r\n= 偷偷把某物带出……\r\n\r\nsmuggle sth across + 边界\r\n= 偷运某物穿过……\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThey smuggled the goods across the border.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nsmuggled\r\n= 偷运\r\n\r\nthe goods\r\n= 货物\r\n\r\nacross the border\r\n= 穿过边境\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n他们把这些货物走私过了边境。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nsmuggle vs sneak\r\n\r\nsneak\r\n= 偷偷地做 / 溜进去\r\n\r\nHe sneaked into the room.\r\n他偷偷溜进了房间。\r\n\r\nsmuggle\r\n= 偷偷运送某物或某人\r\n\r\nHe smuggled a phone into the room.\r\n他偷偷把一部手机带进了房间。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nsneak = 自己偷偷行动\r\nsmuggle = 偷偷把东西 / 人带过去\r\n\r\nsmuggle vs traffic\r\n\r\ntraffic\r\n作动词时也可以表示“非法贩运”。\r\n\r\ndrug trafficking\r\n= 毒品贩运\r\n\r\nhuman trafficking\r\n= 人口贩运\r\n\r\ntraffic 更强调：\r\n\r\n非法交易、贩卖的整个活动\r\n\r\nsmuggle 更强调：\r\n\r\n偷偷运输、跨境运送\r\n\r\nsmuggle vs import\r\n\r\nimport\r\n= 进口\r\n\r\n是正常、合法的贸易行为。\r\n\r\nsmuggle\r\n= 走私\r\n\r\n通常意味着违法和逃避检查。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n常见介词搭配\r\n\r\n✅ smuggle sth into a country\r\n\r\n✅ smuggle sth out of a country\r\n\r\n✅ smuggle sth across the border\r\n\r\nsmuggle 后面可以直接接人或物\r\n\r\nsmuggle goods\r\n走私货物\r\n\r\nsmuggle people\r\n偷运人员\r\n\r\n名词形式是：\r\n\r\nsmuggling\r\n= 走私行为\r\n\r\ndrug smuggling\r\n毒品走私\r\n\r\nsmuggler\r\n= 走私者\r\n\r\n发音注意\r\n\r\nsmuggle：\r\n\r\n/ˈsmʌɡ.əl/\r\n\r\n中间是：\r\n\r\n/ʌɡ/\r\n\r\n不是 /uː/。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n可以想象：\r\n\r\n一个人偷偷把东西藏在包里，躲过海关检查。\r\n\r\n这个动作就是：\r\n\r\nsmuggle\r\n= 偷偷运输\r\n→ 走私 / 偷运\r\n\r\n可以一起记三个词：\r\n\r\nsmuggle\r\n= 走私、偷运\r\n\r\nsmuggling\r\n= 走私行为\r\n\r\nsmuggler\r\n= 走私者\r\n\r\n最好记一句：\r\n\r\nThey smuggled the goods across the border.\r\n他们偷偷把货物运过了边境。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2ac0912cdf0b4c4c8d637e6e93327416.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-28 18:28:44',1,'2026-08-28 18:28:44'),(1529,21,16,'phrase','surge back','surge back','surge back','🎯 核心意思\r\nsurge back = 猛地涌回；迅速回升；强势反弹；突然重新出现\r\n\r\n核心画面：\r\n\r\nsurge = 猛增、猛冲、涌动\r\nback = 回来\r\n\r\n所以 surge back 就是：\r\n\r\n“猛地回来 / 强势回升”。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n水、液体猛地涌回\r\n\r\nThe water surged back into the street.\r\n水猛地涌回街道。\r\n\r\n人群大量涌回\r\n\r\nThe crowd surged back towards the entrance.\r\n人群又猛地涌向入口。\r\n\r\n需求、销量、市场迅速回升\r\n\r\nDemand surged back after the restrictions were lifted.\r\n限制解除后，需求迅速回升。\r\n\r\n情绪、记忆突然涌现\r\n\r\nThe memories surged back.\r\n那些回忆突然涌了回来。\r\n\r\n活力、信心等重新增强\r\n\r\nConfidence surged back after the announcement.\r\n公告发布后，信心迅速恢复。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nConsumer demand surged back in the second half of the year.\r\n消费者需求在下半年迅速反弹。\r\n\r\nTourists surged back into the city after the borders reopened.\r\n边境重新开放后，游客大量涌回这座城市。\r\n\r\nThe crowd surged back towards the gate.\r\n人群猛地重新涌向大门。\r\n\r\nSuddenly, all the memories surged back.\r\n突然间，所有回忆都涌了回来。\r\n\r\nSales surged back after a weak start to the year.\r\n经历年初的疲软后，销售额强劲反弹。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nDemand surged back.\r\n\r\n可以拆成：\r\n\r\ndemand\r\n= 需求\r\n\r\nsurged\r\n= 猛增、急剧上升\r\n\r\nback\r\n= 回到之前的状态\r\n\r\n所以整句最自然的中文是：\r\n\r\n需求迅速回升了。\r\n需求强劲反弹了。\r\n\r\n这里不要机械翻译成：\r\n\r\n“需求涌回来了。”\r\n\r\n因为在经济、市场语境里：\r\n\r\nsurge back\r\n更自然地译成“迅速回升 / 强势反弹”。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nsurge back vs come back\r\n\r\ncome back\r\n= 回来\r\n\r\n比较普通、中性。\r\n\r\nCustomers came back.\r\n顾客回来了。\r\n\r\nsurge back\r\n= 大量、快速、强势地回来\r\n\r\nCustomers surged back.\r\n顾客大量涌回。\r\n\r\nsurge back vs bounce back\r\n\r\nbounce back\r\n= 恢复；反弹\r\n\r\n强调从低谷、困难或下降中恢复。\r\n\r\nSales bounced back after a weak quarter.\r\n销售额在一个疲软季度后恢复了。\r\n\r\nsurge back\r\n更强调：\r\n\r\n速度快\r\n幅度大\r\n力量强\r\n\r\nSales surged back.\r\n销售额强劲反弹。\r\n\r\nsurge back vs return\r\n\r\nreturn\r\n= 返回；恢复\r\n\r\n更中性、更正式。\r\n\r\nDemand returned to normal.\r\n需求恢复正常。\r\n\r\nDemand surged back.\r\n需求迅速反弹。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nsurge back 不是一个特别固定的短语动词\r\n\r\n它更像：\r\n\r\nsurge + back\r\n\r\n其中 back 表示：\r\n\r\n回来\r\n回到之前的状态\r\n\r\nsurge 自带“快速、大量、猛烈”的感觉\r\n\r\n所以 surge back 不只是：\r\n\r\n回来\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\n猛地回来\r\n快速回升\r\n强势反弹\r\n\r\n过去式\r\n\r\nsurge → surged\r\n\r\n✅ Demand surged back.\r\n需求迅速反弹。\r\n\r\n常见相关搭配\r\n\r\nsurge forward\r\n向前猛冲\r\n\r\nsurge into\r\n涌入\r\n\r\nsurge through\r\n涌过；冲过\r\n\r\nsurge in demand\r\n需求激增\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 surge 想成一股大浪：\r\n\r\n🌊 surge = 猛地冲过来\r\n\r\n再加：\r\n\r\nback = 回来\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\n🌊 ← surge back\r\n\r\n= 大浪猛地冲回来\r\n→ 猛地涌回\r\n→ 迅速回升\r\n→ 强势反弹\r\n\r\n最好记两个例子：\r\n\r\nDemand surged back.\r\n需求强劲反弹。\r\n\r\nThe memories surged back.\r\n回忆一下子涌了回来。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/fb40c881e9a947b99e06b8268d044bff.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-28 18:41:49',1,'2026-08-28 18:41:49'),(1530,21,17,'phrase','refer to','refer to','refer to','🎯 核心意思\r\nrefer to = 提到；谈及；指的是；查阅；把……转交给\r\n\r\n这是一个非常常用的短语，核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n“把注意力、话题或事情指向某个人 / 某件事。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n提到；谈及\r\n\r\nHe referred to the problem in the meeting.\r\n他在会议中提到了这个问题。\r\n\r\nThe report refers to several recent cases.\r\n这份报告提到了几个近期案例。\r\n\r\n指的是\r\n\r\nWhat does “it” refer to here?\r\n这里的 it 指的是什么？\r\n\r\nThe word “platform” refers to social media companies in this context.\r\n在这个语境里，platform 指的是社交媒体公司。\r\n\r\n查阅；参考\r\n\r\nPlease refer to the user manual for more information.\r\n更多信息请查阅用户手册。\r\n\r\nRefer to the table below.\r\n请参阅下表。\r\n\r\n这个用法在：\r\n\r\n说明书\r\n技术文档\r\n报告\r\n论文\r\n\r\n里面特别常见。\r\n\r\n把某人转介给某人 / 某机构\r\n\r\nThe doctor referred him to a specialist.\r\n医生把他转诊给了一位专科医生。\r\n\r\nThe case was referred to the police.\r\n这个案件被移交给警方处理。\r\n\r\nrefer to A as B\r\n\r\n= 把 A 称为 B\r\n\r\nPeople often refer to New Zealand as Aotearoa.\r\n人们经常把新西兰称为 Aotearoa。\r\n\r\n被动形式：\r\n\r\nA is referred to as B\r\n= A 被称为 B','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nShe referred to the issue several times.\r\n她多次提到了这个问题。\r\n\r\nWhat does this term refer to?\r\n这个术语指的是什么？\r\n\r\nPlease refer to page 10 for more details.\r\n更多细节请参阅第 10 页。\r\n\r\nThe doctor referred me to a specialist.\r\n医生把我转诊给了一位专科医生。\r\n\r\nThis process is referred to as data validation.\r\n这个过程被称为数据验证。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n最值得记的两个结构是：\r\n\r\nrefer to sth\r\n= 提到某事 / 指的是某事 / 查阅某物\r\n\r\nrefer to A as B\r\n= 把 A 称为 B\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe report refers to behavioural profiling.\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nrefers to\r\n= 提到了\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这份报告提到了行为画像。\r\n\r\n再比如：\r\n\r\nThis practice is referred to as behavioural profiling.\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nis referred to as\r\n= 被称为\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这种做法被称为行为画像。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nrefer to vs mention\r\n\r\nmention\r\n= 提到\r\n\r\n更简单、更口语。\r\n\r\nHe mentioned the problem.\r\n他提到了这个问题。\r\n\r\nrefer to\r\n也表示“提到”，但稍微更正式。\r\n\r\nHe referred to the problem in his report.\r\n他在报告中提到了这个问题。\r\n\r\nrefer to vs mean\r\n\r\nrefer to\r\n= 指的是\r\n\r\nWhat does this word refer to?\r\n这个词指什么？\r\n\r\nmean\r\n= 意思是\r\n\r\nWhat does this word mean?\r\n这个词是什么意思？\r\n\r\n区别：\r\n\r\nrefer to = 它指向什么对象\r\nmean = 它是什么意思\r\n\r\nrefer to vs relate to\r\n\r\nrefer to\r\n= 提到；指的是\r\n\r\nrelate to\r\n= 与……有关\r\n\r\nThis term refers to online platforms.\r\n这个术语指的是网络平台。\r\n\r\nThis issue relates to online safety.\r\n这个问题与网络安全有关。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nrefer 的过去式要双写 r\r\n\r\nrefer\r\n→ referred\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n❌ refered\r\n\r\n“把 A 称为 B”结构是：\r\n\r\n✅ refer to A as B\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThey refer to this process as profiling.\r\n\r\n“被称为”是：\r\n\r\n✅ be referred to as\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThis is referred to as profiling.\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n❌ be referred as\r\n\r\nrefer to 不只是“提到”\r\n\r\n根据语境还可以是：\r\n\r\n提到\r\n指的是\r\n查阅\r\n转交 / 转诊\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 refer to 想象成：\r\n\r\n👉 指向某个东西\r\n\r\n指向一个话题\r\n→ 提到\r\n\r\n指向一个对象\r\n→ 指的是\r\n\r\n指向一份文件\r\n→ 查阅\r\n\r\n把一个人指向专家\r\n→ 转介 / 转诊\r\n\r\n最值得记的四句：\r\n\r\nRefer to the manual.\r\n请查阅说明书。\r\n\r\nWhat does it refer to?\r\n它指的是什么？\r\n\r\nHe referred to the issue.\r\n他提到了这个问题。\r\n\r\nThis is referred to as profiling.\r\n这被称为 profiling。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f42cc8dbf39a429f9342f3759bda6088.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-28 19:35:14',1,'2026-08-28 19:35:14'),(1531,21,18,'vocab','characterisation','characterisation','characterisation','🎯 核心意思\r\ncharacterisation = 描述；刻画；定性；对某人/某事的界定\r\n\r\n核心意思是：\r\n\r\nthe way someone or something is described or presented\r\n= 对某人或某事进行怎样的描述、刻画或定性\r\n\r\n在新闻、法律、政治语境里，经常可以理解为：\r\n\r\n“你把这件事说成什么性质”\r\n“你对这个人的描述方式”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n对某人的描述、刻画\r\n\r\nI disagree with that characterisation of him.\r\n我不同意你对他的这种描述。\r\n\r\n对事情性质的界定 / 定性\r\n\r\nThe minister rejected the characterisation of the policy as a failure.\r\n部长不接受把这项政策定性为失败的说法。\r\n\r\n文学、影视中的“人物塑造”\r\n\r\nThe novel is praised for its strong characterisation.\r\n这部小说因出色的人物塑造而受到赞扬。\r\n\r\n常见结构\r\n\r\ncharacterisation of sb/sth\r\n= 对某人 / 某事的描述、定性\r\n\r\ncharacterisation of A as B\r\n= 把 A 描述 / 定性为 B\r\n\r\naccept / reject / disagree with a characterisation\r\n= 接受 / 拒绝 / 不同意某种描述或定性','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nI don\'t agree with that characterisation of the situation.\r\n我不同意你对这种情况的描述。\r\n\r\nThe lawyer challenged the prosecution\'s characterisation of his client.\r\n律师对控方如何描述其当事人提出了质疑。\r\n\r\nShe rejected the characterisation of the decision as unfair.\r\n她不接受把这个决定说成不公平的这种定性。\r\n\r\nHis characterisation of the problem was too simplistic.\r\n他对这个问题的描述过于简单化。\r\n\r\nThe film is known for its realistic characterisation.\r\n这部电影以真实的人物塑造而闻名。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n你刚才新闻里的原句是：\r\n\r\n“I don’t know if I accept your characterisation of the offender as a ‘naive courier’.”\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nyour characterisation of the offender\r\n= 你对这名罪犯的描述 / 定性\r\n\r\nas a “naive courier”\r\n= 把他描述为“天真的运毒者 / 不谙世事的跑腿者”\r\n\r\n所以整句可以理解为：\r\n\r\n“我不确定我是否接受你把这名罪犯描述成一个‘天真的运毒者’。”\r\n\r\n这里 characterisation 特别适合翻成：\r\n\r\n“描述”\r\n或者更贴合法律语境：\r\n\r\n“定性”\r\n\r\n也就是法官觉得律师把这个人说得太“无辜、天真”了。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\ncharacterisation vs description\r\n\r\ndescription\r\n= 描述\r\n\r\n最普通、最中性。\r\n\r\nHe gave a description of the man.\r\n他描述了那名男子。\r\n\r\ncharacterisation\r\n= 对某人 / 某事的整体刻画或定性\r\n\r\n往往带有：\r\n\r\n“你把他描述成什么样的人”\r\n“你给这件事下了什么性质判断”\r\n\r\n所以新闻和法律语境里，characterisation 比 description 更有“定性”的感觉。\r\n\r\ncharacterisation vs portrayal\r\n\r\nportrayal\r\n= 描绘；塑造\r\n\r\n常用于：\r\n\r\n电影\r\n小说\r\n媒体\r\n\r\nThe film\'s portrayal of the character was realistic.\r\n电影对这个人物的塑造很真实。\r\n\r\ncharacterisation 更广，也常用于正式辩论、法律和分析语境。\r\n\r\ncharacterisation vs assessment\r\n\r\nassessment\r\n= 评估；判断\r\n\r\n强调分析后的评价。\r\n\r\ncharacterisation\r\n强调：\r\n\r\n“用什么方式来描述 / 定义它”。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n英式英语拼写是：\r\n\r\n✅ characterisation\r\n\r\n美式：\r\n\r\ncharacterization\r\n\r\n你学英式英语，所以建议记：\r\n\r\ncharacterisation\r\n\r\n不要只理解成“人物性格”\r\n\r\ncharacterisation 在文学里确实可以表示“人物塑造”，但在新闻、法律语境里更常表示：\r\n\r\n描述方式\r\n定性\r\n界定\r\n\r\n常见结构\r\n\r\n✅ characterisation of sb/sth\r\n\r\n✅ characterisation of A as B\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nthe characterisation of him as inexperienced\r\n= 把他描述成缺乏经验的人\r\n\r\n发音比较长，建议分块\r\n\r\ncharacter + i + sa + tion\r\n\r\n大致：\r\n\r\nKAR-ək-tə-ry-ZAY-shən\r\n\r\n重点落在：\r\n\r\nZAY\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n先记：\r\n\r\ncharacterise\r\n= 描述……的特征；把……刻画成\r\n\r\n再加：\r\n\r\n-ation\r\n= 名词后缀\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncharacterise\r\n→ characterisation\r\n\r\n= 描述 / 刻画 / 定性\r\n\r\n你这次新闻里最好直接记这一组：\r\n\r\nyour characterisation of the offender\r\n= 你对这名罪犯的描述 / 定性\r\n\r\nI don\'t accept your characterisation of him as naive.\r\n= 我不接受你把他描述成“天真”的这种说法。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d1d019fa5b8c4b1c8e41268794b632fa.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 11:35:52',1,'2026-08-29 11:35:52'),(1532,21,19,'phrase','potentially yes','potentially yes','potentially yes','🎯 核心意思\r\npotentially yes = 有可能是；有这个可能；理论上可以；可能可以\r\n\r\n它不是非常固定的短语，而是：\r\n\r\npotentially = 有可能地\r\nyes = 是的\r\n\r\n合起来就是一种比较谨慎的回答：\r\n\r\n“有可能，是的。”\r\n“理论上来说，可以。”\r\n“目前看，有这个可能。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n表示“可能是”\r\n\r\nA: Could this cause a problem?\r\n这会造成问题吗？\r\n\r\nB: Potentially, yes.\r\n有可能，会。\r\n\r\n表示“理论上可以”\r\n\r\nA: Can this system handle more users?\r\n这个系统能支持更多用户吗？\r\n\r\nB: Potentially, yes.\r\n理论上可以。\r\n\r\n表示“有条件地同意”\r\n\r\nA: Could we finish it by Friday?\r\n我们周五前能完成吗？\r\n\r\nB: Potentially, yes, if everything goes smoothly.\r\n有可能，如果一切顺利的话。\r\n\r\n表示自己不想把话说得太绝对\r\n\r\n相比直接说：\r\n\r\nYes.\r\n\r\npotentially, yes\r\n更谨慎，意思接近：\r\n\r\n“Yes, but I’m not completely certain.”','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nCould this approach work?\r\nPotentially, yes.\r\n这种方法可行吗？\r\n有可能，可行。\r\n\r\nCould the change affect performance?\r\nPotentially, yes.\r\n这个改动会影响性能吗？\r\n有可能会。\r\n\r\nCan we increase the number of workers?\r\nPotentially, yes, depending on the machine.\r\n我们可以增加 worker 的数量吗？\r\n有可能，取决于机器性能。\r\n\r\nCould this become a larger issue?\r\nPotentially, yes.\r\n这会不会演变成一个更大的问题？\r\n有这种可能。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n如果有人问：\r\n\r\nCould that happen?\r\n\r\n回答：\r\n\r\nPotentially, yes.\r\n\r\n并不是强烈确认：\r\n\r\n“Yes, definitely.”\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\n“有这种可能。”\r\n\r\n这里 potentially 起到“降低确定性”的作用。\r\n\r\n所以它的语气大概在：\r\n\r\nmaybe → potentially, yes → probably yes → definitely yes\r\n\r\n之间。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\npotentially yes vs maybe\r\n\r\nmaybe\r\n= 也许\r\n\r\n最简单、最口语。\r\n\r\nMaybe.\r\n也许吧。\r\n\r\npotentially, yes\r\n= 有这种可能，是的\r\n\r\n听起来更理性、更正式一点，尤其常见于：\r\n\r\n采访\r\n工作讨论\r\n技术讨论\r\n分析\r\n\r\npotentially yes vs possibly\r\n\r\nPossibly, yes.\r\n= 有可能。\r\n\r\n和 potentially, yes 很接近。\r\n\r\npotentially 更强调：\r\n\r\n“在某些条件下，有这种可能性”。\r\n\r\npotentially yes vs probably yes\r\n\r\nprobably yes\r\n= 很可能是\r\n\r\n确定性更高。\r\n\r\npotentially yes\r\n= 只是存在可能\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\npotentially yes < probably yes\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n更自然的写法通常带逗号\r\n\r\n✅ Potentially, yes.\r\n\r\n因为 potentially 是对整个回答的修饰。\r\n\r\n不等于“很可能”\r\n\r\npotentially\r\n只是：\r\n\r\n“有可能”\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n“很可能”\r\n\r\n口语里很常见于谨慎回答\r\n\r\n尤其当说话人不想给一个绝对承诺时：\r\n\r\nPotentially, yes.\r\n\r\n非常自然。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\npotential = 潜在的；可能的\r\n\r\npotentially = 有可能地\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nPotentially, yes.\r\n= 从可能性上来说，是的\r\n→ 有可能\r\n→ 理论上可以\r\n\r\n最好直接记这个对话：\r\n\r\nCan it work?\r\nPotentially, yes.\r\n\r\n它能行吗？\r\n有可能。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ec2f702766d747c8849022e39921271d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 12:09:05',1,'2026-08-29 12:09:05'),(1533,21,20,'phrase','land sb in','land sb in','land sb in','🎯 核心意思\r\nland sb in = 使某人陷入某种处境；让某人惹上麻烦；把某人弄到……境地\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n某件事把某人“送进”了一个不太好的局面。\r\n\r\n最常见的是：\r\n\r\nland sb in trouble\r\n= 让某人惹上麻烦','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nland sb in trouble\r\n= 使某人陷入麻烦\r\n\r\nThat mistake could land you in trouble.\r\n那个错误可能会让你惹上麻烦。\r\n\r\nland sb in court\r\n= 让某人闹上法庭 / 被告上法庭\r\n\r\nThe dispute could land the company in court.\r\n这场纠纷可能会让公司陷入诉讼。\r\n\r\nland sb in hospital\r\n= 让某人进医院\r\n\r\nThe accident landed him in hospital.\r\n那场事故让他进了医院。\r\n\r\nland sb in prison / jail\r\n= 让某人进监狱\r\n\r\nThe offence could land him in prison.\r\n这项罪行可能会让他入狱。\r\n\r\nland sb in debt\r\n= 让某人陷入债务\r\n\r\nPoor financial decisions landed them in debt.\r\n糟糕的财务决定让他们陷入了债务。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nOne bad decision could land you in serious trouble.\r\n一个错误决定就可能让你惹上大麻烦。\r\n\r\nThe crash landed him in hospital for a week.\r\n那场车祸让他住了一周院。\r\n\r\nFraud could land you in prison.\r\n诈骗可能会让你入狱。\r\n\r\nThat lawsuit could land the company in serious financial difficulty.\r\n那场诉讼可能会让公司陷入严重的财务困境。\r\n\r\nHis comments landed him in hot water.\r\n他的言论让他陷入了麻烦。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n最值得记的是这个结构：\r\n\r\nland + sb + in + 某种处境\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe offence could land him in prison.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThe offence\r\n= 这项罪行\r\n\r\ncould land him\r\n= 可能会使他落到……\r\n\r\nin prison\r\n= 监狱里\r\n\r\n所以整句就是：\r\n\r\n这项罪行可能会让他入狱。\r\n\r\n这里的 land 不是“降落”，而是：\r\n\r\n“把某人弄到某种结果里”。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nland sb in vs get sb into\r\n\r\nget sb into trouble\r\n= 让某人惹上麻烦\r\n\r\n更口语、更普通。\r\n\r\nThat could get you into trouble.\r\n那可能会让你惹上麻烦。\r\n\r\nland sb in trouble\r\n也很自然，但语气更有“结果很严重、把人弄进去了”的感觉。\r\n\r\nThat could land you in serious trouble.\r\n那可能会让你陷入严重麻烦。\r\n\r\nland sb in vs put sb in\r\n\r\nput sb in a difficult situation\r\n= 使某人处于困难境地\r\n\r\n更中性。\r\n\r\nland sb in\r\n通常更有“意外造成不良后果”的感觉。\r\n\r\nland sb in trouble vs be in trouble\r\n\r\nbe in trouble\r\n= 已经有麻烦\r\n\r\nland sb in trouble\r\n= 让某人陷入麻烦\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n常见结构是：\r\n\r\n✅ land sb in trouble\r\n\r\n✅ land sb in prison\r\n\r\n✅ land sb in hospital\r\n\r\n✅ land sb in debt\r\n\r\nland 后面直接接人\r\n\r\n✅ land him in trouble\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ land to him in trouble\r\n\r\n这里的 land 不是“飞机降落”\r\n\r\nland 作动词还有：\r\n\r\nThe plane landed safely.\r\n飞机安全降落。\r\n\r\n但：\r\n\r\nland sb in trouble\r\n是完全不同的引申义。\r\n\r\n很常见于负面结果\r\n\r\n尤其是：\r\n\r\ntrouble\r\nprison\r\nhospital\r\ncourt\r\ndebt\r\nhot water\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 land 想象成：\r\n\r\n“最后落到某个地方”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nland sb in trouble\r\n= 让某人最后“落进麻烦里”\r\n\r\nland sb in prison\r\n= 让某人最后“落进监狱里”\r\n\r\n最好记这句：\r\n\r\nThat could land you in serious trouble.\r\n那可能会让你惹上大麻烦。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/5d079c5b54c143fa8d4db9050c97c0ae.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 12:36:20',1,'2026-08-29 12:36:20'),(1534,21,21,'vocab','reconcile','reconcile','reconcile','🎯 核心意思\r\nreconcile = 调和；使和解；使一致；核对并解决差异\r\n\r\n这个词的核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n“把原本不一致、冲突或对不上的东西，调整到一致。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n调和两种不同的观点 / 要求\r\n\r\nIt is difficult to reconcile these two positions.\r\n很难调和这两种立场。\r\n\r\n使两个人和解\r\n\r\nThe two friends were eventually reconciled.\r\n这两个朋友最终和好了。\r\n\r\n核对账目、数据并解决差异\r\n\r\nWe need to reconcile the bank statement with our internal records.\r\n我们需要把银行对账单和内部记录核对一致。\r\n\r\n这个用法在：\r\n\r\n银行\r\n财务\r\n会计\r\n数据系统\r\n报表\r\n\r\n里非常常见。\r\n\r\nreconcile A with B\r\n\r\n= 使 A 和 B 一致 / 调和 A 和 B\r\n\r\nWe need to reconcile the report with the database.\r\n我们需要让报表数据和数据库数据保持一致。\r\n\r\nreconcile oneself to sth\r\n\r\n= 接受一个不太理想的事实\r\n\r\nHe eventually reconciled himself to the decision.\r\n他最终接受了这个决定。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nWe need to reconcile the two sets of data.\r\n我们需要核对并统一这两组数据。\r\n\r\nThe accountant reconciled the bank statement with the ledger.\r\n会计把银行对账单和分类账进行了核对。\r\n\r\nIt can be difficult to reconcile work and family responsibilities.\r\n要兼顾工作和家庭责任可能很困难。\r\n\r\nThe two sides are trying to reconcile their differences.\r\n双方正试图调和彼此的分歧。\r\n\r\nShe eventually reconciled herself to the fact that the plan had failed.\r\n她最终接受了计划失败这个事实。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n在银行或系统开发语境里，最常见的是：\r\n\r\nreconcile data\r\n= 对账 / 核对数据\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe system should reconcile transaction records with bank statements.\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n系统应该把交易记录与银行对账单进行核对，并找出、解决其中的差异。\r\n\r\n这里 reconcile 不只是：\r\n\r\ncompare\r\n= 比较\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\ncompare + identify discrepancies + make them consistent\r\n\r\n也就是：\r\n\r\n比较\r\n→ 找出差异\r\n→ 处理差异\r\n→ 达到一致\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nreconcile vs compare\r\n\r\ncompare\r\n= 比较\r\n\r\n只是看两者哪里相同、哪里不同。\r\n\r\nreconcile\r\n= 核对并解决差异，使一致\r\n\r\n所以在财务系统里：\r\n\r\ncompare = 比较\r\nreconcile = 对账\r\n\r\nreconcile vs match\r\n\r\nmatch\r\n= 匹配；一致\r\n\r\n强调结果。\r\n\r\nThe values match.\r\n这些值一致。\r\n\r\nreconcile\r\n强调过程。\r\n\r\nWe need to reconcile the values.\r\n我们需要把这些值核对一致。\r\n\r\nreconcile vs resolve\r\n\r\nresolve\r\n= 解决问题\r\n\r\nresolve a discrepancy\r\n= 解决差异\r\n\r\nreconcile\r\n= 通过核对、调整，让两边一致\r\n\r\n常见于数据和账目。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n很常见的结构：\r\n\r\nreconcile A with B\r\n\r\n✅ reconcile the report with the database\r\n核对报表和数据库\r\n\r\nreconcile 不等于只是“检查”\r\n\r\ncheck\r\n= 检查\r\n\r\nreconcile\r\n= 核对并使一致\r\n\r\n名词形式：\r\n\r\nreconciliation\r\n/ˌrek.ənˌsɪl.iˈeɪ.ʃən/\r\n\r\n= 和解；调和；对账\r\n\r\nbank reconciliation\r\n= 银行对账\r\n\r\naccount reconciliation\r\n= 账户对账\r\n\r\n发音注意\r\n\r\nreconcile：\r\n\r\n/ˈrek.ən.saɪl/\r\n\r\n最后是：\r\n\r\n/saɪl/\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n/siːl/\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 reconcile 想成：\r\n\r\n两边数据不一样：\r\n\r\nSystem: 100\r\nBank: 92\r\n\r\n先找出 discrepancy：\r\n\r\n差了 8\r\n\r\n然后调查、调整，最后让：\r\n\r\nSystem = Bank\r\n\r\n这个过程就是：\r\n\r\nreconcile\r\n= 对账 / 调和 / 使一致\r\n\r\n最实用的一句：\r\n\r\nWe need to reconcile the two records.\r\n我们需要把这两条记录核对一致。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/51ca9af6f7a945bdb89cdbcc094b7ae0.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 12:47:03',1,'2026-08-29 12:47:03'),(1535,21,22,'phrase','within one’s earshot','within one’s earshot','within one’s earshot','🎯 核心意思\r\nwithin one’s earshot = 在某人听得见的地方；在某人的听力范围内\r\n\r\n也就是说：\r\n\r\nsomeone is close enough to hear what is being said\r\n= 某人离得足够近，能够听见别人说的话','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nwithin earshot\r\n= 在听得见的范围内\r\n\r\nDon’t say that while he’s within earshot.\r\n他还听得见的时候别说那个。\r\n\r\nwithin someone’s earshot\r\n= 在某人听得到的范围内\r\n\r\nShe lowered her voice because the children were within earshot.\r\n因为孩子们就在听得见的地方，她压低了声音。\r\n\r\nout of earshot\r\n= 在听不见的范围之外\r\n\r\nWait until they’re out of earshot.\r\n等他们走到听不见的地方再说。\r\n\r\ncome within earshot\r\n= 走到能听见的范围内\r\n\r\nHe stopped talking when the manager came within earshot.\r\n经理走到能听见的地方时，他就不说了。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nBe careful what you say when the boss is within earshot.\r\n老板在听得见的地方时，说话要小心。\r\n\r\nI didn’t want to discuss it while the children were within earshot.\r\n孩子们还听得见的时候，我不想讨论这件事。\r\n\r\nShe waited until everyone was out of earshot.\r\n她等到所有人都走到听不见的地方。\r\n\r\nHe whispered so that nobody within earshot could understand him.\r\n他低声说话，以免附近能听见的人听清楚。\r\n\r\nThe suspect was standing within earshot of the conversation.\r\n那名嫌疑人当时站在能听见这段对话的范围内。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nDon’t discuss it within his earshot.\r\n\r\n可以拆成：\r\n\r\nwithin\r\n= 在……范围内\r\n\r\nhis\r\n= 他的\r\n\r\nearshot\r\n= 听力可及的范围\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n别在他听得见的地方讨论这件事。\r\n\r\n不过日常英语里更常见的是：\r\n\r\nDon’t discuss it while he’s within earshot.\r\n\r\n或者：\r\n\r\nDon’t discuss it within earshot of him.\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nwithin earshot vs nearby\r\n\r\nnearby\r\n= 在附近\r\n\r\n只是表示距离近，不一定能听见。\r\n\r\nHe was standing nearby.\r\n他站在附近。\r\n\r\nwithin earshot\r\n= 近到能听见\r\n\r\nHe was standing within earshot.\r\n他站在能听见的范围内。\r\n\r\nwithin earshot vs within hearing distance\r\n\r\nwithin hearing distance\r\n= 在听得到的距离内\r\n\r\n意思非常接近，但更直白。\r\n\r\nwithin earshot\r\n更自然、更地道。\r\n\r\nwithin earshot vs out of earshot\r\n\r\nwithin earshot\r\n= 听得见\r\n\r\nout of earshot\r\n= 听不见\r\n\r\n这两个最好成对记。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n固定词是 earshot\r\n\r\n✅ earshot\r\n❌ ear shot\r\n\r\n很常见的表达是：\r\n\r\nwithin earshot\r\nout of earshot\r\n\r\n不一定非要加 one’s。\r\n\r\nwithin one’s earshot 是对的，但实际口语中更常见：\r\n\r\nwithin earshot of sb\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThey were talking within earshot of the police officer.\r\n他们说话的地方警察听得到。\r\n\r\nearshot 不是“耳朵的一枪”之类的字面意思\r\n\r\n它是固定名词：\r\n\r\nthe distance within which someone can hear\r\n= 能听见声音的范围\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 earshot 想成：\r\n\r\near = 耳朵\r\nshot = 能“够到”的距离\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nwithin earshot\r\n= 声音能够到耳朵\r\n→ 听得见\r\n\r\nout of earshot\r\n= 声音够不到耳朵\r\n→ 听不见\r\n\r\n最好成对记：\r\n\r\nwithin earshot\r\n= 在听得见的范围内\r\n\r\nout of earshot\r\n= 在听不见的范围外。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c9d1ce5b25d04aaaa73a2dd8640a4b45.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 12:49:31',1,'2026-08-29 12:49:31'),(1536,21,23,'phrase','within sight','within sight','within sight','🎯 核心意思\r\nwithin sight = 在看得见的范围内；近在眼前\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\nclose enough to be seen\r\n= 距离足够近，所以能看见\r\n\r\n它既可以表示“物理上看得见”，也可以表示“目标已经很接近”。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n在视线范围内\r\n\r\nThe village was finally within sight.\r\n村庄终于进入视野了。\r\n\r\n保持在看得见的范围内\r\n\r\nKeep the children within sight.\r\n让孩子们一直待在你看得见的地方。\r\n\r\n目标近在眼前\r\n\r\nVictory is within sight.\r\n胜利已经近在眼前。\r\n\r\n成功、解决方案等快要实现\r\n\r\nA solution is now within sight.\r\n解决方案现在已经指日可待。\r\n\r\n常见结构\r\n\r\nwithin sight\r\n= 看得见\r\n\r\nwithin sight of sth\r\n= 在能看见某物的地方\r\n\r\nkeep sb/sth within sight\r\n= 让某人/某物保持在视线内','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThe mountains were within sight.\r\n那些山已经看得见了。\r\n\r\nWe stayed within sight of the coast.\r\n我们一直待在能看见海岸的范围内。\r\n\r\nKeep your luggage within sight at all times.\r\n请始终把行李放在自己看得见的地方。\r\n\r\nAfter years of work, the finish line is finally within sight.\r\n经过多年的努力，终点终于近在眼前。\r\n\r\nAn agreement may now be within sight.\r\n现在可能已经快要达成协议了。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe finish line is within sight.\r\n\r\n字面意思：\r\n\r\n终点线已经看得见了。\r\n\r\n引申意思：\r\n\r\n成功已经非常接近了。\r\n目标快实现了。\r\n\r\n所以 within sight 可以从物理意义：\r\n\r\n“看得见”\r\n\r\n延伸到抽象意义：\r\n\r\n“快要实现 / 近在眼前”。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nwithin sight vs in sight\r\n\r\nin sight\r\n= 看得见；在视野中\r\n\r\nThe ship came into sight.\r\n船进入了视野。\r\n\r\nwithin sight\r\n= 在看得见的范围内\r\n\r\nThe ship was within sight of the coast.\r\n这艘船处于能看见海岸的范围内。\r\n\r\n两者很接近，但 within sight 更强调“在可见范围内”。\r\n\r\nwithin sight vs within earshot\r\n\r\nwithin sight\r\n= 看得见\r\n\r\nwithin earshot\r\n= 听得见\r\n\r\n这两个可以成对记：\r\n\r\nwithin sight\r\n视觉范围内\r\n\r\nwithin earshot\r\n听觉范围内\r\n\r\nwithin sight vs out of sight\r\n\r\nwithin sight\r\n= 看得见\r\n\r\nout of sight\r\n= 看不见\r\n\r\nThe car disappeared out of sight.\r\n那辆车消失在视线之外。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nsight 是“视野、视线”，不是 site\r\n\r\n✅ sight\r\n= 视野；看见\r\n\r\n❌ site\r\n= 地点；场地\r\n\r\n常见搭配：\r\n\r\nwithin sight of + 地点/物体\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nwithin sight of the coast\r\n= 在能看见海岸的地方\r\n\r\n抽象语境里很常见\r\n\r\nVictory is within sight.\r\n胜利在望。\r\n\r\nA deal is within sight.\r\n协议即将达成。\r\n\r\n不要和 at sight 混淆\r\n\r\nat sight\r\n= 一看到就……\r\n\r\nlove at first sight\r\n= 一见钟情\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 sight 想成：\r\n\r\n👁 眼睛能够看到的范围\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nwithin sight\r\n= 在这个视觉范围之内\r\n→ 看得见\r\n\r\nout of sight\r\n= 超出视觉范围\r\n→ 看不见\r\n\r\n最好和 earshot 一起记：\r\n\r\nwithin sight\r\n= 看得见\r\n\r\nwithin earshot\r\n= 听得见\r\n\r\n最实用的一句：\r\n\r\nThe finish line is within sight.\r\n终点已经近在眼前。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e41acd7457aa4873b31c19853b6dd296.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 13:14:22',1,'2026-08-29 13:14:22'),(1537,21,24,'phrase','amount to','amount to','amount to','🎯 核心意思\r\namount to 常见有两个核心意思：\r\n\r\n总计达到；合计为\r\n\r\n等同于；相当于；实际上就是\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\namount to = 最后算下来“达到某个数 / 某种程度”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n总计达到；合计为\r\n\r\nThe repairs amounted to $5,000.\r\n维修费用总计达到 5000 美元。\r\n\r\nHis expenses amounted to more than $10,000.\r\n他的开支总计超过了 1 万美元。\r\n\r\n相当于；等同于\r\n\r\nHis refusal amounted to an admission of guilt.\r\n他的拒绝实际上等同于承认有罪。\r\n\r\nWhat he did amounts to fraud.\r\n他的行为实际上构成欺诈。\r\n\r\n最终产生某种结果\r\n\r\nAll these small changes amount to a major improvement.\r\n这些小变化加起来构成了一个很大的改进。\r\n\r\nnot amount to much\r\n\r\n= 没什么价值；没多大成果；成不了什么\r\n\r\nThe plan didn’t amount to much.\r\n这个计划最后没取得什么成果。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThe total cost amounted to nearly $20,000.\r\n总成本接近 2 万美元。\r\n\r\nThe losses amounted to millions of dollars.\r\n损失总计达到数百万美元。\r\n\r\nHis actions amount to a serious breach of trust.\r\n他的行为实际上构成了严重的失信。\r\n\r\nThis amounts to a complete change in policy.\r\n这实际上等同于政策的彻底改变。\r\n\r\nA few minor errors do not amount to fraud.\r\n几个小错误并不等同于欺诈。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe losses amounted to $2 million.\r\n\r\n可以拆成：\r\n\r\nthe losses\r\n= 损失\r\n\r\namounted to\r\n= 总计达到\r\n\r\n$2 million\r\n= 200 万美元\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n损失总计达到 200 万美元。\r\n\r\n再比如：\r\n\r\nThis amounts to a refusal.\r\n\r\n这里 amount to 不是“总计”，而是：\r\n\r\n= is effectively\r\n= is equivalent to\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这实际上就等同于拒绝。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\namount to vs add up to\r\n\r\nadd up to\r\n= 合计为\r\n\r\n更口语、更直接。\r\n\r\nThe bills add up to $500.\r\n这些账单加起来是 500 美元。\r\n\r\namount to\r\n稍正式一些，尤其常见于新闻、法律、商业语境。\r\n\r\nThe costs amounted to $500.\r\n成本总计达到 500 美元。\r\n\r\namount to vs total\r\n\r\ntotal\r\n也可以作动词：\r\n\r\nThe costs totalled $500.\r\n成本总计 500 美元。\r\n\r\n和 amount to 很接近。\r\n\r\namount to vs equal\r\n\r\nequal\r\n= 等于\r\n\r\n更偏数学或直接结果。\r\n\r\namount to\r\n除了数字，还可以表示：\r\n\r\n“实际上等同于某种行为或后果”\r\n\r\nHis conduct amounted to misconduct.\r\n他的行为实际上构成了不当行为。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\namount to 后面可以接数字\r\n\r\n✅ amount to $10,000\r\n总计达到 1 万美元\r\n\r\n也可以接名词，表示“等同于”\r\n\r\n✅ amount to fraud\r\n构成欺诈\r\n\r\n✅ amount to a refusal\r\n等同于拒绝\r\n\r\n不要把 amount to 只理解成“数量”\r\n\r\n它经常是动词短语：\r\n\r\namount to\r\n= 总计达到 / 等同于\r\n\r\n过去式是：\r\n\r\namounted to\r\n\r\nThe cost amounted to $5,000.\r\n成本总计达到 5000 美元。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n先记 amount：\r\n\r\namount = 数量；总额\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\namount to + 数字\r\n= 总额达到……\r\n\r\n然后把这个意思引申：\r\n\r\n最后算下来，这件事“达到某种性质”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\namount to fraud\r\n= 最后性质上等同于欺诈\r\n\r\n最好记两个句子：\r\n\r\nThe cost amounted to $10,000.\r\n成本总计达到 1 万美元。\r\n\r\nHis actions amounted to fraud.\r\n他的行为实际上构成了欺诈。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/df219d62bc4f40a48ddf33ed25c12d09.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 13:18:45',1,'2026-08-29 13:18:45'),(1538,21,25,'phrase','seem off','seem off','seem off','🎯 核心意思\r\nseem off = 看起来不太对；感觉有点不对劲；显得异常\r\n\r\n这里的 off 不是“关闭”，而是：\r\n\r\nnot quite right\r\n= 不太正常、不太对劲\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nSomething seems off.\r\n= 某件事感觉不太对。\r\n\r\n这个表达非常口语、非常实用。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n事情感觉不对劲\r\n\r\nSomething seems off.\r\n感觉有点不对劲。\r\n\r\n数据、数字看起来有问题\r\n\r\nThese numbers seem off.\r\n这些数字看起来不太对。\r\n\r\n某人的状态看起来不正常\r\n\r\nYou seem a little off today.\r\n你今天看起来有点不在状态。\r\n\r\n味道、气味等感觉异常\r\n\r\nThe milk seems off.\r\n这牛奶好像变质了。\r\n\r\n这里 off 可以直接表示食物“不新鲜 / 坏了”。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nSomething seems off about this report.\r\n这份报告感觉有点不对劲。\r\n\r\nThe total seems off. Can you check it again?\r\n这个总数看起来不太对，你能再检查一下吗？\r\n\r\nHis explanation seemed a bit off.\r\n他的解释听起来有点不对劲。\r\n\r\nYou seem a little off today. Are you okay?\r\n你今天看起来有点不在状态，还好吗？\r\n\r\nThe timing seems off.\r\n这个时间安排感觉不太对。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe numbers seem off.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nthe numbers\r\n= 这些数字\r\n\r\nseem\r\n= 看起来 / 似乎\r\n\r\noff\r\n= 不太对劲\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nThe numbers seem off.\r\n= 这些数字看起来不太对。\r\n\r\n这里非常适合用于工作场景，比如：\r\n\r\n报表\r\n金额\r\nOCR 结果\r\n数据库数据\r\n时间安排\r\n\r\n它比：\r\n\r\nThe numbers are wrong.\r\n\r\n语气更柔和，因为 seem off 只是说：\r\n\r\n“看起来可能有问题”，还没有完全下结论。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nseem off vs seem wrong\r\n\r\nseem wrong\r\n= 看起来是错的\r\n\r\n语气更直接。\r\n\r\nThis number seems wrong.\r\n这个数字看起来是错的。\r\n\r\nseem off\r\n= 感觉不太对\r\n\r\n更委婉、更口语。\r\n\r\nThis number seems off.\r\n这个数字感觉有点不对。\r\n\r\nseem off vs look strange\r\n\r\nlook strange\r\n= 看起来奇怪\r\n\r\n更强调视觉上的奇怪。\r\n\r\nSomething seems off.\r\n则可以是整体感觉不对，不一定是“看起来”。\r\n\r\nseem off vs be off\r\n\r\nbe off\r\n= 本身就不对 / 不正常\r\n\r\nThe calculation is off.\r\n这个计算有误。\r\n\r\nseem off\r\n= 看起来有误\r\n\r\nThe calculation seems off.\r\n这个计算看起来有点问题。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nseem 后面直接接 off\r\n\r\n✅ It seems off.\r\n❌ It seems to off.\r\n\r\nvery 常见的表达是：\r\n\r\nSomething seems off.\r\n\r\n这个句子非常值得直接背。\r\n\r\noff 的意思很多\r\n\r\nturn off\r\n= 关闭\r\n\r\nday off\r\n= 休息日\r\n\r\nfeel off\r\n= 感觉身体或状态不太对\r\n\r\nseem off\r\n= 看起来不太对劲\r\n\r\n所以一定要结合语境。\r\n\r\nseem off 很口语\r\n\r\n在正式报告里，可以改成：\r\n\r\nseem incorrect\r\nappear inconsistent\r\nappear unusual\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 off 想成：\r\n\r\n“偏离正常状态”\r\n\r\n正常：✅\r\noff：↗ 偏了一点\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nseem off\r\n= 看起来偏离了正常状态\r\n→ 感觉不太对劲\r\n\r\n最好记三句：\r\n\r\nSomething seems off.\r\n感觉有点不对劲。\r\n\r\nThese numbers seem off.\r\n这些数字看起来不太对。\r\n\r\nYou seem a little off today.\r\n你今天看起来有点不在状态。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/0ce6abbcb2cf4db392a8124caeba7761.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 19:46:53',1,'2026-08-29 19:46:53'),(1539,21,26,'phrase','the highlight of','the highlight of','the highlight of','🎯 核心意思\r\nthe highlight of = ……中最精彩的部分；……中最值得期待/最令人难忘的部分\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n在一整段经历、活动、比赛、旅行、一天当中，最亮眼、最出彩的那一部分。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nthe highlight of the trip\r\n= 旅行中最精彩的部分\r\n\r\nSeeing the mountains was the highlight of the trip.\r\n看到那些山是这次旅行最精彩的部分。\r\n\r\nthe highlight of the day\r\n= 一天中最开心/最精彩的时刻\r\n\r\nDinner was the highlight of the day.\r\n晚餐是这一天最精彩的部分。\r\n\r\nthe highlight of the event\r\n= 活动中最出彩的部分\r\n\r\nThe live performance was the highlight of the event.\r\n现场表演是这次活动最精彩的部分。\r\n\r\none of the highlights of...\r\n= ……的亮点之一\r\n\r\nThe museum was one of the highlights of our visit.\r\n这个博物馆是我们这次参观的亮点之一。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nMeeting the local people was the highlight of my trip.\r\n认识当地人是我这次旅行最难忘的部分。\r\n\r\nThe final match was the highlight of the tournament.\r\n决赛是整个锦标赛最精彩的部分。\r\n\r\nFor me, the highlight of the evening was the speech.\r\n对我来说，今晚最精彩的部分是那场演讲。\r\n\r\nThat restaurant was definitely one of the highlights of our holiday.\r\n那家餐厅绝对是我们假期中的亮点之一。\r\n\r\nThe highlight of the conference was the keynote presentation.\r\n这次会议最精彩的部分是主题演讲。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe highlight of the trip was visiting Queenstown.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nthe highlight\r\n= 最精彩的部分\r\n\r\nof the trip\r\n= 这次旅行中的\r\n\r\nwas visiting Queenstown\r\n= 是游览 Queenstown\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这次旅行最精彩的部分就是游览 Queenstown。\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\nThe highlight of A was B.\r\n= A 中最精彩的部分是 B。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nthe highlight of vs the best part of\r\n\r\nthe best part of\r\n= 最好的部分\r\n\r\n更口语、更直接。\r\n\r\nThe best part of the trip was the food.\r\n旅行中最棒的部分是美食。\r\n\r\nthe highlight of\r\n更有“亮点、最值得记住”的感觉。\r\n\r\nThe highlight of the trip was the boat tour.\r\n旅行的亮点是乘船游览。\r\n\r\nthe highlight of vs feature\r\n\r\nfeature\r\n= 特点；特色\r\n\r\nA swimming pool is one of the hotel\'s main features.\r\n游泳池是这家酒店的主要特色之一。\r\n\r\nhighlight\r\n= 最出彩、最值得注意的部分\r\n\r\nThe pool was the highlight of our stay.\r\n游泳池是我们住宿期间最棒的部分。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n常见结构是：\r\n\r\n✅ the highlight of the trip\r\n\r\n✅ the highlight of the event\r\n\r\n✅ the highlight of the day\r\n\r\n如果有多个亮点：\r\n\r\none of the highlights of...\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThis was one of the highlights of the year.\r\n这是今年的亮点之一。\r\n\r\nhighlight 既可以作名词，也可以作动词\r\n\r\n名词：\r\n\r\nThe concert was the highlight of the festival.\r\n这场音乐会是节庆的亮点。\r\n\r\n动词：\r\n\r\nThe report highlights several problems.\r\n这份报告强调了几个问题。\r\n\r\nthe highlight of 不一定只是“最好”\r\n\r\n它更强调：\r\n\r\n最亮眼\r\n最值得记住\r\n最出彩\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nhighlight 原本有：\r\n\r\n“高亮、突出显示”\r\n\r\n的意思。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nthe highlight of the trip\r\n就像把旅行里最精彩的一部分“用荧光笔标出来”。\r\n\r\n→ 最亮眼的部分\r\n→ 最大亮点\r\n\r\n最好记一句：\r\n\r\nThe highlight of the trip was the scenery.\r\n这次旅行最精彩的部分是风景。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/706dfbfe7ddf4e4fb9b8b3ce2ba5bc17.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 19:53:33',1,'2026-08-29 19:53:33'),(1540,21,27,'vocab','expertise','expertise','expertise','🎯 核心意思\r\nexpertise = 专业知识；专业技能；专长\r\n\r\n它强调的是：\r\n\r\n通过学习、训练和经验积累出来的高水平能力。\r\n\r\n不是普通的 skill，而是：\r\n\r\nspecialist knowledge or ability\r\n= 某个领域里的专业能力','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n某个领域的专业知识\r\n\r\nShe has expertise in data analysis.\r\n她在数据分析方面有专业知识。\r\n\r\n专业技能、专长\r\n\r\nWe need someone with technical expertise.\r\n我们需要一个有技术专长的人。\r\n\r\n某人的专业判断能力\r\n\r\nI’ll defer to your expertise.\r\n我会听从你的专业判断。\r\n\r\n常见结构','','/static/uploads/english_note_item/54478e1742114c8bbec133f9f8d5dae2.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 19:58:31',1,'2026-08-29 19:58:31'),(1541,21,28,'phrase','get to the bottom of sth','get to the bottom of sth','get to the bottom of sth','🎯 核心意思\r\nget to the bottom of sth = 查清某事的真相；弄清根本原因；彻底调查清楚\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n一直查到“最底层”\r\n→ 不停在表面\r\n→ 找到真正原因或真相','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n查清问题原因\r\n\r\nWe need to get to the bottom of this issue.\r\n我们需要彻底查清这个问题的原因。\r\n\r\n弄清真相\r\n\r\nThe police are trying to get to the bottom of what happened.\r\n警方正在努力查清到底发生了什么。\r\n\r\n排查系统 / 数据问题\r\n\r\nWe need to get to the bottom of these discrepancies.\r\n我们需要彻底查清这些数据不一致的原因。\r\n\r\n常见结构\r\n\r\nget to the bottom of + problem / issue / matter / discrepancy / mystery\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nget to the bottom of the problem\r\n查清问题根源\r\n\r\nget to the bottom of the matter\r\n把这件事彻底查清\r\n\r\nget to the bottom of a discrepancy\r\n查清差异产生的原因','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nI’ll get to the bottom of it.\r\n我会把这件事查清楚的。\r\n\r\nWe need to get to the bottom of why the system failed.\r\n我们需要查清系统为什么会失败。\r\n\r\nThe team is trying to get to the bottom of the data mismatch.\r\n团队正在努力查清数据不匹配的原因。\r\n\r\nThe investigation should help us get to the bottom of what went wrong.\r\n这项调查应该能帮助我们弄清到底出了什么问题。\r\n\r\nHave you managed to get to the bottom of the problem?\r\n你已经查清这个问题的根源了吗？\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe need to get to the bottom of this.\r\n\r\n可以拆成：\r\n\r\nget to\r\n= 到达\r\n\r\nthe bottom\r\n= 最底部\r\n\r\nof this\r\n= 这件事的\r\n\r\n字面上：\r\n\r\n“到达这件事的最底部”\r\n\r\n实际意思：\r\n\r\n不要只看表面，要一直调查到真正的原因。\r\n\r\n所以最自然的中文是：\r\n\r\n我们得把这件事彻底查清楚。\r\n我们得弄清楚问题的根源。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nget to the bottom of vs investigate\r\n\r\ninvestigate\r\n= 调查\r\n\r\n比较正式，只表示“调查”这个动作。\r\n\r\nWe are investigating the issue.\r\n我们正在调查这个问题。\r\n\r\nget to the bottom of\r\n= 不只是调查，而是要查到真正原因\r\n\r\nWe need to get to the bottom of the issue.\r\n我们需要彻底查清问题根源。\r\n\r\nget to the bottom of vs figure out\r\n\r\nfigure out\r\n= 弄明白；想明白\r\n\r\n更口语，范围很广。\r\n\r\nI’m trying to figure out why it failed.\r\n我正在弄清它为什么失败。\r\n\r\nget to the bottom of\r\n更强调：\r\n\r\n事情比较复杂\r\n需要调查\r\n最终找到根因\r\n\r\nget to the bottom of vs find out\r\n\r\nfind out\r\n= 查明；发现\r\n\r\n强调得到某个信息。\r\n\r\nI found out who did it.\r\n我查出了是谁干的。\r\n\r\nget to the bottom of\r\n强调完整调查并找到深层原因。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n固定结构是：\r\n\r\n✅ get to the bottom of sth\r\n\r\n不要漏掉 of：\r\n\r\n❌ get to the bottom sth\r\n\r\n很常见的一句：\r\n\r\nI’ll get to the bottom of it.\r\n\r\n= 我会把它查清楚。\r\n\r\n不一定表示犯罪调查\r\n\r\n它在工作里非常常见，比如：\r\n\r\nbug\r\n数据问题\r\n账目差异\r\n客户投诉\r\n系统故障\r\n\r\n都可以用。\r\n\r\n可以接从句\r\n\r\n✅ get to the bottom of why this happened\r\n\r\n= 查清为什么会发生\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象一个问题像冰山：\r\n\r\n表面：症状\r\n↓\r\n继续查\r\n↓\r\n继续查\r\n↓\r\n最底部：真正原因\r\n\r\n你查到了最底层：\r\n\r\nget to the bottom of it\r\n= 把事情彻底查清楚\r\n\r\n最好记这两句：\r\n\r\nI’ll get to the bottom of it.\r\n我会把这件事查清楚。\r\n\r\nWe need to get to the bottom of what went wrong.\r\n我们需要彻底弄清到底哪里出了问题。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/cb1ff7042724424bb9b7d7d84271420c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 20:13:54',1,'2026-08-29 20:13:54'),(1542,21,29,'phrase','take down','take down','take down','🎯 核心意思\r\ntake down 常见有几个意思：\r\n\r\n拆掉；取下\r\n\r\n写下；记下\r\n\r\n击倒；制服\r\n\r\n删除、下架内容\r\n\r\n打败某人 / 某组织\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n把某样东西“从原来的位置上弄下来”。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n取下；拆掉\r\n\r\nThey took down the old sign.\r\n他们把旧招牌拆下来了。\r\n\r\nWe need to take down the decorations.\r\n我们得把装饰品取下来。\r\n\r\n写下；记下\r\n\r\nCan you take down his phone number?\r\n你能把他的电话号码记下来吗？\r\n\r\nThe officer took down my details.\r\n警官记下了我的个人信息。\r\n\r\n击倒；制服\r\n\r\nThe police took down the suspect.\r\n警方制服了嫌疑人。\r\n\r\n删除 / 下架网络内容\r\n\r\nThe platform took down the post.\r\n平台下架了这条帖子。\r\n\r\nThe video was taken down for violating the rules.\r\n这个视频因为违反规则被下架了。\r\n\r\n打败某人 / 某组织\r\n\r\nThe smaller team took down the champions.\r\n那支较弱的队伍击败了冠军队。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nPlease take down the poster after the event.\r\n活动结束后请把海报取下来。\r\n\r\nI took down everything she said.\r\n我把她说的内容都记了下来。\r\n\r\nThe police quickly took him down.\r\n警方很快把他制服了。\r\n\r\nThe company was ordered to take down the content.\r\n这家公司被要求下架这些内容。\r\n\r\nThe website took down several illegal listings.\r\n这个网站下架了几个违法商品页面。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n你之前提到过：\r\n\r\ntake down order\r\n\r\n这里通常是：\r\n\r\ntakedown order\r\n= 下架令 / 删除令 / 移除命令\r\n\r\n注意这里常写成一个词：\r\n\r\ntakedown\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe court issued a takedown order.\r\n法院发布了下架令。\r\n\r\n而作为动词时是两个词：\r\n\r\ntake down\r\n\r\nThe platform was ordered to take down the post.\r\n平台被要求删除这条帖子。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\ntake down vs remove\r\n\r\nremove\r\n= 移除\r\n\r\n最中性。\r\n\r\nPlease remove the file.\r\n请删除这个文件。\r\n\r\ntake down\r\n更口语，也常用于：\r\n\r\n帖子\r\n网页\r\n招牌\r\n装饰\r\n人\r\n\r\nThe platform took down the post.\r\n平台下架了帖子。\r\n\r\ntake down vs delete\r\n\r\ndelete\r\n= 删除数据、文件、文字\r\n\r\n更偏数字内容。\r\n\r\ntake down\r\n强调让内容“不能再公开显示”。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ndelete a file\r\n删除文件\r\n\r\ntake down a post\r\n下架帖子\r\n\r\ntake down vs write down\r\n\r\nwrite down\r\n= 写下来\r\n\r\n最常见。\r\n\r\ntake down\r\n也可以表示“记下来”，稍正式一点。\r\n\r\nI wrote down his number.\r\n我把他的号码写下来了。\r\n\r\nI took down his number.\r\n我记下了他的号码。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n动词是两个词\r\n\r\n✅ take down\r\n\r\n名词/形容词常写：\r\n\r\ntakedown\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\na takedown notice\r\n下架通知\r\n\r\n代词放中间\r\n\r\n✅ take it down\r\n❌ take down it\r\n\r\n网络语境里非常常见\r\n\r\ntake down a post\r\ntake down a video\r\ntake down a website\r\n\r\n都可以表示：\r\n\r\n删除 / 下架 / 移除\r\n\r\n不要只记“拆掉”\r\n\r\ntake down 的意思很多，要看语境。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 down 想成：\r\n\r\n“从上面弄下来”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ntake down a sign\r\n= 把招牌取下来\r\n\r\ntake down a post\r\n= 把帖子从网上撤下来\r\n\r\ntake down a suspect\r\n= 把嫌疑人放倒 / 制服\r\n\r\ntake down notes/details\r\n= 把信息“落到纸上”记下来\r\n\r\n最好记这三个：\r\n\r\ntake down a post\r\n= 下架帖子\r\n\r\ntake down the details\r\n= 记下信息\r\n\r\ntake down a suspect\r\n= 制服嫌疑人','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f8fe5fb40dae44769b36035f4e941a3a.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 20:18:16',1,'2026-08-29 20:18:16'),(1543,21,30,'phrase','cut it out','cut it out','cut it out','🎯 核心意思\r\ncut it out = 别这样了；住手；停止做某事\r\n\r\n这是一个很常见的口语表达，通常用来让别人停止一个让你烦、让你不舒服或不合适的行为。\r\n\r\n语气可以从：\r\n\r\n“行了，别闹了”\r\n\r\n到\r\n\r\n“住手！”\r\n\r\n取决于语气和场景。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n叫别人停止某种行为\r\n\r\nCut it out!\r\n别这样了！/ 住手！\r\n\r\n停止开玩笑、捣乱\r\n\r\nCome on, cut it out.\r\n行了，别闹了。\r\n\r\n停止烦人的行为\r\n\r\nCut it out, you\'re annoying me.\r\n别这样了，你烦到我了。\r\n\r\ncut sth out\r\n\r\n= 停止做某事 / 戒掉某事\r\n\r\nYou should cut out junk food.\r\n你应该少吃或戒掉垃圾食品。\r\n\r\ncut sth out of sth\r\n\r\n= 把某物从某物中剪掉 / 去掉\r\n\r\nShe cut the picture out of the magazine.\r\n她把那张图片从杂志上剪了下来。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nCut it out! I\'m trying to work.\r\n别闹了！我在工作。\r\n\r\nCome on, guys, cut it out.\r\n行了，你们几个别闹了。\r\n\r\nHe kept making jokes until she told him to cut it out.\r\n他一直开玩笑，直到她叫他别再这样。\r\n\r\nYou need to cut out all that unnecessary spending.\r\n你需要停止那些不必要的开支。\r\n\r\nI cut the article out of the newspaper.\r\n我把那篇文章从报纸上剪了下来。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n如果有人直接说：\r\n\r\nCut it out.\r\n\r\n这里的 it 通常不是指一个具体物体，而是指：\r\n\r\n“你现在正在做的这件事”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nCut it out.\r\n= Stop doing that.\r\n\r\n最自然的中文通常是：\r\n\r\n别这样了。\r\n别闹了。\r\n住手。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\ncut it out vs stop it\r\n\r\nStop it.\r\n= 停下来\r\n\r\n最直接、最通用。\r\n\r\nCut it out.\r\n= 别这样了 / 别闹了\r\n\r\n更口语，也常带一点不耐烦。\r\n\r\ncut it out vs knock it off\r\n\r\nKnock it off.\r\n= 别闹了；住手\r\n\r\n语气和 cut it out 很接近，但有时更强硬一点。\r\n\r\ncut it out vs quit it\r\n\r\nQuit it.\r\n= 别这样了\r\n\r\n也比较口语，但 cut it out 更常见、更自然。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\ncut it out 是固定口语表达\r\n\r\n✅ Cut it out!\r\n\r\n不要按字面理解成：\r\n\r\n“把它剪出来”\r\n\r\n虽然 cut sth out 确实可以表示“剪出来”，但：\r\n\r\nCut it out!\r\n在口语里通常是：\r\n\r\n“别这样了！”\r\n\r\n语气可能比较直接\r\n\r\n对朋友、孩子、熟人很常见。\r\n\r\n对陌生人或正式场合，可能显得有点冲。\r\n\r\n更礼貌可以说：\r\n\r\nCould you stop doing that, please?\r\n你能别这样了吗？\r\n\r\ncut out 还有“戒掉”的意思\r\n\r\ncut out sugar\r\n= 戒糖 / 不吃糖\r\n\r\ncut out smoking\r\n= 戒烟\r\n\r\n过去式不变\r\n\r\ncut → cut → cut\r\n\r\nHe told me to cut it out.\r\n他叫我别再这样。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 cut it out 想成：\r\n\r\n把这个行为“切掉”\r\n\r\n也就是：\r\n\r\n“把你现在这个行为停掉”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nCut it out!\r\n= Stop it!\r\n= 别这样了！\r\n\r\n最值得记的三句：\r\n\r\nCut it out!\r\n别这样了！\r\n\r\nCome on, cut it out.\r\n行了，别闹了。\r\n\r\nHe told them to cut it out.\r\n他叫他们别再这样。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f1ce559fec31456e81d1ed446cabf44c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 20:27:47',1,'2026-08-29 20:27:47'),(1544,21,31,'phrase','pile up','pile up','pile up','🎯 核心意思\r\npile up = 堆积；积累；越积越多\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n东西一层一层“堆起来”\r\n→ 越来越多\r\n→ 积压、累积\r\n\r\n既可以指真实的东西，也可以指：\r\n\r\n工作\r\n债务\r\n问题\r\n邮件\r\n交通\r\n压力','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n物理上的“堆积”\r\n\r\nSnow piled up against the door.\r\n雪堆积在门边。\r\n\r\n工作、任务“积压”\r\n\r\nWork started to pile up while I was away.\r\n我不在的时候，工作开始积压。\r\n\r\n债务、账单“越积越多”\r\n\r\nThe bills are piling up.\r\n账单越积越多。\r\n\r\n问题不断累积\r\n\r\nProblems began to pile up.\r\n问题开始一个接一个出现并累积。\r\n\r\n车辆“连环相撞”\r\n\r\npile-up 作名词时可以表示：\r\n\r\n连环车祸\r\n\r\nThere was a multi-car pile-up on the motorway.\r\n高速公路上发生了多车连环相撞事故。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nMy emails are starting to pile up.\r\n我的邮件开始越积越多了。\r\n\r\nDirty dishes were piling up in the sink.\r\n脏盘子在水槽里越堆越多。\r\n\r\nThe unpaid bills kept piling up.\r\n未付账单一直在不断累积。\r\n\r\nPressure began to pile up as the deadline approached.\r\n随着截止日期临近，压力越来越大。\r\n\r\nThe complaints are piling up.\r\n投诉越来越多了。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe work is piling up.\r\n\r\n可以拆成：\r\n\r\nthe work\r\n= 工作\r\n\r\nis piling up\r\n= 正在越积越多\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n工作正在不断积压。\r\n\r\n这里不是说工作真的“堆成一堆”，而是形象地表示：\r\n\r\n事情越来越多，还没处理完。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\npile up vs build up\r\n\r\nbuild up\r\n= 逐渐积累\r\n\r\n范围更广，可以是：\r\n\r\npressure\r\nconfidence\r\ntraffic\r\ndebt\r\n\r\nPressure built up over time.\r\n压力逐渐积累。\r\n\r\npile up\r\n更有“越堆越多、开始积压”的画面感。\r\n\r\nThe work piled up.\r\n工作堆积起来了。\r\n\r\npile up vs accumulate\r\n\r\naccumulate\r\n= 积累\r\n\r\n更正式。\r\n\r\nDust accumulated on the shelves.\r\n灰尘积在架子上。\r\n\r\npile up\r\n更口语、更形象。\r\n\r\nDust piled up in the corner.\r\n灰尘堆积在角落里。\r\n\r\npile up vs stack up\r\n\r\nstack up\r\n也有“堆起来”的意思，但更强调整齐地叠放。\r\n\r\nThe boxes were stacked up against the wall.\r\n箱子整齐堆在墙边。\r\n\r\npile up\r\n不一定整齐，重点是：\r\n\r\n数量越来越多。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\npile up 可以是不及物\r\n\r\n✅ The bills are piling up.\r\n账单越积越多。\r\n\r\n也可以是及物结构\r\n\r\npile sth up\r\n= 把某物堆起来\r\n\r\nHe piled the boxes up in the corner.\r\n他把箱子堆在角落里。\r\n\r\n名词形式常写成：\r\n\r\npile-up\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\na traffic pile-up\r\n连环车祸 / 严重交通堵塞\r\n\r\n不只用于实物\r\n\r\n非常常见于：\r\n\r\nwork piling up\r\n工作积压\r\n\r\nbills piling up\r\n账单累积\r\n\r\ncomplaints piling up\r\n投诉越来越多\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\npile = 一堆\r\n\r\nup = 向上\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\npile up\r\n= 一层一层往上堆\r\n→ 越来越多\r\n→ 积压 / 累积\r\n\r\n最好记三句：\r\n\r\nThe work is piling up.\r\n工作越积越多。\r\n\r\nThe bills are piling up.\r\n账单越积越多。\r\n\r\nProblems are piling up.\r\n问题越来越多。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d5e4439c6d2a478f871f704d10ae3205.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 20:29:53',1,'2026-08-29 20:29:53'),(1545,21,32,'phrase','stick up for sb','stick up for sb','stick up for sb','🎯 核心意思\r\nstick up for sb = 支持某人；替某人说话；维护某人；为某人辩护\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n别人受到批评、欺负或不公平对待时，你“站出来帮他”。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n替某人说话\r\n\r\nThanks for sticking up for me.\r\n谢谢你替我说话。\r\n\r\n维护某人\r\n\r\nShe always sticks up for her younger brother.\r\n她总是维护她弟弟。\r\n\r\n为自己争取\r\n\r\nYou need to stick up for yourself.\r\n你得为自己据理力争。\r\n\r\n在不公平情况下站出来支持某人\r\n\r\nHe stuck up for his colleague when everyone else criticised her.\r\n当其他人都批评她时，他站出来支持自己的同事。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nI really appreciate you sticking up for me.\r\n我真的很感谢你替我说话。\r\n\r\nShe stuck up for him when he was being treated unfairly.\r\n他受到不公平对待时，她站出来维护他。\r\n\r\nYou should stick up for yourself more.\r\n你应该多为自己争取一点。\r\n\r\nHe always sticks up for his friends.\r\n他总是会维护自己的朋友。\r\n\r\nNobody stuck up for her during the meeting.\r\n会议上没有人替她说话。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nShe stuck up for him.\r\n\r\n可以拆成：\r\n\r\nshe\r\n= 她\r\n\r\nstuck up for\r\n= 站出来维护 / 替……说话\r\n\r\nhim\r\n= 他\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n她站出来维护了他。\r\n她替他说了话。\r\n\r\n这里不是普通的 support，而是带有：\r\n\r\n“别人正在攻击、批评或欺负他，而你站出来帮他”\r\n\r\n这种感觉。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nstick up for sb vs support sb\r\n\r\nsupport sb\r\n= 支持某人\r\n\r\n范围最广。\r\n\r\nI support your decision.\r\n我支持你的决定。\r\n\r\nstick up for sb\r\n= 在别人受到批评、攻击或不公对待时站出来维护\r\n\r\nI stuck up for him when they blamed him.\r\n他们责怪他时，我站出来替他说话。\r\n\r\nstick up for sb vs defend sb\r\n\r\ndefend sb\r\n= 为某人辩护；保护某人\r\n\r\n更正式，也可以是法律或身体上的保护。\r\n\r\nThe lawyer defended him in court.\r\n律师在法庭上为他辩护。\r\n\r\nstick up for sb\r\n更口语，更像日常生活中的“替他说话”。\r\n\r\nstick up for sb vs stand up for sb\r\n\r\nstand up for sb\r\n= 为某人挺身而出\r\n\r\n和 stick up for sb 很接近。\r\n\r\nstand up for sb 更常见，也可以指维护原则、权利。\r\n\r\nstick up for sb 更口语，更强调替某人说话、护着某人。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n结构是：\r\n\r\nstick up for + 人\r\n\r\n✅ stick up for me\r\n\r\n✅ stick up for your friend\r\n\r\n过去式是：\r\n\r\nstick → stuck\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nShe stuck up for me.\r\n她替我说话了。\r\n\r\n不要和 stick-up 混淆\r\n\r\nstick up for sb\r\n= 维护某人\r\n\r\na stick-up\r\n= 持械抢劫\r\n\r\n完全不是一个意思。\r\n\r\n很常见的一个表达：\r\n\r\nstick up for yourself\r\n= 为自己争取 / 维护自己\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把它想象成：\r\n\r\n有人被围着批评。\r\n\r\n你“站起来”挡在他前面：\r\n\r\nstick up for him\r\n= 站出来维护他\r\n\r\n最好记三句：\r\n\r\nThanks for sticking up for me.\r\n谢谢你替我说话。\r\n\r\nShe always sticks up for her friends.\r\n她总是维护朋友。\r\n\r\nYou need to stick up for yourself.\r\n你得为自己争取。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e9e594e9c01141bbbd2d9c55b033b623.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 21:00:54',1,'2026-08-29 21:00:54'),(1546,21,33,'phrase','shoot back','shoot back','shoot back','🎯 核心意思\r\nshoot back 常见有两个意思：\r\n\r\n开枪还击\r\n\r\n很快、很尖锐地回应 / 顶回去\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n对方“打过来” → 你立刻“打回去”\r\n\r\n所以既可以是真正的枪击，也可以是语言上的“反击”。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n开枪还击\r\n\r\nThe soldiers shot back.\r\n士兵们开枪还击。\r\n\r\nThe police were fired upon and shot back.\r\n警方遭到枪击后进行了还击。\r\n\r\n迅速回嘴、顶回去\r\n\r\n“What do you mean?” she shot back.\r\n“你什么意思？”她立刻顶了回去。\r\n\r\nHe shot back with an angry reply.\r\n他愤怒地回了一句。\r\n\r\nshoot back at sb\r\n\r\n= 向某人还击 / 回击某人\r\n\r\nShe shot back at him, “That’s not true.”\r\n她马上回击他说：“那不是真的。”\r\n\r\nshoot back a reply / answer\r\n\r\n= 很快地回一句\r\n\r\nHe shot back a quick response.\r\n他迅速回了一句。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThe soldiers immediately shot back.\r\n士兵们立刻开枪还击。\r\n\r\nShe shot back, “That’s completely unfair.”\r\n她立刻回嘴说：“这完全不公平。”\r\n\r\nHe shot back at the criticism.\r\n他迅速对批评作出了反击。\r\n\r\n“Why should I?” he shot back.\r\n“我为什么要？”他马上顶了回去。\r\n\r\nShe shot back an angry response.\r\n她愤怒地回了一句。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nShe shot back, “That’s not what I said.”\r\n\r\n这里并不是“开枪”。\r\n\r\nshot back\r\n= quickly replied, often angrily or sharply\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n她立刻回嘴说：“我不是那么说的。”\r\n\r\n这里的语气通常有：\r\n\r\n快\r\n直接\r\n有点生气\r\n带反驳意味\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nshoot back vs reply\r\n\r\nreply\r\n= 回答\r\n\r\n最中性。\r\n\r\nShe replied, “No.”\r\n她回答：“不。”\r\n\r\nshoot back\r\n= 立刻、尖锐地回一句\r\n\r\nShe shot back, “No!”\r\n她立刻顶了回去：“不！”\r\n\r\nshoot back vs snap back\r\n\r\nsnap back\r\n= 厉声回嘴；不耐烦地顶回去\r\n\r\n语气通常比 shoot back 更明显地生气。\r\n\r\n“Leave me alone,” she snapped back.\r\n“别烦我，”她厉声回道。\r\n\r\nshoot back\r\n强调“迅速反击”，不一定特别粗鲁。\r\n\r\nshoot back vs fire back\r\n\r\nfire back\r\n和 shoot back 很接近，也可以表示：\r\n\r\n开火还击\r\n语言上迅速反击\r\n\r\nHe fired back at his critics.\r\n他迅速反击了批评者。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nshoot 的过去式是不规则变化\r\n\r\nshoot → shot → shot\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\n✅ She shot back.\r\n❌ She shooted back.\r\n\r\nshoot back 不一定涉及枪\r\n\r\n在新闻、对话、小说里，经常只是：\r\n\r\n“立刻回嘴 / 反驳”\r\n\r\n常见结构\r\n\r\nshoot back\r\nshoot back at sb\r\nshoot back with a reply\r\n\r\n语气通常比 reply 强\r\n\r\nreply = 回答\r\nshoot back = 顶回去 / 迅速反击\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把它想象成：\r\n\r\n对方先“射”一句话过来：\r\n\r\n→ “You’re wrong.”\r\n\r\n你马上“射回去”：\r\n\r\n← “No, I’m not!”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nshoot back\r\n= 快速回击\r\n→ 开枪还击\r\n→ 言语上顶回去\r\n\r\n最好记一句：\r\n\r\n“What do you mean?” she shot back.\r\n“你什么意思？”她立刻顶了回去。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8e0d63de270a418ea6ffd7620e875534.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 21:12:22',1,'2026-08-29 21:12:22'),(1547,21,34,'phrase','shrug it off','shrug it off','shrug it off','🎯 核心意思\r\nshrug it off = 不把某事放在心上；一笑置之；甩掉影响；很快恢复\r\n\r\n核心感觉：\r\n\r\nshrug = 耸肩\r\noff = 甩开\r\n\r\n所以 shrug it off 就像：\r\n\r\n“耸耸肩，把这件事甩掉。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n不把批评、评论放在心上\r\n\r\nHe just shrugged it off.\r\n他根本没把这件事放在心上。\r\n\r\n对尴尬、失败等一笑置之\r\n\r\nShe shrugged off the embarrassment and carried on.\r\n她没把尴尬当回事，继续做自己的事。\r\n\r\n很快摆脱身体上的小问题\r\n\r\nHe shrugged off a minor injury and kept playing.\r\n他没太在意那点小伤，继续比赛。\r\n\r\n摆脱负面影响\r\n\r\nThe company managed to shrug off the criticism.\r\n这家公司设法摆脱了批评带来的影响。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nDon’t worry about what he said. Just shrug it off.\r\n别在意他说的话，别往心里去。\r\n\r\nShe shrugged off the criticism and kept working.\r\n她没把批评放在心上，继续工作。\r\n\r\nHe made a mistake but quickly shrugged it off.\r\n他犯了个错误，但很快就调整过来了。\r\n\r\nThe team shrugged off an early defeat and won the next three games.\r\n这支队伍很快摆脱了早先失利的影响，接下来连赢三场。\r\n\r\nHe tried to shrug off the pain.\r\n他试图不去理会疼痛。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nHe shrugged it off.\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nshrug\r\n= 耸肩\r\n\r\nit\r\n= 那件事 / 那个问题\r\n\r\noff\r\n= 甩掉\r\n\r\n字面画面就是：\r\n\r\n“他耸耸肩，把这件事甩掉了。”\r\n\r\n实际意思：\r\n\r\n他没把这件事当回事。\r\n他没有让这件事影响自己。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nshrug it off vs brush it off\r\n\r\nbrush it off\r\n= 不理会；不当回事\r\n\r\n和 shrug it off 很接近。\r\n\r\nHe brushed off the criticism.\r\n他没把批评当回事。\r\n\r\nshrug off\r\n更有一种：\r\n\r\n“耸耸肩，算了吧”\r\n\r\n的感觉。\r\n\r\nshrug it off vs get over it\r\n\r\nget over it\r\n= 从某件事中恢复过来\r\n\r\n更强调恢复过程。\r\n\r\nIt took him weeks to get over the disappointment.\r\n他花了几周才从失望中恢复过来。\r\n\r\nshrug it off\r\n强调：\r\n\r\n很快不受影响。\r\n\r\nshrug it off vs ignore\r\n\r\nignore\r\n= 忽略\r\n\r\n只是“不理”。\r\n\r\nshrug it off\r\n= 不但不理，而且心理上也不太受影响。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n代词必须放中间\r\n\r\n✅ shrug it off\r\n❌ shrug off it\r\n\r\n但是名词可以放后面：\r\n\r\n✅ shrug off the criticism\r\n\r\nshrug 的过去式是：\r\n\r\nshrugged\r\n\r\n注意双写 g：\r\n\r\nshrug → shrugged\r\n\r\n不一定只是“耸肩”\r\n\r\n真正口语里：\r\n\r\nshrug sth off\r\n经常表示“不放在心上 / 很快摆脱影响”。\r\n\r\n常见搭配\r\n\r\nshrug off criticism\r\n不把批评当回事\r\n\r\nshrug off a defeat\r\n摆脱失败影响\r\n\r\nshrug off an injury\r\n没太受伤病影响\r\n\r\nshrug off concerns\r\n不理会担忧\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象别人批评你：\r\n\r\n“That was terrible.”\r\n\r\n你只是：\r\n\r\n🤷‍♂️\r\n\r\n然后继续走。\r\n\r\n这个动作就是：\r\n\r\nshrug it off\r\n\r\n= 耸耸肩\r\n→ 甩掉它\r\n→ 不往心里去\r\n\r\n最好记两句：\r\n\r\nJust shrug it off.\r\n别往心里去。\r\n\r\nShe shrugged off the criticism.\r\n她没把批评当回事。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/4248c5dc1ee143e6a0bafbca15872955.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-29 21:22:11',1,'2026-08-29 21:22:11'),(1548,21,35,'phrase','wrap up','wrap up','wrap up','🎯 核心意思\r\nwrap up 常见有几个意思：\r\n\r\n结束；收尾\r\n\r\n总结\r\n\r\n包起来；包裹\r\n\r\n穿暖和一点\r\n\r\n最值得你记的是口语里非常常见的：\r\n\r\nwrap up = 结束 / 收尾\r\n\r\n比如会议快结束时：\r\n\r\nLet’s wrap up.\r\n= 我们收尾吧。\r\n= 我们就到这里吧。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n结束；收尾\r\n\r\nLet’s wrap up the meeting.\r\n我们把会议收尾吧。\r\n\r\nWe should wrap up soon.\r\n我们应该快点结束了。\r\n\r\n总结；做最后总结\r\n\r\nLet me wrap up by summarising the main points.\r\n最后我来总结一下主要内容。\r\n\r\n包起来；包装\r\n\r\nShe wrapped up the gift.\r\n她把礼物包了起来。\r\n\r\n穿暖和\r\n\r\nWrap up warm. It’s cold outside.\r\n穿暖和点，外面很冷。\r\n\r\n这是英式英语里很常见的说法。\r\n\r\nbe wrapped up in sth\r\n\r\n这个意思又不一样：\r\n\r\n= 全神贯注于某事；忙于某事\r\n\r\nHe was completely wrapped up in his work.\r\n他完全沉浸在工作里。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nLet’s wrap up for today.\r\n我们今天就到这里吧。\r\n\r\nWe need to wrap up the discussion.\r\n我们需要结束这次讨论了。\r\n\r\nBefore we wrap up, does anyone have any questions?\r\n在我们结束之前，还有人有问题吗？\r\n\r\nI’ll wrap up with a quick summary.\r\n最后我会做一个简短总结。\r\n\r\nShe wrapped the present up carefully.\r\n她仔细地把礼物包了起来。\r\n\r\nMake sure you wrap up warm before you go outside.\r\n出去之前一定要穿暖和点。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如会议里经常听到：\r\n\r\nLet’s wrap up.\r\n\r\n这里不是“包起来”。\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\nLet’s finish what we’re doing.\r\n= 我们把现在这件事结束吧。\r\n\r\n所以自然翻译就是：\r\n\r\n我们收尾吧。\r\n我们今天就到这里吧。\r\n\r\n再比如：\r\n\r\nBefore we wrap up, I have one more question.\r\n\r\n= 在结束之前，我还有一个问题。\r\n\r\n这个表达在会议、采访、课堂和讨论里都非常自然。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nwrap up vs finish\r\n\r\nfinish\r\n= 完成；结束\r\n\r\n最普通。\r\n\r\nLet’s finish the meeting.\r\n我们结束会议吧。\r\n\r\nwrap up\r\n= 收尾、把最后一点处理完然后结束\r\n\r\nLet’s wrap up the meeting.\r\n我们把会议收尾吧。\r\n\r\n所以 wrap up 比 finish 更有：\r\n\r\n“差不多了，把最后一点做完”\r\n\r\n的感觉。\r\n\r\nwrap up vs sum up\r\n\r\nsum up\r\n= 总结\r\n\r\n重点是总结内容。\r\n\r\nLet me sum up the main points.\r\n我来总结一下重点。\r\n\r\nwrap up\r\n既可以“总结”，也可以表示整个活动结束。\r\n\r\nLet me wrap up with three key points.\r\n最后我用三个重点来收尾。\r\n\r\nwrap up vs end\r\n\r\nend\r\n= 结束\r\n\r\n比较中性。\r\n\r\nwrap up\r\n更口语，也更有“进入最后阶段”的感觉。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nwrap up 不只是“包起来”\r\n\r\n很多学习者只记：\r\n\r\nwrap up a gift\r\n= 包礼物\r\n\r\n但在真实口语里：\r\n\r\nwrap up a meeting\r\nwrap up a discussion\r\nwrap up for today\r\n\r\n都非常常见。\r\n\r\n代词放中间\r\n\r\n✅ wrap it up\r\n❌ wrap up it\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nLet’s wrap it up.\r\n我们结束吧。\r\n\r\nwrap it up 语气有时会比较直接\r\n\r\n如果别人说太久：\r\n\r\nOkay, wrap it up.\r\n\r\n可能有：\r\n\r\n“行了，赶紧结束吧。”\r\n\r\n这种催促感。\r\n\r\n过去式：\r\n\r\nwrap → wrapped\r\n\r\n注意双写 p：\r\n\r\nwrap\r\nwrapped\r\nwrapped\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nwrap 本来是：\r\n\r\n“包起来”\r\n\r\n想象一件事情做完后，把它“包起来收好”。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nwrap up a meeting\r\n= 把会议包起来\r\n→ 收尾\r\n→ 结束\r\n\r\n最好记三个高频表达：\r\n\r\nLet’s wrap up.\r\n我们收尾吧。\r\n\r\nBefore we wrap up...\r\n在我们结束之前……\r\n\r\nLet’s wrap up for today.\r\n我们今天就到这里吧。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/7f8e53d1282d448487881b3361f14158.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-30 12:02:43',1,'2026-08-30 12:02:43'),(1549,21,36,'phrase','at the very least','at the very least','at the very least','🎯 核心意思\r\nat the very least = 至少；最起码；再怎么说也……\r\n\r\n它比普通的：\r\n\r\nat least = 至少\r\n\r\n语气更强调。\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\n“即使别的都不算，最低限度也应该这样。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n表示最低要求\r\n\r\nAt the very least, you should apologise.\r\n最起码你应该道歉。\r\n\r\n表示最低程度\r\n\r\nThe repair will cost $500 at the very least.\r\n这次维修最少也要花 500 美元。\r\n\r\n表示“即便别的不说，至少……”\r\n\r\nAt the very least, we now know what caused the problem.\r\n至少，我们现在知道问题是什么造成的了。\r\n\r\n用来强调一个最基本的事实或要求\r\n\r\nThe system should, at the very least, log the error.\r\n这个系统最起码应该把错误记录下来。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nAt the very least, we need to tell them what happened.\r\n最起码，我们得告诉他们发生了什么。\r\n\r\nYou should at the very least check the data before submitting the report.\r\n你提交报告之前，最起码应该检查一下数据。\r\n\r\nIt will take two days at the very least.\r\n这至少也要花两天。\r\n\r\nAt the very least, the application should show an error message.\r\n这个应用最起码应该显示一条错误信息。\r\n\r\nHe could have said thank you, at the very least.\r\n他最起码也应该说声谢谢。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nAt the very least, we should investigate the issue.\r\n\r\n可以拆成：\r\n\r\nat least\r\n= 至少\r\n\r\nvery\r\n= 用来加强“最低限度”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nat the very least\r\n= 最最基本也应该……\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n最起码，我们应该调查一下这个问题。\r\n\r\n这里通常带一点说话人的态度：\r\n\r\n“这已经是最低要求了。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nat the very least vs at least\r\n\r\nat least\r\n= 至少\r\n\r\n最普通。\r\n\r\nWe need at least two people.\r\n我们至少需要两个人。\r\n\r\nat the very least\r\n= 最起码；最低限度也……\r\n\r\n语气更强。\r\n\r\nAt the very least, we need two people.\r\n最起码我们也得有两个人。\r\n\r\nat the very least vs at a minimum\r\n\r\nat a minimum\r\n= 至少；最低限度\r\n\r\n更正式，常用于技术、政策、商业要求。\r\n\r\nAt a minimum, the password must contain eight characters.\r\n密码最少必须包含八个字符。\r\n\r\nat the very least\r\n更适合口语和一般正式表达。\r\n\r\nat the very least vs bare minimum\r\n\r\nthe bare minimum\r\n= 最低限度；最基本要求\r\n\r\n强调“已经不能再少了”。\r\n\r\nHe did the bare minimum.\r\n他只做了最低限度该做的事。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n固定表达是：\r\n\r\n✅ at the very least\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n❌ in the very least\r\n\r\nvery 在这里不是普通的“非常”\r\n\r\n它是在加强 least：\r\n\r\nleast = 最少\r\nthe very least = 最最低限度\r\n\r\n它可以放句首，也可以放句尾\r\n\r\nAt the very least, call me.\r\n最起码给我打个电话。\r\n\r\nCall me, at the very least.\r\n最起码给我打个电话。\r\n\r\n句首更常见、更自然。\r\n\r\n不要和 not in the least 混淆\r\n\r\nnot in the least\r\n= 一点也不\r\n\r\nI\'m not in the least worried.\r\n我一点也不担心。\r\n\r\n和：\r\n\r\nat the very least\r\n= 至少\r\n\r\n完全不是一个意思。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n先记：\r\n\r\nat least = 至少\r\n\r\n再加 very 来加强：\r\n\r\nat the very least\r\n= 就算把标准压到最低，也至少要……\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nAt the very least, say sorry.\r\n最起码说声对不起吧。\r\n\r\n最值得记的一句：\r\n\r\nAt the very least, we should check it again.\r\n最起码，我们应该再检查一次。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a0d2784e3a3e4665b9161807779f51ea.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-31 18:17:52',1,'2026-08-31 18:17:52'),(1550,21,37,'phrase','pore over','pore over','pore over','🎯 核心意思\r\npore over = 仔细阅读；认真研究；反复查看\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n低着头，长时间盯着某个东西认真看，尤其是：\r\n\r\ndocuments\r\nreports\r\nbooks\r\ndata\r\nmaps\r\nrecords','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n仔细阅读文件\r\n\r\nShe spent hours poring over the report.\r\n她花了几个小时仔细研究那份报告。\r\n\r\n认真研究数据\r\n\r\nThe team pored over the data looking for discrepancies.\r\n团队仔细研究数据，寻找其中的不一致。\r\n\r\n仔细查看地图、照片、记录\r\n\r\nHe pored over the map before the trip.\r\n旅行前他仔细研究了地图。\r\n\r\n常见结构\r\n\r\npore over + document / report / data / book / map / records\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\npore over the figures\r\n仔细研究这些数字\r\n\r\npore over the evidence\r\n仔细研究证据\r\n\r\npore over the details\r\n仔细查看细节','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nI spent the evening poring over the documents.\r\n我整个晚上都在仔细研究那些文件。\r\n\r\nShe pored over every detail of the contract.\r\n她仔细研究了合同里的每一个细节。\r\n\r\nThe engineers are poring over the logs to find the cause of the crash.\r\n工程师们正在仔细查看日志，以找出系统崩溃的原因。\r\n\r\nWe pored over the results before making a decision.\r\n我们在作决定之前仔细研究了这些结果。\r\n\r\nHe sat there poring over an old book.\r\n他坐在那里专心研究一本旧书。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe investigators pored over the evidence.\r\n\r\n可以拆成：\r\n\r\nthe investigators\r\n= 调查人员\r\n\r\npored over\r\n= 仔细研究、认真查看\r\n\r\nthe evidence\r\n= 证据\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n调查人员仔细研究了这些证据。\r\n\r\n这里不是简单的：\r\n\r\nread\r\n= 阅读\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\nread very carefully and for a long time\r\n= 花时间仔细研究。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\npore over vs read\r\n\r\nread\r\n= 阅读\r\n\r\n最普通。\r\n\r\nI read the report.\r\n我读了报告。\r\n\r\npore over\r\n= 仔细研读、认真研究\r\n\r\nI pored over the report.\r\n我仔细研究了这份报告。\r\n\r\npore over vs go through\r\n\r\ngo through\r\n= 检查、浏览、逐项查看\r\n\r\nWe went through the report.\r\n我们把报告过了一遍。\r\n\r\npore over\r\n更强调：\r\n\r\n看得很仔细\r\n花时间研究\r\n注意细节\r\n\r\npore over vs scrutinise\r\n\r\nscrutinise\r\n= 仔细审查\r\n\r\n比较正式，强调严格检查。\r\n\r\nThe documents were scrutinised by lawyers.\r\n文件经过律师的仔细审查。\r\n\r\npore over\r\n更有“埋头认真看”的画面感。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n拼写是 pore over\r\n\r\n✅ pore over\r\n❌ pour over\r\n\r\n这是非常常见的错误。\r\n\r\npore over\r\n= 仔细研究\r\n\r\npour\r\n= 倒液体\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\npour water over the plants\r\n= 把水浇到植物上\r\n\r\npore 的过去式是：\r\n\r\npored\r\n\r\n✅ She pored over the report.\r\n\r\n现在分词：\r\n\r\nporing\r\n\r\n✅ They are poring over the data.\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n❌ pouring over the data\r\n\r\n常用于需要认真分析的东西\r\n\r\n尤其是：\r\n\r\nreports\r\ndocuments\r\ndata\r\nevidence\r\nrecords\r\nmaps\r\ndetails\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 pore over 想象成：\r\n\r\n一个人低着头，眼睛几乎贴到纸上，仔细看每一行。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\npore over\r\n= 埋头仔细看\r\n→ 仔细阅读\r\n→ 认真研究\r\n\r\n最好记一句：\r\n\r\nWe spent hours poring over the data.\r\n我们花了几个小时仔细研究这些数据。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/76d7351428ce4440aca58efe6cad014c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-31 18:29:46',1,'2026-08-31 18:29:46'),(1551,21,38,'vocab','revamp','revamp','revamp','🎯 核心意思\r\nrevamp = 改造；翻新；大幅改进；重新设计\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n不是小修小补，而是把原来的东西“重新整一遍”，让它更现代、更好用、更有效。\r\n\r\n常用于：\r\n\r\nwebsite\r\nsystem\r\nprocess\r\ndesign\r\nproduct\r\nstrategy\r\noffice / store','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n改造系统 / 产品\r\n\r\nWe need to revamp the entire system.\r\n我们需要重新改造整个系统。\r\n\r\n重新设计网站 / 页面\r\n\r\nThe company revamped its website last year.\r\n这家公司去年重新设计了网站。\r\n\r\n改进流程 / 战略\r\n\r\nThey are revamping the recruitment process.\r\n他们正在全面改进招聘流程。\r\n\r\n翻新建筑、商店\r\n\r\nThe hotel has been completely revamped.\r\n这家酒店已经被彻底翻新。\r\n\r\n名词：一次全面改造\r\n\r\nThe website needs a complete revamp.\r\n这个网站需要一次彻底改版。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nWe’re planning to revamp the user interface.\r\n我们计划重新改造用户界面。\r\n\r\nThe team revamped the reporting module to make it easier to use.\r\n团队重新设计了报表模块，使它更易于使用。\r\n\r\nThe company is revamping its internal processes.\r\n公司正在全面改进内部流程。\r\n\r\nThe old office was completely revamped.\r\n这间旧办公室被彻底翻新了。\r\n\r\nThe app needs a major revamp.\r\n这个应用需要一次大改版。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe revamped the AI page.\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nrevamped\r\n= 重新设计 / 全面优化\r\n\r\nthe AI page\r\n= AI 页面\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n我们对 AI 页面进行了重新设计和全面优化。\r\n\r\n如果你只是做了一些小调整，revamp 可能有点重。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\n优化几个按钮\r\n调整一些字段\r\n修几个 UI 问题\r\n\r\n更自然可能是：\r\n\r\nimprove\r\nrefine\r\noptimise\r\n\r\n但如果你：\r\n\r\n重新布局\r\n改交互\r\n改视觉\r\n重构很多功能\r\n\r\n那用 revamp 很合适。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nrevamp vs improve\r\n\r\nimprove\r\n= 改进\r\n\r\n最宽泛，可以是小改动，也可以是大改动。\r\n\r\nWe improved the page.\r\n我们改进了这个页面。\r\n\r\nrevamp\r\n= 大改版 / 全面改造\r\n\r\nWe revamped the page.\r\n我们对页面进行了全面改版。\r\n\r\nrevamp vs redesign\r\n\r\nredesign\r\n= 重新设计\r\n\r\n更强调“设计发生变化”。\r\n\r\nrevamp\r\n范围更大，可以同时涉及：\r\n\r\ndesign\r\nfunctionality\r\nstructure\r\nprocess\r\n\r\nrevamp vs renovate\r\n\r\nrenovate\r\n= 翻修、装修\r\n\r\n更常用于：\r\n\r\nhouse\r\nbuilding\r\nroom\r\n\r\nrevamp\r\n既可以用于实体空间，也常用于系统、网站、战略。\r\n\r\nrevamp vs overhaul\r\n\r\noverhaul\r\n= 全面检修 / 彻底改革\r\n\r\n语气通常比 revamp 更重。\r\n\r\nrevamp\r\n= 大幅改进、重新设计\r\n\r\noverhaul\r\n= 从根本上彻底整顿\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nrevamp 不是“小优化”\r\n\r\n如果只是：\r\n\r\nfix a bug\r\nchange a button\r\nadjust a field\r\n\r\n一般不需要用 revamp。\r\n\r\nrevamp 可以直接接宾语\r\n\r\n✅ revamp the website\r\n\r\n✅ revamp the system\r\n\r\n✅ revamp the process\r\n\r\n名词也很常见\r\n\r\na complete revamp\r\n= 一次彻底改造\r\n\r\na major revamp\r\n= 一次大改版\r\n\r\n过去式很简单\r\n\r\nrevamp → revamped\r\n\r\nWe revamped the dashboard.\r\n我们重新改造了仪表盘。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 revamp 想成：\r\n\r\n“把旧东西重新包装、重新设计，让它焕然一新。”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nrevamp a website\r\n= 网站大改版\r\n\r\nrevamp a system\r\n= 系统全面改造\r\n\r\nrevamp a process\r\n= 流程全面优化\r\n\r\n最好记一句：\r\n\r\nWe’re revamping the whole system.\r\n我们正在全面改造整个系统。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f70acb677fc947eba4274197d6b8cd68.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-31 18:35:06',1,'2026-08-31 18:35:06'),(1552,21,39,'vocab','impulse','impulse','impulse','🎯 核心意思\r\nimpulse = 冲动；一时兴起；突然想做某事的念头\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n“还没怎么考虑，突然就很想做某件事。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n冲动；突然的念头\r\n\r\nI had a sudden impulse to call him.\r\n我突然有一种想给他打电话的冲动。\r\n\r\non impulse\r\n\r\n= 一时冲动；心血来潮\r\n\r\nI bought it on impulse.\r\n我是冲动之下买的。\r\n\r\nimpulse to do sth\r\n\r\n= 想做某事的冲动\r\n\r\nShe resisted the impulse to laugh.\r\n她忍住了想笑的冲动。\r\n\r\nact on impulse\r\n\r\n= 凭冲动行事\r\n\r\nTry not to act on impulse.\r\n尽量不要冲动行事。\r\n\r\nimpulse buy / impulse purchase\r\n\r\n= 冲动消费；冲动之下买的东西\r\n\r\nThat jacket was an impulse buy.\r\n那件夹克是我一时冲动买的。\r\n\r\n神经 / 电信号\r\n\r\nnerve impulse\r\n= 神经冲动\r\n\r\nelectrical impulse\r\n= 电信号','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nI bought the watch on impulse.\r\n我一时冲动买了这块手表。\r\n\r\nHe resisted the impulse to shout at her.\r\n他忍住了冲她喊叫的冲动。\r\n\r\nMy first impulse was to leave immediately.\r\n我的第一反应是马上离开。\r\n\r\nDon’t act on impulse. Think about it first.\r\n不要冲动行事，先想一想。\r\n\r\nOnline shopping can encourage impulse buying.\r\n网上购物可能会促进冲动消费。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI bought it on impulse.\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\non impulse\r\n= 一时冲动；心血来潮\r\n\r\n所以整句自然翻译为：\r\n\r\n我一时冲动就把它买了。\r\n\r\n再比如：\r\n\r\nHe had an impulse to leave.\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nan impulse to do sth\r\n= 想做某事的突然冲动\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n他突然很想离开。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nimpulse vs urge\r\n\r\nurge\r\n= 强烈的欲望；冲动\r\n\r\nI had a strong urge to laugh.\r\n我特别想笑。\r\n\r\nimpulse\r\n更强调“突然冒出来，而且可能没经过思考”。\r\n\r\nurge\r\n更强调“欲望很强”。\r\n\r\nimpulse vs instinct\r\n\r\ninstinct\r\n= 本能；直觉\r\n\r\nMy instinct told me something was wrong.\r\n我的直觉告诉我有点不对劲。\r\n\r\nimpulse\r\n= 突然想做某件事的冲动\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ninstinct = 本能告诉你什么\r\nimpulse = 突然想去做什么\r\n\r\nimpulse vs temptation\r\n\r\ntemptation\r\n= 诱惑\r\n\r\nI resisted the temptation to buy it.\r\n我忍住了买它的诱惑。\r\n\r\ntemptation 往往有：\r\n\r\n“知道可能不该做，但还是很想做”\r\n\r\n的感觉。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n高频搭配是：\r\n\r\non impulse\r\n= 一时冲动\r\n\r\nact on impulse\r\n= 冲动行事\r\n\r\nresist an impulse\r\n= 克制冲动\r\n\r\nan impulse to do sth\r\n= 想做某事的冲动\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ I impulse bought it.\r\n\r\n更自然：\r\n\r\n✅ I bought it on impulse.\r\n\r\n或者：\r\n\r\n✅ It was an impulse buy.\r\n\r\nimpulse 通常作名词\r\n\r\n不建议把它直接当普通动词使用。\r\n\r\n发音注意\r\n\r\n/ˈɪm.pʌls/\r\n\r\n最后是：\r\n\r\n/pʌls/\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n/pjuːls/\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象你在商店里看到一块表：\r\n\r\n“I want it!”\r\n\r\n还没仔细考虑价格、需不需要，就买了。\r\n\r\n这种：\r\n\r\n突然冒出来 → 马上想行动\r\n\r\n就是：\r\n\r\nimpulse = 冲动\r\n\r\n最值得记的三组：\r\n\r\non impulse\r\n一时冲动\r\n\r\nact on impulse\r\n冲动行事\r\n\r\nimpulse buy\r\n冲动消费。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b669d2b7ce21484f8c68712978adfc97.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-31 18:43:34',1,'2026-08-31 18:43:34'),(1553,21,40,'vocab','familiarity','familiarity','familiarity','🎯 核心意思\r\nfamiliarity = 熟悉；熟悉程度；了解程度\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n你因为经常接触某个人、事物、系统或领域，所以对它“很熟”。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nfamiliarity with sth\r\n= 对某事物的熟悉程度\r\n\r\nYou need some familiarity with Python.\r\n你需要对 Python 有一定的熟悉程度。\r\n\r\ngain familiarity with sth\r\n= 逐渐熟悉某事物\r\n\r\nIt takes time to gain familiarity with the system.\r\n熟悉这个系统需要一些时间。\r\n\r\n3.形容词 familiar\r\n= 熟悉的；熟知的\r\n\r\nI’m familiar with this framework.\r\n我熟悉这个框架。\r\n\r\n最常见结构：\r\n\r\nbe familiar with sth\r\n= 熟悉某事\r\n\r\n动词 familiarise sb/yourself with sth\r\n= 使某人熟悉……；让自己熟悉……\r\n\r\nYou should familiarise yourself with the new process.\r\n你应该熟悉一下新的流程。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nHis familiarity with the system helped him solve the problem quickly.\r\n他对这个系统的熟悉程度帮助他很快解决了问题。\r\n\r\nI have some familiarity with cloud platforms.\r\n我对云平台有一定了解。\r\n\r\nShe is very familiar with the reporting process.\r\n她非常熟悉这个报表流程。\r\n\r\nPlease familiarise yourself with the documentation before the meeting.\r\n请在会议之前熟悉一下文档。\r\n\r\nIt took me a few days to become familiar with the new interface.\r\n我花了几天时间才熟悉新的界面。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nFamiliarity with the codebase is important.\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nfamiliarity\r\n= 熟悉程度\r\n\r\nwith the codebase\r\n= 对代码库\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n熟悉代码库很重要。\r\n\r\n如果换成形容词：\r\n\r\nYou need to be familiar with the codebase.\r\n你需要熟悉这个代码库。\r\n\r\n如果换成动词：\r\n\r\nYou need to familiarise yourself with the codebase.\r\n你需要让自己熟悉这个代码库。\r\n\r\n这三个可以一起记：\r\n\r\nfamiliarity with sth\r\n= 对某事的熟悉程度\r\n\r\nbe familiar with sth\r\n= 熟悉某事\r\n\r\nfamiliarise yourself with sth\r\n= 让自己熟悉某事\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nfamiliarity vs knowledge\r\n\r\nknowledge\r\n= 知识；了解\r\n\r\n范围更广，可能是理论知识。\r\n\r\nfamiliarity\r\n= 熟悉程度\r\n\r\n更强调：\r\n\r\n“接触过、用过，所以熟悉。”\r\n\r\nI have knowledge of Java.\r\n我有 Java 方面的知识。\r\n\r\nI have familiarity with Java.\r\n我对 Java 比较熟悉。\r\n\r\nfamiliar vs similar\r\n\r\nfamiliar\r\n= 熟悉的\r\n\r\nThis name sounds familiar.\r\n这个名字听起来很熟悉。\r\n\r\nsimilar\r\n= 相似的\r\n\r\nThese two systems are similar.\r\n这两个系统很相似。\r\n\r\n这两个非常容易混。\r\n\r\nfamiliarise vs learn\r\n\r\nlearn\r\n= 学习\r\n\r\nfamiliarise yourself with sth\r\n= 先熟悉一下某事物\r\n\r\n后者不一定表示深入学习，只是让自己先了解、适应。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nfamiliar 后面通常接 with\r\n\r\n✅ I’m familiar with Python.\r\n❌ I’m familiar to Python.\r\n\r\n但如果主语是“某个东西”，可以用：\r\n\r\nThis voice is familiar to me.\r\n这个声音对我来说很熟悉。\r\n\r\nfamiliarity 也常接 with\r\n\r\n✅ familiarity with the system\r\n\r\nfamiliarise yourself with 是高频结构\r\n\r\n✅ familiarise yourself with the process\r\n\r\n英式拼写是：\r\n\r\nfamiliarise\r\n\r\n美式拼写：\r\n\r\nfamiliarize\r\n\r\n词形要一起记\r\n\r\nfamiliar\r\n= 熟悉的\r\n\r\nfamiliarity\r\n= 熟悉程度\r\n\r\nfamiliarise\r\n= 使熟悉\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把这三个词想成一个变化过程：\r\n\r\nfamiliar\r\n= 已经熟悉的\r\n\r\nfamiliarity\r\n= 熟悉程度\r\n\r\nfamiliarise\r\n= 让自己变熟悉\r\n\r\n最好直接记这一组：\r\n\r\nI’m familiar with the system.\r\n我熟悉这个系统。\r\n\r\nI have some familiarity with the system.\r\n我对这个系统有一定熟悉程度。\r\n\r\nI need to familiarise myself with the system.\r\n我需要熟悉一下这个系统。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a138c09f463f44cc9638419a79f9e404.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-31 19:00:57',1,'2026-08-31 19:00:57'),(1554,21,41,'vocab','nostalgia','nostalgia','nostalgia','🎯 核心意思\r\nnostalgia = 怀旧；乡愁；对过去美好时光的怀念\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n“想起过去的人、地方、生活或时光时，产生一种温暖但又有点伤感的情绪。”\r\n\r\n它通常带有一种：\r\n\r\nsweet + sad\r\n= 甜蜜又伤感\r\n\r\n的感觉。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n对过去时光的怀念\r\n\r\nThe old photos filled me with nostalgia.\r\n这些旧照片让我充满了怀旧之情。\r\n\r\n对童年、家乡的怀念\r\n\r\nShe felt a wave of nostalgia for her childhood.\r\n她突然非常怀念自己的童年。\r\n\r\n怀旧情绪\r\n\r\nThe film is full of nostalgia for the 1990s.\r\n这部电影充满了对 20 世纪 90 年代的怀旧情绪。\r\n\r\n常见结构\r\n\r\nnostalgia for + 人/地方/时期\r\n= 对……的怀念\r\n\r\na sense of nostalgia\r\n= 一种怀旧感\r\n\r\na wave of nostalgia\r\n= 一阵怀旧情绪\r\n\r\nfeel nostalgia for sth\r\n= 怀念某事物','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThis song always gives me a sense of nostalgia.\r\n这首歌总会让我产生一种怀旧感。\r\n\r\nHe felt nostalgia for his school days.\r\n他很怀念自己的学生时代。\r\n\r\nThe smell of the food brought back a wave of nostalgia.\r\n食物的味道勾起了他一阵怀旧之情。\r\n\r\nThe movie appeals to people’s nostalgia for the past.\r\n这部电影迎合了人们对过去的怀念。\r\n\r\nSeeing my old neighbourhood made me feel nostalgic.\r\n看到以前住过的街区让我感到很怀旧。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe song filled him with nostalgia.\r\n\r\n可以拆成：\r\n\r\nthe song\r\n= 这首歌\r\n\r\nfilled him with\r\n= 让他充满……\r\n\r\nnostalgia\r\n= 怀旧情绪\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这首歌让他充满了怀旧之情。\r\n\r\n这里的 nostalgia 不是简单的：\r\n\r\nmemory\r\n= 回忆\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\n“因为回忆过去而产生的情绪”。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nnostalgia vs memory\r\n\r\nmemory\r\n= 记忆；回忆\r\n\r\n只是“记得某件事”。\r\n\r\nI have good memories of school.\r\n我对学生时代有很多美好回忆。\r\n\r\nnostalgia\r\n= 因为这些回忆而产生的怀旧感\r\n\r\nI feel nostalgia for my school days.\r\n我很怀念学生时代。\r\n\r\nnostalgia vs homesickness\r\n\r\nhomesickness\r\n= 想家；思乡\r\n\r\n通常指人在外地时想念家乡或家人。\r\n\r\nnostalgia\r\n范围更广，可以怀念：\r\n\r\n童年\r\n旧时光\r\n老地方\r\n以前的生活方式\r\n\r\nnostalgia vs longing\r\n\r\nlonging\r\n= 渴望；思念\r\n\r\n更强调“强烈想要、想念”。\r\n\r\nnostalgia\r\n更强调“回忆过去带来的情绪”。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nnostalgia 是名词\r\n\r\n✅ a sense of nostalgia\r\n\r\n形容词是：\r\n\r\nnostalgic\r\n/nɒˈstæl.dʒɪk/\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI feel nostalgic.\r\n我感到很怀旧。\r\n\r\n常见介词是 for\r\n\r\n✅ nostalgia for the past\r\n\r\n✅ nostalgia for childhood\r\n\r\n不要把 nostalgia 只理解成“乡愁”\r\n\r\n它也可以是：\r\n\r\n怀旧\r\n怀念过去\r\n复古情怀\r\n\r\n发音注意\r\n\r\nnostalgia：\r\n\r\n/nɒˈstæl.dʒə/\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\nno-stal-GI-a\r\n\r\n重音在：\r\n\r\nSTAL\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 nostalgia 想成：\r\n\r\n看到一张旧照片\r\n→ 想起以前的生活\r\n→ 心里很温暖，但又有一点伤感\r\n\r\n这就是：\r\n\r\nnostalgia\r\n= 怀旧\r\n\r\n最好记这一组：\r\n\r\nnostalgia\r\n= 怀旧，名词\r\n\r\nnostalgic\r\n= 怀旧的，形容词\r\n\r\n一句最实用的：\r\n\r\nThis song makes me feel nostalgic.\r\n这首歌让我很怀旧。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/4f8f8d2722ce43848fe44ee1843d14e2.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-31 19:19:56',1,'2026-08-31 19:19:56'),(1555,21,42,'phrase','pull up','pull up','pull up','🎯 核心意思\r\npull up 常见有几个意思：\r\n\r\n停车；停下来\r\n\r\n调出、打开信息或页面\r\n\r\n把某人叫停 / 训斥\r\n\r\n把某物往上拉\r\n\r\n改善表现、追上差距\r\n\r\n最值得你记的，是口语和工作场景里这两个：\r\n\r\npull up a file/page/report\r\n= 调出、打开文件 / 页面 / 报表\r\n\r\npull up somewhere\r\n= 把车停到某处','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n车辆停下来\r\n\r\nA car pulled up outside the house.\r\n一辆车停在了房子外面。\r\n\r\nThe taxi pulled up at the entrance.\r\n出租车停在了入口处。\r\n\r\n调出、打开文件 / 页面 / 信息\r\n\r\nLet me pull up the report.\r\n我把报表调出来。\r\n\r\nCan you pull up the customer record?\r\n你能把客户记录调出来吗？\r\n\r\n这个用法在 IT、办公室、会议里非常常见。\r\n\r\n把某人叫住 / 批评某人\r\n\r\nThe manager pulled him up for being late.\r\n经理因为他迟到而批评了他。\r\n\r\n英式英语里：\r\n\r\npull sb up on/for sth\r\n= 指出某人的问题；批评某人\r\n\r\n把某物往上拉\r\n\r\nHe pulled up his sleeves.\r\n他把袖子往上拉了拉。\r\n\r\n改善、提升\r\n\r\nWe need to pull our performance up.\r\n我们需要把表现提升上来。\r\n\r\n这个用法没有前两个那么常见。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nLet me pull up the latest report.\r\n我把最新报表调出来。\r\n\r\nCan you pull up that file again?\r\n你能再把那个文件调出来吗？\r\n\r\nA black car pulled up beside us.\r\n一辆黑色汽车停在了我们旁边。\r\n\r\nThe teacher pulled him up for talking in class.\r\n老师因为他上课说话而批评了他。\r\n\r\nShe pulled up her sleeves and started working.\r\n她卷起袖子开始干活。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n比如你在工作里说：\r\n\r\nLet me pull up the code.\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\npull up\r\n= 调出来 / 打开\r\n\r\nthe code\r\n= 代码\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n我把代码调出来看一下。\r\n\r\n这比：\r\n\r\nLet me open the code.\r\n\r\n更有一种“我现在把它找出来并显示出来”的感觉。\r\n\r\n再比如：\r\n\r\nLet me pull up the dashboard.\r\n\r\n= 我把 dashboard 调出来。\r\n\r\n这个在演示、会议、技术沟通里很自然。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\npull up vs open\r\n\r\nopen\r\n= 打开\r\n\r\n最直接。\r\n\r\nOpen the file.\r\n打开文件。\r\n\r\npull up\r\n= 调出、找出来并显示\r\n\r\nLet me pull up the file.\r\n我把文件调出来。\r\n\r\npull up vs bring up\r\n\r\nbring up\r\n常见意思很多：\r\n\r\n提起话题\r\n养育\r\n调出某个界面（在某些语境里也可以）\r\n\r\n但在电脑场景里：\r\n\r\npull up a report/page/file\r\n\r\n通常更自然地表示：\r\n\r\n“把它调出来给大家看”。\r\n\r\npull up vs stop\r\n\r\nstop\r\n= 停止\r\n\r\npull up\r\n用于车时常表示：\r\n\r\n把车开到某处然后停下。\r\n\r\nThe car pulled up outside.\r\n车停在外面了。\r\n\r\npull up vs pull over\r\n\r\npull over\r\n= 靠边停车\r\n\r\n通常是主动把车开到路边停下。\r\n\r\npull up\r\n= 车停到某处，不一定强调靠边。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\npull up 不只有“往上拉”\r\n\r\n在工作场景里：\r\n\r\npull up a report\r\npull up a file\r\npull up a record\r\n\r\n都非常常见。\r\n\r\n车辆语境里可以直接不及物\r\n\r\n✅ A car pulled up.\r\n\r\n= 一辆车停下来了。\r\n\r\n代词的位置\r\n\r\n如果表示“把某物调出来”：\r\n\r\n✅ pull it up\r\n❌ pull up it\r\n\r\npull sb up 是另外一个意思\r\n\r\npull sb up\r\n= 叫住某人 / 指出某人的问题\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nHe was pulled up for being rude.\r\n他因为无礼被批评了。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 pull up 想成：\r\n\r\n“把东西拉到你眼前”\r\n\r\n文件 → 拉到屏幕上\r\n= 调出来\r\n\r\n车 → 拉到你面前停下\r\n= 停车\r\n\r\n袖子 → 往上拉\r\n= 卷起来\r\n\r\n所以最值得记的两个：\r\n\r\nLet me pull up the report.\r\n我把报表调出来。\r\n\r\nA car pulled up outside.\r\n一辆车停在了外面。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a7e16bb7a87e4cc3bba0cfb545e91e26.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-31 19:40:36',1,'2026-08-31 19:40:36'),(1556,21,43,'vocab','compose','compose','compose','🎯 核心意思\r\ncompose 常见有几个核心意思：\r\n\r\n创作；作曲；写作\r\n\r\n组成；构成\r\n\r\n使自己镇定下来\r\n\r\n编写、起草（邮件、消息、文本等）','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n创作音乐\r\n\r\nMozart composed many famous works.\r\n莫扎特创作了许多著名作品。\r\n\r\n写作、起草文字\r\n\r\nShe composed a short email to the client.\r\n她给客户写了一封简短的邮件。\r\n\r\n这个用法比较正式。\r\n\r\nbe composed of\r\n\r\n= 由……组成\r\n\r\nThe team is composed of five engineers.\r\n这个团队由五名工程师组成。\r\n\r\ncompose yourself\r\n\r\n= 让自己冷静下来；镇定下来\r\n\r\nHe took a moment to compose himself before speaking.\r\n他在讲话前花了一会儿让自己冷静下来。\r\n\r\n在软件/UI 中“撰写、编辑”\r\n\r\ncompose a message\r\n= 撰写消息\r\n\r\ncompose an email\r\n= 写邮件\r\n\r\n很多邮件应用里的 Compose 按钮就是：\r\n\r\n“写邮件 / 新建邮件”。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nHe composed the music for the film.\r\n他为这部电影创作了音乐。\r\n\r\nI need to compose a reply to this email.\r\n我需要写一封回复邮件。\r\n\r\nThe committee is composed of representatives from several departments.\r\n这个委员会由多个部门的代表组成。\r\n\r\nShe paused for a moment to compose herself.\r\n她停了一会儿，让自己镇定下来。\r\n\r\nPlease compose a short message explaining the issue.\r\n请写一条简短消息说明这个问题。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe system is composed of three modules.\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nis composed of\r\n= 由……组成\r\n\r\nthree modules\r\n= 三个模块\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这个系统由三个模块组成。\r\n\r\n这是技术文档里非常常见的结构。\r\n\r\n再比如：\r\n\r\nLet me compose a quick reply.\r\n\r\n这里 compose = write / draft\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n我来快速写个回复。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\ncompose vs write\r\n\r\nwrite\r\n= 写\r\n\r\n最普通、最常用。\r\n\r\nI wrote an email.\r\n我写了一封邮件。\r\n\r\ncompose\r\n= 撰写、组织文字\r\n\r\n语气稍正式，而且有“认真组织内容”的感觉。\r\n\r\nI composed a formal response.\r\n我起草了一份正式回复。\r\n\r\ncompose vs consist of\r\n\r\nbe composed of\r\n= 由……组成\r\n\r\nThe system is composed of several services.\r\n\r\nconsist of\r\n= 由……组成\r\n\r\nThe system consists of several services.\r\n\r\n意思非常接近。\r\n\r\n注意：\r\n\r\n✅ be composed of\r\n\r\n✅ consist of\r\n\r\ncompose vs create\r\n\r\ncreate\r\n= 创建、创造\r\n\r\n范围很广。\r\n\r\ncompose\r\n更常用于：\r\n\r\nmusic\r\ntext\r\nmessages\r\nformal writing\r\n\r\ncompose yourself vs calm down\r\n\r\ncalm down\r\n= 冷静下来\r\n\r\n更口语。\r\n\r\nCompose yourself.\r\n= 镇定下来。\r\n\r\n更正式，也常用于某人情绪比较激动的场景。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n“由……组成”要用被动\r\n\r\n✅ The team is composed of five people.\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ The team composes of five people.\r\n\r\ncompose 直接作“组成”时，主语通常是组成部分\r\n\r\nFive engineers compose the team.\r\n五名工程师组成这个团队。\r\n\r\n但这种说法不如：\r\n\r\nThe team is composed of five engineers.\r\n\r\n常见。\r\n\r\n不要和 comprise 混淆\r\n\r\nbe composed of\r\n= 由……组成\r\n\r\ncomprise\r\n= 包括；由……组成\r\n\r\nThe system comprises three modules.\r\n\r\ncompose yourself 很值得记\r\n\r\n= 镇定下来\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n可以把 compose 想成：\r\n\r\ncom = together\r\npose = put\r\n\r\n→ 把东西放到一起\r\n→ 组织起来\r\n\r\n所以可以发展出：\r\n\r\n把音符组织起来\r\n→ 作曲\r\n\r\n把文字组织起来\r\n→ 写作\r\n\r\n把成员组织起来\r\n→ 组成\r\n\r\n把情绪重新组织好\r\n→ 镇定下来\r\n\r\n最值得记四个：\r\n\r\ncompose music\r\n= 作曲\r\n\r\ncompose an email\r\n= 撰写邮件\r\n\r\nbe composed of\r\n= 由……组成\r\n\r\ncompose yourself\r\n= 让自己镇定下来','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e4590998d87f4fbd8045c701006c5ed8.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-31 19:50:19',1,'2026-08-31 19:50:19'),(1557,21,44,'vocab','determined','determined','determined','🎯 核心意思\r\ndetermined 最常见有两个意思：\r\n\r\n坚定的；有决心的\r\n\r\n被确定的；由……决定的\r\n\r\n所以一定要看语境。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n坚定的；下定决心的\r\n\r\nShe is determined to succeed.\r\n她下定决心要成功。\r\n\r\n最常见结构：\r\n\r\nbe determined to do sth\r\n= 决心做某事\r\n\r\n坚决的；意志坚定的\r\n\r\nHe gave me a determined look.\r\n他给了我一个坚定的眼神。\r\n\r\n被确定的；由……决定的\r\n\r\nThe final price is determined by demand.\r\n最终价格由需求决定。\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\nbe determined by sth\r\n= 由……决定\r\n\r\n已经查明 / 确定\r\n\r\nThe cause of the problem has not yet been determined.\r\n问题的原因还没有被确定。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nI’m determined to finish this project on time.\r\n我下定决心要按时完成这个项目。\r\n\r\nShe was determined not to give up.\r\n她坚决不放弃。\r\n\r\nHe is a very determined person.\r\n他是一个意志非常坚定的人。\r\n\r\nThe outcome is largely determined by your preparation.\r\n结果很大程度上取决于你的准备。\r\n\r\nThe exact cause has not been determined yet.\r\n确切原因尚未查明。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nHe was determined to prove them wrong.\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nwas determined to\r\n= 下定决心要……\r\n\r\nprove them wrong\r\n= 证明他们错了\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n他下定决心要证明他们错了。\r\n\r\n再比如：\r\n\r\nThe value is determined by the system.\r\n\r\n这里 determined 不是“坚定的”，而是 determine 的过去分词：\r\n\r\nbe determined by\r\n= 由……决定\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这个值由系统决定。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\ndetermined vs decisive\r\n\r\ndetermined\r\n= 有决心的；坚定的\r\n\r\n强调“不轻易放弃”。\r\n\r\nShe is determined to win.\r\n她下定决心要赢。\r\n\r\ndecisive\r\n= 果断的\r\n\r\n强调做决定快、明确。\r\n\r\nHe is a decisive leader.\r\n他是一位果断的领导者。\r\n\r\ndetermined vs persistent\r\n\r\npersistent\r\n= 坚持不懈的\r\n\r\n强调持续做、不放弃。\r\n\r\ndetermined\r\n更强调内心已经下定决心。\r\n\r\ndetermined vs decide\r\n\r\ndecide\r\n= 决定\r\n\r\nI decided to leave.\r\n我决定离开。\r\n\r\nbe determined to\r\n= 下定决心\r\n\r\nI’m determined to leave.\r\n我已经铁了心要离开。\r\n\r\n后者语气明显更强。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n高频结构：\r\n\r\n✅ be determined to do sth\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n❌ be determined doing sth\r\n\r\ndetermined 和 determine 不一样\r\n\r\ndetermine\r\n= 动词：决定；确定\r\n\r\ndetermined\r\n= 形容词：坚定的\r\n\r\n也可以是过去分词：\r\n\r\nbe determined by\r\n= 由……决定\r\n\r\ndetermine 的名词形式：\r\n\r\ndetermination\r\n= 决心；坚定\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nShe showed great determination.\r\n她表现出了很强的决心。\r\n\r\n发音注意\r\n\r\ndetermined：\r\n\r\n/dɪˈtɜː.mɪnd/\r\n\r\n不是把最后读成：\r\n\r\n/maɪnd/\r\n\r\n这里是：\r\n\r\n-mined /mɪnd/\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n记两条线：\r\n\r\ndetermine\r\n= 决定 / 确定\r\n\r\ndetermined\r\n= 已经决定好了\r\n→ 内心坚定\r\n→ 下定决心的\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nI’m determined to do it.\r\n= 我已经决定好了，我一定要做。\r\n\r\n最值得记的两个结构：\r\n\r\nbe determined to do sth\r\n= 下定决心做某事\r\n\r\nbe determined by sth\r\n= 由某事决定','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e25dcfbbd0d44f7e887a4f91afd4cd89.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-31 19:53:53',1,'2026-08-31 19:53:53'),(1558,21,45,'phrase','keep sth under control','keep sth under control','keep sth under control','🎯 核心意思\r\nkeep sth under control = 控制住某事；使某事保持在可控范围内；防止某事失控\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n不是让问题完全消失，而是让它：\r\n\r\n不恶化\r\n不超出范围\r\n仍然可以管理','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n控制问题 / 风险\r\n\r\nWe need to keep the situation under control.\r\n我们需要把局面控制住。\r\n\r\n控制成本 / 开支\r\n\r\nThe company is trying to keep costs under control.\r\n公司正在努力控制成本。\r\n\r\n控制情绪\r\n\r\nHe struggled to keep his anger under control.\r\n他努力控制自己的怒火。\r\n\r\n控制疾病、火势、感染等\r\n\r\nFirefighters managed to keep the fire under control.\r\n消防员设法控制住了火势。\r\n\r\n控制系统负载 / 技术问题\r\n\r\nWe need to keep memory usage under control.\r\n我们需要把内存使用量控制在合理范围内。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThe situation is now under control.\r\n现在局势已经得到控制。\r\n\r\nWe need to keep spending under control.\r\n我们需要控制开支。\r\n\r\nShe managed to keep her emotions under control.\r\n她设法控制住了自己的情绪。\r\n\r\nThe team is working to keep the backlog under control.\r\n团队正在努力控制积压任务的数量。\r\n\r\nBetter monitoring helps keep system failures under control.\r\n更好的监控有助于把系统故障控制在可控范围内。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe need to keep the workload under control.\r\n\r\n可以拆成：\r\n\r\nkeep\r\n= 保持\r\n\r\nthe workload\r\n= 工作量\r\n\r\nunder control\r\n= 在控制之下\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n我们需要把工作量控制在合理范围内。\r\n\r\n这里的重点不是：\r\n\r\nreduce the workload to zero\r\n把工作量降到零\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\nmake sure it doesn’t become unmanageable\r\n确保它不会多到无法处理。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nkeep sth under control vs control sth\r\n\r\ncontrol sth\r\n= 控制某事\r\n\r\n更直接。\r\n\r\nWe need to control costs.\r\n我们需要控制成本。\r\n\r\nkeep sth under control\r\n= 让某事持续保持可控\r\n\r\nWe need to keep costs under control.\r\n我们需要持续把成本控制在合理范围内。\r\n\r\nkeep sth under control vs keep sth in check\r\n\r\nkeep sth in check\r\n= 抑制；限制；防止增长过快\r\n\r\n和 under control 很接近。\r\n\r\nWe need to keep inflation in check.\r\n我们需要遏制通货膨胀。\r\n\r\nkeep sth under control\r\n更强调“总体还在掌控之中”。\r\n\r\nkeep sth under control vs manage sth\r\n\r\nmanage sth\r\n= 管理 / 应付某事\r\n\r\n范围更广。\r\n\r\nkeep sth under control\r\n强调：\r\n\r\n别让它失控。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n固定结构：\r\n\r\n✅ keep sth under control\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n❌ keep sth under the control\r\n\r\n一般不加 the。\r\n\r\nbe under control 和 keep sth under control 要区分\r\n\r\nThe fire is under control.\r\n火势已经得到控制。\r\n\r\nWe need to keep the fire under control.\r\n我们需要继续控制住火势。\r\n\r\n常见宾语非常多\r\n\r\nkeep costs under control\r\n控制成本\r\n\r\nkeep emotions under control\r\n控制情绪\r\n\r\nkeep the situation under control\r\n控制局势\r\n\r\nkeep traffic under control\r\n控制交通\r\n\r\nkeep risks under control\r\n控制风险\r\n\r\n过去式：\r\n\r\nkeep → kept\r\n\r\nThey kept the situation under control.\r\n他们控制住了局面。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 under control 想成：\r\n\r\n某件事被压在“控制范围”里面，没有跑出去。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nkeep sth under control\r\n= 一直把它压在可控范围里\r\n→ 控制住\r\n→ 不让它失控\r\n\r\n最好记三句：\r\n\r\nKeep it under control.\r\n把它控制住。\r\n\r\nWe need to keep costs under control.\r\n我们需要控制成本。\r\n\r\nThe situation is under control.\r\n局势已经得到控制。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/194b4f0b17f44920b0c039d134aa8bf4.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-31 21:33:31',1,'2026-08-31 21:33:31'),(1559,21,46,'vocab','prior','prior','prior','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nprior 最核心的感觉就是：\r\n\r\n“在……之前的 / 先前的 / 优先的”\r\n\r\n日常和工作场景里，最值得掌握的是：\r\n\r\nprior + 名词 = 之前的、先前的\r\nprior to + 名词 / 动名词 = 在……之前','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nprior = 先前的，之前的\r\n\r\n通常放在名词前。\r\n\r\nprior experience\r\n先前的经验 / 相关经验\r\n\r\nprior knowledge\r\n先验知识 / 事先已有的知识\r\n\r\nprior approval\r\n事先批准\r\n\r\nprior notice\r\n提前通知\r\n\r\nprior agreement\r\n事先达成的协议\r\n\r\n例：\r\nYou don’t need any prior experience.\r\n你不需要任何先前经验。\r\n\r\nThis feature worked properly in the prior version.\r\n这个功能在之前的版本中运行正常。\r\n\r\nprior to = 在……之前\r\n\r\n这是非常常见的正式表达，相当于 before。\r\n\r\nprior to + 名词\r\n\r\nPrior to the meeting, I reviewed the report.\r\n开会之前，我看了一遍报告。\r\n\r\nprior to + doing sth\r\n\r\nPrior to deploying the application, we ran several tests.\r\n在部署应用程序之前，我们进行了几轮测试。\r\n\r\n工作汇报、技术文档中很好用。\r\n\r\nprior = 优先于……的、更重要的\r\n\r\n这个意思有，但现代日常英语里没有前两个常见。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nSafety has a prior claim on our attention.\r\n安全问题应优先得到我们的关注。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nI had no prior experience with Python.\r\n我以前没有 Python 方面的经验。\r\n\r\nPlease give us prior notice if you need to cancel the meeting.\r\n如果你需要取消会议，请提前通知我们。\r\n\r\nWe need prior approval before making changes to the database.\r\n修改数据库之前，我们需要事先批准。\r\n\r\nPrior to processing the file, the system checks its status.\r\n在处理文件之前，系统会检查文件状态。\r\n\r\nThe issue had already occurred in a prior release.\r\n这个问题在之前的版本中就已经出现过。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n如果你在技术文档里看到：\r\n\r\nPrior to processing the file, we check whether it has already been processed.\r\n\r\n可以拆成：\r\n\r\nPrior to processing the file\r\n= 在处理文件之前\r\n\r\nwe check whether...\r\n= 我们检查是否……\r\n\r\n这里 prior to processing 比 before processing 更正式，很适合：\r\n\r\n技术文档\r\n\r\n工作汇报\r\n\r\n项目说明\r\n\r\n正式邮件\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nprior vs previous\r\n\r\n两者都可以表示“之前的”。\r\n\r\nprevious 更普通、更日常：\r\n\r\nthe previous version\r\n上一个版本\r\n\r\nthe previous meeting\r\n上一次会议\r\n\r\nprior 更正式，而且经常强调“在某件事情发生之前已经存在”：\r\n\r\nprior experience\r\n先前经验\r\n\r\nprior approval\r\n事先批准\r\n\r\nprior knowledge\r\n已有知识\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\n✅ previous version\r\n非常自然\r\n\r\n✅ prior version\r\n也可以，但更书面\r\n\r\n✅ prior approval\r\n非常自然\r\n\r\n⚠️ previous approval\r\n通常不是你想表达的“事先批准”。\r\n\r\nprior to vs before\r\n\r\n意思基本一样：\r\n\r\nPrior to deployment, we tested the system.\r\n= Before deployment, we tested the system.\r\n\r\n区别：\r\n\r\nbefore → 日常口语、书面都自然\r\nprior to → 更正式、更书面\r\n\r\n口语里一般优先用：\r\n\r\nBefore we deploy it, we need to test it.\r\n\r\n技术文档中则可以写：\r\n\r\nPrior to deployment, the system must be tested.\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nprior 本身通常放在名词前\r\n\r\n✅ prior experience\r\n\r\n✅ prior knowledge\r\n\r\n不太说：\r\n\r\n❌ My experience is prior.\r\n\r\n表示“在……之前”要用 prior to\r\n\r\n✅ prior to the meeting\r\n\r\n✅ prior to deployment\r\n\r\n✅ prior to making changes\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ prior the meeting\r\n\r\nprior to 后面如果接动词，要用 -ing\r\n\r\n✅ prior to starting the service\r\n❌ prior to start the service\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 prior 直接记成：\r\n\r\nprior = “排在前面的”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nprior experience\r\n→ 在现在这份工作“前面”的经验\r\n\r\nprior approval\r\n→ 做事情“前面”就要拿到的批准\r\n\r\nprior to deployment\r\n→ 排在部署“前面”\r\n\r\n最值得你记住的 5 个搭配：\r\n\r\nprior experience = 先前经验\r\nprior knowledge = 事先已有的知识\r\nprior approval = 事先批准\r\nprior notice = 提前通知\r\nprior to = 在……之前','/static/uploads/english_note_item/849cc5856405409ca42415541a0f6d22.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-31 22:05:32',1,'2026-08-31 22:05:32'),(1560,21,47,'phrase','bother with','bother with','bother with','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nbother with sth / doing sth 最常见的意思是：\r\n\r\n“费心去做…… / 麻烦去管…… / 为……操心”\r\n\r\n很多时候带有一种语气：\r\n\r\n“这件事值不值得我花时间、精力去做？”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nbother with sth\r\n= 费心处理某事 / 管某事\r\n\r\nDon’t bother with the old files.\r\n别费心处理那些旧文件了。\r\n\r\nI wouldn’t bother with that feature right now.\r\n我现在不会花时间去弄那个功能。\r\n\r\nbother with doing sth\r\n= 费心去做某事\r\n\r\nWhy bother with writing everything manually?\r\n为什么还要费劲手动写所有东西？\r\n\r\nYou don’t need to bother with restarting the server.\r\n你没必要费心重启服务器。\r\n\r\ncan’t be bothered with sth / doing sth\r\n= 懒得做 / 不想费那个劲\r\n\r\n这个很常见，尤其英式英语。\r\n\r\nI can’t be bothered with cooking tonight.\r\n我今晚懒得做饭。\r\n\r\nHe couldn’t be bothered with checking the details.\r\n他懒得检查那些细节。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nDon’t bother with the report today.\r\n今天别费心弄报告了。\r\n\r\nWhy bother with this complicated process?\r\n为什么还要费劲走这么复杂的流程？\r\n\r\nYou don’t need to bother with installing it manually.\r\n你没必要手动安装它。\r\n\r\nI can’t be bothered with arguing about this.\r\n我懒得为这个争论。\r\n\r\nWe shouldn’t bother with optimizing this part yet.\r\n我们暂时没必要花精力优化这一部分。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nDon’t bother with checking the old records.\r\n\r\n可以理解为：\r\n\r\nDon’t bother\r\n= 别费心 / 没必要折腾\r\n\r\nwith checking the old records\r\n= 去检查旧记录\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n别费心检查旧记录了。\r\n\r\n这里不是说“打扰”，而是说：\r\n\r\n“别浪费时间和精力去做这件事。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nbother with vs bother to do\r\n\r\n两者很接近：\r\n\r\nbother with + 名词 / doing\r\n\r\nDon’t bother with fixing it.\r\n别费心修了。\r\n\r\nbother to + 动词原形\r\n\r\nDon’t bother to fix it.\r\n别费心去修了。\r\n\r\n意思基本相同。\r\n\r\n但口语中：\r\n\r\nWhy bother?\r\n非常常见。\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n“何必呢？”\r\n“何必费那个劲？”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nIt’ll be deleted tomorrow anyway. Why bother?\r\n反正明天就会删掉，何必折腾呢？\r\n\r\nbother with vs deal with\r\n\r\ndeal with\r\n= 处理、应对\r\n\r\nbother with\r\n= 强调“花不花精力去处理”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI’ll deal with the issue tomorrow.\r\n我明天处理这个问题。\r\n\r\nDon’t bother with the issue for now.\r\n现在先别费心管这个问题。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nbother with 后面可以接名词\r\n\r\n✅ bother with the details\r\n\r\n✅ bother with this problem\r\n\r\n接动作时用 doing\r\n\r\n✅ bother with checking it\r\n❌ bother with check it\r\n\r\nbother 单独使用时也可以表示“打扰”\r\n\r\nSorry to bother you.\r\n抱歉打扰你。\r\n\r\n这里和 bother with 的意思不一样。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 bother with 想成：\r\n\r\n“值不值得为这件事费劲？”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nDon’t bother with it.\r\n= 别管它了 / 别费劲了\r\n\r\nWhy bother with it?\r\n= 何必折腾它？\r\n\r\ncan’t be bothered with it\r\n= 懒得管它\r\n\r\n最值得记的三个表达：\r\n\r\nbother with sth = 费心处理某事\r\nbother with doing sth = 费心做某事\r\nWhy bother? = 何必呢？\r\n\r\nSources','/static/uploads/english_note_item/62e18725d4494bfcb55897c498bee563.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-31 22:08:57',1,'2026-08-31 22:08:57'),(1561,21,48,'phrase','wrap my head around sth','wrap my head around sth','wrap my head around sth','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nwrap my head around sth\r\n= 理解某件复杂、奇怪或难以接受的事情\r\n= 搞明白 / 想明白 / 理解透\r\n\r\n它通常不是普通的“知道”，而是强调：\r\n\r\n“这个东西有点复杂，我得花点脑子才能真正理解。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n理解复杂的概念\r\n\r\nI’m still trying to wrap my head around this new system.\r\n我还在努力搞明白这个新系统。\r\n\r\nI can’t quite wrap my head around how this algorithm works.\r\n我还是不太能理解这个算法到底是怎么运作的。\r\n\r\n理解令人惊讶、难以置信的事情\r\n\r\nI still can’t wrap my head around the fact that he quit.\r\n我还是无法理解他居然辞职了这件事。\r\n\r\nIt’s hard to wrap your head around how much the company has changed.\r\n很难想象这家公司变化竟然这么大。\r\n\r\n理解一个复杂情况\r\n\r\nGive me a minute. I’m trying to wrap my head around the problem.\r\n给我一分钟，我正在理清这个问题。\r\n\r\nThere are so many moving parts that it’s hard to wrap my head around everything.\r\n这里涉及的环节太多了，很难一下子全部理清。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nI’m trying to wrap my head around the new architecture.\r\n我正在努力理解这个新的系统架构。\r\n\r\nIt took me a while to wrap my head around the workflow.\r\n我花了一段时间才把这个工作流程搞明白。\r\n\r\nI can’t wrap my head around why the service keeps crashing.\r\n我实在想不明白为什么这个服务一直崩溃。\r\n\r\nShe quickly wrapped her head around the problem.\r\n她很快就理解了这个问题。\r\n\r\nI’m still wrapping my head around all these changes.\r\n我还在消化、理解这些变化。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI can’t wrap my head around how this works.\r\n\r\n拆开看：\r\n\r\nI can’t\r\n= 我没办法\r\n\r\nwrap my head around\r\n= 把脑子“绕着它包起来”\r\n→ 形象地表示“彻底搞懂”\r\n\r\nhow this works\r\n= 它是怎么运作的\r\n\r\n整句自然翻译：\r\n\r\n我还是搞不懂这个东西是怎么运作的。\r\n\r\n这里非常口语，比：\r\n\r\nI don’t understand how this works.\r\n\r\n更有一种：\r\n\r\n“我已经在努力想了，但还是没搞明白。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nwrap my head around vs understand\r\n\r\nunderstand\r\n= 普通的“理解”\r\n\r\nI understand the problem.\r\n我理解这个问题。\r\n\r\nwrap my head around\r\n= 强调这个东西比较复杂、反直觉，需要努力理解\r\n\r\nI’m trying to wrap my head around the problem.\r\n我正在努力把这个问题想明白。\r\n\r\n所以语气上：\r\n\r\nunderstand → 中性\r\nwrap my head around → 更口语、更有画面感，强调“费脑子”\r\n\r\nwrap my head around vs figure out\r\n\r\nfigure out\r\n= 找到答案 / 搞清楚怎么解决\r\n\r\nwrap my head around\r\n= 理解这个东西本身\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI’m trying to wrap my head around the system.\r\n我在努力理解这个系统。\r\n\r\nI’m trying to figure out why it failed.\r\n我在想办法弄清楚它为什么失败。\r\n\r\n一个偏“理解”，一个偏“找到答案”。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n常见结构是：\r\n\r\nwrap one’s head around + 名词\r\n\r\n✅ wrap my head around the problem\r\n\r\n✅ wrap my head around this concept\r\n\r\n后面也可以接从句\r\n\r\n✅ wrap my head around how it works\r\n\r\n✅ wrap my head around why this happened\r\n\r\none’s 要根据主语变化\r\n\r\nI → my\r\nyou → your\r\nhe → his\r\nshe → her\r\nwe → our\r\nthey → their\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nShe can’t wrap her head around it.\r\n她想不明白。\r\n\r\n很常见的否定形式\r\n\r\nI can’t wrap my head around it.\r\n我实在想不明白。\r\n\r\n这个比肯定形式还常见。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把它想象成：\r\n\r\n你的脑袋要“绕住”一个复杂的问题。\r\n\r\nwrap = 包住、裹住\r\nhead = 脑袋\r\naround = 围绕\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nwrap your head around sth\r\n≈ 用脑子把它整个“包起来”\r\n→ 彻底理解它\r\n\r\n最值得记住的三个句子：\r\n\r\nI can’t wrap my head around it.\r\n我实在想不明白。\r\n\r\nI’m trying to wrap my head around this.\r\n我正在努力理解这个。\r\n\r\nIt took me a while to wrap my head around it.\r\n我花了一段时间才把它搞明白。\r\n\r\nSources','/static/uploads/english_note_item/4f81317771a1401290a7a71466377482.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-31 22:14:56',1,'2026-08-31 22:14:56'),(1562,21,49,'phrase','move the needle','move the needle','move the needle','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nmove the needle\r\n= 产生明显影响\r\n= 真正推动结果\r\n= 让关键指标发生变化\r\n\r\n这个表达很常用于：\r\n\r\n工作\r\n\r\n商业\r\n\r\n产品\r\n\r\n营销\r\n\r\n项目管理\r\n\r\n数据分析\r\n\r\n它强调的不是“做了点事情”，而是：\r\n\r\n“这件事有没有真正带来可衡量的变化？”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n对结果产生明显影响\r\n\r\nThis change probably won’t move the needle.\r\n这个改动可能不会带来什么明显效果。\r\n\r\nWe need something that can really move the needle.\r\n我们需要一些真正能推动结果的措施。\r\n\r\n推动关键指标\r\n\r\nThe new campaign helped move the needle on sales.\r\n这次新营销活动确实推动了销售增长。\r\n\r\nThese optimizations could move the needle on performance.\r\n这些优化可能会明显提升性能。\r\n\r\n商业或项目中的“真正有价值的进展”\r\n\r\nWe’ve made a lot of small improvements, but none of them really moved the needle.\r\n我们做了很多小改进，但没有一个真正带来明显变化。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThis feature is useful, but it won’t move the needle.\r\n这个功能有用，但它不会带来实质性的变化。\r\n\r\nWe need to focus on changes that move the needle.\r\n我们需要专注于那些真正能推动结果的改动。\r\n\r\nAdding more workers could move the needle on processing speed.\r\n增加更多 worker 可能会明显提升处理速度。\r\n\r\nThe redesign didn’t really move the needle on user engagement.\r\n这次重新设计并没有真正提升用户参与度。\r\n\r\nLowering the processing time from five minutes to two minutes would definitely move the needle.\r\n把处理时间从五分钟降到两分钟肯定会产生明显影响。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThis optimization won’t move the needle much.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThis optimization\r\n= 这项优化\r\n\r\nwon’t move the needle\r\n= 不会让“指标指针”明显移动\r\n\r\nmuch\r\n= 太多 / 明显地\r\n\r\n整句自然翻译：\r\n\r\n这个优化不会带来太明显的提升。\r\n\r\n这里的 needle 可以想象成仪表盘上的“指针”。\r\n\r\n如果一个变化太小：\r\n\r\n指针几乎不动。\r\n\r\n如果一个变化很大：\r\n\r\n指针明显移动。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nmove the needle\r\n→ 真正改变结果或指标。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nmove the needle vs make a difference\r\n\r\nmake a difference\r\n= 产生影响，范围非常广\r\n\r\nThis change could make a difference.\r\n这个变化可能会有帮助。\r\n\r\nmove the needle\r\n= 更强调“可衡量、明显的结果变化”\r\n\r\nThis change could really move the needle on performance.\r\n这个变化可能会真正明显提升性能。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nmake a difference → 更通用\r\nmove the needle → 更商业化、更偏指标和结果\r\n\r\nmove the needle vs improve\r\n\r\nimprove\r\n= 改善、提高\r\n\r\nWe improved performance by 5%.\r\n我们的性能提高了 5%。\r\n\r\nmove the needle\r\n= 强调这个提升“够不够重要”\r\n\r\nA 1% improvement probably won’t move the needle.\r\n1% 的提升可能没什么实质意义。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n通常用 the needle\r\n\r\n✅ move the needle\r\n❌ move a needle\r\n\r\n很常搭配 on\r\n\r\nmove the needle on + 某个指标\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nmove the needle on sales\r\n推动销售增长\r\n\r\nmove the needle on performance\r\n显著改善性能\r\n\r\nmove the needle on engagement\r\n提升用户参与度\r\n\r\n非常适合工作口语，但偏商业语境\r\n\r\n日常聊天里不是不能用，只是没有工作场景那么常见。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象一个仪表盘。\r\n\r\n如果你的改动没什么效果：\r\n\r\nneedle 几乎不动。\r\n\r\n如果真的有效：\r\n\r\nneedle 明显移动。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nmove the needle\r\n= 让指标指针动起来\r\n= 真正产生结果\r\n\r\n最值得记住的 3 个句子：\r\n\r\nThis won’t move the needle.\r\n这不会带来什么实质性变化。\r\n\r\nWe need something that can move the needle.\r\n我们需要真正有效的东西。\r\n\r\nThis could really move the needle on performance.\r\n这可能会真正明显提升性能。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ff43366855fe4721971294ad78cab2aa.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-08-31 22:21:18',1,'2026-08-31 22:21:18'),(1563,21,50,'phrase','be broadly referred to as','be broadly referred to as','be broadly referred to as','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nbe broadly referred to as\r\n= 被广泛称为……\r\n= 从大的分类上通常被称作……\r\n= 宽泛来说被归类为……\r\n\r\n这里 broadly 很关键。\r\n\r\n它不一定表示“所有人都这么叫”，更多时候表示：\r\n\r\n“不细分具体类别时，通常统一把它叫做……”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n被广泛称为……\r\n\r\nThese technologies are broadly referred to as artificial intelligence.\r\n这些技术通常被广泛称为人工智能。\r\n\r\nThis type of software is broadly referred to as middleware.\r\n这类软件通常被统称为中间件。\r\n\r\n从宽泛分类上被称为……\r\n\r\nA range of these behaviours can be broadly referred to as online abuse.\r\n这一系列行为可以宽泛地归类为网络滥用。\r\n\r\n这里 broadly 有：\r\n\r\n“严格来说里面可能有不同子类别，但总体上可以这么叫。”\r\n\r\n学术 / 技术 / 新闻中用于“统称”\r\n\r\n这类表达很常见：\r\n\r\nbe collectively referred to as\r\n= 被统称为\r\n\r\nbe commonly referred to as\r\n= 通常被称为\r\n\r\nbe broadly referred to as\r\n= 宽泛地称为 / 大体归类为','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThese systems are broadly referred to as AI-powered tools.\r\n这些系统通常被统称为 AI 驱动工具。\r\n\r\nThe entire process can be broadly referred to as document processing.\r\n整个流程可以宽泛地称为文档处理。\r\n\r\nThese problems are broadly referred to as performance issues.\r\n这些问题大体上可以归类为性能问题。\r\n\r\nServices such as AWS and Azure are broadly referred to as cloud platforms.\r\nAWS 和 Azure 这类服务通常被统称为云平台。\r\n\r\nThis category of attacks is broadly referred to as social engineering.\r\n这一类攻击通常被统称为社会工程攻击。\r\n\r\n📖 结构解析\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThese systems are broadly referred to as workflow engines.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThese systems\r\n= 这些系统\r\n\r\nare referred to as\r\n= 被称为\r\n\r\nbroadly\r\n= 从宽泛意义上 / 大体上\r\n\r\nworkflow engines\r\n= 工作流引擎\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这些系统大体上可以被称为工作流引擎。\r\n\r\n注意 refer to 在这里不是：\r\n\r\nrefer to = 提到 / 指的是\r\n\r\n而是这个结构：\r\n\r\nrefer to A as B\r\n= 把 A 称为 B\r\n\r\n主动：\r\n\r\nPeople refer to these systems as workflow engines.\r\n\r\n人们把这些系统称为工作流引擎。\r\n\r\n被动：\r\n\r\nThese systems are referred to as workflow engines.\r\n\r\n这些系统被称为工作流引擎。\r\n\r\n🆚 易混表达对比\r\n\r\nbe broadly referred to as vs be commonly referred to as\r\n\r\nbe commonly referred to as\r\n= 通常被称为\r\n\r\n更强调：\r\n\r\n“这个名称很常用。”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nNew Zealand is commonly referred to as NZ.\r\nNew Zealand 通常简称为 NZ。\r\n\r\nbe broadly referred to as\r\n= 宽泛地归类为 / 统称为\r\n\r\n更强调：\r\n\r\n“这个分类比较大，不追求特别精确。”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThese tools can be broadly referred to as AI tools.\r\n这些工具可以宽泛地统称为 AI 工具。\r\n\r\nbe broadly referred to as vs be collectively referred to as\r\n\r\ncollectively\r\n= 合在一起、作为一个整体\r\n\r\nThese components are collectively referred to as the processing layer.\r\n这些组件统称为处理层。\r\n\r\nbroadly\r\n= 从大的分类上说\r\n\r\nThese technologies are broadly referred to as machine learning.\r\n这些技术从宽泛意义上被称为机器学习。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n固定结构是：\r\n\r\nrefer to A as B\r\n\r\n✅ We refer to this process as extraction.\r\n\r\n被动：\r\n\r\n✅ This process is referred to as extraction.\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ This process is referred as extraction.\r\n\r\n必须有 to。\r\n\r\nas 后面接“名称 / 类别”\r\n\r\n✅ be referred to as a workflow engine\r\n\r\n✅ be referred to as document processing\r\n\r\nbroadly 不等于 simply “很多人”\r\n\r\nbroadly referred to as 往往强调：\r\n\r\n“从宽泛定义上这样叫。”\r\n\r\n如果你只是想说“大家通常这么叫”，commonly referred to as 往往更自然。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n直接把：\r\n\r\nrefer to A as B\r\n\r\n记成：\r\n\r\n“把 A 指作 / 称作 B”\r\n\r\n然后变被动：\r\n\r\nA is referred to as B\r\n= A 被称为 B\r\n\r\n再加 broadly：\r\n\r\nA is broadly referred to as B\r\n= A 从宽泛意义上被称为 B\r\n\r\n最值得记住的三个：\r\n\r\nbe referred to as\r\n= 被称为\r\n\r\nbe commonly referred to as\r\n= 通常被称为\r\n\r\nbe broadly referred to as\r\n= 宽泛地称为 / 大体归类为','/static/uploads/english_note_item/914e2df5f0d54b1085be31d221aded8a.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 19:29:51',1,'2026-09-01 19:29:51'),(1564,21,51,'phrase','point a finger at','point a finger at','point a finger at','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\npoint a finger at sb\r\n= 指责某人\r\n= 把责任推到某人身上\r\n\r\n它通常不是单纯“用手指着某人”，而是带有明显的：\r\n\r\n“责怪、归咎、认为某人有责任”\r\n\r\n这种感觉。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n指责某人\r\n\r\nIt’s easy to point a finger at someone after something goes wrong.\r\n事情出错之后，指责某个人很容易。\r\n\r\nDon’t point a finger at me.\r\n别怪到我头上。\r\n\r\n把责任归咎于某人\r\n\r\nPeople started pointing fingers at the management team.\r\n人们开始把责任归咎于管理团队。\r\n\r\n这里更常见的其实是复数：\r\n\r\npoint fingers at sb\r\n= 纷纷指责某人\r\n\r\n字面意思：用手指着某人\r\n\r\nHe pointed a finger at the man across the room.\r\n他用手指着房间另一边的那个男人。\r\n\r\n但如果没有具体动作场景，point a finger at 很容易让人理解成“指责”。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nWe shouldn’t point a finger at one person before we know what happened.\r\n在弄清楚发生了什么之前，我们不应该指责任何一个人。\r\n\r\nEveryone started pointing fingers at each other.\r\n大家开始互相指责。\r\n\r\nThe report didn’t point a finger at any individual employee.\r\n这份报告没有把责任归咎于任何一个员工。\r\n\r\nInstead of pointing fingers, we should focus on fixing the problem.\r\n与其互相指责，不如专注于解决问题。\r\n\r\nHe pointed a finger at the supplier for the delay.\r\n他把延误的责任归咎于供应商。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThey were quick to point a finger at the development team.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThey were quick to\r\n= 他们很快就……\r\n\r\npoint a finger at\r\n= 指责 / 归咎于\r\n\r\nthe development team\r\n= 开发团队\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n他们很快就把责任归咎于开发团队。\r\n\r\n这里不是说真的“用手指着开发团队”，而是：\r\n\r\n“出了问题以后马上怪开发团队。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\npoint a finger at vs blame\r\n\r\nblame sb\r\n= 直接责怪某人\r\n\r\nDon’t blame me.\r\n别怪我。\r\n\r\npoint a finger at sb\r\n= 更形象，强调“把矛头指向某人”\r\n\r\nDon’t point a finger at me.\r\n别把责任推到我头上。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nblame → 更直接、更普通\r\npoint a finger at → 更形象，有“指责、甩锅”的感觉\r\n\r\npoint a finger at vs accuse\r\n\r\naccuse sb of sth\r\n= 指控某人做了某事\r\n\r\nHe was accused of fraud.\r\n他被指控诈骗。\r\n\r\npoint a finger at\r\n= 不一定是正式指控，可能只是责怪\r\n\r\nPeople pointed fingers at him after the project failed.\r\n项目失败后，人们开始责怪他。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n很多时候复数更自然\r\n\r\n✅ point fingers at someone\r\n= 纷纷指责某人\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nEveryone was pointing fingers at everyone else.\r\n所有人都在互相甩锅。\r\n\r\npoint a finger at 后面接人或组织\r\n\r\n✅ point a finger at the manager\r\n\r\n✅ point a finger at the company\r\n\r\n如果你只是想说“用手指着”\r\n\r\n可以直接说：\r\n\r\npoint at sb / sth\r\n\r\nHe pointed at the screen.\r\n他指着屏幕。\r\n\r\n而：\r\n\r\npoint a finger at sb\r\n\r\n更容易带“责怪”的意味。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n直接想象一个人：\r\n\r\n👉 指着别人说：\r\n\r\n“It was your fault!”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\npoint a finger at sb\r\n= 手指指向谁\r\n= 责任也指向谁\r\n= 指责谁\r\n\r\n最值得记住的三个表达：\r\n\r\npoint a finger at sb\r\n= 指责某人\r\n\r\npoint fingers at sb\r\n= 纷纷指责某人\r\n\r\nstop pointing fingers\r\n= 别再互相指责了','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2427c2a95b2a424494328d1eefc05573.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 19:46:25',1,'2026-09-01 19:46:25'),(1565,21,52,'phrase','a small army of','a small army of','a small army of','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\na small army of + 人\r\n= 一大群…… / 一大批……\r\n\r\n它不是说真的“军队”，而是一个很形象的夸张表达：\r\n\r\n“人数多到像一支小军队一样。”\r\n\r\n通常用来强调：\r\n\r\n人很多\r\n\r\n分工明确\r\n\r\n一起忙着做某件事\r\n\r\n场面有点壮观','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n一大群人\r\n\r\nA small army of reporters was waiting outside.\r\n一大群记者在外面等着。\r\n\r\nA small army of volunteers helped clean up the park.\r\n一大批志愿者帮忙清理了公园。\r\n\r\n强调很多工作人员一起做事\r\n\r\nThe event required a small army of staff.\r\n这场活动需要一大批工作人员。\r\n\r\nIt took a small army of engineers to complete the project.\r\n完成这个项目动用了大量工程师。\r\n\r\n也可以接某类专业人员\r\n\r\na small army of lawyers\r\n一大批律师\r\n\r\na small army of technicians\r\n一大批技术人员\r\n\r\na small army of cleaners\r\n一大批清洁工\r\n\r\na small army of developers\r\n一大批开发人员','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nA small army of workers was brought in to finish the job.\r\n调来了一大批工人完成这项工作。\r\n\r\nThe company hired a small army of developers for the project.\r\n公司为这个项目雇了一大批开发人员。\r\n\r\nThere was a small army of journalists outside the courthouse.\r\n法院外面聚集着一大群记者。\r\n\r\nIt took a small army of people to organise the conference.\r\n组织这次会议需要一大帮人。\r\n\r\nA small army of technicians worked through the night.\r\n一大批技术人员通宵工作。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe launch was supported by a small army of engineers.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThe launch was supported by\r\n= 这次发布得到了……的支持\r\n\r\na small army of engineers\r\n= 一大批工程师\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这次发布背后有一大批工程师提供支持。\r\n\r\n这里 a small army of 很有画面感：\r\n\r\n不是两三个人，\r\n而是“乌泱泱一群人一起干活”。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\na small army of vs a large number of\r\n\r\na large number of\r\n= 大量的\r\n\r\n比较中性、客观。\r\n\r\nA large number of engineers worked on the project.\r\n大量工程师参与了这个项目。\r\n\r\na small army of\r\n= 一大群，带夸张和画面感\r\n\r\nA small army of engineers worked on the project.\r\n一大帮工程师参与了这个项目。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\na large number of → 中性\r\na small army of → 更生动、更口语化\r\n\r\na small army of vs an army of\r\n\r\nan army of\r\n= 大批、大群\r\n\r\na small army of\r\n= 一支“小型军队”那么多\r\n\r\n其实两者语气很接近。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nan army of volunteers\r\n一大批志愿者\r\n\r\na small army of volunteers\r\n一大批志愿者\r\n\r\nsmall 在这里并不是真的表示“少”，而是相对于真正的军队来说“小”，但人数还是很多。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n后面通常接复数名词\r\n\r\n✅ a small army of engineers\r\n\r\n✅ a small army of reporters\r\n\r\n不要按字面翻译成“小军队”\r\n\r\n在大多数语境中应该自然翻译成：\r\n\r\n“一大批”\r\n“一大群”\r\n“一大帮”\r\n\r\n常用于人，不太常用于普通物品\r\n\r\n最自然的是：\r\n\r\n✅ a small army of staff\r\n\r\n✅ a small army of lawyers\r\n\r\n✅ a small army of workers\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象一个办公室里突然来了几十个人：\r\n\r\n👨‍💻👩‍💻👨‍🔧👩‍🔧👨‍💻👩‍💻\r\n\r\n看起来就像：\r\n\r\na small army\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\na small army of people\r\n= 多到像一支小部队的人\r\n= 一大群人\r\n\r\n最值得记住的三个搭配：\r\n\r\na small army of workers\r\n= 一大批工人\r\n\r\na small army of engineers\r\n= 一大批工程师\r\n\r\na small army of volunteers\r\n= 一大批志愿者','/static/uploads/english_note_item/2ee981ea7eca4f84a805c0b28da6becc.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 19:48:34',1,'2026-09-01 19:48:34'),(1566,21,53,'phrase','be on its last legs','be on its last legs','be on its last legs','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nbe on its last legs\r\n= 快不行了\r\n= 快坏了 / 快撑不住了\r\n= 接近报废、结束或崩溃\r\n\r\n这个表达非常形象：\r\n\r\n“只剩最后一点支撑了。”\r\n\r\n常用来形容：\r\n\r\n机器快坏了\r\n\r\n设备快报废了\r\n\r\n系统快撑不住了\r\n\r\n生意快倒闭了\r\n\r\n某种制度、关系或组织快结束了','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n设备 / 机器快坏了\r\n\r\nMy laptop is on its last legs.\r\n我的笔记本电脑快不行了。\r\n\r\nThis old printer is on its last legs.\r\n这台旧打印机快报废了。\r\n\r\n系统 / 服务快撑不住了\r\n\r\nThe server is on its last legs.\r\n这台服务器快撑不住了。\r\n\r\nOur old system is on its last legs and needs to be replaced.\r\n我们的旧系统快不行了，需要更换。\r\n\r\n公司 / 生意 / 项目快结束了\r\n\r\nThe business was on its last legs before the new investment came in.\r\n在新投资进入之前，这家公司已经快撑不下去了。\r\n\r\nThe project is on its last legs.\r\n这个项目已经快走到头了。\r\n\r\n人非常疲惫、快撑不住了\r\n\r\n也可以形容人，但语气会比较重。\r\n\r\nAfter working all night, I was on my last legs.\r\n通宵工作之后，我已经累得快撑不住了。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nMy phone is on its last legs. I probably need a new one.\r\n我的手机快不行了，我可能得换一个新的。\r\n\r\nThe old database server is on its last legs.\r\n那台旧数据库服务器快撑不住了。\r\n\r\nThis washing machine has been on its last legs for months.\r\n这台洗衣机已经苟延残喘好几个月了。\r\n\r\nBy the end of the hike, we were all on our last legs.\r\n徒步结束时，我们所有人都累得快走不动了。\r\n\r\nThe company looked like it was on its last legs.\r\n这家公司看起来已经快撑不下去了。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe old system is on its last legs.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThe old system\r\n= 这个旧系统\r\n\r\nis on its last legs\r\n= 已经快不行了 / 快撑不住了\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这个旧系统已经快撑不住了。\r\n\r\n注意这里不是单纯说：\r\n\r\nThe system is old.\r\n系统很旧。\r\n\r\n而是更进一步：\r\n\r\n“它已经接近极限，可能很快就不能用了。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nbe on its last legs vs be broken\r\n\r\nbe broken\r\n= 已经坏了\r\n\r\nThe printer is broken.\r\n打印机坏了。\r\n\r\nbe on its last legs\r\n= 还没完全坏，但已经快坏了\r\n\r\nThe printer is on its last legs.\r\n打印机已经快报废了。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nbroken → 已经坏了\r\non its last legs → 快坏了，还勉强能用\r\n\r\nbe on its last legs vs wear out\r\n\r\nwear out\r\n= 用坏、磨损到不能用\r\n\r\nThe battery is wearing out.\r\n电池正在老化。\r\n\r\nbe on its last legs\r\n= 已经进入最后阶段\r\n\r\nThe battery is on its last legs.\r\n这块电池已经快彻底不行了。\r\n\r\nbe on its last legs vs dying\r\n\r\ndying\r\n= 快坏了 / 快没电了 / 快结束了\r\n\r\nMy phone battery is dying.\r\n我的手机快没电了。\r\n\r\nMy laptop is on its last legs.\r\n我的电脑已经快报废了。\r\n\r\non its last legs 更有“长期老化、接近寿命终点”的感觉。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n代词要根据主语变化\r\n\r\n单数物品：\r\n\r\nThe printer is on its last legs.\r\n\r\n人：\r\n\r\nI’m on my last legs.\r\n我快撑不住了。\r\n\r\nThey’re on their last legs.\r\n他们已经筋疲力尽了。\r\n\r\n不要理解成真的“最后几条腿”\r\n\r\n这是习语，不按字面翻译。\r\n\r\n很适合描述老设备\r\n\r\n尤其自然：\r\n\r\nlaptop\r\n\r\ncar\r\n\r\nprinter\r\n\r\nserver\r\n\r\nwashing machine\r\n\r\nold system\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象一张已经快散架的桌子：\r\n\r\n前三条腿都坏了，\r\n只剩最后一条腿勉强撑着。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\non its last legs\r\n= 靠最后一点支撑\r\n= 快不行了\r\n\r\n最值得记住的三个句子：\r\n\r\nMy laptop is on its last legs.\r\n我的电脑快报废了。\r\n\r\nThe old system is on its last legs.\r\n旧系统快撑不住了。\r\n\r\nAfter working all night, I was on my last legs.\r\n通宵工作后，我已经累得快撑不住了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9f283f2da6e8466da0774a3ad4697a79.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 20:07:40',1,'2026-09-01 20:07:40'),(1567,21,54,'phrase','gloss over sth','gloss over sth','gloss over sth','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ngloss over sth\r\n= 轻描淡写地带过某事\r\n= 对某个问题避重就轻\r\n= 不认真谈某事，尤其是不方便、尴尬或负面的部分\r\n\r\n它通常带一点负面语气：\r\n\r\n“明明有问题，但只简单提一下，不深入讲。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n对问题轻描淡写\r\n\r\nThe report glossed over several serious issues.\r\n这份报告对几个严重问题轻描淡写地带过了。\r\n\r\n避开尴尬或不利细节\r\n\r\nHe glossed over the reasons for the project’s failure.\r\n他对项目失败的原因避重就轻。\r\n\r\n快速带过，不展开说明\r\n\r\nThe presentation glossed over the technical details.\r\n这次演示对技术细节只是简单带过。\r\n\r\n这里不一定是故意隐瞒，也可能只是“没有展开讲”。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThe manager glossed over the problems with the new system.\r\n经理对新系统的问题轻描淡写地带过了。\r\n\r\nWe shouldn’t gloss over the risks.\r\n我们不应该对这些风险避重就轻。\r\n\r\nShe glossed over what had happened during the meeting.\r\n她对会议期间发生的事情一带而过。\r\n\r\nThe article glosses over the costs involved.\r\n这篇文章对涉及的成本轻描淡写。\r\n\r\nHe tried to gloss over the fact that the deadline had been missed.\r\n他试图淡化已经错过截止日期这件事。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe company glossed over the security concerns.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThe company\r\n= 这家公司\r\n\r\nglossed over\r\n= 轻描淡写地带过 / 避重就轻\r\n\r\nthe security concerns\r\n= 安全方面的担忧\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这家公司对安全方面的担忧轻描淡写地带过了。\r\n\r\n这里的感觉不是：\r\n\r\n“完全没提”\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\n“提了，但没有认真展开，甚至有点故意淡化。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\ngloss over vs ignore\r\n\r\nignore\r\n= 完全忽视、不理会\r\n\r\nThey ignored the problem.\r\n他们完全没有理这个问题。\r\n\r\ngloss over\r\n= 提到了，但轻轻带过\r\n\r\nThey glossed over the problem.\r\n他们对这个问题一带而过。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nignore → 不提 / 不管\r\ngloss over → 提了，但没认真讲\r\n\r\ngloss over vs downplay\r\n\r\ndownplay\r\n= 淡化某件事的重要性或严重性\r\n\r\nThe company downplayed the risks.\r\n公司淡化了风险。\r\n\r\ngloss over\r\n= 不深入谈这个问题\r\n\r\nThe company glossed over the risks.\r\n公司对风险避重就轻。\r\n\r\n区别很接近，但：\r\n\r\ndownplay → 强调“说得不严重”\r\ngloss over → 强调“快速带过、不展开”\r\n\r\ngloss over vs brush aside\r\n\r\nbrush aside\r\n= 不当回事、直接把问题搁置\r\n\r\nHe brushed aside my concerns.\r\n他对我的担忧不以为意。\r\n\r\ngloss over\r\n= 表面上提一下，但不深入\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\ngloss over + 名词\r\n\r\n✅ gloss over the issue\r\n\r\n✅ gloss over the risks\r\n\r\n✅ gloss over the details\r\n\r\n也可以接从句内容\r\n\r\n✅ gloss over what happened\r\n\r\n✅ gloss over the fact that...\r\n\r\n常用于负面问题\r\n\r\n非常常见的搭配：\r\n\r\ngloss over the problem\r\ngloss over the risks\r\ngloss over the details\r\ngloss over the differences\r\ngloss over the failure\r\ngloss over the fact that...\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\ngloss 本身有“表面光泽”的感觉。\r\n\r\n你可以想象：\r\n\r\n给一个问题表面刷上一层亮光，\r\n看起来没那么难看，\r\n但问题本身还在那里。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ngloss over sth\r\n= 给问题表面“抹一层”\r\n= 不深入讲\r\n= 轻描淡写地带过\r\n\r\n最值得记住的三个句子：\r\n\r\nWe shouldn’t gloss over the risks.\r\n我们不应该对风险避重就轻。\r\n\r\nThe report glossed over several major problems.\r\n这份报告轻描淡写地带过了几个重大问题。\r\n\r\nHe glossed over the fact that the project had failed.\r\n他对项目失败这件事避重就轻。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a5f2e073ce7f4d738057cdf1c532484e.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 20:11:24',1,'2026-09-01 20:11:24'),(1568,21,55,'phrase','in depth','in depth','in depth','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nin-depth\r\n= 深入的\r\n= 详细的\r\n= 全面的、透彻的\r\n\r\n它强调的不是“内容很多”这么简单，而是：\r\n\r\n“对一个主题挖得很深，分析得很细。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n深入分析的\r\n\r\nan in-depth analysis\r\n深入分析\r\n\r\nan in-depth study\r\n深入研究\r\n\r\nan in-depth review\r\n深入评审 / 详细审查\r\n\r\n例：\r\nWe conducted an in-depth analysis of the system performance.\r\n我们对系统性能进行了深入分析。\r\n\r\n详细而全面的\r\n\r\nan in-depth discussion\r\n深入讨论\r\n\r\nan in-depth interview\r\n深度访谈\r\n\r\nan in-depth report\r\n深度报告\r\n\r\n例：\r\nThe report provides an in-depth look at the issue.\r\n这份报告对这个问题进行了深入分析。\r\n\r\n技术 / 工作场景中很常见\r\n\r\n非常适合这些搭配：\r\n\r\nin-depth investigation\r\n深入调查\r\n\r\nin-depth testing\r\n深入测试\r\n\r\nin-depth research\r\n深入研究\r\n\r\nin-depth understanding\r\n深入理解','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nWe need a more in-depth analysis of the problem.\r\n我们需要对这个问题做更深入的分析。\r\n\r\nThe team carried out an in-depth review of the workflow.\r\n团队对工作流程进行了深入审查。\r\n\r\nThis article gives an in-depth explanation of how the system works.\r\n这篇文章详细解释了系统是如何工作的。\r\n\r\nWe had an in-depth discussion about the risks.\r\n我们就这些风险进行了深入讨论。\r\n\r\nThe issue requires further in-depth investigation.\r\n这个问题需要进一步深入调查。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nWe need an in-depth review of the current architecture.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nWe need\r\n= 我们需要\r\n\r\nan in-depth review\r\n= 一次深入审查\r\n\r\nof the current architecture\r\n= 对当前架构\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n我们需要对当前架构进行一次深入审查。\r\n\r\n这里 in-depth 比：\r\n\r\ndetailed review\r\n\r\n更强调：\r\n\r\n“不只是看细节，而是深入理解和分析。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nin-depth vs detailed\r\n\r\ndetailed\r\n= 详细的，强调细节多\r\n\r\na detailed report\r\n= 一份很详细的报告\r\n\r\nin-depth\r\n= 深入的，强调分析有深度\r\n\r\nan in-depth report\r\n= 一份深入分析问题的报告\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ndetailed → 细\r\nin-depth → 深\r\n\r\n一份东西可以很 detailed，但不一定 in-depth。\r\n\r\nin-depth vs comprehensive\r\n\r\ncomprehensive\r\n= 全面的，覆盖范围广\r\n\r\nan comprehensive review\r\n= 全面审查\r\n\r\nin-depth\r\n= 深入的，挖得深\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncomprehensive → 广\r\nin-depth → 深\r\n\r\n最容易记成：\r\n\r\ncomprehensive = breadth\r\nin-depth = depth\r\n\r\nin-depth vs thorough\r\n\r\nthorough\r\n= 彻底的、全面仔细的\r\n\r\na thorough inspection\r\n= 彻底检查\r\n\r\nin-depth\r\n= 深入分析\r\n\r\nthorough 更强调“不遗漏”。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n作形容词时通常加连字符\r\n\r\n✅ an in-depth analysis\r\n\r\n✅ an in-depth discussion\r\n\r\n不要写：\r\n\r\n❌ an indepth analysis\r\n\r\n标准写法是：\r\n\r\n✅ in-depth\r\n\r\n如果放在名词后面，通常不用这个结构\r\n\r\n更自然的是：\r\n\r\nThe analysis was very thorough.\r\nThe analysis went into great depth.\r\n\r\n而不是：\r\n\r\n❌ The analysis was in-depth.\r\n\r\n虽然偶尔能见到，但不如放名词前自然。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nin + depth\r\n\r\ndepth = 深度\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nin-depth\r\n= 进入“深度”里面\r\n= 深入的\r\n\r\n直接记这几个高频搭配：\r\n\r\nin-depth analysis = 深入分析\r\nin-depth review = 深入审查\r\nin-depth discussion = 深入讨论\r\nin-depth research = 深入研究\r\nin-depth investigation = 深入调查\r\n\r\nSources','/static/uploads/english_note_item/eb121bffae6a49b790547a3d2e46fae2.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 20:15:05',1,'2026-09-01 20:15:05'),(1569,21,56,'vocab','outsource','outsource','outsource','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\noutsource\r\n= 外包\r\n= 把原本由公司内部完成的工作，交给外部公司或第三方来做\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n“这件事我们不自己做，交给外面的人或公司做。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\noutsource sth\r\n= 把某项工作外包出去\r\n\r\nThe company outsourced its customer support.\r\n公司把客服业务外包了。\r\n\r\nWe decided to outsource the testing work.\r\n我们决定把测试工作外包出去。\r\n\r\noutsource sth to sb / a company\r\n= 把某事外包给某人或某家公司\r\n\r\nThey outsourced the development work to a local software company.\r\n他们把开发工作外包给了一家本地软件公司。\r\n\r\nThe maintenance is outsourced to a third-party provider.\r\n维护工作外包给了第三方服务商。\r\n\r\nbe outsourced\r\n= 被外包\r\n\r\nMost of the IT support is outsourced.\r\n大部分 IT 支持工作都是外包的。\r\n\r\nSome non-core functions have been outsourced.\r\n一些非核心职能已经被外包。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nWe outsource some of our infrastructure maintenance.\r\n我们把部分基础设施维护工作外包出去。\r\n\r\nThe company outsourced payroll processing to another firm.\r\n公司把工资处理业务外包给了另一家公司。\r\n\r\nThey are considering outsourcing part of the project.\r\n他们正在考虑把项目的一部分外包出去。\r\n\r\nThis task could be outsourced instead of handled internally.\r\n这项任务可以外包，而不是由内部团队处理。\r\n\r\nWe don’t want to outsource the core development work.\r\n我们不想把核心开发工作外包出去。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe company outsourced its IT support to a third-party provider.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThe company\r\n= 这家公司\r\n\r\noutsourced\r\n= 外包了\r\n\r\nits IT support\r\n= 它的 IT 支持工作\r\n\r\nto a third-party provider\r\n= 给一家第三方服务商\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这家公司把 IT 支持业务外包给了第三方服务商。\r\n\r\n这里最典型的结构就是：\r\n\r\noutsource A to B\r\n= 把 A 外包给 B\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\noutsource vs hire\r\n\r\nhire\r\n= 雇人 / 招聘\r\n\r\nWe hired two developers.\r\n我们雇了两名开发人员。\r\n\r\noutsource\r\n= 把某项工作交给外部团队或公司\r\n\r\nWe outsourced the development work.\r\n我们把开发工作外包了。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nhire → 人加入你的组织或为你工作\r\noutsource → 工作交给外部组织处理\r\n\r\noutsource vs subcontract\r\n\r\nsubcontract\r\n= 分包、转包\r\n\r\n通常更偏工程、建筑、项目合同。\r\n\r\nThe construction company subcontracted the electrical work.\r\n建筑公司把电气工程分包了出去。\r\n\r\noutsource\r\n= 更广泛\r\n\r\n可以是：\r\n\r\nIT\r\n\r\ncustomer support\r\n\r\npayroll\r\n\r\naccounting\r\n\r\nmanufacturing\r\n\r\ntesting\r\n\r\noutsource vs offshore\r\n\r\noffshore\r\n= 把业务放到海外做\r\n\r\noutsourcing 不一定去国外。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe outsourced the work to a local company.\r\n我们把工作外包给了一家本地公司。\r\n\r\n这叫 outsourcing，\r\n但不叫 offshoring。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\noutsource 后面直接接工作内容\r\n\r\n✅ outsource the testing\r\n\r\n✅ outsource customer support\r\n\r\n不需要：\r\n\r\n❌ outsource for the testing\r\n\r\n表示“外包给谁”用 to\r\n\r\n✅ outsource the work to another company\r\n\r\n名词形式是 outsourcing\r\n\r\noutsourcing\r\n= 外包行为 / 外包模式\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nIT outsourcing\r\n= IT 外包\r\n\r\noutsourcing strategy\r\n= 外包策略\r\n\r\n形容词常见是 outsourced\r\n\r\noutsourced services\r\n= 外包服务\r\n\r\noutsourced staff\r\n= 外包人员\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nout + source\r\n\r\nsource\r\n= 来源\r\n\r\noutsource\r\n= 来源放到外面\r\n→ 资源从公司外部获得\r\n→ 外包\r\n\r\n最值得记住的几个搭配：\r\n\r\noutsource the work\r\n= 把工作外包\r\n\r\noutsource development\r\n= 外包开发\r\n\r\noutsource testing\r\n= 外包测试\r\n\r\noutsource sth to a third party\r\n= 把某事外包给第三方\r\n\r\noutsourcing company\r\n= 外包公司','/static/uploads/english_note_item/f3f85d11dad34fcbb373ad1de967a4ce.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 20:16:44',1,'2026-09-01 20:16:44'),(1570,21,57,'phrase','responsibility vs accountability','responsibility vs accountability','responsibility vs accountability','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n这两个词都可以翻译成“责任”，但重点不一样：\r\n\r\nresponsibility\r\n= 你负责做什么\r\n= 职责、任务责任\r\n\r\naccountability\r\n= 你要对最终结果负责\r\n= 最终责任、问责\r\n\r\n最简单记法：\r\n\r\nresponsibility = doing the work\r\n负责做事\r\n\r\naccountability = owning the result\r\n对结果负责','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nresponsibility = 职责、负责做某事\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\nbe responsible for sth / doing sth\r\n= 负责某事 / 负责做某事\r\n\r\n例：\r\n\r\nI’m responsible for maintaining the system.\r\n我负责维护这个系统。\r\n\r\nThe development team is responsible for implementing the feature.\r\n开发团队负责实现这个功能。\r\n\r\nMy main responsibility is backend development.\r\n我的主要职责是后端开发。\r\n\r\nresponsibility 很常见于：\r\n\r\njob responsibility\r\n工作职责\r\n\r\ntake responsibility\r\n承担责任\r\n\r\nhave responsibility for\r\n负责……\r\n\r\naccountability = 对结果负责、接受问责\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\nbe accountable for sth\r\n= 对某事的结果负责\r\n\r\n例：\r\n\r\nThe project manager is accountable for the final delivery.\r\n项目经理对最终交付负责。\r\n\r\nManagers should be accountable for their decisions.\r\n管理人员应该为自己的决定负责。\r\n\r\nThere needs to be greater accountability.\r\n需要加强问责。\r\n\r\naccountability 很常见于：\r\n\r\nmanagement\r\n管理\r\n\r\ngovernment\r\n政府\r\n\r\nleadership\r\n领导力\r\n\r\npolicy\r\n政策\r\n\r\ncorporate governance\r\n公司治理','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nShe is responsible for preparing the report.\r\n她负责准备报告。\r\n\r\nShe is accountable for the accuracy of the report.\r\n她要对报告的准确性负责。\r\n\r\nThe developer is responsible for writing the code.\r\n开发人员负责写代码。\r\n\r\nThe team lead is accountable for the quality of the final release.\r\n团队负责人要对最终发布的质量负责。\r\n\r\nEveryone has different responsibilities.\r\n每个人都有不同的职责。\r\n\r\nWe need clear accountability for this project.\r\n我们需要明确这个项目最终由谁负责。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n最典型的一组：\r\n\r\nShe is responsible for preparing the report.\r\n\r\nresponsible for\r\n= 负责做\r\n\r\n所以重点是：\r\n\r\n“她的任务是准备报告。”\r\n\r\n而：\r\n\r\nShe is accountable for the accuracy of the report.\r\n\r\naccountable for\r\n= 对结果负责\r\n\r\n重点是：\r\n\r\n“如果报告有错误，她要对此负责。”\r\n\r\n所以一个偏：\r\n\r\n任务\r\n\r\n一个偏：\r\n\r\n结果\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\n对比点	responsibility	accountability\r\n中文	职责、责任	最终责任、问责\r\n核心	谁负责做	谁对结果负责\r\n关注点	task / duty	result / outcome\r\n能否多人承担	很常见	通常强调明确负责人\r\n是否可以委派	可以	通常不能完全转移\r\n常见场景	工作职责、任务	管理、政策、问责\r\n\r\n用软件项目理解最清楚：\r\n\r\nDeveloper\r\nresponsibility = coding\r\n负责写代码\r\n\r\nTester\r\nresponsibility = testing\r\n负责测试\r\n\r\nDevOps\r\nresponsibility = deployment\r\n负责部署\r\n\r\nProject Manager\r\naccountability = final delivery\r\n对最终交付负责\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nresponsibility\r\n→ 我具体要做什么\r\n\r\naccountability\r\n→ 最终出问题谁站出来负责\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n两个词后面都经常搭配 for\r\n\r\n✅ responsible for sth\r\n\r\n✅ accountable for sth\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI’m responsible for maintaining the service.\r\n\r\nThe manager is accountable for the outcome.\r\n\r\naccountability 不太适合直接表示“工作职责”\r\n\r\n如果你想说：\r\n\r\n“这是我的职责。”\r\n\r\n更自然：\r\n\r\nThis is my responsibility.\r\n\r\n而不是：\r\n\r\nThis is my accountability.\r\n\r\naccountable 语气通常比 responsible 更强\r\n\r\nresponsible：\r\n负责这项工作\r\n\r\naccountable：\r\n最后结果不好，你需要解释并承担责任\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n可以想象一个项目出了问题。\r\n\r\n老板问：\r\n\r\nWho was responsible for testing?\r\n谁负责测试？\r\n\r\n这是在问：\r\n\r\n谁本来应该做这个任务。\r\n\r\n老板又问：\r\n\r\nWho is accountable for the failed release?\r\n谁要为这次发布失败负责？\r\n\r\n这是在问：\r\n\r\n最终谁要承担结果。\r\n\r\n所以直接记：\r\n\r\nresponsibility = task\r\n任务责任\r\n\r\naccountability = outcome\r\n结果责任\r\n\r\n最值得记的一句话：\r\n\r\nYou can delegate responsibility, but you still remain accountable.\r\n\r\n你可以把任务分配给别人，但最终责任仍然在你。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/115364fba86d450e9e7457835a954092.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 20:26:42',1,'2026-09-01 20:26:42'),(1571,21,58,'phrase','go viral','go viral','go viral','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ngo viral\r\n= 在网上迅速爆红\r\n= 被大量转发、传播\r\n= 短时间内获得极高关注度\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n“像病毒一样迅速传播开来。”\r\n\r\n最常用于：\r\n\r\n视频\r\n\r\n帖子\r\n\r\n图片\r\n\r\n新闻\r\n\r\n梗 / meme\r\n\r\n某句话或事件','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n视频 / 帖子突然爆火\r\n\r\nThe video went viral overnight.\r\n这个视频一夜之间爆红了。\r\n\r\nHer post went viral on social media.\r\n她的帖子在社交媒体上迅速走红。\r\n\r\n某个内容被疯狂传播\r\n\r\nThe clip quickly went viral.\r\n这段短视频很快就火遍了网络。\r\n\r\nA photo of the incident went viral online.\r\n那起事件的一张照片在网上迅速传播开来。\r\n\r\n某句话 / 挑战 / 梗火起来\r\n\r\nThe phrase went viral after the interview.\r\n采访之后，这句话迅速走红。\r\n\r\nThe challenge went viral on TikTok.\r\n这个挑战在 TikTok 上火了。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThe video went viral within a few hours.\r\n这个视频几个小时内就爆红了。\r\n\r\nNo one expected the post to go viral.\r\n没人想到这个帖子会突然爆火。\r\n\r\nHis reaction video went viral on social media.\r\n他的反应视频在社交媒体上迅速走红。\r\n\r\nThe story went viral and attracted millions of views.\r\n这个故事迅速传播开来，吸引了数百万次浏览。\r\n\r\nA short clip from the interview went viral.\r\n采访中的一个短片突然火了。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe video went viral after it was posted online.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThe video\r\n= 这个视频\r\n\r\nwent viral\r\n= 爆红了 / 疯传了\r\n\r\nafter it was posted online\r\n= 在上传到网上以后\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这个视频上传到网上以后迅速爆红。\r\n\r\n这里 go 是系动词变化：\r\n\r\ngo + adjective\r\n= 变得……\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\ngo bad\r\n= 变坏\r\n\r\ngo wrong\r\n= 出问题\r\n\r\ngo viral\r\n= 变成病毒式传播状态\r\n→ 爆红\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\ngo viral vs become popular\r\n\r\nbecome popular\r\n= 变得受欢迎\r\n\r\n可以是慢慢变火。\r\n\r\nThe show became popular over time.\r\n这个节目慢慢变得受欢迎。\r\n\r\ngo viral\r\n= 短时间内爆发式传播\r\n\r\nThe clip went viral overnight.\r\n这个短片一夜爆红。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nbecome popular → 强调受欢迎\r\ngo viral → 强调快速传播\r\n\r\ngo viral vs trend\r\n\r\ntrend\r\n= 成为热门趋势 / 登上热搜\r\n\r\nThe topic is trending on X.\r\n这个话题正在 X 上成为热门。\r\n\r\ngo viral\r\n= 内容本身大量传播\r\n\r\nThe video went viral.\r\n这个视频疯传了。\r\n\r\n二者经常同时发生，但不完全一样。\r\n\r\ngo viral vs blow up\r\n\r\nblow up\r\n= 突然爆火，口语感更强\r\n\r\nThat song blew up on TikTok.\r\n那首歌在 TikTok 上突然爆火了。\r\n\r\ngo viral\r\n= 更标准、更常见于新闻和日常表达\r\n\r\nThat song went viral on TikTok.\r\n那首歌在 TikTok 上爆红了。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n常用过去式 went viral\r\n\r\n✅ The video went viral.\r\n视频爆火了。\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n❌ The video became viral.\r\n\r\n虽然理论上能理解，但非常不自然。\r\n\r\nviral 本身是形容词\r\n\r\nviral content\r\n= 病毒式传播的内容\r\n\r\na viral video\r\n= 爆款视频 / 疯传视频\r\n\r\ngo viral 不一定是正面的\r\n\r\n负面新闻也可以 go viral。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe embarrassing clip went viral.\r\n那个尴尬的视频疯传了。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nviral 来自 virus\r\n= 病毒\r\n\r\n病毒传播特点：\r\n\r\n快\r\n范围广\r\n人传人\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ngo viral\r\n= 像病毒一样在网上扩散\r\n= 爆红 / 疯传\r\n\r\n最值得记住的三个表达：\r\n\r\nThe video went viral.\r\n这个视频爆火了。\r\n\r\nThe post went viral overnight.\r\n这个帖子一夜爆红。\r\n\r\nIt quickly went viral on social media.\r\n它很快就在社交媒体上疯传开来。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/0bd114acc552434e8d96c29cb40866ac.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 20:34:06',1,'2026-09-01 20:34:06'),(1572,21,59,'phrase','from time to time','from time to time','from time to time','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nfrom time to time\r\n= 有时\r\n= 偶尔\r\n= 时不时\r\n\r\n它强调的是：\r\n\r\n“不是经常发生，但隔一段时间会发生一次。”\r\n\r\n很接近：\r\nsometimes / occasionally','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n偶尔做某事\r\n\r\nI still go there from time to time.\r\n我现在偶尔还是会去那里。\r\n\r\nWe meet for coffee from time to time.\r\n我们偶尔会一起喝咖啡。\r\n\r\n某件事情时不时发生\r\n\r\nThe system slows down from time to time.\r\n这个系统时不时会变慢。\r\n\r\nProblems can occur from time to time.\r\n问题偶尔还是会发生。\r\n\r\n表示某种情况并不持续，只是间歇出现\r\n\r\nEveryone feels stressed from time to time.\r\n每个人偶尔都会感到压力。\r\n\r\nThe connection drops from time to time.\r\n网络连接时不时会断。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nI still talk to my old colleagues from time to time.\r\n我现在偶尔还会和以前的同事聊天。\r\n\r\nThe application crashes from time to time.\r\n这个应用程序偶尔会崩溃。\r\n\r\nWe need to review the configuration from time to time.\r\n我们需要时不时检查一下配置。\r\n\r\nI work from home from time to time.\r\n我偶尔会在家办公。\r\n\r\nIt’s normal to make mistakes from time to time.\r\n偶尔犯错是很正常的。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe server needs to be restarted from time to time.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThe server needs to be restarted\r\n= 服务器需要重启\r\n\r\nfrom time to time\r\n= 偶尔 / 时不时\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这台服务器偶尔需要重启一下。\r\n\r\n这里不是：\r\n\r\n“经常需要重启”\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\n“隔一段时间可能需要重启一次。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nfrom time to time vs sometimes\r\n\r\nsometimes\r\n= 有时\r\n\r\n最普通、最常用。\r\n\r\nI sometimes work late.\r\n我有时工作到很晚。\r\n\r\nfrom time to time\r\n= 偶尔、时不时\r\n\r\n更强调“隔一段时间发生一次”。\r\n\r\nI work late from time to time.\r\n我偶尔也会工作到很晚。\r\n\r\n两者大多数时候可以互换，但 from time to time 更有“间歇性”的感觉。\r\n\r\nfrom time to time vs occasionally\r\n\r\noccasionally\r\n= 偶尔\r\n\r\n意思非常接近，而且 slightly more formal。\r\n\r\nWe occasionally experience network issues.\r\n我们偶尔会遇到网络问题。\r\n\r\nWe experience network issues from time to time.\r\n我们时不时会遇到网络问题。\r\n\r\noccasionally → 更简洁、稍正式\r\nfrom time to time → 更口语、更有节奏感\r\n\r\nfrom time to time vs once in a while\r\n\r\nonce in a while\r\n= 偶尔、偶尔一次\r\n\r\n非常口语。\r\n\r\nI eat fast food once in a while.\r\n我偶尔吃一次快餐。\r\n\r\nfrom time to time\r\n= 中性，口语和书面语都自然。\r\n\r\n大致可以理解成：\r\n\r\nsometimes → 有时\r\nfrom time to time → 时不时\r\noccasionally → 偶尔，稍正式\r\nonce in a while → 偶尔一次，更口语\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n固定搭配不要改介词\r\n\r\n✅ from time to time\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ from times to times\r\n❌ from a time to a time\r\n\r\ntime 都用单数\r\n\r\n✅ from time to time\r\n\r\n位置很灵活\r\n\r\n句尾最自然：\r\n\r\nThe system fails from time to time.\r\n\r\n也可以句首：\r\n\r\nFrom time to time, the system needs to be restarted.\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象时间轴：\r\n\r\n——●——————●————●——————\r\n\r\n事情不是连续发生，\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\n隔一段 time → 出现一次\r\n再隔一段 time → 又出现一次\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nfrom time to time\r\n= 从一个时间点到另一个时间点偶尔出现\r\n= 时不时 / 偶尔\r\n\r\n最值得记住的三个句子：\r\n\r\nI go there from time to time.\r\n我偶尔会去那里。\r\n\r\nThe system slows down from time to time.\r\n系统时不时会变慢。\r\n\r\nWe all make mistakes from time to time.\r\n我们每个人偶尔都会犯错。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/6cd9bca4cf654e17bdb819476fdb1e0d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 20:36:53',1,'2026-09-01 20:36:53'),(1573,21,60,'phrase','let on','let on','let on','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nlet on\r\n= 透露；泄露\r\n= 让别人知道某件原本保密的事\r\n\r\n最常见结构：\r\n\r\nlet on that...\r\n= 透露说……\r\n\r\nlet on about sth\r\n= 透露关于某事的信息\r\n\r\n它通常带有这种感觉：\r\n\r\n“本来不想让别人知道，但还是说漏了 / 暗示出来了。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n透露秘密或信息\r\n\r\nDon’t let on that I told you.\r\n别透露是我告诉你的。\r\n\r\nShe knew what had happened but didn’t let on.\r\n她知道发生了什么，但没有表现出来。\r\n\r\n表现出自己知道某事\r\n\r\nHe didn’t let on that he already knew the answer.\r\n他没有表现出自己已经知道答案。\r\n\r\n这里 let on 不一定是“主动说出来”，也可以是：\r\n\r\n“通过表情、行为让别人看出来”。\r\n\r\nlet on about sth\r\n= 透露关于某事的信息\r\n\r\nHe never let on about the problem.\r\n他从来没透露过那个问题。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nDon’t let on that we’re planning a surprise.\r\n别透露我们正在准备惊喜。\r\n\r\nShe didn’t let on that she was upset.\r\n她没有表现出自己很难过。\r\n\r\nHe let on that the company might cut costs.\r\n他透露公司可能会削减成本。\r\n\r\nI knew the truth, but I didn’t let on.\r\n我知道真相，但没有表现出来。\r\n\r\nThey didn’t let on how serious the situation was.\r\n他们没有透露情况到底有多严重。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nHe didn’t let on that he already knew.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nHe didn’t let on\r\n= 他没有透露 / 没有表现出来\r\n\r\nthat he already knew\r\n= 他其实已经知道了\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n他没有表现出自己其实已经知道了。\r\n\r\n这里和 simply “tell” 不一样。\r\n\r\ntell\r\n= 直接告诉\r\n\r\nlet on\r\n= 无意或有意地透露出来，让别人察觉\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nlet on vs tell\r\n\r\ntell\r\n= 直接告诉别人\r\n\r\nHe told me the truth.\r\n他告诉了我真相。\r\n\r\nlet on\r\n= 透露、让别人察觉\r\n\r\nHe didn’t let on that he knew the truth.\r\n他没有让别人看出来他知道真相。\r\n\r\nlet on vs reveal\r\n\r\nreveal\r\n= 揭露、公开，语气更正式\r\n\r\nThe report revealed several problems.\r\n报告揭露了几个问题。\r\n\r\nlet on\r\n= 更口语，通常强调“别说漏嘴”\r\n\r\nDon’t let on that you know.\r\n别让别人知道你已经知道了。\r\n\r\nlet on vs give away\r\n\r\ngive away\r\n= 不小心泄露秘密、露馅\r\n\r\nHis expression gave away how nervous he was.\r\n他的表情暴露了他的紧张。\r\n\r\nlet on\r\n= 自己透露或表现出来\r\n\r\nHe didn’t let on that he was nervous.\r\n他没有表现出紧张。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nlet on 很常用否定句\r\n\r\nDon’t let on.\r\n别说出去。\r\n\r\nI didn’t let on.\r\n我没表现出来。\r\n\r\nShe never let on.\r\n她从没透露过。\r\n\r\n后面很常接 that 从句\r\n\r\n✅ let on that...\r\n\r\n✅ didn’t let on that...\r\n\r\n过去式还是 let\r\n\r\n现在：\r\nHe lets on.\r\n\r\n过去：\r\nHe let on.\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n❌ letted on\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 let on 想成：\r\n\r\n“把秘密放出来一点点”\r\n\r\nlet = 让\r\non = 开启\r\n\r\n原本信息是关着的，\r\n一 let on，\r\n别人就知道了。\r\n\r\n最值得记住的三个句子：\r\n\r\nDon’t let on.\r\n别说出去。\r\n\r\nDon’t let on that I told you.\r\n别透露是我告诉你的。\r\n\r\nShe knew the truth but didn’t let on.\r\n她知道真相，但没有表现出来。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/7e002bf01ffb4cc7a0e838ede5bebcf6.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 20:40:27',1,'2026-09-01 20:40:27'),(1574,21,61,'vocab','compelling','compelling','compelling','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ncompelling\r\n= 非常有说服力的\r\n= 强有力的\r\n= 引人入胜的、让人忍不住关注的\r\n\r\n它有两个很常见的方向：\r\n\r\n让人信服\r\n\r\n让人非常想看、想听、想继续关注','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n有说服力的，令人信服的\r\n\r\na compelling argument\r\n= 很有说服力的论点\r\n\r\ncompelling evidence\r\n= 强有力的证据\r\n\r\na compelling reason\r\n= 很有说服力的理由\r\n\r\n例：\r\n\r\nShe made a compelling argument for changing the policy.\r\n她提出了一个很有说服力的理由，支持修改这项政策。\r\n\r\nThe evidence is compelling.\r\n这些证据非常有说服力。\r\n\r\n引人入胜的，非常吸引人的\r\n\r\na compelling story\r\n= 引人入胜的故事\r\n\r\na compelling documentary\r\n= 很吸引人的纪录片\r\n\r\na compelling character\r\n= 很有吸引力、很抓人的角色\r\n\r\n例：\r\n\r\nIt’s a compelling story from beginning to end.\r\n这个故事从头到尾都很吸引人。\r\n\r\nThe documentary was surprisingly compelling.\r\n这部纪录片出乎意料地引人入胜。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThere is compelling evidence that the system needs to be redesigned.\r\n有强有力的证据表明这个系统需要重新设计。\r\n\r\nHe gave a compelling explanation for what happened.\r\n他对发生的事情给出了一个很有说服力的解释。\r\n\r\nThat’s a compelling reason to reconsider the plan.\r\n这是一个很有说服力的理由，值得重新考虑这个计划。\r\n\r\nThe book tells a compelling story.\r\n这本书讲了一个非常引人入胜的故事。\r\n\r\nShe is a compelling speaker.\r\n她是一个非常有感染力、很能吸引人的演讲者。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe report presented compelling evidence of serious failures.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThe report presented\r\n= 这份报告提出了\r\n\r\ncompelling evidence\r\n= 强有力、很有说服力的证据\r\n\r\nof serious failures\r\n= 关于严重失败的\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这份报告提出了有关严重失误的强有力证据。\r\n\r\n这里 compelling 不是说证据“有趣”，而是说：\r\n\r\n“证据强到很难反驳。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\ncompelling vs convincing\r\n\r\nconvincing\r\n= 令人信服的\r\n\r\na convincing explanation\r\n= 可信、有说服力的解释\r\n\r\ncompelling\r\n= 更强，往往有“强到很难忽视”的感觉\r\n\r\na compelling argument\r\n= 一个很强、很有说服力的论点\r\n\r\n简单理解：\r\n\r\nconvincing → 让你相信\r\ncompelling → 强到让你很难不相信/不关注\r\n\r\ncompelling vs persuasive\r\n\r\npersuasive\r\n= 有劝服力的\r\n\r\n更强调“说服别人接受观点或采取行动”。\r\n\r\na persuasive speech\r\n= 有说服力的演讲\r\n\r\ncompelling\r\n= 强调论点、证据或内容本身非常有力量\r\n\r\ncompelling evidence\r\n= 强有力的证据\r\n\r\npersuasive evidence 虽然能理解，但不如 compelling evidence 常见。\r\n\r\ncompelling vs fascinating\r\n\r\nfascinating\r\n= 非常有趣、迷人的\r\n\r\nThe documentary was fascinating.\r\n这部纪录片非常有趣。\r\n\r\ncompelling\r\n= 不一定“有趣”，但让你忍不住继续关注\r\n\r\nThe documentary was compelling.\r\n这部纪录片很抓人，让人想继续看。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\ncompelling 不只是“有说服力”\r\n\r\n它还可以表示：\r\n\r\n“非常吸引人、抓人”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\na compelling argument\r\n= 有说服力的论点\r\n\r\na compelling story\r\n= 引人入胜的故事\r\n\r\n不要和 compulsory 混\r\n\r\ncompelling\r\n= 有说服力的 / 吸引人的\r\n\r\ncompulsory\r\n= 强制性的、必修的\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\ncompulsory education\r\n= 义务教育\r\n\r\n来自动词 compel\r\n\r\ncompel\r\n= 迫使\r\n\r\ncompelling\r\n= 强到能“迫使”你相信、注意或继续看\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\ncompel\r\n= 强迫\r\n\r\ncompelling\r\n= 强到让你“不得不”：\r\n\r\n不得不相信\r\n不得不注意\r\n不得不继续看\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncompelling evidence\r\n= 强到让你不得不重视的证据\r\n\r\ncompelling story\r\n= 抓人到让你忍不住继续看的故事\r\n\r\n最值得记住的几个搭配：\r\n\r\ncompelling evidence = 强有力的证据\r\ncompelling argument = 很有说服力的论点\r\ncompelling reason = 很有说服力的理由\r\ncompelling story = 引人入胜的故事\r\ncompelling case = 强有力的论证 / 理由','/static/uploads/english_note_item/c90c3c5fb7284b1cbfd6e71d8d174520.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 20:45:44',1,'2026-09-01 20:45:44'),(1575,21,62,'vocab','cultivate','cultivate','cultivate','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ncultivate\r\n= 培养；培育；发展\r\n= 耕种；栽培\r\n\r\n这个词最核心的画面感是：\r\n\r\n“像种植物一样，花时间把某种东西慢慢培养起来。”\r\n\r\n所以它既可以真的说种地，也可以抽象地说：\r\n\r\n培养习惯\r\n\r\n培养关系\r\n\r\n培养技能\r\n\r\n培养某种文化\r\n\r\n树立某种形象','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n培养、发展某种品质或能力\r\n\r\ncultivate a habit\r\n培养习惯\r\n\r\ncultivate skills\r\n培养技能\r\n\r\ncultivate confidence\r\n培养自信\r\n\r\ncultivate patience\r\n培养耐心\r\n\r\n例：\r\n\r\nYou need to cultivate the habit of reviewing your work.\r\n你需要养成复盘自己工作的习惯。\r\n\r\n培养关系\r\n\r\ncultivate a relationship\r\n= 培养、经营一段关系\r\n\r\nThe company is trying to cultivate stronger relationships with its customers.\r\n公司正在努力与客户建立更牢固的关系。\r\n\r\n这里比 build a relationship 更正式一些，也更强调“长期经营”。\r\n\r\n培养某种环境、文化或氛围\r\n\r\ncultivate a culture of innovation\r\n= 培养创新文化\r\n\r\ncultivate trust\r\n= 建立、培养信任\r\n\r\ncultivate teamwork\r\n= 培养团队合作\r\n\r\n例：\r\n\r\nGood leaders cultivate a culture of trust.\r\n优秀的领导者会营造一种相互信任的文化。\r\n\r\n塑造某种形象\r\n\r\ncultivate an image\r\n= 有意识地塑造一种形象\r\n\r\nHe cultivated an image of being calm and reliable.\r\n他有意识地塑造了一个冷静、可靠的形象。\r\n\r\n耕种、栽培\r\n\r\n这是它比较字面的意思。\r\n\r\ncultivate land\r\n= 耕种土地\r\n\r\ncultivate crops\r\n= 种植农作物\r\n\r\nFarmers cultivate the land every year.\r\n农民每年都会耕种这片土地。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nWe need to cultivate better communication within the team.\r\n我们需要在团队内部培养更好的沟通方式。\r\n\r\nShe has cultivated strong relationships with her clients.\r\n她和客户建立了很牢固的关系。\r\n\r\nThe company wants to cultivate a culture of innovation.\r\n公司希望培养一种创新文化。\r\n\r\nReading regularly helps cultivate critical thinking.\r\n经常阅读有助于培养批判性思维。\r\n\r\nHe has spent years cultivating his professional network.\r\n他花了很多年经营自己的职业人脉。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe company is trying to cultivate a more open culture.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThe company is trying to\r\n= 公司正在努力\r\n\r\ncultivate\r\n= 培养、营造\r\n\r\na more open culture\r\n= 一种更加开放的文化\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n公司正在努力营造一种更加开放的文化。\r\n\r\n这里 cultivate 比 create 更有一种：\r\n\r\n“不是一下子建立出来，而是慢慢培养形成。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\ncultivate vs develop\r\n\r\ndevelop\r\n= 发展、培养\r\n\r\n范围最广。\r\n\r\ndevelop a skill\r\n= 培养一项技能\r\n\r\ncultivate\r\n= 更强调长期、细致地培养\r\n\r\ncultivate patience\r\n= 慢慢培养耐心\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ndevelop → 通用\r\ncultivate → 更有“精心培育”的感觉\r\n\r\ncultivate vs foster\r\n\r\nfoster\r\n= 促进、培养\r\n\r\n常用于：\r\n\r\nfoster cooperation\r\n促进合作\r\n\r\nfoster innovation\r\n促进创新\r\n\r\ncultivate\r\n= 更强调主动、持续地培育\r\n\r\ncultivate trust\r\n= 长期培养信任\r\n\r\nfoster 更像：\r\n\r\n“创造条件让它成长”\r\n\r\ncultivate 更像：\r\n\r\n“亲自去经营、培育它”\r\n\r\ncultivate vs nurture\r\n\r\nnurture\r\n= 培育、呵护\r\n\r\n语气更温和，常用于：\r\n\r\nnurture talent\r\n培养人才\r\n\r\nnurture a child\r\n养育孩子\r\n\r\ncultivate\r\n= 更正式，也更常用于习惯、文化、关系、技能\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\ncultivate 后面直接接名词\r\n\r\n✅ cultivate trust\r\n\r\n✅ cultivate relationships\r\n\r\n✅ cultivate good habits\r\n\r\n不太用于非常短期的事情\r\n\r\ncultivate 本身带有：\r\n\r\n“需要时间慢慢形成”\r\n\r\n所以如果只是一次性的动作，通常不适合。\r\n\r\ncultivated 还可以作形容词\r\n\r\na cultivated person\r\n= 有教养的人\r\n\r\na cultivated taste\r\n= 高雅的品味\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\ncultivate 最初可以理解成：\r\n\r\n“耕地、种植”\r\n\r\n🌱 播种\r\n→ 浇水\r\n→ 长大\r\n\r\n所以抽象地：\r\n\r\ncultivate a habit\r\n= 像种植物一样培养习惯\r\n\r\ncultivate trust\r\n= 慢慢建立信任\r\n\r\ncultivate relationships\r\n= 长期经营关系\r\n\r\n最值得记住的几个搭配：\r\n\r\ncultivate a habit = 培养习惯\r\ncultivate skills = 培养技能\r\ncultivate trust = 培养信任\r\ncultivate relationships = 经营关系\r\ncultivate a culture of innovation = 培养创新文化','/static/uploads/english_note_item/a0bc93f1ad2440d5a4779f2207659231.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 20:48:01',1,'2026-09-01 20:48:01'),(1576,21,63,'phrase','boil down','boil down','boil down','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nboil down\r\n= 归结为\r\n= 简化成最核心的内容\r\n= 最终本质上就是……\r\n\r\n最常见结构：\r\n\r\nboil down to sth\r\n= 归根结底是……\r\n= 本质上可以归结为……\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n“把复杂的东西一直浓缩，最后只剩下最核心的一点。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nboil down to sth\r\n= 归结为……\r\n\r\nIt all boils down to money.\r\n归根结底，都是钱的问题。\r\n\r\nThe decision boils down to cost and performance.\r\n这个决定归根结底取决于成本和性能。\r\n\r\n把复杂内容简化、浓缩\r\n\r\nCan you boil this report down to a few key points?\r\n你能把这份报告浓缩成几个关键点吗？\r\n\r\nWe need to boil the problem down to its core issue.\r\n我们需要把这个问题简化到它最核心的部分。\r\n\r\n字面意思：煮浓、熬浓\r\n\r\nBoil the sauce down until it thickens.\r\n把酱汁熬到变浓。\r\n\r\n这个字面意思正好帮助记忆抽象意思：\r\n\r\n液体越煮越少\r\n→ 最后只剩浓缩精华','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nIt really boils down to trust.\r\n归根结底，这其实就是信任问题。\r\n\r\nThe whole issue boils down to poor communication.\r\n整个问题归根结底是沟通不畅。\r\n\r\nOur choice boils down to two options.\r\n我们的选择最终就剩两个选项。\r\n\r\nCan you boil the explanation down to one sentence?\r\n你能把这个解释浓缩成一句话吗？\r\n\r\nWhen you boil it all down, the main problem is cost.\r\n归根结底，主要问题就是成本。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe problem boils down to a lack of resources.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThe problem\r\n= 这个问题\r\n\r\nboils down to\r\n= 归结为 / 本质上是\r\n\r\na lack of resources\r\n= 资源不足\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这个问题归根结底就是资源不足。\r\n\r\n这里不是说“煮”，而是比喻：\r\n\r\n把所有复杂原因都压缩以后，\r\n核心只剩：\r\n\r\na lack of resources\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nboil down to vs come down to\r\n\r\ncome down to\r\n= 归根结底取决于 / 本质上是\r\n\r\nIt comes down to experience.\r\n归根结底还是经验问题。\r\n\r\nboil down to\r\n= 很接近，但更强调“把复杂内容浓缩后得到核心”\r\n\r\nIt boils down to experience.\r\n说到底，就是经验。\r\n\r\n两者很多场景可以互换。\r\n\r\nboil down to vs be about\r\n\r\nbe about\r\n= 是关于……\r\n\r\nThis issue is about trust.\r\n这个问题是关于信任的。\r\n\r\nboil down to\r\n= 归根结底是……\r\n\r\nThis issue boils down to trust.\r\n这个问题归根结底就是信任。\r\n\r\n语气更强、更有总结感。\r\n\r\nboil down vs summarize\r\n\r\nsummarize\r\n= 总结\r\n\r\nPlease summarize the report.\r\n请总结这份报告。\r\n\r\nboil down\r\n= 浓缩到最核心内容\r\n\r\nPlease boil the report down to three key points.\r\n请把报告浓缩成三个关键点。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nsummarize → 总结\r\nboil down → 浓缩、提炼核心\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n最常见结构是：\r\n\r\n✅ boil down to + 名词\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nboil down to cost\r\nboil down to trust\r\nboil down to one issue\r\n\r\n如果表示“把某物浓缩”，结构是：\r\n\r\nboil sth down to sth\r\n\r\n✅ boil the report down to three points\r\n\r\n你刚才写的是：\r\n\r\nboil dowm ❌\r\n\r\n正确拼写：\r\n\r\nboil down ✅\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n想象一锅汤。\r\n\r\n刚开始：\r\n\r\n很多水、很多内容\r\n\r\n一直 boil：\r\n\r\n水越来越少\r\n\r\n最后：\r\n\r\n只剩最浓的精华\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nboil down to\r\n= 一直浓缩到……\r\n= 最后归结为……\r\n\r\n最值得记住的三个句子：\r\n\r\nIt all boils down to money.\r\n归根结底都是钱。\r\n\r\nThe issue boils down to communication.\r\n这个问题归根结底是沟通。\r\n\r\nCan you boil it down to one sentence?\r\n你能把它浓缩成一句话吗？','/static/uploads/english_note_item/208c73acac0e4e968edca9963b8069f1.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 20:55:17',1,'2026-09-01 20:55:17'),(1577,21,64,'phrase','favor favour','favor favour','favor favour','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nfavor / favour 最核心的意思有两个：\r\n\r\n名词：帮助、恩惠；支持、赞同\r\n\r\n动词：偏爱；支持；有利于\r\n\r\n如果你学英式英语，建议优先记：\r\n\r\nfavour\r\n\r\n因为英式拼写带 u。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\ndo sb a favor\r\n= 帮某人一个忙\r\n\r\nCan you do me a favor?\r\n你能帮我个忙吗？\r\n\r\nCould you do me a small favor?\r\n你能帮我一个小忙吗？\r\n\r\n这是非常高频的日常表达。\r\n\r\nin favor of\r\n= 支持；赞成\r\n\r\nI’m in favor of the proposal.\r\n我赞成这个提议。\r\n\r\nMost of the team were in favor of the change.\r\n团队大多数人都支持这个改动。\r\n\r\nfavor sb / sth\r\n= 偏爱；更支持\r\n\r\nThe manager tends to favor experienced candidates.\r\n经理往往更偏向有经验的候选人。\r\n\r\nThis approach favors simplicity over flexibility.\r\n这种方法更偏重简单性，而不是灵活性。\r\n\r\nbe favored by sth\r\n= 受到……青睐\r\n\r\nThe new design is favored by younger users.\r\n这个新设计更受年轻用户欢迎。\r\n\r\ncircumstances favor sth\r\n= 情况对……有利\r\n\r\nCurrent conditions favor further growth.\r\n当前条件有利于进一步增长。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nCan you do me a favor and check this file?\r\n你能帮我个忙检查一下这个文件吗？\r\n\r\nI’m strongly in favor of simplifying the workflow.\r\n我非常支持简化这个工作流程。\r\n\r\nThe company favors internal development over outsourcing.\r\n公司更倾向于内部开发，而不是外包。\r\n\r\nThe current market conditions favor larger companies.\r\n当前市场环境对大公司更有利。\r\n\r\nShe seems to favor the second option.\r\n她似乎更倾向第二个选项。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe policy favors larger companies.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThe policy\r\n= 这项政策\r\n\r\nfavors\r\n= 更有利于 / 偏向\r\n\r\nlarger companies\r\n= 大公司\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这项政策对大公司更有利。\r\n\r\n这里 favor 不是“喜欢”，而是：\r\n\r\n“让某一方处于更有利的位置。”\r\n\r\n再比如：\r\n\r\nI’m in favor of the change.\r\n\r\nin favor of\r\n= 支持、赞成\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n我支持这个改变。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nfavor vs support\r\n\r\nsupport\r\n= 支持，最普通\r\n\r\nI support the plan.\r\n我支持这个计划。\r\n\r\nbe in favor of\r\n= 赞成，稍正式\r\n\r\nI’m in favor of the plan.\r\n我赞成这个计划。\r\n\r\nfavor 作动词\r\n= 更倾向、偏爱\r\n\r\nI favor option A.\r\n我更倾向 A 方案。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nsupport → 明确支持\r\nfavor → 更偏向、青睐\r\n\r\nfavor vs prefer\r\n\r\nprefer\r\n= 更喜欢\r\n\r\nI prefer tea to coffee.\r\n比起咖啡，我更喜欢茶。\r\n\r\nfavor\r\n= 偏向某个选择，语气更正式\r\n\r\nThe committee favors the first proposal.\r\n委员会更倾向第一个提案。\r\n\r\nprefer 更日常。\r\nfavor 更常见于工作、政策、正式语境。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n英式拼写是 favour\r\n\r\n如果你用英式英语：\r\n\r\n✅ favour\r\n\r\n✅ favourite\r\n\r\n✅ favourable\r\n\r\n美式：\r\n\r\nfavor\r\nfavorite\r\nfavorable\r\n\r\ndo me a favor 是固定搭配\r\n\r\n✅ Do me a favor.\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n❌ make me a favor\r\n\r\nin favor of 后面接名词或 doing\r\n\r\n✅ in favor of the plan\r\n\r\n✅ in favor of changing the system\r\n\r\nfavor 作动词时直接接宾语\r\n\r\n✅ favor option A\r\n\r\n✅ favor experienced candidates\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 favor 想成：\r\n\r\n“把天平稍微往某一边推。”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ndo me a favor\r\n= 给我一点帮助\r\n\r\nbe in favor of\r\n= 站在支持这一边\r\n\r\nfavor option A\r\n= 更偏向 A\r\n\r\n最值得记住的几个表达：\r\n\r\ndo sb a favor = 帮某人一个忙\r\nin favor of = 支持、赞成\r\nfavor one option over another = 更倾向一个选项\r\nfavor experienced candidates = 偏爱有经验的候选人\r\nfavorable conditions = 有利条件','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9e41d7c0ec384dc0bacc8785244bb95f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-01 21:15:21',1,'2026-09-01 21:15:21'),(1578,21,65,'vocab','deem','deem','deem','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ndeem\r\n= 认为；视为；认定\r\n\r\n它比 think 正式得多，常用于：\r\n\r\n法律\r\n\r\n政策\r\n\r\n新闻\r\n\r\n商务文件\r\n\r\n正式报告\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n“经过判断后，把某人或某事正式认定为某种状态。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\ndeem sth + adjective\r\n= 认为某事是……\r\n\r\nThe plan was deemed unsafe.\r\n这个计划被认为是不安全的。\r\n\r\nThe application was deemed incomplete.\r\n这个申请被认定为不完整。\r\n\r\ndeem sb/sth to be + 名词 / 形容词\r\n= 认为某人 / 某事是……\r\n\r\nThe court deemed the evidence to be insufficient.\r\n法院认为这些证据不足。\r\n\r\nThe system was deemed to be reliable.\r\n这个系统被认为是可靠的。\r\n\r\ndeem it + adjective + to do sth\r\n= 认为做某事是……\r\n\r\nThey deemed it necessary to delay the launch.\r\n他们认为有必要推迟发布。\r\n\r\nThe company deemed it appropriate to conduct a further review.\r\n公司认为有必要进行进一步审查。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThe proposal was deemed too expensive.\r\n这项提议被认为成本过高。\r\n\r\nThe regulator deemed the company’s response inadequate.\r\n监管机构认为公司的回应不充分。\r\n\r\nThe issue was deemed serious enough to require further investigation.\r\n这个问题被认为足够严重，需要进一步调查。\r\n\r\nWe deemed it necessary to redesign the workflow.\r\n我们认为有必要重新设计这个工作流程。\r\n\r\nAny document deemed invalid will be rejected.\r\n任何被认定为无效的文件都会被拒绝。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe document was deemed invalid.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThe document\r\n= 这个文件\r\n\r\nwas deemed\r\n= 被认定为 / 被认为\r\n\r\ninvalid\r\n= 无效的\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n这个文件被认定为无效。\r\n\r\n这里如果换成：\r\n\r\nThe document was thought to be invalid.\r\n\r\n也能理解，但 deem 更正式，而且更有“经过判断后作出认定”的感觉。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\ndeem vs think\r\n\r\nthink\r\n= 觉得、认为\r\n\r\n最普通、最口语。\r\n\r\nI think the plan is risky.\r\n我觉得这个计划有风险。\r\n\r\ndeem\r\n= 正式认定\r\n\r\nThe plan was deemed risky.\r\n这个计划被认定为有风险。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nthink → 日常判断\r\ndeem → 正式判断 / 认定\r\n\r\ndeem vs consider\r\n\r\nconsider\r\n= 认为、考虑\r\n\r\n比 think 正式，但仍然很常用。\r\n\r\nWe consider this approach effective.\r\n我们认为这种方法有效。\r\n\r\ndeem\r\n= 更正式、更书面，常带“认定”的感觉\r\n\r\nThis approach was deemed effective.\r\n这种方法被认定为有效。\r\n\r\ndeem vs regard as\r\n\r\nregard A as B\r\n= 把 A 看作 B\r\n\r\nHe is regarded as an expert.\r\n他被视为专家。\r\n\r\ndeem\r\n= 更强调正式判断结果\r\n\r\nThe court deemed him responsible.\r\n法院认定他负有责任。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\ndeem 后面可以直接接形容词\r\n\r\n✅ deem the plan unsafe\r\n\r\n✅ deem the request invalid\r\n\r\n不一定非要加 to be。\r\n\r\n被动语态特别常见\r\n\r\n✅ be deemed necessary\r\n\r\n✅ be deemed appropriate\r\n\r\n✅ be deemed invalid\r\n\r\n✅ be deemed unsafe\r\n\r\n这是 deem 最值得掌握的一组用法。\r\n\r\ndeem 很正式\r\n\r\n日常聊天里一般不会说：\r\n\r\nI deem this restaurant good.\r\n\r\n会显得很生硬。\r\n\r\n更自然：\r\n\r\nI think this restaurant is good.\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 deem 记成：\r\n\r\n“正式盖章认定”\r\n\r\n比如一个文件经过审核：\r\n\r\n✅ VALID\r\n❌ INVALID\r\n\r\n审核人员最终：\r\n\r\ndeem the document invalid\r\n= 正式认定这个文件无效\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ndeem\r\n≈ officially judge / consider\r\n≈ 正式认为、认定\r\n\r\n最值得记住的几个搭配：\r\n\r\nbe deemed necessary\r\n= 被认为有必要\r\n\r\nbe deemed appropriate\r\n= 被认为合适\r\n\r\nbe deemed invalid\r\n= 被认定无效\r\n\r\nbe deemed unsafe\r\n= 被认为不安全\r\n\r\ndeem it necessary to do sth\r\n= 认为有必要做某事','/static/uploads/english_note_item/7a9fb92f0d3f49de906a9db2f03b7f14.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-02 14:21:22',1,'2026-09-02 14:21:22'),(1579,21,66,'vocab','deterioration','deterioration','deterioration','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\ndeterioration\r\n= 恶化；变坏；退化\r\n\r\n核心感觉是：\r\n\r\n“某种状态原本还可以，但随着时间推移越来越差。”\r\n\r\n常用于：\r\n\r\nhealth 健康\r\n\r\ncondition 状况\r\n\r\nrelationship 关系\r\n\r\nperformance 性能\r\n\r\nquality 质量\r\n\r\neconomy 经济\r\n\r\ninfrastructure 基础设施','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n状况恶化\r\n\r\na deterioration in condition\r\n= 状况恶化\r\n\r\nThere has been a noticeable deterioration in the system’s performance.\r\n系统性能出现了明显下降。\r\n\r\n健康恶化\r\n\r\na deterioration in health\r\n= 健康状况恶化\r\n\r\nDoctors were concerned about the rapid deterioration in his condition.\r\n医生担心他的身体状况迅速恶化。\r\n\r\n关系恶化\r\n\r\na deterioration in relations\r\n= 关系恶化\r\n\r\nThe dispute led to a deterioration in relations between the two companies.\r\n这场争端导致两家公司之间的关系恶化。\r\n\r\n质量下降 / 老化\r\n\r\ndeterioration of infrastructure\r\n= 基础设施老化、恶化\r\n\r\nThe report highlights the deterioration of the road network.\r\n这份报告强调了道路网络不断恶化的问题。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nWe have seen a gradual deterioration in system performance.\r\n我们发现系统性能在逐渐下降。\r\n\r\nThe building showed signs of deterioration.\r\n这栋建筑出现了老化迹象。\r\n\r\nThere has been a significant deterioration in service quality.\r\n服务质量出现了明显恶化。\r\n\r\nThe situation has deteriorated rapidly over the past few days.\r\n过去几天情况迅速恶化。\r\n\r\nPoor maintenance can lead to the deterioration of equipment.\r\n维护不当会导致设备状况恶化。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThere has been a deterioration in performance.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThere has been\r\n= 出现了 / 已经发生了\r\n\r\na deterioration\r\n= 恶化 / 下降\r\n\r\nin performance\r\n= 在性能方面\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n性能出现了下降。\r\n\r\n这里 deterioration 比：\r\n\r\na drop in performance\r\n性能下降\r\n\r\n更正式，也更强调：\r\n\r\n“状态是在逐渐变坏。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\ndeterioration vs decline\r\n\r\ndecline\r\n= 下降、衰退\r\n\r\n强调数值、水平或者整体趋势下降。\r\n\r\na decline in sales\r\n= 销售下降\r\n\r\ndeterioration\r\n= 恶化、变差\r\n\r\n更强调“质量或状态越来越糟”。\r\n\r\na deterioration in quality\r\n= 质量恶化\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ndecline → 往下走\r\ndeterioration → 越来越差\r\n\r\ndeterioration vs degradation\r\n\r\ndegradation\r\n= 降级、退化、性能衰减\r\n\r\n技术场景很常见。\r\n\r\nperformance degradation\r\n= 性能退化\r\n\r\ndeterioration\r\n= 更通用，可以形容健康、关系、环境、设备等。\r\n\r\ndeterioration vs worsening\r\n\r\nworsening\r\n= 变得更糟\r\n\r\n更普通、更直接。\r\n\r\nthe worsening situation\r\n= 不断恶化的局势\r\n\r\ndeterioration\r\n= 更正式、更书面\r\n\r\na deterioration in the situation\r\n= 局势恶化\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n最常见搭配是：\r\n\r\ndeterioration in + 某种状态\r\n\r\n✅ deterioration in health\r\n\r\n✅ deterioration in performance\r\n\r\n✅ deterioration in quality\r\n\r\n也可以用：\r\n\r\ndeterioration of + 某个具体事物\r\n\r\n✅ deterioration of the building\r\n\r\n✅ deterioration of infrastructure\r\n\r\n动词是 deteriorate\r\n\r\n✅ The situation deteriorated.\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n❌ The situation deterioration.\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n可以把 deterioration 想成一个状态：\r\n\r\nGOOD → OK → BAD → WORSE\r\n\r\n不是突然坏掉，\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\n一点一点越来越差。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ndeterioration\r\n= 状态持续往坏的方向发展\r\n= 恶化 / 退化\r\n\r\n最值得记住的几个搭配：\r\n\r\ndeterioration in health\r\n= 健康恶化\r\n\r\ndeterioration in performance\r\n= 性能下降\r\n\r\ndeterioration in quality\r\n= 质量恶化\r\n\r\ndeterioration in relations\r\n= 关系恶化\r\n\r\nsigns of deterioration\r\n= 恶化 / 老化的迹象','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9dfd774a6a4743d79d227718a6d65f2b.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-02 14:27:38',1,'2026-09-02 14:27:38'),(1580,21,67,'phrase','be done','be done','be done','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nbe done 最常见有几个意思：\r\n\r\n做完了 / 完成了\r\n\r\n结束了\r\n\r\n某事被做完了\r\n\r\nbe done with sth = 受够了 / 不想再管了 / 和某事结束了','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nbe done = 做完了\r\n\r\nI’m done.\r\n我做完了。\r\n\r\nThe report is done.\r\n报告完成了。\r\n\r\nAre you done with the task?\r\n你这个任务做完了吗？\r\n\r\nbe done = 结束了\r\n\r\nThe meeting is done.\r\n会议结束了。\r\n\r\nWe’re done for today.\r\n我们今天就到这里了。\r\n\r\nbe done = 被完成\r\n\r\nThe work needs to be done by Friday.\r\n这项工作需要在周五之前完成。\r\n\r\nEverything is done.\r\n所有事情都已经处理好了。\r\n\r\nbe done with sth = 做完某事 / 不再需要某物\r\n\r\nI’m done with the report.\r\n报告我已经做完了。\r\n\r\nAre you done with the laptop?\r\n这台电脑你用完了吗？\r\n\r\n这里可以只是普通的“用完 / 做完”。\r\n\r\nbe done with sb/sth = 受够了；不想再继续\r\n\r\n这个语气要根据上下文判断。\r\n\r\nI’m done with this job.\r\n我受够这份工作了 / 我不想再干了。\r\n\r\nI’m done with him.\r\n我和他彻底结束了 / 我不想再和他有关系了。\r\n\r\nI’m done arguing about this.\r\n我不想再为这件事争论了。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nI’m almost done.\r\n我快做完了。\r\n\r\nThe testing is done.\r\n测试已经完成了。\r\n\r\nOnce this is done, we can deploy the application.\r\n这个完成之后，我们就可以部署应用了。\r\n\r\nI’m done with my work for today.\r\n我今天的工作做完了。\r\n\r\nI’m done with this conversation.\r\n我不想再继续这个对话了。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nOnce the processing is done, the result will be saved to the database.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nOnce\r\n= 一旦 / 当……之后\r\n\r\nthe processing is done\r\n= 处理完成\r\n\r\nthe result will be saved\r\n= 结果将被保存\r\n\r\nto the database\r\n= 到数据库中\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n处理完成后，结果将被保存到数据库中。\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n\r\nis done\r\n≈ is completed\r\n\r\n但 done 更自然、更口语一些。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nbe done vs be finished\r\n\r\n两者很多时候都表示“完成”。\r\n\r\nThe work is done.\r\n工作完成了。\r\n\r\nThe work is finished.\r\n工作完成了。\r\n\r\n区别很小，但：\r\n\r\ndone → 更口语、更常见\r\nfinished → 更明确强调“结束 / 完成”\r\n\r\nbe done vs complete\r\n\r\ncomplete 更正式。\r\n\r\nThe migration is complete.\r\n迁移已经完成。\r\n\r\nThe migration is done.\r\n迁移做完了。\r\n\r\n技术文档里 complete 往往更正式，日常汇报中 done 很自然。\r\n\r\nbe done vs be done with\r\n\r\n这两个不要混：\r\n\r\nI’m done.\r\n= 我做完了。\r\n\r\nI’m done with the task.\r\n= 这个任务我做完了。\r\n\r\nI’m done with this.\r\n= 我受够这个了 / 我不想再弄了。\r\n\r\n最后一个非常依赖语气。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nI’m done 不一定是“我完蛋了”\r\n\r\n通常只是：\r\n\r\n我做完了。\r\n\r\n例如老师问：\r\n\r\nAre you finished?\r\n\r\n你可以说：\r\n\r\nI’m done.\r\n\r\nI’m done with it 有两种可能\r\n\r\n= 我已经把它做完了\r\n或\r\n= 我受够它了\r\n\r\n要根据语境判断。\r\n\r\ndone 是 do 的过去分词\r\n\r\ndo → did → done\r\n\r\n✅ It is done.\r\n❌ It is did.\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 done 直接记成：\r\n\r\n“事情已经打上 ✅ 了。”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nI’m done.\r\n= 我的任务 ✅\r\n\r\nIt’s done.\r\n= 这件事 ✅\r\n\r\nWe’re done.\r\n= 我们结束了 ✅\r\n\r\nI’m done with this.\r\n= 这件事到此为止 ❌ 不想继续了\r\n\r\n最值得记住的几个表达：\r\n\r\nI’m done.\r\n= 我做完了。\r\n\r\nIt’s done.\r\n= 做好了。\r\n\r\nWe’re done for today.\r\n= 今天就到这里。\r\n\r\nI’m done with it.\r\n= 我做完它了 / 我受够它了。\r\n\r\nOnce it’s done, we can move on.\r\n= 做完以后，我们就可以继续下一步。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e1f59f9bdc4b4333a9a505915d96cd8c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-02 14:32:56',1,'2026-09-02 14:32:56'),(1581,21,68,'phrase','turn up','turn up','turn up','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nturn up 有几个非常常见的意思：\r\n\r\n出现；到场\r\n\r\n调大音量、温度、亮度等\r\n\r\n被找到；出现结果\r\n\r\n卷起、翻起（较具体）\r\n\r\n最常用的两个一定要掌握：\r\n\r\nturn up = 出现 / 到场\r\nturn sth up = 把……调高','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nturn up = 出现；到场\r\n\r\nHe turned up late for the meeting.\r\n他开会迟到了。\r\n\r\nShe turned up at my house without calling.\r\n她没打电话就直接到我家来了。\r\n\r\nNobody expected him to turn up.\r\n没人想到他会出现。\r\n\r\n这个意思很口语，也很常见。\r\n\r\nturn sth up = 调高\r\n\r\nTurn up the volume.\r\n把音量调大。\r\n\r\nCan you turn the heating up?\r\n你能把暖气调高一点吗？\r\n\r\nTurn the brightness up a little.\r\n把亮度调高一点。\r\n\r\n注意：\r\n\r\nturn up the volume\r\n和\r\nturn the volume up\r\n\r\n都对。\r\n\r\nturn up = 被找到；突然出现\r\n\r\nMy keys finally turned up.\r\n我的钥匙终于找到了。\r\n\r\nSome new evidence has turned up.\r\n出现了一些新证据。\r\n\r\nThe missing document turned up in an old folder.\r\n丢失的文件最后在一个旧文件夹里找到了。\r\n\r\nturn up = 翻起 / 卷起\r\n\r\nHe turned up his collar.\r\n他把衣领翻了起来。\r\n\r\nShe turned up the ends of her jeans.\r\n她把牛仔裤裤脚卷了起来。\r\n\r\n这个意思没有前几个常用。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nHe didn’t turn up for work today.\r\n他今天没来上班。\r\n\r\nShe turned up unexpectedly.\r\n她突然出现了。\r\n\r\nCan you turn the TV up?\r\n你能把电视声音调大一点吗？\r\n\r\nThe missing file eventually turned up.\r\n丢失的文件最后找到了。\r\n\r\nSomething interesting turned up during the investigation.\r\n调查过程中出现了一些有意思的新情况。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nHe turned up at the house unannounced.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nHe turned up\r\n= 他出现了 / 他来了\r\n\r\nat the house\r\n= 到那栋房子\r\n\r\nunannounced\r\n= 没有提前通知地\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n他没有提前通知就直接出现在那栋房子里。\r\n\r\n这里 turn up 很像：\r\n\r\nshow up\r\n= 出现 / 到场\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nturn up vs show up\r\n\r\n两者都可以表示：\r\n\r\n出现 / 到场\r\n\r\nHe turned up late.\r\n他迟到了。\r\n\r\nHe showed up late.\r\n他迟到了。\r\n\r\n区别很小。\r\n\r\nturn up\r\n→ 英式英语里尤其常见\r\n\r\nshow up\r\n→ 美式英语里非常常见\r\n\r\n两者日常口语都很自然。\r\n\r\nturn up vs arrive\r\n\r\narrive\r\n= 到达\r\n\r\n比较中性。\r\n\r\nHe arrived at 8.\r\n他八点到了。\r\n\r\nturn up\r\n= 出现、露面\r\n\r\n更口语，有时带一点“终于来了 / 突然来了”的感觉。\r\n\r\nHe finally turned up at 8.\r\n他终于八点出现了。\r\n\r\nturn up vs find\r\n\r\nfind\r\n= 主动找到\r\n\r\nI found my keys.\r\n我找到钥匙了。\r\n\r\nturn up\r\n= 某物自己“出现了”\r\n\r\nMy keys turned up.\r\n我的钥匙找到了 / 出现了。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n“出现”时不需要宾语\r\n\r\n✅ He turned up late.\r\n\r\n“调高”时要有宾语\r\n\r\n✅ turn up the volume\r\n\r\n✅ turn the volume up\r\n\r\n代词放中间\r\n\r\n✅ turn it up\r\n❌ turn up it\r\n\r\n不要把所有 turn up 都翻译成“出现”\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nTurn up the music.\r\n= 把音乐调大。\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n“让音乐出现”。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 turn up 想成：\r\n\r\nup = 往上\r\n\r\n所以有两个核心画面：\r\n\r\n人“冒出来了”\r\n→ turn up\r\n→ 出现\r\n\r\n数值“往上调”\r\n→ turn sth up\r\n→ 调高\r\n\r\n最值得记住的几个表达：\r\n\r\nturn up late\r\n= 迟到 / 晚出现\r\n\r\nturn up unexpectedly\r\n= 突然出现\r\n\r\nturn up the volume\r\n= 调大音量\r\n\r\nturn the heating up\r\n= 调高暖气\r\n\r\nThe missing file turned up.\r\n= 丢失的文件找到了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/621c4b9b43ea480a88c5b6166755ab14.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-02 14:38:29',1,'2026-09-02 14:38:29'),(1582,21,69,'vocab','harass','harass','harass','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\nharass\r\n= 骚扰；不断烦扰；纠缠\r\n= 通过反复、持续的行为让某人感到害怕、压力、不舒服或被冒犯\r\n\r\n它比 annoy 强很多。\r\n\r\nannoy 只是“烦到别人”，\r\nharass 往往带有：\r\n\r\n“持续、反复、有压迫感，甚至可能涉及违法或不当行为。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n骚扰某人\r\n\r\nHe was accused of harassing his neighbour.\r\n他被指控骚扰邻居。\r\n\r\nShe said she had been harassed online.\r\n她说自己曾遭到网络骚扰。\r\n\r\n持续纠缠、反复联系\r\n\r\nHe kept calling and messaging her, which she considered harassment.\r\n他不断给她打电话、发消息，她认为这构成了骚扰。\r\n\r\nThey were harassed by repeated phone calls.\r\n他们受到反复电话骚扰。\r\n\r\n工作场景中的骚扰\r\n\r\nharass an employee\r\n= 骚扰员工\r\n\r\nworkplace harassment\r\n= 职场骚扰\r\n\r\nsexual harassment\r\n= 性骚扰\r\n\r\n例：\r\n\r\nThe company has a strict policy against workplace harassment.\r\n公司对职场骚扰有严格规定。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nHe was warned not to harass her again.\r\n他被警告不要再骚扰她。\r\n\r\nShe reported that someone had been harassing her online.\r\n她举报说有人一直在网上骚扰她。\r\n\r\nEmployees should be able to work without being harassed.\r\n员工应该能够在不受骚扰的情况下工作。\r\n\r\nRepeated unwanted messages may amount to harassment.\r\n反复发送对方不想收到的信息可能构成骚扰。\r\n\r\nThe law protects people from being harassed or threatened.\r\n法律保护人们免受骚扰或威胁。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nHe was harassing her with repeated messages.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nHe was harassing her\r\n= 他一直在骚扰她\r\n\r\nwith repeated messages\r\n= 通过反复发送消息\r\n\r\n整句：\r\n\r\n他通过不断发消息骚扰她。\r\n\r\n这里重点不是：\r\n\r\n“发了一条烦人的消息”\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\n“反复、持续地进行让对方不舒服的行为。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\n\r\nharass vs annoy\r\n\r\nannoy\r\n= 惹烦、使恼火\r\n\r\nMy neighbour’s music annoys me.\r\n邻居的音乐让我很烦。\r\n\r\nharass\r\n= 持续骚扰、纠缠，严重得多\r\n\r\nHe kept messaging her and harassing her.\r\n他不断给她发消息骚扰她。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nannoy → 烦\r\nharass → 骚扰、纠缠\r\n\r\nharass vs bother\r\n\r\nbother\r\n= 打扰、烦扰\r\n\r\nSorry to bother you.\r\n抱歉打扰你。\r\n\r\nharass\r\n= 明显更严重，通常是不受欢迎的持续行为\r\n\r\nDo not harass other users.\r\n不要骚扰其他用户。\r\n\r\nharass vs bully\r\n\r\nbully\r\n= 欺凌、霸凌\r\n\r\n通常强调通过权力、体格或群体优势欺负别人。\r\n\r\nharass\r\n= 骚扰，形式更广\r\n\r\n例如可以是：\r\n\r\nmessages\r\ncalls\r\ncomments\r\nfollowing someone\r\nthreatening behaviour\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nharass 后面直接接人\r\n\r\n✅ harass someone\r\n❌ harass to someone\r\n\r\n名词是 harassment\r\n\r\nharassment\r\n= 骚扰\r\n\r\n常见：\r\n\r\nonline harassment\r\n= 网络骚扰\r\n\r\nworkplace harassment\r\n= 职场骚扰\r\n\r\nsexual harassment\r\n= 性骚扰\r\n\r\n被动语态很常见\r\n\r\n✅ She was harassed online.\r\n她在网上遭到骚扰。\r\n\r\n✅ He claimed he had been harassed.\r\n他声称自己受到过骚扰。\r\n\r\n这是比较强的词\r\n\r\n如果只是普通“烦人”，不要随便用 harass。\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nMy brother keeps asking me questions.\r\n\r\n如果只是觉得烦，更自然：\r\n\r\nHe keeps bothering me.\r\n\r\n而不是：\r\n\r\nHe keeps harassing me.\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 harass 想成：\r\n\r\n“不是烦你一次，而是反复来。”\r\n\r\n一次打扰：\r\nbother\r\n\r\n让你觉得烦：\r\nannoy\r\n\r\n反复、持续、让你感到压力甚至害怕：\r\nharass\r\n\r\n最值得记住的几个搭配：\r\n\r\nharass someone\r\n= 骚扰某人\r\n\r\nonline harassment\r\n= 网络骚扰\r\n\r\nworkplace harassment\r\n= 职场骚扰\r\n\r\nsexual harassment\r\n= 性骚扰\r\n\r\nbe harassed by someone\r\n= 被某人骚扰','/static/uploads/english_note_item/9b85c7c14e974209995c7323fdef8459.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-02 15:15:08',1,'2026-09-02 15:15:08'),(1583,21,70,'phrase','mitigate the security risk','mitigate the security risk','mitigate the security risk','🎯 核心意思\r\nmitigate the security risk = 降低安全风险 / 缓解安全风险\r\n\r\nmitigate 强调：不能一定把风险完全消除，但可以把风险的程度、影响或发生可能性降低。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\nmitigate the risk\r\n= 降低风险\r\n\r\nmitigate security risks\r\n= 降低各种安全风险\r\n\r\nmitigate the impact\r\n= 减轻影响\r\n\r\nmitigate the damage\r\n= 减少损害\r\n\r\nmitigate potential threats\r\n= 降低潜在威胁\r\n\r\n在软件开发、安全设计、架构说明里非常常见。','💬 中英双语例句\r\nWe introduced a business ID to mitigate the security risk.\r\n我们引入了一个业务 ID 来降低安全风险。\r\n\r\nThis design helps mitigate the risk of unauthorized access.\r\n这个设计有助于降低未经授权访问的风险。\r\n\r\nUsing predictable IDs may expose sensitive data, so we use random identifiers to mitigate the security risk.\r\n使用可预测的 ID 可能会暴露敏感数据，因此我们使用随机标识符来降低安全风险。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\nmitigate the security risk\r\n\r\nmitigate\r\n= make a problem or harmful effect less serious\r\n= 让问题、风险或负面影响变得没那么严重\r\n\r\nthe security risk\r\n= 前面已经提到的那个具体安全风险\r\n\r\n所以整句话可以理解成：\r\n\r\n“采取措施，把这个安全风险压低。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\nmitigate the risk\r\n= 降低、缓解风险\r\n正式、专业，尤其适合技术和安全语境\r\n\r\nreduce the risk\r\n= 降低风险\r\n最普通、最通用\r\n\r\nminimize the risk\r\n= 尽可能把风险降到最低\r\n语气比 mitigate 更强\r\n\r\neliminate the risk\r\n= 完全消除风险\r\n语气最强，表示风险基本不存在\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe can mitigate the risk.\r\n我们可以降低这个风险。\r\n\r\nWe can eliminate the risk.\r\n我们可以彻底消除这个风险。\r\n\r\n两者不能完全互换。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ mitigate down the risk\r\n\r\n因为 mitigate 本身已经有“降低”的含义。\r\n\r\n正确：\r\n\r\n✅ mitigate the risk\r\n\r\n✅ mitigate security risks\r\n\r\n✅ mitigate the risk of data leakage\r\n\r\n另外，security risk 如果是泛指，常用复数：\r\n\r\n✅ mitigate security risks\r\n\r\n如果是前面已经提到的某一个具体风险：\r\n\r\n✅ mitigate the security risk\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n可以把 mitigate 记成：\r\n\r\nHigh Risk → mitigation → Lower Risk\r\n\r\n它的核心不是“消灭”，而是：\r\n\r\n“把严重程度压下来。”\r\n\r\n最值得记的一句：\r\n\r\nWe introduced a business ID to mitigate the risk of unauthorized data access.\r\n我们引入了一个业务 ID，以降低未经授权访问数据的风险。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/bdfa241c30474070b7e337d42f592090.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-03 20:20:02',1,'2026-09-03 20:20:02'),(1584,21,71,'phrase','it s lagging','it s lagging','it s lagging','🎯 核心意思\r\nit’s lagging = 它很卡 / 它有延迟 / 它反应很慢\r\n\r\n这个表达非常自然，常用于：\r\n\r\n电脑\r\n\r\n手机\r\n\r\n软件\r\n\r\n游戏\r\n\r\n视频\r\n\r\n网络\r\n\r\n鼠标、界面操作','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n软件或设备卡顿\r\nThe app is lagging.\r\n这个应用很卡。\r\n\r\n游戏延迟\r\nThe game is lagging badly.\r\n这个游戏卡得很厉害。\r\n\r\n视频或音频不同步、延迟\r\nThe video is lagging.\r\n视频有延迟。\r\n\r\n网络导致反应慢\r\nMy connection is lagging.\r\n我的网络连接有点卡。\r\n\r\n常见搭配：\r\n\r\nlag a bit = 有点卡\r\n\r\nlag badly = 卡得很严重\r\n\r\nstart lagging = 开始卡了\r\n\r\nkeep lagging = 一直卡\r\n\r\nstop lagging = 不再卡顿','💬 中英双语例句\r\nIt’s lagging a bit.\r\n它有点卡。\r\n\r\nMy computer starts lagging when I open too many applications.\r\n我打开太多应用程序时，电脑就开始变卡。\r\n\r\nThe video is lagging behind the audio.\r\n视频画面比声音慢，有延迟。\r\n\r\nThe system was lagging badly just now.\r\n刚才系统卡得很厉害。\r\n\r\nWhy is it lagging so much today?\r\n今天怎么这么卡？\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\nIt’s lagging.\r\n\r\nIt’s = It is\r\nlagging = lag 的现在进行时\r\n\r\n这里用现在进行时，是因为你在描述“此刻正在发生的卡顿”。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nIt’s lagging.\r\n≈ It’s responding slowly right now.\r\n= 它现在反应很慢 / 很卡。\r\n\r\n如果是你刚刚在使用 ChatGPT、网页或程序时感觉很卡，这句话非常合适。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\nIt’s lagging.\r\n= 它有延迟、很卡\r\n\r\n✅ 最适合网络、软件、游戏、电脑\r\n\r\nIt’s slow.\r\n= 它很慢\r\n范围更广，不一定是技术上的“卡顿”\r\n\r\nIt’s freezing.\r\n= 它卡死了 / 画面不动了\r\n程度比 lagging 严重\r\n\r\nIt’s stuck.\r\n= 它卡住了\r\n通常表示操作无法继续\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nIt’s lagging.\r\n还能用，但是很卡。\r\n\r\nIt’s freezing.\r\n画面经常直接不动。\r\n\r\nIt’s stuck.\r\n卡在某个页面或步骤上了。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n❌ It has lagging.\r\n\r\n应该说：\r\n\r\n✅ It’s lagging.\r\n\r\n✅ It has a lot of lag.\r\n\r\nlag 既可以是动词，也可以是名词：\r\n\r\n动词：\r\nThe game is lagging.\r\n\r\n名词：\r\nThere’s a lot of lag.\r\n延迟很严重。\r\n\r\n如果只是普通意义上的“运行慢”，也可以说：\r\nThe system is running slowly.\r\n\r\n但日常技术场景里：\r\nIt’s lagging.\r\n更口语、更形象。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n可以把 lag 想象成：\r\n\r\n你的操作 →→→ 系统反应\r\n\r\n正常：\r\n点击 → 马上响应\r\n\r\nlag：\r\n点击 → ……过一会儿才响应\r\n\r\n所以 lag 的感觉就是：\r\n\r\n“反应总是落后一步。”\r\n\r\n最值得记的三句：\r\n\r\nIt’s lagging.\r\n它很卡。\r\n\r\nIt’s lagging a bit.\r\n它有点卡。\r\n\r\nIt’s lagging badly.\r\n它卡得很厉害。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/afc489ea8b04419c94d290b1c6a08f45.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 10:27:27',1,'2026-09-04 10:27:27'),(1585,21,72,'phrase','quite a lot of','quite a lot of','quite a lot of','🎯 核心意思\r\nquite a lot of = 相当多的 / 挺多的\r\n\r\n语气比 a lot of 更强调一些，但通常没有 extremely many / a huge amount of 那么夸张。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nquite a lot of + 可数名词复数\r\n= 相当多的……\r\n\r\nQuite a lot of people came to the meeting.\r\n相当多的人来参加了会议。\r\n\r\nquite a lot of + 不可数名词\r\n= 相当多的……\r\n\r\nWe spent quite a lot of time on this issue.\r\n我们在这个问题上花了相当多的时间。\r\n\r\nquite a lot\r\n也可以单独使用，不接名词。\r\n\r\nI learned quite a lot from this project.\r\n我从这个项目中学到了很多。\r\n\r\n常见搭配：\r\n\r\nquite a lot of time = 相当多的时间\r\n\r\nquite a lot of work = 相当多的工作\r\n\r\nquite a lot of people = 挺多人\r\n\r\nquite a lot of money = 不少钱\r\n\r\nquite a lot of changes = 相当多的变化','💬 中英双语例句\r\nThere are quite a lot of files to process.\r\n有相当多的文件需要处理。\r\n\r\nWe encountered quite a lot of issues during testing.\r\n我们在测试过程中遇到了不少问题。\r\n\r\nThis feature requires quite a lot of work.\r\n这个功能需要相当多的工作量。\r\n\r\nQuite a lot of users reported the same problem.\r\n有相当多的用户报告了同样的问题。\r\n\r\nI’ve learned quite a lot about OCR from this project.\r\n我通过这个项目学到了很多关于 OCR 的知识。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\nquite a lot of\r\n\r\n结构是：\r\n\r\nquite + a lot of + 名词\r\n\r\n这里的 quite 用来加强 a lot of。\r\n\r\na lot of\r\n= 很多\r\n\r\nquite a lot of\r\n= 相当多 / 挺多 / 比预想中多\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe made a lot of changes.\r\n我们做了很多修改。\r\n\r\nWe made quite a lot of changes.\r\n我们做了相当多的修改。\r\n\r\n第二句的强调程度更明显。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\na lot of\r\n= 很多\r\n最普通、最常见\r\n\r\nquite a lot of\r\n= 相当多 / 挺多\r\n比 a lot of 稍微更强调\r\n\r\na fair bit of\r\n= 不少\r\n更偏口语，通常接不可数名词\r\n\r\nquite a few\r\n= 相当多\r\n只能接可数名词复数\r\n\r\na great deal of\r\n= 大量的\r\n更正式，主要接不可数名词\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nquite a lot of people\r\n\r\n✅ 相当多的人\r\n\r\nquite a few people\r\n\r\n✅ 相当多的人\r\n\r\nquite a lot of time\r\n\r\n✅ 相当多的时间\r\n\r\nquite a few time\r\n❌ 错误，time 在这里是不可数名词\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nquite a lot of 后面既可以接可数名词，也可以接不可数名词：\r\n\r\n✅ quite a lot of people\r\n\r\n✅ quite a lot of time\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ quite lot of\r\n\r\n必须有 a：\r\n\r\n✅ quite a lot of\r\n\r\nquite a lot of 很适合口语和日常工作表达，不算特别正式。\r\n\r\n例如你做项目汇报时可以说：\r\n\r\nWe’ve made quite a lot of changes to the database structure.\r\n我们对数据库结构做了相当多的修改。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n可以把程度理解成：\r\n\r\nsome\r\n一些\r\n\r\na lot of\r\n很多\r\n\r\nquite a lot of\r\n相当多 / 挺多\r\n\r\na huge amount of / a huge number of\r\n非常多\r\n\r\n记住：\r\n\r\nquite = “挺、相当”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nquite a lot of\r\n≈ 挺多的 / 相当多的。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b287c10761a14e7ebea7805a3e036010.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 10:37:00',1,'2026-09-04 10:37:00'),(1586,21,73,'phrase','How come there s so little data in the table','How come there s so little data in the table','How come there s so little data in the table','🎯 核心意思\r\nHow come there’s so little data in the table?\r\n= 为什么表里只有这么少的数据？\r\n= 怎么这个表里的数据这么少？\r\n\r\n这是很自然的口语表达，比 Why is there so little data in the table? 更口语、更随意。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nHow come + 陈述语序\r\n= 为什么……？/ 怎么会……？\r\n\r\nHow come you’re late?\r\n你怎么迟到了？\r\n\r\nHow come it’s not working?\r\n怎么它不能用了？\r\n\r\n注意：How come 后面通常不用疑问句倒装。\r\n\r\nso little + 不可数名词\r\n= 这么少的……\r\n\r\nso little data\r\n这么少的数据\r\n\r\nso little time\r\n这么少的时间\r\n\r\nso little information\r\n这么少的信息\r\n\r\nin the table\r\n= 在这个表里\r\n\r\n在数据库语境中，也可以理解为：\r\n\r\nthe database table\r\n数据库表','💬 中英双语例句\r\nHow come there’s so little data in the table?\r\n为什么这个表里的数据这么少？\r\n\r\nHow come there are so few records in this table?\r\n为什么这个表里只有这么少的记录？\r\n\r\nHow come we have so little test data?\r\n为什么我们的测试数据这么少？\r\n\r\nHow come this table only contains a few rows?\r\n为什么这个表里只有几行数据？\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\nHow come there’s so little data in the table?\r\n\r\nHow come\r\n= 为什么 / 怎么会\r\n\r\nthere’s\r\n= there is\r\n\r\nso little data\r\n= 这么少的数据\r\n\r\nin the table\r\n= 在这个表里\r\n\r\n整句结构：\r\n\r\nHow come + there is + so little data + in the table?\r\n\r\n重点是：\r\n\r\nHow come 后面直接用陈述语序。\r\n\r\n✅ How come there’s so little data?\r\n❌ How come is there so little data?\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\nHow come there’s so little data in the table?\r\n= 怎么这个表里的数据这么少？\r\n更口语、更自然\r\n\r\nWhy is there so little data in the table?\r\n= 为什么这个表里的数据这么少？\r\n更中性、更标准\r\n\r\nWhy does this table contain so little data?\r\n= 为什么这个表包含这么少的数据？\r\n更正式、偏技术表达\r\n\r\nHow come there are so few records in the table?\r\n= 为什么表里的记录这么少？\r\n如果你强调的是“记录条数”，这个更准确。\r\n\r\nlittle vs few：\r\n\r\nlittle + 不可数名词\r\n\r\n✅ little data\r\n\r\n✅ little information\r\n\r\nfew + 可数名词复数\r\n\r\n✅ few records\r\n\r\n✅ few rows\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\ndata 在现代英语里经常当不可数名词使用，所以：\r\n\r\n✅ so little data\r\n\r\n很自然。\r\n\r\n如果强调一条条数据库记录，更适合：\r\n\r\n✅ so few records\r\n\r\nHow come 后面不要倒装：\r\n\r\n❌ How come is there so little data?\r\n\r\n✅ How come there’s so little data?\r\n\r\n如果是在正式会议或汇报中，Why... 通常比 How come... 更稳妥。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n把 How come 直接记成：\r\n\r\nHow come = Why\r\n\r\n但语序不同：\r\n\r\nWhy is it so slow?\r\nHow come it’s so slow?\r\n\r\nWhy is there so little data?\r\nHow come there’s so little data?\r\n\r\n所以最值得记的是：\r\n\r\nHow come + 陈述语序\r\n\r\n你的这句话本身是完全自然的：\r\n\r\nHow come there’s so little data in the table?','/static/uploads/english_note_item/ae1ce0f1b6ee470f9f8a4a641f8a27b7.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 10:41:34',1,'2026-09-04 10:41:34'),(1587,21,74,'phrase','as in','as in','as in','🎯 核心意思\r\nas in = 也就是说…… / 比如……中的…… / 我指的是……\r\n\r\n它常用来进一步解释、澄清前面说的词或意思。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n用来澄清“你具体指哪个意思”\r\nA: Do you mean “table”?\r\nB: As in a database table.\r\nA：你说的是 table 吗？\r\nB：我是指数据库表。\r\n\r\n用来举例说明某个词的具体含义\r\nHe’s a developer, as in a software developer.\r\n他是开发人员，我指的是软件开发人员。\r\n\r\n用来确认对方的意思\r\nAs in, you want me to delete the whole file?\r\n也就是说，你是想让我把整个文件删掉？\r\n\r\n常见结构\r\nas in + 名词\r\nas in a database table\r\n\r\nas in + 句子/解释\r\nAs in, you don’t want to continue?','💬 中英双语例句\r\nI mean “table” as in a database table.\r\n我说的 table 是指数据库表。\r\n\r\nHe said “light”, as in not heavy.\r\n他说的 light 是“不重”的那个意思。\r\n\r\nAs in, you want me to restart the whole process?\r\n也就是说，你想让我把整个流程重新启动？\r\n\r\nDo you mean “field” as in a database field?\r\n你说的 field 是指数据库字段吗？\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n如果你只说：\r\n\r\nAs in?\r\n\r\n意思通常是：\r\n\r\n“你是指……？”\r\n“具体什么意思？”\r\n“比如说？”\r\n\r\n它常用来让对方进一步解释。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nA: The system is unstable.\r\nB: As in?\r\nA: As in, it keeps crashing.\r\n\r\nA：系统不稳定。\r\nB：怎么个不稳定法？\r\nA：就是它一直崩溃。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\nas in\r\n= 具体指…… / 也就是说……\r\n强调解释某个词或含义\r\n\r\nfor example\r\n= 例如\r\n主要用于举例，不一定是在澄清词义\r\n\r\nmeaning\r\n= 意思是……\r\n更直接解释意思\r\n\r\nI mean\r\n= 我的意思是……\r\n更常用于自我修正或补充\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI mean a table, as in a database table.\r\n我的意思是 table，具体是指数据库表。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nas in 不是简单等于 for example。\r\n\r\nfor example 是“举例”，\r\nas in 更偏“具体指这个意思”。\r\n\r\n口语中可以单独说：\r\n\r\nAs in?\r\n\r\n很自然，但语气比较随意。\r\n\r\n如果正式场合，更完整一点可以说：\r\n\r\nDo you mean …?\r\nAre you referring to …?\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n把 as in 记成：\r\n\r\n“as in = the meaning used in …”\r\n\r\n也就是：\r\n\r\n“这里说的这个词，是……那个意思。”\r\n\r\n最值得记的一句：\r\n\r\nI mean “table” as in a database table.\r\n我说的 table，是指数据库表。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/d4dfe0eb31b74daca8a7632b9d0e95ce.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 10:43:40',1,'2026-09-04 10:43:40'),(1588,21,75,'phrase','on the far right','on the far right','on the far right','🎯 核心意思\r\non the far right = 在最右边 / 在最右侧\r\n\r\nfar 在这里不是“很远”的单独意思，而是加强位置：\r\n\r\nright = 右边\r\nfar right = 最右边','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n表示画面、页面、表格中的“最右侧”\r\nThe button is on the far right.\r\n按钮在最右边。\r\n\r\n表示一排东西中的最右边\r\nThe person on the far right is my manager.\r\n最右边的那个人是我的经理。\r\n\r\n常用于描述 UI、图片、图表、幻灯片\r\nYou can see the status column on the far right.\r\n你可以在最右侧看到状态列。\r\n\r\n常见搭配：\r\n\r\non the far left = 在最左边\r\n\r\non the far right = 在最右边\r\n\r\nat the far end = 在最末端\r\n\r\nin the top-right corner = 在右上角','💬 中英双语例句\r\nThe delete button is on the far right.\r\n删除按钮在最右边。\r\n\r\nYou can see the review status on the far right of the table.\r\n你可以在表格最右侧看到审核状态。\r\n\r\nThe chart on the far right shows the failure rate.\r\n最右边的图表显示失败率。\r\n\r\nThe person on the far right is our team lead.\r\n最右边的那个人是我们的组长。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\non the far right\r\n\r\n结构：\r\n\r\non + the far right\r\n\r\n这里的 on 用于表示“位于某一侧”。\r\n\r\nthe far right\r\n= 最右侧\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe icon is on the right.\r\n图标在右边。\r\n\r\nThe icon is on the far right.\r\n图标在最右边。\r\n\r\n加上 far 后，位置更明确，表示“已经靠到最右侧了”。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\non the right\r\n= 在右边\r\n不一定是最右边\r\n\r\non the far right\r\n= 在最右边\r\n强调已经靠到右侧边缘\r\n\r\nat the right\r\n❌ 一般不自然\r\n\r\nto the right\r\n= 在右边 / 向右边\r\n更常表示相对位置或方向\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe button is on the far right.\r\n按钮在最右边。\r\n\r\nThe button is to the right of the search box.\r\n按钮在搜索框的右边。\r\n\r\non the far right vs in the top-right corner：\r\n\r\non the far right\r\n= 最右侧，未必在角落\r\n\r\nin the top-right corner\r\n= 右上角\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n一般要加 the：\r\n\r\n✅ on the far right\r\n❌ on far right\r\n\r\n如果是“某个东西的最右边”，常说：\r\n\r\non the far right of the page\r\n在页面最右边\r\n\r\non the far right of the table\r\n在表格最右边\r\n\r\n描述人物合照时也很常用：\r\n\r\nthe man on the far right\r\n最右边的那个男人\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n把位置想成：\r\n\r\nfar left ← left ← center → right → far right\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nright = 右边\r\nfar right = 最右边\r\n\r\n最值得记的一句：\r\n\r\nThe status column is on the far right of the table.\r\n状态列在表格的最右侧。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/df81df9730554b4aa9e069b9fea214b1.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 11:06:19',1,'2026-09-04 11:06:19'),(1589,21,76,'phrase','but not the other way around','but not the other way around','but not the other way around','🎯 核心意思\r\nbut not the other way around = 但反过来不成立 / 但反之不行 / 但不能倒过来说\r\n\r\n它用来表达：\r\n\r\nA → B 成立\r\n但 B → A 不成立','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n表示逻辑关系不能反过来\r\nA depends on B, but not the other way around.\r\nA 依赖 B，但反过来 B 不依赖 A。\r\n\r\n表示规则或关系是单向的\r\nYou can convert A to B, but not the other way around.\r\n你可以把 A 转成 B，但反过来不行。\r\n\r\n表示影响关系不是双向的\r\nThe frontend depends on the backend, but not the other way around.\r\n前端依赖后端，但反过来后端不依赖前端。\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\nA ..., but not the other way around.\r\n\r\nA can ..., but not the other way around.\r\n\r\nA depends on B, but not the other way around.','💬 中英双语例句\r\nYou can convert a list to a tuple, but not the other way around in this case.\r\n在这个场景下，你可以把 list 转成 tuple，但反过来不行。\r\n\r\nThe child table references the parent table, but not the other way around.\r\n子表引用父表，但反过来父表不引用子表。\r\n\r\nThis module depends on the core service, but not the other way around.\r\n这个模块依赖核心服务，但反过来核心服务不依赖它。\r\n\r\nA manager can approve the request, but not the other way around.\r\n经理可以批准这个请求，但反过来不成立。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\nbut not the other way around\r\n\r\nbut = 但是\r\nnot = 不\r\nthe other way around = 反过来 / 倒过来\r\n\r\n所以整体就是：\r\n\r\n“但是反过来不成立。”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nA depends on B, but not the other way around.\r\n\r\n可以理解成：\r\n\r\nA → B\r\n\r\n✅\r\n\r\nB → A\r\n❌\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\nbut not the other way around\r\n= 但反过来不成立\r\n最自然、最常见\r\n\r\nbut not vice versa\r\n= 但反之不成立\r\n更简洁、更正式一些\r\n\r\nthe reverse is not true\r\n= 反过来并不成立\r\n更正式、更书面\r\n\r\nnot necessarily the other way around\r\n= 反过来不一定成立\r\n语气更弱，不是绝对否定\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nA implies B, but not the other way around.\r\nA 可以推出 B，但 B 不能反推出 A。\r\n\r\nA implies B, but not necessarily the other way around.\r\nA 可以推出 B，但 B 不一定能反推出 A。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nthe other way around 这里不是“另一条路”的意思。\r\n\r\n它是固定表达：\r\n\r\nthe other way around\r\n= 反过来 / 倒过来\r\n\r\n不要说：\r\n\r\n❌ but not another way around\r\n\r\n正确：\r\n\r\n✅ but not the other way around\r\n\r\n如果你想表达“双方都可以”，应该说：\r\n\r\nand vice versa\r\n= 反之亦然\r\n\r\n而：\r\n\r\nbut not the other way around\r\n= 反过来不成立\r\n\r\n两者意思正好相反。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n可以直接记成箭头：\r\n\r\nA → B ✅\r\nB → A ❌\r\n\r\n这就是：\r\n\r\nbut not the other way around\r\n\r\n最值得记的一句：\r\n\r\nThe frontend depends on the backend, but not the other way around.\r\n前端依赖后端，但反过来后端不依赖前端。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/efa01ccb9e20417d978b3e96199c195e.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 11:09:36',1,'2026-09-04 11:09:36'),(1590,21,77,'phrase','It works the other way around too','It works the other way around too','It works the other way around too','🎯 核心意思\r\nIt works the other way around too.\r\n= 反过来也成立。\r\n= 倒过来也行。\r\n= 反方向这样做也有效。\r\n\r\n这个表达强调：\r\n\r\nA → B ✅\r\nB → A ✅\r\n\r\n也就是双向都成立。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n表示逻辑关系双向成立\r\nA implies B, and it works the other way around too.\r\nA 可以推出 B，反过来也成立。\r\n\r\n表示转换可以双向进行\r\nYou can convert A to B, and it works the other way around too.\r\n你可以把 A 转成 B，反过来也可以。\r\n\r\n表示操作或规则反过来也适用\r\nYou can drag the file from left to right, and it works the other way around too.\r\n你可以把文件从左拖到右，反过来也可以。\r\n\r\n表示关系是对称的\r\nThe parent can access the child object, and it works the other way around too.\r\n父对象可以访问子对象，反过来也可以。','💬 中英双语例句\r\nYou can convert a tuple to a list, and it works the other way around too.\r\n你可以把 tuple 转成 list，反过来也可以。\r\n\r\nThe frontend can send data to the backend, and it works the other way around too.\r\n前端可以把数据发送给后端，反过来也可以。\r\n\r\nThis mapping works from A to B, and it works the other way around too.\r\n这个映射从 A 到 B 可行，反过来也可行。\r\n\r\nYou can copy values from the old table to the new one, and it works the other way around too.\r\n你可以把旧表的数据复制到新表，反过来也可以。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\nIt works the other way around too.\r\n\r\nIt works\r\n= 它可行 / 它成立\r\n\r\nthe other way around\r\n= 反过来\r\n\r\ntoo\r\n= 也\r\n\r\n所以整句可以理解为：\r\n\r\n“这个关系反过来也成立。”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nA → B ✅\r\nB → A ✅\r\n\r\n这和你刚才学的：\r\n\r\nbut not the other way around\r\n\r\n正好相反。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\nIt works the other way around too.\r\n= 反过来也成立\r\n很自然、偏口语\r\n\r\nIt works both ways.\r\n= 两边都行 / 双向都成立\r\n更简洁，非常常见\r\n\r\nand vice versa\r\n= 反之亦然\r\n更简洁、更正式一些\r\n\r\nThe reverse is also true.\r\n= 反过来也成立\r\n更正式、更书面\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\nA depends on B, but not the other way around.\r\nA 依赖 B，但反过来不成立。\r\n\r\nA is related to B, and it works the other way around too.\r\nA 和 B 有这种关系，反过来也成立。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nthe other way around 是固定表达：\r\n\r\n✅ the other way around\r\n❌ another way around\r\n\r\ntoo 通常放句尾：\r\n\r\n✅ It works the other way around too.\r\n\r\n如果想说得更简洁，可以直接说：\r\n\r\nIt works both ways.\r\n\r\n注意和下面这句意思相反：\r\n\r\nbut not the other way around\r\n= 反过来不成立\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n直接记成箭头：\r\n\r\nA → B ✅\r\nB → A ✅\r\n\r\n= It works the other way around too.\r\n\r\n如果只有：\r\n\r\nA → B ✅\r\nB → A ❌\r\n\r\n那就是：\r\n\r\nbut not the other way around.\r\n\r\n最值得记的一组对比：\r\n\r\nIt works the other way around too.\r\n反过来也成立。\r\n\r\nBut not the other way around.\r\n但反过来不成立。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/bff9150229044b23b40821a4745133ee.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 11:16:58',1,'2026-09-04 11:16:58'),(1591,21,78,'phrase','take care of','take care of','take care of','🎯 核心意思\r\ntake care of 最常见有 3 个意思：\r\n\r\n照顾\r\n\r\n处理、解决\r\n\r\n负责某事\r\n\r\n你之前那个技术语境里的 take care of，通常是：\r\n\r\n“处理好了 / 已经解决了 / 已经被系统覆盖处理了”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n照顾某人\r\ntake care of + 人\r\n\r\nShe takes care of her grandmother.\r\n她照顾她的奶奶。\r\n\r\nCan you take care of the kids tonight?\r\n你今晚能照看孩子吗？\r\n\r\n处理、解决问题\r\ntake care of + problem / issue / task\r\n\r\nI’ll take care of it.\r\n我来处理。\r\n\r\nDon’t worry. The issue has been taken care of.\r\n别担心，这个问题已经处理好了。\r\n\r\nThis validation rule takes care of that case.\r\n这个验证规则已经处理了那种情况。\r\n\r\n负责某项工作\r\ntake care of + responsibility / task\r\n\r\nI’ll take care of the database migration.\r\n数据库迁移这部分我来负责。\r\n\r\nWho’s taking care of the deployment?\r\n谁负责部署？','💬 中英双语例句\r\nI’ll take care of the issue.\r\n我会处理这个问题。\r\n\r\nThe system automatically takes care of failed tasks.\r\n系统会自动处理失败的任务。\r\n\r\nThat edge case has already been taken care of.\r\n那个边界情况已经处理好了。\r\n\r\nThis part of the code takes care of authentication.\r\n这部分代码负责处理身份认证。\r\n\r\nDon’t worry about the file. I’ll take care of it.\r\n不用担心这个文件，我来处理。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n你之前的语境类似：\r\n\r\nThat was an error, but still it’s taken care of then.\r\n\r\n这里的 taken care of 不是“照顾”。\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\nit’s taken care of\r\n= it has been handled\r\n= it has been dealt with\r\n= 这个问题已经被处理好了\r\n\r\n更自然地理解就是：\r\n\r\n“虽然那是个错误，不过现在已经处理掉了。”\r\n\r\n或者：\r\n\r\n“不过这个情况现在已经被系统处理了。”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\ntake care of\r\n= 处理 / 负责 / 照顾\r\n很口语、很自然\r\n\r\ndeal with\r\n= 处理、应对\r\n更强调面对一个问题\r\n\r\nhandle\r\n= 处理\r\n工作和技术场景很常见\r\n\r\nresolve\r\n= 解决\r\n强调问题已经真正解决\r\n\r\nfix\r\n= 修好 / 修复\r\n更适合 bug、故障、技术问题\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI’ll take care of it.\r\n我来处理。\r\n\r\nI’ll deal with it.\r\n我来应对/处理。\r\n\r\nI’ll handle it.\r\n我来负责处理。\r\n\r\nI’ll fix it.\r\n我会把它修好。\r\n\r\nThe issue has been resolved.\r\n这个问题已经彻底解决。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\ntake care 和 take care of 不一样。\r\n\r\nTake care!\r\n= 保重！\r\n\r\ntake care of something\r\n= 处理某事 / 照顾某人\r\n\r\n不要漏掉 of：\r\n\r\n❌ take care the issue\r\n\r\n✅ take care of the issue\r\n\r\n被动语态非常常见：\r\n\r\nIt’s been taken care of.\r\n= 已经处理好了。\r\n\r\n这句话在工作场景里非常常用。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n把 take care of 想成：\r\n\r\n“把某件事接过来并负责到底”\r\n\r\n所以它既可以是：\r\n\r\ntake care of a person\r\n→ 照顾一个人\r\n\r\n也可以是：\r\n\r\ntake care of a problem\r\n→ 把问题处理掉\r\n\r\n最值得记的一句：\r\n\r\nDon’t worry. It’s already been taken care of.\r\n别担心，已经处理好了。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/021e155833e141c8a80b98001f01821d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 11:21:16',1,'2026-09-04 11:21:16'),(1592,21,79,'phrase','But this setup would take care of that','But this setup would take care of that','But this setup would take care of that','🎯 核心意思\r\nBut this setup would take care of that.\r\n= 不过这个方案会处理掉那个问题。\r\n= 不过按这个配置，就能解决那个情况。\r\n= 但这个设计已经把那个问题考虑并处理掉了。\r\n\r\n这里的 take care of 不是“照顾”，而是：\r\n\r\nhandle / deal with / address\r\n= 处理、应对、解决','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nsetup 指技术方案、配置、系统设计\r\nThis setup works well for multiple files.\r\n这个配置很适合处理多个文件。\r\n\r\ntake care of that 指“处理前面提到的问题”\r\nThis validation rule takes care of that.\r\n这个验证规则可以处理那个问题。\r\n\r\nwould take care of that\r\n= 按照这个方案的话，就能够处理那个问题\r\n\r\n这里的 would 带有一种“在这种设计/条件下会……”的语气。\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\nThis setup would take care of that.\r\n这个方案可以解决那个问题。\r\n\r\nThis logic takes care of that case.\r\n这段逻辑处理了那种情况。\r\n\r\nThe validation should take care of that.\r\n这个校验应该能处理那个问题。','💬 中英双语例句\r\nBut this setup would take care of that.\r\n不过这个方案会处理掉那个问题。\r\n\r\nThe retry mechanism would take care of temporary failures.\r\n重试机制可以处理临时失败。\r\n\r\nThis validation rule should take care of that edge case.\r\n这个验证规则应该可以处理那个边界情况。\r\n\r\nThe scheduler already takes care of failed tasks.\r\n调度器已经会处理失败的任务。\r\n\r\nWe don’t need extra logic because the current setup takes care of that.\r\n我们不需要额外逻辑，因为当前方案已经处理了这个问题。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\nBut this setup would take care of that.\r\n\r\nBut\r\n= 不过 / 但是\r\n\r\nthis setup\r\n= 这个方案 / 这个配置 / 这个设计\r\n\r\nwould\r\n= 会 / 可以\r\n表示在当前所讨论的设计或条件下产生的结果\r\n\r\ntake care of that\r\n= 处理那个问题 / 应对那个情况\r\n\r\n所以整句非常自然地可以翻译成：\r\n\r\n“不过按现在这个方案，那个问题已经能被处理了。”\r\n\r\n或者更口语一点：\r\n\r\n“不过这个设计已经能 cover 那个情况了。”\r\n\r\n在你的软件设计、文件处理、数据关系这些技术讨论里，这个表达很自然。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\ntake care of that\r\n= 处理那个问题\r\n口语自然，语气比较轻松\r\n\r\nhandle that\r\n= 处理那个问题\r\n技术场景非常常见\r\n\r\ndeal with that\r\n= 应对那个问题\r\n更强调面对、处理\r\n\r\naddress that\r\n= 针对并解决那个问题\r\n更正式，会议和技术讨论里常用\r\n\r\nfix that\r\n= 修复那个问题\r\n更适合 bug、故障\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThis setup would take care of that.\r\n这个方案可以处理那个情况。\r\n\r\nThis setup would handle that.\r\n这个方案可以处理那个情况。\r\n\r\nThis setup would address that issue.\r\n这个方案可以解决那个问题。\r\n\r\nThis setup would fix that bug.\r\n这个方案可以修复那个 bug。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\ntake care of that 不一定表示“彻底解决”。\r\n\r\n它更接近：\r\n\r\n“已经有机制处理它了。”\r\n\r\n所以在技术设计里，经常比 fix 更合适。\r\n\r\nsetup 是名词：\r\n\r\n✅ this setup\r\n这个配置 / 这个方案\r\n\r\nset up 是动词：\r\n\r\n✅ We set up the scheduler.\r\n我们配置了调度器。\r\n\r\nwould 在这里不一定是假设得很远。\r\n\r\n它常用于讨论设计：\r\n\r\nThis setup would take care of that.\r\n= 如果按这个设计来，它就能处理那个问题。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n把 take care of that 想成：\r\n\r\n问题出现\r\n→ 系统里已经有对应机制\r\n→ 自动处理掉\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nThis setup would take care of that.\r\n\r\n可以记成：\r\n\r\n“这个方案会把那个问题接住并处理掉。”\r\n\r\n最值得记的一句：\r\n\r\nWe don’t need extra logic. This setup would take care of that.\r\n我们不需要额外逻辑，这个方案已经能处理那个问题。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/986739c510c64ed5bf69e29646253bdf.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 11:24:31',1,'2026-09-04 11:24:31'),(1593,21,80,'phrase','child labor','child labor','child labor','🎯 核心意思\r\n正式意思：\r\n\r\nchild labor\r\n= 童工 / 使用儿童从事劳动\r\n\r\n但在你这个语境里，它是开玩笑、夸张地说：\r\n\r\n“让孩子们干这些简单的活儿。”\r\n\r\n也就是故意把：\r\n\r\nWe’ve got the kids doing it.\r\n我们让孩子们在做。\r\n\r\n夸张说成：\r\n\r\nIt’s the child labor that we have doing it.\r\n这些活儿我们都交给“童工”干了。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n正式含义：童工问题\r\n\r\nChild labor is illegal in many countries.\r\n很多国家禁止童工。\r\n\r\n开玩笑：让孩子帮忙干点简单活\r\n\r\nWe’ve got the child labor helping with the easy jobs.\r\n这些简单活儿我们让“童工”来帮忙了。\r\n\r\n这里的 child labor 是一种幽默、夸张说法。\r\n\r\n常见正常表达\r\n\r\nWe’ve got the kids doing it.\r\n我们让孩子们在做。\r\n\r\nWe have the kids helping out.\r\n我们让孩子们帮忙。\r\n\r\nWe’ve got the kids doing the easy stuff.\r\n我们让孩子们做这些简单的事情。','💬 中英双语例句\r\nIt’s the child labor that we have doing it.\r\n这些活儿我们让“童工”干了。\r\n→ 开玩笑地说：让孩子们干这些简单的事。\r\n\r\nWe’ve got the kids doing the easy jobs.\r\n这些简单的活儿我们让孩子们来做。\r\n\r\nThe kids are helping us sort the boxes. Free child labor!\r\n孩子们在帮我们整理箱子——免费“童工”！\r\n→ 明显是在开玩笑。\r\n\r\nDon’t worry, we’ve got our child labor team on it.\r\n别担心，我们的“童工小队”已经在处理了。\r\n→ 调侃式表达。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\nIt’s the child labor that we have doing it.\r\n\r\nIt’s the child labor\r\n= 是这些“童工”\r\n\r\nthat we have doing it\r\n= 我们让他们在做这件事\r\n\r\n这里真正的意思不是：\r\n\r\n“公司违法雇佣童工。”\r\n\r\n而是带玩笑地说：\r\n\r\n“这种简单活儿就让孩子们来干了。”\r\n\r\n这种幽默来自于“故意把普通小事说得很严重”。\r\n\r\nkids helping out\r\n→ 普通表达\r\n\r\nchild labor\r\n→ 故意夸张，形成笑点\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\nchild labor\r\n= 童工\r\n正式情况下是严肃词汇；特定语境中可以被拿来开玩笑\r\n\r\nthe kids\r\n= 孩子们\r\n最正常、最安全的表达\r\n\r\nthe kids helping out\r\n= 孩子们帮忙\r\n自然、中性\r\n\r\nfree labor\r\n= 免费劳动力\r\n也经常用来开玩笑\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe’ve got some free labor today.\r\n我们今天有点“免费劳动力”。\r\n→ 可能是在调侃家人或孩子来帮忙。\r\n\r\nchild laborer\r\n= 童工这个“人”\r\n\r\nchild labor\r\n= 童工这种现象 / 儿童劳动\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n正式场合不要随便用 child labor 开玩笑。\r\n\r\n因为这个词本身涉及真实的儿童剥削问题。\r\n\r\n朋友、家人、熟悉同事之间明显是玩笑时，别人通常能听懂。\r\n\r\nchild labor 不是指某一个具体孩子。\r\n\r\n❌ a child labor\r\n\r\n✅ child labor\r\n\r\n✅ a child laborer\r\n\r\n你原句中的笑点，主要靠语境。\r\n\r\n如果没有明确的轻松语气：\r\n\r\nIt’s the child labor that we have doing it.\r\n\r\n别人可能真的会理解成“童工”。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n记住两个层次：\r\n\r\n正式：\r\n\r\nchild labor\r\n= 童工问题\r\n\r\n开玩笑：\r\n\r\nkids doing simple jobs\r\n↓ 故意夸张\r\n“child labor”\r\n\r\n所以你这个场景可以记成：\r\n\r\nWe’ve got the kids doing the easy stuff.\r\n正常说法\r\n\r\nIt’s the child labor that we have doing it.\r\n开玩笑说法 😄','/static/uploads/english_note_item/08b9789cca8e412982d4f6db3004f95c.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 11:37:18',1,'2026-09-04 11:37:18'),(1594,21,81,'phrase','go about doing something','go about doing something','go about doing something','🎯 核心意思\r\ngo about doing something = 着手做某事 / 采取某种方式去做某事 / 开始处理某事\r\n\r\n它不只是“开始做”，还常常带有：\r\n\r\n“你打算怎么做这件事？”\r\n“你会用什么方式来处理这件事？”\r\n\r\n这种“做事方式”的感觉。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n着手做某事\r\nWe need to go about fixing this problem carefully.\r\n我们需要谨慎地着手解决这个问题。\r\n\r\n以某种方式处理某事\r\nHow would you go about solving this issue?\r\n你会怎么着手解决这个问题？\r\n\r\n讨论“方法、步骤”时很常见\r\nWhat’s the best way to go about implementing this feature?\r\n实现这个功能，最好的着手方式是什么？\r\n\r\n常见结构：\r\n\r\ngo about doing something\r\n= 着手做某事\r\n\r\nhow to go about doing something\r\n= 该怎么着手做某事\r\n\r\nthe best way to go about doing something\r\n= 做某事的最佳方式','💬 中英双语例句\r\nHow would you go about solving this problem?\r\n你会怎么着手解决这个问题？\r\n\r\nWe need to think about how to go about migrating the data.\r\n我们需要考虑该怎么着手迁移这些数据。\r\n\r\nWhat’s the best way to go about testing this feature?\r\n测试这个功能，最好的方法是什么？\r\n\r\nHe went about fixing the issue in a very systematic way.\r\n他以一种非常系统的方式着手解决这个问题。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\ngo about doing something\r\n\r\ngo about\r\n= 着手处理 / 以某种方式进行\r\n\r\ndoing something\r\n= 做某件事\r\n\r\n所以整体不是简单的：\r\n\r\nstart doing something\r\n\r\n而更像：\r\n\r\n“以某种方式开始并处理这件事。”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nHow would you go about redesigning this module?\r\n\r\n不是单纯问：\r\n\r\n“你会不会重新设计这个模块？”\r\n\r\n而是问：\r\n\r\n“你会怎么着手重新设计这个模块？”\r\n“你的做法和步骤是什么？”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\nstart doing something\r\n= 开始做某事\r\n只强调“开始”\r\n\r\ngo about doing something\r\n= 着手做某事 / 以某种方式做\r\n更强调方法和过程\r\n\r\nset about doing something\r\n= 开始着手做某事\r\n和 go about 很像，但更强调真正开始行动\r\n\r\ndeal with something\r\n= 处理某事\r\n强调应对问题，不强调具体怎么开始\r\n\r\napproach something\r\n= 处理 / 着手某事\r\n更正式\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe started fixing the bug.\r\n我们开始修这个 bug。\r\n\r\nWe went about fixing the bug carefully.\r\n我们很谨慎地着手修这个 bug。\r\n→ 强调处理方式\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\ngo about 后面通常接 doing：\r\n\r\n✅ go about solving the problem\r\n❌ go about to solve the problem\r\n\r\n很常见的问法是：\r\n\r\nHow would you go about doing this?\r\n\r\n= 你会怎么着手做这个？\r\n\r\n不要把 go about 理解成“到处走”。\r\n\r\n虽然 go about 本身在别的语境里可以有“到处活动”的意思，但在：\r\n\r\ngo about doing something\r\n\r\n这个结构里通常是：\r\n\r\n“着手做 / 采取方式做”。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n把它想成：\r\n\r\ngoal\r\n→ figure out the approach\r\n→ start doing it\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ngo about doing something\r\n≈ “想好怎么做，然后着手去做”\r\n\r\n最值得记的一句：\r\n\r\nHow would you go about solving this problem?\r\n你会怎么着手解决这个问题？','/static/uploads/english_note_item/4f5255caadea4a228d0546eed62df48d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 12:02:05',1,'2026-09-04 12:02:05'),(1595,21,82,'phrase','marry it up with','marry it up with','marry it up with','🎯 核心意思\r\nmarry something up with something\r\n= 把某物和另一物匹配起来 / 对应起来 / 结合起来\r\n\r\n这里的 marry 不是“结婚”，而是：\r\n\r\n“把两个相关的东西配到一起，使它们对应上。”','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n把两组数据对应起来\r\nWe need to marry this data up with the records in the database.\r\n我们需要把这些数据和数据库里的记录对应起来。\r\n\r\n把信息和来源匹配起来\r\nCan we marry it up with the original document?\r\n我们能不能把它和原始文件对应起来？\r\n\r\n把两个系统、流程或概念结合起来\r\nWe need to marry the new workflow up with the existing system.\r\n我们需要把新的工作流程和现有系统结合起来。\r\n\r\n常见结构\r\nmarry A up with B\r\n= 把 A 和 B 匹配起来\r\n\r\nmarry it up with something\r\n= 把它和某物对应起来','💬 中英双语例句\r\nWe need to marry the OCR result up with the original document.\r\n我们需要把 OCR 结果和原始文档对应起来。\r\n\r\nCan you marry this record up with the correct job sheet?\r\n你能把这条记录和正确的 job sheet 对应起来吗？\r\n\r\nThe system marries the extracted data up with the production order.\r\n系统会把抽取的数据和生产订单匹配起来。\r\n\r\nWe’re trying to marry the new data up with the old records.\r\n我们正在尝试把新数据和旧记录对应起来。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\nmarry it up with\r\n\r\nmarry\r\n= 原本是“结婚”\r\n\r\nup with\r\n= 和……配到一起\r\n\r\n所以这个表达可以形象地理解为：\r\n\r\n“把两个东西配成一对。”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nOCR result + database record\r\n→ marry them up\r\n→ 找到正确对应关系\r\n\r\n所以在技术、数据、业务流程场景里，常常可以翻译成：\r\n\r\n“匹配起来”\r\n“对应起来”\r\n“关联起来”\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\nmatch A with B\r\n= 把 A 和 B 匹配起来\r\n最直接、最通用\r\n\r\nmarry A up with B\r\n= 把 A 和 B 对应/结合起来\r\n更口语、更形象，英式英语里比较常见\r\n\r\nlink A to B\r\n= 把 A 和 B 连接/关联起来\r\n强调建立关联\r\n\r\nmap A to B\r\n= 把 A 映射到 B\r\n技术语境更正式\r\n\r\nreconcile A with B\r\n= 核对并使 A 和 B 一致\r\n强调检查差异并对账\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe need to match the OCR result with the record.\r\n我们需要把 OCR 结果和记录匹配起来。\r\n\r\nWe need to marry the OCR result up with the record.\r\n我们需要把 OCR 结果和记录对应起来。\r\n\r\nWe need to reconcile the OCR result with the database.\r\n我们需要核对 OCR 结果和数据库数据是否一致。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n不要把这里的 marry 理解成“结婚”。\r\n\r\n这里是比喻用法：\r\n\r\nmarry two things\r\n= 把两样东西结合起来\r\n\r\n常见说法是：\r\n\r\n✅ marry A up with B\r\n\r\n✅ marry A with B\r\n\r\n在口语里，marry up with 很自然。\r\n\r\n如果是正式技术文档，通常更适合：\r\n\r\nmatch\r\nmap\r\nlink\r\nassociate\r\n\r\nmarry up with 更偏口语和会议讨论。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n把它想成：\r\n\r\nA ❤️ B\r\n\r\n两个东西“配成一对”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nmarry A up with B\r\n= 把 A 和 B 配对 / 对应起来\r\n\r\n最值得记的一句：\r\n\r\nWe need to marry the extracted data up with the correct database record.\r\n我们需要把抽取的数据和正确的数据库记录对应起来。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/09fad39584f946c9829fae9f48f89a31.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 13:08:56',1,'2026-09-04 13:08:56'),(1596,21,83,'phrase','track things over time','track things over time','track things over time','🎯 核心意思\r\ntrack things over time\r\n= 持续追踪某些事情的变化\r\n= 长期记录并观察数据或状态\r\n= 看某个指标随着时间怎么变化\r\n\r\n重点不只是“记录一次”，而是：\r\n\r\n现在 → 以后持续记录 → 比较变化趋势','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n持续追踪数据变化\r\nWe need to track these metrics over time.\r\n我们需要长期追踪这些指标的变化。\r\n\r\n观察系统性能趋势\r\nThis dashboard helps us track performance over time.\r\n这个仪表盘可以帮助我们持续观察性能变化。\r\n\r\n记录项目或任务状态\r\nWe can track task failures over time.\r\n我们可以长期追踪任务失败情况。\r\n\r\n观察业务趋势\r\nIt allows us to track customer behaviour over time.\r\n它可以让我们持续观察客户行为的变化。\r\n\r\n常见搭配：\r\n\r\ntrack performance over time\r\n持续跟踪性能\r\n\r\ntrack changes over time\r\n长期观察变化\r\n\r\ntrack progress over time\r\n持续跟踪进展\r\n\r\ntrack trends over time\r\n持续观察趋势\r\n\r\ntrack metrics over time\r\n长期追踪指标','💬 中英双语例句\r\nWe want to track these values over time.\r\n我们想持续追踪这些数值的变化。\r\n\r\nThe report allows us to track processing failures over time.\r\n这个报告可以让我们长期追踪文件处理失败的情况。\r\n\r\nThis dashboard helps us track system performance over time.\r\n这个仪表盘帮助我们持续观察系统性能变化。\r\n\r\nWe can use this data to track accuracy over time.\r\n我们可以使用这些数据长期追踪准确率的变化。\r\n\r\nIt’s useful to track things over time rather than just looking at a single result.\r\n持续追踪变化比只看某一次结果更有用。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\ntrack things over time\r\n\r\ntrack\r\n= 持续记录、追踪\r\n\r\nthings\r\n= 泛指你关心的东西，比如：\r\n\r\n数据\r\n\r\n指标\r\n\r\n错误\r\n\r\n状态\r\n\r\n性能\r\n\r\n用户行为\r\n\r\nover time\r\n= 经过一段时间 / 随着时间推移\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ntrack things over time\r\n\r\n可以理解为：\r\n\r\n“不要只看某一个时间点，而是持续记录，然后看它是怎么变化的。”\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nToday: 90%\r\n↓\r\nNext week: 92%\r\n↓\r\nNext month: 95%\r\n\r\n这就是：\r\n\r\ntrack accuracy over time\r\n长期跟踪准确率变化。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\ntrack something\r\n= 追踪某件事\r\n不一定强调长期变化\r\n\r\ntrack something over time\r\n= 持续追踪并观察它随时间的变化\r\n强调趋势\r\n\r\nmonitor something\r\n= 监控某事\r\n更强调持续观察当前状态\r\n\r\nrecord something\r\n= 记录某事\r\n强调保存数据\r\n\r\nmeasure something\r\n= 测量某个指标\r\n强调得到数值\r\n\r\nanalyse trends\r\n= 分析趋势\r\n强调对已经收集的数据进行分析\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nWe monitor system performance.\r\n我们监控系统性能。\r\n\r\nWe track system performance over time.\r\n我们长期追踪系统性能的变化。\r\n\r\n第二句明显更强调“历史趋势”。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nover time 和 overtime 不一样。\r\n\r\nover time\r\n= 随着时间推移\r\n\r\novertime\r\n= 加班 / 加班时间\r\n\r\n✅ Performance improved over time.\r\n性能随着时间逐渐提升。\r\n\r\n✅ I worked overtime yesterday.\r\n我昨天加班了。\r\n\r\nthings 很口语。\r\n\r\n技术汇报里，如果你知道具体对象，最好直接说：\r\n\r\ntrack metrics over time\r\ntrack performance over time\r\ntrack failure rates over time\r\n\r\n会比 track things over time 更准确。\r\n\r\n不要理解成“追踪时间”。\r\n\r\nover time 修饰的是 track，表示“持续一段时间”。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n想象一张折线图：\r\n\r\n时间 → → → → →\r\n\r\n90 → 92 → 88 → 95 → 97\r\n\r\n你不是只看其中一个数字，而是一直记录并观察变化。\r\n\r\n这就是：\r\n\r\ntrack something over time\r\n= 持续追踪某件事随时间的变化\r\n\r\n最值得记的一句：\r\n\r\nThis dashboard allows us to track performance over time.\r\n这个仪表盘可以让我们长期追踪性能变化。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/16dd28c206a24e1c8a9780c5b624a158.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 13:16:31',1,'2026-09-04 13:16:31'),(1597,21,84,'phrase','wrap up','wrap up','wrap up','🎯 核心意思\r\nwrap-up = 最后的总结 / 收尾部分 / 结束环节\r\n\r\n它常用于：\r\n\r\nmeeting wrap-up = 会议总结\r\n\r\nproject wrap-up = 项目收尾\r\n\r\nfinal wrap-up = 最后总结\r\n\r\nquick wrap-up = 简短总结','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n会议最后的总结\r\nLet’s do a quick wrap-up before we finish.\r\n我们结束前快速总结一下。\r\n\r\n项目收尾阶段\r\nWe’re now in the project wrap-up phase.\r\n我们现在进入项目收尾阶段。\r\n\r\n文章、演讲或汇报最后的总结部分\r\nI’ll give a short wrap-up at the end.\r\n最后我会做一个简短总结。\r\n\r\n活动结束后的总结\r\nThe event wrap-up will be sent out tomorrow.\r\n活动总结明天会发出去。','💬 中英双语例句\r\nLet’s move on to the wrap-up.\r\n我们进入最后总结部分吧。\r\n\r\nI’ll give a quick wrap-up of what we discussed today.\r\n我会快速总结一下我们今天讨论的内容。\r\n\r\nThe project wrap-up includes documentation and final testing.\r\n项目收尾包括文档整理和最终测试。\r\n\r\nBefore we finish, here’s a brief wrap-up.\r\n结束之前，我做一个简短总结。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\n如果你在会议或演示里说：\r\n\r\nLet’s move on to the wrap-up.\r\n\r\n意思就是：\r\n\r\n“我们进入最后的总结部分吧。”\r\n\r\n这里的 wrap-up 是名词，表示：\r\n\r\nthe final summary or closing part\r\n= 最后的总结或收尾部分\r\n\r\n如果说：\r\n\r\nLet’s wrap up.\r\n\r\n这里 wrap up 是动词：\r\n\r\n= 我们收尾吧 / 我们结束吧。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\nwrap-up\r\n= 总结 / 收尾\r\n比较口语，也很常用于会议和项目\r\n\r\nsummary\r\n= 总结\r\n更中性、最通用\r\n\r\nconclusion\r\n= 结论 / 结尾\r\n更正式，强调最终结论\r\n\r\nclosing\r\n= 结束部分 / 收尾\r\n强调“结束”这个环节\r\n\r\nrecap\r\n= 回顾 / 简要重述\r\n强调把前面讲过的内容快速再说一遍\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nHere’s a quick recap.\r\n这里快速回顾一下。\r\n\r\nHere’s a quick wrap-up.\r\n这里快速做个总结并收尾。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nwrap-up 是名词，通常有连字符：\r\n\r\n✅ a quick wrap-up\r\n\r\n✅ the meeting wrap-up\r\n\r\nwrap up 是动词，不加连字符：\r\n\r\n✅ Let’s wrap up the meeting.\r\n我们把会议收尾吧。\r\n\r\n不要混淆：\r\n\r\nwrap-up = 名词\r\nwrap up = 动词\r\n\r\n如果是正式报告结尾，conclusion 往往比 wrap-up 更正式。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n把 wrap 想成“包起来”。\r\n\r\n一场会议讲完以后，把所有内容“包起来”：\r\n\r\ndiscussion → key points → conclusion → finish\r\n\r\n这就是：\r\n\r\nwrap-up\r\n= 总结 + 收尾\r\n\r\n最值得记的一组：\r\n\r\nLet’s wrap up.\r\n我们收尾吧。\r\n\r\nLet’s move on to the wrap-up.\r\n我们进入总结部分吧。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/196a518274de44688838c25b45470a1d.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 13:50:44',1,'2026-09-04 13:50:44'),(1598,21,85,'phrase','owe sb','owe sb','owe sb','🎯 核心意思\r\nowe sb 本身通常不是完整意思，后面常接“欠什么”。\r\n\r\n最常见结构：\r\n\r\nowe sb sth\r\n= 欠某人某物\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI owe you $20.\r\n我欠你 20 美元。\r\n\r\nI owe you a favour.\r\n我欠你一个人情。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\n欠某人钱\r\nowe sb money\r\n= 欠某人钱\r\n\r\nI owe him $100.\r\n我欠他 100 美元。\r\n\r\n欠某人人情\r\nowe sb a favour\r\n= 欠某人一个人情\r\n\r\nI owe you a favour.\r\n我欠你一个人情。\r\n\r\n应该感谢某人\r\nowe sb thanks / an apology\r\n\r\nI owe you an apology.\r\n我欠你一个道歉。\r\n= 我应该向你道歉。\r\n\r\nI owe you a big thank-you.\r\n我得好好谢谢你。\r\n\r\n常见口语\r\nI owe you one.\r\n= 我欠你一个人情。','💬 中英双语例句\r\nI owe you some money.\r\n我欠你一些钱。\r\n\r\nHow much do I owe you?\r\n我欠你多少钱？\r\n\r\nI owe her an apology.\r\n我应该向她道歉。\r\n\r\nThanks for covering my shift. I owe you one.\r\n谢谢你替我顶班，我欠你一个人情。\r\n\r\nWe owe our customers an explanation.\r\n我们应该给客户一个解释。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析（如果有语境）\r\nowe sb 的基本结构可以理解为：\r\n\r\nowe + 人 + 东西\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI owe you $50.\r\n\r\nI = 我\r\nowe = 欠\r\nyou = 你\r\n$50 = 50 美元\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nI owe you $50.\r\n= 我欠你 50 美元。\r\n\r\n如果只说：\r\n\r\nI owe you.\r\n\r\n语法上可以，但具体“欠什么”往往由上下文决定，可能是钱，也可能是人情。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混表达对比\r\nowe sb sth\r\n= 欠某人某物\r\n\r\nowe sth to sb\r\n= 欠某人某物 / 把某事归功于某人\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI owe you $20.\r\n= I owe $20 to you.\r\n我欠你 20 美元。\r\n\r\n但：\r\n\r\nI owe my success to my team.\r\n我的成功归功于我的团队。\r\n\r\npay sb back\r\n= 还某人钱 / 回报某人\r\n\r\nI’ll pay you back tomorrow.\r\n我明天还你钱。\r\n\r\nreturn the favour\r\n= 还人情\r\n\r\nI’ll return the favour next time.\r\n下次我会还你这个人情。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nowe 后面可以直接接人：\r\n\r\n✅ I owe you money.\r\n❌ I owe to you money.\r\n\r\n如果用 owe sth to sb：\r\n\r\n✅ I owe $20 to you.\r\n\r\nowe sb 常常后面还要有宾语：\r\n\r\nowe sb money\r\nowe sb an apology\r\nowe sb a favour\r\n\r\nI owe you one 是固定表达：\r\n\r\n= 我欠你个人情。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n直接记结构：\r\n\r\nowe + 人 + 东西\r\n\r\nI owe you money.\r\n我欠你钱。\r\n\r\nI owe you a favour.\r\n我欠你人情。\r\n\r\nI owe you an apology.\r\n我欠你一个道歉。\r\n\r\n最值得记的句型：\r\n\r\nowe sb sth\r\n= 欠某人某物。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/bcd534274d7444f685a461440a5e686f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-04 13:57:52',1,'2026-09-04 13:57:52'),(1599,21,86,'phrase','get blamed for sth','get blamed for sth','get blamed for sth','🎯 核心意思\r\n因为某事被责怪、被批评、被归咎。\r\n\r\n口语里有时可以理解成：\r\n“因为某事背锅”。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nget blamed for + 名词\r\n因为某件事被责怪\r\n\r\nHe got blamed for the mistake.\r\n他因为这个错误被责怪了。\r\n\r\nget blamed for doing sth\r\n因为做了某事被责怪\r\n\r\nShe got blamed for losing the file.\r\n她因为弄丢文件被责怪了。\r\n\r\nget blamed for something you didn\'t do\r\n因为自己没做的事被责怪 → “背锅”\r\n\r\nI got blamed for something I didn\'t even do.\r\n我明明没做这件事，却被怪到我头上了。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nI don\'t want to get blamed for this.\r\n我不想因为这件事被责怪。\r\n\r\nWhy am I getting blamed for this?\r\n为什么这件事要怪我？\r\n\r\nHe always gets blamed when something goes wrong.\r\n每次一出问题，他总是被责怪。\r\n\r\nIf the system crashes, I might get blamed for it.\r\n如果系统崩了，我可能会因此被怪罪。\r\n\r\nI don\'t want to get blamed for someone else\'s mistake.\r\n我不想替别人的错误背锅。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\nget blamed for sth\r\n= get + blamed + for + 某事\r\n\r\n这里的 get blamed 和 be blamed 意思很接近：\r\n\r\nI was blamed for the delay.\r\n我因为延期被责怪了。\r\n\r\nI got blamed for the delay.\r\n我因为延期挨批了。\r\n\r\nget blamed 更口语一些，也更强调“最后责任落到了某人头上”。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混对比\r\n\r\nget blamed for sth\r\n因为某事被责怪\r\n\r\nbe blamed for sth\r\n因为某事被责怪，较中性\r\n\r\ntake the blame for sth\r\n承担某事的责任\r\n\r\nbe held responsible for sth\r\n被认定对某事负责，比较正式\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\nI got blamed for it.\r\n别人怪我。\r\n\r\nI took the blame for it.\r\n我承担了责任。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n固定搭配是：\r\n\r\n✅ get blamed for sth\r\n❌ get blamed of sth\r\n\r\n另外要区分：\r\n\r\nblame sb for sth\r\n因为某事责怪某人\r\n\r\nThey blamed me for the delay.\r\n他们因为延期责怪我。\r\n\r\nblame sth on sb\r\n把某件事归咎于某人\r\n\r\nThey blamed the delay on me.\r\n他们把延期怪到我头上。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nblame = 责怪\r\n\r\nget blamed\r\n= “受到责怪”\r\n\r\nfor sth\r\n= “因为某事”\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nget blamed for sth\r\n= 因为某事被责怪 / 背锅\r\n\r\n很实用的一句：\r\n\r\nI don\'t want to get blamed for something that\'s outside my control.\r\n我不想因为超出我控制范围的事情而背锅。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e57dfdc4c9064ee6bad4cb423f4b506f.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-06 10:23:44',1,'2026-09-06 10:23:44'),(1600,21,87,'phrase','cramped space','cramped space','cramped space','🎯 核心意思\r\ncramped space = 狭小拥挤的空间；让人觉得伸展不开、活动不方便的地方。\r\n\r\n这里的 cramped 不只是“小”，而是强调：\r\n\r\n空间太小 → 人待在里面感觉局促、不舒服。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\na cramped space\r\n一个狭窄拥挤的空间\r\n\r\nWe had to work in a cramped space.\r\n我们不得不在一个很狭小的空间里工作。\r\n\r\na cramped room\r\n狭小的房间\r\n\r\nThe hotel room was small and cramped.\r\n这个酒店房间又小又局促。\r\n\r\nfeel cramped\r\n感觉局促、伸展不开\r\n\r\nI feel cramped in the back seat.\r\n我坐在后排感觉很挤。\r\n\r\ncramped conditions\r\n拥挤、局促的环境\r\n\r\nThey were living in cramped conditions.\r\n他们住在很拥挤的环境里。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThere isn\'t much room to move in such a cramped space.\r\n在这么狭小的空间里几乎没什么活动空间。\r\n\r\nThe office feels a bit cramped with so many desks.\r\n办公室放了这么多桌子，感觉有点拥挤。\r\n\r\nI don\'t like working in cramped spaces.\r\n我不喜欢在狭小的空间里工作。\r\n\r\nThe technician had to crawl into a cramped space behind the machine.\r\n技术人员不得不钻进机器后面一个很狭小的空间。\r\n\r\nThe car is comfortable in the front, but the back seats feel cramped.\r\n这辆车前排很舒服，但后排感觉比较挤。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\ncramped space\r\n\r\n可以理解为：\r\n\r\ncramped = too small and uncomfortable\r\nspace = 空间\r\n\r\n合起来就是：\r\n\r\na space that is too small to move comfortably\r\n小到让人活动不方便的空间\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nIt\'s difficult to work in such a cramped space.\r\n在这么狭小的空间里工作很困难。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混对比\r\n\r\nsmall space\r\n= 小空间\r\n只是客观描述“小”。\r\n\r\ncramped space\r\n= 狭小、局促的空间\r\n强调“太小了，让人不舒服”。\r\n\r\nconfined space\r\n= 受限制的封闭空间\r\n更正式，常用于工业、安全场景。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\na confined space such as a tank or tunnel\r\n像储罐、隧道这样的受限空间\r\n\r\ncrowded space\r\n= 人很多、拥挤的空间\r\n重点是“人多”，不一定空间本身小。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\na small room\r\n房间小\r\n\r\na cramped room\r\n房间小得让人觉得局促\r\n\r\na crowded room\r\n房间里人很多\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n你写的是：\r\n\r\n❌ cramped spce\r\n\r\n正确拼写：\r\n\r\n✅ cramped space\r\n\r\nspace 中间有 a：\r\n\r\ns-p-a-c-e\r\n\r\n另外 cramped 的结尾虽然写作 -mped，但读音是：\r\n\r\n/kræmpt/\r\n\r\n最后听起来像 “krampt”。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 cramped 想成：\r\n\r\n“空间小到身体都被挤住了。”\r\n\r\nsmall = 小\r\ncramped = 小 + 挤 + 局促\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\ncramped space\r\n= 让人伸展不开的狭小空间\r\n\r\n一个很实用的表达：\r\n\r\nIt\'s a bit cramped in here.\r\n这里有点挤。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/cca682bdb9054340a5f48f746ba9dded.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-06 12:19:28',1,'2026-09-06 12:19:28'),(1601,21,88,'phrase','upset victory','upset victory','upset victory','🎯 核心意思\r\nupset victory = 爆冷获胜；出人意料的胜利。\r\n\r\n这里的 upset 不是“难过的”，而是体育、比赛语境里的：\r\n\r\nupset = 爆冷；意外击败强者\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nan upset victory\r\n= 一场爆冷胜利\r\n= 弱队/不被看好的一方意外赢了','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nscore an upset victory\r\n爆冷获胜\r\n\r\nThe underdog scored an upset victory over the defending champion.\r\n这支不被看好的队伍爆冷击败了卫冕冠军。\r\n\r\npull off an upset victory\r\n成功爆冷取胜\r\n\r\nThey pulled off a stunning upset victory.\r\n他们爆冷拿下了一场令人震惊的胜利。\r\n\r\na surprise / shock upset victory\r\n令人意外的爆冷胜利\r\n\r\nThe team secured a shock upset victory in the final.\r\n这支球队在决赛中爆冷获胜。\r\n\r\nupset victory over sb\r\n爆冷击败某人/某队\r\n\r\nShe claimed an upset victory over the world No. 1.\r\n她爆冷击败了世界第一。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThe young player achieved an upset victory over the top seed.\r\n这名年轻选手爆冷击败了头号种子。\r\n\r\nIt was one of the biggest upset victories in the tournament\'s history.\r\n这是这项赛事历史上最大的爆冷胜利之一。\r\n\r\nThe underdogs celebrated an unexpected upset victory.\r\n这支不被看好的队伍庆祝了一场意外的爆冷胜利。\r\n\r\nNew Zealand pulled off an upset victory against the favourites.\r\n新西兰爆冷击败了赛前热门队伍。\r\n\r\nThe result was a major upset victory for the home side.\r\n这个结果对主队来说是一场重大的爆冷胜利。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\nupset victory\r\n\r\n可以拆成：\r\n\r\nupset\r\n= 爆冷、意外结果\r\n\r\nvictory\r\n= 胜利\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nupset victory\r\n= an unexpected win by the weaker or less-favoured side\r\n实力较弱或不被看好的一方取得的意外胜利\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nThe unseeded player won in an upset victory.\r\n这名非种子选手爆冷获胜。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混对比\r\n\r\nupset victory\r\n= 爆冷获胜\r\n重点是“弱者击败强者”。\r\n\r\nsurprise victory\r\n= 意外的胜利\r\n更宽泛，不一定强调双方实力差距。\r\n\r\nnarrow victory\r\n= 险胜\r\n强调比分接近，不强调爆冷。\r\n\r\nconvincing victory\r\n= 大胜 / 令人信服的胜利\r\n强调赢得很稳。\r\n\r\nlandslide victory\r\n= 压倒性胜利\r\n常用于选举，也可用于比赛。\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\nThey won a narrow victory.\r\n他们险胜了。\r\n\r\nThey won an upset victory.\r\n他们爆冷赢了。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nupset 在这里不是：\r\n\r\n❌ 难过的胜利\r\n\r\n而是体育里的名词/形容词用法：\r\n\r\nan upset\r\n= 爆冷结果\r\n\r\nan upset victory\r\n= 爆冷胜利\r\n\r\n还常见：\r\n\r\ncause an upset\r\n制造冷门\r\n\r\npull off an upset\r\n成功爆冷\r\n\r\nThe team pulled off a huge upset.\r\n这支球队爆出了一个大冷门。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n平常大家预测：\r\n\r\nStrong team → wins\r\n\r\n结果却是：\r\n\r\nUnderdog → wins\r\n\r\n大家都被“打乱预期”了。\r\n\r\nupset 本身就有“打乱、颠覆”的感觉。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nupset victory\r\n= 颠覆预期的胜利\r\n= 爆冷获胜\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nThe underdog pulled off an upset victory.\r\n不被看好的一方爆冷取胜。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/72946029978a44979a85e5163b14aa70.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-06 12:29:14',1,'2026-09-06 12:29:14'),(1602,21,89,'phrase','share of','share of','share of','🎯 核心意思\r\nshare of = ……中的一份；……所占的比例 / 份额。\r\n\r\n最常见的中文意思：\r\n\r\n……的一部分\r\n\r\n……的份额\r\n\r\n……所占比例\r\n\r\n……中的一份','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\na share of sth\r\n某物的一部分 / 一份\r\n\r\nEveryone should get a fair share of the profits.\r\n每个人都应该得到公平的一份利润。\r\n\r\nHe owns a large share of the company.\r\n他拥有这家公司很大一部分股份。\r\n\r\nshare of the market\r\n市场份额\r\n\r\nThe company has increased its share of the market.\r\n这家公司提高了自己的市场份额。\r\n\r\n更常见也可以直接说：\r\n\r\nmarket share\r\n市场份额\r\n\r\nshare of the population\r\n人口中的比例\r\n\r\nOlder people make up a growing share of the population.\r\n老年人在总人口中所占的比例越来越大。\r\n\r\nshare of total + 名词\r\n占总量的比例\r\n\r\nOnline sales now account for a large share of total revenue.\r\n线上销售现在占总收入的很大一部分。\r\n\r\none\'s share of sth\r\n某人应得 / 承担的那一份\r\n\r\nI\'ve done my share of the work.\r\n我已经完成了我该做的那部分工作。\r\n\r\nEveryone has to pay their share of the cost.\r\n每个人都得支付自己应承担的那部分费用。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nChina accounts for a large share of global manufacturing.\r\n中国占全球制造业很大一部分。\r\n\r\nThe company gained a bigger share of the market last year.\r\n去年这家公司获得了更大的市场份额。\r\n\r\nTransport takes up a significant share of household spending.\r\n交通支出占家庭开支的很大比例。\r\n\r\nYoung people represent a smaller share of the population than before.\r\n年轻人在总人口中所占的比例比以前更小了。\r\n\r\nEach team member should do their fair share of the work.\r\n每个团队成员都应该完成自己应承担的那部分工作。\r\n\r\nThe project took up a large share of our time.\r\n这个项目占用了我们很大一部分时间。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\nshare of 的核心逻辑其实很简单：\r\n\r\n整体\r\n↓\r\n其中的一部分\r\n↓\r\na share of the whole\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\na share of the profits\r\n利润中的一部分\r\n\r\na share of the market\r\n市场中的一部分\r\n\r\na share of total sales\r\n总销售额中的一部分\r\n\r\n所以你看到：\r\n\r\na large share of\r\n= 很大一部分\r\n\r\na small share of\r\n= 很小一部分\r\n\r\na growing share of\r\n= 越来越大的比例\r\n\r\na significant share of\r\n= 相当大的比例\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混对比\r\n\r\nshare of\r\n= 某个整体中的份额 / 比例\r\n很常用，既可以表示具体的一份，也可以表示统计比例。\r\n\r\npercentage of\r\n= ……的百分比\r\n更强调具体的百分数。\r\n\r\nA large share of people supported the proposal.\r\n很大一部分人支持这个提议。\r\n\r\n60% of people supported the proposal.\r\n60%的人支持这个提议。\r\n\r\nportion of\r\n= 一部分\r\n更强调“整体切出来的一部分”。\r\n\r\nA large portion of the budget goes to healthcare.\r\n预算中很大一部分用于医疗。\r\n\r\nproportion of\r\n= 比例\r\n比 share of 更正式，统计语境很常见。\r\n\r\nThe proportion of older people is increasing.\r\n老年人的比例正在上升。\r\n\r\npart of\r\n= ……的一部分\r\n最普通、最宽泛。\r\n\r\nThis is part of the problem.\r\n这是问题的一部分。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nshare 后面通常搭配 of\r\n\r\n✅ a large share of the market\r\n\r\n✅ a small share of total revenue\r\n\r\nshare 不一定是“股票”\r\n\r\nshare 确实可以表示：\r\n\r\na share in a company\r\n公司股份\r\n\r\n但：\r\n\r\na share of the population\r\n不是“人口股份”，而是：\r\n\r\n人口中的一部分 / 所占比例。\r\n\r\nmarket share 比 share of the market 更固定\r\n\r\nThe company has a 30% market share.\r\n这家公司拥有30%的市场份额。\r\n\r\nThe company has a large share of the market.\r\n这家公司占据了很大的市场份额。\r\n\r\n两种都自然。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把一个大蛋糕想成整体：\r\n\r\n整个蛋糕 = the whole\r\n\r\n切下来的一块：\r\n\r\na share of the cake\r\n= 蛋糕中的一份\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nshare of = 整体中的一份\r\n\r\n再延伸：\r\n\r\na share of the market\r\n→ 市场中的一块\r\n→ 市场份额\r\n\r\na share of the population\r\n→ 人口中的一块\r\n→ 人口比例\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nshare of = “……里面占的一部分 / 份额”。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/e777a465272b477c8e548ccf608f79ad.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-06 12:36:56',1,'2026-09-06 12:36:56'),(1603,21,90,'phrase','accuse sb of sth','accuse sb of sth','accuse sb of sth','🎯 核心意思\r\naccuse sb of sth\r\n= 指责 / 指控某人做了某事\r\n\r\n常见中文：\r\n\r\n指责某人……\r\n\r\n控告某人……\r\n\r\n指控某人……\r\n\r\n说某人犯了……\r\n\r\n它通常带有一种“认为对方做了错事、坏事或违法的事”的感觉。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\naccuse sb of + 名词\r\n指控某人某件事\r\n\r\nThey accused him of theft.\r\n他们指控他盗窃。\r\n\r\nShe accused me of lying.\r\n她指责我撒谎。\r\n\r\naccuse sb of doing sth\r\n指责某人做了某事\r\n\r\nHe was accused of stealing money.\r\n他被指控偷钱。\r\n\r\nThey accused the company of misleading customers.\r\n他们指责这家公司误导消费者。\r\n\r\nbe accused of sth\r\n被指控……\r\n\r\nHe was accused of fraud.\r\n他被指控诈骗。\r\n\r\nThe politician was accused of corruption.\r\n这名政治人物被指控腐败。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nShe accused him of breaking the agreement.\r\n她指责他违反了协议。\r\n\r\nThe employee was accused of leaking confidential information.\r\n这名员工被指控泄露机密信息。\r\n\r\nThey accused the government of misleading the public.\r\n他们指责政府误导公众。\r\n\r\nDon\'t accuse me of something I didn\'t do.\r\n不要拿我没做过的事情来指责我。\r\n\r\nHe was wrongly accused of cheating.\r\n他被错误地指控作弊。\r\n\r\nThe customer accused the company of hiding important information.\r\n这名顾客指责公司隐瞒重要信息。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n结构：\r\n\r\naccuse + 人 + of + 事情 / doing sth\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThey accused him of lying.\r\n\r\n拆开：\r\n\r\nThey\r\n他们\r\n\r\naccused him\r\n指责他\r\n\r\nof lying\r\n说他撒谎\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\naccuse sb of doing sth\r\n= 指责某人做了某事\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混对比\r\n\r\naccuse sb of sth\r\n= 指控 / 指责某人某事\r\n通常比较严重。\r\n\r\nblame sb for sth\r\n= 因为某事责怪某人\r\n\r\n对比：\r\n\r\nThey blamed him for the mistake.\r\n他们因为这个错误责怪他。\r\n\r\nThey accused him of hiding the mistake.\r\n他们指控他隐瞒了这个错误。\r\n\r\n区别：\r\n\r\nblame → “这件事是你的责任”\r\naccuse → “我认为你做了某件错事”\r\n\r\n再对比：\r\n\r\ncharge sb with sth\r\n= 正式指控某人犯罪\r\n法律语境更强。\r\n\r\nHe was charged with theft.\r\n他被正式指控盗窃。\r\n\r\naccuse him of theft\r\n= 指控他盗窃，不一定已经进入正式法律程序\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n最重要的是介词：\r\n\r\n✅ accuse sb of sth\r\n❌ accuse sb for sth\r\n\r\n要和 blame 区分：\r\n\r\n✅ blame sb for sth\r\n\r\n✅ accuse sb of sth\r\n\r\n可以直接一起记：\r\n\r\nblame sb for sth\r\n因为某事责怪某人\r\n\r\naccuse sb of sth\r\n指控某人做了某事\r\n\r\n另外：\r\n\r\n✅ accuse sb of doing sth\r\n\r\nShe accused me of lying.\r\n她指责我撒谎。\r\n\r\n不能说：\r\n\r\n❌ accuse me to lie\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把它记成两个固定搭配：\r\n\r\nblame → for\r\naccuse → of\r\n\r\nblame me for the problem\r\n因为问题责怪我\r\n\r\naccuse me of causing the problem\r\n指控我造成了问题\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nDon\'t accuse me of something I didn\'t do.\r\n别拿我没做过的事来指控我。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/587eabbbf5cd4512b97842ef170c8a59.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-06 12:41:01',1,'2026-09-06 12:41:01'),(1604,21,91,'phrase','a regular feature of sth','a regular feature of sth','a regular feature of sth','🎯 核心意思\r\na regular feature of sth\r\n= ……中经常出现的特点 / 固定存在的一部分 / 常见现象\r\n\r\n这里的 regular 不是“规则的”，而是：\r\n\r\n经常发生的、固定出现的、反复出现的。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\na regular feature of daily life\r\n= 日常生活中经常出现的一部分 / 常见现象','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\na regular feature of daily life\r\n日常生活中经常出现的事情\r\n\r\nTraffic jams have become a regular feature of city life.\r\n交通堵塞已经成了城市生活中的常见现象。\r\n\r\na regular feature of meetings\r\n会议中固定会出现的环节 / 情况\r\n\r\nTechnical discussions are a regular feature of our weekly meetings.\r\n技术讨论是我们每周会议里的固定内容。\r\n\r\nbecome a regular feature of sth\r\n成为……中的常态 / 固定部分\r\n\r\nRemote work has become a regular feature of modern workplaces.\r\n远程办公已经成为现代职场中的常态。\r\n\r\nbe a regular feature of sth\r\n是……中经常出现的特点\r\n\r\nHeavy rain is a regular feature of winter here.\r\n这里冬季经常下大雨。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nDelays have become a regular feature of the project.\r\n延期已经成了这个项目中经常出现的情况。\r\n\r\nThese reports are now a regular feature of our monthly review.\r\n这些报告现在已经成了我们月度复盘中的固定内容。\r\n\r\nPublic debate is a regular feature of democratic societies.\r\n公众讨论是民主社会中经常出现的一种现象。\r\n\r\nUnexpected errors are a regular feature of complex software systems.\r\n意外错误是复杂软件系统中经常出现的情况。\r\n\r\nBad weather is a regular feature of winter in this region.\r\n恶劣天气是这个地区冬季常见的现象。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\na regular feature of sth\r\n\r\n可以拆成：\r\n\r\nregular\r\n= recurring / frequent / happening repeatedly\r\n经常发生的、反复出现的\r\n\r\nfeature\r\n= characteristic / part / aspect\r\n特点、组成部分、现象\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\na regular feature of sth\r\n≈ something that commonly or repeatedly appears as part of something\r\n某个事物中经常或反复出现的一部分 / 特征\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nStress is a regular feature of his job.\r\n压力是他这份工作中经常存在的一部分。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混对比\r\n\r\na regular feature of\r\n= 经常出现的特点 / 固定组成部分\r\n强调“反复出现、已经很常见”。\r\n\r\na common feature of\r\n= ……的常见特点\r\n强调“很多情况下都有”。\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nHigh staff turnover is a common feature of the industry.\r\n员工流动率高是这个行业的常见特点。\r\n\r\na typical feature of\r\n= ……的典型特征\r\n强调“具有代表性”。\r\n\r\nLarge windows are a typical feature of this style of house.\r\n大窗户是这种房屋风格的典型特征。\r\n\r\na key feature of\r\n= ……的关键特点\r\n强调“重要”。\r\n\r\nSecurity is a key feature of the system.\r\n安全性是这个系统的关键特点。\r\n\r\n对比一下：\r\n\r\na regular feature\r\n→ 经常出现\r\n\r\na common feature\r\n→ 很普遍\r\n\r\na typical feature\r\n→ 很典型\r\n\r\na key feature\r\n→ 很重要\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\n通常说：\r\n\r\n✅ a regular feature of sth\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n❌ a regular feature in sth\r\n\r\n虽然某些语境下 in 也可能成立，但固定表达里 of 更常见。\r\n\r\nregular 在这里不要理解成“有规律的”\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n\r\nPower cuts are a regular feature of life here.\r\n\r\n不是：\r\n\r\n“停电是有规律的特点”\r\n\r\n而是：\r\n\r\n“停电在这里是经常发生的事。”\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\nfeature = 一个事物里“会出现的东西”\r\n\r\nregular = 经常出现\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\na regular feature of sth\r\n= 在某事中反复出现、已经很常见的一部分\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nIt has become a regular feature of our daily work.\r\n它已经成了我们日常工作中经常出现的一部分。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/8ceaecc6632741b59b856a71a1636c17.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-06 13:03:07',1,'2026-09-06 13:03:07'),(1605,21,92,'vocab','fabricate','fabricate','fabricate','🎯 核心意思\r\nfabricate 主要有两个常见意思：\r\n\r\n编造，捏造\r\n尤其指“编造故事、证据、借口、数据”等，通常带有“不真实、欺骗”的意味。\r\n\r\n制造，制作\r\n多用于工业、工程语境，表示“用材料加工制造某个部件或结构”。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\nfabricate a story / excuse / claim\r\n编造故事 / 借口 / 说法\r\n\r\nHe fabricated a story to explain why he was late.\r\n他编了一个故事来解释自己为什么迟到。\r\n\r\nShe was accused of fabricating the whole story.\r\n她被指控捏造了整个故事。\r\n\r\nfabricate evidence / data\r\n伪造证据 / 捏造数据\r\n\r\nThe researcher was found to have fabricated data.\r\n那名研究人员被发现捏造了数据。\r\n\r\nThe police denied fabricating evidence.\r\n警方否认伪造证据。\r\n\r\n这个搭配非常值得学，因为新闻、法律、科研语境中很常见。\r\n\r\nfabricate allegations / accusations\r\n捏造指控\r\n\r\nHe claimed that the allegations had been fabricated.\r\n他声称这些指控是捏造出来的。\r\n\r\nfabricate parts / components / structures\r\n制造零件 / 部件 / 结构\r\n\r\nThe components are fabricated from stainless steel.\r\n这些部件由不锈钢加工制成。\r\n\r\nThe frame was fabricated in a local workshop.\r\n这个框架是在当地车间制造的。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nHe completely fabricated the story.\r\n这个故事完全是他编出来的。\r\n\r\nYou can\'t just fabricate evidence to support your argument.\r\n你不能为了支持自己的观点就捏造证据。\r\n\r\nThe report accused the company of fabricating test results.\r\n报告指控该公司伪造测试结果。\r\n\r\nShe fabricated an excuse for missing the meeting.\r\n她为没有参加会议编了一个借口。\r\n\r\nThese metal parts are fabricated locally.\r\n这些金属部件是在本地加工制造的。\r\n\r\nThe structure was fabricated off-site and assembled later.\r\n这个结构先在场外制造，然后再进行组装。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n如果你看到：\r\n\r\nThe evidence was fabricated.\r\n\r\n这里的 fabricate 几乎肯定不是“制造”，而是：\r\n\r\n证据是伪造的 / 捏造的。\r\n\r\n因为 evidence 本来就应该是真实的，所以 fabricate evidence 自带一种“人为造假”的意味。\r\n\r\n但如果是：\r\n\r\nThe steel frame was fabricated in China.\r\n\r\n这里就是正常的工业含义：\r\n\r\n钢结构是在中国制造加工的。\r\n\r\n所以判断 fabricate 的意思，关键看后面的宾语。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混对比\r\n\r\nfabricate vs make up\r\n\r\nmake up\r\n更口语，常表示“编故事、编借口”。\r\n\r\nHe made up an excuse.\r\n他编了个借口。\r\n\r\nfabricate\r\n更正式，而且更强调“故意捏造、造假”。\r\n\r\nHe fabricated evidence.\r\n他伪造了证据。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nmake up a story\r\n很日常\r\n\r\nfabricate a story\r\n更正式，也更有“故意编造骗人”的感觉\r\n\r\nfabricate vs forge\r\n\r\nfabricate\r\n强调“捏造内容”。\r\n\r\nfabricate evidence\r\n捏造证据\r\n\r\nforge\r\n更强调“伪造文件、签名、货币等具体东西”。\r\n\r\nforge a signature\r\n伪造签名\r\n\r\nforge a passport\r\n伪造护照\r\n\r\nfabricate vs manufacture\r\n\r\nmanufacture\r\n主要就是“工业制造”。\r\n\r\nmanufacture cars\r\n制造汽车\r\n\r\nfabricate\r\n也可以表示制造，但更常用于：\r\n\r\nfabricate metal components\r\n加工制造金属部件\r\n\r\n在工程语境里，fabricate 常有“按设计加工、拼装成部件”的感觉。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\nfabricate 是动词：\r\n\r\nfabricate evidence\r\n伪造证据\r\n\r\n对应名词是：\r\n\r\nfabrication\r\n/ˌfæbrɪˈkeɪʃən/\r\n\r\n可以表示：\r\n\r\n捏造，虚构\r\nThe story was a complete fabrication.\r\n这个故事完全是捏造的。\r\n\r\n制造，加工\r\nmetal fabrication\r\n金属加工\r\n\r\n注意：\r\n\r\nfabricate 本身通常比 invent 更负面。\r\n\r\ninvent a story\r\n可能只是“创作、虚构故事”\r\n\r\nfabricate a story\r\n往往暗示“故意说假话”。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n可以联想：\r\n\r\nfabric = 材料、织物\r\n\r\nfabricate 最初有“把材料加工成东西”的感觉：\r\n\r\n材料\r\n→ 加工\r\n→ 制造出来\r\n\r\n后来也引申成：\r\n\r\n把不存在的事情“制造出来”\r\n→ 编造\r\n→ 捏造\r\n\r\n所以可以记：\r\n\r\nfabricate = “制造”\r\n\r\n制造真的东西\r\n→ 加工制造\r\n\r\n制造假的事实\r\n→ 编造、捏造\r\n\r\n一个非常值得记住的高频搭配：\r\n\r\nfabricate evidence\r\n= 伪造 / 捏造证据\r\n\r\n以及：\r\n\r\nfabricate data\r\n= 捏造数据','/static/uploads/english_note_item/94ff375961114d8b9865d573ebc04672.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-06 13:14:11',1,'2026-09-06 13:14:11'),(1606,21,93,'phrase','a great deal of change','a great deal of change','a great deal of change','🎯 核心意思\r\na great deal of change\r\n= 很大的变化；大量的变化\r\n\r\n这里的 a great deal of 表示：\r\n\r\n很多，大量\r\n\r\n而 change 在这里通常是不可数名词，表示整体上的“变化、改变”。\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\na great deal of change\r\n≈ a lot of change\r\n≈ a large amount of change\r\n\r\n但 a great deal of 比 a lot of 稍正式一些。','🧩 不同含义与常见用法\r\n\r\na great deal of change\r\n发生了很大的变化\r\n\r\nThere has been a great deal of change in the company.\r\n这家公司发生了很大的变化。\r\n\r\nsee / experience a great deal of change\r\n经历很多变化\r\n\r\nThe industry has experienced a great deal of change over the past decade.\r\n这个行业在过去十年经历了很大的变化。\r\n\r\nbring about / cause a great deal of change\r\n带来很大的变化\r\n\r\nThe new technology could bring about a great deal of change.\r\n这项新技术可能会带来很大的变化。\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of change\r\n没有太大变化\r\n\r\nThere hasn’t been a great deal of change since last year.\r\n从去年到现在没有太大的变化。\r\n\r\n这个结构在报告、数据分析里非常常见。','💬 中英双语例句\r\n\r\nThere has been a great deal of change over the past few years.\r\n过去几年发生了很大的变化。\r\n\r\nThe system has gone through a great deal of change.\r\n这个系统经历了很多变化。\r\n\r\nWe’ve seen a great deal of change in customer behaviour.\r\n我们看到客户行为发生了很大的变化。\r\n\r\nThere wasn’t a great deal of change in the results.\r\n结果没有太大的变化。\r\n\r\nThe figures show that there has not been a great deal of change.\r\n数据显示变化并不大。\r\n\r\nThe workplace has undergone a great deal of change since the pandemic.\r\n自疫情以来，工作环境经历了很大的变化。\r\n\r\n📖 原句解析\r\n\r\n如果你看到：\r\n\r\nThere hasn’t been a great deal of change.\r\n\r\n不要逐字理解成：\r\n\r\n“没有一大笔变化”\r\n\r\n这里的 a great deal of 是一个整体：\r\n\r\na great deal of + 不可数名词\r\n= 大量的……\r\n\r\n所以整句：\r\n\r\nThere hasn’t been a great deal of change.\r\n= 没有发生太大的变化。\r\n\r\n这个表达比：\r\n\r\nThere hasn’t been much change.\r\n\r\n稍微更正式、更自然地适合报告、会议、分析场景。\r\n\r\n🆚 近义词／易混对比\r\n\r\na great deal of change\r\n= 很大的变化 / 大量变化\r\n偏正式\r\n\r\na lot of change\r\n= 很多变化\r\n更日常\r\n\r\nmuch change\r\n通常更常出现在否定句和疑问句里\r\n\r\nThere hasn’t been much change.\r\n没有太大变化。\r\n\r\nsignificant change\r\n= 显著变化\r\n强调“变化在程度上很明显”\r\n\r\nThere has been significant change.\r\n已经发生了显著变化。\r\n\r\na dramatic change\r\n= 巨大、剧烈的变化\r\n\r\nThere has been a dramatic change in demand.\r\n需求发生了剧烈变化。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 易错点\r\n\r\na great deal of 后面通常接不可数名词：\r\n\r\n✅ a great deal of change\r\n\r\n✅ a great deal of time\r\n\r\n✅ a great deal of money\r\n\r\n✅ a great deal of attention\r\n\r\n通常不说：\r\n\r\n❌ a great deal of changes\r\n\r\n如果你想表达“很多不同的具体变化”，可以说：\r\n\r\na great many changes\r\nmany changes\r\na lot of changes\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nThe system has undergone many changes.\r\n这个系统经历了很多具体改动。\r\n\r\n而：\r\n\r\nThe system has undergone a great deal of change.\r\n更强调“整体上发生了很大的变化”。\r\n\r\n🧠 记忆方法\r\n\r\n把 a great deal of 直接记成：\r\n\r\n= a lot of\r\n= 大量的\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\na great deal of change\r\n= 很大的变化\r\n\r\n特别值得一起记住这组：\r\n\r\na great deal of change\r\n很多变化\r\n\r\nnot a great deal of change\r\n没有太大变化\r\n\r\n在汇报数据时很好用：\r\n\r\nThere hasn’t been a great deal of change compared with last month.\r\n和上个月相比，没有太大的变化。','/static/uploads/english_note_item/b864a3db4a0b4e379948c41000a88662.png','','',0,0,1,'2026-09-07 14:06:09',1,'2026-09-07 14:06:09');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `english_note_item` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;

--
-- Table structure for table `everyday_sentence`
--

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS `everyday_sentence`;
/*!40101 SET @saved_cs_client     = @@character_set_client */;
/*!50503 SET character_set_client = utf8mb4 */;
CREATE TABLE `everyday_sentence` (
  `id` bigint unsigned NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT COMMENT '主键ID',
  `tag` varchar(100) COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL COMMENT '分类标签',
  `en` text COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL COMMENT '英文句子',
  `cn` text COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL COMMENT '中文释义',
  `note` text COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci COMMENT '备注说明',
  `share_status` tinyint NOT NULL DEFAULT '0' COMMENT '共享状态：0-私有，1-共享',
  `priority_order` int NOT NULL DEFAULT '0' COMMENT '排序值，越小越靠前',
  `created_by` bigint NOT NULL COMMENT '创建人ID',
  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP COMMENT '创建时间',
  `updated_by` bigint DEFAULT NULL COMMENT '修改人ID',
  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP COMMENT '修改时间',
  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)
) ENGINE=InnoDB AUTO_INCREMENT=224 DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci COMMENT='日常英文句子表';
/*!40101 SET character_set_client = @saved_cs_client */;

--
-- Dumping data for table `everyday_sentence`
--

LOCK TABLES `everyday_sentence` WRITE;
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `everyday_sentence` DISABLE KEYS */;
INSERT INTO `everyday_sentence` VALUES (1,'Transport','Just hop on at the yellow line up front.','就在前面黄色线那里上车。','hop on 很口语，表示“上车”。up front = 在前面。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(2,'Campus life','A lot of EAP students have just started, so the buses are pretty full.','很多 EAP 学生刚开学，所以公交车非常满。','pretty full 是很自然的口语表达。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(3,'Study','I haven’t sat IELTS, but I’ve been doing the EAP English course at Lincoln.','我没有考雅思，但我在 Lincoln 上 EAP 英语课程。','sit IELTS 在澳新/英式英语里表示“参加雅思考试”。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(4,'Plans','After I graduate, I’ll think about staying in New Zealand to work, since I’ll have a three-year work visa.','毕业后我会考虑留在新西兰工作，因为我会有三年的工作签证。','think about doing = 考虑做某事。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(5,'Personal story','I came to NZ from China mainly for two reasons. Work back home was crazy and I had no free time, and also, the schooling back home is way too competitive for kids. I just wanted a bit of a different pace.','我来新西兰主要有两个原因：国内工作太忙，没有空闲时间，而且那边的教育对孩子来说太卷了。我只是想要一种稍微不同一点的生活节奏。','back home = 在国内。a different pace = 不同的生活节奏。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(6,'Background','I’ve done software engineering for over ten years.','我做软件工程已经十多年了。','很适合自我介绍和面试。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(7,'Life in NZ','I’ve been in NZ since June last year, only went back home once.','我从去年六月起就在新西兰，中间只回过一次国。','更自然可说：I’ve only gone back home once。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(8,'Shopping','Hey, I’m having a hard time choosing the right type of apple on the self-checkout machine. Could you please help me figure out which one I need?','我在自助结账机器上不知道选哪种苹果，你能帮我一下吗？','也可说：I’m not sure which apple to pick on the self-checkout。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(9,'Opinion','His failure was an inevitable result of his laziness.','他的失败是他懒惰的必然结果。','inevitable = 不可避免的。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(10,'Conversation','That’s a perfect way to put it.','你说得太贴切了 / 这个说法太到位了。','很适合回应别人表达得很准确时使用。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(11,'Encouragement','I was exhausted, but I pushed through it.','我累得不行了，但我还是坚持下来了。','push through = 咬牙坚持过去。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(12,'Encouragement','It feels pointless now, but it won’t always feel this way.','现在感觉没有意义，但不会一直这样。','安慰别人时很自然。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(13,'Opinion','Nothing he says counts.','他说话不算数。','也可理解为“他说的话没分量”。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(14,'Direct speech','You think you’re more important than you really are.','你把自己看得太重了。','语气较直接，使用时注意场合。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(15,'Social issues','I saw some people on social media copying Indian people. Do you think this behavior is offensive?','我看见有些人在社交媒体上模仿印度人，你认为这种行为是冒犯的吗？','offensive = 冒犯的。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(16,'Food','I noticed that many Indian foods are fried.','我注意到很多印度食物都是油炸的。','notice that... 是很常见的观察表达。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(17,'Work / study','Has the problem been solved?','问题解决了吗？','被动语态，适合工作和学习场景。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(18,'Classroom','Do we need to check attendance?','我们今天需要签到吗？','check attendance = 点名 / 签到。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(19,'Daily life','If this problem is solved, I’ll come to your place.','如果这个问题解决了，我就去你那儿。','your place = 你家 / 你那儿。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(20,'Confidence','Nobody looks down on me for using simple words and short sentences.','没有人因为我用简单的词和短句子而看不起我。','look down on = 看不起。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(21,'Daily objects','That thermal carafe is quite a handy thing to have.','那个保温壶真是个很实用的东西。','handy = 方便的、实用的。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(22,'Small talk','Anything you are working on?','你最近在忙什么？','更自然完整可说：Are you working on anything at the moment?',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(23,'Conversation','How did it end?','最后结果怎么样？/ 结局如何？','适合问故事、电影、事件的结局。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(24,'Conversation','How did it go?','怎么样？/ 进展如何？','比 How was it? 更口语自然。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(25,'Interview','Do you have any questions for me?','你还有什么要问我的吗？','面试结尾高频句。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(26,'Interview','Where do you see yourself in the next few years?','你未来几年的职业规划是什么？','经典面试题。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(27,'Banking','Just to confirm, this won’t affect my online banking, right?','我想确认一下，这个不会影响我的网上银行使用，对吗？','Just to confirm... 很适合礼貌确认信息。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(28,'Work','I’m taking some time off.','我在休息一段时间 / 我在请假 / 我在放假。','常见变体：I’m taking some time off next week。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(29,'Work','How long are you off for?','你要休息多久？','be off = 休息 / 不上班。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(30,'Invitation','Don’t worry about bringing anything.','什么都不用带。','也可以说：No need to bring anything。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(31,'Informal','He let rip at the meeting.','他在会上直接开喷。','let rip 很口语，表示猛烈发泄或开骂。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(32,'Workplace','The tape’s run out.','胶带用完了。','run out = 用完。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(33,'Workplace','You might be able to be trained to cross, but I’ll start you on easy stuff today.','你以后可能会被培训去做其他岗位的事情，但今天我会先让你做一些简单的事。','start someone on easy stuff 是很自然的带教表达。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(34,'Feelings','It’s a lot to take in.','信息量有点大 / 有点难一下子消化。','固定表达，常被误说成 take place。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(35,'Opinion','What he said is really insightful.','他说得很有见解。','insightful = 有洞见的。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(36,'Study','I’m stuck on my assessment.','我的作业卡住了，不知道该怎么写了。','be stuck on = 卡在某个地方。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(37,'Conversation','How do you cope with ... ?','你如何应对……？','cope with = 应对、处理。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(38,'Conversation','I haven’t done this for ages.','我好久没做这个了。','for ages 很口语，表示“很久”。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(39,'Advice','Taking the train home is going to be the way to go.','坐火车回家是最好的选择。','the way to go = 最佳选择。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(40,'Study / work','Let’s do a deep dive into how this works.','我们深入了解一下这个是如何运作的。','deep dive = 深入研究。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(41,'Coding','Retain this section of code and remove all other parts.','保留这块代码，把其他部分都删掉。','retain = 保留。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(42,'Small talk','How was your day at work?','你今天工作怎么样？','很自然的日常问候。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(43,'Work','It was good. I was relieved that my boss let me clock out early, so I was able to go home.','挺好的，我松了一口气，老板让我今天早点打卡，所以我能回家了。','clock out = 下班打卡。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(44,'Work','I sat in on a meeting with the department head.','我旁听了一场和部门负责人的会议。','sit in on = 旁听、列席。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(45,'Work','It was a hectic day.','那是忙乱的一天。','hectic = 很忙乱的。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(46,'Work','I’m still settling into my role.','我还在慢慢适应我的岗位。','settle into = 逐渐适应。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(47,'Work schedule','We rotate through weekend shifts.','我们周末轮流上班。','rotate through = 轮流做。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(48,'Daily life','I could use a nap.','我真想小睡一会儿。','委婉表达“我有点累，需要休息”。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(49,'Daily life','I’m worn out after work.','下班后我累坏了。','worn out = 非常疲惫。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(50,'Feelings','I’m so over my job.','我对这份工作彻底厌烦了。','be over something = 受够了。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(51,'Feedback','Some people’s English might be a little mixed up, but that’s not the case with you.','有些人的英语可能有点乱，但你不是这种情况。','that’s not the case with you 很自然。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(52,'Conversation','I am just saying the truth.','我只是实话实说。','更自然口语可说：I’m just telling the truth。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(53,'Money','He made a fortune in the stock market.','他在股市上赚了大钱。','make a fortune = 赚大钱。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(54,'Study','I’m just double-checking the assignment requirements to make sure I haven’t missed anything.','我只是再检查一下作业要求，确保没有漏掉什么。','double-check = 再确认一次。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(55,'Small talk','What are you up to this weekend?','你这周末准备干什么？','非常常见的周末寒暄。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(56,'Small talk','Not much. Just relaxing.','没什么特别安排，就随便放松一下。','回答周末计划时很好用。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(57,'Invitation','Do you want to grab a coffee?','你想喝杯咖啡吗？','grab a coffee = 喝杯咖啡 / 约咖啡。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(58,'Agreement','Definitely / So true / Exactly / Yeah, totally / 100%','表示强烈同意：绝对是 / 太对了 / 没错 / 完全同意。','适合口语回应别人。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(59,'Goodbye','Catch you later.','回头见 / 等会儿见。','轻松友好的告别语。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(60,'Learning advice','Try to get into the habit of speaking English every day.','试着养成每天说英语的习惯。','get into the habit of = 养成……习惯。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(61,'Shopping','It’s not a big deal if you choose the wrong category when you check out.','结账时选错商品类别也不是什么大问题。','not a big deal = 没什么大不了。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(62,'Home','Dinner will be ready in no time.','饭马上就好。','in no time = 很快、马上。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(63,'Goals','I’m on a mission to improve my English fluency.','我正在下定决心提升英语流利度。','be on a mission to... = 下定决心去做。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(64,'Work schedule','I’ll be working till 1 p.m. / I’m gonna work through till 1.','我会一直工作到下午一点。','work through till... 很口语。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(65,'Transport','I’m cycling to work today.','我今天骑自行车上班。','也可说 I’m biking to work today。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(66,'Transport','There’s a bike rack over there.','那边有个停放自行车的架子。','bike rack = 自行车架。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(67,'Opinion','I know it seems wasteful.','我知道这看起来很浪费。','wasteful = 浪费的。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(68,'Work schedule','When’s your day off? / What days are you off?','你哪天休息？/ 你哪几天休息？','be off = 休息、不上班。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(69,'Appearance','He’s really bulked up since last year.','他从去年开始明显练壮了。','bulk up = 变壮、增肌。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(70,'Success','All the hard work paid off.','所有努力都有回报了。','pay off = 得到回报。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(71,'Conversation','I’m being sarcastic.','我是在讽刺 / 我在说反话。','sarcastic = 讽刺的。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(72,'Habits','Occasionally, I watch movies.','我偶尔看电影。','occasionally = 偶尔。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(73,'Presentation','I’ll be brief.','我简单两句。','讲话前非常自然。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(74,'Instructions','Please follow the brief / instructions.','请按照任务说明 / 指示来做。','brief 在这里是任务说明。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(75,'Encouragement','Lower the bar rather than give up.','与其放弃，不如先降低标准。','很适合激励自己。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(76,'Parenting','We should give our child a bit more leeway.','我们应该多给孩子一点自由度 / 宽容一些。','leeway = 余地、自由度。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(77,'Feedback','Looks like you’ve got the hang of it pretty well.','看起来你已经挺快上手了。','get the hang of it = 上手、掌握窍门。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(78,'Workplace','Sometimes it’s a bit hard to work out which category an item should go in.','有时候不太容易弄明白一个商品该归到哪个类别。','work out = 弄明白。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(79,'Conversation','Whatever works best for you.','看你怎么方便 / 怎么方便怎么来。','非常实用、自然。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(80,'Conversation','I haven’t been here for a while.','我有一段时间没来这儿了。','和 I haven’t been here for ages 类似。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(81,'Weather','We can get hit by four seasons in a day.','我们可能一天经历四个季节。','新西兰天气话题高频句。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(82,'Small talk','Is there anything going on outside?','外面在举行什么活动吗？','going on = 正在发生。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(83,'Phone','I haven’t got a lot of battery.','我手机没多少电了。','更自然也可说：I don’t have much battery left。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(84,'Service','Is there anything else I can help you with?','还有别的事情我能帮你吗？','服务场景高频句。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(85,'Family','I want to be reunited with my family.','我想和家人团聚。','be reunited with = 与……重聚。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(86,'Conversation','That’s not happening right now.','现在还实现不了 / 现在还不行。','口语里很自然的婉转否定。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(87,'Conversation','So we’ll see. We shall see.','我们到时候看吧 / 我们走着瞧。','带一点保留判断的语气。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(88,'Progress','It’s just this last little bit.','就只剩最后这一点点了。','很适合描述快完成了。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(89,'Health','This is good for your digestion.','这个对消化有好处。','digestion = 消化。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(90,'Health','This food is high in fiber.','这种食物富含纤维。','high in fiber = 富含纤维。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(91,'Classroom','Are we doing our English class over at that table soon?','我们一会儿要在那张桌子上英语课吗？','over at that table = 在那边那张桌子。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(92,'School','The school holidays are coming up.','学校快放假了。','coming up = 快到了。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(93,'Classroom','I’ll pair you up.','我会把你们两两分组。','pair someone up = 两两分组。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(94,'Classroom','Grab a question strip at random.','随机拿一张问题纸条。','at random = 随机地。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(95,'Work','I got tied up with a client.','我被客户那边的事情耽搁住了。','get tied up with 多用于工作、客户、会议。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(96,'Conversation','We have a lot of furniture here now, but we didn’t last week.','我们现在这里有很多家具，但上周没有这么多。','对比现在和过去时很自然。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(97,'Conversation','Has he come out here?','他来过这里吗？/ 他来这边了吗？','现在完成时结构。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(98,'Time','New Zealand is one hour ahead of Fiji.','新西兰时间比斐济快一个小时。','ahead of = 比……快。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(99,'Work','It’s very labor-intensive.','这非常费人工 / 这很劳动密集。','新西兰更常见拼写也可写作 labour-intensive。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(100,'Health','Sleep is important for your immune system.','睡眠对免疫系统很重要。','immune system = 免疫系统。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(101,'Food / health','This product contains no artificial additives.','这个产品不含人工添加剂。','additives = 添加剂。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(102,'Weekend','I’m going to sleep in and not set an alarm.','我打算睡个懒觉，不设闹钟。','sleep in = 睡懒觉。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(103,'Food','Are you going to treat me to a big meal?','你要请我吃大餐吗？','treat someone to... = 请某人吃/喝。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(104,'Social','I’m catching up with a friend I haven’t seen in a while.','我要和一个好久没见的朋友聚一聚。','catch up with = 叙旧、聊近况。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(105,'Social','I volunteered to babysit for a few hours to help a friend out.','我主动提出帮朋友照看几个小时孩子。','help someone out = 帮某人一把。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(106,'Social','I’m hosting a small get-together at my place for some friends.','我在家邀请一些朋友举办小型聚会。','get-together = 小聚会。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(107,'Social','I’m meeting a friend for coffee.','我要和朋友约着喝咖啡。','轻松自然的日常表达。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(108,'Work','I’m responsible for pricing clothes and popping them onto the shelves, and sometimes I also help at the checkout.','我负责给衣服定价并把它们摆到货架上，有时也会在收银台帮忙。','be responsible for 和 help at the checkout 都很实用。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(109,'Shopping','I’m just trying to get some measurements to see if it’s a queen or a double.','我只是想量一下尺寸，看看它是 queen 还是 double。','get some measurements = 量尺寸。',0,0,1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59',1,'2026-04-04 09:44:59'),(110,'Everyday Speaking','I had butterflies in my stomach the first time you talked to me','•	你第一次和我说话时，我紧张得心里扑通扑通的。\r\n	•	你第一次跟我讲话的时候，我一下子就慌了。\r\n	•	你第一次和我说话时，我心里小鹿乱撞。','1. I had butterflies in my stomach\r\n\r\n这是一个非常常见的习语。\r\n\r\n意思不是字面上的“胃里有蝴蝶”，而是：\r\n感到紧张、忐忑、激动\r\n常用于：\r\n	•	见喜欢的人\r\n	•	上台演讲前\r\n	•	面试前\r\n	•	比赛前\r\n例如：\r\n	•	I always get butterflies in my stomach before an interview.\r\n我面试前总会很紧张。',0,0,1,'2026-04-06 17:11:53',1,'2026-04-06 17:11:53'),(112,'Everyday Speaking','You can do this pretty much anytime.','你基本上任何时候都可以做这件事','You can do this: 你可以做这个\r\npretty much  = 基本上 / 差不多 / 几乎  👉 语气很口语\r\n👉 whenever you want（更自然）\r\n👉 whenever you like\r\n👉 whenever you’re ready',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 06:54:58',1,'2026-04-08 06:54:58'),(113,'Everyday Speaking','That\'s totally okay','👉 完全没问题 / 没关系 / 可以接受','1. 安慰别人 / 表示理解\r\n•	Sorry I’m late.\r\n👉 That’s totally okay.  不用担心，我理解\r\n\r\n2. 表示同意\r\n•	Can I change the time?\r\n👉 That’s totally okay.  可以的，没问题\r\n\r\n3. 降低对方压力（很地道）\r\n•	I didn’t finish it.\r\n👉 That’s totally okay.  没关系，不用紧张\r\n\r\n相似表达\r\n	•	That’s okay.（普通）\r\n	•	No problem.（更直接）\r\n	•	It’s all good.（更口语）\r\n	•	That’s perfectly fine.（稍正式）\r\n\r\n🧠 面试/工作场景用法\r\n👉 很加分的一句：\r\n•	That’s totally okay, we can adjust the plan.  没问题，我们可以调整方案\r\n•	That’s totally okay, I understand the situation.  没关系，我理解这个情况\r\n\r\n👉 That’s totally okay = 完全没问题（很友好很自然）',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 06:59:12',1,'2026-04-08 06:59:12'),(114,'Everyday Speaking','I had butterflies in my stomach the first time you talked to me','第一次你跟我说话的时候，我心里小鹿乱撞','have butterflies in your stomach\r\n表示：紧张  心跳加快  害羞  激动\r\n\r\n常常用于：喜欢一个人/ 面试前 / 上台前\r\n\r\n如果你想更像恋爱语境，可以说：\r\n•	I had butterflies in my stomach the first time you spoke to me.\r\n•	I got butterflies in my stomach the first time you talked to me.\r\n•	The first time you talked to me, I had butterflies in my stomach.\r\n\r\n其中：\r\n•	had butterflies = 当时处于那种紧张心动状态\r\n•	got butterflies = 突然开始紧张心动，更有“那一瞬间”的感觉\r\n\r\n更甜一点的说法\r\n	•	The first time you talked to me, I got butterflies instantly.\r\n	•	You gave me butterflies the first time you talked to me.',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 07:12:18',1,'2026-04-08 07:12:18'),(115,'Everyday Speaking','I hope you live happily ever after','我希望你今后永远幸福','happily ever after 很浪漫、很童话。\r\n常见于：\r\n	•	婚礼祝福\r\n	•	爱情故事\r\n	•	比较感性的表达',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 07:19:29',1,'2026-04-08 07:19:29'),(116,'Everyday Speaking','I binged the whole first season last night.','我昨晚一口气刷完了第一季。','binge 在这里是动词，常见于：\r\n•	binge-watch 狂看、刷剧\r\n•	binge 也可以直接表示“一口气看很多”\r\n所以这句里的 binged 就是：连续看很多集\r\n\r\n更常见说法\r\n•	I binge-watched the whole first season last night.\r\n•	I watched the whole first season in one night.\r\n•	binged / binge-watched 更口语、更地道 ,带一种“停不下来”的感觉\r\n\r\n例句\r\n•	I binged three episodes before bed. 我睡前一口气刷了三集。\r\n•	We binge-watched that show over the weekend. 我们周末狂刷了那部剧。',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 07:24:16',1,'2026-04-08 07:24:16'),(117,'Everyday Speaking','It’s kind of a coming-of-age story.','这有点像一个成长故事。','coming of age 表示：成年 / 心智成长 /	从少年走向成熟\r\n例句\r\n•	It’s a coming-of-age movie about friendship and loss. 这是一部关于友情和失去的成长电影。\r\n•	The novel is basically a coming-of-age story. 这本小说基本上就是个成长故事。\r\n\r\nkind of\r\n这里 kind of 表示：	有点 / 某种程度上算是',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 07:30:48',1,'2026-04-08 07:30:48'),(118,'Everyday Speaking','Do you have any recommendations','👉 你有什么推荐吗？\r\n🌟 回答方式\r\n•	Yeah, I’d recommend…\r\n•	You should check out…\r\n•	I’d suggest…','🗣 使用场景\r\n\r\n1. 问电影 / 书 / 剧\r\n•	Do you have any recommendations for movies? 有什么电影推荐吗？\r\n\r\n2. 问餐厅\r\n•	Do you have any restaurant recommendations? 有什么餐厅推荐吗？\r\n\r\n3. 问学习/工作\r\n•	Do you have any recommendations for improving my English? 有什么提高英语的建议吗？',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 07:41:23',1,'2026-04-08 07:41:23'),(119,'Everyday Speaking','What’s the premise?','这部作品的基本设定是什么？\r\n或者\r\n大概讲的是什么？','premise 在这里是什么意思\r\n\r\n这里的 premise 不是“前提条件”那个意思。\r\n在电影、电视剧、小说里，premise 常表示：\r\n•	故事设定\r\n•	核心概念\r\n•	基本剧情框架\r\n\r\n例子\r\n•	What’s the premise of the movie?  这部电影的设定是什么？\r\n•	The premise is that a group of strangers wake up in a mysterious town.  故事设定是，一群陌生人在一个神秘小镇醒来。\r\n\r\n和 plot 的区别\r\n•	premise = 故事的核心设定、出发点\r\n•	plot = 具体剧情发展\r\n\r\n比如：\r\n•	premise: 一个男孩发现自己会穿越时间\r\n•	plot: 他如何利用这个能力，发生了什么事',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 07:46:15',1,'2026-04-08 07:46:15'),(120,'Everyday Speaking','I\'m trying to be more money-savvy','👉 我正在努力变得更会理财 / 更精打细算','🧠 money-savvy 是什么感觉\r\n\r\nsavvy = 有经验的 / 精明的 / 懂行的\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n•	tech-savvy = 懂技术的\r\n•	business-savvy = 有商业头脑的\r\n•	money-savvy = 会理财的\r\n\r\n🌟 例句\r\n•	I’ve been trying to be more money-savvy lately.  我最近在努力变得更会理财。\r\n•	I’m trying to cut unnecessary expenses and be more money-savvy. 我在减少不必要的开支，让自己更精打细算。',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 07:52:03',1,'2026-04-08 07:52:03'),(121,'Everyday Speaking','Money burns a hole in my pocket.','钱一到手就想花掉。\r\n手里有钱就存不住。','例句\r\n•	Money burns a hole in my pocket. I always end up buying something.\r\n我手里有钱就想花掉，最后总会买点什么。\r\n•	As soon as he gets paid, money burns a hole in his pocket.\r\n他一发工资就想花钱。',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 08:00:19',1,'2026-04-08 08:00:19'),(122,'Everyday Speaking','How to be frugal ?','👉 如何变得节俭 / 如何省钱过日子\r\n👉 be frugal = 理性花钱 + 控制开支 + 有计划地生活','frugal（形容词）\r\n\r\n👉 节俭的、精打细算的（正面词 👍）\r\n•	She lives a frugal lifestyle.  她过着很节俭的生活。\r\n\r\n⚠️ 和这些词的区别：\r\n•	cheap ❌（小气、质量差，偏负面）\r\n•	frugal ✅（理性消费、会管理钱）\r\n\r\n1. 控制开支\r\n•	Track your spending. 记录你的花费\r\n•	Cut unnecessary expenses. 减少不必要的开支\r\n \r\n2. 花钱更理性\r\n•	Think before you buy. 买之前先想一想\r\n•	Avoid impulse buying. 避免冲动消费\r\n \r\n3. 日常省钱习惯\r\n•	Cook at home instead of eating out. 在家做饭\r\n•	Buy only what you need. 只买需要的东西\r\n4. 长期习惯\r\n•	Save a portion of your income.  存一部分收入\r\n•	Look for discounts and deals. 找折扣',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 08:04:14',1,'2026-04-08 08:04:14'),(123,'Everyday Speaking','How are they doing with school ?','👉 他们在学校怎么样？\r\n👉 他们学业进展如何？\r\nwith school = 在学校 / 学业方面','🔁 类似表达\r\n•	How are they doing at school?（更常见 👍）\r\n•	How are they doing in school?\r\n•	How is their school going?（更口语）\r\n🧠 语气区别\r\n•	with school 👉 更偏“整体状态”（压力、适应、表现）\r\n•	at school 👉 更中性，最常用\r\n•	in school 👉 稍正式一点\r\n\r\n\r\n🌟 例句\r\n•	How are your kids doing with school? 你孩子在学校怎么样？\r\n•	How is she doing with school lately? 她最近学业怎么样？',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 08:14:57',1,'2026-04-08 08:14:57'),(124,'Everyday Speaking','Did you go to school around here ?','你是在这附近上的学吗？\r\n• around here  这附近，这一带','语感\r\n这是一句很自然的口语，常用于聊天，想了解对方是不是本地长大的，或者以前是不是在这个区域读书。\r\n\r\n例句\r\n• Did you go to school around here, or did you move here later?\r\n你是在这附近上的学，还是后来才搬到这儿的？\r\n\r\n类似说法\r\n• Did you grow up around here?  你是在这附近长大的吗？\r\n• Did you study around here?  你以前是在这附近读书的吗？',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 08:19:11',1,'2026-04-08 08:19:11'),(125,'Everyday Speaking','I’m a lifelong learner.','我是一个终身学习的人。','例句\r\n• I’m a lifelong learner, so I enjoy picking up new skills.\r\n我是一个终身学习的人，所以我很喜欢学新技能。\r\n• In the IT industry, being a lifelong learner is very important.\r\n在 IT 行业，做一个终身学习者非常重要。\r\n\r\n面试里很好用\r\n\r\n你可以这样扩展：\r\n• I’m a lifelong learner, and I always try to improve my skills.\r\n• I see myself as a lifelong learner, especially in technology, because things change so quickly.\r\n\r\n一句总结\r\n\r\nI’m a lifelong learner\r\n= 我热爱持续学习，并愿意不断成长。',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 08:29:13',1,'2026-04-08 08:29:13'),(126,'Everyday Speaking','It\'s a great fit','这非常合适（人、职位、环境、产品都可以）','1. 面试（超级常用 ⭐）\r\n• I think this role is a great fit for me. 我觉得这个职位很适合我\r\n• My skills are a great fit for this position.  我的技能和这个岗位很匹配\r\n• I believe my experience and skills make me a great fit for this role.\r\n• Based on my background, I think this position is a great fit.\r\n\r\n2. 工作/合作\r\n• This solution is a great fit for our needs. 这个方案很符合我们的需求\r\n\r\n3. 生活\r\n• This apartment is a great fit for us. 这个房子很适合我们\r\n\r\n🔁 类似表达\r\n• It’s a good fit（普通）\r\n• It’s a perfect fit（更强 👍）\r\n• It suits me well（稍正式）\r\n• It matches well（中性）',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 08:32:53',1,'2026-04-08 08:32:53'),(127,'Everyday Speaking','Nice catching up with you','👉 很高兴和你聊聊天 / 叙叙旧','🧠 什么是 catch up\r\ncatch up (with someone) = 👉 很久没见后聊天、更新近况\r\n🗣 使用场景\r\n通常在：\r\n	•	聊天结束时\r\n	•	偶遇老朋友后分别时\r\n	•	电话/视频结束时\r\n🌟 例句\r\n• Nice catching up with you. Let’s do this again soon. 很高兴跟你聊聊，我们改天再约\r\n• It was really nice catching up with you. 跟你聊天真的很开心',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 08:41:47',1,'2026-04-08 08:41:47'),(128,'Everyday Speaking','Excuse me, are these men’s or women’s pants?','我想问一下这条裤子是女士的裤子 还是男士的裤子','🇳🇿 小提示（很实用）\r\n在新西兰/英国更常说：\r\n• trousers（比 pants 更常见）\r\n\r\n👉 所以你也可以说：\r\n• Are these men’s or women’s trousers?',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 17:29:52',1,'2026-04-08 17:29:52'),(129,'Everyday Speaking','Sorry, I forgot to ring these two up.','我忘记把这两个算进去/结账了','• I forgot to ring these two up. 我忘记把这两个算进去/结账了。\r\n• I forgot to scan these two items. 我忘记扫这两个了。\r\n• I forgot to charge for these two items. 我忘记收这两个的钱了。',0,0,1,'2026-04-08 18:00:06',1,'2026-04-08 18:00:06'),(130,'Everyday Speaking','It’s like a camping bed with a tent-style cover','像露营那种折叠床/帐篷床','It’s something like a tent. Once you unfold it, it becomes a bed.\r\n\r\n✅ 1. fold out（最常用⭐）\r\n\r\n👉 展开（从折叠状态 → 使用状态）\r\n\r\n特点：强调“展开后能用”\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• It folds out into a bed. ✅（最地道）\r\n• This sofa folds out.\r\n• The table folds out when you need it.\r\n\r\n👉 🟢 你这个“帐篷床”👉 首选这个词\r\n\r\n✅ 2. unfold\r\n\r\n👉 展开（动作本身，更书面一点）\r\n\r\n特点：强调动作，不强调结果\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• Just unfold it.\r\n• You can unfold the bed.\r\n\r\n👉 🟡 能用，但没有 fold out 自然\r\n\r\n✅ 3. open up\r\n\r\n👉 打开（很口语）\r\n\r\n特点：不一定是“折叠结构”\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• Open it up and you’ll see.\r\n• It opens up into a bed.\r\n\r\n👉 🟢 很口语，但不够精确\r\n\r\n✅ 4. set up\r\n\r\n👉 搭建 / 安装（像搭帐篷）\r\n\r\n特点：强调“搭起来”\r\n\r\n例子\r\n• You can set it up in seconds.\r\n• We set up the tent.\r\n\r\n👉 🟢 如果你强调“像帐篷”，可以用这个',0,0,1,'2026-04-09 08:42:26',1,'2026-04-09 08:42:26'),(131,'Everyday Speaking','I’m on the hunt for a new TV. Do you know if any sales are going on?','👉 我正在找一台新电视。你知道现在有没有在打折吗？','👉 固定搭配：\r\n• on the hunt for… = 正在寻找\r\n\r\n👉  I’m hunting for a new TV. Do you know if any sales are going on?\r\n👉 I’m looking for a new TV. Do you know if there are any sales on?',0,0,1,'2026-04-09 15:25:46',1,'2026-04-09 15:25:46'),(132,'Everyday Speaking','I have been drooling over this giant 65-inch flatscreen TV.','👉 我一直很想要这台65英寸的大平板电视（已经馋它很久了）。','🧠 重点解析\r\n• I have been drooling over…\r\n👉 字面是“流口水”，实际意思是：\r\n非常想要 / 垂涎已久\r\n• giant 65 inch flatscreen TV\r\n👉 超大的65寸平板电视\r\n\r\n🗣️ 类似表达（英文）\r\n• I’ve had my eye on this TV for a while.（更日常）\r\n• I’ve been wanting this TV for ages.',0,0,1,'2026-04-09 15:29:03',1,'2026-04-09 15:29:03'),(133,'Everyday Speaking','It was a deal I couldn’t pass up.','👉 中文意思是：\r\n\r\n这个优惠我实在没法拒绝 / 这个价格太划算了，不买不行。','🧠 重点解析\r\n	•	deal = 优惠 / 好价格\r\n	•	pass up = 放弃（一个机会）\r\n\r\n👉 couldn’t pass up = 不忍错过 / 必须抓住\r\n\r\n• It was too good to miss.\r\n• I couldn’t resist the deal.\r\n• It was a bargain.',0,0,1,'2026-04-09 18:44:41',1,'2026-04-09 18:44:41'),(134,'Everyday Speaking','I need to run a test to see whether it’s a viral or bacterial infection.','我要帮你做一个化验，看看是病毒感染还是细菌感染','🧠 小重点\r\n• viral infection 👉 病毒感染\r\n• bacterial infection 👉 细菌感染\r\n• run a test / do a test / conduct a test 👉 做检查\r\n\r\n👉\r\nWe’ll do a test to see if it’s viral or bacterial.',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 08:17:36',1,'2026-04-10 08:17:36'),(135,'Everyday Speaking','I’ll have to wait for it to go on sale.','我得等它打折再买。','🧠 重点拆解\r\n•I’ll have to… 👉 我不得不 / 我只能……\r\n• wait for… 👉 等待\r\n• go on sale 👉 开始打折 / 进入促销\r\n\r\n🗣️ 类似表达（英文）\r\n• I’ll wait until it’s on sale.（更常用⭐）\r\n• I’m waiting for a discount.\r\n• I’ll buy it when the price drops.',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 08:31:47',1,'2026-04-10 08:31:47'),(136,'Everyday Speaking','I don’t have to splurge on it.','我没必要在这上面花很多钱 / 不用大手大脚买。','🧠 重点解析\r\n•splurge (on something)\r\n👉 挥霍 / 花大钱 / 奢侈消费\r\n\r\n•I don’t have to splurge on a TV.\r\n👉 我没必要买那么贵的电视\r\n\r\n🔁 类似表达（英文）\r\n• I don’t need to spend that much.\r\n• I can save some money on this.\r\n• I don’t need anything fancy.',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 08:40:02',1,'2026-04-10 08:40:02'),(137,'Everyday Speaking','I worked really hard at it, and my co-worker got all the credit for it','👉 我为这件事付出了很多努力，但最后功劳全被我同事拿走了。\r\n\r\nget/take the credit = 拿走功劳','🗣️ 更地道的英文说法（你可以升级用）\r\n• I did all the work, but they got all the credit.\r\n• I put in a lot of effort, but my co-worker took the credit.\r\n• It feels unfair — I worked hard, but didn’t get any recognition.',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 13:15:48',1,'2026-04-10 13:15:48'),(138,'Everyday Speaking','I think the more work I do the less recognition I get','我觉得我做得越多，得到的认可反而越少。','• The harder I work, the less appreciated I feel. 👉 我越努力，越觉得不被重视\r\n• It feels like the more I do, the less I’m valued. 👉 感觉我做得越多，越不被重视',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 13:21:13',1,'2026-04-10 13:21:13'),(139,'Everyday Speaking','Don\'t bottle it up','别把情绪憋在心里 / 别压抑自己\r\nbottle up = 把情绪“装起来不说”','🧠 重点解析\r\n• bottle up  👉 像把东西装进瓶子一样\r\n→ 比喻：把情绪藏起来、不表达\r\n\r\n🗣️ 例句\r\n• You should talk to someone. Don’t bottle it up. 👉 你应该找人聊聊，别憋在心里\r\n• It’s not healthy to bottle up your feelings. 👉 压抑情绪对健康不好\r\n\r\n🔁 类似表达\r\n• Let it out. 👉 说出来\r\n• Talk it out. 👉 说开它\r\n• Open up. 👉 敞开心扉',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 13:24:27',1,'2026-04-10 13:24:27'),(140,'Everyday Speaking','Thank you for letting me get that off my chest','谢谢你让我把这些话说出来（心里轻松多了）。','🧠 重点解析\r\n• get something off my chest\r\n👉 把压在心里的话说出来\r\n👉 倾诉 / 发泄情绪\r\n\r\n🔁 类似表达（英文）\r\n• I really needed to get that off my chest.\r\n• Thanks for listening. I feel much better now.\r\n• It feels good to finally talk about it.',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 13:28:18',1,'2026-04-10 13:28:18'),(141,'Everyday Speaking','I had no idea work was so stressful','我完全没想到工作会这么有压力\r\n• I had no idea… 👉 我完全不知道 / 根本没想到','🗣️ 类似表达（升级版）\r\n• I didn’t realize work could be this stressful. 👉 我没意识到工作可以这么有压力\r\n• Work is way more stressful than I expected. 👉 工作比我想象的压力大多了\r\n• I wasn’t prepared for how stressful work is. 👉 我完全没准备好面对这么大的压力\r\n\r\n🇳🇿 日常口语说法\r\n• Work is actually pretty stressful, eh.\r\n👉 工作其实挺有压力的（Kiwi语气）',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 13:34:57',1,'2026-04-10 13:34:57'),(142,'Everyday Speaking','I\'m just finishing up some renovations on the house','我正在把房子的装修收个尾。','🧠 重点解析\r\n• I’m just finishing up…  👉 我马上就完成 / 正在收尾\r\n• renovations  👉 翻新 / 装修（房子）\r\n\r\n🗣️ 类似表达（英文）\r\n• We’re wrapping up the renovations. 👉 我们在收尾装修\r\n• The renovation is almost done. 👉 装修差不多完成了\r\n• We’re putting the finishing touches on the house. ⭐ 👉 我们在做最后的润色（很地道）\r\n\r\n👉  finish up = 收尾 / 快完成',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 13:54:36',1,'2026-04-10 13:54:36'),(143,'Everyday Speaking','It\'s been worth it','这一切都是值得的。','🧠 重点解析\r\n• It’s been…  👉 到现在为止一直是……\r\n• worth it. 👉 值得（付出的时间/金钱/努力）\r\n\r\n🗣️ 常见搭配\r\n• It’s been worth it in the end.  👉 最后证明是值得的\r\n• All the hard work has been worth it. 👉 所有努力都值得了\r\n• It wasn’t easy, but it’s been worth it. ⭐ 👉 虽然不容易，但很值得\r\n\r\n🎯 一句话记住\r\nworth it = 值回票价 / 值得付出',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 14:06:26',1,'2026-04-10 14:06:26'),(144,'Everyday Speaking','I\'m trying to get in better shape','我正在努力让自己的身体状态变得更好。','🧠 重点解析\r\n• get in shape  👉 让身体变好 / 变得更健康 / 更有型\r\n• better shape. 👉 更好的状态（比现在更好）\r\n\r\n🏋️ 常见搭配\r\n• go to the gym 👉 去健身房\r\n• work out 👉 锻炼\r\n• stay in shape 👉 保持身材\r\n\r\nget in shape = 让身体变好（健身）',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 14:25:21',1,'2026-04-10 14:25:21'),(145,'Everyday Speaking','Are you someone  who is naturally motivated to exercise?','你是那种天生就有动力去运动的人吗？\r\n• naturally motivated 👉 天生有动力的 / 自发的','• Are you someone who enjoys working out? 👉 你是喜欢锻炼的人吗？\r\n• Do you need motivation to exercise? 👉 你需要动力才会去运动吗？\r\n• Do you have to push yourself to work out? 👉 你需要逼自己去运动吗？',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 14:38:49',1,'2026-04-10 14:38:49'),(146,'Everyday Speaking','When I read English sentences, my voice sounds flat and lacks intonation.','👉 我读英文句子的时候语调很平，没有语音起伏','🧠 关键词（很重要）\r\n• flat 👉 平的（没有变化）\r\n• intonation 👉 语调\r\n• expression 👉 情感表达\r\n• monotone 👉 单调的声音',0,0,1,'2026-04-10 15:49:49',1,'2026-04-10 15:49:49'),(147,'Everyday Speaking','Everything here is in the same condition as when it was donated','这里所有的东西 都和捐赠时候的状态是一样的','🧠 关键词\r\n• condition 👉 状态（非常关键）\r\n• donated 👉 被捐赠',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 15:36:05',1,'2026-04-11 15:36:05'),(148,'Everyday Speaking','The forecast said it would be rainy today, but it’s actually sunny. It’s unbelievable!','天气预报说今天会下雨，但实际上是晴天，真让人难以置信。','🗣️ 更口语一点\r\n• They said it was going to rain today, but it’s sunny! So weird.\r\n• The forecast was totally wrong. It’s sunny!',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 16:28:16',1,'2026-04-11 16:28:16'),(149,'Everyday Speaking','The weather forecast isn’t reliable.','天气预报不可靠','🧠 关键词\r\n• reliable 👉 可靠的\r\n• unreliable 👉 不可靠的\r\n• rely on 👉 依赖 / 信任\r\n• unpredictable 👉 难预测\r\n\r\nThe forecast can be inaccurate sometimes.\r\n👉 天气预报有时候不太准确\r\n\r\nThe weather here is so unpredictable.\r\n👉 这里的天气太难预测了（新西兰特别常说）',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 16:33:46',1,'2026-04-11 16:33:46'),(150,'Everyday Speaking','Did you get up to anything over Easter?','👉 复活节有没有去干点啥？（很 Kiwi🔥）','类似的\r\n\r\nDid you go out anywhere over Easter?\r\n👉\r\nDid you go anywhere over Easter?',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 16:58:04',1,'2026-04-11 16:58:04'),(151,'Everyday Speaking','Did you have to lift anything heavy?','👉 你需要搬重东西吗？','🧠 为什么这样更好？\r\n• have to 👉 更常用于“需要/不得不”\r\n• anything 👉 疑问句更自然（比 some 更常用）',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 17:04:55',1,'2026-04-11 17:04:55'),(152,'Everyday Speaking','Can you operate a forklift?','你能开叉车吗','',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 17:48:55',1,'2026-04-11 17:48:55'),(153,'Everyday Speaking','We have so many hangers, but sometimes there are none.','我们现在有很多衣服挂，但是有时候一个都没有','👉\r\nsometimes there are none = 有时候一个都没有\r\n\r\n🗣️ 更口语一点\r\n\r\nWe’ve got heaps of hangers, but sometimes we run out. ⭐（Kiwi说法🔥）\r\n👉\r\n• heaps of = 很多（新西兰常用）\r\n• run out = 用完了',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 17:51:28',1,'2026-04-11 17:51:28'),(154,'Everyday Speaking','Yeah, cash is all good.','可以，用现金没问题。','✅ 类似表达（你可以换着用）\r\n• Cash is fine.\r\n• Cash is okay.\r\n• Yep, cash is fine.\r\n• Yeah, that’s all good.\r\n\r\n👉 all good 超常见：\r\n• All good 👍（没问题）\r\n• Yeah, all good.',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 17:55:28',1,'2026-04-11 17:55:28'),(155,'Everyday Speaking','What is this made from ?','这个是用什么做的？','🔁 和 made of 的区别（重点⭐）\r\n\r\n✅ made of（能看出材料）\r\n• What is this made of? 👉 这个是用什么做的（能看出来）\r\n\r\n👉 例：\r\n• made of wood（木头）\r\n• made of glass（玻璃）\r\n\r\n✅ made from（看不出来原材料）\r\n• What is this made from?  👉 原材料已经改变了（看不出来）\r\n\r\n👉 例：\r\n• paper is made from wood\r\n• wine is made from grapes\r\n\r\n🗣️ 更口语一点\r\n• What’s this made of? ⭐（更常用）\r\n• What material is this?',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 18:01:46',1,'2026-04-11 18:01:46'),(156,'Everyday Speaking','I\'m not going to take it','我不打算买这个了','🗣️ 更口语一点\r\n\r\nActually, I’ll pass on this — I’ll just take the shirt. ⭐\r\n👉 我不要这个了，就拿这件衬衫\r\n\r\nI’ll just take the shirt, thanks.\r\n👉 我就要这件衬衫，谢谢\r\n\r\n🧠 关键词\r\n• pass on 👉 放弃 / 不要（很地道）\r\n• I’ll just… 👉 我就……（很自然）',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 18:17:25',1,'2026-04-11 18:17:25'),(157,'Everyday Speaking','I\'ll leave it','这个我不要了。','• I’ll leave it, thanks.  这个我不要了，谢谢。\r\n• Actually, I’ll leave it and just take the shirt. 其实这个我不要了，我就拿这件衬衫。\r\n\r\n类似说法\r\n• I’ll pass on it.\r\n• I won’t take it.\r\n• I’ll just leave it.',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 18:20:24',1,'2026-04-11 18:20:24'),(158,'Everyday Speaking','Can I leave this here for now and come back for it later?','我可以先把这个放在这里，然后一会过来结账吗？','',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 18:37:59',1,'2026-04-11 18:37:59'),(159,'Everyday Speaking','Take your time, no rush','慢慢来，不着急。','也可以说\r\n• Take your time. There’s no rush.\r\n• No rush, take your time.\r\n\r\n更地道一点\r\n\r\nNo rush at all, take your time.\r\n完全不着急，慢慢来。',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 18:40:44',1,'2026-04-11 18:40:44'),(160,'Everyday Speaking','You need a hand getting it up?','你需要帮忙把它搬上去吗？','• need a hand = 需要帮忙\r\n• getting it up = 把它弄上去 / 搬上去 / 抬上去\r\n例句\r\n• Do you need a hand getting it up the stairs? 你要不要帮忙把它搬上楼？\r\n\r\n更安全、更清楚的说法\r\n\r\n如果你自己想说得更明确，可以说：\r\n• Do you need a hand lifting it up?\r\n• Do you need help getting it upstairs?\r\n• Do you need help carrying it up?',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 18:49:09',1,'2026-04-11 18:49:09'),(161,'Everyday Speaking','I thought about it, and I decided to take it. You can actually see it when I’m wearing it, and I can’t notice it myself. But if it’s a little off, that’s okay','我想了一下，我穿着的时候你能看得见，但是我自己注意不到，如果你能给我一点小的折扣就太好了','a little bit off  👉 便宜一点 / 打一点折\r\na little bit off = a little discount\r\n\r\n很常见的顾客说法\r\n• Could you do a little bit off?  能不能便宜一点？\r\n• Is there any discount on this?  这个有折扣吗？\r\n• Could you take a little off the price? 这个价格能不能稍微降一点？',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 19:03:29',1,'2026-04-11 19:03:29'),(162,'Everyday Speaking','It’s so pretty and puffy','这件衣服蓬蓬的、很好看\r\n\r\npuffy 常表示：\r\n• 蓬松的\r\n• 鼓鼓的\r\n• 很有绒感的','如果你想说“这件衣服蓬蓬的、很好看”，还可以说：\r\n• It’s really pretty and nice and puffy.\r\n• It looks so pretty and puffy.',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 19:06:47',1,'2026-04-11 19:06:47'),(163,'Everyday Speaking','That’s just a little rough patch. It’s not really going to tear or anything. And I won’t notice it when I’m wearing it, because it’s on the back.','那只是有一点点粗糙/磨损，不至于裂开什么的. \r\n之前你没指出来的时候，我穿着的时候根本没发现, 因为它在我的背部','',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 19:15:02',1,'2026-04-11 19:15:02'),(164,'Everyday Speaking','Before you pointed it out, I hadn’t noticed it','你指出来前我根本就没注意到','• I didn’t notice it before you pointed it out.\r\n• I hadn’t even noticed it before you pointed it out.',0,0,1,'2026-04-11 19:17:14',1,'2026-04-11 19:17:14'),(165,'Everyday Speaking','All good to go','一切都准备好了，可以开始了。\r\n或者\r\n都弄好了，没问题了。\r\n这是很口语、很自然的表达，常用于表示：\r\n• 事情已经处理完\r\n• 系统已经配置好\r\n• 准备工作完成\r\n• 可以继续下一步了','• The page is working now. All good to go.  页面现在能用了，一切就绪。\r\n• I finished the setup. We’re good to go. 我已经配置好了，可以开始了。\r\n\r\n更完整一点可以说：\r\n• We’re good to go.\r\n• Everything is good to go.\r\n• It’s all good to go.',0,0,1,'2026-04-12 13:10:52',1,'2026-04-12 13:10:52'),(166,'Everyday Speaking','If there’s something wrong with the item, can we lower the price?','如果商品有问题，我们可以把价格降低吗？','✅ 也可以更口语一点：\r\n\r\n👉 If the item has a flaw, can we get a discount?\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n• has a flaw = 有瑕疵、有小问题\r\n• get a discount = 能便宜一点吗\r\n\r\n📌 如果你是在店里跟店员说，比较自然的说法有：\r\n\r\n👉 Since there’s a flaw, could the price be a little lower?\r\n因为有点瑕疵，价格能不能低一点？\r\n\r\n👉 This item has a small defect. Is there any discount on it?\r\n这个东西有点小瑕疵，可以打折吗？',0,0,1,'2026-04-12 13:14:03',1,'2026-04-12 13:14:03'),(167,'Everyday Speaking','But how do you decide whether to lower it by $10 or $15?','那你们怎么判断到底是便宜 10 块，还是 15 块呢？','✅ 也可以说得更口语一点：\r\n\r\n👉 But how do you decide how much to take off the price — like $10 or $15?\r\n\r\n这里：\r\n• take off the price = 从价格里减掉\r\n• how much to take off = 减多少\r\n\r\n👉 How do you work out how much of a discount to give?\r\n你们怎么决定给多少折扣？\r\n\r\n👉 What do you base the discount on?\r\n你们是根据什么来决定折扣的？',0,0,1,'2026-04-12 13:16:44',1,'2026-04-12 13:16:44'),(168,'Everyday Speaking','Can you try these two clocks for me?\r\nCan you check these two clocks for me?','你能帮我试试这两个钟吗？后者表达更好一些','',0,0,1,'2026-04-12 14:05:42',1,'2026-04-12 14:05:42'),(169,'Everyday Speaking','Can I have some paper for that?','你能给那个拿点纸包一下吗？','还可以说\r\n• Could I get some paper for that?\r\n• Could you wrap that in paper for me?\r\n• Could you wrap that in paper for me?',0,0,1,'2026-04-12 14:16:48',1,'2026-04-12 14:16:48'),(170,'Everyday Speaking','Would you want to do all of them?','你想把这些都做了吗？\r\n\r\n我遇到的真实场景是顾客想用报纸把杯子包上，我就问她你要把这些杯子都包上吗','更明确的说法是：\r\n👉 Could you wrap all of them?',0,0,1,'2026-04-12 14:38:14',1,'2026-04-12 14:38:14'),(171,'Everyday Speaking','Do you take donations here?','你们这里收捐赠吗？','📌 也可以说：\r\n\r\n👉 Do you accept donations here?\r\n\r\n两个区别\r\n\r\ntake donations\r\n• 更口语\r\n• 日常对话很常见\r\n\r\naccept donations\r\n• 更正式一点\r\n• 店员、公告、机构介绍里也很常见',0,0,1,'2026-04-12 14:43:51',1,'2026-04-12 14:43:51'),(172,'Everyday Speaking','Do you think it’s too expensive at $100?','你觉得它卖 100 元会不会太贵？','也可以说\r\n👉 Do you think $100 is too much for it?',0,0,1,'2026-04-12 14:48:29',1,'2026-04-12 14:48:29'),(173,'Everyday Speaking','This item has been sitting here for days.','这个商品已经在这里放了好多天了。','也可以说\r\n👉 This item has been here for days.\r\n更直接一点：\r\n这个东西已经在这儿放了好多天了\r\n\r\n📌 如果你想表达“卖了很久都没卖出去”的感觉\r\n\r\n👉 This item has been sitting here for quite a few days.\r\n👉 This has been here for a long time.\r\n\r\n其中：\r\n• has been sitting here = 一直放在这里\r\n• 很有“摆了很久没动”的感觉\r\n\r\n💬 商店里很自然的说法\r\n• This item has been sitting here for days.\r\n• It’s been here for quite a while.\r\n• This has been here for a long time already.',0,0,1,'2026-04-12 14:51:50',1,'2026-04-12 14:51:50'),(174,'Everyday Speaking','This electric guitar is missing a lot of things, like picks and strings, and it definitely needs some work before you can play it.','这把电吉他缺了很多东西，比如拨片和琴弦，而且肯定还得修整一下才能弹\r\n\r\n我们说店里卖的电吉他，缺少一些琴弦、','• needs work = 还得修、还得调整\r\n• parts and accessories = 部件和配件\r\n• needs setting up = 需要调试/校准一下\r\n• pick / picks = 拨片\r\n• strings = 琴弦\r\n• playable = 可以正常弹奏的',0,0,1,'2026-04-12 15:04:01',1,'2026-04-12 15:04:01'),(175,'Everyday Speaking','I’ll wrap that up in one of the towels.','我会拿一条毛巾把它裹起来','如果店员是想说“我拿条毛巾给你包起来”，最自然就是：\r\n\r\n👉 I’ll wrap it up in a towel.',0,0,1,'2026-04-13 06:10:11',1,'2026-04-13 06:10:11'),(176,'Everyday Speaking','I think it’s mostly clothing, not things like kitchen items.','👉 我觉得主要是衣服，不包括比如厨房用品。\r\n背景是自愿者可以在店里买衣服享受半价的优惠，但是只能是衣服，鞋什么的','✅ 也可以说：\r\n\r\n👉 I think it’s mainly clothing, not, for example, kitchen items.',0,0,1,'2026-04-13 06:14:35',1,'2026-04-13 06:14:35'),(177,'Everyday Speaking','Is it really that good?','它有那么好吗？','如果你想说：“它有这么好吗？”\r\n👉 Is it that good?\r\n\r\n 如果你想说： “它真的这么好吗？”\r\n👉 Is it really that good?',0,0,1,'2026-04-13 06:20:30',1,'2026-04-13 06:20:30'),(178,'Everyday Speaking','Things have been out for ages','这些东西已经在外面放了很久了','for ages\r\n\r\n很口语，意思是：\r\n\r\n👉 很久很久\r\n👉 老长时间了\r\n• I haven’t seen her for ages.  我好久没见她了。\r\n\r\nbe out\r\n\r\n这个短语在不同场景有不同意思：\r\n• 在外面放着 /  摆在外面 /  拿出来了 /  上架了 /  售罄了\r\n\r\n💬 例子\r\n• These things have been out for ages.  这些东西已经摆在外面很久了。\r\n• That stuff has been out for ages.  那些东西已经放在那儿好久了。\r\n• It’s been out for ages. 它已经放在那里很久了。',0,0,1,'2026-04-13 06:34:21',1,'2026-04-13 06:34:21'),(179,'Everyday Speaking','How many things are up here?','上面这里有多少东西？','💬 例子\r\n• How many things are up here?  上面这里有多少东西？\r\n• How many items are up here? 上面这里有多少件商品？\r\n• How many are up here? 上面这里有多少个？',0,0,1,'2026-04-13 06:45:09',1,'2026-04-13 06:45:09'),(180,'Everyday Speaking','So I put it back properly','所以我把它放回正确的位置','例句\r\n👉 So I put it back properly, so we can notice if anything is missing.',0,0,1,'2026-04-13 07:42:47',1,'2026-04-13 07:42:47'),(181,'Everyday Speaking','I noticed that some organisations have already signed up, but there are no job listings at the moment.','我看我们有一些机构入驻，但是目前没有岗位发布','📌 几个关键词\r\n\r\n机构入驻\r\n可以根据语境翻成：\r\n• have joined\r\n• have signed up\r\n• have come on board\r\n\r\n其中：\r\n👉 have signed up = 已经注册加入\r\n👉 have come on board = 已经加入进来了，更口语一点\r\n\r\n岗位发布，可以说：\r\n• job postings\r\n• job listings\r\n• positions posted\r\n\r\n最常见的是：\r\n\r\n👉 job postings\r\n👉 job listings\r\n\r\n还可以这样说：\r\n1. 更口语\r\n👉 I can see that a few organisations are on there already, but there aren’t any jobs posted yet.\r\n\r\n2. 更正式一点\r\n👉 I can see that some organisations have registered, but no positions have been posted so far.\r\n\r\n🎯 最推荐你记这句\r\n\r\n👉 I can see that some organisations have joined, but there aren’t any job postings at the moment.',0,0,1,'2026-04-15 08:21:00',1,'2026-04-15 08:21:00'),(182,'Everyday Speaking','Do employers usually screen resumes using a system, or do they do it manually? If they use a system, is my PDF resume more likely to be filtered out if it can’t be parsed properly?','雇主筛选简历是通过系统 还是人工？如果通过系统我的pdf格式的是不是容易因为识别不了被淘汰掉','• filtered out = 被筛掉\r\n• parsed properly = 被正确解析\r\n👉 Do employers usually screen resumes using a system, or do they do it manually? If they use a system, is my PDF resume more likely to be filtered out if it can’t be parsed properly?',0,0,1,'2026-04-15 08:24:56',1,'2026-04-15 08:24:56'),(183,'Everyday Speaking','Will they require live coding or algorithm questions during the interview?','他们会要求现场写代码算法之类的吗？\r\n也可以这么说：Will they ask me to write code or solve algorithms on the spot?','📌 两个表达的区别\r\nwrite code or solve algorithms on the spot\r\n\r\n👉 更口语\r\n👉 重点是“现场写代码、现场做算法题”\r\n\r\nlive coding\r\n\r\n👉 很常见的面试术语\r\n👉 指“现场编码”\r\n\r\n👉 Do they usually ask candidates to do live coding or algorithm questions in the interview?\r\n他们通常会在面试中要求候选人做现场编码或算法题吗？\r\n\r\n👉 Will there be any live coding or technical tests?\r\n会有现场编码或者技术测试吗？',0,0,1,'2026-04-15 08:28:10',1,'2026-04-15 08:28:10'),(184,'Everyday Speaking','Which one tends to be weighted more heavily?','哪一个比重更大呢？','carry more weight / be weighted more heavily\r\n\r\n👉 比重更大 / 更被看重\r\n\r\n🎯 最推荐你记这句\r\n\r\n👉 Do they focus more on technical questions, or on things like teamwork and collaboration? Which one tends to be weighted more heavily?',0,0,1,'2026-04-15 08:36:21',1,'2026-04-15 08:36:21'),(185,'Everyday Speaking','I go even a step further','👉 我甚至更进一步\r\n👉 我还会再多做一步\r\n👉 我会做得比这更多\r\n\r\n💬 常见结构\r\n• go a step further\r\n• go even a step further\r\n• take it a step further','✅ 基本意思\r\n\r\n这个表达用来强调：\r\n\r\n👉 你不只是做到基本要求\r\n👉 你还会主动做更多\r\n👉 你比一般预期走得更远一步\r\n\r\n💬 例子\r\n\r\n1. 工作态度\r\n\r\n👉 I don’t just fix the problem — I go even a step further and try to prevent it from happening again.\r\n我不只是解决问题——我还会更进一步，尽量防止它再次发生。\r\n\r\n2. 服务意识\r\n\r\n👉 I always try to help customers, and sometimes I go even a step further to make sure they feel supported.\r\n我总是尽量帮助客户，有时候我还会更进一步，确保他们感受到支持。\r\n\r\n3. 学习场景\r\n\r\n👉 I don’t only memorize new words. I go even a step further and try to use them in real conversations.\r\n我不只是记新单词，我还会更进一步，尝试在真实对话中使用它们。',0,0,1,'2026-04-17 10:44:05',1,'2026-04-17 10:44:05'),(186,'Everyday Speaking','Sorry, do you have anything smaller? I’m a bit short on change.','不好意思，你有小一点的吗？我这边零钱有点不够','Do you have any small change?\r\n你有零钱吗？\r\n\r\n如果你在收银/二手店场景，想问顾客有没有小面额现金，可以说：\r\n\r\nDo you have any smaller notes or coins?\r\n你有小一点的纸币或硬币吗？\r\n\r\n或者更自然、礼貌：\r\n\r\nDo you happen to have any smaller notes?\r\n你刚好有小一点的纸币吗？\r\n\r\n如果是因为找不开钱，可以说：\r\n\r\nSorry, do you have anything smaller? I’m a bit short on change.\r\n不好意思，你有小一点的吗？我这边零钱有点不够。\r\n\r\n注意：\r\nsome 通常用于肯定句；疑问句里更常用 any。',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 07:02:46',1,'2026-05-03 07:02:46'),(187,'Everyday Speaking','Are you ready to check out','你准备好结账了吗？','在商店 / 二手店 / 收银场景里可以用。\r\n\r\n更自然、更礼貌的说法：\r\n\r\nAre you ready to check out?\r\n您准备结账了吗？\r\n\r\nWould you like to check out now?\r\n您现在要结账吗？\r\n\r\nAre you all ready to check out?\r\n都选好准备结账了吗？\r\n\r\n如果你是店员，最推荐：\r\n\r\nAre you all ready to check out?\r\n\r\n听起来更亲切自然。\r\n这里 check out = 结账。',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 07:21:58',1,'2026-05-03 07:21:58'),(188,'Everyday Speaking','I’m not sure, sorry. I’ll go ask someone. Won’t be a moment.','如果你要离开去问同事可以这么说：\r\n我不太确定，不好意思。我去问一下，很快回来。','在店里最自然、口语化可以这样说：\r\n\r\nI’m not too sure, sorry. Let me check with someone. Just a sec.\r\n不太确定，不好意思。我去问一下别人，稍等一下。\r\n\r\n更 Kiwi / 日常一点：\r\n\r\nI’m not sure, sorry. I’ll just check for you.  我不太确定，不好意思。我帮你查一下。\r\n\r\n最推荐你在二手店用这一句：\r\n\r\nI’m not too sure, sorry. I’ll just check with someone for you.\r\n\r\n也可以加一句：\r\n\r\nJust give me a second. 稍等我一下。',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 07:54:50',1,'2026-05-03 07:54:50'),(189,'Everyday Speaking','I just wanted to check what price this would be','我只是想确认一下这个多少钱。','',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 08:00:03',1,'2026-05-03 08:00:03'),(190,'Everyday Speaking','Sorry, the price tag has come off this one. I’ll just check the price for you.','不好意思，这件的价格标签掉了。我帮你确认一下价格。','如果你说价格标签“掉了”，最自然是：\r\n\r\nThe price tag has come off.\r\n价格标签掉了。\r\n\r\n更口语一点：\r\n\r\nSorry, this one’s missing its price tag. I’ll just check for you.\r\n不好意思，这件没有价格标签了。我帮你查一下。\r\n\r\n最推荐你记这句：\r\n\r\nSorry, this one’s missing its price tag. I’ll just check with someone for you.',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 08:08:55',1,'2026-05-03 08:08:55'),(191,'Everyday Speaking','He’s asking if he can get this for 70 dollars.','他想问他能否以70元的价格买这个','价格前面更自然用 for 而不是at ，at 一般是以多少折扣，比如 at half price',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 08:10:15',1,'2026-05-03 08:10:15'),(192,'Everyday Speaking','Do I need to calculate the half price manually and enter it, or should I ring it up at full price and then apply a 50% discount?','我需要自己手动算半价然后输入，还是先按原价录入，再打 50% 折扣？','如果你是在店里收银，英文可以这样问同事：\r\n\r\nWhen I’m checking someone out, should I enter the half-price amount directly, or is there a discount option I should apply at the end?\r\n\r\n中文意思：\r\n\r\n我结账的时候，是应该直接输入半价后的金额，还是最后有一个折扣选项可以用？',0,0,1,'2026-05-03 08:13:08',1,'2026-05-03 08:13:08'),(193,'Everyday Speaking','Hi, I’d like to buy six tins of milk powder. Do you have an unopened box of six?','你好，我想买 6 罐奶粉。你们有未开封的一整箱 6 罐吗？\r\n\r\ntin = 罐\r\nsix tins = 6 罐\r\na full box = 一整箱\r\nan unopened box/carton = 未开封的整箱\r\nsealed box = 密封原箱','I’m after six tins of milk powder. Do you have a sealed box of six?\r\n我想买 6 罐奶粉。你们有一整箱密封的 6 罐装吗？\r\n\r\n如果你想强调“不要散罐，要原箱”：\r\n\r\nDo you have an unopened carton of six?\r\n你们有未开封的一箱 6 罐吗？\r\n\r\nCould I get a full unopened box instead of individual tins?\r\n我可以要一整箱未开封的，不要单独散罐吗？',0,0,1,'2026-05-07 06:43:02',1,'2026-05-07 06:43:02'),(194,'Everyday Speaking','What’s the expiry date?','有效期到什么时候？','What’s the expiry date on this milk powder?\r\n这个奶粉的有效期到什么时候？\r\n\r\n如果你想问“这一箱里面的有效期都一样吗？”可以说：\r\n\r\nDo all the tins in the box have the same expiry date?\r\n这一箱里的每一罐有效期都一样吗？\r\n\r\n如果你想问“有没有日期更新一点的？”可以说：\r\n\r\nDo you have any with a later expiry date?\r\n你们有没有有效期更晚一点的？\r\n\r\n店里最自然的一整句：\r\n\r\nHi, I’d like to buy six tins of milk powder. Do you have an unopened box of six? Also, what’s the expiry date?\r\n你好，我想买 6 罐奶粉。你们有未开封的一整箱 6 罐吗？另外，有效期是什么时候？',0,0,1,'2026-05-07 06:50:57',1,'2026-05-07 06:50:57'),(195,'Everyday Speaking','It looked a bit dodgy because there were a few price tags stuck on it.','看起来有点可疑，因为上面贴了好几个价格标签。','dodgy 是新西兰、澳洲、英国口语里很常见的词。\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n可疑的\r\n不太对劲的\r\n不靠谱的\r\n有点问题的\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nThat price tag looks a bit dodgy.\r\n那个价格标签看起来有点可疑。\r\n\r\nThis website looks dodgy.\r\n这个网站看起来不太靠谱。\r\n\r\nThe deal sounds a bit dodgy.\r\n这个交易听起来有点可疑。\r\n\r\n6. stuck on it\r\n\r\n这是重点。\r\n\r\nstuck 是 stick 的过去分词。\r\n\r\nstick something on something\r\n把某物贴在某物上\r\n\r\nstuck on it\r\n贴在它上面\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nThere were a few price tags stuck on it.\r\n有几个价格标签贴在它上面。\r\n\r\n这里的 stuck on it 是在修饰 price tags：\r\n\r\nprice tags stuck on it\r\n贴在它上面的价格标签\r\n\r\n例句：\r\n\r\nThere was a sticker stuck on the bottom.\r\n底部贴着一个贴纸。\r\n\r\nThere were labels stuck all over the box.\r\n盒子上到处贴着标签。\r\n\r\nSomeone had stuck another tag on it.\r\n有人又在上面贴了一个标签。',0,0,1,'2026-05-10 07:00:25',1,'2026-05-10 07:00:25'),(196,'Everyday Speaking','I found it over there on the reduced rack.','我是在那边打折货架上找到它的','on the reduced rack\r\n\r\n这是重点。\r\n\r\nreduced = 降价的 / 打折的\r\nrack = 衣架 / 货架 / 挂衣架\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nthe reduced rack 打折货架 / 降价区的衣架\r\n\r\non the reduced rack 在打折货架上\r\n\r\n在新西兰店里也经常听到：\r\n\r\nreduced to clear  降价清仓\r\n\r\nclearance rack 清仓货架\r\n\r\nsale rack 打折货架',0,0,1,'2026-05-10 07:05:24',1,'2026-05-10 07:05:24'),(197,'Everyday Speaking','I will check with my manager. Just a second.\r\nI’m not too sure, but I’ll check with my manager. Just a moment.','我和我的经理确认一下,马上就好\r\n我不太确定，我帮你问一下经理。稍等一下。','',0,0,1,'2026-05-10 07:09:15',1,'2026-05-10 07:09:15'),(198,'Everyday Speaking','Sorry, we’re short on change today. If you’re paying cash, we’ll need the exact amount.','不好意思，我们今天零钱不够。如果你付现金，需要刚好的金额。','',0,0,1,'2026-05-10 08:20:39',1,'2026-05-10 08:20:39'),(199,'Everyday Speaking','This page shows what the homepage looks like when users are not logged in.','这个页面展示了用户未登录时首页的样子。','',0,0,1,'2026-05-12 18:24:56',1,'2026-05-12 18:24:56'),(200,'Everyday Speaking','As you can see here, the Real World Common conservation group is set as the default group. So once the user logs in successfully, the data they can view and the records they create in the system will all be associated with this default group.','如你在这里看到的，Real World Common conservation group 是默认组。所以用户登录后，他们能查看的数据以及创建的记录都会和这个默认组相关联。','更口语、适合 presentation 的版本：\r\n\r\nAs you can see here, the Real World Common conservation group is the default group. So after the user logs in, both the data they can view and the records they create will be linked to this default group.',0,0,1,'2026-05-12 18:35:27',1,'2026-05-12 18:35:27'),(201,'Everyday Speaking','In this dropdown menu, we can add a search box. Then, as the user types, the list will be filtered to show only matching items. Apart from that, we can add pagination as well. This would make the list cleaner and easier to navigate, especially when there are a lot of items.','在这个下拉菜单里，我们可以加一个搜索框。然后用户输入内容时，列表会自动过滤，只显示匹配的选项。除此之外，我们也可以添加分页功能。这样当数据很多时，列表会更清晰，也更容易浏览。','',0,0,1,'2026-05-12 18:44:18',1,'2026-05-12 18:44:18'),(202,'Everyday Speaking','Because without a default group, every time the user logs in, the system will ask them to choose a group first before showing any data. This would add an extra step and make the user experience less convenient.','因为如果不设置一个默认组，每次用户成功登陆后系统会在选择展示数据前都会提示用户选择一个组，着非常影响用户体验','',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 08:03:30',1,'2026-05-13 08:03:30'),(203,'Everyday Speaking','Different user roles have different display styles.','不同的角色有不同的展示风格','如果你想说“不同角色看到的页面样式/内容不一样”，可以说：\r\n\r\nThe interface is displayed differently depending on the user’s role.\r\n\r\n或者：\r\n\r\nThe page layout changes depending on the user’s role.\r\n\r\n完整一点：\r\n\r\nDifferent user roles have different display styles, so the interface can be adapted based on the user’s permissions and responsibilities.',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 08:47:12',1,'2026-05-13 08:47:12'),(204,'Everyday Speaking','This part is a bit repetitive.','这个内容有一点重复了','更自然一点：\r\n\r\nThis content feels a bit repetitive.\r\n\r\n如果你是在 presentation 里给建议，可以说：\r\n\r\nI think this section is a bit repetitive, so we could make it more concise.\r\n\r\n中文意思：\r\n我觉得这一部分有点重复，所以我们可以让它更简洁一些。\r\n\r\n也可以更委婉一点：\r\n\r\nThere is a little overlap in this section, so we might be able to simplify it.\r\n\r\n这个表达更适合小组讨论。',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 08:50:07',1,'2026-05-13 08:50:07'),(205,'Everyday Speaking','These are two different role concepts. Only the Super Admin has a system-level role, while other users only have roles within their groups. So on this page, we shouldn’t show ordinary users’ system roles or allow them to be changed. Their group roles should only be updated by the coordinator of the specific group.','这是两个不同概念的角色。目前只有系统管理员拥有系统级别的角色，其他用户只拥有组内角色。所以这里不应该展示普通用户的系统角色，也不应该允许在这个页面修改。组内角色应该只能由对应组的协调者来统一管理。','',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 15:23:25',1,'2026-05-13 15:23:25'),(206,'Everyday Speaking','So you need to clear the in-progress tickets first','如果是在 Jira / sprint 语境里，更自然：\r\n\r\nSo you need to complete or move the in-progress tickets first.\r\n\r\n如果你想表达“先处理掉这些正在进行中的 ticket”，可以说：\r\n\r\nSo you need to deal with the in-progress tickets first.\r\n\r\n更适合 presentation / team discussion：\r\n\r\nBefore moving on, we need to clear the in-progress tickets first.','如果是在 Jira / sprint 语境里，更自然：\r\n\r\nSo you need to complete or move the in-progress tickets first.\r\n\r\n如果你想表达“先处理掉这些正在进行中的 ticket”，可以说：\r\n\r\nSo you need to deal with the in-progress tickets first.\r\n\r\n更适合 presentation / team discussion：\r\n\r\nBefore moving on, we need to clear the in-progress tickets first.\r\n\r\ntask ticket   任务单  Add login validation\r\n\r\nbug ticket  缺陷单   Fix navbar display issue\r\n\r\nstory ticket  用户故事   As an admin, I can manage users\r\n\r\nimprovement ticket   优化任务   Improve dropdown search\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n所以你需要先处理掉 / 完成那些正在进行中的任务。\r\n\r\n这里的 in-progress tickets 就是：\r\n\r\n正在进行中的任务 / 当前还没完成的 Jira 任务\r\n\r\n更自然中文理解：\r\n\r\nticket = 项目管理系统里的一个工作项。\r\n在 Jira 里特别常见。',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 15:25:44',1,'2026-05-13 15:25:44'),(207,'Everyday Speaking','You’ve done a great job on Sprint 1.','你在 Sprint 1 做得很棒。','',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 15:28:01',1,'2026-05-13 15:28:01'),(208,'Everyday Speaking','It’s hard to find a car park today.','今天停车位很难找','',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 15:59:11',1,'2026-05-13 15:59:11'),(209,'Everyday Speaking','So, you’re doing a Master’s? Is it research-based, or is it mainly coursework? Do you have to write any research papers, or is it mostly lectures and assignments?','所以你在读硕士对吗？这是研究型硕士，还是主要是授课型硕士？你需要写研究论文吗，还是主要是上课和作业？','',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 16:33:48',1,'2026-05-13 16:33:48'),(210,'Everyday Speaking','My master is coursework-based.And sometimes we get really busy. I\'m taking two subjects this semester,and there are a lot of assessments','我的硕士是授课型的，有时候我们会很忙。我这个学期读了两门课会有很多作业','',0,0,1,'2026-05-13 16:36:23',1,'2026-05-13 16:36:23'),(211,'Everyday Speaking','I’ve been exploring some technology-based ways to help people find cheaper groceries. I noticed that grocery prices can vary quite a lot between different stores, even within the same supermarket chain, such as Pak’nSave. So I’m thinking of developing a system, possibly an app, where users can enter their shopping list, and the system will recommend which stores to visit to get the lowest total price overall.','我最近一直在研究一些技术方法，看看怎么找到更便宜的食品杂货。我发现不同商店之间的价格差异挺大的，甚至像 Pak’nSave 这种同一个连锁超市，不同门店价格也可能不一样。所以我在想做一个系统，可能是一个 app，你把购物清单输入进去，它就告诉你应该去哪几家店买，这样总体价格最低。','',0,0,1,'2026-05-14 07:16:21',1,'2026-05-14 07:16:21'),(212,'Everyday Speaking','I saw you posted on WeChat Moments.','我看见你发微信朋友圈了','',0,0,1,'2026-05-14 07:22:26',1,'2026-05-14 07:22:26'),(213,'Everyday Speaking','Okay, we’re going to go through this and look at what loneliness really means. Loneliness is not just about being physically alone or having no people around us. It’s more than that.','好的，我们接下来会一起看一下什么是真正的孤独。孤独并不只是身体上一个人待着，或者身边没有人。它不只是这些。','',0,0,1,'2026-05-14 08:07:58',1,'2026-05-14 08:07:58'),(214,'Everyday Speaking','It’s about feeling unable to communicate our deeper thoughts and emotions, or to express what truly matters to us in our relationships with others.','它是关于一种感觉：我们无法表达自己更深层的想法和情绪，也无法在与他人的关系中表达真正对我们重要的东西。','',0,0,1,'2026-05-14 08:13:55',1,'2026-05-14 08:13:55'),(215,'Everyday Speaking','When I first landed in New Zealand, I was overwhelmed by a deep sense of sadness.','当我第一次抵达新西兰时，我被一种深深的悲伤感淹没了。','如果你想强调“全身都被这种感觉包围”：\r\n\r\nWhen I first landed in New Zealand, I felt a deep sadness wash over me.\r\n\r\n这个很自然，也很有画面感：\r\n\r\nwash over me = 一种情绪突然涌上来 / 淹没我。\r\n最推荐你用：\r\n\r\nWhen I first landed in New Zealand, I felt a deep sadness wash over me.',0,0,1,'2026-05-14 08:50:26',1,'2026-05-14 08:50:26'),(216,'Everyday Speaking','Because I didn’t know anyone here. I had booked a room online, but I wasn’t even sure whether it was a scam. It was my first time staying in a stranger’s house in a foreign country, and I felt an indescribable sense of unease.','因为这里的人我一个也不认识。我在网上订了房间，但我甚至不确定那是不是骗局。那是我第一次在异国他乡住进一个陌生人的家里，我有一种说不出的不安。','更有故事感一点：\r\n\r\nI didn’t know a single person here. I had booked a room online, but I had no idea whether it was real or just a scam. It was my first time staying in a stranger’s house in a foreign country, and I felt this indescribable unease deep inside me.\r\n\r\n几个好用表达：\r\n\r\nI didn’t know a single person here.\r\n这里我一个人都不认识。\r\n\r\nI wasn’t sure whether it was a scam.\r\n我不确定这是不是骗局。\r\n\r\nin a foreign country\r\n在异国他乡\r\n\r\nan indescribable sense of unease\r\n一种说不出的不安\r\n\r\ndeep inside me\r\n在我内心深处',0,0,1,'2026-05-14 08:51:40',1,'2026-05-14 08:51:40'),(217,'Everyday Speaking','Do you want to get it delivered?','你想让送货吗？\r\n\r\n✅ want it delivered\r\n✅ want to get it delivered','更礼貌、店里更自然的说法：\r\n\r\nWould you like it delivered?\r\n您需要送货吗？\r\n\r\n如果你想用新西兰口语确认语气，可以说：\r\n\r\nYou want it delivered, do you?\r\n你是想让它送货，对吧？',0,0,1,'2026-05-17 08:47:08',1,'2026-05-17 08:47:08'),(218,'Everyday Speaking','It’s worth mentioning that','意思是：\r\n\r\n值得一提的是……\r\n\r\n它后面要接一个完整句子。','✅ 用法结构\r\n\r\nIt’s worth mentioning that + 句子\r\n\r\n例句\r\n\r\nIt’s worth mentioning that I also have experience with Python and data processing.\r\n值得一提的是，我也有 Python 和数据处理经验。\r\n\r\nIt’s worth mentioning that this project is closely related to my previous work experience.\r\n值得一提的是，这个项目和我之前的工作经验非常相关。\r\n\r\nIt’s worth mentioning that I have worked with business systems across finance, e-commerce, and telecommunications.\r\n值得一提的是，我曾经做过金融、电商和通信领域的业务系统。\n\nExamples:\n更正式一点\r\n\r\nIt is also worth noting that…\r\n也值得注意的是……\r\n\r\n这个更适合申请、报告、论文。',0,0,1,'2026-05-19 16:21:21',1,'2026-05-19 16:21:21'),(219,'Everyday Speaking','The river flows through a narrow gorge.','过一条狭窄的峡谷','',0,0,1,'2026-05-20 16:06:36',1,'2026-05-20 16:06:36'),(220,'Everyday Speaking','Different perspectives can help us consider an issue more comprehensively.','不同的观点可以帮助我们更全面地考虑一个问题。','更口语一点：\r\n\r\nDifferent viewpoints help us look at a problem from more angles.\r\n不同的观点能帮助我们从更多角度看待一个问题。\r\n\r\n如果是课堂讨论/小组合作里说，可以说：\r\n\r\nHearing different opinions can help us understand the issue more fully.\r\n听到不同的意见可以帮助我们更全面地理解这个问题。',0,0,1,'2026-05-28 07:47:43',1,'2026-05-28 07:47:43'),(221,'Everyday Speaking','How are you finding Christchurch?','你觉得 Christchurch 怎么样？\r\n你在 Christchurch 感觉怎么样？','2. 句子结构\r\n\r\nHow are you finding + 地方 / 事情 / 课程 / 工作？\r\n\r\n意思是：\r\n\r\n你觉得……怎么样？\r\n\r\n例子：\r\n\r\nHow are you finding Christchurch?\r\n你觉得基督城怎么样？\r\n\r\nHow are you finding New Zealand so far?\r\n到目前为止，你觉得新西兰怎么样？\r\n\r\nHow are you finding the course?\r\n你觉得这门课怎么样？\r\n\r\nHow are you finding your new job?\r\n你觉得你的新工作怎么样？\r\n\r\n4. 自然回答方式\r\n\r\n简单回答\r\n\r\nI’m finding Christchurch really nice.\r\n我觉得基督城很不错。\r\n\r\nI’m finding it quite peaceful.\r\n我觉得这里挺安静的。\r\n\r\nI’m finding it a bit quiet, but very comfortable.\r\n我觉得这里有点安静，但很舒服。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n5. 更适合你的回答\r\n\r\nI’m finding Christchurch really nice. It’s quieter than Beijing, and the lifestyle is more relaxed. I’m still getting used to the language and local culture, but overall I like it here.\r\n\r\n中文意思：\r\n\r\n我觉得基督城很不错。它比北京安静，生活节奏也更轻松。我还在适应语言和当地文化，但总体来说我很喜欢这里。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n6. 面试 / 聊天中更自然的回答\r\n\r\nI’m finding it really good so far. People are friendly, and the pace of life is much more relaxed. It’s a bit different from what I was used to in China, but I’m enjoying it.\r\n\r\n中文意思：\r\n\r\n到目前为止我觉得挺好的。这里的人很友好，生活节奏也轻松很多。和我以前在中国习惯的生活有点不同，但我挺享受这里的。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n7. 记忆技巧 🧠\r\n\r\nHow are you finding…?\r\n\r\n不要理解成：\r\n\r\n你怎么找到……？\r\n\r\n而要理解成：\r\n\r\n你觉得……怎么样？\r\n\r\n一句话记住：\r\n\r\nfind = feel about / think about\r\n\r\n所以：\r\n\r\nHow are you finding Christchurch?\r\n= What do you think of Christchurch?',0,0,1,'2026-06-09 14:22:37',1,'2026-06-09 14:22:37'),(222,'Everyday Speaking','Could you walk me through your end-to-end business workflow? For instance, how does user data get input, what processing steps are involved, how does it flow into your ERP system, and what results or outcomes does the user receive from that system?','你能带我了解一下你们端到端的业务流程吗？\r\n\r\n例如：用户数据是如何录入的？中间会经过哪些处理步骤？这些数据是如何流转到你们的 ERP 系统中的？最终，系统会向用户或业务方输出什么结果或成果？','',0,0,1,'2026-06-22 10:43:43',1,'2026-06-22 10:43:43'),(223,'Everyday Speaking','I wonder if that’s a normal situation or an exception.','我想知道这是一个正常的情况还是例外情况','🎯 核心意思\r\n\r\n这句话是在不确定某个情况是否正常时，用来礼貌询问：\r\n\r\nI wonder if…\r\n我想知道是否……\r\n\r\na normal situation\r\n一种正常情况\r\n\r\nor an exception\r\n还是一个例外 / 异常情况\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🧩 常见用法\r\n\r\n① I wonder if…\r\n\r\n= 我想知道是否……\r\n\r\n这是很常用、也比较委婉的表达。\r\n\r\nI wonder if this is expected.\r\n我想知道这是不是预期的。\r\n\r\nI wonder if we need to handle this case.\r\n我想知道我们是否需要处理这种情况。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n② normal situation\r\n\r\n= 正常情况\r\n\r\nIs this a normal situation?\r\n这是正常情况吗？\r\n\r\n不过技术讨论里，经常更自然地说：\r\n\r\nIs this normal?\r\n这正常吗？\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n③ an exception\r\n\r\n= 一个例外 / 特殊情况\r\n\r\nThis is an exception.\r\n这是一个例外情况。\r\n\r\nWe need to handle this exception separately.\r\n我们需要单独处理这个异常情况。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n💬 例句\r\n\r\nI wonder if that’s a normal situation or an exception.\r\n我想知道这是一种正常情况，还是一个例外。\r\n\r\nI wonder if this happens regularly or only in exceptional cases.\r\n我想知道这种情况是经常发生，还是只在特殊情况下发生。\r\n\r\nI wonder if this is expected behavior or an exception.\r\n我想知道这是预期行为，还是异常情况。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n⚠️ 常见错误\r\n\r\n❌ I wonder it that…\r\n✅ I wonder if…\r\n\r\nwonder 后面询问“是否”，通常用：\r\n\r\nwonder if\r\n或\r\nwonder whether\r\n\r\n例如：\r\n\r\nI wonder whether this is normal.\r\n我想知道这是否正常。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n❌ an exception one\r\n\r\n✅ an exception\r\n\r\n因为 exception 本身就是名词，不需要再加 one。\r\n\r\n⸻\r\n\r\n🔍 对比学习\r\n\r\nI wonder if…\r\n\r\n语气比较委婉：\r\n\r\nI wonder if this is normal.\r\n我想知道这是否正常。\r\n\r\nIs this normal?\r\n\r\n更直接：\r\n\r\nIs this normal?\r\n这正常吗？\r\n\r\nexpected behavior\r\n\r\n= 预期行为\r\n\r\n在软件开发语境里比 normal situation 更专业：\r\n\r\nI wonder if this is expected behavior or an exception.\r\n我想知道这是预期行为还是异常情况。\r\n\r\n⭐ 技术讨论里，我最推荐你记住：\r\n\r\nI wonder if this is expected behavior or an exception.\r\n\r\n= 我想知道这是预期行为，还是异常情况。',0,0,1,'2026-08-17 18:51:49',1,'2026-08-17 18:51:49');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `everyday_sentence` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;

--
-- Table structure for table `interview_answer_section`
--

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS `interview_answer_section`;
/*!40101 SET @saved_cs_client     = @@character_set_client */;
/*!50503 SET character_set_client = utf8mb4 */;
CREATE TABLE `interview_answer_section` (
  `id` bigint unsigned NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT COMMENT '主键ID',
  `question_id` bigint unsigned NOT NULL COMMENT '面试题ID',
  `section_type` varchar(50) COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci NOT NULL COMMENT '分段类型，如 situation/action/result/learning',
  `section_title` varchar(100) COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci DEFAULT NULL COMMENT '分段标题',
  `content_en` longtext COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci COMMENT '英文内容',
  `content_cn` longtext COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci COMMENT '中文内容',
  `sort_order` int NOT NULL DEFAULT '0' COMMENT '排序值',
  `created_by` bigint NOT NULL COMMENT '创建人ID',
  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP COMMENT '创建时间',
  `updated_by` bigint DEFAULT NULL COMMENT '更新人ID',
  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP COMMENT '更新时间',
  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),
  KEY `idx_question_id` (`question_id`),
  KEY `idx_section_type` (`section_type`)
) ENGINE=InnoDB AUTO_INCREMENT=17 DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci COMMENT='面试题答案结构分段表';
/*!40101 SET character_set_client = @saved_cs_client */;

--
-- Dumping data for table `interview_answer_section`
--

LOCK TABLES `interview_answer_section` WRITE;
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `interview_answer_section` DISABLE KEYS */;
INSERT INTO `interview_answer_section` VALUES (1,1,'situation','Situation','I worked on a web application project with several teammates, and each of us was responsible for a different part of the system, such as frontend, app client, and backend.','我参与了一个 Web 应用项目，团队成员分别负责前端、客户端和后端等不同部分。',1,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(2,1,'action','What I Did','I mainly handled backend API design and development. I aligned with teammates on project structure, coding style, and interface contracts, and I kept regular communication during development and integration.','我主要负责后端 API 设计与开发，并在开发和联调过程中持续和队友沟通，提前确认接口规范。',2,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(3,1,'result','Result','We completed the project on time, and the final system worked well as a whole.','我们按时完成了项目，整个系统最终运行良好。',3,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(4,1,'learning','What I Learned','I learned that good teamwork is not only about completing your own tasks, but also about communication, coordination, and helping the whole team move forward.','我学到，良好的团队合作不仅是完成自己的任务，更重要的是沟通、协作和推动团队整体向前。',4,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(5,2,'situation','Situation','In a cloud drive project, a teammate and I had different opinions on how to standardize API responses.','在一个云盘项目中，我和一位同事在 API 返回格式的设计方案上有分歧。',1,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(6,2,'action','What I Did','I explained the benefits of a unified response wrapper, listened to his concerns about returning raw data, and discussed possible trade-offs with him.','我说明了统一返回格式的好处，也认真听取了他关于原始数据返回场景的顾虑，并一起讨论折中方案。',2,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(7,2,'result','Result','We created an annotation-based switch to control when wrapping should apply. The solution resolved the disagreement and was later adopted by other teams.','我们最终做了一个基于注解的开关功能，既解决了分歧，这个方案后来也被部门其他团队采纳。',3,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(8,2,'learning','What I Learned','I learned that team conflict should be handled by focusing on the problem, respecting different viewpoints, and finding a practical solution.','我学到，处理团队分歧时，关键在于聚焦问题本身、尊重不同观点，并共同寻找可执行的解决方案。',4,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(9,5,'situation','Situation','A teammate was facing an integration issue between frontend and backend because the API response did not match what the frontend expected.','一位队友在前后端联调时遇到了问题，因为 API 返回格式和前端预期不一致。',1,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(10,5,'action','What I Did','I checked the API response, explained the backend logic, and helped adjust the response structure to make it easier for the frontend to use.','我检查了接口返回，解释了后端逻辑，并帮助调整返回结构，让前端更容易接入。',2,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(11,5,'result','Result','The issue was resolved quickly, and my teammate could continue working without further delay.','问题很快得到解决，队友也能继续推进工作而没有进一步延误。',3,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(12,5,'learning','What I Learned','I learned that helping teammates improves both project efficiency and trust within the team.','我学到，主动帮助队友不仅能提升项目效率，也能增强团队之间的信任。',4,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(13,7,'situation','Situation','Our team underestimated the time needed for integration and testing, and compatibility issues appeared when we combined different modules.','我们团队低估了联调和测试所需时间，当不同模块整合在一起时出现了兼容性问题。',1,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(14,7,'action','What I Did','I helped identify the highest-priority issues, rechecked module interfaces, and improved communication to solve the most critical problems first.','我帮助团队先识别最优先的问题，重新检查模块接口，并加强沟通来优先解决最关键的问题。',2,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(15,7,'result','Result','Although the project became more stressful than expected, we still completed the main requirements.','虽然项目过程比预期更紧张，但我们最终还是完成了主要需求。',3,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16'),(16,7,'learning','What I Learned','I learned that teamwork is not only about dividing tasks. It also requires continuous alignment during the whole project.','我学到，团队合作不只是分工，还需要在整个项目过程中持续保持对齐。',4,1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16',1,'2026-04-07 14:35:16');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `interview_answer_section` ENABLE KEYS */;
